^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="PERSON CLASS file patch."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,2,0)="User documentation for this patch in PDF (Portable Document Format) is"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,3,0)="available on the Infrastructure Home Page at"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,4,0)="http://www.vista.domain.ext/softserv/infrastr.uct/ under New"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,5,0)="Person file.  The PDF documentation may also be retrieved from the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,6,0)="anonymous directories at Hines, Albany, and Salt Lake City with the "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,7,0)="filename of 'XU_8_27.pdf'. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,9,0)="This patch adds a new file PERSON CLASS (8932.1) with data.  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,10,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,11,0)="NOTE: The file PERSON CLASS is in global ^USC.  This will be a NEW global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,12,0)="for most sites. Please be sure to place this global and add it to your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,13,0)="translation tables.  This is a static file."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,14,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,15,0)="The patch also:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,16,0)="Adds a PERSON CLASS field to the NEW PERSON file.  This multiple includes"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,17,0)="the following fields:  NUMBER (.001),  PERSON CLASS (.01), EFFECTIVE DATE"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,18,0)="(2), EXPIRATION DATE (3)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,20,0)="Adds the PERSON CLASS field to the following options: Edit an Existing"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,21,0)="User, Add a New User to the System, and Reactivate a User."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,23,0)="Adds three  new menu options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,25,0)="PERSON CLASS EDIT ,(XU-PERSON CLASS EDIT), to the User Management menu."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,26,0)="This option only allows entry of PERSON CLASS data."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,28,0)="User PC Build Print, (XUSER PC BUILD) to print the entries of the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,29,0)="individuals in the NEW PERSON file who hold the Provider key AND have a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,30,0)="Verify Code.  It prints these fields:  NAME, PROVIDER CLASS (free text),"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,31,0)="and PROVIDER TYPE (set of codes).  The last two fields may contain data"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,32,0)="only at sites that have implemented Decision Support System (DSS).  This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,33,0)="option is not attached to a menu but may be added to the secondary menu of"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,34,0)="any user who will be working on this project."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,36,0)="User PC Build Edit, (XUSER PC BUILD EDIT), a straight DIE option to allow"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,37,0)="fast entry of PERSON CLASS data.  This option is not attached to a menu"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,38,0)="but may be added to the secondary menu of a user who will be performing"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,39,0)="data entry."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,40,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,41,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,42,0)=" routine         new checksum"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,43,0)=" XUA4A72           1853480"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,44,0)=" ========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,46,0)=" Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,47,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,48,0)="   1.  This is a new routine and will not be mapped on any systems."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,49,0)="   2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,50,0)="        This option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,51,0)="   3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,52,0)="        system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,53,0)="        On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,54,0)="        options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,55,0)="             Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,56,0)="             Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,57,0)="             Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,58,0)="             Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,59,0)="   4.  Users can remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,60,0)="   5.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,61,0)="       option:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,62,0)="             Install Package(s)  'XU*8.0*27'"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,63,0)="   6.  MSM Sites - Answer YES to the question 'Want to MOVE routines to"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,64,0)="       other CPUs?'. Enter the names of your Compute and Print server(s)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,65,0)="   7.  AXP Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,66,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,67,0)=" ========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,68,0)=" SUPPORTED REFERENCE."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,69,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,70,0)=" $$GET^XUA4A72(duz[, date])"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,71,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,72,0)="   Returns the 'IEN^Profession^Specialty^Sub-specialty^Effect date"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,73,0)="   ^Expired date^VA code' for the person identified by the DUZ in effect"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,74,0)="   on the date passed in (TODAY if no date passed in). The date is in"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,75,0)="   internal format."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,77,0)="   Returns -1 if DUZ doesn't point to a valid user or user has never had a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,78,0)="   Person Class assigned. Returns -2 if no active Person Class on that"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,79,0)="   date.   "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,81,0)="   $$IEN2CODE^XUA4A72(ien)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,82,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,83,0)="   Returns the VA CODE from the Person Class file that corresponds to "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,84,0)="   the IEN number passed in.  If the IEN isn't valid it returns the empty"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,85,0)="   string."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,86,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,87,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",18,1,88,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,0)="42^2960923^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,0)="^^47^47^2960923"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,1,0)="*** Patch for MSM sites ***"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,3,0)="This patch changes ZU (for MSM) to look in the TASKMAN SITE PARAMETERS"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,4,0)="file for the TASK PARTITION SIZE field. If this field has data then a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,5,0)="call is made to the MSM utility %PARTSIZ to change the jobs partition"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,6,0)="size limit.  TASKMAN will also use this value in its job command when"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,7,0)="starting a new submanager.  This will allow sites to reduce the default"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,8,0)="partition size in SYSGEN, increasing the number of disk buffers."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,9,0)="This will allow sites to adjust partition site for running PCE.  Look"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,10,0)="to the Cookbook to come out with recommendations on settings.  If unsure"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,11,0)="what value to use leave the TASK PARTITION SIZE field blank and your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,12,0)="current sysgen value will be used."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,15,0)="routine             new checksum"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,16,0)="ZTM0                  5451877"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,17,0)="ZUMSM                 2237614"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,18,0)="========================================================================= "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,19,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,21,0)=" 1.  This patch is only for MSM sites."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,22,0)=" 2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,23,0)="     option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,24,0)=" 3.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,25,0)="     options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,26,0)="        Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,27,0)="        Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,28,0)="        Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,29,0)="        Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,30,0)="        Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,31,0)=" 4.  Stop TASKMAN."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,32,0)=" 5.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,33,0)="     options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,34,0)="        Install Package(s)  'XU*8.0*42'"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,35,0)=" 6.  MSM Sites - Answer YES to the question 'Want to MOVE routines to"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,36,0)="     other CPUs?'. Enter the names of your Compute and Print server(s)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,37,0)=" 7.  After installing this patch, you need to one routine from "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,38,0)="      your productions account to the manager account:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,39,0)="      ZTM0"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,40,0)="      and in the manager account rename"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,41,0)="      ZTM0        to %ZTM0"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,42,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,43,0)="       Example: ZL ZTM0 ZS %ZTM0"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,44,0)="       "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,45,0)=" 8.  Restart TASKMAN."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",19,1,47,0)=" ==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,0)="35^2961008^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,0)="^^26^26^2961008"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,1,0)="This is an update to %ZOSV2 for VAX/ALPHA sites only. It supports updates"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,2,0)="to VPM (Kernel Toolkit's VMS Performance Monitor) and must be installed"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,3,0)="prior to installing Kernel Toolkit patch XT*7.3*17."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,5,0)="ROUTINE        CHECKSUM"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,6,0)="-------       ----------"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,7,0)="ZOSV2VXD  value = 9513833 "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,9,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,10,0)="  1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,11,0)="     option will load the KIDS package in this message onto your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,12,0)="  2. Answer NO to the question: "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,13,0)="     'Shall I preserve what is on disk in a separate back-up message ?' "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,14,0)="  3. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,15,0)="     'Verify Checksums in Transport Global' and verify that all routines "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,16,0)="     have the correct checksum.  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,17,0)="  4. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,18,0)="'Install Package(s).' Select the package and proceed with install."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,20,0)="  5. After installing this patch, you need to move the routine from "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,21,0)="     your production account to the manager account: "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,23,0)="     ZOSV2VXD"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,25,0)="  6. Rename the routine to, ""%ZOSV2."" If this routine is mapped, be sure"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",20,1,26,0)="to disable mapping of this routine."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,0)="44^2961028^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,0)="^^186^186^2961028"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,1,0)=" This patch contains the following features:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,3,0)=" DAY-0996-41414"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,4,0)=" -Fixes undef error in XPDIK when install patch with DD's."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,5,0)=" FRE-0996-60791, ANN-0996-41556"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,6,0)=" -Fixes subscript error when converting a package."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,7,0)=" REN-1095-62643, BOI-1095-53144, MUS-0696-70425"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,8,0)=" -Fixes nouci errors when MenuMan's Micro-surgery runs on MSM sites."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,9,0)=" BEC-0996-21668"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,10,0)=" -Fixes bug that left ^XTMP(""XPDI"", global for certain patches."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,11,0)="-Fixes bug when Environment Check Routine is run during the load process and"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,12,0)="  the variable XPDQUIT or XPDABORT is set to 2. The Install file would be"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,13,0)="  incomplete and the install would get an undef error."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,14,0)="-New message, if the Install file is incomplete the user will get the message"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,15,0)="  '**INSTALL FILE CORRUPTED**', and the install will abort."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,16,0)="-New Alerts will be sent to the installer if an error occurs during the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,17,0)="  install process or if a CPU is not updated."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,18,0)="-New options: Routines by Patch Number, Display Patches for a Package,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,19,0)="  Rollup Patches into a Build, and Check Routines on Other CPUs."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,20,0)="-New type of Build, MULTI-PACKAGE. It contains a list of other Builds."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,21,0)="-New field, REQUIRED BUILD #11, in file BUILD #9.6."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,22,0)="-New field, SIGNON/PRODUCTION VOLUME SET #9, in file VOLUME SET #14.5."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,23,0)="-KIDS will support HL7 type fields in the Protocol file, #101."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,24,0)="-KIDS will also support the following files as components:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,25,0)="  MAIL GROUP #3.8"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,26,0)="  HL7 APPLICATION PARAMETER #771"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,27,0)="  HL LOWER LEVEL PROTOCOL PARAMETER #869.2"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,28,0)="  HL LOGICAL LINK #870"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,29,0)="=============================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,30,0)="                    **** INSTALL INSTRUCTIONS ****"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,31,0)="=============================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,32,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,33,0)="This patch should be installed during off-peak hours. Users can be on the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,34,0)="system, but no other users should be using KIDS while you install this patch."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,35,0)="Since this patch is an update to KIDS, no other patches should be installed"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,36,0)="during the installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,37,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,38,0)="**MSM sites must manually move the routines XPDIJ and XPDCPU to their other"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,39,0)="  CPUs. KIDS cannot automatically move these routines for you.**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,40,0)="=============================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,41,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,42,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,43,0)="  1.  These routines are usually mapped on systems that allow mapping,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,44,0)="      so you will need to disable mapping for the effected routines."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,45,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,46,0)="      option will load the KIDS Distribution onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,47,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,48,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the patch in the Transport"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,49,0)="      global."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,50,0)="  4.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,51,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,52,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,53,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,54,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,55,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,56,0)="         Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,57,0)="  5.  MSM Sites - Answer YES to the question 'Want to MOVE routines to"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,58,0)="      other CPUs?'. Enter the names of your Compute and Print server(s)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,59,0)="  6.  MSM Sites - D ^%RCOPY to move the routine XPDIJ and XPDCPU to your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,60,0)="      other CPUs."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,61,0)="  7.  Move the routine ZTPTCH to your Manager Account(s) and rename as %ZTPTCH"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,62,0)="      on all systems where the users can signon through ZU."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,63,0)="  8.  AXP Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,64,0)="  9.  MSM Sites - You should edit the SIGNON/PRODUCTION VOLUME SET field using"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,65,0)="      the 'Volume Set Edit' option under the 'Edit Taskman Parameters' menu."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,66,0)="      Enter 'YES' for your Compute and Printer servers. Enter 'NO' for your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,67,0)="      File servers."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,68,0)=" 10.  MSM Sites - Drop into programmer mode and DO KICK^XQ7. This will start"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,69,0)="      Micro-surgery on all the servers you just edited in the VOLUME SET file."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,70,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,71,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,72,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,73,0)="   The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,74,0)="       ;;8.0;KERNEL;**[patch list]**;Jul 10, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,76,0)=" Name           Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",21,1,77,0)=" -----------------------------------------------------------"
