^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,25,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,26,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,27,0)="========================================================================= "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,28,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,29,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,30,0)="  1.  DSM sites - Some of these routines may be mapped,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,31,0)="      so you will need to disable mapping for the affected routines. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,32,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,33,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,34,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,35,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,36,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,37,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,38,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,39,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,40,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,41,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,42,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,43,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,44,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,45,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,46,0)="  4.  Users can remain on the system. This patch can be loaded any"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,47,0)="      non-peak time."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,48,0)="      This patch can also be queued for install at non-peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,49,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,50,0)="  5.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,51,0)="      option:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,52,0)="        Install Package(s)  'XU*8.0*115'"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,53,0)="                             =========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,54,0)="                             "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,55,0)="        No Options or Protocols need to be placed out-of-order."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,56,0)="        Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,57,0)="                                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,58,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,59,0)="  6.  DSM Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",105,1,60,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",106,0)="124 SEQ #111^2990914^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,0)="118 SEQ #112^2991002^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,0)="^^175^175^2991002"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,1,0)="HOU-0399-73122 "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,2,0)="  As part of the overall work the error that this site was getting has been"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,3,0)="  fixed. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,4,0)="  ZTLOAD will reject requests to queue to a device the has QUEUING field "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,5,0)="  set to NOT ALLOWED."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,6,0)="  ZTLOAD1, ZTLOAD2, ZISUTL"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,8,0)="SAG-0699-40716"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,9,0)="LIT-0199-70997"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,10,0)="MOM-0799-52593"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,11,0)="AMA-0799-72651"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,12,0)="SPO-0799-52388"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,13,0)="  This patch has updates to allow Cache sites to run taskman on two or more"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,14,0)="  nodes at the same time.  How locking was being used with the IO queue was"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,15,0)="  changed to use ^%ZTSCH(""DEV"",io) in its place. This should allow more than"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,16,0)="  one sub-manager to look at the ""IO"" list at the same time.  If there is a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,17,0)="  delay in one device it will not delay other devices.  The submanagers now"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,18,0)="  keep a list of available submanagers as well as there count. The option"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,19,0)="  ""XUTM QCLEAN"" will reset the count as part of its work.  Each lock timeout"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,20,0)="  was checked for constancy.  Changes to make the STARTUP flag in the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,21,0)="  OPTION SCHEDULE file work better."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,22,0)="  ZTM*, XUTMK, XUTMG19"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,23,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,24,0)="  The code to share licenses when GUI and Telnet users from the same work"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,25,0)="  station are connected is in place and ZU now calls it.  There will be a "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,26,0)="  broker patch to follow that will complete the work. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,27,0)="  ZOSVONT, ZOSVVXD, ZOSVMSM, ZUONT, ZUVXD"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,28,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,29,0)="SAG-0599-42045  ZISTCPS There wasn't any way to stop the listener other than"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,30,0)="HL7 Team        ZTLOAD  the use of JOBEXAM/FORCEX.  Changed to have listener"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,31,0)="                ZTLOAD2 check for LOGON INHIBIT and call $$S^%ZTLOAD to see if"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,32,0)="                        the task has been asked to stop."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,33,0)="                ZTER    The entry point UNWIND^%ZTER would return 0 to a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,34,0)="                        calling function.  This has been changed to -9 to"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,35,0)="                        make it easier to tell if return is from the "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,36,0)="                        error trap.         "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,37,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,38,0)="Routine Summary"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,39,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,40,0)="of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",107,1,41,0)=" ;;8.0;KERNEL;<patchlist>;Jul 10, 1995"
