^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,112,0)="NOTE: When patch has completed loading proceed with the following steps:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,115,0)="    1.  From Programmers Mode, execute the following routine:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,117,0)="        >D ^XUYDEV "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,120,0)="    2.  Next the routine will display:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,122,0)="        The Following Data Has Been Added To File #8989.518"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,123,0)="        ===================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,124,0)="        DEVICE"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,125,0)="        DEV"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,126,0)="        Device"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,127,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,129,0)="        Press the return key to continue or '^' to exit:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",115,1,130,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,0)="140 SEQ #121^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,0)="^^72^72^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,1,0)="    Y2K Waiver Request ID#:Y2KW0001   Y2K Waiver Status: Approved"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,2,0)="    this patch may be installed during the Y2K Moratorium, AFTER "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,3,0)="    1/15/2000."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,5,0)="1.  BRX-1197-11294."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,6,0)="    When using the 'Option Access By User' option and a user has not"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,7,0)="    previously logged on to the system, the Last on date is displayed"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,8,0)="    errouneously.  Routine XQ55 have been revised to display a null"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,9,0)="    last on date, should last on date for a user contain a blank date"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,10,0)="    and time."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,13,0)="Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,14,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,15,0)="Martinsburg, WV - 613"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,16,0)="Bronx, NY - 526"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,19,0)="Routine Summary:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,20,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,21,0)="The following routine(s) are included in this patch.  The second line of"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,22,0)="each routine will look like:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,24,0)="            <tab>;;8.0;KERNEL;**[Patch List]**;09/20/96"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,26,0)="Checksums:   CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,27,0)="=========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,29,0)="Rtn Nm            Chksum Before   Chksum After             Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,30,0)="====================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,31,0)="XQ55                   10774418       10830712                140"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,34,0)="Installation Instruction:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,35,0)="========================"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,36,0)="1. Users are allowed to be on the system during the Installation."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,38,0)="2. Routine mapping is NOT recommended for these routines."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,40,0)="3. Use the ""INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE"" option on the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,41,0)="loads the patch into a Transport Global onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,43,0)="4. You Do Not need to stop TaskMan or the background filers."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,44,0)="   (AXP Sites - Place TaskMan in a WAIT state."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,45,0)="   OpenM/Cache Sites - STOP TaskMan.)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,48,0)="5. On the KIDS menu, select the ""Installation"" menu and use the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,49,0)="   following options to install the Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,51,0)="  Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,52,0)="  Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,53,0)="  Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,54,0)="  Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,56,0)="  Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,57,0)="             INSTALL NAME:  XU*8.0*140"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,58,0)="                            =========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,60,0)="  Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,61,0)="                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,62,0)="  Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,63,0)="  Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,64,0)="                   ==   "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,66,0)="6. AXP Sites - Answer NO to the question ""Want to MOVE routines"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,67,0)="   to other CPUs?"""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,69,0)="7. If the routines were unmapped, the mapped set should be rebuilt"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,70,0)="   once the installation has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",116,1,72,0)="8. AXP and OpenM/Cache Sites Only - Remove TaskMan from a WAIT/STOP state."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,0)="141 SEQ #122^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,0)="^^91^91^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,1,0)="While investigating NOIS DAY-0200-40034 a leap year problem was found in"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,2,0)="SCH^XLFDT. This would affect tasks scheduled for the last day of the month."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,3,0)="Taskman uses this routine to evaluate the RESCHEDULING FREQUENCY field in "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,4,0)="the Option Scheduling file."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,5,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,6,0)="Also fixed is a looping problem if the schedule requests a day beyond the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,7,0)="end of the month. Like 30th of each month for February or 31st for April."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,8,0)="Now it will default to the LAST DAY of the month.  This would make a schedule"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,9,0)="of ""1M(30@2200)"" for February be eveluated as ""1M(L@2200)""."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,10,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,11,0)="Sites should use the following to see if any tasks are affected by evaluating"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,12,0)="the QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME field to see if it appropriate for the task."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,13,0)="Look for task that should have been scheduled for Feb 29,2000."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,14,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,15,0)="Select OPTION: PRINT FILE ENTRIES  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,16,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,17,0)="OUTPUT FROM WHAT FILE: // 19.2  OPTION SCHEDULING"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,18,0)="                                          (13 entries)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,19,0)="SORT BY: NUMBER// 2  QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,20,0)="START WITH QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME: FIRST// FEB 15,2000  (FEB 15, 2000)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,21,0)="GO TO QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME: LAST// MAR 1,2000  (MAR 01, 2000@24:00)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,22,0)="  WITHIN QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME, SORT BY: "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,23,0)="FIRST PRINT FIELD: .01  NAME"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,24,0)="THEN PRINT FIELD: 2;L19  QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,25,0)="THEN PRINT FIELD: 6;L20  RESCHEDULING FREQUENCY"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,26,0)="THEN PRINT FIELD: "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,27,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,28,0)="  *************************"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,29,0)="Heading (S/C): OPTION SCHEDULING LIST  Replace "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,30,0)="STORE PRINT LOGIC IN TEMPLATE: "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,31,0)="START AT PAGE: 1// "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,32,0)="DEVICE:   SYSTEM"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,33,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,34,0)="...SORRY, HOLD ON..."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,35,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,36,0)="OPTION SCHEDULING LIST                         FEB  9,2000  12:44    PAGE 1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,37,0)="                                QUEUED TO RUN AT     RESCHEDULING"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,38,0)="NAME                            WHAT TIME            FREQUENCY"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,39,0)="----------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,40,0)="JOES SPECIAL                    FEB 28,2000  22:00   1M(L@2200)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,41,0)="XUTM PROBLEM DEVICES            FEB 28,2000  21:00   1M(15@2100,L@2100)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,42,0)="----------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,43,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,44,0)="Routine Summary"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,45,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,46,0)="of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,47,0)=" ;;8.0;KERNEL;<patchlist>;Jul 10, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,48,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,49,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,50,0)="Routine         Old       New      2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,51,0)="XLFDT2        3530137   3576737    **71,86,141**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,52,0)="XLFDT3        6415507   5174266    **71,120,141**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,53,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,54,0)="List of preceding patches: 86, 120"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,55,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,56,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,57,0)="========================================================================= "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,58,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,59,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,60,0)=">>>Users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,61,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,62,0)="  1.  DSM sites - Some of these routines are usually mapped,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,63,0)="      so you will need to disable mapping for the affected routines. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,64,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,65,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,66,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,67,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,68,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,69,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,70,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,71,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,72,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,73,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,74,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,75,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,76,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,77,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,78,0)="  4.  Users can remain on the system. This patch can be loaded any"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,79,0)="      non-peakpeak time."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,80,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,81,0)="  5.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,82,0)="      option:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,83,0)="        Install Package(s)  'XU*8.0*141'"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,84,0)="                             =========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,85,0)="                             "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,86,0)="        No Options or Protocols need to be placed out-of-order."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,87,0)="        Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,88,0)="                                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,89,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,90,0)="  6.  DSM Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",117,1,91,0)=" ========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",118,0)="137 SEQ #123^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,0)="130 SEQ #124^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,0)="^^78^78^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,1,0)="    This patch may not be installed during the Y2K Leap Year Lockdown"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,2,0)="    period of 2/28/2000 to 3/3/2000."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,5,0)="1.  MWV-0997-20795."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,6,0)="    When setting defaults to a print type option, then accessing the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,7,0)="    option thru Edit option, Edit option overwrites any defaults that"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,8,0)="    were previously set, should a template be selected.  The routine"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,9,0)="    XQ5 has been revised to display to user a list of current defaults."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,11,0)="    Inaddition input template XUEDITOPT has been revised to allow Broker"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,12,0)="    type options to prompt for RPCKEY and RULES fields."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,16,0)="Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,17,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,18,0)="Martinsburg, WV - 613"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,19,0)="Bronx, NY - 526"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,22,0)="Routine Summary:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,23,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,24,0)="The following routine(s) are included in this patch.  The second line of"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,25,0)="each routine will look like:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,26,0)=" "
