^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,32,0)="Rtn Nm         Chksum Before     Chksum After            Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,33,0)="===================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,34,0)="XQ5                 13875754         16374150              44,130"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,37,0)="Installation Instruction:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,38,0)="========================"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,39,0)="1. Users are allowed to be on the system during the Installation."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,41,0)="2. Routine mapping is NOT recommended for these routines.  If you"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,42,0)="are using routine mapping, review your mapped set and ensure that"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,43,0)="these routines are NOT in your mapped routine set before proceeding"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,44,0)="and rebuild your map set afterward before reactivating TaskMan."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,46,0)="3. Use the ""INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE"" option on the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,47,0)="loads the patch into a Transport Global onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,49,0)="4. You Do Not need to stop TaskMan or the background filers."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,50,0)="   (AXP Sites - Place TaskMan in a WAIT state."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,51,0)="   OpenM/Cache Sites - STOP TaskMan.)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,54,0)="5. On the KIDS menu, select the ""Installation"" menu and use the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,55,0)="   following options to install the Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,57,0)="  Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,58,0)="  Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,59,0)="  Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,60,0)="  Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,62,0)="  Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,63,0)="             INSTALL NAME:  XU*8.0*130"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,64,0)="                            =========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,66,0)="  Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,67,0)="                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,68,0)="  Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,69,0)="  Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,70,0)="                   ==   "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,72,0)="6. AXP Sites - Answer NO to the question ""Want to MOVE routines"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,73,0)="   to other CPUs?"""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,75,0)="7. If the routines were unmapped, the mapped set should be rebuilt"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,76,0)="   once the installation has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",119,1,78,0)="8. AXP and OpenM/Cache Sites Only - Remove TaskMan from a WAIT/STOP state."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",120,0)="122^3000313^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",120,1,0)="^^1^1^3000313"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",120,1,1,0)="RUM updates."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",121,0)="144 SEQ #126^3000405^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,0)="106 SEQ #127^3000417^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,0)="^^35^35^3000417"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,1,0)="Get discription from the web."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,3,0)="========================================================================= "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,4,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,5,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,6,0)="  1.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,7,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,8,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,9,0)="  2.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,10,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,11,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,12,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,13,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,14,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,15,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,16,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,17,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,18,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,19,0)="  3.  Users can remain on the system. This patch can be loaded any"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,20,0)="      non-peakpeak time."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,21,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,22,0)="  4.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,23,0)="      option:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,24,0)="        Install Package(s)  'XU*8.0*106'"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,25,0)="                             =========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,26,0)="                             "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,27,0)="        No Options or Protocols need to be placed out-of-order."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,28,0)="        Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,29,0)="                                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,30,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,31,0)="  5.  After the install there is a part of the conversion that must"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,32,0)="      be done by a user."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,33,0)="      Now ""D MANUAL^XUINPCH2"" to convert the ones that need user input."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",122,1,35,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",123,0)="134 SEQ #128^3000417^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",123,1,0)="^^1^1^3000417"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",123,1,1,0)="See XU*8.0*134 of the National Patch Module for full documentation."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",124,0)="145 SEQ #129^3000417^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",125,0)="146 SEQ #130^3000501^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,0)="142 SEQ #131^3000502^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,0)="^^76^76^3000502"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,1,0)="This Patch installs a routine that can do a DNS lookup to convert a "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,2,0)="domain name to an IP address. This routine has two supported API's."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,3,0)="The change by VISN's to the 10. private IP addressing pushed the need"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,4,0)="for this patch. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,5,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,6,0)="***************IMPORTANT*********************************************"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,7,0)="This patch is used by HL7 patch HL*1.6*63."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,8,0)="The POST install will enter the address of one of the national "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,9,0)="DNS servers.  PLEASE CHANGE TO THE CORRECT ONE FOR YOUR SITE."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,10,0)="IF YOU ARE INSTALLING THIS PATCH IN A TEST ENVIRONMENT ALONG WITH HL7"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,11,0)="PATCH 63, DO NOT POINT TO A PRODUCTION DNS! THIS COULD RESULT IN"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,12,0)="TRANSMITTING TEST HL7 MESSAGES TO A SITE'S PRODUCTION SYSTEM."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,13,0)="The install will test for a HL7 test parameter and not install the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,14,0)="default DNS address in this case.  PLEASE CHECK."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,15,0)="********************************************************************** "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,16,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,17,0)="See DBIA# 3056 for documentation on the API's."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,18,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,19,0)="There is a entry point for testing: TEST^XLFNSLK"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,20,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,21,0)="Routine Summary"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,22,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,23,0)="of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,24,0)=" ;;8.0;KERNEL;<patchlist>;June 25, 1999"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,25,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,26,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,27,0)="Routine         Old       New      2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,28,0)="XLFNSLK                 7523173    **142**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,29,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,30,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,31,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,32,0)="========================================================================= "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,33,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,34,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,35,0)=">>>Users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,36,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,37,0)="  1.  DSM sites - This is a new routine."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,38,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,39,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,40,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,41,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,42,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,43,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,44,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,45,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,46,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,47,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,48,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,49,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,50,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,51,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,52,0)="  4.  Users can remain on the system. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,53,0)="      This patch can be queued and installed at any time."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,54,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,55,0)="  5.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,56,0)="      option:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,57,0)="        Install Package(s)  'XU*8.0*142'"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,58,0)="                             =========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,59,0)="                             "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,60,0)="        No Options or Protocols need to be placed out-of-order."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,61,0)="        Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,62,0)="                                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,63,0)="   6. The POST install has entered the address of one of the national "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,64,0)="      DNS servers.  PLEASE CHANGE TO THE CORRECT ONE FOR YOUR SITE."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,65,0)="      From the EVE menu > Operations Management > Kernel Management Menu"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,66,0)="      > Enter/Edit Kernel Site Parameters.  Go to the third screen and"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,67,0)="      enter the correct DNS IP address for your site."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,68,0)="      Here are the national DNS IP address's"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,69,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,70,0)="      152.127.1.12  ns1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,71,0)="      152.128.1.12  ns2"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,72,0)="      152.129.1.12  ns3"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,73,0)="      152.130.1.12  ns4"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,74,0)="      152.131.1.12  ns5"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,75,0)="      152.132.1.12  ns6"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",126,1,76,0)=" ========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,0)="136 SEQ #132^3000502^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,0)="^^140^140^3000502"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,1,0)="This patch addresses some of the problems that taskman is having with"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,2,0)="the ORB NOTIFICATION RESOURCE and the ORW THREAD RESOURCE."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,3,0)="Working with West LA and Seattle, a locking conflict was identified"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,4,0)="when Taskman was trying to allocate resource devices."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,5,0)="With this change taskman skips the lock of ^%ZTSCH(""DEV"",IO) to prevent"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,6,0)="two tasks from trying to open the same device at the same time.  The "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,7,0)="resource device has its own lock to control this."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,8,0)="This should fix a number of NOIS reports."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,9,0)="NJH-0100-20258, NTH-0100-70436, CLE-0100-40398, CTX-0100-70947,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,10,0)="CLE-0200-40051, BAY-0100-31168, TAM-0100-32225, JAC-0100-72572,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,11,0)="JAC-0200-70074, CTX-0300-70786"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,13,0)="Three new fields were added to the TASKMAN SITE PARAMETERS file."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,14,0)="""Balance Interval"" to control how offen the manager does the Balance code."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,15,0)="""Auto Delete Tasks"" to control if the sub-manager will set ZTREQ to ""@"""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,16,0)=" before the task starts."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,17,0)="""Manager Startup Delay"" to control how long the manager waits when starting."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,18,0)=" This field isn't used for a RESTART."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,19,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,20,0)="TAM-0100-32225"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,21,0)="A problem in the use of ZTREQ to re-schedule a task was fixed with a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,22,0)="change to %ZTLOAD3.  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,23,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,24,0)="MAC-0300-61865"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,25,0)="If there was an error in the loadbalance routine the variable ZTOVERLD would"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,26,0)="be undefined, ZTM6."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,27,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,28,0)="Also fix is a incorrect label in the ShareLic code of ZOSVONT."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,29,0)="LIT-0300-71933, FGH-0300-32520"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,30,0)=" Routine %LICENSE not in DMS 7.2 as expected. ZOSVVXD."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,31,0)=" The need for %ZOSV1 eleminated,  Routine ZOSV1VXD deleted by install."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,32,0)=" ZTMGRSET updated to reflect this change."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,33,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,34,0)="CML-1299-4077 XUTMQ3 "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,35,0)="Changed to adapt to the new Taskman ""IO"" list."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,36,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,37,0)="ALB-1299-50759 %ZIS2 "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,38,0)="Problem with the HFS parameters in the device file not being used when"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,39,0)="called from Taskman and ZTIO was used to setup the device."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,40,0)="                     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,41,0)="ZIS6 was changed to consolidate the resource device checking."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",127,1,42,0)=""
