^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,19,0)="========================================================================= "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,20,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,22,0)=">>>Users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,23,0)=">>>Taskman does not need to be stopped."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,25,0)="  1.  DSM sites - Some of these routines are usually mapped,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,26,0)="      so you will need to disable mapping for the affected routines. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,27,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,28,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,29,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,30,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,31,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,32,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,33,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,34,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,35,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,36,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,37,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,38,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,39,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,40,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,41,0)="  4.  Users can remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,42,0)="      This patch can be queued and installed at any time."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,43,0)="      TASKMAN can remain running."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,44,0)="           "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,45,0)="  5.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,46,0)="      option:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,47,0)="        Install Package(s)  'XU*8.0*183'"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,48,0)="                             =========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,49,0)="         "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,50,0)="        Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// YES "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,51,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,52,0)="        No Options or Protocols need to be placed out-of-order."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,53,0)="        Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,54,0)="                                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,55,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,56,0)="  6.  DSM Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",156,1,57,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",157,0)="188 SEQ #164^3010202^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,0)="180 SEQ #165^3010423^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,0)="^^128^128^3010423"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,1,0)="NOIS: DAY-1000-42520   Vista Security (Verify Code) "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,2,0)="These changes are required to meet VHA DIRECTIVE 6210 "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,3,0)="Available at http://vaww.domain.ext/publ/direc/health/direct/vha6210d.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,4,0)="The rules listed below are from the Document ""VA Account and Password "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,5,0)="Management Interim Policy"" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,7,0)=" a.     Controls shall be implemented to require strong passwords.  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,8,0)="        Passwords shall be at least eight characters in length, and "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,9,0)="        contain three of the following four kinds of characters: "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,10,0)="        letters  (upper case and lower), numbers, and, characters "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,11,0)="        that are neither letters nor numbers (like ""#"", ""@"" or ""$""). "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,12,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,13,0)=" b.     Passwords shall be changed no less frequently than every 90 days.  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,14,0)="        Information systems shall not permit re-assignment of the last "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,15,0)="        three passwords used.  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,16,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,17,0)=" c.     Accounts that have been inactive for 90 days shall be disabled.  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,19,0)=" d.     To preclude password guessing, an intruder lock out feature "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,20,0)="        shall suspend accounts after five invalid attempts to log on.  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,21,0)="        Where round-the-clock system administration service is available, "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,22,0)="        system administrator intervention shall be required to clear a "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,23,0)="        locked account.  Where round-the-clock system administration "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,24,0)="        service is not available, accounts shall remained locked out "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,25,0)="        for at least ten minutes.  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,27,0)="Here is what was done based on the requirement from VHA POLICY:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,28,0)="Item a. Because VistA has been case-insensitive for many years, we chose"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,29,0)="        to retain this characteristic. This means that VistA only has three "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,30,0)="        sets of characters to build a password from: alpha, numeric and "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,31,0)="        punctuation. The change from the past requirements is the new "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,32,0)="        requirement for punctuation characters and an increase in length "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,33,0)="        from 6 to 8 characters."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,34,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,35,0)="        The Kernel XUS2 routine was changed to require that "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,36,0)="        verify codes be composed of the following three groups of "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,37,0)="        characters: alpha, numeric, and punctuation."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,38,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,39,0)="Item b. This rule was implemented by changing the valid range in the data "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,40,0)="        dictionary and then checking the value in the KERNEL SYSTEM "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,41,0)="        PARAMETERS file (#8989.3) and resetting the value if it is found "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,42,0)="        to be greater than 90. Kernel has long kept old verify codes based "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,43,0)="        on the date they were changed. A change has been made to limit the "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,44,0)="        time frame for removal in option ""Purge Log of Old Access and Verify "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,45,0)="        Codes"" [XUSERAOLD]."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,47,0)="Item c. This rule was implemented by making changes to the scheduled Kernel "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,48,0)="        option 'Automatic Deactivation of Users' [XUAUTODEACTIVEATE] routine "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,49,0)="        XUSTERM1. This option has been changed to check each user's last "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,50,0)="        sign-on date and if it is more than 90 days old, sets the DISUSER "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,51,0)="        field for that user.  If this happens the user will get a ""No Access "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,52,0)="        Allowed for this User.""  message when they trying to logon."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,53,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,54,0)="        Note: The DISUSER field is shown on the 'User Inquiry' and is on the "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,55,0)="        second page of the Kernel option ""Edit an Existing User"" [XUSEREDIT].  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,57,0)="Item d. Kernel has always implemented a form of 'lockout'. Changes where made "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,58,0)="        to the Kernel System parameters file DEFAULT # OF ATTEMPTS and DEFAULT "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,59,0)="        LOCK-OUT TIME field's. The values in the KSP were checked and changed "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,60,0)="        to meet the new limits for these fields."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,61,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,63,0)="        Note: In addition, the sign-on code was changed to echo "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,64,0)="              an asterisk (*) for each character entered. This "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,65,0)="              follows the Microsoft Windows login style, which is "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,66,0)="              a change from the VMS login style."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,68,0)="Routine Summary"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,69,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,70,0)="of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,71,0)=" ;;8.0;KERNEL;<patchlist>;Jul 10, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,73,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,74,0)="Routine         Old       New      2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,75,0)="XUINPCH4          n/a    786391    **180**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,76,0)="XUS           8139177   8362765    **16,26,49,59,149,180**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,77,0)="XUS2         14055468  15802718    **59,180**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,78,0)="XUS4          3275391   3759854    **180**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,79,0)="XUSPURGE      6034721   4746135    **180**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,80,0)="XUSRB         6139976   6227685    **11,16,28,32,59,70,82,109,115,165,150,180**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",158,1,81,0)="XUSTERM1     12539120  11515045    **102,180**"
