^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,76,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,77,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,78,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,79,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,80,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,81,0)=">>>Users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,82,0)=">>>Taskman does not need to be stopped."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,83,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,84,0)="  1.  DSM sites - Some of these routines are usually mapped,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,85,0)="      so you will need to disable mapping for the affected routines."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,86,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,87,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,88,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,89,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,90,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,91,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,92,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,93,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,94,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,95,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,96,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,97,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,98,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,99,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,100,0)="  4.  Users can remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,101,0)="      This patch can be queued for install at non-peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,102,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,103,0)="  5.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,104,0)="      option:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,105,0)="        Install Package(s)  'XU*8.0*208'"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,106,0)="                             =========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,107,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,108,0)="        Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,109,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,110,0)="        No Options or Protocols need to be placed out-of-order."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,111,0)="        Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,112,0)="                                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,113,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,114,0)="  6.  DSM Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,115,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",171,1,116,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,0)="199 SEQ #179^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,0)="^^131^131^3011210"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,1,0)="Patch XU*8*199: IOPAR Corrupting Tasks"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,2,0)="================================"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,4,0)="Per the patch description below, this patch was intended to correct a problem "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,5,0)="identified in NOIS reports NOIS: NAS-0700-31644, CHA-0700-32007, "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,6,0)="MIW-0201-40662, DAY-0401-41059, and BRX-0501-10502."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,9,0)="Problem Statement:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,10,0)="=============="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,12,0)="The Text Integration Utility (TIU) has been encountering run away jobs at some "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,13,0)="sites due to the IO variable IOPAR being left behind by an earlier task.  After "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,14,0)="a lot of work by the sites, National Vista Support (NVS), and TIU developers, "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,15,0)="the following pattern has been identified:  Because the IOPAR variable is left"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,16,0)="behind by an earlier task, it overrides the normal Open parameter in the DEVICE "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,17,0)="file (#3.5) if either conditions exist:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,19,0)="  * When TIU (or any routine making a call %ZTLOAD) queues to a Host File "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,20,0)="    System (HFS) device, they could experience this problem depending on what "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,21,0)="    devices had been used before."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,23,0)="  * If TaskMan opens the device for a task which cannot be opened,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,24,0)="    TaskMan reschedules the task incorrectly using that same IOPAR variable, "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,25,0)="    which is still in the symbol table."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,28,0)="Patch Solution:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,29,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,31,0)="Several places in the code have been fixed to ensure that extra IO variables "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,32,0)="are not left behind after tasks have finished processing. This patch corrects "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,33,0)="the problem that the TIU has come across by changing the routine %ZTMS2 to kill "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,34,0)="the IOPAR variable before setting up the task. The %ZTMS2 routine now kills all "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,35,0)="IO variables before setting up a call to open a device. In addition, any "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,36,0)="special IO variables for that device are killed when the routine %ZISC is "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,37,0)="called to closed the device. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,39,0)="This patch also introduces a new extrinsic function UNIQUE^ZISUTL, which "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,40,0)="creates a unique IO parameter. This parameter takes the string $H_""-""_$J and "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,41,0)="runs a CRC32 on it to get a 10 digit number.  If UNIQUE^ZISUTL is called using "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,42,0)="a parameter, it will concatenate the number just before the last period (.) in "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,43,0)="the parameter string. Here are some examples on this:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,45,0)="   W $$UNIQUE()       >>2987896688"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,46,0)="   W $$UNIQUE(""last"") >>last_9041564"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,47,0)="   W $$UNIQUE(""$USR:[USER.FORT.EDIT]TEST.TMP"")"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,48,0)="                >>$USR:[USER.FORT.EDIT]TEST_2603399923.TMP"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,50,0)="Routine Summary"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,51,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,52,0)="of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,53,0)=" ;;8.0;KERNEL;<patchlist>;JUL 10, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,55,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,56,0)="Routine         Old       New      2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,57,0)="ZIS           9454725   9332342    **18,23,69,112,199**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,58,0)="ZIS1         10540675   9968286    **18,49,69,104,112,199**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,59,0)="ZISC          8004258   8130420    **24,36,49,69,199**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,60,0)="ZISUTL        2307058   2825748    **18,24,34,69,118,127,199**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,61,0)="ZTMS2         7001305   7090453    **2,18,23,36,67,118,127,163,167,175,199**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,63,0)="List of preceding patches: 112, 175"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,64,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,65,0)="========================================================================= "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,66,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,68,0)=">>>Do not allow users to log in to the system during installation."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,69,0)=">>>Users may remain on the system. They may get EDITED error if they"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,70,0)="   are selecting a device at the time."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,71,0)=">>>Taskman does need to be in a wait state."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,73,0)="  1.  DSM sites - Some of these routines are usually mapped,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,74,0)="      so you will need to disable mapping for the affected routines."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,75,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,76,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,77,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,78,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,79,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,80,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,81,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,82,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,83,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,84,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,85,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,86,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,87,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,88,0)="         "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,89,0)=" 4.  Users could remain on the system. They may get a EDITED error if they"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,90,0)="     are selecting a device at the time."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,91,0)="     This patch can not be queued."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,92,0)="     Also place TASKMAN in a wait state. (DO WAIT^ZTMKU)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,93,0)="     Inhibit users from login into the system. (If you install when few"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,94,0)="     users are on the system and the possibility of some CLOBER errors is"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,95,0)="     acceptable, then users can stay on the system.)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,96,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,97,0)="  5.  In Programmer mode:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,98,0)="      Use ""D ^XPDKRN"" then"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,99,0)="         Install Package(s)  'XU*8.0*199'"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,100,0)="                              ========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,101,0)="                              "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,102,0)="        Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// YES"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,103,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,104,0)="        No Options or Protocols need to be placed out-of-order."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,105,0)="        Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,106,0)="                                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,107,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,108,0)="  8.  After installing this patch,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,109,0)="      Cache Sites - you don't need to move anything, skip this step. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,110,0)="      DSM/MSM sites - you need to move several routines from "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,111,0)="      your production account to each manager account:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,112,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,113,0)="ZIS"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,114,0)="ZIS1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,115,0)="ZISC"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,116,0)="ZISUTL"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,117,0)="ZTMS2"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,118,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,119,0)="  9.  And in the manager account,  (OpenM sites remain in VAH)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,120,0)="      All sites:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,121,0)="      DO RELOAD^ZTMGRSET"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,122,0)="      Select the System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,123,0)="      Patch number to load: 199"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,124,0)="                            ==="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,125,0)="       "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,126,0)=" 10.  DSM Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,127,0)=" 11.  Enable user's login."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,128,0)="      Remove TASKMAN from the wait state. (DO RUN^ZTMKU)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,129,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,130,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",172,1,131,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",173,0)="209 SEQ #180^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",173,1,0)="^^3^3^3011210"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",173,1,1,0)="This patch enhances the Master File Server"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",173,1,2,0)="message handler and the IFR clean up code"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",173,1,3,0)="to compensate for HL7 package problems."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",174,0)="212 SEQ #181^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,0)="216 SEQ #182^3020108^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,0)="^^94^94^3020108"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,1,0)="Patch XU*8.0*216"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,3,0)="NOIS: ALT-1101-22356, DAY-1101-41446, BAY-1101-32090, WAS-1101-22142,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,4,0)="      DAY-1101-42557, LAS-1101-62483, MAC-1101-62500, NOL-1201-70575"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,5,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,6,0)="Test Sites: Dayton, OH; White River Junction Vt;"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,7,0)="            So. Nevada Healthcare System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,9,0)="Patch XU*8*199, IOPAR Corrupting Tasks, was released on 11/21/01. After the "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,10,0)="release of Patch XU*8*199, a new problem was discovered in the use and "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,11,0)="setting of the IOCPU variable. Unfortunately, this underlying problem was "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,12,0)="not discovered during the testing phase. To cause the problem you had to "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,13,0)="use OPEN^%ZISH to open the host file and use ^%ZISC to close it, then "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,14,0)="without calling ^%ZIS use OPEN^%ZISH again to open a host file when you "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,15,0)="call ^%ZISC the file would not get closed. Patch XU*8*216 corrects this "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,16,0)="problem. If sites installed any local modifications to correct this "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,17,0)="problem, based on advice provided by NVS in NOIS, please remove them prior "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,18,0)="to or immediately after the installation of this patch.  We regret the "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,19,0)="error and any inconvenience this has caused. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,20,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,21,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,22,0)="Routine Summary"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,23,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,24,0)="of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,25,0)=" ;;8.0;KERNEL;<patchlist>;JUL 10, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,26,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,27,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,28,0)="Routine         Old       New      2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,29,0)="ZISC          8130420   8069178    **24,36,49,69,199,216**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,30,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,31,0)="List of preceding patches: 199"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,32,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,33,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,34,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,35,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,36,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,37,0)=">>>If you accept a slight risk of jobs getting a CLOBBER/EDITED error"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,38,0)=">>>users and TaskMan may remain running.  Otherwise stop all other"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,39,0)=">>>jobs on the system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,40,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,41,0)="  1.  DSM sites - Some of these routines are usually mapped,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,42,0)="      so you will need to disable mapping for the affected routines."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,43,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,44,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,45,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,46,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,47,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,48,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,49,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,50,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,51,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,52,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,53,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,54,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,55,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,56,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,57,0)=" 4.   Inhibit users from login into the system. (If you install when few"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,58,0)="      users are on the system and the possibility of some CLOBER errors is"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,59,0)="      acceptable, then users and TaskMan can stay on the system.)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,60,0)="      Also place TASKMAN in a wait state. (DO WAIT^ZTMKU)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,61,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,62,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,63,0)="  5.  In Programmer mode:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,64,0)="      Use ""D ^XPDKRN"" then"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,65,0)="         Install Package(s)  'XU*8.0*216'"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,66,0)="                              =========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,67,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,68,0)="        Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,69,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,70,0)="        No Options or Protocols need to be placed out-of-order."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,71,0)="        Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,72,0)="                                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,73,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,74,0)="  8.  After installing this patch,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,75,0)="      Cache Sites - you don't need to move anything, skip this step."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,76,0)="      DSM/MSM sites - you need to move several routines from"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,77,0)="      your production account to each manager account:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,78,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,79,0)="ZISC"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,80,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,81,0)="  9.  And in the manager account,  (OpenM sites remain in VAH)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,82,0)="      All sites:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,83,0)="      DO RELOAD^ZTMGRSET"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,84,0)="      Select the System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,85,0)="      Patch number to load: 216"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,86,0)="                            ==="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,87,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,88,0)=" 10.  DSM Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,89,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,90,0)=" 11.  Enable user's login."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,91,0)="      Remove TASKMAN from the wait state. (DO RUN^ZTMKU)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,92,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,93,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",175,1,94,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",176,0)="200 SEQ #183^3020108^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,0)="205 SEQ #184^3020204^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,0)="^^84^84^3020204"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,1,0)="This patch adds some new fields to the TERMINAL TYPE file (#3.2) in support of "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,2,0)="Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) and barcode printers."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,4,0)="The new field, CONTROL CODES (#55), is a multiple of control codes. The "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,5,0)="applications that use this field will have to describe to the sites how to "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,6,0)="populate it. Before any new abbreviations are added to this file see that they "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,7,0)="have been added to Integration Agrement #3435 first. The CONTROL CODE field "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,8,0)="contains MUMPS code."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,11,0)="Field  #         Name"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,12,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,13,0)="      .001       NUMBER"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,14,0)="      .01        CTRL CODE ABBREVIATION"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,15,0)="      1          FULL NAME"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,16,0)="      2          CONTROL CODE "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,18,0)="NOIS: PUG-0101-51613"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,19,0)="Adds the 'Alternate Syntax for Device Specification' to the Device"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,20,0)="Handler help."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,21,0)="Adds a new HELP FRAME 'XUDOC DEVICE ALT SYNTAX' and updates %ZIS7 to"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,22,0)="to use the new HELP FRAME.  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,24,0)="Routine Summary"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,25,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,26,0)="of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,27,0)=" ;;8.0;KERNEL;<patchlist>;JUL 10, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,29,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,30,0)="Routine         Old       New      2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,31,0)="ZIS7          3002967   2928520    **205**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,33,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,35,0)="========================================================================= "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,36,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,38,0)=">>>Users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,39,0)=">>>Taskman does not need to be stopped."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,40,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,41,0)="  1.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,42,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,43,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,44,0)="  2.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,45,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,46,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,47,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,48,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,49,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,50,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,51,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,52,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,53,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,54,0)="  3.  Users can remain on the system. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,55,0)="      TASKMAN can remain running."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,56,0)="           "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,57,0)="  4.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,58,0)="      option:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,59,0)="        Install Package(s)  'XU*8.0*205'"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,60,0)="                             =========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,61,0)="         "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,62,0)="        Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,63,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,64,0)="        No Options or Protocols need to be placed out-of-order."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,65,0)="        Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,66,0)="                                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,67,0)="  5.  After installing this patch,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,68,0)="      Cache Sites - you don't need to move anything, skip this step. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,69,0)="      DSM/MSM sites - you need to move one routine from "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,70,0)="      your production account to each manager account:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,71,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,72,0)="ZIS7"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,73,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,74,0)="  6.  And in the manager account,  (OpenM sites remain in VAH)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,75,0)="      All sites:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,76,0)="      DO RELOAD^ZTMGRSET"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,77,0)="      Select the System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,78,0)="      Patch number to load: 205"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,79,0)="                            ==="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,80,0)="       "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,81,0)="  7.  DSM Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,82,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,83,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",177,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,0)="215 SEQ #185^3020204^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,0)="^^88^88^3020204"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,1,0)="Patch XU*8*215"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,3,0)="This patch introduces the following three enhancements."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,5,0)="1. A new function named GETPEER has been created to get the IP address of "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,6,0)="the caller to the TCP service. It has been designed to specifically work "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,7,0)="with a device connected as a TCP/IP listener in support of RPCBroker."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,9,0)="2. In SHARELIC^%ZOSV, the call made to the Cache operating system utility "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,10,0)="^%LICENSE have, in some cases, been resulting in errors which changed "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,11,0)="the way other errors get handled. This has been resolved by seeing that  "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,12,0)="$ECODE variable is cleared after the call."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,14,0)="3. Correctly add together the enterprise and division licenses in the "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,15,0)="$$AVJ^%ZOSV call.  $$AVJ is used by Kernel to check how many available jobs "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,16,0)="are on the system.  Only a few sites have division licenses. Most have "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,17,0)="enterprise licenses."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,19,0)="Routine Summary"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,20,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,21,0)="of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,22,0)=" ;;8.0;KERNEL;<patchlist>;Jul 10, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,24,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,25,0)="Routine         Old       New      2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,26,0)="ZOSVONT       5179130   5640784    **34,94,107,118,136,215**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,27,0)="ZOSVVXD       7443216   7675098    **13,65,71,94,107,118,136,215**"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,29,0)="List of preceding patches: 136"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,30,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,32,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,33,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,35,0)=">>>Users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,36,0)=">>>Taskman does not need to be stopped."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,38,0)="  1.  DSM sites - Some of these routines are usually mapped,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,39,0)="      so you will need to disable mapping for the affected routines."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,41,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,42,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,44,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,45,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,46,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,47,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,49,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,50,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,51,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,52,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,54,0)=" 4.  Users can remain on the system. This patch can be loaded any"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,55,0)="     non-peak time."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,56,0)="     This patch can not be queued."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,57,0)="     TASKMAN can remain running."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,59,0)="  5.  In Programmer mode:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,60,0)="      Use ""D ^XPDKRN"" then"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,61,0)="         Install Package(s)  'XU*8.0*215'"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,62,0)="                              =========="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,64,0)="        Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,66,0)="        No Options or Protocols need to be placed out-of-order."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,67,0)="        Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? NO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,68,0)="                                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,70,0)="  8.  After installing this patch,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,71,0)="      Cache Sites - you don't need to move anything, skip this step."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,72,0)="      DSM/MSM sites - you need to move several routines from"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,73,0)="      your production account to each manager account:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,75,0)="ZOSVONT"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,76,0)="ZOSVVXD"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,78,0)="  9.  And in the manager account,  (OpenM sites remain in VAH)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,79,0)="      All sites:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,80,0)="      DO RELOAD^ZTMGRSET"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,81,0)="      Select the System"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,82,0)="      Patch number to load: 215"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,83,0)="                            ==="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,85,0)=" 10.  DSM Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,87,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",178,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",179,0)="202 SEQ #186^3020204^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",180,0)="221 SEQ #187^3020226^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",181,0)="211 SEQ #188^3020315^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",181,1,0)="^^2^2^3020315"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",181,1,1,0)="See patch XU*8*211 in the National Patch Module on FORUM for complete"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",181,1,2,0)="information on this patch."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,0)="173 SEQ #189^3020516^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,0)="^^166^166^3020516"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,1,0)="** WARNING ** WARNING ** WARNING ** WARNING ** WARNING ** WARNING **"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,3,0)="If your site does not purge old alerts the post install routine,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,4,0)="which reindexes the ""B"" cross-reference of the FILE: ALERT TRACKING"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,5,0)="(# 8992.1), may take considerably longer than would be the case if you"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,6,0)="regularly purge.  In that case, you will want to schedule the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,7,0)="installation so the post installation routine may run on a weekend or"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,8,0)="overnight."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,10,0)="--------------------------- End of Warning -------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,12,0)="1. Surrogates for processing alerts may have an end date and time for the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,13,0)="surrogate relationship.  The actual removal of the surrogate has been"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,14,0)="performed when the next alert was sent to an individual.  This resulted,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,15,0)="however, in the user still appearing to have a surrogate after the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,16,0)="stated end time if another user tried to set them as their surrogate."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,17,0)="This patch modifies the processing so that the removal of the specified"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,18,0)="surrogate happens on any surrogate related look-up after the specified end"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,19,0)="time.  This will correct the problem that had been reported (E3R #14940)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,21,0)="2. Code has been modified to correct problems identified with setting"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,22,0)="surrogates (BRX-1000-10427, COS-0401-41366, WRJ-1201-11337)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,24,0)="3. The problem indicated as a mismatch in XQAID values (ISL-0200-52883) is"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,25,0)="handled by a re-indexing of the ""B"" cross-reference in FILE: ALERT"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,26,0)="TRACKING (#8992.1) in the post-installation routine."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,28,0)="4. A small change was made in XQALERT to clarify the way in which alerts"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,29,0)="are referenced from the menu system (ISL-0898-51279) and to correct a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,30,0)="potential problem with matching the ""B"" cross-reference in FILE: ALERT"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,31,0)="TRACKING (#8992.1)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,33,0)="5. A cross-reference was added to FIELD: SURROGATE (#.02) of FILE: ALERT"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,34,0)="(#8992) to permit rapid lookup of users who have specified a selected user"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,35,0)="as their surrogate (E3R #15158).  This is made available via the ""XQAL"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,36,0)="SURROGATE FOR WHICH USERS"" (View Surrogate for Which Users) option on the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,37,0)="XQALERT MGR menu.  The supported reference API SUROFOR^XQALSURO has been"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,38,0)="added for other applications to access this data."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,40,0)="    D SUROFOR^XQALSURO(.LIST,USERDUZ)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,42,0)="will return data in the variable LIST.  The value of LIST indicates the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,43,0)="number of entries returned.  The array list will return the users DUZ"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,44,0)="value in file 200 and the NAME (.01) field from file 200 separated by an"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,45,0)="'^'."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,46,0)="      LIST = 3"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,47,0)="      LIST(1) = ""54^LNAME1,FNAME1"""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,48,0)="      LIST(2) = ""75^LNAME2,FNAME2"""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,49,0)="      LIST(3) = ""247^LNAME3,FNAME3"""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,51,0)="The post-install routine, XQAL173P, also builds the cross-reference for"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,52,0)="current surrogates.  This routine is set to be removed following the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,53,0)="installation."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,55,0)="6. In addition, it was noted that while interactive specification of a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,56,0)="surrogate checked for cyclic relationships among surrogates, the API for"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,57,0)="non-interactive setting of a surrogated (SETSURO^XQALSURO) simply set the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,58,0)="specified surrogate.  While this API can continue to be used, a new API"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,59,0)="(SETSURO1^XQALSURO) has been created which should be used to obtain a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,60,0)="return value (1 if successful, 0 if not successful) indicating whether the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,61,0)="surrogate could be set."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,63,0)="  S VAL=$$SETSURO1^XQALSURO(USERDUZ,SURODUZ,STRTDATE,ENDDATE)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,66,0)="Where USERDUZ and SURODUZ are the internal entry numbers in file 200 for"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,67,0)="the user and selected surrogate, respectively.  STRTDATE and ENDDATE are"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,68,0)="optional date/time values for when the surrogate relationship should"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,69,0)="start and end.  If STRTDATE is not specified, the surrogate becomes active"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,70,0)="immediately.  If ENDDATE is not specified, the surrogate remains active"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,71,0)="until another surrogate is specified or the surrogate is removed."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",182,1,73,0)=" "
