^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,0)="316 SEQ #263^3030912^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,0)="^^181^181^3030912"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,1,0)="This patch provides several reporting options for Alerts, including"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,2,0)="ones that: list users with large number of alerts in the ALERTS file"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,3,0)="(#8992); list alerts for a specified user from a specified date; list"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,4,0)="alerts for a specified patient for a specified day or date range. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,5,0)="Since the retention period for alerts in the ALERT TRACKING file"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,6,0)="(#8992.1) is currently a site parameter, some users may have alerts"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,7,0)="in the ALERTS file that no longer are present in the ALERT TRACKING file,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,8,0)="data from both sources is used when necessary."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,10,0)="This patch adds the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,12,0)="Report Menu for Alerts (XQAL REPORTS MENU)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,14,0)="This menu provides several options for generating reports on alerts for"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,15,0)="users or patients."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,18,0)="User Alerts Count Report  (XQAL USER ALERTS COUNT)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,20,0)="This option is used to generate a report on users who have more than a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,21,0)="specified number of alerts in the ALERTS file (#8992).  The report covers"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,22,0)="a specified range of dates, and can be sorted by user name, number of"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,23,0)="alerts, or by service/section.  In addition, the report in each of these"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,24,0)="formats may be generated by Divisions if desired."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,26,0)="For each user who has the specified number of alerts or more, the report"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,27,0)="includes the user name, the section/service for the user, the number of"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,28,0)="alerts in the ALERTS file, the last sign-on date, the number of Critical"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,29,0)="alerts or Abnormal Imaging alerts, and the date of the oldest alert."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,31,0)="The counting of alerts may also be restricted to those alerts which contain "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,32,0)="specific text or phrases."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,35,0)="Critical Alerts Count Report (XQAL CRITICAL ALERT COUNT)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,37,0)="This option is used to generate a report of users who have more than a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,38,0)="specified number of alerts containing the word 'critical' or the words"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,39,0)="'abnormal imaging' between the specified start and end dates. The report"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,40,0)="is presented in descending order for the number of critical/abnormal"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,41,0)="imaging alerts present."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,43,0)="For each user who has the specified number of critical/abnormal"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,44,0)="imaging alerts or more, the report includes the user name, the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,45,0)="section/service for the user, the number of alerts in the ALERTS file, the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,46,0)="last sign-on date, the number of Critical alerts or Abnormal Imaging"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,47,0)="alerts, and the date of the oldest alert."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,50,0)="List Alerts for a user from a specified date (XQAL ALERT LIST FROM DATE)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,52,0)="This option is used to obtain a list of alerts from the ALERT TRACKING"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,53,0)="file (#8992.1) for a specified user for a specified date range.  The user"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,54,0)="may select all of the alerts to be displayed, or enter specific text or"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,55,0)="phrases to select only alerts which contain the specified text.  In the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,56,0)="latter case, the user may also select to see only those alerts which match"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,57,0)="the criteria and are only info only alerts, only action alerts, or both."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,59,0)="The listing includes the internal entry number for the alert in the ALERT"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,60,0)="TRACKING file, the date and time the alert was generated, the message"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,61,0)="text of the alert, and information about any option or routine to be"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,62,0)="executed for processing the alert."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,65,0)="Patient Alert List for specified date (XQAL PATIENT ALERT LIST)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,67,0)="This option is used to obtain a list of alerts for a specified patient"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,68,0)="from the ALERT TRACKING file (#8992.1) for a selected date range (it is"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,69,0)="recommended that this range be only a few days at most, since every entry"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,70,0)="in the ALERT TRACKING file in the selected date range must be checked to"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,71,0)="provide a complete listing of alerts for a patient)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,73,0)="A prompt is provided to obtain a quick scan listing of dates with at least"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,74,0)="some alerts for the patient on it based on OR and DVB alerts (other"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,75,0)="patient related alerts need to be identified by looking at each alert's"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,76,0)="message text and are included in the full list, but not the quick scan)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,78,0)="The user may select all of the alerts to be displayed, or enter specific"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,79,0)="text or phrases to select only alerts which contain the specified text. "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,80,0)="In the latter case, the user may also select to see only those alerts"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,81,0)="which match the criteria and are info only alerts, only action alerts,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,82,0)="or both."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,84,0)="The listing includes the internal entry number for the alert in the ALERT"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,85,0)="TRACKING file, the date and time the alert was generated, the message"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,86,0)="text of the alert, and information about any option or routine to be"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,87,0)="executed for processing the alert."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,90,0)="View data for Alert Tracking file entry  (XQAL VIEW ALERT TRACKING ENTRY)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,92,0)="This option can be used to obtain a listing of data in captioned format for"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,93,0)="selected entries in the ALERT TRACKING file (#8992.1).  The internal entry"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,94,0)="numbers for the entries to be listed must be entered individually."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,97,0)="There were no NOIS or E3Rs related to this patch."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",254,1,98,0)=" "
