^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",272,0)="309 SEQ #282^3040702^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",273,0)="332 SEQ #283^3040802^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",273,1,0)="^9.49011^2^2^3040802"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",273,1,1,0)="See patch XU*8*332 in the National Patch Module on FORUM for complete"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",273,1,2,0)="information on this patch."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,0)="285 SEQ #284^3040903^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,0)="^^464^464^3040903"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,1,0)="Read the WARNING below carefully prior to installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,3,0)="This patch addresses a patient safety issue in which alerts sent to an"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,4,0)="inactive user were not received by anyone.  If there are no active"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,5,0)="recipients or surrogates among the list of specified recipients the alert"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,6,0)="will be directed to the appropriate BACKUP REVIEWER as determined from the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,7,0)="PARAMETERS file.  If there is no identifiable BACKUP REVIEWER entry, the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,8,0)="alert will be sent to members of the ""XQAL UNPROCESSED ALERTS"" mail"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,9,0)="group.  If there are no active members specified for that mail group, the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,10,0)="alert will be sent as a last resort to members of G.PATCH."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,13,0)="*************************** WARNING ************************************"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,15,0)="The number of alerts generated to inactive users may be very large.  Your"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,16,0)="staff may need assistance in dealing with them and, in the case of unsigned"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,17,0)="documents, (many of the alerts) someone available to sign them.  You will"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,18,0)="not see alerts to inactive users from CPRS unless patch OR*3*200 (which will "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,19,0)="be released shortly after this patch) has been installed."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,21,0)="*************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,23,0)="In the roll-and-scroll or List Manager environment, this patch causes"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,24,0)="alerts which contain the text ""CRITICAL"" or ""ABNORMAL IMA"" are displayed in"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,25,0)="reverse video to cause these alert to stand out in the midst of many other"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,26,0)="alerts."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,28,0)="It was found that sending an alert to a mail group, only the individual"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,29,0)="members were identified.  This has been modified to include other mail"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,30,0)="groups which are members of the mail group as well."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,32,0)="The XQAL UNPROCESSED ALERTS mail group is created by this patch and during"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,33,0)="the Post-Init phase the individual installing the patch will be set up as"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,34,0)="a member of the mail group.  We recommend that this mail group be"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,35,0)="populated with a few individuals who can forward otherwise undelivered"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,36,0)="alerts on to a proper individuals."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,38,0)="An option was earlier provided for establishing individuals as BACKUP"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,39,0)="REVIEWER entries in the PARAMETER FILE, but the original option did not"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,40,0)="provide an easy way in which to delete or edit the entry.  This has been"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,41,0)="corrected in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,43,0)="This patch also corrects undefined errors which occur sporadically at"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,44,0)="DELETEA+7^XQALDEL and at DELA+1^XQALDEL."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,46,0)="For Developers, a new input variable during generation of alerts is"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,47,0)="XQADFN.  This value should contain the DFN value for the patient if the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,48,0)="alert is patient related.  Use of this variable will provide a more"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,49,0)="reliable indicator of the patient than that previously used (the second"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,50,0)="comma piece of the value of XQAID as used by CPRS)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,54,0)="For Developers this patch adds the following APIs as Supported References:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,56,0)="This patch creates a new entry point for setting up alerts. SETUP1^XQALERT"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,57,0)="is now recommended for creation of an alert.  It is used in the form"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,58,0)="  S RETVAL=$$SETUP1^XQALERT"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,59,0)="the value returned is a string with the first '^'-piece a 1 if the alert"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,60,0)="was delivered to at least one valid recipient or 0 if the alert could not"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,61,0)="be delivered.  In the latter case, the variable XQALERR will be defined"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,62,0)="and contain a string explaining why the alert was not delivered.  The second"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,63,0)="'^'-piece is the IEN in the Alert Tracking file for the alert and the third"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,64,0)="'^'-piece is the complete value of XQAID for the alert.  The second or third"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,65,0)="piece values may be used by an application to retain a reference to the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,66,0)="alert in the ALERT TRACKING file (#8992.1)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,69,0)="The original entry point SETUP^XQALERT for creating an alert did not"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,70,0)="return any indication if an alert was not deliverable for any reason. This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,71,0)="entry point is still valid for backward compatibility, but no longer"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,72,0)="recommended."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,74,0)="$$ACTVSURO^XQALSURO(IENVALUE) - returns the currently active surrogate for"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,75,0)="the user specified.  This includes potential surrogates of the current"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,76,0)="surrogate. To determine the currently active surrogate for the user with"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,77,0)="DUZ of IENVALUE, use"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,78,0)="   S ACTIVE=$$ACTVSURO^XQALSURO(IENVALUE)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,79,0)="If the returned value is greater than zero, it will indicate the active"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,80,0)="surrogate.  If the returned value is not greater than zero (actually -1),"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,81,0)="it will indicate that there are no currently active surrogates for the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,82,0)="user."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,84,0)="$$CHEKUSER^XQALSET(IENVALUE) - Returns 0 if no valid user or surrogate,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,85,0)="otherwise returns IEN of user or his currently active surrogate"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,87,0)="Addition of the ALERT RECIPIENT TYPE file (#8992.2)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,88,0)="---------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,90,0)="The ALERT RECIPIENT TYPE file was added to contain indicators as to why"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,91,0)="an alert was sent."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,92,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,93,0)="8992.2,.01    NAME                   0;1 FREE TEXT (Required)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,95,0)="              INPUT TRANSFORM:  K:$L(X)>45!($L(X)<3)!'(X'?1P.E) X"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,96,0)="              LAST EDITED:      OCT 17, 2003"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,97,0)="              HELP-PROMPT:      Answer must be 3-45 characters in length."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,98,0)="              DESCRIPTION:      This file is used to maintain a list of"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,99,0)="                                recipient types for alerts.  It is used in"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,100,0)="                                tracking for what reason a user was sent an"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,101,0)="                                alert."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,102,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,103,0)="              CROSS-REFERENCE:  8992.2^B"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,104,0)="                                1)= S ^XTV(8992.2,""B"",$E(X,1,30),DA)="""""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,105,0)="                                2)= K ^XTV(8992.2,""B"",$E(X,1,30),DA)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,108,0)="The following is the global map structure of the new multiple:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,110,0)="^XTV(8992.2,D0,0)= (#.01) NAME [1F] ^"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,114,0)="Changes to the ALERT TRACKING file (#8992.1)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,115,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,117,0)="This patch adds the following three (3) multiples to the Alert Tracking"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,118,0)="file."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,121,0)="8992.11,1       RECIPIENT TYPE       1;0 POINTER Multiple #8992.111"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,122,0)="                                 (Add New Entry without Asking)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,123,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,125,0)="8992.111,.01     RECIPIENT TYPE       0;1 POINTER TO ALERT RECIPIENT TYPE FILE"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,126,0)="                                   (#8992.2) (Required)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,127,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,128,0)="                  LAST EDITED:    OCT 20, 2003"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,129,0)="                  HELP-PROMPT:    This is a pointer to a file of different"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,130,0)="                                  recipient types (i.e., the reason someone"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,131,0)="                                  was sent the alert)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,132,0)="                  DESCRIPTION:    This field is used to track how a specific"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,133,0)="                                  recipient was selected for receiving the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,134,0)="                                  alert. The initial recipients are those to"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,135,0)="                                  whom the alert was initially directed"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,136,0)="                                  (INITIAL RECIPIENT).  Other recipients"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,137,0)="                                  may be the result of forwarding."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,138,0)="                                  Recipients of the alert from forwarding"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,139,0)="                                  are noted by the type of forwarding involved"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,140,0)="                                  (FWD BY USER, EMAIL SURROGATE, CHIEF/"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,141,0)="                                  SUPERVISOR, BACKUP REVIEWER, or"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,142,0)="                                  LAST HOPE)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,143,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,144,0)="                                  Marked as a specific category are those to"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,145,0)="                                  whom the alert was directed, but who were"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,146,0)="                                  not available to receive an alert due to"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,147,0)="                                  lack of access (marked with the suffix"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,148,0)="                                  ""-UNDELIVERABLE"" added to the basis for the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,149,0)="                                  alert being sent to the user)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,150,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,151,0)="                                  Those who have alerts forwarded to their"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,152,0)="                                  surrogate or receive the alert while acting"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,153,0)="                                  as a surrogate for another user are"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,154,0)="                                  indicated by entries in fields #.02 (SENT"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,155,0)="                                  TO SURROGATE) and #.03 (ACTING AS"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,156,0)="                                  SURROGATE) respectively. In addition,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,157,0)="                                  those who are acting as surrogates are"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,158,0)="                                  identified in the current field by the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,159,0)="                                  suffix ""-SURROGATE"" added to the basis"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,160,0)="                                  for the alert being received. Since the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,161,0)="                                  recipient may be acting as surrogate for"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,162,0)="                                  more than one user, the actual users for"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,163,0)="                                  which the message was sent on a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,164,0)="                                  surrogate basis are indicated in the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,165,0)="                                  SURROGATE FOR sub-file (#8992.113)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,166,0)="                                  under the RECIPIENT sub-file."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,167,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,168,0)="                                  The values stored for this field are"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,169,0)="                                  pointers to entries in the ALERT RECIPIENT"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,170,0)="                                  TYPE file (#8992.2)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,172,0)="                  CROSS-REFERENCE:8992.111^B"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,173,0)="                               1)= S ^XTV(8992.1,DA(2),20,DA(1),1,""B"",$E(X,1,3"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,174,0)="                               0),DA)="""""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,175,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,176,0)="                               2)= K ^XTV(8992.1,DA(2),20,DA(1),1,""B"",$E(X,1,3"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,177,0)="                               0),DA)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,178,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,179,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,180,0)="8992.111,.02      SENT TO SURROGATE  0;2 POINTER TO NEW PERSON FILE (#200)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,181,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,182,0)="                  LAST EDITED:  FEB 21, 2003"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,183,0)="                  HELP-PROMPT:  This is the individual that was sent the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,184,0)="                                alert in a surrogate capacity instead of the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,185,0)="                                originally specified recipient."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,186,0)="                  DESCRIPTION:  This field is used to identify the surrogate"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,187,0)="                                to whom the alert was sent instead of this"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,188,0)="                                originally specified recipient."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,189,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,190,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,191,0)="8992.111,.03      ACTING AS SURROGATE 0;3 SET"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,192,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,193,0)="                                'Y' FOR YES;"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,194,0)="                                'N' FOR NO;"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,195,0)="                  LAST EDITED:  FEB 20, 2003"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,196,0)="                  HELP-PROMPT:  Enter Y (YES) if this recipient received the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,197,0)="                                alert acting as surrogate for another user."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,198,0)="                  DESCRIPTION:  This field is used to identify those"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,199,0)="                                recipients who were sent the alert"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,200,0)="                                because they were selected as an active"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,201,0)="                                surrogate for the originally intended"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,202,0)="                                user.  In most cases only the Y (YES)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,203,0)="                                entries will be entered."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,204,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,205,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,206,0)="8992.111,.04      ALERT DATE/TIME    0;4 DATE"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,207,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,208,0)="                  INPUT TRANSFORM:S %DT=""ESTXR"" D ^%DT S X=Y K:Y<1 X"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,209,0)="                  LAST EDITED:  FEB 21, 2003"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,210,0)="                  HELP-PROMPT:  This is the date and time the alert was"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,211,0)="                                sent/forwarded to the current recipient with"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,212,0)="                                this recipient type"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,213,0)="                  DESCRIPTION:  This is the date and time the alert was"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,214,0)="                                sent/forwarded to the current recipient with"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,215,0)="                                this recipient type"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,216,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,217,0)="The following is the global map structure of the new multiple:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,218,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,219,0)="^XTV(8992.1,D0,20,D1,1,0)=^8992.111PA^^  (#1) RECIPIENT TYPE"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,220,0)="^XTV(8992.1,D0,20,D1,1,D2,0)= (#.01) RECIPIENT TYPE [1P] ^ (#.02) SENT TO"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,221,0)="                           ==>SURROGATE [2P] ^ (#.03) ACTING AS SURROGATE"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,222,0)="                           ==>[3S] ^ (#.04) ALERT DATE/TIME [4D] ^"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,223,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,224,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,225,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,226,0)="8992.11,2       FORWARDED DATE/TIME  2;0 DATE Multiple #8992.112"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,227,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,228,0)="                  LAST EDITED:  FEB 21, 2003"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,229,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,230,0)="8992.112,.01      FORWARDED DATE/TIME  0;1 DATE (Multiply asked)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,231,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,232,0)="                    INPUT TRANSFORM:S %DT=""ESTXR"" D ^%DT S X=Y K:Y<1 X"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,233,0)="                    LAST EDITED:  FEB 21, 2003"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,234,0)="                    HELP-PROMPT:  This is the date/time that the alert was"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,235,0)="                                  forwarded to the current recipient"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,236,0)="                    DESCRIPTION:  This field is used to track the date/time of"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,237,0)="                                  forwarding of the alert to this recipient."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,238,0)="                                  This is a multiple field to track instances"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,239,0)="                                  in which multiple copies of the alert may be"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,240,0)="                                  forwarded to a single recipient for various"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,241,0)="                                  reasons.  This multiple field will indicate"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,242,0)="                                  when it was forwarded and the basis for"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,243,0)="                                  forwarding of the alert."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,244,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,245,0)="                    CROSS-REFERENCE:8992.112^B"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,246,0)="                               1)= S ^XTV(8992.1,DA(2),20,DA(1),2,""B"",$E(X,1,3"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,247,0)="                               0),DA)="""""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,248,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,249,0)="                               2)= K ^XTV(8992.1,DA(2),20,DA(1),2,""B"",$E(X,1,3"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,250,0)="                               0),DA)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,251,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,252,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,253,0)="8992.112,.02      FORWARDING CATEGORY 0;2 POINTER TO ALERT RECIPIENT TYPE FILE"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,254,0)="                                (#8992.2)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,255,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,256,0)="                    LAST EDITED: OCT 20, 2003"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,257,0)="                    HELP-PROMPT:This field points to a file containing the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,258,0)="                                different reasons for forwarding."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,259,0)="                    DESCRIPTION:This field is used to track the basis on which"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,260,0)="                                the alert is forwarded to the current"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,261,0)="                                recipient.  The alert might be forwarded"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,262,0)="                                to the recipient by a user directly, or by"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,263,0)="                                programmed forwarding related to alerts not"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,264,0)="                                being processed within a specified time to"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,265,0)="                                EMAIL SURROGATE, CHIEF/SUPERVISOR; BACKUP"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,266,0)="                                REVIEWER, or LAST RESORT."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,267,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,268,0)="                                Entries for this field are pointers to the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,269,0)="                                values in the ALERT RECIPIENT TYPE file"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,270,0)="                                (#8992.2)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,271,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,272,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,273,0)="8992.112,.03      FORWARDED BY OR FOR 0;3 POINTER TO NEW PERSON FILE (#200)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,274,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,275,0)="                    LAST EDITED: APR 04, 2003"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,276,0)="                    HELP-PROMPT:This is the individual that forwarded the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,277,0)="                                alert, or the alert was forwarded for."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,278,0)="                    DESCRIPTION:This is a record of the individual who"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,279,0)="                                forwarded the alert, or on whose behalf the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,280,0)="                                alert was forwarded if it was forwarded"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,281,0)="                                automatically."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,282,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,283,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,284,0)="8992.112,1.01     FORWARDING COMMENT 1;1 FREE TEXT"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,285,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,286,0)="                    INPUT TRANSFORM:K:$L(X)>240!($L(X)<1) X"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,287,0)="                    LAST EDITED: FEB 20, 2003"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,288,0)="                    HELP-PROMPT:Answer must be 1-240 characters in length."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,289,0)="                    DESCRIPTION:This is the comment which was sent to the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,290,0)="                                recipient along with the forwarded alert."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,291,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,292,0)="The following is the global map structure of the new multiple:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,293,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,294,0)="^XTV(8992.1,D0,20,D1,2,0)=^8992.112D^^  (#2) FORWARDED DATE/TIME"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,295,0)="^XTV(8992.1,D0,20,D1,2,D2,0)= (#.01) FORWARDED DATE/TIME [1D] ^ (#.02)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,296,0)="                           ==>FORWARDING CATEGORY [2P] ^ (#.03) FORWARDED BY"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,297,0)="                           ==>OR FOR [3P] ^"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,298,0)="^XTV(8992.1,D0,20,D1,2,D2,1)= (#1.01) FORWARDING COMMENT [1F] ^"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,299,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,300,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,301,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,302,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,303,0)="8992.11,3       SURROGATE FOR        3;0 POINTER Multiple #8992.113"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,304,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,305,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,306,0)="8992.113,.01      SURROGATE FOR        0;1 POINTER TO NEW PERSON FILE (#200)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,307,0)="                                   (Multiply asked)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,308,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,309,0)="                      LAST EDITED: FEB 20, 2003"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,310,0)="                      HELP-PROMPT:Enter the NEW PERSON entry for which the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,311,0)="                                  current recipient is acting as surrogate on"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,312,0)="                                  this alert."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,313,0)="                      DESCRIPTION:This field is used to track which user or"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,314,0)="                                  users the current recipient is receiving the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,315,0)="                                  current alert while acting as surrogate."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,316,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,317,0)="                      CROSS-REFERENCE:8992.113^B"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,318,0)="                               1)= S ^XTV(8992.1,DA(2),20,DA(1),3,""B"",$E(X,1,3"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,319,0)="                               0),DA)="""""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,320,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,321,0)="                               2)= K ^XTV(8992.1,DA(2),20,DA(1),3,""B"",$E(X,1,3"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,322,0)="                               0),DA)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,323,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,324,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,325,0)="8992.113,.02      DATE/TIME - SURROGATE FOR 0;2 DATE"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,326,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,327,0)="                      INPUT TRANSFORM:S %DT=""ESTXR"" D ^%DT S X=Y K:Y<1 X"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,328,0)="                      LAST EDITED: FEB 20, 2003"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,329,0)="                      HELP-PROMPT:Enter the date/time that this alert was"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,330,0)="                                received while acting as a surrogate for the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,331,0)="                                intended recipient."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,332,0)="                      DESCRIPTION:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,333,0)="                                This field has the date/time when the alert"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,334,0)="                                was sent to the current recipient while"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,335,0)="                                acting as a surrogate for the originally"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,336,0)="                                intended recipient."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",274,1,337,0)=" "
