^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,0)="366 SEQ #313^3051020^1"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,0)="^^279^279^3051020"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,1,0)=" Patch XU*8*366 (RETURN ALERTS FROM SURROGATE) resolves a patient safety"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,2,0)=" issue (PSI-04-036) by modifying the handling of alerts sent to surrogates"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,3,0)=" to return unprocessed alerts to the originally intended recipient of the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,4,0)=" alert after a surrogacy period ends.  As a byproduct of the changes made,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,5,0)=" it is now possible to schedule multiple different (temporal) surrogate"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,6,0)=" periods in advance."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,8,0)=" Alerts are sent to the specified surrogate, or surrogates if there is a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,9,0)=" sequence of consecutive periods of surrogacy.  When a user requests a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,10,0)=" listing of alerts AND THERE ARE NO CURRENT SURROGATES (either due to the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,11,0)=" end of the surrogacy period or removal of the last surrogate) alerts which"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,12,0)=" were sent to the surrogate(s) and have not been processed by the surrogate"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,13,0)=" are returned to the user as new alerts with a comment indicating they were"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,14,0)=" returned from the surrogate.  If the surrogate was not an intended"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,15,0)=" recipient of the alert(s), either as an initially specified recipient or"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,16,0)=" by receiving the alert by forwarding from another recipient, the alert will"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,17,0)=" be deleted from the surrogate.  If the surrogate was an intended recipient"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,18,0)=" of the alert it will also remain with the surrogate."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,20,0)=" A consequence of the modifications made to track the periods of surrogacy"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,21,0)=" is the ability to add multiple surrogate periods with different start times."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,22,0)=" The  most recent active start time determines which of the surrogate periods"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,23,0)=" is active.  Therefore, the termination date/time for a given period of"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,24,0)=" surrogacy, if specified, only determines the end of the surrogacy if no"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,25,0)=" other surrogacy period starts prior to that time.  It does not determine"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,26,0)=" the actual end time if another period of surrogacy starts before the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,27,0)=" specified end time (or there was no end time specified).  A pair of"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,28,0)=" users can be specified in advance as mutual surrogates with opposite rolls,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,29,0)=" as long as the periods of surrogacy do not overlap resulting in a circular"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,30,0)=" relationship."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,32,0)=" In the Roll and Scroll environment, selection of Surrogate processing will"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,33,0)=" list current surrogate(s) and give the option to remove one or more of the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,34,0)=" surrogates, and the option to add a surrogate, which if it is a later start"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,35,0)=" date/time than a currently active or scheduled surrogate, will become active"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,36,0)=" at the date/time specified."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,38,0)=" A new supported reference (SUROLIST^XQALSURO) has been added to provide a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,39,0)=" list of current and scheduled surrogates for a user."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,41,0)=" D SUROLIST^XQALSURO(XQAUSER,.XQALIST)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,43,0)=" where XQALIST is passed by reference.  On return XQALIST contains the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,44,0)=" number of entries returned, and an array containing the current and"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,45,0)=" scheduled surrogates with '^'-separated values for internal entry number in"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,46,0)=" the NEW PERSON file (#200), the value for the NAME field (#.01) from the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,47,0)=" NEW PERSON file (#200), the start date/time for the surrogacy period and the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,48,0)=" end date/time for the surrogacy period.  If a surrogate has no end date/time"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,49,0)=" value and is followed by another surrogate, the first surrogate will show an"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,50,0)=" end date/time value equal to the start date/time of the following surrogate."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,52,0)=" returns  XQALIST=count"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,53,0)="          XQALIST(1)=IEN2^NEWPERSON,USER2^STARTDATETIME^ENDDATETIME"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,54,0)="          XQALIST(2)=3^NAME,USER3^3050407.1227^3050409"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,56,0)=" The supported reference to remove surrogates (REMVSURO^XQALSURO) has been"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,57,0)=" modified to add two additional OPTIONAL arguments which specify the IEN of"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,58,0)=" a surrogate and the start date/time for that surrogate session to be removed"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,59,0)=" (these values can be obtained with the SUROLIST^XQALSURO call described"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,60,0)=" above).  If these two optional arguments are not specified, the call to"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,61,0)=" REMVSURO^XQALSURO will remove the current or next scheduled surrogate entry"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,62,0)=" (as it has in the past)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,64,0)=" These features will become active in windowed applications, such as CPRS,"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,65,0)=" only after the applications implement code changes to take advantage of the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,66,0)=" new functionality included in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,68,0)=" The following field (and sub-file) was added to the ALERT file (#8992):"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,70,0)=" 8992,2        SURROGATE              2;0 DATE Multiple #8992.02"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,72,0)="               DESCRIPTION:      This field is a multiple based on the start"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,73,0)="                                 date/time for a surrogate relationship.  This"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,74,0)="                                 will permit multiple surrogate relationships"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,75,0)="                                 to be scheduled."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,77,0)="                                 Since a start date/time for the surrogate"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,78,0)="                                 relationship is required, if the user does not"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,79,0)="                                 enter one, then the NOW as the current"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,80,0)="                                 date/time will be used."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,83,0)=" 8992.02,.01     SURROGATE START DATE/TIME 0;1 DATE (Required) (Multiply asked)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,85,0)="                 INPUT TRANSFORM:  S %DT=""ESTX"" D ^%DT S X=Y K:Y<1 X"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,86,0)="                 LAST EDITED:      NOV 12, 2004"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,87,0)="                 HELP-PROMPT:     This is the START DATE/TIME for the surrogate"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,88,0)="                 DESCRIPTION:      This is the starting date and time for a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,89,0)="                                   surrogate relationship."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,91,0)="                 CROSS-REFERENCE:  8992.02^B"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,92,0)="                                   1)= S ^XTV(8992,DA(1),2,""B"",$E(X,1,30),DA)="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,93,0)="                                   """""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,94,0)="                                   2)= K ^XTV(8992,DA(1),2,""B"",$E(X,1,30),DA)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,97,0)=" 8992.02,.02     SURROGATE USER         0;2 POINTER TO NEW PERSON FILE (#200)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,98,0)="                                    (Required)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,99,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,100,0)="                 LAST EDITED:      NOV 12, 2004"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,101,0)="                 HELP-PROMPT:      This is the user who will be the surrogate"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,102,0)="                                   during the time period specified"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,103,0)="                 DESCRIPTION:      This is a pointer to the user in the NEW"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,104,0)="                                   PERSON file who will be acting as the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,105,0)="                                   surrogate for the time period specified."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,108,0)=" 8992.02,.03     END DATE TIME          0;3 DATE"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,110,0)="                 INPUT TRANSFORM:  S %DT=""ESTX"" D ^%DT S X=Y K:Y<1 X"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,111,0)="                 LAST EDITED:      NOV 12, 2004"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,112,0)="                 HELP-PROMPT:      This is an optional date/time for when the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,113,0)="                                   surrogate relationship will be terminated."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,114,0)="                 DESCRIPTION:      This is an optional date/time for when the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,115,0)="                                   surrogate relationship will be terminated."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,116,0)="                                   If there is no value entered, then the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,117,0)="                                   relationship will continue until it is"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,118,0)="                                   specifically terminated."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,121,0)=" 8992.02,.04     NEEDS RETURN           0;4 SET"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,123,0)="                                   '1' FOR YES;"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,124,0)="                                   '0' FOR NO;"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,125,0)="                 LAST EDITED:      MAR 16, 2005"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,126,0)="                 HELP-PROMPT:      This is a flag which is used to determine"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,127,0)="                                   whether alerts have been returned to the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,128,0)="                                   intended recipient or not"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,129,0)="                 DESCRIPTION:      This field is used as a flag to indicate"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,130,0)="                                   whether the alerts have been returned to the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,131,0)="                                   intended recipient or not."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,132,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,133,0)="                 CROSS-REFERENCE:  8992.02^AC"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,134,0)="                                   1)= S ^XTV(8992,DA(1),2,""AC"",$E(X,1,30),DA)="
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,135,0)="                                   """""
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,137,0)="                                   2)= K ^XTV(8992,DA(1),2,""AC"",$E(X,1,30),DA)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,138,0)="                                 3)= This x-ref is used to track alerts needing"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,139,0)="                                 return from surrogates"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,140,0)="                                 This cross reference is used to identify"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,141,0)="                                 periods for which any alerts forwarded to a"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,142,0)="                                 surrogate have not been returned to the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,143,0)="                                 intended recipient."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,145,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,146,0)=" The following field was added to the sub-file for the SURROGATE FOR field (#3)"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,147,0)=" of the ALERT TRACKING file (#8992.1):"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,150,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,151,0)=" 8992.113,.03      DATE-TIME RETURNED 0;3 DATE"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,152,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,153,0)="                       INPUT TRANSFORM:S %DT=""ESTXR"" D ^%DT S X=Y K:Y<1 X"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,154,0)="                       LAST EDITED: MAR 16, 2005"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,155,0)="                       HELP-PROMPT:This is the date-time that the alert was"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,156,0)="                                 returned to the originally intended recipient"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,157,0)="                       DESCRIPTION:"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,158,0)="                                This field is a record for the date-time that"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,159,0)="                                an alert for which this recipient was acting as"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,160,0)="                                a surrogate was returned to the originally"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,161,0)="                                intended recipient of the alert."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,162,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,163,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,164,0)=" In addition the AUD cross-reference was added to the ALERT DATE/TIME field"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,165,0)=" (#.04) the sub-file associated with the RECIPIENT TYPE field (#1) of the"
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,166,0)=" ALERT TRACKING file (#8992.1)."
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,167,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,3,22,21,"PAH",302,1,168,0)=" "
