^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,0)="47 SEQ #41^2970610^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,0)="^^48^48^2970610"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,1,0)="MailMan patch XM*7.1*47 contains the following bug fix:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,3,0)="NOIS:       TOG-0597-11935"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,4,0)="Rtn:        ^XMA7"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,5,0)="Test Site:  Togus, ME"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,6,0)="When using the 'user information' option, in the list showing users for whom"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,7,0)="the user may act as surrogate, the first user in the list shows"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,8,0)="'no privileges', no matter which privileges have been granted."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,9,0)="This patch fixes that bug."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,10,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,11,0)="This user may act as surrogate for:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,13,0)="USER,ONE                             (No Privileges)  <== bug"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,14,0)="USER,TWO                             (Read and Write Privileges)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,15,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,16,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,17,0)="This patch should be installed after hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,18,0)="minimum.  You should put the XMUSER Option out of order."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,19,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,21,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,22,0)="1.  If any of these routines is mapped (on systems which allow mapping),"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,23,0)="    disable mapping for the affected routine(s)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,24,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,25,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,26,0)="3.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,27,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,28,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,29,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,30,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,31,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,32,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,33,0)="4.  MSM Sites - Answer YES to the question 'Want to MOVE routines to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,34,0)="    other CPUs?'. Enter the names of your Compute and Print server(s)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,35,0)="5.  AXP Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,36,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,37,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,38,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,39,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,40,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,42,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,43,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,44,0)="----------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,45,0)="XMA7          10079999        10080629        10,47"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,46,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,47,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",20,1,48,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,0)="40 SEQ #42^2970819^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,0)="^^68^68^2970819"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,1,0)="MailMan patch XM*7.1*40 contains the following enhancements:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,3,0)="NOIS:       MCM-0197-51792"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,4,0)="Rtns:       ^XMA1,^XMJMQ,^XMJMQ1,^XMJMP1,^XMXUTIL,^XMYPRE1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,5,0)="DD:         file 3.9, field .01 of RECIPIENT multiple - adds ""C"" xref to DD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,6,0)="Test Site:  Miles City,MT; Bronx,NY"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,7,0)="Improves the query (Q,QD,QN,Q name) function:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,8,0)="1) makes coding clearer"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,9,0)="2) makes 'Q name' perform more like a FileMan lookup for local addressees"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,10,0)="   a) recognizes partial last name, partial first name for the first time ever"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,11,0)="   b) query by addressee's DUZ for the first time ever"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,12,0)="   c) query by addressee's nickname for the first time ever"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,13,0)="3) enables 'Q name' to work on remote addressees for the first time ever!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,14,0)="   a) recognizes partial last name"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,15,0)="   b) recognizes partial last name, partial first name"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,16,0)="   c) recognizes partial last name, partial domain"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,17,0)="   d) (does not work with I: or CC: remote addressees)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,18,0)="4) enables 'Q name' to work on devices and servers (D. and S.) for the first"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,19,0)="   time ever"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,20,0)="3) improves display aesthetics"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,21,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,22,0)="The following concerns the RECIPIENT multiple of the MESSAGE file:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,23,0)="The ""C"" cross reference data has always existed for the .01 field (RECIPIENT)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,24,0)="But... the DD has the ""C"" xref on field 1 (LAST RESPONSE READ)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,25,0)="So... We switch the xref in the DD from field 1 to field .01. as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,26,0)="Routine XMYPRE1 deletes the ""C"" xref on field 1 (LAST RESPONSE READ)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,27,0)="The partial DD in this patch sets the ""C"" xref on field .01 (RECIPIENT)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,28,0)="Since the actual ""C"" xref data has always been on field .01, we don't need"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,29,0)="to do anything with the ""C"" xref data - just leave it alone."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,30,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,31,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,32,0)="This patch should be installed after hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,33,0)="minimum.  You should put the XMUSER Option out of order."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,34,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,36,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,37,0)="1.  If any of these routines is mapped (on systems which allow mapping),"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,38,0)="    disable mapping for the affected routine(s)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,39,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,40,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,41,0)="3.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,42,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,43,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,44,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,45,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,46,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,47,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,48,0)="4.  MSM Sites - Answer YES to the question 'Want to MOVE routines to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,49,0)="    other CPUs?'. Enter the names of your Compute and Print server(s)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,50,0)="5.  AXP Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,51,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,52,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,53,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,54,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,55,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,57,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,58,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,59,0)="----------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,60,0)="XMA1           9580091         9717771        31,36,40"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,61,0)="XMJMP1         * new *        11388791        40"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,62,0)="XMJMQ          * new *        14561364        40"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,63,0)="XMJMQ1         * new *         3291603        40"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,64,0)="XMXUTIL        * new *         2338705        40"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,65,0)="XMYPRE1        * new *           32634        40"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,66,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,67,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",21,1,68,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,0)="44 SEQ #43^2970819^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,0)="^^143^143^2970819"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,1,0)="MailMan patch XM*7.1*44 contains the following enhancements:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,3,0)="NOIS:       OKL-0497-70538"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,4,0)="E3R:        9173,9994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,5,0)="Rtns:       ^XMA32A,^XMADJF1,^XMGAPI3,^XMZTERM,^XMZTERM1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,6,0)="Options:    XMMGR,XMMGR-TERMINATE-ONE,XMMGR-TERMINATE-MANY,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,7,0)="            XMMGR-TERMINATE-SUGGEST,XMMGR-PURGE-MESSAGE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,8,0)="Test Sites: Oklahoma City, OK; Prescott, AZ; St. Louis, MO; Houston, TX"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,10,0)="Broadcast mail is now delivered only to users who have an access code, a verify"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,11,0)="code, a primary menu, and a mail box."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,13,0)="Four new options have been added to XMMGR-DISK-SPACE-MANAGEMENT menu:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,14,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,15,0)="----------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,16,0)="NAME: XMMGR-PURGE-MESSAGE               MENU TEXT: Purge a message"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,17,0)="DESCRIPTION:  This option enables you to purge any message."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,18,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,19,0)="Purge means:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,20,0)="-delete the message from all user mailboxes"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,21,0)="-delete the message from the MESSAGE global ^XMB(3.9"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,22,0)="-delete all responses from the MESSAGE global ^XMB(3.9"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,23,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,24,0)="Purge is not reversible.  The message is gone forever."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,25,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,26,0)="----------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,27,0)="NAME: XMMGR-TERMINATE-ONE               MENU TEXT: Terminate one mail user"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,28,0)="DESCRIPTION:   This option lets you remove the mailbox of any user"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,29,0)="who meets the criteria of either the XMMGR-TERMINATE-MANY option or the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,30,0)="XMMGR-TERMINATE-SUGGEST option."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,31,0)="As a result, the user will not receive any mail.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,32,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,33,0)="Remember,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,34,0)="-Whenever you give a user a new access code,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,35,0)=" the system gives the user a mailbox if he doesn't already have one."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,36,0)="-Whenever a user logs on,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,37,0)=" the system gives the user a mailbox if he doesn't already have one."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,38,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,39,0)="----------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,40,0)="NAME: XMMGR-TERMINATE-MANY              MENU TEXT: Terminate many mail users"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,41,0)="DESCRIPTION:   This option goes through the MAIL BOX global and removes any"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,42,0)="mailbox if"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,43,0)="- the user is not in the NEW PERSON file."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,44,0)="- the user has no access code and was not terminated."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,45,0)="- the user has no access code and was terminated w/o mailbox retention."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,46,0)="- the user has an access code and primary menu, but no verify code, AND "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,47,0)="  - has never signed on, since being added before a cutoff date.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,48,0)="  OR "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,49,0)="  - last signed on before a cutoff date."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,50,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,51,0)="Remove means:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,52,0)="- Delete user's private mail groups"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,53,0)="- Remove user from membership in all groups"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,54,0)="- Remove user as an authorized sender from all groups "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,55,0)="- Remove user from anyone's list of surrogates"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,56,0)="- Delete user's latered-messages list"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,57,0)="- Delete user's mail box"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,58,0)="As a result, the user will not receive any mail."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,59,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,60,0)="This option can be run in 'test' or 'real' mode.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,61,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,62,0)="The report lists, in DUZ order:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,63,0)="-The user's DUZ and name"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,64,0)="-Whether the user has an access code, verify code, and primary menu"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,65,0)="-When the user was added to the NEW PERSON file"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,66,0)="-When the user last signed on"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,67,0)="-When the user was terminated (if applicable)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,68,0)="-If the user was terminated, then whether the site manager chose to delete"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,69,0)=" the user's mailbox.  (It's generally a good idea to go ahead and delete"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,70,0)=" the mailbox upon termination.) "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,71,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,72,0)="----------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,73,0)="NAME: XMMGR-TERMINATE-SUGGEST"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,74,0)="MENU TEXT: Terminate mail user suggestions"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,75,0)="DESCRIPTION:   This option goes through the MailBox global and reports on"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,76,0)="users who perhaps should have their mail access terminated.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,77,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,78,0)="Users are included in the report if"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,79,0)="- the user was terminated before a manager-supplied cutoff date"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,80,0)="  and allowed to keep a mailbox."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,81,0)="- the user has an access code, verify code, and primary menu,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,82,0)="  but last signed on before a manager-supplied cutoff date.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,83,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,84,0)="This option does not terminate mail access.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,85,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,86,0)="The report page breaks on Service/Section and includes the following "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,87,0)="information: "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,88,0)="-User's DUZ and name"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,89,0)="-Whether the user has an access code, a verify code, and a primary menu"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,90,0)="-When the user last signed on"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,91,0)="-When the user was terminated (if applicable)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,92,0)="-If the user was terminated, then whether the site manager chose"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,93,0)=" to delete the user's mailbox.  (Remember, you should usually answer 'yes'"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,94,0)=" to this question, unless the user is coming back and needs to have his mail"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,95,0)=" retained.)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,96,0)="-How many new messages the user has.  (New messages are never purged, except "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,97,0)=" during purge-by-date purges.) "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,98,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,99,0)="Finally there are two blank columns.  One is headed ""Term User Mbox"""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,100,0)="(Terminate user mailbox), and the other is headed ""Deact VISTA Access"""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,101,0)="(Deactivate VISTA Access).  Besides being of interest to the Site Manager,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,102,0)="this report is also designed to be submitted to other services. The intent is"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,103,0)="that the other services would check one of the columns for each user in the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,104,0)="report and return the report to the Site Manager to act on. "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,105,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,106,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,107,0)="This patch should be installed after hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,108,0)="minimum.  You should put the XMUSER Option out of order.  The filers should"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,109,0)="be shut down.  ^XMADJF1 is probably mapped on your system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,110,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,112,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,113,0)="1.  If any of these routines is mapped (on systems which allow mapping),"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,114,0)="    disable mapping for the affected routine(s)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,115,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option to load"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,116,0)="    the patch into a transport global."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,117,0)="3.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,118,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,119,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,120,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,121,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,122,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,123,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,124,0)="4.  MSM Sites - Answer YES to the question 'Want to MOVE routines to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,125,0)="    other CPUs?'. Enter the names of your Compute and Print server(s)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,126,0)="5.  AXP Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,127,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,128,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,129,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,130,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,131,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,132,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,133,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,134,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,135,0)="----------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,136,0)="XMA32A         9601895        10911370        27,37,44"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,137,0)="XMADJF1        8481461         8709221        44"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,138,0)="XMGAPI3        2791662         3149530        29,44"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,139,0)="XMZTERM        * new *        15108400        44"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,140,0)="XMZTERM1       * new *        14445630        44"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,141,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,142,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",22,1,143,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,0)="46 SEQ #44^2970819^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,0)="^^42^42^2970819"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,1,0)="MailMan patch XM*7.1*46 contains the following bug fix:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,3,0)="NOIS:       PAL-0597-61414"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,4,0)="Rtn:        ^XMA2C"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,5,0)="Test Site:  Palo Alto, CA"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,6,0)="If a user terminates the original message immediately after having copied it,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,7,0)="the first user in the recipient multiple is terminated, which is not"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,8,0)="necessarily the user.  This patch fixes this bug. "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,10,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,11,0)="This patch should be installed after hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,12,0)="minimum.  You should put the XMUSER Option out of order."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,13,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,15,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,16,0)="1.  If any of these routines is mapped (on systems which allow mapping),"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,17,0)="    disable mapping for the affected routine(s)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,18,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,19,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,20,0)="3.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,21,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,22,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,23,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,24,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,25,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,26,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,27,0)="4.  MSM Sites - Answer YES to the question 'Want to MOVE routines to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,28,0)="    other CPUs?'. Enter the names of your Compute and Print server(s)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,29,0)="5.  AXP Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,30,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,31,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,32,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,33,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,34,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,36,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,37,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,38,0)="----------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,39,0)="XMA2C          3972504         4143045        46"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,40,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,41,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",23,1,42,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,0)="52 SEQ #45^2971016^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,0)="^^42^42^2971016"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,1,0)="MailMan patch XM*7.1*52 contains the following fix"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,3,0)="NOIS:       IVM-0997-32203,WNY-0197-11745"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,4,0)="Rtn:        ^XMADJF1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,5,0)="Test Site:  Atlanta, GA"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,6,0)="Responses to messages with 9+ digit message numbers were being added to the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,7,0)="message whose number was the 1st 8 digits of the message number.  For example,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,8,0)="a response to message number 123456789 was added to message number 12345678."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,9,0)="This patch makes sure that responses are added to the correct message."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,10,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,11,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,12,0)="This patch should be installed with no users on the system and with the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,13,0)="filers shut down."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,14,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,16,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,17,0)="1.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,18,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,19,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,20,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,21,0)="3.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,22,0)="    Transport Global: "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,23,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,24,0)="       Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,25,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,26,0)="       Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,27,0)="       Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,28,0)="4.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,29,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,30,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,31,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",24,1,32,0)="ROUTINES:"
