^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,0)="^^42^42^2971028"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,1,0)="MailMan patch XM*7.1*48 contains the following bug fix:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,3,0)="NOIS:       BRK-0197-10525"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,4,0)="Rtn:        ^XMS"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,5,0)="Test Site:  Brockton, MA"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,6,0)="Code $S($D(...):^(),1:"""") replaced with $G(...)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,7,0)="Code is functionally equivalent, but former code was causing problems at"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,8,0)="the site."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,10,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,11,0)="This patch should be installed during off-peak hours when network mail"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,12,0)="activity is low.  This patch can be installed with users on the system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,13,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,15,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,16,0)="1.  If any of these routines is mapped (on systems which allow mapping),"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,17,0)="    disable mapping for the affected routine(s)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,18,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,19,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,20,0)="3.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,21,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,22,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,23,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",25,1,24,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
