^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",34,1,49,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",34,1,50,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",34,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",34,1,52,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",34,1,53,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",34,1,54,0)="----------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",34,1,55,0)="XMSMAIL        4652921         5893340        59"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",34,1,56,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",34,1,57,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,0)="64 SEQ #59^2980712^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,0)="^^35^35^2980712"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,1,0)="MailMan patch XM*7.1*64 re-introduces an entry point which was inadvertently"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,2,0)="left out of a routine in a previous patch (XM*7.1*55)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,3,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,4,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,5,0)="This patch may be installed at any time.  It will not interfere with any"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,6,0)="user activity."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,7,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,9,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,10,0)="1.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,11,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,12,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,13,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,14,0)="3.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,15,0)="    Transport Global: "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,16,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,17,0)="       Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,18,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,19,0)="       Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,20,0)="       Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,21,0)="4.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,22,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,23,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,24,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,25,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,26,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,27,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,29,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,30,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,31,0)="----------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,32,0)="XMUT5R1        2356802         2364104        55,64"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,33,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,34,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",35,1,35,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,0)="65 SEQ #60^2980725^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,0)="^^45^45^2980725"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,1,0)="MailMan patch XM*7.1*65 addresses a problem experienced on FORUM."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,3,0)="Someone from a remote site sent a message to G.EVERYBODY@FORUM.  This group"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,4,0)="is used to broadcast messages VA-wide.  There are four authorized senders"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,5,0)="for the group, one of which is POSTMASTER.  The background job which receives"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,6,0)="messages from remote sites has its XMDUZ set to .5, which is the POSTMASTER."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,7,0)="So MailMan considered this remote sender to be authorized to address the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,8,0)="group.  This is not acceptable."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,10,0)="This patch adds a restriction to addressing groups with authorized senders,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,11,0)="namely, remote senders cannot send mail to such groups."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,13,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,14,0)="This patch should be installed after-hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,15,0)="minimum.  You should put the XMUSER option out of order. The filers should"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,16,0)="be shut down."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,17,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,18,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,19,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,20,0)="1.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,21,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,22,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,23,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,24,0)="3.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,25,0)="    Transport Global: "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,26,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,27,0)="       Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,28,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,29,0)="       Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,30,0)="       Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,31,0)="4.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,32,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,33,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,34,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,35,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,36,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,37,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,39,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,40,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,41,0)="-------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,42,0)="XMA21G        11073971        11358760        31,36,65"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,43,0)="XMR            6876928         6901880        30,34,65"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,44,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",36,1,45,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,0)="58 SEQ #61^2980831^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,0)="^^41^41^2980831"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,1,0)="MailMan patch XM*7.1*58 addresses the following NOIS:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,2,0)="BRK-0897-10428, BRX-1196-10659, & HOU-0897-71511"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,3,0)="and was tested at those respective sites:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,4,0)="Brockton, MA; Bronx, NY; Houston, TX"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,5,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,6,0)="Aborts occasionally occurred during remote transmission when one transmission"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,7,0)="task was attempting to add a record to the transmit audit multiple, just as"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,8,0)="another task was killing the multiple.  This patch fixes that."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,10,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,11,0)="This patch should be installed after-hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,12,0)="minimum.  You should put the XMUSER option out of order. The filers should"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,13,0)="be shut down."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,14,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,15,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,16,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,17,0)="1.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,18,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,19,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,20,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,21,0)="3.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,22,0)="    Transport Global: "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,23,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,24,0)="       Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,25,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,26,0)="       Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,27,0)="       Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,28,0)="4.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",37,1,29,0)=""
