^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,23,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,24,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,25,0)="Note: This patch should be installed after-hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,26,0)="minimum."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,27,0)="1.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,28,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,29,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,30,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,31,0)="3.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,32,0)="    Transport Global: "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,33,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,34,0)="       Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,35,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,36,0)="       Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,37,0)="       Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,38,0)="    Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,39,0)="4.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",39,1,40,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,0)="70 SEQ #64^2990201^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,0)="^^42^42^2990201"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,1,0)="MailMan patch XM*7.1*70 is a patch for a patch released in error (XM*7.1*68)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,2,0)="It fixes a bug as described in NOIS TAM-1098-30390."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,3,0)="Test site is Tampa, FL."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,4,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,5,0)="If a remote address begins with ""F."", MailMan thinks the address is a fax."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,6,0)="This patch ensures that MailMan does not confuse a fax address with a remote"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,7,0)="address."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,9,0)="Note: This patch should be installed after-hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,10,0)="minimum."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,11,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,12,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,13,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,14,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,15,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,17,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,18,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,19,0)="-------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,20,0)="XMAD1A         6312375         7330837        36,70"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,21,0)="XMJMQ         15112719        15192669        40,57,70"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,22,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,23,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,24,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,25,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,26,0)="Note: This patch should be installed after-hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,27,0)="minimum."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,28,0)="1.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,29,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,30,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,31,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,32,0)="3.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,33,0)="    Transport Global: "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,34,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,35,0)="       Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,36,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,37,0)="       Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,38,0)="       Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,39,0)="    Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,40,0)="                                                                          =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,41,0)="4.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",40,1,42,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,0)="67 SEQ #65^2990201^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,0)="^^61^61^2990201"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,1,0)="MailMan patch XM*7.1*67 adds a new key, 'XM NO BROADCASTS',"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,2,0)="in response to an Initial Requirements Analysis (IRA):"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,3,0)="""MailMan - Screen Out Selected Users""."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,4,0)="Coincidentally, it also fulfills the suggestion of E3R 10653."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,5,0)="This patch was tested at Wilkes-Barre, PA."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,6,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,7,0)="Any user possessing the key 'XM NO BROADCASTS'"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,8,0)="will NOT receive ANY broadcast messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,10,0)="This IRA was initiated because users with accounts in multiple sites were"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,11,0)="seeing the same broadcast message everywhere they logged on.  These users"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,12,0)="wanted a way to avoid broadcast messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,13,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,14,0)="When and if you assign this key to a user, you should advise them that"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,15,0)="they will not see any broadcast messages at all."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,16,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,17,0)="This patch also deletes two keys which are not used by MailMan:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,18,0)="XMPRIORITY and XMPRIORITY-OVERRIDE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,19,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,20,0)="Note: This patch may be installed at any time."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,21,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,22,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,23,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,24,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,25,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,27,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,28,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,29,0)="-------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,30,0)="XMADJF1        8724294         9044468        44,52,67"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,31,0)="XMGAPI3        3149530         3505605        29,44,67"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,32,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,33,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,34,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,35,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,36,0)="Note: This patch may be installed at any time."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,37,0)="1.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,38,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,39,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,40,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,41,0)="3.  On the Manage MailMan:Local Delivery Management menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,42,0)="    option to stop the background filer:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,43,0)="       STOP background filer"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,44,0)="   Are you sure you want the BACKGROUND FILERS to STOP delivering mail? NO//YES"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,45,0)="                                                                            ==="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,46,0)="   << Background filer will stop soon. >>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,47,0)="4.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,48,0)="    Transport Global: "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,49,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,50,0)="       Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,51,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,52,0)="       Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,53,0)="       Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,54,0)="    Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,55,0)="                                                                          =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,56,0)="5.  On the Manage MailMan:Local Delivery Management menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,57,0)="    option to start the background filer:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,58,0)="       START background filer"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,59,0)="   << Background filer will start soon. >>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,60,0)="6.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",41,1,61,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,0)="69 SEQ #66^2990316^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,0)="^^39^39^2990316"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,1,0)="MailMan patch XM*7.1*69 fixes a bug as described in NOIS ISH-0199-40487."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,2,0)="Test site:  CIOFO-HINES."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,3,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,4,0)="Under certain conditions, a message which is in the process of arriving"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,5,0)="from another site may be deleted from the Postmaster's ARRIVING basket,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,6,0)="thus preventing it from being delivered, and causing it to eventually be"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,7,0)="purged from the system.  This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,9,0)="Note: This patch may be installed at any time."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,10,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,11,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,12,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,13,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,14,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,16,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,17,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,18,0)="-------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,19,0)="XMA3          14693914        14700672        37,54,69"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,20,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,21,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,22,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,23,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,24,0)="Note: This patch may be installed at any time."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,25,0)="1.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,26,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,27,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,28,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,29,0)="3.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,30,0)="    Transport Global: "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,31,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,32,0)="       Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,33,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,34,0)="       Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,35,0)="       Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,36,0)="    Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,37,0)="                                                                          =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,38,0)="4.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",42,1,39,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,0)="50^2990803^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,0)="^^1001^1001^2990803"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,1,0)="Patch XM*7.1*50.  The BIG patch!  It is important that you read this patch"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,2,0)="description and follow the install instructions."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,3,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,4,0)="Test Sites:  DOMAIN.EXT; GATEWAY.DOMAIN.EXT; Indianapolis, IN;"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,5,0)="             Montana HCS, MT; San Francisco, CA; SAIC Corp.;"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,6,0)="             German Heart Institute, Berlin, Germany; San Francisco CIOFO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,7,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,8,0)="The changes included in this patch are so extensive, that several of the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,9,0)="MailMan manuals have been rewritten.  The full patch description and the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,10,0)="new manuals are in PDF documents on the infrastructure web site at:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,11,0)="http://www.vista.domain.ext/"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,12,0)="softserv/infrastr.uct/notebook/active/xm_patch_50_notebook.htm"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,13,0)="- XM*7.1*50 Patch Description"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,14,0)="- MailMan V.7.1 & XM*7.1*50 Release Notes"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,15,0)="- MailMan V.7.1 & XM*7.1*50 Getting Started"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,16,0)="- MailMan V.7.1 & XM*7.1*50 User Manual"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,17,0)="- MailMan V.7.1 & XM*7.1*50 Programmer Manual"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,18,0)="- MailMan V.7.1 & XM*7.1*50 Technical Manual"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,19,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,20,0)="Highlights of the patch:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,21,0)="- Addresses 54 distinct NOIS and 40 distinct E3R."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,22,0)="- For those sites requesting it, performs, along with follow-on patch"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,23,0)="  XM*7.1*51, automatic domain name change from .DOMAIN.EXT to .DOMAIN.EXT, as"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,24,0)="  well as domain rename. This patch adds the new domain names as synonyms to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,25,0)="  the current domain names.  XM*7.1*51 will actually change the domain names."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,26,0)="  (XM*7.1*51 will be released after all sites have installed XM*7.1*50.)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,27,0)="- Adds many new APIs."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,28,0)="- Replaces the old user help frames with an entire new set of help frames."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,29,0)="  (The IRM help frames have not been updated.)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,30,0)="- Makes many changes to the MailMan DDs."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,31,0)="- Renames file 3.7 from MAIL BOX to MAILBOX."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,32,0)="- Renames file 4.3 from KERNEL SITE PARAMETERS to MAILMAN SITE PARAMETERS."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,33,0)="- Improves global integrity checker."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,34,0)="- Improves message search."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,35,0)="- Insists that users must have a mailbox and an access code in order to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,36,0)="  receive messages.  This is to ensure that messages do not accumulate in"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,37,0)="  inactive mailboxes, never to be deleted.  It is very important that any"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,38,0)="  ficticious user be properly set up so that mail deliveries to these users"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,39,0)="  are not stopped."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,40,0)="- Implements message filtering."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,41,0)="- Improves local message delivery system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,42,0)="- Adds 'full screen' user interface for managing and reading messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,43,0)="- Rewrites 'classic' user interface to improve maintainability."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,44,0)="- Most ^XMA* routines have been superseded by other routines."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,45,0)="- (new) ^XMJ* routines comprise the user interface."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,46,0)="- (new) ^XMK* routines perform message posting."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,47,0)="- (new) ^XMT* routines perform message delivery."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,48,0)="- (new) ^XMX* routines comprise the APIs."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,49,0)="- (new) ^XMV* routines comprise user identity."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,50,0)="- ^XMR* has been rewritten."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,51,0)="- Improves the remote message xref, ^XMBX(3.9,""AI"", by enabling it to handle"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,52,0)="longer message IDs.  Specifically, the xref has changed"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,53,0)="from: ^XMBX(3.9,""AI"",site@msgid,xmz)=fm date/time"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,54,0)="to:   ^XMBX(3.9,""AI"",site,msgid,xmz)=fm date "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,55,0)="The post-init will reconfigure the xref.  (This could take anywhere from 1/2"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,56,0)="hour to several hours, depending on how large the global is.)  Here's a tip:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,57,0)="You can cut down the time that this will take by running option"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,58,0)="XMMGR-PURGE-AI-XREF (AI x-Ref Purge of Received Network Messages)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,59,0)="prior to installing this patch.  This will reduce the number of xrefs in the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,60,0)="AI xref global."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,61,0)="- Enables message number recycling.  To do this,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,62,0)="--A new field (17.1, MAX DIGITS FOR MESSAGE NUMBER) has been added to file"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,63,0)="4.3, to let each site decide how large the numbers may get before they"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,64,0)="recycle and start again (from 100000).  The post-init will set it to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,65,0)="the maximum length of your site's existing message numbers.  (If it's less"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,66,0)="than 7, it will be set to 7.  If it's greater than 14, it will be set to 14.)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,67,0)="You may change it afterward."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,68,0)="--A new field (31, LOCAL CREATE DATE) has been added to file 3.9.  The post-"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,69,0)="init will go through the file 3.9, populate the new field with the date"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,70,0)="the message was sent, and create the new ""C"" xref.  (This will take about"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,71,0)="1 hour per 200,000 messages.)  Here's a tip:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,72,0)="You can cut down the time that this will take by running option"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,73,0)="XMPURGE-BY-DATE (Purge Messages by Origination Date)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,74,0)="and XMAUTOPURGE (Automatic Purge of MailMan Messages)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,75,0)="prior to installing this patch.  This will reduce the number of messages"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,76,0)="in file 3.9."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,77,0)="--The message purge processes have been changed to operate off LOCAL"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,78,0)="CREATE DATE.  The date purge routine is now much faster, since it has an"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,79,0)="appropriate xref to work with.  The weekday unreferenced messages purge can"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,80,0)="focus better and thus be more efficient."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,81,0)="--Other fields have changed their focus from message number to the LOCAL"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,82,0)="CREATE DATE:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,83,0)="File 3.7, MailBox:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,84,0)="3.7,1.2   MESSAGE @ REINSTATEMENT becomes DATE @ REINSTATEMENT (The post-"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,85,0)="init will change any existing message numbers in this field to their equiv-"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,86,0)="alent dates."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,87,0)="File 4.3, MailMan Site Parameters:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,88,0)="4.3,4.301 NO-PURGE MESSAGES BUFFER becomes NO-PURGE DAYS BUFFER (The post-"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,89,0)="init will set this field to null, which defaults to 2 days.  You may change"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,90,0)="it afterward."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,91,0)="4.302,3   FIRST MESSAGE TO PROCESS  becomes START PURGE DATE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,92,0)="4.302,4   LAST MESSAGE TO PROCESS   becomes STOP PURGE DATE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,93,0)="4.302,8   LAST MESSAGE PROCESSED    becomes LAST DATE PROCESSED"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,94,0)="4.3,4.304 WEEKDAY MESSAGES TO PURGE becomes WEEKDAY DAYS TO PURGE (Any value"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,95,0)="your site has in this field will be changed by the post-init from number of"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,96,0)="messages to the equivalent number of days.  You may change it afterward.)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,97,0)="4.3,142   NO-PURGE DAYS BUFFER      becomes NO-PURGE DAYS BUFFER (LOCAL)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,98,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,99,0)="NOTES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,100,0)="a. This patch should be installed after hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,101,0)="minimum.  It should not be queued, because TaskMan should not be running."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,102,0)="b. This patch requires Kernel patches XU*8.0*67, XU*8.0*112, and XU*8.0*113."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,103,0)="c. For any site running MAS (all VAMCs), this patch requires FileMan patch"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,104,0)="DI*22.0*1.  Caution: KIDS will not check for this patch because not all"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,105,0)="sites run MAS.  It is up to each site running MAS to check for DI*22.0*1."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,106,0)="d. All MailMan users, including fictitious users, must have an access code,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,107,0)="or they will no longer receive mail."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,108,0)="e. To shorten installation time, which runs about 1 hour per 200,000 messages"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,109,0)="in file 3.9, you might consider running the message purges the day before"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,110,0)="the installation:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,111,0)="- XMMGR-PURGE-AI-XREF (AI x-Ref Purge of Received Network Messages)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,112,0)="- XMPURGE-BY-DATE (Purge Messages by Origination Date)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,113,0)="- XMAUTOPURGE (Automatic Purge of MailMan Messages)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,114,0)="f. DSM sites running SlotMaster may see routine mapping problems with ZSLOT"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,115,0)="users, even after disabling mapping.  Therefore, such sites should consider"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,116,0)="the following steps:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,117,0)="- Shutdown ZSLOT on all nodes."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,118,0)="- Disable all mapped XM routines."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,119,0)="- Load this patch."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,120,0)="- Enter manual edits."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,121,0)="- Rebuild mapped routine sets."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,122,0)="- Shutdown/restart all DSM configurations."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,123,0)="An alternative to the above steps is to disable all mapped XM routines about"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,124,0)="a week before you load this patch.  That way you wouldn't need to shutdown"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,125,0)="ZSLOT or shutdown/restart DSM configurations."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,126,0)="g. If your site is running POP3, you should immediately load patch XM*7.1*71"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,127,0)="after installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,128,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,129,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,130,0)="This patch deletes the following routines:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,131,0)="XMZTERM      (replaced by XMUTERM in this patch)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,132,0)="XMZTERM1     (replaced by XMUTERM1 in this patch)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,133,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,134,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,135,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,136,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,138,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,139,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,140,0)="----------------------------------------------------------"
