^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,617,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,618,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,619,0)="NOTES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,620,0)="a. This patch should be installed after hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,621,0)="minimum.  It should not be queued, because TaskMan should not be running."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,622,0)="b. This patch requires Kernel patches XU*8.0*67, XU*8.0*112, and XU*8.0*113."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,623,0)="c. For any site running MAS (all VAMCs), this patch requires FileMan patch"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,624,0)="DI*22.0*1.  Caution: KIDS will not check for this patch because not all"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,625,0)="sites run MAS.  It is up to each site running MAS to check for DI*22.0*1."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,626,0)="d. All MailMan users, including fictitious users, must have an access code,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,627,0)="or they will no longer receive mail."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,628,0)="e. To shorten installation time, which runs about 1 hour per 200,000 messages"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,629,0)="in file 3.9, you might consider running the message purges the day before"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,630,0)="the installation:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,631,0)="- XMMGR-PURGE-AI-XREF (AI x-Ref Purge of Received Network Messages)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,632,0)="- XMPURGE-BY-DATE (Purge Messages by Origination Date)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,633,0)="- XMAUTOPURGE (Automatic Purge of MailMan Messages)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,634,0)="f. DSM sites running SlotMaster may see routine mapping problems with ZSLOT"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,635,0)="users, even after disabling mapping.  Therefore, such sites should consider"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,636,0)="the following steps:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,637,0)="- Shutdown ZSLOT on all nodes."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,638,0)="- Disable all mapped XM routines."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,639,0)="- Load this patch."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,640,0)="- Enter manual edits."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,641,0)="- Rebuild mapped routine sets."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,642,0)="- Shutdown/restart all DSM c nfigurations."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,643,0)="An alternative to the above steps is to disable all mapped XM routines about"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,644,0)="a week before you load this patch.  That way you wouldn't need to shutdown"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,645,0)="ZSLOT or shutdown/restart DSM configurations."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,646,0)="g. If your site is running POP3, you should immediately load patch XM*7.1*71"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,647,0)="after installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,648,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,649,0)="INSTRUCTIONS:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,650,0)="1. This patch replaces routine ^XMRPCTS1, which contains your site's TWIX"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,651,0)="   routing info.  Before you install this patch, copy the current TWIX info"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,652,0)="   from that routine at your site.  After you install this patch, edit"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,653,0)="   the new ^XMRPCTS1 to set your site's current TWIX info.  Specifically:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,654,0)="XMRPCTS1     ;(KC-VAMC)/XXX-Simple PCTS front end to MailMan ;03/19/98  11:10"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,655,0)="     ;;7.1;MailMan;**6,50**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,656,0)="     N XMUS,XMFM,XMSTR,XMRI,XMTO,XMABORT"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,657,0)="     ;+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,658,0)="     ;All should be sent to XXX@VHA.DMIA the local PCTS Domain"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,659,0)="     ;Edit these for your site.               <---Copy your site's TWIX info"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,660,0)="     S XMUS=""XXXX"" ;Local routing indicator   <---from this line"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,661,0)="     S XMFM=""YYYY"" ;from line                 <---and this line"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,662,0)="     I XMUS=""XXXX""!(XMFM=""YYYY"") S %=""FIX Routing codes !!!""_XMPCTS0(""ERR"")"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,663,0)="     ;-------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,664,0)="2.  The TIME ZONE field in file 4.3 must have your site's time zone in it."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,665,0)="    Please check and ensure that it is there."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,666,0)="3.  DSM SITES: Disable all mapped XM routines.  In step 13, we'll rebuild"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,667,0)="    the map set with *different* routines, because many have become obsolete."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,668,0)="4.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option to load"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,669,0)="    the patch into a transport global."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,670,0)="5.  On the Manage MailMan:Local Delivery Management menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,671,0)="    option to stop the background filer:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,672,0)="       STOP background filer (XMAD)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,673,0)="Are you sure you want the BACKGROUND FILERS to STOP delivering mail NO// YES"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,674,0)="                                                                         ==="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,675,0)="<<< Mail Deliveries will stop momentarily. >>>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,676,0)="<<   Background filer will stop before delivering the next message !!! >>>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,677,0)="6.  Stop TaskMan.  You may also wish to shut down HL7 filers/LLP's and other"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,678,0)="    background tasks which may attempt to create new messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,679,0)="7.  Place option XMUSER out of order.  (We do it ourselves, instead of letting"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,680,0)="KIDS do it, because we're going to place XMUSER back in order during the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,681,0)="post-init.)  To place XMUSER out of order, enter FileMan, and:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,682,0)="VA FileMan 21.0"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,683,0)="Select OPTION: ENTER OR EDIT FILE ENTRIES  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,684,0)="               =========================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,685,0)="INPUT TO WHAT FILE: OPTION// <press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,686,0)="                             =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,687,0)="EDIT WHICH FIELD: ALL// OUT OF ORDER MESSAGE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,688,0)="                        ====================    "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,689,0)="THEN EDIT FIELD: <press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,690,0)="                 =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,691,0)="Select OPTION NAME: XMUSER          MailMan Menu"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,692,0)="                    ======"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,693,0)="OUT OF ORDER MESSAGE: Loading MailMan patch XM*7.1*50"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,694,0)="                      ==============================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,695,0)="Select OPTION NAME: <press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,696,0)="                    =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,697,0)="Select OPTION: <press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,698,0)="               =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,699,0)="8.  If you journal the global ^XMBX, your journal space may fill up when the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,700,0)="    ^XMBX(3.9,""AI"", xref global is reconfigured.  You may wish to disable"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,701,0)="    journaling.  To disable journaling:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,702,0)="8a. DSM SITES: You may disable journaling for a particular global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,703,0)="    >D ^%GLOMAN"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,704,0)="     =========="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,705,0)="    Global Management Utility"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,706,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,707,0)="    Global > ^XMBX"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,708,0)="              ===="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,709,0)="    ^XMBX is currently defined"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,710,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,711,0)="      1. Show GLOBAL Characteristics"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,712,0)="      2. Change Access Privileges"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,713,0)="      3. Change Journaling Capability"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,714,0)="      4. Change DATA GROWTH AREA"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,715,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,716,0)="    Enter option > 3"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,717,0)="                   ="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,718,0)="    Journaling [E=Enabled/D=Disabled]   <E>   D"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,719,0)="                                              ="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,720,0)="     - Characteristics updated"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,721,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,722,0)="      1. Show GLOBAL Characteristics"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,723,0)="      2. Change Access Privileges"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,724,0)="      3. Change Journaling Capability"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,725,0)="      4. Change DATA GROWTH AREA"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,726,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,727,0)="    Enter option > <press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,728,0)="                   =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,729,0)="    Global > ^<press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,730,0)="              =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,731,0)="8b. CACHE SITES: You may disable journaling for a specific job:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,732,0)="    %SYS>D DISABLE^%NOJRN"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,733,0)="         ================"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,734,0)="8c. MSM SITES: Consult MSM documentation for how to disable journaling."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,735,0)="9.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,736,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,737,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,738,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,739,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,740,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,741,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,742,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME:    XM*7.1*50     Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,743,0)="                         ========="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,744,0)="     => <header>  ;Created on <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,745,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,746,0)=" This Distribution was loaded on <date/time> with header of "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,747,0)=" <header>  ;Created on <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,748,0)=" It consisted of the following Install(s):"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,749,0)=" XM*7.1*50"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,750,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,751,0)="    XM*7.1*50"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,752,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,753,0)=" Install Questions for XM*7.1*50"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,754,0)=" Incoming Files:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,755,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,756,0)="    3.6       BULLETIN  (Partial Definition)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,757,0)=" Note:  You already have the 'BULLETIN' File."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,758,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,759,0)="    3.7       MAILBOX"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,760,0)=" *BUT YOU ALREADY HAVE 'MAIL BOX' AS FILE #3.7!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,761,0)=" Shall I write over your MAIL BOX File? YES// <press enter>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,762,0)="                                              ============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,763,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,764,0)="    3.73      MESSAGES TO BE NEW AT A LATER DATE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,765,0)=" Note:  You already have the 'MESSAGES TO BE NEW AT A LATER DATE' File."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,766,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,767,0)="    3.8       MAIL GROUP  (Partial Definition)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,768,0)=" Note:  You already have the 'MAIL GROUP' File."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,769,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,770,0)="    3.9       MESSAGE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,771,0)=" Note:  You already have the 'MESSAGE' File."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,772,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,773,0)="    4.2       DOMAIN  (Partial Definition)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,774,0)=" Note:  You already have the 'DOMAIN' File."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,775,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,776,0)="    4.2997    REMOTE USER DIRECTORY  (Partial Definition)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,777,0)=" Note:  You already have the 'REMOTE USER DIRECTORY' File."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,778,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,779,0)="    4.2999    MESSAGE STATISTICS  (Partial Definition)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,780,0)=" Note:  You already have the 'MESSAGE STATISTICS' File."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,781,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,782,0)="    4.3       MAILMAN SITE PARAMETERS"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,783,0)=" *BUT YOU ALREADY HAVE 'KERNEL SITE PARAMETERS' AS FILE #4.3!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,784,0)=" Shall I write over your KERNEL SITE PARAMETERS File? YES// <press enter>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,785,0)="                                                            ============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,786,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,787,0)=" Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES// YES"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,788,0)="                                                                   ==="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,789,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,790,0)=" ----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,791,0)=" NOTE:  If you want users to be able to use MailMan during the post-init,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,792,0)=" it's important that you answer NO to the following question,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,793,0)=" otherwise KIDS will place all options in this patch out of order until"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,794,0)=" the install is finished:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,795,0)=" ----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,796,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,797,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,798,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,799,0)="        ... <lots of installation stuff is shown> ..."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,800,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,801,0)=" ----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,802,0)=" NOTE: When the POST-INIT starts, continue with steps 10 through 17."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,803,0)=" The following is displayed when the post-init starts:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,804,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,805,0)=" Running Post-Install Routine: ^XMYPOST9"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,806,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,807,0)="Fire xrefs on 'timezone' field of the MailMan site parms file."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,808,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,809,0)="Check/Redo AI xref..."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,810,0)=" ----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,811,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,812,0)="        ... <lots of installation stuff is shown> ..."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,813,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,814,0)=" XM*7.1*50 Installed. "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,815,0)="               <shows date and time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,816,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,817,0)=" Install Message sent #<shows message number>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,818,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,819,0)=" Starting Menu Rebuild:  <shows date and time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,820,0)="        ... <shows rebuilding of menus> ..."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,821,0)=" Install Completed."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,822,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,823,0)="10. Start TaskMan.  If you shut down HL7 filers/LLPs or any other background"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,824,0)="    tasks, you may restart them."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,825,0)="11. Start the background filer."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,826,0)="    On the Manage MailMan:Local Delivery Management menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,827,0)="    option to start the background filer:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,828,0)="       START background filer"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,829,0)="   << Background filer will start soon. >>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,830,0)="12. Place option XMUSER back in order by entering FileMan and:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,831,0)="VA FileMan 21.0"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,832,0)="Select OPTION: ENTER OR EDIT FILE ENTRIES  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,833,0)="               =========================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,834,0)="INPUT TO WHAT FILE: OPTION// <press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,835,0)="                             =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,836,0)="EDIT WHICH FIELD: ALL// OUT OF ORDER MESSAGE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,837,0)="                        ====================    "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,838,0)="THEN EDIT FIELD: <press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,839,0)="                 =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,840,0)="Select OPTION NAME: XMUSER          MailMan Menu"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,841,0)="                    ======"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,842,0)="OUT OF ORDER MESSAGE: Loading MailMan patch XM*7.1*50"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,843,0)="           Replace @"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,844,0)="                  === "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,845,0)="   SURE YOU WANT TO DELETE? Y  (Yes)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,846,0)="                           ==="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,847,0)="Select OPTION NAME: <press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,848,0)="                    =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,849,0)="Select OPTION: <press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,850,0)="               =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,851,0)="13. DSM SITES: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,852,0)="    Many routines have become obsolete and should be removed from the map"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,853,0)="    set.  Here is a new recommended list of routines to map, should your"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,854,0)="    site choose to map routines:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,855,0)="    Minimum                           Additional"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,856,0)="    -------                           ----------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,857,0)="    XM                                XMBPOST"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,858,0)="    XMC1                              XMC,XMC1*"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,859,0)="    XMJ*                              XMD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,860,0)="    XML1CRC,XML4CRC*,XMLSWP*          XMK*"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,861,0)="    XMR,XMR0*                         XML"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,862,0)="    XMS,XMS0*                         XMR1*"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,863,0)="                                      XMS1,XMSMAIL"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,864,0)="                                      XMVVITAE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,865,0)="                                      XMXSEC"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,866,0)="                                      XMXUTIL"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,867,0)="14. This patch replaces routine ^XMRPCTS1, which contains your site's TWIX"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,868,0)="    routing info.  In step 1, you copied the TWIX info for your site from"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,869,0)="    that routine.  Now, edit the new ^XMRPCTS1 to set your site's TWIX info."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,870,0)="    Specifically:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,871,0)="XMRPCTS1     ;(KC-VAMC)/XXX-Simple PCTS front end to MailMan ;03/19/98  11:10"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,872,0)="     ;;7.1;MailMan;**6,50**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,873,0)="     N XMUS,XMFM,XMSTR,XMRI,XMTO,XMABORT"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,874,0)="     ;+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,875,0)="     ;All should be sent to XXX@VHA.DMIA the local PCTS Domain"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,876,0)="     ;Edit these for your site.               <---Put your site's TWIX info"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,877,0)="     S XMUS=""XXXX"" ;Local routing indicator   <---at this line"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,878,0)="     S XMFM=""YYYY"" ;from line                 <---and this line"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,879,0)="     I XMUS=""XXXX""!(XMFM=""YYYY"") S %=""FIX Routing codes !!!""_XMPCTS0(""ERR"")"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,880,0)="     ;-------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,881,0)="15. For those sites using class III ^ASKX820, you should edit routine"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,882,0)="^ASKX820.  It calls ENT^XMAD1, an illegal entry point which no longer exists."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,883,0)="Replace it with a call to ENT1^XMD."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,884,0)="16. For those sites running class III WordManager, you will have to find the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,885,0)="    WordManager routine containing D OK^XMA22.  For version 5.01, it's in"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,886,0)="    routine ^WMWTWM.  It may be in other routines in other versions."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,887,0)="    OK^XMA22 is an undocumented entry point into MailMan which no longer"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,888,0)="    exists.  Edit the WordManager routine as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,889,0)="Replace:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,890,0)="        S ^XMB(3.9,XMZ,2,0)=""^^""_(J-1)_""^""_(J-1)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,891,0)="EDIT    ;"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,892,0)="        S DIE=""^XMB(3.9,"",DA=XMZ,DR="".01;3"" D ^DIE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,893,0)="REC     ;"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,894,0)="        S XMMG=$P(^DIC(3,DUZ,0),""^"",1) D DES^XMA21 G:X=""^"" EXIT"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,895,0)="SEND    ;"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,896,0)="        S XMR="""",XMTEXT=""^XMB(3.9,XMZ,2,"" D OK^XMA22,EN1^XMD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,897,0)="EXIT    U TRM S R7=ZR7,TRM=$I K ZR7,ZMM"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,898,0)="with:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,899,0)="        S ^XMB(3.9,XMZ,2,0)=""^^""_(J-1)_""^""_(J-1)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,900,0)="EDIT    ;"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,901,0)="        ;S DIE=""^XMB(3.9,"",DA=XMZ,DR="".01;3"" D ^DIE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,902,0)="REC     ;"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,903,0)="        ;S XMMG=$P(^DIC(3,DUZ,0),""^"",1) D DES^XMA21 G:X=""^"" EXIT"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,904,0)="SEND    ;"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,905,0)="        ;S XMR="""",XMTEXT=""^XMB(3.9,XMZ,2,"" D OK^XMA22,EN1^XMD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,906,0)="ERS     ; EDIT, REC, SEND"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,907,0)="        N XMV,XMRESTR,XMINSTR,XMSUBJ,XMABORT"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,908,0)="        S XMABORT=0"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,909,0)="        S XMSUBJ=XMSUB"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,910,0)="        D INIT^XMVVITAE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,911,0)="        D ES^XMJMSO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,912,0)="        D BODY^XMJMS(XMDUZ,XMZ,XMSUBJ,.XMRESTR,.XMABORT)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,913,0)="        I XMABORT D KILLMSG^XMXUTIL(XMZ) G EXIT"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,914,0)="        D INIT^XMXADDR"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,915,0)="        D TOWHOM^XMJMT(XMDUZ,""Send"",.XMINSTR,.XMRESTR,.XMABORT)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,916,0)="        D:'XMABORT SENDMSG^XMJMSO(XMDUZ,XMZ,XMSUBJ,.XMINSTR,.XMRESTR,.XMABORT)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,917,0)="        D:XMABORT KILLMSG^XMXUTIL(XMZ)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,918,0)="        D CLEANUP^XMXADDR"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,919,0)="EXIT    U TRM S R7=ZR7,TRM=$I K ZR7,ZMM"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,920,0)="17. For those sites using class III ^BJMAIL*, you should edit routine ^BJMAIL"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,921,0)="to correct its egregious violations of the SAC.  If you don't, MailMan will"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,922,0)="will not function properly.  Once you have edited ^BJMAIL, you may delete"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,923,0)="routine ^BJMAIL1, since it will no longer be used.  Edit ^BJMAIL as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,924,0)="Replace:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,925,0)="MSG    Q:'$D(T)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,926,0)="  ... thru ..."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,927,0)="WRITE  ;Write a message - not part of the main program."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,928,0)="With:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,929,0)="MSG     ;"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,930,0)="        N XMINSTR"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,931,0)="        Q:'$D(T)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,932,0)="        Q:'$O(T(0))"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,933,0)="        D GROUP"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,934,0)="        Q:$O(TO(""""))="""""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,935,0)="        I $G(CONFIRM) S XMINSTR(""FLAGS"")=$G(XMINSTR(""FLAGS""))_""R"""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,936,0)="        I $G(PRIO) S XMINSTR(""FLAGS"")=$G(XMINSTR(""FLAGS""))_""P"""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,937,0)="        I $G(INFO) S XMINSTR(""FLAGS"")=$G(XMINSTR(""FLAGS""))_""I"""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,938,0)="        I '$D(FROM) S FROM=.5"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,939,0)="        D SETFROM^XMD(.FROM,.XMINSTR)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,940,0)="        I '$D(TITLE) S TITLE=""Title not specified by sender"""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,941,0)="        I $L(TITLE)>65 S TITLE=$E(TITLE,1,65)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,942,0)="        I $L(TITLE)<3 S TITLE=TITLE_""..."""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,943,0)="        D SENDMSG^XMXAPI(FROM,TITLE,""T"",.TO,.XMINSTR)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,944,0)="        K CONFIRM,FROM,GROUP,INFO,PRIO,T,TITLE,TO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,945,0)="        Q"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,946,0)="GROUP   ;"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,947,0)="        Q:$G(GROUP)="""""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,948,0)="        I +GROUP=GROUP S:$D(^XMB(3.8,GROUP,0)) TO($P(^XMB(3.8,GROUP,0),U))="""" Q"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,949,0)="        S TO(""G.""_GROUP)="""""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,950,0)="        Q"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,951,0)="WRITE   ;Write a message - not part of the main program"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,952,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,953,0)=" ----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,954,0)=" NOTE: Once the POST-INIT stops, continue with steps 18 through the end."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,955,0)=" ----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,956,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,957,0)="18.  If you disabled journaling in step 8, you should enable it again here."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,958,0)="18a. DSM SITES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,959,0)="    >D ^%GLOMAN"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,960,0)="    Global Management Utility"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,961,0)="    Global > ^XMBX"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,962,0)="              ===="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,963,0)="    ^XMBX is currently defined"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,964,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,965,0)="      1. Show GLOBAL Characteristics"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,966,0)="      2. Change Access Privileges"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,967,0)="      3. Change Journaling Capability"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,968,0)="      4. Change DATA GROWTH AREA"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,969,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,970,0)="    Enter option > 3"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,971,0)="                   ="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,972,0)="    Journaling [E=Enabled/D=Disabled]   <D>   E"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,973,0)="                                              ="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,974,0)="     - Characteristics updated"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,975,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,976,0)="      1. Show GLOBAL Characteristics"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,977,0)="      2. Change Access Privileges"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,978,0)="      3. Change Journaling Capability"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,979,0)="      4. Change DATA GROWTH AREA"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,980,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,981,0)="    Enter option > <press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,982,0)="                   =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,983,0)="    Global > ^<press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,984,0)="              =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,985,0)="18b. CACHE SITES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,986,0)="    %SYS>D ENABLE^%NOJRN"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,987,0)="         ==============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,988,0)="18c. MSM SITES: Consult MSM documentation for how to enable journaling."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,989,0)="19. For those sites running POP3, you should load patch XM*7.1*71 immediately"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,990,0)="    after loading this patch.  Other sites may load patch XM*7.1*71 at their"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,991,0)="    leisure."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,992,0)="20. On the KIDS:Utilites menu, use the following option to review the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,993,0)="install:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,994,0)="    Install File Print"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,995,0)="Review the automatic domain name changes which occurred during the post-init."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,996,0)="If there were any errors noted for a particular domain, that domain did not"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,997,0)="have its new name added as a synonym.  (Error messages are preceded by ***,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,998,0)="and tell you what was wrong.)  You must correct the error manually and add"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,999,0)="the synonym manually.  Remember, you are not to change any domain name."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,1000,0)="Just add the new name as a synonym. "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",43,1,1001,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,0)="71 SEQ #68^2990803^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,0)="^^92^92^2990803"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,1,0)="Patch XM*7.1*71"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,3,0)="Test Site:  DOMAIN.EXT"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,4,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,5,0)="In response to E3R #10591, and management directive,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,6,0)="this patch raises the class III POP3 server routines to class I,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,7,0)="and incorporates them into MailMan."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,9,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed after hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,10,0)="minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*50."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,11,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,12,0)="Class III routines ^XMRPOPA, ^XMRPOPB, and ^XMRPOPC are replaced by class I"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,13,0)="routine ^XMRPOP.  These class III routines should be deleted after the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,14,0)="install."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,15,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,16,0)="Class III routine ^XMUCXPOP becomes Class I.  Even though you may already"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,17,0)="have it on your system, this patch treats it as a new routine, because it is"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,18,0)="new to MailMan."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,19,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,20,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,21,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,22,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",44,1,23,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
