^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,0)="85 SEQ #87^2991003^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,0)="^^56^56^2991003"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,1,0)="Patch XM*7.1*85"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,3,0)="NOIS: TAM-0899-32035"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,4,0)="Test Site:  Tampa, FL"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,5,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,6,0)="If a message looks as if it's from a remote site (piece 2 of the zero node"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,7,0)="contains ""@""), but it's really a local message, MailMan aborts trying to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,8,0)="figure out who it's from.  This patch prevents MailMan from aborting."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,10,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed after hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,11,0)="minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*50."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,12,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,13,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,14,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,15,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,16,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,18,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,19,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,20,0)="----------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,21,0)="XMXREPLY       4925239         5097167        50,85"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,22,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,23,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,24,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,26,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,27,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed after hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,28,0)="minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*50."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,29,0)="1.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,30,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,31,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,32,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,33,0)="3.  You do not need to stop TaskMan or the background filers."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,34,0)="4.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,35,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,36,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,37,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,38,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,39,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,40,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,41,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME:    XM*7.1*85     Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,42,0)="                         ========="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,43,0)=" Install Questions:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,44,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,45,0)="                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,46,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,47,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,48,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,49,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,50,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,51,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,52,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <It's up to you.  You may queue it if you wish.>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,53,0)="                ------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,54,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,55,0)="5.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",62,1,56,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,0)="89 SEQ #88^2991003^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,0)="^^64^64^2991003"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,1,0)="Patch XM*7.1*89"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,3,0)="NOIS:  MON-0999-50325, MON-0999-50323"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,4,0)="Test Site:  Montana HCS"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,5,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,6,0)="This patch fixes several problems:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,7,0)="1. If a message is forwarded to * (broadcast to all users), the message"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,8,0)="now becomes 'information only'.  It didn't used to."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,9,0)="2. If a broadcast message has responses, and a user reads the message, the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,10,0)="user is told 'you haven't read response x', whether the user read response"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,11,0)="x or not.  The user won't be pestered about response x any more."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,12,0)="3. If a message is sent to FRED@ANOTHERSITE, and then later forwarded to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,13,0)="FRED at this site, Q does not show FRED; only QD does."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,14,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,15,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed after hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,16,0)="minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*87."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,17,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,18,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,19,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,20,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,21,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,23,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,24,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",63,1,25,0)="----------------------------------------------------------"
