^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,119,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,120,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed after hours, when user activity is at a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,121,0)="minimum.  It requires FileMan patch DI*22.0*17 and MailMan patches XM*7.1*72,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,122,0)="XM*7.1*79, XM*7.1*95, XM*7.1*100, XM*7.1*101, and XM*7.1*121."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,123,0)="1.  Users may be on the system during patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,124,0)="2.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,125,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,126,0)="3.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,127,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,128,0)="4.  You do not need to stop TaskMan or the background filer.  Users may be"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,129,0)="    on the system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,130,0)="5.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,131,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,132,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,133,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,134,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,135,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,136,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,137,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME:    XM*7.1*110    Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,138,0)="                         =========="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,139,0)=" Install Questions:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,140,0)=" Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES// YES"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,141,0)="                                                                   ==="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,142,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,143,0)="                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,144,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,145,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,146,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,147,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,148,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,150,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <It's up to you.  You may queue it if you wish.>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,151,0)="                ------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,152,0)="6.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",97,1,153,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,0)="124 SEQ #123^3000525^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,0)="^^58^58^3000525"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,1,0)="Patch XM*7.1*124"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,3,0)="NOIS: TAM-0400-30289"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,4,0)="Test Site:  Tampa, FL"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,5,0)="The API MOVEMSG^XMXAPI should not require XMK (basket number) when"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,6,0)="XMZ (message IEN in MESSAGE file) is used to identify a message,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,7,0)="but it does.  This patch corrects that."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,9,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,10,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*110."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,11,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,13,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,14,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,15,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,17,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,18,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,19,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,20,0)="XMXMSGS        9819629         9944188        50,110,124"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,21,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,22,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,23,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,24,0)="This patch introduces no new routines."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,25,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,27,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,28,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,29,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*110."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,30,0)="1.  Users may be on the system during installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,31,0)="2.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,32,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,33,0)="3.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,34,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,35,0)="4.  You do not need to stop TaskMan or the background filer."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,36,0)="    Users may be on the system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,37,0)="5.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,38,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,39,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,40,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,41,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,42,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,43,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,44,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME:    XM*7.1*124    Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,45,0)="                         =========="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,46,0)=" Install Questions:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,47,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,48,0)="                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,49,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,50,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,51,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,52,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,53,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,54,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,55,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <It's up to you.  You may queue it if you wish.>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,56,0)="                ------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,57,0)="6.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",98,1,58,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,0)="127 SEQ #124^3000626^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,0)="^^160^160^3000626"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,1,0)="Patch XM*7.1*127"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,3,0)="NOIS: REN-1099-63025"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,4,0)="Test Site:  Reno, NV"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,5,0)="If a message is queued to print later, and the user has chosen to print"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,6,0)="a range of responses, which includes the last response, then when it comes"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,7,0)="time to print the message, if more responses have since arrived, then"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,8,0)="they'll be printed, too."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,10,0)="NOIS: REN-0300-62618"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,11,0)="Test Site:  Reno, NV"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,12,0)="Ensure that MailMan does not decrement new message counters below zero."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,13,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,14,0)="Thanks to additional test sites:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,15,0)="Puget Sound HCS"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,16,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,17,0)="E3R 2731, 5983, 6044 - At the ""Enter message action: IGNORE//"" prompt, two"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,18,0)="new actions have been added to let you access user and mail group help:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,19,0)="  HG   Help:Group Information"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,20,0)="  HU   Help:User Information"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,21,0)="Existing help frames have been updated."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,22,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,23,0)="E3R 3521 - At the ""Enter message action: IGNORE//"" prompt, a new"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,24,0)="action has been added to let you easily print to the VA FileMan Browser:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,25,0)="  BR   Print to the Browser"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,26,0)="Existing help frames have been updated, and a new help frame,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,27,0)="XM-U-M-BROWSER, has been created."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,28,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,29,0)="E3R 5451, 13225 - When filtering a message during message delivery to your"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,30,0)="mailbox, you can now automatically set the message vaporize date.  You can"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,31,0)="also specify that the message should not be made new.  You can set these"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,32,0)="new fields under Personal Preferences:Message Filter Edit."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,33,0)="This will only apply to new messages which you have not seen before.  It"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,34,0)="won't apply to responses or forwarded messages with responses. It won't"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,35,0)="apply when you filter messages which are already in your mailbox. "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,36,0)="A new help frame, XM-U-P-FILTER ACTIONS, has been added, and existing help"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,37,0)="frames have been updated."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,38,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,39,0)="E3R 5100, 13891 - When addressing a message, if an addressee is not found in"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,40,0)="the local user file, MailMan now asks ""Do you want to check the REMOTE USER"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,41,0)="DIRECTORY? No//"".  Also, if we do check it and find an entry, MailMan now"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,42,0)="asks ""OK?"", instead of simply selecting it.  This should prevent unwanted"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,43,0)="addressees, because the REMOTE USER DIRECTORY entry might not be what the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,44,0)="sender wants."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,45,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,46,0)="E3R 6861 - If a user has read all the responses of a message, then when he"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,47,0)="goes to read the message, only the message header is displayed, followed by"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,48,0)="the ""Enter message action: IGNORE//"" prompt.  Inexperienced users may not"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,49,0)="know to enter 'B' to Backup.  MailMan now gives the following information:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,50,0)="""You are at the end of this message.  Enter 'B' to Backup and review it."""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,51,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,52,0)="E3R 13475 - When showing information about a mail group"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,53,0)="(option XMHELPGROUP), in addition to showing member groups, also show"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,54,0)="groups to which the group belongs (Is a member group of:)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,55,0)="To accomplish this, a whole-file cross reference, ""AD"", is added to the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,56,0)=".01 field (MEMBER GROUP NAME) of the MEMBER GROUP multiple of file 3.8."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,57,0)="The post-init, which comes with this patch, will populate the xref."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,58,0)="Existing help frames have been updated."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,59,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,60,0)="Additionally:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,61,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,62,0)="- The ""RI"" (Reply and include responses) command now has a new capability to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,63,0)="let you include responses from another message. This capability is also"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,64,0)="available when creating a new message (""IM"" Include Message)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,65,0)="A new help frame, XM-U-M-INCLUDE MESSAGE, has been added, and existing help"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,66,0)="frames updated."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,67,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,68,0)="- The SCRAMBLE^XMXEDIT API now checks to ensure that the key and hint"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,69,0)="conform to the limitations set by the data dictionary."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,70,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,71,0)="- Those APIs which return error text"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,72,0)="in ^TMP(""XMERR"",$J,<error number>,""TEXT"",i), now also"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,73,0)="return, for errors whose text is in the DIALOG file:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,74,0)="^TMP(""XMERR"",$J,<error number>)=<dialog file ien>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,75,0)="^TMP(""XMERR"",$J,""E"",<dialog file ien>,<error number>)="""""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,76,0)="and, for a very small subset of errors,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,77,0)="if something is wrong with one of the input parameters:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,78,0)="^TMP(""XMERR"",$J,<error number>,""PARAM"",""ID"")=<parameter name>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,79,0)="^TMP(""XMERR"",$J,<error number>,""PARAM"",""VALUE"")=<parameter value>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,80,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,81,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,82,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*110."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,83,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,84,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,85,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,86,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",99,1,87,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
