^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,22,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,23,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,24,0)="This patch introduces no new routines."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,25,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,27,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,28,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,29,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*143."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,30,0)="1.  Users may be on the system during installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,31,0)="2.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,32,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,33,0)="3.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,34,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,35,0)="4.  You do not need to stop TaskMan or the background filer."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,36,0)="    Users may be on the system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",128,1,37,0)="5.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
