^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",131,1,58,0)="6.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",131,1,59,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,0)="165 SEQ #157^3010202^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,0)="^^313^313^3010202"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,1,0)="This is an informational patch for DSM sites only.  Other sites may"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,2,0)="disregard.  DSM sites, you must manually perform updates.  It is important"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,3,0)="that you read this patch and follow the instructions to update your"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,4,0)="XMINET_ALPHA.COM file."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,5,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,6,0)="Patch XM*7.1*165"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,7,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,8,0)="NOIS: none"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,9,0)="Test Sites:  FORUM"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,10,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,11,0)="This patch repeats information in AXP ALERT*117, an excerpt of which follows:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,13,0)="TO:   AXP/VMS DSM SITES"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,14,0)="FROM: National AXP/VMS Technical Support Team"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,15,0)="RE:   AXP ALERT*117  HLSEVEN and XMINETMM ""Openfail errors"""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,16,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,17,0)="HLSEVEN has uncovered a VMS TCP/IP problem regarding DSM not being able to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,18,0)="open a BG device for use. This problem is related to multi-processor CPU"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,19,0)="systems (i.e. ES40, 4100) with more than one CPU. It is not VMS or UCX"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,20,0)="(TCPIP) version specific, as we have identified the problem on systems"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,21,0)="running VMS 6.2-1H3 to VMS 7.2.1 and also UCX version 4.2 ECO 3 as well as"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,22,0)="TCPIP version 5.0A. A condition can occur where the server site will fail"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,23,0)="to open the BGnnnn: device and the HLSEVEN.LOG will report the following"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,24,0)="errors:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,25,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,26,0)="%DSM-F-OPENERR, error opening device or file"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,27,0)="-DSM-E-ERRCODE, Error Code = 0"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,28,0)="-SYSTEM-F-BADPARAM, bad parameter value"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,29,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,30,0)="VistA uses two types of ""listen services"", HLSEVEN and XMINETMM. Tests have"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,31,0)="shown that the XMINETMM service is also prone to the same symptoms as seen"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,32,0)="by the HLSEVEN service. These tests were run on the FORUM system and have"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,33,0)="produced retries during heavy activity periods. Therefore, the AXP, HLSEVEN"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,34,0)="and Mailman teams have agreed to jointly release the following Alert and"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,35,0)="Informational patches. "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,36,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,37,0)="AXP Alert*117"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,38,0)="HL*1.6*70"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,39,0)="XM*7.1*165"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,40,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,41,0)="The following is an excerpt from Compaq Engineering acknowledging our"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,42,0)="findings and their description of the problem."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,43,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,44,0)="********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,45,0)="Compaq"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,46,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,47,0)="Engineering thinks the problem here is a race between the INETACP, which"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,48,0)="has just created the process via $CREPRC(), and the process just created."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,49,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,50,0)="The INETACP doesn't relinquish its ownership of the BG device for the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,51,0)="accepted connection (which it passes in SYS$NET process logical) until"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,52,0)="sometime after $CREPRC() returns success status.  If the process gets to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,53,0)="run first it may have trouble assigning this BG momentarily.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,54,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,55,0)="This situation only occurs for listen services; nolisten services"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,56,0)="(like FTP) are handled very differently."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,57,0)="*********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,58,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,59,0)="Although this problem has been acknowledged, Compaq is reluctant to issue a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,60,0)="patch to the current version of TCPIP V5.0 due to its complexity. They have "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,61,0)="agreed to provide a fix in a future release. This future release should be "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,62,0)="TCPIP Services for VMS version 5.1, due sometime next year (2001). As an "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,63,0)="interim ""work-around"" solution, new HLSEVEN.COM and XMINET_ALPHA.COM command "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,64,0)="procedures have been written to compensate for this ""race condition"". "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,65,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,66,0)="XMINET_ALPHA.COM Descriptions"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,67,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,68,0)="This command procedure has been edited to check the status of the BG device"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,69,0)="prior to entering DSM. It contains two IF-THEN-ELSE statements. The first"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,70,0)="is a loop to count to 10. The command procedure will terminate after 10"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,71,0)="tries to gain access to the BG device. The second is a loop to test the bit"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,72,0)="mask status [stat=f$getdvi(""''x'"",""STS"")] of the BG device. It was found"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,73,0)="that with a bit mask value of 65552, DSM could not open the BG device but a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,74,0)="bit mask value of 16 allowed DSM to open the BG device. If the bit mask"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,75,0)="value is not equal to 16, then the command procedures will wait one second"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,76,0)="and try again. "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,77,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,78,0)="Typical log file entries:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,79,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,80,0)="Note - New log files will not be generated if the XMINET_ALPHA.LOG file"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,81,0)="version number has reached 32767. To generate new log files, delete all"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,82,0)="XMINET_ALPHA.LOG files and new ones will be generated starting with version"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,83,0)="1. Please also note that empty log files may be normal. If the current log"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,84,0)="file for the latest connection is still open and the connection is still"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,85,0)="active, the file will be empty and nothing will be displayed. Very busy"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,86,0)="XMINETMM services may see this and they can also generate failure to purge"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,87,0)="error messages. Keeping more log files in the purge statement in the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,88,0)="command procedures can avoid purge error messages - adjust accordingly."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,89,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,90,0)="Successful connection with no retries"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,91,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,92,0)="$type hlseven.log"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,93,0)="$!HLSEVEN.COM-for incoming connect requests"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,94,0)="$!-------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,95,0)="$ set noon        !Don't stop"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,96,0)="$ set noverify    !change as needed   "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,97,0)="Opening _BG8534:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,98,0)="_BG8534: is now ready for use - entering DSM"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,99,0)="  HLSEVEN     job terminated at  2-NOV-2000 07:55:38.44"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,100,0)="$"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,101,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,102,0)="Unsuccessful connection after maximum retries"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,103,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,104,0)="$type hlseven.log"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,105,0)="$!HLSEVEN.COM-for incoming connect requests"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,106,0)="$!-------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,107,0)="$ set noon        !Don't stop"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,108,0)="$ set noverify    !change as needed   "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,109,0)="Opening _BG8215:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,110,0)="1> _BG8215: not ready!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,111,0)="2> _BG8215: not ready!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,112,0)="3> _BG8215: not ready!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,113,0)="4> _BG8215: not ready!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,114,0)="5> _BG8215: not ready!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,115,0)="6> _BG8215: not ready!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,116,0)="7> _BG8215: not ready!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,117,0)="8> _BG8215: not ready!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,118,0)="9> _BG8215: not ready!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,119,0)="10> _BG8215: not ready!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,120,0)="Could not open _BG8215: - exiting"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,121,0)="  HLSEVEN     job terminated at  2-NOV-2000 07:50:40.84"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,122,0)="$"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,123,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,124,0)="A successful connection after 2 retries"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,125,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,126,0)="$type hlseven.log"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,127,0)="$!HLSEVEN.COM-for incoming connect requests"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,128,0)="$!-------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,129,0)="$ set noon        !Don't stop"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,130,0)="$ set noverify    !change as needed   "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,131,0)="Opening _BG8215:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,132,0)="1> _BG8215: not ready!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,133,0)="2> _BG8215: not ready!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,134,0)="_BG8215: is now ready for use - entering DSM"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,135,0)="  HLSEVEN     job terminated at  2-NOV-2000 07:50:40.84"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,136,0)="$"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,137,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,138,0)="The XMINET_ALPHA.COM command procedure is included below, and can be copied"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,139,0)="& pasted into a VMS file directly from this message. Alternatively, the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,140,0)="XMINET_ALPHA.COM (XM7_1P165.COM) file will be available for downloading from"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,141,0)="the [.SOFTWARE] directories at the following ftp sites:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,142,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,143,0)="Hines                   152.129.1.110"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,144,0)="Albany                  152.127.1.5"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,145,0)="Salt Lake City          152.131.2.1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,146,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,147,0)="To install:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,148,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,149,0)="Disable the UCX XMINETMM service"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,150,0)="$ UCX DISABLE SERVICE XMINETMM (UCX Version 4.2)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,151,0)="or"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,152,0)="$ TCPIP DISABLE SERVICE XMINETMM (TCPIP Version 5.0A) "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,153,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,154,0)="Using either method, place this new XMINET_ALPHA.COM procedure in the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,155,0)="SYS$LOGIN directory of the XMINETMM user. Be sure to edit accordingly. "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,156,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,157,0)="Copy and Paste Method:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,158,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,159,0)="$ SET DEFAULT USER$:[XMINETMM] or equivalent of the XMINETMM user."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,160,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,161,0)="Copy file from below into your Windows buffer by highlighting the entire"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,162,0)="text of the XMINET_ALPHA.COM file below."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,163,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,164,0)="$ CREATE XMINET_ALPHA.COM"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,165,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,166,0)="Paste the contents of your windows buffer and use CTRL Z to close file."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,167,0)="Then check/edit XMINET_ALPHA.COM to ensure that the DSM command line is"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,168,0)="correct for your system.  (You may use your previous version of"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,169,0)="XMINET_ALPHA.COM file as a reference.  The entry SOC^XMRUCX is correct."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,170,0)="SOC25^XMRUCX should no longer be used.)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,171,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,172,0)="Using FTP Method:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,173,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,174,0)="To retrieve from [.SOFTWARE] directories listed above:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,175,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,176,0)="$FTP 152.127.1.5"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,177,0)="220 ISC1A2.ISC-ALBANY.DOMAIN.EXT FTP Server (Version 5.0) Ready."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,178,0)="Connected to 152.127.1.5. "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,179,0)="Name (152.127.1.5:dsmmgr): ANONYMOUS"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,180,0)="331 Guest login OK, send ident as password."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,181,0)="Password: "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,182,0)="230 Guest login OK, access restrictions apply."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,183,0)="FTP> SET DEF [.SOFTWARE]"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,184,0)="250-CWD command successful."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,185,0)="250 New default directory is VA4$:[ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE]"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,186,0)="FTP> GET XM7_1P165.COM XMINET_ALPHA.COM"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,187,0)="200 TYPE set to IMAGE."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,188,0)="200 PORT command successful."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,189,0)="150 Opening data connection for VA4$:[ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE]XM7_1P165.COM;"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,190,0)=" (152.127.1.6,3281)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,191,0)="226 Transfer complete."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,192,0)="local: SYS$:[DSMMGR]XMINET_ALPHA.COM;1  remote: XM7_1P165.COM"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,193,0)="144638 bytes received in 00:00:00.04 seconds (3284.83 Kbytes/s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,194,0)="FTP> EXIT"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,195,0)="221 Goodbye."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,196,0)="$"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,197,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,198,0)="Check/edit XMINET_ALPHA.COM to ensure that the DSM command line is"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,199,0)="correct for your system.  (You may use your previous version of"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,200,0)="XMINET_ALPHA.COM file as a reference.  The entry SOC^XMRUCX is correct."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,201,0)="SOC25^XMRUCX should no longer be used.)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,202,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,203,0)="$ COPY XMINET_ALPHA.COM USER$:[XMINETMM] or equivalent of the XMINETMM user."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,204,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,205,0)="Before enabling the XMINETMM service, be sure to check the file ownership"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,206,0)="and protection. "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,207,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,208,0)="Enable the UCX XMINETMM service"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,209,0)="$ UCX ENABLE SERVICE XMINETMM (UCX Version 4.2)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,210,0)="or"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,211,0)="$ TCPIP ENABLE SERVICE XMINETMM (TCPIP Version 5.0A)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,212,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,213,0)="Please note that Mailman puts a leading space before the ""$"" of each DCL"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,214,0)="command line in the XMINET_ALPHA.COM file as it is documented. If you choose"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,215,0)="to cut and paste the file from this message, you will need to edit it to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,216,0)="remove the spaces before enabling the services."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,217,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,218,0)="*** Cut here ***"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,219,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,220,0)="$!XMINET_ALPHA.COM - for incoming connect requests"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,221,0)="$!-------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,222,0)="$ set noon        !don't stop"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,223,0)="$ set noverify    !change as needed   "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,224,0)="$! set verify     !change as needed"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,225,0)="$ purge/keep=5 sys$login:*.log !Purge log files only"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,226,0)="$ set proc/priv=(share)  !Required for MBX device"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,227,0)="$ x=f$trnlnm(""sys$net"")  !This is our MBX device"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,228,0)="$! "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,229,0)="$ write sys$output ""Opening ""+x !This can be viewed in the log file"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,230,0)="$! Check status of the BG device before going to DSM"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,231,0)="$ cnt=0"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,232,0)="$ CHECK:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,233,0)="$ stat=f$getdvi(""''x'"",""STS"")"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,234,0)="$ if cnt .eq. 10"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,235,0)="$ then"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,236,0)="$ write sys$output ""Could not open ''x' - exiting"""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,237,0)="$ goto EXIT"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,238,0)="$ else"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,239,0)="$       if stat .ne. 16"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,240,0)="$       then"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,241,0)="$       cnt=cnt+1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,242,0)="$       write sys$output ""''cnt'> ''x' not ready!"""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,243,0)="$       wait 00:00:01 !Wait one second to assure connection"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,244,0)="$       goto CHECK"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,245,0)="$       else"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,246,0)="$       write sys$output ""''x' is now ready for use - entering DSM"""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,247,0)="$!-------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,248,0)="$! **Be sure this command line is correct for your system"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,249,0)="$! **and if access control is enabled, that this account has"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,250,0)="$! **access to this uci,vol & routine."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,251,0)="$!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,252,0)="$ DSM/E=DSMMGR/U=VAH/V=ROU/DATA=""''X'"" SOC^XMRUCX"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,253,0)="$!-------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,254,0)="$       endif"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,255,0)="$ endif"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,256,0)="$ EXIT:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,257,0)="$ logout/brief"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,258,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,259,0)="*** end cut here ***"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,260,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,261,0)="IMPORTANT!!!   IMPORTANT!!!   IMPORTANT!!!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,262,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,263,0)="This XMINET_ALPHA.COM file is a generic file to be used and EDITED by all"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,264,0)="VMS/DSM sites. Please refer to the comment lines in the command procedure."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,265,0)="THIS COMMAND PROCEDURE MAY NOT WORK AS DISTRIBUTED."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,266,0)="Please verify that the DSM command line is correct for your site."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,267,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,268,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,269,0)="is at a minimum."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,270,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,271,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,272,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,273,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,274,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,275,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,276,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,277,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,278,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,279,0)="This patch has no routines."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,280,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,281,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,282,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,283,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,284,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,285,0)="is at a minimum."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,286,0)="1.  Users may be on the system during installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,287,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,288,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,289,0)="3.  You do not need to stop TaskMan or the background filer."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,290,0)="    Users may be on the system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,291,0)="4.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,292,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,293,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,294,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,295,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,296,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,297,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,298,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME:    XM*7.1*165    Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,299,0)="                         =========="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,300,0)=" Install Questions:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,301,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,302,0)="                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,303,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,304,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,305,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,306,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,307,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,308,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,309,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <It's up to you.  You may queue it if you wish.>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,310,0)="                ------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,311,0)="5.  Now read and follow the instructions in the Patch Description to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,312,0)="update your XMINET_ALPHA.COM file."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",132,1,313,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,0)="135 SEQ #158^3010228^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,0)="^^57^57^3010228"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,1,0)="Patch XM*7.1*135"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,3,0)="NOIS: NAS-1099-33188"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,4,0)="Test Site:  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,5,0)="Instead of going to ^XUSCLEAN when incoming net mail is finished, simply"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,6,0)="quit.  Also, make the SOC25 entry point identical to the SOC entry point."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,7,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,8,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,9,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*50."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,10,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,11,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,12,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,13,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,14,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,16,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,17,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,18,0)="-----------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,19,0)="XMRUCX          841742          478788        27,34,50,135"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,20,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,21,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,22,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,23,0)="This patch introduces no new routines."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,24,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,26,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,27,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,28,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*50."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,29,0)="1.  Users may be on the system during installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,30,0)="2.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,31,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,32,0)="3.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,33,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,34,0)="4.  You do not need to stop TaskMan or the background filer."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,35,0)="    Users may be on the system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,36,0)="5.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,37,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,38,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,39,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,40,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,41,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,42,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,43,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME:    XM*7.1*135    Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,44,0)="                         =========="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,45,0)=" Install Questions:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,46,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,47,0)="                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,48,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,49,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,50,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,51,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,52,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,53,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,54,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <It's up to you.  You may queue it if you wish.>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,55,0)="                ------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,56,0)="6.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",133,1,57,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,0)="158 SEQ #159^3010228^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,0)="^^101^101^3010228"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,1,0)="Patch XM*7.1*158"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,3,0)="Test Site:  Puget Sound HCS"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,4,0)="NOIS: RIC-1100-21104"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,5,0)="An incoming message from a top-level domain that is not recognized by"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,6,0)="MailMan can cause problems.  This patch prepares MailMan for that"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,7,0)="eventuality."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,9,0)="These top-level domains are no longer added to file 4.2996, INTERNET"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,10,0)="SUFFIX.  They continue to be added to file 4.2, DOMAIN."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,11,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,12,0)="A new bulletin, XM DOMAIN ADDED, now notifies G.POSTMASTER of these"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,13,0)="new domains."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,14,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,15,0)="The pre-init, XMYPOSTD deletes all entries from the INTERNET SUFFIX"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,16,0)="file 4.2996.  A new DD will be brought in for this file, along with"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,17,0)="all its data.  It is populated with all the internationally recognized"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,18,0)="top-level domains.  You will not be able to edit that file, except for"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,19,0)="adding notes."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,20,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,21,0)="A 'B' xref is added to the .01 field of the TRANSMISSION SCRIPT multiple"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,22,0)="of the DOMAIN file 4.2.  The post-init, POST^XMYPOSTD, sets the 'B' xref."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,23,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,24,0)="NOTE: This patch requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*50."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,25,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,26,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,27,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,28,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,29,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,31,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,32,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,33,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,34,0)="XMR0B          8875848         8051092        4,6,13,34,42,62,50,158"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,35,0)="XMYPOSTD       * NEW *         3967175        158"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,36,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,37,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,38,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,39,0)="This patch introduces the following new routines:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,40,0)="XMYPOSTD  has no user callable entry points."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,41,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,43,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,44,0)="NOTE: This patch requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*50."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,45,0)="1.  Users should not be on the system during patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,46,0)="2.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,47,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,48,0)="3.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,49,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,50,0)="4.  On the Manage MailMan:Local Delivery Management menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,51,0)="    option to stop the background filer:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,52,0)="       STOP background filer"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,53,0)="Are you sure you want the BACKGROUND FILERS to STOP delivering mail? NO// YES"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,54,0)="                                                                          ==="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,55,0)="<< Background filer will stop soon. >>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,56,0)="5.  Stop TaskMan.  Shut down the listeners.  You may also wish to shut down"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,57,0)="    HL7 filers/LLP's and other background tasks which may attempt to create"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,58,0)="    new messages.  During the installation of this patch, we do not want any"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,59,0)="    messages coming in or going out.  Users should not be on the system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,60,0)="6.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,61,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,62,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,63,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,64,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,65,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,66,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,67,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME:    XM*7.1*158     Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,68,0)="                         =========="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,69,0)=" Install Questions:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,70,0)="Incoming Files:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,71,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,72,0)="   4.2996    INTERNET SUFFIX  (including data)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,73,0)="Note:  You already have the 'INTERNET SUFFIX' File."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,74,0)="I will OVERWRITE your data with mine."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,75,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,76,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// YES"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,77,0)="                                                       ==="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,78,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// YES"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,79,0)="                                                                       ==="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,80,0)=" Enter options you wish to mark as 'Out Of Order': XMUSER       MailMan Menu"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,81,0)="                                                   ======"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,82,0)=" Enter options you wish to mark as 'Out Of Order': <press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,83,0)="                                                   =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,84,0)=" Enter protocols you wish to mark as 'Out Of Order': <press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,85,0)="                                                     =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,86,0)=" Delay Install (Minutes):  (0-60): 0// <press return>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,87,0)="                                       =============="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,88,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,89,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,90,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,91,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,92,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <Do not queue this.>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,93,0)="                --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,94,0)="7.  Start TaskMan.  If you shut down HL7 filers/LLP's and other"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,95,0)="    background tasks in step 4, be sure to restart them, too."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,96,0)="8.  On the Manage MailMan:Local Delivery Management menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,97,0)="    option to start the background filer:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,98,0)="       START background filer"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,99,0)="<< Background filer will start soon. >>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,100,0)="9.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",134,1,101,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,0)="166 SEQ #160^3010228^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,0)="^^94^94^3010228"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,1,0)="     ************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,2,0)="     It is important that you read the information in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,3,0)="               You may have to manually fix something."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,4,0)="     ************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,5,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,6,0)="Patch XM*7.1*166"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,7,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,8,0)="NOIS: TUC-0101-60657"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,9,0)="Test Sites:  Tucson, AZ"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,10,0)="If a site lists itself as the PARENT in file 4.3, MAILMAN SITE PARAMETERS,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,11,0)="that can cause problems.  This patch puts a screen on that field in the DD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,12,0)="to prevent this from happening."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,13,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,14,0)="The pre-init for this patch will check to ensure that your site does not"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,15,0)="have itself as its PARENT.  If it does, the PARENT field will be deleted"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,16,0)="and you will have to enter the correct PARENT."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,17,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,18,0)="If field 3, PARENT, in file 4.3 is filled in, you should ensure that it"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,19,0)="does not point to its own domain.  It should be the domain considered"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,20,0)="the parent of your facility.  The parent domain is the domain to which"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,21,0)="mail is sent, when your facility doesn't quite know what to do with it."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,22,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,23,0)="For example,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,24,0)="1. The parent domain of the MailMan development account, "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,25,0)="MAILMAN.ISC-SF.DOMAIN.EXT, is ISC-SF.DOMAIN.EXT."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,26,0)="(The parent domain should NOT be MAILMAN.ISC-SF.DOMAIN.EXT)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,27,0)="2. The parent domain of ISC-SF.DOMAIN.EXT is DOMAIN.EXT. It could also"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,28,0)="be GK.DOMAIN.EXT or whatever domain your site uses to send mail to the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,29,0)="internet.  (The parent domain should NOT be ISC-SF.DOMAIN.EXT)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,30,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,31,0)="The account that you install this patch in probably matches one of the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,32,0)="examples.  If not, the parent domain should be the domain through which"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,33,0)="you route messages to remote sites over the internet."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,34,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,35,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,36,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*50."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,37,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,38,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,39,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,40,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,41,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,43,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,44,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,45,0)="-----------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,46,0)="XMYPRE10       * new *         1299000        166"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,47,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,48,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,49,0)="This patch introduces no new routines."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,50,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,52,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,53,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,54,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*50."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,55,0)="1.  Users may be on the system during installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,56,0)="2.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,57,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,58,0)="3.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,59,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,60,0)="4.  You do not need to stop TaskMan or the background filer."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,61,0)="    Users may be on the system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,62,0)="5.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,63,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,64,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,65,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,66,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,67,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,68,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,69,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME:    XM*7.1*166    Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,70,0)="                         =========="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,71,0)=" Install Questions:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,72,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,73,0)="                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,74,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,75,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,76,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,77,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,78,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,79,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,80,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <It's up to you, you may queue it if you wish.>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,81,0)="                -----------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,82,0)="6.  Check the Install File Print.  If you see this, you need to take action."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,83,0)="If you don't see it, you're OK:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,84,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,85,0)="***********************************************"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,87,0)="Field 3, PARENT, in file 4.3 was deleted."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,88,0)="You must enter a new PARENT."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,89,0)="See the patch description for how to choose one."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,91,0)="***********************************************"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,92,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,93,0)="7.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",135,1,94,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,0)="170 SEQ #161^3010319^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,0)="^^70^70^3010319"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,1,0)="Patch XM*7.1*170"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,3,0)="Test Site:  Hines"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,4,0)="NOIS: HIN-0201-42151"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,5,0)="Put quotes around an address containing blanks when sending messages to"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,6,0)="remote sites."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,8,0)="NOTE: This patch requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*50."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,9,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,11,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,12,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,13,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,15,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,16,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,17,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,18,0)="XMS0A          9199959         9159707        2,13,55,50,170"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,20,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,22,0)="This patch introduces no new routines."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,23,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,25,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,26,0)="NOTE: This patch requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*50."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,27,0)="1.  Users should not be on the system during patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,28,0)="2.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,29,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,30,0)="3.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,31,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,32,0)="4.  On the Manage MailMan:Local Delivery Management menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,33,0)="    option to stop the background filer:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,34,0)="       STOP background filer"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,35,0)="Are you sure you want the BACKGROUND FILERS to STOP delivering mail? NO// YES"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,36,0)="                                                                          ==="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,37,0)="<< Background filer will stop soon. >>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,38,0)="5.  Stop TaskMan.  Shut down the listeners.  You may also wish to shut down"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,39,0)="    HL7 filers/LLP's and other background tasks which may attempt to create"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,40,0)="    new messages.  During the installation of this patch, we do not want any"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,41,0)="    messages coming in or going out.  Users should not be on the system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,42,0)="6.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,43,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,44,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,45,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,46,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,47,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,48,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,49,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME:    XM*7.1*170     Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,50,0)="                         =========="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,51,0)=" Install Questions:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,53,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,54,0)="                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,55,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,56,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,57,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,58,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,59,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,61,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <Do not queue this.>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,62,0)="                --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,63,0)="7.  Start TaskMan.  If you shut down HL7 filers/LLP's and other"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,64,0)="    background tasks in step 4, be sure to restart them, too."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,65,0)="8.  On the Manage MailMan:Local Delivery Management menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,66,0)="    option to start the background filer:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,67,0)="       START background filer"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,68,0)="<< Background filer will start soon. >>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,69,0)="9.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",136,1,70,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,0)="172 SEQ #162^3010319^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,0)="^^72^72^3010319"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,1,0)="Patch XM*7.1*172"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,3,0)="E3R 15488"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,4,0)="Test Sites: FORUM"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,5,0)="Add the following message actions at the Message Action: Ignore// prompt:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,6,0)="QC  - Show all users who are current on the message (read all responses)."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,7,0)="QNC - Show all users who are not current on the message."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,8,0)="QT  - Show all users who have terminated the message."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,10,0)="Help Frames are updated."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,11,0)="Dialogs have been added."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,13,0)="A new API, QX^XMXUTIL3, has been added, to perform the above actions."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,14,0)="See DBIA 2737 for details."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,15,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,16,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,17,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*137 & XM*7.1*154."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,18,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",137,1,19,0)=""
