^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,0)="181 SEQ #174^3010529^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,0)="^^59^59^3010529"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,1,0)="Patch XM*7.1*181"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,3,0)="NOIS: DAY-0401-42491"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,4,0)="Test Site:  Dayton, OH"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,5,0)="When adding a new member to a mail group, and choosing to forward existing"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,6,0)="group messages to the new member, MailMan asks for a date range of messages"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,7,0)="to search.  If the oldest message on the system is less than one year old,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,8,0)="then MailMan should give a default date of the oldest message, instead of a"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,9,0)="date from a year ago.  This patch fixes that."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,10,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,11,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,12,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*163."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,13,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,14,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,15,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,16,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,17,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,19,0)="              Before          After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,20,0)="Name          Checksum        Checksum        Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,21,0)="-----------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,22,0)="XMVGRP        10944118        11414072        163,181"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,23,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,24,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,25,0)="This patch introduces no new routines."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,26,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,28,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,29,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,30,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*163."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,31,0)="1.  Users may be on the system during installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,32,0)="2.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,33,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,34,0)="3.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,35,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,36,0)="4.  You do not need to stop TaskMan or the background filer."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,37,0)="    Users may be on the system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",149,1,38,0)="5.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
