^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,31,0)="3.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,32,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,33,0)="4.  You do not need to stop TaskMan or the background filer."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,34,0)="    Users may be on the system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,35,0)="5.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,36,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,37,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,38,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,39,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,40,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,41,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,42,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME:    XM*7.1*191    Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,43,0)="                         =========="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,44,0)=" Install Questions:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,45,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,46,0)="                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,47,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,48,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,49,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,50,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,51,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,52,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,53,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <It's up to you.  You may queue it if you wish.>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,54,0)="                ------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,55,0)="6.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",162,1,56,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,0)="192 SEQ #188^3010906^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,0)="^^91^91^3010906"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,1,0)="Patch XM*7.1*192"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,3,0)="NOIS ISW-0701-21674"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,4,0)="Test Sites: OIFO-Washington; Oklahoma City"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,5,0)="This patch concerns options XMMGR-TERMINATE-MANY and XMMGR-TERMINATE-SUGGEST,"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,6,0)="which check to see if users should have their mailboxes deleted, because they"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,7,0)="haven't used MailMan in a while, or because there's something screwy about"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,8,0)="them in the NEW PERSON file, such as a missing access or verify code or main"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,9,0)="menu, or they were terminated and were allowed to keep their mailbox.  This"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,10,0)="patch closes some loopholes which caused some users to be targeted for"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,11,0)="mailbox deletion, when they really shouldn't have been."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,13,0)="Some users never log on, but have forwarding addresses and have all their"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,14,0)="mail forwarded.  Previously, these options might have deleted their"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,15,0)="mailboxes.  Now, a report suggests further investigation."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,16,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,17,0)="Some users never log on, but have surrogates read and answer their mail."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,18,0)="Previously, these options might have deleted their mailboxes.  Now, they"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,19,0)="are left alone."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,20,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,21,0)="Some users don't log on traditionally, so their last logon date might be"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,22,0)="really old.  However, they do manage to read mail, one way or another."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,23,0)="Previously, these options might have suggested their mailboxes be deleted."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,24,0)="Now they are left alone."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,25,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,26,0)="Two more columns have been added to the XMMGR-TERMINATE-SUGGEST report."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,27,0)="If a user has been DISUSER'd, the user is included in the report, and that"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,28,0)="fact is noted on the report.  Also, if the user has any surrogates, one of"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,29,0)="them is shown.  (Space limitations prevent showing more than one.)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,30,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,31,0)="Option descriptions are updated."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,32,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,33,0)="Additionally, if a user's mailbox is deleted, MailMan now looks to see if"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,34,0)="the user is a coordinator or organizer of any mail group.  If so, MailMan"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,35,0)="replaces the user with the Postmaster.  Previously, those fields were not"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,36,0)="checked at all."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,37,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,38,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,39,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*180."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,40,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,41,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,42,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,43,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,44,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,46,0)="           Before       After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,47,0)="Name       Checksum     Checksum     Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,48,0)="-----------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,49,0)="XMUTERM    13770249      7174403     50,125,180,192"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,50,0)="XMUTERM1   14564305     17136578     50,125,192"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,51,0)="XMUTERM2    * NEW *     10569752     192"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,52,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,53,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,54,0)="This patch introduces the following new routine:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,55,0)="XMUTERM2 - no user-callable entry points"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,56,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,58,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,59,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,60,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*180."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,61,0)="1.  Users may be on the system during installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,62,0)="2.  DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,63,0)="    affected routine(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,64,0)="3.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,65,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,66,0)="4.  You do not need to stop TaskMan or the background filer."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,67,0)="    Users may be on the system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,68,0)="5.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,69,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,70,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,71,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,72,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,73,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,74,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,75,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME:    XM*7.1*192    Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,76,0)="                         =========="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,77,0)=" Install Questions:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,78,0)=" Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES// YES"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,79,0)="                                                                   ==="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,80,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,81,0)="                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,82,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,83,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,84,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,85,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,86,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,87,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,88,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <It's up to you.  You may queue it if you wish.>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,89,0)="                ------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,90,0)="6.  DSM Sites: After patch has installed, rebuild your map set, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",163,1,91,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,0)="193 SEQ #189^3010906^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,0)="^^79^79^3010906"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,1,0)="            * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,2,0)="                    !! A T T E N T I O N !!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,3,0)="            You must manually CHECK an entry in the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,4,0)="                 COMMUNICATIONS PROTOCOL FILE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,5,0)="                 and CORRECT it, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,6,0)="            * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,7,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,8,0)="Patch XM*7.1*193"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,10,0)="NOIS ISW-0801-20974"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,11,0)="Test Sites: OIFO Washington"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,13,0)="If you use the MailMan option for transferring VistA email messages via"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,14,0)="disk/tape to another site, you will have problems if the SEND field"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,15,0)="setting for the TAPE entry in the Communications Protocol file is wrong."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,16,0)="The SEND field for the TAPE entry must be set to:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,17,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,18,0)="SEND: W XMSG,! ; S XMTRAN=""S: ""_XMSG D TRAN^XMC1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,19,0)="            =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,20,0)="Most of the entries we have found for this don't have the "",!"" following"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,21,0)="the ""W XMS"".  Without the "",!"" you don't get the line feed at the end of"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,22,0)="each line. This causes a buffer overflow when you try to receive the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,23,0)="message.  Please look at your entry, and edit, if necessary:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,24,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,25,0)="Using FileMan:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,26,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,27,0)="Select OPTION: ENTER OR EDIT FILE ENTRIES  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,28,0)="               ====="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,29,0)="INPUT TO WHAT FILE: COMMUNICATIONS PROTOCOL// <press enter>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,30,0)="EDIT WHICH FIELD: ALL// SEND"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,31,0)="                        ===="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,32,0)="THEN EDIT FIELD: <press enter>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,33,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,34,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,35,0)="Select COMMUNICATIONS PROTOCOL NAME: TAPE"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,36,0)="                                     ===="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,37,0)="SEND: W XMSG ; S XMTRAN=""S: ""_XMSG D TRAN^XMC1  Replace MSG With MSG,!"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,38,0)="                                                        ===      ====="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,39,0)="  Replace <press enter>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,40,0)="   W XMSG,! ; S XMTRAN=""S: ""_XMSG D TRAN^XMC1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,41,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,42,0)="Select COMMUNICATIONS PROTOCOL NAME:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,43,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,44,0)="NOTE: This patch may be installed at any time.  Even though the patch is"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,45,0)="informational, please install it, so that the patch installation message"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,46,0)="is sent to FORUM.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*50."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,47,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,48,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,49,0)="ROUTINES:  This patch contains no routines"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,50,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,51,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,53,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,54,0)="NOTE: This patch may be installed at any time.  Even though the patch is"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,55,0)="informational, please install it, so that the patch installation message"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,56,0)="is sent to FORUM.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*50."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,57,0)="1.  Users may be on the system during installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,58,0)="2.  On the PackMan menu, use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option.  This loads "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,59,0)="    the patch into a Transport Global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,60,0)="3.  You do not need to stop TaskMan or the background filer."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,61,0)="    Users may be on the system."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,62,0)="4.  On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,63,0)="    Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,64,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,65,0)="       Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,66,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME:    XM*7.1*193    Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,67,0)="                         =========="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,68,0)=" Install Questions:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,69,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,70,0)="                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,71,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,72,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,73,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,74,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,75,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,76,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,77,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <It's up to you.  You may queue it if you wish.>"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,78,0)="                ------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",164,1,79,0)="==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,0)="196 SEQ #190^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,0)="^^76^76^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,1,0)="Patch XM*7.1*196"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,3,0)="NOIS: DUB-0801-31849, TOG-1099-10040, FAV-0300-71554, MON-1099-50906"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,4,0)="Test Site:  Dublin, GA; Fayetteville, AR; Montana HCS"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,5,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,6,0)="If a surrogate with just read privilege (not send) assumes a user's"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,7,0)="identity, and that user has an unsent message in the buffer, the surrogate"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,8,0)="is thrown off the system.  This patch takes a gentler approach.  The"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,9,0)="surrogate can now decide whether to delete the unsent message and then"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,10,0)="read and reply to messages normally, or to leave the unsent message alone"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,11,0)="and still be able to read messages, but not reply to them."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,13,0)="If a surrogate with send privilege assumes a user's identity, and"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,14,0)="that user is logged on and composing a message, the surrogate is thrown"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,15,0)="off the system.  This patch takes a gentler approach.  The surrogate is"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,16,0)="told that the session is concurrent with another, and is not thrown off."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,17,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,18,0)="If a user starts up a second MailMan session while in the middle of"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,19,0)="editing a message in the first MailMan session, the user may be thrown"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,20,0)="off the system.  This patch takes a gentler approach.  The user is told"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,21,0)="that the session is concurrent with another, and is not thrown off."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,22,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,23,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when user activity"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,24,0)="is at a minimum.  It requires MailMan patch XM*7.1*189."
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,25,0)="============================================================================ "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,26,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,27,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,28,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,29,0)="       ;;7.1;MailMan;**[patch list]**;Jun 02, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,31,0)="             Before       After"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,32,0)="Name         Checksum     Checksum     Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,33,0)="----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,34,0)="XM           11099027     11391363     17,35,50,140,144,149,168,196"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,35,0)="XMJMR        20744645     10586054     50,107,127,189,196"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,36,0)="XMJMR1        * NEW *     10598504     196"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,37,0)="XMJMRO        5033137      5040542     50,89,110,127,172,196"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,38,0)="XMJMS         6300984      7995221     50,120,130,189,196"
^DIC(9.4,4,22,1,"PAH",165,1,39,0)="XMYPRE7         35006        25031     127,148,196"
