^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,210,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,211,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,212,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,213,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,214,0)="1.  Recommend the patch installer review the Installation Guide"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,215,0)="documentation for detailed installation and implementation information."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,216,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,217,0)="2.  This patch can be loaded with users on the system.  Installation will"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,218,0)="take less than 1 minute."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,219,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,220,0)="3.  Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed in the ROUTINE"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,221,0)="SUMMARY section are mapped, they should be removed from the mapped set at"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,222,0)="this time."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,223,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,224,0)="4.  Impacts of files:"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,225,0)="       a.  The size of File 15 is dependent upon the number of potential"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,226,0)="duplicates found and is thus also dependent upon the size of the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,227,0)="File.  It may be purged using the application options, however note that"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,228,0)="information regarding those pairs already merged will not be purged."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,229,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,230,0)="       b.  The size of File 15.1 is minimal.  This file contains the"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,231,0)="working components of Duplicate Resolution as they pertain to a primary"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,232,0)="file.  It will expand as additional primary files are added."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,233,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,234,0)="       c.  The size of File 15.2 is minimal.  It may be purged using the"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,235,0)="application options."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,236,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,237,0)="       d.  The size of File 15.3 is minimal.  The number of entries is"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,238,0)="dependent upon the number of record pairs merged."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,239,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,240,0)="       e.  The size of File 15.4 is dependent upon the number of record"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,241,0)="pairs merged and their associated data.  Note that not all associated data"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,242,0)="is retained, but rather pointer values.  This is an independent global"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,243,0)="with the intent that it can be saved off to a static environment for"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,244,0)="archive purposes."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,245,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,246,0)="5.  This patch contains 46 routines.  The following routines are necessary"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,247,0)="for the operation of Patient Merge, but are not included with this patch"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,248,0)="as they were previously released as part of Toolkit:"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,249,0)="       XDRDADJ                 XDRDFPD         XDRDPDTI        XDRDSCOR"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,250,0)="       XDRMPACK                XDRMRG          XDRMRG1         XDRMSG"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,251,0)="       XDRU1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,252,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,253,0)="6.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select the"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,254,0)="Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,255,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,256,0)="7.  From this menu, you may elect to use the following options (when"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,257,0)="prompted for the INSTALL NAME, enter XT*7.3*23):"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,258,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,259,0)="       a.  Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,260,0)="message of any routines exported with the patch.  It will NOT backup any"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,261,0)="of the other changes."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,262,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,263,0)="       b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,264,0)="allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch is"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,265,0)="installed.  It compares all components of the patch (routines and"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,266,0)="options)."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,267,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,268,0)="       c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,269,0)="you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the transport"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,270,0)="global."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,271,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,272,0)="8.  Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package XT*7.3*23."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,273,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,274,0)="9.  When prompted ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,275,0)="Protocols? YES//"" respond ""NO""."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,276,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,277,0)="10.  If any routines were unmapped as a part of step 3, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",9,1,278,0)="returned to the mapped set once the installation has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",10,0)="28 SEQ #18^2981016^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",11,0)="29 SEQ #19^2981016^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",12,0)="30 SEQ #20^2981016^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,0)="27 SEQ #21^2981105^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,0)="^^67^67^2981105"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,1,0)="F#25580312      XINDX10   Was getting a UNDEF when XINDEXing a Build"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,2,0)="ISW-0698-21653            with a partial file send."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,3,0)="                          "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,4,0)="ISH-1197-40901  XINDX10   When doing a XINDEX of a BUILD the count of"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,5,0)="ISA-0698-11515            routines indexed was wrong.  The count of"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,6,0)="                          routines now lists anything that starts with"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,7,0)="                          a '|' as a Faux Routines."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,8,0)="                          i.e. Routines: 11  Faux Routines: 5"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,10,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,11,0)="ISA-0698-11515  XINDX11   The KIDS build pre/post install routines were"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,12,0)="                          not included."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,13,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,14,0)="Local Error log XTRMON    Incorrect starting value when monitoring ALL"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,15,0)="                          routines."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,16,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,17,0)="Message from Ed @ Micronetics about changes they made to use with MSM."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,18,0)="Only updates to the standard and general fixes were included."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,19,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,20,0)="Message from Pat Redington @ SLC about a problem running XINDEX on a"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,21,0)="partial file build."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,22,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,23,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,24,0)="Routine         Old       New      2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,25,0)="XINDEX        8229005   8423982    **20,27**"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,26,0)="XINDX10      13440865  13730836    **20,27**"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,27,0)="XINDX11       7648100   7252133    **20,27**"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,28,0)="XINDX2        5457656   5618431    **20,27**"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,29,0)="XINDX3        3946423   4134014    **20,27**"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,30,0)="XINDX5        7001485   6939608    **20,27**"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,31,0)="XINDX6       10238332  10371813    **20,27**"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,32,0)="XINDX7        7680200   7896227    **20,27**"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,33,0)="XINDX8        6232391   6601958    **20,27**"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,34,0)="XINDX9        4248028   4321464    **20,27**"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,35,0)="XTRMON        2510222   2618426    **27**"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,36,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,37,0)="List of preceding patches: 20, 27"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,38,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,39,0)="========================================================================= "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,40,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,41,0)=" 1.  DSM sites- These routines aren't usually mapped "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,42,0)="     so you will probably not have to disable mapping."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,43,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,44,0)=" 2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,45,0)="     option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,46,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,47,0)=" 3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,48,0)="     system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,49,0)="     On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,50,0)="     options:"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,51,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,52,0)="         Verify Checksum's in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,53,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,54,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,55,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,56,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,57,0)=" 4.  Users can remain on the system. "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,58,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,59,0)=" 5.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,60,0)="     option:"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,61,0)="        Install Package(s)  'XT*7.3*27'"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,62,0)="                             ========="
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,63,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,64,0)="  6.  DSM Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set, If needed."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,65,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,66,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",13,1,67,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",14,0)="32 SEQ #22^2981120^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",15,0)="33 SEQ #23^2981125^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",16,0)="26 SEQ #24^2981214^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^2^2^2981214"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",16,1,1,0)="This build contains files, routines, and options in support of generic"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",16,1,2,0)="parameters functionality exported with patch XT*7.3*26."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",17,0)="34 SEQ #25^2990303^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,0)="35 SEQ #26^2990417^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^61^61^2990417"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="This patch fixes two NOIS's for the XPAR package."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,3,0)="NOIS              RTN   Description"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,4,0)="                        "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,5,0)="IND-1298-71717 XPARDD   When making a call to EN^XPAR and the data is "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,6,0)="                        a set of codes, sometimes it would talk.  This"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,7,0)="                        unwanted behavior has been fixed. "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,9,0)="PUG-0399-51652 XPAREDT2 When displaying some types of data, the two columns "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,10,0)="                        could run into each other.  Moved columns apart"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,11,0)="                        and use a $E to limit the size.                        "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,13,0)="Routine Summary"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,14,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,15,0)="of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,16,0)=" ;;7.3;TOOLKIT;<patchlist>;Apr 25, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,17,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,18,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,19,0)="Routine         Old       New      2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,20,0)="XPARDD        7153031   7342389    **26,35**"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,21,0)="XPAREDT2      6057876   6104530    **26,35**"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,22,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,23,0)="List of preceding patches: 26"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,24,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,25,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,26,0)="========================================================================= "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,27,0)="Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,28,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,29,0)="  1.  DSM sites - Some of these routines maybe mapped,"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,30,0)="      so you will need to disable mapping for the affected routines. "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,31,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,32,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,33,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,34,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,35,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,36,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,37,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,38,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,39,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,40,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,41,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,42,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,43,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,44,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,45,0)="  4.  Users can remain on the system. This patch can be loaded any"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,46,0)="      non-peak time."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,47,0)="      This patch can be queued for install at non-peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,48,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,49,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,50,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,51,0)="  5.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,52,0)="      option:"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,53,0)="        Install Package(s)  'XT*7.3*35'"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,54,0)="                             ========="
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,55,0)="                             "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,56,0)="        No Options or Protocols need to be placed out-of-order."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,57,0)="        Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? NO"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,58,0)="                                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,59,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,60,0)="  6.  DSM Sites, after patch has installed, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",18,1,61,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",19,0)="37 SEQ #27^2990427^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",20,0)="38 SEQ #28^2990602^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",21,0)="40 SEQ #29^2990626^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",22,0)="36 SEQ #30^2990914^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",23,0)="42 SEQ #31^2991002^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",24,0)="43 SEQ #32^2991003^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",25,0)="44 SEQ #33^2991123^1"
^DIC(9.4,5,22,13,"PAH",26,0)="45 SEQ #34^3000313^1"
