^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,189,0)="                                                                             "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,190,0)="GENERAL INFORMATION"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,191,0)="===================                                                        "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,192,0)="DO NOT NEED TO BE INSTALLED.  When Order Entry Version 3.0 (CPRS) is           "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,193,0)="installed, this patch will be installed along with it.  Install this"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,194,0)="patch ONLY if your site was one of the test sites listed in the TEST"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,195,0)="SITES section so your site will have the final changes made in the"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,196,0)="Dietetics routines.                                                          "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,197,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,198,0)="When this patch is being installed with Order Entry, it should be installed"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,199,0)="into the test UCI first then the production UCI.  It can be installed at"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,200,0)="anytime.  Install times of this patch at the test sites were less than 15"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,201,0)="minutes.  No Dietetics options need to be disabled.  Dietetics users do"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,202,0)="not need to be logged off the system.                                           "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,203,0)="                                                                            "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,204,0)="DOCUMENTATION                                                               "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,205,0)="=============                                                               "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,206,0)="The documentation for this patch contains in detail the HL7"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,207,0)="message interface between Dietetics and Order Entry.  Documentation for "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,208,0)="this patch will be mailed from NCD (National Center for Documentation).  "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,209,0)="This shipment will contain pages the site can append in the "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,210,0)="Dietetics Version 5.0 Technical Manual.  These pages are available in a "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,211,0)=".PDF file in the following IRM Field Offices ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE directories. "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,212,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,213,0)="                                                                         "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,214,0)="                       IRM FIELD OFFICE                      FTP Address"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,215,0)="                       ----------------                      -----------"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,216,0)="                       Hines                                 152.129.1.110"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,217,0)="                       Albany                                152.127.1.5"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,218,0)="                       Salt Lake                             152.131.2.1"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,219,0)="                                                                          "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,220,0)="                       FILE"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,221,0)="                       ----                                              "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,222,0)="                       FH5_0P6.PDF                                          "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,223,0)="                                                                            "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,224,0)="All VAMCs are encouraged to log into TCP/IP host using FTP to obtain it."
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,225,0)="The .PDF file can be read on a PC using the Adobe Acrobat Reader browser"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,226,0)="program.  The .PDF file is a BINary file, so you must make sure"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,227,0)="when using the file transfer, to enter the appropriate command for BINary"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,228,0)="file transfer.                                                            "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,229,0)="                                                                            "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,230,0)="If there are any questions, your supporting CIOFO Customer Service Clinical "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,231,0)="2 Team will address them.                                                     "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,232,0)="                                                                            "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,233,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS                                                   "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,234,0)="=========================                                                   "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,235,0)="                                                                          "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,236,0)="This Patch is created with Kernel V8 KIDS.  Follow these instructions:      "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,237,0)="1) Use Packman option 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' to load the KIDS build"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,238,0)="   onto your system.                                                        "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,239,0)="2) On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the               "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,240,0)="   option 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' to verify that all     "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,241,0)="   routines have the correct checksums.                                     "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,242,0)="3) From the 'Installation' Menu of KIDS, use the option                     "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,243,0)="   'Install Package(s)'.  Select the package 'FH*5.0*6' and proceed with"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,244,0)="   install.                                                                 "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,245,0)="4) If you are a MSM site move the routines to the other servers.            "
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,246,0)="5) On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",17,1,247,0)="6) Delete post-init FHIPST and FHXUTL (after running to completion)."
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",18,0)="15 SEQ #15^2990417^1"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^1^1^2990417"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="Refer to the Patch Description."
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",19,0)="16 SEQ #17^2990417^1"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",20,0)="23 SEQ #23^2991210^1"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",20,1,0)="^^3^3^2991210"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",20,1,1,0)="This patch corrects a help prompt which indicates that certain"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",20,1,2,0)="two-digit date entries are valid when actually they are not valid"
^DIC(9.4,9,22,3.3,"PAH",20,1,3,0)="in the year 2000 and beyond."
