^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,228,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,229,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,230,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,231,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,232,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,233,0)="1. Using the KIDS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,234,0)="   From the Kernel Installation and Distribution Systems (KIDS)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,235,0)="   Menu, select the Installation Menu [XPD INSTALLATION MENU]:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,236,0)="   Select Installation Option: Load a Distribution"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,237,0)="   Enter a Host File: LAB_Y2K.KID"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,238,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,239,0)="   KIDS Distribution saved on Mar 23, 1998@13:22:30"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,240,0)="   Comment: LR*5.2*203  LR*5.2*201  LA*5.2*42  Y2K Enhancements  3-23-98"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,241,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,242,0)="   This Distribution contains Transport Globals for the following"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,243,0)="   Package(s):"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,244,0)="        LR*5.2*203"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,245,0)="        LR*5.2*201"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,246,0)="        LA*5.2*42"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,247,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,248,0)="   Use INSTALL NAME: LR*5.2*203 to install this distribution"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,249,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,250,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,251,0)="2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,252,0)="   removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,253,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,254,0)="3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your system."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,255,0)="   You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,257,0)="4. On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu,"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,258,0)="   use the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,259,0)="       Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,260,0)="       Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,261,0)="       Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,262,0)="       Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,263,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,264,0)="   **** It is strongly recommended to do a KIDS Backup ****"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,265,0)="   ****         before installing the build.           ****"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,266,0)="   ****     The PRINT, COMPARE and VERIFY functions    ****"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,267,0)="   ****  should be performed for each of the patches   ****"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,268,0)="   ****         included in this distribution.         ****"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,269,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,270,0)="5. Primary Laboratory Options should be placed out of service"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,271,0)="   and Laboratory Users should be off the system."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,272,0)="   Menu option Laboratory [LRMENU] or the local equivalent."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,273,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,274,0)="   Routine LAB for lab automated instruments interfaced thru"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,275,0)="   a LSI should not be running."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,276,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,277,0)="   If site has direct-connected interfaces for lab automated"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,278,0)="   instruments these should not be running."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,279,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,280,0)="   The HL7 background job (HLLP) for the Lab Universal Interface"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,281,0)="   should be stopped."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,282,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,283,0)="   The routine LA7UIIN to process incoming HL7 messages should not"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,284,0)="   be running. It will shutdown automatically after 5 minutes if"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,285,0)="   no messages have been received."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,286,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,287,0)="   If using auto download, the routine LA7ADL should not be running."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,288,0)="   Use option Start/Stop Auto Download Background Job"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,289,0)="   [LA7 ADL START/STOP]."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,290,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,291,0)="6. Installation time is less than 10 minutes during off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,292,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,293,0)="7. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,294,0)="   'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*203' and"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,295,0)="   proceed with the install."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,296,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,297,0)="8. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,298,0)="   be returned to the mapped set once the installation has run"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,299,0)="   to completion."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,300,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",9,1,301,0)="9. If installation is successful, delete routine LA42 and LR201."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,0)="44 SEQ #30^2981016^1"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^191^191^2981016"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,1,0)=" This patch will prevent a null subscript error from occurring when using"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,2,0)=" option LEDI Setup [LA7V SETUP] after the installation of the HL7 patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,3,0)=" HL*1.6*14."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,5,0)=" 1. Problem: A null subscript error was occurring at VER+3 in routine"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,6,0)="             LA7VSTP because the software was not properly quitting when"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,7,0)="             checking for the existence of an entry in HL7 MESSAGE TYPE"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,8,0)="             file (#771.2)."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,10,0)="   Solution: The code has been changed to use a FileMan DIC call to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,11,0)="             perform the lookup of an entry in this file."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,14,0)=" Associated NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,15,0)=" ---------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,16,0)=" BAY-0798-32112"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,19,0)=" Routine Summary"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,20,0)=" ---------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,22,0)="  The following is a list of routines included in this patch. The second"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,23,0)="  line of each routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,25,0)=" <tab>;;5.2;AUTOMATED LAB INSTRUMENTS;**[patch list]**;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,27,0)="                CHECK^XTSUMBLD Results"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,29,0)=" Routine    Before Patch   After Patch    Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,30,0)=" ------     ------------   -----------    ----------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,32,0)=" LA44          NA          2463527            44"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,33,0)=" LA7VSTP    25404911       24725864          27,44"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,36,0)=" INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,37,0)=" -------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,38,0)=" The patch is distributed in KIDS format in a PackMan message."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,40,0)=" The install time for this patch is less than 2 minutes. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,41,0)=" can be installed when Laboratory users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,42,0)=" However the following conditions apply:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,44,0)="    -Users should not be using option LEDI Setup [LA7V SETUP]."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,45,0)="     The LEDI Setup [LA7V SETUP] option will be placed out of service"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,46,0)="     during this install."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,48,0)=" Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,49,0)=" Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC)."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,51,0)=" If the routine LA7VSTP is a mapped routine, appropriate action should be"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,52,0)=" taken to disable the mapped routine at the beginning of the patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,53,0)=" installation process and to insure proper updating of mapped routines"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,54,0)=" afterward.  Also, if the routine LA7VSTP resides in multiple locations"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,55,0)=" within the system configuration, all routine directories should be updated"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,56,0)=" appropriately."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,58,0)=" NOTE: MailMan and KERNEL patches must be current on the target system to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,59,0)="       avoid problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,60,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,61,0)=" NOTE: This KIDS install places the option LEDI Setup [LA7V SETUP]"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,62,0)="       out of service during the install. The option is not added or"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,63,0)="       changed by this patch. If KIDS prompts:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,65,0)="       ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,66,0)="        Install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,68,0)="       The site can answer ""NO"" if they choose since the option"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,69,0)="       is unchanged."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,71,0)="       Additionally, if performing the KIDS Compare option, KIDS will"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,72,0)="       report that this option is being changed. This is a false"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,73,0)="       message since the option is only being disabled during the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,74,0)="       install by KIDS. It is included in the KIDS build only for the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,75,0)="       purpose of being disabled during the install by KIDS."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,78,0)=" 1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,80,0)=" 2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,81,0)="     option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,83,0)=" 3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,84,0)="     system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,86,0)=" 4.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,87,0)="     select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,89,0)=" 5.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,90,0)="     all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,92,0)=" 6.  If you wish to preserve a copy of the routines exported in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,93,0)="     prior to installation, you should use the 'Backup a Transport Global'"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,94,0)="     option at this time.  You may also compare the routine in your"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,95,0)="     production account to the routine in the patch by using the 'Compare"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,96,0)="     a Transport Global to Current System' option (see note above)."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,97,0)="     These options can both be found under the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,99,0)=" 7.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,100,0)="     and select the package 'LA*5.2*44'.  When prompted 'Want to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,101,0)="     DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES//',"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,102,0)="     choose 'NO'. KIDS will disable the appropriate option during the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,103,0)="     install (see note above)."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,105,0)=" 8.  On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,107,0)=" 9.  Routine LA44 can be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,108,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,110,0)=" *****************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,111,0)=" Below is an example of the dialogue seen during the KIDS install:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,113,0)="Select Installation Option: 6  Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,114,0)="Select INSTALL NAME:    LA*5.2*44        Loaded from Distribution  10/7/98@13:20"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,115,0)=":18"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,116,0)="     => LA*5.2*44"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,118,0)="This Distribution was loaded on Oct 07, 1998@13:20:18 with header of"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,119,0)="LA*5.2*44"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,120,0)="It consisted of the following Install(s):"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,121,0)="LA*5.2*44"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,123,0)="   LA*5.2*44"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,124,0)="Will first run the Environment Check Routine, LA44"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,125,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,127,0)="                        --- Environment Check is Ok ---"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,129,0)="Install Questions for LA*5.2*44"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,130,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,131,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,132,0)="Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,133,0)=" "
