^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",10,1,191,0)=" *****************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,0)="45 SEQ #31^2981214^1"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^200^200^2981214"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,1,0)=" This patch will address a fix to printing of Lab shipping manifests."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,3,0)=" Problem: The patient demographics were not printing under certain"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,4,0)="          conditions on the manifest when a new page was started."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,5,0)="          If a new page is started because of a change in shipping"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,6,0)="          condition or container and the last patient on the previous"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,7,0)="          and current page are the same, the patient demographics would"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,8,0)="          not print on the current page."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,10,0)=" Solution: When there is a change in shipping condition or container then"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,11,0)="           force the printing of the patient demographics."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,16,0)="  Associated NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,17,0)="  --------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,19,0)="  TOG-0898-12117"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,20,0)="  WRJ-0998-10878 "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,21,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,22,0)="  Test Sites"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,23,0)="  ----------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,25,0)="  Milwaukee VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,26,0)="  Togus VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,27,0)="  White River Junction VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,29,0)=" ----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,31,0)=" ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,32,0)=" ---------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,34,0)="  The following is a list of routines included in this patch. The second"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,35,0)="  line of each routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,37,0)="  <tab>;;5.2;AUTOMATED LAB INSTRUMENTS;**[patch list]**; Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,39,0)="                   CHECK^XTSUMBLD results"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,41,0)="    Routine Name   Before Patch   After Patch    Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,42,0)="    ------------   ------------   -----------   --------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,43,0)="    LA45              N/A          2463531           45"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,44,0)="    LA7SMP          15780871       15792287         27,45"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,46,0)=" INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,47,0)=" -------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,48,0)=" The install time for this patch is less than 2 minutes if menus are not"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,49,0)=" rebuilt. If menus are rebuilt then install time on a heavily used system"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,50,0)=" will be approximately 25 minutes. This patch can be installed when"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,51,0)=" Laboratory users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,52,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,53,0)=" However the following conditions apply:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,55,0)="    - Printing of a Laboratory shipping manifest should not be occurring."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,56,0)="      The option Print Shipping Manifest [LA7S MANIFEST PRINT] will be"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,57,0)="      disabled during the install by the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,59,0)="      Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,60,0)="      Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC)."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,62,0)=" NOTE: MailMan and KERNEL patches must be current on the target system to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,63,0)="       avoid problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,67,0)=" 1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,69,0)=" 2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,70,0)="     option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,72,0)=" 3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,73,0)="     system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,75,0)=" 4.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,76,0)="     select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,78,0)=" 5.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,79,0)="     all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,81,0)=" 6.  If you wish to preserve a copy of the routines exported in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,82,0)="     prior to installation, you should use the 'Backup a Transport Global'"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,83,0)="     option at this time.  You may also compare the routine in your"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,84,0)="     production account to the routine in the patch by using the 'Compare"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,85,0)="     a Transport Global to Current System' option.  These options can"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,86,0)="     both be found under the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,88,0)=" 7.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,89,0)="     and select the package 'LA*5.2*45'.  When prompted 'Want to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,90,0)="     DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES//',"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,91,0)="     choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,92,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,93,0)=" 8.  On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,95,0)=" 9.  Routine LA45 can be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,98,0)=" *****************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",11,1,99,0)=" Below is an example of the dialogue seen during the KIDS install:"
