^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",17,1,195,0)=" Install Message sent #21510"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",17,1,196,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",17,1,197,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",17,1,198,0)="Install Completed"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,0)="56 SEQ #38^3000816^1"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^225^225^3000816"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LA*5.2*56 contains no changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,2,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,5,0)="DESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,6,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,8,0)="1. When the Lab LEDI software needs to build a HL7 message to return lab"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,9,0)="test results (ORU) to the collecting facility, the message building could"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,10,0)="fail at the host laboratory facility with the error undefined variable"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,11,0)="LA(""I"") in routine PID+4^LA7VORU causing the collecting facility not"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,12,0)="to receive a result message. This problem occurs when the host lab's entry"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,13,0)="for the collecting facility in the INSTITUTION file (#4) has an internal"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,14,0)="entry number which is different from the VA Station Number and the "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,15,0)="collecting facility is a division of an integrated facility. The software"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,16,0)="is attempting to return the results to the collecting facility instead of"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,17,0)="the primary facility's computer system. If no associated HL7 protocol was"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,18,0)="identified message building was continuing with the HL7 and Lab environment"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,19,0)="not properly initialized. The software would error when it referenced "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,20,0)="variable LA(""I"") that was not defined during this initialization."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,22,0)="Routine LA7VMSG has been changed to retrieve the VA Station Number from"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,23,0)="the INSTITUTION file for an integrated collecting facility's primary"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,24,0)="system entry when the station number is used in building the result (ORU)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,25,0)="message."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,26,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,27,0)="2. Routine LA7VMSG has been changed to determine if a link back to the "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,28,0)="integrated facility's primary system does not exist. If a link does not"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,29,0)="exist, the results are returned via the collecting facility."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,31,0)="3. Routine LA7VMSG has been split into two routines (LA7VMSG and LA7VMSG1)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,32,0)="because it exceeded the maximum routine size of 10k as specified by the SAC. "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,34,0)="4. Recording of an error condition in the Lab Messaging Error Log has been "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,35,0)="added when the software is unable to find the appropriate entry in the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,36,0)="PROTOCOL file (#101) to use in building the HL7 message. This can occur"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,37,0)="when no entry is found in the PROTOCOL file or the HL7 package is unable to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,38,0)="initialize the HL7 message environment for message building. The error that"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,39,0)="will be recorded is #28 in LA7 MESSAGE LOG BULLETINS file (#62.485)."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,40,0)="The error text will be:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,41,0)="  Msg # |1| encountered the following HL7 generation error: |2|."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,42,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,43,0)="   where |1| is the LA7 MESSAGE QUEUE file (#62.49) entry number"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,44,0)="         |2| is the conditions:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,45,0)="             1. Invalid/undefined protocol xxx"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,46,0)="             2. Call to INIT^HLFNC2 failed for protocol xxx"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,47,0)="             xxx - being the name of the protocol in the PROTOCOL file."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,50,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,51,0)="ASSOCIATED NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,52,0)="---------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,53,0)=" CON-0400-10572"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,56,0)="TEST SITES"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,57,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,58,0)="  Connecticut HCS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,59,0)="  Boston HCS "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,61,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,62,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,63,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,65,0)="  The following is a list of routines included in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,66,0)="  The second line of each routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,68,0)="  <tab>;;5.2;AUTOMATED LAB INSTRUMENTS;**[Patch List]**;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,70,0)="                    CHECK^XTSUMBLD results"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,71,0)="                    Checksum       Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,72,0)="   Routine Name     Before Patch   After Patch    Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,73,0)="   ------------     ------------   -----------    ------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,74,0)="   LA56             N/A            4543424        **56**(Deleted by KIDS)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,75,0)="   LA7VMSG          22442510       16357149       **27,50,56**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,76,0)="   LA7VMSG1         N/A            3358807        **56**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,77,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,78,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,80,0)="************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,82,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,83,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,85,0)="  The install time for this patch is less than 5 minutes. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,86,0)="  can be installed when Laboratory users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,87,0)="  Suggested time to install: non-peak requirement hours. Verification"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,88,0)="  of lab test results should be suspended. The install will disable"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,89,0)="  several Lab verifying options as specified in #7 below."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,92,0)="NOTE: Kernel, MailMan and HL7 patches must be current on the target system"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,93,0)="      to avoid problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,95,0)="      Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,96,0)="      Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC)."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,99,0)="  1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,101,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,102,0)="      option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,104,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,105,0)="      system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,107,0)="  4.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,108,0)="      select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,110,0)="  5.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,111,0)="      all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,113,0)="  6.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,114,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,115,0)="        Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,116,0)="        Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,117,0)="        Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,119,0)="      If you wish to preserve a copy of the routines exported in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,120,0)="      prior to installation, you should use the 'Backup a Transport Global'"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,121,0)="      option at this time.  You may also compare the routines in your"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,122,0)="      production account to the routines in the patch by using the 'Compare"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,123,0)="      a Transport Global to Current System' option."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,125,0)="  7.  The install will disable the following Lab verifying options during"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,126,0)="      patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,127,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,128,0)="      Enter/verify data (auto instrument) [LRVR]"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,129,0)="      Enter/verify data (Work list) [LRVRW]"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,130,0)="      Enter/verify data (Load list) [LRVRW2]"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,131,0)="      Batch data entry (chem, hem, tox, etc.) [LRSTUF]"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,132,0)="      Group verify (EA, EL, EW) [LRGV]"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,133,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,134,0)="  8.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,135,0)="      and select the package 'LA*5.2*56'.  When prompted 'Want to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,136,0)="      DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES//',"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,137,0)="      choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,138,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,139,0)="  9. On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,141,0)=" 10. Routine LA56 will be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,142,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,143,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,144,0)="POST-INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS: NONE"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,145,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,146,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,147,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",18,1,149,0)="************************************************************************"
