^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,0)="52 SEQ #39^3000816^1"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,0)="^^261^261^3000816"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,1,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LA*5.2*52 contains no changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,2,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,4,0)="This patch fixes several reported errors and corrects several Vista"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,5,0)="Programming Standards and Conventions (SAC) violations."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,7,0)="1. This patch fixes a reported undefined variable error occurring at"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,8,0)="LAKDIFF3+10^LAKDIFF3."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,10,0)="Routine LAKDIFF3 was changed to kill variable LRORD before calling"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,11,0)="EXPLODE^LRGP2 to build the list of tests on the work list. Users would"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,12,0)="encounter an undefined error when attempting to select a second or"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,13,0)="subsequent accession because the array LRORD was not cleaned up after"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,14,0)="processing the first accession."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,15,0)="NOIS: CON-0899-12137, FAV-0899-71050, FRE-1099-60326, HAM-0899-20524,"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,16,0)="      SLC-0999-50329, WAS-1299-21602"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,18,0)="2. This patch fixes a reported illegal number error at WLN^LAKDIFF."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,20,0)="Routine LAKDIFF was changed to use a DIR call to allow the user to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,21,0)="select the accession number. This call will prevent the user from"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,22,0)="entering a number that is outside the range of possible accession"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,23,0)="numbers (1-9999999) or contains a decimal."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,24,0)="NOIS: MAD-1295-40263, SLC-0696-50890"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,26,0)="3. It corrects the following Vista Programming Standards and Conventions"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,27,0)="violations that were observed in routines LAKDIFF, LAKDIFF1, LAKDIFF2,"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,28,0)="and LAKDIFF3 during a software review as part of patch development:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,30,0)=" a. Removed direct global read of global ^%ZIS(2) which contains the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,31,0)="    TERMINAL TYPE file.  Routine LAKDIFF was retrieving code to set"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,32,0)="    cursor positioning. Call changed to use Kernel supplied supported"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,33,0)="    references PREP^XGF."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,35,0)=" b. Removed user input READS which were not terminated by a carriage"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,36,0)="    return. These were converted to use the Kernel supplied supported"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,37,0)="    references READ^XGF."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,39,0)=" c. Removed direct global references to the DD global. These were"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,40,0)="    converted to FileMan supplied supported references ^DI"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,42,0)=" d. Variable DTIME was being set but was not documented in Technical"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,43,0)="    manual. Changed setting of DTIME to Kernel supported reference"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,44,0)="    $$DTIME^XUP."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,46,0)="4. Users are now allowed to select the accession date. Previously the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,47,0)="software defaulted to the current date."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,49,0)="5. When displaying the CBC profile the software previously only displayed"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,50,0)="verified results from FILE LAB DATA (#63). The software will now display"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,51,0)="any unverified results that have been entered on the work list."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,52,0)="These results are preceded with an ""*"" to denote the status of unverified."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,54,0)="6. When determining the number of days back for delta checking the "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,55,0)="software was using 60 days. This patch changes the logic to calculate the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,56,0)="number of days back for delta checks by using the value the site specifies"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,57,0)="in FILE LABORATORY SITE (#69.9), FIELD DAYS BACK FOR DELTA CHECKS (#20)."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,59,0)="7. The user can now select if the cell differential and RBC morphology"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,60,0)="display updates on each key press. The user is prompted if they want the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,61,0)="display updated with each key press upon entering the option. If the user"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,62,0)="selects NO then the display can be updated by entering a ""?"" during cell"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,63,0)="differential and RBC morphology entry. Selecting YES provides a continuously"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,64,0)="updating display. On systems with slow response times, selecting NO may"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,65,0)="improve performance. User's preferences for this function will be saved"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,66,0)="using Kernel's generic parameter utility. The parameter definition is named"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,67,0)="LA KDIFF DISPLAY UPDATE which will be added to the PARAMETER DEFINITION"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,68,0)="file (#8989.51) by the KIDS install."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,70,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,71,0)="ASSOCIATED NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,72,0)="---------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,73,0)=" CON-0899-12137"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,74,0)=" FAV-0899-71050"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,75,0)=" FRE-1099-60326"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,76,0)=" HAM-0899-20524"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,77,0)=" MAD-1295-40263"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,78,0)=" PHI-0300-21262"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,79,0)=" SLC-0696-50890"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,80,0)=" SLC-0999-50329"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,81,0)=" WAS-1299-21602"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,83,0)="TEST SITES"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,84,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,85,0)=" Connecticut HCS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,86,0)=" Fresno VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,87,0)=" Hampton VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,88,0)=" Philadelphia VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,90,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,91,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,92,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,93,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,94,0)="  The following is a list of routines included in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,95,0)="  The second line of each routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,97,0)="  <tab>;;5.2;AUTOMATED LAB INSTRUMENTS;**[Patch List]**;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,99,0)="                    CHECK^XTSUMBLD results"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,101,0)="                    Checksum       Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,102,0)="   Routine Name     Before Patch   After Patch    Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,103,0)="   ------------     ------------   -----------    ------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,104,0)="   LA52             N/A            4557885        **52**(Deleted by KIDS)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,105,0)="   LAKDIFF          9922081        7244730        **13,52**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,106,0)="   LAKDIFF1         8917764        5795474        **52**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,107,0)="   LAKDIFF2         9640378        2778086        **52**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,108,0)="   LAKDIFF3         2515859        1523847        **52**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,109,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,110,0)="************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,112,0)="Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,113,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,115,0)="  The install time for this patch is less than 5 minutes. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,116,0)="  can be installed with Laboratory users on the system."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,118,0)="  Suggested time to install: non-peak requirement hours."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,119,0)="  Recommend that the patch be installed when option Keypad differential"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,120,0)="  for CRT's [LA KB DIFF] is not being used."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,122,0)="NOTE: Kernel, MailMan and HL patches must be current on the target system"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,123,0)="      to avoid problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,125,0)="      Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,126,0)="      Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC). Patch will send patch installation"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,127,0)="      alerts to Lab mail group LMI."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,129,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,130,0)="  1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,131,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,132,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,133,0)="      option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,134,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,135,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,136,0)="      system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,138,0)="  4.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,139,0)="      select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,141,0)="  5.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,142,0)="      all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,143,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,144,0)="  6.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,145,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,146,0)="        Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,147,0)="        Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,148,0)="        Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,150,0)="      If you wish to preserve a copy of the routines exported in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,151,0)="      prior to installation, you should use the 'Backup a Transport Global'"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,152,0)="      option at this time.  You may also compare the routines in your"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,153,0)="      production account to the routines in the patch by using the 'Compare"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,154,0)="      a Transport Global to Current System' option."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,156,0)="  7.  The install will disable the following Lab option during patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,157,0)="      installation."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,158,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,159,0)="      Keypad differential for CRT's [LA KB DIFF]"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,160,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,161,0)="  8.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,162,0)="      and select the package 'LA*5.2*52'.  When prompted 'Want to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,163,0)="      DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES//',"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,164,0)="      choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,165,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,166,0)="  9.  On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,167,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,168,0)=" 10.  Routine LA52 will be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,169,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,172,0)="Post-Installation Instructions: NONE"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,174,0)="************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,175,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",19,1,176,0)="Installation example:"
