^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",22,1,188,0)=" LA*5.2*59 Installed."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",22,1,189,0)="               Apr 24, 2001@13:34:05"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",22,1,190,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",22,1,191,0)=" Install Message sent #52035"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,0)="60 SEQ #43^3020204^1"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,0)="^^188^188^3020204"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,1,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LA*5.2*60 contains no changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,2,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,4,0)="Patch LA*5.2*60 addresses a fix to the option Keypad differential for"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,5,0)="CRT's [LA KB DIFF]. It was determined, during testing of another patch,"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,6,0)="that the lab verifying process would trigger the transmission of the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,7,0)="wrong patient's results when verifying an accession received via Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,8,0)="Electronic Data Interchange (LEDI). The variable LRORU3 is used by the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,9,0)="lab verifying process to trigger the building of a HL7 result (ORU) message"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,10,0)="to transmit the test results to the requesting facility. Patch LA*5.2*60"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,11,0)="changes routine LAKDIFF3 to set the variable LRORU3 based on the current"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,12,0)="accession before calling the lab verifying process."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,13,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,14,0)="The ""Heads-Up on Patient Safety Alert"" issued on 18 January 2002 regarding"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,15,0)="the electronic transmission of an incorrect result from a LEDI Host"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,16,0)="laboratory to a Collecting Laboratory is resolved by patch LA*5.2*60."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,18,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,19,0)="ASSOCIATED NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,20,0)="---------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,21,0)=" NONE"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,24,0)="TEST SITES"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,25,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,26,0)=" Milwaukee VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,29,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,30,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,31,0)="  The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,32,0)="  of each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,33,0)="  <tab> ;;5.2;AUTOMATED LAB INSTRUMENTS;<patchlist>;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,35,0)="                    Checksum       Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,36,0)="   Routine Name     Before Patch   After Patch    Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,37,0)="   ------------     ------------   -----------    ------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,38,0)="   LA60             N/A            4331834        **60** (Deleted by KIDS)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,39,0)="   LAKDIFF3         1523847        1615579        **52,60**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,41,0)=" List of preceding patches: 52"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,42,0)=" Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,43,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,45,0)="************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,47,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,48,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,50,0)="  The install time for this patch is less than 1 minute. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,51,0)="  can be installed when Laboratory users are on the system. Users should"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,52,0)="  not be using option Keypad differential for CRT's [LA KB DIFF] during"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,53,0)="  patch installation. The KIDS install will disable this option during"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,54,0)="  installation. Suggested time to install: anytime the option LA KB DIFF"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,55,0)="  is not being used."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,58,0)="NOTE: Kernel patches must be current on the target system to avoid"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,59,0)="      problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,61,0)="      Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,62,0)="      Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC)."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,65,0)="  1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,67,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,68,0)="      option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,70,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,71,0)="      system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,73,0)="  4.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,74,0)="      select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,76,0)="  5.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,77,0)="      all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,79,0)="  6.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,80,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,81,0)="        Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,82,0)="        Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,83,0)="        Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,85,0)="      If you wish to preserve a copy of the routines exported in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,86,0)="      prior to installation, you should use the 'Backup a Transport Global'"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,87,0)="      option at this time.  You may also compare the routines in your"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,88,0)="      production account to the routines in the patch by using the 'Compare"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,89,0)="      a Transport Global to Current System' option."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,92,0)="  7.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,93,0)="      and select the package 'LA*5.2*60'.  When prompted 'Want KIDS to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,94,0)="      INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// choose 'NO'.  When prompted"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,95,0)="      'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols?"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,96,0)="      YES//', choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,98,0)="      Note: Option Keypad differential for CRT's [LA KB DIFF] will be"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,99,0)="      disabled during installation by KIDS."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,100,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,101,0)="  8. On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,102,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,103,0)="  9. Routine LA60 will be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,105,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,106,0)="POST-INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,107,0)="==============================="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,108,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,109,0)="None"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,112,0)="************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,113,0)="Installation example: "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,115,0)="Select Installation Option: 6  Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,116,0)="Select INSTALL NAME: LA*5.2*60   Loaded from Distribution  1/30/02@15:07:57"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,117,0)="     => LA*5.2*60"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,119,0)="This Distribution was loaded on Jan 30, 2002@15:07:57 with header of"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,120,0)="   LA*5.2*60 "
