^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,178,0)=" Updating Routine file......"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,179,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,180,0)=" Updating KIDS files......."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,181,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,182,0)=" LA*5.2*60 Installed."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,183,0)="               Jan 30, 2002@15:10:22"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,184,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,185,0)=" Install Message sent #xxxxx"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,187,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",23,1,188,0)="Select Installation Option:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,0)="46^3020226^1"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,0)="^^343^343^3020226"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,1,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LA*5.2*46 contains no changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,2,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,4,0)="========================================"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,6,0)="This patch adds support for sending/receiving Laboratory Electronic"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,7,0)="Data Interchange (LEDI) orders/results with non-VA facilities"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,8,0)="(commercial reference laboratories)."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,10,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,11,0)="As of the release date of this software, there is no national solution to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,12,0)="implement a laboratory electronic HL7 standard interface to a facility or"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,13,0)="other entity outside the VA wide area network.  National communication"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,14,0)="security concerns are still being debated by the Department of Veterans"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,15,0)="Affairs (VA) and are awaiting resolution.  At present, a VA medical center,"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,16,0)="which intends to utilize this software in conjunction with an interface to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,17,0)="a commercial reference laboratory or other non-VA information system entity,"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,18,0)="will need to coordinate with the vendor an acceptable communication method."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,19,0)="Any implementation will need to be approved by the facility and VISN"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,20,0)="Information Security Officer (ISO) and meet current VA security requirements"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,21,0)="for external electronic connections. See VHA Directive 6212, Security of"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,22,0)="External Electronic Connections and VHA Directive 6210, Automated Information"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,23,0)="Systems (AIS) Security for additional information and guidance. Additional"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,24,0)="security information may be obtained from the Health Information Security"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,25,0)="Service (HISS) web page at http://vaww.domain.ext/miss."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,26,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,27,0)="Implementation of a HL7 messaging interface between the VA VistA Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,28,0)="package and a non-VA information system consists basically of three parts:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,29,0)=" - VistA Laboratory LEDI II software."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,30,0)=" - certified communication software and hardware"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,31,0)=" - non-VA information system capable of sending and receiving laboratory HL7"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,32,0)="   order and result messages."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,33,0)="All three must be functional to utilize the capabilities of this LEDI II"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,34,0)="software patch. The implementation,setup, and configuration of vendor provided"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,35,0)="hardware and software is NOT addressed by this documentation.  Consult the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,36,0)="vendor provided documentation and instructions to interface to the VistA"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,37,0)="Laboratory package."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,38,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,40,0)="Additionally support is added for TCP/IP protocol as a communication"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,41,0)="protocol for the transmission of LEDI HL7 messages. This requires"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,42,0)="patch HL*1.6*19 to have been successfully installed. The implementation"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,43,0)="of this protocol in place of the current MailMan protocol will"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,44,0)="significantly increase transmission speed of messages and reduce system"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,45,0)="overhead/storage. Both systems that will be exchanging HL7 messages,"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,46,0)="using the TCP/IP protocol will need to coordinate the switch to this"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,47,0)="new transmission method. There will be two logical links established"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,48,0)="to exchange messages a server (listener) logical link to receive and"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,49,0)="process messages and a client link to transmit messages."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,51,0)="A new shipping code SM40 - Required Shipping Info Updated has been added"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,52,0)="to file LAB ELECTRONIC CODES (#64.061). This code is used when recording"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,53,0)="this event in file LAB SHIPPING EVENT (#62.85)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,55,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,56,0)="Comments can now contain "";""character. Previously the "";"" character was"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,57,0)="used to parse comments into multiple lines and filed in the database using"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,58,0)="a classical FileMan DIE call. FileMan parsed the fields to edit using"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,59,0)="the "";"" character in the DR string. The new call uses a FileMan database"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,60,0)="server call, which does not have this restriction."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,63,0)="New fields have been added and existing fields modified within the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,64,0)="CHEM TEST subfile of file AUTO INSTRUMENT (#62.4) to support the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,65,0)="following features when processing result messages. These features"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,66,0)="are site-selectable. See data dictionary field description for each"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,67,0)="field for further information. Using option LEDI Setup [LA7V SETUP],"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,68,0)="the section on Auto Instrument settings will prompt for these additional"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,69,0)="fields."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,71,0)="1. Process NTE segments following OBX segments. Comments found attached"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,72,0)="   to specific test results are stored as comments. The field REMARK PREFIX"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,73,0)="   #18 in CHEM TEST subfile can be used to specify a comment prefix that"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,74,0)="   will be made part of the comment."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,75,0)="2. Store test reference ranges, abnormal flags and name of performing"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,76,0)="   laboratory. This patch stores these parameters as comments with the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,77,0)="   results. This information is prefixed with the field REMARK PREFIX."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,78,0)="3. Specify whether final or incomplete results are processed."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,80,0)="The fields that are new/modified are:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,81,0)="    ACCEPT RESULTS FOR THIS TEST"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,82,0)="    STORE REMARKS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,83,0)="    REMARK PREFIX"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,84,0)="    STORE PRODUCER'S ID"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,85,0)="    STORE REFERENCE RANGE"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,86,0)="    STORE ABNORMAL FLAGS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,88,0)="New fields have been added to the LAB SHIPPING CONFIGURATION file (#62.9)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,89,0)="to allow collecting facilities to specify required patient/specimen"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,90,0)="information to be sent with shipping manifest. This can include specimen"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,91,0)="volume, weight, collection end date/time (collection duration),"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,92,0)="patient height and weight (NOIS ALB-1099-51591). LOINC codes are used to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,93,0)="identify patient height, weight and specimen weight when appropriate."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,94,0)="Editing these fields is performed using option Edit Shipping Configuration"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,95,0)="[LA7S EDIT 62.9]. The fields are:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,97,0)="    USE NON-VA CODES"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,98,0)="    TEST/PROFILE sub-file"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,99,0)="      DIVISION"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,100,0)="      REQUIRE PATIENT HEIGHT"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,101,0)="      PATIENT HEIGHT"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,102,0)="      PATIENT HEIGHT UNITS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,103,0)="      PATIENT HEIGHT LOINC CODE"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,104,0)="      REQUIRE PATIENT WEIGHT"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,105,0)="      PATIENT WEIGHT"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,106,0)="      PATIENT WEIGHT UNITS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,107,0)="      PATIENT WEIGHT LOINC CODE"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,108,0)="      REQUIRE COLLECTION VOLUME"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,109,0)="      COLLECTION VOLUME"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,110,0)="      COLLECTION VOLUME UNITS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,111,0)="      COLLECTION VOLUME LOINC CODE"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,112,0)="      REQUIRE COLLECTION END D/T"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,114,0)="The process of building a shipping manifest now allows the user to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,115,0)="specify the starting and ending accession numbers to check within an"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,116,0)="accession area. This feature can shorten manifest building time when"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,117,0)="searching a yearly accession area with a large number of accessions."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,118,0)="It allows the site to skip the accession numbers that have been"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,119,0)="completed earlier in a year and no longer need to be checked to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,120,0)="determine it any of the tests meet the criteria for building to a"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,121,0)="manifest."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,123,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,124,0)="The process of closing a shipping manifest now performs a check of"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,125,0)="certain required information. The required information check is for:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,126,0)=" 1. Each test has an order NLT code assigned."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,127,0)=" 2. If shipping to a facility that does not use VA NLT codes for"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,128,0)="    test ordering, the appropriate non-VA test codes/names"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,129,0)="    have been designated for all tests on the manifest."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,130,0)=" 3. Site-specified required patient/specimen information has been"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,131,0)="    entered."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,132,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,134,0)="The process of building orders in the file LAB PENDING ORDER (#69.6)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,135,0)="has been enhanced to use information from the file LAB SHIPPING"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,136,0)="CONFIGURATION (#62.9) to create orders based on the host facilities"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,137,0)="specified collection sample and urgency."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,138,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,140,0)="The LEDI result (ORU) messages will now include the test interpretation"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,141,0)="found in LABORATORY TEST file (#60) as a comment (NTE segment) following"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,142,0)="the test results. Test results to be stored will be checked against the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,143,0)="FileMan input transform for the data name used to store the results in"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,144,0)="file LAB DATA (#63). If the results do not pass the FileMan input"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,145,0)="transform then an error message will be generated via the Lab"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,146,0)="Universal Interface error reporting process. Results values that are"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,147,0)="""canc"", ""pending"" or ""comment"" will be stored."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,150,0)="The option Display Lab Universal Interface Message [LA7 PRINT LAB UI"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,151,0)="MESSAGE] has been modified to prompt the user if the Kernel Browser"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,152,0)="should be used to display a message. If the browser is not selected then"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,153,0)="a standard ""scroll and roll"" display of the selected message(s) is"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,154,0)="produced."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,155,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,156,0)="Option Retransmit LEDI Lab Results [LA7S RESULTS RETRANSMIT] will allow"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,157,0)="a user to retransmit the laboratory test results for selected accession(s)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,158,0)="to the collecting/submitting facility."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,159,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,160,0)="The install will update several files during the post-install as necessary:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,161,0)=" - It was found that the original release of LEDI failed to update the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,162,0)="   field SHIP VIA #.04 in file LAB SHIPPING MANIFEST (#62.8) when a manifest"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,163,0)="   is created. This information will update existing manifests with"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,164,0)="   information from the related file LAB SHIPPING CONFIGURATION (#62.9)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,165,0)="   entry."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,166,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,167,0)=" - The processing routine specified in file LA7 MESSAGE PARAMETER (#62.48)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,168,0)="   for entries related to LEDI has been changed. Existing entries will be"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,169,0)="   updated as appropriate."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,171,0)=" NOIS HIN-0998-40287 corrected an undefined variable error when building a"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,172,0)="   result message."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,174,0)=" NOIS BOS-0498-10163 reported an undefined error when attempting to lock"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,175,0)=" LAB SHIPPING MANIFEST file (#62.8). Due to a typographically error the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,176,0)=" character ""$"" was omitted from a $DATA intrinsic function."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,177,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,178,0)=" NOIS TAM-0401-31867 reported that option Lab Messaging File Integrity"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,179,0)=" Checker [LA7 CHECK FILES] option allowed queuing the report to the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,180,0)=" ""HOME"" device. The option will now prevent queuing to the HOME device."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,181,0)=" It also removes ""HOME"" as the device default value."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,182,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,183,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,184,0)="ASSOCIATED E3R"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,185,0)="--------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,186,0)="E3R #15348, RETRANSMIT FUNCTION FOR LEDI"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",24,1,187,0)=" "
