^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,0)="61 SEQ #45^3020626^1"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,0)="^^384^384^3020626"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,1,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LA*5.2*61 contains no changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,2,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,4,0)="Patch LA*5.2*61 addresses several NOIS'es involving the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,5,0)="Electronic Data Interchange (LEDI) software. "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,6,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,7,0)="  ********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,8,0)="  *                                                                  *"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,9,0)="  * Collecting facilities: Upon host laboratory installation of this *"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,10,0)="  * patch, the HL7 Result (ORU) message will no longer contain the   *"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,11,0)="  * performing laboratory comment. See item #7 for instructions.     *"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,12,0)="  *                                                                  *"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,13,0)="  * Host facilities: Notify your collection facilities of scheduled  *"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,14,0)="  * patch installation.                                              *"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,15,0)="  *                                                                  *"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,16,0)="  ********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,18,0)="1. NOIS HWH-0202-42779 and LAS-0402-61457 reported a problem in the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,19,0)="building of a HL7 Order (ORM) message. Under certain circumstances, the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,20,0)="software was passing the collecting facility station number instead of"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,21,0)="an INSTITUTION file (#4) internal entry number to a Lab HL7 field building"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,22,0)="routine. Construction of the collecting facility's HL7 Order (ORM) message"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,23,0)="ORC segment's field ENTERING ORGANIZATION (ORC-17) placed the VA station"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,24,0)="number in the field's second sub-component instead of the first"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,25,0)="sub-component. This occurs when the collecting facility's VA station"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,26,0)="number is alphanumeric. When processing the ORM message at the host"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,27,0)="facility the building of the LAB PENDING ORDERS ENTRY file (#69.6)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,28,0)="either identified the wrong collecting facility or was unable to identify"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,29,0)="a collecting facility. Option Referral Patient Multi-purpose Accession"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,30,0)="[LRLEDI] is unable to extract the test orders from file #69.6 when the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,31,0)="host facility attempts to process the shipping manifest. Routine LA7VORM1"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,32,0)="has been changed to pass a pointer for file #4 instead of the VA station"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,33,0)="number to the ORC-17 field building routine."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,35,0)="2. During review of NOIS HWH-0202-42779 a problem with the ""CH"" and"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,36,0)="""CH1"" MUMPS cross-references on COLLECTING FACILITY (#.02) and HOST"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,37,0)="FACILITY (#.03) fields respectively of the LAB SHIPPING CONFIGURATION"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,38,0)="file (#62.9) was identified. Multiple entries in this cross-reference"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,39,0)="pointed to the same entry in the file. The ""KILL"" logic for these cross-"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,40,0)="references does not perform correctly, leaving incorrect entries in"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,41,0)="the ""CH"" cross-reference. These two MUMPS cross-references are replaced"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,42,0)="by a single new style FileMan Regular INDEX file cross-reference named"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,43,0)="""CH"". The cross-reference ""ASC"" on LAB MESSAGING LINK field (#.07) will"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,44,0)="be removed due to its lack of use by the laboratory software."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,45,0)="The KIDS pre-install will delete these fields and cross-references"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,46,0)="during patch installation. Patch LA*5.2*61 will install these fields with"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,47,0)="the new cross-reference ""CH"" and re-index the ""CH"" cross-reference."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,49,0)="3. NOIS CON-0302-10181 reported the option Edit Shipping Configuration"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,50,0)="[LA7S EDIT 62.9] was prompting the user to edit unexpected fields"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,51,0)="within the TEST/PROFILE (#60) subfile, specifically fields ACCESSION"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,52,0)="AREA (#.02) and SPECIMEN (#.03), when a host facility configures a"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,53,0)="shipping configuration to receive specimens from a collecting facility."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,54,0)="It was determined that variables setup for a FileMan DIC API call to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,55,0)="select an entry in file #62.9 were later interacting with a FileMan DIE"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,56,0)="API call to edit the selected entry. The routine LA7SCE has been modified"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,57,0)="to kill required FileMan DIC input variables before making the FileMan"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,58,0)="DIE call."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,60,0)="4. NOIS PHI-0302-20433 reported a problem with the setting of the ""Q"""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,61,0)="cross-reference on field STATUS (#2) in LA7 MESSAGE QUEUE file (#62.49)."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,62,0)="The setting of the cross-reference could fail when other fields that the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,63,0)="cross-reference is dependent on have not been valued. A previous patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,64,0)="changed lab code to use FileMan DBS calls instead of classic FileMan"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,65,0)="calls. These DBS calls file data by field number. Previously FileMan"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,66,0)="filed the fields in the order specified in the DR variable. This causes"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,67,0)="the MUMPS cross-references to fail at times when the other fields the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,68,0)="cross-reference is dependent on, have not been filed or updated."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,69,0)="A similar problem potentially exists for the ORU cross-reference on this"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,70,0)="same field. These two MUMPS cross-references are replaced by new style"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,71,0)="FileMan Regular INDEX file cross-reference named ""Q"" and ""AC"" respectively."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,72,0)="The KIDS pre-install will delete these fields and cross-references during"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,73,0)="patch installation. Patch LA*5.2*61 will install this field with the new"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,74,0)="cross-references."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,76,0)="5. NOIS BHS-0302-10236 reported a problem with an accession/test building"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,77,0)="multiples times on a shipping manifest. This was caused when a test is"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,78,0)="specified multiple times on the shipping configuration but with different"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,79,0)="specimen types. The logic to build the test onto the manifest was not"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,80,0)="clearing a flag to indicate that a test should be added to the manifest"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,81,0)="when checking the test for each of the possible specimens to build."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,82,0)="Routine LA7SM1 will now set and clear the flag to add a test when the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,83,0)="configuration specifies the same test for multiple specimens. "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,85,0)="6. NOIS LON-0402-60012 reported a problem when a host facility uses ""dummy"""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,86,0)="tests to report patient results. These ""dummy"" results along with the "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,87,0)="patient's actual test results were transmitted in an HL7 ORU Result message"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,88,0)="to the collecting facility. These test results were encoded with the parent"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,89,0)="test's result NLT and LOINC codes due to lack of proper result code mapping."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,90,0)="Routines LA7VOBX1 and LA7VHLU1 will now attempt to identify test results"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,91,0)="which are associated with LABORATORY TEST file (#60) tests that are TYPE ="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,92,0)="BOTH or OUTPUT to determine if a specific test result is returned to the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,93,0)="collecting facility. "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,94,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,95,0)="7. NOIS BHS-0302-10236 reported a problem with the generation of the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,96,0)="performing laboratory comment that is automatically added to the HL7"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,97,0)="Result (ORU) message. The name of the performing laboratory was based"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,98,0)="on the name of the primary facility. This name is incorrect when testing"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,99,0)="is performed by a division of an integrated facility. To correct this "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,100,0)="problem the software will no longer generate a performing laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,101,0)="comment. "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,102,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,103,0)="Collecting facilities wanting a comment indicating the name of the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,104,0)="performing laboratory should turn on the generation of the performing"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,105,0)="laboratory comment when processing the results at the collecting facility."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,106,0)="To turn on the generation of the performing laboratory comment use the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,107,0)="option LEDI Setup [LA7V SETUP]. Under the host facility automated"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,108,0)="instrument section for each test, enter a remark prefix in field REMARK"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,109,0)="PREFIX (#19) and ""YES"" at the field STORE PRODUCER'S ID (#20). The"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,110,0)="performing laboratory comment can then be generated based on field OBX-15"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,111,0)="Producer's ID in the OBX segment for each test result found in the HL7"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,112,0)="Result (ORU) message. The comment generated by the software will be "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,113,0)="remark prefix_""results from ""_name of performing institution from "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,114,0)="INSTITUTION file (#4). If the REMARK PREFIX field is blank then the test"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,115,0)="name of the corresponding test from LABORATORY TEST file (#60) is used."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,117,0)="Example:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,118,0)="     remark prefix=""Theophylline """
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,119,0)="       institution=""REGION 7 ISC,TX (DEMO)"""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,120,0)=" generated comment=""Theophylline results from REGION 7 ISC,TX (DEMO)"""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,121,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,122,0)="8. NOIS IND-0402-42261 reported a problem with building and sending HL7"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,123,0)="Result (ORU) messages to the collecting facility. Accessions with UID's"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,124,0)="that are alphanumeric were skipped during message building due to code"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,125,0)="that was treating the UID as numeric. Routine LA7VMSG1 will now handle"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,126,0)="alphanumeric UID's and return results to the collecting facility."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,127,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,128,0)="9. Due to changes to routine LA7VORU, which resulted in the routine size "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,129,0)="exceeding the VA Vista Programming Standards and Conventions (SAC) of"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,130,0)="10,000 characters, the routine was split into two routines, LA7VORU"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,131,0)="and LA7VORUA."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,132,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,134,0)="ASSOCIATED NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,135,0)="---------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,136,0)=" BHS-0302-10236"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,137,0)=" CON-0302-10181"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,138,0)=" HWH-0202-42779"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,139,0)=" IND-0402-42261"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,140,0)=" LAS-0402-61457"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,141,0)=" LON-0402-60012"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,142,0)=" PHI-0302-20433"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,143,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,145,0)="TEST SITES"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,146,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,147,0)=" Boston HCS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,148,0)=" Indianapolis VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,149,0)=" Lexington VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,150,0)=" Long Beach HCS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,151,0)=" Louisville VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,152,0)=" Milwaukee VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,153,0)=" Philadelphia VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,154,0)=" Southern Nevada HCS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,155,0)=" VA Heartland - East, VISN 15"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,156,0)=" VA Heartland - West, VISN 15 "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,157,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,158,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,159,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,160,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,161,0)="  The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,162,0)="  of each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,163,0)="  <tab> ;;5.2;AUTOMATED LAB INSTRUMENTS;<patchlist>;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,164,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,165,0)="                    Checksum       Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,166,0)="   Routine Name     Before Patch   After Patch    Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,167,0)="   ------------     ------------   -----------    ------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,168,0)="   LA61             N/A            9395003        **61** (Deleted by KIDS)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,169,0)="   LA7QRY1          3509927        3555910        **46,61**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,170,0)="   LA7SCE           11402708       11501726       **27,46,61**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,171,0)="   LA7SM1           8553973        8587872        **27,46,61**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,172,0)="   LA7VHLU1         2011157        2323481        **46,61**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,173,0)="   LA7VHLU2         3873916        4100825        **46,61**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,174,0)="   LA7VMSG1         8200340        8227296        **56,46,61**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,175,0)="   LA7VOBX1         3799868        3981059        **46,61**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,176,0)="   LA7VORM1         7601990        7594289        **27,51,46,61**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,177,0)="   LA7VORU          8070282        6241961        **27,46,61**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,178,0)="   LA7VORUA         N/A            2199285        **61**"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,179,0)="            "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,180,0)=" List of preceding patches: 46"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,181,0)=" Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums.  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,182,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,183,0)="************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,184,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,185,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,186,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,187,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,188,0)="  The install time for this patch is less than 10 minute. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,189,0)="  can be installed when Laboratory users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,190,0)="  Suggested time to install: non-peak requirement hours."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,191,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,192,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,193,0)="NOTE: Kernel patches must be current on the target system to avoid"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,194,0)="      problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,195,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,196,0)="      Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,197,0)="      Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC)."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,198,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,200,0)="  1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,201,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,202,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,203,0)="      option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,204,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,205,0)="  3.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,206,0)="      select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,207,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,208,0)="  4.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,209,0)="      all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,210,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,211,0)="  5.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,212,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,213,0)="        Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,214,0)="        Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,215,0)="        Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,216,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,217,0)="  6.  Perform the following steps if applicable: "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,218,0)="      All Lab LEDI (LA7V*) related HL v1.6 LLPs should be shutdown."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,219,0)="      Use the HL menu option Start/Stop Links [HL START] to shutdown"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,220,0)="      these LLPs if they are running."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,221,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,222,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,223,0)="  7.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,224,0)="      and select the package 'LA*5.2*61'.  When prompted ""Want KIDS to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,225,0)="      Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES//', choose 'NO'"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,226,0)="      When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,227,0)="      YES//', choose 'NO'.  When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,228,0)="      Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES//', choose 'YES'."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,229,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,230,0)="      All LA7V* protocols should be placed out of service during the install."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,231,0)="      This can be accomplished by answering the KIDS install questions:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,232,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,233,0)="        Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols?"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,234,0)="        YES//', choose 'YES'."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,235,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,236,0)="        Enter options you wish to mark as 'Out Of Order': <RET>"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,237,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,238,0)="        Enter protocols you wish to mark as 'Out Of Order': LA7V*"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,239,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,240,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,241,0)="      Note: KIDS will disable the following options during installation."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,242,0)="       Edit Shipping Configuration [LA7S EDIT 62.9]"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,243,0)="       Enter/verify/modify data (manual) [LRENTER]"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,244,0)="       Enter/verify data (auto instrument) [LRVR]"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,245,0)="       Enter/verify data (Work list) [LRVRW]"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,246,0)="       Enter/verify data (Load list) [LRVRW2]"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,247,0)="       Referral Patient Multi-purpose Accession [LRLEDI]"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,248,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,249,0)="  8. On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,250,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,251,0)=" Note: Routine LA61 will be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,252,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,253,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,254,0)="POST-INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,255,0)="==============================="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,257,0)="1. Restart any LA7V* HL v1.6 LLP's shutdown as part of the patch"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,258,0)="installation process. Use the Start LLP [HL START] option to restart"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,259,0)="LA7V* HL v1.6 LLP's."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,260,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,261,0)="2. LEDI Host laboratories should notify their LEDI collecting facilities"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,262,0)="of removal of performing laboratory comment from HL7 Result (ORU) messages."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,263,0)="See item #7 in patch description above for actions collecting facilities"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,264,0)="should take."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,265,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,266,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,267,0)="************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",25,1,268,0)="Installation example:"
