^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",29,0)="69 SEQ #49^3040302^1"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",29,1,0)="^^2^2^3040302"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",29,1,1,0)="Lab API's for extracting Chemistry, Cytopathology, Surgical Pathology"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",29,1,2,0)="and Microbiology data."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",30,0)="70 SEQ #50^3041111^1"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",30,1,0)="^^1^1^3041111"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",30,1,1,0)="Refer to the National Patch Module"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,0)="64^3041228^1"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,0)="^^263^263^3041228"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,1,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LA*5.2*64 does not"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,2,0)="contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,3,0)="DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,4,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,5,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LA*5.2*64 does not"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,6,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical elements"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,7,0)="functions."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,9,0)="RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LA*5.2*64 have no effect on Blood Bank"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,10,0)="software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,11,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,12,0)="VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION:  Because of the nature of the changes"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,13,0)="made, no specific validation requirements exist as a result of installation"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,14,0)="of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,15,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,16,0)="======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,17,0)="This patch adds support for sending/receiving Laboratory Electronic"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,18,0)="Data Interchange (LEDI) orders/results with Department of Defense (DoD)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,19,0)="facilities and implements enhancements to general LEDI functionality."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,22,0)="1. The process of building orders in the LAB PENDING ORDERS ENTRY file"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,23,0)="(#69.6) has been enhanced to use additional information from the HL7 Order"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,24,0)="(ORM) message. It will store the following information when available in the"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,25,0)="LAB PENDING ORDERS ENTRY file (#69.6):"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,26,0)=" - patient's race"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,27,0)=" - order comments"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,28,0)=" - test results that accompany an order "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,29,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,30,0)="2. The new option Start a Shipping Manifest [LA7S MANIFEST START] will"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,31,0)="allow a manifest to be started without performing a manifest build."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,32,0)="Specimens can then be added manually, instead of automatically, using"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,33,0)="option Add/Remove a Shipping Manifest Test [LA7S MANIFEST TEST ADD/REMOVE]."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,34,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,35,0)="3. The new option Edit Relevant Clinical Information [LA7S MANIFEST"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,36,0)="CLINICAL INFO] is used to enter relevant clinical information that"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,37,0)="should accompany a test order on a manifest."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,39,0)="4. Converted supported API calls $$FMDATE^HLFNC and $$HLDATE^HLFNC to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,40,0)="recommended Kernel supported API's $$HL7TFM^XLFDT and $$FMTHL7^XLFDT"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,41,0)="respectively."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,43,0)="5. Routine LA7VHL changed to call HL7 supported API RSPINIT^HLFNC2 to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,44,0)="obtain message delimiters that HL7 package will use when building MSH"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,45,0)="header of application acknowledgement message. Previous call to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,46,0)="INIT^HLFNC would return incorrect headers under certain conditions."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,47,0)="See patch HL*1.6*101 for additional information."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,49,0)="6. Routine LA7VMSG1 changed to check if $QUERY of ^TMP global has"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,50,0)="returned a null value. Under certain conditions an illegal function call"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,51,0)="error could be observed."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,53,0)="7. Changed routines LA7VLL, LA7VSTP, and LA7VSTP1 to setup LA7V* logical"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,54,0)="links without <space> between ""LA7V"" and station number. Allows HL7 package"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,55,0)="to display logical links for DoD sites which utilize DoD DMIS ID codes as"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,56,0)="facility identifiers similar to VA station numbers. HL7 package only"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,57,0)="displays first 8 characters of logical link name. Option LEDI Setup"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,58,0)="[LA7V SETUP] will only support creation of TCP logical links."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,60,0)="8. Routine LA7PURG is changed to purge shipping manifests from LAB"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,61,0)="SHIPPING MANIFEST file (#62.8) when all related accessions have been"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,62,0)="purged from ACCESSION file (#68) (E3R #18036). Orders in the LAB PENDING"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,63,0)="ORDERS ENTRY file (#69.6) are purged when the date completed is >365"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,64,0)="days, when the order transmitted date is >720 days or when the order"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,65,0)="transmitted date is >360 and the order status is Results/data Received."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,67,0)="9. When selecting a shipping manifest the list of entries to select"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,68,0)="from will list the manifests in inverse order with the most recent"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,69,0)="being displayed first. (E3R #18036)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,71,0)="10. Requesting provider's office phone, voice and digital pager numbers"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,72,0)="will be printed on working copies of shipping manifest. (E3R #17914)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,74,0)="11. Four new alerts/mail bulletins are generated when processing LEDI"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,75,0)="HL7 messages. These alerts and corresponding bulletins are addressed to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,76,0)="the mail group designated to receive the NEW RESULTS alert specified"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,77,0)="by the site in LA7 MESSAGE PARAMETER file (#62.48) for LEDI type"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,78,0)="interfaces."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,80,0)="   a. Mail bulletin: LA7 ABNORMAL RESULTS RECEIVED"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,81,0)="   Mail bulletin created by Laboratory package when processing a LEDI"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,82,0)="   interface type HL7 result (ORU) message which contains laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,83,0)="   testing results that are flagged as critical or abnormal.  Values"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,84,0)="   that are critical will always trigger the alert and bulletin. Values"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,85,0)="   that are abnormal low or high will be triggered when site has flagged"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,86,0)="   the corresponding test in AUTO INSTRUMENT file (#62.4), NOTIFY ABNORMAL"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,87,0)="   FLAGS field (#22) within the CHEM TEST multiple (#30) for the interface."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,89,0)="   b. Mail bulletin: LA7 AMENDED RESULTS RECEIVED"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,90,0)="   Mail bulletin created by Laboratory package when processing a LEDI"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,91,0)="   interface type HL7 result (ORU) message which contains laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,92,0)="   testing results that are flagged as amended."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,93,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,94,0)="   c. Mail bulletin: LA7 UNITS/NORMALS CHANGED"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,95,0)="   Mail bulletin created by Laboratory package when processing a LEDI"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,96,0)="   interface type HL7 result (ORU) message which contains laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,97,0)="   test result units and/or normals different from values specified for"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,98,0)="   test in LABORATORY TEST file (#60) and which are flagged to be used"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,99,0)="   for reference testing purposes."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,101,0)="   d. Mail bulletin: LA7 ORDER STATUS CHANGED"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,102,0)="   Mail bulletin created by Laboratory package when processing a LEDI"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,103,0)="   interface type HL7 message."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,104,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,105,0)="   Bulletin will be generated for the following conditions:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,107,0)="   - When an order acknowledgment (ORR) message contains laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,108,0)="   test order status changes that indicate the order is not correct or"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,109,0)="   cannot be performed/completed. Currently only supported on LEDI"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,110,0)="   interfaces with DoD facilities."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,112,0)="   - When an order result (ORU) message indicates that a laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,113,0)="   test has been added by the reference laboratory to the original order."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,115,0)="12. Corrected a spelling error in set of codes for LAB SHIPPING"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,116,0)="CONFIGURATION file (#62.9), COLLECTING FACILITY'S SPEC ID field (#.05)."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,118,0)="13. Internal review determined that the specimen container was not printing"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,119,0)="on working copies of shipping manifests. When printing working versions"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,120,0)="of a shipping manifest the specimen container will be printed."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,121,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,122,0)="14. A new error bulletin #47 has been added to LA7 MESSAGE LOG BULLETINS"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,123,0)="file (#62.485). When processing LEDI orders if any of the following are"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,124,0)="incomplete - local test, local urgency, local topography or local collection"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,125,0)="sample then the bulletin will be triggered. This is to insure that orders"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,126,0)="sent by the collecting facility are not missed when processed during LEDI"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,127,0)="Referral Patient Accessioning. If this bulletin is triggered it indicates"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,128,0)="that the host site's shipping configuration is not properly configured to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,129,0)="process orders from it's collecting site."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,130,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",31,1,131,0)="  "
