^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",32,1,198,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",32,1,199,0)=" Install Message sent #xxxx"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,0)="67^3050611^1"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,0)="^^182^182^3050611"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,1,0)="Blood Bank Clearance"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,2,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,3,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LA*5.2*67 does not"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,4,0)="contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,5,0)="DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,7,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LA*5.2*67 does not"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,8,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical elements"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,9,0)="functions."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,11,0)="RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LA*5.2*67 have no effect on Blood Bank"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,12,0)="software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,14,0)="========================================"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,16,0)="This patch adds support for Laboratory Point of Care (POC) interfaces."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,17,0)="It utilizes existing functionality provided by Laboratory Universal"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,18,0)="Interface (UI) and Laboratory Electronic Data Interchange (LEDI) software."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,19,0)="It supports the transmission, processing and storing of POC test results"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,20,0)="in the VistA Laboratory package. The ability of POC interfaces to subscribe"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,21,0)="to VistA HL7 ADT messages for patient demographics and location information"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,22,0)="is provided as needed. Support for 5 separate POC interfaces is provided."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,25,0)="NOTE: THIS PATCH WILL BE INSTALLED WITH PATCH LR*5.2*290"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,28,0)="1. NOIS DAN-0105-41616/Remedy HD0000000071211 reported undefined DUZ(""AG"") "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,29,0)="variable when processing Lab HL7 messages. The following new 'non-human'"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,30,0)="entries will be installed in NEW PERSON file (#200). These entries have"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,31,0)="the approval of VA VistA Data Base Administrator."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,33,0)=" NAME: LRLAB,HL             NAME COMPONENTS: 200"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,34,0)="  SIGNATURE BLOCK PRINTED NAME: HL LRLAB"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,36,0)=" NAME: LRLAB,POC            NAME COMPONENTS: 200"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,37,0)="  SIGNATURE BLOCK PRINTED NAME: POC LRLAB"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,39,0)="User LRLAB,HL will be used by Laboratory when processing HL7 messages "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,40,0)="to insure a consistent Kernel environment with respect to the system-wide"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,41,0)="DUZ variable array."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,43,0)="User LRLAB,POC will be used by Laboratory when creating POC orders and"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,44,0)="accessions to indicate that these orders and accessions were created by"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,45,0)="the POC interface background process. Sites should assign to the user"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,46,0)="LRLAB,POC those divisions that will be used by POC interfaces to accession"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,47,0)="POC results into VistA Laboratory package."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,50,0)="Additionally, the following changes have been made:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,52,0)="2. Removed prompt to save alert when viewing lab messaging alert in routine"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,53,0)="LA7UXQA. This functionality is now part of Kernel Alert processing."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,55,0)="3. When logging lab messaging processing errors, FileMan DIE call in"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,56,0)="routine LA7LOG was converted to FileMan DBS call."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,58,0)="4. Lab messaging will now check that LA7TASK NIGHTY option is scheduled"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,59,0)="in TaskMan. If not scheduled then an alert notifying members of mail group"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,60,0)="LAB MESSAGING will be generated. The alert message will read ""Lab Messaging"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,61,0)="- Option LA7TASK NIGHTY is not scheduled in TaskMan"". Documentation"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,62,0)="regarding tasking can be found in the VistA Laboratory LEDI User Guide and"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,63,0)="on-line via the DESCRIPTION field of the OPTION file (#19) for this entry."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,65,0)="5. Result of 'canc' was not being processed if the test was configured to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,66,0)="only accept 'final' type results (HL7 Table 0085 - Observation result"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,67,0)="status codes interpretation codes C, F, or U. Changed routine LA7VIN5A to"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,68,0)="accept and process ""canc' result with status code X."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,71,0)="ASSOCIATED E3R"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,72,0)="--------------"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",33,1,73,0)=" "
