^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,327,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,328,0)="9. It corrects a defect identified during patch development with"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,329,0)="processing input parameters for the GCPR^LA7QRY API. If the input"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,330,0)="parameter LA7SC specified specific subscripts to search then the API"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,331,0)="would search those subscripts for any search code even when specific "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,332,0)="search codes were passed to the API in the LA7SC array."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,333,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,334,0)="10. Converts several FileMan DBS calls on INSTITUTION file (#4) to using"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,335,0)="supported API's $$NS^XUAF4 and $$STA^XUAF4."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,336,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,337,0)="11. It corrects a defect identified during patch development with"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,338,0)="processing input parameters for the GCPR^LA7QRY API. If the input"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,339,0)="parameters LA7SDT and LA7EDT specified specific results available date"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,340,0)="range the API could return anatomic pathology results which have not"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,341,0)="been released. This API has been corrected to check the REPORT RELEASE"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,342,0)="DATE field (#.11) for subscripts ""CY"", EM"", ""SP""."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,343,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,344,0)="12. Remedy ticket HD0000000096207 reported a problem with the error code"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,345,0)="returned by the Lab API LA7QRY. A FileMan DBS error code was erroroneously"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,346,0)="being returned to the calling application. Routines LA7QRY, LA7QRY1, and "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,347,0)="LA7QRY2 has been modified to use a different name spaced variable LA7QERR"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,348,0)="to return to the calling application any error conditions. Additionally,"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,349,0)="routine LA7VOBX1 has been modified to use another name spaced variable"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,350,0)="LA7DDERR to handle FileMan DBS error conditions related to FileMan data"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,351,0)="dictionary calls."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,352,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,353,0)="13. It corrects a defect identified by MyHeatheVet regarding encoding of "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,354,0)="the following fields in the OBR segment relating to anatomic pathology "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,355,0)="reports:"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,356,0)=" OBR-32 - Principal result interpreter"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,357,0)=" OBR-33 - Assistant result interpreter"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,358,0)=" OBR-34 - Technician"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,359,0)=" OBR-35 - Transcriptionist"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,360,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,361,0)="The name component of these fields was being encoded with the wrong HL7"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,362,0)="delimiter (component separator). The name component will be encoded with "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,363,0)="the subcomponent separator per the HL7 standard."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,364,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,365,0)="14. To integrate the VistA-Office EHR with the regular VistA system as"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,366,0)=" well as adding functionality also available in the Indian Health Services"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,367,0)=" system, the GQPR^LA7QRY API has been modified to allow for VistA-Office"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,368,0)=" EHR to use data specifically geared toward clinical operations, whether"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,369,0)=" in a hospital or a standalone clinic. The use of an Electronic"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,370,0)=" Health Record number as opposed to a SSN for patient identification is"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,371,0)=" supported as an identifier accepted as input to this API."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,372,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,373,0)=" The entry point GCPR^LA7QRY remains unchanged. However, the parameter"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,374,0)=" used to pass the patient identifier should contain a 2nd piece indicating"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,375,0)=" the type of identifier contained in the 1st piece."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,376,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,377,0)=" It supports the following types of patient identifiers"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,378,0)="   SS = Social Security number"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,379,0)="   PI = VA MPI Integration Control Number"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,380,0)="   MR = medical record number of patient in file PATIENT/IHS (#9000001)"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,381,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,382,0)=" To regular VistA users this modification will not be seen."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,383,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,384,0)="15. To support HDR-Historical which uses the GRPR^LA7QRY API to extract"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,385,0)="historical laboratory test results, the input parameter LA7SC to GCPR^LA7QRY"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,386,0)="supports a 2nd piece. When the 2nd piece of input parameter LA7SC equals"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,387,0)="1 the API will return results encoded using VUID's when available."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,388,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,389,0)="16. Remedy tickets HD0000000141922/HD0000000148089 reported a problem with"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,390,0)="failure of generation of MailMan bulletin LA7 ORDER STATUS CHANGED at"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,391,0)="collection laboratory facility. Routine LA7VMSG1 changed to set interface"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,392,0)="type to set flag in Lab HL7 ORU message indicating an order status change"
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,393,0)="to trigger bulletin generation at collecting site."
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,394,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,11,22,5.03,"PAH",36,1,395,0)="  "
