^DIC(9.4,13,0)="VA FILEMAN^DI^FM INIT"
^DIC(9.4,13,4,0)="^9.44PA^^0"
^DIC(9.4,13,14,0)="^9.4014^2^2"
^DIC(9.4,13,14,1,0)="DD"
^DIC(9.4,13,14,2,0)="DM"
^DIC(9.4,13,14,"B","DD",1)=""
^DIC(9.4,13,14,"B","DM",2)=""
^DIC(9.4,13,22,0)="^9.49I^9^3"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,0)="21.0^2941222^2980408"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^37^37"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,0)="19^2960924^1"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,0)="^^144^144^2960924"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,1,0)="This patch fixes several problems: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,3,0)="1.  When an audit flag on a field is EDITED OR DELETED, the field gets "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,4,0)="audited when there is no pre-existing data and the field is being stuffed "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,5,0)="using /// or //// syntax. This patch corrects the problem by not auditing "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,6,0)="fields with no pre-existing data and the audit flag is EDITED OR DELETED."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,7,0)="This problem was reported by nois ISA-0593-10022. (DIE, DIEZ2) "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,9,0)="2.  When a compiled input template contains the syntax '////@', the '@' is"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,10,0)="stuffed in the field.  This was reported in the FB VENDOR UPDATE template"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,11,0)="in file 161.2.  This template needs to be recompiled after this patch is"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,12,0)="installed.  (DIEZ2) "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,14,0)="3.  On a range read, an input that is totally outside of the range is "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,15,0)="accepted.  For example, using a DIR call like this, S DIR(0)=""L^1:4"", if"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,16,0)="the user typed in 5-6, Y comes back as 4.  (DIR3)"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,18,0)="4.  With the release of V21, set-of-code processing within ^DIE was"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,19,0)="enhanced to make input to set-of-code single-valued-fields case"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,20,0)="insensitive.  This change however caused the syntax"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,21,0)="'field///external_code' to fail when the 'external_code' is an exact match"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,22,0)="to a code but is also a partial match to another code.  Prior to V21, the"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,23,0)="first match to 'external_code' was selected. This patch fixes this"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,24,0)="problem.  The related nois is ISW-0895-21058.  There are no known"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,25,0)="templates that needed to be recompiled at this time.  (DIED, DIEZ1, DIR1)"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,27,0)="5.  This patch will make set-of-code ^DIR calls case insensitive unless an"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,28,0)="'X' flag is passed.  Prior to the patch, an 'M' flag was required to be "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,29,0)="passed to allow case insensitivity.  This patch will no longer require an"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,30,0)="'M' flag to be passed. (DIR1)"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,32,0)="6.  Suppose a DIE call is made with DIE(""NO^"")="""", and the template"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,33,0)="specified in DR is compiled."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,35,0)="    a.  If the user timed out, FileMan behaved as if an ""^"" was entered, "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,36,0)="    printed the message 'EXIT NOT ALLOWED ??' and reprompted.  In "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,37,0)="    effect, then, the process would never timeout.  This change makes "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,38,0)="    FileMan exit on timeout.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,39,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,40,0)="    b.  If the compiled template contained the .01 field of a multiple, "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,41,0)="    and that .01 field was the first field in the multiple defined in the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,42,0)="    template, if the user entered an ^, FileMan would correctly print the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,43,0)="    message 'EXIT NOT ALLOWED ??' but would take the user to the next "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,44,0)="    field defined in the template.  This change makes FileMan reprompt for"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,45,0)="    a value for the .01 field."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,47,0)="    The related NOIS is BRK-0796-10872."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,48,0)="    (DIE17)"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,50,0)="7.  Back out change to DICN made in patch DI*21*12 (described as item #2"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,51,0)="    in that patch).  That change inadvertently made a response in a"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,52,0)="    YN^DICN call required. (DICN)"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,54,0)="Routine Summary: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,55,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,57,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,58,0)="these routines now look like:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,59,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,60,0)="  <tab>;;21.0;VA FileMan;**[patch list]**;Dec 28, 1994 "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,61,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,62,0)="CHECK^XTSUMBLD results: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,63,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,64,0)="  Routine Name   Before Patch    After Patch     Patch List "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,65,0)="  ============   ============    ===========     =========="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,66,0)="  DICN           7484792         7476631         12,19"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,67,0)="  DIE            9505864         9523669         19"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,68,0)="  DIE17          6822014         6896286         19"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,69,0)="  DIED           6344409         6449521         1,13,19"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,70,0)="  DIEZ1          7657833         7774560         1,13,19"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,71,0)="  DIEZ2          7389106         7311012         19"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,72,0)="  DIR1           7726690         7765832         6,13,19"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,73,0)="  DIR3           3582829         3670507         19"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,75,0)="Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,76,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,77,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,78,0)="    1.  The routines DICN, DIE, DIED, DIE17, DIR1, DIR3 are usually mapped"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,79,0)="on systems that allow mapping, AXP sites will need to disable mapping for"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,80,0)="these routines."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,82,0)="    2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,83,0)="option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  The environment check"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,84,0)="routine DIENV will run automatically."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,86,0)="    DIENV is sent in order to prevent the inadvertent queueing of the"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,87,0)="installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,88,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,89,0)="    3.  The patch has now been loaded into a transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,90,0)="system. You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,92,0)="    4.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,93,0)="options: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,94,0)="           Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,95,0)="           Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,96,0)="           Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,97,0)="           Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,99,0)="    5.  Inhibit users from login into the system.  The consequence of"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,100,0)="having users on the system while installing this patch are that users"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,101,0)="editing records will get a 'source routine edited' error, the edits will"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,102,0)="be lost and records may be left in an inconsistent state.  Note that most"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,103,0)="of these routines are heavily used in DHCP applications."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,105,0)="    6.  AXP Sites - Place Taskman in a WAIT State.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,106,0)="        MSM Sites - STOP Taskman.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,108,0)="    7.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,109,0)="option: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,110,0)="           Select Installation Option: Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,111,0)="           Select INSTALL NAME: DI*21.0*19 "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,112,0)="                                =========="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,114,0)="           Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,115,0)="Options, and Protocols?"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,117,0)="    8.  MSM Sites - Answer YES to the question 'Want to MOVE routines to "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,118,0)="other CPUs?'.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,119,0)="     Then enter the names of your other Compute and Print server(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,120,0)="     NOTE: You will then see the following message: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,121,0)="       TASKMAN is not running. You must run the routine XPDCPU in the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,122,0)="production UCI for each of the VOLUME SETS you have listed once the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,123,0)="installation starts!! "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,125,0)="    9.  MSM Sites - After the installation begins, you will be prompted to"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,126,0)="enter a DEVICE.  After the device has been entered, KIDS will pause.  At"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,127,0)="this time, you need to go to each of the CPUs that were entered in step 8,"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,128,0)="and start a job that will allow them to receive the patched routines.  On"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,129,0)="each one, you do the following:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,130,0)="    a) >D ^XUP    This will set up the programming environment.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,131,0)="       ======"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,132,0)="    b) >D ^XPDCPU  This starts the job that receives the patched routines."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,133,0)="        ========="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,134,0)="    c) Select INSTALL NAME: DI*21.0*19 "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,135,0)="                            =========="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,136,0)="The installation will then continue.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,138,0)="    10.  AXP Sites - After the patch has been installed, rebuild your map "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,139,0)="set.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,141,0)="    11.  AXP Sites - Remove Taskman from WAIT State.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,142,0)="         MSM Sites - Restart Taskman.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,143,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",1,1,144,0)="    12.  Enable user's login.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,0)="25^2960924^1"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^98^98^2960924"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,1,0)="This patch fixes the following problems: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,3,0)=" 1.  When merging data using KIDS, there is a case where existing data at"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,4,0)="the target site gets overwritten by incoming data.  When a file being"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,5,0)="exported contains pointers, and the pointed-to-file is being exported"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,6,0)="as well, MERGING and RESOLVING POINTERS will cause the existing pointer"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,7,0)="values on the first file to get overwritten by the incoming data.  This"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,8,0)="patch fixes this problem by not overwriting existing data."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,9,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,10,0)=" 2.  The DBS calls FILE^DID and $$GET1^DID return an incorrect value for a"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,11,0)="file's READ ACCESS."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,12,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,13,0)="Routine Summary: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,14,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,15,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,16,0)=" The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,17,0)="these routines now look like:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,18,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,19,0)="   <tab>;;21.0;VA FileMan;**[patch list]**;Dec 28, 1994 "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,20,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,21,0)=" CHECK^XTSUMBLD results: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,22,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,23,0)="   Routine Name   Before Patch    After Patch     Patch List "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,24,0)="   ============   ============    ===========     =========="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,25,0)="   DIQGDDT        7439422         7439520         25"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,26,0)="   DITR           5710355         5514796         6,25"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,28,0)="Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,29,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,31,0)="     1.  Routine mapping is NOT recommended for these routines. If you are"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,32,0)="using routine mapping, ensure that these routines are NOT in your mapped"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,33,0)="routine set before proceeding."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,35,0)="     2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,36,0)="option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  The environment check"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,37,0)="routine DIENV will run automatically.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,38,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,39,0)="     DIENV is sent in order to prevent the inadvertent queueing of the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,40,0)=" installation of this patch.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,41,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,42,0)="     3.  The patch has now been loaded into a transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,43,0)="system. You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,44,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,45,0)="     4.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,46,0)="following options:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,47,0)="            Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,48,0)="            Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,49,0)="            Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,50,0)="            Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,51,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,52,0)="     5.  Inhibit users from login into the system.  Any user who is logged"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,53,0)="in and using an application which uses the DBS calls $$GET1^DID and"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,54,0)="FILE^DID run the risk of getting <CLOBBER> errors.  Any user using"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,55,0)="FileMan's 'Transfer File Entries' option run the risk of getting an error"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,56,0)="in the midst of a transfer.  A database record may be left in a corrupted"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,57,0)="state.  Any init that may be running or any KIDS installation that brings"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,58,0)="in data may leave the records in a corrupted state."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,59,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,60,0)="     6.  AXP Sites - Place Taskman in a WAIT State.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,61,0)="         MSM Sites - STOP Taskman.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,62,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,63,0)="     7.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,64,0)="following option:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,65,0)="            Select Installation Option: Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,66,0)="            Select INSTALL NAME: DI*21.0*25"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,67,0)="                                 =========="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,68,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,69,0)="            Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,70,0)="Options, and Protocols?"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,71,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,72,0)="     8.  MSM Sites - Answer YES to the question 'Want to MOVE routines to"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,73,0)="other CPUs?'."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,74,0)="      Then enter the names of your other Compute and Print server(s).  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,75,0)="      NOTE: You will then see the following message: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,76,0)="        TASKMAN is not running. You must run the routine XPDCPU in the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,77,0)=" production UCI for each of the VOLUME SETS you have listed once the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,78,0)=" installation starts!! "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,79,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,80,0)="     9.  MSM Sites - After the installation begins, you will be prompted"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,81,0)="to enter a DEVICE.  After the device has been entered, KIDS will pause."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,82,0)="At this time, you need to go to each of the CPUs that were entered in step"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,83,0)="8, and start a job that will allow them to receive the patched routines."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,84,0)="On each one, you do the following:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,85,0)="     a) >D ^XUP    This will set up the programming environment.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,86,0)="         ======"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,87,0)="     b) >D ^XPDCPU  This starts the job that receives the patched"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,88,0)="routines.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,89,0)="         ========="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,90,0)="     c) Select INSTALL NAME: DI*21.0*25"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,91,0)="                             =========="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,92,0)="The installation will then continue.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,93,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,94,0)="     10.  AXP Sites - After the patch has been installed, rebuild your map"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,95,0)="set. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,96,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,97,0)="     11.  AXP Sites - Remove Taskman from WAIT State.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",2,1,98,0)="          MSM Sites - Restart Taskman.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,0)="27^2960925^1"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^119^119^2960925"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="Description: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,2,0)="============ "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,4,0)="This patch fixes two problems: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,6,0)="1.  It prevents the allocation errors that have plagued PCMM sites. These  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,7,0)="Finder errors arose from stack overflow caused when using PCMM to lookup  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,8,0)="Patients. The Finder was not detecting and protecting itself from pointer  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,9,0)="chains that loop back on themselves, causing the Finder to go into "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,10,0)="recursion until it ran out of stack space. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,12,0)="There are two other independent problems at these sites that this patch "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,13,0)="does not fix: the problem with WRITE commands in the data dictionaries of "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,14,0)="some of the files involved, which must be manually replaced by the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,15,0)="application or local developers; and a PCMM bug that caused allocation "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,16,0)="errors when a patient lookup value produced too many possible matches, "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,17,0)="which is fixed by an upcoming PCMM patch. These problems were reported by "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,18,0)="the following NOISes: SPO-0896-50876, POR-0896-50871, IND-0796-40935, "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,19,0)="ALB-0796-51236, and MGY-0796-30889. (DICF, DICF2, DICF5) "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,21,0)="2.  It makes the Finder tolerate being called by the FileMan Database "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,22,0)="Server (DBS) when DIERR is already defined. This change is needed by "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,23,0)="patch DI*21*8, which is simultaneously under development. Because this "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,24,0)="fix changed the routine DICF, also changed by the fix to the problem "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,25,0)="described above, it was moved out of DI*21*8 and into DI*21*27 to make "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,26,0)="the simultaneous development of these two patches easier to coordinate. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,27,0)="(DICF) "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,29,0)="Routine Summary: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,30,0)="================ "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,32,0)="The following routines are included in this patch. The second line of "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,33,0)="these routines now looks like: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,35,0)="  <tab>;;21.0;VA FileMan;**[patch list]**;Dec 28, 1994 "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,37,0)="CHECK^XTSUMBLD results: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,39,0)="  Routine Name   Before Patch    After Patch     Patch List "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,40,0)="  ============   ============    ===========     ========== "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,41,0)="  DICF           6981054         7062808         17,27 "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,42,0)="  DICF2          5350507         5355774         27 "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,43,0)="  DICF5          2906278         3301437         17,27 "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,45,0)="Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,46,0)="========================== "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,48,0)="    1.  Although routine mapping is NOT recommended for these routines, "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,49,0)="your mapped set may include routines not usually recommended for mapping. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,50,0)="If these routines are in your local map set, disable mapping for them "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,51,0)="before proceeding with the installation, and rebuild your map set "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,52,0)="afterward before reactivating TaskMan."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,54,0)="    2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,55,0)="option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  The environment "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,56,0)="check routine, DIENV, will run automatically."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,58,0)="    DIENV is sent to prevent the inadvertent queuing of the installation "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,59,0)="of this patch. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,61,0)="    3.  The patch has now been loaded into a transport global on your "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,62,0)="system. You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,64,0)="    4.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,65,0)="following options:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,67,0)="           Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,68,0)="           Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,69,0)="           Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,70,0)="           Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,72,0)="    5.  Inhibit users from login into the system.  The consequence of "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,73,0)="having users on the system while installing this patch are that users "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,74,0)="looking up records will get a 'source routine edited' error.  Although "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,75,0)="these routines are not heavily used in DHCP applications yet, they are "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,76,0)="used increasingly in new application such as PCMM. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,78,0)="    6.  AXP Sites - Place Taskman in a WAIT State. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,79,0)="        MSM Sites - STOP Taskman. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,81,0)="    7.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,82,0)="following option:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,84,0)="              Select Installation Option: Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,85,0)="              Select INSTALL NAME: DI*21.0*27"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,86,0)="                                   =========="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,87,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,88,0)="              Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,89,0)="Options, and Protocols?"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,90,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,91,0)="    8.  MSM Sites - Answer YES to the question 'Want to MOVE routines to "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,92,0)="other CPUs?'."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,93,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,94,0)="     Then enter the names of your other Compute and Print server(s)."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,96,0)="     NOTE: You will then see the following message:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,98,0)="       TASKMAN is not running. You must run the routine XPDCPU in the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,99,0)="production UCI for each of the VOLUME SETS you have listed once the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,100,0)="installation starts!! "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,101,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,102,0)="    9.  MSM Sites - After the installation begins, you will be prompted "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,103,0)="to enter a DEVICE.  After the device has been entered, KIDS will pause.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,104,0)="At this time, you need to go to each of the CPUs that were entered in "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,105,0)="step 8, and start a job that will allow them to receive the patched "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,106,0)="routines.  On each one, you do the following: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,108,0)="    a) >D ^XUP    This will set up the programming environment. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,109,0)="        ====== "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,110,0)="    b) >D ^XPDCPU This starts the job that receives the patched routines. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,111,0)="        ========= "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,112,0)="    c) Select INSTALL NAME: DI*21.0*27 "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,113,0)="                            ========== "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,114,0)="The installation will then continue. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,115,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,116,0)="    10.  AXP Sites - Remove Taskman from WAIT State. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,117,0)="         MSM Sites - Restart Taskman. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",3,1,119,0)="    11.  Enable users' login."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,0)="8^2961003^1"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^159^159^2961003"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="1.  Most of the routines included in this patch support Laboratory's"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,2,0)="archiving functions described in patch LR*5.2*59."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,4,0)="    A.  Changes to EN^DIAXU API: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,6,0)="With patch DI*21*8, the extract tool has been enhanced to use FileMan's"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,7,0)="database server calls (DBS) in order to take advantage of the more"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,8,0)="intelligent error handling in the DBS calls. This change has resulted in a"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,9,0)="number of changes to the input and output variables of the EN^DIAXU entry"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,10,0)="point.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,12,0)="The complete API description is available on the Software Service web page"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,13,0)="at URL:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,14,0)="http://www.vista.domain.ext/softserv/infrastr.uct/fileman/docs/pm/ft_diaxu"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,15,0)=".htm"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,17,0)="    B.  New API: EXTRACT^DIAXU: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,19,0)="EXTRACT^DIAXU is a new entry point, introduced by patch DI*21*8. The main"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,20,0)="new features introduced with this entry point for extracting data are:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,22,0)="     * More than one record can be extracted in a call. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,23,0)="     * Subrecords can be extracted as individual transactions. Previously,"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,24,0)="       an entire record including all subrecords had to be extracted as a "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,25,0)="       single entity. "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,26,0)="     * DBS-style error reporting is used.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,28,0)="The complete API description is available on the Software Service web page"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,29,0)="at URL:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,30,0)="http://www.vista.domain.ext/softserv/infrastr.uct/fileman/docs/pm/ft_diax2"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,31,0)=".htm"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,33,0)="2.  This patch also contains a fix for the DIVR routine.  When you use the"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,34,0)="'Utility Functions/Verify Fields' option to check a date/time field that"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,35,0)="can contain seconds, if the data has a time between 1 and 59 seconds after"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,36,0)="midnight (nnnnnnn.000001 through nnnnnnn.000059) the data was flagged as"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,37,0)="not valid."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,39,0)="3.  The DIV routine in this patch has been modified to provide a way for"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,40,0)="customized input transforms to skip certain checks when the 'Verify"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,41,0)="Fields' Utility Function is used.  The variable to check is DIUTIL.  It is"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,42,0)="set equal to the string ""VERIFY FIELDS"" when the 'Verify Fields' option is"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,43,0)="running.  (DIV)"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,45,0)="4.  The changes made by some of the init routines in this patch are"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,46,0)="necessary to make some corrections to FM's files.  The new post-install"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,47,0)="routine, DIPOST, will make these corrections automatically.  IT IS NOT"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,48,0)="NECESSARY TO REINITIALIZE FILEMAN."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,50,0)="Routine Summary: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,51,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,53,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,54,0)="these routines now look like:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,55,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,56,0)="  <tab>;;21.0;VA FileMan;**[patch list]**;Dec 28, 1994 "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,57,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,58,0)="CHECK^XTSUMBLD results: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,7,"PAH",4,1,59,0)="  "
