^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,138,0)="Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,139,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,140,0)="This patch can be installed with VISTA users online.  However, it is "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,141,0)="recommended that it be Queued for a time of generally least activity.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,142,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,143,0)="     1.  AXP sites: Review your mapped routine set.  If any of the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,144,0)="routine(s) listed in the ROUTINE SUMMARY section are mapped, they "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,145,0)="should be removed from the mapped set at this time.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,146,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,147,0)="     2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,148,0)="This option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,150,0)="     3.  The patch has now been loaded into a transport global on your "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,151,0)="system. You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,152,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,153,0)="     4.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,154,0)="following options: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,155,0)="            Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,156,0)="            Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,157,0)="            Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,158,0)="            Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,159,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,160,0)="     5.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,161,0)="following option: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,162,0)="            Select Installation Option: Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,163,0)="            Select INSTALL NAME: DI*22.0*2"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,164,0)="                                 =========="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,165,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,166,0)="            Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,167,0)="Options, and Protocols? "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,168,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,169,0)="     6.  AXP Sites - After the patch has been installed, rebuild your "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",10,1,170,0)="map set, if necessary.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,0)="17 SEQ #11^2991210^1"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^122^122^2991210"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="Miscellaneous bug fixes in the FileMan lookup ^DIC routines"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,3,0)="Routines: DIC1, DIC2, DIC3"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,4,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,5,0)="Support the undocumented ""U"" flag so that MailMan can get the same display"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,6,0)="on one of their lookups as they did in V21. This supports a lookup on the"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,7,0)="index with no transforms. I.e., the code expects the lookup value to be an"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,8,0)="internal format (of a pointer, date, etc.), and will look on the index for"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,9,0)="a match, and will not try to convert the lookup value in any way. Reported"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,10,0)="by Gary Beuschel on a local message at the San Francisco ISC."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,12,0)="Routines: DIC, DIC1"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,13,0)="==================="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,14,0)="Make the ""Y"" flag in DIC(0) work the same as it did in version 21.  This"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,15,0)="undocumented flag is supposed to make ^DIC return a list of entry numbers"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,16,0)="that match the lookup value in Y(n) where 'n' is an IEN. The FIND^DIC call"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,17,0)="is now a better way to do the same thing. Reported by Lucille Barrios on a"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,18,0)="FORUM mail message."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,20,0)="Routines: DICLIX1, DICU11"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,21,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,22,0)="I found during my testing that in cases where the Lister decides to build"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,23,0)="a temporary index on a pointer or variable pointer because it's the"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,24,0)="fastest way to return the list in order, I needed to save the internal"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,25,0)="pointer or variable pointer on the temporary list, in case the user asked"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,26,0)="to have it returned in the output."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,28,0)="Routine: DICA"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,29,0)="============="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,30,0)="With the ""E"" flag, UPDATE^DIE assumes that the values passed in the FDA"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,31,0)="are in external form. Also, for LAYGO/Finding (?+) nodes, the value of the"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,32,0)=".01 field is used as a lookup value to see if an existing record should be"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,33,0)="edited, or a new record added. Prior to this change, the Updater used the"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,34,0)="internal form of the .01 as a lookup value, rather than the external form."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,35,0)="If the .01 is a pointer or variable, this meant the lookup would fail. For"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,36,0)="DINUM'd pointers, this resulted in the Dialog error message #302, ""Entry"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,37,0)="'xxx' already exists"" to be returned."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,40,0)="NOIS "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,41,0)="===="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,42,0)="DAY-1099-42880"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,44,0)="Thanks to Test Sites "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,45,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,47,0)="Routine Summary: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,48,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,49,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,50,0)="these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,51,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,52,0)="  <tab>;;22.0;VA FileMan;**[patch list]**;Mar 30, 1999 "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,53,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,54,0)="CHECK^XTSUMBLD results: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,55,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,56,0)="  Routine Name   Before Patch    After Patch     Patch List "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,57,0)="  ============   ============    ===========     =========="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,58,0)="  DIC            9848200         9925689         4,17"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,59,0)="  DIC1           8559944         8596617         1,4,17"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,60,0)="  DIC2           4974600         5005952         4,17"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,61,0)="  DIC3           7291022         7365376         1,16,4,17"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,62,0)="  DICA           8533062         8533782         1,4,17"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,63,0)="  DICLIX1        2988293         3152916         17"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,64,0)="  DICU11         3617845         3663044         17"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,66,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,67,0)="Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,68,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,69,0)="** It is HIGHLY recommended that ALL Users and VISTA Background jobs to be"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,70,0)="STOPPED.  Failure to do so may result in a 'source routine edited' error,"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,71,0)="the edits will be lost and records may be left in an inconsistent state."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,72,0)="** "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,74,0)="     1.  AXP sites: Review your mapped routine set.  If any of the"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,75,0)="routine(s) listed in the ROUTINE SUMMARY section are mapped, they should"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,76,0)="be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,78,0)="     2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,79,0)="option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,81,0)="         The environment check routine DIENVWRN will run automatically."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,82,0)="Routine DIENVWRN is sent in order to prevent the inadvertent queuing"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,83,0)="during the installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,85,0)="     3.  The patch has now been loaded into a transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,86,0)="system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,88,0)="     4.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,89,0)="following options:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,91,0)="            Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,92,0)="            Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,93,0)="            Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,94,0)="            Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,96,0)="     5.  Inhibit users' login into the system.  The consequence of having"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,97,0)="users on the system while installing this patch are that users editing"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,98,0)="records will get a 'source routine edited' error, the edits will be lost"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,99,0)="and records may be left in an inconsistent state.  Note that most of these"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,100,0)="routines are heavily used in DHCP applications."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,101,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,102,0)="     6.  AXP Sites - Place TaskMan in a WAIT State.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,103,0)="         OpenM/Cache Sites - STOP TaskMan.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,105,0)="     7.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,106,0)="following option:"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,108,0)="            Select Installation Option: Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,109,0)="            Select INSTALL NAME: DI*22.0*17"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,110,0)="                                 =========="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,112,0)="         Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,113,0)="and Protocols? "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,115,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,116,0)="     8.  AXP Sites - After the patch has been installed, rebuild your map"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,117,0)="set, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,119,0)="     9.  AXP Sites - Remove TaskMan from WAIT State.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,120,0)="         OpenM/Cache Sites - Restart TaskMan.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",11,1,122,0)="    10.  Enable users' login.  "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,0)="21 SEQ #12^2991210^1"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^96^96^2991210"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="Y2K Waiver Exemption ID#:  Y2KWE0031"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,2,0)="  This patch may be installed at any time during the Y2K Moratorium"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,3,0)="  (including the 12/15/1999 thru 1/15/2000 Y2K lockdown)."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,5,0)="This patch fixes a problem that occurs when you edit a pointer field that"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,6,0)="has a screen and allows LAYGO into the pointed-to file. If the variable D"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,7,0)="happens to be set when the input transform of the pointer field is"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,8,0)="executed and isn't changed by the input transform, ^DIE is passing it to"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,9,0)="MIX^DIC1 to do the lookup on the pointed-to file, even though D isn't a"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,10,0)="valid list of index names."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,12,0)="The problem can manifest itself as bad variable name errors at S+2^DIQ:1"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,13,0)="or null subscript errors at N5+16^DICN0 when the DEBTOR field (#9) of the"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,14,0)="ACCOUNTS RECEIVABLE file (#430) is edited."
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,16,0)="NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,17,0)="===="
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,18,0)="ALX-1299-70504"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,19,0)="BAC-1299-40203"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,20,0)="DUR-1299-30293"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,21,0)="NCH-1199-42549"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,22,0)="NCH-1299-40048"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,23,0)="OKL-1199-72669"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,24,0)="REN-1199-62529"
^DIC(9.4,13,22,8,"PAH",12,1,25,0)=" "
