^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,0)="134 SEQ #104^2961115^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^40^40^2961115"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="This is a Patch for a Patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,3,0)="It was discovered that 2 separate AP reports were not functioning"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,4,0)="correctly after installation of LR*5.2*72"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,6,0)="First--It was discovered after patch LR*5.2*72 was released that the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,7,0)="Autopsy Status Report did not capture Autopsies done after the load date"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,8,0)="of the patch.  This actually is the symptom of two separate problems:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,10,0)="1.  The routine LRAUSTA which was supposed to be part of patch LR*5.2*72"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,11,0)="was never exported with the patch.  Since this report is rarely run by the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,12,0)="sites, this was never noticed during the testing of the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,14,0)="2.  During the LRAPFIX data conversion, the ^LR(""AAUA"", node was rebuilt"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,15,0)="using the new accession # format, however the old ^LR(AAUA"", node was not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,16,0)="deleted.  This is why the routine was picking up the Autopsies logged in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,17,0)="previous to the loading of the patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,19,0)="The other problem was reported by the Bronx.  A null subscript error would"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,20,0)="occur during the option Malignancy review  [LRAPQAMR] if the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,21,0)="conditions were met:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,22,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,23,0)="     1.  There were reports positive for malignancy during the time period"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,24,0)="the report was requested for."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,26,0)="     2.  The user responds ""YES"" to the prompt:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,27,0)="         Do you want corresponding permanent pathology reports to print"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,28,0)="following search ? NO// Y  (YES)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,30,0)="The null subscript error would occur because the routine LRAPQAMR  was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,31,0)="attempting to get a patient's LRDFN from the ^LR(LRXREF,LRY,LRAN,0)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,32,0)="reference when in fact this reference should have been updated to reflect"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,33,0)="the new format of this node after the data conversion of LR*5.2*72.  The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,34,0)="correct reference should have been ^LR(LRXREF,LRY,LRABV,LRAN,0).  The code"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,35,0)="was changed to this new reference as well as inserting Quit statements for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,36,0)="the $O command."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",11,1,40,0)="Both of these issues will be resolved with this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",12,0)="137 SEQ #105^2961120^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^1^1^2961120"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="FIX FOR LRDPA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",13,0)="141 SEQ #106^2961123^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",13,1,0)="^^1^1^2961123"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",13,1,1,0)="UNDEF IN WORKLOAD ROUTINE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",14,0)="128^2961129^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",15,0)="139 SEQ #108^2961210^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",15,1,0)="^^7^7^2961210"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",15,1,1,0)="This patch must be loaded by ALL sites who have loaded LR*5.2*72.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",15,1,2,0)="patch corrects problems encountered with the option Log-in regular"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",15,1,3,0)="(invoices) [LRBLILR] and  Select units for patients [LRBLPIC] after"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",15,1,4,0)="LR*5.2*72.  For a complete description of this patch, refer to the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",15,1,5,0)="description in the patch message from the Forum Patch Module.  The actual"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",15,1,6,0)="patch message itself MUST be forwarded to the BB Supervisor and/or LIM at"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",15,1,7,0)="every site."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",16,0)="107 SEQ #109^2961224^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^4^4^2961224"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",16,1,1,0)="Multidivisional Printer Problems- This patch is for multidivisional sites that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",16,1,2,0)="wish to print lab collect order copies at separate divisions.  Also, this"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",16,1,3,0)="patch allows the site to change the default label printer from LABLABEL to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",16,1,4,0)="a division specific printer."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",17,0)="152 SEQ #110^2970122^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,0)="132 SEQ #111^2970321^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^20^20^2970321"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="Under the auspices of the Program Office for Infectious Diseases "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,2,0)="VAHQ the Laboratory Emerging Pathogens Initiative (EPI) software "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,3,0)="package is to allow the Department of Veterans Affairs (DVA) to track "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,4,0)="Emerging Pathogens on the national level without the necessity for "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,5,0)="additional local data entry. Using this objective information, plans can "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,6,0)="be formulated on the national level for intervention strategies and "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,7,0)="resource needs. Results of aggregate data can also be shared with "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,8,0)="appropriate public health authorities for planning on the national level "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,9,0)="for the non-VA and private health care sectors."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,10,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,11,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,13,0)="The Laboratory EPI program is designed to automatically provide data "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,14,0)="on emerging pathogens to Veterans Affairs Headquarters (VAHQ) "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,15,0)="without additional individual data entry at the site level. The data will "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,16,0)="be sent to Austin Automation Center (AAC) for initial processing and "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,17,0)="coupling with denominator data related to workload. VAHQ data "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,18,0)="retrieval and analysis can then be accomplished."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,19,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",18,1,20,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,0)="158 SEQ #112^2970326^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,0)="^^85^85^2970326"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,1,0)="Patch LR*5.2*158"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,2,0)="Default PCE Provider/Phlebotomy Workload Capture"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,4,0)="Purpose of the Patch:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,5,0)="This patch contains two enhancements. (1) Provide a PIMS certified Default"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,6,0)="Provider to be used for laboratory Patient Care Database workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,7,0)="collected via PCE API. (2) Correct excessive counting of laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,8,0)="phlebotomy workload."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,10,0)="-----------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,11,0)="Routine List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,12,0)="                  Before         After            Patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,13,0)="Routine          Check Sum     Check Sum          List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,15,0)="LRCAPPH         9623897         10294589     1,19,127,136,138,158"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,16,0)="LRCAPPH1        7546206         4949612      127,136,138,158"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,18,0)="-----------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,19,0)="Files/Fields"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,21,0)="File: LABORATORY SITE (#69.9)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,22,0)="Field:  PCE DEFAULT PROVIDER (#617)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,23,0)="File: LAB ORDER ENTRY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,24,0)="Field: PCE ENC (#30)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,26,0)="------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,27,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,29,0)="1. All users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,30,0)="2. No options need be placed out of order."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,31,0)="3. Install patch during non-peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,32,0)="4. Laboratory specimens should not be accessioned or verified during"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,33,0)="   installation of the patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,34,0)="5. The Auto-Instruments 'LAB' job does not have to be stopped."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,35,0)="6. Installation time of this patch is less than ten minutes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,36,0)="7. Journal requires no special attention."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,37,0)="8. No options are contained in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,39,0)="NOIS List (Partial List)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,40,0)="==========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,41,0)="MILW-1196-41783"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,42,0)="MOU-1196-31178"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,43,0)="SEP-1196-62013"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,44,0)="MAD-0297-41389"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,45,0)="==========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,46,0)="Test Site:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,47,0)="Alpha Test Site: Long Beach"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,49,0)="------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,50,0)="Patch Description:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,52,0)="This patch provides a new field, PCE DEFAULT PROVIDER, in the LABORATORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,53,0)="SITE (#69) file to support the Laboratory PCE API workload data capture."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,54,0)="The default provider is defined locally based on PCE/PIMS workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,55,0)="provider screening criteria. It is the responsibility of the LIM to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,56,0)="coordinate with the PCE/PIMS Coordinator to ensure that this field is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,57,0)="properly defined and maintained."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,59,0)="Failure to enter a default provider will cause PCE and Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,60,0)="phlebotomy workload data NOT TO BE PROCESSED. NONE of the workload data is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,61,0)="lost. No default provider causes the workload data processing software to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,62,0)="stop and wait until the field is properly defined."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,64,0)="The software logic will check the ordering provider for no termination"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,65,0)="date and person class for the encounter date. If the ordering provider"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,66,0)="fails this check the default provider will be used instead."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,68,0)="A cleanup utility will be provided to deal with previous provider"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,69,0)="rejection errors by reprocessing encounters using the default provider"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,70,0)="instead of the ordering provider of record."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,71,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,72,0)="Second Enhancement:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,74,0)="Laboratory phlebotomy counts were being credited for non patient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,75,0)="specimens. Also other factors were inflating phlebotomy workload. A code"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,76,0)="change now screens all workload to ensure that only patients from the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,77,0)="Patient (#2) file are processed. Software logic has been change to capture"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,78,0)="1 phlebotomy count for each LAB ORDER with a collection type of Send"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,79,0)="Patient (SP), Immediate Collect (I) or Lab Collect (LC)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,81,0)="The inflated phlebotomy counts coincide with the installation of patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,82,0)="LR*5.2*138. It is recommended that the manual counts be used for the date"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,83,0)="range between this patch and LR*5.2*138 instead of the LMIP generated"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,84,0)="totals. After this patch is installed the manual totals should match"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",19,1,85,0)="auto-captured phlebotomy totals +/- 5%. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",20,0)="150 SEQ #113^2970401^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",20,1,0)="^^1^1^2970401"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",20,1,1,0)="Workload Archiving Patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",21,0)="160 SEQ #114^2970421^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",21,1,0)="^^2^2^2970421"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",21,1,1,0)="MISCELLANEOUS- HOUSEKEEPING"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",21,1,2,0)="-includes fix for wrong lab sample when a UA is ordered"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",22,0)="165 SEQ #115^2970528^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",22,1,0)="^^1^1^2970528"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",22,1,1,0)="MISSING COLLECTION TYPE PROMPT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",23,0)="140 SEQ #118^2970709^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,0)="143 SEQ #119^2970717^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,0)="^^143^143^2970717"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,1,0)="LR*5.2*143 Patch Description:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,2,0)="DSS Clinical Data Extract API"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,3,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,4,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,6,0)="Routine Name      Before Patch       After Patch    Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,7,0)="LRCAPDAR              NA               5854094         143"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,8,0)="LRCAPDSS            5467821            5610986       127,143"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,9,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,10,0)="File Installed:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,11,0)="LAB DSS LAR EXTRACT  ^LAR(64.036)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,13,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,15,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,16,0)="NOTE: This patch is invoked by patch ECX*2*18 and does not function"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,17,0)="independently. There are no laboratory options associated with the patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,19,0)="1. All users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,20,0)="2. No options need be placed out of order."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,21,0)="3. Install patch during non-peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,22,0)="4. This patch has no effect on routine laboratory operations."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,23,0)="5. The Auto-Instruments 'LAB' job(s) does not have to be stopped."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,24,0)="6. Installation time of this patch is less than ten minutes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,25,0)="7. Journalling requires no special attention."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,27,0)="==========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,28,0)="NOIS List "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,29,0)="None"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,30,0)="DSS Program Office Request"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,31,0)="==========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,32,0)="Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,33,0)="Alpha Test Site: Long Beach"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,34,0)="Beta Test Sites : Portland, Murfreesboro"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,36,0)="----------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,37,0)="Functionality:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,39,0)="The Laboratory Clinical Extraction API replaces the earlier clinical data"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,40,0)="extraction software that utilized the LABORATORY SITE file (#69) and the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,41,0)="ACCESSION file (#68). In an earlier guideline, DSS requested that the LIM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,42,0)="adjust the purge date for these two files to retain 300 days of data. This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,43,0)="request could not be done by numerous sites because of the lack of disk"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,44,0)="storage capacity. Patch LR*5.2*143 will relieve the sites from retaining"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,45,0)="300 days of ORDERS and ACCESSION, and the normal PURGE OLD ORDERS AND"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,46,0)="ACCESSION option date range can be restored."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,48,0)="Implementation:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,50,0)="The DSS LAR Data (Patch LR*5.2*143 and the companion DSS patch ECX*2*18)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,51,0)="extract utilizes the LAB DATA file (#63) and does not require the LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,52,0)="ORDERS file (#69) or the ACCESSION file (#68). Implementation of the DSS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,53,0)="LAR API DOES require that the LIM link the 12 DSS LAR tests in the DSS LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,54,0)="TEST file (#727.2) to all local corresponding tests in the LABORATORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,55,0)="TESTS file (#60). For DSS purposes, these corresponding laboratory tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,56,0)="must be linked to the WKLD CODE file and must be individually orderable"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,57,0)="(atomic) tests. The link between LABORATORY TESTS file and the WKLD CODE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,58,0)="file is accomplished by assigning a WKLD CODE. The NATIONAL LABORATORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,59,0)="TEST field (#64) of the LABORATORY TESTS file (#60) provides this linkage."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,60,0)="The NATIONAL LABORATORY TEST field is not used by LMIP data capture"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,61,0)="software and will not effect LMIP counts. Patch LR*5.2*127 provided a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,62,0)="menu, ""National Laboratory Test"" [LR70 60-64], to link the LABORATORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,63,0)="TESTS file to the WKLD CODE file. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,65,0)="NOTE: When linking the DSS LAR tests to local laboratory tests, only"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,66,0)="atomic Laboratory Tests are selectable. Panel tests are NOT permitted to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,67,0)="be linked to any DSS survey test."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,69,0)="The DSS LAR extract also requires the LIM to identify all specimens that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,70,0)="are derived from blood or urine, i.e., plasma, serum, clean catch. The LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,71,0)="DSS LAR API will use these specimens to screen patient's results in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,72,0)="LAB DATA file and extract information for the 12 DSS tests."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,74,0)="The local DSS Coordinator will seek the LIM's assistance to identify tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,75,0)="and specimens. This should require less than 30 minutes to complete. The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,76,0)="LIM is not required to actually initiate the data extraction. This will be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,77,0)="done by the local DSS Coordinator."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,79,0)="The LIM SHOULD coordinate the purging/archiving of the LAB DATA and the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,80,0)="WKLD DATA files with the DSS Coordinator."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,82,0)="The data for the DSS LAR extract will be stored during processing in a new"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,83,0)="file LAB DSS LAR (#64.036) and the data is stored in the global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,84,0)="^LAR(64.036). This global will be purged by the calling DSS option when"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,85,0)="the data has been transferred to the DSS laboratory clinical database."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,86,0)="Normally this file will be empty. The design and functionality are the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,87,0)="same used by the WKLD LOG file (#64.03) for the DSS LAB extract. Neither"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,88,0)="the LIM nor the Laboratory Package is responsible for purging data from"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,89,0)="the WKLD LOG file (#64.03) or the LAB DSS LAR file (#64.036)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,92,0)="------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,93,0)="Laboratory Management Index Program (LMIP) and DSS sendout tests setup and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,94,0)="referral lab identification guidelines:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,96,0)="LMIP and DSS are reviewing data collected for laboratory sendout testing."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,97,0)="The collected data indicates that a consistent nation wide coding method"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,98,0)="for capturing sendout tests is not being used.  Each site should review"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,99,0)="the WKLD Codes for sendout tests to assure that it follows these"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,100,0)="guidelines:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,101,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,102,0)="Each sendout test should be coded with an appropriate specific WKLD Code"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,103,0)="prefix. If there is not an appropriate specific WKLD Code available,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,104,0)="submit a request for WKLD Code addition(s) to the P&LMS Informatics Manage"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,105,0)="at the Dallas CIOFO. Forms are available in Patch LR*5.2*138 for making"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,106,0)="these requests."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,108,0)="Each sendout test should have a .8XXX suffix. All nationally recognized"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,109,0)="sendout laboratories have a suffix code numbers in the range of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,110,0)=".8000-.8999. Each sendout test should be assigned an .8XXX suffix"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,111,0)="indicating the laboratory that the specimen was sent for analysis. If the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,112,0)="same sendout test is sent to two or more laboratories, one method, is to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,113,0)="have a separate test for each sendout laboratory. Separate test for each"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,114,0)="sendout laboratory will allow different normal ranges and specimen"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,115,0)="requirements and test cost. At the very least the sendout tests should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,116,0)="coded to include the ordered test and the sendout laboratory whenever"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,117,0)="possible. In certain situations, sendout testing represents a significant"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,118,0)="percentage of total patient care cost. This cost requires better tracking"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,119,0)="to determine patient's overall treatment cost."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,121,0)="The Lab DSS API (routine LRCAPDSS) will be enhanced by patch LR*5.2*143 to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,122,0)="extract all sendout tests based on the .8XXX suffix. It is not necessary"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,123,0)="to set the DSS Feeder Key to 'YES'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,125,0)="Example "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,126,0)="CEA done at VA Milwaukee"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,127,0)="86617.8694  CEA~VA MILWAUKEE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,128,0)="CEA done at Smith Kline Beecham"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,129,0)="86617.8001  CEA~SMITH KLINE BEECHAM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,130,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,131,0)="With the new Lab DSS API enhancement, WKLD Codes conforming to any of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,132,0)="following patterns will be extracted and passed to the DSS Workload API."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,134,0)="WKLD CODE marked as Billable Procedure [LMIP Unit] (Austin Database)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,135,0)="WKLD CODE with the suffix of .9999 (DSS ACC)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,136,0)="WKLD CODE with the suffix of .8XXX (Sendout laboratory destination )"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,137,0)="WKLD CODE with the DSS Feeder Key (#14) field in the WKLD CODE file (#64)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,138,0)="marked YES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,140,0)="Note:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,141,0)="National Laboratory Tests (NLT)and WKLD Codes can be considered to be the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,142,0)="same codes. NLT is the name of the VistA Package responsible for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",24,1,143,0)="distributing and updating WKLD Code files."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",25,0)="164 SEQ #120^2970728^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,0)="171 SEQ #121^2970728^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,0)="^^81^81^2970728"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,1,0)=" Patch LR*5.2*171 is a complete replacement for patch LR*5.2*140."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,2,0)=" If you have not already installed Patch LR*5.2*140, do not install it."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,4,0)="  Patch LR*5.2*140 corrected the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,6,0)="  1.  The problem of erratic printing from the Group data "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,7,0)="      review (verified & EM) [LRGVP] option has been resolved. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,8,0)="      Tests that were STAT or had critical results are "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,9,0)="      displayed with control characters that produce the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,10,0)="      reverse video. The control characters caused erratic "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,11,0)="      printing in which the printer had to be powered off "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,12,0)="      and on to clear the problem."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,13,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,14,0)="  2.  The problem of Incorrectly reported as comments not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,15,0)="      stored when the combined text strings are greater than 68"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,16,0)="      characters has been resolved. In addition a date/time stamp"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,17,0)="      and DUZ ID of the person making the change has been added "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,18,0)="      to each incorrectly reported as comment."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,19,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,20,0)="  3.  Data names in the LAB DATA file (#63) have been limited to 50 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,21,0)="      characters."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,22,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,23,0)="  4.  The option Review Data Names [LR REVIEW DATA NAMES] will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,24,0)="      permit the user to review the data base for entries > 50"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,25,0)="      characters."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,26,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,27,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,28,0)="   Reference NOIS:   KAN-0395-40200"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,29,0)="                     MAN-O694-10052"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,30,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,31,0)="   E3R               E3R #9370"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,33,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,34,0)="   Test Site(s):     Muskogee, OK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,35,0)="                     Asheville, NC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,36,0)="                     Lexington, KY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,37,0)="                     Loma Linda, CA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,39,0)="  This patch corrects these issues and also the following issues."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,40,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,41,0)="  1.  When using the Enter/Verify/Modify data (manual) [LRENTER] option to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,42,0)="      edit more than one result on a verified accession, an undefined"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,43,0)="      variable DIE occurred."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,45,0)="  2.  When using the Enter/Verify/Modify data (manual) [LRENTER]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,46,0)="      to edit a result,the user is allowed to edit the results"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,47,0)="      without entering their initials."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,49,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,50,0)="   Reference NOIS:   NYN-0797-10830"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,51,0)="                     MAN-0797-10794"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,52,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,53,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,54,0)="   Test Site(s):     Manchester, NH"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,55,0)="                     New York, NY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,56,0)="                     Durham, NC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,57,0)="                     "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,58,0)="  Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,59,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,60,0)="    1.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,61,0)="        option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,62,0)="    2.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,63,0)="        system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,64,0)="        On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,65,0)="        options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,66,0)="           Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,67,0)="           Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,68,0)="           Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,69,0)="           Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,70,0)="    3.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,71,0)="        options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,72,0)="           Install Package(s)  'LR*5.2*171'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,73,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,74,0)="    4.  Assign the option Review Data Names [LR REVIEW DATA NAMES] to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,75,0)="        appropriate lab person(s)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,77,0)="    5.  Remove the Environment Check Routine, LR171, from your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,78,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,80,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",26,1,81,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",27,0)="172 SEQ #122^2970808^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",27,1,0)="^^2^2^2970808"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",27,1,1,0)="  Printer does not set-up properly when running cume reports manually."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",27,1,2,0)="  Adding LRPARAM to LRAC resolves this problem."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,0)="163^2970819^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,0)="^^51^51^2970819"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,1,0)="Build Patch Description LR*5.2*163"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,3,0)=" This patch upgrades the National Laboratory Test (NLT) codes. The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,4,0)=" following enhancements are provided. The CPT/HCPCS CODES Version 6.0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,5,0)=" is a required package for this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,7,0)="   1.  All existing Current Procedural Terminology (CPT) codes in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,8,0)=" WKLD CODE file (#64) will be removed. The 1997 CPT codes will be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,9,0)=" linked to existing codes. After installation, all relevant WKLD CODES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,10,0)=" will have assigned CPT codes. This will cause a 2 to 4 fold increase"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,11,0)=" in the workload Patient Care Encounter (PCE) Application Programmer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,12,0)=" Interface (API) traffic."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,13,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,14,0)=" The workload API is dependent on orderable tests being linked to a NLT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,15,0)=" code. National Laboratory File menu [LR70 60-64] option has sub-menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,16,0)=" options to link the LABORATORY TEST file (#60) entries to NLT codes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,17,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,18,0)="   2.  The routine LRCAPAMP that is used by the Recompile Phase 1 LMIP"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,19,0)=" data [LR WKLD LMIP 1 REPEAT] option was not resetting all file entries."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,20,0)=" In certain situations, workload data could be lost."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,21,0)=" NOTE: Remember to recompile each division individually before repeating"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,22,0)=" any additional data compiling."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,24,0)="   3.  The Workload code list [LRCAPD] option has been enhanced to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,25,0)=" display CPT codes and additional fields to be used by Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,26,0)=" Electronic Data Interchange (LEDI). NOTE: It is recommended that a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,27,0)=" new list be generated with this option."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,28,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,29,0)="   4.  The Edit or Print WKLD CODES [LR WKLD CODE EDIT PRINT] option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,30,0)=" now allows the user to edit all fields for any WKLD CODE in the file."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,31,0)=" This option should be restricted to the Laboratory Information"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,32,0)=" Manager's (LIM's) menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,33,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,34,0)="   5.  The Add a new WKLD code to file [LRCAP CODE ADD] option now"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,35,0)=" prompts for test cost and price."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,36,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,37,0)="   7.  The PRICE field (#8) has been added to the WKLD CODE file (#64)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,38,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,39,0)="   8.  Any conversion errors are stored in the LAB NLT/CPD CODE (#64.81)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,40,0)=" If no errors are generated during the CPT code linkage, this file will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,41,0)=" be empty after install is completed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,42,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,43,0)="   9.  The PCE/VSIT ON field (#615) in LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9) will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,44,0)=" be set to ""PCE/VSIT ONLY"" which transmits CPT codes only to the workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,45,0)=" API. No Clinic Stop Code data will be transmitted."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,46,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,47,0)="  10  When using the Manual Linking of file 60 64 [LR7O 60-64 MANUAL]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,48,0)=" option to change an NLT code assigned to a test in the LABORATORY TEST"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,49,0)=" file (#60), a FileMan error ""??"" would occur. This resulted in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,50,0)=" previous associated test in WKLD CODE file (#64) not being deleted. The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",28,1,51,0)=" routine LR7OU4 corrects this error."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",29,0)="177 SEQ #124^2970827^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",29,1,0)="^^1^1^2970827"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",29,1,1,0)="Fixes the undefined in LRWU5."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",30,0)="121^2970828^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",31,0)="156 SEQ #126^2971118^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",31,1,0)="^^8^8^2971118"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",31,1,1,0)="There is a problem of unknown origin where 7 nines (9999999) are getting"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",31,1,2,0)="stored in the LAB DATA file (# 63), the ACCESSION file (# 68),"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",31,1,3,0)="and the Cumulative Reports Global (^LAC(""LRAC""). This patch replaces the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",31,1,4,0)="these erroneous data nodes with the laboratory inverse date. Initial search"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",31,1,5,0)="of the database is extensive and will take up to two hours. This is a one"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",31,1,6,0)="time occurrence. A background task should be scheduled to run daily to clean"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",31,1,7,0)="up any new occurrences."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",31,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,0)="169 SEQ #127^2971127^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,0)="^^46^46^2971127"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,1,0)="Build Description LR*5.2*169"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,3,0)="Functionality:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,4,0)=" This patch corrects the <UNDEF> error at TEST+3^LRCAPDAR ^(64)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,5,0)=" The program has been modified to accept the new file structure put in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,6,0)=" place by the Decision Support System Extracts (DSS) patch ECX*2*18."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,8,0)=" Implementation:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,9,0)=" The DSS Laboratory Results (LAR) EXTRACT (patch LR*5.2*169 and the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,10,0)=" companion DSS patch ECX*2*26) extract utilizes the LAB DATA file (#63)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,11,0)=" and does not require the LAB ORDER ENTRY file (#69) or the ACCESSION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,12,0)=" file (#68). Implementation of the DSS LAR Application Programmer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,13,0)=" Interface (API) DOES require that the Laboratory Information Manager"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,14,0)=" (LIM) link the 12 DSS LAR tests in the DSS LAB TESTS file (#727.2) to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,15,0)=" all local corresponding tests in the LABORATORY TEST file (#60). "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,17,0)=" Linking of DSS clinical tests has NO EFFECT ON WORKLOAD DATA CAPTURE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,18,0)=" You should link the atomic test in LABORATORY TEST (#60) file that is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,19,0)=" used to report the result. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,20,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,21,0)=" For DSS purposes, these corresponding laboratory tests must be linked"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,22,0)=" to the WKLD CODE file (#64) and must be individually orderable (atomic)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,23,0)=" tests. The link between LABORATORY TEST file (#60) and the WKLD CODE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,24,0)=" file (#64) is accomplished by assigning a WKLD CODE. The NATIONAL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,25,0)=" NATIONAL VA LAB CODE field (#64) of the LABORATORY TEST file (#60)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,26,0)=" provides this linkage."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,27,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,28,0)=" The NATIONAL VA LAB CODE field (#64) is not used by LMIP data capture"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,29,0)=" software and will not effect LMIP counts. Patch LR*5.2*127 provided a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,30,0)=" menu, National Laboratory File [LR7O 60-64], to link the LABORATORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,31,0)=" TEST file (#60) to the WKLD CODE file (#64). "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,32,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,33,0)=" NOTE: When linking the DSS LAR tests to local laboratory tests, only"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,34,0)=" atomic Laboratory Tests are selectable. Panel tests are NOT permitted to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,35,0)=" be linked to any DSS survey test."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,37,0)=" The DSS LAR extract also requires the LIM to identify all specimens"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,38,0)=" that are derived from blood or urine, i.e., plasma, serum, clean"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,39,0)=" catch. The LAB DSS LAR API will use these specimens to screen patient's"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,40,0)=" results in the LAB DATA file (#63) and extract information for the 12"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,41,0)=" DSS tests."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,42,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,43,0)=" The local DSS Coordinator will seek the LIM's assistance to identify"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,44,0)=" tests and specimens. This should require less than 30 minutes to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,45,0)=" complete. The LIM is not required to actually initiate the data"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",32,1,46,0)=" extraction. This step will be completed by the local DSS Coordinator."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",33,0)="90 SEQ #128^2971127^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",33,1,0)="^^7^7^2971127"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",33,1,1,0)="This patch contains a Description of problems, their associated Risk"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",33,1,2,0)="Analysis, routines, input templates and DD's for the VistA Blood Bank"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",33,1,3,0)="software.  It is accompanied by two additional INFORMATION ONLY patches,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",33,1,4,0)="LR*5.2*92 (Validation Scenarios) and LR*5.2*147 (Documentation Changes)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",33,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",33,1,6,0)="See the individual patch messages from the Forum Patch Module for complete"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",33,1,7,0)="information on these patches:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",34,0)="174 SEQ #131^2971127^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",34,1,0)="^^2^2^2971127"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",34,1,1,0)="Fixes undefined for the option Reprint cumulative on a given patient [LRAC PT]."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",34,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,0)="162 SEQ #132^2971127^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,0)="^^35^35^2971127"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,1,0)="Workload Archiving Patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,3,0)=" *************************NOTE************************************* "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,4,0)="   Patches LR*5.2*59 and LR*5.2*150 MUST be installed prior to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,5,0)="    installing this patch.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,7,0)="  *******************************************************************  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,9,0)=" 1)  This patch makes the Purge Wkld Data file 64.1 [LRAR PURGE 64.1] option "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,10,0)="     and the Purge Lab Monthly Workloads file 67.9 [LRAR PURGE 67.9] option "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,11,0)="     queued options.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,12,0)=" 2)  The ARCHIVE TASK NUMBER field (#18) in the LAB ARCHIVAL ACTIVITY file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,13,0)="     (#95.11) is now deleted upon completion of the task.  The Write Data"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,14,0)="     to Off-line Media options, [LRAR WRITE MEDIA 67.99999] and [LRAR WRITE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,15,0)="     MEDIA 64.19999], then check for data in this field as a test of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,16,0)="     completion of archive.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,17,0)=" 3)  For information: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,18,0)="     When archiving the LAB MONTHLY WORKLOADS file (#67.9), the date range "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,19,0)="     selected for archiving must be in entire month chunks due to the file "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,20,0)="     structure of File 67.9."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,21,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,22,0)="     For instance if you select a date range from March 1, 1994 to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,23,0)="     April 1,1994, you will archive the entire months of March and April.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,25,0)=" This patch to the Laboratory package does not contain any changes to the VISTA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,26,0)=" BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA DIRECTIVE 97-033 titled VISTA BLOOD BANK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,27,0)=" SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,29,0)="  Reference NOIS:      HIN-0297-41349                 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,30,0)="                              "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,31,0)="  Reporting Site:      Hines, IL "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,32,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,33,0)="  Test Site(s):        Hines, IL "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,34,0)="                       Minneapolis, MN              "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",35,1,35,0)="                              "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,0)="186 SEQ #133^2971222^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,0)="^^52^52^2971222"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,1,0)="At Open M sites a Merge of a global into itself causes an error.  A check has"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,2,0)="been added to make sure the global values are different before doing the merge."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,5,0)="This patch should also be installed at non-Open M sites, even though they are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,6,0)="not getting the error."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,7,0)=" This patch to the Laboratory package does not contain any changes to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,8,0)=" VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA DIRECTIVE 97-033 titled VISTA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,9,0)=" BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,10,0)=" Reference NOIS:   PRE-0797-60641"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,11,0)=" Reporting Sites:  Prescott, AZ"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,12,0)=" Testing Sites:    Prescott, AZ"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,13,0)=" ROUTINE SUMMARY:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,14,0)=" ================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,16,0)=" The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,18,0)=" <tab>     ;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;**[patch list]**; Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,20,0)="                       Checksum Values"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,22,0)=" Routine Name           Before Patch    After Patch     Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,23,0)=" ------------           ------------    -----------    -----------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,24,0)=" LROR6A                 15782769        16122062       24,100,128,186"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,25,0)="        Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,26,0)="        =========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,27,0)="        1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,28,0)="           option will load the KIDS package in this message onto your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,29,0)="           system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,30,0)="        2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they should"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,31,0)="           be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,32,0)="        3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,33,0)="           system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,34,0)="           global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,35,0)="           On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,36,0)="           following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,37,0)="               Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,38,0)="               Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,39,0)="               Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,40,0)="               Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,41,0)="        4. Users may remain on the system, but installation should be done"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,42,0)="           at off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,43,0)="        5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,44,0)="        6. Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak hours"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,45,0)="           and less than 5 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,46,0)="        7. Installation of this patch requires no additional memory space."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,47,0)="        8. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,48,0)="           'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*186' and proceed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,49,0)="           with the install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,50,0)="        9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,51,0)="           returned to the mapped set once the installation has run to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",36,1,52,0)="           completion."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",37,0)="182 SEQ #134^2971231^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",37,1,0)="^^2^2^2971231"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",37,1,1,0)="This patch fixes problems encountered when user enter comments on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",37,1,2,0)="lab specimens during accessioning."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",38,0)="173 SEQ #135^2980205^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",38,1,0)="^^3^3^2980205"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",38,1,1,0)="This patch corrects a variety of problems with Anatomic Pathology reports."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",38,1,2,0)=" See the Description on the Forum patch module for full information on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",38,1,3,0)="this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",39,0)="198 SEQ #137^2980318^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",39,1,0)="^^3^3^2980318"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",39,1,1,0)="This patch fixes the undefined error that occurs when non package"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",39,1,2,0)="(X) variable is killed by VADPT."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",39,1,3,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",40,0)="153^2980318^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",40,1,0)="^^2^2^2980318"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",40,1,1,0)="Please refer to the 'LABORATORY ELECTRONIC DATA INTERCHANGE (LEDI) Patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",40,1,2,0)="LA*5.2*27 and patch LR*5.2*153 INSTALLATION GUIDE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,0)="203^2980417^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,0)="^^303^303^2980417"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,1,0)="  Reference NOIS:        None"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,3,0)="  Reporting Site:        N/A"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,4,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,5,0)="  Test Site(s)--Alpha Platform w/ DSM OS:  Milwaukee, Brockton"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,6,0)="                                           North Chicago"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,9,0)="  DESCRIPTION:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,10,0)="  ============"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,11,0)=" In accordance with the evaluation performed using established policies"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,12,0)=" and VHA Directive 97-033, documented on the patch change control summary"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,13,0)=" and consultation with the FDA on 3/3/1998, this patch does not need to be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,14,0)=" submitted to the FDA for approval.  Changes only involve print routines"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,15,0)=" and have no affect on safety critical requirements and has no associated"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,16,0)=" risks.   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,17,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,18,0)="  A COPY OF THIS PATCH MESSAGE MUST BE FORWARDED TO THE BLOOD BANK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,19,0)="  SUPERVISOR AND THE  LABORATORY INFORMATION  MANAGER (LIM)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,20,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,21,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,22,0)="  PROBLEM:  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,23,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,24,0)="  With the upcoming turn of the century (Y2K) the Office of the Chief"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,25,0)="  Information Office Technical Services has issued a guidelines document"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,26,0)="  for VISTA Software Y2K requirements. This guideline lays out the core"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,27,0)="  essentials to meet or exceed OMB, GAO and congressional requirements for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,28,0)="  Year 2000 requirements.  The VISTA Blood Bank Software v 5.2 was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,29,0)="  evaluated and found to have no existing problems as far as date storage"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,30,0)="  and evaluation.  The date in all instances is already stored internally"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,31,0)="  in a format which allows the definite determination of proper century."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,32,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,33,0)="  The Y2K guidelines document states that applications are required to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,34,0)="  expand the external date displays on reports or forms which can be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,35,0)="  considered legally binding documents between the VA and the veteran, an"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,36,0)="  agent of the veteran, or a service- or product- provider to the VA."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,37,0)="  Using this statement as a guideline it was determined that the reports"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,38,0)="  generated by the following options were to be modified to display the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,39,0)="  date using a 4 digit year format rather than the traditional dd/mm/yr"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,40,0)="  format currently used:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,41,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,42,0)="  Print single BB patient report [LRBLP PRINT SINGLE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,43,0)="  Print all BB patient reports on print queue [LRBLP PRINT ALL ON QUEUE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,44,0)="  Blood bank consultation reports [LRBLCN]  **> Locked with LRBLSUPER"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,45,0)="  Print units with final disposition [LRBLRUF] **> Locked with LRBLSUPER"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,46,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,48,0)="  RISK ANALYSIS:  Since the coding changes only affect the format of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,49,0)="  year printed on the report and have no functionality changes, the risk"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,50,0)="  is NONE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,51,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,52,0)="  EFFECT ON FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS/ INTENDED USES: Problem does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,53,0)="  involve a software safety critical requirement and does NOT change the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,54,0)="  scope of a design safeguard or intended use."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,56,0)="  POTENTIAL IMPACT ON SITES:  There is no potential impact on the sites"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,57,0)="  from the installation of LR*5.2*203."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,58,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,59,0)="  VALIDATION TESTING REQUIREMENTS:  Although the changes do not involve"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,60,0)="  any requirements or functional specifications, it is necessary to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,61,0)="  perform the following steps in order to confirm that the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,62,0)="  chartable reports are printing dates using a 4 digit year format:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,63,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,64,0)="  OPTION: Print single BB patient report [LRBLP PRINT SINGLE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,65,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,66,0)="  This option should generate a chartable patient report where the date"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,67,0)="  format uses a 4 digit year regardless of whether the work was done"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,68,0)="  before or after installation of the patch.  To verify this:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,69,0)="  1) Select the option Print single BB patient report [LRBLP PRINT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,70,0)="     SINGLE]."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,71,0)="  2) At the prompt Select Patient Name: type in a name of a patient who"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,72,0)="     has previous Blood Bank results."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,73,0)="  3) At the prompt Print component requests  ? NO//  press the ENTER key"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,74,0)="     to accept NO as the response."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,75,0)="  4) At the prompt DEVICE: select a valid printer name or print the report"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,76,0)="     to the screen. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,77,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,78,0)="          Examine the report to verify that all instances of the date are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,79,0)="          formatted to include all four digits of the year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,80,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,81,0)="          Repeat steps 1 through 4 above with the following exception:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,82,0)="          During step 3) answer YES to print component requests. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,84,0)="          Examine the report to verify that all instances of the date are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,85,0)="          formatted to include all four digits of the year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,86,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,87,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,88,0)="      OPTION: Print all BB patient reports on print queue [LRBLP PRINT ALL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,89,0)="              ON QUEUE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,90,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,91,0)="  This option is used to print a batch of chartable patient reports.  The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,92,0)="  format of the individual patient reports should be identical to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,93,0)="  reports printed using the option Print single BB patient report [LRBLP"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,94,0)="  PRINT SINGLE].  To verify the correct date format on these reports"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,95,0)="  perform the following steps:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,96,0)="  1) Select the option Print all BB patient reports on print queue [LRBLP"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,97,0)="     PRINT ALL ON QUEUE]."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,98,0)="  2) At the prompt Save reports for reprinting ? NO// answer YES."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,99,0)="  3) At the prompt Print component requests  ? NO/ answer YES."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,100,0)="  4) At the prompt DEVICE: select a valid printer name or print the report"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,101,0)="     to the screen."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,102,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,103,0)="          Examine the report to verify that all instances of the date are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,104,0)="          formatted to include all four digits of the year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,105,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,106,0)="          Repeat steps 1 through 4 above with the following exceptions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,107,0)="          During step 2) answer  NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,108,0)="          During step 3) answer NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,109,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,110,0)="          Examine the report to verify that all instances of the date are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,111,0)="          formatted to include all four digits of the year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,112,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,113,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,114,0)="     OPTION: Blood bank consultation reports [LRBLCN]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,115,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,116,0)="  This option is available for those sites wishing to use VistA to  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,117,0)="  generate a Chartable Consultative report on patients who after Blood"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,118,0)="  Bank serological testing are found to have either an allo-antibody or a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,119,0)="  positive Direct Coombs. If this option is used at a site, then a sample"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,120,0)="  report should be printed for each type of Consultative report generated"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,121,0)="  and then reviewed to determine that all dates print using a 4 digit year"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,122,0)="  format.  This will need to be completed by a user with the LRBLSUPER key"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,123,0)="  performing the following steps:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,125,0)="   1) Select the option Blood bank consultation reports [LRBLCN]."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,126,0)="   2) At the prompt Select CONSULTATION: type in a ""?"".  You will see a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,127,0)="      listing of each type of consultative report used at your facility."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,128,0)="      ANTIBODY or DIRECT COOMBS TEST REPORT."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,129,0)="   3) At the prompt Select Patient Name:  choose a name of a patient that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,130,0)="      is known to have an identified allo antibody or positive Direct"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,131,0)="      Coombs test, whichever is appropriate."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,132,0)="   4) At the prompt DEVICE: select a valid printer name or print the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,133,0)="      report to the screen."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,134,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,135,0)="        Examine the report to verify that all instances of the date are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,136,0)="          formatted to include all four digits of the year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,138,0)="          Repeat steps 1-4 as necessary to provide an example of each "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,139,0)="          type of consultative report generated at your facility."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,141,0)="     OPTION: Print units with final disposition [LRBLRUF]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,142,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,143,0)="  This option is designed for a site to print a permanent hard copy of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,144,0)="  BLOOD INVENTORY file (#65) prior to the use of the option Remove units"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,145,0)="  with final disposition [LRBLSER] to purge the BLOOD INVENTORY file (#65)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,146,0)="  for a specified date range. This functionality is provided for those"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,147,0)="  sites who may have a need or desire to not keep all BLOOD INVENTORY data"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,148,0)="  on line indefinitely.  It is not recommended that this option be run on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,149,0)="  a routine basis.  However, if necessary the option is available."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,150,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,151,0)="  Because of the implications of generating this report, it is recommended"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,152,0)="  that if a site wishes to verify that the printing of dates uses a 4"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,153,0)="  digit year that this verification be done in a test environment.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,154,0)="  report should be locked with the LRBLSUPER key so will need to have a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,155,0)="  user with that key perform the testing if performed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,156,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,157,0)="  To verify the correct date format on these reports perform the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,158,0)="  steps:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,159,0)="  1) Select the option Print units with final disposition [LRBLRUF]."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,160,0)="  2) If this option has been used in the past you may be prompted with the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,161,0)="     following.  *** ANSWER NO AT THE PROMPT TO DELETE THE LIST ***"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,162,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,163,0)="      There is a list of units printed by USER,PREVIOUS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,164,0)="      They should be deleted before printing another list. OK ? YES// N"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,165,0)="      (NO)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,166,0)="  3) At the prompt Start with Date TODAY//  choose a date far enough in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,167,0)="     the past so that there will be unit with a final disposition entered."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,168,0)="  4) At the prompt Go    to   Date TODAY// choose a date more recent than"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,169,0)="     the Start with Date."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,170,0)="  5) At the DEVICE: prompt, choose a valid printer name."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,171,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,172,0)="  Examine the report to verify that all instances of the date are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,173,0)="  formatted to include all four digits of the year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,174,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,175,0)=" -----------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,176,0)="  Software Availability:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,177,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,178,0)="  This patch is available from one of the CIO Field Offices listed below."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,179,0)="  All VAMC's are encouraged to use their FTP capability to obtain the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,180,0)="  software from the appropriate directory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,181,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,182,0)="  CIO Field Office           FTP Address             Directory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,183,0)="  ----------------          -------------        -----------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,184,0)="  Hines                     152.129.1.110        anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,185,0)="  Albany                    152.127.1.5          anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,186,0)="  Salt Lake                 152.131.2.1          anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,187,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,188,0)="  File Name:LAB_Y2K.KID"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,189,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,190,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,191,0)="  Y2K routine changes included with this patch:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,192,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,193,0)="  Routine         Line Tag      Purpose of change"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,194,0)="  -------         ---------     -----------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,195,0)="  LRBLJPA1           R+2       Format output to accommodate 4 digit year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,196,0)="                     R+5       Format output to accommodate 4 digit year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,197,0)="                      Y        Expand date format to print a 4 digit year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,198,0)="                     H+3       Format output to accommodate 4 digit year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,199,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,200,0)="  LRBLPBR1            T        Expand date format to print a 4 digit year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,201,0)="                     N+3       Format output to accommodate 4 digit year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,202,0)="                     L+1       Format output to accommodate 4 digit year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,203,0)="                      R        Format output to accommodate 4 digit year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,204,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,205,0)="  LRUCN              ASK+1     Expand date format to print a 4 digit year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,206,0)="                      H        Format output to accommodate 4 digit year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,207,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,208,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,209,0)=" During initial evaluation of LRBL namespaced routines it was reported"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,210,0)=" that 26 routines would need renovation to be Y2K compliant.  After"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,211,0)=" further evaluation, it was determined that only two LRBL namespaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,212,0)=" routines would need to be modified.  The routines originally reported but"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,213,0)=" not modified are:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,214,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,215,0)=" LRUDEL      LRBLDEX1      LRBLDEX2     LRBLJPA      LRBLJPA2"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,216,0)=" LRBLJPP     LRBLJTS       LRBLJTS1     LRBLPC       LRBLPC1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,217,0)=" LRBLPR      LRBLPR1       LRBLPRA      LRBLPT       LRBLPT1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,218,0)=" LRBLPTR1    LRBLPUS       LRBLPX       LRBLPX1      LRBLRCT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,219,0)=" LRBLSET     LRBLTA        LRBLTA1      LRBLTXA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,220,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,221,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,222,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,223,0)=" ========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,224,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,225,0)="Note: This build contains LR*5.2*201 and LA*5.2*42 therefore, the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,226,0)="environment for installation must satisfy all three patches. There are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,227,0)="special considerations made for Automated instruments which are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,228,0)="not directly associated with Blood Bank."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,229,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,230,0)=" 1.  The following patches must be installed prior to installation of this"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,231,0)="     patch: LR*5.2*153, LA*5.2*27, LA*5.2*37, DI*21.0*44, XU*8.0*71."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,232,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,233,0)=" 2.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution Systems (KIDS)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,234,0)="              Menu, select the Installation Menu [XPD INSTALLATION MENU]:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,235,0)="               Select INSTALLATION OPTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,236,0)="                Select Installation Option: Load a Distribution"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,237,0)="                Enter a Host File: LAB_Y2K.KID"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,238,0)="              Dialog:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,239,0)="           KIDS Distribution saved on Mar 23, 1998@13:22:30"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,240,0)=" Comment: LR*5.2*203  LR*5.2*201  LA*5.2*42  Y2K Enhancements  3-23-98"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,241,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,242,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,243,0)=" This Distribution contains Transport Globals for the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,244,0)=" Package(s):"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,245,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,246,0)="      LR*5.2*203"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,247,0)="      LR*5.2*201"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,248,0)="      LA*5.2*42"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,249,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,250,0)=" Want to Continue with Load? YES// "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,251,0)=" Loading Distribution..."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,252,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,253,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,254,0)="       It is strongly recommended to do a KIDS Backup before installing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,255,0)="       the build."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,257,0)="  3. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they should"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,258,0)="       be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,259,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,260,0)="  4. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,261,0)="       'Verify Checksums in Transport Global' and verify that all routines"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,262,0)="       have the correct checksum."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,263,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,264,0)="  5. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, you may use the option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,265,0)="    'Print Transport Global' to view what will be installed on your system"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,266,0)="     prior to the Install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,267,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,268,0)="  6. Users can remain on the system.  Installation should take less than"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,269,0)="     ten minutes during non-peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,270,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,271,0)="  7. Primary Laboratory Options should be placed out of service"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,272,0)="     and Laboratory Users should be off the system. Disable the menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,273,0)="     option Laboratory [LRMENU] or the local equivalent during the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,274,0)="     install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,275,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,276,0)="     Routine LAB or lab automated instruments interface thru the LSI"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,277,0)="     should be stopped."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,278,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,279,0)="     If the site has direct-connect interfaces for lab automated"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,280,0)="     instruments, these should be stopped."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,281,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,282,0)="     The HL7 background job (HLLP) for the Lab Universal Interface"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,283,0)="     should be stopped."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,284,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,285,0)="     The routine LA7UIIN to process incoming HL7 messages should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,286,0)="     not be running. This routine will shutdown automatically after 5"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,287,0)="     minutes if no messages have been received."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,288,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,289,0)="     If using auto download for Lab automated instruments, the routine"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,290,0)="     LA7ADL should be stopped. Use the option 'Start/Stop Auto Download"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,291,0)="     Background Job' [LA7 ADL START/STOP]."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,292,0)="     if no "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,293,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,294,0)="  8. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,295,0)="    'Install Package(s)' Select the package  LR*5.2*203 and proceed with"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,296,0)="     install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,297,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,298,0)="  9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 3, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,299,0)="     returned to the mapped set once the installation has run to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,300,0)="     completion. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,301,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,302,0)=" 10. After installation is complete, remove the routines LR201 and LA42 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",41,1,303,0)="     from your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,0)="201^2980417^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,0)="^^462^462^2980417"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,1,0)="PATCH DESIGNATION: LR*5.2*201           PACKAGE: LAB SERVICE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,2,0)="  VERSION: 5.2                          PATCH NUMBER: 201"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,3,0)="  PATCH SUBJECT: Y2K LABORATORY (LR) PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,4,0)="  PRIORITY: MANDATORY                   STATUS OF PATCH: UNDER DEVELOPMENT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,5,0)="  DATE PATCH FIRST ENTERED: JAN 27, 1998"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,8,0)="CATEGORY OF PATCH: ROUTINE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,9,0)="CATEGORY OF PATCH: DATA DICTIONARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,12,0)=" PATCH DESCRIPTION:   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,13,0)=" This is the Year 2000 (Y2K) compliance patch containing the changes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,14,0)=" necessary to accommodate the year 2000.  2 digit (YY) year dates are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,15,0)=" replaced with 4 digit (CCYY) century year dates in laboratory routines"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,16,0)=" for patients' permanent clinical record. 2 digit year dates are replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,17,0)=" in other laboratory routines where space was available.  Because of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,18,0)=" lack of space, labels are still printed with 2 digit year dates."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,19,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,20,0)=" Warning:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,21,0)=" Local label routines that call DD^LRX or DT^LRX will need to be modified"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,22,0)=" to call DDOLD^LRX or DTOLD^LRX to print 2-digit dates."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,23,0)="                                "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,24,0)=" Patch LR*5.2*201 VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE V5.2 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,25,0)=" DEVICE PRODUCT LABELING STATEMENT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,26,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,27,0)=" March 10, 1998"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,28,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,29,0)=" VISTA Laboratory Package patch LR*5.2*201 contains changes to software "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,30,0)=" controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 97-033, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,31,0)=" VERSION 5.2.  The following routines listed as part of Group B in the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,32,0)=" directive were modified to be Y2K compliant:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,33,0)=" LRU, LRUA, LRUPT.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,34,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,35,0)=" These are shared routines that are used by Blood Bank as well as general "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,36,0)=" Laboratory software.  They were modified to display a date using a 4"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,37,0)=" digit century year format and formatting was changed when necessary to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,38,0)=" accommodate the extra two characters in the year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,39,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,40,0)=" The above change has been reviewed by the VISTA Blood Bank Developer and "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,41,0)=" found to have no impact on the VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE version 5.2 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,42,0)=" control functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,43,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,44,0)=" PROBLEM:   With the upcoming turn of the century (Y2K) the Office of the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,45,0)=" Chief Information Office Technical Services has issued a guidelines "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,46,0)=" document for VISTA Software Y2K requirements.  This guideline lays out"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,47,0)=" the core essentials to meet or exceed OMB, GAO and congressional"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,48,0)=" requirements for Year 2000 requirements.  Laboratory software has been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,49,0)=" modified to meet or exceed these guidelines."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,50,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,51,0)=" RISK ANALYSIS:   Changes made by patch LR*5.2*201 have no effect on Blood"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,53,0)=" Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,54,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,56,0)=" EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS:  Patch LR*5.2*201 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,57,0)=" alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,58,0)=" elements functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,59,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,60,0)=" POTENTIAL IMPACT ON SITES:  This patch contains changes to a routine "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,61,0)=" identified in Veterans Health Administration (VHA) Directive 97-033. The "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,62,0)=" changes have no effect in Blood Bank functionality or medical device "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,63,0)=" control functions. There is no adverse potential to sites."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,64,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,65,0)=" VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION:  There are no required validation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,66,0)=" scenarios to be completed by sites after installing LR*5.2*201."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,67,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,69,0)=" -----------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,70,0)=" Software Availability:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,71,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,72,0)=" This patch is available from one of the CIO Field Offices listed below."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,73,0)=" All VAMC's are encouraged to use their FTP capability to obtain the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,74,0)=" software from the appropriate directory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,75,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,76,0)=" CIO Field Office           FTP Address             Directory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,77,0)=" ----------------          -------------        -----------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,78,0)=" Hines                     152.129.1.110        anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,79,0)=" Albany                    152.127.1.5          anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,80,0)=" Salt Lake                 152.131.2.1          anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,81,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,82,0)=" File Name:LAB_Y2K.KID"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,84,0)="Note: This patch is issued as a part of a KIDS Distribution in which"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,85,0)="the Transport Global contains all three Laboratory Y2K patches."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,86,0)="The install order and patches are:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,87,0)="LR*5.2*203 Blood Bank"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,88,0)="LR*5.2*201 Laboratory Service"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,89,0)="and LA*5.2*42 Automated Instruments."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,90,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,91,0)=" Data dictionary changes include:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,92,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,93,0)=" Modified the write ""ID"" nodes for:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,94,0)=" ^DD(62.3,0,""ID"",.02) = W:$D(^(""0"")) "" "",$$FMTE^XLFDT($P(^(""0""),U,2),""5Z"")"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,95,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,96,0)=" ^DD(67,0,""ID"",.03) = W ""   "",$$FMTE^XLFDT($P(^(0),U,3),""5Z"")"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,97,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,98,0)=" ^DD(67.1,0,""ID"",3) = W:$D(^(""0"")) ""   "",$$FMTE^XLFDT($P(^(""0""),U,3),""5Z"")"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,99,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,100,0)=" ^DD(69.91,0,""ID"",2) = W:$D(^(""0"")) "" "",$$FMTE^XLFDT($P(^(""0""),U,3),""5Z"")"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,101,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,102,0)=" New Data Dictionary:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,103,0)=" ^DD(68,.097,0)= NON LAB ACCESSION AREA^S^1:YES;0:NO;^0;21^Q"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,105,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,106,0)=" Routine Listing:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,107,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,108,0)=" Name       Line Tag            Description"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,109,0)=" -------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,110,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,111,0)=" LR5XCNV                        OBSOLETE ROUTINE - deleted"
