^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,459,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,460,0)="   The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,461,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",42,1,462,0)="   <tab>     ;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;**[patch list]**; Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,0)="155 SEQ #141^2980417^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,0)="^^118^118^2980417"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,1,0)=" Reference NOIS:         HIN-0297-40272, DEN-0697-51422"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,3,0)=" Reporting Site:        Hines, Long Beach"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,5,0)=" Test Site(s)   Hines, Madison, Long Beach"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,7,0)=" DESCRIPTION:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,8,0)=" ============"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,9,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,10,0)=" This patch to the Laboratory package does not contain any changes to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,11,0)=" VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA Directive 97-033 titled VISTA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,12,0)=" BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,15,0)=" 1.  HIN-0297-40272"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,16,0)="     Two problems were discovered with the QA functions for the Autopsy"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,17,0)="     Accession Area."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,19,0)="     # 1:  The user wasn't prompted to enter any QA codes while"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,20,0)="           executing the option QA codes entry/edit [LRAPQACD] and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,21,0)="           choosing the Autopsy Accession Area."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,23,0)="     # 2:  When using the option QA outcome review cases [LRAPQOR], not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,24,0)="           all of the information was printing.  Prior to patch LR*5.2*72,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,25,0)="           the actual Autopsy accession # and date of autopsy would print"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,26,0)="           on the 2nd part of the report."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,28,0)=" 2.  It was reported that after patch LR*5.2*72 that the report format"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,29,0)="     for Autopsy data review [LRAPAURV] did not accommodate the new"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,30,0)="     accession # format."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,32,0)=" ROUTINE SUMMARY:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,33,0)=" ================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,34,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,35,0)=" The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,37,0)=" <tab>     ;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;**[patch list]**; Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,39,0)="                       Checksum Values"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,41,0)=" Routine Name      Before Patch    After Patch     Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,42,0)=" ============      ============    ===========     =========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,43,0)=" LRAPQACD          1985498         1982867          72,85,155"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,44,0)=" LRAPQOR2          5647114         5107599             155"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,45,0)=" LRAURV            8143951         8364694             155"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,47,0)=" Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,48,0)=" ================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,50,0)=" 1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,51,0)="      option will load the KIDS package in this message onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,53,0)=" 2. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,54,0)="      'Verify Checksums in Transport Global' and verify that all routines"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,55,0)="      have the correct checksum."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,57,0)=" 3. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, you may use the option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,58,0)="    'Print Transport Global' to  view what will be installed on your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,59,0)="     system prior to the Install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,60,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,61,0)="  4. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they should"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,62,0)="     be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,64,0)="  5. Users can remain on the system.  Patch installation should take less"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,65,0)="     than 5 minutes.  No options need to be placed out of service.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,66,0)="     Install during non-peak times."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,67,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,68,0)="  6. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,69,0)="     'Install Package(s)' Select the package  LR*5.2*155 and proceed with "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,70,0)="     install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,71,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,72,0)="  7. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 4, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,73,0)="     returned to the mapped set once the installation has run to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,74,0)="     completion. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,77,0)=" Below is an example of the dialogue seen during the KIDS load."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,79,0)=" Select Installation Option: INStall Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,80,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME: LR*5.2*155          Loaded from Distribution"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,81,0)=" 3/26/98@13:49"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,82,0)=" :39"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,83,0)="     => LR*5.2*155"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",43,1,84,0)=" "
