^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,321,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,322,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,323,0)=" FILE SECURITY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,324,0)=" -------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,325,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,326,0)=" There are four new fields added by this patch which have FileMan Write"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,327,0)=" Access equal to ""@"". This is required for security purposes. To edit these"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,328,0)=" fields requires the user to have FileMan Programmers Access. The fields"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,329,0)=" affected are:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,330,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,331,0)="  - ALTERNATE LABEL ENTRY (#5.2) and ALTERNATE LABEL ROUTINE (#5.3) of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,332,0)="    ACCESSION file (#68)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,333,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,334,0)="  - ALTERNATE LABEL ENTRY (#.04) and ALTERNATE LABEL ROUTINE (#.05) within"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,335,0)="    LABEL DEVICE multiple field (#360) of the LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,336,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,337,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,338,0)=" INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,339,0)=" -------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,340,0)=" The install time for this patch is less than 5 minutes. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,341,0)=" can be installed when Laboratory users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,342,0)=" However the following conditions apply:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,343,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,344,0)="    - Label printing should not be occurring"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,345,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,346,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,347,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,348,0)=" NOTE: MailMan and KERNEL patches must be current on the target system to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,349,0)="       avoid problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,350,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,351,0)="       Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,352,0)="       Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC). The LIM/ADPAC needs to perform the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,353,0)="       file setup as explained in the post-installation instructions if"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,354,0)="       applicable."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,355,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,356,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,357,0)=" 1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,358,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,359,0)=" 2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,360,0)="     option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,361,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,362,0)=" 3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,363,0)="     system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,364,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,365,0)=" 4.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,366,0)="     select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,367,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,368,0)=" 5.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,369,0)="     all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,370,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,371,0)=" 6.  If you wish to preserve a copy of the routines exported in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,372,0)="     prior to installation, you should use the 'Backup a Transport Global'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,373,0)="     option at this time.  You may also compare the routine in your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,374,0)="     production account to the routine in the patch by using the 'Compare"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,375,0)="     a Transport Global to Current System' option.  These options can"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,376,0)="     both be found under the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,377,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,378,0)=" 7.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,379,0)="     and select the package 'LR*5.2*161'.  When prompted 'Want to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,380,0)="     DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES//',"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,381,0)="     choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,382,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,383,0)=" 8. On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,384,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,385,0)=" 9. Routine LR161 can be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,386,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,387,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,388,0)=" *****************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,389,0)=" Below is an example of the dialogue seen during the KIDS install:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,390,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,391,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,392,0)=" Select Installation Option: 6  Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,393,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME:  LR*5.2*161   Loaded from Distribution  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",55,1,394,0)=" 5/2/97@17:11:20"
