^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,85,0)=" ----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,87,0)=" ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,88,0)=" ---------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,90,0)="  The following is a list of routines included in this patch. The second"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,91,0)="  line of each routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,92,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,93,0)="  <tab>;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;**[patch list]**; Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,95,0)="                   CHECK^XTSUMBLD results"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,97,0)="    Routine Name   Before Patch   After Patch    Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,98,0)="    ------------   ------------   -----------   --------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,99,0)="    LR217            N/A          2463818           217"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,100,0)="    LRX            14065673       13923654      65,153,201,217"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,101,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,102,0)=" INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,103,0)=" -------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,104,0)=" The install time for this patch is less than 2 minutes. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,105,0)=" can be installed when Laboratory users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,106,0)=" However the following conditions apply:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,108,0)="    - Accessioning should not be occurring."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,109,0)="      Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,110,0)="      Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,112,0)=" NOTE: MailMan and KERNEL patches must be current on the target system to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,113,0)="       avoid problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,115,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,117,0)=" 1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,119,0)=" 2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,120,0)="     option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,122,0)=" 3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,123,0)="     system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,125,0)=" 4.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,126,0)="     select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,127,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,128,0)=" 5.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,129,0)="     all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,130,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,131,0)=" 6.  If you wish to preserve a copy of the routines exported in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,132,0)="     prior to installation, you should use the 'Backup a Transport Global'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,133,0)="     option at this time.  You may also compare the routine in your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,134,0)="     production account to the routine in the patch by using the 'Compare"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,135,0)="     a Transport Global to Current System' option.  These options can"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,136,0)="     both be found under the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,138,0)=" 7.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,139,0)="     and select the package 'LR*5.2*217'.  When prompted 'Want to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,140,0)="     DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES//',"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,141,0)="     choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,142,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,143,0)=" 8.  On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,145,0)=" 9.  Routine LR217 can be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,146,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,147,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,148,0)=" *****************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",56,1,149,0)=" Below is an example of the dialogue seen during the KIDS install:"
