^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,0)="176 SEQ #159^2981016^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,0)="^^42^42^2981016"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,1,0)="This patch fixes the problem of not being able to choose the option Interim"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,2,0)="report for selected tests [LRRP3] from the Ward Lab Menu. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,3,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,4,0)=" Before this patch: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,5,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,6,0)="       Select Ward lab menu Option: Interim "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,7,0)="         1  Interim report "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,8,0)="         2  Interim report by provider "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,9,0)="         3  Interim report for selected tests as ordered "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,10,0)="         4  Interim reports for 1 location (manual queue) "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,11,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,12,0)=" The option Interim report for selected tests [LRRP3] could not be chosen.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,13,0)=" This patch resolves this problem by changing the menu text of the option "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,14,0)=" [LRRP3] from Interim report for selected tests to Interim report for chosen "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,15,0)=" tests.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,16,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,17,0)="  Reference NOIS:      MAN-0496-12206 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,18,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,19,0)="  Reporting Site:      Manchester, NH "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,20,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,21,0)="  Test Site(s):                       "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,22,0)="                              "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,23,0)="                              "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,24,0)="  Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,25,0)="    =========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,26,0)="        1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,27,0)="           option will load the KIDS package in this message onto your system. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,28,0)="        2. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,29,0)="           system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,30,0)="           On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,31,0)="           options: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,32,0)="               Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,33,0)="               Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,34,0)="               Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,35,0)="               Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,36,0)="        3. Users may remain on the system, but installation should be done at "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,37,0)="           off peak hours.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,38,0)="        4. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,39,0)="           'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*176' and proceed "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,40,0)="           with the install.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,41,0)="        5. Delete routine LR176.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",61,1,42,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",62,0)="214 SEQ #160^2981104^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",62,1,0)="^^1^1^2981104"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",62,1,1,0)="See National Patch Module for LR*5.2*214."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",63,0)="219 SEQ #161^2981105^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",63,1,0)="^^3^3^2981105"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",63,1,1,0)="This is a patch for VISTA Laboratory Software, version 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",63,1,2,0)="A detailed description of this patch is included in the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",63,1,3,0)="distribution message."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,0)="211 SEQ #162^2981119^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,0)="^^16^16^2981119"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,1,0)="This patch corrects two problems:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,2,0)="1. The first problem (as reported by Washington in NOIS # WAS-1297-20917)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,3,0)="is encountered when using the VIC card magnetic stripe to identify"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,4,0)="patients within the Lab module. Prior to patch LR*5.2*211, the system"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,5,0)="would not recognize the data transmitted from the Veteran's ID Card as a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,6,0)="valid patient identifier.  With the installation of patch LR*5.2*211, the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,7,0)="data contained in the magnetic stripe will be interpreted appropriately."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,8,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,9,0)="2. The second problem (as reported by Indianapolis in NOIS #"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,10,0)="IND-0498-41683) is encountered when attempting to add a patient through"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,11,0)="the LRDPA routine. After installing patch LR*5.2*153, general lab users"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,12,0)="can no longer add patients to the PATIENT file (#2) even though the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,13,0)="ALLOW LAB TO ADD PATIENTS field (#13) of the LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,14,0)="is set to YES. Part of patch LR*5.2*153 was intended to eliminate first"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,15,0)="level addition of entries to the Patient file, but provide a second level"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",64,1,16,0)="entry.  Patch LR*5.2*211 restores this second level entry ability."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",65,0)="220 SEQ #163^2981229^1"
