^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",72,0)="166^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",72,1,0)="^^4^4^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",72,1,1,0)="This patch includes the routines, files and data dictionary changes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",72,1,2,0)="to support CPRS version 1.  It is included with the CPRS Master build"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",72,1,3,0)="and should not be installed independent of CPRS.  Refer to the CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",72,1,4,0)="Installation Guide for installation instructions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",73,0)="228 SEQ #171^2990420^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",73,1,0)="^^3^3^2990420"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",73,1,1,0)="This is a patch for VISTA Laboratory Software, version 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",73,1,2,0)="A detailed description of this patch is included in the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",73,1,3,0)="distribution message."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,0)="215^2990427^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,0)="^^29^29^2990427"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,1,0)="NLT Mapping to LOINC LR*5.2*215"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,2,0)="The purpose of the National Laboratory Test (NLT) Mapping to the Logical"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,3,0)="Observation Identifier Names and Codes (LOINC) is to provide the mapping of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,4,0)="Chemistry tests result codes, and the standardization of files used in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,5,0)="Laboratory Software Package. Standardizing codes allows the movement of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,6,0)="tests results from one computer system to another.  This includes sharing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,7,0)="information with both Veterans Health Information Systems and Technology"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,8,0)="Architecture (VistA) and Non-VistA computer systems.  The LOINC committee"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,9,0)="including the largest clinical laboratories in the United States, and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,10,0)="Veteran Affairs, has agreed to use LOINC to identify test results."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,11,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,12,0)="NLT Mapping to the Logical Observation Identifier Names and Codes (LOINC)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,13,0)="has the following features:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,14,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,15,0)="Provides a method to communicate across laboratories in support of Clinical"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,16,0)="Information Resource Network (CIRN) by mapping VistA lab test to LOINC codes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,17,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,18,0)="Provides sets of universal names and ID codes for identifying laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,19,0)="and clinical test results."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,20,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,21,0)="Allows the creation of a uniform naming convention for clinical terms."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,22,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,23,0)="Allows the merging of clinical data across sites (where terminology may vary"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,24,0)="widely.)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,25,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,26,0)="Requires the adoption of naming or coding conventions, and the mapping of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,27,0)="local terminology to these conventions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,28,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",74,1,29,0)="Maps the WKLD CODE file(#64) file to LOINC codes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",75,0)="239 SEQ #173^2990510^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",75,1,0)="^^1^1^2990510"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",75,1,1,0)="LR*5.2*239 FIX FOR LR*5.2*215"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",76,0)="231 SEQ #175^2990602^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",76,1,0)="^^3^3^2990602"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",76,1,1,0)="This patch provides a link between Anatomic Pathology and the Women's"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",76,1,2,0)="Health Program.  For full details see the patch message in the Forum Patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",76,1,3,0)="Module."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,0)="234 SEQ #176^2990719^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,0)="^^24^24^2990719"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,1,0)="RECONCILE AUTOPSY DATA DISCREPANCY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,3,0)="This patch corrects a problem with option [LRAPQOR] QA Outcome Review Cases."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,4,0)="This report's function is to break out by treating specialty, the number of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,5,0)="autopsies performed over a given period of time.  On the last page of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,6,0)="report, it lists the total number of autopsies performed in the given date"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,7,0)="range.  Under this total, the number of autopsies, subtotaled by treating"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,8,0)="specialty, are listed.  These subtotals are not reconciling back to the grand"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,9,0)="total number of autopsies."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,11,0)="Upon investigation, it has been determined that in-patient autopsy numbers for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,12,0)="patients whose treating specialty had changed since they were originally logged"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,13,0)="in, were being totaled in the wrong treating specialty, or omitted from the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,14,0)="report all together.  This resulted in subtotals not reconciling back to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,15,0)="grand total.  The solution is to create an 'Exceptions List' at the bottom of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,16,0)="the report.  This list displays the autopsy accession number, it's current"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,17,0)="treating specialty from the FACILITY TREATING SPECIALTY field (#.09) of the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,18,0)="PATIENT MOVEMENT file (#405), and its original treating specialty from the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,19,0)="TREATING SPECIALTY AT DEATH field (#14.6) of the LAB DATA file (#63).  It also"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,20,0)="displays the total number of exceptions listed.  The subtotals by treating"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,21,0)="specialty plus the total number of exceptions now reconciles back to the grand"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,22,0)="total number of autopsies performed.  This also gives the site the necessary"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,23,0)="information to update the LAB DATA file (#63) with the current treating"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",77,1,24,0)="specialty number."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",78,0)="235 SEQ #177^2990719^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",78,1,0)="^^3^3^2990719"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",78,1,1,0)="This is a patch for VISTA Laboratory Software, version 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",78,1,2,0)="A detailed description of this patch is included in the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",78,1,3,0)="distribution message."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,0)="221 SEQ #178^2990719^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,0)="^^684^684^2990719"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,1,0)="Patch LR*5.2*221 VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,2,0)="Version 5.2 DEVICE PRODUCT LABELING STATEMENT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,3,0)="============================================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,5,0)="The VISTA Laboratory software patch LR*5.2*221 contain the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,6,0)="changes to the BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2 controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,7,0)="97-033."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,9,0)="BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE V.5.2 Changes:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,11,0)="1. Routines LRCENDEL, LROS, LRTSTJAN, and LRTSTOUT have been modified to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,12,0)="accommodate the new ordered test status of NOT PERFORMED."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,14,0)="2. The ACCESSION file (#68), subfile (#68.04), *RESULT field (#5) marked"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,15,0)="for deletion several years ago has been renamed to DISPOSITION field (#5)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,16,0)="This DISPOSITION field (#5) is used to enter a DISPOSITION status for an"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,17,0)="accessioned test that is NOT PERFORMED."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,19,0)="3. The LAB DATA file (#63), Service field (#14.1) was modified to include"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,20,0)="an input transform. This modification is consistent with the changes being"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,21,0)="exported as part of VA FileMan V. 22."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,23,0)="The above software changes have been reviewed by the VISTA Blood Bank"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,24,0)="Developer and found to have no impact on the VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE V."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,25,0)="5.2 controlled functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,27,0)="PROBLEM: A new disposition for accessioned tests called NOT PERFORMED has"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,28,0)="been created. This disposition is assigned to a test that is not performed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,29,0)="for any type of reason. This will replace the past practice of canceling"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,30,0)="or deleting tests which had no results entered."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,32,0)="RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*221 have no effect on Blood"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,33,0)="Bank Software V. 52 functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,35,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*221 does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,36,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical element"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,37,0)="functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,39,0)="POTENTIAL IMPACT ON SITES: This patch contains changes to files and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,40,0)="routines identified in Veterans Health Administration (VHA) Directive"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,41,0)="97-033. The changes have no effect to Blood Bank functionality or medical"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,42,0)="device control functions. There is no adverse potential to sites."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,44,0)="VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION: There are no required validation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,45,0)="scenarios to be completed by sites after installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,47,0)="Patch Description:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,49,0)="The VISTA Laboratory software patch LR*5.2*221 contain several"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,50,0)="enhancements across several functions and procedures. One major"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,51,0)="enhancement or change in business practice is the handling of tests that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,52,0)="will not be done (performed) for various reasons. It is clear that there"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,53,0)="are legitimate reasons that an ordered procedure will not be performed by"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,54,0)="the laboratory service. This enhancement does not prevent the laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,55,0)="personnel from following established guidelines."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,57,0)="This patch provides another status called ""Not Performed"" (NP). Not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,58,0)="Performed is considered a test completion status. The software treats NP"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,59,0)="status the same as verified test except there is no test result. Instead"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,60,0)="of storing a result, NP enhancement stores a comment indicating the reason"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,61,0)="for the NP status."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,63,0)="Example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,64,0)=" *CALCIUM Not Performed: 02/11/19999 9:02pm by 104"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,65,0)=" *NP Reason: Hemolyzed Specimen"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,66,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,67,0)="You will note that NP comments start with the ""*"" that differentiate this"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,68,0)="comment from other types of comments. NP comment and reason is stored in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,69,0)="the LAB Data file (#63) and in the LAB ORDER ENTRY (#69). The CPRS order"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,70,0)="is marked as 'Discontinued' and displayed on the 'Active Orders' screen"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,71,0)="when the LAB ORDER CANCEL notification in CPRS is enabled. If this is not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,72,0)="acceptable then the CPRS order can be marked as Complete when 'SERVICE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,73,0)="CORRECTION' is used as an Order Cancellation Reason."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,75,0)="NP is different than ""canc"". Canc is a result that is stored in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,76,0)="patient's clinical record."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,78,0)="This enhancement allows the conveyance of the following information to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,79,0)="health care provider:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,81,0)="1. The ordered procedure has been given a status of 'Not Performed' and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,82,0)="the reason for the status."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,83,0)="2. It prevents numerous software errors resulting from missing data nodes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,84,0)="in the database."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,86,0)="3. Creates an audit trail of what ultimately happened to all tests ordered"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,87,0)="or accessioned."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,89,0)="Associated NOISs:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,90,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,91,0)="CHY-0798-51245, ALN-1198-11196, ASH-0898-30554, ATG-0698-31312,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,92,0)="WNY-0698-11221, CLA-0598-20635 CMO-1198-41253, DEN-0898-50267,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,93,0)="DUB-0898-30615, FGH-1198-32348, GAI-0698-32344, HAM-1098-21436,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,94,0)="LAS-0698-60208, LEX-0898-41581, LEX-1198-40049, COM-0498-60788,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,95,0)="MIN-0798-40025, MON-0798-51662, MUS-1098-71863, NAS-1098-31373,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,96,0)="OKL-0698-71939, SAG-0498-42248, SLC-1198-50813, TAM-0798-30677,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,97,0)="TAM-1298-31153, TOG-0898-11351, LEB-1298-22078, TAM-1298-31153,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,98,0)="CLA-1198-22013, ALX-1198-71715, ALX-0898-71684, ASH-0898-30675,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,99,0)="BEC-0998-20129, BYN-0598-11025, DAY-0798-42525, DEN-1098-50461,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,100,0)="EKH-0998-40137, GAI-0898-30690, GNH-0498-41065, HAM-0898-21544,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,101,0)="HUN-0798-20942, LEB-1298-22078, LOM-0498-60884, NAS-1098-31373,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,102,0)="OKL-0698-70962, PHI-0598-20045, PHO-1298-60877, SDC-0598-60879,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,103,0)="SLC-0998-50822, WIC-0898-41805, WPB-1198-31834, WAS-1098-31246,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,104,0)="WNY-0998-11152, BAY-0798-31877, FHM-0897-51017, NCH-0596-40125,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,105,0)="CLA-0598-20356, CIN-0998-41790, CMO-0998-41772, COS-0898-41373,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,106,0)="NJH-1298-21603, EKH-0998-40488, GAI-0698-31676, MWV-0598-21363,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,107,0)="SAM-1098-20301, IOW-1298-41014, BAN-0897-11956, PHO-0798-60573,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,108,0)="CHS-0398-42380, MAD-1098-41673,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,110,0)="Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,111,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,112,0)="Long Beach, CA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,113,0)="Milwaukee, WI"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,114,0)="Loma Linda, CA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,115,0)="North Chicago, IL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,116,0)="West Palm Beach, FL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,118,0)="Added Cross Reference:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,119,0)="====================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,120,0)="--A new 'AE' MUMPS cross-reference has been created in the LAB ORDER (#69)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,121,0)="file, Subfile SPECIMEN # (#1), subfile TEST (#6), field CANCEL BY (#10)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,122,0)="This X-Ref is used to identify canceled test that must be sent to PCE for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,123,0)="credit. The data can be used by the billing software."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,125,0)="DATA Dictionary Changes:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,126,0)="========================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,127,0)="ACCESSION file (#68):"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,128,0)="The *RESULT field (#5) of the Test subfield (#68.04) name has been changed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,129,0)="to DISPOSITION field (#5)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,130,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,131,0)="LAB ORDER ENTRY file (#69):"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,132,0)="A new cross-reference has been created on the CANCEL BY field (#10) of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,133,0)="TEST subfield (#69.03) to track tests which have disposition of Not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,134,0)="Performed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,135,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,136,0)="LOAD/WORKLIST file (#68.2)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,137,0)="A new UID VERIFICATION field (#2.1) has been added to the LOAD/WORKLIST"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,138,0)="file (#68.2), PROFILE multiple (#50)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,140,0)="LAB DATA file (#63)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,141,0)="The LOCATION field (#14.1) in the LAB DATA file (#63) input transform has"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,142,0)="changed to conform to FileMan Version 22 variable cleanup."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,143,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,144,0)="Changes Made By Patch LR*5.2*221:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,145,0)="================================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,146,0)="In the past, laboratory users were able to delete all traces of an order"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,147,0)="and specimens from various files (database). This would create a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,148,0)="discrepancy between ward-printed documents and laboratory data files. In"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,149,0)="addition, if the tests were downloaded to automated instruments or LEDI"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,150,0)="Host Laboratory, the result entry could produce corrupt Laboratory patient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,151,0)="records."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,152,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,153,0)="It was also possible in certain situations for deleted accession numbers"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,154,0)="or order numbers to be assigned to two different patients."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,156,0)="The major component of this patch is to maintain a record of all ordered"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,157,0)="procedures, ensuring that integrity of accession numbers is preserved."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,158,0)="This is accomplished in the following manner:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,159,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,160,0)="1. Accessioned tests must be either canceled (canc), result entered and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,161,0)="verified (this includes entering test comment) or designated 'Not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,162,0)="Performed' and a reason entered. The date, time, and the person entering"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,163,0)="the 'Not Performed' reason will be stored in the laboratory patient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,164,0)="record. In addition, the ACCESSION file (#68), and where appropriate, LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,165,0)="ORDER ENTRY file (#69) will be updated to reflect the 'Not Performed'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,166,0)="status. The CPRS order status is changed to completed if 'SERVICE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,167,0)="CORRECTION' is used as the 'Cancellation Reason'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,168,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,169,0)="2. If the site makes use of Interim Reports, in addition to the current"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,170,0)="function, the software will also display those accessions that have the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,171,0)="status of 'Not Performed'. The software will not display the 'Not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,172,0)="Performed' tests if there are any results entered but not verified."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,174,0)="3. If it is determined at a later point, that a 'Not Performed' test"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,175,0)="should be performed, the software will allow results to be entered and the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,176,0)="'Not Performed' reason can be removed by the user."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,177,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,178,0)="4. The new 'Not Performed' test status corrects numerous problems with"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,179,0)="Remove An Accession [LRDELOG] option or Delete Entire Order or individual"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,180,0)="tests [LRCENDEL] option were being used."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,181,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,182,0)="*****  CAUTION  ******  CAUTION  ******  CAUTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,183,0)="ONCE AN ACCESSION NUMBER HAS BEEN ASSIGNED IT CANNOT BE DELETED!"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,184,0)="THIS NEW RESTRICTION MAY CAUSE CONCERN IN CERTAIN AREAS OF THE LAB THAT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,185,0)="MAKE A PRACTICE OF DELETING AN ACCESSION NUMBER AND RE-ASSIGNING IT TO A"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,186,0)="DIFFERENT PATIENT IN ORDER TO CORRESPOND TO MANUAL LOG BOOK ENTRIES. THIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,187,0)="PRACTICE OF RE-ASSIGNING ACCESSION NUMBERS SOMETIMES OCCURS IN HISTOLOGY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,188,0)="AND CYTOLOGY DEPARTMENTS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,189,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,190,0)="Routine Summary:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,191,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,192,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,193,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,194,0)="<tab>   ;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;**[patch list]**;Sep 27,1994 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,195,0)="Routines:        Before       After           Patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,196,0)="                 Check        Check           List"
