^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,240,0)="Required Patches:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,241,0)="================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,242,0)="LA*5.2*27"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,243,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,244,0)="LA*5.2*47 [Note: This is the Automated Instrument portion of LR*5.2*221]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,245,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,246,0)="LR*5.2*116"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,247,0)="LR*5.2*121"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,248,0)="LR*5.2*153"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,249,0)="LR*5.2*185"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,250,0)="LR*5.2*190"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,251,0)="LR*5.2*191"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,252,0)="LR*5.2*195"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,253,0)="LR*5.2*201"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,254,0)="LR*5.2*202"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,255,0)="LR*5.2*223"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,257,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,258,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,259,0)="This patch is compatible with OERR 2.5 and both versions of CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,260,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,261,0)="          1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,262,0)="          PackMan menu. This option will load the KIDS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,263,0)="          package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,264,0)="          2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,265,0)="          mapped, they should be removed from the mapped set"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,266,0)="          at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,267,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,268,0)="          3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,269,0)="          global on your system. You now need to use KIDS to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,270,0)="          install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,271,0)="          "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,272,0)="          On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,273,0)="          use the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,274,0)="                 Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,275,0)="                 Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,276,0)="                 Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,277,0)="                 Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,278,0)="          4. Users may remain on the system, but installation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,279,0)="             should be done during off peak hours and when"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,280,0)="             the Laboratory computer users are idle."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,281,0)="          5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,282,0)="          6. Installation time is less than 10 minutes during"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,283,0)="             offpeak hours, and less than 15 minutes during"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,284,0)="             peak hours which is NOT RECOMMENDED."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,285,0)="          7. Installation of this patch does not require any"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,286,0)="             additional memory space."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,287,0)="          8. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,288,0)="             run the option 'Install Package(s)'. Select the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,289,0)="             package 'LR*5.2*221' and proceed with the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,290,0)="             install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,291,0)="          9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,292,0)="             they should be returned to the mapped set once"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,293,0)="             the installation has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,294,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,295,0)="Enhancements:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,296,0)="============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,297,0)="1. The 'Etiology WKLD Code (Force)' [LRCAPF] option has been corrected to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,298,0)="accept WKLD Codes that do not have the suffix code of .0000 (Generic)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,299,0)="NOIS: CHY-0798-51245"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,300,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,301,0)="2. The WKLD Code capture routines have been modified not to count tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,302,0)="marked as 'Not Performed'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,303,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,304,0)="3. The 'Delete entire order or individual tests' [LRCENDEL] option has"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,305,0)="been modified to place tests in the status of  'Not Performed' rather than"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,306,0)="deleting the test or order from the file (database). Thus preventing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,307,0)="electronic white out of the ordered procedures. This enhancement corrects"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,308,0)="problems of undefined errors after tests have been deleted. NOISs:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,309,0)="ALN-1198-11196, ASH-0898-30554, ATG-0698-31312, WNY-0698-11221,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,310,0)="CLA-0598-20635 CMO-1198-41253, DEN-0898-50267, DUB-0898-30615,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,311,0)="FGH-1198-32348, GAI-0698-32344 HAM-1098-21436, LAS-0698-60208,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,312,0)="LEX-0898-41581, LEX-1198-40049, OM-0498-60788, MIN-0798-40025,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,313,0)="MON-0798-51662, MUS-1098-71863, NAS-1098-31373, OKL-0698-71939"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,314,0)="SAG-0498-42248, SLC-1198-50813, TAM-0798-30677, AM-1298-31153,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,315,0)="TOG-0898-11351"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,316,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,317,0)="4. The 'General report for selected tests' [LRGEN] option has been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,318,0)="corrected to display the full year and century with test results properly"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,319,0)="aligned when less than 19 tests were requested. There are hosts of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,320,0)="associated NOIS called. This may not represent a complete list. NOISs:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,321,0)="LEB-1298-22078, TAM-1298-31153, CLA-1198-22013, ALX-1198-71715,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,322,0)="ALX-0898-71684, ASH-0898-30675, BEC-0998-20129, BYN-0598-11025,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,323,0)="DAY-0798-42525, DEN-1098-50461, EKH-0998-40137, GAI-0898-30690,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,324,0)="GNH-0498-41065, HAM-0898-21544, HUN-0798-20942, LEB-1298-22078,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,325,0)="LOM-0498-60884, NAS-1098-31373, OKL-0698-70962, PHI-0598-20045,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,326,0)="PHO-1298-60877, SDC-0598-60879, SLC-0998-50822, WIC-0898-41805,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,327,0)="WPB-1198-31834"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,328,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,329,0)="5. The 'Group Verify (EA, EL, EW)' [LRGV] option has been enhanced to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,330,0)="store the Result NLT code with the verified results. The user cannot"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,331,0)="directly observe this."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,332,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,333,0)="6. The Clear instrument/worklist data [LRINSTCLR] option has been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,334,0)="enhanced. The changes to this option implements selective clearing of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,335,0)="instrument data from the LAH global. When entries are made in the LAH"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,336,0)="global to store instrument data pending verification, the date of creation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,337,0)="and result updating is now recorded. This date will be used to selectively"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,338,0)="remove data from the LAH global based on the date original result was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,339,0)="received or last updated."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,340,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,341,0)="The Clear instrument/worklist data [LRINSTCLR] option will now allow"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,342,0)="clearing by either of the following ways:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,343,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,344,0)="a. Data received before the selected date (optional time) is purged. If"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,345,0)="you enter a date only then data received before that date is cleared. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,346,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,347,0)="b. If you enter a date/time then data received before that date/time is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,348,0)="cleared."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,349,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,350,0)="Example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,351,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,352,0)="If you enter Sept 4, 1998 then data received through Sept 3, 1998 is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,353,0)="cleared. If you enter Sept 4, 1998 @1200 then data through Sept 4, 1998"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,354,0)="115959 is cleared."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,355,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,356,0)="The following routines support this enhancement:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,357,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,358,0)="a. LAGEN - Changes made to set date/time of entry creation and last"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,359,0)="update. Last update can be different than creation date if data is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,360,0)="retransmitted (overlay data = yes) or additional results received."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,361,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,362,0)="b. LRLLS - Clear instrument data option that does actual clearing based on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,363,0)="user's parameters. User can purge by date/time or blanket purge when using"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,364,0)="option Clear instrument/worklist data [LRINSTCLR]."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,365,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,366,0)="c. LRVR1 - Verifying routine with changes to setup date/time information"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,367,0)="when manual data entry is used during Enter/Verify Automated Instrument"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,368,0)="[LRVR] option."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,369,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,370,0)="d. LRVRW - Verifying routine with changes to setup date/time information"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,371,0)="when load/work list data entry is used during the Enter/verify data (Work"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,372,0)="list) [LRVRW] option. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,373,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,374,0)="e. If during the clearing process an entry in LAH is found with no"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,375,0)="date/time for creation/update then the current date/time is added to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,376,0)="entry. This entry is then eligible for clearing the next time the option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,377,0)="is run and it meets the date/time parameter."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,378,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,379,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,380,0)="7. The routine LRNUM has been modified to control the echo of stored data."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,381,0)="This is not readily apparent to the user."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,382,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,383,0)="8. The 'Order/test status' [LROS] option has been enhanced to display"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,384,0)="tests having the 'Not Performed' status. Also spacing was increased to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,385,0)="accommodate accession area abbreviation of 5 characters. NOIS:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,386,0)="WAS-1098-31246"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,387,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,388,0)="9. The 'Itemized routine lab collection' [LRPHITEM] option and 'Receipt of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,389,0)="routine lab collection from wards' [LRPHEXCPT] option has been enhanced to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,390,0)="conform to the 'Not Performed' status assignment. Order and accessioned"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,391,0)="tests are no longer deleted. NOIS: WNY-0998-11152"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,392,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,393,0)="10. The 'Interim report' [LRRP2] option has been enhanced to display"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,394,0)="orders that contain only 'Not Perform' status and no results entered or"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,395,0)="verified."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,396,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,397,0)="11. The option 'Turnaround times By Urgency' [LR TAT URGENCY] has been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,398,0)="modified to count only those tests that have been counted for Workload. In"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,399,0)="order for a test to be counted it must have WKLD Code assigned and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,400,0)="verified results. NOIS: BAY-0798-31877"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,401,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,402,0)="12. Various non-Microbiology Result Entry options were modified to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,403,0)="accommodate 'Not Performed' test status."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,404,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,405,0)="13. The option 'Ward lab menu' [LRWARDM] entry action routine has been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,406,0)="corrected not to set the variable LREND if no ward is selected. If no ward"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,407,0)="was selected unpredictable software behavior could result. NOISs:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,408,0)="FHM-0897-51017, NCH-0596-40125, CLA-0598-20356"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,409,0)="14. The INCOMPLETE TEST STATUS REPORT [LRWRKINC] option sorting/searching"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,410,0)="capability was enhanced."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,411,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,412,0)="Example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,413,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,414,0)="If you answer ""YES"" to the prompt: Specify detailed sort criteria? No//"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,415,0)="Then you will be able to specify:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,416,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,417,0)="   -  If controls should be excluded."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,418,0)="   -  Specific tests to search for."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,419,0)="   -  A lab arrival time. This will exclude uncollected specimens, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,420,0)="      and specimens with a later arrival time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,421,0)="   -  Exclude non-required tests."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,422,0)="   -  Exclude selected test(s) from report."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,423,0)="   -  If report is generated for specific test(s) which are "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,424,0)="      panels, then the user can have the report check the tests that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,425,0)="      make up the panel."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,426,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,427,0)="15. The 'Incomplete test status report' [LRWRKINC] option has been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,428,0)="modified to honor tests having 'Not Performed' status and not include them"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,429,0)="on the incomplete test list."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,430,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,431,0)="16. Test that have rolled over can be verified by either the original"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,432,0)="accession number or the rolled over accession number and the test will be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,433,0)="marked completed on both accession numbers. NOISs: CIN-0998-41790,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,434,0)="CMO-0998-41772, COS-0898-41373, NJH-1298-21603"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,435,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,436,0)="17. Correct problem of the Collection List not assigning correct accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,437,0)="numbers when queued in a multidivisional setting. NOIS: EKH-0998-40488"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,438,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,439,0)="18. Correct the option 'Interim report by provider' [LRRD] not correctly"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,440,0)="handling providers names with more than 20 characters. NOISs:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,441,0)="GAI-0698-31676, MWV-0598-21363, SAM-1098-20301"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,442,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,443,0)="19. Merged accessions [LRACC MERGE] will now download to auto-instruments."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,444,0)="Option would not accept partial accession number. Also merged tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,445,0)="maintain the primary ordered test linkage. NOISs: IOW-1298-41014,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,446,0)="BAN-0897-11956"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,447,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,448,0)="20. Incorrect data is extracted if the site has the 'COLLECT WKLD LOG FILE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,449,0)="DATA' field (#616) of the LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9) set to yes during"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,450,0)="DSS Workload extraction procedure. The DSS Package has exclusive rights to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,451,0)="the WKLD LOG file (#64.03). The DSS Coordinator must sanction any local"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,452,0)="field use of this file. This patch will set the field to null before"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,453,0)="starting to process workload extraction requests. Also the default"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,454,0)="provider was being extracted from the incorrect global location. NOIS:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,455,0)="PHO-0798-60573"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,456,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,457,0)="21. Corrects a typographical error in referencing the XTMP global. NOIS:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,458,0)="TAM-0698-31132"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,459,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,460,0)="22. The Merge Accessions [LRACC MERG] option has been modified to comply"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,461,0)="with NP protocol. The test(s) that are merged into another accession will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,462,0)="have NP designation set and a delete notification is sent to CPRS as a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,463,0)="Discontinued Order. The reverse is true for the accession receiving the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,464,0)="merged test."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,465,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,466,0)="23. During verification by automated instrument, using the Enter/verify"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,467,0)="data (auto instrument) [LRVR] option, Enter/verify data (Load list)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,468,0)="[LRVRW2] option or Enter/verify data (Work list) [LRVRW] option, the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,469,0)="building of the test list could cause an error when a user selects a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,470,0)="loadlist profile with many tests. This would create a string too long"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,471,0)="error. The lists of tests to be verified are now stored in the TMP global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,472,0)="instead of local arrays. This change will allow the site to place as many"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,473,0)="tests as required under a single profile. Collecting sites, using the LEDI"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,474,0)="software, will now be able to place all tests sent to a host lab under a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,475,0)="single profile on the worklist. The routines LRGP2 and LRVR1 have been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,476,0)="enhanced to correct this problem. NOISs: CHS-0398-42380,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,477,0)="MAD-1098-41673"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,478,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,479,0)="Examples:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,480,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,481,0)="Accessioning [LR IN] menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,482,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,483,0)="The name of the Delete entire order or individual tests [LRCENDEL] option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,484,0)="and Delete test from an accession [LRTSTOUT] option was not changed. Tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,485,0)="are no longer deleted but will have a disposition (status) of 'NOT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,486,0)="PERFORMED'. The test(s) will have a complete date assigned and will not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,487,0)="appear in Incomplete Load/Worklist. Both options use the same logic."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,488,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,489,0)="Select Accessioning menu Option: del"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,490,0)="    1    Delete entire order or individual tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,491,0)="    2    Delete test from an accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,492,0)="CHOOSE 1-2: 1  Delete entire order or individual tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,493,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,494,0)="ENTER ORDER NUMBER: 440"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,495,0)="Order  Test        Urgency   Status     Accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,496,0)="  -Lab Order # 440                           Provider: BEAR,GUMMY O."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,497,0)="  BLOOD    SERUM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,498,0)="  UREA NITROGEN     ROUTINE  Collected      01/05/1999@22:55 CH 0105 4"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,499,0)="   : ~For Test: UREA NITROGEN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,500,0)="   : ~DEMO NP option "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,501,0)="AARDVARK,JIMMY JR.            333-22-2444"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,502,0)="Change entire order? No// Y  (Yes)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,503,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,504,0)="Cancellation Reason: ?  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,505,0)=" Answer with ORDER REASON NAME, or SYNONYM, or CODE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,506,0)=" Do you want the entire ORDER REASON List? Y  (Yes)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,507,0)="Choose from:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,508,0)="   CLOTTED SPECIMEN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,509,0)="   DUPLICATE TESTS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,510,0)="   HEMOLYZED SPECIMEN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,511,0)="   INSUFFICIENT SPECIMEN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,512,0)="   OTHER CANCEL REASON"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,513,0)="   PATIENT UNAVAILABLE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,514,0)="   REQUESTING PHYSICIAN CANCELLED"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,515,0)="   SERVICE CORRECTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,516,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,517,0)="*[This next prompt is new - It allows the use of entries in the LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,518,0)="DESCRIPTION file (#62.5)  that have special screens. The default screens"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,519,0)="are GENERAL, ORDER and LAB. If you wish to include additional screens,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,520,0)="enter them here.]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,521,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,522,0)="Select NP comment Lab Description screen: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,523,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,524,0)="Not Perform Reason : NS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,525,0)="  (NO SPECIMEN RECEIVED) [Description file expanded text]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,526,0)="Satisfactory Comment ? Yes//   YES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,527,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,528,0)="*[This is what a not performed accession/order will look like.]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,529,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,530,0)="Select Accessioning menu Option: ORDER/Test status"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,531,0)="Select Patient Name:    AARDVARK,JIMMY JR.         04-04-44     333222444 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,532,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,533,0)="                           *** WARNING ***"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,534,0)="                       *** RESTRICTED RECORD ***"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,535,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,536,0)="DATE to begin review: TODAY//  (JAN 05, 1999)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,537,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,538,0)="  Test              Urgency   Status                            Accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,539,0)="  -Lab Order # 440                           Provider: BEAR,GUMMY O."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,540,0)="  BLOOD    SERUM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,541,0)="  UREA NITROGEN             *Canceled by: STALLING,FRANK  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,542,0)="   : *NP Reason:NO SPECIMEN RECEIVED"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,543,0)="   : *NP Action:01/05/1999@22:57"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,544,0)="   : ~For Test: UREA NITROGEN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,545,0)="   : ~DEMO NP option "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,546,0)="Orders for date: 01/04/1999  OK? Yes// ^"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,547,0)="Select Patient Name: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,548,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,549,0)="24. Lab Descriptions cancellation comments cannot contain a semicolon ';'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,550,0)="If semi-colon is entered, it will be converted to a dash '-'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,551,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,552,0)="25. The 'Accessioning test ordered by Ward order entry' [LROE] option now"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,553,0)="requires the user to enter a collection date/time. 'NOW' is an acceptable"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,554,0)="entry. The default answer to the question 'Do you have the entire order?'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,555,0)="has been removed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,556,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,557,0)="26. A new UID VERIFICATION field (#2.1) has been added to LOAD/WORKLIST"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,558,0)="file (#68.2), PROFILE multiple (#50)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,559,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,560,0)="Example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,561,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,562,0)="When verifying by Lab Universal Identifier (UID) the site can configure"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,563,0)="how accessions are selected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,564,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,565,0)="If ""PROFILE ACCESSION AREA ONLY"" is selected then only those UIDs which"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,566,0)="are from the accession area designated for this profile can be selected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,567,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,568,0)="If ""ANY ACCESSION AREA"" is selected then a UID from any accession area"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,569,0)="can be selected. Note that an accession from a different area should have"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,570,0)="tests that would be in this editing profile."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,571,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,572,0)="The routine LRVRA behavior is controlled by the entries in this field."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,573,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,574,0)="27. The routine LRVER1 has been enhanced to store LOINC code when tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,575,0)="are verified manually."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,576,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,577,0)="28. The LOCATION (#14.1) field in the LAB DATA file (#63) input transform"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,578,0)="has changed to conform to FileMan Version 22 variable cleanup."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,579,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,580,0)="29. The routine LRVR4 has been modified not to expand lab descriptions"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,581,0)="when processing instrument comments. This can have undesirable effects -"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,582,0)="expands comments when it is not required, makes comments too long and they"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,583,0)="will not be stored."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,584,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,585,0)="30. Incremental locks have been added to routines LROE and LR7OF5 to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,586,0)="correct CPRS orders not being receipted properly."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,587,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,588,0)="31. In the past, those entries in the LAB DESCRIPTION file (#62.5) not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,589,0)="having a screen defined would be expanded when entering comments. This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,590,0)="prevented the use of the same code for two different areas. For example 1+"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,591,0)="in microbiology may have a different expansion in blood bank. The software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,592,0)="logic has been enhanced to allow the same code to expand appropriately"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,593,0)="depending on the screen. The same code can be used more than once."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,594,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,595,0)="The following example displays how to determine which Lab Descriptions"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,596,0)="that does not have a screen using the Search and Edit combinations of VA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,597,0)="FileMan 21.0."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,598,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,599,0)="Examples:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,600,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,601,0)="VA FileMan 21.0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,602,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,603,0)="Select OPTION: SEARCH FILE ENTRIES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,604,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,605,0)="OUTPUT FROM WHAT FILE: LAB DESCRIPTIONS//"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,606,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,607,0)="  -A- SEARCH FOR LAB DESCRIPTIONS FIELD: SCREEN "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,608,0)="  -A- CONDITION: NULL  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,609,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,610,0)="  -B- SEARCH FOR LAB DESCRIPTIONS FIELD: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,611,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,612,0)="IF: A//     SCREEN NULL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,613,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,614,0)="STORE RESULTS OF SEARCH IN TEMPLATE: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,615,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,616,0)="SORT BY: NAME// "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,617,0)="START WITH NAME: FIRST// "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,618,0)="FIRST PRINT FIELD: .01  NAME  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,619,0)="THEN PRINT FIELD: EXPANSION    "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,620,0)="THEN PRINT FIELD: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,621,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,622,0)="  *************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,623,0)="Heading (S/C): LAB DESCRIPTIONS SEARCH  Replace "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,624,0)="DEVICE:   TELNET    Right Margin: 80// "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,625,0)="LAB DESCRIPTIONS SEARCH                        MAY 10,1999  10:36    PAGE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,626,0)=1
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,627,0)="NAME   EXPANSION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,628,0)="-------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,629,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,630,0)="DV     TEST PERFORMED AT DALLAS, TX VAMC LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,631,0)="LX     TEST PERFORMED AT LEXINGTON, KY VAMC LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,632,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,633,0)="                         2 MATCHES FOUND."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,634,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,635,0)="Using the results of the search edit those Lab Description(s) missing a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,636,0)="screen."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,637,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,638,0)="Select OPTION: ENTER OR EDIT FILE ENTRIES  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,639,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,640,0)="INPUT TO WHAT FILE: LAB DESCRIPTIONS// "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,641,0)="EDIT WHICH FIELD: ALL// .01  NAME  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,642,0)="THEN EDIT FIELD: SCREEN    "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,643,0)="THEN EDIT FIELD: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,644,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,645,0)="Select LAB DESCRIPTIONS NAME: DV          TEST PERFORMED AT DALLAS, TX"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,646,0)="VAMC LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,647,0)="NAME: DV// "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,648,0)="SCREEN: ?"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,649,0)="     Choose from: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,650,0)="       L        LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",79,1,651,0)="       E        AP EM"
