^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,77,0)="        Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,78,0)="        =========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,79,0)="        1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,80,0)="           option will load the KIDS package in this message onto your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,81,0)="           system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,82,0)="        2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they should"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,83,0)="           be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,84,0)="        3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,85,0)="           system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,86,0)="           global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,87,0)="           On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,88,0)="           following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,89,0)="               Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,90,0)="               Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,91,0)="               Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,92,0)="               Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,93,0)="        4. Users may remain on the system, but installation should be done"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,94,0)="           at off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,95,0)="        5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,96,0)="        6. Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak hours"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,97,0)="           and less than 5 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,98,0)="        7. Installation of this patch requires no additional memory space."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,99,0)="        8. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,100,0)="           'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*242' and proceed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,101,0)="           with the install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,102,0)="        9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,103,0)="           returned to the mapped set once the installation has run to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",89,1,104,0)="           completion."
