^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,1,0)="A Y2K problem was logged in NOIS regarding the reports generated in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,2,0)="'[LRAPSEARCH] Search options, anat path' menu.  This menu performs searches on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,3,0)="Anatomic Pathology accessions based on morphology, disease, etiology,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,4,0)="procedure, function, or diagnosis code.  The menu is shown below:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,6,0)="   MC     MORPHOLOGY code search, SNOMED [LRAPSM]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,7,0)="   DC     DISEASE code search, SNOMED [LRAPSD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,8,0)="   EC     ETIOLOGY code search, SNOMED [LRAPSE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,9,0)="   PC     PROCEDURE code search, SNOMED [LRAPSP]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,10,0)="   FC     FUNCTION code search, SNOMED [LRAPSF]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,11,0)="   IC     ICD9CM code search [LRAPSI]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,12,0)="   AX     MULTIAXIAL code search, SNOMED [LRAPSEM]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,14,0)="NOIS calls were logged because data was being omitted from the reports for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,15,0)="year 2000 accessions.  Below is an example of the report generated by menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,16,0)="item '[LRAPSM] MORPHOLOGY code search, SNOMED':"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,18,0)="SURGICAL PATHOLOGY (SP) SEARCH(Dec 30, 1999=>Jan 03, 2000)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,19,0)=" # = Not VA patient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,20,0)="SNOMED TOPOGRAPHY CODE: ALL--                 SNOMED MORPHOLOGY CODE: ALL--"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,21,0)="-----------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,22,0)="        NAME       ID  SEX AGE  ACC #      ORGAN/TISSUE       MORPHOLOGY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,23,0)="HOBBS,JOHN H       9801  M 63  SP 99 4814     SKIN OF CHEST   BASAL CELL CARCI"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,24,0)="                                                              RX0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,25,0)="                                              SKIN OF HEAD    BASAL CELL CARCI"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,26,0)="                                                              RX0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,27,0)="JENKINS,CLARENCE   3133  M 41  SP 99 4808     TRACHEA         HEMORRHAGE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,28,0)="LAMBE,NORMAN B.    5487  M"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,29,0)="MONEY,CLAUDE C     4599  M"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,30,0)="NELSON,DIANE M     4856  F"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,31,0)="NELSON,KENNETH R   1674  M 51  SP 99 4820     SKIN OF UPPER E PSORIASIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,32,0)="OWENS,ERNEST D     5310  M"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,34,0)="Notice that some of the names listed show no data in the Age, Acc #,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,35,0)="Organ/tissue, and Morphology columns.  These are year 2000 accessions.  All"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,36,0)="1999 accessions still reported correctly."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,38,0)="It was discovered that the two digit year was being used as a subscript in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,39,0)="the ^TMP global which stores that data temporarily so that it may be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,40,0)="printed.  The two digit year subscript is extracted from dates in the LAB DATA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,41,0)="file (#63) as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,43,0)="Surgical Pathology:  DATE/TIME SPECIMEN RECEIVED field (#.1) of SURGICAL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,44,0)="                     PATHOLOGY (sub-field #8, Sub-file #63.08)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,45,0)="Cytopathology:       DATE/TIME SPECIMEN RECEIVED field (#.1) of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,46,0)="                     CYTOPATHOLOGY (sub-field #9, Sub-file #63.09)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,47,0)="Electron Microscopy: DATE/TIME SPECIMEN RECEIVED field (#.1) of EM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,48,0)="                     (sub-field #2, Sub-file #63.02)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,49,0)="Autopsy:             AUTOPSY DATE/TIME field (#11)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,51,0)="The year subscript is created by extracting the second and third characters"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,52,0)="of the date.  For example, if the date is 2991031.0800, the year subscript"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,53,0)="will be 99.  If the date is 3001031.0800, the year subscript will be 00."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,55,0)="Here is an example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,57,0)="^TMP(545305223,99,2) = AU 99 2^20^M^WINKERBEAN,FUNKY^5533^10/14^2"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,58,0)="^TMP(545305223,99,2,151,0) = BRAIN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,59,0)="^TMP(545305223,99,2,151,41770) = ABSCESS, DRAINING"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,60,0)="^TMP(545305223,""00"",1) = AU 00 1^81^M^FULTON,CHESTER E.^5537^1/13^2"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,61,0)="^TMP(545305223,""00"",1,395,0) = SKIN BETWEEN FOURTH AND FIFTH TOES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,62,0)="^TMP(545305223,""00"",1,395,""02060"") = SADDLE SHAPE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,64,0)="The second subscript is the two digit year.  Subscript ""00"" was confusing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,65,0)="the code causing it to quit before executing the portion of code that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,66,0)="prints the age, accession number, organ/tissue, and morphology."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,68,0)="The problem has been corrected by including the century indicator when"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,69,0)="creating the second subscript.  For year 1999, the subscript will be 299."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,70,0)="For year 2000, the subscript will be 300.  See below:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,72,0)="^TMP(545305223,299,2) = AU 99 2^20^M^WINKERBEAN,FUNKY^5533^10/14^2"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,73,0)="^TMP(545305223,299,2,151,0) = BRAIN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,74,0)="^TMP(545305223,299,2,151,41770) = ABSCESS, DRAINING"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,75,0)="^TMP(545305223,300,1) = AU 00 1^81^M^FULTON,CHESTER E.^5537^1/13^2"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,76,0)="^TMP(545305223,300,1,395,0) = SKIN BETWEEN FOURTH AND FIFTH TOES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,77,0)="^TMP(545305223,300,1,395,""02060"") = SADDLE SHAPE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,79,0)="This change to the ^TMP global structure has corrected the problem."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",91,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",92,0)="245 SEQ #191^3000125^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",92,1,0)="^^3^3^3000125"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",92,1,1,0)="This is a patch for VISTA Laboratory Software, version 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",92,1,2,0)="A detailed description of this patch is included in the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",92,1,3,0)="distribution message."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",93,0)="246 SEQ #192^3000125^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",93,1,0)="^^3^3^3000125"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",93,1,1,0)="This is a patch for VISTA Laboratory Software, version 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",93,1,2,0)="A detailed description of this patch is included in the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",93,1,3,0)="distribution message."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",94,0)="240 SEQ #193^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",94,1,0)="^^2^2^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",94,1,1,0)="This patch fixes an UNDEF in the routine LRVER1 at line EX2+1.  This is a patch "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",94,1,2,0)="to patch LR*5.2*239."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,0)="206 SEQ #194^3000501^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,0)="^^68^68^3000501"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,1,0)="  This patch fixes the following problems in the option Add a new"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,2,0)="  data name [LRWU5] that allows you to add a new data name to the LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,3,0)="  DATA file (#63)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,5,0)="  1.  Option does not allow you to enter a value less than zero for the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,6,0)="      minimum or maximum value for numeric data names."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,8,0)="  2.  Option does not allow you to designate decimals for the minimum or"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,9,0)="      maximum value for numeric data names."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,11,0)="  This patch to the Laboratory package does not contain any changes to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,12,0)="  VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,13,0)="  VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,15,0)="  Associated NOIS: NOL-1197-71309"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,17,0)="        Test Site: Asheville, NC "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,18,0)="                   Montgomery, AL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,19,0)="                   Muskogee, OK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,20,0)="                   New Orleans, LA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,22,0)="   Reporting Site: New Orleans, LA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,25,0)=" ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,26,0)=" ==============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,28,0)="  The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,30,0)="  <tab>     ;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;**[patch list]**; Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,32,0)="                        Checksum Values"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,34,0)="  Routine Name       Before Patch    After Patch    Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,35,0)="  ------------       ------------    -----------    ----------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,36,0)="  LRWU5                13485455       11320832      140,171,177,206"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,39,0)="  Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,40,0)="  ========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,41,0)="   It is recommended that this release be installed during off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,43,0)="    1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,44,0)="       This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,45,0)="       system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,46,0)="    2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they should"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,47,0)="       be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,48,0)="    3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,49,0)="       system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,50,0)="            On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,51,0)="            following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,52,0)="                Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,53,0)="                Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,54,0)="                Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,55,0)="                Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,56,0)="    4. Users may remain on system and no options need to be placed out of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,57,0)="       service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,58,0)="    5. Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak hours"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,59,0)="       and less than 5 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,60,0)="    6. Installation of this patch requires no additional memory space."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,61,0)="    7. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,62,0)="       'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*206' and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,63,0)="       proceed with the install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,64,0)="    8. When Prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,65,0)="       YES//', respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,66,0)="    9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,67,0)="       returned to the mapped set once the installation has run to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",95,1,68,0)="       completion."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,0)="254 SEQ #195^3000525^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,0)="^^95^95^3000525"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,1,0)="This patch to the Laboratory package does not contain any changes to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,2,0)="VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled VISTA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,3,0)="BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,5,0)="This patch will install the CareVue interface package under the namespace"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,6,0)="LA7D as a Class I national patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,8,0)="1. Problem:  Current CareVue interface is Class III software."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,10,0)="   Solution: The code has been validated, brought up to national"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,11,0)="             standard and released as a Class I national patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,13,0)="This patch can be installed as a stand-alone if CareVue package is not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,14,0)="needed, however if CareVue IS NEEDED then patch LA*5.2*53 MUST be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,15,0)="installed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,17,0)="The laboratory routines LRVER3A and LRMIUT have been modified to work with"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,18,0)="this interface.  These routines have been locally modified at the sites"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,19,0)="and the sites must ensure that precautions are taken to prevent loss of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,20,0)="local modifications when patches to Laboratory are installed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,22,0)="Associated NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,23,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,24,0)="None"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,26,0)="Test Sites"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,27,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,28,0)="Philadelphia, PA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,29,0)="Martinsburg, WVA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,31,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,32,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,33,0)="The following is a list of routines included in this patch.  The second"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,34,0)="line of each routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,36,0)="<tab>;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;**[patch list]**;;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,38,0)="        CHECK^XTSUMBLD Results"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,40,0)="Routine Name    Before Patch     After Patch   Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,41,0)="------------    ------------     -----------   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,43,0)="LRVER3A           9561045        10780359      1,5,42,100,121,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,44,0)="                                               153,190,221,254"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,45,0)="LRMIUT            3226335         3673249      254"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,47,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,48,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,49,0)="The patch is distributed in KIDS format in a PackMan message."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,51,0)="     1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,52,0)="        This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,53,0)="        your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,55,0)="     2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,56,0)="        should be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,58,0)="     3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,59,0)="        your system. You now need to use KIDS to install the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,60,0)="        Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,62,0)="        On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,63,0)="        following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,64,0)="           Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,65,0)="           Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,66,0)="           Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,67,0)="           Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,69,0)="     4. It is recommended that this release be installed during off"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,70,0)="        peak hours.  To prevent a possible problem with the tasking"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,71,0)="        of the next days laboratory orders, do not install this package"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,72,0)="        at the same time as the following nightly tasked jobs:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,74,0)="              LRTASK ROLLOVER"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,75,0)="              LRTASK NIGHTLY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,76,0)="              LRTASK CONJAM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,77,0)="              LRTASK CUM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,79,0)="     5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,81,0)="     6. Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,82,0)="        hours and less than 5 minutes during peak hours"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,84,0)="     7. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,85,0)="        option 'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*254'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,86,0)="        and proceed with the install. When prompted 'Want to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,87,0)="        DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,88,0)="        YES//', choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,90,0)="     8. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,91,0)="        should be returned to the mapped set once the installation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,92,0)="        has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,93,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,94,0)="     9. Please refer to Patch LA*5.2*53 for further instructions "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",96,1,95,0)="        regarding CareVue.               "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,0)="243 SEQ #196^3000626^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,0)="^^929^929^3000626"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,3,0)="Subject: CPT CODE MODIFIERS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,5,0)="Category: DATA DICTIONARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,6,0)="          ENHANCEMENT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,7,0)="          ROUTINE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,9,0)="Description:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,10,0)="============"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,12,0)="The Laboratory CPT Code Modifier enhancement patch LR*5.2*243 provides the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,13,0)="Laboratory Version 5.2 software application the ability to transmit"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,14,0)="Current Procedural Terminology (CPT) codes and Modifiers to the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,15,0)="Care Encounter (PCE) workload capture Application Interface (API). The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,16,0)="transmission of workload in the form of CPT codes is done in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,17,0)="background (no user interaction is required). Because of the background"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,18,0)="method of workload reporting several new fields were created and the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,19,0)="Laboratory software logic was modified."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,21,0)="CPT modifier provides the means by which the reporting physician can"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,22,0)="indicate that a service or procedure that has been performed has been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,23,0)="altered by some specific circumstances but not changed in its definition"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,24,0)="or code. The judicious application of modifiers obviates the necessity for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,25,0)="separate procedure listing that may describe the modifying circumstances."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,28,0)="NOTE: ONLY PATIENT ORDERS FROM HOSPITAL LOCATION WITH THE TYPE OF CLINIC,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,29,0)="MODULE, OR OTHER WILL RECEIVE CPT WORKLOAD CREDIT. THE SOFTWARE USES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,30,0)="LOCATION TYPE TO DETERMINE IF THE ORDER IS FOR AN OUT-PATIENT OR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,31,0)="IN-PATIENT."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,33,0)="Enhancements and Modifications:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,34,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,36,0)="Laboratory CPT Code Modifiers Patch LR*5.2*243 contains the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,37,0)="enhancements and changes:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,39,0)="NOTE: The asterisk ('*') indicates significant enhancements or file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,40,0)="structure changes. Two asterisks ('**') indicate new fields that will be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,41,0)="used by subsequent releases."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,43,0)="*1. The CPT Code Modifiers Patch LR*5.2*243 patch automatically removes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,44,0)="CPT workload credit for any test(s) with the status of NOT PERFORMED (NP)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,46,0)="*2. When the Laboratory workload reporting LRNIGHTY background job is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,47,0)="tasked, a secondary program examines the WKLD CODE file (#64) to determine"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,48,0)="if any CPT code(s) are inactive in the CPT file (#81) or if other file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,49,0)="pointers are broken. If inactive code(s) are found, a VA Mailman message"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,50,0)="is automatically generated and sent once a day to the LMI Mail Group"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,51,0)="containing information about the code(s) and the action(s) taken by the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,52,0)="software."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,54,0)="*3. The enhanced Laboratory workload software processes the workload data"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,55,0)="in LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9), PCE DEFAULT PROVIDER field (#617) and LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,56,0)="OOS LOCATION field (#.8) even if these two fields are not defined. A VA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,57,0)="Mailman report is automatically generated and sent to the LMI mail group"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,58,0)="once a day indicating those orders requiring additional attention because"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,59,0)="the default fields were not defined."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,61,0)="*4. The automated Venipuncture workload reporting functionality used the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,62,0)="same criteria as the Laboratory workload reporting."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,64,0)="5. The enhanced Laboratory software will now acknowledge the actual user"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,65,0)="entering lab test orders in LAB ORDER ENTRY file (#69) for the PCE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,66,0)="Registered Encounter rather than the user that started or tasked the PCE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,67,0)="Workload background job."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,69,0)="6. The LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9) locking logic is modified to correct"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,70,0)="the problem of not being able to edit the LABORATORY SITE file (#69) while"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,71,0)="the LRNIGHTY background job is running."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,72,0)="Option Changes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,74,0)="*7. Add tests to a given accession [LRADD TO ACC] option is modified to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,75,0)="activate the PCE Workload API. Any test(s) added to an accession will now"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,76,0)="receive PCE Workload credit."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,78,0)="8. Order/test status [LROS] option is modified to correctly display"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,79,0)="test(s) added to an accession."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,81,0)="9. Enter/verify data (auto instrument) [LRVR] option is enhanced to allow"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,82,0)="users to edit, add, or subtract atomic test(s) from the test list before"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,83,0)="beginning the verification of an atomic test(s) and to continue to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,84,0)="next accession number if the current accession is not collected. This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,85,0)="enhancement applies to both verifying by accession number or UID"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,86,0)="(Universal Identification)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,88,0)="*10. Batch data entry [LRSTUF] option is modified to capture LMIP workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,89,0)="counts."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,91,0)="11. Results entry (batch) [LRMISTUF] is modified to capture LMIP workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,92,0)="counts."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,93,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,94,0)="12. The Bypass normal data entry [LRFAST] option is modified to accept the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,95,0)="response of ""YES"" at the ""Do you want to enter draw times?"" prompt."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,97,0)="13. The Accessioning tests ordered by ward order entry [LROE] option is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,98,0)="modified to accurately determine if the tasked ROLLOVER ACCESSION [LRTASK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,99,0)="ROLLOVER] option is actually running."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,101,0)="14. The Review by order number [LRCENLKUP] option date displays is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,102,0)="converted to use Kernel date conversion utilities."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,104,0)="15. Edit or Print WKLD CODES [LR WKLD CODE EDIT PRINT] option is enhanced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,105,0)="to print all WKLD CODES, even if they have not been activated. This will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,106,0)="correct the problem of WKLD CODES that have a suffix of .0000 not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,107,0)="printing."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,108,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,109,0)="16. Workload Report [LRCAPR1] option has been enhanced to allow the user"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,110,0)="to select combinations of LEDI collecting institutions or Hospital"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,111,0)="locations."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,113,0)="17. When verifying Microbiology specimens the user is prompted for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,114,0)="additional workload. A screen has been added to allow only a number"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,115,0)="between 1 to 25. This is to prevent inadvertent entering of WKLD CODE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,116,0)="number instead of the multiply by number."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,118,0)="Laboratory Menu and Option Changes:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,119,0)="============================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,120,0)="LIM workload menu [LR LIM/WKLD MENU]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,122,0)="The LIM workload menu [LR LIM/WKLD MENU] is modified to add the new"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,123,0)="InActive WKLD CODE File CPT Codes Print [LRCAPCPTI] option."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,125,0)="New Option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,127,0)="InActive WKLD CODE File CPT Codes Print [LRCAPCPTI] option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,129,0)="The new Inactive WKLD CODE File CPT Codes Print [LRCAPCPTI] option scans"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,130,0)="the WKLD CODE file (#64) for code(s) that are no longer allowed or code(s)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,131,0)="that are inactive in the CPT file (#81). The ""WKLD CODE - CODE CHECK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,132,0)="REPORT"" is then generated displaying all CPT code(s) that are no longer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,133,0)="allowed, code(s) that are inactive and why they are inappropriate,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,134,0)="laboratory test names linked to WKLD code(s) (i.e., laboratory test names"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,135,0)="listed on the report will not receive PCE Workload credit), and code(s)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,136,0)="requiring a different entry in the CPT file (#81) in order to capture PCE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,137,0)="Workload data."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,138,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,139,0)="The new Inactive WKLD CODE File CPT Codes Print [LRCAPCPTI] option is also"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,140,0)="useful when a new CPT Code file is released (i.e., new CPT code files are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,141,0)="usually distributed annually). The new CPT Code files may contain codes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,142,0)="that are no longer allowed or codes that are inactive in the VISTA CPT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,143,0)="file (#81). When CPT codes defined in the WKLD CODE file (#64) are deemed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,144,0)="inactive in the CPT file (#81), then the software enters a date in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,145,0)="WKLD CODE file (#64), Inactive Date field (#3) for those inactive codes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,146,0)="The Laboratory PCE interface checks each CPT code in the WKLD CODE file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,147,0)="(#64) before sending CPT workload to the PCE API. Whenever CPT code(s) are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,148,0)="no longer allowed or has been inactivated a VA Mailman message containing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,149,0)="the ""WKLD CODE - CODE CHECK REPORT"" is sent once a day to the LMI mail"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,150,0)="group."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,151,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,152,0)="Example: WKLD CODE - CODE CHECK REPORT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,154,0)="Subj: WKLD CODE - CODE CHECK REPORT 12/14/99@14:44:25  [#83460]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,155,0)="From: POSTMASTER  In 'IN' basket.   Page 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,156,0)="-----------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,157,0)="Lab Order Number 100 has no Institution for the ordering location"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,158,0)="==================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,159,0)="86081.0000 [1]  ABO Cell and Rh(D) Typing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,160,0)="86083  BLOOD TYPING;ANTIBODY SCREEN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,161,0)="Is an inactive CPT code."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,162,0)="Associated Tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,163,0)="     ABO/RH TYPING  {1101}"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,164,0)="Inactivation date of Dec 13, 1999 has been entered"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,165,0)="****************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,166,0)="Listing of all offending codes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,167,0)="   ICPT     82534"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,168,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,169,0)="****** END OF EXAMPLE ********"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,171,0)="====================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,172,0)="Data Dictionary Change Summary:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,174,0)="The following file and field changes occur with the installation of VISTA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,175,0)="Laboratory CPT Code and Modifiers Patch LR*5.2*243."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,177,0)="WKLD CODE file (#64)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,178,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,179,0)=" The WKLD CODE file (#64) was modified to convert existing file data to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,180,0)="a new data structure, new fields were created, and existing fields were"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,181,0)="modified to support the Laboratory workload reporting enhancements of CPT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,182,0)="codes and modifiers."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,183,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,184,0)="1) CODE field (#18) multiple has been changed from a free text field to a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,185,0)="variable pointer."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,187,0)="2) CODE field (#.01) has been changed from a free text field to a variable"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,188,0)="pointer. This field is screened to allow only active code entries to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,189,0)="MORPHOLOGY FIELD file (#61.1), ICD DIAGNOSIS file (#80), and CPT file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,190,0)="(#81)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,191,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,192,0)="3) CODE subfile (#64.018) was modified to add the new CODE NOTES field"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,193,0)="(#6). This new word processing field is used for tracking general notes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,194,0)="regarding a particular code."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,195,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,196,0)="4) WKLD Code Notes field (#24) is a new word processing field used for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,197,0)="storing general notes regarding inactive or erroneous code(s) that is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,198,0)="automatically removed by the software."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,200,0)="5) LOINC Code field (#4) was changed to point to the LOINC CODE file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,201,0)="(#95.3)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,202,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,203,0)="6) The new Default LOINC Code field (#25) points to the LOINC CODE file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,204,0)="(#95.3).  This field is used to identify the default LOINC code.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,205,0)="field is usually used when the specimen is not clinically significant"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,206,0)="(i.e. body fluids). 'L FOR LOINC' was removed from the set of codes in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,207,0)="field TYPE (#64.018,5)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,208,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,209,0)="LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,210,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,211,0)="1) LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9), DIVISION PARAMETERS field (#618) multiple"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,212,0)="is a new field exported with this patch. These new fields are used to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,213,0)="customize the automated Venipuncture workload reporting functionality."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,214,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,215,0)="2) The new DIVISION PARAMETERS field (#.01) points to the INSTITUTION file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,216,0)="(#4). This field allows the LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9) to be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,217,0)="multi-divisional for Venipuncture workload reporting."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,218,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,219,0)="3) The new VENIPUNCTURE DEFAULT ACC AREA subfile (#618) points to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,220,0)="ACCESSION file (#68). This new field is used by the Venipuncture workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,221,0)="reporting background job to determine the accession area for the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,222,0)="INSTITUTION to be use for Venipuncture workload reporting."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,223,0)="Associated NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,224,0)="==============="
