^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,297,0)="Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,298,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,299,0)="************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,300,0)="LABORATORY CURRENT PROCEDURAL TERMINOLOGY (CPT) CODES AND MODIFIERS PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,301,0)="LR*5.2*243 INSTALLATION AND IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE in PDF format is provided"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,302,0)="with this patch. Please refer to this document for details and specific"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,303,0)="instructions. The patch description does not include ALL implementation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,304,0)="considerations or complete file setup instructions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,305,0)="************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,306,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,307,0)="The VISTA Laboratory CPT Codes and Modifiers Patch LR*5.2*243 Installation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,308,0)="and Implementation Guide is available in PDF (i.e., LR_CPTIG.PDF) at the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,309,0)="following FTP addresses:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,310,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,311,0)="Office of Information Field Office FTP Address               Directory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,312,0)="======================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,313,0)="Albany                       152.127.1.5            anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,314,0)="Hines                        152.131.2.110          anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,315,0)="Salt Lake City               152.131.2.1            anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,316,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,317,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,318,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,319,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,320,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,321,0)="Users may remain on the system, but installation should be done during off"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,322,0)="peak hours and when the Laboratory computer users are idle. None of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,323,0)="laboratory tasked jobs need to be stopped."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,324,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,325,0)="         1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,326,0)="         menu. This option will load the KIDS package onto your  system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,327,0)="         2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,328,0)="         they should be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,329,0)="         3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,330,0)="         on your system. You now need to use KIDS to install the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,331,0)="         Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,332,0)="         4. On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,333,0)="         following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,334,0)="                Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,335,0)="                Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,336,0)="                Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,337,0)="                Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,338,0)="         5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,339,0)="         6. Installation time is less than 15 minutes during off peak"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,340,0)="            hours,and less than 30 minutes during"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,341,0)="            peak hours which is NOT RECOMMENDED."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,342,0)="         7. Installation of this patch require minimal "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,343,0)="            disk space."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,344,0)="         8. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,345,0)="            'Install Package(s)'. Select the package "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,346,0)="            'LR*5.2*243' and proceed with the install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,347,0)="         9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,348,0)="            should be returned to the mapped set once the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,349,0)="            installation has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,350,0)="           "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,351,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,352,0)="Example of install dialog:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,353,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,354,0)="Select INSTALL NAME:    LR*5.2*243     Loaded from Distribution"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,355,0)="2/29/00@15:51:34"
