^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,441,0)="**** End of Example of Install dialog *******"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,442,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,443,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,444,0)="Post Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,445,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,446,0)="After the new file structures have been installed the post installation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,447,0)="software will perform the following:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,448,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,449,0)="1. Review each code to determine if the code is valid and has not been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,450,0)="inactivated in the CPT file (#81). If the code is inactive or erroneous,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,451,0)="the code is removed. The software will record the code removal in the WKLD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,452,0)="CODE NOTES field (#24). A MailMan message addressed to the local LMI mail"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,453,0)="group will be generated if any codes are removed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,454,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,455,0)="2. The data in the file is converted to the new data structure of the WKLD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,456,0)="CODE file (#64)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,457,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,458,0)="3. ASSOCIATED NAMES in the WKLD CODE file (#64) are updated to reflect"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,459,0)="current linkages."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,460,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,461,0)="4. The Post Installation routine will set the WKLD CODE (#64) file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,462,0)="BILLABLE PROCEDURE (#4) field to yes for the codes:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,463,0)="Venipunture Outpatient [89343.0000]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,464,0)="Venipunture Travel Time [89341.0000]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,465,0)="**** Note: If the laboratory is does not perform venipuncture functions,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,466,0)="the BILLIABLE PROCEDURE field should be set to 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,467,0)="'Edit or Print WKLD CODES [LR WKLD CODE EDIT PRINT] option can be used to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,468,0)="edit the BILLABLE PROCEDURE field."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,469,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,470,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,471,0)="************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,472,0)="LABORATORY CURRENT PROCEDURAL TERMINOLOGY (CPT) CODES AND MODIFIERS PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,473,0)="LR*5.2*243 INSTALLATION AND IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE in PDF format is provided"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,474,0)="with this patch. Please refer to this document for details and specific"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,475,0)="instructions. The patch description does not include ALL implementation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,476,0)="considerations or complete file setup instructions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,477,0)="************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,478,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,479,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,480,0)="PCE Workload Capture Setup:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,481,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,482,0)="The Laboratory Information Manager (LIM) or the Information Resource"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,483,0)="Management (IRM) service must do setup several procedure files/fields."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,484,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,485,0)="NOTE: The asterisk (*) indicates new enhancements for patch LR*5.2*243."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,486,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,487,0)="1. The LAB SERVICE package V. 5.2 must be installed. This is done by IRM."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,488,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,489,0)="2. PCE workload must be turned on for Laboratory. Someone other than the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,490,0)="LIM usually does this."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,491,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,492,0)="3. PCE PATIENT CARE ENCOUNTER Version 1.0 must be loaded on the system and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,493,0)="fully patched.  This is done by IRM."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,494,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,495,0)="4. The LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9), WKLD STATS ON field (#17) must be set"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,496,0)="to YES. This is usually done by the LIM."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,497,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,498,0)="5. The LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9), PCE/VSIT ON field (#615) definition"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,499,0)="entry should be defined other than OFF, the recommended entry is PCE/VSIT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,500,0)="ONLY. The VA FileMan Enter Edit [DIEDIT] option is used to defined the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,501,0)="PCE/VSIT ON field (#615). This is done by the LIM or IRM."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,502,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,503,0)="6. The LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9), PCE DEFAULT PROVIDER field (#617)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,504,0)="should have a valid active provider identified. This is usually the Chief"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,505,0)="of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine (P&LMS). The PCE DEFAULT PROVIDER"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,506,0)="field (#617) in the past was required for the background job to run. This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,507,0)="patch no longer requires a valid entry in this field. This field is used"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,508,0)="whenever the ordering provider is not a valid active provider; the default"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,509,0)="provider is substituted instead of the inactive provider. If the ordering"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,510,0)="provider and the default provider are both invalid the order will be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,511,0)="marked and skipped. A report will be sent to the local mail group G.LMI"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,512,0)="indicating the observed problem. This usually done by the LIM."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,513,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,514,0)="7. The LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9), DEFAULT LAB OOS LOCATION (#.8) field"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,515,0)="must have a valid HOSPITAL LOCATION defined. This field is defined by"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,516,0)="using the Create Laboratory OOS Locations [LR WKLD LOCATION] option. This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,517,0)="option will correctly name the DEFAULT LAB OOS location entry. This is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,518,0)="usually done by the LIM."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,519,0)="NOTE: This is a critical field entry. The CPT Workload capture will not be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,520,0)="performed if this field has no entry or the entry is correct. All DEFAULT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,521,0)="LAB OOS LOCATION names must begin with 'LAB DIV '"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,522,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,523,0)="8. The MAILMAN SITE PARAMETERS file (#4.3), DEFAULT INSTITUTION field"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,524,0)="(#217) must be defined. This is done by IRM."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,525,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,526,0)="* 9. The LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9), DEFAULT BLOOD SPECIMEN field (#100)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,527,0)="must have a valid blood specimen defined. This is done by the LIM."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,528,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,529,0)="10. Each Accession area that should have workload collected must have the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,530,0)="accession area activated. The accession area is activated by using the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,531,0)="Turn on workload stats for accession area [LR WKLD STATS ON ACC AREA]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,532,0)="option. This is done by the LIM."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,533,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,534,0)="11. Each accession area can have a default Occasion of Service (OOS)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,535,0)="location defined. This allows each accession area to be assigned a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,536,0)="specific DEFAULT OOS LOCATION. Multi-divisional sites most often use this."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,537,0)="The default OOS location can be defined by using the Edit ACC Area OOS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,538,0)="Locations [LR WKLD ACC AREA LOCATION] option. A DEFAULT OOS LOCATION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,539,0)="should be defined for each institution generating workload. This is done"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,540,0)="by the LIM."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,541,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,542,0)="12. Every orderable test in LABORATORY TEST file (#60) must be linked to a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,543,0)="NATIONAL VA LAB CODE (also referred to as WKLD CODE or NLT codes). The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,544,0)="NATIONAL VA LAB CODE is linked by using the Semi-automatic Linking of file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,545,0)="60 to 64 [LR7O 60-64 AUTO] and Manual Linking of file 60 to 64 [LR7O 60-64"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,546,0)="MANUAL] options. This is done by the LIM."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,547,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,548,0)="13. Each WKLD CODE linked in the above step must be assigned valid CPT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,549,0)="codes, these CPT codes will be used to report workload to the Patient Care"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,550,0)="Encounter (PCE) workload API. This is done by using the Edit or Print WKLD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,551,0)="CODES [LR WKLD CODE EDIT PRINT] option. This is done by the LIM."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,552,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,553,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,554,0)="Software Logic:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,555,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,556,0)="After the file setup steps have been completed, the software logic of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,557,0)="background job will use the above-defined fields. The software will scan"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,558,0)="collected orders, extract all valid CPT codes, and pass the CPT workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,559,0)="data to the PCE workload API. In addition, the software will also will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,560,0)="capture LMIP venipuncture workload for ALL patients without regard for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,561,0)="location type."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,562,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,563,0)="NOTE: Outpatient locations are entries in HOSPITAL LOCATION file (#44)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,564,0)="that have the TYPE field (#2) defined as; CLINIC, MODULE or OTHER."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,565,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,566,0)="The software uses the cross reference of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,567,0)="^LR(69,""AA"",ORDER NUMBER, SPECIMEN) to determine what orders have been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,568,0)="collected. The software orders through the cross-reference and examines"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,569,0)="each order number using the following:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,570,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,571,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,572,0)="1. The order status must be collected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,573,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,574,0)="2. The order must be for a Patient from the PATIENT file (#2)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,575,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,576,0)="*3. For venipuncture (specimen collection) workload capture ONLY,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,577,0)="collection type must be one of the following:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,578,0)="Laboratory Collect (LC) = Venipuncture Travel Time - 89341.0000"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,579,0)="Immediate Collect (I) = Venipuncture Travel Time - 89341.0000"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,580,0)="Send Patient (SP) = Venipuncture Outpatient - 89343.0000"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,581,0)="*Note: Collection type is only used for venipuncture workload capture."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,582,0)="Collection type has no bearing on CPT workload capture."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,583,0)="Both In-Patient and Outpatient receive LMIP venipuncture workload credit."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,584,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,585,0)="4. The ordering provider is validated as a current active provider. If the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,586,0)="ordering provider is not valid, the default provider will be used if the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,587,0)="default provider is valid. If neither of the providers is valid, the order"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,588,0)="is marked appropriately and skipped."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,589,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,590,0)="5. CPT workload is only collected for Out-Patients based on HOSPITAL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,591,0)="LOCATION file (#44) that have the TYPE field (#2) defined as: CLINIC,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,592,0)="MODULE, or OTHER LOCATION. Venipuncture workload is NOT controlled by"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,593,0)="HOSPITAL LOCATION type."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,594,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,595,0)="*6. This patch uses the INSTITUTION field (#3) of the HOSPITAL LOCATION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,596,0)="file (#44) to determine the institution that should receive CPT workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,597,0)="credit. If the INSTITUTION field (#3) is not defined then the DEFAULT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,598,0)="INSTITUTION is used."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,599,0)="NOTE: See step 8 of the Setup instructions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,600,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,601,0)="7. Each test is checked to ensure that it does not have the status of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,602,0)="CANCEL or NOT PERFORMED before CPT workload is processed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,603,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,604,0)="8. Each test is checks the accession area's LAB OOS LOCATION. If defined"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,605,0)="the accession area's LAB OOS LOCATION is used."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,606,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,607,0)="9. Each collected test will be checked for a NATIONAL VA LAB CODE field"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,608,0)="(#64) in the LABORATORY TEST file (#60)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,609,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,610,0)="10. The NATIONAL VA LAB CODE field (#64) point to the WKLD CODE file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,611,0)="(#64). The software checks the WKLD CODE file (#64), CODE field (#18) for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,612,0)="CPT codes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,613,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,614,0)="*11. This patch has changed the data dictionary definition of the CODE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,615,0)="field (#18) to a variable pointer. The patch installation  will converts"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,616,0)="all valid codes to the new file structure and reset the cross-references."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,617,0)="If the code is invalid, the code is removed. A note will be entered in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,618,0)="WKLD CODE file (#64), WKLD CODE NOTES field (#24) indicating when the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,619,0)="removal occurred."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,620,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,621,0)="*12. Each CPT code is checked to make sure it is valid (active). Each CPT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,622,0)="code is checked for allowed modifiers. If there are multiple occurrences"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,623,0)="of identical CPT codes, the software will automatically add the modifier"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,624,0)="DISTINCT PROCEDURAL SERVICE (59) to each succeeding CPT code if this"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,625,0)="modifier is allowable."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,626,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,627,0)="13. The specimen DATE/TIME OF COLLECTION is used as the encounter date"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,628,0)="time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,629,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,630,0)="NOTE: If the scan of order passes all of the checks and there are valid"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,631,0)="CPT codes associated with the collected (accessioned) test, CPT workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,632,0)="data is passed to the PCE workload API."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,633,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,634,0)="Listing of elements passed to PCE workload API."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,635,0)="$$DATA2PCE^PXAPI"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,636,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,637,0)="OOS location"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,638,0)="Reporting Institution"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,639,0)="Provider"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,640,0)="Encounter Date/time"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,641,0)="Patient Pointer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,642,0)="Stop Code number of the ordering location."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,643,0)="Service Category of OOS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,644,0)="Encounter type of Ancillary"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,645,0)="CPT codes for each collected test as defined in WKLD CODE file."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,646,0)="*CPT modifier if appropriate."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,647,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,648,0)="*14. If an Order Test is marked as NOT PERFORMED by the laboratory and CPT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,649,0)="workload has already been sent to PCE, a background job will automatically"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,650,0)="send delete CPT workload messages for that order to the PCE Workload API."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,651,0)="NOTE: If the Not Performed test is ultimately verified, no CPT workload is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,652,0)="sent after NOT PERFORMED delete has been sent."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,653,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,654,0)="15. The PCE API passes back to the Laboratory software application the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,655,0)="encounter number used to store the PCE API passed information. It is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,656,0)="possible for one order to have multiple encounter number based on the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,657,0)="ACCESSION AREA's OOS definition. The PCE encounter number is displayed on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,658,0)="various order status screens in the Visit Number(s)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,659,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,660,0)="Example: Order/test status screen - Visit Number(s): show the PCE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,661,0)="encounter numbers."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,662,0)="Test              Urgency   Status                            Accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,663,0)="  -Lab Order # 162690                        Provider: The man"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,664,0)="     Visit Number(s): 99999;"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,665,0)="  BLOOD  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,666,0)="  CBC PROFILE   ROUTINE Test Complete 12/02/1999@07:41 HE 1202 10"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,667,0)="  -Lab Order # 162690                        Provider: The man"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,668,0)="     Visit Number(s): 99999;"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,669,0)="  BLOOD SERUM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,670,0)="  MAGNESIUM     ROUTINE Test Complete 12/02/1999@08:02 DA 1202 32"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,671,0)="  CHEM 7        ROUTINE Test Complete 12/02/1999@08:02 DA 1202 32"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,672,0)="  -Lab Order # 163491                        Provider: The man"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,673,0)="     Visit Number(s): 99999;"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,674,0)="  BLOOD SERUM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,675,0)="  URIC ACID     ROUTINE Test Complete 12/02/1999@14:37 DA 1202 234"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,676,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,677,0)="By using the User's Visit Review [PXQ USER REVIEW] option User's Visit"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,678,0)="Review one can determine what CPT workload has been captured for a given"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,679,0)="order. This is an example of the option. The Visit Number(s) information"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,680,0)="is entered at the 'Enter VISIT (UNIQUE ID or '1239):' prompt. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,681,0)="     Select one of the following:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,682,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,683,0)="          P         Patient List of Visits"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,684,0)="          I         Internal Entry Number of VISIT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,685,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,686,0)="Select by (P)atient or (I)en: P// Internal Entry Number of VISIT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,687,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,688,0)="Enter VISIT (UNIQUE ID or `1239): `99999"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,689,0)="  12-2-1999@06:57:38     PATIENT,SICK     "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,690,0)="LAB DIV 623 OOS ID 108 29TRC-MUS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,691,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,692,0)="     Select one of the following:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,693,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,694,0)="          D         Default (first field of each file/subfile)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,695,0)="          A         All fields in a file/subfile (except 'NULL')"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,696,0)="          C         Customized by User (Default plus added fields) "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,697,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,698,0)="~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,699,0)="To customize your display use VA FileMan to add entries in file PCE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,700,0)="CUSTOMIZE REPORT, with your NAME, FILE/SUBFILE#s, and FIELD#s that you"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,701,0)="want to have included in the report."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,702,0)="~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,703,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,704,0)="Enter '^^' to exit option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,705,0)="Format of Print out: // All fields in a file/subfile (except 'NULL')"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,706,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,707,0)="DEVICE: HOME// TELNET    Right Margin: 80// "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,708,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,709,0)="**************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,710,0)="***  R E C O R D    O F    R E L A T E D    E N T R I E S  ***"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,711,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,712,0)="         The Following is the VISIT file entry and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,713,0)="          ALL records pointing back to this entry."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,714,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,715,0)="               VISIT RECORD    --- #999999"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,716,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,717,0)="               DATE/TIME --- DEC 02, 1999@06:57:38"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,718,0)="               PATIENT   --- PATIENT,SICK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,719,0)="               LOCATION  --- LAB DIV 623 OOS ID 108"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,720,0)="----------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,721,0)="    FILE = VISIT #9000010  RECORD #99999"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,722,0)="        VISIT/ADMIT DATE&TIME              = DEC 02, 1999@06:57:38"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,723,0)="        DATE VISIT CREATED                 = DEC 02, 1999@07:28:51"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,724,0)="        TYPE                               = VA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,725,0)="        PATIENT NAME                       = PATIENT,SICK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,726,0)="        LOC. OF ENCOUNTER                  = MUSKOGEE, OK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,727,0)="        SERVICE CATEGORY                   = DAILY HOSPITALIZATION "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,728,0)="        DSS ID                             = LABORATORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,729,0)="        DEPENDENT ENTRY COUNT              = 3"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,730,0)="        DELETE FLAG                        = "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,731,0)="        PARENT VISIT LINK                  = "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,732,0)="        DATE LAST MODIFIED                 = DEC 02, 1999@07:28:52"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,733,0)="        CHECK OUT DATE&TIME                = "
