^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,832,0)="        ****END OF EXAMPLE****"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,833,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,834,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,835,0)="*Venipuncture Workload Capture:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,836,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,837,0)="************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,838,0)="LABORATORY CURRENT PROCEDURAL TERMINOLOGY (CPT) CODES AND MODIFIERS PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,839,0)="LR*5.2*243 INSTALLATION AND IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE in PDF format is provided"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,840,0)="with this patch. Please refer to this document for details and specific"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,841,0)="instructions. The patch description does not include ALL implementation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,842,0)="considerations or complete file setup instructions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,843,0)="************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,844,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,845,0)="1. *Patch LR*5.2*243 will automatically collects venipuncture workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,846,0)="data identical to other types of collected workload data. Venipuncture"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,847,0)="workload data will appear on workload reports broken down by standard"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,848,0)="reporting criteria."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,849,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,850,0)="2. Originally, LMIP workload reporting did not include venipuncture as a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,851,0)="billable procedure; therefore, the software entered a manual style tally"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,852,0)="of totals for the institution by day. Now LMIP workload does allow"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,853,0)="venipuncture workload. This patch automatically captures venipuncture by"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,854,0)="institution, by date, by WKLD CODE, and by event time and stores them in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,855,0)="the WKLD DATA (#64.1) file. Certain data elements are required when"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,856,0)="recording workload. One of the required data elements is accession area."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,857,0)="Therefore, some accession area must be utilized to satisfy the required"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,858,0)="data field. This patch provides new fields that can be used to customize"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,859,0)="data collection."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,860,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,861,0)="3. The venipuncture workload ACTUALLY indicates that the laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,862,0)="obtained at least one specimen from the patient."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,863,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,864,0)="NOTE: THE SPECIMEN OBTAINED MAY NOT BE A BLOOD SPECIMEN. WHAT THE DEFAULT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,865,0)="CODES (venipuncture) INDICATES IS THAT THE LAB COLLECTED A SPECIMEN FOR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,866,0)="THIS PARTICULAR ORDER. ONLY 1 SPECIMEN COLLECTION WORKLOAD UNIT PER ORDER"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,867,0)="IS CAPTURED REGARDLESS OF THE NUMBER OF ACTUAL SPECIMENS COLLECTED FOR THE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,868,0)="ORDER."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,869,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,870,0)="4. Specimen Collection workload codes of Venipuncture Travel Time"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,871,0)="[89341.0000] is the default code for Lab Collect (LC) and Immediate"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,872,0)="Collect (I). Specimen Collection WKLD CODE of Venipuncture Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,873,0)="[89343.0000] is default code for Send Patient (SP). "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,874,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,875,0)="5. *Venipuncture workload is captured based on INSTITUTION field (#3) in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,876,0)="the HOSPITAL LOCATION file (#44) of the ordering location. If no"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,877,0)="INSTITUTION is defined, the default institution defined by MAILMAN will be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,878,0)="used."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,879,0)="* There is a new field exported with this patch. The DIVISION PARAMETERS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,880,0)="field (#618) is a multiple in the LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9). There are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,881,0)="two fields in the DIVISION PARAMETERS field (#618) multiple that can be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,882,0)="used to customize the venipuncture workload collection."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,883,0)="   - DIVISION PARAMETER field (#.01) points to the INSTITUTION file (#4)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,884,0)="This field will allow the LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9) to be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,885,0)="multi-divisional."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,886,0)="   - PHLEBOTOMY DEFAULT ACC AREA field (#618) points to the ACCESSION file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,887,0)="(#68)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,888,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,889,0)="6. * The software will examine the ordering location for the INSTITUTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,890,0)="that location is assigned. The software will look up in the LABORATORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,891,0)="SITE file (#69.9), DIVISION PARAMETERS subfile (#) to get the ACCESSION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,892,0)="area to be used when storing venipuncture workload. The MAJ. SECT and the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,893,0)="SUBSECTION fields in WKLD DATA (#64.1) file will be set to ACCESSION area"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,894,0)="defined."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,895,0)="Note: The default venipuncture ACCESSION area is HEMATOLOGY."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,896,0)="          LAB DIVISION is CLINICAL PATHOLOGY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,897,0)="          Date and Time is the SPECIMEN COLLECTION date/time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,898,0)="          The LAB TEST is the first collected test in the order."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,899,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,900,0)="7. * The Venipuncture workload capture assumes that there is an accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,901,0)="area that begins with the letters 'HEM'. If there is no accession area"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,902,0)="beginning with the letters 'HEM', then venipuncture default accession area"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,903,0)="will be the accession area having the internal entry number of 10 in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,904,0)="ACCESSION file (#68)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,905,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,906,0)="8. ** This patch creates a new multiple in the LABORATORY SITE file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,907,0)="(#69.9), DIVISION PARAMETERS field (#618). This new multiple will be used"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,908,0)="to allow in the future, each institution to have the opportunity to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,909,0)="completely define separate laboratory parameter definitions. The first"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,910,0)="entry in this multiple is PHLEBOTOMY DEFAULT ACC AREA field (#618). This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,911,0)="field will allow each institution to define what accession area"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,912,0)="venipuncture workload should be assigned. If this field is not defined"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,913,0)="then the default Hematology accession area outlined above will be used."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,914,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,915,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,916,0)="This is a listing of captured venipuncture workload data."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,917,0)="DATE: DEC 02, 1999"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,918,0)="WKLD CODE: +Venipuncture Outpatient     UNIT WEIGHT: 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,919,0)="ACCESSION WKLD CODE TIME: 12.5713       LAB TEST: GLUCOSE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,920,0)="  WEIGHT MULTIPLIER: 1                  LAB DIVISION: CLINICAL PATHOLOGY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,921,0)="  MAJ. SECT.: SEND OUT                    SUBSECTION: SEND OUT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,922,0)="  ACC NO.: CH 1202 15                         PATIENT: NOSE,LIMP"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,923,0)="  ORIGINAL ACC DATE: DEC 02, 1999"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,924,0)="   DATE ORDERED: DEC 02, 1999@12:57:13"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,925,0)="  SPECIMEN NO.: 1                              SPECIMEN: BLOOD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,926,0)="  REPORT ROUTING LOCATION: 2S            PROVIDER: GINSBURG,RONNIE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,927,0)="  LOG IN PERSON: STALLING,FRANK         LOCATION TYPE: WARD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,928,0)="  ORDERING LOCATION: 7 ATU                   URGENCY: ROUTINE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",97,1,929,0)="  VERIFY TECH.: STALLING,FRANK           WORK AREA: SEND OUT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,0)="263 SEQ #197^3000626^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,0)="^^934^934^3000626"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,3,0)="Subject: CPT CODE MODIFIERS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,5,0)="Category: DATA DICTIONARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,6,0)="          ENHANCEMENT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,7,0)="          ROUTINE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,9,0)="Description:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,10,0)="============"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,12,0)="The Laboratory CPT Code Modifier enhancement patch LR*5.2*263 provides the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,13,0)="Laboratory Version 5.2 software application the ability to transmit"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,14,0)="Current Procedural Terminology (CPT) codes and Modifiers to the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,15,0)="Care Encounter (PCE) workload capture Application Interface (API). The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,16,0)="transmission of workload in the form of CPT codes is done in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,17,0)="background (no user interaction is required). Because of the background"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,18,0)="method of workload reporting several new fields were created and the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,19,0)="Laboratory software logic was modified."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,21,0)="CPT modifier provides the means by which the reporting physician can"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,22,0)="indicate that a service or procedure that has been performed has been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,23,0)="altered by some specific circumstances but not changed in its definition"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,24,0)="or code. The judicious application of modifiers obviates the necessity for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,25,0)="separate procedure listing that may describe the modifying circumstances."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,28,0)="NOTE: ONLY PATIENT ORDERS FROM HOSPITAL LOCATION WITH THE TYPE OF CLINIC,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,29,0)="MODULE, OR OTHER WILL RECEIVE CPT WORKLOAD CREDIT. THE SOFTWARE USES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,30,0)="LOCATION TYPE TO DETERMINE IF THE ORDER IS FOR AN OUT-PATIENT OR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,31,0)="IN-PATIENT."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,33,0)="Enhancements and Modifications:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,34,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,36,0)="Laboratory CPT Code Modifiers Patch LR*5.2*263 contains the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,37,0)="enhancements and changes:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,39,0)="NOTE: The asterisk ('*') indicates significant enhancements or file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,40,0)="structure changes. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,43,0)="*1. The CPT Code Modifiers Patch LR*5.2*263 patch automatically removes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,44,0)="CPT workload credit for any test(s) with the status of NOT PERFORMED (NP)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,46,0)="*2. When the Laboratory workload reporting LRNIGHTY background job is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,47,0)="tasked, a secondary program examines the WKLD CODE file (#64) to determine"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,48,0)="if any CPT code(s) are inactive in the CPT file (#81) or if other file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,49,0)="pointers are broken. If inactive code(s) are found, a VA Mailman message"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,50,0)="is automatically generated and sent once a day to the LMI Mail Group"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,51,0)="containing information about the code(s) and the action(s) taken by the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,52,0)="software."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,54,0)="*3. The enhanced Laboratory workload software processes the workload data"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,55,0)="in LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9), PCE DEFAULT PROVIDER field (#617) and LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,56,0)="OOS LOCATION field (#.8) even if these two fields are not defined. A VA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,57,0)="Mailman report is automatically generated and sent to the LMI mail group"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,58,0)="once a day indicating those orders requiring additional attention because"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,59,0)="the default fields were not defined."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,61,0)="*4. The automated Venipuncture workload reporting functionality used the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,62,0)="same criteria as the Laboratory workload reporting."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,64,0)="5. The enhanced Laboratory software will now acknowledge the actual user"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,65,0)="entering lab test orders in LAB ORDER ENTRY file (#69) for the PCE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,66,0)="Registered Encounter rather than the user that started or tasked the PCE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,67,0)="Workload background job."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,69,0)="6. The LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9) locking logic is modified to correct"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,70,0)="the problem of not being able to edit the LABORATORY SITE file (#69) while"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,71,0)="the LRNIGHTY background job is running."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,72,0)="Option Changes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,74,0)="*7. Add tests to a given accession [LRADD TO ACC] option is modified to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,75,0)="activate the PCE Workload API. Any test(s) added to an accession will now"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,76,0)="receive PCE Workload credit."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,78,0)="8. Order/test status [LROS] option is modified to correctly display"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,79,0)="test(s) added to an accession."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,81,0)="9. Enter/verify data (auto instrument) [LRVR] option is enhanced to allow"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,82,0)="users to edit, add, or subtract atomic test(s) from the test list before"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,83,0)="beginning the verification of an atomic test(s) and to continue to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,84,0)="next accession number if the current accession is not collected. This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,85,0)="enhancement applies to both verifying by accession number or UID"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,86,0)="(Universal Identification)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,88,0)="*10. Batch data entry [LRSTUF] option is modified to capture LMIP workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,89,0)="counts."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,91,0)="11. Results entry (batch) [LRMISTUF] is modified to capture LMIP workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,92,0)="counts."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,93,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,94,0)="12. The Bypass normal data entry [LRFAST] option is modified to accept the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,95,0)="response of ""YES"" at the ""Do you want to enter draw times?"" prompt."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,97,0)="13. The Accessioning tests ordered by ward order entry [LROE] option is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,98,0)="modified to accurately determine if the tasked ROLLOVER ACCESSION [LRTASK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,99,0)="ROLLOVER] option is actually running."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,101,0)="14. The Review by order number [LRCENLKUP] option date displays is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,102,0)="converted to use Kernel date conversion utilities."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,104,0)="15. Edit or Print WKLD CODES [LR WKLD CODE EDIT PRINT] option is enhanced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,105,0)="to print all WKLD CODES, even if they have not been activated. This will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,106,0)="correct the problem of WKLD CODES that have a suffix of .0000 not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,107,0)="printing."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,108,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,109,0)="16. Workload Report [LRCAPR1] option has been enhanced to allow the user"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,110,0)="to select combinations of LEDI collecting institutions or Hospital"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,111,0)="locations."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,113,0)="17. When verifying Microbiology specimens the user is prompted for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,114,0)="additional workload. A screen has been added to allow only a number"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,115,0)="between 1 to 25. This is to prevent inadvertent entering of WKLD CODE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,116,0)="number instead of the multiply by number."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,118,0)="Laboratory Menu and Option Changes:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,119,0)="============================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,120,0)="LIM workload menu [LR LIM/WKLD MENU]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,122,0)="The LIM workload menu [LR LIM/WKLD MENU] is modified to add the new"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,123,0)="InActive WKLD CODE File CPT Codes Print [LRCAPCPTI] option."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,125,0)="New Option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,127,0)="InActive WKLD CODE File CPT Codes Print [LRCAPCPTI] option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,129,0)="The new Inactive WKLD CODE File CPT Codes Print [LRCAPCPTI] option scans"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,130,0)="the WKLD CODE file (#64) for code(s) that are no longer allowed or code(s)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,131,0)="that are inactive in the CPT file (#81). The ""WKLD CODE - CODE CHECK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,132,0)="REPORT"" is then generated displaying all CPT code(s) that are no longer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,133,0)="allowed, code(s) that are inactive and why they are inappropriate,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,134,0)="laboratory test names linked to WKLD code(s) (i.e., laboratory test names"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,135,0)="listed on the report will not receive PCE Workload credit), and code(s)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,136,0)="requiring a different entry in the CPT file (#81) in order to capture PCE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,137,0)="Workload data."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,138,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,139,0)="The new Inactive WKLD CODE File CPT Codes Print [LRCAPCPTI] option is also"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,140,0)="useful when a new CPT Code file is released (i.e., new CPT code files are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,141,0)="usually distributed annually). The new CPT Code files may contain codes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,142,0)="that are no longer allowed or codes that are inactive in the VISTA CPT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,143,0)="file (#81). When CPT codes defined in the WKLD CODE file (#64) are deemed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,144,0)="inactive in the CPT file (#81), then the software enters a date in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,145,0)="WKLD CODE file (#64), Inactive Date field (#3) for those inactive codes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,146,0)="The Laboratory PCE interface checks each CPT code in the WKLD CODE file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,147,0)="(#64) before sending CPT workload to the PCE API. Whenever CPT code(s) are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,148,0)="no longer allowed or has been inactivated a VA Mailman message containing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,149,0)="the ""WKLD CODE - CODE CHECK REPORT"" is sent once a day to the LMI mail"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,150,0)="group."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,151,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,152,0)="Example: WKLD CODE - CODE CHECK REPORT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,154,0)="Subj: WKLD CODE - CODE CHECK REPORT 12/14/99@14:44:25  [#83460]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,155,0)="From: POSTMASTER  In 'IN' basket.   Page 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,156,0)="-----------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,157,0)="Lab Order Number 100 has no Institution for the ordering location"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,158,0)="==================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,159,0)="86081.0000 [1]  ABO Cell and Rh(D) Typing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,160,0)="86083  BLOOD TYPING;ANTIBODY SCREEN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,161,0)="Is an inactive CPT code."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,162,0)="Associated Tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,163,0)="     ABO/RH TYPING  {1101}"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,164,0)="Inactivation date of Dec 13, 1999 has been entered"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,165,0)="****************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,166,0)="Listing of all offending codes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,167,0)="   ICPT     82534"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,168,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,169,0)="****** END OF EXAMPLE ********"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,171,0)="====================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,172,0)="Data Dictionary Change Summary:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,174,0)="The following file and field changes occur with the installation of VISTA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,175,0)="Laboratory CPT Code and Modifiers Patch LR*5.2*263."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,177,0)="WKLD CODE file (#64)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,178,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,179,0)=" The WKLD CODE file (#64) was modified to convert existing file data to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,180,0)="a new data structure, new fields were created, and existing fields were"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,181,0)="modified to support the Laboratory workload reporting enhancements of CPT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,182,0)="codes and modifiers."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,183,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,184,0)="1) CODE field (#18) multiple has been changed from a free text field to a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,185,0)="variable pointer."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,187,0)="2) CODE field (#.01) has been changed from a free text field to a variable"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,188,0)="pointer. This field is screened to allow only active code entries to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,189,0)="MORPHOLOGY FIELD file (#61.1), ICD DIAGNOSIS file (#80), and CPT file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,190,0)="(#81)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,191,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,192,0)="3) CODE subfile (#64.018) was modified to add the new CODE NOTES field"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,193,0)="(#6). This new word processing field is used for tracking general notes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,194,0)="regarding a particular code."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,195,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,196,0)="4) WKLD Code Notes field (#24) is a new word processing field used for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,197,0)="storing general notes regarding inactive or erroneous code(s) that is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,198,0)="automatically removed by the software."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,200,0)="5) LOINC Code field (#4) was changed to point to the LOINC CODE file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,201,0)="(#95.3)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,202,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,203,0)="6) The new Default LOINC Code field (#25) points to the LOINC CODE file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,204,0)="(#95.3).  This field is used to identify the default LOINC code.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,205,0)="field is usually used when the specimen is not clinically significant"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,206,0)="(i.e. body fluids). 'L FOR LOINC' was removed from the set of codes in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,207,0)="field TYPE (#64.018,5)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,208,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,209,0)="LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,210,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,211,0)="1) LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9), DIVISION PARAMETERS field (#618) multiple"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,212,0)="is a new field exported with this patch. These new fields are used to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,213,0)="customize the automated Venipuncture workload reporting functionality."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,214,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,215,0)="2) The new DIVISION PARAMETERS field (#.01) points to the INSTITUTION file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,216,0)="(#4). This field allows the LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9) to be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,217,0)="multi-divisional for Venipuncture workload reporting."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,218,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,219,0)="3) The new VENIPUNCTURE DEFAULT ACC AREA subfile (#618) points to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,220,0)="ACCESSION file (#68). This new field is used by the Venipuncture workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,221,0)="reporting background job to determine the accession area for the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,222,0)="INSTITUTION to be use for Venipuncture workload reporting."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,223,0)="Associated NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,224,0)="==============="
