^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,836,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,837,0)="        ****END OF EXAMPLE****"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,838,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,839,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,840,0)="*Venipuncture Workload Capture:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,841,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,842,0)="************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,843,0)="LABORATORY CURRENT PROCEDURAL TERMINOLOGY (CPT) CODES AND MODIFIERS PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,844,0)="LR*5.2*263 INSTALLATION AND IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE in PDF format is provided"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,845,0)="with this patch. Please refer to this document for details and specific"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,846,0)="instructions. The patch description does not include ALL implementation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,847,0)="considerations or complete file setup instructions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,848,0)="************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,849,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,850,0)="1. *Patch LR*5.2*263 will automatically collects venipuncture workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,851,0)="data identical to other types of collected workload data. Venipuncture"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,852,0)="workload data will appear on workload reports broken down by standard"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,853,0)="reporting criteria."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,854,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,855,0)="2. Originally, LMIP workload reporting did not include venipuncture as a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,856,0)="billable procedure; therefore, the software entered a manual style tally"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,857,0)="of totals for the institution by day. Now LMIP workload does allow"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,858,0)="venipuncture workload. This patch automatically captures venipuncture by"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,859,0)="institution, by date, by WKLD CODE, and by event time and stores them in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,860,0)="the WKLD DATA (#64.1) file. Certain data elements are required when"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,861,0)="recording workload. One of the required data elements is accession area."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,862,0)="Therefore, some accession area must be utilized to satisfy the required"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,863,0)="data field. This patch provides new fields that can be used to customize"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,864,0)="data collection."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,865,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,866,0)="3. The venipuncture workload ACTUALLY indicates that the laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,867,0)="obtained at least one specimen from the patient."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,868,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,869,0)="NOTE: THE SPECIMEN OBTAINED MAY NOT BE A BLOOD SPECIMEN. WHAT THE DEFAULT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,870,0)="CODES (venipuncture) INDICATES IS THAT THE LAB COLLECTED A SPECIMEN FOR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,871,0)="THIS PARTICULAR ORDER. ONLY 1 SPECIMEN COLLECTION WORKLOAD UNIT PER ORDER"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,872,0)="IS CAPTURED REGARDLESS OF THE NUMBER OF ACTUAL SPECIMENS COLLECTED FOR THE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,873,0)="ORDER."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,874,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,875,0)="4. Specimen Collection workload codes of Venipuncture Travel Time"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,876,0)="[89341.0000] is the default code for Lab Collect (LC) and Immediate"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,877,0)="Collect (I). Specimen Collection WKLD CODE of Venipuncture Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,878,0)="[89343.0000] is default code for Send Patient (SP). "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,879,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,880,0)="5. *Venipuncture workload is captured based on INSTITUTION field (#3) in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,881,0)="the HOSPITAL LOCATION file (#44) of the ordering location. If no"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,882,0)="INSTITUTION is defined, the default institution defined by MAILMAN will be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,883,0)="used."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,884,0)="* There is a new field exported with this patch. The DIVISION PARAMETERS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,885,0)="field (#618) is a multiple in the LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9). There are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,886,0)="two fields in the DIVISION PARAMETERS field (#618) multiple that can be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,887,0)="used to customize the venipuncture workload collection."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,888,0)="   - DIVISION PARAMETER field (#.01) points to the INSTITUTION file (#4)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,889,0)="This field will allow the LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9) to be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,890,0)="multi-divisional."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,891,0)="   - VENIPUNCTURE DEFAULT ACC AREA field (#618) points to the ACCESSION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,892,0)="file (#68)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,893,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,894,0)="6. * The software will examine the ordering location for the INSTITUTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,895,0)="that location is assigned. The software will look up in the LABORATORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,896,0)="SITE file (#69.9), DIVISION PARAMETERS subfile (#) to get the ACCESSION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,897,0)="area to be used when storing venipuncture workload. The MAJ. SECT and the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,898,0)="SUBSECTION fields in WKLD DATA (#64.1) file will be set to ACCESSION area"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,899,0)="defined."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,900,0)="Note: The default venipuncture ACCESSION area is HEMATOLOGY."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,901,0)="          LAB DIVISION is CLINICAL PATHOLOGY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,902,0)="          Date and Time is the SPECIMEN COLLECTION date/time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,903,0)="          The LAB TEST is the first collected test in the order."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,904,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,905,0)="7. * The Venipuncture workload capture assumes that there is an accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,906,0)="area that begins with the letters 'HEM'. If there is no accession area"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,907,0)="beginning with the letters 'HEM', then venipuncture default accession area"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,908,0)="will be the accession area having the internal entry number of 10 in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,909,0)="ACCESSION file (#68)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,910,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,911,0)="8. ** This patch creates a new multiple in the LABORATORY SITE file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,912,0)="(#69.9), DIVISION PARAMETERS field (#618). This new multiple will be used"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,913,0)="to allow in the future, each institution to have the opportunity to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,914,0)="completely define separate laboratory parameter definitions. The first"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,915,0)="entry in this multiple is VENIPUNCTURE DEFAULT ACC AREA field (#618). This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,916,0)="field will allow each institution to define what accession area"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,917,0)="venipuncture workload should be assigned. If this field is not defined"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,918,0)="then the default Hematology accession area outlined above will be used."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,919,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,920,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,921,0)="This is a listing of captured venipuncture workload data."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,922,0)="DATE: DEC 02, 1999"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,923,0)="WKLD CODE: +Venipuncture Outpatient     UNIT WEIGHT: 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,924,0)="ACCESSION WKLD CODE TIME: 12.5713       LAB TEST: GLUCOSE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,925,0)="  WEIGHT MULTIPLIER: 1                  LAB DIVISION: CLINICAL PATHOLOGY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,926,0)="  MAJ. SECT.: SEND OUT                    SUBSECTION: SEND OUT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,927,0)="  ACC NO.: CH 1202 15                         PATIENT: NOSE,LIMP"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,928,0)="  ORIGINAL ACC DATE: DEC 02, 1999"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,929,0)="   DATE ORDERED: DEC 02, 1999@12:57:13"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,930,0)="  SPECIMEN NO.: 1                              SPECIMEN: BLOOD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,931,0)="  REPORT ROUTING LOCATION: 2S            PROVIDER: GINSBURG,RONNIE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,932,0)="  LOG IN PERSON: STALLING,FRANK         LOCATION TYPE: WARD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,933,0)="  ORDERING LOCATION: 7 ATU                   URGENCY: ROUTINE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",98,1,934,0)="  VERIFY TECH.: STALLING,FRANK           WORK AREA: SEND OUT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,0)="218 SEQ #198^3000626^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,0)="^^522^522^3000626"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,1,0)="Patch LR*5.2*218 VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE DEVICE PRODUCT LABELING"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,2,0)="STATEMENT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,4,0)="February 9, 2000"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,6,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LR*5.2*218 contains changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,7,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,8,0)="Changes include: The fields PRINTER TYPE (#.02) and LABEL STOCK (#.03)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,9,0)="within the LABEL DEVICE multiple of the LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,10,0)="have been changed.  A new code for Zebra ZPL II compatible printers has"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,11,0)="been added. Use this code to designate Zebra printers. The label stock of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,12,0)="15/16x3 has been renamed 1x3 for clarity."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,14,0)="All of the above changes have been reviewed by the VISTA Blood Bank"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,15,0)="Developer and found to have no impact on the VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,16,0)="control functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,18,0)="PROBLEM:   The patch will add support for label printing within the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,19,0)="Laboratory software for Zebra Technologies Corporation thermal printers."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,20,0)="Blood Bank Caution Tag labels are not included in this support."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,21,0)="This software is written to utilize the functions and features of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,22,0)="Zebra Programming Language II - ZPL II(TM)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,24,0)="RISK ANALYSIS:   Changes made by patch LR*5.2*218 have no effect on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,25,0)="Blood Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,27,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS:  Patch LR*5.2*218 does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,28,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical elements"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,29,0)="functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,31,0)="POTENTIAL IMPACT ON SITES:  This patch contains changes to a file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,32,0)="identified in Veterans Health Administration (VHA) Directive 99-053,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,33,0)="group B listing. The changes have no effect in Blood Bank functionality"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,34,0)="or medical device control functions. There is no adverse potential to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,35,0)="sites."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,38,0)="VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION:  There are no required validation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,39,0)="scenarios to be completed by sites after installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,42,0)="- Patch LR*5.2*218 will add support for label printing within the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,43,0)="  Laboratory software for Zebra Technologies Corporation thermal printers."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,44,0)="  This software is written to utilize the functions and features of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,45,0)="  Zebra Programming Language II - ZPL II(TM)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,47,0)="- It will adjust the label layout of the 2nd 1x2 label on the 10 part label"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,48,0)="  stock when printed on the Intermec 3000/4000 series printer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,49,0)="  (see item #7 below)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,51,0)="- It will correct problems reported in NOIS: ATG-1298-31334, BAY-0999-30794,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,52,0)="  TAM-1299-32916 (see items #8, 9, 10 below)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,54,0)=" 1. This software has been specifically tested with the following models:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,55,0)="      Zebra Stripe S-600 printer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,56,0)="      Zebra Stripe S-500 printer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,57,0)="      Zebra Stripe S-300 printer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,58,0)="      Zebra A-Series 300 printer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,59,0)="      Zebra S-Series 105SE printer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,60,0)="      Intermec 4100 printer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,62,0)="    Specific site equipment was as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,63,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,64,0)="    Chicago HCS: Zebra S-300 using 1x2 label stock"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,65,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,66,0)="    Lebanon VAMC: Zebra S-500 using 1x2 label stock"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,67,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,68,0)="    Maryland HCS-Perry Point Division: Zebra S-600 using 1x2 label stock"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,70,0)="    Milwaukee VAMC: Zebra A300, S-500 and 105SE using 1x2 label stock"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,71,0)="                    Intermec 4100 using 1x2 label stock"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,72,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,73,0)="    North Chicago VAMC: Zebra S-600 using 2.5x4 10 part label stock"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,74,0)="                        Intermec 4100 using 2.5x4 10 part label stock"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,75,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,77,0)=" 2. The following VISTA TERMINAL TYPE file (#3.2) printer settings should "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,78,0)="    be/can be used as examples for ...."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,80,0)="    NAME: P-ZEBRA S300 LABEL PTR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,81,0)="      RIGHT MARGIN: 0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,82,0)="      PAGE LENGTH: 99999"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,83,0)="      FORM FEED: $C(0)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,84,0)="      OPEN EXECUTE: W $C(2),""^PON^LH0,0"",$C(3)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,85,0)="      CLOSE EXECUTE: S IONOFF=1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,86,0)="      DESCRIPTION: Zebra Stripe S-300 Thermal Printer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,88,0)="    NAME: P-ZEBRA S500 LABEL PTR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,89,0)="      RIGHT MARGIN: 0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,90,0)="      PAGE LENGTH: 99999"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,91,0)="      FORM FEED: $C(0)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,92,0)="      OPEN EXECUTE: W $C(2),""^PON^LH0,0"",$C(3)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,93,0)="      CLOSE EXECUTE: S IONOFF=1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,94,0)="      DESCRIPTION: Zebra Stripe S-500 Thermal Printer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,96,0)="    NAME: P-ZEBRA S600 LABEL PTR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,97,0)="      RIGHT MARGIN: 0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,98,0)="      PAGE LENGTH: 99999"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,99,0)="      FORM FEED: $C(0)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,100,0)="      OPEN EXECUTE: W $C(2),""^PON^LH0,0"",$C(3)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,101,0)="      CLOSE EXECUTE: S IONOFF=1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,102,0)="      DESCRIPTION: Zebra Stripe S-600 Thermal Printer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,103,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,104,0)="    NAME: P-ZEBRA S-Series 105SE LABEL PTR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,105,0)="      RIGHT MARGIN: 0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,106,0)="      PAGE LENGTH: 99999"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,107,0)="      FORM FEED: $C(0)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,108,0)="      OPEN EXECUTE: W $C(2),""^PON^LH0,0"",$C(3)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,109,0)="      CLOSE EXECUTE: S IONOFF=1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,110,0)="      DESCRIPTION: Zebra S-Series 105SE Thermal Printer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,112,0)="    NAME: P-ZEBRA A300 LABEL PTR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,113,0)="      RIGHT MARGIN: 0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,114,0)="      PAGE LENGTH: 99999"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,115,0)="      FORM FEED: $C(0)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,116,0)="      OPEN EXECUTE: W $C(2),""^PON^LH0,0"",$C(3)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,117,0)="      CLOSE EXECUTE: S IONOFF=1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,118,0)="      DESCRIPTION: Zebra A-300 Thermal Printer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,120,0)=" 3. The following VISTA DEVICE file (#3.5) label setting should be/can be "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,121,0)="    used as an example for ...."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,123,0)="    NAME: LABLABEL                          $I: _LTA387:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,124,0)="      ASK DEVICE: NO                        ASK PARAMETERS: NO"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,125,0)="      SIGN-ON/SYSTEM DEVICE: NO             LOCATION OF TERMINAL: LABLABEL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,126,0)="      SUPPRESS FORM FEED AT CLOSE: YES      *MARGIN WIDTH: 0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,127,0)="      *FORM FEED: $C(0)                     *PAGE LENGTH: 99999"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,128,0)="      SUBTYPE: P-ZEBRA S500 LABEL PTR       TYPE: TERMINAL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,129,0)="      LAT SERVER NODE: DSV38                LAT SERVER PORT: PORT_7"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,130,0)="      VMS DEVICE TYPE: NOT SPOOLED          LAT PORT SPEED: 96"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,131,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,132,0)="    The device should be defined and setup in the operating system as"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,133,0)="    a printer. The following communication parameters have been found"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,134,0)="    to work well:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,135,0)="                   baud rate: 9600"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,136,0)="                   stop bits: 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,137,0)="                      parity: none"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,138,0)="     communication handshake: xon/xoff control"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,140,0)="    No special jumping or wiring should be required."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,141,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,142,0)="    It is important that initial configuration and media calibration"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,143,0)="    be performed on the printer per the printer's user guide before"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,144,0)="    attempting to print labels."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,145,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,146,0)=" 4. The field PRINTER TYPE (#.02) within the LABEL DEVICE multiple of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,147,0)="    the LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9) has been changed. A new code for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,148,0)="    Zebra ZPL II compatible printers has been added. Use this code to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,149,0)="    designate Zebra printers."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,150,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,151,0)="    Note: Patch LR*5.2*161 introduced this field. This patch had code ""2"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,152,0)="    represent INTERMEC 4100. In patch LR*5.2*218 this has been changed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,153,0)="    to represent INTERMEC 3000/4000 SERIES to reflect the fact that this"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,154,0)="    software will also work with Intermec 3400/4100/4400 series printers."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,156,0)="    Example of setting up this printer in the laboratory software:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,157,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,159,0)="    Select VA FileMan Option: 1  Enter or Edit File Entries"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,160,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,161,0)="    INPUT TO WHAT FILE: LABORATORY SITE//"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,162,0)="    EDIT WHICH FIELD: ALL// LABEL DEVICE      (multiple)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,163,0)="       EDIT WHICH LABEL DEVICE SUB-FIELD: ALL//"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,164,0)="    THEN EDIT FIELD:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,165,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,166,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,167,0)="    Select LABORATORY SITE SITE NAME: MILWAUKEE, WI 53295"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,168,0)="    Select LABEL DEVICE: LABLABEL// LABLABEL     LABLABEL      _LTA387:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,169,0)="         ...OK? Yes//   (Yes)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,171,0)="      LABEL DEVICE: LABLABEL//"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,172,0)="      PRINTER TYPE: ZEBRA ZPL II COMPATIBLE// ?"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,173,0)="         Enter the type of label printer attached to this device."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,174,0)="         Choose from:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,175,0)="           0        OTHER"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,176,0)="           1        INTERMEC 3000/4000 SERIES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,177,0)="           2        ZEBRA ZPL II COMPATIBLE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,178,0)="      PRINTER TYPE: ZEBRA ZPL II COMPATIBLE//"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,179,0)="      LABEL STOCK: 1X2//"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,180,0)="      ALTERNATE LABEL ENTRY:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,181,0)="      ALTERNATE LABEL ROUTINE:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,182,0)="      DEFAULT ACCESSION AREA: CHEMISTRY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,183,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,184,0)=" 5. There is no downloading of a label format required for Zebra type"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,185,0)="    printers. The label format is part of the label printing process."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,186,0)="    This is a change from Laboratory's previous experience with Intermec"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,187,0)="    model printers which require a separate downloading of the label"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,188,0)="    format prior to label printing."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,189,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,190,0)=" 6. A new option Lab Zebra Label Utility [LR BAR ZEBRA UTILITY] is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,191,0)="    added by this patch. This option will be added to the menu option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,192,0)="    Lab liaison menu [LRLIAISON] by this KIDS install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,193,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,194,0)="    NAME: LR BAR ZEBRA UTILITY        MENU TEXT: Lab Zebra Label Utility"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,195,0)="      TYPE: run routine               CREATOR: 0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,196,0)="      PACKAGE: LAB SERVICE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,197,0)="      DESCRIPTION: This option is used to perform several configuration"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,198,0)="                   functions that relate to the Zebra label printers."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,200,0)="      It allows the user to:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,201,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,202,0)="          1         Configuration Update"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,203,0)="          2         Print Configuration Label"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,204,0)="          3         Adjust Tear Off Position"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,205,0)="          4         Label Top Position"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,206,0)="          5         Set Darkness"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,207,0)="          6         Mode Protection (Stripe printers only)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,208,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,209,0)="      Some functions are applicable to specific models of Zebra"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,210,0)="      printers. Based on the firmware version installed in a printer,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,211,0)="      the effect of these functions may vary. Parameters allowed by"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,212,0)="      these functions may be different due to changes in firmware."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,213,0)="      Consult the ZPL II Programming Guide, specific model User's Guide"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,214,0)="      and Firmware Release Notes for specific information."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,215,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,216,0)="      ROUTINE: EN^LRBARCFA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,217,0)="      UPPERCASE MENU TEXT: LAB ZEBRA LABEL UTILITY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,218,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,219,0)=" 7. It was reported to Lab Development subsequent to release of patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,220,0)="    LR*5.2*161 that depending on label stock and printer alignment,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,221,0)="    the 2nd (right side) 1x2 label on the 10 part label stock prints"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,222,0)="    very close to the left margin when using Intermec 4000 series"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,223,0)="    printers. The routine LRBARB has been changed to move the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,224,0)="    information over 15 dots to the right. This hopefully will provide"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,225,0)="    enough of a buffer to allow for variation in label stock and printer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,226,0)="    calibration and still print legible labels. Site will need to download"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,227,0)="    format 12 for this change to take affect. Use option Lab Bar Code"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,228,0)="    Label Formatter [LR BAR CF] to perform this function."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,229,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,230,0)=" 8. NOIS: ATG-1298-31334 reported an undefined error when printing future"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,231,0)="    collection labels on controls using option Print future collection"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,232,0)="    labels [LRUFCL]. When printing future collection labels for the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,233,0)="    current day and the site has accessioned controls, the option would"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,234,0)="    error because controls do not have a location entered in file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,235,0)="    LAB ORDER ENTRY (#69). This patch corrects this situation by not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,236,0)="    attempting to print labels for controls or orders with no location."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,237,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,238,0)=" 9. NOIS: BAY-0999-30794 reported that the option Print single future"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,239,0)="    collection label [LRUFCLS] would display a misleading message when"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,240,0)="    attempting to print labels for an order when one of the specimens on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,241,0)="    the order has no active tests. This can occur when all tests on a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,242,0)="    specimen have been cancelled. The message has been changed to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,243,0)="    indicate that only the specimen with no active tests will not be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,244,0)="    printed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,245,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,246,0)="10. NOIS: TAM-1299-32916 reported that when the laboratory order number"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,247,0)="    went over 999,999 that the last digit of the order number was truncated"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,248,0)="    on the label when printed on Intermec printers. The label formats for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,249,0)="    1x2 and 10 part labels for Intermec and Zebra label printers have been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,250,0)="    adjusted to print the order number to 7 digits. The text ""order #"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,251,0)="    which precedes the order number on the label has been standardized"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,252,0)="    across label formats printed by Intermec and Zebra printers."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,253,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,254,0)="    The test label available for printing within the Laboratory software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,255,0)="    now prints a 7 digit order number."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,256,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,257,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,258,0)=" "
