^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,301,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,302,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,303,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,304,0)=" INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,305,0)=" -------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,306,0)=" The install time for this patch is less than 10 minutes without menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,307,0)=" rebuilding. Install time will be increased if KIDS performs menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,308,0)=" rebuilding. Alerts will be generated and sent to local mail group LMI"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,309,0)=" when the transport global is loaded, patch installation starts and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,310,0)=" ends."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,311,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,312,0)=" This patch can be installed when Laboratory users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,313,0)=" However the following conditions apply:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,314,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,315,0)="    - Accessioning/label printing should not be occurring."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,316,0)="    - Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,317,0)="      Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,318,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,319,0)=" NOTE: MailMan and KERNEL patches must be current on the target system to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,320,0)="       avoid problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,321,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,322,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,323,0)=" 1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,324,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,325,0)=" 2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,326,0)="     option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,327,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,328,0)=" 3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,329,0)="     system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,330,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,331,0)=" 4.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,332,0)="     select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,333,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,334,0)=" 5.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,335,0)="     all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,336,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,337,0)=" 6.  If you wish to preserve a copy of the routines exported in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,338,0)="     prior to installation, you should use the 'Backup a Transport Global'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,339,0)="     option at this time.  You may also compare the routine in your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,340,0)="     production account to the routine in the patch by using the 'Compare"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,341,0)="     a Transport Global to Current System' option.  These options are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,342,0)="     both found under the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,343,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,344,0)=" 7.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,345,0)="     and select the package 'LR*5.2*218'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,346,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,347,0)="     When prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,348,0)="     Install? YES//"", choose 'YES'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,349,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,350,0)="     When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,351,0)="     and Protocols? YES//',  choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,352,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,353,0)=" 8.  On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,354,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,355,0)=" 9.  Routine LR218 will be deleted after successful patch installation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,356,0)="     by KIDS."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,357,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,358,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,359,0)=" *****************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,360,0)=" Below is an example of the dialogue seen during the KIDS install:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,361,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,362,0)="Select Installation Option: 6  Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,363,0)="Select INSTALL NAME:    LR*5.2*218        Loaded from Distribution  10/8/98@11:2"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",99,1,364,0)="6:30"
