^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,114,0)="          Install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,115,0)="         ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,116,0)="         ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols?"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,117,0)="          YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,118,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,119,0)="         The site should answer ""NO"" to all three questions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,120,0)="             Note: You may not receive all three prompts at your site.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,121,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,122,0)="          1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,123,0)="             This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,124,0)="             your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,125,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,126,0)="          2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,127,0)="             should be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,128,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,129,0)="          3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,130,0)="             your system. You now need to use KIDS to install the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,131,0)="             Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,132,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,133,0)="             On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,134,0)="             following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,135,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,136,0)="                 Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,137,0)="                 Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,138,0)="                 Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,139,0)="                 Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,140,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,141,0)="          4. Users may remain on the system, installation may be done at"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,142,0)="             any time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,143,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,144,0)="          5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,145,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,146,0)="          6. Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,147,0)="             hours and less than 5 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,148,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,149,0)="          7. Installation of this patch requires no additional memory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,150,0)="             space."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,151,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,152,0)="          8. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,153,0)="             option 'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*260'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,154,0)="             and proceed with the install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,155,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,156,0)="          9. The post-init routine, LR260, will perform the three final"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,157,0)="             automated functions in the installation.  These steps are:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,159,0)="                   A. Three entries will be added to the LREPI REMINDER"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,160,0)="                      LINK (#69.51) file.  These are ""VA-NATIONAL EPI DB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,161,0)="                      UPDATE"", ""VA-HEP C RISK ASSESSMENT"", and "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,162,0)="                      ""VA-NATIONAL EPI RX EXTRACT""."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,163,0)="                   B. Three entries will be added to the LAB "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,164,0)="                      SEARCH/EXTRACT (#69.5) file.  These are ""HEPATITIS C"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,165,0)="                      ANTIBODY NEG"", ""HEPATITIS A ANTIBODY POS"", and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,166,0)="                      ""HEPATITIS B POS"".  Please refer to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,167,0)="                      LR*5.2*260 TECHNICAL/USERS MANUAL for instructions"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,168,0)="                      on adding tests to these entries."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,169,0)="                   C. The NCH CHOLESTEROL and NCH PAP SMEAR entries will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,170,0)="                      be inactivated in the LAB SEARCH/EXTRACT (#69.5)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,171,0)="                      file."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,172,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,173,0)="             You will be notified after each step if any problems were"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,174,0)="             encountered."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,175,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,176,0)="         10. The post-init routine, LR260, will be automatically deleted"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,177,0)="             when the installation has completed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,178,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,179,0)="         12. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,180,0)="             be returned to the mapped set once the installation has run"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,181,0)="             to completion."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,182,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,183,0)="         13. LABORATORY SEARCH/EXTRACT PATCH LR*5.2*260 HEPATITIS EMERGING"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,184,0)="             PATHOGENS INITIATIVE (EPI) TECHNICAL AND USER GUIDE in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,185,0)="             Portable Document Format (LR_260TUG.PDF) is provided with"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,186,0)="             this patch. Please refer to this documentation for details"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,187,0)="             and specific instructions. The patch description does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,188,0)="             include ALL implementation considerations or complete setup"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,189,0)="             instructions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,190,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,191,0)="This document is available on the following Office of Information Field"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,192,0)="             Offices' ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE directories."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,193,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,194,0)="       OI Field Office             FTP Address        Directory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,195,0)="       ================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,196,0)="       Albany                      152.127.1.5        ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,197,0)="       Hines                       152.129.1.110      ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,198,0)="       Salt Lake City              152.131.2.1        ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,200,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,201,0)="         14. Please do not do this until specifically requested to do so."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,202,0)="             After the patch installation and set up has been completed,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,203,0)="             the data for your site will be validated by the EPI program"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,204,0)="             office.  At this time you will be asked to add "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,205,0)="             XXX@Q-EPI.DOMAIN.EXT to the MEMBERS - REMOTE field (#12) of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,206,0)="             MAIL GROUP file (#3.8) for the EPI mail group."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,207,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,208,0)="     VA FileMan 22.0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,209,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,210,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,211,0)="     Select OPTION: 1  ENTER OR EDIT FILE ENTRIES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,212,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,213,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,214,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,215,0)="     INPUT TO WHAT FILE: MAIL GROUP// "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,216,0)="     EDIT WHICH FIELD: ALL// MEMBERS - REMOTE    (multiple)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,217,0)="        EDIT WHICH MEMBERS - REMOTE SUB-FIELD: ALL// "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,218,0)="     THEN EDIT FIELD: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",100,1,219,0)="  "
