^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",101,0)="256 SEQ #200^3001106^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",101,1,0)="^^3^3^3001106"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",101,1,1,0)="This is a patch for VISTA Laboratory Software, version 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",101,1,2,0)="A detailed description of this patch is included in the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",101,1,3,0)="distribution message."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,0)="264 SEQ #201^3001127^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,0)="^^166^166^3001127"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,2,0)=" VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE V5.2 DEVICE PRODUCT LABELING STATEMENT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,3,0)="============================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,4,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,5,0)=" June 10, 1999 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,7,0)=" VISTA Laboratory Package patch LR*5.2*264 contains no changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,8,0)=" controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,9,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,10,0)=" All changes have been reviewed by the VISTA Blood Bank Developer and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,11,0)=" found to have no impact on the VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE control"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,12,0)=" functions.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,13,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,14,0)=" RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*264 have no effect on Blood"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,15,0)=" Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,16,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,17,0)=" EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*264 does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,18,0)=" alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical element"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,19,0)=" functions. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,20,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,21,0)=" POTENTIAL IMPACT ON SITES: This patch contains no changes to files and "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,22,0)=" routines identified in Veterans Health Administration (VHA) Directive"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,23,0)=" 99-053. The changes that are made have no effect to Blood Bank"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,24,0)=" functionality or medical device control functions. There is no adverse"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,25,0)=" potential to sites."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,27,0)=" VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION: There are no required validation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,28,0)=" scenarios to be completed by sites after installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,30,0)="Patch Description:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,31,0)="==========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,33,0)="1) There is a unique set of circumstances that will cause the PCE workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,34,0)="update background software program (LRCAPPH1) to produce a software error."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,35,0)="The error situation is created when an orderable test has no accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,36,0)="area assigned and is ordered from an outpatient location.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,37,0)="   When the laboratory accessions the specimen, the appropriate accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,38,0)="area is selected. The selected accession area is not updated in the LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,39,0)="ORDER ENTRY file (#69).  PCE workload data has been credited for that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,40,0)="order/accession.  The test is then subsequently Not Performed(NP) and PCE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,41,0)="workload has already been credited, the PCE workload update background"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,42,0)="software will error for a lack of accession area definition in the LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,43,0)="ORDER ENTRY file.  This patch will correct this situation by using the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,44,0)="default DSS Location value instead of attempting to determine the specific"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,45,0)="accession area used to accession the test.  This error is only manifested"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,46,0)="under these sequence of events.  If the order/accession is NP before PCE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,47,0)="workload is credited, no error will occur."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,49,0)="The software will remove PCE encounters that do not have CPT workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,50,0)="because all of the CPT Codes for the order have been Not Performed (NP)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,51,0)="Order Status screen will display the encounter number with appended text"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,52,0)="to explain CPT workload transactions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,54,0)="Example:  XXX indicates the encounter number."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,55,0)="   -CPT CANC indicates at least one of the CPT workload credits have been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,56,0)="removed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,57,0)="-ENC DEL indicates that all CPT workload has been removed and the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,58,0)="encounter has been deleted."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,60,0)="Visit Number(s): XXX-CPT CANC-ENC DEL;"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,62,0)="2) The option Results entry (batch) [LRMISTUF] allows for three methods of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,63,0)="input batch data. Patch LR*5.2*263 disabled the third option of 'Just"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,64,0)="Prompt'. Patch LR*5.2*264 restores this functionality."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,66,0)="3) The option Workload Report [LRCAPR1] allows for the reporting of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,67,0)="quality control in the report. If the QC specimens are accessioned"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,68,0)="automatically by the nightly background job, there is no ward location"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,69,0)="defined. The report would not report any of these specimens on the report."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,70,0)="The routine LRCAPR2 corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,72,0)="4) In certain situations, Laboratory was passing to the PCE API incorrect"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,73,0)="date/time, which resulted in corrupted date/time fields in PCE. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,74,0)="corrects this problem. Laboratory will no longer pass time that includes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,75,0)="seconds to the PCE API. This will reduce the number of visit numbers"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,76,0)="generated per order."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,78,0)="NOTE: Scheduling patch SD*5.3*227 will provide the functionality to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,79,0)="correct previous PCE data containing the erroneous date/time values."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,80,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,81,0)="  Related NOIS:  CON-0600-12803   SDC-0700-62722   HVH-0700-11960"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,82,0)="                 WRJ-0600-12784   SDC-0700-62542   SAG-0700-41748"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,83,0)="                 NIN-0800-41201   ATG-0700-32318   BUT-0700-21675"
