^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,123,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,124,0)="         Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,125,0)="         =========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,127,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,128,0)="All users may remain on the system. However Laboratory Users should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,129,0)="idle during installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,130,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,131,0)="No laboratory background jobs need to be stopped. No options need to be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,132,0)="placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,134,0)="Installation time of this patch is less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,135,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,137,0)="         1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,138,0)="            menu. This option will load the KIDS package in this "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,139,0)="            message onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,140,0)="         2. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,141,0)="            on your system. You now need to use KIDS to install "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,142,0)="            the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,143,0)="            On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,144,0)="            the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,145,0)="                Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,146,0)="                Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,147,0)="                Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,148,0)="                Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,149,0)="         3. Users may remain on the system, but installation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,150,0)="            should be done at off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,151,0)="         4. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,152,0)="         5. Installation time is less than 5 minutes during off "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,153,0)="            peak hours and less than 15 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,154,0)="         6. Installation of this patch requires no additional "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,155,0)="            memory space."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,156,0)="         7. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,157,0)="            option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,158,0)="            'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*264' "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,159,0)="            and proceed with the install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,160,0)="         8. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,161,0)="            install? YES//' respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,162,0)="         9. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE scheduled Options, Menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,163,0)="            Options, and Protocols? YES//' respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,164,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,165,0)="After the install has been completed. All users can now resume normal"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,166,0)="activities."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,0)="265 SEQ #202^3010103^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,0)="^^86^86^3010103"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,1,0)="VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE V5.2 DEVICE PRODUCT LABELING STATEMENT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,2,0)="============================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,3,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,4,0)=" June 10, 1999 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,6,0)=" VISTA Laboratory Package patch LR*5.2*265 contains no changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,7,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,8,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,9,0)=" All changes have been reviewed by the VISTA Blood Bank Developer and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,10,0)="found to have no impact on the VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE control"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,11,0)="functions.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,12,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,13,0)=" RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*265 have no effect on Blood"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,14,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,15,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,16,0)=" EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*265 does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,17,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical element"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,18,0)="functions. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,19,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,20,0)=" POTENTIAL IMPACT ON SITES: This patch contains no changes to files and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,21,0)="routines identified in Veterans Health Administration (VHA) Directive"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,22,0)="99-053. The changes that are made have no effect to Blood Bank"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,23,0)="functionality or medical device control functions. There is no adverse"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,24,0)="potential to sites."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,26,0)=" VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION: There are no required validation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,27,0)="scenarios to be completed by sites after installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,29,0)=" This patch is informational only. The routines referenced in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,30,0)="are distributed and installed with OERR V3.0 patch OR*3*97."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,32,0)="    DESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,34,0)=" This project consists of five patches that bring all HL/7 date"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,35,0)="conversions, both to and from VA FileMan format, into compliance with the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,36,0)="current HL/7 standard.  The previous standard for HL/7 dates (V2.2) listed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,37,0)="the date in YYYYMMDDHHMMSS format.  The degree of precision was listed as"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,38,0)="a separate parameter.  The new standard format (V2.3) is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,39,0)="[YYYY[MM[DD[HH[MM[SS]]]]]-zzzz] where the bracketed sections are optional"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,40,0)="depending on the existence of the subsequent set. Also, if either the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,41,0)="seconds or the minutes/seconds combination consist only of zeroes, the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,42,0)="minutes (if zeroes) and seconds will be omitted.  The length of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,43,0)="date/time string specifies the degree of precision.  In addition, a ZULU"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,44,0)="time offset (-zzzz)is also included.  This is the number of hours between"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,45,0)="Greenwich Mean Time and the local time where the date/time string was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,46,0)="created."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,48,0)="These patches are combined into a single build for ease of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,49,0)=" installation at VHA facilities: OR_3_97.KID"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,52,0)="The build is available at the following locations:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,54,0)="       OI Field Office            FTP Address        Directory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",103,1,55,0)="       ================================================================"
