^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,13,0)=" RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*265 have no effect on Blood"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,14,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,15,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,16,0)=" EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*265 does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,17,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical element"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,18,0)="functions. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,19,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,20,0)=" POTENTIAL IMPACT ON SITES: This patch contains no changes to files and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,21,0)="routines identified in Veterans Health Administration (VHA) Directive"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,22,0)="99-053. The changes that are made have no effect to Blood Bank"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,23,0)="functionality or medical device control functions. There is no adverse"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,24,0)="potential to sites."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,26,0)=" VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION: There are no required validation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,27,0)="scenarios to be completed by sites after installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,29,0)=" This patch is informational only. The routines referenced in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,30,0)="are distributed and installed with OERR V3.0 patch OR*3*97."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,32,0)="    DESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,34,0)=" This project consists of five patches that bring all HL/7 date"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,35,0)="conversions, both to and from VA FileMan format, into compliance with the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,36,0)="current HL/7 standard.  The previous standard for HL/7 dates (V2.2) listed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,37,0)="the date in YYYYMMDDHHMMSS format.  The degree of precision was listed as"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,38,0)="a separate parameter.  The new standard format (V2.3) is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,39,0)="[YYYY[MM[DD[HH[MM[SS]]]]]-zzzz] where the bracketed sections are optional"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,40,0)="depending on the existence of the subsequent set. Also, if either the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,41,0)="seconds or the minutes/seconds combination consist only of zeroes, the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,42,0)="minutes (if zeroes) and seconds will be omitted.  The length of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,43,0)="date/time string specifies the degree of precision.  In addition, a ZULU"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,44,0)="time offset (-zzzz)is also included.  This is the number of hours between"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,45,0)="Greenwich Mean Time and the local time where the date/time string was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,46,0)="created."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,48,0)="These patches are combined into a single build for ease of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,49,0)=" installation at VHA facilities: OR_3_97.KID"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,52,0)="The build is available at the following locations:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,54,0)="       OI Field Office            FTP Address        Directory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,55,0)="       ================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,56,0)="       Albany                     152.127.1.5        ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,57,0)="       Hines                      152.129.1.110      ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,58,0)="       Salt Lake City             152.131.2.1        ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,60,0)="The NOIS calls addressed are:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,61,0)="        Refer to OR*3*97"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,63,0)="  Requesting Site: Central Office, Washington, DC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,65,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,66,0)="     Test Site(s): "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,67,0)="        Refer to OR*3*97"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,69,0)="   Reference NOIS: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,70,0)="        Refer to OR*3*97"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,72,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,73,0)=" ==============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,74,0)="  The following Laboratory package routines are distributed and installed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,75,0)="with CPRS patch OR*3*97."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,77,0)="  The second line of each routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,78,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,79,0)=" <tab>;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;**[patch list]**;;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,80,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,81,0)="         CHECK^XTSUMBLD Results"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,82,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,83,0)=" Routine Name    Before Patch     After Patch   Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,84,0)=" ------------    ------------     -----------   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,85,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,86,0)="LR7OU0             7183809         6871123      121,187,265"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",105,0)="261 SEQ #203^3010103^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",105,1,0)="^^2^2^3010103"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",105,1,1,0)="LR*5.2*261"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",105,1,2,0)="Job hangs in LRWLST1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,0)="266^3010122^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,0)="^^224^224^3010122"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,1,0)=" EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patches LA*5.2*58 and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,2,0)="LR*5.2*266 do not contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,3,0)="defined by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,4,0)="5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,6,0)=" EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patches LA*5.2*58 and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,7,0)="LR*5.2*266 do not alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,8,0)="critical elements functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,10,0)=" RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patches LA*5.2*58 and LR*5.2*266 have no"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,11,0)="effect on Blood Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,13,0)="**NOTE**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,15,0)="Patches LA*5.2*58 and LR*5.2*266 are being released in a single"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,16,0)="distribution.  Because of this, patch descriptions for LA*5.2*58 and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,17,0)="LR*5.2*266 are identical and contain routine summaries for both sets of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,18,0)="routines."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,20,0)="**NOTE**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,22,0)="The laboratory routines LRVER3A and LRMIUT are being modified by this"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,23,0)="patch.  These routines may have been locally modified at the sites.  The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,24,0)="sites must ensure that precautions are taken to prevent loss of local"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,25,0)="modifications when patches to Laboratory are installed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,27,0)="**NOTE**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,29,0)="When initially setting up the FOREIGN INTERFACE file (#62.487), the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,30,0)="FOREIGN COMPUTER INTERFACE NAME field (#.01) should ALWAYS be set to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,31,0)="""CAREVUE"" (all caps, no leading or trailing spaces, and no quotes).  The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,32,0)="routines that access this file are looking specifically for CAREVUE.  The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,33,0)="routines will not be able to process the results for CareVue ward patients"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,34,0)="if this is not done."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,36,0)="This patch contains changes to Class I CareVue code and requires that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,37,0)="patch LA*5.2*53 and LR*5.2*263 be installed before LA*5.2*58.  Patches"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,38,0)="LA*5.2*58 and LR*5.2*266 are contained in the same KID file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,39,0)="(LA_52_P58.KID) and will be installed together."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,41,0)="This patch includes the following changes:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,43,0)="1.  This patch updates the documentation released with the CareVue"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,44,0)="Interface patch (LA*5.2*53)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,46,0)="2.  This patch makes changes to the routines LRVER3A and LRMIUT, and will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,47,0)="create a new routine (LA7DLOC).  Currently, two routines (LRVER3A and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,48,0)="LRMIUT) contain the Class I software for the CareVue interface. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,49,0)="will modify these routines to call the new routine (LA7DLOC).  LA7DLOC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,50,0)="contains the Class I code for determining if a patient is located in a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,51,0)="CareVue ward.  The current condition of the Class I code checks the CHEM,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,52,0)="HEM, TOX, RIA, SER, etc. field (#4) and the Microbiology field (#5) of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,53,0)="Lab Data file (#63), but the updated routines will call LA7DLOC and will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,54,0)="look in the Ward Location field (#.1) of the Patient file (#2).  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,55,0)="shows the current location of the patient.  There were problems with"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,56,0)="patients that were not transferred to the CareVue ward until after the lab"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,57,0)="order was taken. The old routine was checking where the patient was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,58,0)="located when the order was taken, and not the current location of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,59,0)="patient."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,61,0)="3.  Updates to the HL/7 date conversion routines. The previous standard"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,62,0)="for HL/7 dates listed the date in YYYYMMDDHHMMSS format.  The degree of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,63,0)="precision was listed as a separate parameter.  The new standard format is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,64,0)="[YYYY[MM[DD[HH[MM[SS]]]]]-zzzz] where the bracketed sections are optional"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,65,0)="depending on the existence of the subsequent set. Also, if either the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,66,0)="seconds or the minutes/seconds combination consist only of zeroes, the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,67,0)="minutes (if zeroes) and seconds will be omitted.  The length of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,68,0)="date/time string specifies the degree of precision. In addition, a ZULU"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,69,0)="time offset (-zzzz) is also included.  This is the number of hours between"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,70,0)="Greenwich Mean Time and the local time where the date/time string was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,71,0)="created.  Routines LA7DVM and LA7DVEXT have been modified to use the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,72,0)="Kernel function ($$FMTHL7^XLFDT) to convert dates from FileMan to HL7"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,73,0)="instead of the HL/7 date conversion utility ($$HDATE^HLFNC)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,75,0)="4.  This patch will use TaskMan to transfer data to the CareVue system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,76,0)="Currently, TaskMan is not invoked. This could cause a problem verifying a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,77,0)="result if an error was encountered in the CareVue routines."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,79,0)="5.  This patch changes the LA7D EDIT FOREIGN INTERFACE (Edit Foreign"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,80,0)="Interface Parameters) option.  It is now easier to add a Ward to a Foreign"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,81,0)="Computer System Name."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,83,0)="6.  This patch updates the Processing RTN field (#771) and the Response"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,84,0)="Processing RTN field (#772) of the Protocol file (#101) for the LA7D"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,85,0)="CARELIFE RESULTS and LA7D CARELIFE SERVER entries. The letter ""Q"" will be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,86,0)="entered by the post-init routine LR266 if no entry exists."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,88,0)="NOIS - MIA-0600-30434"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,89,0)="   Reported an error, MISSING PROCESSING ROUTINE, when sending the HL7"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,90,0)="   message from VistA to CareVue.  The letter ""Q"" will be entered by"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,91,0)="   the post-init routine LR266 if no entry exists."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,92,0)="NOIS - MWV-0900-21094"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,93,0)="   Reported that all CareVue ward patients tests were not being sent to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,94,0)="   the CareVue system.  It was discovered that these patients were ones"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,95,0)="   who were transferred from a non-CareVue ward to a CareVue ward after"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,96,0)="   the tests were ordered. The patient was bypassed since the location"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,97,0)="   at time of order was not a CareVue ward.  This patch will correct"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,98,0)="   this by looking at the Ward Location field (#.1) in the Patient file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,99,0)="   (#2) for the current location of the patient."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,101,0)="Associated NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,102,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,103,0)="MIA-0600-30434"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,104,0)="MWV-0900-21094"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,105,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,106,0)="Test Sites"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,107,0)="=========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,108,0)="Martinsburg, West Virginia"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,111,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,112,0)="================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,113,0)="The following is a list of routines included in patch LA*5.2*58. The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,114,0)="second line of each routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,115,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,116,0)="<tab>;;5.2;AUTOMATED LAB INSTRUMENTS;**[patch list]**;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,117,0)=" "
