^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,140,0)="The documentation and distribution files for patches LA*5.2*58 and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,141,0)="LR*5.2*266 may be obtained using FTP from the appropriate National VistA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,142,0)="Support directory:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,143,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,144,0)="    OI FIELD OFFICE       FTP ADDRESS             DIRECTORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,145,0)="    ===============       ===========             =========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,146,0)="     HINES               152.129.1.110      [ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,147,0)="     SALT LAKE CITY      152.131.2.1        [ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,148,0)="     ALBANY              152.127.1.5        [ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,150,0)="File names are:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,151,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,152,0)=" ASCII FILE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,153,0)="  LA_52_P58.KID     -  KIDS distribution for LA*5.2*58 and LR*5.2*266"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,154,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,155,0)=" BINARY FILE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,156,0)="  LA7DIG.PDF        -  CareVue Installation Guide"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,157,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,158,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,159,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,160,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,161,0)="  NOTE: This KIDS install does not place any options out of service"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,162,0)="        during the install and no user options are affected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,163,0)="        If KIDS prompts:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,164,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,165,0)="        ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,166,0)="         Install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,167,0)="        ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,168,0)="        ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,169,0)="        Protocols? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,171,0)="        The site should answer ""NO"" to all three questions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,172,0)="            Note: You may not receive all three prompts at your site.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,173,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,174,0)="     1. Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,175,0)="        patches LA*5.2*58 or LR*5.2*266 are mapped, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,176,0)="        removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,177,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,178,0)="     2. From the Kernel Installation & Distribution System menu (XPD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,179,0)="        MAIN), select the Installation menu option, then the option,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,180,0)="        Load a Distribution. Enter your directory name and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,181,0)="        LA_52_P58.KID at the Host File prompt."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,182,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,183,0)="     3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,184,0)="        your system. You now need to use KIDS to install the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,185,0)="        Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,187,0)="        On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,188,0)="        following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,189,0)="           Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,190,0)="           Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,191,0)="           Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,192,0)="           Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,193,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,194,0)="     4. It is recommended that this release be installed during off"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,195,0)="        peak hours.  To prevent a possible problem with the tasking"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,196,0)="        of the next days laboratory orders, do not install this package"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,197,0)="        at the same time as the following nightly tasked jobs:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,198,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,199,0)="              LRTASK ROLLOVER"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,200,0)="              LRTASK NIGHTLY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,201,0)="              LRTASK CONJAM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,202,0)="              LRTASK CUM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,203,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,204,0)="     5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,205,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,206,0)="     6. Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,207,0)="        hours and less than 5 minutes during peak hours"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,208,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,209,0)="     7. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,210,0)="        option 'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LA*5.2*58'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,211,0)="        and proceed with the install. When prompted 'Want to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,212,0)="        DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,213,0)="        YES//', choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,214,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,215,0)="     8. This patch updates the Processing RTN field (#771) and the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,216,0)="        Response Processing RTN field (#772) of the Protocol file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,217,0)="        (#101) for the LA7D CARELIFE RESULTS and LA7D CARELIFE SERVER"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,218,0)="        entries. The letter ""Q"" will be entered by the post-init"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,219,0)="        routine LR266 if no entry exists.  The LR266 routine will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,220,0)="        automatically be deleted after the patch is installed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,221,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,222,0)="     9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,223,0)="        should be returned to the mapped set once the installation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,224,0)="        has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,0)="248 SEQ #205^3010202^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,0)="^^737^737^3010202"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,1,0)="Subject: RESOLVE ANATOMIC PATHOLOGY LOGIN/REPORT PROBLEMS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,3,0)="Category:  ROUTINE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,4,0)="           DATA DICTIONARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,5,0)="           ENHANCEMENT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,6,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,7,0)="Description:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,8,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,10,0)="This patch is to resolve a number of Anatomic Pathology problems related to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,11,0)="log-in and reporting."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,13,0)="******************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,14,0)="Patch LR*5.2*248 VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,15,0)="DEVICE PRODUCT LABELING STATEMENT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,17,0)="August 23, 2000"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,19,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LR*5.2*248 contains changes to software "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,20,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,22,0)="The changes have been reviewed by the VISTA Blood Bank Developer and found to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,23,0)="have no impact on the VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE control functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,25,0)="PROBLEM:   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,26,0)="# 1.  Changes have been made to routines LRU and LRUPA to eliminate "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,27,0)="      unnecessary form feeds seen in some Anatomic Pathology reports."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,28,0)="      Blood Bank reports are unaffected.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,30,0)="# 2.  Changes have been made to routine LRUPT to include the Autopsy"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,31,0)="      accessions number on the report produced by the Show list "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,32,0)="      of accessions for a patient [LRUPT] option.  Changes have also been "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,33,0)="      made to this routine to fix a problem that occurs when an accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,34,0)="      is collected in one year but tests are performed in the next year. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,35,0)="      In this case, some of these tests are omitted from the report created"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,36,0)="      by the Show list of accessions for a patient [LRUPT] option.  The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,37,0)="      option now displays the previously omitted tests."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,39,0)="RISK ANALYSIS:  Changes made by patch LR*5.2*248 have no effect on Blood "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,40,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,42,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS:  Patch LR*5.2*248 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,43,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical elements "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,44,0)="functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,46,0)="POTENTIAL IMPACT ON SITES:  This patch contains changes to a file "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,47,0)="identified in Veterans Health Administration (VHA) Directive 99-053, group "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,48,0)="B listing. The changes have no effect in Blood Bank functionality or "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,49,0)="medical device control functions. There is no adverse potential to sites."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,51,0)="VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION:  There are no required validation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,52,0)="scenarios to be completed by sites after installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,53,0)="******************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,55,0)="Documentation Retrieval"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,56,0)="======================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,58,0)="The VISTA Laboratory Anatomic Pathology User Manual V. 5.2 released in "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,59,0)="October 1994, has been revised to include an Appendix B section and is "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,60,0)="distributed with the release of this patch. Appendix B consists of file "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,61,0)="changes, newly created fields, option modifications, and examples of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,62,0)="reformatted reports."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,64,0)="The revised AP User Manual is available in the Portable Document Format "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,65,0)="(PDF) file (i.e., LR5_2APUM.PDF) at the following Office of Information "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,66,0)="Field Office (OIFO) ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE account directories and VA Intranet "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,67,0)="web site location:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,69,0)="All sites are encouraged to use their FTP capability to obtain the PDF file."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,71,0)="Anonymous Software Accounts:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,73,0)="       IRM FIELD OFFICE     FTP ADDRESS        DIRECTORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,74,0)="       ================     ===========        ========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,75,0)="       ALBANY               152.127.1.5        [ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,76,0)="       HINES                152.129.1.110      [ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,77,0)="       SALT LAKE            152.131.2.1        [ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,78,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,79,0)="The following options have been modified with the release of this patch:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,81,0)="        Supplementary Report, Anat Path [LRAPDSR]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,82,0)="        Autopsy supplementary report [LRAPAUSR]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,83,0)="        Accession list by date [LRUPAD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,84,0)="        Show List of Accessions for a Patient [LRUPT]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,85,0)="        Modify anat path gross/micro/dx/frozen section [LRAPM]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,86,0)="        Lab orders by collection type [LRRP5] "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,87,0)="        Verify/Release Reports, Anat Path [LRAPR]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,88,0)="        Enter old anat path records [LRAPOLD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,89,0)="        Log-in, anat path [LRAPLG]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,90,0)="        Autopsy Protocol and SNOMED Coding [LRAPAUDAB]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,91,0)="        Autopsy Protocol/Supplementary Report [LRAPAUPT]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,92,0)="        Print path gross/micr/dx/fr.sect modifications [LRAPQAM]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,93,0)="        Print path modifications [LRAPMOD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,94,0)="        Print final path reports by accession # [LRAPFICH]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,95,0)="        Print all reports on queue [LRAP PRINT ALL ON QUEUE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,96,0)="        Print single report only [LRAP PRINT SINGLE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,97,0)="        Clinical Hx/Gross Description/FS [LRAPDGD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,98,0)="        FS/Gross/Micro/Dx [LRAPDGM]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,99,0)="        FS/Gross/Micro/Dx/SNOMED Coding [LRAPDGS]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,100,0)="        FS/Gross/Micro/Dx/ICD9CM Coding [LRAPDGI]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,101,0)="        Spec Studies-EM;Immuno;Consult;Pic, Anat Path [LRAPDSS]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,102,0)="        Provisional anatomic diagnoses [LRAPAUPAD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,103,0)="        Autopsy protocol [LRAPAUDAP]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,104,0)="        Autopsy protocol & ICD9CM coding [LRAPAUDAA]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,105,0)="        Final autopsy diagnoses date [LRAPAUFAD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,106,0)="        Special studies, autopsy [LRAPAUDAS]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,107,0)="        SNOMED coding, anat path [LRAPX]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,108,0)="        ICD9CM coding, anat path [LRAPICD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,109,0)="        Supplementary report release, anat path [LRAPRS]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,111,0)="Patch LR*5.2*248 adds the following new fields:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,113,0)="LAB DATA file (#63)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,114,0)=" AUTOPSY SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT (field #32.4, sub-file 63.324)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,115,0)="  SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED multiple (field #2, sub-file 63.3242) (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,116,0)="   SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #.01)                         (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,117,0)="   PERSON MODIFYING TEXT (field #.02)                                 (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,118,0)="   PREMODIFICATION TEXT (field #1, sub-file 63.32421)                 (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,120,0)=" SURGICAL PATHOLOGY(field #8, sub-file 63.08)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,121,0)="  SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT (field #1.2, sub-file 63.817)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,122,0)="   SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #2, sub-file 63.8172)         (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,123,0)="    SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #.01)                        (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,124,0)="    PERSON MODIFYING TEXT (field #.02)                                (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,125,0)="    PREMODIFICATION TEXT (field #1, sub-file 63.81721)                (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,127,0)=" EM (Electron Microscopy)(field #2, sub-file 63.02)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,128,0)="  SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT (field #1.2, sub-file 63.207)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,129,0)="   SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #2, sub-file 63.2072)         (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,130,0)="    SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #.01)                        (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,131,0)="    PERSON MODIFYING TEXT (field #.02)                                (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,132,0)="    PREMODIFICATION TEXT (field #1, sub-file 63.20721)                (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,134,0)=" CYTOPATHOLOGY (field #9, sub-file 63.09)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,135,0)="  SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT (field #1.2, sub-file 63.907)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,136,0)="   SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #2, sub-file 63.9072)         (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,137,0)="    SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #.01)                        (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,138,0)="    PERSON MODIFYING TEXT (field #.02)                                (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,139,0)="    PREMODIFICATION TEXT (field #1, sub-file 63.90721)                (New)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,140,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,141,0)="The Anatomic Pathology problems addressed by this patch are as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,142,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,143,0)="A.  ANATOMIC PATHOLOGY LOGIN/DATA ENTRY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,145,0)="1.  SYSTEM HANGS DURING LOG-IN, ANAT PATH [LRAPLG] OPTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,146,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,147,0)="When two or more users are trying to login in patients using the Log-in, anat"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,148,0)="path [LRAPLG] option the system hangs after the patient location is entered"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,149,0)="because the record in the ACCESSION file (#68) is locked.  The solution is to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,150,0)="put a five second time out on the lock with the message ""Someone else is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,151,0)="logging in specimens.  Please wait and try again.""  For example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,152,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,153,0)="Select Patient Name: DOE,JOHN  01-01-69     511111211     YES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,154,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,155,0)="PATIENT LOCATION: BON-DOM CLINIC//"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,156,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,157,0)="Someone else is logging in specimens.  Please wait and try again."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,159,0)="NOIS:  MUS-0395-70386, SHR-0595-70238"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,160,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,161,0)="2. CONTINUOUS LOOP OCCURS IN LOG-IN, ANAT PATH [LRAPLG] OPTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,162,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,163,0)="If a user is entering data using the option Log-in, anat path [LRAPLG] and the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,164,0)="user does not have the LRLAB, LRSUPER, LRVERIFY, or LRLIASON security keys,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,165,0)="the patient location prompt does not appear.  If the patient is a new patient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,166,0)="with no data in the LAB DATA file (#63), the code tries to file '???' as the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,167,0)="patient location. The Fileman DIE call does not accept '???' for patient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,168,0)="location so it attempts to retrieve the patient location again.  The result is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,169,0)="an endless loop which prints ""This is the requesting location.""  For example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,171,0)="Assign SURGICAL PATHOLOGY accession #:  2 ? YES//   (YES)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,172,0)="Date/time Specimen taken: TODAY//   (DEC 11, 1995)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,173,0)="     This is the requesting location."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,174,0)="     This is the requesting location."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,175,0)="     This is the requesting location."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,177,0)="The fix to the problem is to replace the '???' with 'UNKNOWN' which is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,178,0)="accepted by Fileman.  NOIS:  DUB-0895-32241, LEB-0899-22335, SAM-0499-22281,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,179,0)="WRJ-0298-11480, SAM-0598-20421"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,180,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,181,0)="3.  ERROR OCCURS WHEN USING ENTER OLD ANAT PATH RECORDS [LRAPOLD] OPTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,182,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,183,0)="When using the Enter old anat path records [LRAPOLD] option, the variable LRA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,184,0)="is not defined causing an undefined variable error while attempting to send"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,185,0)="female patient data to Women's Health.  For example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,187,0)="Enter Accession number: 377"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,188,0)="DATE REPORT COMPLETED: Mar 06, 1984//   (MAR 06, 1984)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,189,0)="PATHOLOGIST: LAB STAFF  LAB STAFF       LS     --              "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,190,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,191,0)="RECORDING THAT AN ERROR OCCURRED ---"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,192,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,193,0)="               Sorry 'bout that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,194,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,195,0)="          $STACK=8  $ECODE=,M6,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,196,0)="          $ZERROR=ADD+6^LRWOMEN:1, %DSM-E-UNDEF, undefined variable LRA,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,197,0)="-DSM-I-ECODE, MUMPS error code: M6"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,198,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,199,0)="To correct this error, the code now checks the LRA variable before "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,200,0)="proceeding.  NOIS:  OKL-0799-72578, FAV-0999-71182, AUG-1299-32707,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,201,0)="ANN-0200-42620, WRJ-0500-10974."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,202,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,203,0)="4.  ACCESSION NUMBER/PATIENT NAME PROMPT DOES NOT FUNCTION PROPERLY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,204,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,205,0)="A number of Anatomic Pathology data entry options use a common prompt to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,206,0)="request accession lookup by number or patient name.  The prompt is:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,207,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,208,0)="          Select Accession Number/Pt name:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,209,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,210,0)="The options are:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,211,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,212,0)="          Clinical Hx/Gross Description/FS [LRAPDGD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,213,0)="          FS/Gross/Micro/Dx [LRAPDGM]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,214,0)="          FS/Gross/Micro/Dx/SNOMED Coding [LRAPDGS]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,215,0)="          FS/Gross/Micro/Dx/ICD9CM Coding [LRAPDGI]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,216,0)="          Supplementary Report, Anat Path [LRAPDSR]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,217,0)="          Spec Studies-EM;Immuno;Consult;Pic, Anat Path [LRAPDSS]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,218,0)="          Provisional anatomic diagnoses [LRAPAUPAD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,219,0)="          Autopsy protocol [LRAPAUDAP]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,220,0)="          Autopsy protocol & SNOMED coding [LRAPAUDAB]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,221,0)="          Autopsy protocol & ICD9CM coding [LRAPAUDAA]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,222,0)="          Final autopsy diagnoses date [LRAPAUFAD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,223,0)="          Autopsy supplementary report [LRAPAUSR]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,224,0)="          Special studies, autopsy [LRAPAUDAS]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,225,0)="          SNOMED coding, anat path [LRAPX]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,226,0)="          ICD9CM coding, anat path [LRAPICD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,227,0)="          Modify anat path gross/micro/dx/frozen section [LRAPM]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,228,0)="          Verify/release reports, anat path [LRAPR]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,229,0)="          Supplementary report release, anat path [LRAPRS]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,230,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,231,0)="When an accession number is entered at this prompt, data is retrieved "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,232,0)="properly.  However, when a patient name is entered another patient name"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,233,0)="prompt appears requiring the user to re-enter the patient name.  A"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,234,0)="different name can even be used at the second prompt.  For example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,235,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,236,0)="Select Accession Number/Pt name: JONES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,237,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,238,0)="Select Patient Name: SMITH"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,239,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,240,0)="A second problem also occurs at this prompt.  In most data entry options, the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,241,0)="data entry year prompt appears just before the accession number/patient name"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,242,0)="prompt. For example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,243,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,244,0)="Data entry for 2000 ? YES//   (YES)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,245,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,246,0)="Select Accession Number/Pt name: 1  for 2000"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,247,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,248,0)="If the accession number is used for lookup, only accessions for the year "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,249,0)="chosen are allowed to be entered.  However, if patient name is used for "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,250,0)="lookup, all accessions found for the patient are presented to the user.  If "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,251,0)="the user chooses an accession for a year that is not the same as the year "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,252,0)="entered at the original prompt, it is possible that accession data for the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,253,0)="wrong patient is presented to the user.  This occurs because the lookup "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,254,0)="uses the year entered at the original prompt, not the actual year of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,255,0)="accession when locating the data in the ACCESSION file (#68). "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,257,0)="These problems have been resolved by modifying the prompt to perform lookup "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,258,0)="for both accession number and patient name, eliminating the second prompt."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,259,0)="The prompt has also been modified to present only accessions for the chosen"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,260,0)="year when looking up the accession by patient name.  Help text has been added"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,261,0)="to the prompt as well.  NOIS: HAM-1199-22006, HAM-1100-21233, BOI-0400-52235"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,262,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,263,0)="B.  ANATOMIC PATHOLOGY REPORTS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,264,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,265,0)="1.  UNNECESSARY FORM FEEDS OCCUR WHILE PRINTING ANATOMIC PATHOLOGY REPORTS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,266,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,267,0)="Several Anatomic Pathology reports are violating the DHCP Programming"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,268,0)="Standards and Conventions (SAC) by starting with a forum feed before printing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,269,0)="the report and printing two form feeds at the end of the report.  These "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,270,0)="reports, the Surgical Pathology, Cytopathology and Electron Microscopy"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,271,0)="Preliminary, Final and Supplementary Reports, the Autopsy Protocol and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,272,0)="Supplementary reports, and the Final Pathology Report by Accession Number have"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,273,0)="been corrected by removing the unnecessary form feeds so that the reports now"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,274,0)="conform to standards.  The related options for these reports are:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,275,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,276,0)="     Print all reports on queue [LRAP PRINT ALL ON QUEUE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,277,0)="     Print single report only [LRAP PRINT SINGLE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,278,0)="     Print final path reports by accession # [LRAPFICH]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,279,0)="     Autopsy protocol/supplementary report [LRAPAUPT]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,280,0)="     Print path modifications [LRAPMOD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,281,0)="     Print path gross/micr/dx/fr.sect modifications [LRAPQAM]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,282,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,283,0)="NOIS:  WPB-0696-30073, IND-1097-41646"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,284,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,285,0)="2.  NOT ABLE TO DISTINGUISH BETWEEN THE PATIENT AND THE PHYSICIAN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,286,0)="    ON THE FOOTER OF THE AUTOPSY PROTOCOL REPORT."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,287,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,288,0)="The autopsy protocol report is generated by the Print all reports on queue"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,289,0)="[LRAP PRINT ALL ON QUEUE], Print single report only [LRAP PRINT SINGLE], and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,290,0)="Autopsy protocol/supplementary report [LRAPAUPT] options.  The footer of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,291,0)="autopsy protocol report has been modified to distinguish the patient's name"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,292,0)="from the physician's name because it is easy for those reading the report to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,293,0)="confuse the two names.  Labels ""Patient:"" and ""Physician:"" were added in front"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,294,0)="of the names so that they are now easy to identify.  The spacing of the other"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,295,0)="fields has been adjusted to allow for better readability.  For example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,296,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,297,0)="Pathologist:  DOE,JOHN                                  wty| Date Nov 24, 1999|"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,298,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,299,0)="Dallas CIOFO                                                  AUTOPSY PROTOCOL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,300,0)="Patient: SMITH,JOHN                       567-44-5533  SEX:M  DOB:Sep 09, 1979"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,301,0)="MEDICINE               Physician:  DOE,JANE                   AGE AT DEATH:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,302,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,303,0)="Also, the field spacing of the header for the weights, measures, and coding"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,304,0)="section of the report has been redesigned for better readability.  For "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,305,0)="example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,306,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,307,0)="Jan 10, 2000 11:08    Dallas CIOFO                                    Pg: 9"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,308,0)="ANATOMIC PATHOLOGY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,309,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,310,0)="SMITH,JOHN                      567-44-5533         DOB:Sep 09, 1979"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,311,0)="Acc #: AU 99 2                  AUTOPSY DATA        Age:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,312,0)="Date/time Died                                      Date/time of Autopsy"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,313,0)="May 07, 1999                    FULL AUTOPSY        Oct 14, 1999 17:19"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,314,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,315,0)="NOIS: None"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,316,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,317,0)="3.  CREATE AN AUDIT TRAIL FOR THE SUPPLEMENTARY ANATOMIC PATHOLOGY REPORTS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,318,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,319,0)="It is possible to edit a supplementary report with no audit trail after the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,320,0)="report has been released.  This patch will create an audit trail when a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,321,0)="released supplementary report is edited or when the entire pathology report "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,322,0)="is edited.  The audit trail information such as who modified the report, the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,323,0)="date/time the modification was made, and the original text before the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,324,0)="modification occurred will appear on the supplementary report. New fields have"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,325,0)="been created to store this data.  The fields are:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,326,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,327,0)="a.) SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,328,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,329,0)="When a user modifies an existing report, the date/time of the modification is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,330,0)="stored in this field.  If the user creates a new supplementary report for a "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,331,0)="released pathology report, this audit information is also stored."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,332,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,333,0)="b.) PERSON MODIFYING TEXT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,334,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,335,0)="The DUZ of the user who created or modified the report is stored in this"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,336,0)="field."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,337,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,338,0)="c.) PREMODIFICATION TEXT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,339,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,340,0)="This is the original text, as it existed before the modification occurred."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,341,0)="This is for existing reports only."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,342,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,343,0)="Since supplementary reports are included in the autopsy, surgical pathology,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,344,0)="electron microscopy, and cytopathology sections, these three fields were "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,345,0)="added for each section in the LAB DATA file (#63) as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,346,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,347,0)="LAB DATA file (#63)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,348,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,349,0)="AUTOPSY SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT (field #32.4, sub-file 63.324)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,350,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,351,0)="New fields:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,352,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,353,0)="   Multiple field SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #2, sub-file 63.3242)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,354,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,355,0)="          Consisting of:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,356,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,357,0)="               SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #.01)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,358,0)="               PERSON MODIFYING TEXT (field #.02)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,359,0)="               PREMODIFICATION TEXT (field #1, sub-file 63.32421)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,360,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,361,0)="SURGICAL PATHOLOGY(field #8, sub-file 63.08)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,362,0)="   SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT (field #1.2, sub-file 63.817)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,363,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,364,0)="New fields:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,365,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,366,0)="   Multiple field SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #2, sub-file 63.8172)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,367,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,368,0)="          Consisting of:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,369,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,370,0)="               SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #.01)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,371,0)="               PERSON MODIFYING TEXT (field #.02)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,372,0)="               PREMODIFICATION TEXT (field #1, sub-file 63.81721)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,373,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,374,0)="EM (Electron Microscopy)(field #2, sub-file 63.02)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,375,0)="   SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT (field #1.2, sub-file 63.207)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,376,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,377,0)="New fields:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,378,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,379,0)="   Multiple field SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #2, sub-file 63.2072)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,380,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,381,0)="          Consisting of:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,382,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,383,0)="               SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #.01)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,384,0)="               PERSON MODIFYING TEXT (field #.02)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,385,0)="               PREMODIFICATION TEXT (field #1, sub-file 63.20721)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,386,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,387,0)="CYTOPATHOLOGY (field #9, sub-file 63.09)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,388,0)="   SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT (field #1.2, sub-file 63.907)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,389,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,390,0)="New fields:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,391,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,392,0)="   Multiple field SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #2, sub-file 63.9072)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,393,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,394,0)="          Consisting of:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,395,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,396,0)="               SUPPLEMENTARY REPORT MODIFIED (field #.01)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,397,0)="               PERSON MODIFYING TEXT (field #.02)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,398,0)="               PREMODIFICATION TEXT (field #1, sub-file 63.90721)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,399,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,400,0)="Any option that allows the input of supplementary reports has been modified"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,401,0)="to store these three pieces of information multiple times for each "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,402,0)="modification to a supplementary report.  This is not visible to the user.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,403,0)="These options include Supplementary Report, Anat Path [LRAPDSR] and Autopsy"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,404,0)="supplementary report [LRAPAUSR]."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,405,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,406,0)="All options that print supplementary report information have been modified "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,407,0)="to display the audit information as well.  These options include:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,408,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,409,0)="              Print all reports on queue [LRAP PRINT ALL ON QUEUE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,410,0)="              Print single report only [LRAP PRINT SINGLE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,411,0)="              Print final path reports by accession # [LRAPFICH]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,412,0)="              Print path modifications [LRAPMOD]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,413,0)="              Autopsy Protocol/Supplementary Report [LRAPAUPT]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,414,0)="              Print path gross/micr/dx/fr.sect modifications [LRAPQAM]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,415,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,416,0)="This information is displayed for preliminary reports, final reports, autopsy"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,417,0)="protocol, and autopsy supplementary reports."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,418,0)="E3R: 3687 NOIS: SAM-0599-21489, DAY-0499-40904, SLC-1199-52531,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,419,0)="SLC-1199-51746"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,420,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,421,0)="4.  THE DUZ OF THE TECHNOLOGIST, RATHER THAN THE INITIALS, APPEARS ON"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,422,0)="    THE 'TECH' COLUMN OF THE ACCESSION LIST BY DATE [LRUPAD] OPTION REPORT."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,423,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,424,0)="The Accession List by Date [LRUPAD] option report is incorrectly displaying a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,425,0)="numeric value that has no meaning to the user in the 'Tech' column.  The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,426,0)="software has been modified to print the initials of the technologist who"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,427,0)="verified the report.  For example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,428,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,429,0)="Jan 10, 2000 11:20    Dallas CIOFO                                    Pg: 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,430,0)="CHEMISTRY (Jan 01, 1999-Jan 10, 2000)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,431,0)="# = Not VA patient                                         %=Test not verified"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,432,0)="Acc #   Date  Patient             ID    Loc   Spec/sample    Test         Tech"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,433,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,434,0)="    1   01/04 STAHLMAN,ALBERTA    1263  W3E   SERUM          %LYTES         FS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,435,0)="    2   01/04 STAHLMAN,ALBERTA    1263  W3E   SERUM          %CALCIUM       FS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,436,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,437,0)="NOIS:  ALN-0395-10067"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,438,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,439,0)="5.  A PATHOLOGIST IS ABLE TO ENTER A FUTURE DATE/TIME WHEN USING"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,440,0)="    VERIFY/RELEASE REPORTS, ANAT PATH [LRAPR] OPTION TO RELEASE A"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,441,0)="    PATHOLOGY REPORT."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,442,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,443,0)="When using option Verify/release reports, anat path [LRAPR] to release a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,444,0)="pathology report, the pathologist may enter a future date/time at the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,445,0)="'Report Release Date/Time' prompt.  Only current date/time should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,446,0)="allowed.  The prompt has been replaced with a yes/no question as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,447,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,448,0)="Release report?  No//"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,449,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,450,0)="!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,451,0)="! PLEASE NOTE:  With the old prompt, the user was able to enter an   !"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,452,0)="! 'N' for NOW to store the current date/time.  A response of 'N'     !"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,453,0)="! at the new prompt will result in a 'No' which will leave the       !"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,454,0)="! report unreleased.                                                 !"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,455,0)="!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,456,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,457,0)="If  the user answers 'Yes', the current date/time is stored in the REPORT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,458,0)="RELEASE DATE/TIME field (#.11) of the SURGICAL PATHOLOGY sub-file (#63.08),"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,459,0)="field (#8) of the LAB DATA file (#63) for the SURGICAL PATHOLOGY section.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,460,0)="For the CYTOPATHOLOGY section, the current date/time is stored in the REPORT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,461,0)="RELEASE DATE/TIME field (#.11) of the CYTOPATHOLOGY sub-file (#63.09), "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,462,0)="sub-field (#9).  For the ELECTRON MICROSCOPY (EM) section, the current "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,463,0)="date/time is stored in the REPORT RELEASE DATE/TIME field (#.11) of the EM "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,464,0)="sub-file (#63.02),sub-field (#2).  For the AUTOPSY section, the current "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,465,0)="date/time is stored in the AUTOPSY RELEASE DATE/TIME field (#14.7) of the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,466,0)="LAB DATA file (#63).  If the report has already been released, the following "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,467,0)="text will appear:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,468,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,469,0)="         Report released JAN 06, 2000@16:47:32 by YOUNG,TIM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,470,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,471,0)="The user will then be prompted for another accession number or patient "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,472,0)="name."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,473,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,474,0)="The ""@"" sign response to unrelease Provisional Anatomical Diagnosis reports"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,475,0)="awaiting Final Anatomical Diagnosis has been changed to a YES/NO response "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,476,0)="(i.e.,Unrelease report? NO//YES).  NOIS:  REN-0197-61357"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,477,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,478,0)="6.  WEIGHTS, MEASURES, AND CODING PRINT ON AUTOPSY REPORT REGARDLESS OF"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,479,0)="    ANSWER TO YES/NO QUESTION ON AUTOPSY PROTOCOL REPORT."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,480,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,481,0)="When option Print all reports on queue [LRAP PRINT ALL ON QUEUE] or option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,482,0)="Print single report only [LRAP PRINT SINGLE] is used for the AUTOPSY section"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,483,0)="to create the Autopsy Protocol Report, the question 'Print weights, measures"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,484,0)="and coding (if present): ? YES// ' is asked.  Regardless of the user's"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,485,0)="response to this question (Yes or No), the weights, measures, and coding"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,486,0)="information is printed on the report.  The Autopsy Protocol report has been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,487,0)="corrected so that if the user answers 'No' to this question, the weights,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,488,0)="measures, and coding information will not print on the report. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,489,0)="NOIS: DAY-0595-40195"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,490,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,491,0)="7.  ACCESSION NUMBER WRAPS ON SURGICAL PATHOLOGY REPORTS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,492,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,493,0)="When using option Print single report only [LRAP PRINT SINGLE] or option "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,494,0)="Print all reports on queue [LRAP PRINT ALL ON QUEUE]to print pathology "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,495,0)="reports, if the accession number is too large, it wraps to the next line "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,496,0)="when the report prints.  This problem was resolved by adjusting the print "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,497,0)="position of the accession number so that no wrapping will occur."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,498,0)="NOIS:  MAR-0398-22377"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,499,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,500,0)="8.  SYNONYMS MAY CAUSE INCORRECT TESTS TO BE DISPLAYED ON THE LAB ORDERS BY "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,501,0)="    COLLECTION TYPE [LRRP5] OPTION REPORT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,502,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,503,0)="The Lab Orders by Collection Type [LRRP5] report may indicate incorrect"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,504,0)="tests as being ordered if a particular test has a SYNONYM (field #2, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,505,0)="sub-file #60.1) of the LABORATORY TEST file (#60) that is identical to the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,506,0)="internal entry number (IEN) of the look-up test. For example, suppose "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,507,0)="GLUCOSE has an IEN of 175 in the LABORATORY TEST file (#60) and FERRITIN "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,508,0)="has a SYNONYM (#2) of 175 in file #60.  When the code is executed, the return"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,509,0)="value is Ferritin and not Glucose. The fix to this problem is to concatenate"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,510,0)="an accent/grave (`)character to the beginning of the lookup value before"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,511,0)="performing a lookup with DIC(0). When the accent grave (`) character is "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,512,0)="used, the lookup is limited to the internal entry numbers only and thus"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,513,0)="ignoring the SYNONYM (#2).  NOIS:  IND-0797-40657."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,514,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,515,0)="9.  PROBLEMS WITH SHOW LIST OF ACCESSIONS FOR A PATIENT [LRUPT] OPTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,516,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,517,0)="Two different problems were reported with this option.  They are:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,518,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,519,0)="(A)  When running the Show list of accessions for a patient [LRUPT] option,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,520,0)="'??' displays where the accession should be when using the Autopsy section."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,521,0)="This option will now display the accession number on the report for the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,522,0)="Autopsy section.  NOIS:  AUG-0398-32638"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,523,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,524,0)="(B)  There is also a problem with certain tests not appearing when this option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,525,0)="is run, even though the missing tests do appear on other accession list"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,526,0)="reports.  For example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,527,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,528,0)="CHEMISTRY           DANGERFIELD,RODNEY ID: 222-33-4444  TESTS ORDERED"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,529,0)="Spec Date/time  Acc #           Site/specimen              Tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,530,0)="01/15/93 10:11  CH 0115 9       SERUM                     1)CALCIUM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,531,0)="12/26/92 11:00  CH 0115 8       SERUM       "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,532,0)="11/13/92 16:14  CH 1113 6       SERUM                     1)GLUCOSE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,533,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,534,0)="Notice that the test is missing on the second line.  It was discovered that "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,535,0)="this occurred on accessions in which the user enters a collection date for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,536,0)="the previous year but the order date is in the current year.  For example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,537,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,538,0)="ACCESSION: CH 0115 8     ORDER #: 183   PATIENT: DANGERFIELD,RODNEY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,539,0)="                                                 222-33-4444"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,540,0)="  LOCATION:GEN MED                      DATE ORDERED: 01/15/93"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,541,0)="                                    **  COLLECTED: 12/26/92 11:00  **"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,542,0)="  PRACTITIONER: BABCOCK,LISA            LAB ARRIVAL: 01/15/93 08:23"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,543,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,544,0)="This scenario occurred because routine ^LRUPT was using the wrong year when "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,545,0)="looking for information in the ACCESSION file (#68.)  LRUPT has now been "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,546,0)="corrected to use the correct year.  NOIS:  SYR-0193-10004"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,547,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,548,0)="10.  TYPO IN CODE EXECUTED WITH THE DISPLAY STAINS/BLOCKS FOR A PATIENT "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,549,0)="     [LRAPST] OPTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,550,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,551,0)="The carat (^) is missing from the global entry in routine AU^LRAPST1 which"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,552,0)="causes an error that no autopsy accession exists for this patient even if one"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,553,0)="does exist.  The carat has now been added and the routine will now properly"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,554,0)="indicate whether an autopsy accession number exists for the patient."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,555,0)="NOIS: AUG-0398-32638"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,556,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,557,0)="11.  REPORTS NOT QUEUED TO THE COMPLETED REPORT QUEUE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,558,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,559,0)="A modification to routine LRAPM, released in patch LR*5.2*231, inadvertently"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,560,0)="prevents reports generated by the [LRAPM] Modify anat path"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,561,0)="gross/micro/dx/frozen section option, from being queued to the completed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,562,0)="reports print queue if the patient is male.  The code has now been corrected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,563,0)="NOIS:  There is no NOIS associated with this item."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,564,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,565,0)="12.  ANATOMIC PATHOLOGY REPORTS BECOME UNRELEASED WHEN NO CHANGES ARE MADE "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,566,0)="     USING THE MODIFY ANAT PATH GROSS/MICRO/DX/FROZEN SECTION [LRAPM] OPTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,567,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,568,0)="A problem was reported regarding the use of the Modify anat path"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,569,0)="gross/micro/dx/frozen section [LRAPM] option to modify the gross description"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,570,0)="of a released/verified report.  Even though the user returned through all the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,571,0)="prompts without making changes and the report is tagged as not modified, the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,572,0)="report became ""UNRELEASED"" making it unavailable for providers to view.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,573,0)="error has now been corrected so that if no changes are made to the report, the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,574,0)="release date/time remains in place. NOIS: BHS-0600-12155"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,575,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,576,0)="Reference NOIS list:   LEB-0899-22335"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,577,0)="                       DAY-0499-40904"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,578,0)="                       SAM-0599-21489"
