^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,286,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,287,0)="         Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,288,0)="         =========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,289,0)="The Host File for this patch can be obtained from the ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,290,0)="directory at one of the following OI Field Offices:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,291,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,292,0)="  OI FIELD OFFICE     FTP ADDRESS      DIRECTORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,293,0)="  Albany              152.127.1.5      anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,294,0)="  Hines               152.129.1.110    anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,295,0)="  Salt Lake           152.131.2.1      anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,296,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,297,0)="The file name is LR52_258.KID "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,298,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,299,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,300,0)="         1. From the Kernel Installation & Distribution System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,301,0)="            select the 'Installation Menu'. Select the option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,302,0)="            Load a distribution."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,303,0)="            Select [disk storage location]LR52_258.KID"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,304,0)="         2. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,305,0)="            on your system. You now need to use KIDS to install "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,306,0)="            the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,307,0)="            On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,308,0)="            the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,309,0)="                Print Transport Global (Patch size is very large)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,310,0)="                Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,311,0)="                Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,312,0)="                Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,313,0)="         3. Users may remain on the system however Laboratory "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,314,0)="            users must be idle. This to say the laboratory users should"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,315,0)="            not accessioning, instrument downloads or test verification"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,316,0)="            during the install. Installation should be done during off"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,317,0)="            peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,318,0)="         4. No options need to be placed out of service. No"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,319,0)="            laboratory background jobs have to be stopped."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,320,0)="         5. Installation time is less than 15 minutes during off "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,321,0)="            peak hours and less than 35 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,322,0)="         6. Installation of this patch requires minimal additional "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,323,0)="            disk space. Review your map set for the routine"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,324,0)="            LRCAPDAR. The routine LRCAPDAR should not be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,325,0)="            currently mapped. If LRCAPDAR is mapped you must"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,326,0)="            rebuild map sets after installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,327,0)="         7. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,328,0)="            option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,329,0)="            'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*258' "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,330,0)="            and proceed with the install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,331,0)="         8. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,332,0)="            install? YES//' respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,333,0)="         9. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE scheduled Options, Menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,334,0)="            Options, and Protocols? YES//' respond NO. Respond to Rebuild"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,335,0)="            Menu Trees? YES// YES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,336,0)="        10. After successful installation, routines LR258 and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,337,0)="            LR258PO should be removed from the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,338,0)="After the install has been completed. All users can now resume normal"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,339,0)="activities of accessioning and test verfications."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,340,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,341,0)="Laboratory Information Manager (LIM) should review the mail message"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,342,0)="containing the workload codes additions to determine if there is a need to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,343,0)="link or re-link laboratory tests. Before linking any workload code the CPT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,344,0)="coding should be reviewed for appropriateness."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,0)="268 SEQ #207^3010405^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,0)="^^235^235^3010405"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,1,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LR*5.2*268 contains no changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,2,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,4,0)="This patch will addresses a fix to the options Long form accession list"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,5,0)="[LRACC1] and Long form accession list for microbiology [LRMIACC1]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,6,0)="regarding the printing of completed accessions from non-daily accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,7,0)="areas. The problem was reported in NOIS CIN-0299-41416. Additional"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,8,0)="problems (item 2-8) were identified for these two options during the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,9,0)="software review for patch development. Listed below are the problems and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,10,0)="the corrective actions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,11,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,12,0)="1.  NOIS CIN-0299-41416 reported that when using the combination of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,13,0)="listing by date and NOT wanting only incomplete entries, the report"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,14,0)="did not print all entries (completed and incomplete accessions). "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,16,0)="The reports have been corrected to print completed accessions when the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,17,0)="user answers ""NO"" to the prompt ""Do you want only incomplete entries?""."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,18,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,19,0)="2.  At the prompt ""Do you want only incomplete entries?"" if the user"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,20,0)="entered a ""?"" the software would bypass the prompt and proceed to the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,21,0)="next prompt for device selection. Entering a ""?"" will now present the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,22,0)="user with a help message and return to the prompt. This defect was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,23,0)="identified during software review."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,25,0)="3.  Printing of the lab order number and the patient name could print"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,26,0)="together when the order number exceeds five digits. Also patients with "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,27,0)="long names could cause the printing of the patient's identifier (SSN)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,28,0)="to wrap to the next line of the display. The printing of accession and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,29,0)="patient information on the report has been adjusted to provide sufficient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,30,0)="space to avoid this information printing together. This defect was "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,31,0)="identified during software review."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,33,0)="4.  The patch corrects a Vista Programming Standards and Conventions"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,34,0)="(SAC) violation that was identified during software review as part of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,35,0)="patch development. The patch removes direct global read of global ^VA(200)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,36,0)="which contains the NEW PERSON (#200) file.  Routine LRWRKLS1 was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,37,0)="retrieving user's name. Call to the file has been changed to Kernel"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,38,0)="supported reference (DBIA # 10060) using FileMan DBS call $$GET1^DIQ."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,39,0)="This defect was identified during software review."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,41,0)="5.  The patch converts a call to routine LRAFUNC1 to display date/time"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,42,0)="values. This routine is being phased out. Call has been replaced with"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,43,0)="calls to Kernel supported XLFDT date/time function."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,45,0)="6. Various non-interactive calls to %DT in routines LRWRKLST and LRWRKLS1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,46,0)="have been replaced with calls to corresponding Kernel supported XLFDT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,47,0)="date/time functions to determine current date/time and display other"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,48,0)="date/time values associated with the accession."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,50,0)="7. When selecting a listing for a specific test and incompletes only"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,51,0)="criteria the report would print information for some accessions before"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,52,0)="applying the selection criteria. The report has been changed to print"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,53,0)="patient and accession information when the accession meets the specified"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,54,0)="selection criteria. This defect was identified during software review."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,56,0)="8. The options Long form accession list [LRACC1] and Long form accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,57,0)="list for microbiology [LRMIACC1] will now honor stop requests when tasked."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,58,0)="Users can call the TaskMan User [XUTM USER] option to stop tasks that they"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,59,0)="started."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,62,0)="ASSOCIATED NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,63,0)="---------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,64,0)=" CIN-0299-41416 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,65,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,67,0)="ASSOCIATED E3R'S"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,68,0)="----------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,69,0)=" None"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,72,0)="TEST SITES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,73,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,74,0)=" Cincinnati VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,75,0)=" Milwaukee VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,78,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,79,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,80,0)="  The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,81,0)="  of each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,82,0)="  <tab> ;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;<patchlist>;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,84,0)="                    Checksum       Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,85,0)="   Routine Name     Before Patch   After Patch    Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,86,0)="   ------------     ------------   -----------    ------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,87,0)="   LR268            N/A            4332160        **268** (Deleted by KIDS)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,88,0)="   LRWRKLS1         6588663        4126947        **121,153,185,268**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,89,0)="   LRWRKLST         9455120        6742016        **1,17,38,153,185,221,268**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,91,0)="List of preceding patches: 221"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,92,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,93,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,94,0)="************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,96,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,97,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,99,0)="  The install time for this patch is less than 5 minutes. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,100,0)="  can be installed when Laboratory users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,101,0)="  Suggested time to install: non-peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,102,0)="  The install will disable several Lab options as specified in #7 below."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,105,0)="NOTE: Kernel patches must be current on the target system"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,106,0)="      to avoid problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,108,0)="      Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,109,0)="      Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,112,0)="  1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,114,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,115,0)="      option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,117,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,118,0)="      system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,120,0)="  4.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,121,0)="      select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,123,0)="  5.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,124,0)="      all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,125,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,126,0)="  6.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,127,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,128,0)="        Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,129,0)="        Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,130,0)="        Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,131,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,132,0)="      If you wish to preserve a copy of the routines exported in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,133,0)="      prior to installation, you should use the 'Backup a Transport Global'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,134,0)="      option at this time.  You may also compare the routines in your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,135,0)="      production account to the routines in the patch by using the 'Compare"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,136,0)="      a Transport Global to Current System' option."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,138,0)="  7.  The install will disable the following Lab options during patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,139,0)="      installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,141,0)="      Long form accession list [LRACC1]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,142,0)="      Long form accession list for microbiology [LRMIACC1]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,143,0)="      Lookup accession [LR LOOKUP ACCESSION]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,145,0)="  8.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,146,0)="      and select the package 'LR*5.2*268'.  When prompted 'Want to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,147,0)="      DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES//',"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,148,0)="      choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,150,0)="  9. On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,151,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,152,0)=" 10. Routine LR268 will be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,154,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,155,0)="POST-INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,156,0)="==============================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,157,0)="None"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,159,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,160,0)="************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,161,0)="Installation example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,162,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,163,0)="Select Installation Option: 6  Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,164,0)="Select INSTALL NAME: LR*5.2*268 Loaded from Distribution  12/8/00@11:51:43"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,165,0)="     => LR*5.2*268"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,166,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,167,0)="This Distribution was loaded on Dec 08, 2000@11:51:43 with header of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,168,0)="   LR*5.2*268"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,169,0)="   It consisted of the following Install(s):"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,170,0)="     LR*5.2*268"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,171,0)="Checking Install for Package LR*5.2*268"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,172,0)="Will first run the Environment Check Routine, LR268"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,174,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,175,0)="                        --- Environment Check is Ok ---"
