^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",110,1,192,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",110,1,193,0)=" Install Message sent #25038"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",111,0)="267 SEQ #209^3010423^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,0)="^^7^7^3010423"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,1,0)="This patch provides the VistA Blood Bank Software the ability to read and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,2,0)="interpret blood product barcode labels using the ISBT 128 system.  The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,3,0)="ability to read and interpret blood product labels using the Codabar"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,4,0)="system is unaffected.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,6,0)="A full description of this patch can be found in the Forum Patch Module"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,7,0)="listing for patch LR*5.2*267."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",112,0)="232^3010906^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",112,1,0)="^^5^5^3010906"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",112,1,1,0)="This patch allows you to map Lab tests to a default LOINC code."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",112,1,2,0)="National training will be provided to aid sites in mapping the sites' tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",112,1,3,0)="to LOINC codes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",112,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",112,1,5,0)="The LAB LOINC (95.3) file is updated to LOINC (R) version 1.0N."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,0)="269 SEQ #211^3011106^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,0)="^^267^267^3011106"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,1,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LR*5.2*269 contains no changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,2,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,5,0)="DESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,6,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,7,0)="This patch will address fixes to defects reported in NOIS LEX-1098-42357"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,8,0)="and PHI-0201-21212 and compliance changes for Standards and Conventions"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,9,0)="Programming Standards (SAC) violations for the group verify process."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,11,0)="1. When using option Group verify (EA, EL, EW) [LRGV] that the warning"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,12,0)="message ""THIS DATA APPEARS TO BELONG TO SOMEONE ELSE"" was displayed on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,13,0)="each accession to be verified. This defect was caused by the inappropriate"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,14,0)="use of the $TEST function. Routine LRGV1 will now skip result data in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,15,0)="the ^LAH global if the data does not belong to the same accession area,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,16,0)="accession date and accession number. NOIS LEX-1098-42357 and PHI-0201-21212"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,18,0)="2. During patch development software review the following SAC violations"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,19,0)="were identified."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,21,0)="   a. Routine LRGV2 contained a direct global read of the ^DD global to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,22,0)="   retrieve the name of the corresponding dataname from LAB DATA file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,23,0)="   (#63), CHEM, HEM, TOX, RIA, SER, etc. subfile (#4). Defect corrected"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,24,0)="   with change to Kernel supported reference (DBIA # 2052) using"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,25,0)="   FileMan DBS call $$GET1^DID."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,27,0)="   b. Routine LRGV1 contained locks on ^LAH global without timeouts."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,28,0)="   Defect corrected by adding timeouts to locking of ^LAH global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,30,0)="   c. Routine LRGV contained code to set variables IO and IOSL. Defect"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,31,0)="   corrected by removing code."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,33,0)="3. During patch development software review the following defects were"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,34,0)="   identified and corrected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,36,0)="   a. Comments associated with results could possibly be duplicated"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,37,0)="   when moved from the ^LAH global to the LAB DATA file (#63), CHEM,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,38,0)="   HEM, TOX, RIA, SER, etc. subfile (#4), COMMENT field (#.99)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,39,0)="   Defect corrected in routine LRGV2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,41,0)="   b. Monthly accession areas would not be processed. Routine LRGP1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,42,0)="   was not calculating accession date correctly for monthly accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,43,0)="   areas. The defect was reported by Lloyd Milligan of Sea Island"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,44,0)="   Systems, Inc."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,45,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,46,0)="   c. When processing/verifying by tray/cup and a corresponding entry in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,47,0)="   the ^LAH global did not exist for the tray/cup combination then"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,48,0)="   processing would stop and leave remaining entries unprocessed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,49,0)="   Routine LRGV will now continue to process remaining entries."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,51,0)="   d. If results exist for different accession areas but the same"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,52,0)="   accession numbers then routine LRGP was not handling these results"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,53,0)="   properly and keeping them separate. Routine has been corrected to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,54,0)="   keep results for different accessions but the same accession number"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,55,0)="   separate based on accession area and accession date."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,57,0)="   e. Option Group unverified review (EA, EL, EW) [LRGP] could print"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,58,0)="   results for accessions that are not for the same accession area,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,59,0)="   accession date and accession number. Routine LRGP will now skip result"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,60,0)="   data in the ^LAH global if the data does not belong to the same accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,61,0)="   area, accession date and accession number."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,63,0)="   f. Option Group unverified review (EA, EL, EW) [LRGP] could print"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,64,0)="   the wrong date/time on the printed report if the reported was queued"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,65,0)="   via TaskMan. Option was printing the date/time that the user originally"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,66,0)="   setup the report. Report will now print the date/time that the report"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,67,0)="   actually starts to print."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,69,0)="   g. Option Group verify (EA, EL, EW) [LRGV] would verify flagged results"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,70,0)="   which contained critical results and or a delta check when the user"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,71,0)="   indicated that these results should not be group verified. The option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,72,0)="   will now only verify results that are critical or have a delta check"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,73,0)="   when the user indicates that flagged results should be verified."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,75,0)="   h. Option Group verify (EA, EL, EW) [LRGV] was storing verified results"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,76,0)="   in LAB DATA file (#63) without NLT order and result codes, test units,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,77,0)="   performing facility, and results flags. The option will now store these"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,78,0)="   result parameters."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,80,0)="   i. Option Group verify (EA, EL, EW) [LRGV] will now allow the user to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,81,0)="   abort from a verifying session and will pause when the display screen"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,82,0)="   is filled. The test results being verified will print on the report."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,85,0)="4. The options Group verify (EA, EL, EW) [LRGV] and Group unverified"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,86,0)="review (EA, EL, EW) [LRGP] will now honor stop requests when tasked."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,87,0)="Users can call the TaskMan User [XUTM USER] option to stop tasks that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,88,0)="they started."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,90,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,91,0)="ASSOCIATED NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,92,0)="---------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,93,0)=" LEX-1098-42357"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,94,0)=" PHI-0201-21212"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,97,0)="ASSOCIATED E3R'S"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,98,0)="----------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,99,0)=" None"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,101,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,102,0)="TEST SITES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,103,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,104,0)=" Durham VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,105,0)=" Lexington VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,106,0)=" Philadelphia VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,108,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,109,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,110,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,111,0)="  The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,112,0)="  of each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,113,0)="  <tab> ;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;<patchlist>;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,115,0)="                    Checksum       Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,116,0)="   Routine Name     Before Patch   After Patch    Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,117,0)="   ------------     ------------   -----------    ------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,118,0)="   LR269            N/A            4831472        **269** (Deleted by KIDS)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,119,0)="   LRGP             6947313        5798854        **153,269**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,120,0)="   LRGP1            8924262        3988622        **112,269**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,121,0)="   LRGV             13358239       7051872        **269**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,122,0)="   LRGV1            5973234        3094124        **112,153,269**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,123,0)="   LRGV2            11151687       3432003        **121,153,269**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,125,0)="List of preceding patches: 153"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,126,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,127,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,128,0)="************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,129,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,130,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,131,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,132,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,133,0)="  The install time for this patch is less than 5 minutes. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,134,0)="  can be installed when Laboratory users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,135,0)="  Suggested time to install: non-peak requirement hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,136,0)="  The install will disable several Lab options as specified in #7 below."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,138,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,139,0)="NOTE: Kernel patches must be current on the target system"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,140,0)="      to avoid problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,141,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,142,0)="      Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,143,0)="      Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,145,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,146,0)="  1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,147,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,148,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,149,0)="      option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,150,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,151,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,152,0)="      system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,154,0)="  4.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,155,0)="      select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,156,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,157,0)="  5.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,158,0)="      all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,159,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,160,0)="  6.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,161,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,162,0)="        Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,163,0)="        Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,164,0)="        Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,165,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,166,0)="      If you wish to preserve a copy of the routines exported in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,167,0)="      prior to installation, you should use the 'Backup a Transport Global'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,168,0)="      option at this time.  You may also compare the routines in your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,169,0)="      production account to the routines in the patch by using the 'Compare"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,170,0)="      a Transport Global to Current System' option."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,172,0)="  7.  The install will disable the following Lab options during patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,173,0)="      installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,174,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,175,0)="         Group verify (EA, EL, EW) [LRGV]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,176,0)="         Group unverified review (EA, EL, EW) [LRGP]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,177,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,178,0)="  8.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,179,0)="      and select the package 'LR*5.2*269'.  When prompted 'Want to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,180,0)="      DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES//',"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,181,0)="      choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,182,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,183,0)="  9. On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,184,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,185,0)=" 10. Routine LR269 will be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,187,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,188,0)="POST-INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,189,0)="==============================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,190,0)="None"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,191,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,192,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,193,0)="************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,194,0)="Installation example:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,195,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,196,0)="Select Installation Option: 6  Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,197,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,198,0)="Select INSTALL NAME: LR*5.2*269  Loaded from Distribution  10/31/01@14:08:53"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,199,0)="     => LR*5.2*269 TEST v6"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",113,1,200,0)=" "
