^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,1,0)="This patch to the Laboratory package does not contain any changes to the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,2,0)="VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled VISTA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,3,0)="BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,5,0)="Copyright 1995, 1996, 1997, Regenstrief Institute and the Logical "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,6,0)="Observation Identifier Names and Codes (LOINC) Committee. All rights "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,7,0)="reserved. LOINC is a trademark of the Regenstrief Institute."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,9,0)="This patch contains enhancements that improve several reports"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,10,0)="associated with LOINC mapping. In addition there is new functionality"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,11,0)="provided for re-transmitting PCE CPT workload."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,13,0)="Obsolete Options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,14,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,15,0)="The Print Default LOINC/LOINC Code by Lab Tests [LR LOINC PRINT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,16,0)="DEFAULT/LOINC] option is obsolete and will be placed out of order."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,18,0)="New Options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,19,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,20,0)="1. The PCE Retransmit [LRCAPCEX] option is new with this patch. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,21,0)="This option will reset entries in the LAB ORDER ENTRY (#69) file to allow"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,22,0)="resending of PCE workload for a given date range. This option is useful if"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,23,0)="WKLD CODE did not have CPT code assigned when PCE workload reporting"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,24,0)="software initially ran.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,25,0)="***CAUTION***  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,26,0)="This option will only attempt to resend PCE workload if NO PCE workload"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,27,0)="was reported FOR THE ENTIRE SPECIMEN ORDER NUMBER during the initial scan"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,28,0)="of collected orders. All original requirements for PCE workload reporting"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,29,0)="are enforced.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,30,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,31,0)="This option maybe useful if linked CPT codes were inactivated during the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,32,0)="yearly upgrade of the CPT (#81) file. The LIM can edit the WKLD CODE (#64)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,33,0)="file with current valid CPT codes and run this option.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,34,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,35,0)="This option cannot be run while the normal PCE workload reporting"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,36,0)="background software is running.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,37,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,38,0)="The option will scan the date range entered, printing a dot (""."") for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,39,0)="every 20th. order processed. Then the option will determine if the order"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,40,0)="should be reported to PCE. As the data is processed, every 20th. order"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,41,0)="number is printed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,42,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,43,0)="This option cannot be queued. Option invokes the routine LRCAPPHX"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,45,0)="Modified Options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,46,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,47,0)="1. Map/Unmap Antimicrobial Default LOINC Code [LR LOINC MAP ANTIMICROBIAL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,48,0)="] option was modified to correct problems with unmapping a LOINC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,49,0)="code from several different WKLD CODEs."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,51,0)="2. Print Lab Tests Mapped/Not Mapped to LOINC Codes [LR LOINC PRINT 60/LO"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,52,0)="INC MAP] option has been enhanced to provide the following three methods"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,53,0)="to print LOINC mapped data:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,54,0)="   1) Print all unmapped tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,55,0)="   2) Print all mapped tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,56,0)="   3) Print individual tests."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,58,0)="The option functionality was improved by the creation of an additional"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,59,0)="cross-reference ^LAM(""AL""."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,61,0)="3. Link Result NLT Manual [LR7O MAN RESULT NLT] option was generating an"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,62,0)="undefined error if the default WKLD CODE was accepted. This problem has"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,63,0)="been corrected. The option now properly honors '^' when entered. The "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,64,0)="option will allow any WKLD CODE to be selected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,66,0)="4. Map/Unmap Antimicrobial Default LOINC Code [LR LOINC MAP ANTIMICROBIAL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,67,0)="] option has been modified to have the look and feel of other LOINC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,68,0)="mapping  options. Note this option only sets the DEFAULT LOINC CODE (#25)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,69,0)="of the WKLD CODE (#64) file."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,70,0)="[It is highly recommended that a different suffixed WKLD CODE be created"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,71,0)="to be used for antimicrobial drug mapping. The WKLD CODE selected must be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,72,0)="different than the WKLD CODE used for blood analysis.]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,74,0)="5. Extract VistA Lab Test Names [LR LOINC EXTRACT LAB NAMES] options has"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,75,0)="been modified to replace '*' or '?' with spaces that occur in test names."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,76,0)="This is to prevent RELMA mapping program errors. The extraction logic has"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,77,0)="been enhanced to find duplicate laboratory test and synonym names."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,79,0)="6. National Laboratory File [LR7O 60-64] menu was exported with an"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,80,0)="erroneous routine attached. The entire menu option is deleted and rebuilt"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,81,0)="with this install. The menu contains the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,82,0)="1) Semi-automatic Linking of file 60 to 64 [LR7O 60-64 AUTO]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,83,0)="2) Manual Linking of file 60 to 64 [LR7O 60-64 MANUAL]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,84,0)="3) Result NLT Auto Linker [LR7O AUTO RESULT NLT]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,85,0)="4) Link Result NLT Manual [LR7O MAN RESULT NLT]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,86,0)="The routine PSDNDES has been removed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,88,0)="7. Map Lab Tests to LOINC Codes [LR LOINC MAP] option has been enhanced to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,89,0)="allow mapping of all laboratory test. In the initial release, only 'CH'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,90,0)="subscripted tests were selectable. This restriction has been removed. Only"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,91,0)="'CH' subscripted tests are mapped to TIME ASPECT LOINC codes. Other type"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,92,0)="tests (i.e. Microbiology, Anatomic Pathology) are only mapped to DEFAULT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,93,0)="LOINC CODE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,95,0)="8. Print a Single LOINC CODE [LR LOINC PRINT LOINC CODE] option has been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,96,0)="modified to display the LOINC CODE check digit beside the LOINC CODE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,98,0)="9. The following options will now allow selection of any subscript."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,99,0)="1)      Find LOINC for Vista Lab Test [LR LOINC LOOKUP]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,100,0)="2)      Unmap/Delete Lab Tests to Default LOINC Code"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,101,0)="        [LR LOINC UNMAP/DELETE DEFAULT]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,102,0)="3)      Validate LOINC Mapping [LR LOINC VALIDATE]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,104,0)="10. Where appropriate, FileMan lookup and options will now display the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,105,0)="LOINC code plus the check digit. In the past only the LOINC code was "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,106,0)="shown (i.e. 1-8). This will provide required data for entry into RELMA "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,107,0)="LOINC lookup window."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,108,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,109,0)="11. The National Laboratory File [LR7O 60-64] option will be added to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,110,0)="LOINC Main Menu [LRLOINC] option."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,113,0)="Data Dictionary Changes:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,114,0)="================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,115,0)="62.06       ANTIMICROBIAL SUSCEPTIBILITY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,116,0)="    Screen removed from NATIONAL VA LAB CODE #64"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,118,0)="64          WKLD CODE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,119,0)="Partial DD: DEFAULT LOINC CODE #25"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,120,0)="   Trigger to remove data from field when DEFAULT LOINC CODE is deleted."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,121,0)="Partial DD: subDD: SPECIMEN #64.01"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,122,0)="            subDD: TIME ASPECT #64.02      fld: TEST #3"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,123,0)="  Creates and populates the ^LAM(""AL"") cross reference"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,125,0)="68.2        LOAD/WORK LIST                                 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,126,0)="Partial DD:       fld: WKLK METHOD #.14"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,127,0)="  Modifies the triggers use to populate fields:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,128,0)="      WKLD CODE METHOD NAME #.15"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,129,0)="      WKLD CODE SUFFIX #.16"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,130,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,131,0)="95.3       LAB LOINC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,132,0)="  CHECK DIGIT (#15) has been made an identifier to improve display and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,133,0)="lookup."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,134,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,135,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,136,0)="Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,137,0)="================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,138,0)="    Long Beach, CA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,139,0)="    Muskogee, OK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,140,0)="    Durham, NC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,141,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,142,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,143,0)="Routines Summary:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,144,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,145,0)="The second line of the routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,146,0)="<tab>  ;;5.2; LAB SERVICE;**[patch list]**; Sep 27,1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,147,0)="            Checksum values"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,149,0)="Routine       Before Patch       After Patch       Patch list."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,150,0)="LR278             NA             5505096           278 (deleted by KIDS)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,151,0)="LR7OU641     12240284            12410597          153,201,278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,152,0)="LRCAPD       9261934             9516457           105,163,153,278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,153,0)="LRCAPPHX          NA             5799903           278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,154,0)="LRLNC0       11822735            14797379          215,232,278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,155,0)="LRLNC1       3760103             2227160           215,278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,156,0)="LRLNC1A           NA             750293            278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,157,0)="LRLNCDEL     5416724             6004798           232,278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,158,0)="LRLNCLK      2054143             2106203           232,278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,159,0)="LRLNCMD      8362694             6826367           232,278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,160,0)="LRLNCNLT     6478052             6013193           215,278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,161,0)="LRLNCPMP     4831240             7461913           215,232,278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,162,0)="LRLNCPRT     4848636             4889813           215,278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,163,0)="LRLNCV       4009739             3900781           232,278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,164,0)="LRLNCX       6971341             7117683           232,278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,165,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,166,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,167,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,168,0)="Installation should be done during off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,169,0)="Laboratory personnel may be on the system during install but should"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,170,0)="not be active."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,172,0)="Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak hours "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,173,0)="and less than 5 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,174,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,175,0)="Installation of this patch requires no additional memory space."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,177,0)="This patch is released as a KERNEL Installation and Distribution Systems"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,178,0)="(KIDS) MailMan message."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,179,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,180,0)="  1.  START FROM KERNEL "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,181,0)="      From the KERNEL Installation and Distribution Systems (KIDS)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,182,0)="      Menu, select the Installation menu [XPD INSTALLATION MENU]:  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,183,0)="           Edits and Distribution ...  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,184,0)="           Utilities ...  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,185,0)="           Installation ...  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,186,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,187,0)="  2.  SELECT INSTALLATION OPTION "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,188,0)="      NOTE:  The following are OPTIONAL:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,189,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,190,0)="     a.  Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,191,0)="          message of any routines exported with this patch. It will not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,192,0)="          backup any other changes, such as DDs or templates.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,193,0)="     b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System.  NOTE:  This option "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,194,0)="          will produce a long report due to new files and is not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,195,0)="          recommended."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,196,0)="     c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will allow "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,197,0)="          you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,198,0)="          transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,199,0)="  3. SELECT INSTALLATION OPTION: Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,200,0)="     Select INSTALL NAME: LR*5.2*278"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,201,0)="  4. When prompted ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,202,0)="     install? Yes//"" respond ""NO""."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,203,0)="  5. When asked ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install? YES//"","
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,204,0)="     respond ""NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,205,0)="  6. When prompted ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,206,0)="     Protocols? YES//, respond ""NO""."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,207,0)="  7. Lab users may resume their normal activities."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",114,1,208,0)="  8. Routine LR278 will be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",115,0)="275 SEQ #213^3011231^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",115,1,0)="^^6^6^3011231"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",115,1,1,0)="This patch was developed to fix defects in the VistA Blood Bank Software v"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",115,1,2,0)="5.2 that have been discovered to cause chronic user and database integrity"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",115,1,3,0)="problems."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",115,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",115,1,5,0)="A full description of this patch can be found in the Forum Patch Module"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",115,1,6,0)="listing for patch LR*5.2*275."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,0)="280 SEQ #214^3020108^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,0)="^^263^263^3020108"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,2,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LR*5.2*280 contains no changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,3,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,6,0)="This patch will address fixes to defects reported in NOIS DAY-1101-42242"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,7,0)="and HWH-1101-42338 when using the option Link Result NLT Manual [LR7O MAN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,8,0)="RESULT NLT] to map result NLT codes to a site's LABORATORY TEST file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,9,0)="(#60)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,11,0)="1. When using the option Link Result NLT Manual [LR7O MAN RESULT NLT] the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,12,0)="option was exiting the user to the Kernel menu system after mapping a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,13,0)="single test.  This resulted in a user answering the option prompts for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,14,0)="each test to be mapped.  This patch will change the option dialog to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,15,0)="allow the user to select and map multiple tests after answering the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,16,0)="option prompts.  To exit or abort from the option the user should enter"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,17,0)="a ""^"" which will return the user to the Kernel menu system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,18,0)="NOIS DAY-1101-42242 and HWH-1101-42338"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,20,0)="2. FileMan inquires in to files LABORATORY TEST (#60) and WKLD CODE (#64)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,21,0)="was not displaying the check sum digit for all LOINC codes. An output"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,22,0)="transform has been added to include the check digit with the LOINC code."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,24,0)="3. In the LABORATORY TEST (#60) file, subfile SITE/SPECIMEN (#100), LOINC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,25,0)="CODE (#95.3) field was not being updated for atomic 'CH' subscript tests."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,26,0)="This has been corrected. It has been reported that the zero node of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,27,0)="SITE/SPECIMEN field do not exist. This patch will create the zero node if"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,28,0)="required during mapping."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,29,0)="   SPO-120-50468 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,31,0)="4. During patch development/software review the following defects were"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,32,0)="   identified and corrected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,34,0)="   A. In the option Result NLT Auto Linker [LR7O AUTO RESULT NLT] if"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,35,0)="   a user requested printing of a List of Result NLT Linked Codes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,36,0)="   and device selection was unsuccessful or aborted then the Kernel IO*"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,37,0)="   variables were not being restored to the user's home device. This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,38,0)="   patch will now call HOME^%ZIS when device selection is unsuccessful"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,39,0)="   or aborted by the user to restore the user's home device settings."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,41,0)="   B. If a user selects the semi-auto method of linking, the option was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,42,0)="   exiting the user from the option when a Result NLT was not selected"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,43,0)="   and mapped to an entry in the LABORATORY TEST file (#60). This patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,44,0)="   will allow the user to continue mapping tests. To exit or abort from"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,45,0)="   the option the user should enter a ""^"" which will return the user to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,46,0)="   the Kernel menu system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,48,0)="   C. The entry in LABORATORY TEST file (#60) was only being locked "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,49,0)="   when using the manual method of linking. The Semi-auto method was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,50,0)="   not locking the file.  This patch will lock the entry being edited"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,51,0)="   in LABORATORY TEST file (#60) when either method is selected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,53,0)="5. When mapping certain LOINC codes a FileMan error of 'undefined "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,54,0)="   variable ^(4) is' generated because of the lookup screen. This error"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,55,0)="   has been corrected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,56,0)="   SHR-1201-70505"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,59,0)="ASSOCIATED NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,60,0)="---------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,61,0)=" DAY-1101-42242"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",116,1,62,0)=" HWH-1101-42338"
