^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,6,0)="Patch LR*5.2*222 will be distributed and installed with patch LA*5.2*46"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,7,0)="LEDI INTERFACE TO NON-VA SYSTEM (LEDI II)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,9,0)="This patch adds additional support when using the option Referral Patient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,10,0)="Multi-purpose Accession [LRLEDI] to accession specimens thru the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,11,0)="Electronic Data Interface (LEDI). The changes contained in this patch are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,12,0)="implemented in conjunction with patch LA*5.2*46. Patch LA*5.2*46 now builds"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,13,0)="the file LAB PENDING ORDERS ENTRY (#69.6) with additional information"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,14,0)="concerning mapping to local test urgency. This patch introduces changes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,15,0)="that utilize the local urgency information stored in file #69.6 when"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,16,0)="accessioning LEDI specimens at the host laboratory."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,18,0)="As of the release date of this software, there is no national solution to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,19,0)="implement a laboratory electronic HL7 standard interface to a facility or"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,20,0)="other entity outside the VA wide area network.  National communication"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,21,0)="security concerns are still being debated by the Department of Veterans"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,22,0)="Affairs (VA) and are awaiting resolution.  At present, a VA medical center,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,23,0)="which intends to utilize this software in conjunction with an interface to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,24,0)="a commercial reference laboratory or other non-VA information system entity,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,25,0)="will need to coordinate with the vendor an acceptable communication method."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,26,0)="Any implementation will need to be approved by the facility and VISN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,27,0)="Information Security Officer (ISO) and meet current VA security requirements"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,28,0)="for external electronic connections. See VHA Directive 6212, Security of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,29,0)="External Electronic Connections and VHA Directive 6210, Automated Information"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,30,0)="Systems (AIS) Security for additional information and guidance. Additional"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,31,0)="security information may be obtained from the Health Information Security"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,32,0)="Service (HISS) web page at http://vaww.domain.ext/miss."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,33,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,34,0)="Implementation of a HL7 messaging interface between the VA VistA Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,35,0)="package and a non-VA information system consists basically of three parts:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,36,0)=" - VistA Laboratory LEDI II software."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,37,0)=" - certified communication software and hardware"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,38,0)=" - non-VA information system capable of sending and receiving laboratory HL7"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,39,0)="   order and result messages."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,40,0)="All three must be functional to utilize the capabilities of this LEDI II"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,41,0)="software patch. The implementation,setup, and configuration of vendor provided"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,42,0)="hardware and software is NOT addressed by this documentation.  Consult the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,43,0)="vendor provided documentation and instructions to interface to the VistA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,44,0)="Laboratory package."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,47,0)="NOIS HUN-1100-21862 reported discrepancies in patient names due to Network"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,48,0)="Health Exchange not maintaining name changes. This patch removes the use"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,49,0)="of the Network Health Exchange package to lookup patient information"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,50,0)="(patient name, patient identifier and date of birth). The link in file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,51,0)="REFERRAL PATIENT (#67), field Patient Name (#3) to file VAMC NETWORK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,52,0)="PATIENT (#537010) is removed as a variable pointer."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,53,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,54,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,55,0)="NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,56,0)="===="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,57,0)="HUN-1100-21862"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,58,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,59,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,60,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,61,0)="  The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,62,0)="  of each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,63,0)="  <tab> ;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;<patchlist>;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,65,0)="                    Checksum       Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,66,0)="   Routine Name     Before Patch   After Patch    Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,67,0)="   ------------     ------------   -----------    ------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,68,0)="   LR222            N/A            6987123        **222** (Deleted by KIDS)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,69,0)="   LRDPAREF         6854898        5111405        **153,222**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,70,0)="   LRORDB           3786248        3782224        **153,222**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,72,0)=" List of preceding patches: 153"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,73,0)=" Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",117,1,75,0)="  "
