^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,0)="271 SEQ #217^3020423^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,0)="^^129^129^3020423"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,1,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LR*5.2*271 contains no changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,2,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,4,0)="This patch addresses a fix to defects reported in NOIS BAF-0101-N2560"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,5,0)="and BED-0201-12399. Additional problems (item 2) were identified during"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,6,0)="software review for patch development. Listed below are the problems and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,7,0)="the corrective actions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,8,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,9,0)="1. NOIS'es BAF-0101-N2560 and BED-0201-12399 reported when looking up"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,10,0)="monthly accessions that the software was defaulting to the wrong year."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,11,0)="Routine LRWU4 has been corrected to default to the current year when a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,12,0)="user enters the accession date in the format MM00."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,14,0)="2. The following defects were identified during the software review as"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,15,0)="part of patch development."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,17,0)="  a. When a user enters a partial accession and is prompted for an"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,18,0)="accession date the software was not defaulting to past dates. Defect"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,19,0)="corrected by including ""P"" in the variable %DT when calling FileMan's"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,20,0)="%DT date processing routine."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,22,0)="  b. Routine LRFASTS called by option Fast Bypass Data Entry/Verify"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,23,0)="[LRFASTS] does not handle non-daily accession areas correctly. The routine"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,24,0)="was using the order date as the accession date which is only correct when"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,25,0)="the accession area associated with a test is daily. LRFASTS has been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,26,0)="corrected to retrieve the accession area, date and number for a test from"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,27,0)="LAB ORDER ENTRY file (#69). It will now function correctly when processing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,28,0)="acccessions from non-daily acession areas, i.e. monthly, quarterly and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,29,0)="yearly."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,31,0)="  c. Routine LRVERA was handling accession selection similiar to LRWU4."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,32,0)="This routine has been changed to call LRWU4."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,34,0)="  d. The entry for Quarterly accession transform in the EXECUTE CODE file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,35,0)="(#62.07) contains code that creates an invalid FileMan date for the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,36,0)="accession date. The post install for this patch will check the EXECUTE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,37,0)="CODE file (#62.07) and ACCESSION file (#68) for entries using the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,38,0)="Quarterly accession transform and correct the code."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,40,0)=" "
