^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,79,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,80,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,82,0)="  The install time for this patch is less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,83,0)="  Suggested time to install: non-peak requirement hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,86,0)="NOTE: Kernel patches must be current on the target system"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,87,0)="      to avoid problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,89,0)="      Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,90,0)="      Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,92,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,93,0)="  1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,95,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,96,0)="      option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,98,0)="  3.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,99,0)="      select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,101,0)="  4.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,102,0)="      all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,104,0)="  5.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,105,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,106,0)="        Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,107,0)="        Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,108,0)="        Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,110,0)="  6.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,111,0)="      and select the package 'LR*5.2*271'. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,112,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,113,0)="        When prompted ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,114,0)="        of Install? //YES"", respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,115,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,116,0)="        When prompted ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,117,0)="        YES//"", respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,119,0)="        When prompted ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options and Menu Options?"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,120,0)="        YES//"", respond YES.  When prompted ""Enter options you wish to mark"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,121,0)="        as 'Out of Order':"", enter the following to disable all Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,122,0)="        options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,123,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,124,0)="           LR*"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,125,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,127,0)="  7. On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",119,1,129,0)="  NOTE: Routine LR271 will be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,0)="282 SEQ #218^3020516^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,0)="^^86^86^3020516"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,1,0)=" This patch resolves the following problem:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,3,0)=" CPRS calls a Lab API [INTERIM^LR7OGM] that extracts and formats"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,4,0)=" lab data for reports on the LAB tab.  For results longer than"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,5,0)=" 7 characters, the data is being truncated and formatted incorrectly."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,6,0)=" This patch will correct the formatting of long results, by not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,7,0)=" truncating the results and breaking the line so that units and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,8,0)=" reference ranges continue on the next line."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,10,0)=" This patch to the Laboratory package does not contain any changes to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,11,0)=" VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA DIRECTIVE 97-033 titled VISTA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,12,0)=" BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,14,0)=" PROBLEM: CPRS calls a Lab API [INTERIM^LR7OGM] that extracts and formats"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,15,0)=" lab data for reports on the LAB tab.  For results longer than"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,16,0)=" 7 characters, the data is being truncated and formatted incorrectly."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,18,0)=" RISK ANALYSIS:   Changes made by patch LR*5.2*282 have no effect on Blood"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,19,0)=" Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,21,0)=" EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS:  Patch LR*5.2*282 does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,22,0)=" alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical elements"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,23,0)=" functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,25,0)=" POTENTIAL IMPACT ON SITES:  Patch LR*5.2*282 contains no changes to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,26,0)=" routines identified in Veterans Health Administration (VHA) Directive"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,27,0)=" 97-033. There is no adverse potential to sites."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,29,0)=" VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION:  There are no required validation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,30,0)=" scenarios to be completed by sites after installing LR*5.2*282."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,32,0)=" TEST SITES FOR THIS PATCH:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,33,0)=" =========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,34,0)=" North Texas HCS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,35,0)=" Denver"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,36,0)=" Tennessee Valley HCS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,37,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,38,0)=" RELATED NOIS:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,39,0)=" ============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,40,0)=" TNV-0801-30277"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,41,0)=" NTH-0202-72720"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,42,0)=" DEN-1298-51612"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,43,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,44,0)=" ROUTINE SUMMARY:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,45,0)=" ================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,46,0)=" The following is a list of the routine(s) included in this patch.  The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,47,0)=" second line of each of these routine(s) will look like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,49,0)="     <tab>;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;**[patch list]**;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,51,0)="                            CHECK^XTSUMBLD results"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,52,0)=" Routine name         Before Patch          After Patch         Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,53,0)=" ============         ============          ===========         =========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,54,0)=" LR7OGMP                   5364802              5548341        187,246,282"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,56,0)=" INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,57,0)=" =========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,58,0)=" This patch should be loaded during non-peak hours to minimize disruption"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,59,0)=" to users.  Installation will take less than 1 minute.  Users may remain"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,60,0)=" on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,61,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,62,0)=" 1.  Use the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,63,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,64,0)=" 2.  Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,65,0)="     ROUTINE SUMMARY section are mapped, they should be removed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,66,0)="     from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,67,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,68,0)=" 3.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,69,0)="     the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,70,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,71,0)=" 4.  From this menu, you may elect to use the following options"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,72,0)="     (when prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter LR*5.2*282):"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,73,0)="         a.  Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,74,0)="         b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,75,0)="         c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,76,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,77,0)=" 5.  Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package LR*5.2*282."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,78,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,79,0)=" 6.  When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES//'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,80,0)="     respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,81,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,82,0)=" 7.  When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,83,0)="     Protocols? YES//', respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,84,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,85,0)=" 8.  If routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should be returned"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",120,1,86,0)="     to the mapped set once the installation has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,0)="272 SEQ #219^3020906^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,0)="^9.49011^254^254^3131115^^"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,1,0)=" EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*272 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,2,0)="contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,3,0)="DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,4,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,5,0)=" EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*272 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,6,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,7,0)="elements functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,8,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,9,0)=" RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*272 have no effect on Blood "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,10,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,11,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,12,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,13,0)=" Nineteen NOIS calls are addressed in this patch.  These are:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,15,0)="  LAH-0301-61651 - LAB RESULTS FOR URINE NOT TRIGGERING ALERT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,16,0)="   Providers who had notification for lab results enabled were not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,17,0)="   receiving alerts for urinalysis. A line of code has been added at"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,18,0)="   label SNEAK+39 in routine LR7OB3 to correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,20,0)="  HIN-0301-40344 - SPELLING NOTED"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,21,0)="   The word ""Finished"" was misspelled in routine LRDRAW. The word"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,22,0)="   ""Report Completed"" has replaced ""Finished"". A report"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,23,0)="   header has been expanded to include the date and time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,25,0)="  ISF-0899-61570 - LAB FILES ALLOWING LAYGO TO FILE 200"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,26,0)="   The following fields were modified to not allow LAYGO in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,27,0)="   NEW PERSON file (#200)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,28,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,29,0)="   LAB DATA (file #63)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,30,0)="     CHEM,HEM,TOX,RIA,SER,etc.(mult) (field #4)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,31,0)="       VERIFY PERSON  (field #.04)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,32,0)="                               "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,33,0)="   LAB ORDER ENTRY (file #69)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,34,0)="     SPECIMEN (mult) (field #1)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,35,0)="       ENTERING PERSON (field #1)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,36,0)="       COLLECTOR (field #12)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,38,0)="  PHO-0699-61637 - QMONTH GIVING ORDER FOR EVERY DAY, NOT EVERY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,39,0)="                   MONTH"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,40,0)="   NTH-0399-71865 - QMONTHLY DOESN'T WORK WHEN ORDERING LABS IN CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,41,0)="   The 30 day limit imposed by the MAX DAYS FOR CONTINUOUS ORDERS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,42,0)="   sub-field (#6) in the HOSPITAL SITE FIELD (#9) of the LABORATORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,43,0)="   SITE file (#69.9) has been changed to allow up to 370 days."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,45,0)="  FRE-0599-60964 - IMMEDIATE COLLECT ALWAYS ON"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,46,0)="   The IMMED COLLECT ON sub field (#8) of the IMMED LAB COLLECT DIV."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,47,0)="   multiple (#5.1) in the LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9) was not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,48,0)="   properly checked. The logic in the $$ON^LR7OV4 API has been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,49,0)="   changed to properly determine the status of this field."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,51,0)="  CHY-0798-52175 - GRAPH RESULTS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,52,0)="  MOU-0498-32262 - PROBLEM WITH 0.0 VALUES ON QC DISPLAY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,53,0)="   Values such as 0.0 are not displaying using the Quality control"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,54,0)="   display (Levey-Jennings) option.  If the techs manually edit"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,55,0)="   these values to 0, they will display on the graph.  Changes have"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,56,0)="   been made to allow 0.0 and 0 to display correctly."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,58,0)="  PUG-1297-50924 - OPTION REQUIRES LOWER CASE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,59,0)="   The Fast Lab Test Order (Routine) [LROW ROUTINE] will not accept"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,60,0)="   lowercase answers.  Changes have been made to line label % in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,61,0)="   routine LRORD1 to remove case sensitivity from this option."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,63,0)="  MUS-0996-71712 - NAT'L LAB TEST FILE LINKING SUBSCRIPT ERROR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,64,0)="   A Logic flaw in the lab code caused a National Lab Test file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,65,0)="   linking subscript error.  All instances of the flawed code have"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,66,0)="   been corrected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,68,0)="  ALN-0496-10819 - SERUM ANTIBIOTIC LEVELS LESS THAN 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,69,0)="   Sites were having problems putting in antibiotic levels in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,70,0)="   micro package that were less than 1.0.  Results of .75 etc would"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,71,0)="   echo question marks back to the user.  Input transform located"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,72,0)="   in the ANTIBIOTIC LEVEL field (#2)of sub-field of file (#63.42)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,73,0)="   located in the LAB DATA file (#63) has been corrected to allow"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,74,0)="   results with 2 decimal places to be entered."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,76,0)="  TEM-0895-72227 - SEPARATE REPORT LOCATIONS NOT WORKING"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,77,0)="   The site was instructed to put a prefix on their HOSPITAL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,78,0)="   LOCATION file (#44), so that they could differentiate after"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,79,0)="   the integration. A problem arose when the cumulative used the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,80,0)="   abbreviation that was active at the time of the order.  After"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,81,0)="   integration the location names and abbreviations contained"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,82,0)="   the prefix, which caused the names in the Lab globals to no"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,83,0)="   longer match file (#44).  This patch enables the printing of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,84,0)="   cumulative reports when multiple same name abbreviations have"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,85,0)="   been detected in the LAB REPORTS file (#64.5)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,87,0)="  BUF-0895-11662 - USERS CHOOSE DEAD PROVIDER"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,88,0)="  ALB-1099-52504 - LAB PACKAGE ALLOWS SELECTION OF TERMINATED USERS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,89,0)="   Users are able to choose a provider that recently died as the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,90,0)="   person ordering the lab tests.  Label P in routine LRWU1 has "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,91,0)="   been modified to use the DISUSER flag to check for terminated"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,92,0)="   users."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,93,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,94,0)="  SAM-0895-20499 - CHECK FILES FOR INCONSISTENCIES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,95,0)="   Warnings were printed even though the ""DO YOU WANT WARNINGS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,96,0)="   REPORTED? No//"" prompt was answered with NO.  Extensive"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,97,0)="   modifications have been made to the routines called by the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,98,0)="   Check files for inconsistencies [LRCHKFILES] option to correct"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,99,0)="   this problem."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,101,0)="  AMA-0695-70804 - E VARIABLE FOR %DT NOT WORKING"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,102,0)="   The date/time stamp printed to screen, but not to a printer."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,103,0)="   The reports were using the string 'S X=""N"",%DT=""ET"" D ^%DT"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,104,0)="   to print date/time.  The call has been updated to use"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,105,0)="   '$$FMTE^XLFDT($$NOW^XLFDT,"""").'  The call to STAMP^LRX is no"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,106,0)="   longer used."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,108,0)="  HUN-0501-21203 - INCORRECT SPELLING IN LOADLIST."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,109,0)="   An incorrect spelling in the EXPAND PANELS ON PRINT field "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,110,0)="   (#.06) Of the LOAD/WORK LIST file (#68.2) has been corrected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,112,0)="  LEX-0201-41741 - IMMEDIATE COLLECT SETTINGS BEING OVERRIDDEN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,113,0)="   Immediate collect times are being rejected if seconds are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,114,0)="   entered.  Label VALID+10 in routine LR7OV4 has been modified"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,115,0)="   to allow the entry"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,116,0)="   of seconds in the collect time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,118,0)="  HIN-0701-42680 - QUESTION RE: Y2K DATE FORMAT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,119,0)="   The Y2K conversions changed the format of the date generated"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,120,0)="   by PRTEST+5^LRSORA2 from MMM DD 'YY to MMM DD 'YYYY.  The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,121,0)="   apostrophe in the new format is not necessary.  The routine"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,122,0)="   has been modified to eliminate the extraneous data."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,123,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,125,0)=" Reference NOIS:   LAH-0301-61651"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,126,0)="                   HIN-0301-40344"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,127,0)="                   ALB-1099-52504"
