^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,204,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,205,0)="List of preceding patches: 45, 126, 153, 163, 187, 190, 201, 256"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,206,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,207,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,208,0)="   NOTE: The ""before"" checksums may not match for the LRAC14,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,209,0)="         LRACKL, and LARACKL1 routines if your site was a test"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,210,0)="         site for the unreleased patch LR*5.2*170."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,211,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,212,0)="  Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,213,0)="  =========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,214,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,215,0)="  NOTE: This KIDS install does not place any options out of service"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,216,0)="        during the install and no user options are affected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,217,0)="        If KIDS prompts:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,218,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,219,0)="        ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,220,0)="         Install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,221,0)="        ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,222,0)="        ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,223,0)="        Protocols? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,224,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,225,0)="        The site should answer ""NO"" to all three questions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,226,0)="            Note: You may not receive all three prompts at your site.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,227,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,228,0)="        1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,229,0)="           This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,230,0)="           your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,231,0)="        2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,232,0)="           should be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,233,0)="        3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,234,0)="           your system. You now need to use KIDS to install the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,235,0)="           Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,236,0)="           On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,237,0)="           following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,238,0)="               Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,239,0)="               Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,240,0)="               Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,241,0)="               Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,242,0)="        4. Users may remain on the system, but installation should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,243,0)="           done at off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,244,0)="        5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,245,0)="        6. Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,246,0)="           hours and less the 5 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,247,0)="        7. Installation of this patch requires no additional memory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,248,0)="           space."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,249,0)="        8. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,250,0)="           option 'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*272'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,251,0)="           and proceed with the install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,252,0)="        9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,253,0)="           be returned to the mapped set once the installation has run"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",121,1,254,0)="           to completion."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",122,0)="285 SEQ #220^3021025^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",122,1,0)="^^1^1^3021025"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",122,1,1,0)="See patch description for details."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,0)="288 SEQ #221^3021209^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,0)="^^114^114^3021209"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,1,0)="This patch is being released in support of the VBECS (Vista Blood "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,2,0)="Establishment Computer Software) Blood Bank Modernization Project.  In "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,3,0)="the future, data will be transitioned from the existing M database to a "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,4,0)="Microsoft SQL database.  The API's release in this patch will allow the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,5,0)="Health Summary and Surgery packages to transition to the new database "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,6,0)="when it is released."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,8,0)=" Get Transfusion Data"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,9,0)="      TRAN^VBECA4     This API will be a shell to an API that already"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,10,0)="                      exists (XTRCT^GMTSLRTE).  The new API will pass"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,11,0)="                      the DFN, the TMP subscript location, the inverse"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,12,0)="                      end and inverse beginning date of search in a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,13,0)="                      call to the existing routine."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,15,0)=" Get All Available Units"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,16,0)="      AVUNIT^VBECA4   This API will be a shell to an API that already"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,17,0)="                      exists (XTRCT^GMTSLRBE).  The new API will pass"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,18,0)="                      the DFN, the TMP subscript location, the inverse"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,19,0)="                      end and beginning date, and the max number of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,20,0)="                      records in a call to the existing routine."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,22,0)=" Blood Product Lookup for Surgery"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,23,0)="      ^VBECA5A        The VBECA5A API has been created to allow the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,24,0)="                      Surgery package to convert the existing pointer"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,25,0)="                      fields  used to list available Blood Products"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,26,0)="                      contained in the Blood Product file (#66), with a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,27,0)="                      free text field.  The transition of the Blood"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,28,0)="                      Bank system from the existing M based system to a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,29,0)="                      .NET/SQL based system will eliminate the ability"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,30,0)="                      of the Surgery package to access the Blood Product"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,31,0)="                      data using the current method."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,33,0)=" EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*288 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,34,0)="contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,35,0)="DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,37,0)=" EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*288 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,38,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,39,0)="elements functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,41,0)=" RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*288 have no effect on Blood "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,42,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",123,1,43,0)=" "
