^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,88,0)="        3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,89,0)="           your system. You now need to use KIDS to install the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,90,0)="           Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,91,0)="           On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,92,0)="           following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,93,0)="               Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,94,0)="               Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,95,0)="               Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,96,0)="               Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,97,0)="        4. Users may remain on the system, but installation should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,98,0)="           done at off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,99,0)="        5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,100,0)="        6. Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,101,0)="           hours and less the 5 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,102,0)="        7. Installation of this patch requires no additional memory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,103,0)="           space."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,104,0)="        8. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,105,0)="           option 'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*292'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,106,0)="           and proceed with the install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,107,0)="        9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,108,0)="           be returned to the mapped set once the installation has run"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",124,1,109,0)="           to completion."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,0)="283 SEQ #223^3021220^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,0)="^^444^444^3021220"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,1,0)="LAB RESULTS REPORTING LR*5.2*283"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,3,0)="Associated patches: (v)LR*5.2*201  <<= must be installed BEFORE `LR*5.2*283'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,4,0)="                    (v)LR*5.2*279  <<= must be installed BEFORE `LR*5.2*283'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,5,0)="                    (v)XU*8*217    <<= must be installed BEFORE `LR*5.2*283'    "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,6,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,7,0)="Subject: LAB RESULTS REPORTING"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,9,0)="Category:  ROUTINE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,10,0)="           ENHANCEMENT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,11,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,12,0)="Description:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,13,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,14,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,15,0)=" *************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,16,0)="     KERNEL PATCH XU*8*217 MUST BE INSTALLED BEFORE LR*5.2*283"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,17,0)=" *************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,19,0)="This patch to the Laboratory package does not contain any changes to the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,20,0)="VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by the VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,21,0)="VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,23,0)="The purpose of the LAB RESULTS REPORTING patch, LR*5.2*283, is to enhance"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,24,0)="the VistA Laboratory software to print the name and address of the laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,25,0)="that performed a test procedure on patients' laboratory reports.  Currently"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,26,0)="the physical address of the laboratory where the test is performed is not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,27,0)="provided on laboratory reports, which is a Joint Commission on "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,28,0)="Accreditation of Healthcare Organizations (JCAHO) and College of American "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,29,0)="Pathologists (CAP) deficiency.  This patch will resolve any existing data"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,30,0)="quality issues concerning the lack of the performing laboratory name and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,31,0)="address on patient's reports therefore bringing VA laboratories"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,32,0)="into compliance with JCAHO and CAP standards."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,33,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,34,0)="All Cumulative and Interim Reports are modified to include the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,35,0)="performing lab site (PLS) name and address information in the body of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,36,0)="report.  The performing lab site for each test is noted by the internal"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,37,0)=" entry number of the performing lab site in the INSTITUTION file (#4)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,38,0)="All Cumulative Report options are modified to the interim report format and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,39,0)="will include the address page(s) which will be printed at the end of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,40,0)="report.  Site codes are available for chemistry tests only.  There will be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,41,0)="no site codes printed for microbiology or anatomic pathology tests at this"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,42,0)="time because they are unavailable."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,44,0)="********************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,45,0)="Below is an example of modified interim report format with the performing "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,46,0)="lab site names, addresses and site codes printed on a separate page:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,48,0)="Printed at:                                                                 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,49,0)="                                             page 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,50,0)="Dallas Medical Center (428)   123 Lancaster Dallas, TX 75050"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",125,1,51,0)=" "
