^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,377,0)="LIM:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,378,0)=" Review description for LR*5.2*274 use KIDS Utilities Build File Print "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,379,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,380,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,381,0)="  End of installation example. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,382,0)=" ==============================================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,383,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,384,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,385,0)="Post Install instruction:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,386,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,387,0)="The Laboratory Information Manager (LIM) should obtain from the Anatomic "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,388,0)="Pathology department, a list containing CPT codes for the procedures most "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,389,0)="frequently performed.  The entries on this list need to be ranked by "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,390,0)="frequency (i.e. most frequently used procedure is #1, next frequently "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,391,0)="used procedure is #2, etc.) This list will provide a template for the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,392,0)="display listing. Next, the LIM need to select a NLT code from the WKLD "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,393,0)="CODE (#64) file with the corresponding CPT code. Next, using the option "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,394,0)="Edit or Print WKLD CODES[LR WKLD CODE EDIT PRINT] option, edit the ES "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,395,0)="DISPLAY ORDER (#26) field by entering the sequence number from the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,396,0)="frequency list and edit the CODE (#18) field multiple with the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,397,0)="appropriate CPT Code(s). "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,398,0)="Editing of the WKLD CODE file can be done with the Edit or Print WKLD "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,399,0)="CODES [LR WKLD CODE EDIT PRINT] option."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,400,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,401,0)="================================================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,402,0)="User Information: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,403,0)="The user performing the CPT coding for tissue exam using the LAB CPT "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,404,0)="BILLING [LRCAPES] option can enter the ES DISPLAY ORDER number (the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,405,0)="sequence number from the frequency list) to select CPT codes. The user "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,406,0)="can enter double question marks '??' to see a list of CPT codes "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,407,0)="selectable by entering the ES DISPLAY ORDER numbers. If the appropriate "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,408,0)="code does not appear on the list, the user can enter the individual CPT "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,409,0)="code number(s) separated by commas."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,410,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,411,0)="The coding software ensures that all CPT codes selected are active. If "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,412,0)="the user does not have the PROVIDER security key, a valid active provider "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,413,0)="must be entered. The user reviews the accessioned test(s) and the CPT "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,414,0)="codes selected. The user is prompted to accept or reject the information."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,415,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,416,0)="After accepting the previous information the software will determine, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,417,0)="using the TYPE (#2) field of the HOSPITAL LOCATION (#44) file, if the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,418,0)="location entered is an outpatient location. Those locations with the type "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,419,0)="of clinic, module or other are considered to be out patient location. CPT "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,420,0)="coding is ONLY PASSED FOR OUT PATIENT LOCATION TYPES. If the specimen is "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,421,0)="assigned to a Patient as defined by an entry in the PATIENT (#2) file, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,422,0)="the specified CPT codes are passed immediately to the Laboratory/PCE API. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,423,0)="The date/time of the visit is set to specimen collection date/time. If "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,424,0)="the time is not specified, a default of 12:01 is used. The PCE API "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,425,0)="returns the visit number which is stored in the PCE ENC (#30) field of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,426,0)="the ACCESSION NUMBER (#1) sub-file of the DATE (#.01) sub-file of the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,427,0)="ACCESSION (#68) file."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,428,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,429,0)="The software will also store the WKLD CODES associated with the CPT codes "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,430,0)="selected. These WKLD CODE are added to the Laboratory LMIP workload for "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,431,0)="that accession. This is done regardless of the location type."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,432,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,433,0)="Example of File setup"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,434,0)="==============================================================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,435,0)=" The example does not represent true clinical situation, it is used only "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,436,0)="for demonstration purposes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",126,1,437,0)=" "
