^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,70,0)="List of preceding patches: 272"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,71,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,74,0)="  Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,75,0)="  =========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,77,0)="  NOTE: This KIDS install does not place any options out of service"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,78,0)="        during the install and no user options are affected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,79,0)="        If KIDS prompts:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,80,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,81,0)="        ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,82,0)="         Install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,83,0)="        ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,84,0)="        ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,85,0)="        Protocols? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,87,0)="        The site should answer ""NO"" to all three questions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,88,0)="            Note: You may not receive all three prompts at your site.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,89,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,90,0)="        1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,91,0)="           This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,92,0)="           your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,93,0)="        2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,94,0)="           should be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,95,0)="        3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,96,0)="           your system. You now need to use KIDS to install the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,97,0)="           Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,98,0)="           On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,99,0)="           following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,100,0)="               Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,101,0)="               Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,102,0)="               Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,103,0)="               Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,104,0)="        4. Users may remain on the system, but installation should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,105,0)="           done at off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,106,0)="        5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,107,0)="        6. Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,108,0)="           hours and less the 5 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,109,0)="        7. Installation of this patch requires no additional memory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,110,0)="           space."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,111,0)="        8. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,112,0)="           option 'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*293'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,113,0)="           and proceed with the install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,114,0)="        9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,115,0)="           be returned to the mapped set once the installation has run"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",129,1,116,0)="           to completion."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,0)="289 SEQ #228^3030802^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,0)="^^509^509^3030802"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,1,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*289 does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,2,0)="contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,3,0)="DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,5,0)="LR*5.2*289 is a mandated installation of the estimated Glomerular Filtration"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,6,0)="Rate (eGFR) delta check routine. Site(s) can setup the two new laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,7,0)="tests, Creatinine (including eGFR) and eGFR, in either a new or an existing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,8,0)="Serum Creatinine test. One of the new tests holds the input value (test "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,9,0)="result) and the other test holds the calculated output value. Both tests need"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,10,0)="to be setup in the same panel, which can be in either a new panel or, an"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,11,0)="existing panel."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,13,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,14,0)="Background"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,16,0)="Chronic kidney disease is a major public health problem. Adverse outcomes of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,17,0)="chronic kidney disease can be prevented through early detection and treatment."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,18,0)="Earlier stages of chronic kidney disease can be detected through routine"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,19,0)="laboratory measurements."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,21,0)="The USRDS provides reliable nationwide data regarding the incidence, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,22,0)="prevalence, treatment patterns, outcomes, and cost of kidney failure treated "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,23,0)="by dialysis and transplantation, the most severe stage of chronic kidney "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,24,0)="disease. This guideline provides a definition of chronic kidney disease as"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,25,0)="well as definitions and estimates of prevalence of earlier stages of kidney"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,26,0)="disease."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,28,0)="Chronic kidney disease is defined according to the presence or absence of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,29,0)="kidney damage and level of kidney function-irrespective of the type of kidney "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,30,0)="disease (diagnosis). Among individuals with chronic kidney disease, the stages"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,31,0)="are defined based on the level of kidney function. Identifying the presence"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,32,0)="and stage of chronic kidney disease in an individual is not a substitute for "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,33,0)="accurate assessment of the cause of kidney disease, extent of kidney damage, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,34,0)="level of kidney function, comorbid conditions, complications of decreased "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,35,0)="kidney function, or risks for loss of kidney function or cardiovascular"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,36,0)="disease in that patient. Defining stages of chronic kidney disease requires "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,37,0)="""categorization"" of continuous measures of kidney function, and the ""cut-off "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,38,0)="levels"" between stages are inherently arbitrary. Nonetheless, staging of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,39,0)="chronic kidney disease will facilitate application of clinical practice "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,40,0)="guidelines, clinical performance measures and quality improvement efforts to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,41,0)="the evaluation, and management of chronic kidney disease."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,43,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,44,0)="Reasons for estimated Glomerular Filtration Rate (eGFR)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,46,0)="In February 2002, the National Kidney Foundation recognized the Glomerular"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,47,0)="Filtration Rate as an indicator of renal function.  The eGFR is calculated"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,48,0)="rather than measured, and the Washington, DC Medical Center has developed a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,49,0)="routine known as a delta check that performs the calculation.  The Washington"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,50,0)="delta check uses the serum creatinine result, age, and sex from the local"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,51,0)="VISTA Laboratory package. The new program will calculate the eGFR for African-"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,52,0)="Americans and others according to the accepted calculation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,54,0)="It is important to note that National Kidney Foundation's ""Kidney Disease"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,55,0)="Outcomes Quality Initiative (K/DOQI) Clinical Practice Guidelines for Chronic"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,56,0)="Kidney Disease: Evaluation, Classification, and Stratification"" has stages of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,57,0)="kidney disease based on eGFR and also action plan as per Guidelines 1 & 2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,58,0)="These guidelines are published in the American Journal of Kidney Diseases Vol."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,59,0)="39, No 2, supplement 1, February 2002."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,61,0)="Adverse outcomes of chronic kidney disease can often be prevented or delayed "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,62,0)="through early detection and treatment. Earlier stages of chronic kidney "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,63,0)="disease can be detected through routine laboratory measurements. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,65,0)="  * The presence of chronic kidney disease should be established, based on "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,66,0)="    presence of kidney damage and level of kidney function (glomerular "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,67,0)="    filtration rate [GFR]), irrespective of diagnosis."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,69,0)="  * Among patients with chronic kidney disease, the stage of disease should "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,70,0)="    be assigned based on the level of kidney function, irrespective of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,71,0)="    diagnosis, according to the K/DOQI CKD classification Table 10. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,74,0)="            Table 10: Stages of Chronic Kidney Disease"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,75,0)="            "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,76,0)="                                                GFR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,77,0)="  Stage       Description                 (mL/min/1.73m^2)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,78,0)="_____________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,79,0)="  1           Kidney damage with               >=90"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,80,0)="              normal or increasing GFR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,81,0)="---------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,82,0)="  2           Kidney damage with               60-89"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,83,0)="              mild decreasing GFR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,84,0)="---------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,85,0)="  3           Moderate decreasing GFR          30-59"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,86,0)="---------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,87,0)="  4           Severe decreasing GFR            15-29"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,88,0)="---------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,89,0)="  5           Kidney failure               <15(or dialysis)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,90,0)="_____________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,92,0)="    Notes: Chronic kidney disease is defined as either kidney damage "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,93,0)="    or GFR <60 mL/min/1.73m^2 for >=3 months. Kidney damage is defined "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,94,0)="    as pathologic abnormalities or markers of damage, including "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,95,0)="    abnormalities in blood or urine tests or imaging studies."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,97,0)="VHA is probably one of the few organizations nationwide that has the potential"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,98,0)="to report eGFR whenever serum creatinine is done.  This will help us identify"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,99,0)="patients with kidney disease early and take preventive action.  We will save"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,100,0)="about $55,000 per year per patient for preventing or delaying dialysis. This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,101,0)="does not take into account the morbidity associated with dialysis that will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,102,0)="be prevented."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,104,0)="Raye-Anne Dorn, National Tumor Registry Coordinator, has submitted a New"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,105,0)="Service Request for the creation of a laboratory test, the estimated"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,106,0)="Glomerular Filtration Rate, eGFR.  Thakor G. Patel, MD, Chief of Renal"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,107,0)="Diseases at Veterans Administration Central Office, endorses the request. The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,108,0)="endorser is seeking an alternative to the creatinine clearance test, a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,109,0)="laboratory test that measures renal function and requires all urine collected"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,110,0)="over a 24-hour period.  The request cites the difficulty of collecting such a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,111,0)="specimen, particularly from elderly patients.  Additionally, the Veterans"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,112,0)="Health Administration (VHA) Renal Program Office has recommended a standard"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,113,0)="process throughout VHA for performing and reporting the eGFR. The request is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,114,0)="to release this locally created delta check as Class 1 software."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,115,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,116,0)="The four-variable MDRD Study equation is recommended.  Although it has"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,117,0)="short-comings, it has been more rigorously evaluated than the Cockcroft and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,118,0)="Gault equation, and performs better in patients with kidney disease, gives"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,119,0)="results in units of ml/min/1.73 m^2, and does not require measurement of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,120,0)="weight.  Performance can be improved by calibration of the VA lab results"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,121,0)="with the MDRD Study lab (Cleveland Clinic).  Is there a VA ""central lab,"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,122,0)="that other labs relate to?  If so, it should be possible to ""calibrate"" that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,123,0)="lab to the MDRD Study lab.  (Of course, there is no Cockcroft Gault central"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,124,0)="lab, so calibration is an uncorrectable error with the use of the Cockcroft"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,125,0)="and Gault equation.)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,127,0)="The view is that it is difficult to interpret GFR values above about 60"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,128,0)="ml/min/1.73 m^2, due to differences in creatinine calibration among labs, and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,129,0)="uncertainty in the measurement of GFR in that range.  This is the reason"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,130,0)="that the NKF defined CKD Stage 3 as GFR <60, and that there are few"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,131,0)="differences in the action plan for CKD stages 1 and 2 (kidney damage and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,132,0)="GFR either greater than or less than 90).  It is important to instruct"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,133,0)="practitioners about the limitations of GFR estimates above 60."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,134,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,135,0)="Stages of chronic kidney disease (R, O). Among individuals with chronic kidney"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,136,0)="disease, the stage is defined by the level of GFR, with higher stages"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,137,0)="representing lower GFR levels."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,138,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,139,0)="          Table 12. Definition and Stages of Chronic Kidney Disease"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,141,0)="     GFR                 With Kidney Damage*         Without Kidney Damage*"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,142,0)="                       __________________________   __________________________"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,143,0)="Stages (mL/min/1.73^2) With HBP**   Without HBP**   With HBP**   Without HBP**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,144,0)="______________________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,145,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,146,0)=" 1      >=90             1***         1***          ""High blood      ""Normal"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,147,0)="                                                    pressure"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,148,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,149,0)=" 2      60-89            2***         2***          ""High blood       ""eGFR"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,150,0)="                                                   pressure with"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,151,0)="                                                     eGFR"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,152,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,153,0)=" 3      30-59            3***         3***             3***             3***"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,154,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,155,0)=" 4      15-29            4***         4***             4***             4***"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,156,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,157,0)=" 5      <15(or           5***         5***             5***             5***"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,158,0)="         dialysis)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,159,0)="______________________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,160,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,161,0)="*   Kidney damage is defined as pathologic abnormalities or markers of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,162,0)="    damage, including abnormalities in blood or urine tests or imaging"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,163,0)="    studies."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,164,0)="**  High blood pressure is defined as >= 140/90 in adults and >90th"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,165,0)="    percentile for height and gender in children."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,166,0)="*** Represent chronic kidney disease; numbers designate stage of chronic"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,167,0)="    kidney disease."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,168,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,169,0)="    May be normal in infants and in the elderly."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,170,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,171,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,172,0)="Table 12 illustrates the classification of individuals based on the presence"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,173,0)="or absence of markers of kidney disease and level of GFR, according to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,174,0)="definition and staging of chronic kidney disease proposed by this guideline."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,175,0)="In addition, it includes columns for the presence or absence of high blood"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,176,0)="pressure, because of the complex relationship of high blood pressure and "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,177,0)="chronic kidney disease."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,178,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,179,0)="All individuals with GFR <60 mL/min/1.73 m2 for 3 months are classified as"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,180,0)="having chronic kidney disease, irrespective of the presence or absence of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,181,0)="kidney damage. The rationale for including these individuals is that reduction"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,182,0)="in kidney function to this level or lower represents loss of half or more of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,183,0)="the adult level of normal kidney function, which may be associated with a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,184,0)="number of complications (Part 6)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,185,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,186,0)="All individuals with kidney damage are classified as having chronic kidney"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,187,0)="disease, irrespective of the level of GFR. The rationale for including"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,188,0)="individuals with GFR 60 mL/min/1.73 m2 is that GFR may be sustained at normal"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,189,0)="or increased levels despite substantial kidney damage and that patients with"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,190,0)="kidney damage is at increased risk of the two major outcomes of chronic kidney"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,191,0)="disease: loss of kidney function and development of cardiovascular disease"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,192,0)="(Part 7)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,193,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,194,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,195,0)="The four-variable MDRD Study equation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,196,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,197,0)="Estimated GFR (ml/min/1.73m^2)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,198,0)="     = 186 x (Scr)^-1.154 x (Age)^-0.203 x (0.742 if female) x (1.210 if"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,199,0)="        African - American)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,200,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,201,0)="      where:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,202,0)="        Scr = serum creatinine in mg/dL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,203,0)="        Age = age, in years"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,204,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,205,0)="(""four-variable"" (abbreviated) equation in Levey AS, JASN vol. 11:2000;"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,206,0)="   abstract - A0828) (see below)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,207,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,208,0)="A0828                                                  F138 (PS)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,209,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,210,0)="A. Simplified Equation To Predict Glomerular Filtration Rate from Serum"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,211,0)="Creatinine, Andrew S. Levey,(1) Tom Greene,(2) John W. Kusek,(3) Gerald J."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,212,0)="Beck,(2) MDRD Study Group. (1) Boston, MA, (2) Cleveland, OH, (3) Bethesda,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,213,0)="MD."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,214,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,215,0)="We recently developed and validated an equation to predict GFR from serum "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,216,0)="creatinine (Pcr), which is more accurate than creatinine clearance measured"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,217,0)="from 24-hour urine samples or predicted from the Cockcroft-Gault (CG) equation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,218,0)="(Levey AS, Ann Intern Med 1999; l30:877-884). GFR is expressed as ml/min/l.73"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,219,0)="m^2.  Required variables include Pcr (mg/dl), age (y), race (black vs."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,220,0)="non-black), gender, serum urea nitrogen (SUN, mg/dl), and albumin (alb.g/dl)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,221,0)="In clinical practice and in retrospective studies, measurements of SUN and "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,222,0)="alb may not be available.  Below, we list the full MDRD Study prediction"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,223,0)="equation (6 variables), as well as alternative prediction equations including"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,224,0)="fewer variables derived from measurements in the same 1628 patients."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,225,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,226,0)="       GFR = 170 x Pcr-0.999 x age -0.176 x 1.180 (if black)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,227,0)="              x 0.762 (if female) x SUN-0.170 x alb+0.318"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,228,0)="       GFR = 270 x Pcr-l.007 x age -0.180 x 1.178 (if black)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,229,0)="              x 0.755 (if female) x SUN-0.169"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,230,0)="       GFR = 186 x Pcr-l.154 x age -0.203 x 1.212 (if black)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,231,0)="              x 0.742 (if female)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,232,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,233,0)="The table below compares the performance of these equations and the CG"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,234,0)="equation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,235,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,236,0)="                       R 2     median A        75th % A        90th % A"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,237,0)="       6 variable      .903    11.3            19.8%           28.4%"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,238,0)="       5 variables     .899    11.6%           19.9%           29.4%"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,239,0)="       4 variable      .892    12.1%           20.5%           29.7%"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,240,0)="       CG              .842    13.8%           26.4%           40.5%"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,241,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,242,0)="A=absolute value of the median (50th), 75th and 90th percentiles of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,243,0)="distribution of the differences between measured GFR and predicted GFR or Ccr"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,244,0)="for each equation (includes bias correction for CG equation).  We conclude"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,245,0)="that simplified versions of the MDRD Study prediction equation provide more"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,246,0)="accurate estimates of GFR than measured or estimated creatinine clearance."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,247,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,248,0)="Example of Screen:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,249,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,250,0)="ACCESSION:                    CH 0205 3      CH 0205 4"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,251,0)="                              2/5 12:01d    2/5 12:50d"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,252,0)="CREATININE //1.2"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,253,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,254,0)="  (MISSING PARAMETER)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,255,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,256,0)="   ** eGFR: 74.6  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,257,0)="VOLUME //932  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,258,0)="ELAPSED TIME //5.5  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,259,0)="COMPUTED CREATININE CLEARANCE //23  L"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,260,0)="CREATININE EGFR     74.6//  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,261,0)="Select COMMENT: MISSING PARAMETER // "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,262,0)="  COMMENT: MISSING PARAMETER // "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,263,0)="Select COMMENT: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,264,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,265,0)="  ***************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,266,0)="  *                               NOTE:                                     *"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,267,0)="  * If the patients race is 'Undeclared' or 'Unanswered', the COMMENT field *"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,268,0)="  * will be populated with 'MISSING PARAMETER' text. The doctor will be able*"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,269,0)="  * view this information within CPRS. The delta check will calculate the   *"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,270,0)="  * formula without the race variable. The doctor will need to evaluate this*"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,271,0)="  * when viewing the reports in CPRS.                                       *"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,272,0)="  ***************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,273,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,274,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,275,0)="New Fields"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,276,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,277,0)=" There are four new fields: three TEST NAME FOR INPUT VALUEs (#60.1, #60.2,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,278,0)=" #60.3) and one TEST NAME FOR TEST OUTPUT VALUE (#61.1), which are stored in "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,279,0)=" the file DELTA CHECKS (#62.1). The new fields are pointers to file LABORATORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,280,0)=" TEST (#60). The new fields will be used by the delta check routine to get "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,281,0)=" the DATA NAME (#400) field, which is a pointer to CHEM, HEM, TOX, RIA, SER, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,282,0)=" etc. DD File SUB-FIELD (#63.04). When the delta check routine is invoked, the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,283,0)=" routine calculates the eGFR from the test result, age, gender, and race. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,284,0)=" The results of the calculation are stored in the local array LRSB(DATA NAME)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,285,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,286,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,287,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,288,0)="File/Field    Field Name               Node;Piece   Field Type"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,289,0)="-------------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,290,0)="62.1,60.1     TEST NAME FOR INPUT VALUE 1 5;1 POINTER TO LABORATORY TEST FILE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,291,0)="              (#60)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,292,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,293,0)="              LAST EDITED:     SEP 24, 2002 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,294,0)="              DESCRIPTION:     This field is a pointer to a test that will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,295,0)="                               contain the result value of the first incoming"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,296,0)="                               test. The result value should be stored in the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,297,0)="                               variable LRSB(X) - where X is the data name IEN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,298,0)="                               from ^DD(63.04.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,299,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,300,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,301,0)="62.1,60.2     TEST NAME FOR INPUT VALUE 2 5;2 POINTER TO LABORATORY TEST FILE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,302,0)="              (#60)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,303,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,304,0)="              LAST EDITED:     SEP 24, 2002 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,305,0)="              DESCRIPTION:     This field is a pointer to a test that will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,306,0)="                               contain the result value of the second incoming"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,307,0)="                               test. The result value should be stored in the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,308,0)="                               variable LRSB(X) - where X is the data name IEN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,309,0)="                               from ^DD(63.04.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,310,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,311,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,312,0)="62.1,60.3     TEST NAME FOR INPUT VALUE 3 5;3 POINTER TO LABORATORY TEST FILE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,313,0)="              (#60)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,314,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,315,0)="              LAST EDITED:     SEP 24, 2002 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,316,0)="              DESCRIPTION:     This field is a pointer to a test that will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,317,0)="                               contain the result value of the third incoming"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,318,0)="                               test. The result value should be stored in the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,319,0)="                               variable LRSB(X) - where X is the data name IEN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,320,0)="                               from ^DD(63.04.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,321,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,322,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,323,0)="62.1,61.1     TEST NAME FOR OUTPUT VALUE 1 5;4 POINTER TO LABORATORY TEST FILE "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,324,0)="              (#60)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,325,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,326,0)="              LAST EDITED:     SEP 24, 2002 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,327,0)="              DESCRIPTION:     This field is a pointer to a test that will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,328,0)="                               contain the calculated value of the first"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,329,0)="                               outgoing test. The calculated value should be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,330,0)="                               stored in the variable LRSB(X) - where X is the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,331,0)="                               data name IEN from ^DD(63.04.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,332,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,333,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,334,0)="The eGFR delta check will need to be associated a new or existing Serum"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,335,0)="Creatinine test. The tests called EGFR and CREATININE (INCLUDES EGFR) will "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,336,0)="need to be setup and then associated with the Serum Creatinine. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,337,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,338,0)="Example of Laboratory Test Setup: (THIS IS A DISPLAY OF ENTRIES IN THE FILE,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,339,0)="NOT A CAPTURED EXAMPLE OF A SETUP USING FILEMAN)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,340,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,341,0)="NAME: CREATININE,SERUM                  TYPE: OUTPUT (CAN BE DISPLAYED)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,342,0)="  SUBSCRIPT: CHEM, HEM, TOX, SER, RIA, ETC."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,343,0)="  LOCATION (DATA NAME): CH;689024;1     FIELD: DD(63.04,689024,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,344,0)="  HIGHEST URGENCY ALLOWED: ROUTINE      COMBINE TEST DURING ORDER: YES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,345,0)="  PRINT NAME: CREAT                   DATA NAME: CREATININE-EGFR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,346,0)="SITE/SPECIMEN: SERUM                    REFERENCE LOW: 0.7"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,347,0)="  REFERENCE HIGH: 1.5                   UNITS: mg/dl"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,348,0)="  TYPE OF DELTA CHECK: EGFR             LOINC CODE: 2160-0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,349,0)="COLLECTION SAMPLE: BLOOD                MIN VOL (in mls.): .2"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,350,0)="  SINGLE DAY MAX ORDER FREQ: 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,351,0)="INSTITUTION: WASHINGTON                 ACCESSION AREA: CHEMISTRY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,352,0)="VERIFY WKLD CODE: Creatinine            VERIFY WKLD CODE #: 82565.0000"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,353,0)="  CIS TEST CODE: CH017"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,354,0)="SITE NOTES DATE: JAN 17, 2002"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,355,0)=" NOTE:   Created per Raye-Ann Dorn.  Part of Creatinine (Includes EGFR) panel."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,356,0)="  NATIONAL VA LAB CODE: Creatinine      RESULT NLT CODE: Creatinine"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,357,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,358,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,359,0)="NAME: EGFR                              TYPE: OUTPUT (CAN BE DISPLAYED)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,360,0)="  SUBSCRIPT: CHEM, HEM, TOX, SER, RIA, ETC."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,361,0)="  LOCATION (DATA NAME): CH;689023;1     FIELD: DD(63.04,689023,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,362,0)="  HIGHEST URGENCY ALLOWED: ROUTINE      PRINT NAME: EGFR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,363,0)="  DATA NAME: EGFR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,364,0)="SITE/SPECIMEN: SERUM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,365,0)="SYNONYM: ESTIMATED GLOMERULAR FILTRATION RATE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,366,0)="SYNONYM: GLOMERULAR FILTRATION RATE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,367,0)="INSTITUTION: WASHINGTON                 ACCESSION AREA: CHEMISTRY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,368,0)="SITE NOTES DATE: JAN 17, 2002"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,369,0)=" NOTE:   Per Raye-Ann Dorn.  Part of Creatinine (Includes EGFR) panel."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,370,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,371,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,372,0)="NAME: CREATININE (INCLUDES EGFR)        TYPE: BOTH"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,373,0)="  SUBSCRIPT: CHEM, HEM, TOX, SER, RIA, ETC."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,374,0)="  LAB COLLECTION SAMPLE: BLOOD          HIGHEST URGENCY ALLOWED: ROUTINE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,375,0)="  PRINT NAME: CR EGFR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,376,0)="NUMBER: 1                               LAB TEST: CREATININE,SERUM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,377,0)="NUMBER: 2                               LAB TEST: EGFR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,378,0)="COLLECTION SAMPLE: BLOOD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,379,0)="INSTITUTION: WASHINGTON                 ACCESSION AREA: CHEMISTRY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,380,0)="SITE NOTES DATE: JAN 17, 2002"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,381,0)=" NOTE:   Per Raye-Ann Dorn.  Includes CREATININE EGFR and EGFR with a delta"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,382,0)=" check of EGFR."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,383,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,384,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,385,0)="If setting up the eGFR delta check, use FILEMAN to setup the new DELTA CHECK"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,386,0)="fields. The TEST NAME FOR INPUT VALUE 1 field (#60.1) and TEST NAME FOR OUTPUT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,387,0)="VALUE 1 field (#61.1) are pointers to DATA NAME field (#400) of the LABORATORY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,388,0)="TEST (#60) files. These fields will be needed to run the delta check."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,389,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,390,0)="Example of Delta Check Setup: (THIS IS A DISPLAY OF ENTRIES IN THE FILE,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,391,0)="NOT A CAPTURED EXAMPLE OF A SETUP USING FILEMAN)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,392,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,393,0)="NAME: EGFR                              XECUTABLE CODE: D STRT^LREGFR(DFN,X)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,394,0)=" DESCRIPTION:   Created 10/17/01 by SDV for Dr. TG Patel and Raye-Ann Dorn."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,395,0)=" Test is CREATININE-EGFR and its delta test is EGFR which Lon Paredes set and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,396,0)=" tested. On 08/01/2002, JAH modified and sent out as Class I software. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,397,0)="SITE NOTES DATE: AUG 01, 2002"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,398,0)="  TEST NAME FOR INPUT VALUE 1: CREATININE,SERUM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,399,0)="  TEST NAME FOR OUTPUT VALUE 1: EGFR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,400,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,401,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,402,0)="Setting Up INPUT and OUTPUT VALUE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,403,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,404,0)="Use FILEMAN to enter the INPUT and OUTPUT VALUE(s). These two pointers will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,405,0)="store the file LABORATORY TEST (#60) IEN in the file DELTA CHECKS (#62.1). "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,406,0)="This information will be used to acquire the field DATA NAME (#400) for "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,407,0)="the Laboratory test, which was setup to call the delta check routine. Below"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,408,0)="is an example of a session:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,409,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,410,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,411,0)="Select OPTION: ENTER OR EDIT FILE ENTRIES "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,412,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,413,0)="INPUT TO WHAT FILE: DISABILITY CONDITION// DELTA CHECKS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,414,0)="EDIT WHICH FIELD: ALL// ??"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,415,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,416,0)="   Choose from:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,417,0)="   .01          NAME"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,418,0)="   10           XECUTABLE CODE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,419,0)="   20           OVERFLOW 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,420,0)="   30           DESCRIPTION  (word-processing)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,421,0)="   31           SITE NOTES DATE  (multiple)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,422,0)="   60.1         TEST NAME FOR INPUT VALUE 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,423,0)="   60.2         TEST NAME FOR INPUT VALUE 2"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,424,0)="   60.3         TEST NAME FOR INPUT VALUE 3"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,425,0)="   61.1         TEST NAME FOR OUTPUT VALUE 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,426,0)="    FOLLOW A FIELD NAME WITH ';""CAPTION""' TO HAVE THE FIELD ASKED AS 'CAPTION:'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,427,0)="         OR WITH ';T' TO USE THE FIELD 'TITLE' AS CAPTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,428,0)="EDIT WHICH FIELD: ALL// 60.1  TEST NAME FOR INPUT VALUE 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,429,0)="THEN EDIT FIELD: 61.1  TEST NAME FOR OUTPUT VALUE 1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,430,0)="THEN EDIT FIELD:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,431,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,432,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,433,0)="Select DELTA CHECKS NAME: EGFR "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,434,0)="TEST NAME FOR INPUT VALUE 1: CREATININE,SERUM//"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,435,0)="TEST NAME FOR OUTPUT VALUE 1: EGFR//"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,436,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,437,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,438,0)="ASSOCIATED NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,439,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,440,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,441,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,442,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,443,0)="TEST SITES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,444,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,445,0)="Washington D.C."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,446,0)="VA Wilmington"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,447,0)="Long Beach VAMC Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,448,0)="VAMHCS, PERRY POINT DIVISION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,449,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,450,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,451,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,452,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,453,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,454,0)="of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,455,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,456,0)="   ;;5.2;LAB SERVICES;<patchlist>;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,457,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,458,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,459,0)="Routine         Old     New        2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,460,0)="-----------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,461,0)="LREGFR          n/a     2309496    **289**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,462,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,463,0)="  Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,464,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,465,0)="************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,466,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,467,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,468,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,469,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,470,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,471,0)="The install time for this patch is less than five minutes. This patch can be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,472,0)="installed when Laboratory users are on the system. Suggested time to install:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,473,0)="non-peak requirement hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,474,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,475,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,476,0)="NOTE: Kernel patches must be current on the target system to avoid problems"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,477,0)="loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,478,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,479,0)="      Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,480,0)="      Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,481,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,482,0)="1.     If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,483,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,484,0)="2.     Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,485,0)="       option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,486,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,487,0)="3.     On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS), select"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,488,0)="       the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,489,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,490,0)="4.     Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,491,0)="       all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,492,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,493,0)="5.     On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,494,0)="       options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,495,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,496,0)="        Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,497,0)="        Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,498,0)="        Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,499,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,500,0)="6.     Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,501,0)="       select the package LR*5.2*289.  When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,502,0)="       LOGONs during the install? YES//' choose 'NO'.  When prompted 'Want to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,503,0)="       DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols?"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,504,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,505,0)="       YES//', choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,506,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,507,0)="7.     On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,508,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",130,1,509,0)="*****************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,0)="287 SEQ #229^3030813^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,0)="^^188^188^3030813"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,1,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LR*5.2*287 contains no changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,2,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,4,0)="Patch LR*5.2*287 corrects a defect reported in NOIS ALB-0602-52815."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,5,0)="Duplicate comments were not being stored with results when verifying "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,6,0)="automated instrument or load work list data. This patch will allow the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,7,0)="site to specify on a load/work list basis whether duplicate comments"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,8,0)="will be stored with lab results when verifying the accession."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,10,0)="A new field STORE DUPLICATE COMMENTS (#2.2) in PROFILE multiple (#68.23)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,11,0)="of file LOAD/WORK LIST (#68.2) will determine if duplicate comments are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,12,0)="stored when processing results from a load/work list. When the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,13,0)="result verifying software is processing comments associated with a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,14,0)="load/work list result, this field determines how duplicate comments are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,15,0)="processed. If set to ""NO"" (default if no value) then a comment that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,16,0)="matches a previously stored comment will not be stored with the result."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,17,0)="If set to ""YES"" then the duplicate check is not performed and the comment"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,18,0)="is stored with the results irregardless if the comment already exists."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,19,0)="Setting it to ""YES"" will allow the handling of multiple line comments which"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,20,0)="contain the same comment more than once and are still clinically significant."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,22,0)="Edit the default parameters Load/Work list. [LRLLE DFT] option has been"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,23,0)="modified to allow configuring this field."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,26,0)="ASSOCIATED NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,27,0)="---------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,28,0)=" ALB-0602-52815 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,31,0)="TEST SITES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,32,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,33,0)=" Albuquerque VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,36,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,37,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,38,0)="  The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,39,0)="  of each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,40,0)="  <tab> ;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;<patchlist>;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,42,0)="                 Checksum      Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,43,0)=" Routine Name  Before Patch  After Patch  Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,44,0)=" ------------  ------------  -----------  ------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,45,0)=" LR287            N/A            5220883  **287** (Deleted by KIDS)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,46,0)=" LRVR4            8885386        8885642  **14,42,121,153,221,263,279,283,287**"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,48,0)=" List of preceding patches: 283"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,49,0)=" Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,51,0)="************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,54,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,55,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,57,0)="  The install time for this patch is less than 5 minute. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,58,0)="  can be installed when Laboratory users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,59,0)="  Suggested time to install: non-peak requirement hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,62,0)="NOTE: Kernel patches must be current on the target system to avoid"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,63,0)="      problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,65,0)="      Patch installation needs to be coordinated with the Laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,66,0)="      Information Manager (LIM/ADPAC)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,69,0)="  1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for them."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,71,0)="  2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option of the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,72,0)="      option will load the KIDS patch onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,74,0)="  3.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,75,0)="      select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,77,0)="  4.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,78,0)="      all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,80,0)="  5.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,81,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,82,0)="        Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,83,0)="        Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,84,0)="        Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,86,0)="  6.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,87,0)="      and select the package 'LR*5.2*287.  When prompted 'Want KIDS to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,88,0)="      INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// choose 'NO'.  When prompted"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,89,0)="      'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols?"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,90,0)="      YES//', choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,92,0)="      Note: KIDS will disable the following options during patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,93,0)="      installation:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,94,0)="         Enter/verify data (auto instrument) [LRVR]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,95,0)="         Enter/verify data (Work list) [LRVRW]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,96,0)="         Enter/verify data (Load list) [LRVRW2]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,97,0)="         Edit the default parameters Load/Work list. [LRLLE DFT]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,99,0)="  7. On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,100,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,101,0)="NOTE: Routine LR287 will be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,102,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,103,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",131,1,104,0)=" ************************************************************************"
