^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,80,0)="  Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,81,0)="  =========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,83,0)="  NOTE: This KIDS install does not place any options out of service"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,84,0)="        during the install and no user options are affected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,85,0)="        If KIDS prompts:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,86,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,87,0)="        ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,88,0)="         Install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,89,0)="        ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,90,0)="        ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,91,0)="        Protocols? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,92,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,93,0)="        The site should answer ""NO"" to all three questions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,94,0)="            Note: You may not receive all three prompts at your site.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,95,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,96,0)="        1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,97,0)="           This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,98,0)="           your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,99,0)="        2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,100,0)="           should be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,101,0)="        3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,102,0)="           your system. You now need to use KIDS to install the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,103,0)="           Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,104,0)="           On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,105,0)="           following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,106,0)="               Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,107,0)="               Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,108,0)="               Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,109,0)="               Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,110,0)="        4. Users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,111,0)="        5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,112,0)="        6. Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,113,0)="           hours and less the 5 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,114,0)="        7. Installation of this patch requires no additional memory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,115,0)="           space."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,116,0)="        8. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,117,0)="           option 'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*301'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,118,0)="           and proceed with the install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,119,0)="        9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,120,0)="           be returned to the mapped set once the installation has run"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",133,1,121,0)="           to completion."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",134,0)="297^3030924^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",134,1,0)="^^4^4^3030924"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",134,1,1,0)="HIPAA Code Set Versioning project."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",134,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",134,1,3,0)="See patch LR*5.2*297 in the National Patch Module for complete "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",134,1,4,0)="information on this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",135,0)="299 SEQ #233^3031002^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",135,1,0)="^^1^1^3031002"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",135,1,1,0)="See patch description for details."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,0)="310 SEQ #234^3031002^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,0)="^^126^126^3031002"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,1,0)="Installation of LR*5.2*301 (Released 9/15/03) has created a potential "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,2,0)="patient safety issue.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,4,0)="After installation of patch LR*5.2*301, Blood Bank units that are "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,5,0)="positive for an antigen that corresponds to a patient's antibody are not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,6,0)="detected by the Blood Bank Software during unit selection, unit "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,7,0)="crossmatch or unit issue.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,9,0)="Because the patient's antibody is displayed on the screen during the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,10,0)="patient processing, this should initiate each facility's own internal "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,11,0)="processes for performing the actual antigen typing on all units.  The "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,12,0)="potential for patient harm is possible but the likelihood that such an "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,13,0)="event actually occurred is low.  As a precaution, a facility should "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,14,0)="review transfusion records of any patients with an antibody that occurred "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,15,0)="since the installation of LR*5.2*301 to ensure that proper antigen "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,16,0)="testing did get performed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,19,0)="Emergency patch LR*5.2*310 is being released to restore the routines, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,20,0)="LR7OR1, LRDPA1 and LRDPA2 to their pre-patch LR*5.2*301 state.  If you "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,21,0)="have installed patch LR*5.2*301, because of the potential patient safety "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,22,0)="issues, is it recommended that you immediately install patch LR*5.2*310. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,23,0)="Directive 2001-023 dictates it be installed within 24 hours for an "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,24,0)="Emergency patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,26,0)="For those sites that did NOT install LR*5.2*301, since it has now been "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,27,0)="marked as ""Entered In Error"" in the Patch Module, LR*5.2*301 should not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,28,0)="be installed and is no longer available in the patch module.  The sites "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,29,0)="that did not install LR*5.2*301, MUST still install LR*5.2*310 even "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,30,0)="though the routines before and after install remain the same.  This is "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,31,0)="required because LR*5.2*310 will make a change to the 2nd line, adding "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,32,0)="310 to the patch list, which will be required in future patches."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,33,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,35,0)="****************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,37,0)="The following checksums are for those sites that have installed "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,38,0)="patch LR*5.2*301.  The Checksums Before Patch for sites that have not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,39,0)="installed patch LR*5.2*301 will match the After Patch checksums listed "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,40,0)="below."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,41,0)=" "
