^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,85,0)="  Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,86,0)="  =========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,88,0)="  NOTE: This KIDS install does not place any options out of service"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,89,0)="        during the install and no user options are affected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,90,0)="        If KIDS prompts:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,91,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,92,0)="        ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,93,0)="         Install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,94,0)="        ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,95,0)="        ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,96,0)="        Protocols? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,98,0)="        The site should answer ""NO"" to all three questions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,99,0)="            Note: You may not receive all three prompts at your site.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,100,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,101,0)="        1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,102,0)="           This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,103,0)="           your system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,104,0)="        2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,105,0)="           should be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,106,0)="        3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,107,0)="           your system. You now need to use KIDS to install the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,108,0)="           Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,109,0)="           On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,110,0)="           following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,111,0)="               Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,112,0)="               Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,113,0)="               Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,114,0)="               Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,115,0)="        4. Users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,116,0)="        5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,117,0)="        6. Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,118,0)="           hours and less the 5 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,119,0)="        7. Installation of this patch requires no additional memory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,120,0)="           space."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,121,0)="        8. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,122,0)="           option 'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'LR*5.2*310'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,123,0)="           and proceed with the install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,124,0)="        9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,125,0)="           be returned to the mapped set once the installation has run"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",136,1,126,0)="           to completion."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",137,0)="307 SEQ #235^3031126^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",137,1,0)="^^5^5^3031126"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",137,1,1,0)="This patch implements a request from DSS to expand the lab results "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",137,1,2,0)="site/specimen entries to include feces as an additional choice. At "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",137,1,3,0)="present the only two choices are blood and urine. The test ""Occult "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",137,1,4,0)="Blood"" is almost always performed on stool (i.e. feces) samples, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",137,1,5,0)="therefore feces is needed as a possible choice."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,0)="259^3040507^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,0)="^^122^122^3040507"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,1,0)="Description:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,2,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,3,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,4,0)="This patch to the Laboratory package does not contain any changes to the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,5,0)="VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by the VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,6,0)="VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,7,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,8,0)="VISTA Laboratory Anatomic Pathology Electronic Signature (Patch LR*5.2*259) "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,9,0)="software release implements the new electronic signature functionality "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,10,0)="within the Autopsy, Cytology, Electron Microscopy, and Surgical Pathology "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,11,0)="sections for the Autopsy protocol, Standard Form 515 (SF 515), and "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,12,0)="supplementary reports. This new electronic signature functionality can be "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,13,0)="to activated or deactivated by the discretion of the site. The new Turn "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,14,0)="Electronic Signature On/Off [LRAP ESIG SWITCH] option is used to activate "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,15,0)="or deactivate the new electronic signature functionality. The electronic "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,16,0)="signature functionality is activated during the verification/release "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,17,0)="process of the Autopsy and AP reports. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,18,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,19,0)="Pathologists may now view and electronically sign reports rather than "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,20,0)="printing a paper copy for viewing and signature. The electronic signature "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,21,0)="name is obtained from the NEW PERSON file (#200), ELECTRONIC SIGNATURE CODE "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,22,0)="field (#20.4). All electronically signed released reports are stored in TIU "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,23,0)="containing the electronic signature name, date, and time displayed on the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,24,0)="last page of the reports (near the bottom). Only authorized users are "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,25,0)="allowed to electronically sign reports. Non-authorized users will receive a "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,26,0)="message indicating that they are not authorized to electronically sign "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,27,0)="reports."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,28,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",138,1,29,0)="  "
