^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,300,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,301,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,302,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,303,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,304,0)="  The install time for this patch is less than 2 minutes. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,305,0)="  can be installed when Laboratory users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,306,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,307,0)="NOTE: Kernel patches must be current on the target system"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,308,0)="      to avoid problems loading and/or installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,309,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,310,0)="  1.  If any of the above routines are mapped, disable mapping for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,311,0)="      them."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,312,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,313,0)="  2.  Use the 'Load a Distribution"" option to load the Host file on to your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,314,0)="      system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,315,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,316,0)="  3.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,317,0)="      system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the transport   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,318,0)="      global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,319,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,320,0)="  4.  On the 'Kernel Installation & Distribution System' Menu (KIDS),"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,321,0)="      select the 'Installation' menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,322,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,323,0)="  5.  Use the 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' option and verify "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,324,0)="      that all routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,325,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,326,0)="  6.  On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,327,0)="      following options:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,328,0)="        Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,329,0)="        Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,330,0)="        Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,331,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,332,0)="      If you wish to preserve a copy of the routines exported in this "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,333,0)="      patch prior to installation, you should use the 'Backup a "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,334,0)="      Transport Global' option at this time.  You may also compare the  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,335,0)="      routines in your production account to the routines in the patch  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,336,0)="      by using the 'Compare a Transport Global to Current System' "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,337,0)="      option."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,338,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,339,0)="  7.  Use the 'Install Package(s)' option under the 'Installation' menu"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,340,0)="      and select the package 'LR*5.2*281'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,341,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,342,0)="      If prompted ' Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,343,0)="      Install? YES//' choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,344,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,345,0)="      If prompted ' Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,346,0)="      YES// ' choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,347,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,348,0)="      If prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,349,0)="      Protocols? YES//', choose 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,350,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,351,0)="  8.  On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,352,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",140,1,353,0)="  9.  Routine LR281 will be deleted after successful patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,0)="313 SEQ #238^3040802^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,0)="^^274^274^3040802"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,1,0)="Description"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,2,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,3,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,4,0)="This patch corrects several defects reported with the eGFR delta check"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,5,0)="released in patch LR*5.2*289 DELTA CHECK FOR EGFR TEST."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,8,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*313 does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,9,0)="contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,10,0)="DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,12,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*313 does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,13,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical elements"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,14,0)="functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,16,0)="RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*313 have no effect on Blood"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,17,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,19,0)="VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION:  Because of the nature of the changes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,20,0)="made, no specific validation requirements exist as a result of installation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,21,0)="of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,23,0)="1. NOIS DUR-0803-30566 and NYH-1203-10526 reported the eGFR calculation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,24,0)="delta check was not triggered when processing creatinine results via"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,25,0)="option Enter/verify data (autoinstrument) [LRVR]. The delta check will be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,26,0)="triggered when the creatinine value is entered and/or changed or when the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,27,0)="eGFR has not been calculated. If the eGFR is a required test and the result"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,28,0)="is 'pending' then the delta check will attempt to calculate the eGFR."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,30,0)="2. The comment ""MISSING PARAMETER"" generated when the patient's race is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,31,0)="'Undeclared' or 'Unanswered' is changed to ""For eGFR: Race unknown, if"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,32,0)="African American multiply result by 1.210""."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,34,0)="3. The delta check will determine the patient's race using the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,35,0)="criteria:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,36,0)=" a. If specimen for a PATIENT file (#2) patient, the race is determine "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,37,0)="    using supported API VADPT."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,38,0)=" b. If specimen for a REFERRAL PATIENT file (#67) patient, the race is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,39,0)="    determined based on RACE field (#.06) in REFERRAL PATIENT file."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,40,0)=" c. All other patient types will not use race as a parameter in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,41,0)="    calculation. These patient types will generate the 'race unknown'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,42,0)="    comment."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,44,0)="4. During patch development it was determined that the lock placed on the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,45,0)="accession being verified could be prematurely released. This defect could"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,46,0)="allow two or more users to edit the accession concurrently. The delta check"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,47,0)="has been changed to eliminate the releasing of the lock. The lock will now"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,48,0)="be released by the lab verifying options."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,50,0)="5. During patch testing a potential safety issue was identified with the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,51,0)="delta check with regards to display of abnormal/critical creatinine values."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,52,0)="The delta check displayed eGFR exception messages as part of the display"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,53,0)="of creatinine abnormal/critical flags. These eGFR exception messages will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,54,0)="be added as accession comments and not displayed as part of the creatinine"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,55,0)="result display."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,57,0)="The eGFR exception messages that will be added as comments are."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,58,0)="    Condition                             Comment"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,59,0)="    ---------                             -------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,60,0)=" no patient age   - ""For eGFR: **eGFR not Calculated - No Age Recorded**"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,61,0)=" no patient sex   - ""For eGFR: **eGFR not Calculated - No Sex Recorded**"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,62,0)=" race unknown     - ""For eGFR: Race unknown, if African American multiply"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,63,0)="                     result by 1.210"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,64,0)=" delta check"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,65,0)=" incorrectly"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,66,0)=" configured       - ""For eGFR: **eGFR not Calculated - Delta check not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,67,0)="                     configured**"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,68,0)="                     Note: this comment generated when field TEST NAME FOR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,69,0)="                           OUTPUT VALUE 1 (#61.1) is blank for the eGFR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,70,0)="                           delta check entry in DELTA CHECKS file (#62.1)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,71,0)=" creatinine"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,72,0)=" changed and eGFR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,73,0)=" not in editing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,74,0)=" profile          - ""For eGFR: **eGFR not in test editing profile -"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,75,0)="                     Creatinine Changed**"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,76,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,77,0)="When no patient age or sex is identified, ""canc"" will be entered as the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,78,0)="eGFR test result."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,79,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,80,0)="6. NOIS  FGH-0304-32518 reported the eGFR calculation was being performed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,81,0)="and the result added to the accession when there was no ordered test for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,82,0)="the eGFR. This prevents user from verifying and releasing test results."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,83,0)="The eGFR delta check will check for the eGFR test in the test editing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,84,0)="profile selected by the user. If the eGFR test is not in the editing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,85,0)="profile then it will not be calculated. If the creatinine value is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,86,0)="changed, the eGFR test is not in the editing profile and there is a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,87,0)="previous eGFR result then the exception message ""For eGFR: **eGFR not in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,88,0)="test editing profile - Creatinine Changed**"" will be generated"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,90,0)="7. When the eGFR delta check is called by option Group data review"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,91,0)="(verified & EM) [LRGVP] the delta check will quit with no action taken."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,92,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,93,0)="8. See patch LR*5.2*289 DELTA CHECK FOR EGFR TEST for instructions on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,94,0)="setting up and configuring the eGFR delta check."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",141,1,96,0)=""
