^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,132,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,133,0)="  Host File:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,134,0)="  =========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,135,0)="  Because this is part of a multi-package build this patch will be available"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,136,0)="  only as a host file. The name of the file is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,137,0)="  CLINICAL_REMINDERS_INDEX.KID."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,138,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,139,0)=" Sites will retrieve VistA software from the following FTP addresses.  The"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,140,0)=" preferred method is to FTP the files from download.vista.domain.ext.  This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,141,0)=" transmits the files from the first available FTP server. Sites may also"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,142,0)=" elect to retrieve software directly from a specific server as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,143,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,144,0)=" Albany          ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext  <ftp://ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,145,0)=" Hines           ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext   <ftp://ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,146,0)=" Salt Lake City  ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext     <ftp://ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,147,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,148,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,149,0)=" Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,150,0)=" ============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,151,0)=" 1. Detailed installation instructions may be found in the Installation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,152,0)=" Guide, PXRMIG-P12.PDF."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,153,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,154,0)=" 2. After successful installation, the init routine GMPLP27I may be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,155,0)=" deleted."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",146,1,156,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,0)="286^3041228^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,0)="^^427^427^3041228"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,1,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LR*5.2*286 contains changes to software"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,2,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 99-053, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,3,0)="VERSION 5.2.  Change includes:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,4,0)="   The addition of the ""USE FOR REFERENCE TESTING"" field (#13) to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,5,0)="   ""SITE/SPECIMEN SUB-FIELD"" (#60.01) of the LABORATORY TEST file (#60)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,6,0)="   The addition of the ""USE FOR REFERENCE TESTING"" field to the ""LR ATOMIC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,7,0)="    TESTS"" Input Template."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,9,0)="The above change has been reviewed by the VISTA Blood Bank Developer and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,10,0)="found to have no impact on the VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE version 5.2"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,11,0)="control functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,13,0)="RISK ANALYSIS:   Changes made by patch LR*5.2*286 have no effect on Blood"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,14,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,15,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,16,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS:  Patch LR*5.2*286 does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,17,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical elements"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,18,0)="functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,19,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,20,0)="POTENTIAL IMPACT ON SITES:  This patch contains changes to a Data"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,21,0)="Dictionary identified in Veterans Health Administration (VHA) Directive"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,22,0)="99-053. The changes have no effect in Blood Bank functionality or medical"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,23,0)="device control functions. There is no adverse potential to sites."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,25,0)="VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION:  There are no required validation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,26,0)="scenarios to be completed by sites after installing LR*5.2*286."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,27,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,28,0)="========================================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,30,0)="Patch LR*5.2*286 VA/DOD LAB INTEROPERABILITY will be distributed and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,31,0)="installed with patch LA*5.2*64 VA/DOD LAB INTEROPERABILITY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,33,0)="This patch adds support for sending/receiving Laboratory Electronic"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,34,0)="Data Interchange (LEDI) orders/results with Department of Defense (DoD)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,35,0)="facilities."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,37,0)="Laboratory result verification has been enhanced to allow the designation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,38,0)="of a performing laboratory and the use of the performing laboratory's"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,39,0)="units, normals, and normalcy status in results reporting."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,40,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,41,0)="1. User during the verification process is able to specify the performing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,42,0)="laboratory. The performing laboratory is selected from the list of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,43,0)="available entries in the site's INSTITUTION file (#4). The selection of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,44,0)="entries is screened as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,45,0)="   a. User can select the division they are logged on."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,46,0)="   b. User can select an institution that is configured in the LAB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,47,0)="      SHIPPING CONFIGURATION file (#62.9) as a host facility with their"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,48,0)="      division as the collecting facility."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,50,0)="2. During acceptance and verification of results received from a reference"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,51,0)="laboratory via an HL7 interface (LEDI), the performing laboratory, results,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,52,0)="units, normals and normalcy status contained in the HL7 message are stored"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,53,0)="""as is""."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,54,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,55,0)="3. Receipt of amended reports from a reference laboratory will generate a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,56,0)="MailMan bulletin containing the particulars of the amended report. This"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,57,0)="bulletin is sent to the members of the mail group specified for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,58,0)="""New Result"" alerts in LA7 MESSAGE PARAMETER file (#62.48) for the interface."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,60,0)="4. Amended reports received via a LEDI HL7 interface can be processed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,61,0)="via the Enter/verify/modify data (manual) option [LRENTER]."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,63,0)="5. Users using the Enter/verify/modify data (manual) option [LRENTER] to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,64,0)="enter results manually from a reference laboratory can use the units and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,65,0)="normals specified in LABORATORY TEST file (#60) by configuring USE FOR"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,66,0)="REFERENCE TESTING field (#13) within the SITE/SPECIMEN subfile (#100)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,67,0)="If this field is not enabled for reference laboratory result data entry,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,68,0)="then the user is prompted for units, normals, high and low reference ranges"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,69,0)="to store with the results. The Edit atomic tests option [LRDIEATOMIC]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,70,0)="allows Labortory Information Manager (LIM) to designate this functionality"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,71,0)="for affected tests."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,73,0)="6. NOIS DEN-1299-52099, NYH-0700-11942, PHI-0803-21507, TAM-0400-31033, and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,74,0)="WPB-0900-32221 reported the defect of normalcy status (low/high/critical"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,75,0)="low/critical high) being incorrectly evaluated when the test result is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,76,0)="zero (0). Evaluation of normalcy status will properly deal with test"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,77,0)="results of zero (0)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,79,0)="7. Changing normalcy status and units will trigger the generation of audit"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,80,0)="trail comments."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,82,0)="8. During verification, the ordering provider's phone and pager information"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,83,0)="is displayed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,85,0)="9. Display of lab results in the Computerized Patient Record System"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,86,0)="Graphical User Interface (CPRS GUI) and Laboratory Interim Reports has"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,87,0)="been modified to display units and normals associated with results at time"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,88,0)="of verification. Results that are derived from a Set of Codes will be"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,89,0)="reported using the external form of the code."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,91,0)="10. Display of performing laboratory has been added to CPRS GUI display of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,92,0)="results."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,93,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,94,0)="11. NOIS DAY-0303-40775 reported a defect in display of lab results with"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,95,0)="embedded spaces. When lab results contained embedded spaces these spaces"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,96,0)="were being removed prior to the display of the lab result. The removal of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,97,0)="theses spaces resulted in corruption of the result. Routines LR7OB63 and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,98,0)="LR7OR2 have been corrected to trim leading and trailing spaces but leave"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,99,0)="embedded spaces."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,101,0)="12. Enter/verify data (auto instrument) [LRVR] and Enter/verify/modify"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,102,0)="data (manual) [LRENTER] options will display patient information from"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,103,0)="PAT. INFO. field (#.091) in LAB DATA file (#63) during result verification."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,104,0)="(E3R #13408)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,105,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,106,0)="13. Alignment of test results during verification process has been adjusted"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,107,0)="to avoid display of previous and current test results together. Results"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,108,0)="will be displayed right-justified under the date/time of each specimen.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,109,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,110,0)="14. NOIS ALB-0100-50284, FAV-1103-70892 reported a failure of UID creation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,111,0)="and storage when creating a non-daily accession that is in common with"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,112,0)="another accession area. The failure occurs on the creation of the first"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,113,0)="accession for a given accession area and date. After the first accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,114,0)="for an accession date is created and stored in ACCESSION file (#68)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,115,0)="subsequent accessions have the UID stored properly. Failure was due to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,116,0)="missing subfile zeroth nodes for the ACCESSION DATE multiple (#68.01) and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,117,0)="ACCESSION NUMBER multiple (#68.02) of the ACCESSION file (#68) when calling"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,118,0)="FileMan to store the UID. Routine LRWLST1 will now check and set the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,119,0)="subfile's zeroth nodes before calling FileMan."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,121,0)="  FileMan calls have been converted from classic FileMan DIE calls to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,122,0)="FileMan Database Server calls (DBS). When an error condition is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,123,0)="encountered during a FileMan DBS call, the Laboratory package will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,124,0)="generate a mail message with the subject ""FileMan DBS call failed during"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,125,0)="accessioning in routine LRWLST1"". This message will be sent to the local"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,126,0)="mail group ""LMI"". It will contain debugging information to assist site"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,127,0)="and National VistA Support in resolving the condition that produced the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,128,0)="error."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,129,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,130,0)="15. NOIS BON-0196-71728 reported a problem with storing the appropriate"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,131,0)="treating specialty associated with an accession. A bad or incorrect"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,132,0)="pointer to FACILITY TREATING SPECIALTY file (#45.7) could be stored in"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,133,0)="the TREATING SPECIALTY (#6.6) field within the ACCESSION NUMBER field"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,134,0)="(#68.02) multiple within the ACCESSION DATE field (#68.01) multiple of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,135,0)="the ACCESSION file (#68). When a specimen is accessioned for a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,136,0)="non-inpatient and the user selects an inpatient ordering location the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,137,0)="software would use the specialty from SPECIALITY file (#42.4) that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,138,0)="is associated with the WARD LOCATION file (#42) entry linked to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,139,0)="HOSPITAL LOCATION file (#44)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,141,0)="   Routine LRWLST1 will determine treating specialty based on the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,142,0)="associated TREATING SPECIALTY field (#9.5) in the HOSPITAL LOCATION file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,143,0)="(#44) when the patient is not an inpatient. When a patient is an inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,144,0)="then treating specialty will be determined from the PATIENT file (#2),"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,145,0)="TREATING SPECIALTY field (.103). Treating specialty will only be stored"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,146,0)="in ACCESSION file (#68) when the patient is from PATIENT file (#2)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,147,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,148,0)="16. The following defects were identified during the software review as"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,149,0)="part of patch development."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,150,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,151,0)="  a. Ordering location and ordering provider will not be stored on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,152,0)="accessions that are related to LAB CONTROL NAME file (#62.3) entries."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,154,0)="  b. During accessioning if accession area is locked by another process,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,155,0)="the message displayed to user was ""Accession area is locked by another"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,156,0)="user."" Message will now include the name of the accession area that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,157,0)="the software is waiting on lock."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,158,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,159,0)="  c. Interim report options and displays will display month portion of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,160,0)="date/times using the three letter abbreviation instead of the two number"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,161,0)="designation to eliminate potential confusion with day portion of dates."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,162,0)="Time is displayed using 24 hour time format."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,163,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,164,0)="  d. Interim report could display the wrong ordering and collecting site"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,165,0)="when the specimen was received from an integrated facility. Report will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,166,0)="display the correct ordering and collecting site."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,167,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,168,0)="  e. Referral Patient Multi-purpose Accession option [LR LEDI] was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,169,0)="prompting the user for CPRS Nature of Order which is not used during"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,170,0)="accessioning of non-PATIENT file (#2) patients. Routine LROW3 is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,171,0)="modified to only prompt the user for CPRS Nature of Order when"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,172,0)="accessioning a patient from the PATIENT file (#2)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,173,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,174,0)="  f. Previous test versions of previous LEDI versions may have installed "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,175,0)="two versions of the ""D"" cross reference in LAB PENDING ORDERS ENTRY file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,176,0)="(#69.6). The post-install will delete and reindex the ""D"" cross reference"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,177,0)="on file #69.6."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,178,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,179,0)="  g. Entering of accession number during lab results verification will "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,180,0)="check for invalid values or numbers out of range (1-999999)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,181,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,182,0)="17. Referral Patient Multi-purpose Accession option [LR LEDI] will check"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,183,0)="for pending orders when performing accessioning without a bar code scanner."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,184,0)="It will display to the user and store order comments that accompanies"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,185,0)="electronic orders with order in LAB ORDER ENTRY file (#69)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,187,0)="18. When using the Enter/verify/modify data (manual) option [LRENTER] to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,188,0)="amend previously released results user can now enter their verifying"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,189,0)="initials in mixed case. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,190,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,191,0)="19. NOIS CHS-0303-40534 reported a defect which prevented results for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,192,0)="reflex tests added to a LEDI order at the host laboratory being returned"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,193,0)="electronically to the collecting laboratory. Routine LRWLST11 was storing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,194,0)="the collecting site as both the collecting site and ordering site in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,195,0)="order created in LAB ORDER ENTRY file (#69). When a collecting site is a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,196,0)="member of an integrated facility the collecting site is the site collecting"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,197,0)="the specimen and the ordering site is the primary facility of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,198,0)="integrated institution. Reflex test added by the host site would have the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,199,0)="incorrect ordering site assigned which prevents the LEDI software from"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,200,0)="returning the results of the reflex test to the collecting facility. Defect"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,201,0)="has been corrected to store the correct ordering and collecting sites on"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,202,0)="LEDI accessions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,203,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,204,0)="20. NOIS BRK-0499-10720, MAR-0603-21152 reported a defect during lab"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,205,0)="result verification using option Enter/verify/modify data (manual)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,206,0)="[LRENTER] which caused the previous patient demographics to be displayed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,207,0)="when entering results on an accession. If the previous selected accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,208,0)="was in an uncollected state, the option was skipping the uncollected"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,209,0)="accession and incrementing the default accession number to the next"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,210,0)="available accession. If the user selects this or another accession, the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,211,0)="patient demographics of the selected accession were not being displayed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,212,0)="Instead, the patient demographics of the uncollected accession were"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,213,0)="displayed. Routine LRVER will now display the patient demographics of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,214,0)="currently selected accession."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,215,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,216,0)="21. NOIS SFC-1103-60132 reported a defect during display of lab results"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,217,0)="in the CPRS GUI. When a critical flag becomes part of the data for a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,218,0)="patient in CPRS, the line of data containing the flag becomes split"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,219,0)="after the * following the high or low flag, and the units along with"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,220,0)="the reference range gets bumped to the next line down. Routine LR7OGMP"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,221,0)="increases the space allocated to display this information from 37 to 38"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,222,0)="characters to display units/normals on same line."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,223,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,224,0)="22. When displaying results that are a Set of Codes data type, the result"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,225,0)="will be displayed using the external value for the set of codes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,226,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,227,0)="23. NOIS NYH-0700-11942 reported a defect with critical value flag not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,228,0)="being triggered when entering a value of 0. Value of 0 will be evaluated"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,229,0)="when performing high/low/critical value checks."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,230,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,231,0)="24. When verifying results from a reference laboratory using Enter/verify"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,232,0)="data (auto instrument) option [LRVR], any test results that have not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,233,0)="been verified will be displayed to the user after verification. The display"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,234,0)="will list the test names, results, abnormal flags and units if available. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,235,0)="This display will list the test(s) as not reviewed. This may indicate that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,236,0)="additional or reflex testing has been added by the reference laboratory."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,237,0)="These additional tests may need to be added to the accession to process"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,238,0)="these results."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,239,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,240,0)="25. During verification of laboratory results, comments for a previous"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,241,0)="result are displayed along with the previous result when entering"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,242,0)="results manually or by automated instrument for user selected tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,243,0)="(E3R #18490). Users can indicate which tests should have previous"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,244,0)="test comments displayed during verification by flagging the test using"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,245,0)="General Lab User Parameters option [LR USER PARAM] located on the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,246,0)="Information-help menu [LRHELP]."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,247,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,248,0)="26. NOIS SDC-0904-61304  Reported a defect with the display of text"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,249,0)="results in CPRS when using the Laboratory Results-All Test By Date and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,250,0)="Laboratory Results-Selected Tests By Date. When a text result was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,251,0)="displayed that exceeded 10 characters and the test has no units or"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,252,0)="normals specified, the display of the result was corrupted with <spaces>"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,253,0)="inserted into the text. Test results will be displayed without corruption."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,254,0)="Units, reference ranges, and site codes will be displayed on the following"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,255,0)="line when test results print in area usually reserved for these parameters."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,257,0)="27. NOIS IND-0498-42538 reported a defect in display of test comments during"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,258,0)="lab test result verification when encountering an 'end-of-page' condition."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,259,0)="All test comments will now be displayed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,260,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,261,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,262,0)=" PATIENT SAFETY ISSUES RESOLVED IN THIS PATCH:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,263,0)=" ============================================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,264,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,265,0)=" PSI-040260/NOIS HVH-0604-10572 - ""Not Performed test Resulted"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,266,0)=" - No Alert Generated"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,267,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,268,0)="This patch corrects defects in software used to set laboratory tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,269,0)="to a Not-Performed (NP) state. The NP state was introduced by patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,270,0)="LR*5.2*221 in 1999.  The functionality introduced by this patch replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,271,0)="the ""delete-a-test"" functionality. Instead of deleting tests, tests are"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,272,0)="now set to a not-performed state."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,273,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,274,0)="However, tests in the NP state could still be edited such that the NP"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,275,0)="state is replaced with an actual result. Results entered into NP tests"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,276,0)="were not treated in the same manner as results entered through the normal"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,277,0)="results entry pathways. File updates to ACCESSION file (#68), LAB ORDER"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,278,0)="ENTRY file (#69), and ORDER file (#100) as well as alerts were not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,279,0)="generated. This situation was documented in NOIS HVH-0604-10572"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,280,0)="- ""Not Performed test Resulted - No Alert Generated"". This was identified"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,281,0)="as a potential patient safety risk. With concurrence from the Pathology"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,282,0)="& Laboratory Medicine Program Office, the appropriate mechanism for"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,283,0)="handling the situation is to disable editing of NP tests. If the test is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,284,0)="designated as NP and the user wants to edit the test result, they will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,285,0)="now have to order the test(s) in a new accession."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,286,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,287,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,288,0)="ASSOCIATED E3R"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,289,0)="--------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,290,0)=" E3R #13408, ADDING INFECTION WARNING TO PROCESS DATA OPTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,291,0)=" E3R #16060, CORRECT ALIGNMENT PROBLEM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,292,0)=" E3R #17904, LEDI BETWEEN VA AND DOD SITES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,293,0)=" E3R #18490, COMMENTS DISPLAY FORPRVIOUS RESULTS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",147,1,294,0)=" "
