^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",150,1,250,0)=" Updating Routine file......"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",150,1,251,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",150,1,252,0)=" Updating KIDS files......."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",150,1,253,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",150,1,254,0)=" LR*5.2*303 Installed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",150,1,255,0)="               Dec 21, 2004@13:40:27"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",150,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",150,1,257,0)=" Install Message sent #xxx"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,0)="311^3050311^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,0)="^^133^133^3050311"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,2,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*311 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,3,0)="contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,4,0)="DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,6,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*311 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,7,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,8,0)="elements functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,10,0)="RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*311 have no effect on Blood "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,11,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,13,0)="VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION:  Because of the nature of the changes "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,14,0)="made, no specific validation requirements exist as a result of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,15,0)="installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,18,0)="  NOTE: This patch is part of a multi-KIDS build that includes PXRM*2*1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,19,0)="        (CLINICAL REMINDERS), WV*1*16 (WOMEN'S HEALTH) and OR*3*210"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,20,0)="        (ORDER ENTRY/RESULTS REPORTING) (CPRS). Please see the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,21,0)="        description for PXRM*2*1 for information on retrieving the host"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,22,0)="        file containing these patches."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,25,0)="1) Currently the ADD^LRWOMEN utility notifies a Women's Health package"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,26,0)="utility whenever a Cytology or Surgical Pathology report is verified for a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,27,0)="female patient. This functionality was provided with LR*5.2*231."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,29,0)="After installation of patch LR*5.2*311, the ADD^LRWOMEN utility will also"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,30,0)="notify a new CPRS utility (LAB^ORB3LAB) for all patients, not just female"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,31,0)="patients. Integration Agreement #4287 grants the LABORATORY package"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,32,0)="permission to call the ORB3LAB routine."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,34,0)="2) The code in the MOVE entry point of the LRWOMEN routine was replaced "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,35,0)="with a QUIT command. With the release of LR*5.2*259, this entry point is "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,36,0)="no longer called. The entry point will be deleted in a future patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,38,0)="3) A new entry point, SNOMED, is added to the LRWOMEN routine. This entry "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,39,0)="point is called by the new indexes created with this patch (see #4 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,40,0)="below) when a SNOMED code is changed for a Cytology or Surgical Pathology "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,41,0)="entry. This entry point will call a Women's Health package routine."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,42,0)="Integration Agreement #4525 grants the LABORATORY package permission to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,43,0)="call the WVLABCHK routine."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,45,0)="4) Two new-style indexes are added to the LAB DATA (#63) file. These "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,46,0)="indexes will be executed when a SNOMED code is changed for a Cytology or "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,47,0)="Surgical Pathology entry."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,49,0)="The first index is on Subfile 63.12, Field .01 (ORGAN/TISSUE)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,50,0)=" FILE: 63.12"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,51,0)=" NAME: AC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,52,0)=" SHORT DESCRIPTION: Notify Women's Health of SNOMED change"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,53,0)=" TYPE: MUMPS    "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,54,0)=" EXECUTION: FIELD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,55,0)=" ROOT TYPE: INDEX FILE  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,56,0)=" ROOT FILE: 63.12"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,57,0)=" USE: ACTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,58,0)=" DESCRIPTION:   This MUMPS cross reference calls SNOMED^LRWOMEN any time a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,59,0)=" change to a SNOMED code is made.  The SNOMED line tag notifies the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,60,0)=" Women's Health package that a SNOMED change has been made on an already"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,61,0)=" verified pathology report for a female patient."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,62,0)=" SET LOGIC: Q:$D(DIU(0))  D SNOMED^LRWOMEN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,63,0)=" KILL LOGIC: Q"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,64,0)=" ORDER NUMBER: 1                       "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,65,0)=" TYPE OF VALUE: FIELD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,66,0)=" FILE: 63.12           "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,67,0)=" FIELD: .01"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,68,0)=" SUBSCRIPT NUMBER: 1       "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,69,0)=" COLLATION: forwards"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,71,0)="The second index is on Subfile 63.912, Field .01 (CYTOPATH ORGAN/TISSUE)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,72,0)=" FILE: 63.912"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,73,0)=" NAME: AC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,74,0)=" SHORT DESCRIPTION: Notify Women's Health of SNOMED change"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,75,0)=" TYPE: MUMPS      "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,76,0)=" EXECUTION: FIELD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,77,0)=" ROOT TYPE: INDEX FILE        "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,78,0)=" ROOT FILE: 63.912"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,79,0)=" USE: ACTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,80,0)=" DESCRIPTION:   This MUMPS cross reference calls SNOMED^LRWOMEN any time a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,81,0)=" change to a SNOMED code is made.  The SNOMED line tag notifies the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,82,0)=" Women's Health package that a SNOMED change has been made on an already"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,83,0)=" verified pathology report for a female patient."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,84,0)=" SET LOGIC: Q:$D(DIU(0))  D SNOMED^LRWOMEN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,85,0)=" KILL LOGIC: Q"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,86,0)=" ORDER NUMBER: 1                      "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,87,0)=" TYPE OF VALUE: FIELD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,88,0)=" FILE: 63.912   "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,89,0)=" FIELD: .01"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,90,0)=" SUBSCRIPT NUMBER: 1    "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,91,0)=" COLLATION: forwards"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,92,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,93,0)="Documentation:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,94,0)="=============="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,95,0)="There are no documentation changes for this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,98,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,99,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,101,0)="Below is a list of the routines included in this patch. The second line of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,102,0)="each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,104,0)=" <tab> ;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;**[patch list]**;Sep 27, 1994 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,105,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,107,0)="                Checksum        Checksum"
