^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,110,0)=" LR311PST       new             3501668         311"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,111,0)=" LRWOMEN        953781          627506          231,248,311"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,113,0)="Associated NOIS: <None>"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,115,0)="Associated E3Rs: <None>"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,117,0)="Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,118,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,119,0)=" Loma Linda, CA - VMS/Cache"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,120,0)=" Northern California HCS - VMS/DSM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,121,0)=" Washington, DC VAMC - VMS/DSM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,123,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,124,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,125,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,127,0)="This patch can be installed with users on the system.  However, it is "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,128,0)="recommended that installation occur when there is no Anatomic Pathology"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,129,0)="activity or activity is at a minimum.  This will prevent 'Cannot return to"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,130,0)="source routine' errors.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,131,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,132,0)="This patch is part of a multi-KIDS transport global. Please see the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",151,1,133,0)="description for PXRM*2*1 for instructions to load and install this patch. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,0)="302^3050525^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,0)="^^810^810^3050525"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,1,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*302 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,2,0)="contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,3,0)="DIRECTIVE 2004-058 titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,5,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*302 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,6,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,7,0)="elements functions. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,8,0)="RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*302 have no effect on Blood "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,9,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,11,0)="****************************IMPORTANT**********************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,12,0)="There is considerable PRE-installation file verification and preparation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,13,0)="to be performed by staff familiar with the use of FileMan and Laboratory "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,14,0)="file structure.  Failure to perform this pre-install testing before "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,15,0)="attempting to install this patch significantly increases the risk of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,16,0)="encountering errors, during or post installation.  The key element to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,17,0)="ensuring a successful installation of the patch depends upon existing "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,18,0)="files not containing corrupt data.  If corrupt data is present in the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,19,0)="affected files, when the fields are re-pointed during the post "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,20,0)="installation update phase, errors will occur.  Please read and follow all "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,21,0)="of the instructions outlined in this patch description."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,22,0)="***********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,24,0)="Technical post-install notes are included at the end of the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,25,0)="description. These technical notes can be used by the IRM service to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,26,0)="prevent or resolve issues surrounding the installation of this patch. It "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,27,0)="is impossible to anticipate all potential situations that exist; but the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,28,0)="notes address the most common. The key element ensuring successful "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,29,0)="installation of the patch depends upon existing files not containing "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,30,0)="corrupt data."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,32,0)="This patch will update the WKLD CODE (#64) file and replace several "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,33,0)="laboratory standardized files associated with National Laboratory Test "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,34,0)="(NLT) package and Logical Observation Identifier Naming Codes (LOINC) "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,35,0)="coding. (See list below) This patch will remove certain WKLD CODE (#64) "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,36,0)="file duplicates. This patch will also correct certain field definitions "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,37,0)="that produce invalid warnings produced by the FileMan Verify Field "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,38,0)="option. In order to implement the numerous file/field corrections, it is "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,39,0)="necessary to completely replace certain referenced NLT and LOINC files. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,40,0)="To ensure that this patch does not introduce any new data validation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,41,0)="errors, it is desirable that the data currently stored pointing to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,42,0)="replaced files is valid and errors resolved."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,45,0)="File #    File Name                     Update Method"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,46,0)="64.061    LAB ELECTRONIC CODES          Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,47,0)="64.062    LAB ELECTRONIC SUBTYPES       Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,48,0)="64.2      WKLD SUFFIX CODES             Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,49,0)="64.3      WKLD INSTRUMENT MANUFACTURER  Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,50,0)="64.81     LAB NLT/CPT CODES             Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,51,0)="95.3      LAB LOINC                     Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,52,0)="95.31     LAB LOINC COMPONENT           Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,54,0)="*64        WKLD CODE           Updated with new terms."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,56,0)="============================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,57,0)="LOINC Copyright acknowledgement:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,58,0)="LOINC was Copyrighted 1995, 1996, 1997, by Regenstrief Institute and the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,59,0)="Logical Observation Identifier Names and Codes (LOINC) Committee.  All "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,60,0)="rights reserved. LOINC is a trademark of the Regenstrief Institute."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,61,0)="Contact information:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,62,0)="LOINC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,63,0)="C/o Regenstrief Institute"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,64,0)="1001 West 10th Street, RHC-5"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,65,0)="Indianapolis, Indiana 46202 USA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,67,0)="========================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,68,0)="VistA Laboratory Package LAB LOINC (#95.3) file does not support all of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,69,0)="the fields contained in the LOINC database. Refer to the LOINC user's "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,70,0)="manual for more field details. The following fields are imported and "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,71,0)="supported within VistA."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,73,0)="#    Loinc Term      VistA name"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,74,0)="1    LOINC_NUM       CODE + CHECK DIGIT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,75,0)="2    COMPONENT       COMPONENT + LAB LOINC COMPONENT (95.31)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,76,0)="3    PROPERTY        PROPERTY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,77,0)="4    TIME_ASPECT     TIME ASPECT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,78,0)="5    SYSTEM          SYSTEM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,79,0)="6    SCALE_TYPE      SCALE TYPE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,80,0)="7    METHOD_TYPE     METHOD TYPE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,81,0)="9    CLASS           CLASSTYPE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,82,0)="10   SOURCE          SOURCE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,83,0)="14   DT_LAST_CH      DATE LAST CHANGED"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,84,0)="15   CHNG_REAS       CHANGE REASON"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,85,0)="16   CHNG_TYPE       CHANGE TYPE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,86,0)="19   STATUS          STATUS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,87,0)="20   MAP_TO          MAP TO"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,88,0)="23   VA_CD           VA CODE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,89,0)="59   SHORTNAME       SHORTNAME"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,92,0)="Because several standardized files are being completely replaced, the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,93,0)="pre-install routine will extract and save the values of the fields "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,94,0)="pointing to the replaced files. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,96,0)="The complete WKLD SUFFIX CODES (#64.2) file is saved into "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,97,0)="^XTMP(""LRNLT642"") global for 90 days. The ^XTMP(""LRNLT642"") file can be "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,98,0)="used to assist those sites that may have mistakenly added terms to the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,99,0)="(#64.2) file. Those local terms not included in the installed file should "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,100,0)="be formally requested by notifying the National Laboratory Test "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,101,0)="Coordinator using the form provided on the VistA laboratory Documentation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,102,0)="Web Page. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,103,0)="http://vista.domain.ext/clinicalspecialties/lab/"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,105,0)="Forward your completed request form to the Exchange distribution group:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,106,0)=" VHAISD LAB NLT_LOINC"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,108,0)="==========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,110,0)="This patch will completely remove certain files, replace the files with a "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,111,0)="standardized copy and then re-point the saved field entries to the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,112,0)="standardized copy. It is high desirable to determine that current fields "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,113,0)="and files are free of incorrect data. This will ensure that the patch "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,114,0)="installation will not introduce any new errors."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,115,0)="     Failure to ensure FileMan verification of fields option can be run "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,116,0)="without generating warnings will result in unresolved errors, which could "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,117,0)="have unpredictable results. The patch installation will not be affected "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,118,0)="by an invalid field. The patch will generate error message indicating "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,119,0)="those files/fields that could not be successfully re-pointed after the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,120,0)="standardized have been installed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,122,0)="*** Examples of a single file verify:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,123,0)="Select OPTION NAME: VA FileMan"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,125,0)="          VA FileMan Version 22.0"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,127,0)="Select VA FileMan Option: Utility Functions"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,129,0)="Select Utility Functions Option: VERify Fields"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,130,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,131,0)="MODIFY WHAT FILE: WKLD CODE// 60  LABORATORY TEST  (1059 entries)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,132,0)="VERIFY WHICH FIELD: ALL"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,133,0)="DO YOU MEAN ALL THE FIELDS IN THE FILE? YES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,134,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,135,0)="DEVICE: HOME//"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,137,0)="While the entire file should pass the verify fields check, the fields "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,138,0)="listed below are the critical entries that should not produce any "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,139,0)="warnings. If there are any warnings for these fields, they should be "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,140,0)="rectified before the patch is installed or the post install re-pointing "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,141,0)="procedure will not perform properly."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,142,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,143,0)="This is a list of files and fields that will be re-pointed after the LAB "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,144,0)="ELECTRONIC CODES (#64.061) is installed. These fields should be free of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,145,0)="verify field warnings. Errors or warnings in other fields WILL NOT affect "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,146,0)="the post-install re-pointing process but should be addressed as soon a "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,147,0)="possible."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,149,0)="To ensure that there are not any existing pointer problems, files and "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,150,0)="fields need to be validated. Data and file validation is done with the FM "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,151,0)="Verify Fields option. Only those fields pointing to the replaced files "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,152,0)="and the WKLD CODE file are an issue."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,154,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,155,0)="File #     File Name               Field #  Field Name"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,156,0)="======     =========               =======  =========="
