^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,738,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,739,0)=" LR*5.2*302 Installed.                Dec 09, 2004@02:13:10"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,740,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,741,0)="Install Completed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,742,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,743,0)="Loading of patch LR*5.2*302 completed on Dec 09, 2004@01:57:10"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,744,0)="LIM: Review description for LR*5.2*302 use KIDS:Utilities: Build File "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,745,0)="Print"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,746,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,747,0)="Installation of patch LR*5.2*302 completed on Dec 09, 2004@02:13"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,748,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,749,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,750,0)="  POST INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,751,0)="  ============================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,752,0)="Review installed LOINC codes to ensure that codes with the status of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,753,0)="Deprecated (DEL) are not used in your current mapping of LOINC codes. In "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,754,0)="some cases, deprecated LOINC codes [LAB LOINC (#95.3) file, MAP TO (#21) "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,755,0)="field] will have the suggested replacement LOINC code populated."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,756,0)="Note:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,757,0)="If your site is a HOST LEDI site, changing of any LOINC or NLT codes "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,758,0)="should be coordinated the collection site to ensure that both sites agree "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,759,0)="in LOINC and NLT mappings."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,760,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,761,0)="LR*5.2*302 Technical Install Notes:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,762,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,763,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,764,0)="This patch is attempting to clean-up the following files:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,765,0)="File #    File Name                     Update Method"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,766,0)="64.061    LAB ELECTRONIC CODES          Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,767,0)="64.062    LAB ELECTRONIC SUBTYPES       Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,768,0)="64.2      WKLD SUFFIX CODES             Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,769,0)="64.3      WKLD INSTRUMENT MANUFACTURE   Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,770,0)="64.81     LAB NLT/CPT CODES             Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,771,0)="95.3      LAB LOINC                     Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,772,0)="95.31     LAB LOINC COMPONENT           Replaced"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,773,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,774,0)="*64       WKLD CODE                     Updated"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,775,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,776,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,777,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,778,0)="The currently installed files are not compatible with the incoming LOINC "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,779,0)="V2.13. Therefore these files are being completely removed and a fresh "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,780,0)="version is being installed. When the new versions are installed certain "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,781,0)="pointers in other files could be broken or incorrect."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,782,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,783,0)="To address this problem, the pre-install routine will save the existing "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,784,0)="data in external format in the ^XTMP(""LR302"",FILE,IEN,FLD)=DATA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,785,0)="This file will be purged in 90 days."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,786,0)="All the fields that point to the replaced files will be saved before the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,787,0)="old files are purged."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,788,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,789,0)="The post-install routine will:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,790,0)="1) Add any missing WKLD CODE to your system and create a mail message "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,791,0)="containing the added codes. If this process is successful the LAB NLT/CPT "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,792,0)="CODES (#64.81) should be empty of WKLD CODES."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,793,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,794,0)="2) Compare your previous WKLD SUFFIX CODES (#64.2) to the file installed "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,795,0)="by the patch. A MailMan message is created listing any locally added. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,796,0)="These codes must be requested via the mail group indicated in the patch "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,797,0)="description. Codes should not be locally added to any of the NLT Package "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,798,0)="files."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,799,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,800,0)="3) Re-index WKLD CODE file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,801,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,802,0)="4) Re-point the fields stored in the ^XTMP(""LR302"",FILE,IEN,FLD)=DATA "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,803,0)="file. If errors occur during the re-pointing process the wording ""ERROR"" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,804,0)="will appear during the post-install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,805,0)="The error is stored in this format."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,806,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,807,0)="S ^XTMP(""LR302"",""LRERR"",LRCNT)=LRFILE_U_LRIEN_U_LRFLD_U_LRDATA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,808,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,809,0)="The file will be purged in 90 days."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",152,1,810,0)="You will have to manually enter the appropriate value."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,0)="290^3050611^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,0)="^^171^171^3050611"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,1,0)="Blood Bank Clearance"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,2,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,3,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*290 does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,4,0)="contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,5,0)="DIRECTIVE 99-053 titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,7,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*290 does not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,8,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical elements"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,9,0)="functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,11,0)="RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*290 have no effect on Blood"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,12,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,14,0)="========================================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,16,0)="This patch adds support for Laboratory Point of Care (POC) interfaces."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,17,0)="It utilizes existing functionality provided by Laboratory Universal"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,18,0)="Interface (UI) and Laboratory Electronic Data Interchange (LEDI) software."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,19,0)="It supports the transmission, processing and storing of POC test results"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,20,0)="in the VistA Laboratory package. The ability of POC interfaces to subscribe"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,21,0)="to VistA HL7 ADT messages for patient demographics and location information"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,22,0)="is provided as needed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,25,0)="NOTE: THIS PATCH WILL BE INSTALLED WITH LA*5.2*67"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,28,0)="1. Laboratory orders created by this interface will have a CPRS Nature of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,29,0)="Order 'AUTO' assigned."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,31,0)="2. It creates a 'non-human' user 'LRLAB,POC' in NEW PERSON file (#200)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,32,0)="which is used to create the order and accession associated with the point"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,33,0)="of care test result. This entry has been approved by the VA VistA Data Base"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,34,0)="Administrator. Local site personnel should assign divisions to this user "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,35,0)="that corresponds to the accession areas used for POC results."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,37,0)="3. Options Summary list (supervisors') [LR SUP SUMMARY] and Summary list"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,38,0)="(extended supervisors') [LRLISTE] have been modified to display the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,39,0)="performing user, performing laboratory, LOINC code and Equipment Instance"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,40,0)="Identifier (EII) for each test result when the long or extended format is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,41,0)="chosen. The EII contains the vendor's make/model/serial number of the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,42,0)="instrument/equipment that produced the test result. When the vendor's"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,43,0)="instrument interface transmits this information, it will be stored with"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,44,0)="the test results."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,46,0)="4. CPRS Lab Display of Recent Results will display performing laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,47,0)="name and address of tests in accordance with College of American Pathology"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,48,0)="(CAP) requirements. Routine LR7OGMG was modified to add performing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,49,0)="laboratory information to comments section of the CPRS display."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,50,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,51,0)="5. NOIS MAR-0105-20968 reported the CPRS Lab Worksheet did not display the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,52,0)="external value of 'set of codes' data types. Values that are set of codes"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,53,0)="will be displayed using the external value of the set of codes. Routine"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,54,0)="LR7OGG was modified to return external values of set of codes to CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,57,0)="ASSOCIATED E3R"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",153,1,58,0)="--------------"
