^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",177,0)="354 SEQ #275^3060824^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",177,1,0)="^^2^2^3060824"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",177,1,1,0)="This patch corrects 2 PROBLEMS WITH THE TURNAROUND TIME REPORT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",177,1,2,0)="(LR CAPTT)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",178,0)="359 SEQ #276^3060824^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,0)="329 SEQ #277^3060923^1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,0)="^^295^295^3060923"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,1,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*329 does"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,2,0)="not contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,3,0)="by VHA DIRECTIVE 2004-058 titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,5,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*329 does"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,6,0)="not alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,7,0)="elements functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,9,0)="RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*329 have no effect on Blood"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,10,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,13,0)="1. Remedy ticket HD0000000088913 reported the Laboratory software was"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,14,0)="creating Laboratory Unique Identifiers (UID) which used the prefix '00'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,15,0)="instead of the site's two character identifier assigned to each accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,16,0)="area. This situation exists when the UIDs from old previously purged"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,17,0)="accessions are still in the ""C"" cross-reference of the ACCESSION file"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,18,0)="(#68), many from when the UID was first implemented in 1995."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,20,0)="One of the checks performed during UID creation is to check if the UID"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,21,0)="being generated exists in the ""C"" cross-reference. If it does and it is not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,22,0)="for the accession being created then the software replaces the accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,23,0)="area identifier the site has specified for the accession area and uses ""00"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,24,0)="in its place to insure creation of a unique identifier."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,26,0)="Example: LRO(68,""C"",1550180008,25,2950118,8)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,27,0)="Where: LRO = LRO global"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,28,0)="        68 = ACCESSION file (#68)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,29,0)="       ""C"" = cross reference"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,30,0)=" 155018008 = UID"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,31,0)="        25 = accession area"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,32,0)="   2950118 = accession date (Jan 18 1995)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,33,0)="         8 = accession number portion"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,34,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,35,0)="If the software wanted to assign the normally generated accession UID"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,36,0)="1550180008 to accession area 25, accession date of Jan 18 2005, accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,37,0)="number of 18 but found the UID already exist for 1995 accession for the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,38,0)="same day and number then UID generating software would replace 15 with 00"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,39,0)="to create a UID 0050180008 to allow accessioning to continue. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,40,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,41,0)="Note: The UID generating software will always produce an unique number."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,42,0)="No two accessions will ever have the same UID based on the ""C"" cross reference."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,44,0)="The routine LROC is modified to check for purged accessions and remove"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,45,0)="purged accession's UID from the ""C"" and ""D"" cross reference of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,46,0)="ACCESSION (#68) file. This will correct the problem of 10 year"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,47,0)="overlapping accession UID. This routine is invoked by Purge old orders"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,48,0)="& accessions option [LROC]."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,50,0)="Note: After installation of this patch the Laboratory software will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,51,0)="continue to create UIDs using the ""00"" prefix when an existing accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,52,0)="is still currently on the system and using the UID. This is to assure that"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,53,0)="the UID assigned to an accession is unique. The Laboratory software is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,54,0)="capable of handling UIDs correctly when the UID has a ""00"" prefix. There"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,55,0)="is no inherent requirement that a specific UID conform exactly to its"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,56,0)="related accession."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,58,0)="2. The check and purge of these cross-references will be tasked by the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,59,0)="post-install of this patch to cleanup any existing entries in file #68."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,60,0)="The post-install of this patch tasks a back-ground job to cleanup any"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,61,0)="existing entries in file #68 that have been previously purged. After"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,62,0)="this back-ground job has run to completion, the ""C"" and ""D"" should not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,63,0)="contain any UIDs related to purged accessions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,65,0)="3. As part of developer review, the Purge old orders & accessions option"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,66,0)="[LROC] has been made 'TaskMan aware'. Stopping of this tasked process can"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,67,0)="be accomplished using standard TaskMan utilities."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",179,1,69,0)=" "
