^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,172,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,174,0)="Overview of NOIS / Remedy Tickets:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,175,0)="================================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,177,0)="BRX-0704-11083 / HD0000000070862"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,178,0)="Problem:  Pathologists are complaining about changes in procedure done"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,179,0)="by the Electronic Signature patch. When a supplemental report is added "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,180,0)="the system un-verifies the parent report. This unverified report becomes "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,181,0)="available for other Pathologists and transcriptionists to edit it. Before "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,182,0)="once a report was verified it could not be changed. The Chief Pathologist "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,183,0)="is very concerned with the legal and clinical ramifications of this change."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,184,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,185,0)="Resolution: The resolution of this issue is contained in the section "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,186,0)="above that describes the resolution to patient safety issues #1 and #2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,187,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,188,0)="CPH-0904-40215 / HD0000000070983 - "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,189,0)="Problem:  Our pathologists are concerned that post patch 259, addition of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,190,0)="supplemental reports (additional information) must be added under MM Modify "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,191,0)="option, thus un-releasing the original report, and necessitating the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,192,0)="re-release of both original and supplemental reports.  They feel modified "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,193,0)="reports should be reserved for edition/correction of previous released "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,194,0)="reports. They feel this is a patient safety issue.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,195,0)="The post 259 options [LRAPDSR] and [LRAPDSS] are redundant when they are "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,196,0)="operable only with un-released reports.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,197,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,198,0)="Resolution: The resolution of this issue is contained in the section "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,199,0)="above that describes the resolution to patient safety issues #1 and #2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,200,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,201,0)="MIA-0604-31201 / HD0000000070788 - "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,202,0)="Problem:  According to our lab folks in Anatomic path they used to go in to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,203,0)="an option called Supplementary Report, Anat Path to make a correction to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,204,0)="the original after it is released.  They don't want to go under the edit "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,205,0)="modify to reopen the report any ideas on how they can go into the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,206,0)="supplementary to attach to the original accession report or something like "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,207,0)="that.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,208,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,209,0)="Resolution: The resolution of this issue is contained in the section "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,210,0)="above that describes the resolution to patient safety issues #1 and #2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,211,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,212,0)="PRO-0604-10213 / HD0000000070762 - "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,213,0)="Problem:  Our LAB Service Chief does not want IRM to install patch "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,214,0)="LR*5.2*259 for the following  Patient Safety, integrity, and additional "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,215,0)="keystrokes reasons.  For example the Surgical Pathology Reports, the new "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,216,0)="patch, takes the Supplemental report feature away (ie. For a special "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,217,0)="stain), it's replaced with a modified report feature, which allows you to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,218,0)="make changes to the original report in addition to adding.  Also, while  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,219,0)="using the  modify report feature, while your in it, it makes the original "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,220,0)="report unavailable for the Providers to view.  He feels that this is a "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,221,0)="Major Patient Safety issue, that if a Doctor is with the patient, he won't "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,222,0)="be able to view the report.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,223,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,224,0)="Resolution: The resolution of this issue is contained in the section "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,225,0)="above that describes the resolution to patient safety issues #1 and #2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,226,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,227,0)="SLC-0604-50484 / HD0000000070766 - "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,228,0)="Problem:  I've just reviewed the NOIS MEM-0504-71296, and we are struggling "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,229,0)="with the same issues of supplementary reports that they are. (Post install "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,230,0)="of patch LR*5.2*259).  We currently do not have the electronic signature "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,231,0)="turned on.  The concern is, that once a report is unreleased, the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,232,0)="previously released portion of the report is not viewable on CPRS, and the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,233,0)="way we operate here is that the secretaries transcribe the report, and the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,234,0)="pathologist signs them sometime later.  We have only had the patch "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,235,0)="installed for a couple of days, and the path lab has already received calls "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,236,0)="that reports have ""disappeared"" on CPRS ... are there any suggestions for a "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,237,0)="process change that could help with this?  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,238,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,239,0)="Resolution: The resolution of this issue is contained in the section "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,240,0)="above that describes the resolution to patient safety issues #1 and #2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,241,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,242,0)="SLC-0604-50594 / HD0000000070769 - "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,243,0)="Problem:  Post installation of LA*5.2*259 we have encountered the usual "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,244,0)="problems with any software install that changes the daily routine of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,245,0)="workflow, but there is a problem that we feel does affect patient care .  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,246,0)="We now have to ""unrelease"" a report prior to adding a supplementary report, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,247,0)="the secretaries then transcribe the supplemental report, then the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,248,0)="pathologists must review/correct and sign it prior to the secretaries "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,249,0)="re-releasing the report.  This leaves a window of several hours during "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,250,0)="which the original report is not viewable on the computer, we have already "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,251,0)="received calls about ""disappearing"" path reports.  Our pathologists feel "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,252,0)="that a supplemental report should truly be regarded as an addendum to the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,253,0)="original report, and should not make the original report unviewable while "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,254,0)="the supplemental report is being processed.    "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,255,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,256,0)="Resolution: The resolution of this issue is contained in the section "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,257,0)="above that describes the resolution to patient safety issues #1 and #2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,258,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,259,0)="SLC-0604-51082 / H00000000070778 -"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,260,0)="Problem:  We have found a problem with the electronic signature patch.  Our "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,261,0)="transcriptionist mistakenly selected the field to add a date to the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,262,0)="supplementary report field (thru edit/modify), but didn't add text to the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,263,0)="free text field.  He was unable to sign a supplementary report (the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,264,0)="computer says it doesn't exist), but when he tries to release the original "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,265,0)="report, it says that the supplementary needs to be released first.  The lab "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,266,0)="figured out a way to release this, but it is an issue.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,267,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,268,0)="Resolution: The resolution of this issue is contained in the section "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,269,0)="above that describes the resolution to patient safety issues #1 and #2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,270,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,271,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,272,0)="TEST SITES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,273,0)="=========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,274,0)="Ann Arbor VAMC  - CACHE/VMS, large site"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,275,0)="Boston HCS      - CACHE/VMS, large integrated site"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,276,0)="Long Beach VAMC - CACHE/VMS, large site"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,277,0)="Providence VAMC - CACHE/VMS, medium site"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,278,0)="Salem VAMC      - CACHE/VMS, medium site"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,279,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,280,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,281,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,282,0)="The following is a list of the routines included  in this patch.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,283,0)="The second line of each of these routines look like:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,284,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,285,0)="   <tab> ;;5.2;LAB SERVICE;**<patch list>;Sep 27, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,286,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",187,1,287,0)="Using old logic:"
