^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,78,0)="Installation Sequence "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,79,0)="======================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,80,0)="The files listed below represent the patches that have either been "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,81,0)="released or will be part of the controlled phased release.  The first 5 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,82,0)="patches have been released and already installed.  Patches starting with "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,83,0)="number 6 and are prefixed with an (*)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,84,0)="will need to follow the sequence listed below when your phased "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,85,0)="installation occurs."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,87,0)="  1. OR*3.0*243 (released 8/20/08)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,88,0)="  2. XT*7.3*116 (released ????"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,89,0)="  3. SR*3.0*168 (released ???"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,90,0)="  4. ECX*3*102  (released 8/25/08)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,91,0)="  5. LR*5.2*387 (released ???"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,92,0)="  6. *LR*5.2*335"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,93,0)="  7. *LR*5.2*367"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,94,0)="  8. *VBECS Bundle (consisting of VBECS 1.0 and LR*5.2*325)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,95,0)="  9. *VBEC*1.0*1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,96,0)=" 10. *OR*3.0*212"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,98,0)="Documentation Retrieval:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,99,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,100,0)="Documentation is available for the entire VBECS package on the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,101,0)="ANONYMOUS.SOFTWRE directory at one of the following Office of Information "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,102,0)="(OI) Field Offices.  Sites may retrieve documentation in either the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,103,0)=""".PDF"" or ""DOC"" format in one of the following ways:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,105,0)="1.      The preferred method is to FTP the files from :"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,106,0)="Download.vista.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,108,0)="2.      Sites may also elect to retrieve documentation directly from a "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,109,0)="specific server as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,110,0)="       Albany                  ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,111,0)="       Hines                   ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,112,0)="       Salt Lake City          ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,114,0)="NOTE:  The documentation files listed below will be listed in each of the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,115,0)="VBECS and LR patches that are part of the VBECS package and associate "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,116,0)="patches, they only need to be downloaded once."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,118,0)="File Name                                   Retrieval format:  Binary"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,119,0)="===========                                 =========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,121,0)="Known Defects and Anomalies.doc"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,122,0)="Known Defects and Anomalies.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,123,0)="VBECS Application Interfacing Support Software Installation and User "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,124,0)="Configuration Guide.doc"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,125,0)="VBECS Application Interfacing Support Software Installation and User "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,126,0)="Configuration Guide.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,127,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 1.4.0.0 Installation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,128,0)="Guide.doc"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,129,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 1.4.0.0 Installation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,130,0)="Guide.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,131,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 1.4.0.0 Technical "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,132,0)="Manual-Security Guide.doc"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,133,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 1.4.0.0 Technical "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,134,0)="Manual-Security Guide.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,135,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) Version 1.4.0.0 User "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,136,0)="Guide Version.doc"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,137,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) Version 1.4.0.0 User "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,138,0)="Guide Version.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,141,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,142,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,143,0)="This patch may be loaded with users on the system.  You may wish to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,144,0)="install it during non-peak hours.  Installation will take less than 2 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,145,0)="minutes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,146,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,147,0)=" 1.  Use the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE option on the Packman menu.  [Note: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,148,0)="     TEXT PRINT/DISPLAY option in the PackMan menu will display the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,149,0)="     patch text only.]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,150,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,151,0)=" 2.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,152,0)="     the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,154,0)=" 3.  From this menu, you may elect to use the following options (when"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,155,0)="     prompted for the INSTALL NAME, enter LR*5.2*387)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,156,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,157,0)="     (a)  Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,158,0)="          message of any routines exported with the patch.  It will NOT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,159,0)="          backup any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,160,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,161,0)="     (b)  Compare Transport Global to Current System - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,162,0)="          allow you to view all changes that will be made when the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,163,0)="          patch is installed.  It compares all components of the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,164,0)="          (routines, DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,165,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,166,0)="     (c)  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,167,0)="          you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,168,0)="          transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,169,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,170,0)="     (d)  Print Transport Global - this option will allow you to view the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,171,0)="          components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,172,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,173,0)=" 4.  Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package LR*5.2*387."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,174,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,175,0)=" 5.  When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,176,0)="     YES//', respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,177,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,178,0)=" 6.  When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",206,1,179,0)="     Protocols? YES//', respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,0)="335^3090609.153312^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,0)="^^496^496^3090609"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,1,0)="LR*5.2*335 is being exported as part of the VBECS package release. The "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,2,0)="installation of this patch will be controlled by a phase release. An "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,3,0)="Implementation Manager will be assigned to your site and will contact "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,4,0)="your POC for VBECS and will provide your site with the location of the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,5,0)="KIDS Host Files prior to your scheduled installation date installation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,6,0)="Sequence."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,8,0)="Select elements of VistA data must be transferred to the VBECS Blood Bank "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,9,0)="system prior to its initial operation. This will preserve patient related "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,10,0)="clinically and historically relevant information. This patch will install "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,11,0)="the software necessary to prepare the data for extraction from the VistA "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,12,0)="database, and extract the data to text files for transfer to the VBECS "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,13,0)="system. Some of the VistA data will be standardized to nationally "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,14,0)="recognized Blood Bank definitions during the extraction. Logical checks "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,15,0)="in the software will ensure data integrity. Once the data on the VistA "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,16,0)="side have been evaluated and converted to the new database, specific "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,17,0)="VistA Blood Bank options will be deactivated (placed out of order) so "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,18,0)="that the legacy database cannot be altered. These options are listed "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,19,0)="below under ""The following options are placed out of order."" More details "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,20,0)="can be found in the ""Blood Bank Pre-Implementation Data Validation, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,21,0)="Mapping, and Conversion ADPAC Guide"" document. The inadvertent or "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,22,0)="unintentional deactivation of these options could cause a disruption in "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,23,0)="Blood Bank operations. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,25,0)="Please read and follow the instructions in the ""Blood Bank "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,26,0)="Pre-Implementation Data Validation, Mapping, and Conversion Installation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,27,0)="and User Guide"" before proceeding with the installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,30,0)="BLOOD BANK CLEARANCE: 1/6/2009"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,31,0)="VISTA Laboratory Package patch LR*5.2*335 contains changes to software "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,32,0)="controlled by VHA DIRECTIVE 2004-058, titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,33,0)="Changes include:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,34,0)="Access is restricted on the following files:"
