^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,434,0)="Known Defects and Anomalies.doc"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,435,0)="Known Defects and Anomalies.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,436,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,437,0)="  Installation Information:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,438,0)="  =========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,439,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,440,0)="This patch is exported as part of the VBECS Blood Bank System and allows "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,441,0)="the conversion of limited existing Blood Bank data from VistA to VBECS. "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,442,0)="Please refer to the ""Blood Bank Pre-Implementation Data Validation, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,443,0)="Mapping, and Conversion Installation and User Guide"" for installation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,444,0)="information. The files listed below may be obtained via FTP. The "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,445,0)="installation of VBECS and its related patches are being handled as a "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,446,0)="controlled release. The implementation manager will contact you with the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,447,0)="location of the KIDS Host Files prior to your scheduled installation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,448,0)="date. The documentation files will be available for download in advance "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,449,0)="of installation through the anonymous download site as shown below."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,450,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,451,0)="  Installation Files: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,452,0)="  ==================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,453,0)="The following files are exported for LR*5.2*335:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,454,0)="   LR_52_335.KID"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,455,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,456,0)="   VBECSBATCH.COM"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,457,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,458,0)="LR_52_335.KID and VBECSBATCH.COM files will be made available by the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,459,0)="Implementation Manager prior to your site's implementation schedule along "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,460,0)="with instruction to retrieve."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,461,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,462,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,463,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,464,0)="This patch may be loaded with users on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,465,0)="Installation will take less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,466,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,467,0)="    1) Use the 'LOAD A DISTRIBUTION' option on the KIDS Installation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,468,0)="       menu. The Host File name is LR_52_335.KID. Answer YES to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,469,0)="       question: ""Want to Continue with Load? YES//"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,470,0)="    2) From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,471,0)="       select the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,472,0)="    3) From this menu, you may elect to use the following options"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,473,0)="       (when prompted for the INSTALL NAME, enter LR*5.2*335)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,474,0)="       a) Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,475,0)="          message of any routines exported with the patch. It will NOT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,476,0)="          backup any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,477,0)="       b) Compare Transport Global to Current System - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,478,0)="          allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,479,0)="          is installed. It compares all components of the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,480,0)="          (routines, DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,481,0)="       c) Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,482,0)="          you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,483,0)="          transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,484,0)="       d) Print Transport Global - this option will allow you to view the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,485,0)="          components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,486,0)="    4) Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,487,0)="       LR*5.2*335."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,488,0)="    5) When prompted ""Enter the Coordinator for Mail Group 'VBECS DATA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,489,0)="       CONVERSION':"" Enter the name of the person who will manage the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,490,0)="       VBECS DATA CONVERSION mailgroup."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,491,0)="    6) When prompted  'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,492,0)="       of Install? YES//  respond YES "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,493,0)="    7) When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,494,0)="       YES//', respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,495,0)="    8) When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",207,1,496,0)="       Protocols? YES//', respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,0)="367^3090609.153351^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,0)="^^200^200^3090609"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,1,0)="The installation of LR*5.2*367 will be controlled by phase release to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,2,0)="support the new blood bank software Vista Blood Establishment Computer "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,3,0)="System, VBECS. An Implementation Manager will be assigned to your site "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,4,0)="and will contact your POC for VBECS and will provide your site with the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,5,0)="location of the KIDS Host Files prior to your scheduled installation date."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,7,0)="This patch will allow the VistA Blood Establishment Computer System "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,8,0)="(VBECS) to use HL7 order update messages to complete orders created "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,9,0)="through the Blood Bank Accession Area.  The functionality will complete "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,10,0)="the accession for the specified test and the associated Computerized "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,11,0)="Patient Record System (CPRS) order"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,13,0)="ROUTINE: LR7OVB"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,14,0)="========"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,16,0)="OPTIONS: None"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,17,0)="========"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,19,0)="PROTOCOL: LR7O VBECS RECEIVE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,20,0)="========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,22,0)="BLOOD BANK CLEARANCE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,24,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*367 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,25,0)="contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by VHA "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,26,0)="DIRECTIVE 2004-053 titled VISTA BLOOD BANK SOFTWARE VERSION 5.2."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,28,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*367 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,29,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,30,0)="elements functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,32,0)="RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*367 have no effect on Blood "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,33,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,35,0)="VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION: Because of the nature of the changes "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,36,0)="made, no specific validation requirements exist as a result of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,37,0)="installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,40,0)="ASSOCIATED Remedy Tickets: None"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,41,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,43,0)="ASSOCIATED NSR/E3R: None"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,44,0)="==================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,46,0)="XINDEX Warnings:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,47,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,48,0)="XINDEX displays the following warning. The referenced routine (^ORMVBEC) "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,49,0)="will be installed with patch OR*3*212. This patch is part of the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,50,0)="controlled release of VBECS and will be installed as part of the VBECS "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,51,0)="system installation."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,53,0)="LR7OVB   * *  105 Lines,  4318 Bytes, Checksum: B19945746"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,54,0)="   COMPLETE+38  F - Reference to routine '^ORMVBEC'. That isn't in this "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,55,0)="UCI."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,57,0)="--- Routine Detail ---"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,58,0)="*****   ERRORS & WARNINGS IN LR7OVB   *****"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,59,0)="   COMPLETE+38  F - Reference to routine '^ORMVBEC'. That isn't in this "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,60,0)="UCI."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,62,0)="*****   INDEX OF LR7OVB   *****"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,64,0)="TEST SITES:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,65,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,66,0)="HEARTLAND-EAST HCS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,67,0)="PHILADELPHIA, PA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,68,0)="SAN DIEGO, CA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,70,0)="REQUIRED BUILDS: None"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,71,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,73,0)="Installation Information:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,74,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,76,0)="This patch LR*5.2*367 is being exported as part of the VBECS package "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,77,0)="release. This installation of these patches will be controlled by phase "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,78,0)="release. An Implementation Manager will be assigned to your site and will "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,79,0)="contact your POC for VBECS and will provide your site with the location "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,80,0)="of the KIDS Host Files prior to your scheduled installation date "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,81,0)="Installation Sequence"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,83,0)="Installation Sequence "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,84,0)="======================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,85,0)="The files listed below represent the patches will be part of the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,86,0)="controlled phased release.  Follow the sequence listed below when your "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,87,0)="phased installation occurs."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,89,0)="  1. LR*5.2*335"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,90,0)="  2. LR*5.2*367"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,91,0)="  3. VBECS Bundle (consisting of VBEC*1*0 and LR*5.2*325)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,92,0)="  4. VBEC*1.0*1"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,93,0)="  5. OR*3.0*212 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,95,0)="Documentation Retrieval:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,96,0)="========================"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,97,0)="Although this is a controlled, phased released, the user & technical "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,98,0)="documentation will be available to all sites when the patch is officially "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,99,0)="released and the phased implementations start.  This will allow sites the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,100,0)="opportunity to retrieve the documents before their phased installation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,101,0)="date"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,102,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,104,0)="Documentation is available for the entire VBECS package on the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,105,0)="ANONYMOUS.SOFTWRE directory at one of the following Office of Information "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,106,0)="(OI) Field Offices.  Sites may retrieve documentation either the "".PDF"" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,107,0)="or ""DOC"" format in one of the following ways:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,108,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,109,0)="The preferred method is to FTP the files from :"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,110,0)="        download.vista.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,112,0)="This transmits files from the first available FTP server.  Sites may also "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,113,0)="elect to retrieve documentation directly from a "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,114,0)="specific server as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,115,0)="       Albany                  ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,116,0)="       Hines                   ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,117,0)="       Salt Lake City          ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,119,0)="NOTE:  The documentation files listed below will be listed in each of the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,120,0)="VBECS and LR patches that are part of the VBECS package and associate "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,121,0)="patches, they only need to be downloaded once."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,123,0)="File Name:                                  Retrieval format:  Binary"
