^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,156,0)="Installation Files: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,157,0)="==================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,159,0)="LR_52_367.KID"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,160,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,161,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,162,0)="The host file LR_52_367 will be made available by the Implementation "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,163,0)="Manager prior to your site's implementation schedule along with "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,164,0)="instruction to retrieve."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,165,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,166,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,167,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,168,0)="This patch may be loaded with users on the system."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,169,0)="Installation will take less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,171,0)="The installation of VBECS and its related patches are being handled as a "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,172,0)="controlled release. The implementation manager will contact you with the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,173,0)="location of the KIDS Host Files prior to your scheduled installation date."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,174,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,175,0)="    1) Use the 'LOAD A DISTRIBUTION' option on the KIDS Installation"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,176,0)="       menu. The Host File name is LR_52_367.KID .  Answer YES to the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,177,0)="       question: ""Want to Continue with Load? YES//"""
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,178,0)="    2) From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,179,0)="       select the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,180,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,181,0)="    3) From this menu, you may elect to use the following options"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,182,0)="       (when prompted for the INSTALL NAME, enter LR*5.2*367)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,183,0)="       a) Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,184,0)="          message of any routines exported with the patch.  It will NOT"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,185,0)="          backup any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,186,0)="       b) Compare Transport Global to Current System - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,187,0)="          allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,188,0)="          is installed.  It compares all components of the patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,189,0)="          (routines, DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,190,0)="       c) Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,191,0)="          you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,192,0)="          transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,193,0)="       d) Print Transport Global - this option will allow you to view the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,194,0)="          components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,195,0)="    4) Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,196,0)="       LR*5.2*367."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,197,0)="    5) When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,198,0)="       YES//', respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,199,0)="    6) When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",208,1,200,0)="       Protocols? YES//', respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,0)="325^3090609.153457^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,1,0)="^^113^113^3090609"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,1,1,0)="LR*5.2*325 is being exported as part of the VBECS_BUNDLE_1.KID package "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,1,2,0)="release.  The installation of this bundle will be controlled by phase "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,1,3,0)="release.  An Implementation Manager will be assigned to your site and "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,1,4,0)="will contact your POC for VBECS and will provide your site with the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,1,5,0)="location of the KIDS Host Files prior to your scheduled installation date "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,1,6,0)="Installation Sequence.  The VBECS BUNDLE is a host file that consists of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,1,7,0)="both VBEC*1*0 and LR*5.2*325.  Installation of the VBECS BUNDLE will "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,1,8,0)="automatically install both VBEC*1*0 and LR*5.2*325"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,1,10,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,1,11,0)="========="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",209,1,12,0)="LR325 "
