^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,411,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,412,0)="LIM: Review description for LR*5.2*334 use KIDS:Utilities: Build File "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,413,0)="Print"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,414,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,415,0)="POST INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,416,0)="============================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,417,0)="Review installed LOINC codes to ensure that codes with the status of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,418,0)="Deprecated (DEL) are not used in your current mapping of LOINC codes. In "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,419,0)="some cases, deprecated LOINC codes [LAB LOINC (#95.3) file, MAP TO (#21) "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,420,0)="field] will have the suggested replacement LOINC code populated."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,421,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,422,0)="Note:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,423,0)="If your site is a HOST LEDI site, changing of any LOINC or NLT codes "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,424,0)="should be coordinated with the collection site to ensure that both sites "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,425,0)="agree in LOINC and NLT mappings."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,426,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,427,0)="Note:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,428,0)=" Please refer to the VistA NLT/LOINC V2.14 UPDATE Patch LR*5.2*334 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,429,0)=" Implementation Guide which provides the Laboratory Information "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,430,0)=" Manager (LIM) a task-oriented approaches with step-by-step "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",233,1,431,0)=" instructions and examples for mapping LOINC V2.14 codes."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",234,0)="350^3120924.154553^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",234,1,0)="^^1^1^3120924"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",234,1,1,0)="Refer to National Patch Module."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",235,0)="420 SEQ #333^3121101.11574^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",236,0)="418 SEQ #334^3121214.113346^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",236,1,0)="^^10^10^3121214"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",236,1,1,0)="This patch is a VM patch that addresses 3 LOINC-related issues in the Lab"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",236,1,2,0)="package."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",236,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",236,1,4,0)="1.      Option LR LOINC LOOKUP won't accept default."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",236,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",236,1,6,0)="2.      Option LR LOINC PRINT RESULT NLT prints MI (Microbiology) and BB "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",236,1,7,0)="    (Blood Bank) tests when it should only print CH (Chemistry) tests."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",236,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",236,1,9,0)="3.      Option LR LOINC PRINT RESULT NLT prints profiles (cosmic tests)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",236,1,10,0)="    when it should only print individual tests (atomic tests)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",237,0)="423 SEQ #335^3130410.174221^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",237,1,0)="^^10^10^3130410"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",237,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",237,1,2,0)="This patch is a VM patch that addresses 2 issues in the Lab package."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",237,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",237,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",237,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",237,1,6,0)="1.      In building the collection list, if an order fails to accession,"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",237,1,7,0)="    sometimes subsequent orders fail to accession for the same reason"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",237,1,8,0)="    even though the subsequent orders are ok."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",237,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",237,1,10,0)="2.      Laboratory-related locking issues when doing accessioning"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",238,0)="426 SEQ #336^3130422.104503^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",238,1,0)="^^1^1^3130422"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",238,1,1,0)="INPUT TRANSFORM ERROR IS CAUSING DATA VERIFICATION ERROR."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,0)="417 SEQ #337^3130614.090729^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,0)="^^22^22^3130614"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,1,0)="This patch is a VM patch that addresses 7 HOWDY-related issues in the Lab"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,2,0)="package."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,4,0)="1.      Option LRHY PPOC LABEL PRINT does not print an accession label"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,5,0)="    when only one accession is selected from a group of 2 or more "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,6,0)="    accessions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,8,0)="2.      Option LRHY PPOC LABEL PRINT has sequence numbers, accession"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,9,0)="    numbers, and collection samples running together on the screen."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,11,0)="3.      MI subscripted (Microbiology) tests will not accession in HOWDY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,12,0)="    if the MI test is on its own order and the site/specimen is not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,13,0)="    urine."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,15,0)="4.  The option LRHY PATIENT WAIT TIME reports inaccurate times."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,17,0)="5.  True accession number not appearing on LRHY PATIENT WAIT TIME"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,18,0)="    report."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,20,0)="6.  <SUBSCRIPT> error in option LRHY TRACK COLLECTION."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",239,1,22,0)="7.  Invalid link in HOWDY document."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",240,0)="429 SEQ #338^3130918.113944^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",240,1,0)="^^3^3^3130918"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",240,1,1,0)="This patch is a VM patch that replaces a direct read of file #80 (ICD"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",240,1,2,0)="Diagnosis) with a call to a standard API ($$ICDDX^ICDCODE) in the form"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",240,1,3,0)="LREPI9."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",241,0)="432 SEQ #339^3130930.101059^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",241,1,0)="^^4^4^3130930"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",241,1,1,0)="This is general maintenance patch for the laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",241,1,2,0)="package by the Vista Maintenance team that addresses"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",241,1,3,0)="issues related to screening for file #44 (Hospital"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",241,1,4,0)="Location) and an accessioning issue."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",242,0)="427^3130930.101808^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",243,0)="425 SEQ #341^3130930.10191^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",243,1,0)="^^10^10^3130930"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",243,1,1,0)="The following Lab changes or enhancements are included in this build:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",243,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",243,1,3,0)=" 1) CPRS API for Lab to call when a test is modified"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",243,1,4,0)=" 2) Changes to identify File 60 changes that impact CPRS Quick Orders"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",243,1,5,0)=" 3) National Lab Release: Hospital Location Change Management Tool"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",243,1,6,0)=" 4) National Lab Release: Lab Test File 60 Audit Tool"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",243,1,7,0)=" 5) National Lab Release: Inactivation of Collection Samples File Entries"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",243,1,8,0)=" 6) National Lab Release: Inactivation of Topography File Entries"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",243,1,9,0)=" 7) National Lab Release: Lapsed Orders"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",243,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",244,0)="436 SEQ #342^3140114.151802^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",244,1,0)="^^6^6^3140114"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",244,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue(s):"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",244,1,2,0)="1. When printing a CAPTIONED template report in VA FileMan with the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",244,1,3,0)="printing of computed fields turned on for the ACCESSION (#68) file all of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",244,1,4,0)="the values printed for the HOSPITAL ID (#.09) computed field will be the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",244,1,5,0)="same. It will print a different value for each different AREA (#.01) and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",244,1,6,0)="use that value for all patients with accessions in that AREA (#.01)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",245,0)="430 SEQ #343^3140221.101309^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",245,1,0)="^^5^5^3140221"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",245,1,1,0)="This is a general maintenance patch for the laboratory"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",245,1,2,0)="package by the Vista Maintenance team that addresses"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",245,1,3,0)="issues with the Howdy software relating to exclusionary"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",245,1,4,0)="functionality and also issues with the Howdy Wait Time"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",245,1,5,0)="report and the Howdy Track Collection report."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",246,0)="435 SEQ #344^3140303.143828^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",246,1,0)="^^2^2^3140303"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",246,1,1,0)="This patch is a VM patch that addresses issues in the lab package"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",246,1,2,0)="related to the VHIC 4.0 card."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",247,0)="416 SEQ #345^3140303.143838^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",247,1,0)="^^11^11^3140303"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",247,1,1,0)="This patch is a VM patch that addresses 3 issues in the Lab package."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",247,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",247,1,3,0)="1.  Option LRCENLKUP (Review By Order Number) gives misleading"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",247,1,4,0)="    information when 1 sample of a multi-sample order is not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",247,1,5,0)="    collected."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",247,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",247,1,7,0)="2.  The option LRAPFICH (Print final path reports by accession number)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",247,1,8,0)="    prints the wrong year on the SNOMED CODE LISTING which is printed"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",247,1,9,0)="    at the end of the pathology report for some AP accessions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",247,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",247,1,11,0)="3.  Autopsy reports not viewable in CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",248,0)="433 SEQ #346^3140304.121014^17"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",248,1,0)="^^10^10^3140304"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",248,1,1,0)="Lab Version 5.2 Patch 433 - Anatomical Pathology Image Framework"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",248,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",248,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",248,1,4,0)="Routines:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",248,1,5,0)="LR7OB63D    new value = 29564352"
