^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,1,0)="Nov 23, 2016 - V14 - The following defect was corrected by a modification "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,2,0)="to CRE863^LRAPLG1 routine that will restore the NOW// default instead of "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,3,0)="presenting a date and time."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,5,0)="423457: LI log in, anatomic path field of DATE/TIME SPECIMEN RECEIVED "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,6,0)="should default to NOW//"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,8,0)="Oct 6, 2016 - V13 - Added the following as required patches: "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,9,0)="LR*5.2*259,291,350,422,433,450"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,11,0)="Oct 5, 2016 - V12 - This release enhances the ""Delete accession #, anat"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,12,0)="path"" option to update CPRS status to discontinued."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,14,0)="Corrects - Defect 373204 -  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,15,0)="VLE ANATOMIC PATHOLOGY - VistA LR462/OR405 SURGERY CASE DOES NOT DISPLAY "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,16,0)="ON PATIENT DURING SPECIMEN LOGIN IN VISTA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,19,0)="Fix - M error when the accession has been cancelled using the ""Delete"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,20,0)="accession #, anat path""option and then a user tries to utilize the ""Delete"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,21,0)="entire order or individual test"" option for the same order number. - "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,22,0)="there was a typo in the legacy code in the LROS routine."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,25,0)="Sept 14, 2016 - V11 - Fixes 'no routine' error in APSUB^ORMBLDLR that was "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,26,0)="still calling LR7OAPMG which was changed with V10 to LR7OAPKM. Problem "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,27,0)="found by developer once CPRS32 v16 GUI was available. The routine "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,28,0)="LR7OAPMG has been added back into this build and will be removed at a "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,29,0)="later date."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,31,0)="Sept 8 - V10 - Fixes the following defects:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,32,0)="Defect # 373205 Surgeon Physician not displaying in VistA  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,33,0)="When submitted by is blank - the Surgeon does not display."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,35,0)="Defect # 373204 "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,36,0)="The surgery case look up fails during log"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,38,0)="Sept 1, 2016 - V9 - Fixes Undefined varible."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,39,0)="Defect # - 371975 - Undefined variable when login the specimen in VistA "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,40,0)="if Surgeon/Physician is not selected in CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,43,0)="AUG 25, 2016 - V8 - Fixes default bleed over problems with the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,44,0)="Pathologist and Submitted by fields in AP."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,45,0)="AUG 12, 2016 - V7 - Fixes defect 357639:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,47,0)="Defect: 357639 - VLE ANATOMIC PATHOLOGY - DURING SPECIMEN LOGIN IN VISTA, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,48,0)="PATHOLOGIST FIELD POPULATES NAME OF SURGEON USED FOR A PRIOR ORDER"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,50,0)="JULY 17, 2016 - V6 packman created and sent to forum - corrects problem "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,51,0)="in LRPLG1 routine."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,52,0)="JULY 15, 2016 - V5 packman created and sent to forum - corrects hard "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,53,0)="errors found by QA"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,54,0)="JULY 15, 2016 - V4 packman created and sent to forum"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,55,0)="JUNE 30, 2016 - V1 packman created and sent to forum"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,56,0)="JUNE 29, 2016 - V1 kids file to QA for do no harm testing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,58,0)="The build for this patch is distributed in support of the VLE "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,59,0)="Anatomic Pathology order dialog enhancements. It contains a modification "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,60,0)="to the LABORATORY TEST (#60), LAB ORDER ENTRY (#69), LABORATORY SITE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,61,0)="(#69.9) and adds the new file LR CPRS PARAMETERS (#69.71)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,63,0)="1-      Anatomic Pathology specimen log-in option has been modified to "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,64,0)="prompt the user for an order number. This order number will be created "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,65,0)="by CPRS after patches OR*3.0*405 and LR*5.2*469 are installed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,66,0)="2-      If a user enters an order number, the process deviates from the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,67,0)="current Log-in,anat path option in that it displays any data entered via"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,68,0)="CPRS AP order dialog. The fields presented could include any of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,69,0)="following:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,70,0)="   a.      SURGEON/PHYSICIAN"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,71,0)="   b.      SPECIMEN SUBMITTED BY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,72,0)="   c.      SURGERY CASE #"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,73,0)="   d.      SPECIMEN DESCRIPTION/SPECIMEN (multiple)"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,74,0)="   e.      BRIEF CLINCAL DESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,75,0)="   f.      PREOPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,76,0)="   g.      OPERATIVE FINDINGS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,77,0)="   h.      POSTOPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,78,0)="3-      If Surgical Case(s) are found for this patient in the last 7 days "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,79,0)="they will be presented to the user for selection. If a case is selected "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,80,0)="the data from the Surgical Case will be displayed and the user will be "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,81,0)="asked if they wish to include this in the appropriate field in the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,82,0)="Anatomic Pathology accession."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,83,0)="4-      If Surgical Case information is added to Anatomic Pathology "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,84,0)="fields it will display first and followed by the information obtained "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,85,0)="from the CPRS order."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,86,0)="5-      All other data entry/edit actions will be done via existing "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,87,0)="Anatomic Pathology options."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,91,0)="Blood Bank Review:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,92,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,93,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*462 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,94,0)="contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by ProPath"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,95,0)="standard titled: BBM Team Review of VistA Patches."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,97,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*462 does not "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,98,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical elements"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,99,0)="functions."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,101,0)="RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*462 have no effect on Blood "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,102,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,104,0)="VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION: Because of the nature of the changes "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,105,0)="made, no specific validation requirements exist as a result of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,106,0)="installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,107,0)=" "
