^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,244,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,245,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,246,0)="Documentation Retrieval Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,247,0)="------------------------------------- "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,248,0)="Updated documentation describing the new functionality introduced by this "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,249,0)="patch is available."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,250,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,251,0)="The preferred method is to FTP the files from "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,252,0)="ftp://download.vista.domain.ext/."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,253,0)="This transmits the files from the first available FTP server. Sites may "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,254,0)="also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific server as "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,255,0)="follows:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,257,0)=" Albany         ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext  <ftp://ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,258,0)=" Hines          ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext   <ftp://ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,259,0)=" Salt Lake City ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext     <ftp://ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,260,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,261,0)="Documentation can also be found on the VA Software Documentation Library "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,262,0)="at: http://www4.domain.ext/vdl/"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,263,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,264,0)="Title                         File Name                       FTP Mode"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,265,0)="-----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,266,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,267,0)="          "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,268,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,269,0)="Patch Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,270,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,271,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,272,0)="Pre/Post Installation Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,273,0)="-------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,274,0)="This patch will install new fields to the LABORATORY TEST (#60), LAB "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,275,0)="ORDER ENTRY (#69) and LABORATORY SITE PARAMETERS (#69.9) files. It will "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,276,0)="also install a new file, LR CPRS SCREEN (#69.71), four new ""LR7OAP"" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,277,0)="options, a print template for the LR CPRS SCREEN file and an edit "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,278,0)="template for the LABORATORY TEST file."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,279,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,280,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,281,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,282,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,283,0)="strongly recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours when "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,284,0)="LAB usage is at a minimum."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,285,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,286,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,287,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,288,0)="--------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,289,0)="This installation will install the components necessary to support the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,290,0)="CPRS AP Order Dialog functionality released with OR*3.0*405."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,291,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,292,0)="1.  Choose the PackMan message containing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,293,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,294,0)="2.  Choose the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option.  "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,295,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,296,0)="3.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,297,0)="    the Installation Menu.  From this menu, you may elect to use the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,298,0)="    following options. When prompted for the INSTALL NAME enter the patch "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,299,0)="    LR*5.2*462:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,300,0)="    a.  Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,301,0)="        message of any routines exported with this patch. It will not"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,302,0)="        backup any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,303,0)="    b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,304,0)="        allow you to view all changes that will be made when this patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,305,0)="        is installed.  It compares all components of this patch"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,306,0)="        (routines, DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,307,0)="    c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,308,0)="        you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,309,0)="        transport global."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,310,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,311,0)="4.  From the Installation Menu, select the Install Package(s) option and"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,312,0)="    choose the patch to install."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,313,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,314,0)="5.  When prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,315,0)="    Install? NO//'     "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,316,0)="    Respond: NO"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,317,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,318,0)="6.  When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,319,0)="    NO//'"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,320,0)="    Respond: NO"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,321,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,322,0)="7.  When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,323,0)="    and Protocols? NO//' "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,324,0)="    Respond: NO"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,325,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,326,0)="8.  If prompted 'Delay Install (Minutes):  (0 - 60): 0//' respond 0."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,327,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,328,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,329,0)="Post-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,330,0)="-------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",277,1,331,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,0)="469 SEQ #376^3170112.145517^54"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,0)="^^843^843^3170112"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,1,0)="Sept 30, 2016 - V9 - fixes defect #371947 by changing the values for the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,2,0)="HIDE FROM DESCRIPTION field (#.02) of the SPECIMEN multiple (#3) of the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,3,0)="LR AP DIALOG CONFIG file (#69.73) has been deleted in which the previous "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,4,0)="values were YES"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,6,0)="Defect #371947 - During Sprint 12 Review demo the SMEs asked if the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,7,0)="specimen could automatically populate in the Specimen Description [field]"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,8,0)="as that would be important.  The specimen is usually a part of the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,9,0)="description.  Stuti replied that a decision was made to remove the"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,10,0)="specimen from the Specimen Description; she also pointed out that there is"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,11,0)="a character limitation in Specimen Description.  Dev state that there is a"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,12,0)="""switch"" in the configuration to turn it on."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,14,0)="Sept 14, 2016 - V8 - contains modifications to the LR AP DIALOG CONFIG "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,15,0)="file in the following way:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,16,0)="     Each specimen of each orderable item within LR AP DIALOG CONFIG has"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,17,0)="     had the field HIDE FROM DESCRIPTION nullified so that the GUI will"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,18,0)="     move the specimen name into the specimen description when building"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,19,0)="     the specimen description."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,21,0)="AUG 12, 2016 - V7 packman created and sent to forum - contains modified "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,22,0)="aorderable item and specimen lookups"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,23,0)="AUG 1, 2016 - V6 packman created and sent to forum - fixes unresolved "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,24,0)="pointers problem on install due to order dialog prompts that will not be "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,25,0)="populated until OR*3.0*405 is installed."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,26,0)="JULY 21, 2016 - V5 packman created and sent to forum"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,27,0)="JULY 18, 2016 - V4 packman created and sent to forum"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,28,0)="JULY 15, 2016 - V3 packman created and sent to forum"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,29,0)="JUNE 30, 2016 - V1 packman created and sent to forum"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,30,0)="JUNE 29, 2016 - V1 kids file to QA for do no harm testing"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,32,0)="The build for this patch is distributed in support of the VLE "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,33,0)="Anatomic Pathology order dialog enhancements. It contains the new file LR "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,34,0)="AP DIALOG CONFIG (#69.73)."
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,36,0)="1-      The LR AP DIALOG CONFIG(#69.73) file is used to support the "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,37,0)="building and functioning of the CPRS AP DIALOG for the following thirteen "
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,38,0)="tests/orderable items:"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,39,0)="     BONE MARROW"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,40,0)="     BRONCHIAL BIOPSY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,41,0)="     BRONCHIAL CYTOLOGY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,42,0)="     DERMATOLOGY"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,43,0)="     FINE NEEDLE ASPIRATE"
^DIC(9.4,14,22,5.9,"PAH",278,1,44,0)="     GASTROINTESTINAL ENDOSCOPY"
