^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,96,0)="Installation Instruction:"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,97,0)="========================"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,98,0)="1. This patch can be loaded with users on the system."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,99,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,100,0)="2. Routine mapping is NOT recommended for these routines.  If you are"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,101,0)="using routine mapping, review your mapped set and ensure that these"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,102,0)="routines are NOT in your mapped routine before proceeding and rebuild"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,103,0)="your map set afterward before reactivating TaskMan."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,105,0)="3. Use the ""INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE"" option on the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,106,0)="will load the KIDS package into your system."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,108,0)="4. The patch has now been loaded into a transport global and you will"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,109,0)="use KIDS to install the transport global.  On the KIDS menu, under the"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,110,0)="'Installation' menu, use the following options"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,112,0)="2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,113,0)="3 Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,114,0)="4 Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,115,0)="5 Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,116,0)="6 Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,118,0)="             INSTALL NAME:  GEC*2.0*19"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,119,0)="             (Optional) At the prompt: 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,120,0)="                             Options and Menu Options?' enter NO."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,122,0)="5. MSM-DOS Sites - Answer YES to the question 'Want to MOVE routines to"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,123,0)="other CPU's?'.  Enter the names of your Compute and Print server(s)."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,125,0)="6. If routines were unmapped as part of step 3, they should be returned"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",3,1,126,0)="to the mapped set once the installation has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",4,0)="23 SEQ #20^3000204^1"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^65^65^3000204"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="   Y2K Waiver Request ID#:Y2KW0001   Y2K Waiver Status: Approved"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",4,1,2,0)="   This patch may be installed during the Y2K Moratorium, either"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",4,1,3,0)="   BEFORE 12/15/99 or AFTER 1/15/2000.  This patch MAY NOT be"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",4,1,4,0)="   installed between 12/15/99 and 1/15/2000(the Y2K Lockdown Period)."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",4,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",4,1,6,0)="1. MUS-1299-70853."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",4,1,7,0)="   When trying to purge old batches via GENERIC CODE SHEET, routines"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",4,1,8,0)="   not allowing purge of batches with a suffix.  Routine GECSPURG and"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",4,1,9,0)="   GECSPUR1 has been revised to allow deletion of selected batches."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",4,1,10,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",4,1,11,0)=" "
