^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,41,0)="NOTE OF IMPORTANCE:"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,42,0)="Routine will automatically execute in the Post-Install immediately after"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,43,0)="the installation of this package.  This routine should not be queued to"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,44,0)="run at a later time."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,46,0)="1. Users are allowed to be on the system during the Installation."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,48,0)="2. Routine mapping is NOT recommended for these routines.  If you"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,49,0)="are using routine mapping, review your mapped set and ensure that"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,50,0)="these routines are NOT in your mapped routine set before proceeding"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,51,0)="and rebuild your map set afterward before reactivating TaskMan."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,53,0)="3. Use the ""INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE"" option on the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,54,0)="loads the patch into a Transport Global onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,56,0)="4. You Do Not need to stop TaskMan or the background filers."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,57,0)="   (AXP Sites - Place TaskMan in a WAIT state."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,58,0)="   OpenM/Cache Sites - STOP TaskMan.)"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,61,0)="5. On the KIDS menu, select the ""Installation"" menu and use the"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,62,0)="   following options to install the Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,64,0)="  Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,65,0)="  Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,66,0)="  Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,67,0)="  Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,69,0)="  Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,70,0)="             INSTALL NAME:  GEC*2.0*25"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,71,0)="                            =========="
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,73,0)="  Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,74,0)="                                                        =="
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,75,0)="  Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,76,0)="  Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,77,0)="                   ==   "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,79,0)="6. AXP Sites - Answer NO to the question ""Want to MOVE routines"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,80,0)="   to other CPUs?"""
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,82,0)="7. If the routines were unmapped, the mapped set should be rebuilt"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,83,0)="   once the installation has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",6,1,85,0)="8. AXP and OpenM/Cache Sites Only - Remove TaskMan from a WAIT/STOP state."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",7,0)="26 SEQ #23^3000626^1"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^2^2^3000626"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",7,1,1,0)="This routine corrects a problem with the background job hanging"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",7,1,2,0)="when trying to set the status."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",8,0)="27 SEQ #24^3010103^1"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",8,1,0)="^^2^2^3010103"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",8,1,1,0)="This patch will store the mailman error when code sheets are"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",8,1,2,0)="not transmitted."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",9,0)="28 SEQ #25^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",9,1,0)="^^2^2^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",9,1,1,0)="This patch contains internal changes to support the Accounts"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",9,1,2,0)="Receivable Millenium Bill patch PRCA*4.5*170."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",10,0)="29 SEQ #26^3020315^1"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^7^7^3020315"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",10,1,1,0)="An error can occur with HSIF Revenue Funds during the transmission of the "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",10,1,2,0)="Accounts Receivable monthly information to FMS.  This error occurs during "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",10,1,3,0)="the transmission of a TR document and is due to the BATCH TYPE field "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",10,1,4,0)="(#.7) in the GENERIC CODE SHEET TRANSACTION TYPE/SEGMENT file (#2101.2) "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",10,1,5,0)="being incorrect."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",10,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",10,1,7,0)="This patch corrects that error."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",11,0)="30 SEQ #27^3020408^1"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^2^2^3020408"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="This patch corrects a problem with the Transfer (TR) document that is "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",11,1,2,0)="used to transfer dollars from the MCCF fund to the HSIF fund."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",12,0)="31 SEQ #28^3020423^1"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^4^4^3020423"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve an issue with MCCF/HSIF TR documents that are "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",12,1,2,0)="transmitted to FMS.  In some instances, references to ""TR"" will be "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",12,1,3,0)="changed to ""CR"" in the data that is transmitted.  This patch is being "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",12,1,4,0)="released in conjunction with Accounts Receivable patch PRCA*4.5*178."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",13,0)="33 SEQ #29^3040330^1"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",13,1,0)="^^3^3^3040330"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",13,1,1,0)="This patch corrects the issue where by an undefined variable error is"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",13,1,2,0)="occuring when a user attempts to exit an option by entering a caret (^)"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",13,1,3,0)="at the prompt."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",14,0)="34 SEQ #30^3051020^1"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",14,1,0)="^^3^3^3051020"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",14,1,1,0)="This patch increases the number of possible unique batch numbers that can "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",14,1,2,0)="be generated for modified billing documents being sent to FMS from 1000 "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",14,1,3,0)="to 12250."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",15,0)="36 SEQ #31^3120829.111156^17"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",15,1,0)="^^2^2^3120829"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",15,1,1,0)="This patch changes the retention period for the Generic Code Sheet Purge "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",15,1,2,0)="option from 365 days to 7 years."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",16,0)="35 SEQ #32^3130205.124121^17"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^2^2^3130205"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",16,1,1,0)="Inactivate code sheet transaction types 994.00, 994.01, 994.02, 994.10,"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",16,1,2,0)="and 994.90."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",17,0)="37 SEQ #34^3130516.174432^17"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",17,1,0)="^^3^3^3130516"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",17,1,1,0)="This patch addresses a change request with the IO variable for the code"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",17,1,2,0)="sheet printing in the Keypunch a Code Sheet option running under the"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",17,1,3,0)="Linux operating system."
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",18,0)="39 SEQ #35^3160902.134223^54"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^1^1^3160902"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="1. Modify 'PRC GECS PURGE' for improved date control "
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",19,0)="40^3180130.150817^54"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",19,1,0)="^^2^2^3180130"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",19,1,1,0)="1. Modify GEC document for correct date in CTL segment for IFCAP orders"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",19,1,2,0)="   and 1358 when Date Committed not in current Fiscal Year"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",20,0)="41 SEQ #37^3260316.131745^90"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",20,1,0)="^^1^1^3260316"
^DIC(9.4,28,22,6,"PAH",20,1,1,0)="Please see patch description on Forum for patch description details."
