^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,228,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,229,0)="List of preceding patches: 14, 15, 26, 34, 35, 43, 49, 50"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,230,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,231,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,232,0)="Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,233,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,234,0)="  1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,235,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,236,0)="  2.  DSM SITES: Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed in"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,237,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,238,0)="      the Routine Summary section are mapped, they should be removed from "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,239,0)="      the mapped set at this time.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,240,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,241,0)="  3.  Shutdown all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers, and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,242,0)="      the Link Manager. Use the opitons:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,243,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,244,0)="       Shut Down All Logical Links"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,245,0)="       Stop all incoming filers"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,246,0)="       Stop all outgoing filers"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,247,0)="       TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,248,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,249,0)="      For DSM sites ONLY, if you have an HL7 UCX Service associated"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,250,0)="      with the account(uci/directory) where you are installing this patch,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,251,0)="      please disable this service."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,252,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,253,0)="  4.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,254,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,255,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,256,0)="  5.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,257,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,258,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,259,0)="      options: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,260,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,261,0)="         2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,262,0)="         3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,263,0)="         4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,264,0)="         5 Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,265,0)="         6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,266,0)="             INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*57"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,267,0)="                           ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,268,0)="         Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,269,0)="         and Protocols?'.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,270,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,271,0)="  6.  Startup all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers. Use the "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,272,0)="      'Restart/Start All Links and Filers' option.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,273,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,274,0)="      For DSM sites ONLY, if you previously disabled an HL7 UCX Service"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,275,0)="      for this installation, you may now enable it."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,276,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,277,0)="  7.  DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,278,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,279,0)="  8.  Start Link Manager using the option: ""TCP/IP"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,280,0)="        Link Manager Start/Stop."""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,281,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,282,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,283,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,284,0)="For a complete and up-to-date set of documents, tutorials and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,285,0)="presentations (and access to the HL7 Standard) please"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,286,0)="visit the OpenVista Website (frequently) at:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,287,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,288,0)="http://vista2.domain.ext/openvista/"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,289,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,290,0)="At this site, you'll be able to find the new DEVELOPER MANUAL as well as"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,291,0)="supplemental information on DYNAMIC ADDRESSING and TCP/IP SUPPORT."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,292,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,293,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,294,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,295,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,296,0)="             Interface Configuration with Patch 57"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,297,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,298,0)="This section explains what has changed with Patch 57, and how the various"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,299,0)="files and fields will be used and the new business rules associated with"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,300,0)="validating a message header."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,301,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,302,0)="                   Event Point Protocols"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,303,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,304,0)="An event point protocol is a specific type of HL7 protocol defined in file"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,305,0)="101. It represents the sending side of a particular HL7 transaction. It"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,306,0)="does not have to be a VISTA event point. However, if the event point"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,307,0)="originates in VISTA, several fields have been renamed along with changes"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,308,0)="to underlying code to more clearly define how VISTA HL7 uses them. When a"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,309,0)="message is being generated in VISTA, the header will contain the data from"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,310,0)="these fields and is delivered to each of the subscribers found in the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,311,0)="SUBSCRIBERS multiple. Note that the ITEM multiple is no longer used for"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,312,0)="HL7 transactions."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,313,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,314,0)="Event Driver Protocol Key Fields"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,315,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,316,0)="770.1     SENDING APPLICATION (P771), [770;1]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,317,0)="770.3     TRANSACTION MESSAGE TYPE (P771.2'), [770;3]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,318,0)="770.4     EVENT TYPE (P779.001'), [770;4]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,319,0)="770.6     PROCESSING ID (S), [770;6]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,320,0)="770.8     ACCEPT ACK CODE (P779.003'), [770;8]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,321,0)="770.9     APPLICATION ACK TYPE (P779.003'), [770;9]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,322,0)="770.95    VERSION ID (*P771.5'), [770;10]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,323,0)="772       RESPONSE PROCESSING ROUTINE (K), [772;E1,245]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,324,0)="775       SUBSCRIBERS (Multiple-101.0775), [775;0]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,325,0)="          .01  SUBSCRIBERS (M*P101), [0;1]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,326,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,327,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,328,0)="                      Subscriber Protocols"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,329,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,330,0)="This type of protocol contains all of the parameters for and is always"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,331,0)="associated with the RECEIVING SYSTEM. The logical link field can be used"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,332,0)="to describe a single point-to-point interface between a sending and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,333,0)="receiving system. If this interface included two VISTA systems, the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,334,0)="logical link would always point to the remote system. All other settings"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,335,0)="in the interface definition would remain the same on both systems. The"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,336,0)="RESPONSE MESSAGE TYPE and EVENT TYPE are now used only for responses. "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,337,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,338,0)="When a message is received, the following validation checks are performed."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,339,0)="On the receiving system, the HL7 package parses the inbound message header"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,340,0)="and identifies the Sending Application, Receiving Application, Message"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,341,0)="Type, Event Type and version. If the event type is missing, it validates"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,342,0)="that the version is less than 2.2. It validates the sending and receiving"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,343,0)="application by checking them against the Application Parameter file. If"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,344,0)="they are missing or ""Inactive"" an error is logged. It then looks up the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,345,0)="Event Driver protocol using the AHL1 cross-reference or, if missing the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,346,0)="event type, uses the new AHL21 cross-reference on file 101. Delivery to"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,347,0)="the Subscriber protocol is then based on Receiving Application. An error"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,348,0)="is recorded if either the event driver or subscriber protocol cannot be"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,349,0)="found. Next, HL7 sets the logical link for the ""return path"" based on the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,350,0)="entry in the logical link field, (field 770.7). HL7 then checks to see if"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,351,0)="the sending and/or receiving facility fields are required for each"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,352,0)="application in the transaction (file 771). If the sending or receiving"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,353,0)="facility is required and the header is blank an error is logged. If the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,354,0)="facility information in the header differs from data in file 771 an error"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,355,0)="is logged. If no data exists in the application parameter file but the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,356,0)="facility information is required, HL7 expects the header to contain the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,357,0)="new default facility data. The receiving facility data is checked against"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,358,0)="the receiving system's site parameter settings and the sending facility"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,359,0)="data is checked against the logical link definition (file 870). If the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,360,0)="sending facility data (Domain name) is present and cannot resolve to a"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,361,0)="logical link, an error is logged, otherwise, the logical link of the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,362,0)="sending facility is used as the return path for responses regardless of"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,363,0)="how the subscriber protocol logical link field was defined."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,364,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,365,0)="Subscriber Protocol Key Fields:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,366,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,367,0)="770.11    RESPONSE MESSAGE TYPE (P771.2'), [770;11]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,368,0)="770.2     RECEIVING APPLICATION (P771), [770;2]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,369,0)="770.4     EVENT TYPE (P779.001'), [770;4]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,370,0)="770.6     PROCESSING ID (S), [770;6]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,371,0)="770.7     LOGICAL LINK (P870'), [770;7]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,372,0)="771       PROCESSING ROUTINE (K), [771;E1,245]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,373,0)="773.1     SENDING FACILITY REQUIRED? (S), [773;1]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,374,0)="773.2     RECEIVING FACILITY REQUIRED? (S), [773;2]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,375,0)="773.3     SECURITY REQUIRED? (S), [773;3]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,376,0)="773.4     DATE/TIME OF MESSAGE REQUIRED? (S), [773;4]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,377,0)="774       ROUTING LOGIC (K), [774;E1,245]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,378,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,379,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,380,0)="                   Application Parameter File"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,381,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,382,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,383,0)="This file contains the basic settings needed to describe an application"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,384,0)="that either sends or receives a message. "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,385,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,386,0)="**Note that the fields pertaining to VISTA HL7 version 1.5 have been"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,387,0)="  marked for removal from the system."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,388,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,389,0)="The default field separator is the up-caret (""^"") and the default encoding"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,390,0)="characters are ""~|\&."" Developers are not required to use these defaults."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,391,0)="The preferred characters for the sake of message readability is the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,392,0)="vertical bar (""|"") as a field separator and ""~^\&"" as the encoding"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,393,0)="characters. Note that the ""^""-character cannot be placed first in the list"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,394,0)="due to VA Fileman limitations."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,395,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,396,0)=".01       NAME (RFX), [0;1]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,397,0)="2         ACTIVE/INACTIVE (S), [0;2]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,398,0)="3         FACILITY NAME (F), [0;3]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,399,0)="4         MAIL GROUP (P3.8'), [0;4]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,400,0)="5         *HL7 SEGMENT (Multiple-771.05), [SEG;0]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,401,0)="          .01  HL7 SEGMENT (MRP771.3'), [0;1]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,402,0)="          2    FIELDS USED IN THIS SEGMENT (RF), [F;1]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,403,0)="6         *HL7 MESSAGE (Multiple-771.06), [MSG;0]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,404,0)="          .01  HL7 MESSAGE (MRP771.2'), [0;1]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,405,0)="          1    PROCESSING ROUTINE (RF), [R;E1,17]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,406,0)="7         COUNTRY CODE (P779.004'), [0;7]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,407,0)="100       HL7 FIELD SEPARATOR (F), [FS;E1,2]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,408,0)="101       HL7 ENCODING CHARACTERS (F), [EC;E1,4]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,409,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,410,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,411,0)="                        Logical Links"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,412,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,413,0)="The Logical Link File (870) and the HL LOWER LEVEL PROTOCOL PARAMETERS"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,414,0)="file (869.2) have been merged into 870. The pointer from 870 to 869.2 has"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,415,0)="been changed to point to file 869.1 (HL LOWER LEVEL PROTOCOL TYPE). Users"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,416,0)="may now define parameters for multiple LLP's under the same Logical Link"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,417,0)="definition and simply change the ""type"" pointer as needed. A number of"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,418,0)="fields in 869.2 have been removed since the standard does not allow the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,419,0)="settings to be altered. Since there has always been a 1:1 correspondence"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,420,0)="of Logical Links to LLP Parameters, users should be able to safely remove"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,421,0)="file 869.2 after installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,422,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,423,0)="     Properly Defined VISTA-to-VISTA Interface (Before HL*1.6*57)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,424,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,425,0)="The following is an example of a PROPERLY defined point-to-point interface"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,426,0)="between two VISTA Systems. In this example, the Sending System initiates"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,427,0)="an ADT message to the Receiving System and expects an Acknowledgement."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,428,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,429,0)="4.1    Event Point Protocol Stored on Sending System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,430,0)="(Interface Workbench View):"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,431,0)="(1) JC ADT SERVER"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,432,0)="    Text: Test tcp links"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,433,0)=" Package:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,434,0)="   Message Type Rcvd: ADT                      Accept Acknowledgement: AL"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,435,0)="     Event Type Rcvd: A01                 Application Acknowledgement: NE"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,436,0)="            Priority: <DEFAULT>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,437,0)="       Processing ID: DEBUG"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,438,0)="          Version ID: 2.3"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,439,0)="        Entry Action: <NONE>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,440,0)="         Exit Action: <NONE>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,441,0)=" Process ACK Routine: Q"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,442,0)=" Subscribers: JC ADT RECV          "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,443,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,444,0)="(VA FileMan View):"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,445,0)="  NAME: JC ADT SERVER                    ITEM TEXT: Test tcp links"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,446,0)="  TYPE: event driver                    CREATOR: CLEMENS,JOHN"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,447,0)="  ITEM: JC ADT RECV"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,448,0)="  TIMESTAMP: 56930,57258             "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,449,0)="  SERVER APPLICATION: JC ADT SERVER"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,450,0)="  770.3 MESSAGE TYPE RECEIVED: ADT            "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,451,0)="  770.4 EVENT TYPE: A01"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,452,0)="  PROCESSING ID: DEBUG                 "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,453,0)="  ACCEPT ACK CODE: AL"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,454,0)="  APPLICATION ACK TYPE: NE             "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,455,0)="  VERSION ID: 2.3"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,456,0)="  GENERATE/PROCESS ACK ROUTINE: Q"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,457,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,458,0)="           Subscriber Protocol Stored on Sending System"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,459,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,460,0)="(Interface Workbench View):"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,461,0)="(1) JC ADT RECV"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,462,0)="    Text: TEST SUBSCRIBER USING TCP LINK"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,463,0)=" Package:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,464,0)="    Message Type Rcvd: ACK                 Sending Facility Required: NO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,465,0)="    Message Type Sent: ADT               Receiving Facility Required: NO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,466,0)=" Event Type Rcvd/Sent: A01             Date/Time of Message Required: YES"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,467,0)="             Priority: IMMEDIATE                   Security Required:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,468,0)="        Processing ID: DEBUG                            Logical Link:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,469,0)="           Version ID: 2.3"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,470,0)="        Routing Logic: <NONE>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,471,0)="         Entry Action: <NONE>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,472,0)="          Exit Action: <NONE>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,473,0)="      Process Routine: D REC^JCHL7TST "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,474,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,475,0)="(VA Fileman View): "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,476,0)="NAME: JC ADT RECV"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,477,0)="  ITEM TEXT: TEST SUBSCRIBER USING TCP LINK"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,478,0)="  DISABLE: YES                          "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,479,0)="  TYPE: subscriber"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,480,0)="  CREATOR: CLEMENS,JOHN                 "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,481,0)="  TIMESTAMP: 56930,56581"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,482,0)="  CLIENT (SUBSCRIBER): JC TEST RECV     "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,483,0)="  770.3 MESSAGE TYPE RECEIVED: ACK"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,484,0)="  770.4 EVENT TYPE: A01                       "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,485,0)="  PRIORITY: IMMEDIATE"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,486,0)="  PROCESSING ID: DEBUG                  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,487,0)="  VERSION ID: 2.3"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,488,0)="  770.11 MESSAGE TYPE GENERATED: ADT           "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,489,0)="  GENERATE/PROCESS ROUTINE: D REC^JCHL7TST"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,490,0)="  SENDING FACILITY REQUIRED?: NO        RECEIVING FACILITY REQUIRED?: NO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,491,0)="  DATE/TIME OF MESSAGE REQUIRED?: YES       "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,492,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,493,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,494,0)="        Event Point Protocol Stored on the Receiving System"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,495,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,496,0)="On the receiving system, the event point protocol is set up the same as on"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,497,0)="the sending system, however, the subscriber protocol must be set up"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,498,0)="differently (see below)."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,499,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,500,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,501,0)="          Subscriber Protocol Stored on the Receiving System"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,502,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,503,0)="(VA Fileman View):"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,504,0)="NAME: JC ADT RECV"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,505,0)="  ITEM TEXT: TEST SUBSCRIBER USING TCP LINK"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,506,0)="  DISABLE: YES                          "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,507,0)="  TYPE: subscriber"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,508,0)="  CREATOR: CLEMENS,JOHN                 "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,509,0)="  TIMESTAMP: 56930,56581"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,510,0)="  CLIENT (SUBSCRIBER): JC ADT RECV     "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,511,0)="  770.3 MESSAGE TYPE RECEIVED: ADT"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,512,0)="  770.4 EVENT TYPE: A01                       "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,513,0)="  PRIORITY: IMMEDIATE"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,514,0)="  PROCESSING ID: DEBUG                  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,515,0)="  VERSION ID: 2.3"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,516,0)="  770.11 MESSAGE TYPE GENERATED: ACK           "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,517,0)="  GENERATE/PROCESS ROUTINE: D REC^JCHL7TST"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,518,0)="  SENDING FACILITY REQUIRED?: NO        RECEIVING FACILITY REQUIRED?: NO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,519,0)="  DATE/TIME OF MESSAGE REQUIRED?: YES       "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,520,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,521,0)="Notice that the data for 770.3 and 770.11 must be reversed in order for"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,522,0)="HL7 to generate an ACK with the proper message type (ACK~A01) defined in"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,523,0)="the header."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,524,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,525,0)="If the receiving system is capable of initiating the same transaction to"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,526,0)="the sending system in this example, a new set of protocols and unique"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,527,0)="sending and receiving application definitions must be supplied."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,528,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,529,0)="      Properly Defined VISTA-to-VISTA Interface (After HL*1.6*57)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,530,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,531,0)="After Patch 57 is installed, you will see the following differences:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,532,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,533,0)="On the sending system, field 770.3 and 770.4 of the EVENT POINT PROTOCOL"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,534,0)="are used to generate the header of the initial message. "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,535,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,536,0)="Important consequence: The same setup can be exported to the receiving"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,537,0)="system because field 770.11 is correctly defined as ""ACK"" before and after"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,538,0)="the installation of patch 57 and field 770.11 is used to generate the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,539,0)="response. If an ack is not required (as is currently the case for many"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,540,0)="CIRN definitions) for a given interface the subscriber configuration is of"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,541,0)="no consequence. "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,542,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,543,0)="Therefore:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,544,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,545,0)="1.     No conversion of properly defined interfaces (see above) is"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,546,0)="necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,547,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,548,0)="2.     If the receiving system needs to initiate the same transaction as"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,549,0)="well as receive it, the same two protocols can be used for both cases."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,550,0)="Note that some interface setups may be improperly defined, but work anyway"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,551,0)="because of unusual circumstances. All interfaces currently in production"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,552,0)="should be reviewed based on this document."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,553,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,554,0)="To assist with this, an ""interface debugger"" routine (^HLERCHK) has been"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,555,0)="supplied with patch 57 to examine one or all interfaces."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,556,0)="Use this as a general tool for interface troubleshooting after"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,557,0)="installing the patch. It examines each HL7 Event Driver Protocol,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,558,0)="Subscriber Protocols, and Application Definitions and generates a report"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,559,0)="of potential problems. It can be used with pre-Patch 57 setups as a guide"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,560,0)="for converting an interface to post-57 format. However, if it reports"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,561,0)="issues with a pre-57 setup, this should not be interpreted as an"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,562,0)="indication that the interface is not set up correctly."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,563,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,564,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,565,0)="      Event Point Protocol (for both Sending and Receiving System)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,566,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,567,0)="NAME: JC ADT SERVER                     TYPE: event driver"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,568,0)="  CREATOR: CLEMENS,JOHN"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,569,0)=" DESCRIPTION:   Testing message transmissions "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,570,0)="        SENDING APPLICATION: JC NXT SEND"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,571,0)="  770.3 TRANSACTION MESSAGE TYPE: ADT         "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,572,0)="  770.4 EVENT TYPE: A01"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,573,0)="        PROCESSING ID: PRODUCTION             "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,574,0)="        ACCEPT ACK CODE: AL"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,575,0)="        VERSION ID: 2.2                       "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,576,0)="        PROCESSING ROUTINE: Q"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,577,0)="        RESPONSE PROCESSING ROUTINE: Q        "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,578,0)="        SENDING FACILITY REQUIRED?: YES"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,579,0)="        RECEIVING FACILITY REQUIRED?: NO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,580,0)="        SUBSCRIBERS: JC ADT RECV"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,581,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,582,0)="    Subscriber Protocol (for both Sending and Receiving System)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,583,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,584,0)="NAME: JC ADT RECV                       TYPE: subscriber"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,585,0)="  CREATOR: CLEMENS,JOHN                 "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,586,0)="        RECEIVING APPLICATION: JC KRN REC"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,587,0)="  770.3 TRANSACTION MESSAGE TYPE: ADT         "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,588,0)="  770.4 EVENT TYPE: A01"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,589,0)="        PROCESSING ID: PRODUCTION"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,590,0)="        VERSION ID: 2.2                       "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,591,0)="  770.11 RESPONSE MESSAGE TYPE: ACK"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,592,0)="        PROCESSING ROUTINE: Q                 "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,593,0)="        SENDING FACILITY REQUIRED?: NO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",35,1,594,0)="        RECEIVING FACILITY REQUIRED?: NO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,0)="60 SEQ #50^3000405^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,0)="^^84^84^3000405"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,1,0)="This patch "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,2,0)="1. Resolves an issue with how to address responses to messages"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,3,0)="arriving over a Mailman-type Logical Link. "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,5,0)="If ROUTING LOGIC is defined, the response will be dynamically addressed"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,6,0)="using the SOURCE DOMAIN provided by querying Mailman. In some cases this"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,7,0)="could result in a response being returned over a logical link that is"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,8,0)="different from the one the message arrived on. Specifically, the source"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,9,0)="domain will resolve to one of the VA-namespaced logical links exported"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,10,0)="with HL*1.6*39. If this is the case, it is important to insure that the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,11,0)="links on both the sending and receiving systems are properly configured"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,12,0)="and enabled."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,14,0)="If there is no routing logic defined on the subscriber protocol, Vista HL7"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,15,0)="will assume that the link defined on the subscriber protocol is the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,16,0)="correct return path and Mailman will not be queried."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,18,0)="2. Fixes a corrupted node found on the logical link, LR NCH-L which"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,19,0)="prevented patch HL*1.6*57 from converting this link."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,22,0)=" The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,23,0)="each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,24,0)="  ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;<patchlist>;Oct 13, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,26,0)=" CHECK^XTSUMBLD results: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,27,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,28,0)=" Routine Name   Before Patch    After Patch     Patch List "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,29,0)=" ============   ============    ===========     ========== "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,30,0)=" HLTP01         5262489         5578885         **2,25,34,47,60**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,31,0)=" HLPAT60        **NEW**         805414"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,34,0)="Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,35,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,36,0)="  1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,38,0)="  2.  DSM SITES: Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed in"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,40,0)="      the Routine Summary section are mapped, they should be removed from "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,41,0)="      the mapped set at this time.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,43,0)="  3.  Shutdown all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers, and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,44,0)="      the Link Manager. Use the options:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,46,0)="       Shut Down All Logical Links"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,47,0)="       Stop all incoming filers"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,48,0)="       Stop all outgoing filers"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,49,0)="       TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,51,0)="  4.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,52,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,54,0)="  5.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,55,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,56,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,57,0)="      options: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,59,0)="         2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,60,0)="         3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,61,0)="         4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,62,0)="         5 Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,63,0)="         6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,64,0)="             INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*60"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,65,0)="                           ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,67,0)="        Answer 'YES' to 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees upon Completion"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,68,0)="        of Install?'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,70,0)="        Answer 'NO' to 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install?'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,71,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,72,0)="        Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,73,0)="        and Protocols?'.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,75,0)="  6.  Startup all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers. Use the "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,76,0)="      'Restart/Start All Links and Filers' option.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,78,0)="      For DSM sites ONLY, if you previously disabled an HL7 UCX Service"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,79,0)="      for this installation, you may now enable it."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,81,0)="  7.  DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,83,0)="  8.  Start Link Manager using the option: ""TCP/IP"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",36,1,84,0)="        Link Manager Start/Stop."""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,0)="58 SEQ #51^3000417^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,0)="^^99^99^3000417"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,2,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,3,0)="1. ISB-1299-31632, AUS-1299-N1595: Errors when using HL7 Ping option. After"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,4,0)="   error, ping doesn't work for any site."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,5,0)="2. DET-1199-41731:  Undefined error when transmitting HL7 messages."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,6,0)="3. TAM-1199-32092:  The option HL TASK RESTART, start wrong number of"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,7,0)="   outbound filers."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,8,0)="4. Support for CPRS Remote Patient Data View project."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,9,0)="5. Cleans up application variables between inbound transactions."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,11,0)="Routine Modifications:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,12,0)="======================"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,13,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,14,0)="these routines now look like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,15,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,16,0)=" ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;<patchlist>;Oct 13, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,18,0)="CHECK^XTSUMBLD results: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,19,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,20,0)=" Routine Name   Before Patch    After Patch     Patch List "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,21,0)=" ============   ============    ===========     =========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,22,0)=" HLCS2          10072062        10270936        14,40,43,49,57,58"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,23,0)=" HLCSTCP         5152314         5155167        19,43,49,57,58"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,24,0)=" HLCSUTL         5134775         6479348        2,19,58"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,25,0)=" HLMA            5502295         6284735        19,43,58"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,26,0)=" HLMA2           7268935         7530649        19,43,57,58"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,27,0)=" HLSUB           5277110         5501510        14,57,58"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,28,0)=" HLTP3          14050232        14451393        19,43,57,58  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,29,0)=" HLTP31          1680845         1651062        57,58"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,31,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,32,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,33,0)="  1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,35,0)="  2.  DSM SITES: Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed in"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,36,0)="      the Routine Summary section are mapped, they should be removed from"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,37,0)="      the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,39,0)="  3.  Use the option 'Stop All Messaging Background Processes' to disable"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,40,0)="      all links and filers."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,42,0)="      For DSM sites ONLY, if you have an HL7 UCX Service associated"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,43,0)="      with the account(uci/directory) where you are installing this patch,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,44,0)="      please disable this service."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,46,0)="  4.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,47,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,49,0)="  5.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,50,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,51,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,52,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,54,0)="         2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,55,0)="         3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,56,0)="         4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,57,0)="         5 Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,58,0)="         6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,59,0)="             INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*58"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,60,0)="                           ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,61,0)="         Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,62,0)="         and Protocols?'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,64,0)="  6.  Startup all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers. Use the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,65,0)="      'Restart All Links and Filers' option."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,67,0)="  7.  DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,69,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,70,0)="New Public Functions (only for TCP messages)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,72,0)="   $$MSGLINE(msgid)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,73,0)="     return the number of lines in a message header and text"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,74,0)="      input: msgid = message id"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,75,0)="     output:  return number of lines"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,77,0)="   $$MSG^HLCSUTL(msgid, ref)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,78,0)="     return the message header and text in the given reference"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,79,0)="      input: msgid = message id"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,80,0)="               ref = closed local or global reference to place message"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,81,0)="     output:  return 1 for success and 0 if message doesn't exist"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,82,0)="     The message is returned with blank lines between each line."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,83,0)="     example:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,85,0)="ref(1)=MSH^~|\&^VOICERAD^^RADIOLOGY^^20000110145151-0800^^ORU~R01^1231^T^2.2"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,86,0)="ref(2)="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,87,0)="ref(3)=PID^^^100~10~M11^^JONES~JOHN~J^^19421112^M^^^^^^^^^^123456789"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,88,0)="ref(4)="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,89,0)="ref(5)=OBR^^^^7089898.8543-1~043091-66~L^^^199104301200^""^""^^^^^""^^3232~HARR"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,90,0)="IS~JACK^^^^MEDICINE^^199104301010"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,91,0)="ref(6)="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,92,0)="ref(7)=OBX^^TX^I~IMPRESSION~L^^HEART NORMAL SIZE"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,93,0)="ref(8)="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,94,0)="ref(9)=OBX^^ST^D~DIAGNOSTIC CODE~L^^NORMAL"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,95,0)="ref(10)="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,96,0)="ref(11)=OBX^^TX^R~REPORT~L^^Heart appears to be of normal size."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,97,0)="ref(12)="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,98,0)="ref(13)=OBX^^TX^R~REPORT~L^^No infiltrate or abnormal mass noted."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",37,1,99,0)="ref(14)="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,0)="63 SEQ #52^3000516^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,0)="^^119^119^3000516"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,1,0)="This patch introduces DNS support for Vista HL7. In order to conduct HL7"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,2,0)="message exchange between sites using TCP, the TCP/IP address of each site"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,3,0)="running an HL7 service must be known by all other sites. If the address is"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,4,0)="changed, such as from ""152.x.x.x"" to ""10.x.x.x,"" or when the HL7 service"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,5,0)="is moved to a different computer, or when multiple computers are able to"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,6,0)="support HL7 services at a single domain, other sites can use DNS to"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,7,0)="""discover"" this information without interruption in message exchange."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,8,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,9,0)="When a connection attempt over a TCP Logical Link fails, a call will be"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,10,0)="made to the locally specified Domain Name Server (found in the Kernel Site"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,11,0)="Parameters) to retrieve the current IP address. This feature was"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,12,0)="introduced in Kernel patch XU*8*142. One or more IP addresses may be"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,13,0)="registered on the DNS systems. The DNS was initially seeded with IP"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,14,0)="information supplied by HL*1.6*39 and any subsequent changes made to date"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,15,0)="to the VA* and MPI logical links. These IP addresses are associated"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,16,0)="specifically with the service ""HL7"" on the DNS and the port 5000. The port"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,17,0)="number is currently fixed for HL7 and should not be changed. If only one"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,18,0)="IP address is returned, it will be stored in the site's local Logical Link"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,19,0)="file and used for subsequent connections. If more than one IP is returned,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,20,0)="each address will be tried in sequence until a successful connection is"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,21,0)="made. The successful IP address will then be stored and used until the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,22,0)="next connection attempt that fails."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,23,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,24,0)="Queries to the DNS will work only if the Logical Link (file 870) points to"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,25,0)="the correct Domain (file 4.2). Review the link definitions paying"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,26,0)="particular attention to those links in your VISN and verify that the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,27,0)="Domain field is defined correctly."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,28,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,29,0)="The Logical Link that represents your site should be configured as a"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,30,0)="""multithreaded listener"" to receive INBOUND connection requests. The IP"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,31,0)="address and port for this listener is known by all other sites and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,32,0)="referenced by them to establish a connection. Changing the IP address will"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,33,0)="prevent sites from establishing a connection. Therefore, if you wish to"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,34,0)="establish a new IP address, your VA DNS must be updated in advance of the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,35,0)="change. It must contain an entry in the format, HL7.yoursite.domain.ext,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,36,0)="and your new TCP/IP address. For example, DNS will contain an entry for"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,37,0)="Bay Pines VA looking like, ""HL7.BAY-PINES.DOMAIN.EXT."" This entry will"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,38,0)="return a TCP/IP address of 152.130.80.5. "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,40,0)="Please note that the HL7 development team is not involved with maintenance"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,41,0)="of the VA's DNS systems. Questions should be refered to your local or"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,42,0)="VISN-level DNS administrator, or via MS Exchange to the group, ""VHA CIO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,43,0)="DNS ADMIN."""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,44,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,45,0)="Following the installation of this patch you should enable your TCP/IP"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,46,0)="listener for inbound HL7 connections. Detailed instructions for this may"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,47,0)="be found in the HL7 Document, ""Vista HL7 Site Manager and Developer"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,48,0)="Manual"" released as HL*1.6*56. Here, you will find information for both"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,49,0)="Cache and for configuring UCX/TCP services under the VMS operating system."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,50,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,51,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,52,0)="each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,53,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,54,0)="   ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;<patchlist>;Oct 13, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,55,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,56,0)="  CHECK^XTSUMBLD results: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,57,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,58,0)="  Routine Name   Before Patch    After Patch     Patch List "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,59,0)="  ============   ============    ===========     ========== "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,60,0)="  HLCSTCP2       10328595        11299763        **19,43,49,57,63**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,61,0)="  HLMA           6284735         7929932         **19,43,58,63**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,62,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,63,0)=" List of preceding patches: 57, 58"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,64,0)=" Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,65,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,66,0)=" Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,67,0)=" =========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,68,0)="   1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,69,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,70,0)="   2.  DSM SITES: Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,71,0)="       in the Routine Summary section are mapped, they should be removed"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,72,0)="       from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,73,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,74,0)="   3.  Shutdown all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers, and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,75,0)="       the Link Manager. Use the options:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,76,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,77,0)="         Filer and Link Management Options -> "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,78,0)="             SA     Stop All Messaging Background Processes"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,79,0)="             LM     TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,80,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,81,0)="   4.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,82,0)="       option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,83,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,84,0)="   5.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,85,0)="       system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,86,0)="       On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,87,0)="       options: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,88,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,89,0)="          2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,90,0)="          3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,91,0)="          4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,92,0)="          5 Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,93,0)="          6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,94,0)="              INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*63"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,95,0)="                            ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,96,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,97,0)="         Answer 'NO' to 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees upon Completion"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,98,0)="         of Install?'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,99,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,100,0)="         Answer 'NO' to 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install?'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,101,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,102,0)="         Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,103,0)="         and Protocols?'.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,104,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,105,0)="   6.  Startup all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers. Use the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,107,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,108,0)="         Filer and Link Management Options ->"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,109,0)="             RA     Restart/Start All Links and Filers"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,110,0)="         (Note that links that do not have ""autostart"" enabled will need"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,111,0)="          to be restarted manually)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,112,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,113,0)="       For DSM sites ONLY, if you previously disabled an HL7 UCX Service"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,114,0)="       for this installation, you may now enable it."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,115,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,116,0)="   7.  DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,117,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,118,0)="   8.  Start Link Manager using the option: ""TCP/IP"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",38,1,119,0)="         Link Manager Start/Stop."""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,0)="61 SEQ #53^3000525^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,0)="^^60^60^3000525"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,1,0)="This patch solves the following problems:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,3,0)=" 1. NOIS MWV-1297-20006: Requeuer screen didn't show the correct"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,4,0)="    information in columns ""Queue Size"" and ""Pending."""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,5,0)=" 2. Fixes the DICN-Error nodes problems for ""IN"" queue of HL LOGICAL LINK"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,6,0)="    file(#870)."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,9,0)="Test sites :"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,11,0)=" 1. Fayetteville"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,12,0)=" 2. Martinsburg"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,15,0)="Routine Summary:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,16,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,17,0)="The following is a list of the routines included in this patch.  The"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,18,0)="second line of each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,20,0)="     <tab>;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;**[patch list]**;Oct 13, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,23,0)="Checksums:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,24,0)="=========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,26,0)="  Routine Name    Checksum Before    Checksum After       Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,27,0)="  ------------    ---------------    --------------    ------------------"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,28,0)="    HLCSQUE           4308358           4338251              14,61"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,29,0)="    HLCSREQ           1749378           1790153               61"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,32,0)="    From CHECK^XTSUMBLD "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,35,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,36,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,37,0)="  1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,38,0)="  2.  Stop all the Logical links, incoming and outgoing filers."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,39,0)="  3.  DSM SITES: Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed in"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,40,0)="      the Routine Summary section are mapped, they should be removed from"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,41,0)="      the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,42,0)="  4.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,43,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,44,0)="  5.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,45,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,46,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,47,0)="      options:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,49,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,50,0)="         Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,51,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,52,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,53,0)="         Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,54,0)="         INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*61"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,55,0)="                       ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,56,0)="         Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,57,0)="         and Protocols?'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,58,0)="  6.  DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,59,0)="  7.  Restart all the Logical links, incoming and outgoing filers, which"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",39,1,60,0)="      have been stopped in step #2."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,0)="59 SEQ #54^3000612^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,0)="^^125^125^3000612"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,1,0)="1. Introduces HL7 version 2.3.1 MESSAGE STRUCTURE components:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,2,0)="        -Introduces a new file (#779.005) to hold the new HL7 MESSAGE"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,3,0)="         STRUCTURE CODES."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,4,0)="        -Adds a new field, MESSAGE STRUCTURE (#770.5), to the Protocol"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,5,0)="         file. When defined, the MESSAGE STRUCTURE will be added to the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,6,0)="         version 2.3.1 message header."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,8,0)="2. The message type of outbound messages was incorrectly stored in file"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,9,0)="   773. This has been fixed."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,11,0)="3. In file 771, HL APPLICATION PARAMETER, the input transforms for FIELD"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,12,0)="   SEPARATOR and ENCODING CHARACTERS have been modified to prevent reuse"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,13,0)="   of the field separator in the encoding characters. Each of the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,14,0)="   characters defined must be unique."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,16,0)="4. HL*1.6*57 introduced a new menu structure. However, the old, obsolete"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,17,0)="   menus were not removed. This patch will remove them."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,19,0)="5. Fixes a problem with STUB records left behind in file 870 (Logical"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,20,0)="   Link) resulting in freezing of links and the System Link Monitor as"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,21,0)="   well as causing queues to grow until disk space is used up."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,23,0)="NOTE: Some sites may have a considerable number of messages needing to be"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,24,0)="purged from file 870. Please consider disabling journalling of ^HLCS() for"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,25,0)="about a week after installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,27,0)="6.  Changes the PROCESSING ID field of file 101 to be no longer required."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,28,0)="Note that HL7 message headers are populated with information for"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,29,0)="'TRAINING' or 'PRODUCTION' taken from the HL7 site parameters. Use the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,30,0)="option, SITE PARAMETER EDIT, to verify that your production account is"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,31,0)="identified as such and your test/training account is identified as"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,32,0)="'TRAINING.' The event driver protocol PROCESSING ID field is now used only"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,33,0)="for DEBUG mode. Debug mode will override your site parameter setting. Make"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,34,0)="sure the protocol is set to 'debug' on both the sending and receiving"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,35,0)="system."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,37,0)="7. Corrects a problem with creating new subscriptions when a user edits"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,38,0)="the zero node of file 774."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,40,0)="This patch resolves the following NOIS calls:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,42,0)="        AMA-0300-70683"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,43,0)="        ISD-0300-71919"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,44,0)="        HOU-0400-71933"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,46,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,47,0)="each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,48,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,49,0)="   ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;<patchlist>;Oct 13, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,50,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,51,0)="  CHECK^XTSUMBLD results: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,52,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,53,0)="  Routine Name  Before Patch    After Patch     Patch List "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,54,0)="  ============  ============    ===========     ========== "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,55,0)="  HLCSHDR       7364841         7637619         **37,19,57,59**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,56,0)="  HLCSHDR1      7750238         8586633         **19,57,59**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,57,0)="  HLCSQUE       4338251         4440270         **14,61,59**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,58,0)="  HLCSQUE1      1150239         1371156         **14,59**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,59,0)="  HLFNC2        5397412         5365297         **2,26,57,59**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,60,0)="  HLTP4         7805100         7964901         **19,57,59**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,61,0)="  HLTPCK1A      14402537        14751742        **2,25,34,57,59**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,62,0)="  HLTPCK2A      15262342        15611547        **19,57,59**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,63,0)="  HLUTIL2       5387464         5486507         **19,43,57,59**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,64,0)="  HLTPCK1       4288888         4452787         **8,36,59**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,65,0)="  HLTPCK2       3804314         3962788         **19,59**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,66,0)="  HLTP3         14451393        14649677        **19,43,57,58,59**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,67,0)="  HLSUB         5501510         5552075         **14,57,58,59**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,69,0)=" List of preceding patches: 14, 36, 57, 58, 61"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,70,0)=" Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,71,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,72,0)=" Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,73,0)=" =========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,74,0)="   1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,75,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,76,0)="   2.  DSM SITES: Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,77,0)="       in the Routine Summary section are mapped, they should be removed"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,78,0)="       from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,79,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,80,0)="   3.  Shutdown all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers, and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,81,0)="       the Link Manager. Use the options:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,82,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,83,0)="         Filer and Link Management Options -> "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,84,0)="             SA     Stop All Messaging Background Processes"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,85,0)="             LM     TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,86,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,87,0)="   4.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,88,0)="       option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,89,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,90,0)="   5.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,91,0)="       system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,92,0)="       On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,93,0)="       options: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,94,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,95,0)="          2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,96,0)="          3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,97,0)="          4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,98,0)="          5 Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,99,0)="          6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,100,0)="              INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*59"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,101,0)="                            ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,102,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,103,0)="         Answer 'NO' to 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees upon Completion"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,104,0)="         of Install?'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,105,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,106,0)="         Answer 'NO' to 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install?'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,107,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,108,0)="         Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,109,0)="         and Protocols?'.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,110,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,111,0)="   6.  Startup all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers. Use the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,113,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,114,0)="         Filer and Link Management Options ->"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,115,0)="             RA     Restart/Start All Links and Filers"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,116,0)="         (Note that links that do not have ""autostart"" enabled will need"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,117,0)="          to be restarted manually)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,118,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,119,0)="       For DSM sites ONLY, if you previously disabled an HL7 UCX Service"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,120,0)="       for this installation, you may now enable it."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,121,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,122,0)="   7.  DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,123,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,124,0)="   8.  Start Link Manager using the option: ""TCP/IP"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",40,1,125,0)="         Link Manager Start/Stop."""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,0)="64 SEQ #55^3000612^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,0)="^^134^134^3000612"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,2,0)=" 1. Added new status, AWAITING RESPONSE, to the HL7 MESSAGE STATUS file."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,3,0)=" 2. New parameter, HL(""ACKTIME""), will reset the Acknowledgement Timeout,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,4,0)="    for the one message. This parameter can be passed in GENERATE^HLMA or"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,5,0)="    DIRECT^HLMA APIs."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,6,0)=" 3. Retransmission alerts are no longer generated."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,7,0)=" 4. DEVNOTOPN errors will no longer be recorded."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,8,0)=" 5. New APIs:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,9,0)="        $$MSGSTAT^HLUTIL = returns status of a message"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,10,0)="        $$MSGACT^HLUTIL  = outgoing message action, cancel or requeue"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,11,0)="        $$CHKLL^HLUTIL   = check setup of Logical Link"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,12,0)="        $$FLD^HLCSUTL    = returns a field from a message segment"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,13,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,14,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,15,0)="Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,16,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,17,0)="  1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,19,0)="  2.  DSM SITES: Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed in"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,21,0)="      the Routine Summary section are mapped, they should be removed from "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,22,0)="      the mapped set at this time.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,24,0)="  3.  Shutdown all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers, and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,25,0)="      the Link Manager. Use the options:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,27,0)="        Filer and Link Management Options -> "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,28,0)="            SA     Stop All Messaging Background Processes"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,29,0)="            LM     TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,30,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,31,0)="      For DSM sites ONLY, disabled all HL7 UCX Services "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,32,0)="      for this installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,34,0)="  4.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,35,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,37,0)="  5.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,38,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,39,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,40,0)="      options: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,42,0)="         2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,43,0)="         3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,44,0)="         4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,45,0)="         5 Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,46,0)="         6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,47,0)="             INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*64"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,48,0)="                           ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,49,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,50,0)="        Answer 'NO' to 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install?'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,51,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,52,0)="        Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,53,0)="        and Protocols?'.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,55,0)="  6.  Startup all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers. Use the "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,57,0)="        Filer and Link Management Options ->"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,58,0)="            RA     Restart/Start All Links and Filers"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,59,0)="        (Note that links that do not have ""autostart"" enabled will need to"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,60,0)="        be restarted manually)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,61,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,62,0)="      For DSM sites ONLY, if you previously disabled an HL7 UCX Service"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,63,0)="      for this installation, you may now enable it."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,65,0)="  7.  DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,67,0)="  8.  Start Link Manager using the option: ""TCP/IP"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,68,0)="        Link Manager Start/Stop."""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,69,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,70,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,71,0)="Routine Information:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,72,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,73,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,74,0)="of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,75,0)=" ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;<patchlist>;JUL 17,1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,76,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,77,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,78,0)="Routine         Old         New            2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,79,0)="========     ========     ========     =====================     "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,80,0)="HLCSAC        2497076      2564816     **43,64**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,81,0)="HLCSTCP       5155167      5175308     **19,43,49,57,58,64**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,82,0)="HLCSTCP1      4965932      5081718     **19,43,57,64**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,83,0)="HLCSTCP2     11299763     11197019     **19,43,49,57,63,64**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,84,0)="HLCSUTL       6479348      6969973     **2,19,58,64**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,85,0)="HLMA2         7530649      7925412     **19,43,57,58,64**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,86,0)="HLTF0         3173064      3232637     **12,19,64**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,87,0)="HLUTIL        2643574      3175738     **36,19,57,64**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,88,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,89,0)="List of preceding patches: 57, 58, 63"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,90,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,91,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,92,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,93,0)="Documentation:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,94,0)="=============="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,95,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,96,0)="$$MSGSTAT^HLUTIL(X)      ;message status"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,97,0)="   input value:  X = message id"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,98,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,99,0)="  return value: status^status updated^error msg.^error type pointer^queue"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,100,0)="                position or # of retries^# open failed^ack timeout"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,101,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,102,0)="        status:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,103,0)="                 0 = message doesn't exist"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,104,0)="                 1 = pending transmission"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,105,0)="               1.5 = being tranmitted"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,106,0)="               1.7 = awaiting response, # of retries"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,107,0)="                 2 = awaiting application ack"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,108,0)="                 3 = successfully completed"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,109,0)="                 4 = error"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,110,0)="                 8 = being generated"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,111,0)="                 9 = awaiting processing"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,112,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,113,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,114,0)="$$MSGACT^HLUTIL(X,HLIENACT)      ;outgoing message action"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,115,0)="   input value:       X = message id"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,116,0)="               HLIENACT = 1-cancel; 2-requeue"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,117,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,118,0)="  return value:       1 = action sucessful"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,119,0)="                      0 = action failed"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,120,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,121,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,122,0)="$$CHKLL^HLUTIL(X)        ;check setup of Logical Link"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,123,0)="   input value:   X = institution number or name"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,124,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,125,0)="  return value:   1 = setup OK"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,126,0)="                  0 = LL setup incorrect"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,127,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,128,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,129,0)="$$FLD^HLCSUTL(NODE,FLD)   ;This function will return the value for the field"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,130,0)="   input value:   NODE = HLNODE from the HLNEXT call, passed by reference"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,131,0)="                   FLD = number, field position in segment"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,132,0)="          note:    HL(""FS"") must be defined"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,133,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",41,1,134,0)="  return value:  value for the field in this segment"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,0)="65 SEQ #56^3000711^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,0)="^^85^85^3000711"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,2,0)=" 1. Corrects problem creating an acknowledgement message MSH for a serial"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,3,0)="    connection."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,4,0)=" 2. Enhancements to the System Link Monitor.  Display is now alphabetical"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,5,0)="    and views can also be defined. Use the 'Site Parameter Edit' option"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,6,0)="    to create Link Monitor VIEWS."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,7,0)=" 3. New computed field in file 773, MESSAGE SIZE. This field counts the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,8,0)="    number of characters in a message.  It can be used in FileMan reports."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,9,0)=" 4. Update the INITIAL MESSAGE field in file 773 for a response to a Direct"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,10,0)="    Connect message. This is for the Remote Data View project."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,11,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,12,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,13,0)="Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,14,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,15,0)="  1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,17,0)="  2.  DSM SITES: Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed in"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,19,0)="      the Routine Summary section are mapped, they should be removed from "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,20,0)="      the mapped set at this time.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,22,0)="  3.  Shutdown all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers, and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,23,0)="      the Link Manager. Use the options:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,25,0)="        Filer and Link Management Options -> "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,26,0)="            SA     Stop All Messaging Background Processes"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,27,0)="            LM     TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,28,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,29,0)="      For DSM sites ONLY, disabled all HL7 UCX Services "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,30,0)="      for this installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,32,0)="  4.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,33,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,35,0)="  5.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,36,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,37,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,38,0)="      options: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,40,0)="         2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,41,0)="         3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,42,0)="         4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,43,0)="         5 Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,44,0)="         6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,45,0)="             INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*65"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,46,0)="                           ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,47,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,48,0)="        Answer 'NO' to 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install?'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,49,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,50,0)="        Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,51,0)="         and Protocols?'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,52,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,53,0)="  6.  Startup all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers. Use the "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,55,0)="        Filer and Link Management Options ->"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,56,0)="            RA     Restart/Start All Links and Filers"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,57,0)="        (Note that links that do not have ""autostart"" enabled will need to"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,58,0)="        be restarted manually)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,59,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,60,0)="      For DSM sites ONLY, if you previously disabled an HL7 UCX Service"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,61,0)="      for this installation, you may now enable it."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,63,0)="  7.  DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,65,0)="  8.  Start Link Manager using the option: ""TCP/IP"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,66,0)="        Link Manager Start/Stop."""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,67,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,68,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,69,0)="Routine Information:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,70,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,71,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,72,0)="of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,73,0)=" ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;<patchlist>;JUL 17,1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,74,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,75,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,76,0)="Routine         Old         New            2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,77,0)="========     ========     ========     =====================     "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,78,0)="HLCSHDR       7637619      7573404     **37,19,57,59,65**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,79,0)="HLCSMON      10703763     11036657     **34,40,48,49,65**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,80,0)="HLCSMON1      5535017      3592657     **15,40,49,65**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,81,0)="HLCSUTL       6969973      7737730     **2,19,58,64,65**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,82,0)="HLMA2         7925412      7999576     **19,43,57,58,64,65**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,83,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,84,0)="List of preceding patches: 49, 59, 64"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",42,1,85,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,0)="66 SEQ #57^3001004^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,0)="^^152^152^3001004"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,2,0)=" *** PLEASE NOTE THE FOLLOWING:  ***"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,4,0)="     This patch requires patch XU*8.0*168 HL7 date fix."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,5,0)="     Also, this patch corrects the interpretation of midnight when"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,6,0)="     converting FileMan to HL7 date/time formats and vice versa."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,7,0)="     In addition, the Vista HL7 Functions $$HLDATE^HLFNC(X,Y) and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,8,0)="     $$FMDATE^HLFNC(X) now call the Kernel functions $$FMTHL7^XLFDT(X)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,9,0)="     and $$HL7TFM^XLFDT(X) respectively.  Furthermore, ZULU offsets"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,10,0)="     are added to HL7 date/time formats whenever time is included."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,12,0)="     Also, please install this patch prior to installing patch RG*1*4."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,13,0)="     This patch is needed by the CPRS Remote Data Views."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,14,0)="     If RG*1*4 is already installed, install this patch as soon"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,15,0)="     as posssible."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,17,0)="     Future patch XM*7.1*51, which will change the domain names for"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,18,0)="     all sites which have requested it, will not be released until all"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,19,0)="     sites have installed HL*1.6*66."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,21,0)="  **********************************"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,23,0)="This patch addresses the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,24,0)=" 1. ISA-0600-10916  Correct problem with HLDATE^HLFNC when midnight is"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,25,0)="    used."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,26,0)=" 2. CHS-0499-43088  Corrects a problem with Mailman Logical Links when"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,27,0)="    mail group has no members. Updated to use new Mailman API's and send a"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,28,0)="    message to the HL7 mail group."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,29,0)=" 3. ISF-0600-61155  Prevents an UNDEFINED when the subscription control"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,30,0)="    number is not passed into GET^HLSUB."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,31,0)=" 4. ISB-0600-32294  Prevents the loss of the 'AC' cross reference"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,32,0)="    on pending messages."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,33,0)=" 5. WIM-0700-20527     PROBLEM ON SYSTEMS LINK MONITOR.  Patch HL*1.6*65"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,34,0)="    introduced some new enhancements to the HL7 System Link Monitor."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,35,0)="    However, this patch also introduced a new bug that prevented users"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,36,0)="    from backing up a screen when in 'Screened' mode.  This patch corrects"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,37,0)="    this problem with the monitor."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,38,0)=" 6. General variable cleanup in routine HLTP3 associated with Dynamic"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,39,0)="    Addressing and Enhanced Headers.  This patch fixes the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,40,0)="    Invalid Message Control ID in MSA Segment that was encountered with"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,41,0)="    patch RG*1*4 CPRS REMOTE DATA VIEWS."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,42,0)=" 7. Related NOISes:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,43,0)="    ELP-0700-72334     Undefined Variable @ SF+14~HLTPCK2A"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,44,0)="    LAS-0700-62279     MESSAGE ERROR FROM NEW ORLEANS"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,45,0)="    BIR-0700-32233     Undefined Variable"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,46,0)="    MUR-0800-30482     <UNDEF(ECODE)>SF+14^HLTPCK2A"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,47,0)="    PRE-0800-60365     $ZE= <UNDEFINED>SF+14^HLTPCK2A"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,48,0)="    This patch fixes the undefined variable at SF+14^HLTPCK2A.  This was"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,49,0)="    first encountered after the staff at New Orleans VAMC changed their"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,50,0)="    domain entry to include the '.MED' in front of the '.DOMAIN.EXT' suffix."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,51,0)="    Afterwards, sites receiving CIRN/HL7 messages from New Orleans would"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,52,0)="    encounter this error.  In addition, this patch changes the way that it"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,53,0)="    performs a FileMan lookup of the Domain Name.  Previously, it was only"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,54,0)="    based only on the .01/Name field.  After this patch is installed, the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,55,0)="    lookup process will work with either the Name or Synonym."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,56,0)=" 8. Related NOISes:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,57,0)="    AUG-0800-32024     LINK HAS NEGATIVE NUMBERS"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,58,0)="    AUG-0800-31661     HL7 INTERFACE NOT WORKING"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,59,0)="    AUS-0800-N0079     Negative Numbers on Monitor"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,60,0)="    ISB-0800-30179     Entries in the 'AC' x-ref but with a status of 3"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,61,0)="    This patch fixes the problem where sites encountered negative"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,62,0)="    numbers in the 'TO SEND' column of the HL7 System Link Monitor."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,63,0)="    These negative numbers were a result of the HL7 code inadvertently"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,64,0)="    changing the status of messages to 'SUCCESSFULLY COMPLETED'"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,65,0)="    in the wrong file.  Although the 'AC' cross-reference existed"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,66,0)="    for these messages, the status of 'SUCCESSFULLY COMPLETED' prevented"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,67,0)="    these message from being delivered."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,68,0)="    In addition, the use of $$REPROC^HLUTIL(IEN, routine) extrinsic"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,69,0)="    function after this patch is installed, will update the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,70,0)="    DATE/TIME PROCESSED field(#100) in the HL7 MESSAGE ADMINISTRATION"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,71,0)="    file (#870)."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,73,0)="Routine Information:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,74,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,75,0)="The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,76,0)="each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,77,0)=" ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;<patchlist>;JUL 17,1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,79,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,80,0)=" Routine         Old         New            2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,81,0)=" ========     ========     ========     =====================     "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,82,0)=" HLCSMM        2836421      2312930     **17,35,57,66**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,83,0)=" HLCSMON      11036657     11192960     **34,40,48,49,65,66**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,84,0)=" HLCSTCP2     11197019     11334736     **19,43,49,57,63,64,66**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,85,0)=" HLFNC         5785780      5669016     **38,42,51,66**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,86,0)=" HLMA          7929932      7962943     **19,43,58,63,66**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,87,0)=" HLSUB         5552075      5558527     **14,57,58,59,66**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,88,0)=" HLTP3        14649677     14792516     **19,43,57,58,59,66**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,89,0)=" HLTP31        1651062      1770560     **57,58,66**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,90,0)=" HLTPCK2A     15611547     16050022     **19,57,59,66**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,91,0)=" HLUTIL        3175738      3187029     **36,19,57,64,66**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,92,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,93,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,94,0)=" List of preceding patches: 51, 58, 59, 63, 64, 65"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,95,0)=" Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,97,0)="External patch dependency:  XU*8.0*168    HL7 date fix."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,99,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,100,0)="Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,101,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,102,0)="  1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,104,0)="  2.  DSM SITES: Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed in"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,105,0)="      the Routine Summary section are mapped, they should be removed from "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,106,0)="      the mapped set at this time.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,108,0)="  3.  Shutdown all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers, and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,109,0)="      the Link Manager. Use the options:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,111,0)="        Filer and Link Management Options -> "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,112,0)="            SA     Stop All Messaging Background Processes"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,113,0)="            LM     TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,115,0)="      For DSM sites ONLY, disabled all HL7 UCX Services "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,116,0)="      for this installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,118,0)="  4.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,119,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,121,0)="  5.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,122,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,123,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,124,0)="      options: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,125,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,126,0)="         2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,127,0)="         3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,128,0)="         4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,129,0)="         5 Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,130,0)="         6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,131,0)="             INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*66"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,132,0)="                           ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,134,0)="        Answer 'NO' to 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install?'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,135,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,136,0)="        Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,137,0)="         and Protocols?'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,138,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,139,0)="  6.  Startup all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers. Use the "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,141,0)="        Filer and Link Management Options ->"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,142,0)="            RA     Restart/Start All Links and Filers"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,143,0)="        (Note that links that do not have ""autostart"" enabled will need to"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,144,0)="        be restarted manually)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,145,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,146,0)="      For DSM sites ONLY, if you previously disabled an HL7 UCX Service"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,147,0)="      for this installation, you may now enable it."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,149,0)="  7.  DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,150,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,151,0)="  8.  Start Link Manager using the option: ""TCP/IP"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",43,1,152,0)="        Link Manager Start/Stop."""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,0)="67 SEQ #58^3010122^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,0)="^^137^137^3010122"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,1,0)="          * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *  * * * * * * * * * *"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,2,0)="                                   ATTENTION"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,3,0)="        Read this patch.  If you are a Cache/NT site, you MIGHT have to"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,4,0)="                             PERFORM MANUAL EDITS!"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,5,0)="          * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *  * * * * * * * * * *"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,6,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,7,0)="Patch HL*1.6*67"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,9,0)="NOIS: PUG-0800-52938"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,10,0)="Test Site: Milwaukee, WI; Puget Sound HCS; Grand Junction, CO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,11,0)="When sending HL7 transactions to other VA sites over TCP links, Cache/NT"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,12,0)="sites must send an initial HELO to overcome buffering issues.  However,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,13,0)="the initial HELO is not part of the HL7 standard, and may cause a reject"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,14,0)="error when sent to a COTS system."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,15,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,16,0)="This patch adds a new field, SAY HELO, to file 870, HL LOGICAL LINK,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,17,0)="so that for every logical link, the Cache/NT site can decide whether or"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,18,0)="not to send the initial HELO.  The default will be NO, since it is not"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,19,0)="part of the HL7 standard."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,20,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,21,0)="The form HL7 LOGICAL LINK has been updated to include this field.  Only"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,22,0)="Cache/NT sites should set it, since it does not apply to other sites,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,23,0)="and will be ignored at other sites."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,24,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,25,0)="At Cache/NT sites with patch HL*1.6*39 (which distributed VA Logical Link"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,26,0)="definitions) installed, the post-init will go through file 870,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,27,0)="HL LOGICAL LINK, and for every TCP link to a VA site (if the name of the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,28,0)="link starts with 'VA', OR if the link is 'MPIVA'), set SAY HELO to YES."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,29,0)="It will show you which links it has set.  You should review the list and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,30,0)="manually correct any which shouldn't have been set, or set any that were"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,31,0)="missed."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,32,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,33,0)="The post-init will NOT run at:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,34,0)="- Cache/NT sites which have not installed patch HL*1.6*39."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,35,0)="- non-Cache/NT sites."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,36,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,37,0)="Here's the new field:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,38,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,39,0)="STANDARD DATA DICTIONARY #870 -- HL LOGICAL LINK FILE"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,40,0)="STORED IN ^HLCS(870,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,41,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,42,0)="DATA        NAME                GLOBAL        DATA"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,43,0)="ELEMENT     TITLE               LOCATION      TYPE"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,44,0)="---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,45,0)="870,400.07  SAY HELO             400;7 SET"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,46,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,47,0)="                            'Y' FOR YES; "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,48,0)="                            'N' FOR NO; "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,49,0)="            LAST EDITED:    NOV 02, 2000 "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,50,0)="            HELP-PROMPT:    Send initial HELO for Cache/NT TCP links? "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,51,0)="            DESCRIPTION:    This field is applicable only to Cache/NT sites"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,52,0)="                            with TCP links.  If you are not a Cache/NT"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,53,0)="                            site, or this is not a TCP link, this field "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,54,0)="                            does not apply, AND will be ignored.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,55,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,56,0)="                            If this TCP link is for a VA site, answer YES.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,57,0)="                            If this TCP link is for a COTS system, answer"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,58,0)="                            NO.  This is the default.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,59,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,60,0)="          TECHNICAL DESCR:  When sending HL7 transactions to other VA sites"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,61,0)="                            over TCP links, Cache/NT sites must send an"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,62,0)="                            initial HELO to overcome buffering issues. "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,63,0)="                            However, the initial HELO is not part of the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,64,0)="                            HL7 standard, and may cause a reject error when"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,65,0)="                            sent to a COTS system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,66,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,67,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when activity is at"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,68,0)="a minimum.  It requires HL7 patch HL*1.6*66."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,69,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,70,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,71,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,72,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,73,0)="       ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;**[patch list]**;JUL 17,1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,74,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,75,0)="             Before       After"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,76,0)="Name         Checksum     Checksum     Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,77,0)="---------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,78,0)="HLCSTCP2     11334736     11552851     19,43,49,57,63,64,66,67"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,79,0)="HLPAT67       * new *      2870677     67"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,80,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,81,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,82,0)="This patch introduces the following new routine:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,83,0)="HLPAT67 is a post-init and has no user-callable entry points."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,84,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,85,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,86,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,87,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when activity is at"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,88,0)="a minimum.  It requires HL7 patch HL*1.6*66."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,89,0)="1. Users may be on the system during the installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,90,0)="2. DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,91,0)="   affected routine(s)."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,92,0)="3. Shutdown all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers, and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,93,0)="   the Link Manager. Use the options:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,95,0)="     Filer and Link Management Options -> "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,96,0)="         SA     Stop All Messaging Background Processes"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,97,0)="         LM     TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,98,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,99,0)="4. DSM sites: Disable all HL7 UCX Services for this installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,100,0)="5. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu to load the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,101,0)="   KIDS package into a Transport global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,102,0)="6. On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,103,0)="   Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,104,0)="         2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,105,0)="         3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,106,0)="         4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,107,0)="         5 Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,108,0)="         6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,109,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*67     Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,110,0)="                      ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,111,0)=" Install Questions for HL*1.6*67"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,112,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,113,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,114,0)="                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,115,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,116,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,117,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,118,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,119,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,120,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,121,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <Do NOT queue it!>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,122,0)="                ------------------"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,123,0)="7. Cache/NT sites: Once the patch is installed, review the list of "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,124,0)="HL LOGICAL LINKs whose SAY HELO field was set to YES by the post-init, and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,125,0)="make sure they were all links to VA sites, and that no TCP links to VA sites"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,126,0)="were left out.  (If the name started with 'VA' it was considered a VA site.)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,127,0)="8. Startup all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers. Use the "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,129,0)="     Filer and Link Management Options ->"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,130,0)="         RA     Restart/Start All Links and Filers"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,131,0)="   (Note: Links which do not have ""autostart"" enabled will need to"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,132,0)="          be restarted manually)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,133,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,134,0)="9. DSM Sites: If you previously disabled an HL7 UCX Service for this"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,135,0)="   installation, you may now enable it."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,136,0)="10. DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",44,1,137,0)="11. Start Link Manager using the option: ""TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop."""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,0)="68 SEQ #59^3010122^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,0)="^^92^92^3010122"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,1,0)="Patch HL*1.6*68"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,3,0)="NOIS: MIW-0900-41651"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,4,0)="Test Site: Milwaukee, WI"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,5,0)="This patch 'news' variables in routine ^HLCSMM so that they do not leak out"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,6,0)="and cause problems.  ^HLCSMM uses MailMan to send HL7 messages for MailMan"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,7,0)="type Logical Links."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,9,0)="The following improvements are also made:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,10,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,11,0)="1. Ignores domain closures and security key requirements, so that it will"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,12,0)="send to FOC-AUSTIN, even if that domain is closed or has a security key."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,13,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,14,0)="2. Sites may again use the auto-startup feature for MailMan type Logical"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,15,0)="Links.  If DUZ is 0 or undefined, DUZ will be set to .5 (POSTMASTER), for"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,16,0)="the purpose of sending the messages."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,17,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,18,0)="3. Error message has been improved.  If the message is not sent for some"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,19,0)="reason, the error message will clearly state the reason why.  Sites are"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,20,0)="reminded to ensure that the mail group which receives error messages is"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,21,0)="populated.  To do this:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,22,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,23,0)="W $$PARAM^HLCS2.  Piece 8 should be the name of a mail group.  You should "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,24,0)="be in that mail group.  This group receives error messages if there's any "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,25,0)="problems in creating the HL7 MailMan messages.  The subject is"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,26,0)="""Error handing HL7 message off to Mailman""."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,27,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,28,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when activity is at"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,29,0)="a minimum.  It requires HL7 patch HL*1.6*66."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,30,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,31,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,32,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,33,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,34,0)="       ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;**[patch list]**;JUL 17,1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,35,0)=""
