^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,91,0)="9. DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",45,1,92,0)="10. Start Link Manager using the option: ""TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop."""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",46,0)="73 SEQ #61^3010326^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",46,1,0)="^^1^1^3010326"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",46,1,1,0)="Patch to the HLCSMON routine."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",47,0)="72 SEQ #62^3010326^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",47,1,0)="^^1^1^3010326"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",47,1,1,0)="Fix free-text stored instead of internal entry number problem."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,0)="69 SEQ #63^3010405^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,0)="^^121^121^3010405"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,2,0)="This patch addresses the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,4,0)=" 1.  ISH-1000-42883  wrong processing routine being executed for VistA HL7 apps"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,6,0)=" 2.  SDC-1100-60210  Problem with HL7/Radiology link"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,8,0)=" The wrong processing routine is being executed (EN^RGADT)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,9,0)=" for non-MPI/PD applications.  This causes a MPI/PD exception to be"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,10,0)=" generated and sent to Forum."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,12,0)=" This problem was originally indentified in Milwaukee when the Dictaphone"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,13,0)=" application tried to execute a MPI/PD processing routine (EN^RGADT)."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,15,0)=" Most recently, the problem appeared at the Birmingham VAMC.  Some user"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,16,0)=" inactivated a Lab interface application which caused an endless loop"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,17,0)=" creating application acks that were never received/processed because the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,18,0)=" VistA HL7 application was inactivated."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,20,0)=" The problem lies in the CONT^HLTP3 subroutines, the HL(""EIDS"") variable,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,21,0)=" defining the subscribing protocol, is not defined.  The software sets the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,22,0)=" HL(""EIDS"") variable to HLEIDS.  The value of HLEIDS is not reliable, in"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,23,0)=" most cases the variable has not been properly set/killed."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,25,0)=" In addition, the inbound filers were not locking the cross-reference"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,26,0)=" ^HLMA(""AC"",""I"",... in order to flush to global cache buffers."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,28,0)=" In this case, the HL7 link receiving a message for an application"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,29,0)=" kills the cross-reference(entry in the inbound tcp/ip queue),"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,30,0)=" releases other locks, the inbound filers kicks in and grabs the lock at a"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,31,0)=" different parent level ^HLMA(ien), checks for the existence of"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,32,0)=" ^HLMA(""AC"",""I"",LLien,MSGien) and since no locking was performed on this"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,33,0)=" cross-reference, this piece of code thinks this entry exists.  Hence, the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,34,0)=" inbound filers begin to process this message, finds"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,35,0)=" variables left around from a previous message(MPI/PD or HL7 itself),"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,36,0)=" invokes code that uses these variables to set other HL7 variables when"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,37,0)=" these variables itself are not setup properly.  This in turn causes the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,38,0)=" code to call the MPI/PD application which in turn fires off exception"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,39,0)=" messages to Forum."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,41,0)=" These problems may be triggered by an inbound HL7 message that was not"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,42,0)=" properly constructed in terms of the HL7 MSH segment.  The VistA HL7"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,43,0)=" software needs from the MSH segment, the Sending/Receiving Application"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,44,0)=" names, Message Type, Event Type and Version ID."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,45,0)=" The HL7 Protocol setups may also have triggered this problem if the data"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,46,0)=" in the MSH segment of an inbound message does not match the interface"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,47,0)=" definition setups."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,49,0)=" Therefore, sites will still need to correct problems with their local"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,50,0)=" interfaces. This patch only prevents the wrong application from being"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,51,0)=" executed."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,53,0)="Routine Information:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,54,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,55,0)=" The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,56,0)=" of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,57,0)="  ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;<patchlist>;Oct 13, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,59,0)=" CHECK^XTSUMBLD checksum results:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,61,0)=" Routine Name     Before Patch  After Patch    Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,62,0)=" ============     ============  ===========    ===================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,63,0)=" HLTP3            14792516      15038079       19,43,57,58,59,66,69"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,65,0)=" List of preceding patches: 66"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,66,0)=" Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,69,0)="Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,70,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,71,0)="  1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,73,0)="  2.  DSM SITES: Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed in "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,74,0)="      the Routine Summary section are mapped, they should be removed from "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,75,0)="      the mapped set at this time.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,77,0)="  3.  Shutdown all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers, and "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,78,0)="      the Link Manager. Use the options: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,80,0)="        Filer and Link Management Options -> "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,81,0)="            SA     Stop All Messaging Background Processes "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,82,0)="            LM     TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,84,0)="      For DSM sites ONLY, disabled all HL7 UCX Services "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,85,0)="      for this installation.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,87,0)="  4.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,88,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,90,0)="  5.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,91,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,92,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the following "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,93,0)="      options: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,95,0)="         2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,96,0)="         3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,97,0)="         4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,98,0)="         5 Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,99,0)="         6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,100,0)="             INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*69 "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,101,0)="                           ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,102,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,103,0)="        Answer 'NO' to 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install?'.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,105,0)="        Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,106,0)="         and Protocols?'.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,108,0)="  6.  Startup all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers. Use the "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,110,0)="        Filer and Link Management Options -> "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,111,0)="            RA     Restart/Start All Links and Filers "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,112,0)="        (Note that links that do not have ""autostart"" enabled will need to "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,113,0)="        be restarted manually) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,115,0)="      For DSM sites ONLY, if you previously disabled an HL7 UCX Service "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,116,0)="      for this installation, you may now enable it.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,118,0)="  7.  DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,120,0)="  8.  Start Link Manager using the option: ""TCP/IP "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",48,1,121,0)="        Link Manager Start/Stop."" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,0)="76 SEQ #64^3010815^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,0)="^^198^198^3010815"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,1,0)="The test sites for Patch HL*1.6*76 are:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,2,0)="======================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,4,0)="  1. White River Junction VAMC."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,5,0)="  2. Butler VAMC."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,6,0)="  3. Tuscaloosa VAMC."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,7,0)="  4. Wilmington VAMC."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,8,0)="  5. San Francisco VAMC."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,9,0)="  6. Loma Linda VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,12,0)="This Patch Addresses the Following NOIS Calls:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,13,0)="=============================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,15,0)="  1. ISH-0700-41306   Enhanced Message Header issue: 'AA' received before 'CA'"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,16,0)="  2. BRX-0701-12759   VANJHL7 in error state"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,17,0)="  3. BRX-0701-12760   Undefined error CHKMSG+6^HLCSTCP2"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,18,0)="  4. POR-0701-52464   problem with VANJH LINK"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,19,0)="  5. BHS-0701-12356   VABED Link"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,20,0)="  6. ERI-0701-22675   Possible run-away HL7 job on Sun 7/29/01"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,23,0)="This patch is composed of the following five parts:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,24,0)="==================================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,26,0)="  1. Part 1 addresses out of order HL7 acknowledgements on Cache' "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,27,0)="     systems.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,28,0)="  2. Part 2 addresses non-persistent TCP/IP client links, which are not "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,29,0)="     maintaining a connection during the retention period. "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,30,0)="  3. Part 3 addresses the near SACC routine size limit (10K) of the HL7 routine"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,31,0)="     HLCSTCP2."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,32,0)="  4. Part 4 addresses direct connect handling network errors properly."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,33,0)="     Read errors encountered through the direct connect were affecting"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,34,0)="     both the Institution File Redesign (IFR) clean-up and the activation "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,35,0)="     of Integrated Billing (IB)."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,36,0)="  5. Part 5 addresses direct connect handling of M LOCKS."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,39,0)="Part 1 - The out of order HL7 acknowledgements on Cache' systems are related"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,40,0)="to the inconsistent use of OPEN parameters between client"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,41,0)="and server (listener) processes.  These acknowledgements are communicating"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,42,0)="over a TCP/IP socket on Cache' systems."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,44,0)="The VISTA HL7 package makes use of the following Kernel APIs"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,45,0)="to open a TCP/IP socket:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,47,0)="   1. CALL^%ZISTCP -- Used by the client.  This API uses STREAM mode."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,48,0)="   2. LISTEN^%ZISTCP -- Used by the single-threaded listener.  This API uses"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,49,0)="      packet mode."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,50,0)="   3. LISTEN^%ZISTCPS -- Used by the multi-threaded listener.  This API uses"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,51,0)="      packet mode."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,53,0)="When initiated from Cache' to DSM systems, HL7 messages should look like this:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,55,0)="   Order     Cache'                                  DSM"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,56,0)="   =====     ======                                  ==="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,57,0)="     1       client sends message----------------> listener"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,58,0)="     2       client <--------------------listener sends Commit ACK"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,59,0)="     3       listener <------------------client sends Application Response"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,60,0)="     4       listener sends Commit ACK------------> client"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,62,0)="However, with the inconsistent parameters used by the Kernel"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,63,0)="APIs, listed above, the following HL7 message scenario occurs:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,65,0)="   Order     Cache'                                  DSM"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,66,0)="   =====     ======                                  ==="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,67,0)="     1       client sends message----------------> listener"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,68,0)="     4       client <--------------------listener sends Commit ACK"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,69,0)="     2       listener <------------------client sends Application Response"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,70,0)="     3       listener sends Commit ACK------------> client"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,72,0)="Notice that the Commit ACK (Order #4) for the initial message (Order #1)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,73,0)="arrives after the application response message (Order #2). This is happening"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,74,0)="because the client process is using stream mode (Kernel API CALL^%ZISTCP)."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,75,0)="Steam mode is causing the initial message to wait for the full timeout"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,76,0)="to expire on the READ before the client process actually sees"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,77,0)="what was just read.  Therefore, if the READ TIMEOUT is set to 30 seconds,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,78,0)="the client will sit on the READ command for the entire 30 seconds"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,79,0)="while the listener process receives the application response"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,80,0)="as soon as it is available."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,83,0)="Part 2 - The second part of this patch will help reduce the OPEN failure rate"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,84,0)="that may be related to rapid OPENS and CLOSES by maintaining the connection"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,85,0)="during the retention period."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,87,0)="Part 3 - This patch creates the new HL7 routine HLCSTCP3 to accommodate"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,88,0)="the spillover in excess of 10K from HLCSTCP2."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,90,0)="Part 4 - The Institution File Redesign (IFR) Patch XU*8*206 may encounter"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,91,0)="problems with the clean-up process if network problems are present."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,92,0)="During the clean-up, IFR will download the Master Institution File from FORUM."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,93,0)="This is done via an HL7 feature called ""direct connect"".  The VISTA HL7"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,94,0)="developers have discovered a problem when read errors are encountered"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,95,0)="across the wide area network when using the direct connect."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,96,0)="Once this read error is encountered, it causes an error in the direct connect"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,97,0)="and the connection is dropped and the IFR clean-up encounters an error."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,98,0)="When this happens, the direct connect does not clear the cross reference"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,99,0)="it created.  Subsequently, when the clean-up is restarted,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,100,0)="an I/O problem will be encountered.  Patch HL*1.6*76 addresses"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,101,0)="these issues by passing back to the calling application information regarding"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,102,0)="any error it encounters.  Furthermore, it cleans up the cross reference"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,103,0)="it created and closes the device before returning to the calling application."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,104,0)="In addition, the post-init routine HLPAT76 will find all incomplete messages"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,105,0)="that were affected by READ errors prior to this patch.  This post-init will"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,106,0)="set the status of these messages so that they do not affect other messages in"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,107,0)="the queue."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,108,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,109,0)="Part 5 - After the Integrated Billing (IB) patch IB*2*150 was activated,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,110,0)="many sites encountered several entries in their Lock Table.  This was a result"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,111,0)="of the direct connect locking ^HLMA global nodes and never releasing the locks."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,112,0)="This IB patch utilizes an Integrated Billing Background Filer to send"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,113,0)="several HL7 messages.  To achieve this, this filer calls the direct connect"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,114,0)="API to send these messages.  However, each HL7 message sent adds two entries"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,115,0)="into the Lock Table causing some sites to fill up their Lock Table."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,116,0)="This HL7 patch fixes this problem by having the direct connect API"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,117,0)="properly release the locks when it no longer needs them."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,120,0)="Routine Information:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,121,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,123,0)=" The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line of each"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,124,0)=" of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,125,0)="  ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;<patchlist>;JUL 17,1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,127,0)="                  Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,128,0)=" Routine         Old       New      2nd Line"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,129,0)=" HLCSTCP2     11552851   11428718    **19,43,49,57,63,64,66,67,76**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,130,0)=" HLCSTCP3          new    1935770    **76**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,131,0)=" HLMA2         7999576    8028267    **19,43,57,58,64,65,76**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,132,0)=" HLPAT76           new    1888010    **76**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,134,0)=" List of preceding patches: 65, 67"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,135,0)=" Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,137,0)=" This patch introduces the following new routines: HLCSTCP3 and HLPAT76."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,138,0)=" Routine HLPAT76 is a post-init and has no user-callable entry points."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,140,0)="Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,141,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,142,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,143,0)="  1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during this installation.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,145,0)="  2.  DSM SITES: Review your mapped set. If any of the routines listed in "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,146,0)="      the Routine Summary section are mapped, they should be removed from "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,147,0)="      the mapped set at this time.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,149,0)="  3.  Use the VISTA HL7 Filer and Link Management options, listed below, to "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,150,0)="      shutdown (1) all Logical Links, (2) the incoming and outgoing filers, and "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,151,0)="      (3) the Link Manager. Use the options: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,152,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,153,0)="        Filer and Link Management Options -> "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,154,0)="            SA     Stop All Messaging Background Processes "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,155,0)="            LM     TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,156,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,157,0)="      DSM SITES ONLY: Disable all HL7 UCX Services for this installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,159,0)="  4.  Use the option INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE located on the PackMan menu to load "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,160,0)="      the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,161,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,162,0)="  5.  Patch HL*1.6*76 has now been loaded into a Transport global on your "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,163,0)="      system. The next step is to use KIDS to install the Transport global. To "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,164,0)="      do this, follow the KIDS menu path to the Installation menu:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,165,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,166,0)="         KIDS  Kernel Installation & Distribution System"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,167,0)="            Installation"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,168,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,169,0)="      On the Installation menu, use the following options: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,171,0)="         2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,172,0)="         3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,173,0)="         4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,174,0)="         5 Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,175,0)="         6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,176,0)="             INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*76 "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,177,0)="                           ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,178,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,179,0)="         Answer 'NO' to 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install?'.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,180,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,181,0)="         Answer 'NO' to 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,182,0)="         and Protocols?'.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,183,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,184,0)="  6.  Follow the HL7 menu path to the option Restart/Start All Links and Filers"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,185,0)="      to startup all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,187,0)="         Filer and Link Management Options -> "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,188,0)="            RA  Restart/Start All Links and Filers "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,189,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,190,0)="         NOTE: Links that do not have ""Autostart"" enabled will need to "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,191,0)="               be restarted manually) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,192,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,193,0)="      DSM SITES ONLY: If you previously disabled an HL7 UCX Service "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,194,0)="      for this installation, you may enable it now enable it.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,195,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,196,0)="  7.  DSM SITES: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,197,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",49,1,198,0)="  8.  Start Link Manager using the option: TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop. "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",50,0)="80 SEQ #65^3010906^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,0)="77 SEQ #66^3010906^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,0)="^^90^90^3010906"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,1,0)="Test sites:    Grand Junction,  El Paso, San Francisco, Big Spring"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,3,0)="NOIS:          ELP-0801-70936, GRJ-0801-51450, MAN-0701-12428,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,4,0)="               PRO-0801-11300"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,6,0)="Note:          This patch requires that KIDS build HL*1.6*76"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,7,0)="               be installed."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,9,0)="Patch HL*1.6*76 fixed problems encountered when a recent Integrated"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,10,0)="Billing patch was released.  (There was no problem with the Integrated"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,11,0)="Billing (IB) patch. But after the patch, IB used some parts of the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,12,0)="HL7 package differently than before.) Some problems were fixed by"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,13,0)="HL*1.6*76, but problems remained.  After patch HL*1.6*76 was installed,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,14,0)="READ and WRITE errors remained, but were more specific to Cache sites."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,15,0)="This patch fixes the additional problems not fixed by HL*1.6*76."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,17,0)="The two routines included in this patch are shown below, along with"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,18,0)="each routine's second line."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,20,0)="  Routine    Second Line"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,21,0)="  =========  ========================================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,22,0)="  HLCSTCP2   ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;**19,43,49,57,63,64,66,67,76,77"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,23,0)="             **;JUL 17,1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,24,0)="  HLCSTCP3   ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;**76,77**;JUL 17, 1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,26,0)="The VA Kernel checksums for these routines (calculated using"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,27,0)="CHECK^XTSUMBLD) are listed below."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,29,0)="                Checksum        Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,30,0)="  Routine Name  Before Patch    After Patch     Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,31,0)="  ============  ============    ===========     ====================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,32,0)="  HLCSTCP2      11428718        12129232        **19,43,49,57,63,64,66,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,33,0)="                                                67,76,77**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,34,0)="  HLCSTCP3       1935770         2092970        **19,57,59,72,80**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,36,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums after patch"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,37,0)="installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,39,0)=" Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,40,0)=" =========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,42,0)="   NOTICE:  Do no proceed unless patch HL*1.6*76 has been installed."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,44,0)="   1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,46,0)="   2.  AXP/DSM SITES: Review your mapped routine set.  If any of the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,47,0)="       routines listed in the ROUTINE SUMMARY section are mapped, they"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,48,0)="       should be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,50,0)="   3.  Shutdown all Logical Links, incoming and outgoing filers, and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,51,0)="       the Link Manager using the Filer and Link Management options"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,52,0)="       listed below."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,54,0)="          Stop All Messaging Background Processes [HL STOP ALL]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,55,0)="          TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop [HL START/STOP LINK MANAGER]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,57,0)="      AXP/DSM SITES ONLY: Disable all HL7 UCX Services for this"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,58,0)="      installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,60,0)="   4.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,61,0)="       option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,63,0)="   5.  This patch is now loaded into a transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,64,0)="       system. The next step is to use KIDS to install the Transport"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,65,0)="       global. This is done using the 'Installation' menu's 'Install"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,66,0)="       Package(s) [XPD INSTALL BUILD]' menu option. When using this"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,67,0)="       menu option to install the patch build, you will be asked"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,68,0)="       several questions.  The questions, and the answers you should"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,69,0)="       supply, are shown below."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,71,0)="       INSTALL NAME: <HL*1.6*77>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,72,0)="       Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install?  <NO>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,73,0)="       Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,74,0)="         and Protocols?  <NO>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,76,0)="   6.  Start up all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers using"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,77,0)="       the Filer and Link Management Option's 'Restart/Start All Links"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,78,0)="       and Filers [HL TASK RESTART]' menu option."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,80,0)="       (Note that links that do not have ""autostart"" enabled will need"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,81,0)="       to be restarted manually.)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,83,0)="      AXP/DSM SITES ONLY: If you previously disabled an HL7 UCX Service"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,84,0)="      for this installation, you may enable it now enable it."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,86,0)="   7.  AXP/DSM Sites:  After the patch has been installed, rebuild your"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,87,0)="       map set, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,89,0)="   8.  Start Link Manager using the 'TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop [HL"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",51,1,90,0)="       START/STOP LINK MANAGER]' menu option."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,0)="81 SEQ #67^3011016^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,0)="^^72^72^3011016"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,1,0)="Patch HL*1.6*81, Correct setup for sites using DNS and HL7"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,2,0)="=========================================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,4,0)="Category:  INFORMATIONAL"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,6,0)="Description:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,7,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,9,0)="               * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,10,0)="               READ THIS IMPORTANT INFORMATIONAL PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,11,0)="               * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,14,0)="This Patch Addresses the Following NOIS Call:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,15,0)="---------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,17,0)="ISB-0901-31233, HL7 DNS uses and helpful Websites"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,20,0)="Problem Scenario:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,21,0)="-----------------"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,23,0)="Through monitoring the HL7 Network between Veterans Affairs Medical"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,24,0)="Centers (VAMC) and the Master Patient Index (MPI), a need has arisen for"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,25,0)="clarification on the use of HL7 and Domain Name Servers (DNS). Mainly, the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,26,0)="IP address where the HL7 Listener is running at the sites must match the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,27,0)="IP address associated with the HL7 domain name in the DNS."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,30,0)="Patch Solution:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,31,0)="---------------"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,33,0)="The express purpose of this Informational Patch is to make sites aware of"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,34,0)="the HL7 Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) web site. It addresses"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,35,0)="information on DNS support as it relates to HL7. Specifically, it provides"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,36,0)="information on how to ensure that sites are correctly set up to use the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,37,0)="DNS with respect to HL7. This is addressed in the FAQ beginning at the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,38,0)="question ""How do I correctly set up my site to use DNS?"". "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,40,0)="Here is the URL for the HL7 FAQ web site:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,42,0)="    http://vaww.vista.domain.ext/hl7/hl7_faq.htm."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,45,0)="Note: Even though this is an informational patch, please be sure to "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,46,0)="      install it so the FORUM Patch tracking system gets updated."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,48,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,49,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,51,0)="1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,53,0)="2.  Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu. This"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,54,0)="    option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,56,0)="3.  This patch is now loaded into a transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,57,0)="    system. The next step is to use KIDS to install the Transport"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,58,0)="    global. To do this, use the 'Installation [XPD INSTALLATION"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,59,0)="    MENU]' menu.  On this menu, use the following options in the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,60,0)="    order shown below:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,62,0)="      3  Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,63,0)="      6  Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,65,0)="    When using the 'Install Package(s)' option to install the patch "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,66,0)="    build, you will be asked the following questions.  The questions"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,67,0)="    asked and the answers you should supply are shown below:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,69,0)="      INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*81"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,70,0)="      Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install?  <NO>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,71,0)="      Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",52,1,72,0)="      Protocols?  <NO>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,0)="75 SEQ #68^3011106^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,0)="^^174^174^3011106"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,1,0)="The test sites for Patch HL*1.6*75 are Bay Pines VAMC, Palo Alto VAMC, "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,2,0)="and San Francisco VAMC."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,5,0)="PATCH DESCRIPTION:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,6,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,8,0)="Currently if the System Link Monitor displays a client logical link in"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,9,0)="an Error STATE and you use the HL START option to attempt to start it"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,10,0)="back up, the option forces you to stop the process before you can re-"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,11,0)="enable it to continue the communication process."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,13,0)="Note: Entries in the HL LOGICAL LINKS file (#870) that are in an Error "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,14,0)="      STATE can be identified on the System Link Monitor by the word "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,15,0)="      Error in the STATE column."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,17,0)="The following is a screen capture of the HL7 System Link Monitor with a"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,18,0)="client logical link in an Error STATE."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,21,0)="HL7 System Link Monitor"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,22,0)="======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,23,0)="              SYSTEM LINK MONITOR for ISC SALT LAKE CITY (T System)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,25,0)="                MESSAGES  MESSAGES   MESSAGES  MESSAGES  DEVICE  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,26,0)="     NODE       RECEIVED  PROCESSED  TO SEND   SENT      TYPE     STATE"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,28,0)="     VADAN      38        38         38        38         NC      Error"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,33,0)="     Incoming filers running => 1            TaskMan running "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,34,0)="     Outgoing filers running => 1            Link Manager running"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,36,0)="     Select a Command:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,37,0)=" (N)EXT  (B)ACKUP  (A)LL LINKS  (S)CREENED  (V)IEWS  (Q)UIT  (?) HELP:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,38,0)="======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,41,0)="The following screen capture shows the two steps required to re-enable "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,42,0)="the client logical link (VADAN) shown in the previous screen capture."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,45,0)="Step 1 (Screen Capture Begins Here)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,46,0)="======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,47,0)="      Select Communications Server Option:  Start/Stop Links "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,49,0)="      This option is used to launch the lower level protocol for the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,50,0)="      appropriate device.  Please select the node with which you want"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,51,0)="      to communicate"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,53,0)="      Select HL LOGICAL LINK NODE:    VADAN"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,55,0)="      The LLP was last started on APR 14, 2000 11:20:58."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,57,0)="      Okay to shut down this job? YES"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,59,0)="      The job for the VADAN Lower Level Protocol will be shut down."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,60,0)="======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,61,0)="(Screen Capture Ends Here For Step 1)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,64,0)="Step 2 (Screen Capture Begins Here)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,65,0)="======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,67,0)="      Select Communications Server Option:  Start/Stop Links"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,69,0)="      This option is used to launch the lower level protocol for the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,70,0)="      appropriate device.  Please select the node with which you want"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,71,0)="      to communicate"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,73,0)="      Select HL LOGICAL LINK NODE:    VADAN"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,75,0)="      The LLP was last shutdown on APR 17, 2000 13:32:47."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,76,0)="      This LLP has been enabled!"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,77,0)="======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,78,0)="(Screen Capture Ends Here For Step 2)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,81,0)="Before this patch (Patch HL*1.6*75), using the option Start/Stop Links "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,82,0)="to re-enable a client logical link in an Error STATE was a two-step "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,83,0)="process. After this patch has been installed, using the option "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,84,0)="Start/Stop Links to re-enable a client logical link in an Error STATE "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,85,0)="will become a one-step process. However, this will only apply to client "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,86,0)="logical links in which the SHUTDOWN LLP field is set to YES while in an "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,87,0)="Error STATE. (See the following explanation ""Description of What Causes "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,88,0)="an Error State"" for more information on Error States.)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,91,0)="Description of What Causes an Error State"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,92,0)="======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,93,0)="Error STATEs can be related to retransmissions.  If the number of retry "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,94,0)="attempts has been exceeded, an alert is sent and the word Error appears "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,95,0)="in the STATE column on the System Link Monitor for that client logical "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,96,0)="link. This relates to the EXCEED RE-TRANSMIT ACTION field (#200.021) in "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,97,0)="the HL LOGICAL LINKS file. If the EXCEED RE-TRANSMIT ACTION field is "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,98,0)="set to Restart, the client logical link quits and the Link Manager "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,99,0)="queues (restarts) the link. If the EXCEED RE-TRANSMIT ACTION field is "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,100,0)="set to Shutdown, then the client logical link quits and the Link "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,101,0)="Manager will not attempt to restart the Link. In this particular case,"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,102,0)="the SHUTDOWN LLP field (#14) is set to YES in the HL LOGICAL LINKS "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,103,0)="file."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,105,0)="The other condition in which the value Error gets stuffed in the STATE "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,106,0)="field (#4) is when the client logical link gets an unexpected error. If "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,107,0)="the client logical link encounters an error other than the expected "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,108,0)="errors: OPENERR, NOTOPEN, DEVNOTOPN, WRITE, or READ, it logs the error "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,109,0)="in the error trap and shuts down the client logical link."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,111,0)="In this case, the SHUTDOWN LLP field is set and the client logical link "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,112,0)="has to be restarted manually."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,113,0)="======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,115,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,116,0)="THIS PATCH ADDRESSES THE FOLLOWING ISSUE:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,117,0)="========================================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,119,0)="  1.  E3R #14227, MAKE HL START ALITTLE SMARTER  [#31168789]"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,122,0)="ROUTINE INFORMATION: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,123,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,125,0)="The following routine is included in this patch. The second line of the "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,126,0)="routine now looks like this: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,127,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,128,0)=" ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;<patchlist>;Oct 13, 1995 "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,129,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,130,0)="                 Checksum "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,131,0)=" Routine         Old         New            2nd Line  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,132,0)=" ========      ========     ========     ===================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,134,0)=" HLCSLNCH      12643769     13101795     **6,19,43,49,57,75**"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,135,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,136,0)=" List of preceding patches: 57"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,138,0)=" Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,141,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,142,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,143,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,144,0)="  1.  Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,145,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,146,0)="  2.  DSM SITES: Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,147,0)="      in the Routine Summary section are mapped, they should be removed "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,148,0)="      from the mapped set at this time.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,150,0)="  3.  Use the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE option on the PackMan menu. This "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,151,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system.   "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,152,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,153,0)="  4.  The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,154,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,155,0)="      To do this, on the KIDS menu under Installation, use the "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,156,0)="      following options: "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,157,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,158,0)="         2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,159,0)="         3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,160,0)="         4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,161,0)="         5 Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,162,0)="         6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,163,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,164,0)="             INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*75 "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,165,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,166,0)="                           ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,167,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,168,0)="        Answer NO to the prompt 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,169,0)="        install?'.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,171,0)="        Answer NO to the prompt 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,172,0)="        Menu Options'."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",53,1,174,0)="  5.  DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,0)="82 SEQ #69^3011121^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,0)="^^80^80^3011121"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,1,0)="Patch HL*1.6*82"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,3,0)="NOIS: ISF-0600-61085"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,4,0)="Test Sites: FO-OAKLAND"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,5,0)="If you call the APIs GENERATE^HLMA or DIRECT^HLMA, with HLL(""LINKS"") pre-"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,6,0)="set, but incorrectly, the API should return an error, but it doesn't. This"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,7,0)="patch ensures that an error is returned, before any message is created."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,9,0)="If HLL(""LINKS"") is set in the routing logic or the entry action of a"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,10,0)="protocol during the APIs GENERATE^HLMA or DIRECT^HLMA, and any of the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,11,0)="protocols in HLL(""LINKS"") is not a subscriber type protocol, the message"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,12,0)="is created, but an error is returned."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,14,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when activity is at"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,15,0)="a minimum.  It requires HL7 patch HL*1.6*76."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,16,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,18,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,19,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,20,0)="       ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;**[patch list]**;JUL 17,1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,22,0)="             Before       After"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,23,0)="Name         Checksum     Checksum     Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,24,0)="---------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,25,0)="HLCS2        10270936     10941124     14,40,43,49,57,58,82"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,26,0)="HLMA          7962943      9200711     19,43,58,63,66,82"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,27,0)="HLMA2         8028267      8331015     19,43,57,58,64,65,76,82"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,28,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,30,0)="This patch introduces no new routines."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,31,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,33,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,34,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when activity is at"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,35,0)="a minimum.  It requires HL7 patch HL*1.6*76."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,36,0)="1. Users may be on the system during the installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,37,0)="2. DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,38,0)="   affected routine(s)."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,39,0)="3. Shutdown all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers, and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,40,0)="   the Link Manager. Use the options:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,42,0)="     Filer and Link Management Options -> "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,43,0)="         SA     Stop All Messaging Background Processes"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,44,0)="         LM     TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,46,0)="4. DSM sites: Disable all HL7 UCX Services for this installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,47,0)="5. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu to load the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,48,0)="   KIDS package into a Transport global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,49,0)="6. On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,50,0)="   Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,51,0)="         2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,52,0)="         3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,53,0)="         4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,54,0)="         5 Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,55,0)="         6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,56,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*82     Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,57,0)="                      ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,58,0)=" Install Questions for HL*1.6*82"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,60,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,61,0)="                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,62,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,63,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,64,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,65,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,66,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,68,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <Do NOT queue it!>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,69,0)="                ------------------"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,70,0)="7. Startup all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers. Use the "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,72,0)="     Filer and Link Management Options ->"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,73,0)="         RA     Restart/Start All Links and Filers"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,74,0)="   (Note: Links which do not have ""autostart"" enabled will need to"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,75,0)="          be restarted manually)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,76,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,77,0)="8. DSM Sites: If you previously disabled an HL7 UCX Service for this"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,78,0)="   installation, you may now enable it."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,79,0)="9. DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",54,1,80,0)="10. Start Link Manager using the option: ""TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop."""
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,0)="83 SEQ #70^3011121^1"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,0)="^^75^75^3011121"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,1,0)="Patch HL*1.6*83"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,3,0)="NOIS: ISA-0800-11764"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,4,0)="Test Sites: FO-ALBANY"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,5,0)="If VistA HL7 is processing an HL7 message, and calls the API UPD^HLSUB"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,6,0)="to add/update a subscription, and the 5th parameter indicates that the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,7,0)="termination date should be deleted, and there's already a subscription"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,8,0)="with a termination date, it fails to delete the termination date."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,9,0)="This patch fixes that. "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,11,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when activity is at"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,12,0)="a minimum.  It requires HL7 patch HL*1.6*66."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,13,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,15,0)="ROUTINES:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,16,0)="The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,17,0)="       ;;1.6;HEALTH LEVEL SEVEN;**[patch list]**;JUL 17,1995"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,19,0)="             Before       After"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,20,0)="Name         Checksum     Checksum     Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,21,0)="---------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,22,0)="HLSUB         5558527      5395528     14,57,58,59,66,83"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,23,0)="* Checksums produced by CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,25,0)="This patch introduces no new routines."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,26,0)="============================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,28,0)="INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,29,0)="NOTE: This patch should be installed during off hours, when activity is at"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,30,0)="a minimum.  It requires HL7 patch HL*1.6*66."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,31,0)="1. Users may be on the system during the installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,32,0)="2. DSM Sites: If any of these routines is mapped, disable mapping for the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,33,0)="   affected routine(s)."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,34,0)="3. Shutdown all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers, and"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,35,0)="   the Link Manager. Use the options:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,37,0)="     Filer and Link Management Options -> "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,38,0)="         SA     Stop All Messaging Background Processes"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,39,0)="         LM     TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,41,0)="4. DSM sites: Disable all HL7 UCX Services for this installation."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,42,0)="5. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu to load the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,43,0)="   KIDS package into a Transport global on your system.  "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,44,0)="6. On the KIDS:Installation menu, use the following options to install the"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,45,0)="   Transport Global:"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,46,0)="         2 Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,47,0)="         3 Print Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,48,0)="         4 Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,49,0)="         5 Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,50,0)="         6 Install Package(s) "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,51,0)=" Select INSTALL NAME: HL*1.6*83     Loaded from Distribution  <date/time>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,52,0)="                      ========="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,53,0)=" Install Questions for HL*1.6*83"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,55,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,56,0)="                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,57,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,58,0)="                                                                       =="
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,59,0)=" Enter the Device you want to print the Install messages."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,60,0)=" You can queue the install by enter a 'Q' at the device prompt."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,61,0)=" Enter a '^' to abort the install."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,63,0)=" DEVICE: HOME// <Do NOT queue it!>"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,64,0)="                ------------------"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,65,0)="7. Startup all Logical Links and incoming and outgoing filers. Use the "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,67,0)="     Filer and Link Management Options ->"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,68,0)="         RA     Restart/Start All Links and Filers"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,69,0)="   (Note: Links which do not have ""autostart"" enabled will need to"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,70,0)="          be restarted manually)"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,71,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,72,0)="8. DSM Sites: If you previously disabled an HL7 UCX Service for this"
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,73,0)="   installation, you may now enable it."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,74,0)="9. DSM Sites: Rebuild your mapped set if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,33,22,1.4,"PAH",55,1,75,0)="10. Start Link Manager using the option: ""TCP/IP Link Manager Start/Stop."""
