^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,143,0)="Software and Documentation Retrieval Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,144,0)="---------------------------------------------------- "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,145,0)="Software being released as a host file and/or documentation describing the"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,146,0)="new functionality introduced by this patch are available."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,147,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,148,0)="The preferred method is to retrieve files from download.vista.domain.ext."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,149,0)="This transmits the files from the first available server. Sites may also"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,150,0)="elect to retrieve files directly from a specific server. "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,151,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,152,0)="Sites may retrieve the software and/or documentation directly using Secure"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,153,0)="File Transfer Protocol (SFTP) from the ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE directory at the"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,154,0)="following OI Field Offices:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,155,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,156,0)="Albany:                 fo-albany.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,157,0)="Hines:                  fo-hines.domain.ext    "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,158,0)="Salt Lake City:         fo-slc.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,159,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,160,0)="Documentation can also be found on the VA Software Documentation Library "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,161,0)="at: http://www4.domain.ext/vdl/"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,162,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,163,0)="Pre/Post Installation Overview"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,164,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,165,0)="There are no Pre-installation routines associated with this patch."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,166,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,167,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,168,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,169,0)="-------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,170,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,171,0)="recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,172,0)="potential disruption to users.  This patch should take less than 5 "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,173,0)="minutes to install."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,174,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,175,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,176,0)="Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,177,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,178,0)="1.      Choose the PackMan message containing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,179,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,180,0)="2.      Choose the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option.  "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,181,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,182,0)="3.      From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,183,0)="        the Installation Menu.  From this menu, you may elect to use the "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,184,0)="        following options. When prompted for the INSTALL NAME enter"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,185,0)="        OR*3.0*420."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,187,0)="        a.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,188,0)="            allow you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,189,0)="            the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,190,0)="        b.  Print Transport Global - This option will allow you to view"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,191,0)="            the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,192,0)="        c.  Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,193,0)="            allow you to view all changes that will be made when this "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,194,0)="            patch is installed.  It compares all components of this patch"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,195,0)="            (routines, DD's, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,196,0)="        d.  Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,197,0)="            message of any routines exported with this patch. It will not"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,198,0)="            backup any other changes such as DD's or templates."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,200,0)="4.      From the Installation Menu, select the Install Package(s) option "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,201,0)="        and choose the patch to install."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,202,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,203,0)="5.      When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,204,0)="        NO// Press <Enter>"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,205,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,206,0)="6.      When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,207,0)="        and Protocols? NO// Press <Enter>"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,208,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,209,0)="7.      If prompted ""Delay Install (Minutes):  (0 - 60): 0// enter 0."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,210,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,211,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,212,0)="Post-Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,213,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,214,0)="A site Pharmacy CAC/ADPAC will have to set the OR CPRS LAB DISPLAY "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,215,0)="ENABLEd parameter to a value of ""Yes"" using he XPAR MENU TOOLS option "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",366,1,216,0)="in order for this functionality to be accessed."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",367,0)="440 SEQ #376^3170629.151432^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",368,0)="457^3170629.161327^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",368,1,0)="^^2^2^3170629"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",368,1,1,0)="This patch will fix the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",368,1,2,0)="1. Drug Interaction Order Checks"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",369,0)="436 SEQ #378^3170726.130606^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",370,0)="461 SEQ #379^3170726.135722^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",371,0)="458 SEQ #380^3170907.180912^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",371,1,0)="^^1^1^3170907"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",371,1,1,0)="NOTIFICATIONS SHOWING 'MANDATORY' WHEN THEY ARE NOT"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",372,0)="454 SEQ #381^3171101.124149^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",372,1,0)="^^1^1^3171101"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",372,1,1,0)="Please see forum for a complete patch description."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",373,0)="401 SEQ #382^3171102.112624^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",373,1,0)="^^1^1^3171102"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",373,1,1,0)="Option ORK EDITABLE BY USER, ORQQPL4 RPC fix"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",374,0)="448 SEQ #383^3171102.122222^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",375,0)="434^3171127.135526^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",376,0)="429^3171227.134012^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",376,1,0)="^^1^1^3171227"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",376,1,1,0)="The description of this patch can be found in the National Patch Module."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",377,0)="456 SEQ #386^3171227.162659^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",377,1,0)="^^1^1^3171227"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",377,1,1,0)="FLAGGED ORDER SURROGATE NOTIFICATION ISSUE"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",378,0)="467 SEQ #387^3180103.133945^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",379,0)="449 SEQ #388^3180103.13405^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",379,1,0)="^^1^1^3180103"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",379,1,1,0)="See patch description for details."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",380,0)="459 SEQ #389^3180129.165808^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",380,1,0)="^^3^3^3180129"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",380,1,1,0)="Patch OR*3.0*459 addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",380,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",380,1,3,0)="1. Anti-Coagulation Show Rate not displaying correct information"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,0)="465 SEQ #390^3180228.164821^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,1,0)="^^12^12^3180228"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,1,1,0)="This patch corrects 3 issues within the ORDER ENTRY/RESULTS REPORTING "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,1,2,0)="package:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,1,4,0)="1. The hard error <UNDEFINED>EN+3^LEXAFIL occasionally and sporadically"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,1,5,0)="   occurs when the user uses a function in CPRS that calls the Remote"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,1,6,0)="   Procedure Call (RPC) ORWPCE4 LEX."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,1,8,0)="2. The automated monthly controlled substance report to providers is "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,1,9,0)="   sending the internal id for Prescription instead of the external id."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,1,11,0)="3. Users can't remove themselves from patient lists of type ""Patient "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",381,1,12,0)="   Manual"" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",382,0)="428 SEQ #391^3180301.151218^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",382,1,0)="^^7^7^3180301"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",382,1,1,0)="Patch OR*3.0*428 addresses the following two issues:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",382,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",382,1,3,0)="1. Undefined error at IN+27^ORDV06B when running the All Medications "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",382,1,4,0)="Report in CPRS for Inpatient orders.     "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",382,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",382,1,6,0)="2.  Undefined error at IN+41^ORDV06B when running the All Medications "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",382,1,7,0)="report in CPRS for Oupatient or Non-VA orders."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",383,0)="450 SEQ #393^3180301.152704^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",383,1,0)="^^6^6^3180301"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",383,1,1,0)="Patch OR*3.0*450 will address the following two issues:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",383,1,2,0)="Note: issue 2 is documentation only"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",383,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",383,1,4,0)="1. Flagged Orderable Item Alert not processing all inpatient items in an "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",383,1,5,0)="   order"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",383,1,6,0)="2. CPRS GUI Technical Manual update Lab test order ""other"" clarification"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",384,0)="382^3180302.14082^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",385,0)="469^3180302.141035^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",385,1,0)="^^1^1^3180302"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",385,1,1,0)="MOCHA 2.1 follow-up"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",386,0)="474 SEQ #396^3180403.165236^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",386,1,0)="^^4^4^3180403"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",386,1,1,0)="The purpose of this build is to resolve the problem with Anticoagulation "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",386,1,2,0)="Management Tool (AMT) and how it deals with edits and complications."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",386,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",386,1,4,0)="R18005975FY18 - Problem with Complications"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",387,0)="471 SEQ #397^3180403.1655^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",387,1,0)="^^1^1^3180403"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",387,1,1,0)="ORDER DETAILS, DRUG RESTRICTION, & RENEWED ORDER ISSUES"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",388,0)="443 SEQ #398^3180425.172833^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",388,1,0)="^^2^2^3180425"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",388,1,1,0)="This patch corrects a single issue - an error the CPRS Debug report that "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",388,1,2,0)="only occurs if there is unexpected data in the XTMP debug log."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",389,0)="462 SEQ #399^3180501.143738^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",389,1,0)="^^9^9^3180501"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",389,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",389,1,2,0)="Patch OR*3.0*462 addresses these 2 issues:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",389,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",389,1,4,0)="I10009975FY16 - If a user edits an existing diet Quick Order using option "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",389,1,5,0)="[ORCM QUICK ORDERS], the system allows a REGULAR/NPO diet to be ordered "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",389,1,6,0)="with another diet."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",389,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",389,1,8,0)="I10480945FY16 - Medication orders flagged by a pharmacist that are then "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",389,1,9,0)="updated by the pharmacists cannot then be un-flagged in CPRS or PSJ OE."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",390,0)="451 SEQ #400^3180501.144023^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",390,1,0)="^^8^8^3180501"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",390,1,1,0)="This patch corrects 2 issues within the ORDER ENTRY/RESULTS REPORTING "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",390,1,2,0)="package:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",390,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",390,1,4,0)="1. The show rate calculation skips over visits with an INR that repeats"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",390,1,5,0)="the previous visit's INR."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",390,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",390,1,7,0)="2. When a patient comes in early - 48 hours before the next draw date -"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",390,1,8,0)="then it is counted as a missed appointment."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",391,0)="452 SEQ #401^3180601.150658^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",392,0)="480 SEQ #402^3180601.161616^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",392,1,0)="^^3^3^3180601"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",392,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue: "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",392,1,2,0)="1. Prevent truncation of drug data returned from Pharmacy when finishing "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",392,1,3,0)="an order."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,0)="414 SEQ #403^3180601.162705^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,0)="^^13^13^3180601"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,1,0)="This patch corrects 3 issues within the ORDER ENTRY/RESULTS REPORTING "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,2,0)="package:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,4,0)="1. Orderable Items with a value in the Type field of Neither appear as an"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,5,0)="   available lab test when ordering in CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,7,0)="2. When the last creatinine lab has a ""canc"" result then the CrCL"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,8,0)="   calculation will skip all results with the same specimen and go on to"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,9,0)="   look at lab results for other specimens. "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,11,0)="3. When a weight or height entry in to the patient's vitals is marked as"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,12,0)="   Pass, Unavailable or Refused the CrCL value for the patient disappears"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",393,1,13,0)="   even though there is a previous valid entry."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",394,0)="463 SEQ #404^3180601.162744^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",395,0)="475 SEQ #405^3180601.162902^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",395,1,0)="^^1^1^3180601"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",395,1,1,0)="Bug fixes to RTC Orders"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",396,0)="482 SEQ #406^3180706.120901^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",396,1,0)="^^1^1^3180706"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",396,1,1,0)="Lab labels print when not requested"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",397,0)="481^3180706.154355^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",397,1,0)="^^1^1^3180706"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",397,1,1,0)="MOCHA 2.1B Warranty Issues"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,0)="477 SEQ #408^3181004.145021^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,0)="^^61^61^3181004"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,1,0)="This patch addresses two (2) issues:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,3,0)="1.  The PHARMACY ORDERABLE ITEM file (#50.7) NAME field (#.01) is "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,4,0)="    not always synced with ORDERABLE ITEM file (#101.43) NAME field"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,5,0)="    (#.01)."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,6,0)="2.  Room-Bed default printer parameters are ignored during the ordering "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,7,0)="    process."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,9,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,10,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,11,0)="1. I7370452FY16 - PHARMACY ORDERABLE ITEMS / ORDERABLE ITEMS"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,12,0)="   I10581756FY16 (d) "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,14,0)="   Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,15,0)="   --------"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,16,0)="   The PHARMACY ORDERABLE ITEMS file (#50.7) NAME field (#.01) is  "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,17,0)="   not always synced with the ORDERABLE ITEMS file (#101.43) NAME"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,18,0)="   field (#.01)."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,20,0)="   The NAME field (#.01) in the ORDERABLE ITEMS file (#101.43) is  "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,21,0)="   a combination of the NAME field (#.01), max length 40, in the "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,22,0)="   PHARMACY ORDERABLE ITEMS file (#50.7) and the NAME field (#.01), "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,23,0)="   max length 30, in the DOSAGE FORM file (#50.606).  There is a  "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,24,0)="   space between the two fields and a space at the end of the field."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,25,0)="   This could produce a NAME that is 72 characters in length.  "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,27,0)="   The problem is that the maximum length for the NAME field (#.01)"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,28,0)="   in the ORDERABLE ITEMS file (#101.43) is 63 characters.  This  "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,29,0)="   can result in truncation, as well as failed update ""pushes"" when  "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,30,0)="   the combination of the Pharmacy Orderable Items Name and Dosage"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,31,0)="   Form Name is greater than 63 characters."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,33,0)="   The maximum field length for the NAME field (#.01) in the "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,34,0)="   ORDERABLE ITEMS file (#101.43) needs to be increased to 72 "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,35,0)="   characters."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,37,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,38,0)="   -----------"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,39,0)="   A Data Dictionary update has been made to the NAME Field (#.01) in "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,40,0)="   the ORDERABLE ITEM file (#101.43) to increase the maximum field "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,41,0)="   length limit to 72 characters."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,43,0)="2. I17614498FY18 - ROOM-BED PRINT DEVICE PARAMETER ISSUES"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,44,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,45,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,46,0)="   --------"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,48,0)="   If a default label printer is defined for a Room-Bed using any of the"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,49,0)="   parameters ""ORPF CHART COPY PRINT DEVICE "", ""ORPF LABEL PRINT DEVICE"","
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,50,0)="   ""ORPF REQUISITION PRINT DEVICE"" and ""ORPF WORK COPY PRINT DEVICE"", the"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,51,0)="   parameter setting is ignored during the CPRS ordering process."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,53,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,54,0)="   -----------"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,56,0)="   Modify routine ORWD2 to determine whether a ""device"" parameter"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,57,0)="   definition exists for the patient's Room-Bed. The ""device"" parameter "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,58,0)="   descriptions were updated to clarify that the location(s) for each "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,59,0)="   Room-Bed must have the corresponding ""prompt"" parameter defined in"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,60,0)="   order for the Room-Bed device to display.  The CPRS Technical Manual"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",398,1,61,0)="   was also updated to include that clarification."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,0)="487 SEQ #409^3181004.145147^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,0)="^^28^28^3181004"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,1,0)="Issues:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,3,0)="1. When invoking option PSSJI DRUG:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,5,0)="   a) An error occurs if an additive is defined to have ""UNIT DOSE "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,6,0)="      MEDICATIONS"" usage defined as ""quick order only""."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,8,0)="   b) Quick order restrictions are removed if ""IV MEDICATIONS"" and/or "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,9,0)="      ""IV ADDITIVES"" usages are defined as ""quick order only."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,11,0)="2. When invoking option PSSJI SOLN:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,13,0)="   a) An error occurs if a solution is defined to have 'UNIT DOSE "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,14,0)="      MEDICATIONS"" usage defined as ""quick order only""."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,16,0)="   b) Quick order restrictions are removed if ""IV MEDICATIONS"" and/or "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,17,0)="      ""IV SOLUTIONS"" usages are defined as ""quick order only""."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,19,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,20,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,22,0)="Modified routines PSSVIDRG and ORMFN to preserve quick order settings on "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,23,0)="additives and solutions.  These changes also prevented the error which "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,24,0)="occurred when a solution or additive was defined to have unit doses as "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,25,0)="""quick order only""."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,27,0)="Routine PSSVIDRG is included in patch PSS*1.0*229 which will be installed "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",399,1,28,0)="along with routine ORMFN in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",400,0)="492 SEQ #410^3181102.152649^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",400,1,0)="^^1^1^3181102"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",400,1,1,0)="LAB LABELS INCORRECTLY PRINTED"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",401,0)="483^3181102.153821^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",402,0)="441 SEQ #413^3181203.181418^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",402,1,0)="^^1^1^3181203"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",402,1,1,0)="Please see forum for a complete description of patch OR*3.0*441"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",403,0)="484 SEQ #414^3181206.161842^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",404,0)="435 SEQ #415^3181206.161919^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",404,1,0)="^^1^1^3181206"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",404,1,1,0)="Please see forum for a complete description of patch OR*3.0*435"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",405,0)="490 SEQ #416^3190102.174114^54"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",405,1,0)="^^273^273^3190102"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",405,1,1,0)="The One Consult Admin Key Consult project is being designed to improve "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",405,1,2,0)="the current business process used by VistA providers when an imaging order"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",405,1,3,0)="is referred to a Community Care provider. Currently, a user creates a new"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",405,1,4,0)="consult, then signs the order on the orders tab."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",405,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",405,1,6,0)="The goal of this project is to automatically sign the consult if the "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",405,1,7,0)="consult service name contains -DS or -ADMIN, and the user has the key"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",405,1,8,0)="""GMRC ADMIN RBP TO CC"", and then send the consult to community care."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",405,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",405,1,10,0)=" "
