^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,38,0)="Blood Bank Team Coordination:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,39,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,40,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*535 does not "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,41,0)="contain any changes to the VISTA BLOOD BANK Software as defined by "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,42,0)="ProPath standard titled: BBM Team Review of VistA Patches."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,44,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch LR*5.2*535 does not "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,45,0)="alter or modify any software design safeguards or safety critical "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,46,0)="elements functions."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,48,0)="RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch LR*5.2*535 have no adverse effect on "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,49,0)="Blood Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,51,0)="VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS BY OPTION: Because of the nature of the changes "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,52,0)="made, no specific validation requirements exist as a result of "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,53,0)="installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,55,0)="Software and Documentation Retrieval Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,57,0)="Documentation describing the new functionality introduced by this patch "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,58,0)="is available on the VA Software Documentation Library at:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,59,0)="http://www.domain.ext/vdl/application.asp?appid=182"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,61,0)="Refer to the VBECS 2.3.2 Rev F Release Notes for a list of the user "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,62,0)="documentation associated with this revision letter patch."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,64,0)="Additional VBECS information can be accessed on the VBECS SharePoint site "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,65,0)="at:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,66,0)="https://dvagov.sharepoint.com/sites/oitepmovbecs"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,69,0)="Patch Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,70,0)="-------------------"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,72,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,73,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,74,0)="recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,75,0)="potential disruption to users.  This patch should take less than 5 "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,76,0)="minutes to install."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,78,0)="No options need to be disabled during installation."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,81,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,83,0)=" 1. Choose the PackMan message containing this build. Then select the"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,84,0)="    INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option to load the build."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,86,0)=" 2. From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select the"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,87,0)="    Installation Menu.  From this menu, "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,89,0)="    A. Select the Verify Checksums in Transport Global option to confirm "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,90,0)="       the integrity of the routines that are in the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,91,0)="       When prompted for the INSTALL NAME enter the patch name OR*3.0*527."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,92,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,93,0)="    B. Select the Backup a Transport Global option to create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,94,0)="       message of any routines exported with this patch. It will not"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,95,0)="       backup any other changes such as DDs or templates. "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,97,0)="    C. You may also elect to use the following options: "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,98,0)="         i.  Print Transport Global - This option will allow you to view"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,99,0)="             the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,100,0)="         ii. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,101,0)="             will allow you to view all changes that will be made when"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,102,0)="             this patch is installed.  It compares all of the components"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,103,0)="             of this patch, such as routines, DDs, templates, etc."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,105,0)="    D. Select the Install Package(s) option and choose the patch to"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,106,0)="       install. "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,107,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,108,0)="       i.  If prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,109,0)="           of Install? NO//', answer No"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,111,0)="      ii. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,112,0)="          NO//', answer No"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,113,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,114,0)="      iii. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,115,0)="           Options, and Protocols? NO//', answer No"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,117,0)="Post-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,118,0)=" N/A"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,120,0)="Back-Out/Roll Back Plan:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,121,0)="------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,122,0)=" This patch consists of three routines. During the VistA Installation "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,123,0)=" Procedure the installer should back up the modified routines by the"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,124,0)=" use of the 'Backup a Transport Global' action (step 2B in"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,125,0)=" the Installations Instructions)."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,126,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,127,0)=" If rollback/backout is required, the installer can restore the routines"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,128,0)=" using the MailMan message that were saved prior to installing the"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,129,0)=" patch."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,130,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,131,0)=" If assistance is needed to rollback/backout the patch, please log a "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",435,1,132,0)=" Service Now ticket."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",436,0)="534 SEQ #450^3200928.091246^17"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",436,1,0)="^^5^5^3200928"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",436,1,1,0)="This patch addresses two (2) issues:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",436,1,2,0)="1. The ""Display the Notifications a User Can Receive"" option does not "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",436,1,3,0)="   display the ORB PROCESSING FLAG parameter edits based on Team."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",436,1,4,0)="2. Results might erroneously flag as ""critical"" in two CPRS reports on "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",436,1,5,0)="   the Labs tab."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",437,0)="512 SEQ #451^3200928.135006^17"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",437,1,0)="^^1^1^3200928"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",437,1,1,0)="Clinically indicated date is changing when using T+XXX or +XXX function."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",438,0)="528 SEQ #452^3201015.123349^17"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",438,1,0)="^^1^1^3201015"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",438,1,1,0)="See patch description for information regarding modifications."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",439,0)="519^3201112.175219^17"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",440,0)="524 SEQ #455^3210304.101731^17"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",440,1,0)="^^3^3^3210304"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",440,1,1,0)="The purpose of this patch is to swap the display of Imperial and Metric "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",440,1,2,0)="measurements on the CPRS coversheet display of Vitals. See the patch for "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",440,1,3,0)="a full description."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",441,0)="540 SEQ #456^3210304.153924^17"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",441,1,0)="^^4^4^3210304"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",441,1,1,0)="This patch corrects the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",441,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",441,1,3,0)="If lengthy drug-drug interaction message is transmitted to a remote email "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",441,1,4,0)="address, a buffer error might occur and stall MailMan transmissions."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",442,0)="476^3210310.120602^17"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",442,1,0)="^^1^1^3210310"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",442,1,1,0)="Please see OR*3.0*476 Patch Description for more info."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",443,0)="437^3210322.124637^17"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",443,1,0)="^^10^10^3210322"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",443,1,1,0)="The patch modifies OR routine ""OROTHCL"" and RPC ""OROTHCL GET"" to update"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",443,1,2,0)="the comments and description to indicate that this code and RPC, in"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",443,1,3,0)="addition to Other Than Honorable (OTH), will display the following"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",443,1,4,0)="information on the CPRS button at the top of the screen and in the"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",443,1,5,0)="associated pop-up window:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",443,1,6,0)="- Presumptive Psychosis (PP) status based on the settings in the PATIENT"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",443,1,7,0)="  file (#2) and in the INSURANCE VERIFICATION PROCESSOR file (#355.33) "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",443,1,8,0)="- Inactive Patient Record Flags (PRF) assigned to the patient and a"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",443,1,9,0)="  history of PRF changes.  "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",443,1,10,0)="There are no actual code changes made to these components."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",444,0)="545b^3210420"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",444,1,0)="^^5^5^3210420"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",444,1,1,0)="Backup of OR*3.0*545 on Apr 20, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",444,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",444,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",444,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",444,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",445,0)="545 SEQ #460^3210420.150317^17"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",445,1,0)="^^4^4^3210420"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",445,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",445,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",445,1,3,0)="The order check message might not be accurate when signing a Clinic"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",445,1,4,0)="Infusion order."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",446,0)="544b^3210422"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",446,1,0)="^^5^5^3210422"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",446,1,1,0)="Backup of OR*3.0*544 on Apr 22, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",446,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",446,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",446,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",446,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",447,0)="544 SEQ #461^3210422.12331^17"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",447,1,0)="^^4^4^3210422"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",447,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the issue of a hard M error during the patient look "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",447,1,2,0)="up using the last 5 digits of the social security number or the last "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",447,1,3,0)="letter of the last name and the last 5 digits of the social security "
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",447,1,4,0)="number."
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",448,0)="529b^3210427"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",448,1,0)="^^5^5^3210427"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",448,1,1,0)="Backup of OR*3.0*529 on Apr 27, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,35,22,3,"PAH",448,1,2,0)=" "
