^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",28,1,2,0)="and enhancements provided by this patch."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",29,0)="30 SEQ #29^3030123^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",29,1,0)="^^2^2^3030123"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",29,1,1,0)="Refer to the National Patch Module for complete details of the "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",29,1,2,0)="changes/enhancements included in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",30,0)="31 SEQ #30^3030301^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",30,1,0)="^^2^2^3030301"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",30,1,1,0)="See the National Patch module for details of the changes included in this "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",30,1,2,0)="patch."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",31,0)="34 SEQ #31^3030802^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",31,1,0)="^^1^1^3030802"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",31,1,1,0)="Disassociate Results"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",32,0)="33^3030924^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",32,1,0)="^^2^2^3030924"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",32,1,1,0)="Refer to the National Patch Module for complete details of the "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",32,1,2,0)="enhancements included in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",33,0)="32 SEQ #33^3031002^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",33,1,0)="^^2^2^3031002"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",33,1,1,0)="See the National Patch Module for full details of the enhancements "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",33,1,2,0)="included in this build. "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",34,0)="35 SEQ #34^3031002^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",34,1,0)="^^2^2^3031002"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",34,1,1,0)="Please refer to the National Patch Module for a complete list of the "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",34,1,2,0)="enhancements included in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",35,0)="41 SEQ #35^3050426^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",35,1,0)="^^2^2^3050426"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",35,1,1,0)="See the National Patch Module for complete details of the enhancements "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",35,1,2,0)="included in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",36,0)="40 SEQ #36^3050506^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",36,1,0)="^^2^2^3050506"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",36,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the problem where a consult service can become a"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",36,1,2,0)="subservice within its own subservice hierarchy."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",37,0)="38 SEQ #37^3050506^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",37,1,0)="^^4^4^3050506"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",37,1,1,0)="This patch corrects the inaccurate identification of the location of "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",37,1,2,0)="comments when viewing an SF513 for an IFC.  It also corrects the situation"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",37,1,3,0)="where the extraneous text, ""Clinical Procedure Report"", is displayed"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",37,1,4,0)="inappropriately when performing a detailed display."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",38,0)="43 SEQ #38^3050611^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",38,1,0)="^^3^3^3050611"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",38,1,1,0)="Modify Consult/Request Completion Time Statistics process to take into "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",38,1,2,0)="consideration when the consult was completed the same day as the request "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",38,1,3,0)="date."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",39,0)="37 SEQ #39^3050905^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",39,1,0)="^^2^2^3050905"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",39,1,1,0)="See the National Patch Module for the details of enhancements included in "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",39,1,2,0)="this patch."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",40,0)="39 SEQ #40^3050905^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",40,1,0)="^^1^1^3050905"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",40,1,1,0)="LIST MANAGER ALLOWS FORWARDING USING TERMINATED USER"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",41,0)="45 SEQ #41^3060213^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",41,1,0)="^^2^2^3060213"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",41,1,1,0)="This patch corrects a situation where the Significant Finding for a"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",41,1,2,0)="consult is not stored."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",42,0)="49 SEQ #42^3060410^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",42,1,0)="^^2^2^3060410"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",42,1,1,0)="This patch adds a new Kernel look-up screen in support of Orders Data "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",42,1,2,0)="Standardization."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",43,0)="52^3060807^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",43,1,0)="^^1^1^3060807"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",43,1,1,0)="CONSULT/SCHEDULING LINK"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",44,0)="51 SEQ #44^3060824^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",44,1,0)="^^2^2^3060824"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",44,1,1,0)="This patch adds a call to Imaging, at the request of the Imaging "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",44,1,2,0)="package, to allow Imaging to process Consult HL7 messages."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",45,0)="42 SEQ #45^3060923^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",45,1,0)="^^5^5^3060923"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",45,1,1,0)="This patch exports one consult service.  The service will create or "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",45,1,2,0)="replace an entry in the REQUEST SERVICES (#123.5) file.  This patch also "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",45,1,3,0)="modifies an API routine to accept the Service Name as well as the Service "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",45,1,4,0)="IEN as input.  Thes changes are being made at the request of the Home "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",45,1,5,0)="Telehealth Project group."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",46,0)="50 SEQ #46^3070627.232833^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",46,1,0)="^^7^7^3070627"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",46,1,1,0)="This patch corrects group updating to store the appropriate Last Action "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",46,1,2,0)="Taken and to update Inter-Facility Consults at the partnering facility.  "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",46,1,3,0)="It also removes an inappropriate time zone stamp in the display of Consult"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",46,1,4,0)="activities and prevents Services set-up as Inter-Facility from being "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",46,1,5,0)="added as a Related Service to a Consult Procedure.  This patch also "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",46,1,6,0)="provides a list of consults which have the Significant Finding stored as "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",46,1,7,0)="an ampersand."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",47,0)="53 SEQ #47^3070904.220755^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",47,1,0)="^^4^4^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",47,1,1,0)="This patch corrects a couple of printing issues, a consult forwarding"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",47,1,2,0)="issue, an administrative completion issue, and duplicate service names."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",47,1,3,0)="It also adds an additional warning when creating Consult Services and"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",47,1,4,0)="additional information in the Consult documentation."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",48,0)="47 SEQ #48^3070904.223557^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",48,1,0)="^^3^3^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",48,1,1,0)="This patch corrects Consult alerts being sent to users who do not wish to "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",48,1,2,0)="receive them, missing Consult alerts and invalid data displaying on "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",48,1,3,0)="alerts."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",49,0)="55 SEQ #49^3070904.224502^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",49,1,0)="^^2^2^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",49,1,1,0)="This patch modifies alert recipients in certain circumstances.  It also "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",49,1,2,0)="modifies an api used to determine a users update authority."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",50,0)="57 SEQ #50^3070905.012221^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",50,1,0)="^^4^4^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",50,1,1,0)="This build is for patch GMRC*3*57.  The patch creates a new service in "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",50,1,2,0)="123.5 that supports the VA Suicide Hotline."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",50,1,3,0)="One post install routine adds the new serivce and also includes in the "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",50,1,4,0)="sub-service of the All Services grouper."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",51,0)="60 SEQ #51^3080722.143333^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",52,0)="61 SEQ #52^3090420.155229^1"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",52,1,0)="^^4^4^3090420"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",52,1,1,0)="This patch modifies the SF 513 report to allow for a longer "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",52,1,2,0)="Consult Name than 38 characters to print, and the patch also corrects "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",52,1,3,0)="the Completion Time Statistics and Print Completion Time Statistics to"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",52,1,4,0)="print for the actual date entered."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",53,0)="67 SEQ #53^3090422.113355^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",54,0)="58 SEQ #54^3090422.123113^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",54,1,0)="^^7^7^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",54,1,1,0)="This patch makes updates to the IFC Patient Error Report (#201) by "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",54,1,2,0)="including the Ordered Service for first report received at 3 hours, by "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",54,1,3,0)="setting the priority of the SUICIDE HOTLINE Consult messages, and by "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",54,1,4,0)="correcting the ""from"" in the 24 hour report.  This patch also creates two "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",54,1,5,0)="new error reports #702 ""Service is Disabled"" and #703 ""Procedure is "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",54,1,6,0)="Inactive"" to alert the user when a service/procedure is "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",54,1,7,0)="disabled/inactivated by the Consulting Site."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",55,0)="62 SEQ #55^3090623.103637^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",55,1,0)="^^4^4^3090623"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",55,1,1,0)="This patch corrects the Service Consults Schedule-Management "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",55,1,2,0)="Report to allow printing of all services under the Service/Specialty"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",55,1,3,0)="entered regardless of where it falls in the hierarchy.  Help text"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",55,1,4,0)="is also added to menu OPTION - GMRC RPT SD SCH-MGT CONSULTS."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,0)="63 SEQ #56^3090708.145603^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,0)="^^14^14^3090708"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,1,0)="This patch reformats the Consult Service reports (PC, CC, CP, IFC, IR, "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,2,0)="NU, and SC) total section to print the totals like the Consult "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,3,0)="Performance Monitor Report.  Consult Reports (SC, IFC, IR, NU, PI, and "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,4,0)="PR) will now print a total service total line even if the total is "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,5,0)="zero, if the report is ran for an individual service or the grouper and "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,6,0)="for all statuses.  Zero service total lines will not print when the "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,7,0)="report is ran for All Services, but a listing of those services will"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,8,0)="be listed at the end of the report.  In addition, the ""ALL SERVICES"" total"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,9,0)="section will not count a service twice if it can be found in multiple"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,10,0)="groupers.  The patch also corrects the issue where a ""Quit"" was received"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,11,0)="in the middle of the report which also caused incorrect page numbers and"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,12,0)="the down arrow to stop working.  The undefined error at SETUP CONSULT"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,13,0)="SERVICE has been corrected, and an alert issue in Vista has been fixed to"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",56,1,14,0)="allow multiple commands to be performed on the consult alert."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",57,0)="65 SEQ #57^3090828.101547^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,0)="69 SEQ #58^3090828.101556^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,0)="^^22^22^3090828"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,1,0)="CPRS internal ClearQuest ticket 17822. Remedy ticket 292869 "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,2,0)="and 293770. Added comments during Edit/Resubmit action in CPRS GUI are "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,3,0)="not wrapping at 74 characters. As a result, comments are being stored on "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,4,0)="a single node of the Request/Processing Activity multiple in file 123."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,6,0)="Long comments are hard to read in CPRS GUI due to the need to scroll to "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,7,0)="the right to read the entire text.  Also for InterFacility Consults,"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,8,0)="comments of length greater than 255 characters will not transmit via HL7."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,10,0)="This routine will search through ^GMR(123 and reformat comments when the "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,11,0)="following conditions are all true:"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,12,0)="Comment is a result of the Edit/Resubmit process, NOT just Add Comment."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,13,0)="  Comment is longer than 80 characters AND stored on a single global node"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,14,0)="   OR"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,15,0)="  Comment maybe be stored on more than one global node (i.e. user entered "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,16,0)="  carriage returns) but has lines of text exceeding 80 characters"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,18,0)="Routine will create a backup of comments before reformatting in a "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,19,0)="temporary array, ^XTMP(""GMRC_PRE69"",$J).  Temporary array is set to "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,20,0)="expire 45 days from the date of execution."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,21,0)="Routine will also send MailMan to installer containing the global "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",58,1,22,0)="location and text of any comments found prior to being reformatted."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",59,0)="44 SEQ #59^3090831.122945^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",59,1,0)="^^2^2^3090831"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",59,1,1,0)="This patch adds a call to Prosthetics, at the request of the Prosthetics "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",59,1,2,0)="package, to allow Prosthetics to process Consult HL7 messages."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",60,0)="70 SEQ #60^3100223.162457^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",60,1,0)="^^4^4^3100223"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",60,1,1,0)="This patch searches for Consult Results that are attached to the wrong "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",60,1,2,0)="patient record.  A Mailman message is sent to the installer with a report "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",60,1,3,0)="of those records, so they can be evaluated by the site and corrected, if "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",60,1,4,0)="needed."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",61,0)="68 SEQ #61^3101028.133248^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",61,1,0)="^^3^3^3101028"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",61,1,1,0)="This patch corrects an issue which causes an Inter-Facility Consult (IFC)"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",61,1,2,0)="to not transmit correctly to the consulting site and appear as a local"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",61,1,3,0)="consult."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",62,0)="66^3110308.135203^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",62,1,0)="^^1^1^3110308"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",62,1,1,0)="GMRC changes in support of CPRS GUI v28"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",63,0)="64^3110308.13572^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",63,1,0)="^^7^7^3110308"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",63,1,1,0)="This patch stores and provides an audit of the PREVIOUS ATTENTION TO "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",63,1,2,0)="field.  The value is displayed in the Details section of the Consult"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",63,1,3,0)="order.  In Vista, the patch prompts the user with the current ATTENTION "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",63,1,4,0)="value which they are then allowed to change, if needed.  This patch also"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",63,1,5,0)="prevents consults in a status of ""PR"" and consults with unsigned or"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",63,1,6,0)="uncosigned notes from being forwarded to a new service.  The patch also "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",63,1,7,0)="corrects the lock in GMRCGUIA which was missing a time out value."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,0)="71 SEQ #64^3110810.172416^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,0)="^^14^14^3110810"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,1,0)="This patch will address the following 3 items:"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,3,0)="1. In CPRS GUI, users can forward to a tracking only service when they "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,4,0)="   have update authority at the parent level.  However, when using CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,5,0)="   List Manager in VistA, users cannot forward to a tracking only service"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,6,0)="   when they have update authority at the parent level."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,8,0)="2. When users change the SERVICE USAGE of a Consult Service to 'Grouper "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,9,0)="   Only' or 'Disabled', they are not warned when there are any RELATED "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,10,0)="   SERVICES tied to the Consult Service."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,12,0)="3. The Consult/Request Tracking Technical Manual and the Consult/Result"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,13,0)="   Tracking User Manual do not state that the alert CONSULT/REQUEST"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",64,1,14,0)="   UPDATED is sent when a consult is scheduled."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",65,0)="72 SEQ #65^3111128.153053^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",65,1,0)="^^1^1^3111128"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",65,1,1,0)="Tracking Issues"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",66,0)="74 SEQ #66^3121101.115548^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",66,1,0)="^^4^4^3121101"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",66,1,1,0)="This patch searches for Consult Results that are attached to the wrong "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",66,1,2,0)="patient record.  A Mailman message is sent to the installer with a report "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",66,1,3,0)="of those records, so they can be evaluated by the site and corrected, if "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",66,1,4,0)="needed."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",67,0)="46 SEQ #67^3130211.114712^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",67,1,0)="^^5^5^3130211"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",67,1,1,0)="This patch prevents alerts being sent to the user performing the"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",67,1,2,0)="action that generated the alert and makes sure the persons receiving"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",67,1,3,0)="alerts is similar between VistA and CPRS GUI.  It also corrects a"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",67,1,4,0)="word used inappropriately when returning a user's update authority"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",67,1,5,0)="and adds a file lock timeout value where needed."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",68,0)="76 SEQ #68^3130828.161919^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",68,1,0)="^^5^5^3130828"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",68,1,1,0)="This patch corrects the wording in the description for the "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",68,1,2,0)="GMRC RPT PER MON report.  Also, the addition of clarification"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",68,1,3,0)="wording for the Group Update function of Consult Alterts."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",68,1,4,0)="The clarification wording addresses PSPO #2198.  Consults"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",68,1,5,0)="Update Manual is also being updated."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",69,0)="73^3140902.125225^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,0)="82 SEQ #70^3150421.085028^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,0)="^^73^73^3150421"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,1,0)="This patch implements the New Service Request (NSR) 20130715 which masks "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,2,0)="the first 5 digits of the patients social security number with 'X's on "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,3,0)="the Standard Form (SF) 513 Consult Form.  This code modification has been"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,4,0)="reviewed by Patient Safety and the SSN Reduction team because the"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,5,0)="513 has two other unique identifiers (name and DOB)."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,7,0)="This NSR is part of the VistA Intake Program (VIP) which delivers"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,8,0)="VistA modifications developed at sites as class I VistA software."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,10,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,11,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,12,0)="recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,13,0)="potential disruption to users.  This patch should take less than 5 "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,14,0)="minutes to install."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,16,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,17,0)="1.      Choose the PackMan message containing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,18,0)="2.      Choose the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option.  "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,19,0)="3.      From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,20,0)="the Installation Menu.  From this menu, you may elect to use the "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,21,0)="following options. When prompted for the INSTALL NAME enter GMRC*3.0*"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,22,0)="a.      Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,23,0)="message of any routines exported with this patch. It will not backup any "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,24,0)="other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,25,0)="b.      Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,26,0)="allow you to view all changes that will be made when this patch is "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,27,0)="installed.  It compares all components of this patch (routines, DDs, "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,28,0)="templates, etc.).c.      Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,29,0)=" allow you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,30,0)="transport global."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,31,0)="to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,32,0)="4. From the Installation Menu, select the Install Package(s) option "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,33,0)="   and choose the patch to install."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,34,0)="5. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,35,0)="   NO//'"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,36,0)="      This patch does not require logons to be inhibited."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,38,0)="6. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,39,0)="   and Protocols? NO//' "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,40,0)="      This patch does not require any items to be disabled."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,42,0)="Routine Information:"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,43,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,44,0)="GMRCP5D"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,47,0)="User Information:  "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,48,0)="  Entered By  :   DOUGLAS HALL         Date Entered  :   DEC  15,2015"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,49,0)="  Completed By:                        Date Completed:   "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,50,0)="  Released By :                        Date Released : "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,53,0)="Routine Information:"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,54,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,57,0)="Routine Name: GMRCP5D"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,58,0)=" Description of Changes:"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,59,0)="  Before"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,60,0)="  *****************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,61,0)="  .D BLD(""HDR"",SUB,1,0,GMRCSN)"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,62,0)="  *****************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,63,0)="  After"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,64,0)="  *****************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,65,0)="  .D BLD(""HDR"",SUB,1,0,""XXX-XX-""_$P(GMRCSN,""-"",2,3)"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,66,0)="  *****************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,67,0)="  End of Differences"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,70,0)="=========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,71,0)="User Information:  "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,72,0)="  Entered By  :   HALL,DOUGLAS         Date Entered  :   JAN 15,2015"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",70,1,73,0)="  Completed By:                        Date Completed:   "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",71,0)="75 SEQ #71^3150428.173709^17"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",72,0)="85 SEQ #72^3160105.13464^54"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",72,1,0)="^^2^2^3160105"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",72,1,1,0)="Remove diagnosis code validation from processing of new and edit/resubmit "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",72,1,2,0)="consult orders."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",73,0)="81^3160310.165911^54"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",73,1,0)="^^2^2^3160310"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",73,1,1,0)="Handles the GMRC portion of changing EARLIEST DATE in 123 to CLINICIALLY "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",73,1,2,0)="INDICATED DATE."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",74,0)="80^3160407.160229^54"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",75,0)="83 SEQ #75^3160504.130104^54"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",75,1,0)="^^2^2^3160504"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",75,1,1,0)="Implement the NEW style AG cross-reference in the REQUEST/CONSULTATION "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",75,1,2,0)="file 123 for all entries that do not have an appointment scheduled."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",76,0)="86 SEQ #76^3170427.170315^54"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",77,0)="90 SEQ #78^3170830.164932^54"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",77,1,0)="^^2^2^3170830"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",77,1,1,0)="Added a call to Health Management Platform (HMP) API to initiate an "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",77,1,2,0)="unsolicited sync action to send a comment as it is added to the consult."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",78,0)="89 SEQ #81^3180403.153156^54"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",78,1,0)="^^4^4^3180403"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",78,1,1,0)="The Consult Closure Tool allows users to track consults, associated "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",78,1,2,0)="follow-up appointments, and associated progress notes.  Consults may be "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",78,1,3,0)="closed interactively.  A consult/note report may be printed.  A CPRS team "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",78,1,4,0)="may be updated."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",79,0)="92 SEQ #82^3180403.154709^54"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",79,1,0)="^^4^4^3180403"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",79,1,1,0)="This patch corrects a hard error that continues to occur with "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",79,1,2,0)="Inter-Facility Consults.  The background routine GMRCIBKG has been "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",79,1,3,0)="changed to return the correct Station Number so that Inter-Facility "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",79,1,4,0)="Consults processes correctly. "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",80,0)="91 SEQ #83^3180601.150744^54"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",80,1,0)="^^2^2^3180601"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",80,1,1,0)="Adds override mechanism for Send additional alerts on consult comments. "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",80,1,2,0)="Released with OR*3*452."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,0)="98^3180601.155053^54"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,0)="^^258^258^3180601"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,1,0)="This patch fixes a data integrity issue related to the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,3,0)="1. I16857061FY18 - If a scheduler makes or cancels an appointment for a "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,4,0)="                   consult and the current time ends in a zero (like "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,5,0)="                   9:40), then the event recorded in the consult will"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,6,0)="                   display at the end of the consult event history instead"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,7,0)="                   of in sequence."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,9,0)="This issue requires a fix to repair existing data effected by the issue."
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,10,0)="This patch is bundled with a Scheduling patch that addresses this and "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,11,0)="other issues. Below is a list of all the applications involved in this"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,12,0)="bundle along with their patch number:"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,14,0)="   APPLICATION/VERSION                                   PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,15,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,16,0)="   SCHEDULING (SD) V. 5.3                                SD*5.3*679"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,17,0)="   CONSULT/REQUEST TRACKING (GMRC) V. 3.0                GMRC*3.0*98"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,19,0)="Patch Components"
^DIC(9.4,44,22,3,"PAH",81,1,20,0)="================"
