^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,1,0)="Patch DG*5.3*172, which is included in the Clinical Information Resource"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,2,0)="Network (CIRN) Pre-implementation software Version 0.5 release, contains"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,3,0)="two components."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,4,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,5,0)="First, the patch provides a partial Data Dictionary (DD) update that adds"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,6,0)="two new fields to the PATIENT file (#2). These new fields are listed"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,7,0)="below."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,8,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,9,0)="     991.06     CMOR ACTIVITY SCORE"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,10,0)="     991.07     SCORE CALCULATION DATE"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,11,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,12,0)="These fields facilitate the functionality of the CIRN software utility,"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,13,0)="Start/Restart CMOR Score Calculation [RGCIRN CMOR START] option, which"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,14,0)="calculates a metric used for determining the CIRN Master of Record (CMOR)"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,15,0)="site. This metric is based on patient activity at the site for the present"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,16,0)="Fiscal Year (FY) plus the prior two FYs. In essence, the software reviews"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,17,0)="indicators of patient activity and assigns points for activity. The result"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,18,0)="is a standard measurement that the system can utilize in determining the"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,19,0)="CMOR site for each patient."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,20,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,21,0)="Second, the patch delivers the utilities related to the MARITAL STATUS"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,22,0)="file (#11) and RELIGION file (#13) clean-up during the implementation"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,23,0)="phase. The utilities (1) analyze the MARITAL STATUS and RELIGION files for"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,24,0)="non-standard entries, (2) allow the user to specify, for each non-standard"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,25,0)="entry, which standard entry should be mapped with associated patients,"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,26,0)="(3) actually re-point the associated patients to the standard entries,"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,27,0)="(4) delete the non-standard entries after re-pointing, and (5) delete the"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,28,0)="files, templates, and user options after the clean-up process has been"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,29,0)="completed. A description of the MARITAL STATUS and RELIGION files clean-up"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,30,0)="follows."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,31,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,32,0)="Analysis Step:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,33,0)="When the patch is first installed, an analysis step is automatically run."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,34,0)="This analysis step reviews all files and fields on the local system that"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,35,0)="point to the MARITAL STATUS and RELIGION files. The resultant analysis"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,36,0)="data is then stored in a temporary file, the MARITAL/RELIGION CONVERSION"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,37,0)="file (# 390.1), for later processing. See the conversion step for more"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,38,0)="information on this later process."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,39,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,40,0)="The second part of the analysis reviews the MARITAL STATUS and RELIGION"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,41,0)="files. It adds standard entries to these files that are missing and"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,42,0)="searches for non-standard entries. This analysis data is also stored in a"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,43,0)="temporary file, the MARITAL/RELIGION MAPPING file (# 390.2), for later"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,44,0)="processing. See the mapping step for more information on this later"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,45,0)="process."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,46,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,47,0)="Mapping Step:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,48,0)="Any non-standard entries found during the analysis step must be mapped to"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,49,0)="a valid standard entry. This information is used during the conversion"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,50,0)="step to map patients who are associated with the non-standard entries."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,51,0)="There are two menu options in the CIRN Pre-Implementation Menu [RGPR"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,52,0)="PRE-IMP MENU] for mapping these entries."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,53,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,54,0)="     Marital Status File - Map Non-Standard Entries"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,55,0)="          [DG172 PRE-IMP MAR STAT MAP]"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,56,0)="     Religion File - Map Non-Standard Entries"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,57,0)="          [DG172 PRE-IMP RELIGION MAP]"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,58,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,59,0)="The mapping data designated by the user is then stored in File #390.2."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,60,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,61,0)="Conversion Step:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,62,0)="After the mapping of non-standard entries is complete, a conversion"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,63,0)="process is run which re-points non-standard entries to the designated"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,64,0)="standard entries. The options, also in the CIRN Pre-Implementation Menu,"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,65,0)="to begin and stop the conversion process are listed below."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,66,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,67,0)="     Begin Religion/Marital Status Conversion"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,68,0)="          [DG172 PRE-IMP START CONVERSION]"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,69,0)="     Stop Religion/Marital Status Conversion"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,70,0)="          [DG172 PRE-IMP STOP CONVERSION]"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,71,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,72,0)="The conversion process will update each file/field that points to the"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,73,0)="MARITAL STATUS and RELIGION files based on the analysis data stored in"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,74,0)="File #390.1."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,75,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,76,0)="As the conversion process is running, the progress is stored in two files."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,77,0)="The first File # 390.1 stores the last entry processed for each file/field"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,78,0)="that needs to be converted. As each file/field is converted, it is flagged"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,79,0)="as finished."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,80,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,81,0)="The second File #390.2 stores the number of times a non-standard entry was"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,82,0)="found and converted across all files/fields."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,83,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,84,0)="After the conversion process is complete, an e-mail message is generated"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,85,0)="and delivered to the user of the Begin Religion/Marital Status Conversion"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,86,0)="option. The message reports the number of conversions that took place for"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,87,0)="each non-standard entry."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,88,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,89,0)="Un-Install Step:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,90,0)="After the conversion is finished, the two temporary files, File #390.1 and"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,91,0)="File #390.2, are deleted along with the non-standard entries from the"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,92,0)="MARITAL STATUS and RELIGION files. Associated templates and menu options"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,93,0)="are also deleted."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,94,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,95,0)="The complete CIRN Pre-Implementation Menu, prior to conversion, is listed"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,96,0)="below."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,97,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,98,0)="Select CIRN Pre-Implementation Menu Option:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,99,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,100,0)="     Pseudo-SSN Report"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,101,0)="     Eligibility Code Files Report"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,102,0)="     Marital Status File - Map Non-Standard Entries"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,103,0)="     Religion File - Map Non-Standard Entries"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,104,0)="     Begin Religion/Marital Status Conversion"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,105,0)="     Stop Religion/Marital Status Conversion"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,106,0)="     CIRN Master of Record Menu ..."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,107,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,108,0)="The following options will be deleted after the conversion is completed."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,109,0)="     Marital Status File - Map Non-Standard Entries"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,110,0)="     Religion File - Map Non-Standard Entries"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,111,0)="     Begin Religion/Marital Status Conversion"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",102,1,112,0)="     Stop Religion/Marital Status Conversion"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",103,0)="199 SEQ #180^2981026^1"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",104,0)="194 SEQ #181^2981104^1"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,0)="^^1^1^2981104"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",104,1,1,0)="See National Patch Module"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",105,0)="189^2981104^1"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",105,1,0)="^^3^3^2981104"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",105,1,1,0)="This build is part of the overall patch SD*5.3*149, and provides the"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",105,1,2,0)="capability to capture GAF scores as part of the Census record and a call"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",105,1,3,0)="to send GAF data to the Mental Health package from the scan forms."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",106,0)="198 SEQ #183^2981105^1"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,0)="^^1^1^2981105"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",106,1,1,0)="SEE NATIONAL PATCH MODULE FOR DESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",107,0)="193 SEQ #184^2981112^1"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,0)="^^1^1^2981112"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",107,1,1,0)="See National Patch Module"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",108,0)="147^2981125^1"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,0)="^^2^2^2981214^"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,1,0)="See National Patch Module for description of changes included in this"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",108,1,2,0)="patch."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",109,0)="132 SEQ #186^2981214^1"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,0)="^^6^6^2981214"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,1,0)="This patch will change the POST-KOREAN END DATE (#.05) and BRIEF  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,2,0)="DESCRIPTION (#20) fields in the PERIOD OF SERVICE (#21) file to"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,3,0)="prevent overlapping with VIETNAM ERA period of service."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,5,0)="The END DATE (#.05) field will be changed from 8/4/1964 to 2/27/1961"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",109,1,6,0)="and the BRIEF DESCRIPTION (#20) field will be changed to 2/1/55-2/27/61."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",110,0)="175 SEQ #187^2981214^1"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",110,1,0)="^^2^2^2981214"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",110,1,1,0)="The changes included in this patch are described in the description"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",110,1,2,0)="of patch DG*5.3*175 in the National Patch Module."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,0)="210 SEQ #188^2981214^1"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,0)="^^13^13^2981214"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,1,0)="This patch updates the PTF CENSUS DATE File (#45.86) for the first"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,2,0)="quarter of FY 1999 (10/1/1998-12/31/1998).  The closeout date for this"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,3,0)="census is 1/15/1999."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,5,0)="The DATE(#.01), CLOSEOUT DATE (#.02), OK TO XMIT PTF TRANSACTIONS (#.03),"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,6,0)="CURRENTLY ACTIVE?(#.04), and CENSUS PERIOD  START DATE (#.05) fields in"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,7,0)="the PTF CENSUS DATE file (#45.86)  will be updated as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,9,0)=" DATE: DEC 31, 1998                      "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,10,0)=" CLOSEOUT DATE: JAN 15, 1999"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,11,0)=" OK TO XMIT PTF TRANSACTIONS: MAR 31, 1997"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,12,0)=" CURRENTLY ACTIVE?: YES                "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",111,1,13,0)=" CENSUS PERIOD START DATE: OCT 01, 1998"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",112,0)="211 SEQ #189^2981214^1"
