^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",641,1,0)="^^4^4^3100818"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",641,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",641,1,2,0)="MPI SUPPORT FOR JOINT VA/DOD MEDICAL CENTER  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",641,1,3,0)="Refer to patch DG*5.3*821 in the FORUM Patch Module for a complete"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",641,1,4,0)="description."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",642,0)="661^3100901.114315^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",643,0)="799 SEQ #731^3100902.134905^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",643,1,0)="^^2^2^3100902"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",643,1,1,0)="Modifications to Patient Registration to prevent the 'Edit a Means Test'"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",643,1,2,0)="prompt if the on file MT belongs to another site."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",644,0)="817 SEQ #732^3101004.165416^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",644,1,0)="^^4^4^3101004"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",644,1,1,0)=" This patch will allow a PTF record for a FEE BASIS patient with a means"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",644,1,2,0)=" test status of ""Required"" to be closed and transmitted to Austin. It will"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",644,1,3,0)=" also allow setting of 501 transmissions flag for PTF's with more than 25"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",644,1,4,0)=" records."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",645,0)="823 SEQ #733^3101019.111703^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",645,1,0)="^^2^2^3101019"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",645,1,1,0)="The patch is to fix an error with the IF statement logic in the Vista "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",645,1,2,0)="PIMS VAFHAPV1 API."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",646,0)="828 SEQ #734^3101028.172504^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",646,1,0)="^^1^1^3101028"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",646,1,1,0)="Cannot view patient registration data for patient on LINUX OS."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",647,0)="833^3110104.142753^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",647,1,0)="^^1^1^3110104"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",647,1,1,0)="2010 Means Test Threshold Updates"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",648,0)="825 SEQ #736^3110127.091105^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",648,1,0)="^^3^3^3110127"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",648,1,1,0)="SUPPORT FOR NATIONAL HEALTH INFORMATION EXCHANGE"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",648,1,2,0)="Refer to patch DG*5.3*825 in the FORUM Patch Module for a complete"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",648,1,3,0)="description."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",649,0)="754^3110308.134908^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",650,0)="839 SEQ #738^3110311.101054^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",650,1,0)="^^3^3^3110311"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",650,1,1,0)=" This patch will change the PTF(Patient Treatment File) Census "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",650,1,2,0)=" closeout date from the 14th day of the month following the"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",650,1,3,0)=" census date to the 7th."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",651,0)="773 SEQ #739^3110314.104831^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",651,1,0)="^^3^3^3110314"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",651,1,1,0)="This patch prevents registration from updating the IVM means test status."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",651,1,2,0)="Please refer to the National Patch Module (NPM) for a full description of"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",651,1,3,0)="this patch."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",652,0)="831 SEQ #740^3110411.113314^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",652,1,0)="^^3^3^3110411"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",652,1,1,0)="This patch will correct the ""before DOB"" on the Potential Catastrophic "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",652,1,2,0)="Edit of Patient Identifying Data alert. It will also add ED observation "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",652,1,3,0)="for API to ask readmit question."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,0)="830 SEQ #741^3110620.174104^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,0)="^^19^19^3110620"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,1,0)="This patch will correct the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,3,0)="The [DG CO-PAY TEST FUTURE LIST] Copay Exempt Test Needing Update "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,4,0)="At Next Appt report menu option is incorrectly including future-appointed "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,5,0)="patients whose latest, expired or soon-to expire Co-pay Exemption Tests "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,6,0)="have been converted by IVM.  These cases need to be excluded from the"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,7,0)="report."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,9,0)="The [DG DEATH ENTRY] Death Entry option is not allowing the entry of a"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,10,0)="time value when entering the date of death."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,12,0)="Patch Components"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,13,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,15,0)="Files & Fields Associated:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,17,0)="File Name (Number)         Field Name (Number)  New/Modified/Deleted"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,18,0)="------------------         -------------------  --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",653,1,19,0)="PATIENT       (2)          DATE OF DEATH (.351)  Modified "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",654,0)="824 SEQ #742^3110808.120946^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",654,1,0)="^^2^2^3110808"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",654,1,1,0)="This patch fixes the listing of a patient on the call list when the patient"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",654,1,2,0)="is scheduled for an appointment in a non-count clinic."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",655,0)="844 SEQ #743^3110829.15552^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",655,1,0)="^^1^1^3110829"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",655,1,1,0)="TREATING SPECIALTY UPDATES"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",656,0)="787 SEQ #744^3110908.095424^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",656,1,0)="^^1^1^3110908"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",656,1,1,0)="DG*5.3*787 patch corrects two SAC (Standards and Conventions) violations."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",657,0)="840^3110919.111544^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",657,1,0)="^^2^2^3110919"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",657,1,1,0)="This patch contains VistA changes to support technology and business "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",657,1,2,0)="changes that are occurring with the implementation of Public Law 111-163."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",658,0)="829^3110923.143553^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,0)="838 SEQ #747^3111115.173433^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,0)="^^55^55^3111115"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,1,0)="This patch has enhancements to the Veterans Health Information Systems "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,2,0)="and Technology Architecture (VistA) system to support technology and "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,3,0)="business changes that are occurring with the implementation of the "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,4,0)="Enrollment System Redesign (ESR) Preferred Facility project, Change "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,5,0)="Request (CR) 9620."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,7,0)="Currently, a Veteran selects a Preferred Facility (PF) at the time of "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,8,0)="application for enrollment. The Preferred Facility information is rarely "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,9,0)="updated by the Veteran and is not linked to the location where the "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,10,0)="Veteran actually receives care. As a result, the value of the preferred "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,11,0)="facility assignment is limited. CR 9620 specifies changes needed in the "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,12,0)="way that a Veteran's Preferred Facility is entered and stored in ESR and "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,13,0)="VistA. These changes are necessitated by the requirements of the "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,14,0)="Veterans Benefit Handbook Project."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,17,0)="***NOTE***"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,18,0)="This patch needs to be released and loaded at the same time as ESR 3.5."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,21,0)="This patch modifies the Registration v5.3 application as described below:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,23,0)="1. Modify VistA to lock the Preferred Facility to prevent users from "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,24,0)="changing the field once ESR has assigned it."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,26,0)="2. Modify VistA to display to a VistA user the following help text when "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,27,0)="a VistA user attempts to edit the Preferred Facility field."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,29,0)="    ""Preferred Facility can only be edited/modified by an ESR user, "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,30,0)="     please contact HEC to request changes/edits"""
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,32,0)="3. Modify VistA to upload SOURCE DESIGNATION from ESR. Source "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,33,0)="Designation field (#27.03) is automatically assigned by the ESR or VistA"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,34,0)="system and is a new field in the PATIENT file (#2). Valid Source"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,35,0)="Designation's are:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,36,0)="        a. V = VistA"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,37,0)="        b. E = ESR"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,38,0)="        c. PA = PCP Active"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,39,0)="        d. PI = PCP Inactive"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,41,0)="4. Modify VistA to allow a user to ONLY change Preferred Facility if a"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,42,0)="veteran's PF Source Designation is PCP Inactive (PI) or VistA (V)."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,44,0)="5. Modify VistA to trigger a Z07 HL7 message to be sent to ESR when a "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,45,0)="Preferred Facility has been assigned/modified."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,47,0)="6. Modify VistA to store the Preferred Facility and associated Source"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,48,0)="Designation in the Patient file (#2). If VistA receives a Z11 HL7 "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,49,0)="message with Preferred Facility, display what ESR sent in the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,50,0)="Enrollment [DGEN PATIENT ENROLLMENT] menu.  If no Z11 has been received, "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,51,0)="display the most recent Preferred Facility assigned."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,53,0)="7. Preferred Facility shall be changed to a required field and must be "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,54,0)="entered by a VistA user when the veteran is first registered/enrolled in "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",659,1,55,0)="the VA Medical Center."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",660,0)="834 SEQ #748^3111212.151418^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",660,1,0)="^^11^11^3111212"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",660,1,1,0)="1. This patch introduces an additional check on the Dependent's Effective"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",660,1,2,0)="Date when entering a new dependent using the Spouse/Dependent Add (""DA"")"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",660,1,3,0)="protocol on the Family Demographic Data, Screen <8> in the Load/Edit"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",660,1,4,0)="Patient Data (DG LOAD PATIENT DA TA) option on the Registration Menu."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",660,1,5,0)="This check will prevent the effective date from being prior to the"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",660,1,6,0)="Veteran's Date of Birth."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",660,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",660,1,8,0)="2. This patch adjust's a check introduced with DG*5.3*799 which was to"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",660,1,9,0)="prevent sites from editing MT's through the registration menu's that they"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",660,1,10,0)="don't own.  The original check did not differentiate between parent and"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",660,1,11,0)="divisions of the parent."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",661,0)="848^3111215.12505^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",662,0)="836^3120323.125234^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",662,1,0)="^^2^2^3120323"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",662,1,1,0)="Distributes API's for Patient Record Flag retrival in support of"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",662,1,2,0)="High Risk Mental Health Initiative"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",663,0)="797^3120329.183625^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",663,1,0)="^^1^1^3120329"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",663,1,1,0)="Military Service Data Sharing (MSDS) project"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",664,0)="837 SEQ #752^3120423.142248^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",664,1,0)="^^4^4^3120423"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",664,1,1,0)="MESSAGING ENHANCEMENTS FOR NEW FIELDS"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",664,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",664,1,3,0)="Refer to patch DG*5.3*837 in the FORUM Patch Module for a complete"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",664,1,4,0)="description."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",665,0)="845 SEQ #753^3120829.110009^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",665,1,0)="^^2^2^3120829"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",665,1,1,0)="This patch will add two new entries to the HL LOGICAL LINK (#870)"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",665,1,2,0)="file.  The entries are for two new vendors, Authentidate and Cardiocom."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",666,0)="856 SEQ #754^3120829.113158^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",666,1,0)="^^4^4^3120829"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",666,1,1,0)="TREATING FACILITY LIST (#391.91) FILE ISSUES"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",666,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",666,1,3,0)="Refer to patch DG*5.3*856 in the FORUM Patch Module for a complete"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",666,1,4,0)="description."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",667,0)="841^3120829.1144^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",668,0)="842^3120829.114523^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",668,1,0)="^^3^3^3120829"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",668,1,1,0)="This patch contains VistA changes to support technology and business"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",668,1,2,0)="changes that are occurring with the implementation of Pension Data "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",668,1,3,0)="Sharing."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",669,0)="832 SEQ #757^3121115.110452^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",669,1,0)="^^7^7^3121115"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",669,1,1,0)="1. Modify search to insure that Secondary Diagnosis Codes 10-13 in"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",669,1,2,0)="   Patient Treatment File (PTF) will be searched when running option"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",669,1,3,0)="   'Diagnostic Code PTF Record Search'."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",669,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",669,1,5,0)="2. XINDEX errors caused by $N(ext) command in cross reference triggers in"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",669,1,6,0)="   Patient Movement File (#405) which are in violation of SACC"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",669,1,7,0)="   (Standards & Conventions Committee) standards."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",670,0)="851^3121213.112907^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",670,1,0)="^^3^3^3121213"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",670,1,1,0)="This patch contains VistA changes to support technology and business"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",670,1,2,0)="changes that are occurring with the implementation of Permanent"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",670,1,3,0)="Address Verification."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",671,0)="860^3130103.113847^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",672,0)="846 SEQ #760^3130304.164718^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",672,1,0)="^^11^11^3130304"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",672,1,1,0)="This patch addresses 3 issues:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",672,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",672,1,3,0)="There is a misspelled word in data dictionary help text in the PATIENT "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",672,1,4,0)="File (#2) "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",672,1,5,0)="for CANCELLATION REMARKS (#.98) "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",672,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",672,1,7,0)="The NAME field of the PATIENT TYPE File (#391) is allowed to be changed."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",672,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",672,1,9,0)="There is a misspelled word in database help text in the PATIENT TYPE File "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",672,1,10,0)="(#391) "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",672,1,11,0)="for EDIT MISSING DATA? (#102) "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",673,0)="866 SEQ #761^3130408.144849^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",673,1,0)="^^5^5^3130408"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",673,1,1,0)="Patch DG*5.3*866 addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",673,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",673,1,3,0)="        1.  Pseudo Social Security Number Calculator allows duplicates."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",673,1,4,0)="            This is creating an issue for the New Born Project with"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",673,1,5,0)="            with multiple births and bill processing."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",674,0)="849^3130516.125603^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",674,1,0)="^^1^1^3130516"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",674,1,1,0)="DGPF NEW CAT1 FLAG AND CONVERSION"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",675,0)="870 SEQ #763^3130716.10421^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",675,1,0)="^^4^4^3130716"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",675,1,1,0)="Patch DG*5.3*870 modifies 2 Registration routines to accommodate the new  "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",675,1,2,0)="International Classification of Disease Tenth Revision (ICD10) code "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",675,1,3,0)="structure.  The ICD10 new code structure is being expanded and allowing "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",675,1,4,0)="for letters and numbers to be used."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",676,0)="868 SEQ #764^3130819.1502^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",676,1,0)="^^6^6^3130819"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",676,1,1,0)="Patch DG*5.3*868 addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",676,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",676,1,3,0)="       1.  Inactive International Classification of Diseases (ICD) code "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",676,1,4,0)="           cannot be assigned to Patient Treatment File (PTF)"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",676,1,5,0)="           due to system sending date and time of movement."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",676,1,6,0)="           Date is only required information."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",677,0)="857 SEQ #765^3130823.110539^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",677,1,0)="^^3^3^3130823"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",677,1,1,0)="VIC 4.02 MPI INTEGRATION"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",677,1,2,0)="Refer to patch DG*5.3*857 in the FORUM Patch Module for a complete"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",677,1,3,0)="description."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",678,0)="864^3130829.111129^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",679,0)="861 SEQ #767^3130829.111145^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",679,1,0)="^^10^10^3130829"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",679,1,1,0)="This patch addresses 3 issues:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",679,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",679,1,3,0)="1. Medicaid inconsistency check isn't working when a field consistency"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",679,1,4,0)="   edit check that is processed prior to it is set to DON'T CHECK. "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",679,1,5,0)="2. When the SOCIAL SECURITY NUMBER field (#.09) of the PATIENT file (#2) "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",679,1,6,0)="   is updated, the PRIMARY LONG ID field (#.363) and the PRIMARY SHORT ID"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",679,1,7,0)="   field (#.364) of the PATIENT file (#2) are not updated accordingly. "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",679,1,8,0)="3. An undefined error is occurring during an attempt to close a Patient"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",679,1,9,0)="   Treatment File (PTF) (#45) record via LOAD/EDIT PTF DATA [DG LOAD "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",679,1,10,0)="   PATIENT DATA] Option."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",680,0)="863 SEQ #768^3130905.13014^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",680,1,0)="^^3^3^3130905"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",680,1,1,0)="MASTER VETERAN INDEX VISTA ISSUES - ITERATION 10"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",680,1,2,0)="Refer to patch DG*5.3*863 in the FORUM Patch Module for a complete"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",680,1,3,0)="description."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",681,0)="847 SEQ #769^3131023.161747^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",681,1,0)="^^5^5^3131023"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",681,1,1,0)="This patch addresses 4 issues:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",681,1,2,0)="In PATIENT file (#2), the trigger is not working correctly for"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",681,1,3,0)="fields ADDRESS CHANGE SOURCE (#.119), CELLULAR NUMBER CHANGE "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",681,1,4,0)="SOURCE (#.1311), PAGER NUMBER CHANGE SOURCE (#.1313), and EMAIL ADDRESS"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",681,1,5,0)="CHANGE SOURCE (#.137)."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,0)="867^3131212.141029^17"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,0)="^^348^348^3131212"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,1,0)="                           ***NOTICE***"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,2,0)="Users should be made aware that processing of Newborn claims must ONLY be"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,3,0)="entered in VistA. No entry in FBCS should be performed."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,4,0)="                           ***********"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,5,0)="This patch, along with FB*3.5*146 and IB*2.0*499, is being released as a"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,6,0)="bundle, and all three will be automatically installed in the correct order."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,8,0)="This patch has enhancements that extend the capabilities of the Veterans"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,9,0)="Health Information Systems and Technology Architecture (VistA) Patient"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,10,0)="Registration system (DG), Fee Basis System (FB), and Integrated Billing"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,11,0)="(IB)."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,13,0)="Below is a list of all the applications involved in this project along with"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,14,0)="their patch number:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,16,0)="    APPLICATION/VERSION                                   PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,17,0)="    ---------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,18,0)=" PATIENT REGISTRATION (DG) V 5.3                       DG*5.3*867"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,19,0)=" FEE BASIS (FB) V 3.5                                  FB*3.5*146"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,20,0)=" INTEGRATED BILLING (IB) 2.0                           IB*2.0*499"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,22,0)="The patches (DG*5.3*867, FB*3.5*146, and IB*2.0*499) are being released in the"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,23,0)="Kernel Installation and Distribution System (KIDS) multi-build distribution"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,24,0)="NEWBORN DG FB IB BUNDLE 1.0"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,26,0)="The purpose of the Caregivers: Newborn Claims Processing Enhancement Project"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,27,0)="is to enhance VistA Fee Basis application in support of compliance with"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,28,0)="Public Law 111-163, the Caregiver and Veterans Omnibus Health Services Act"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,29,0)="of 2010. This law makes changes to sections of Title 38, United States Code"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,30,0)="to furnish health care services to a newborn child of a Woman Veteran who"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,31,0)="is receiving maternity care furnished by the Department of Veterans Affairs"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,32,0)="(VA) for not more than seven days after the birth of the child."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,34,0)="The scope of these enhancements is to capture information on healthcare"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,35,0)="services provided to newborn children of Women Veterans. Affected functions"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,36,0)="include eligibility determination, enrollment and registration, documentation"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,37,0)="of referrals and authorization for care, claims processing, and payment. Only"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,38,0)="modification to the Fee Basis (FB) and the Registration (DG) packages are"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,39,0)="necessary to meet the requirements of this enhancement. The Integrated"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,40,0)="Billing (IB) Patch is included to provide required data for the Fee Basis"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,41,0)="install to reference."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,44,0)="The primary purpose of this enhancement is to allow the Electronic Filing of"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,45,0)="Newborn claims."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,47,0)="Functional Description"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,48,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,49,0)="The following features and functions have been added to the Fee Basis workflow"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,50,0)="process applying to both Civil Hospital and Medical Fee:"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,52,0)=" 1. A new Patient Type of NEWBORN OF VETERAN has been added to the TYPE OF"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,53,0)="PATIENT file (#391). This new selection will be available on Registration"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,54,0)="Screen <7>."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,56,0)=" 2. A sponsor is required for all Newborns determined by having the DOB less"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,57,0)="than one (1) year from the present date. An inconsistency check has been added"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,58,0)="to check the presence of a sponsor. If an inconsistency is found the"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,59,0)="inconsistency check will prompt the user to return to Screen <15> in"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,60,0)="registration to enter a Sponsor."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,62,0)=" 3. All Sponsors for Newborns must be listed as eligible for care. An"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,63,0)="inconsistency check will check the status of the Sponsors Eligibility. The"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,64,0)="check will trigger if the Sponsor has no Eligibility status."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,66,0)="All other statuses (i.e. Pending Verification, Verified, and Pending"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,67,0)="Re-verification) are acceptable."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,69,0)=" 4. Fee Authorization dates associated with Newborns have checks in place to"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,70,0)="not allow Authorization dates that fall outside the accepted range of Newborn"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,71,0)="Authorization. The range is DOB to DOB+7. The system will warn the user and"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,72,0)="not accept an Authorization date that falls outside the appropriate range for"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,73,0)="a Newborn."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,75,0)=" 5. When a Veteran Mother of a Sponsored Newborn is reviewed in the"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,76,0)="Registration screens, Screen <15> will display the Newborn(s), with the"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,77,0)="additional header of ""Sponsored Newborn""."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,79,0)=" 6. The FAMILY PREFIX ""NB Newborn of Vet"" has been added to the Help text in"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,80,0)="the FAMILY PREFIX field (#.03) in the SPONSOR RELATIONSHIP file (#355.81)"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,82,0)=" 8. The following default values were added when entering a Newborn with a"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,83,0)="date of birth of less than one (1) year from present date. Defaults will "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,84,0)="only  be assigned when specified screens are accessed during the"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,85,0)="registration process: PATIENT DATA, SCREEN <2> Marital field is defaulted"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,86,0)="to NEVER MARRIED. APPLICANT/SPOUSE EMPLOYMENT DATA, SCREEN <4> Status"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,87,0)="field is defaulted to NOT EMPLOYED. FAMILY DEMOGRAPHIC DATA, SCREEN <8>"
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,88,0)="Married Last Year field is defaulted to NO."
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,47,22,5.9,"PAH",682,1,90,0)=" "
