^DIC(9.4,48,0)="SCHEDULING^SD^APPOINTMENTS,PROFILES,LETTERS,AMIS REPORTS"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,0)="^^17^17^2960626^^^^"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,1,0)="The DHCP Scheduling package allows a user to Schedule appointments for"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,2,0)="the following types of appointments:"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,3,0)="                Scheduled"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,4,0)="                C&P"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,5,0)="                Collateral"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,6,0)="It also allows entry of an unscheduled appointment at any time during a day"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,7,0)="on which the clinic being scheduled into meets.  From these appointments,"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,8,0)="various output reports are produced such as, but not limited to, file room"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,9,0)="list, appointment list, routing slips, letters for cancellations, no-shows,"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,10,0)="and pre-appointment.  There is an additional capability where additional"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,11,0)="clinic stop credits can be directly entered and associated with a particular"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,12,0)="patient and date.  AMIS reporting is handled via a set of extract routines"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,13,0)="that summarize the data found by reading through the appointments and"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,14,0)="additional clinic stops and the 10/10 and unscheduled visits (outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,15,0)="credit given to Admitting/Screening) and storing the information by patient"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,16,0)="and visit date in the OCP File.  The AMIS 223 report and the OPC"
^DIC(9.4,48,1,17,0)="file to be sent to the Austin DPC are generated using this file."
^DIC(9.4,48,4,0)="^9.44PA^44^26"
