^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",215,1,0)="^^1^1^3030417"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",215,1,1,0)="See patch SD*5.3*289 in the NPM for complete information on this patch."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",216,0)="288 SEQ #258^3030430^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,0)="296^3030603^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,0)="^^24^24^3030603"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,1,0)="In response to Policy Board (NLB) comment on the VHA Veterans Equitable"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,2,0)="Resource Allocation (VERA) process, the CBO requests the removal of:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,4,0)="(1) the current restriction that blocks transmission of outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,5,0)="encounters (ACRP) to the National Patient Care Database (NPCD) if a"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,6,0)="veteran's updated financial assessment (Means Test) information is not"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,7,0)="complete, and "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,8,0)="(2) the restriction that blocks the ability to schedule"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,9,0)="future appointments for veterans whose financial assessments need"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,10,0)="updating."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,12,0)="Current policy establishes a requirement to block transmission of "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,13,0)="outpatient encounters (ACRP) to the National Patient Care Database if the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,14,0)="patient's current Means Test status equals ""Required.""  This leads to"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,15,0)="under-reported workload and inaccurate information in national"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,16,0)="databases.  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,18,0)="Software has been implemented which blocks the ability to schedule future "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,19,0)="appointments for veterans whose financial assessment needs updating.  VHA "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,20,0)="Directive 2002-019, dated April 4, 2002, provided guidance to facilities "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,21,0)="on the implementation of the appointment blocking software.  If a "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,22,0)="veteran's financial assessment needs updating, the software prevents the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,23,0)="ability to make future appointments for the veteran.  This restriction "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",217,1,24,0)="shall also be removed at the request of the CBO.  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",218,0)="286^3030604^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",218,1,0)="^^2^2^3030604"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",218,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",218,1,2,0)="ADD STATION NUMBER TO HL7 PRIMARY CARE MESSAGE"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",219,0)="257 SEQ #261^3030715^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",219,1,0)="^^5^5^3030715"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",219,1,1,0)="The visit deletion process allows now to delete a dependent credit/stop visit"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",219,1,2,0)="if the primary stop/code addition visit has to be deleted after all entries"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",219,1,3,0)="are removed."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",219,1,4,0)="The Institution, if passed to PCE, is now accepted and properly filed."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",219,1,5,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",220,0)="291 SEQ #262^3030715^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",220,1,0)="^^7^7^3030715"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",220,1,1,0)="1. A new report may be generated for selected patients from a list of "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",220,1,2,0)="patients entered by their names or SSN. That option was added to the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",220,1,3,0)="existing process of generating reports."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",220,1,4,0)="2. The Summary option was modified to allow the user to specify which Stop "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",220,1,5,0)="Code Pair to include. This modification permits print selection to be limited"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",220,1,6,0)="to the clinic with the selected stop code pair."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",220,1,7,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",221,0)="284 SEQ #263^3030802^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",221,1,0)="^^4^4^3030802"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",221,1,1,0)="1.  Add code '370M' to PCMM HL7 ERROR CODE (#404.472) file."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",221,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",221,1,3,0)="2.  Fix routine SCMCHLR9 allowing '^' to quit 'PCMM Error Transmission "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",221,1,4,0)="    Report' when abundant number of errors can be displayed."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,0)="302 SEQ #265^3030821^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,0)="^^16^16^3030821"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,1,0)="Due to the changes brought in by patch SD*5.3*296, reports are needed to"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,2,0)="identify patients who require a Means Test and who have had encounters "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,3,0)="transmitted with a MT indicator of U.  This patch provides the this"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,4,0)="report."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,6,0)="The new report option is called Encounters Transmitted with MT Status of U"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,7,0)="[SCRPW TRANS MT EQUAL U RPT]. It will be added to the Incomplete Encounter"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,8,0)="Reports [SCENI IEMM REPORTS MENU] menu when this patch is installed."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,9,0)="This report conforms to requirements related to the VERA allocation"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,10,0)="process, where at least one encounter within the Fiscal Year must include"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,11,0)="a valid Means Test status for the patient.  The patient will be included"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,12,0)="on the report only if ALL the patient's encounters within the date range"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,13,0)="selected have a current MT Status (at encounter Transmission) equal to"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,14,0)="Required.  This will focus the list on patients who have no valid MT"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,15,0)="status in the National Patient Care Database (NPCD) for the date range"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",222,1,16,0)="chosen.  The current FY is the suggested date range for this report."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,0)="300^3030912^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,0)="^^39^39^3030912"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,1,0)="This is the Phase I patch of the Transitional Pharmacy Benefit Project"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,2,0)="(TPB). This project provides functionality for the ""Medication Prescribed "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,3,0)="by Non-VA Physicians"" to accommodate the Veterans Health Administration "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,4,0)="(VHA) Directive 2003-047 that allows Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,5,0)="to furnish medications from non-VA physicians.  It mandates that for"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,6,0)="eligible veterans that meet certain criteria, VHA will fill prescriptions"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,7,0)="written by non-VA physicians and dentists. To determine eligibility, a"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,8,0)="patient must meet the following criteria:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,10,0)="1) The patient must be a veteran."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,12,0)="2) The veteran must be enrolled for VA health care system before July 25, "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,13,0)="2003."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,15,0)="3) Before July 25,2003, the veteran must have requested their first "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,16,0)="   primary care appointment with the VA."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,18,0)="4) The veteran must have no active prescriptions dispensed by the local "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,19,0)="   VHA pharmacy, excluding Supply and Investigational items, for the past "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,20,0)="   485 days from October 22, 2003."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,22,0)="5) The veteran must be waiting more than 30 days for their first "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,23,0)="   appointment with a Primary Care Physician on or after October 22, "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,24,0)="   2003, or the veteran is deemed eligible via an Electronic Wait"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,25,0)="   List/Scheduling extract run at each local site."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,28,0)="When the post-init of the combined build is run, the routines exported in"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,29,0)="patch SD*5.3*300 will scan the PATIENT file (#2) and the SD WAIT LIST"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,30,0)="file (#409.3), and will build a temporary storage global of patients who"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,31,0)="may be eligible for this benefit."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,34,0)="This patch is being sent out as a combined build, along with patch "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,35,0)="PSO*7*145."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,38,0)="For KIDS Build and documentation retrieval information, please refer to "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",223,1,39,0)="patch PSO*7*145."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",224,0)="310 SEQ #267^3030912^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",224,1,0)="^^2^2^3030912"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",224,1,1,0)="This API will return 0,1,-1, depending on whether the patient has an "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",224,1,2,0)="appointment."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",225,0)="283 SEQ #268^3030912^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",225,1,0)="^^1^1^3030912"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",225,1,1,0)="Release III of the Scheduling Replacement APIs."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",226,0)="307 SEQ #269^3030912^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",226,1,0)="^^1^1^3030912"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",226,1,1,0)="See patch SD*5.3*307 in the NPM for complete information on this patch."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,0)="314 SEQ #270^3030912^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,0)="^^22^22^3030912"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,1,0)="This patch releases functionality that provides Outpatient Pharmacy V. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,2,0)="7.0 information about primary care appointments and encounters. In "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,3,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0, when a patient is displayed on the patient "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,4,0)="information screen, and that patient is eligible for the Transitional "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,5,0)="Pharmacy Benefit, that patient's nearest primary care appointment or "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,6,0)="encounter will display. That functionality will begin with the release of "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,7,0)="patch PSO*7*146. The primary care criteria is based on the DSS ID and "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,8,0)="Credit Stop Pairs that were defined in patches SD*5.3*300 and "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,9,0)="PSO*7.0*145. The functionality to provide Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0 this "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,10,0)="information is released in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,11,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,12,0)="A change has also been made to the call Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0 uses "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,13,0)="to determine a default institution and station number, when a patient is "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,14,0)="manually added to the TPB ELIGIBILITY file (#52.91). The default "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,15,0)="institution and station number is currently retrieved from the clinic of "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,16,0)="the nearest scheduled appointment for that patient. The change made in "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,17,0)="this patch is to first look for the nearest primary care appointment, and "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,18,0)="use that clinic to get the default institution and station number. If "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,19,0)="there is no primary care appointment for that patient, then the software "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,20,0)="will look for the nearest appointment, regardless of whether it is a "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,21,0)="primary care appointment, and use that clinic to determine the default "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",227,1,22,0)="institution and station number. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",228,0)="317^3030924^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",229,0)="295^3030924^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",229,1,0)="^^2^2^3030924"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",229,1,1,0)="Please see the National Patch Module for details"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",229,1,2,0)="of the enhancements included in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",230,0)="311 SEQ #274^3031002^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",230,1,0)="^^1^1^3031002"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",230,1,1,0)="See patch SD*5.3*311 in the NPM for complete information on this patch."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",231,0)="316 SEQ #275^3031002^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,0)="292^3031023^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,0)="^^14^14^3031023"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,2,0)="Patches SD*5.3*292 and TIU*1.0*168 combined build."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,4,0)="OQP is interested in gathering data for a performance indicators involving"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,5,0)="Scheduling and TIU. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,7,0)="This patch addresses the indicator; it measures the percentages of "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,8,0)="outpatient encounters in ambulatory care with a completed or amended "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,9,0)="electronic progress notes signed by the primary care provider for that "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,10,0)="encounter. The report identifies the encounter, finds any progress note "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,11,0)="associated with the encounter, it looks at the progress note and reports "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,12,0)="the date the PN was signed by the provider. It then looks at the results "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,13,0)="and reports the encounter as compliant or non compliant based on "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",232,1,14,0)="nationally or locally defined criteria."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",233,0)="303 SEQ #278^3031023^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",233,1,0)="^^11^11^3031023"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",233,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the ENDOFILE error message received in 'Cancel Clinic"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",233,1,2,0)="Availability' [SDCANCEL] when queuing the print job is not performed. It "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",233,1,3,0)="also addresses 'Restore Clinic Availability' [SDRESTORE] when an "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",233,1,4,0)="undefined variable (DH) occurs due to missing appointment patterns for "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",233,1,5,0)="that day of week."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",233,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",233,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",233,1,8,0)="This patch addresses the following NOIS message(s):"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",233,1,9,0)="---------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",233,1,10,0)="CMO-0600-41899   CANCEL CLINIC AVAILABILITY GIVES END OF FILE ERROR"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",233,1,11,0)="MAC-0200-60343   UNDEFINED SYMBOL, DH IN SDUNC ROUTINE."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",234,0)="321 SEQ #279^3031023^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",234,1,0)="^^1^1^3031023"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",234,1,1,0)="This is an emergency patch for the routine SCMSVUT1."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",235,0)="305^3031107^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",236,0)="322 SEQ #281^3031121^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",236,1,0)="^^6^6^3031121"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",236,1,1,0)="This patch fixes a problem with one of the options distributed in patch"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",236,1,2,0)="SD*5.3*292. When users selected to run the [SCRPW PM DETAILED REPORT]"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",236,1,3,0)="PERFORMANCE MONITOR DETAILED REPORT and the users opted to run the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",236,1,4,0)="report for individual providers, the report will fail to generate any"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",236,1,5,0)="information because of a bad reference to one of the arrays in routine "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",236,1,6,0)="SDPMUT2."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",237,0)="290^3031126^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",237,1,0)="^^6^6^3031126"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",237,1,1,0)="This patch will provide patient appointment wait time statistics to the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",237,1,2,0)="National Database in Austin, Tx.  An initial seeding routine will scan"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",237,1,3,0)="patient appointments from 9.01.2002 to present and appointment data"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",237,1,4,0)="meeting specified criteria will be wrapped in a HL7 batch message and"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",237,1,5,0)="transmitted to AAC.  Subsequent, bi-weekly, transmissions will update the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",237,1,6,0)="National Database."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,0)="318 SEQ #283^3031231^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,0)="^^26^26^3031231"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,1,0)="This report was requested in support of the Transitional Pharmacy Benefit "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,2,0)="project. It will be used by each medical center to report the number of "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,3,0)="patients who have rescheduled their primary care appointment until the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,4,0)="medication supplied under the Transitional Pharmacy Benefit program is "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,5,0)="exhausted."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,7,0)="A query is made to the Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0 package to get a list "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,8,0)="of TPB eligible patients for a given date range. From this list, the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,9,0)="patients' appointments are examined to determine if they have cancelled "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,10,0)="or not attended their appointments and then been rebooked to TPB "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,11,0)="associated clinics. If so, their cancellation and rebook details are "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,12,0)="displayed. Otherwise the appointment closest to the report run date is "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,13,0)="shown."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,15,0)="This patch adds a new option, Transitional Pharmacy Benefit Deferred Appt "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,16,0)="Report [SD TRANS RX CANC APPT REPORT] to the Outputs menu [SDOUTPUT]."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,18,0)="Routine SDPHARM1, which provides scheduling information to the Outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,19,0)="Pharmacy V 7.0 package, has been updated to use the new Scheduling "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,20,0)="Application Programmer Interface calls, instead of direct global reads to "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,21,0)="retrieve data from the APPOINTMENT subfile (#2.98) of the PATIENT file "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,22,0)="(#2)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,24,0)="This patch removes the routines SDPBE and SDPHARM which generated "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,25,0)="information on Transitional Pharmacy Benefits Eligibility in an earlier "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",238,1,26,0)="phase of the project and are no longer required."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",239,0)="329 SEQ #285^3040131^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",239,1,0)="^^1^1^3040131"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",239,1,1,0)="ACRP AD HOC REPORT DOES NOT RECOGNIZE PRIMARY DX"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",240,0)="324 SEQ #286^3040302^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",240,1,0)="^^1^1^3040302"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",240,1,1,0)="Undefined variable in Trend of Facilities Report."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,0)="333^3040324^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,0)="^^16^16^3040324"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,1,0)="This patch contains several enhancements and modifications to the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,2,0)="Patient Appointment Information Transmission, originally released in "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,3,0)="patch SD*5.3*290."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,5,0)="   - New components are added to SCH.11, SCH6, and SCH.7 segments of"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,6,0)="     HL7 transmission."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,7,0)="   - The appointment selection logic for update runs has been modified."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,8,0)="   - Rejection error codes have been expanded."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,9,0)="   - Independent reports, reflecting the transmission status, have been "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,10,0)="     developed by AAC and the Messaging and Interface Services Team."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,11,0)="   - New report options added to print Transmission and Acknowledgement"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,12,0)="     Summaries.  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,13,0)="   - Release Notes have been updated with additional, detailed"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,14,0)="     technical information."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,15,0)="   - An expanded 409.6 file will permanently store detailed transmission"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",241,1,16,0)="     information."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",242,0)="293^3040324^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",242,1,0)="^^1^1^3040324"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",242,1,1,0)="Confidential Address Imm"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",243,0)="335 SEQ #289^3040427^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",244,0)="313 SEQ #290^3040427^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",244,1,0)="^^1^1^3040427"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",244,1,1,0)="Rollup of Additional Encounter Performance Measures to AAC."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",245,0)="349 SEQ #291^3040507^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",245,1,0)="^^1^1^3040507"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",245,1,1,0)="This patch includes some modification and fixes to PAIT."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",246,0)="336 SEQ #292^3040521^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",246,1,0)="^^3^3^3040521"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",246,1,1,0)="Fix locking mechanism in SCRPW16 and dis-allow today's date from checkout "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",246,1,2,0)="process.  Also, the Encounter Action Required Report is incorrectly "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",246,1,3,0)="indicating Environmental Contaminants when it should be MST."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",247,0)="323 SEQ #293^3040702^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",247,1,0)="^^2^2^3040702"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",247,1,1,0)="This patch fixes an undefined variable error in option SCENI IEMM ERROR "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",247,1,2,0)="CORRECTION."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",248,0)="330 SEQ #294^3040702^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",248,1,0)="^^3^3^3040702"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",248,1,1,0)="Remove form feed before the each patient appointment letter when printing "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",248,1,2,0)="scheduling letters. Change the state printed in the address to the 2 "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",248,1,3,0)="letter abbreviation."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",249,0)="338 SEQ #295^3040702^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",249,1,0)="^^1^1^3040702"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",249,1,1,0)="Undefined variable error in routine SCRPI01."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",250,0)="337 SEQ #296^3040702^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",250,1,0)="^^1^1^3040702"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",250,1,1,0)="PERFORMANCE MONITOR SUMMARY REPORT ERROR"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",251,0)="301 SEQ #298^3040802^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",251,1,0)="^^1^1^3040802"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",251,1,1,0)="New Scheduling Replacement API"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",252,0)="354 SEQ #299^3040802^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",252,1,0)="^^1^1^3040802"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",252,1,1,0)="REMOVAL OF CHECK OUT PARAMETERS FOR CLINIC PROFILE."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",253,0)="359 SEQ #300^3040802^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",253,1,0)="^^3^3^3040802"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",253,1,1,0)="This patch corrects a problem associated with NOIS ISB-0700-30733 which "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",253,1,2,0)="has error codes in file TRANSMITTED OUTPATIENT ENCOUNTER ERROR CODE file "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",253,1,3,0)="incorrectly marked as VISTA rather than NPCD."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",254,0)="325^3040802^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",255,0)="378 SEQ #302^3040802^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",255,1,0)="^^3^3^3040802"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",255,1,1,0)="Incomplete Encounter Errors still appear on error list after being "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",255,1,2,0)="corrected until user selects Retransmit Encounter.  They should be "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",255,1,3,0)="automatically removed after being corrected."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",256,0)="371 SEQ #303^3040802^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",256,1,0)="^^10^10^3040802"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",256,1,1,0)="Inclusion of additional fields for HL7 message transmissions to AAC. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",256,1,2,0)="The routine SDPMHLS, responsible for creating the structure of the HL7 "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",256,1,3,0)="message, has been modified to allow inclusion of data for "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",256,1,4,0)="progress notes pending signatures and encounters without progress notes."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",256,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",256,1,6,0)="Totals for unique encounter providers and unique stop codes at the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",256,1,7,0)="division level should also now match the sum of the totals for these "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",256,1,8,0)="values of each facility in that division."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",256,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",256,1,10,0)="Also removes reference to 'DSS' in mail group SD PM NOTIFICATION TIU."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",257,0)="365 SEQ #304^3040903^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",257,1,0)="^^2^2^3040903"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",257,1,1,0)="CORRECT 'ASTAT','T' CROSS-REFERENCE IN THE PCMM HL7 TRANSMISSION LOG FILE "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",257,1,2,0)="AND SET THE STATUS FIELD TO 'A'."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",258,0)="375 SEQ #305^3040903^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",259,0)="381 SEQ #306^3040903^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",259,1,0)="^^2^2^3040903"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",259,1,1,0)="Fix form feed problem between report and patient letters when "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",259,1,2,0)="auto-rebooking a single ""No-Show"" appointment."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",260,0)="345 SEQ #307^3040924^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",260,1,0)="^^1^1^3040924"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",260,1,1,0)="D140 Error Code fix."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",261,0)="388 SEQ #308^3041015^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",261,1,0)="^^1^1^3041015"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",261,1,1,0)="DSS Request for FY2005 Stop Codes"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",262,0)="340 SEQ #309^3041015^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",262,1,0)="^^1^1^3041015"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",262,1,1,0)="BAD ADDRESS INDICATOR NEEDS TO STOP PRINTING SCHEDULING LETTERS."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",263,0)="341 SEQ #310^3041015^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",263,1,0)="^^1^1^3041015"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",263,1,1,0)="Fix for 9020 Errors/MST for non-vets."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",264,0)="343 SEQ #311^3041015^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",264,1,0)="^^1^1^3041015"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",264,1,1,0)="FUTURE APPOINTMENTS NOT PRINTING ON ROUTING SLIPS. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",265,0)="351^3041015^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",266,0)="339^3041016^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",266,1,0)="^^1^1^3041016"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",266,1,1,0)="CPT Codes not printing and Error Message Cleanup"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",267,0)="395^3041111^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",268,0)="376 SEQ #314^3041124^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",268,1,0)="^^6^6^3041124"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",268,1,1,0)="Two main purposes of this patch are:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",268,1,2,0)="- inclusion of Combat Veteran and Military History into PAIT"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",268,1,3,0)="- automatic verification of PAIT transmission data via a Forum.S.Server"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",268,1,4,0)="Additionally, several fixes/modifications are included following their "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",268,1,5,0)="identification in NOIS calls."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",268,1,6,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",269,0)="387^3041228^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",270,0)="397 SEQ #316^3050118^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",270,1,0)="^^5^5^3050118"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",270,1,1,0)="1. Correct Wait List Parameter Edit for Service/Specialty for '^'"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",270,1,2,0)="   deletion error."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",270,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",270,1,4,0)="2. Correct Wait List Enter/Edit pointing to different Service/Specialty"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",270,1,5,0)="   after data entry when viewing Inquiry or Report."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",271,0)="396 SEQ #317^3050204^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",271,1,0)="^^1^1^3050204"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",271,1,1,0)="Action required for inpatient appointments."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",272,0)="384 SEQ #318^3050204^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",272,1,0)="^^1^1^3050204"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",272,1,1,0)="ERROR IN SDM0 FOR DIR(0) STRING."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",273,0)="393 SEQ #319^3050204^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",273,1,0)="^^1^1^3050204"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",273,1,1,0)="No Transmitted Data Message."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",274,0)="399 SEQ #320^3050204^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",274,1,0)="^^4^4^3050204"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",274,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",274,1,2,0)="1. UNDEFINED IN WAIT LIST REPORTING"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",274,1,3,0)="2. MUMPS ERROR IN WAIT LIST STAT REPORT"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",274,1,4,0)="3. NULL SUBSCRIPT IN WAIT LIST REPORTING "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",275,0)="409 SEQ #321^3050311^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",275,1,0)="^^3^3^3050311"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",275,1,1,0)="ACRP Report error. CRI1+17^SCRPW45. The report ODPS Outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",275,1,2,0)="Diagnosis/Procedure Code Search generates an error when the ""'"" single "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",275,1,3,0)="quote is entered at the IF: prompt."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",276,0)="357 SEQ #322^3050311^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",276,1,0)="^^4^4^3050311"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",276,1,1,0)="THIS PATCH ADDRESS A PROBLEM WITH THE SCRPW SC VETS AWAITING APPTS "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",276,1,2,0)="REPORT. IF A PATIENT HAS NO DATE ENTERED IN THE PATIENT FILE THIS PATIENT "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",276,1,3,0)="IS INCORRECTLY BEING REPORTED ON THIS REPORT. A CORRECTION WAS MADE TO "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",276,1,4,0)="CORRECT THIS ERROR."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",277,0)="379 SEQ #323^3050311^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",277,1,0)="^^1^1^3050311"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",277,1,1,0)="CORRECTS DUPLICATE DISPLAY AND LETTERS IN CANCEL AVAILABILITY."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",278,0)="356 SEQ #324^3050311^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",278,1,0)="^^4^4^3050311"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",278,1,1,0)="THIS PATCH CORRECTS 2 PROBLEMS. THE FIRST FIXES THE DATE PROMPT IN THE "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",278,1,2,0)="PRE-APPOINTMENT LETTERS. THE SECOND GIVES THE ABILITY TO PRINT A "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",278,1,3,0)="CANCELLATION LETTER WHEN RESCHEDULING AN APPOINTMENT FOR THE SAME "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",278,1,4,0)="DATE/TIME IN A DIFFERENT CLINIC."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",279,0)="408 SEQ #325^3050311^1"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",279,1,0)="^^2^2^3050311"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",279,1,1,0)="Dis-allow scheduling appointments on days where availablity has been "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",279,1,2,0)="canceled via the option ""SET UP A CLINIC""."
