^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",491,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",491,1,45,0)="TEAM POSITION HISTORY FILE (#404.59)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",491,1,46,0)=".03    STATUS"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",491,1,47,0)="  FIELD INDEX: AC (#209)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",491,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",491,1,49,0)="The entry points in routine SCMCHLX called by the cross references and"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",491,1,50,0)="indexes were modified to exit immediately."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",492,0)="665 SEQ #549^3170629.171432^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",493,0)="669 SEQ #550^3170629.171511^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",494,0)="663^3170928.165625^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",494,1,0)="^^5^5^3170928"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",494,1,1,0)="This patch provides Fiscal Year 2018 updates to the CLINIC STOP (#40.7)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",494,1,2,0)="file as requested by the Office of Finance, Managerial Cost Accounting "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",494,1,3,0)="Office (MCAO).  Associated patch EC*2.0*136 inactivates any DSS Units in"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",494,1,4,0)="Event Capture set to Send No Records to PCE with an associated Stop Code "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",494,1,5,0)="being inactivated by the SD patch."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,0)="646 SEQ #552^3170929.16433^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,0)="^^13^13^3170929"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,1,0)="This patch adds consistency checks for DIRECT PATIENT SCHEDULING? field "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,2,0)="(#61) and DISPLAY CLIN APPT TO PATIENTS? field (#62) in the HOSPITAL "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,3,0)="LOCATION file (#44) when creating a new clinic or editing an existing "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,4,0)="clinic by using the Set up a Clinic [SDBUILD] menu option."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,6,0)="This effort was requested by the Veterans Health Administration (VHA) "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,7,0)="Access and Clinic Administration Program (ACAP) in support of the VistA "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,8,0)="Scheduling Enhancements (VSE) project."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,10,0)="Additional changes added to fix hard error when calling Wait List or "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,11,0)="Recall Reminder whenever the help text for Select LANGUAGE DATE/TIME: "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,12,0)="prompt invoked while executing the Make Appointment option in [SDAM "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",495,1,13,0)="APPT MGT] Appointment Management."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",496,0)="664 SEQ #553^3171005.140054^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",496,1,0)="^^7^7^3171005"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",496,1,1,0)="SD*5.3*664 provides updates to the OUTPATIENT CLASSIFICATION STOP CODE"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",496,1,2,0)="EXCEPTION file (#409.45) as requested by the VISN 20 Veteran Equitable "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",496,1,3,0)="Resource Allocation Coordinator and approved by the Office of Community "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",496,1,4,0)="Care - Policy and Planning."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",496,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",496,1,6,0)="After the installation of this patch, the OUTPATIENT CLASSIFICATION STOP"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",496,1,7,0)="CODE EXCEPTION file (#409.45) will be locked down."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",497,0)="650 SEQ #554^3171006.15484^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",497,1,0)="^^11^11^3171006"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",497,1,1,0)="This patch release includes three bug fixes:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",497,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",497,1,3,0)="1. Fixes an issue that prevented from printing an extra blank page before"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",497,1,4,0)="   printing the actual pre-appointment letter when make appointment."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",497,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",497,1,6,0)="2. Fixes an issue that prevented from printing an extra blank page before"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",497,1,7,0)="   printing the actual cancel appointment letter in the Appointment "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",497,1,8,0)="   Management."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",497,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",497,1,10,0)="3. Fixes some misspelling words on the fields and indexed in the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",497,1,11,0)="   Outpatient Encounter file (#409.68)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,0)="648 SEQ #555^3171127.133526^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,1,0)="^^12^12^3171127"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,1,1,0)="This patch fixes the following three (3) issues:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,1,3,0)="1. When running Recall Reminder nightly background job, Clean Up Clinic"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,1,4,0)="   Recall Entries [SDRR CLEAN-UP], Delete Reason APPT SCHEDULED is missing"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,1,5,0)="   in the RECALL REMINDERS REMOVED file (#403.56)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,1,7,0)="2. When entering a patient into Recall Reminder, customer requests to "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,1,8,0)="   limit the clinic that the patient should be scheduled in with only the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,1,9,0)="   clinic TYPE is clinic."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,1,11,0)="3. When running the Recall Patient Inquiry, if queuing is selected, the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",498,1,12,0)="   error <NOTOPEN>ALL+1^SDRRINQ1 occurred."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",499,0)="670 SEQ #556^3171128.124549^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",499,1,0)="^^4^4^3171128"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",499,1,1,0)="This patch corrects an issue where no data was appearing on the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",499,1,2,0)="Transmission History Report - Full  [SCDX AMBCAR XMIT HIST FULL] when "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",499,1,3,0)="called to a Print Queue.  The data would appear when called to the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",499,1,4,0)="screen. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",500,0)="671 SEQ #557^3171128.124638^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",501,0)="666 SEQ #559^3171227.133139^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",501,1,0)="^^1^1^3171227"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",501,1,1,0)="PCMM API Date check function."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",502,0)="672 SEQ #560^3180129.170032^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",503,0)="654 SEQ #561^3180130.144957^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",503,1,0)="^^9^9^3180130"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",503,1,1,0)="This patch release addresses the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",503,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",503,1,3,0)="1. Fixes an issue that could prevent date sent fields from updating when "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",503,1,4,0)="   displaying patient's recall letter or card on the computer screen."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",503,1,5,0)="2. Fixes an issue where warning message would not create in MailMan for"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",503,1,6,0)="   patient with Bad Address Indicator."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",503,1,7,0)="3. Fixes an incorrect word in the MailMan message for patients with Bad"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",503,1,8,0)="   Address."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",503,1,9,0)="4. Fixes incorrect Canadian address format."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",504,0)="677^3180403.16542^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",504,1,0)="^^3^3^3180403"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",504,1,1,0)="SD*5.3*677 provides Fiscal Year 2018 Mid-Year updates to the CLINIC STOP "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",504,1,2,0)="(#40.7) file as requested by the Office of Finance, Managerial Cost "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",504,1,3,0)="Accounting Office (MCAO)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",505,0)="680 SEQ #564^3180403.173908^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",505,1,0)="^^5^5^3180403"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",505,1,1,0)="This patch (SD*5.3*680) addresses this one (1) issue:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",505,1,2,0)="(1)  I16592426FY17 - Self Identified Gender"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",505,1,3,0)="   -       SDL--PREAPPOINTMENT LETTERS Print Template and VistA"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",505,1,4,0)="           routines SDEC40, SDECU, and SDLT are modified and"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",505,1,5,0)="           remove gender implication(s)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",506,0)="684 SEQ #565^3180501.144515^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",506,1,0)="^^5^5^3180501"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",506,1,1,0)=" This patch will address 1 issue:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",506,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",506,1,3,0)=" 1. Canceling clinic availability for a date that has previously been"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",506,1,4,0)="    removed from availability will incorrectly restore availability for"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",506,1,5,0)="    that date."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,0)="679^3180601.155053^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,0)="^^433^433^3180601"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,1,0)="This patch contains the VistA components necessary to support the 1.5 "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,2,0)="release of VistA Scheduling Enhancements (VSE) as well as addressing the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,3,0)="following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,5,0)="1. I15980703FY17 - If user has begun to schedule an appointment on a "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,6,0)="                   holiday and ability to book appointments on holidays "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,7,0)="                   is turned off in the meantime, the appointment can be"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,8,0)="                   booked."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,9,0)="2. R16256976FY17 - If user enters a zip code in the Veteran's permanent"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,10,0)="                   address on the Patient Info form, and the name of the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,11,0)="                   associated county is contained in another county in the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,12,0)="                   same state (such as ROBERTS and ROBERTSON), an error"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,13,0)="                   message would be displayed."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,14,0)="3. I16857061FY18 - If a scheduler makes or cancels an appointment for a "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,15,0)="                   consult and the current time ends in a zero (like "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,16,0)="                   9:40), then the event recorded in the consult will"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,17,0)="                   display at the end of the consult event history instead"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,18,0)="                   of in sequence."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,20,0)="The third issue requires a fix to repair existing data effected by the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,21,0)="issue. That repair is done in a separate patch, which will be bundled"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,22,0)="with this one. Below is a list of all the applications involved in this"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,23,0)="bundle along with their patch number:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,25,0)="   APPLICATION/VERSION                                   PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,26,0)="   ---------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,27,0)="   SCHEDULING (SD) V. 5.3                                SD*5.3*679"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,28,0)="   CONSULT/REQUEST TRACKING (GMRC) V. 3.0                GMRC*3.0*98"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,29,0)=" "
