^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,194,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,195,0)="New Service Requests (NSRs)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,196,0)="----------------------------  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,197,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,198,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,200,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,201,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,202,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,203,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,204,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,205,0)="Service Desk Manager (SDM) Ticket(s) & Overview"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,206,0)="-----------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,207,0)="1. I15980703FY17 ENH REQ: VSE issue: Scheduling ""clinics"" on a specific "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,208,0)="                 holiday opens up ALL holidays to scheduling."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,209,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,210,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,211,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,212,0)="When setting up clinics, VistA recognizes holidays and offers the option "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,213,0)="to schedule in selected clinics on holidays as a second step in the clinic"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,214,0)="set up process (includes education day)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,215,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,216,0)="The clinic day is initially set as a holiday. Then, to be able to "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,217,0)="schedule on a selected holiday such as Education Day, Doreen or Michelle"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,218,0)="would go back in and answer ""yes"" to the question in VistA ""Schedule on"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,219,0)="holidays?"" to be able to subsequently go in and open up slots to be"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,220,0)="scheduled into on particular holidays. VistA allows this without opening"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,221,0)="up ALL holidays. It seems, however, that VSE does NOT. In VSE, this opens"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,222,0)="up ALL holidays to scheduling, ie. it shows the clinics as open for"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,223,0)="scheduling. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,224,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,225,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,226,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,227,0)="The VSE GUI Client has been corrected to check that the slot is available "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,228,0)="before attempting to book a holiday appointment."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,229,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,230,0)="2. R16256976FY17 VS GUI 2.0.0.12 - New Issue? - Error pop up indicating "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,231,0)="county does not belong in state - OVAC Edit "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,232,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,233,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,234,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,235,0)="When you enter the zip code, the state/county populate correctly, but when"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,236,0)="you click OK, you get ""County GREEN does not belong to state GREEN."""
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,237,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,238,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,239,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,240,0)="The code that looks up the county ID in the state has been corrected so "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,241,0)="that it no longer encounters this error when one county's name (in this"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,242,0)="instance Green county) is contained in another (in this instance, Green"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,243,0)="Lake county)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,244,0)="In addition, the error message has been corrected so that the actual state"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,245,0)="name is displayed rather than displaying the county name a second time."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,246,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,247,0)="3. I16857061FY18 Consults are showing activities out of order in CPRS; "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,248,0)="                 VistA FM shows activities in correct chronological order"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,249,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,250,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,251,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,252,0)="Our site is experiencing issues with Consults where the activities being "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,253,0)="recorded are out of order. I originally thought this was a result of the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,254,0)="CONSULT TOOLBOX tool, but there are multiple sites reporting this issue, "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,255,0)="and the consensus is that this is being caused by VSE."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,257,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,258,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,259,0)="The code that saves the SCHEDULED or STATUS CHANGE event when the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,260,0)="appointment is scheduled or canceled was corrected to save the timestamp"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,261,0)="correctly."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,262,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,263,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,264,0)="Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,265,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,266,0)="TBA"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,267,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,268,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,269,0)="Documentation Retrieval Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,270,0)="------------------------------------ "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,271,0)="Updated documentation describing the new functionality introduced by this "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,272,0)="patch is available."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,273,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,274,0)="The preferred method is to FTP the files from "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,275,0)="ftp://download.vista.domain.ext/."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,276,0)="This transmits the files from the first available FTP server. Sites may "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,277,0)="also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific server as "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,278,0)="follows:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,279,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,280,0)=" Hines          ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext   <ftp://ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,281,0)=" Salt Lake City ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext     <ftp://ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,282,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,283,0)="Documentation can also be found on the VA Software Documentation Library "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,284,0)="at:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,285,0)="http://www4.domain.ext/vdl/"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,286,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,287,0)="Title                                          File Name          FTP Mode"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,288,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,289,0)="VistA Scheduling Enhancements GUI User Guide   VSE_VA_GUI_UG.PDF  Binary"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,290,0)="VistA Scheduling Enhancements Technical Manual VSE_TM.PDF         Binary"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,291,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,292,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,293,0)="Patch Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,294,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,295,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,296,0)="Pre/Post Installation Overview"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,297,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,298,0)="This patch should take less than 5 minutes to install."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,299,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,300,0)="This patch should not be installed with VistA Scheduling GUI users on the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,301,0)="system and it is recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,302,0)="minimize potential disruption to other users."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,303,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,304,0)="This patch contains no PRE Installation processing."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,305,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,306,0)="The other patch bundled with this one (GMRC*3.0*98) contains a "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,307,0)="post-install routine that will repair bad data created by the consult"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,308,0)="comment issue."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,309,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,310,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,311,0)="Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,312,0)="-------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,313,0)="This installation will update routines that support VistA Scheduling GUI "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,314,0)="Application Programming Interfaces (APIs)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,315,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,316,0)="1.  OBTAIN PATCHES"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,317,0)="    --------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,318,0)="    Obtain the host file SD_GMRC_VSE_BUNDLE_1_5.KID, which contains the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,319,0)="    following patches:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,320,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,321,0)="        SD*5.3*679"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,322,0)="        GMRC*3.0*98"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,323,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,324,0)="     Sites can retrieve VistA software from the following FTP addresses."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,325,0)="     The preferred method is to FTP the files from:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,326,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,327,0)="                    download.vista.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,328,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,329,0)="     This will transmit the files from the first available FTP server."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,330,0)="     Sites may also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,331,0)="     server as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,332,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,333,0)="       Hines                   ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,334,0)="       Salt Lake City          ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,335,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,336,0)="     The SD_GMRC_VSE_BUNDLE_1_5.KID host file is located in the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,337,0)="     anonymous.software directory. Use the American Standard Code for "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,338,0)="     Information Interchange (ASCII) Mode when downloading the file."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,339,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,340,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,341,0)="  2.  START UP KIDS"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,342,0)="      -------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,343,0)="      Start up the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu option"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,344,0)="      [XPD MAIN]:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,345,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,346,0)="         Edits and Distribution ..."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,347,0)="         Utilities ..."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,348,0)="         Installation ..."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,349,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,350,0)="      Select Kernel Installation & Distribution System Option: "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,351,0)="Installation"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,352,0)="                                                               ---"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,353,0)="         Load a Distribution"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,354,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,355,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,356,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,357,0)="         Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,358,0)="         Restart Install of Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,359,0)="         Unload a Distribution"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,360,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,361,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,362,0)="      Select Installation Option:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,363,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,364,0)="3.  LOAD TRANSPORT GLOBAL FOR MULTI-BUILD"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,365,0)="    -------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,366,0)="    From the Installation menu, select the Load a Distribution option."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,367,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,368,0)="    When prompted for ""Enter a Host File:"", enter the full directory path"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,369,0)="    where you saved the host file SD_GMRC_VSE_BUNDLE_1_5.KID (e.g.,"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,370,0)="    SYS$SYSDEVICE:[ANONYMOUS]SD_GMRC_VSE_BUNDLE_1_5.KID)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,371,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,372,0)="    When prompted for ""OK to continue with Load? NO//"", enter ""YES."""
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,373,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,374,0)="    The following will display:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,375,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,376,0)="      Loading Distribution..."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,377,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,378,0)="        SD GMRC VSE BUNDLE 1.5"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,379,0)="        SD*5.3*679"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,380,0)="        GMRC*3.0*98"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,381,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,382,0)="      Use INSTALL NAME: SD GMRC VSE BUNDLE 1.5 to install this"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,383,0)="      distribution."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,384,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,385,0)="4.  RUN OPTIONAL INSTALLATION OPTIONS FOR MULTI-BUILD"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,386,0)="    -------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,387,0)="    From the Installation menu, you may select to use the following"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,388,0)="    options (when prompted for the INSTALL NAME, enter"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,389,0)="    SD GMRC VSE BUNDLE 1.5):"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,390,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,391,0)="    a.  Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,392,0)="        message of any routines exported with this patch. It will not"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,393,0)="        backup any other changes such as data dictionaries or templates."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,394,0)="    b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,395,0)="        allow you to view all changes that will be made when this patch"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,396,0)="        is installed.  It compares all components of this patch"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,397,0)="        (routines, data dictionaries, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,398,0)="    c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,399,0)="        you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,400,0)="        transport global."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,401,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,402,0)="5.  INSTALL MULTI-BUILD"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,403,0)="    -------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,404,0)="    This is the step to start the installation of this KIDS patch.  This"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,405,0)="    will need to be run for the SD GMRC VSE BUNDLE 1.5 build."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,406,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,407,0)="    a.  Choose the Install Package(s) option to start the patch"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,408,0)="        install."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,409,0)="    b.  When prompted for the ""Select INSTALL NAME:"", enter "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,410,0)="        SD GMRC VSE BUNDLE 1.5"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,411,0)="    c.  When prompted ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,412,0)="        Install? NO//"", enter NO."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,413,0)="    d.  When prompted ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,414,0)="        NO//"", enter NO."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,415,0)="    e.  When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,416,0)="and"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,417,0)="        Protocols? NO//' "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,418,0)="          Respond with 'YES'"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,419,0)="          Options to mark as out of order:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,420,0)="             Clinical Scheduling Procedure Calls [SDECRPC]"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,421,0)="             Scheduling Manager's Menu           [SDMGR]"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,422,0)="             Supervisor Menu                     [SDSUP]"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,423,0)="             Scheduling Menu                     [SDUSER]"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,424,0)="             Clinic Letter Report                [SDRR CLINIC LETTER "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,425,0)="REPORT]"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,426,0)="    f.  If prompted 'Delay Install (Minutes):  (0 - 60): 0//' respond 0. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,427,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,428,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,429,0)="Post-Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,430,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,431,0)="In order to verify the patch post-installation routine was run "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,432,0)="successfully, please examine the Install File for this patch and "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",507,1,433,0)="report any error messages to Product Support."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",508,0)="683 SEQ #568^3180601.155134^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",509,0)="674 SEQ #569^3180706.152201^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",509,1,0)="^^7^7^3180706"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",509,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following 2 issues:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",509,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",509,1,3,0)=" 1. Clinic availabilities with future start dates display as available "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",509,1,4,0)="    prior to the future requested date."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",509,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",509,1,6,0)=" 2. The Clinic Utilization & Capacity Data transmissions to Austin"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",509,1,7,0)="    should no longer be transmitted."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",510,0)="689 SEQ #572^3180906.155007^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",510,1,0)="^^2^2^3180906"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",510,1,1,0)="Patch SD*5.3*689 corrects a missing date of the clinic issue on the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",510,1,2,0)="No-Show Report."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",511,0)="685 SEQ #573^3180906.155306^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",511,1,0)="^^5^5^3180906"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",511,1,1,0)="Patch SD*5.3*685 corrects an undefined error when selecting 'Print Cards"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",511,1,2,0)="by Team' from the Clinic Recall Print Menu [SDRR PRINT MENU] option."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",511,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",511,1,4,0)="This patch also corrects an indent issue when printing patient's "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",511,1,5,0)="confidential address for recall letters and cards."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",512,0)="696 SEQ #575^3180925.152415^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",512,1,0)="^^3^3^3180925"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",512,1,1,0)="SD*5.3*696 provides Fiscal Year 2019 updates to the CLINIC STOP file "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",512,1,2,0)="(#40.7) as requested by the Office of Finance, Managerial Cost Accounting "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",512,1,3,0)="Office (MCAO)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",513,0)="640 SEQ #576^3181102.145123^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",513,1,0)="^^11^11^3181102"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",513,1,1,0)="This patch release contains the shutdown of the HL7 Ambulatory Care "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",513,1,2,0)="nightly transmission (ACRP) that goes out from each VistA instance "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",513,1,3,0)="each day to the National Patient Care Database (NPCDB). The NPCDB is being"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",513,1,4,0)="shut down in Austin and the Corporate Data Warehouse (CDW) is replacing "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",513,1,5,0)="the database as the authoritative source. The VistA extracts done to "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",513,1,6,0)="populate the CDW will replace the need for the HL7 transmission."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",513,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",513,1,8,0)="Austin Information Technology Center (AITC) has also requested the Monthly"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",513,1,9,0)="Additional Performance Monitors HL7 data transmissions stop being "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",513,1,10,0)="transmitted from VistA instances to Data Management Interface (DMI) at "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",513,1,11,0)="AITC."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",514,0)="682^3181102.153821^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",515,0)="719 SEQ #578^3181206.161324^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,0)="705 SEQ #579^3181206.162046^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,0)="^^14^14^3181206"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,1,0)="This patch will include code changes for several routines for two New "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,2,0)="Service Requests (NSRs) that were approved by the Software Modification "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,3,0)="Waiver Committee associated with Scheduling Package in VistA."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,4,0)="The following will be addressed in this patch:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,5,0)="1) Add A Blank Line Between Appointments in Print Scheduling "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,6,0)="Letters[SDPRLETTERS]."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,7,0)="2) Modifications to Patient Scheduling Letters - modifications were made "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,8,0)="to VistA Scheduling option Display Appointments[SDDISPPEND] to add the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,9,0)="physical address of the site in the header. Changes were also made to "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,10,0)="display the Primary Care provider, Associate Provider and team, as well "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,11,0)="as the physical location for an appointment. Clinic appointments were "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,12,0)="screened for administrative clinics, and finally, output of Social "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,13,0)="Security Number(SSN) was truncated to four digits instead of outputting "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",516,1,14,0)="the entire SSN."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",517,0)="703 SEQ #580^3190102.174327^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",517,1,0)="^^3^3^3190102"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",517,1,1,0)="This patch will include code changes for several routines for three NSR's "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",517,1,2,0)="that were approved by the Software Modification Waiver Committee "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",517,1,3,0)="associated with Scheduling Package in VistA."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",518,0)="721 SEQ #581^3190402.142016^54"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",518,1,0)="^^11^11^3190402"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",518,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue(s):"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",518,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",518,1,3,0)="1. An undefined error occurs when running the Edit Computer"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",518,1,4,0)="Generated Appointment Type [SDACS CGEDIT] option with the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",518,1,5,0)="OUTPATIENT ENCOUNTER (#409.68) file entry is missing the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",518,1,6,0)="PATIENT (#.02) field."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",518,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",518,1,8,0)="2. The Edit Computer Generated Appointment Type [SDACS CGEDIT]"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",518,1,9,0)="option does not contain the necessary patient information for"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",518,1,10,0)="the affected end user (AEU) to determine the appointment type"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",518,1,11,0)="for computer generated appointments."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",519,0)="724 SEQ #583^3190708.165508^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",519,1,0)="^^4^4^3190708"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",519,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one issue:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",519,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",519,1,3,0)="1. Sites are getting an <UNDEFINED>MORE+2^SDC error when they attempt to"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",519,1,4,0)="   cancel a clinic availability."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",520,0)="713^3190722.171057^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",520,1,0)="^^2^2^3190722"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",520,1,1,0)="SD*5.3*713 - Please refer to the patch description in Forum for "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",520,1,2,0)="installation instructions."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",521,0)="727 SEQ #585^3190812.151905^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",521,1,0)="^^4^4^3190812"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",521,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one issue:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",521,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",521,1,3,0)="1. when queuing Recall Clinic Letter Report, an <UNDEFINED>SORT+14^SDRRREP"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",521,1,4,0)="   error occurred."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",522,0)="707 SEQ #586^3190815.160342^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",522,1,0)="^^2^2^3190815"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",522,1,1,0)="CCRA-HSRM Scheduling HL7 Interfaces for processing Make"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",522,1,2,0)="Appointment: SIU-S12, CANCEL: SIU-S15, and NOSHOW: SIU-S26 messages."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",523,0)="717 SEQ #587^3190819.120821^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",523,1,0)="^^294^294^3190819"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",523,1,1,0)="This patch corrects the problem of appointment processing in VistA"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",523,1,2,0)="Scheduling (VS) GUI not invoking the event driver protocol (SDAM "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",523,1,3,0)="APPOINTMENT"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",523,1,4,0)="EVENTS) that roll and scroll VistA does. This protocol allows other apps"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",523,1,5,0)="to tie functionality, including interfaces to external systems such as"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",523,1,6,0)="Pyxis, Omnicell, and EDIS,to appointment events. Actions currently being"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",523,1,7,0)="executed for appointment events in legacy VistA will also be executed for"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",523,1,8,0)="appointments when those events (make appointment, check in, undo check in,"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",523,1,9,0)="check out, undo check out, cancel appointment, no show) are triggered by"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",523,1,10,0)="the GUI. (However, this patch does not require a GUI update.)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",523,1,11,0)="  "
