^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,268,0)="Service Desk Manager (SDM) Ticket(s) & Overview"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,269,0)="-----------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,270,0)="1. R18120703FY18  Cancel Audit Data Error after selecting ALL in Audit "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,271,0)="Report"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,272,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,273,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,274,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,275,0)="In the Audit Report, when the user chooses ALL in order to run the report "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,276,0)="for"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,277,0)="all schedulers, the system hangs for several minutes attempting to load "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,278,0)="data,"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,279,0)="then finally returns an RPCException when the connection times out. This "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,280,0)="also"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,281,0)="terminate's the user's connection to VistA until they close and reopen VS "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,282,0)="GUI. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,283,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,284,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,285,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,286,0)="The data for the Audit Report is now compiled by a nightly job so that "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,287,0)="much"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,288,0)="less data needs to be transmitted to the client in order to use the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,289,0)="report."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,290,0)="Users will now be able to run the report for all schedulers without"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,291,0)="encountering the timeout."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,292,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,293,0)="2. R17856900FY18, R18564968FY18, R18648321FY18 Reactivating completed "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,294,0)="consults"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,295,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,296,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,297,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,298,0)="If an appointment is created for a consult, then the consult is marked as"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,299,0)="complete, then finally the appointment is canceled, the consult returns "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,300,0)="to the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,301,0)="active status instead of remaining complete. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,302,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,303,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,304,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,305,0)="In this situation, the consult will now remain in the complete status."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,306,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,307,0)="3. R17415367FY18 Incorrect lock handling in RM Grid"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,308,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,309,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,310,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,311,0)="When a user selects a request in the RM grid, the request is locked until"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,312,0)="another request is selected. If the user exits the program, the lock is "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,313,0)="not"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,314,0)="released. If a VistA user tries to use the previously locked request, they"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,315,0)="will be prevented from doing so. (To exacerbate this, the GUI was not "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,316,0)="handling"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,317,0)="locks correctly and would give the lock to any user that tried to get it "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,318,0)="even"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,319,0)="if another user held the lock, so this issue was not visible to GUI"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,320,0)="users.)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,321,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,322,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,323,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,324,0)="The request that a user had locked when they log out is now unlocked"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,325,0)="correctly. In addition, if a user tries to work a request in the GUI that"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,326,0)="another user has locked, they will receive a message that the request is"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,327,0)="locked and which user holds the lock. Finally, a VistA option on the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,328,0)="Supervisor menu has been added that will release all locks held by a user."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,329,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,330,0)="4. R17039175FY18 Consult lookup interaction errors"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,331,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,332,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,333,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,334,0)="When using clinic lookup in the VS GUI, if the user pauses typing, the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,335,0)="input "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,336,0)="is wiped out and has to be re-entered. A pop-up window appears if the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,337,0)="user's "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,338,0)="input results in more than 50 matches and the input is erased. In "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,339,0)="addtion, "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,340,0)="the user cannot refine the list of clinics returned by typing additional "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,341,0)="characters."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,342,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,343,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,344,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,345,0)="GUI changes made, eliminating the pop-up window and responding to the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,346,0)="user's"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,347,0)="input including narrowing the list of returned values when each additional"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,348,0)="character is entered. A new RPC was created for the GUI to support this"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,349,0)="change. The new RPC returns a more limited amount of data so that the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,350,0)="GUI can respond more quickly to the user's input."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,351,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,352,0)="5. R18477670FY18 Remote facility not updated when appointments made for "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,353,0)="IFCs"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,354,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,355,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,356,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,357,0)="When scheduling an appointment for an IFC, the remote facility is not "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,358,0)="notified."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,359,0)="RPC code for VS GUI did not include functionality in VistA Scheduling for "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,360,0)="the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,361,0)="generation of IFC notifications."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,362,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,363,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,364,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,365,0)="Modified the RPC code to call a VistA Scheduling API that generates IFC "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,366,0)="notifications."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,367,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,368,0)="Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,369,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,370,0)="TBA"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,371,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,372,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,373,0)="Documentation Retrieval Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,374,0)="------------------------------------ "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,375,0)="Updated documentation describing the new functionality introduced by this "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,376,0)="patch is available."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,377,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,378,0)="The preferred method is to FTP the files from "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,379,0)="ftp://download.vista.domain.ext/."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,380,0)="This transmits the files from the first available FTP server. Sites may "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,381,0)="also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific server as "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,382,0)="follows:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,383,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,384,0)=" Hines          ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext   <ftp://ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,385,0)=" Salt Lake City ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext     <ftp://ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,386,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,387,0)="Documentation can also be found on the VA Software Documentation Library "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,388,0)="at:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,389,0)="http://www4.domain.ext/vdl/"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,390,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,391,0)="Title                                          File Name          FTP Mode"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,392,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,393,0)="VistA Scheduling Enhancements GUI User Guide   VSE_VA_GUI_UG.PDF  Binary"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,394,0)="VistA Scheduling Enhancements Technical Manual VSE_TM.PDF         Binary"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,395,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,396,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,397,0)="Patch Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,398,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,399,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,400,0)="Pre/Post Installation Overview"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,401,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,402,0)="Post-installation, there are 3 tasks: 1) re-index the SDEC CONTACT file,"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,403,0)="2) schedule the audit statistics compiler to run early each morning in "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,404,0)="TaskMan and 3) compile enough previous audit statistics for reporting "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,405,0)="users."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,406,0)="These tasks will be detailed in the Post-Installation Instructions "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,407,0)="section."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,408,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,409,0)="Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,410,0)="-------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,411,0)="Install Time - less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,412,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,413,0)="   1. Use the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,414,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,415,0)="   2. From the Kernel Installation & Distribution System menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,416,0)="      the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,417,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,418,0)="   3. From this menu, you may select to use the following options"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,419,0)="      (when prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter SD*5.3*686):"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,420,0)="          a.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,421,0)="allow"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,422,0)="              you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,423,0)="              transport global."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,424,0)="          b.  Print Transport Global - This option will allow you to view"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,425,0)="              the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,426,0)="          c.  Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,427,0)="will"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,428,0)="              allow you to view all changes that will be made when this "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,429,0)="              patch is installed.  It compares all components of this"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,430,0)="              patch (routines, DD's, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,431,0)="          d.  Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,432,0)="              message of any routines exported with this patch. It will "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,433,0)="not"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,434,0)="              backup any other changes such as DD's or templates."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,435,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,436,0)="   4. Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package SD*5.3*686."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,437,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,438,0)="   5. When prompted ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? NO//"""
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,439,0)="      respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,440,0)="   6. When prompted ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,441,0)="      Protocols? NO//"", respond NO"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,442,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,443,0)="Post-Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,444,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,445,0)="1.  RE-INDEX THE SDEC CONTACT FILE"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,446,0)="    ------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,447,0)="    VA FileMan 22.2"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,448,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,449,0)="    Select OPTION: UTILITY FUNCTIONS  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,450,0)="                   ----"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,451,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,452,0)="    Select UTILITY OPTION: 4  RE-INDEX FILE"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,453,0)="                           -"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,454,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,455,0)="    MODIFY WHAT FILE: SD Audit Statistics// 409.86  SDEC CONTACT"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,456,0)="                                            ------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,457,0)="                                              (0 entries)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,458,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,459,0)="    THERE ARE 3 INDICES WITHIN THIS FILE"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,460,0)="    DO YOU WISH TO RE-CROSS-REFERENCE ONE PARTICULAR INDEX? No// Y  (Yes)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,461,0)="                                                                 -"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,462,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,463,0)="    What type of cross-reference (Traditional or New)? Traditional// NEW"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,464,0)="                                                                     ---"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,465,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,466,0)="              File: SDEC CONTACT (#409.86)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,467,0)="    Select Subfile: 3  DATE/TIME of CONTACT  (Subfile #409.863)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,468,0)="                    -"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,469,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,470,0)="    Current Indexes on subfile #409.863:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,471,0)="      1404   'AD' whole file index (resides on file #409.86)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,472,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,473,0)="    Which Index do you wish to re-cross-reference? 1404//   AD"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,474,0)="                                                            --"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,475,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,476,0)="    Do you want to delete the existing 'AD' cross-reference? YES"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,477,0)="                                                             ---"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,478,0)="    Do you want to re-build the 'AD' cross reference? YES  ...DONE! "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,479,0)="                                                      ---"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,480,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,481,0)="2.  SCHEDULE THE AUDIT REPORT JOB"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,482,0)="    -----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,483,0)="    Access the TASKMAN MANAGEMENT option then select Schedule/Unschedule "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,484,0)="    options. Schedule the SDEC AUDIT REPORT JOB option to run at some "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,485,0)="point "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,486,0)="    in the early morning tomorrow (such as 1:00 am) with a rescheduling"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,487,0)="    frequency of one day (1D)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,488,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,489,0)="3.  COMPILE DATA FOR THE AUDIT REPORT"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,490,0)="    ---------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,491,0)="    Access the SDEC COMPILE AUDIT REPORT option. Enter the date range "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,492,0)="that "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,493,0)="    you want to be able to report statistics for.  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,494,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,495,0)="    NOTE: You can run the option as many times as needed to compile the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,496,0)="    report statistics. Compiling will be skipped if it has already been "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,497,0)="done"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,498,0)="    for a day. It is recommended that you compile a single day the first "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,499,0)="time"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,500,0)="    you use the option to gauge the amount of time required at your "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,501,0)="facility."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,502,0)="    Compiling audit statistics can be done at any time after installation "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,503,0)="that"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,504,0)="    is convenient, but users will only be able to get data on the audit"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",533,1,505,0)="    report that has been compiled."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",534,0)="740 SEQ #598^3200211.095525^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",534,1,0)="^^4^4^3200211"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",534,1,1,0)="This patch addresses issues within a Scheduling RPC where the Cache/MUMPS"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",534,1,2,0)="TSTART, TCOMMIT, and TROLLBACK commands are currently being used. These "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",534,1,3,0)="commands are not used in standard VistA code. These commands are being"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",534,1,4,0)="removed and the code rewritten to adhere to standard VistA coding."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",535,0)="737 SEQ #599^3200311.11245^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",535,1,0)="^^7^7^3200311"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",535,1,1,0)="Pending appointments list in VSE does not show CHECKED IN status if "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",535,1,2,0)="appointment checked in using VPS Kiosks.  This occurs because VPS code "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",535,1,3,0)="only updates the appointment in the Location file (#44).  It does not "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",535,1,4,0)="call the VSE check-in API."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",535,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",535,1,6,0)="Code change made to SDEC50 to look in Location file for check-in "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",535,1,7,0)="date/time if not found in the Appointment file (#409.84)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",536,0)="736 SEQ #600^3200324.16533^70"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",536,1,0)="^^3^3^3200324"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",536,1,1,0)="SD*5.3*736 provides Fiscal Year 2020 Mid-Year updates to the CLINIC STOP"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",536,1,2,0)="(#40.7) file as requested by the Office of Finance, Managerial Cost"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",536,1,3,0)="Accounting Office (MCAO)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,0)="744 SEQ #601^3200325.122618^70"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,0)="^^14^14^3200325"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,1,0)="This patch is to correct a problem after patch SD*5.3*722 was released"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,2,0)="and overlayed previous code released in patch SD*5.3*717 for two routines "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,3,0)="(SDEC07B and SDEC08 only)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,5,0)="This patch corrects the problem of appointment processing in VistA"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,6,0)="Scheduling (VS) Graphical User Interface (GUI) not invoking the event"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,7,0)="driver protocol (SDAM APPOINTMENT EVENTS) that roll and scroll VistA "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,8,0)="does. This protocol allows other apps to tie functionality, including"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,9,0)="interfaces to external systems such as Pyxis, Omnicell, and Emergency"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,10,0)="Department Information System (EDIS), to appointment events. Actions"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,11,0)="currently being executed for appointment events in legacy VistA will also"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,12,0)="be executed for appointments when those events."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",537,1,14,0)="Only the make appointment and cancel appointment have been affected."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",538,0)="714 SEQ #602^3200402.172958^70"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",539,0)="747 SEQ #603^3200410.160143^70"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",539,1,0)="^^6^6^3200410"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",539,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",539,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",539,1,3,0)="1. Patients with an EMERGENCY RESPONSE INDICATOR (#.181) in the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",539,1,4,0)="   PATIENT (#2) file equal to Pandemic (""P"") are displaying on the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",539,1,5,0)="   Incomplete Encounter Error Report [SCENI IEMM ERROR REPORT] with an "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",539,1,6,0)="   error code of 3400 (Invalid Emergency Response Indicator)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",540,0)="735 SEQ #604^3200506.12032^70"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,0)="726 SEQ #605^3200514.164731^70"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,1,0)="^^12^12^3200514"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,1,3,0)="1. Active clinic grid availabilities are disappearing, and other "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,1,4,0)="availabilities are displaying with open slots when patients are already"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,1,5,0)="scheduled."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,1,7,0)="2. Clinic availability disappears after remapping for a clinic with a"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,1,8,0)="future inactivation date."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,1,10,0)="3. The VistA clinic grid displays the wrong date when appointments are"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,1,11,0)="scheduled prior to the HOUR CLINIC DISPLAY BEGINS (#1914) field in the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",541,1,12,0)="HOSPITAL LOCATION (#44) file and clinic is remapped."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",542,0)="743 SEQ #606^3200515.094228^70"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",542,1,0)="^^1^1^3200515"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",542,1,1,0)="Patch to set APP PROXY ALLOWED for Visual Scheduling Enhancment RPCs"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",543,0)="746 SEQ #607^3200624.143026^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",544,0)="694 SEQ #608^3200625.14373^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",545,0)="748 SEQ #610^3200707.164506^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",545,1,0)="^^5^5^3200707"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",545,1,1,0)="Patch SD*5.3*748 addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",545,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",545,1,3,0)="1. Create new option to update missing Unique Visit IDs in Encounters"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",545,1,4,0)="   and update software to also update TIU Documents when the Visit ID"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",545,1,5,0)="   is missing."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",546,0)="739 SEQ #611^3200709.16154^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",546,1,0)="^^8^8^3200709"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",546,1,1,0)="Patch SD*5.3*739 addresses two issues:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",546,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",546,1,3,0)="1. Resolves an issue that was causing an UNDEFINED error when running"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",546,1,4,0)="   Display Appointments [SDDISPPEND] if EXCLUDE ADMIN CLINICS is YES"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",546,1,5,0)="   in the Scheduling Parameters [SD PARAM PARAMETERS] option."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",546,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",546,1,7,0)="2. Fixes an issue that could prevent user override a block time from "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",546,1,8,0)="   making an appointment in appointment management."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",547,0)="764 SEQ #612^3200819.112855^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",548,0)="754 SEQ #613^3200824.161145^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",548,1,0)="^^2^2^3200824"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",548,1,1,0)="The description of this build can be found in the National Patch Module "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",548,1,2,0)="under SD*5.3*754."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",549,0)="762 SEQ #614^3200824.161255^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",549,1,0)="^^2^2^3200824"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",549,1,1,0)="Update the VistA Scheduling (VS) Graphical User Interface (GUI) to version"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",549,1,2,0)="1.7.0.1 R1 to match a new GUI version that must be created."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",550,0)="753 SEQ #615^3200923.154126^65"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",550,1,0)="^^11^11^3200923"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",550,1,1,0)="Patch SD*5.3*753 addresses the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",550,1,2,0)="                                         "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",550,1,3,0)="1. The Multiple Appointment Book [SDMULTICLINIC] option does not"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",550,1,4,0)="   allow unlimited overbooks."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",550,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",550,1,6,0)="2. Clinic Grids which have all availability canceled will not"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",550,1,7,0)="   display in Vista after remapping."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",550,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",550,1,9,0)="3. Clinic Grids which have all availability canceled and have at"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",550,1,10,0)="   least one appointment canceled will display as fully available"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",550,1,11,0)="   after the clinic is remapped."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",551,0)="752^3200928.091229^17"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",551,1,0)="^^9^9^3200928"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",551,1,1,0)="SD*5.3*752 provides Fiscal Year 2021 updates to the CLINIC STOP (#40.7) "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",551,1,2,0)="file as requested by the Office of Finance, Managerial Cost Accounting "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",551,1,3,0)="Office (MCAO)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",551,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",551,1,5,0)="When inactivating stop codes in the CLINIC STOP (#40.7) file, the DSS "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",551,1,6,0)="UNITS (#724) file also needs to be updated.  Therefore, this patch is"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",551,1,7,0)="being released along with Event Capture patch EC*2.0*151 that inactivates"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",551,1,8,0)="the DSS Units.  Both patches will be bundled together with this Scheduling"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",551,1,9,0)="patch being the primary."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",552,0)="766 SEQ #617^3200930.174857^17"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",552,1,0)="^^5^5^3200930"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",552,1,1,0)="Patch SD*5.3*766 addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",552,1,2,0)="                                         "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",552,1,3,0)="1. The Correct Unique Visit ID  [SCENI IEMM VISIT CORRECTION] "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",552,1,4,0)="   option updates all child visits to the parent visit automatically."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",552,1,5,0)="   Also, it only updates the first TIU Document associated with a Visit."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",553,0)="745 SEQ #618^3201001.125955^17"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",553,1,0)="^^1^1^3201001"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",553,1,1,0)="Please refer to the patch description for details regarding this patch."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,0)="758 SEQ #620^3201021.100816^17"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,0)="^^13^13^3201021"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,1,0)="Patch SD*5.3*758 addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,2,0)="                                         "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,3,0)="1. Return to Clinic (RTC) orders are moving to ""active"" status"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,4,0)="   after the appointment is moved and the clinic availability "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,5,0)="   cancelled."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,7,0)="2. Appointments that were canceled by the patient show as"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,8,0)="   ""Canceled by Clinic"" after the clinic availability "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,9,0)="   is cancelled."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,11,0)="3. When blocking a clinic grid for a partial day, the block"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,12,0)="   displays incorrectly (early) when it is for less than 1 hour,"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",554,1,13,0)="   and after the scheduled availability."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",555,0)="768 SEQ #621^3201112.175229^17"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",556,0)="771 SEQ #622^3201208.082606^17"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",556,1,0)="^^4^4^3201208"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",556,1,1,0)="Patch SD*5.3*771 marks the Enter/Edit Wait List (Sch/PCMM) [SD WAIT LIST"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",556,1,2,0)="ENTER/EDIT] option Out of Order, and marks the Wait List Entry [SD WAIT"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",556,1,3,0)="LIST ENTRY] protocol Disabled, ahead of the Electronic Wait List (EWL)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",556,1,4,0)="decommission."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",557,0)="750 SEQ #623^3201208.083055^17"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",557,1,0)="^^2^2^3201208"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",557,1,1,0)="This patch will update the Patient Centered Management Module (PCMM Web) "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",557,1,2,0)="server entries in the VistA HealtheVet Web Services Client (HWSC)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",558,0)="756 SEQ #624^3201217.172047^17"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",558,1,0)="^^1^1^3201217"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",558,1,1,0)="Please see the detailed patch description on Forum."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",559,0)="770b^3210315"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",559,1,0)="^^5^5^3210315"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",559,1,1,0)="Backup of SD*5.3*770 on Mar 15, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",559,1,2,0)=" "
