^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,41,0)="JIRA tasks:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,42,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,43,0)="1) Jira #VSE-635 - Review Consults/Procedure RPCs"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,45,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,46,0)="The VS GUIs RPCs related to Consults/Procedures need to be reviewed to"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,47,0)="determine what optimizations can be made to help improve the response time"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,48,0)="of the VS GUI while processing these records."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,50,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,51,0)="The VS GUI Trace Logs were reviewed and the new SDEC GET PAT CONSULT BY "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,52,0)="Internal Entry Number (IEN) RPC was created to return 17 key fields needed"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,53,0)="to help populate the VS GUI screens related to the review and processing"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,54,0)="of the Consults and Procedures."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,56,0)="2) Jira #VSE-717 - Create new RPC to return a single Consult in "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,57,0)="JavaScript Object Notation (JSON) format."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,59,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,60,0)="The VS GUI is being updated to utilize RPCs returning data in JSON"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,61,0)="format. Create new SDEC GET PAT CONSULT BY IEN RPC in JSON format."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,63,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,64,0)="The new SDEC GET PATIENT CONSULT JSON RPC was created to return the 17"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,65,0)="key fields needed to help populate the VS GUI screens related to the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,66,0)="review and processing of the Consults and Procedures."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,68,0)="3) Jira #VSE-664 - Create Patient Search RPC to return basic Patient "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,69,0)="information"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,71,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,72,0)=" a) While the Passed in Social Security Number (SSN) 9N format identifier"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,73,0)="    was properly executed, those SSNs that contained Hyphens (""-"") were"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,74,0)="    not being recognized properly (i.e. nnn-nn-nnnn)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,75,0)=" b) Modification was needed to only allow four numerics (4D) to be passed "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,76,0)="    in with Alpha last name. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,77,0)=" c) Patients with a SENSITIVE data flag were not being Masked with the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,78,0)="    ""Sensitive"" message."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,79,0)=" d) A space was missing between the type of letter and the ""Letter not"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,80,0)="    defined"" message."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,82,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,83,0)=" a) Modifications were made to recognize the hyphen within the SSN."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,84,0)=" b) The passing in of a format of First Alpha of Last Name concatenated"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,85,0)="    with Numerics has changed from its prior functionality. Now, only A4N"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,86,0)="    format is valid, as we have invalidated the A1N, A2N, A3N formatted"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,87,0)="    type entries."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,88,0)=" c) Modifications were made to add the Patient Sensitivity Flag as the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,89,0)="    8th piece of data in the returned string of the RPC SDEC GET PATIENT "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,90,0)="    DEMOG."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,91,0)=" d) Added a missing ""space"" in the Warning message for ""letter not"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,92,0)="    defined""(i.e. from ""Pre-AppointmentLetter not defined for Clinic VSE"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,93,0)="    OG CLINIC.""to ""Pre-Appointment Letter not defined for Clinic VSE OG"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,94,0)="    CLINIC."")"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,96,0)="4) Jira #VSE-663 - Create new RPC in JSON format to send the list of"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,97,0)="recalls associated with a given patient."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,99,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,100,0)="The VS GUI is being updated to utilize RPCs returning data in JSON"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,101,0)="format. Create new, trimmed version of SDEC RECGET in JSON format. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,102,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,103,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,104,0)="The new SDEC GET PATIENT RECALLS JSON RPC was created to return the 20"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,105,0)="key fields needed to help populate the VS GUI screens related to the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,106,0)="review and processing of Recalls."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,108,0)="5) Jira #VSE-724 -  Create new RPC to return a single Appointment Request "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,109,0)="in JSON format."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,110,0)="               "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,111,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,112,0)="The VS GUI is being updated to utilize RPCs returning data in JSON"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,113,0)="format. Create new SDEC GET APPT REQ BY IEN JSON format."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,115,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,116,0)="The new SDEC GET APPT REQ BY IEN JSON RPC was created to return the 39"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,117,0)="key fields needed to help populate the VS GUI screens related to the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,118,0)="review and processing of the Appointment Requests."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,120,0)="6) Jira #VSE-634 - Create new RPC that will return a single recall "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,122,0)="Problem: The VS GUI is in need of an RPC that will return a single Recall "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,123,0)="based on the IEN being passed to Vista."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,125,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,126,0)="The new SDEC GET PATIENT RECALL BY IEN was created to return the 20"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,127,0)="key fields needed to help populate the VS GUI screens related to the"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,128,0)="review and processing of a single Recall."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,129,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,130,0)="7) Jira #VSE-684 - Pending RTC Order Cleanup Option Enhancement:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,131,0)="Confirmation Message"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,132,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,133,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,134,0)="Request an enhancement to the RTC Cleanup tool to have it present with "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,135,0)="user with a confirmation message before it runs.  This will allow the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,136,0)="user to change their mind after selecting the OPTION."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,138,0)="Resolution:  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,139,0)="Both SDEC PENDING RTC - FULL and SDEC PENDING RTC - DATE options were "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,140,0)="modified to include a confirmation message to ensure that the user wants "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,141,0)="to run the cleanup tool."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,142,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,143,0)="8) Jira #VSE-685 - Pending RTC Order Cleanup Option Enhancement: Date "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,144,0)="Clarification"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,145,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,146,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,147,0)="Request an enhancement to the RTC Cleanup tool (SDEC PENDING RTC - DATE) "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,148,0)="to define that the date being prompted for is the Create date."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,150,0)="Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,151,0)="SDEC PENDING RTC - DATE was modified to present the user with a prompt "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,152,0)="for what SDEC REQUEST Create dates should be searched on.   The "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,153,0)="information prior to the prompt also informs the user that the Cleanup "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,154,0)="Tool will select RTCs based on create date."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,156,0)="9) Jira # VSE-686 - Pending RTC Order Cleanup Option Enhancement: Print "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,157,0)="Results"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,159,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,160,0)="Request an enhancement for the RTC Order Cleanup Options to return a "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,161,0)="report of the RTC and Orders that were updated via the tool."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,162,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,163,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,164,0)="Added a report to both the SDEC PENDING RTC - FULL and SDEC PENDING RTC - "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,165,0)="DATE OPTION.  The user will now be prompted for a DEVICE and a report "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,166,0)="with information regarding both the ORDER and the RTC will be printed for "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,167,0)="any RTC that was selected and cleaned up."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,168,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,169,0)="10) Jira # VSE-734 - Create new RPC that will return, in JSON format, a "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,170,0)="single recall based on the IEN being passed to Vista."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,172,0)="Problem: VS GUI is in need of an RPC that will return a single Recall "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,173,0)="in JSON format based on the IEN being passed into Vista. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,174,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,175,0)="Resolution: The new SDEC GET PATIENT RECALL BY IEN JSON RPC was created to"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,176,0)="return the 20 key fields needed to help populate the VS GUI screens"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,177,0)="related to the review and processing of Recalls. This RPC passes back a "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,178,0)="single record to the GUI based on the IEN being passed into Vista."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,179,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,180,0)="11) Jira #VSE-728 - Correct defect with new contact creation"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,181,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,182,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,183,0)="If a Service (Field 1.1) is passed into the RPC SDEC NEW CONTACT, it will "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,184,0)="be concatenated with the Main Sequence (Field 2.2)."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,185,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,186,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,187,0)="When setting into the global, include the system delimiter (^) in front "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,188,0)="of the service."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,189,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,190,0)="12) Jira #VSE-730 - Prevent appointment cancelation if it is in a"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,191,0)="Checked-In status."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,192,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,193,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,194,0)="When canceling an appointment, the Appointment file (409.84) would have "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,195,0)="its status changed to Cancel prior to performing all validation.  This "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,196,0)="would cause the appointment to become stuck."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,197,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,198,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,199,0)="Ensure all validation is complete prior to updating any files."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,200,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,201,0)="13) Jira #VSE-693 - Modify Patient Letter to Remove Title (Mr/Ms)"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,202,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,203,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,204,0)="Requested modification to patient letters printed from VS GUI to "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,205,0)="print name only (with no title/prefix) in the salutation"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,206,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,207,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,208,0)="Modifications were completed to eliminate the Title of Mr/Ms from the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,209,0)="following letters: Pre-appointment, No-Show, Cancellation by Patient, and"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,210,0)="Cancellation by Clinic"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,211,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,212,0)="14) Jira #VSE-800 - VS GUI crashing when cancelling VVS Appointment"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,213,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,214,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,215,0)="When cancelling a VVS Appointment using Access/Verify when challenged for "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,216,0)="Authentication and choosing cancel, the VS GUI could crash."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,217,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,218,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,219,0)="Verify authentication was completed before proceeding and if not, return "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,220,0)="to the previous process."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,221,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,222,0)="15) Jira #VSE-168 - Tasks Tab - Patient Search Functionality"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,223,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,224,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,225,0)="Patient Search was not 508 compliant."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,226,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,227,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,228,0)="Replaced Patient Search function with pop-up search. Addressed all 508 "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,229,0)="requirements for the Patient Search function in the tasks tab."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,230,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,231,0)="16) Jira #VSE-188 - New Appointment - Remediate 508 findings in New "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,232,0)="Appointment form"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,233,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,234,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,235,0)="New Appointment Form was not 508 compliant. "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,236,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,237,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,238,0)="Addressed all 508 findings in the New Appointment form in VS GUI."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,239,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,240,0)="17) Jira #VSE-562 - Edit a VVS Appointment from VS GUI"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,241,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,242,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,243,0)="I want to be able to edit a VVS appointment from VS GUI, so that I do not "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,244,0)="have to use multiple applications to modify a single appointment."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,245,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,246,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,247,0)="A button was added on the edit Appointment Form that allows users to edit "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,248,0)="the corresponding video appointment."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,249,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,250,0)="18) Jira #VSE-688 - View a VVS Appointment"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,251,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,252,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,253,0)="I want to view an existing VVS appointment from VS GUI, so that I can "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,254,0)="access VVS appointment details without using multiple applications."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,255,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,256,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,257,0)="A button was added to the View Appointment Form that allows users to view "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,258,0)="the corresponding video appointment."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,259,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,260,0)="19) Jira #VSE-689 - Resend VVS Appointment Link"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,261,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,262,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,263,0)="As a scheduler, I want the ability to resend the VVS appointment link to "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,264,0)="video visit participants from VS GUI, so that I can ensure all "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,265,0)="participants have the link available at appointment time without using "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,266,0)="multiple applications."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,267,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,268,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,269,0)="A button was added to the VVS Appointment Form to allow users to re-send "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,270,0)="the VVS appointment link."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,271,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,272,0)="20) Jira #VSE-718 - Update GUI to use new SDEC GET PAT CONSULT BY IEN RPC"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",579,1,273,0)=" "
