^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,0)="854 SEQ #742^3241115.143209^89"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,0)="^^27^27^3241115"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,1,0)="The code flow in routine SCMCWS1 is changed. After the first query to "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,2,0)="PCMM is unsuccessful using the DFN and Site number. The SCVALUE variable "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,3,0)="will be returned as false.  Then the current ICN on file in VistA for the "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,4,0)="patient is found and sent to PCMM for other PACT assignments. These will "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,5,0)="likely be remote assignments and will be stored in the Outpatient Profile "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,6,0)="File(#404.41), CPRS PC WINDOW CACHE Field (#.07) . If nothing is found "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,7,0)="using the ICN the SCVALUE variable is returned as false and the popup "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,8,0)="reflects."
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,9,0)="A secondary query will use the  Integration Control Number (ICN) instead "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,10,0)="of DFN to find assignments. Any positive results from the secondary query "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,11,0)="using the ICN would be any remote assignments. The remote assignments "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,12,0)="found in PCMM will added to the Outpatient Profile File (#404.41), CPRS PC"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,13,0)="WINDOW CACHE Field (#.07), and displayed in the CPRS PCMM Details Popup "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,14,0)="window. If the secondary query using the ICN does not return results then "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,15,0)="""no remote assignments"" will be added to the Outpatient Profile File "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,16,0)="(#404.41), CPRS PC WINDOW CACHE Field (#.07) and displayed in the CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,17,0)="PCMM Details Popup"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,19,0)="The CPRS PCMM HEADER and the CPRS PCMM DETAIL Popup window display "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,20,0)="message will be changed to better reflect no PACT assignments. If there "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,21,0)="are no results from the secondary query. The CPRS PCMM Header currently "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,22,0)="displays the message ""No PACT assigned at any VA location"". This default "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,23,0)="information comes from routine SCMCSW1 and will be changed to ""No PACT "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,24,0)="assigned at this VA location(Click for more) "". The CPRS PCMM Details "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,25,0)="popup will reflect ""There is no local or remote assignment for this "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,26,0)="patient at this time.  Please contact local PCMM Coordinator to"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",681,1,27,0)="review.""  "
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",682,0)="893 SEQ #743^3241126.123443^89"
^DIC(9.4,48,22,5.28,"PAH",682,1,0)="^^79^79^3241126"
