^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",66,1,0)="^^1^1^3010103"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",66,1,1,0)="Reasonable Charges v1.1 and related updates."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",67,0)="140 SEQ #130^3010103^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",67,1,0)="^^1^1^3010103"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",67,1,1,0)="TRANSFER PRICING UPDATE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",68,0)="139 SEQ #131^3010103^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",68,1,0)="^^10^10^3010103"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",68,1,1,0)="This patch fixes the List Plans by Insurance Company option.  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",68,1,2,0)="The SHORT ID was not listing for those patients that "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",68,1,3,0)="had an Eligibility of Tricare/Champus.  This patch also fixes "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",68,1,4,0)="the updating of the COVERED BY HEALTH INSURANCE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",68,1,5,0)="fields in the patient file when the verify coverage of insurance"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",68,1,6,0)="prompt is answered. This patch also fixes the due date for the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",68,1,7,0)="patients Means Test.  After the leap year date of 2/29 the due dates "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",68,1,8,0)="for the means test are off by 1.  This  patch fixes this."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",68,1,9,0)="This patch also adds the new Outpatient Co-pay Rate of $50.80 into the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",68,1,10,0)="Charge Master."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,0)="143 SEQ #133^3010228^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,0)="^^18^18^3010228"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,1,0)="This patch fixes two data related problems with sending "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,2,0)="specific data to the fiscal intermediary for billing "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,3,0)="Tricare patients. The fiscal intermediary is requiring "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,4,0)="the DEA# be sent in place of Prescriber ID for a "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,5,0)="provider reference. For the drug, a zero was being "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,6,0)="sent to the fiscal intermediary as the number of"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,7,0)="ingredients in a prescription.  The fiscal intermediary "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,8,0)="is requiring a 1 (non-compound drug) or a 2 (compound drug)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,9,0)="for the number of ingredients.  Claims are being rejected "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,10,0)="at some sites because the fiscal intermediary is requiring "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,11,0)="more specific data values for these two fields."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,12,0)="Some sites are not having any problems with this and do "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,13,0)="not want to change and send more specific values for these "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,14,0)="two fields.  Two new fields have been added to "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,15,0)="the IB SITE PARAMETERS file so the sites can choose "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,16,0)="to send the DEA# vs the Prescriber ID,  and choose "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,17,0)="to send the more specific 1 or 2 for the compound code "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",69,1,18,0)="as opposed to a zero."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",70,0)="130 SEQ #134^3010228^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",70,1,0)="^^1^1^3010228"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",70,1,1,0)="Support for AR Third Party Payments report."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",71,0)="149 SEQ #135^3010228^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",71,1,0)="^^1^1^3010228"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",71,1,1,0)="Fix for Insurance Buffer delay problem."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",72,0)="141 SEQ #136^3010319^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",72,1,0)="^^1^1^3010319"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",72,1,1,0)="IB Insurance Buffer API for 1010EZ."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",73,0)="146 SEQ #137^3010326^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",73,1,0)="^^1^1^3010326"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",73,1,1,0)="MRA Extract patch."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",74,0)="51^3010329^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",74,1,0)="^^1^1^3010329"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",74,1,1,0)="BILLING ENHANCEMENTS FOR EDI"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",75,0)="151 SEQ #139^3010405^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",75,1,0)="^^10^10^3010405"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",75,1,1,0)="This patch corrects two problems."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",75,1,2,0)="1.  The first problem affects HCFA-1500 bills that were created"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",75,1,3,0)="prior to the installation of patch IB*2.0*51.  If there was already data"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",75,1,4,0)="in the BLOCK 31 data field (screen 8 of the ENTER/EDIT BILLING SCREENS),"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",75,1,5,0)="but not in the provider multiple, there should have been an error on"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",75,1,6,0)="authorization of this bill, but the edit check was erroneously passing."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",75,1,7,0)="2.  The second problem affects institutional claims that have professional"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",75,1,8,0)="components that require a separate HCFA 1500 bill to be produced.  The TC"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",75,1,9,0)="modifier should not be copied over to the professional bill when the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",75,1,10,0)="automatic copy from the institutional to the professional bill is done."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",76,0)="145^3010412^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",76,1,0)="^^10^10^3010412"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",76,1,1,0)="Changes have been made to routines IBOMTC and IBOMTC1 to"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",76,1,2,0)="identify Purple Heart patients. When the Cat C Activities report is run,"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",76,1,3,0)="the PH indicator is checked and Purple Heart patients are flagged on"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",76,1,4,0)="the report.  Purple Heart patients will be identified by an '*' in"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",76,1,5,0)="front of their name.  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",76,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",76,1,7,0)="The report has also been edited to give the user a choice of listing only"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",76,1,8,0)="Purple Heart recipients or both Purple Heart and non recipients. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",76,1,9,0)="If the user chooses to list only Purple Heart recipients, the report"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",76,1,10,0)="starting date is defaulted to November 30, 1999."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",77,0)="123 SEQ #141^3010517^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",77,1,0)="^^4^4^3010517"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",77,1,1,0)="This is the KIDS distribution for patch IB*2*123, Diagnostic"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",77,1,2,0)="Measures Phase IV. The accompanying Accounts Receivable patch"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",77,1,3,0)="is PRCA*4.5*167. This patch also fixes the problem reported in"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",77,1,4,0)="the Third Party Follow-up Report - NOIS #OKL-0100-72387."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",78,0)="154 SEQ #142^3010529^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",78,1,0)="^^3^3^3010529"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",78,1,1,0)="This patch updates the ACCOUNTS RECEIVABLE CATEGORY (#.06) in the RATE TYPE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",78,1,2,0)="(#399.3) file for the DENTAL entry from ""INELIGIBLE HOSP"" to ""EMERGENCY/"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",78,1,3,0)="HUMANITARIAN""."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",79,0)="150 SEQ #143^3010608^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",79,1,0)="^^1^1^3010608"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",79,1,1,0)="IB*2*150 OUTPATIENT MEDICATION COPAY CAP PHASE 1, PATCH 1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",80,0)="148 SEQ #144^3010625^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",80,1,0)="^^1^1^3010625"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",80,1,1,0)="Reasonable Charges v1.2"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,0)="152 SEQ #145^3010710^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,0)="^^35^35^3010710"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,1,0)="This patch contains fixes to minor problems introduced by patch IB*2*51"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,2,0)="NOIS entries fixed include:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,4,0)="SPO-0501-50868   If there is a print order on duplicate procedures for a"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,5,0)="HCFA 1500 bill, only the first duplicate procedure prints, although the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,6,0)="total charges reflect the total of the duplicate procedures."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,8,0)="DUR-0501-30976   There was a hard error encountered when duplicate"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,9,0)="procedures existed with different box 24 free text or box 24K data."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,11,0)="ALT-0501-20830   Sites with a marital status file whose internal entry"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,12,0)="numbers differ from the national standard are getting erroneous data on"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,13,0)="the HCFA 1500 and UB92 bills."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,15,0)="LOM-0401-62250   Multiple page UB92's printed an extra page if the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,16,0)="description portion of box 44 exceeded one page."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,18,0)="LOM-0401-61961  The patient's name was not printing in boxes 12 and 13"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,19,0)="on the HCFA 1500 if the bill was for other than reimbursable insurance."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,21,0)="LOM-0501-61752: The treatment authorization code was not printing in"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,22,0)="box 63 of the UB92 if the bill was for other than reimbursable insurance."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,23,0)="This same problem was found with the INSURANCE CO NUMBER (box 60),"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,24,0)="RELEASE OF INFORMATION (box 52) and ASSIGNMENT OF BENEFITS (box 53)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,26,0)="SLC-0501-51272: The help text on the PERFORMED BY field of the PROVIDERS"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,27,0)="multiple (#222) of the BILL CLAIMS file (#399) should not reference"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,28,0)="SLF000 as a valid entry.  This can be seen on screen 8 of the BILLING"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,29,0)="SCREENS in the PROVIDERS edit group."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,31,0)="STC-0501-42551: Most Commonly Used Outpt CPT Codes Rpt is missing the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,32,0)="procedure short name."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,34,0)="CHY-0501-52377: The insured's id number was not printing in box 1A o"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",81,1,35,0)="the HCFA 1500 if the bill was for other than reimbursable insurance."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",82,0)="142 SEQ #146^3010802^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",82,1,0)="^^9^9^3010802"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",82,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",82,1,2,0)="PASSING OF REASON CANCEL TO AR:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",82,1,3,0)="==============================="
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",82,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",82,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",82,1,6,0)="This is the Passing Of Reason Cancel to AR KID's Distribution for Patch"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",82,1,7,0)="IB*2.0*142. For specific information relating to the installation of this"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",82,1,8,0)="KID's distribution please see the National Patch Module section Patch"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",82,1,9,0)="Description subsection Installation Instructions."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",83,0)="158 SEQ #147^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",83,1,0)="^^1^1^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",83,1,1,0)="FIX RX COPAY RESET/REMOVE CHARGES"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",84,0)="160 SEQ #148^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",84,1,0)="^^1^1^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",84,1,1,0)="Update Claims Tracking to accept the original fill of a Prescription."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",85,0)="153 SEQ #149^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",85,1,0)="^^1^1^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",85,1,1,0)="ELIMINATE MEANS TEST CATEGORY"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",86,0)="159 SEQ #150^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",86,1,0)="^^2^2^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",86,1,1,0)="This is the KIDS distribution for patch IB*2*159, Diagnostic Measures"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",86,1,2,0)="Updates."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",87,0)="157 SEQ #151^3011016^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",87,1,0)="^^2^2^3011016"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",87,1,1,0)="This patch changes the NUMBER OF DAYS PT CHARGES HELD field (#7.04)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",87,1,2,0)="in the IB SITE PARAMETERS file #350.9 from 150 to 90."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",88,0)="164 SEQ #152^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",88,1,0)="^^4^4^3011210"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",88,1,1,0)="This is the first phase of the LTC COPAYMENTS project. This software"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",88,1,2,0)="change will not become effective until the LTC REG is passed into law,"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",88,1,3,0)="which is expected in DEC 2001. Once the law is passed, another patch"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",88,1,4,0)="will be sent to the field which will ACTIVATED this software change."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",89,0)="166 SEQ #153^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",89,1,0)="^^1^1^3011210"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",89,1,1,0)="STOP OUTPATIENT COPAY BILLING PENDING IMPLEMENTATION"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",90,0)="156 SEQ #154^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",90,1,0)="^^1^1^3011210"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",90,1,1,0)="OUTPATIENT MEDICATION COPAY CAP PHASE 1, PATCH 2 AND PHASE 2"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",91,0)="168 SEQ #155^3020116^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",92,0)="167 SEQ #156^3020204^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",92,1,0)="^^2^2^3020204"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",92,1,1,0)="This patch implements functionality to support the outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",92,1,2,0)="visit co-payment regulation."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",93,0)="174 SEQ #159^3020327^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",93,1,0)="^^1^1^3020327"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",93,1,1,0)="IB update due to Prosthetics Encounter changes (RMPR*3*62)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",94,0)="137^3020423^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",94,1,0)="^^6^6^3020423"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",94,1,1,0)="This patch contains the functionality to begin electronic billing through"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",94,1,2,0)="the clearinghouse WebMD.  See the patch module and release notes that"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",94,1,3,0)="accompany this patch for further documentation."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",94,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",94,1,5,0)="INCLUDES NOIS: RIC-0501-22630 "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",94,1,6,0)="               ROS-0601-52681"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",95,0)="177 SEQ #161^3020516^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",95,1,0)="^^1^1^3020516"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",95,1,1,0)="Update of visit copay tiers."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",96,0)="171 SEQ #162^3020528^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",96,1,0)="^^1^1^3020528"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",96,1,1,0)="IB*2*171 MILL BILL LTC, PHASE 2, PATCH 1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",97,0)="178 SEQ #163^3020528^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",97,1,0)="^^11^11^3020528"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",97,1,1,0)="The patch contains modification of Outpatient Copay (RX) software to "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",97,1,2,0)="limit execution of RPC ""IBARXM QUERY ONLY"" with VAMC, M&ROC and RO-OC"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",97,1,3,0)="facilities only."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",97,1,4,0)="Besides this, the patch also contains a new RPC, ""IBARXM QUERY SUPPRESS"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",97,1,5,0)="USER"" to replace ""IBARXM QUERY ONLY"". The new RPC does not transmit user"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",97,1,6,0)="data to remote side. Two existing calls have been modified to suppress"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",97,1,7,0)="sending user data to remote side:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",97,1,8,0)="IBARXM TRANS BILL"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",97,1,9,0)="IBARXM TRANS DATA"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",97,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",97,1,11,0)="The patch resolves NOIS # BUT-0502-21665."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",98,0)="161 SEQ #164^3020605^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",98,1,0)="^^1^1^3020605"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",98,1,1,0)="ClaimsManager Interface"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",99,0)="181 SEQ #165^3020724^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",99,1,0)="^^2^2^3020724"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",99,1,1,0)="This patch contains maintenance fixes and updates for Electronic Billing "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",99,1,2,0)="(EDI) Patch IB*2*137."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",100,0)="186 SEQ #166^3020814^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",101,0)="189 SEQ #167^3020906^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",101,1,0)="^^1^1^3020906"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",101,1,1,0)="Corrects bad EDI IDs in insurance company file."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",102,0)="176^3020927^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",102,1,0)="^^2^2^3020927"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",102,1,1,0)="Patch IB*2*176 was created to implement the Long Term Care (LTC) "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",102,1,2,0)="Copayment requirements."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",103,0)="196 SEQ #169^3020927^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",103,1,0)="^^2^2^3020927"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",103,1,1,0)="This is an emergency patch to fix the problem of batches not being found "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",103,1,2,0)="when a confirmation message is received by the EDI server from Austin."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",104,0)="179 SEQ #170^3020927^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",104,1,0)="^^1^1^3020927"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",104,1,1,0)="Hold all Inpatient MT bills for GMT."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",105,0)="187 SEQ #171^3020927^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",105,1,0)="^^1^1^3020927"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",105,1,1,0)="Visit Copay Phase 2 project."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",106,0)="191 SEQ #172^3020927^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",106,1,0)="^^1^1^3020927"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",106,1,1,0)="EDI Maintenance patch."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,0)="193 SEQ #173^3020927^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,0)="^^18^18^3020927"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,1,0)="On July 31st, 2002 the EDI system's method of identifying EDI routing ids "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,2,0)="for insurance companies in Vista was changed.  As a result of this "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,3,0)="change, a problem occurred in Vista whereby the text PAYID was "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,4,0)="erroneously inserted into some insurance company EDI routing ids."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,6,0)="Patch IB*2*189 corrected the problem of the bad id being stored and"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,7,0)="deleted the text PAYID from the EDI routing id fields. Any claims"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,8,0)="submitted after this patch was installed would not have been affected by"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,9,0)="this problem, but claims submitted between July 31st and the installation"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,10,0)="of patch 189 may have been sent to the wrong payers."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,12,0)="In an effort to help the sites identify and resubmit these claims, this "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,13,0)="patch was created.  The options included in this patch must be run by the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,14,0)="IRM staff as the elements of this patch are used solely to correct this"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,15,0)="specific problem and will not become part of official VistA software.  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,16,0)="Integrated Billing must be involved to review the report of misrouted"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,17,0)="claims to indicate the ones the site does NOT want to automatically"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",107,1,18,0)="resubmit."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",108,0)="195 SEQ #174^3021025^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",108,1,0)="^^3^3^3021025"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",108,1,1,0)="The patch resolves the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",108,1,2,0)="  NOIS NJH-0102-22792"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",108,1,3,0)="  NOIS MAN-0802-10732"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",109,0)="198 SEQ #175^3021025^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",109,1,0)="^^1^1^3021025"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",109,1,1,0)="API CHANGE AND CLEAN UP DATE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",110,0)="162 SEQ #176^3021108^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",110,1,0)="^^6^6^3021108"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",110,1,1,0)="This patch fixes the problem when prescriptions billed through the RNA"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",110,1,2,0)="engine are rejected with a error of 'NDC is not covered' for claims sent"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",110,1,3,0)="to the Fiscal Intermediary."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",110,1,4,0)="Resubmitting a pharmacy claim to the Fiscal Intermediary allows the user"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",110,1,5,0)="to choose a product selection reason code which will allow the correct"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",110,1,6,0)="code to be submitted to the Fiscal Intermediary for billing acceptance."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",111,0)="188 SEQ #177^3021209^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",111,1,0)="^^1^1^3021209"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",111,1,1,0)="LTC PHASE III"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",112,0)="183^3021220^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",112,1,0)="^^1^1^3021220"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",112,1,1,0)="GEOGRAPHIC MEANS TEST, IB PART 2"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",113,0)="163 SEQ #179^3030109^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",113,1,0)="^^3^3^3030109"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",113,1,1,0)="This patch deletes obsolete options from IB menus and from the IB package."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",113,1,2,0)="It will also make some changes to the List Manager screens for the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",113,1,3,0)="Insurance Co Edit."
