^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,226,0)="SOFTWARE AND DOCUMENTATION RETRIEVAL"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,227,0)="===================================="
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,228,0)="The software for this patch is being distributed in host file "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,229,0)="BPS_1_0.KID.  The host file will contain seven KIDS builds."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,230,0)="The builds contained in the BPS 1.0 multi-package distribution are:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,231,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,232,0)="     Package                    Patches"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,233,0)="     -------                    ----------------------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,234,0)="     ECME                       BPS*1.0*1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,235,0)="     Pharmacy Data Management   PSS*1.0*81"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,236,0)="     Integrated Billing         IB*2.0*223, IB*2.0*251"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,237,0)="     Accounts Receivable        PRCA*4.5*202"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,238,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,239,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,240,0)="Please refer to the 'Software and Documentation Retrieval' section of the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,241,0)="BPS*1.0*1 patch description for instructions on how to acquire the patch "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,242,0)="software and documentation."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,243,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,244,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,245,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,246,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,247,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,248,0)="1. Use VA FileMan to add the new domain, EPHARMACY.VITRIA-EDI.AAC.DOMAIN.EXT, "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,249,0)="to the DOMAIN file (#4.2). The installation instructions are included in "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,250,0)="the patch description for the XM*DBA*160 patch. This domain must be in "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,251,0)="place before the installation of the IB*2*251 patch that is included in "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,252,0)="the BPS 1.0 Master Build."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,253,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,254,0)="2. Download the KIDS file BPS_1_0.KID via FTP. This file needs to be "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,255,0)="retrieved in ASCII format."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,257,0)="3. Review mapped sets for the PSS*, IB*, and PRCA*namespaces.  If the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,258,0)="routines are mapped, they should be removed from the mapped set at this "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,259,0)="time."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,260,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,261,0)="4. From the Kernel Installation & Distribution System menu, select the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,262,0)="Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,263,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,264,0)="5.  From this menu, select the Load a Distribution option. When prompted "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,265,0)="for a file name, enter "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,266,0)="the directory name where you FTPd the build, followed by BPS_1_0. In our "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,267,0)="example, the file name is USER$:[ANONYMOUS]BPS_1_0.KID. Determine the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,268,0)="location where you stored your build to decide the correct file name "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,269,0)="entry."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,270,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,271,0)="6. At the ""Want to Continue with Load? YES//"" prompt, enter YES."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,272,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,273,0)="7. At the ""Want to RUN the Environment Check Routine: YES//"" prompt, "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,274,0)="answer YES."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,275,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,276,0)="8. From this menu, the installer may select to use the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,277,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,278,0)="(When prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter BPS 1.0)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,279,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,280,0)="    a. Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,281,0)="message of any routines exported with the patch. It will NOT backup any "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,282,0)="other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,283,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,284,0)="    b. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,285,0)="allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch is "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,286,0)="installed. It compares all components of the patch (routines, DDs, "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,287,0)="templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,288,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,289,0)="    c. Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will ensure the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,290,0)="integrity of the routines that are in the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,291,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,292,0)="9. At the ""Select Installation Option:"" prompt, enter 6 Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,293,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,294,0)="10. At the ""Select INSTALL NAME:"" prompt, enter BPS 1.0."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,295,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,296,0)="11. When prompted, ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,297,0)="Install? YES//"" respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,298,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,299,0)="12. When prompted, ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,300,0)="YES//"" respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,301,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,302,0)="13. When prompted, ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,303,0)="Protocols? YES//"" respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,304,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,305,0)="14. When prompted, ""Device:Home//"" respond with the correct device and DO "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,306,0)="NOT queue this to P-Message."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,307,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,308,0)="15. If routines were unmapped as part of step 3, they should be returned "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",193,1,309,0)="to the mapped set once the installation has run to completion. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,0)="251^3041029^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,0)="^^50^50^3041029"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,1,0)="The Healthcare Insurance Portability and Accountability Act National "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,2,0)="Council for Prescription Drug Programs (HIPAA NCPDP) initiative, whose "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,3,0)="ultimate goal is to provide functionality allowing electronic transmission"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,4,0)="of Outpatient Pharmacy (OP) prescription claims to payers and the receipt "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,5,0)="of claim responses (including drug utilization review responses and "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,6,0)="warnings) on a real-time basis, is being developed and introduced in a "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,7,0)="phased implementation strategy. This deployment strategy was utilized due "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,8,0)="to the complexity of the functionality and the number of product line "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,9,0)="dependencies."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,11,0)="The first release of this two part implementation is BPS*1*0, comprised of"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,12,0)="the new Electronic Claims Management Engine (ECME) package (in the BPS "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,13,0)="namespace), plus the patches PSS*1*81, IB*2.0*223, IB*2.0*251, and "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,14,0)="PRCA*4.5*202, which are listed here in order of installation. BPS*1*0 is a"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,15,0)="dormant release that only allows each site to perform preliminary setup "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,16,0)="work and to confirm that the software does not adversely affect other "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,17,0)="packages."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,19,0)="This is the IB*2.0*251 patch and it provides modified and new components "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,20,0)="associated with the following specific requirements:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,21,0)="* Send Interface Version Number in e-IIV Registration Message."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,22,0)="* Update Pharmacy Benefits Manager (PBM) Table"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,23,0)="* Update NCPDP Processor Table"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,24,0)="* Update Payer Table"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,25,0)="* Update Plan Table"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,26,0)="* Update Pharmacy Plan Table"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,27,0)="* Provide Pharmacy Plan NCPDP Claim Submission Status and Information via"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,28,0)="Callable Routine"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,29,0)="* Display Pharmacy Plan Information Based on User Selected Sort Criteria"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,30,0)="* Display Qualified Group Plans to Help Link Pharmacy Plan to Group"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,31,0)="Insurance Plan"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,32,0)="* Link Pharmacy Plan to Group Insurance Plan"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,33,0)="* Link Pharmacy Plan to Multiple Group Insurance Plan"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,34,0)="* Link Test Payer Sheet to Pharmacy Plan"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,35,0)="* Edit Pharmacy Benefits Manager (PBM) Local Active Flag"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,36,0)="* Edit NCPDP Processor Local Active Flag"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,37,0)="* Edit Payer Local Active Flag"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,38,0)="* Edit Plan / Pharmacy Plan Local Active Flag"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,39,0)="* Edit HIPAA NCPDP Flag"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,40,0)="* Store and Track Banking Identification Numbers (BIN) and Processing"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,41,0)="Control Numbers (PCN) From Patient Insurance Cards"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,43,0)="The Vitria Interface Engine (IE) BusinessWare product will be utilized in "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,44,0)="this project.   The IE will provide:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,45,0)="* HL7 message routing tables for directing incoming and outgoing VistA"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,46,0)="HL7 messages"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,47,0)="* HL7 message translation mechanisms for handling various versions of"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,48,0)="VistA compatible HL7 messages"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,49,0)="* HL7 message error handling capability"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",194,1,50,0)="* Data mapping utility"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",195,0)="155^3041029^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",195,1,0)="^^5^5^3041029"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",195,1,1,0)="This patch contains the functionality to begin electronically requesting"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",195,1,2,0)="and receiving MEDICARE REMITTANCE ADVICE (MRA) from MEDICARE for those"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",195,1,3,0)="patients who have MEDICARE coverage as well as other coverage that is"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",195,1,4,0)="secondary to MEDICARE. See the patch module and release notes that"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",195,1,5,0)="accompany this patch for further documentation."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",196,0)="275 SEQ #263^3041111^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",197,0)="290 SEQ #264^3041124^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",197,1,0)="^^2^2^3041124"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",197,1,1,0)="This patch removes the printing of the SSN from the UB92 and the HCFA"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",197,1,2,0)="1500 claim forms when they are printed locally."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,0)="288 SEQ #265^3041228^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,0)="^^31^31^3041228"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,1,0)="MRA (Medicare Remittance Advice) Enhancements"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,3,0)="1.  Allow Medicare to populate the ""AE"" x-ref in the Bill/Claims file"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,4,0)="2.  Allow Denied MRAs for duplicate claim/service to be screened off of "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,5,0)="the MRA management worklist"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,6,0)="3.  Correct the MRA Statistics report for the auto-generated claim data"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,7,0)="4.  Fix the person/non-person indicator for Fee Basis providers (File "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,8,0)="364.7/ien's 1034-1037)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,9,0)="5.  Fix the period in names to correct suffix problem (IBCEFG1)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,10,0)="6.  Remove redundant code; Fix state for license # extract for Non-VA "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,11,0)="providers (IBCEF71)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,12,0)="7.  Move the Medicare assigned number 670899 hospital provider number and "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,13,0)="professional provider number to the new location in file 355.92.  Only "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,14,0)="the MEDICARE (WNR) entry is modified."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,15,0)="8.  Restore changes to billing screen 5 when the principle diagnosis is "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,16,0)="missing.  The field prompt will tell the users if the diagnosis code is "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,17,0)="required or not.  It will say either UNSPECIFIED or UNSPECIFIED [NOT "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,18,0)="REQUIRED]."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,19,0)="9.  Set the 837 test transmission queue to be ""MCT""."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,20,0)="10.  Add a new IB edit so that the subscriber's date of birth must exist "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,21,0)="for all insurances on the claim."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,22,0)="11.  When cloning an MRA bill and manually changing the payer sequence to "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,23,0)="be secondary, update the CLAIM MRA STATUS field to indicate that an MRA "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,24,0)="is not needed for this new claim."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,25,0)="12.  Fix a hard error when accessing the non-VA provider add/edit"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,26,0)="functionality using the option NON-VA Facility Data [IBCE PRVNVA FAC EDIT]."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,27,0)="The error occurs because the code is used by both list manager and option"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,28,0)="functions and the list manager variables are not set in the option call."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,29,0)="The fix is to make the calls to the  list manager specific code conditional"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,30,0)="on it being called via a list manager action. (IBCEP8)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",198,1,31,0)="13.  Cancelled claims cannot appear on the CSA screen."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",199,0)="267 SEQ #266^3041228^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",199,1,0)="^^5^5^3041228"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",199,1,1,0)="This patch is a re-release of IB*2.0*256 to standardize existing"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",199,1,2,0)="VistA Integrated Billing calls.  All direct IB touch points will"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",199,1,3,0)="be replaced with standard API's available to all VistA packages."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",199,1,4,0)="This patch is enhancing the API call INSUR^IBBAPI that"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",199,1,5,0)="returns Insurance information."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",200,0)="295 SEQ #267^3041228^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",200,1,0)="^^2^2^3041228"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",200,1,1,0)="This patch installs the CY-2005 Medicare Deductible rate and the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",200,1,2,0)="base pension rates for determining co-pay exemption."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",201,0)="297^3050204^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",201,1,0)="^^1^1^3050204"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",201,1,1,0)="Update to insurance API and Insurance Clean Up"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",202,0)="291 SEQ #269^3050204^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",202,1,0)="^^10^10^3050204"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",202,1,1,0)="This patch contains the following changes:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",202,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",202,1,3,0)="1.  Adds a parameter to the insurance company to specify whether the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",202,1,4,0)="provider's SSN is to print on the HCFA and the UB92."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",202,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",202,1,6,0)="2.  Adds the capability to override the GROUP# field on transmitted claims."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",202,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",202,1,8,0)="3.  Fixes a problem where the ?ID action on screen 8 of the edit bill"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",202,1,9,0)="screens displays the wrong provider type for other than attending/rendering"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",202,1,10,0)="providers."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,0)="294 SEQ #270^3050204^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,0)="^^16^16^3050204"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,1,0)="MRA ISSUES RESOLUTIONS AND BUG FIXES"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,3,0)="1.  MRA statistics report changes."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,4,0)="  1a.  Include totals for all divisions or all selected divisions when"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,5,0)="       more than 1 division is included in the report."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,6,0)="  1b.  Corrected a bug in which MRA request transmissions on the same date"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,7,0)="       as the ending date for the report were not being counted."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,8,0)="  1c.  Corrected a bug in which MRA secondary transmissions were being "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,9,0)="       counted. Now, only MRA request transmissions during the report date"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,10,0)="       range are included in this report."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,12,0)="2.  If a professional claim already exists, prevent the creation of a new"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,13,0)="professional claim when requesting an MRA for an institutional claim.  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,14,0)="The payer sequence of the existing professional claim was changed to be a "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,15,0)="secondary claim and thus VistA was not detecting it.  The change in this "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",203,1,16,0)="patch removes the check on the payer sequence in the case of MRA claims."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",204,0)="271 SEQ #271^3050311^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",204,1,0)="^^8^8^3050311"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",204,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following NOIS messages:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",204,1,2,0)="------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",204,1,3,0)="BAY-0204-31962         IIV inquiries are increasing"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",204,1,4,0)="FGH-0304-32103         Important IIV Msg-Monetary Amount"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",204,1,5,0)="UNY-0204-11346         ERROR - CHK+23^IBCNEHLQ"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",204,1,6,0)="WPB-0904-32212         ERROR - EN+43^IBCNEDE2:1, %DSM-E-NULLSUBSCR"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",204,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",204,1,8,0)="This patch also includes several enhancements for the IIV interface."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",205,0)="285 SEQ #272^3050311^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",205,1,0)="^^2^2^3050311"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",205,1,1,0)="This patch distributes the latest DRG Reasonable Charges files."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",205,1,2,0)="This is Version 2.3 with an effective date of 01/01/2005."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",206,0)="287 SEQ #273^3050311^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",206,1,0)="^^1^1^3050311"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",206,1,1,0)="Reasonable Charges v2.2.  Enhancements only, no charges."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",207,0)="298 SEQ #274^3050506^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",207,1,0)="^^2^2^3050506"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",207,1,1,0)="Patch IB*2.0*298 is the release of the Reasonable Charges v2.4 update."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",207,1,2,0)="These charges are effective 04/11/2005."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",208,0)="279 SEQ #275^3050525^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",208,1,0)="^^1^1^3050525"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",208,1,1,0)="This patch corrects invalid Care Unit combination pointers if any exist."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",209,0)="249 SEQ #276^3050525^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,0)="306 SEQ #277^3050625^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,0)="^^15^15^3050625"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,1,0)="The purpose of this patch is to update VistA DSS Stop Codes for outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,2,0)="copay in the IB CLINIC STOP CODE BILLABLE TYPES file (#352.5), which "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,3,0)="begins May 2, 2005. The required copay for the smoking cessation"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,4,0)="counseling (individual and group) codes will be changed to a non-copay"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,5,0)="status."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,7,0)="The patch will update the billable type for the following stop codes in"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,8,0)="the file."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,10,0)="   Clinic Stop  Description            Effective   Billable      Override"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,11,0)="   Code                                Date        Type          Flag"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,12,0)="   -----------  ---------------------  ----------  ------------  ---------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,13,0)="   533707       SMOKING CESSATION IND  05/02/2005  Non-Billable  Y"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,14,0)="   566707       SMOKING CESSATION GRP  05/02/2005  Non-Billable  Y"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",210,1,15,0)="   707          SMOKING CESSATION      05/02/2005  Non-Billable  Y"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",211,0)="307 SEQ #278^3050709^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",211,1,0)="^^1^1^3050709"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",211,1,1,0)="CMAC 2005"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",212,0)="301 SEQ #279^3050813^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",212,1,0)="^^8^8^3050813"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",212,1,1,0)="CBO Data Extract enhancements"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",212,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",212,1,3,0)="Routine IBJVDEQ"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",212,1,4,0)="Make sure the claim has been authorized before proceeding with the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",212,1,5,0)="extract."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",212,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",212,1,7,0)="Routine IBRFN4"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",212,1,8,0)="Provide a callable API for IB information."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,0)="296 SEQ #280^3050905^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,0)="^^115^115^3050905"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,1,0)="Routines: IBCE837, IBCE837A"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,2,0)="  Changes to allow test claims to be resubmitted from previously"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,3,0)="  transmitted claims."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,5,0)="Routines: IBCESRV"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,6,0)="  Changes server logic for reports to send test message flag if msg"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,7,0)="  received in test queue."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,9,0)="Routines: IBCEM01, IBCEM02, IBCEM03"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,10,0)="  Allows selection of existing batches or individual claims to be"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,11,0)="  re-submitted as test claims from the original EDI resubmit bill/batch"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,12,0)="  options."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,14,0)="Routine: IBCNSGE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,15,0)="  Insurance Company EDI Parameter Report"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,17,0)="Routine: IBCEF2"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,18,0)="  Pull the id from the insurance company file if the claim is an MRA "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,19,0)="  secondary and the id exists. If there is no id, force PPRNT or IPRNT. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,21,0)="Routine IBCEF21"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,22,0)="  Two procedures moved out of IBCEF2 and into IBCEF21 for space."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,24,0)="Routine: IBCEF31"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,25,0)="  Ensure that the electronic insurance type field for the Medicare (WNR) "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,26,0)="  entry is always 3:MEDICARE.  This is the 3.09 field in file 36."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,28,0)="Routine: IBCEF4"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,29,0)="  Change to return a true value if the claim is being resubmitted as a"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,30,0)="  test claim."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,32,0)="Routine: IBCEF"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,33,0)="  Bug fix to the $$NOPUNCT function.  Allow the exclusions parameter to "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,34,0)="  function properly."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,36,0)="Routine: IBCBB2"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,37,0)="  Change to allow 8 diagnoses codes. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,39,0)="Routine: IBY296PR (new)  (pre-install)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,40,0)="  Pre-install changes the data element for entry #1015 in file 364.7"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,42,0)="Routine: IBCERPT"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,43,0)="  Changed to output "" * * TEST RESULTS * * "" on reports from the MCT queue"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,45,0)="Routine: IBCEPTU (new)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,46,0)="  Utility code added to allow lookup of last transmitted date when a"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,47,0)="  transmission entry is deleted for an entry in file 361.4"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,49,0)="Routine: IBCEPTR"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,50,0)="  Report of data stored in file 361.4."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,52,0)="Routine: IBCESRV, IBCESRV2"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,53,0)="  Changed to capture the MCT messages for claims resubmitted for test and"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,54,0)="  send them to be stored in the new test claim message file"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,56,0)="Routine: IBCEPTM (new)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,57,0)="  Stores the transmission and test status message data in file 361.4"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,59,0)="Routines: IBCEPTC, IBCEPTC1, IBCEPTC2 (new)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,60,0)="  New routines for the list manager display and resubmission of"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,61,0)="  previously transmitted claims as test claims."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,63,0)="Routine IBCE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,64,0)="  Modify the IB nightly job section to call the Purge routine for file "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,65,0)="  361.4."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,67,0)="Routines IBCEU0, IBCEU1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,68,0)="  Fix LCOB segment pieces (modifiers and payer id)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,70,0)="Routine IBCEOB1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,71,0)="  Fix split MRA filing problem.  Keep track of VistA line numbers across "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,72,0)="  multiple split MRAs in file 361.1."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,74,0)="Routine IBCCC2"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,75,0)="  Remove the code which deletes the BILL COPIED FROM field when "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,76,0)="  processing an MRA claim into a secondary MRA claim."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,78,0)="Routine IBCEP0B"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,79,0)="  Added a new parameter to the call PARAMS^IBCNSC1 to fix an undefined "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,80,0)="  variable error that was occuring as a result of Patch 291. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,82,0)="Routine IBCERP3"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,83,0)="  Report of bill batches waiting Austin receipt more than 1 day.  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,84,0)="  Modification to routine to make it more similar to routine IBCEBUL by "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,85,0)="  checking to see if there are any bills in the batch before including it "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,86,0)="  on this report."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,88,0)="Routine IBCERP5"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,89,0)="  Modify the batch status detail report to show claims from test batches "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,90,0)="  stored in file 361.4."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,92,0)="New field FILE 364.2:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,93,0)=" .14 CLAIM RESUBMITTED TEST"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,95,0)="Entries modified in file 364.7:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,96,0)=" #136 (changed entry for group #/group name exclusion CI3-3)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,97,0)=" #137 (changed entry for group #/group name exclusion CI3-4)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,98,0)=" #830 (changed to fix problem with LCOB records)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,99,0)=" #985 (changed to fix problem with LCOB records)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,100,0)=" #1006 (changed data element, ins type OI1-17)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,101,0)=" #1015 (changed data element, version info GEN-7)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,102,0)=" #1039 (new entry for current payer sequence CI1-14)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,103,0)=" #1040 (new entry for MRA secondary indicator CI1-15)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,105,0)="Entries modified in file 364.6:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,106,0)=" #1321 (new entry for current payer sequence CI1-14)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,107,0)=" #1322 (new entry for MRA secondary indicator CI1-15)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,108,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,109,0)="New File: 361.4 EDI TEST CLAIM STATUS MESSAGE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,110,0)="  Holds the test transmission and all test status messages received in"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,111,0)="  the test queue (MCT) for claims resubmitted as test."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,113,0)="NOIS ENTRIES INCLUDED:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,114,0)="UNY-0205-10041  SYNTAX ERROR 1/31 -MISSING LCOB-02"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",213,1,115,0)="LEX-0205-40005  SYNTAX ERROR 1/27 - LCOB/LCAS Prob."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",214,0)="260^3050905^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",214,1,0)="^^1^1^3050905"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",214,1,1,0)="Clinical Indicator Data Capture IB support."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",215,0)="309 SEQ #282^3051020^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",215,1,0)="^^3^3^3051020"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",215,1,1,0)="This patch will replace all the direct global references to Pharmacy data"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",215,1,2,0)="in the Integrated Billing package. The direct references will be replaced"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",215,1,3,0)="with API calls to the Pharmacy package."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",216,0)="317 SEQ #283^3051020^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",216,1,0)="^^1^1^3051020"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",216,1,1,0)="CLAIMS TRACKING ENHANCEMENT"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",217,0)="277 SEQ #284^3051115^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",217,1,0)="^^5^5^3051115"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",217,1,1,0)="This patch will address two issues;"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",217,1,2,0)="1. The Re-Generated Unbilled Amounts Report that is printing the CPT IEN "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",217,1,3,0)="instead of the CPT Code."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",217,1,4,0)="2. The Undefined error received while using Assign Reason Not Billable "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",217,1,5,0)="[IBT EDIT REASON NOT BILLABLE] option."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",218,0)="315 SEQ #285^3051115^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",218,1,0)="^^1^1^3051115"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",218,1,1,0)="PFSS ACCOUNT FILE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",219,0)="299 SEQ #286^3051202^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",219,1,0)="^^5^5^3051202"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",219,1,1,0)="When 'ACCEPTING' entries from the insurance buffer, it was discovered"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",219,1,2,0)="that some of the GROUP/PLAN fields (#.04 thru # .09) in the INSURANCE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",219,1,3,0)="BUFFER (#355.33) were not being updated in the INSURANCE file (#355.3)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",219,1,4,0)="Upon further review, a coding problem was found and corrected in the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",219,1,5,0)="INSURANCE BUFFER routine IBCNBMI."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",220,0)="326 SEQ #287^3051202^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",220,1,0)="^^3^3^3051202"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",220,1,1,0)="This patch will install the October 2005 Tortiously Liable, Cost-Based"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",220,1,2,0)="and, Interagency rates into the Charge Master, with an effective date "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",220,1,3,0)="of 10/01/05."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",221,0)="325 SEQ #288^3051202^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",221,1,0)="^^2^2^3051202"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",221,1,1,0)="This patch updates the Reasonable Charges files and distributes them with "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",221,1,2,0)="a new version number and new effective date."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",222,0)="330 SEQ #289^3051202^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",222,1,0)="^^2^2^3051202"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",222,1,1,0)="THIS PATCH WILL CHANGE THE MEDICATION COPAY TO $8 AND THE ANNUAL CAP"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",222,1,2,0)="TO $960 EFFECTIVE JANUARY 1, 2006"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",223,0)="328 SEQ #290^3051202^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",223,1,0)="^^1^1^3051202"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",223,1,1,0)="VISTA-OFFICE EHR FILE ENHANCEMENT"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",224,0)="333 SEQ #291^3051202^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",224,1,0)="^^3^3^3051202"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",224,1,1,0)="This patch will install the November 2005 Tortiously Liable, Cost-Based"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",224,1,2,0)="and, Interagency rates into the Charge Master, with an effective date "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",224,1,3,0)="of 11/03/2005."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",225,0)="329 SEQ #292^3051221^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",225,1,0)="^^1^1^3051221"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",225,1,1,0)="CMAC 2005 update for 'Non-Facility' charges."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,0)="316 SEQ #293^3051221^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,0)="^^17^17^3051221"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,1,0)="Patch attends to the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,3,0)="1) To help protect the users from sending out too many IIV inquiries in a "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,4,0)="given day, the HL7 MAXIMUM NUMBER field has been modified to be a "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,5,0)="required field."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,7,0)="2) To help protect the users from extracting too many IIV inquiries in a "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,8,0)="given day for a given IIV data extract, the MAXIMUM EXTRACT NUMBER field "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,9,0)="has been modified to be a required field."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,11,0)="3) Based on a decision from the VA Chief Business Office, it was decided "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,12,0)="that the most popular payer function should be removed. Any mention of "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,13,0)="this functionality should be eradicated from the IIV system."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,15,0)="4) IIV routines will automatically disable and enable journaling itself "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,16,0)="while doing the purge. A log of purges will now be kept in global ^ "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",226,1,17,0)="XTMP(""IBCNEKIT""."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",227,0)="331^3060112^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",228,0)="318^3060213^.5"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",228,1,0)="^^3^3^3060213"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",228,1,1,0)="Add SERVICE CONNECTED BILLABLE APPOINTMENT TYPE (#352.1) to correspond "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",228,1,2,0)="to the new SERVICE CONNECTED APPOINTMENT TYPE (#409.1) released by "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",228,1,3,0)="SD*5.3*394."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",229,0)="286 SEQ #296^3060213^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",229,1,0)="^^1^1^3060213"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",229,1,1,0)="This patch is the IB part of PFSS."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",230,0)="300 SEQ #297^3060213^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",230,1,0)="^^6^6^3060213"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",230,1,1,0)="The main purpose of this build is to restructure the way the HL7 messages"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",230,1,2,0)="are created for IIV.  In addition to encoding and decoding of HL7"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",230,1,3,0)="delimiters, asterisks will be removed from the data prior to transmission"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",230,1,4,0)="of the HL7 messages since asterisks are X12 delimiters.  The build also"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",230,1,5,0)="removes the application dependency of the IIV interface on the IP address"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",230,1,6,0)="and port number for routing.  Thus, making DBIA #4241 obsolete."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",231,0)="334 SEQ #298^3060308^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",231,1,0)="^^2^2^3060308"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",231,1,1,0)="Patch IB*2.0*334 is the release of the Reasonable Charges v2.6 update."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",231,1,2,0)="These charges are effective 01/01/2006."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",232,0)="322 SEQ #299^3060308^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",232,1,0)="^^8^8^3060308"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",232,1,1,0)="In preparation for the e-Pharmacy software package, insurance"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",232,1,2,0)="staff need to match their pharmacy group plans to the appropriate"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",232,1,3,0)="VA National Plan.  (For more detailed background information"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",232,1,4,0)="regarding this matching process, please refer to the web site"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",232,1,5,0)="http://vaww.vistau.domain.ext/VistaU/e-bp/e-pharmacy.htm and"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",232,1,6,0)="download the e-Pharmacy Claims Insurance Process User Guide"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",232,1,7,0)="There is other information available at this web site that you"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",232,1,8,0)="will find helpful regarding the e-Pharmacy project.)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",233,0)="321 SEQ #300^3060410^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",234,0)="292 SEQ #301^3060504^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",234,1,0)="^^2^2^3060504"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",234,1,1,0)="This patch modifies the Claims Tracking software to accept same date/time "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",234,1,2,0)="entries."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",235,0)="336 SEQ #302^3060504^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",235,1,0)="^^3^3^3060504"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",235,1,1,0)="Pharmacy Claims Tracking fix related to CIDC (patch IB*2.0*260)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",235,1,2,0)="Reason Not Billable will now be assigned appropriately for items"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",235,1,3,0)="entered prior to the CIDC patch."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",236,0)="340 SEQ #303^3060504^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",236,1,0)="^^6^6^3060504"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",236,1,1,0)="Patch IB*2*340 contains a single routine that supports the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",236,1,2,0)="implementation of patch PRCA*4.5*241.  This AR patch is the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",236,1,3,0)="last in a series of patches that adjusts the accounts of"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",236,1,4,0)="veterans affected by Hurricane Katrina.  Please refer to the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",236,1,5,0)="patch description for more specific information on patch"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",236,1,6,0)="IB*2*340."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",237,0)="323 SEQ #304^3060504^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",237,1,0)="^^3^3^3060504"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",237,1,1,0)="THIS PATCH WILL ADDRESS SEVERAL BUGS RELATED TO E-MRA."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",237,1,2,0)="THESE BUGS ARE INCLUDED IN THE PATCH DESCRIPTION WITH THEIR RESPECTIVE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",237,1,3,0)="REMEDY TICKETS."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",238,0)="276^3060525^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",238,1,0)="^^4^4^3060525"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",238,1,1,0)="HIPAA NCPDP Global project"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",238,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",238,1,3,0)="supports the electronic transmission outpatient prescription claims and "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",238,1,4,0)="billing collection and management."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",239,0)="308 SEQ #306^3060525^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",239,1,0)="^^1^1^3060525"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",239,1,1,0)="This patch is the inter-facility copay part of the PFSS project."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",240,0)="338 SEQ #307^3060526^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",240,1,0)="^^2^2^3060526"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",240,1,1,0)="The purpose of this patch is to add a value code of 'A0' (Special Zip"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",240,1,2,0)="Code Reporting) to the MCCR Utility file (#399.1)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",241,0)="335 SEQ #308^3060526^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",241,1,0)="^^2^2^3060526"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",241,1,1,0)="When the site executes the [IB COPY AND CANCEL] option, an undefined error"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",241,1,2,0)="generates at line <UNDEFINED>OUTPT+89^IBCEF11."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",242,0)="332 SEQ #309^3060608^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",242,1,0)="^^2^2^3060608"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",242,1,1,0)="Modify IB to handle the billing of the new and updated Treating Specialties"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",242,1,2,0)="being released, primarily for NHCU.  This patch supports DG*5.3*683."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",243,0)="337 SEQ #310^3060614^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",243,1,0)="^^2^2^3060614"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",243,1,1,0)="The Chief Business Office has requested to update the DSS Stop Codes"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",243,1,2,0)="to reflect the FY 06 Co-pay rates."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",244,0)="324 SEQ #311^3060711^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",244,1,0)="^^4^4^3060711"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",244,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one issue. The issue is about the batch which "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",244,1,2,0)="didn't process through the outside trading partner WebMD when the claim"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",244,1,3,0)="was missing the procedure for the modifier on the institutional service"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",244,1,4,0)="line."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",245,0)="327 SEQ #312^3060807^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",245,1,0)="^^3^3^3060807"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",245,1,1,0)="Prevents a claim from being an MRA request claim when Medicare (WNR) is "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",245,1,2,0)="the secondary insurance and prevents the deletion of MRA secondary "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",245,1,3,0)="insurance."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",246,0)="312 SEQ #313^3060807^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",246,1,0)="^^1^1^3060807"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",246,1,1,0)="IB SUNSETTING OF OPTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",247,0)="302 SEQ #314^3060807^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",247,1,0)="^^1^1^3060807"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",247,1,1,0)="ADD NEW ADJUSTMENT CODE TO AUTO BILL GENERATION LIST"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",248,0)="320 SEQ #315^3060807^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",248,1,0)="^^1^1^3060807"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",248,1,1,0)="eClaims Plus Iteration 2"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",249,0)="305 SEQ #316^3060923^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",249,1,0)="^^1^1^3060923"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",249,1,1,0)="Companion patch for PRCA*4.5*232 - Vista AR IB extract -phase II -part II."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",250,0)="341 SEQ #317^3060923^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",250,1,0)="^^5^5^3060923"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",250,1,1,0)="This patch will correct a problem where the nightly billing job"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",250,1,2,0)="was failing when voice activated records from Radiology had"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",250,1,3,0)="triggered an entry into billing file #350 and had left the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",250,1,4,0)="USER ADDING ENTRY field null.  The changes in this patch will"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",250,1,5,0)="trap that condition and store the Postmaster DUZ rather than null."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,0)="342^3060923^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,0)="^^13^13^3060923"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,1,0)="This patch supports the National Council for Prescription Drug Programs "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,2,0)="(NCPDP) standard which was adopted under the Healthcare Insurance"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,3,0)="Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA) for pharmacy claims. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,4,0)="is one of six to be released.  Three patches will be released in a KIDS"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,5,0)="multi-build distribution containing: BPS*1*3, PSO*7*247, and IB*2*342.  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,6,0)="Three patches will be released individually and they are: PRCA*4.5*247,"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,7,0)="PSX*2*62, and PSS*1*115."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,9,0)="Enhancements included in the release of the six patches are a new option "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,10,0)="that will enable the user to reopen a closed Electronic Claims Management"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,11,0)="Engine (ECME) claim; updates to the Rx Activity Log; and permanent storage"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,12,0)="of Claims activity information as reported by the ECME Billing Events"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",251,1,13,0)="Report."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",252,0)="350 SEQ #319^3061122.222145^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",252,1,0)="^^2^2^3061122"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",252,1,1,0)="UPDATE VALID GROUP NUMBER VALUES & ADD NEW ADJUSTMENT CODE TO AUTO"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",252,1,2,0)="BILL LIST"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",253,0)="355 SEQ #320^3061122.222431^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",253,1,0)="^^1^1^3061122"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",253,1,1,0)="REASONABLE CHARGES V2.7 UPDATE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",254,0)="358 SEQ #321^3061122.223019^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",255,0)="304 SEQ #322^3061122.223717^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",255,1,0)="^^7^7^3061122"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",255,1,1,0)="This patch addresses two issues. The first issue is regarding the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",255,1,2,0)="Automated Biller not billing the legitimate Claims Tracking entry when "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",255,1,3,0)="the answer to the NEED RELATED TO OCCUPATION or the NEED RELATED TO AN "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",255,1,4,0)="ACCIDENT field for the patient is UNKNOWN or NULL."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",255,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",255,1,6,0)="The second issue is about a syntax error that site encountered when they"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",255,1,7,0)="were trying to compile routine IBCSC4B in Cache."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",256,0)="293 SEQ #323^3061122.232053^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",256,1,0)="^^6^6^3061122"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",256,1,1,0)="This patch addresses 2 issues. The first is that site requested to change"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",256,1,2,0)="the heading ""Last test date"" to ""Last RX Copayment Exemption date"" in the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",256,1,3,0)="DG Patient Inquiry option to match up to the data. The second issue is"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",256,1,4,0)="about a bug behind discovered in the IB's IVM backbilling functionality."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",256,1,5,0)="If the veteran has an appointment in a billable clinic but also has a non"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",256,1,6,0)="billable stop code added, charges are not being generated."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",257,0)="360 SEQ #324^3061211.162843^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",257,1,0)="^^1^1^3061211"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",257,1,1,0)="REASONABLE CHARGES V2.8 UPDATE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",258,0)="354 SEQ #325^3061227.143338^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",258,1,0)="^^5^5^3061227"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",258,1,1,0)="This patch will distribute 3 DSS Stop Codes:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",258,1,2,0)="197 - POLYTRAUMA INDIVIDUAL"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",258,1,3,0)="198 - POLYTRAUMA GROUP"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",258,1,4,0)="199 - TELEPHONE/POLYTRAUMA"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",258,1,5,0)="which will be added to IB CLINIC STOP CODE BILLABLE TYPES [#352.5]."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",259,0)="362^3061227.15073^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",260,0)="351 SEQ #327^3070627.212719^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",260,1,0)="^^2^2^3070627"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",260,1,1,0)="The Chief Business Office has requested to update the DSS Stop Codes"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",260,1,2,0)="to reflect the FY 07 Co-pay rates."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",261,0)="343 SEQ #328^3070629.190253^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",261,1,0)="^^1^1^3070629"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",261,1,1,0)="NPI Modifications for the IB Package"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",262,0)="348 SEQ #329^3070904.221158^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",262,1,0)="^^1^1^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",262,1,1,0)="New CMS-1500 claim form"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",263,0)="365 SEQ #330^3070904.222435^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",263,1,0)="^^1^1^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",263,1,1,0)="Reasonable Charges v2.9"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,0)="356 SEQ #331^3070904.223902^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,0)="^^16^16^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,1,0)="This Maintenance Update addresses the following issues reported in Remedy:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,2,0)=" 1) HD63676  - Non Providers Not Screened in Procedures Multiple"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,3,0)=" 2) HD64317  - IB315 entry file 350.8/*232"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,4,0)=" 3) HD64380  - Held Charges Report (PTH-1104-20448)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,5,0)=" 4) HD64425  - PROVIDER ID QUERY REPORT - TOTAL IS WRONG"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,6,0)=" 5) HD64697  - ADD OUTSIDE LAB CHARGES TO MAP"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,7,0)=" 6) HD64863  - IBJDF51 Spreadsheet (Trans # creates problem)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,8,0)=" 7) HD65904  - Problem with Miscellaneous Bills Follow-up Reports"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,9,0)=" 8) HD117969 - CHAMPVA/TRICARE Follow-Up Report Detail vs. Summary problem"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,10,0)=" 9) HD118376 - MRA Filing Error"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,11,0)="      123700 - Message storage errors on bill."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,12,0)="10) HD131138 - Missing Mail Group - CMOP transmissions fail."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,13,0)="11) HD134835 - Insurance Buffer Error"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,14,0)="      131701 - Error <UNDEF>BR+1^DIE0"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,15,0)="12) HD137911 - <UNDEFINED>BULL1+5^IBTUBUL"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",264,1,16,0)="      145085 - Error Running Send Test Unbilled Amounts Bulletin option"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,0)="345 SEQ #332^3070904.23065^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,0)="^^28^28^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,1,0)="1.      Additional Source of Information Codes in Insurance Buffer and "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,2,0)="Patient Insurance File."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,4,0)="2.      Modifications to existing Pre-Registration Report to remove "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,5,0)="hard-coding and allow SOI Code selection."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,7,0)="3.      Include missing patient name in buffer file when processing "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,8,0)="message responses."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,10,0)="4.      Reduce the number of blank inquires being sent via Remote Query."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,12,0)="5.      Auto-Populate the Patient Insurance file with the patient's DOB & "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,13,0)="SSN information at processing time."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,15,0)="6.      Replace Payer ID with Payer Name to improve readability of the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,16,0)="Buffer entry error information."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,18,0)="7.      Correct the totals for companies without National IDs in the eIV "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,19,0)="Statistical Report."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,21,0)="8.      Bypass new buffer entry creation upon message response by "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,22,0)="verifying if the buffer entry has been previously accepted."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,24,0)="9.       The CBO extract was modified to transmit SOI codes with a value"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,25,0)="greater than '4' without resetting them to a value of '1' (Interview)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,27,0)="10.      Modify Response Report to Display Benefit Status as well as all"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",265,1,28,0)="notes associated with benefit."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",266,0)="339 SEQ #333^3070905.001649^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",266,1,0)="^^1^1^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",266,1,1,0)="IB implementation of Project 112/SHAD Classification."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",267,0)="349 SEQ #334^3070905.01154^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",267,1,0)="^^1^1^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",267,1,1,0)="UB-04 claim form."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",268,0)="347 SEQ #335^3070905.013156^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",268,1,0)="^^5^5^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",268,1,1,0)="This patch is being released in conjunction with the Pharmacy "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",268,1,2,0)="Reengineering Encapsulation effort. While no new functionality for "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",268,1,3,0)="Integrated Billing package is released with this patch all direct global "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",268,1,4,0)="references to the Outpatient Pharmacy files have been replaced by this "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",268,1,5,0)="effort."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",269,0)="367 SEQ #336^3070905.013604^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",269,1,0)="^^4^4^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",269,1,1,0)="This patch adds and modifies Stop Codes to the IB CLINIC STOP CODE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",269,1,2,0)="BILLABLE TYPES (#352.5) file, fixes a SUBSCRIPT error in the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",269,1,3,0)="Electronic Error Report and fixes problems in billing where the RX"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",269,1,4,0)="COPAY status is incorrectly flipping from NON-EXEMPT to EXEMPT."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",270,0)="375 SEQ #337^3070905.013854^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",270,1,0)="^^7^7^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",270,1,1,0)="The CBO has requested that these three things be done by this patch. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",270,1,2,0)="First, it will automatically update the transmission status for certain "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",270,1,3,0)="EDI bills that are authorized but not yet transmitted. Second, the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",270,1,4,0)="CLAIM MRA STATUS field will be updated to 'NO MRA NEEDED' for authorized "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",270,1,5,0)="bills if there are no MRAs on file. Third, a list will be produced for "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",270,1,6,0)="sites to deal with individually: this list will be of authorized claims "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",270,1,7,0)="with the AR status of other than an active status."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",271,0)="364 SEQ #338^3070905.013924^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",271,1,0)="^^6^6^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",271,1,1,0)="IB*2*364 is being released to support the Treating Specialty changes "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",271,1,2,0)="released in patch: DG*5.3*729 (Project: PTF Fields No Longer Needed)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",271,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",271,1,4,0)="Treating Specialties file (#42.4) is being updated by patch DG*5.3*729."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",271,1,5,0)="This patch IB*2*364 will update Integrated Billing to properly handle the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",271,1,6,0)="billing of the new and changed Treating Specialties."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",272,0)="366 SEQ #339^3070905.013955^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",273,0)="361 SEQ #340^3071212.201804^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",273,1,0)="^^5^5^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",273,1,1,0)="This patch adds a new field for INSURED'S SEX to both the PATIENT file"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",273,1,2,0)="and the INSURANCE BUFFER file.  A post-init routine will auto-populate"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",273,1,3,0)="this field for existing insurance policies to the best of its ability."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",273,1,4,0)="All screens that allow adding/editing/displaying of policy holder"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",273,1,5,0)="information will be modified to use the new field."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",274,0)="359 SEQ #341^3071212.205435^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",274,1,0)="^^9^9^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",274,1,1,0)="This patch insures that while navigating in the Claims"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",274,1,2,0)="Tracking Edit Option after the user switches patients "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",274,1,3,0)="while in the View Patient (VP) menu and returns to the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",274,1,4,0)="list of the patients claims that the claims that are "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",274,1,5,0)="listed are actually the indicated patients claims.  It"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",274,1,6,0)="also adds adjustment code CO 194 to the list of codes"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",274,1,7,0)="automatically processed and modifies function call"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",274,1,8,0)="GETWNR^IBCNSMM1 to return only Part A or Part B"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",274,1,9,0)="Medicare plans like it is supposed to."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",275,0)="369 SEQ #342^3071212.210436^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",275,1,0)="^^1^1^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",275,1,1,0)="IB API'S to support the SD ASCD (SCAM) project."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",276,0)="374 SEQ #343^3071212.212007^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",276,1,0)="^^1^1^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",276,1,1,0)="IB ENHANCEMENTS"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",277,0)="378 SEQ #344^3071212.212036^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",277,1,0)="^^1^1^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",277,1,1,0)="Update Stop Codes to reflect Fiscal Year 2008 changes."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",278,0)="303 SEQ #345^3071212.212739^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",278,1,0)="^^5^5^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",278,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one issue. The Edit Returned Bill option on the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",278,1,2,0)="Return Bill Menu [IB RETURN BILL MENU] has been modified to only allow "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",278,1,3,0)="the editing of a returned bill if it is not an ""electronically"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",278,1,4,0)="transmittable"" bill. For returned electronically transmittable "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",278,1,5,0)="bills/claims the IB COPY AND CANCEL option will need to be used."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",279,0)="363^3071212.214902^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",279,1,0)="^^3^3^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",279,1,1,0)="The general purpose of this patch is to meet the requirements for the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",279,1,2,0)="VistA Integrated Billing (IB) software application in support of the Phase"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",279,1,3,0)="4 ePharmacy enhancements, Iteration 1."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",280,0)="381 SEQ #347^3071212.221957^1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",280,1,0)="^^1^1^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",280,1,1,0)="PHARMACY ENCAPSULATION API AND EPHARMACY FOLLOW UP PATCH"
