^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,150,0)="Documentation Retrieval Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,151,0)="------------------------------------ "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,152,0)="Updated documentation describing the new functionality introduced by this "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,153,0)="patch is available."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,154,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,155,0)="The preferred method is to FTP the files from "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,156,0)="ftp://download.vista.domain.ext/. This transmits the files from the first"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,157,0)="available FTP server. Sites may also elect to retrieve software directly"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,158,0)="from a specific server as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,159,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,160,0)=" Albany         ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext  <ftp://ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,161,0)=" Hines          ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext   <ftp://ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,162,0)=" Salt Lake City ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext     <ftp://ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,163,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,164,0)="Documentation can also be found on the VA Software Documentation Library "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,165,0)="at: http://www4.domain.ext/vdl/"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,166,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,167,0)="Title                         File Name                       FTP Mode"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,168,0)="-----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,169,0)="<Documentation title>       "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,172,0)="Patch Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,174,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,175,0)="Pre/Post Installation Overview"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,176,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,177,0)="<Provide a brief overview of what the pre/post installation entails.  The"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,178,0)="actual instructions will be listed below in the Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,179,0)="section. Note whether pre/post installation routines can be deleted after"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,180,0)="they run or whether they are automatically deleted.>"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,181,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,182,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,183,0)="Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,184,0)="-------------------------       "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,185,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,186,0)="  ******************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,187,0)="  *  You should install this patch during non-peak hours, when no  *"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,188,0)="  *  Integrated Billing or Accounts Receivable users are on the    *"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,189,0)="  *  system.                                                       *"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,190,0)="  ******************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,191,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,192,0)="There are no options to disable. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,193,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,194,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,195,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,196,0)="<Provide a brief description of what the pre-installation will be doing. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,197,0)="List pre-installation instructions (i.e., links, filers, or batch"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,198,0)="transmissions that need to be stopped, jobs unscheduled, etc.), if"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,199,0)="applicable.>"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,200,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,201,0)="1.  Obtain the Patch."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,202,0)="    Obtain the host file PRCA_275_IB_447_16.KID, which contains the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,203,0)="    following two patch installs:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,204,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,205,0)="        PRCA*4.5*275"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,206,0)="        IB*2.0*447"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,207,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,208,0)="    Sites can retrieve VistA software from the following FTP addresses."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,209,0)="    The preferred method is to FTP the files from:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,210,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,211,0)="                   download.vista.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,212,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,213,0)="    This will transmit the files from the first available FTP server."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,214,0)="    Sites may also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,215,0)="    server as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,216,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,217,0)="      Albany                  ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,218,0)="      Hines                   ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,219,0)="      Salt Lake City          ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,220,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,221,0)="    The PRCA_275_IB_447_16.KID host file is located in the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,222,0)="    anonymous.software directory.  Use ASCII Mode when downloading the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,223,0)="    file."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,224,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,225,0)="3.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,226,0)="    the Installation Menu.  From this menu, you may elect to use the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,227,0)="    following option. When prompted for the INSTALL enter the patch #(ex."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,228,0)="    PRCA*4.5*275):"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,229,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,230,0)="    a.  Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,231,0)="        message of any routines exported with this patch. It will not"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,232,0)="        backup any other changes such as DD's or templates."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,233,0)="    b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,234,0)="        allow you to view all changes that will be made when this patch"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,235,0)="        is installed.  It compares all components of this patch"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,236,0)="        (routines, DD's, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,237,0)="    c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,238,0)="        you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,239,0)="        transport global."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,240,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,241,0)="4.  From the Installation Menu, select the Install Package(s) option and"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,242,0)="    choose the patch to install."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,243,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,244,0)="5.  When prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,245,0)="    Install? NO//'     "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,246,0)="    <Provide the installer with guidance on whether or not menu trees need"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,247,0)="    to be rebuilt.  For instance the menu trees do not need rebuilt if "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,248,0)="    there are no menus involved in the patch or their system rebuilds menu"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,249,0)="    trees nightly using TaskMan. If they must answering YES to rebuild"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,250,0)="    the menu trees warn them that it could affect users on the system and"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,251,0)="    installation times will increase.>"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,252,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,253,0)="6.  When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,254,0)="    NO//'"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,255,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,256,0)="    <to inhibit logons.>"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,257,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,258,0)="7.  When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,259,0)="    and Protocols? NO// "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,260,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,261,0)="    <Provide the installer with guidance on whether or not to disable"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,262,0)="    scheduled Options, menu options, and protocols.>"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,263,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,264,0)="8.  If prompted ""Delay Install (Minutes):  (0 - 60): 0// respond 0."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,265,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,266,0)="9.  When prompted ""Enter the Coordinator for Mail Group 'MDA'"""
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,267,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,268,0)="    Enter:  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,269,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,270,0)="Post-Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,271,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,272,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,273,0)="<Provide a brief description of what the pre-installation will be doing. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,274,0)="List pre-installation instructions (i.e., links, filers, or batch"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,275,0)="transmissions that need to be stopped, jobs unscheduled, etc.), if"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",362,1,276,0)="applicable.>"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",363,0)="468 SEQ #433^3120305.142559^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",363,1,0)="^^1^1^3120305"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",363,1,1,0)="Reasonable Charges v3.9"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",364,0)="473 SEQ #434^3120418.115055^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",364,1,0)="^^1^1^3120418"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",364,1,1,0)="HIPAA 5010 maintenance support patch."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",365,0)="477 SEQ #435^3120829.102759^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",365,1,0)="^^1^1^3120829"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",365,1,1,0)="FY2012 ADDITIONAL DSS STOP CODE UPDATE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",366,0)="469 SEQ #436^3120829.103428^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",366,1,0)="^^2^2^3120829"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",366,1,1,0)="The purpose of this patch is to update the MCCR Utility file and the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",366,1,2,0)="Revenue Code file for FY2012."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",367,0)="454^3120829.1144^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",367,1,0)="^^1^1^3120829"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",367,1,1,0)="INSTITUTIONAL LTC CD PATIENT EXEMPTION"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",368,0)="480 SEQ #438^3120925.092557^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",368,1,0)="^^2^2^3120925"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",368,1,1,0)="This patch updates Integrated Billing Clinic Stop Codes to reflect "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",368,1,2,0)="Fiscal Year 2013 changes."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",369,0)="478 SEQ #439^3120925.110639^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",369,1,0)="^^1^1^3120925"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",369,1,1,0)="Add Evaluation and Management codes to the Type of Visit file <#357.69>."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",370,0)="484 SEQ #440^3121107.150508^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",370,1,0)="^^1^1^3121107"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",370,1,1,0)="Reasonable Charges v3.11"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",371,0)="475 SEQ #441^3121116.093413^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",371,1,0)="^^3^3^3121116"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",371,1,1,0)="This patch contains the TCP/IP address update of the HL7 Logical Link "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",371,1,2,0)="'IIV EC' connected to a new technical server located at the Financial"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",371,1,3,0)="Service Center (FSC) in Austin, Texas."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",372,0)="486 SEQ #442^3121129.143013^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",372,1,0)="^^2^2^3121129"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",372,1,1,0)="Add CAMP LEJEUNE TREATMENT as a new entry in the CLAIMS TRACKING "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",372,1,2,0)="NON-BILLABLE REASONS file (#356.8)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",373,0)="485^3130103.114459^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",374,0)="476 SEQ #444^3130122.171725^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",374,1,0)="^^2^2^3130122"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",374,1,1,0)="IB*2.0*476 t1 build contains the first iteratin of the IB portion"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",374,1,2,0)="of the deliverables for the 5010 VistA Fee Basis phase II project."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",375,0)="459^3130212.103759^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",375,1,0)="^^4^4^3130212"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",375,1,1,0)="This patch addresses two issues. The first issue is regarding the Claims"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",375,1,2,0)="Matching report [RCDP CLAIMS MATCH] not display the corresponding first"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",375,1,3,0)="party debts. The second issue is about the incorrect charge type NURSING"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",375,1,4,0)="HOME CARE (NSC) showing on the patient's bill."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",376,0)="491 SEQ #446^3130227.173942^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",376,1,0)="^^1^1^3130227"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",376,1,1,0)="Reasonable Charges v3.12"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",377,0)="492 SEQ #447^3130304.164705^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",377,1,0)="^^1^1^3130304"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",377,1,1,0)="FY2013 MIDYEAR STOP CODE UPDATES"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",378,0)="448 SEQ #448^3130318.141034^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",378,1,0)="^^4^4^3130318"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",378,1,1,0)="THIS PATCH MAKES MODIFICATIONS TO THE FUNCTION THAT DETERMINES THE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",378,1,2,0)="START OF CARE DATE.  THIS WILL ALLOW THE CORRECT START OF CARE DATE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",378,1,3,0)="TO BE DISPLAYED WHEN AN OUTPATIENT EVENT TAKES PLACE ON A DATE THAT"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",378,1,4,0)="OCCURS BETWEEN THE ADMIT AND DISCHARGE DATES OF AN INPATIENT EVENT."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",379,0)="474 SEQ #449^3130326.11095^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",379,1,0)="^^5^5^3130326"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",379,1,1,0)="This patch contains two issues. The first issue is about some non billable"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",379,1,2,0)="HCPCS codes for prosthetic items which need to be filtered out of the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",379,1,3,0)="Claims Tracking module. The second issue concerns the '^' key which is"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",379,1,4,0)="entered and does not exit out of the [IBCR ADJUSTMENT ENTER/EDIT] option"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",379,1,5,0)="as expected."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",380,0)="457 SEQ #450^3130327.171518^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",381,0)="483 SEQ #451^3130429.141522^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",381,1,0)="^^6^6^3130429"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",381,1,1,0)="This patch addresses two issues. The first issue is about the Technical"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",381,1,2,0)="Component (TC) Modifier added to the procedure on the institutional bill."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",381,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",381,1,4,0)="The second issue is about the 'Modifier 26 Deleted from Procedures (1)'"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",381,1,5,0)="message is mistakenly displayed for Modifier 58 in the [IB EDIT BILLING"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",381,1,6,0)="INFO] option."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",382,0)="501 SEQ #453^3130614.085849^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",382,1,0)="^^3^3^3130614"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",382,1,1,0)="This patch is about the administrative charge update based on a new"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",382,1,2,0)="dispensing fee $13.18 for third party pharmacy prescription claims with"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",382,1,3,0)="an effective date of January 1st, 2013."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",383,0)="458 SEQ #454^3130724.113705^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",383,1,0)="^^1^1^3130724"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",383,1,1,0)="Reasonable Charges Billing Enhancements 2013."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",384,0)="496 SEQ #455^3130801.135924^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",384,1,0)="^^4^4^3130801"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",384,1,1,0)="This patch addresses two issues. The first issue contains a new source of"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",384,1,2,0)="insurance information added to the SOURCE OF INFORMATION file (#355.12)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",384,1,3,0)="The second issue is about a typo on the help prompt of the CLAIMS (RX) "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",384,1,4,0)="STATE field (#.185) in the INSURANCE file (#36)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",385,0)="490 SEQ #456^3130813.110724^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",385,1,0)="^^2^2^3130813"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",385,1,1,0)="The purpose of this patch is to update the MCCR Utility file and the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",385,1,2,0)="Revenue Code file and the Place of Service file for FY2013."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",386,0)="481 SEQ #457^3130905.130216^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",386,1,0)="^^1^1^3130905"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",386,1,1,0)="Update for unsupported ICD fields."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",387,0)="502 SEQ #458^3130911.115007^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",387,1,0)="^^3^3^3130911"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",387,1,1,0)="This patch updates Integrated Billing Clinic Stop Codes to reflect "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",387,1,2,0)="Fiscal Year 2014 changes and corrects the selection logic used to "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",387,1,3,0)="validate stop codes."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",388,0)="464 SEQ #459^3130930.102613^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",388,1,0)="^^8^8^3130930"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",388,1,1,0)="This patch addresses 3 issues. The first issue concerns a large number of"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",388,1,2,0)="rated disabilities repeatedly displaying without providing the SC AT TIME"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",388,1,3,0)="OF CARE prompt in order for the user to edit."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",388,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",388,1,5,0)="The second issue is about a typo in the '(Enter '6' to list disabilites)'"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",388,1,6,0)="message following the 'SC Care: YES' field on screen <1> in the Enter/Edit"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",388,1,7,0)="Billing Information option. The last issue is about a misspelled word in"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",388,1,8,0)="the 'CHARGE PENDING REIVEW PASSED TO AR' bulletin subject line."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",389,0)="508 SEQ #460^3131113.123026^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",389,1,0)="^^1^1^3131113"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",389,1,1,0)="Reasonable Charges v3.13"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",390,0)="507 SEQ #461^3131210.165453^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",390,1,0)="^^1^1^3131210"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",390,1,1,0)="Add Evaluation and Management codes to the Type of Visit file <#357.69>."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,0)="499^3131212.141029^17"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,0)="^^342^342^3131212"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,1,0)="                               ***NOTICE***"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,2,0)=" Users should be made aware that processing of Newborn claims must ONLY be"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,3,0)=" entered in VistA. No entry in FBCS should be performed."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,4,0)="                               ***********"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,5,0)=" This patch, along with DG*5.3*867 and FB*3.5*146, is being released as a"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,6,0)=" bundle, and all three will be automatically installed in the correct order."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,8,0)=" This patch has enhancements that extend the capabilities of the Veterans"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,9,0)=" Health Information Systems and Technology Architecture (VistA) Patient"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,10,0)=" Registration system (DG), Fee Basis System (FB), and Integrated Billing"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,11,0)=" (IB)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,13,0)=" Below is a list of all the applications involved in this project along with"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,14,0)=" their patch number:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,16,0)="     APPLICATION/VERSION                                   PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,17,0)="     ---------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,18,0)="  PATIENT REGISTRATION (DG) V 5.3                       DG*5.3*867"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,19,0)="  FEE BASIS (FB) V 3.5                                  FB*3.5*146"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,20,0)="  INTEGRATED BILLING (IB) 2.0                           IB*2.0*499"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,22,0)=" The patches (DG*5.3*867, FB*3.5*146, and IB*2.0*499) are being released in"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,23,0)=" the Kernel Installation and Distribution System (KIDS) multi-build"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,24,0)=" distribution NEWBORN DG FB IB BUNDLE 1.0."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,26,0)=" The purpose of the Caregivers: Newborn Claims Processing Enhancement Project"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,27,0)=" is to enhance VistA Fee Basis application in support of compliance with"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,28,0)=" Public Law 111-163, the Caregiver and Veterans Omnibus Health Services Act"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,29,0)=" of 2010. This law makes changes to sections of Title 38, United States Code"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,30,0)=" to furnish health care services to a newborn child of a Woman Veteran who"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,31,0)=" is receiving maternity care furnished by the Department of Veterans Affairs"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,32,0)=" (VA) for not more than seven days after the birth of the child."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,34,0)=" The scope of these enhancements is to capture information on healthcare"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,35,0)=" services provided to newborn children of Women Veterans. Affected functions"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,36,0)=" include eligibility determination, enrollment and registration, documentation"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,37,0)=" of referrals and authorization for care, claims processing, and payment. Only"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,38,0)=" modification to the Fee Basis (FB) and the Registration (DG) packages are"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,39,0)=" necessary to meet the requirements of this enhancement. The Integrated"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,40,0)=" Billing (IB) Patch is included to provide required data for the Fee Basis"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,41,0)=" install to reference."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,44,0)=" The primary purpose of this enhancement is to allow the Electronic Filing of"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,45,0)=" Newborn claims."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,47,0)=" Functional Description"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,48,0)=" ------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,49,0)=" The following features and functions have been added to the Fee Basis"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,50,0)=" workflow process applying to both Civil Hospital and Medical Fee:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,52,0)="  1. A new Patient Type of NEWBORN OF VETERAN has been added to the TYPE OF"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,53,0)=" PATIENT file (#391). This new selection will be available on Registration"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,54,0)=" Screen <7>."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,56,0)="  2. A sponsor is required for all Newborns determined by having the DOB less"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,57,0)=" than one (1) year from the present date. An inconsistency check has been"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,58,0)=" added to check the presence of a sponsor. If an inconsistency is found the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,59,0)=" inconsistency check will prompt the user to return to Screen <15> in"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,60,0)=" registration to enter a Sponsor."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,62,0)="  3. All Sponsors for Newborns must be listed as eligible for care. An"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,63,0)=" inconsistency check will check the status of the Sponsors Eligibility. The"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,64,0)=" check will trigger if the Sponsor has no Eligibility status."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,66,0)=" All other statuses (i.e. Pending Verification, Verified, and Pending"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,67,0)=" Re-verification) are acceptable."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,69,0)="  4. Fee Authorization dates associated with Newborns have checks in place to"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,70,0)=" not allow Authorization dates that fall outside the accepted range of Newborn"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,71,0)=" Authorization. The range is DOB to DOB+7. The system will warn the user and"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,72,0)=" not accept an Authorization date that falls outside the appropriate range"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,73,0)=" for a Newborn."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,75,0)="  5. When a Veteran Mother of a Sponsored Newborn is reviewed in the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,76,0)=" Registration screens, Screen <15> will display the Newborn(s), with the"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,77,0)=" additional header of ""Sponsored Newborn""."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,79,0)="  6. The FAMILY PREFIX ""NB Newborn of Vet"" has been added to the Help text in"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,80,0)=" the FAMILY PREFIX field (#.03) in the SPONSOR RELATIONSHIP file (#355.81)"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,82,0)="  7. ""NON-VA FOR FEMALE VET+NEWBORN 17.38"" was added to the VA ADMITTING"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,83,0)=" REGULATION file (#43.4). This new Admitting Regulation is available when"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,84,0)=" editing the 7078."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,86,0)="  8. The following default values were added when entering a Newborn with a"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,87,0)=" date of birth of less than one (1) year from present date. Defaults will only"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,88,0)=" be assigned when specified screens are accessed during the registration"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,89,0)=" process:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,90,0)=" PATIENT DATA, SCREEN <2> Marital field is defaulted to NEVER MARRIED."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,91,0)=" APPLICANT/SPOUSE EMPLOYMENT DATA, SCREEN <4> Status field is defaulted to NOT"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,92,0)=" EMPLOYED. FAMILY DEMOGRAPHIC DATA, SCREEN <8> Married Last Year field is"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,93,0)=" defaulted to NO."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",391,1,95,0)=" "
