^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,236,0)="-----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,237,0)="Integrated Billing User Guide                      ib_2_0_um.doc Binary"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,238,0)="Integrated Billing Technical Manual/Security Guide ib_2_0_tm.doc Binary"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,239,0)="Integrated Billing Deployment, Installation, "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,240,0)="     Back-Out, and Rollback Guide   "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,241,0)="              FY16RevenueIBVIP_Deployment_Installation_Guide.doc Binary "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,242,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,243,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,244,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,245,0)="Patch Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,246,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,247,0)="Pre/Post Installation Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,248,0)="-------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,249,0)="The post installation routine, IBY568PO, is not automatically deleted"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,250,0)="as part of the installation process. You may delete it after"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,251,0)="installation if you desire."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,252,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,253,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,254,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,255,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,257,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,258,0)="--------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,259,0)="This process will install new and updated routines and other "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,260,0)="components listed above. There is a post-install routine that will add "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,261,0)="entries to a number of files."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,262,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,263,0)="The patch will be released in conjunction with an Accounts Receivable"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,264,0)="patch, PRCA*4.5*315 and an Outpatient Pharmacy patch, PSO*7.0*463."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,265,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,266,0)="  ************************ NOTE ************************"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,267,0)="  IF A USER IS ON THE SYSTEM AND USING THESE PROGRAMS "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,268,0)="  AN EDITED ERROR WILL OCCUR.  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,269,0)="  The patch should be installed when NO Outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,270,0)="  Pharmacy users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,271,0)="  ******************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,272,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,273,0)=" Installation will take less than 1 minute."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,274,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,275,0)=" Suggested time to install: non-peak requirement hours."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,276,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,277,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,278,0)="  1. Obtain the file IB_2_568_PRCA_PSO_BUNDLE_T1.KID."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,279,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,280,0)="  2. From the Kernel Installation & Distribution System menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,281,0)="     the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,282,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,283,0)="  3. Use Load a Distribution using IB_2_568_PRCA_PSO_BUNDLE_T1.KID when"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,284,0)="     prompted to Enter a Host File name.  You may need to append a"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,285,0)="     directory name."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,286,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,287,0)="  4. From this menu, you may select to use the following options"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,288,0)="     (when prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter IB*2.0*568):"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,289,0)="         a.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,290,0)="             allow you to ensure the integrity of the routines that "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,291,0)="             are in the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,292,0)="         b.  Print Transport Global - This option will allow you to "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,293,0)="             view the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,294,0)="         c.  Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,295,0)="             will allow you to view all changes that will be made when "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,296,0)="             this patch is installed.  It compares all components of "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,297,0)="             this patch (routines, DD's, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,298,0)="         d.  Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,299,0)="             backup message of any routines exported with this patch. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,300,0)="             It will not backup any other changes such as DD's or "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,301,0)="             templates."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,302,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,303,0)="  5. When prompted ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,304,0)="     NO//""  respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,305,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,306,0)="  6. When prompted ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,307,0)="     and Protocols? NO//"" respond NO. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,308,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,309,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,310,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,311,0)="Post-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,312,0)="-------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",491,1,313,0)="There are no special tasks to perform after this patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",492,0)="595 SEQ #565^3180706.121051^54"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",493,0)="619 SEQ #566^3180706.122038^54"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",493,1,0)="^^4^4^3180706"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",493,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the Technical Component (TC) modifier which "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",493,1,2,0)="needs to be automatically removed from any procedure on institutional"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",493,1,3,0)="bills for Medicare in the Enter/Edit Billing Information [IB EDIT BILLING "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",493,1,4,0)="INFO] option."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",494,0)="616 SEQ #567^3180706.13172^54"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",494,1,0)="^^8^8^3180706"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",494,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following 2 issues:"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",494,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",494,1,3,0)="1.  An undefined error occurs when running the Held Charges Report"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",494,1,4,0)="LM [IB OUTPUT HELD CHARGES LM] option."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",494,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",494,1,6,0)="2.  When running the Enter/Edit Billing Information [IB EDIT BILLING INFO]"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",494,1,7,0)="option, the user will not be prompted for the PROCEDURE DESCRIPTION field"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",494,1,8,0)="when they enter a partial match CPT code."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",495,0)="596^3180706.1519^54"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",496,0)="591^3180907.122413^54"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",496,1,0)="^^1^1^3180907"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",496,1,1,0)="MCCF EDI TAS EPHARMACY BUILDS 3 & 4"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",497,0)="622 SEQ #570^3180907.131617^54"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",497,1,0)="^^4^4^3180907"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",497,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one issue."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",497,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",497,1,3,0)="-Fix an undefined error at line IBCSCH+7 in routine IBCSCH in the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",497,1,4,0)=" Enter/Edit Billing Information [IB EDIT BILLING INFO] option. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",498,0)="626 SEQ #571^3181004.161941^54"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",498,1,0)="^^2^2^3181004"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",498,1,1,0)="This patch updates Integrated Billing Clinic Stop Codes to reflect "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",498,1,2,0)="Fiscal year 2019 changes, effective 10/01/2018."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,0)="614 SEQ #572^3181101.16241^54"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,0)="^^15^15^3181101"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,1,0)=" The Mental Health Suicide Prevention - Suicide High Risk Patient "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,2,0)=" Enhancements effort incorporates the Modifying High Risk patient"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,3,0)=" Copayments and the Display Patient Record Flag (PRF) effort and ownership"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,4,0)=" management and transfer initiatives.  The goal of this effort is to"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,5,0)=" improve the delivery of targeted Mental Health care for individuals at"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,6,0)=" high risk for suicide.  Modification of copayments for Veterans assessed"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,7,0)=" as being at high risk for suicide involves making changes to the existing"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,8,0)=" VistA and payment systems to support regulatory change processes aimed at"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,9,0)=" removing financial barriers that may prevent these Veterans from engaging"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,10,0)=" in enhanced care, which includes more frequent contacts and dispensing"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,11,0)=" medications in smaller amounts more frequently, as safety precautions.  "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,12,0)=" The Display PRF effort enhances the current VistA system and Delphi"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,13,0)=" graphical user interface to address deficiencies in the functionality of"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,14,0)=" the existing PRF package that interfere with effective management of "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",499,1,15,0)=" coordination of care for high risk individuals. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",500,0)="592 SEQ #573^3181102.144935^54"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",500,1,0)="^^2^2^3181102"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",500,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",500,1,2,0)="MCCF EDI TAS EBILLING BUILD 3 DENTAL"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",501,0)="625 SEQ #574^3181102.153933^54"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",501,1,0)="^^2^2^3181102"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",501,1,1,0)="This patch addresses updates of Cost Based and Inter Agency rates with an"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",501,1,2,0)="effective date of 08/28/2018 in the CHARGE ITEM file (#363.2)."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",502,0)="609^3181204.155032^54"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",503,0)="635^3190103.171127^54"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",503,1,0)="^^5^5^3190103"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",503,1,1,0)="This patch, IB*2.0*635, is one of three VistA 2019 threshold patches. It "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",503,1,2,0)="addresses the annual updates for the Pharmacy Copay Thresholds. Patch "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",503,1,3,0)="DG*5.3*973 will update the thresholds for the Means Tests and the Maximum"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",503,1,4,0)="Annual Pension Rate. Patch EAS*1.0*170 will address the annual updates for"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",503,1,5,0)="the GMT Thresholds."
