^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",670,1,12,0)="    TRICARE PHARMACY              14.78"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",670,1,13,0)="    TRICARE REIMB. INS.           14.78"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",671,0)="779 SEQ #737^3250129.095807^89"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",672,0)="814 SEQ #738^3250212.152248^89"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",672,1,0)="^^1^1^3250212"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",672,1,1,0)="IB*2.0*814"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",673,0)="818 SEQ #739^3250219.13304^89"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",673,1,0)="^^3^3^3250219"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",673,1,1,0)="Integrated Billing patch, IB*2.0*818, is a fix for the annual updates"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",673,1,2,0)="for the Pharmacy Copay Thresholds patch IB*2.0*808 after receiving "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",673,1,3,0)="incorrect rates from business."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",674,0)="761 SEQ #740^3250227.093203^89"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",675,0)="804 SEQ #741^3250324.113956^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",676,0)="805 SEQ #742^3250324.120439^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",676,1,0)="^^2^2^3250324"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",676,1,1,0)="This patch fixes a potential undefined error that occurs when creating "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",676,1,2,0)="a bill with at least 16 diagnosis codes."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",677,0)="819 SEQ #743^3250403.082221^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",677,1,0)="^^1^1^3250403"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",677,1,1,0)="FY25 Mid Year Stop Code Changes for Veteran Copays "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",678,0)="803 SEQ #744^3250407.12303^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",678,1,0)="^^1^1^3250407"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",678,1,1,0)="Hospice IB Error Encountered Message Issue"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",679,0)="796 SEQ #745^3250501.134341^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",680,0)="823 SEQ #746^3250515.123455^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",680,1,0)="^^1^1^3250515"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",680,1,1,0)="V1"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",681,0)="798^3250529.075153^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",682,0)="762^3250602.12062^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",683,0)="767 SEQ #749^3250709.09212^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",684,0)="826 SEQ #750^3250709.093925^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",684,1,0)="^^8^8^3250709"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",684,1,1,0)="The purpose of the patch is to remove the HEADER code from the List "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",684,1,2,0)="Template IBNCPDP LSTMN CT. The Current code in this field is D "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",684,1,3,0)="HDR^IBNCPDPC this line in the routine IBNCPDPC no longer exists. The call "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",684,1,4,0)="replacing this in D HDR^IBTRED, which is the current header call for "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",684,1,5,0)="claims tracking. The error occurs in the worklflow of a user "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",684,1,6,0)="processingclaims in the 'ECME User Screen' option, then the call the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",684,1,7,0)="'IBNCPDP LSTMNCT' from this option to add comments then tries to return "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",684,1,8,0)="to the 'ECMEUser Screen'"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",685,0)="824 SEQ #751^3250729.160116^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",685,1,0)="^^7^7^3250729"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",685,1,1,0)="When an attempt to assign an NPI to a Non/Other VA Provider using the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",685,1,2,0)="IBCE PROVIDER MAINT option. And a previous record in the Institution File "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",685,1,3,0)="#4 used the NPI has no effective date yet retains the ""ANPI"" cross"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",685,1,4,0)="reference in file four, an incorrect error is presented and the user is "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",685,1,5,0)="not allowed to assign the NPI again. This remediation now checks for an "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",685,1,6,0)="effective date before allowing the message to present and denial of "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",685,1,7,0)="re-assignment of the NPI."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",686,0)="769 SEQ #752^3250903.083125^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",686,1,0)="^^8^8^3250903"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",686,1,1,0)="Utilizing the existing infrastructure put into place with"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",686,1,2,0)="IB*2.0*704, this patch facilitates the exchange of Copay Information"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",686,1,3,0)="between existing copay interfaces within Vista that will be"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",686,1,4,0)="synchronized to create a bi-directional integrated Copay Accumulators"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",686,1,5,0)="platform with Oracle.  Previously this interface utilized Data Access"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",686,1,6,0)="Service (DAS) as the middleware, but updates will be made to use Veterans"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",686,1,7,0)="Data Integration and Federation (VDIF) to facilitate the communication"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",686,1,8,0)="between VistA and Oracle Health. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",687,0)="746 SEQ #753^3250903.09053^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",688,0)="806 SEQ #754^3251022.133251^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",689,0)="817 SEQ #755^3251022.133534^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",690,0)="830 SEQ #756^3251022.134403^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",690,1,0)="^^1^1^3251022"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",690,1,1,0)="FY26 IB STOP CODE UPDATE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",691,0)="829 SEQ #757^3251118.152212^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",691,1,0)="^^1^1^3251118"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",691,1,1,0)="FY26 CBIAR UPDATE"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",692,0)="835 SEQ #758^3260107.115424^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",692,1,0)="^^1^1^3260107"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",692,1,1,0)="IB*2.0*835"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,0)="828 SEQ #759^3260114.122648^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,0)="^^19^19^3260114"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,1,0)="After patch IB*2.0*796 was released users noticed that while using the "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,2,0)="Claims tracking Editor processes"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,3,0)=", the posting of answers to two questions were not being posted as they "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,4,0)="did before the patch when a user "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,5,0)="entered the comments option of the Claims Tracking page and returned to "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,6,0)="do other steps.  When they return "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,7,0)="to the main screen their answers were not displayed to show them their "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,8,0)="entry stayed posted. The answers were only posted after extras steps were "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,9,0)="taken to display the results."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,11,0)="First After the user entered comments in the ""Billing Info Edit"" option. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,12,0)="then returned and ran the View/Edit Episode option. Then"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,13,0)="""Review Info"" option. Changed the ""TRACKED AS RANDOM SAMPLE?: NO// "" to "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,14,0)="yes or no. If they changed to ""YES"" then and ""R"" should show in the ""UR"" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,15,0)="column by the item selected for Reviewed. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,17,0)="Second after the user added comments then returned to add reason not "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,18,0)="billable the ""BILL"" column should display ""YES"" or ""NO"" but did not until "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",693,1,19,0)="extra steps are performed to verify their action was recorded."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",694,0)="820 SEQ #760^3260114.122802^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",694,1,0)="^^7^7^3260114"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",694,1,1,0)="Patients not displaying on the ""IB MT REV PEND CHARGES       Release "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",694,1,2,0)="Charges 'Pending Review""  option list as expected. When the previous "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",694,1,3,0)="primary means test on file is marked the patient does not AGREE TO PAY "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",694,1,4,0)="DEDUCTIBLE. And the income IVM test is marked the patient AGREE TO PAY "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",694,1,5,0)="DEDUCTIBLE.  The code should add the patient to the ""IB MT REV PEND "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",694,1,6,0)="CHARGES       Release Charges 'Pending Review"" option for review before "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",694,1,7,0)="going to Accounts Receivable. "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",695,0)="812^3260114.123259^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",696,0)="842 SEQ #762^3260114.125416^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",696,1,0)="^^2^2^3260114"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",696,1,1,0)="Integrated Billing patch, IB*2.0*842 addresses the annual updates"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",696,1,2,0)="for the Pharmacy Copay Thresholds."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",697,0)="839 SEQ #763^3260210.130741^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",697,1,0)="^^4^4^3260210"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",697,1,1,0)="Integrated Billing patch, IB*2.0*839, updates the administrative"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",697,1,2,0)="charge based on the following rate types, with new dispensing fee for"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",697,1,3,0)="third party pharmacy prescription claims, with an effective date of"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",697,1,4,0)="January 1st, 2026."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",698,0)="840 SEQ #764^3260316.124534^90"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",698,1,0)="^^4^4^3260316"
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",698,1,1,0)="Integrated Billing patch, IB*2.0*840, will update the administrative "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",698,1,2,0)="charge based on TRICARE rate types with new dispensing fee for third "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",698,1,3,0)="party pharmacy prescription claims with an effective date of January 1st, "
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",698,1,4,0)="2026."
^DIC(9.4,49,22,10,"PAH",699,0)="795 SEQ #765^3260316.124617^90"
