^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,132,0)="Documentation Retrieval Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,133,0)="------------------------------------ "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,134,0)="Updated documentation describing the new functionality introduced by this "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,135,0)="patch is available."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,137,0)="The preferred method is to FTP the files from "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,138,0)="ftp://download.vista.domain.ext/."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,139,0)="This transmits the files from the first available FTP server. Sites may "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,140,0)="also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific server as "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,141,0)="follows:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,142,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,143,0)=" Albany         ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext  <ftp://ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,144,0)=" Hines          ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext   <ftp://ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,145,0)=" Salt Lake City ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext     <ftp://ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext>"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,146,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,147,0)="Documentation can also be found on the VA Software Documentation Library "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,148,0)="at: http://www4.domain.ext/vdl/"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,150,0)="Title                         File Name                       FTP Mode"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,151,0)="-----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,152,0)="<Documentation title>       "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,154,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,155,0)="Patch Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,156,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,157,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,158,0)="Pre/Post Installation Overview"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,159,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,160,0)="<Provide a brief overview of what the pre/post installation entails.  The"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,161,0)="actual instructions will be listed below in the Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,162,0)="section. Note whether pre/post installation routines can be deleted after"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,163,0)="they run or whether they are automatically deleted.>"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,164,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,165,0)="**** Please note, if you select the option below, Compare Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,166,0)="     to Current System, and select #1 Full Comparison, you will get a"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,167,0)="     system error:  <UNDEFINED>S+1^DIQ ^IBA(364.6,1937,0) due to a known"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,168,0)="     issue with the KIDS Full Compare option (see Remedy Ticket"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,169,0)="     HD0000000449128). You can run any of the other 3 compare options"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,170,0)="     without issue."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,172,0)="Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,173,0)="-------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,174,0)="  ******************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,175,0)="  *  You should install this patch during non-peak hours, when no  *"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,176,0)="  *  Integrated Billing or Accounts Receivable users are on the    *"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,177,0)="  *  system.                                                       *"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,178,0)="  ******************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,179,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,180,0)="There are no options to disable."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,181,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,182,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,183,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,184,0)="<Provide a brief description of what the pre-installation will be doing. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,185,0)="List pre-installation instructions (i.e., links, filers, or batch"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,186,0)="transmissions that need to be stopped, jobs unscheduled, etc.), if"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,187,0)="applicable.>"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,188,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,189,0)="1.  Choose the PackMan message containing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,190,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,191,0)="2.  Choose the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option.  "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,192,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,193,0)="3.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,194,0)="    the Installation Menu.  From this menu, you may elect to use the"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,195,0)="    following option. When prompted for the INSTALL enter the patch #(ex."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,196,0)="    XXX*X.X*XX):"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,197,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,198,0)="    a.  Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,199,0)="        message of any routines exported with this patch. It will not"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,200,0)="        backup any other changes such as DD's or templates."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,201,0)="    b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,202,0)="        allow you to view all changes that will be made when this patch"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,203,0)="        is installed.  It compares all components of this patch"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,204,0)="        (routines, DD's, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,205,0)="    c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,206,0)="        you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,207,0)="        transport global."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,208,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,209,0)="4.  From the Installation Menu, select the Install Package(s) option and"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,210,0)="    choose the patch to install."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,211,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,212,0)="5.  When prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,213,0)="    Install? NO//'     "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,214,0)="    <Provide the installer with guidance on whether or not menu trees need"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,215,0)="    to be rebuilt.  For instance the menu trees do not need rebuilt if "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,216,0)="    there are no menus involved in the patch or their system rebuilds menu"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,217,0)="    trees nightly using TaskMan. If they must answering YES to rebuild "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,218,0)="    the menu trees warn them that it could affect users on the system and"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,219,0)="    installation times will increase.>"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,220,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,221,0)="6.  When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,222,0)="    NO//'"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,223,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,224,0)="    <to inhibit logons.>"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,225,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,226,0)="7.  When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,227,0)="    and Protocols? NO// "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,228,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,229,0)="    <Provide the installer with guidance on whether or not to disable "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,230,0)="    scheduled Options, menu options, and protocols.>"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,231,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,232,0)="8.  If prompted ""Delay Install (Minutes):  (0 - 60): 0// respond 0."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,233,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,234,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,235,0)="Post-Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,236,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,237,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,238,0)="<Provide a brief description of what the pre-installation will be doing. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,239,0)="List pre-installation instructions (i.e., links, filers, or batch"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,240,0)="transmissions that need to be stopped, jobs unscheduled, etc.), if"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",219,1,241,0)="applicable.>"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",220,0)="284 SEQ #253^3120418.115045^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",220,1,0)="^^1^1^3120418"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",220,1,1,0)="5010 EPAY ENHANCEMENTS"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",221,0)="282 SEQ #254^3120829.10592^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",221,1,0)="^^3^3^3120829"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",221,1,1,0)="This patch fixes an issue found in the Accounts Receivable Bad Debt "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",221,1,2,0)="report. This defect causes ""No Fault Auto"" receivables to be incorrectly "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",221,1,3,0)="accounted for on the Bad Debt Report."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,0)="283 SEQ #255^3120829.12223^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,1,0)="^^12^12^3120829"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,1,1,0)="This patch resolves the following three issues:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,1,3,0)="1. For manual creation of deposits, AR must be changed to allow users to "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,1,4,0)="   create a deposit record with a Deposit Ticket Number that is six digits"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,1,5,0)="   long, with no restrictions on the first three digits. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,1,7,0)="2. For the Third Party EDI Lockbox process, AR must be changed to accept"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,1,8,0)="   any nine-digit deposit number."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,1,10,0)="3. Four reports have been modified to display all of the 9-digit deposit "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,1,11,0)="   number. They are EFT Deposit Reconciliation Report, Daily Activity"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",222,1,12,0)="   Report, EFT Unmatched Aging Report, and Unapplied EFT Deposits Report."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",223,0)="266 SEQ #256^3120912.105542^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",223,1,0)="^^6^6^3120912"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",223,1,1,0)="Veterans Health Administration (VHA) Chief Financial Officer - Office "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",223,1,2,0)="Resources Management has requested to inactivate one (1) existing revenue "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",223,1,3,0)="source code and add five (5) new revenue source codes to the REVENUE "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",223,1,4,0)="SOURCE CODE file (#347.3)."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",223,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",223,1,6,0)="This update will be effective October 1, 2012."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",224,0)="280^3130212.103759^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",224,1,0)="^^3^3^3130212"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",224,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",224,1,2,0)="This patch addresses one issue about the incorrect charge type NURSING"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",224,1,3,0)="HOME CARE (NSC) showing on the patient's bill."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",225,0)="292 SEQ #258^3130326.110943^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",225,1,0)="^9.49011^2^2^3130326"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",225,1,1,0)="This patch will support those sites that have migrated to full Linux "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",225,1,2,0)="operating system for transmitting their CBO Data Extract files."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,0)="293 SEQ #259^3130416.102512^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,0)="^^34^34^3130416"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,1,0)="The HIPAA 5010 D.0 Level II Phase 2 project includes the following"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,2,0)="modifications to the Electronic Payments V. 4.5 application:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,4,0)="1. Duplicate Receipt Numbers"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,5,0)="   -------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,6,0)="   Modified VistA to create a unique receipt number for the user when"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,7,0)="   creating a receipt in order to post payments without manual"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,8,0)="   intervention. Previously, it was possible for VistA to create an"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,9,0)="   already used receipt number and this would cause the user to re-enter"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,10,0)="   data because VistA did not recognize the duplicate receipt number"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,11,0)="   until later in the creation of receipt process."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,13,0)="2. Manual Receipts - EFT Selection"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,14,0)="   -------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,15,0)="   Modified VistA so that the user is unable to select a MATCHED EFT"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,16,0)="   when performing the Manual Match EFT-ERA. Due to this modification the"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,17,0)="   user will NOT be able to see or select a MATCHED EFT when using the"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,18,0)="   option MANUALLY MATCH EFT-ERA."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,20,0)="   Once the match is made, the EFT will NOT be listed on the Unmatched"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,21,0)="   Aging Report."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,23,0)="3. EFT Unmatched Aging Report & ERA Unmatched Aging Reports"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,24,0)="   --------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,25,0)="   Modified VistA so that only non-duplicate EFTs that are unmatched and"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,26,0)="   have a payment amount greater than zero appear on the EFT Unmatched"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,27,0)="   Aging Report.  VistA was also modified so that only non-duplicate ERAs"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,28,0)="   that are unmatched and have a payment amount greater than zero appear"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,29,0)="   on the ERA Unmatched Aging Report."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,31,0)="4. Unapplied EFT Deposit Report"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,32,0)="   ---------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,33,0)="   Modified VistA to prevent duplicate EFTs from displaying on the"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",226,1,34,0)="   Unapplied EFT Deposit Report. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,0)="296 SEQ #260^3131119.120853^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,0)="^^14^14^3131119"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,1,0)="This patch addresses two issues."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,3,0)="The first issue implements two changes to the Automatic Payment Process"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,4,0)="Server [RCDP AUTOMATIC PAYMENTS] option that processes deposit files"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,5,0)="containing records of veterans' cash and check payments of their copayment"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,6,0)="bills to the national Lockbox.  Vista Accounts Receivable (AR) will begin"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,7,0)="to receive new types of deposit files that represent withholdings of VA"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,8,0)="Compensation and Pension (C&P) benefits or amounts owed to the veteran by "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,9,0)="the US Treasury, which must be applied to veteran's delinquent accounts "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,10,0)="in the same manner as cash/check payments."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,12,0)="The second issue is about the account lookup keys which will be included"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,13,0)="in the new Treasury and Compensation & Pension (C&P) withholding deposit"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",227,1,14,0)="files to identify the correct veteran in VistA."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",228,0)="295^3140106.161658^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",228,1,0)="^^1^1^3140106"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",228,1,1,0)="EPHARMACY OPERATING RULES"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",229,0)="260 SEQ #262^3140226.143542^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",229,1,0)="^^6^6^3140226"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",229,1,1,0)="This patch will add ""THANK YOU FOR YOUR PAYMENT"" to the bottom of the "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",229,1,2,0)="payment receipt."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",229,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",229,1,4,0)="The second item this patch will fix is replacing special characters in "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",229,1,5,0)="the transaction description of the PD segment that caused the CCPC "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",229,1,6,0)="transmission rejected by AAC."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",230,0)="297 SEQ #263^3140619.09312^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",230,1,0)="^^6^6^3140619"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",230,1,1,0)="After VistA changed Deposit Ticket numbers to be retained for seven (7) "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",230,1,2,0)="years, site users are experiencing issues with duplicate deposit numbers. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",230,1,3,0)="This is causing an increasing number of Deposit Ticket have to be manually"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",230,1,4,0)="reconciled and there is no workaround for this issue."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",230,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",230,1,6,0)="This patch will fix this issue."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",231,0)="299 SEQ #264^3140701.143019^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",231,1,0)="^^5^5^3140701"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",231,1,1,0)="This patch addresses two issues. The first issue involves the criteria"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",231,1,2,0)="checks to identify a bill for VA care or non-VA care in the CBO Data"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",231,1,3,0)="Extract process. The second issue is about the DMC Referred Report Print "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",231,1,4,0)="[PRCA RCDMC REFERRED RPT] option that opens the device twice resulted"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",231,1,5,0)="in the user being prompted twice for a message subject."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",232,0)="265 SEQ #265^3140917.095339^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",232,1,0)="^^9^9^3140917"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",232,1,1,0)="This patch contains three issues. The first issue is about the patient"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",232,1,2,0)="statements not successfully transmitting in Austin for printing. The "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",232,1,3,0)="second issue is regarding some erroneous admission and ending dates"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",232,1,4,0)="appearing on the patient statements."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",232,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",232,1,6,0)="The third issue concerns an undefined error when running the [RCDPE EOB"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",232,1,7,0)="TRANSFER REPORTS] option."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",232,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",232,1,9,0)="."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",233,0)="300 SEQ #266^3140929.140439^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",234,0)="306 SEQ #267^3140930.142639^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",234,1,0)="^^1^1^3140930"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",234,1,1,0)="Reverse DMC deposit"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",235,0)="281 SEQ #268^3141022.102812^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",235,1,0)="^^10^10^3141022"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",235,1,1,0)="The purpose of this patch is to replace direct global reads into the ICD"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",235,1,2,0)="OPERATION/PROCEDURE file (#80.1) and the ICD DIAGNOSIS file (#80) with a"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",235,1,3,0)="DRG API $$CODEC^ICDEX instead."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",235,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",235,1,5,0)="This patch updates one routine in the CBO Data Extract process. A DRG"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",235,1,6,0)="Grouper API is being used to retrieve the ICD-9/ICD-10 procedure code"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",235,1,7,0)="or ICD-9/ICD-10 diagnosis code for the data extract process to format"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",235,1,8,0)="and place them in a flat file via a nightly process. The nightly process"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",235,1,9,0)="in the Accounts Receivable Nightly Process Background Job option will then"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",235,1,10,0)="ftp the data directly to the Boston Allocation Resource Center (ARC)."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",236,0)="302^3150209.124323^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",237,0)="298^3150514.101153^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",237,1,0)="^^1^1^3150514"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",237,1,1,0)="TEST"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",238,0)="309 SEQ #271^3160115.154301^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",238,1,0)="^^5^5^3160115"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",238,1,1,0)="The purpose of this patch is to (1) add the additional suspense types to"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",238,1,2,0)="the Suspension Type field (#90) of the AR Transaction file (#433) for the"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",238,1,3,0)="Suspend an AR bill [PRCAC TR SUSPENDED] option, and (2) use a function to"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",238,1,4,0)="automatically generate the 'Brief Comment' for the selective suspension"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",238,1,5,0)="type in the Brief Account Profile [PRCAY ACCOUNT PROFILE] option."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,0)="303^3160701.141132^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,0)="^^13^13^3160701"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,1,0)="MCCF (Medical Care Collection Fund) Enhancement for uniform use of"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,2,0)="CARC/RARC (Claims Adjustment Rason Codes/Remittance Advice"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,3,0)="Reason Codes) Codes"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,5,0)="This patch implements changes to the Veterans Health Information Systems "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,6,0)="and Technology Architecture (VistA) Accounts Receivable (AR) software"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,7,0)="requested by the Veterans Health Administration (VHA) Chief Business"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,8,0)="Office (CBO) business Solutions to comply with legislative changes"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,9,0)="mandated by the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act of"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,10,0)="1996 (HIPAA) as amended by Public Law (P.L.) 111-148, The Patient"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,11,0)="Protection and Affordable Care Act (PPACA), Section 1104."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",239,1,13,0)="This patch implements the following:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",240,0)="304 SEQ #273^3160701.143229^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",240,1,0)="^^1^1^3160701"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",240,1,1,0)="MEDICAL CARE COLLECTION FUND (MCCF) ENHANCEMENTS PROJECT - ePAYMENTS"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",241,0)="316 SEQ #274^3160916.134124^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",242,0)="308 SEQ #275^3160923.155509^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",242,1,0)="^^3^3^3160923"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",242,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the request about Phase II algorithm adjustments"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",242,1,2,0)="that determine whether an episode of care is identified as VA CARE vs."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",242,1,3,0)="NON-VA CARE in the Vista CBO Data Extract (VDE) process."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",243,0)="301^3170103.154426^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",243,1,0)="^^3^3^3170103"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",243,1,1,0)="This patch contains VistA changes to support technology and"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",243,1,2,0)="business changes that are occurring with the implementation of"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",243,1,3,0)="the Treasury Cross Servicing project."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",244,0)="312 SEQ #277^3170123.144555^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",245,0)="317 SEQ #278^3170403.143227^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",246,0)="310 SEQ #280^3170419.121056^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",247,0)="322 SEQ #279^3170427.16465^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",247,1,0)="^^2^2^3170427"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",247,1,1,0)="1. Insure the Implied bill# entered in Receipt Processing payment entry"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",247,1,2,0)="   posts to the intended implied bill first."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",248,0)="323 SEQ #281^3170427.165746^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",248,1,0)="^^3^3^3170427"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",248,1,1,0)="1. Reject transmission processing:  Clear CS flag for '3E' reject code, "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",248,1,2,0)="   absolute value check that is causing reject batches being tossed aside "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",248,1,3,0)="   and adding new reject reasons to file 348.5"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",249,0)="324 SEQ #282^3170427.174952^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",249,1,0)="^^2^2^3170427"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",249,1,1,0)="1. Modify internal resolution of reject reason display on profile view of "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",249,1,2,0)="   bills."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",250,0)="307 SEQ #283^3170627.153512^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",250,1,0)="^^1^1^3170627"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",250,1,1,0)="Consolidated Patient Statement"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",251,0)="325 SEQ #284^3170727.123^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",251,1,0)="^^8^8^3170727"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",251,1,1,0)="Convert all scripts for handling Treasury Cross Service Project (TCSP)"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",251,1,2,0)="exceptions between Vista and Treasury to user option with improved"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",251,1,3,0)="controls. These scripts were provided to sites by the TCSP developers"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",251,1,4,0)="to handle mismatched Vista debtor/bills with the Treasury status for"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",251,1,5,0)="the same debtor/bills. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",251,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",251,1,7,0)="The sites are currently running these unwieldly scripts that need IT"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",251,1,8,0)="intervention to execute in programmer mode."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",252,0)="320 SEQ #285^3170830.150249^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",252,1,0)="^^2^2^3170830"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",252,1,1,0)="This patch is listed as an Emergency patch only due to install timing "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",252,1,2,0)="issues for data collection for the DATA Act."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",253,0)="327 SEQ #286^3170929.164244^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",253,1,0)="^^7^7^3170929"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",253,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following two issues:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",253,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",253,1,3,0)="1) The weekly TCSP (Treasury Cross Service) batch run at site will error"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",253,1,4,0)="   when the debtor is not defined in the debtor file."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",253,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",253,1,6,0)="2) AR/RC Reconcile Roll-up emails have single mail address no longer"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",253,1,7,0)="   used."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",254,0)="318 SEQ #287^3171005.140326^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",255,0)="331 SEQ #288^3171102.134632^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",255,1,0)="^^3^3^3171102"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",255,1,1,0)="The weekly TCSP (Treasury Cross Service) batch run at site does not set "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",255,1,2,0)="the correct address information in the C2CA message segment for veterans "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",255,1,3,0)="living in a foreign country."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",256,0)="319 SEQ #289^3171102.134727^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",256,1,0)="^^9^9^3171102"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",256,1,1,0)="Patch PRCA*4.5*319 addresses the following Accounts Receivable issues:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",256,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",256,1,3,0)="1. The ERA Worklist [RCDPE EDI LOCKBOX WORKLIST] option produces error:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",256,1,4,0)="   <UNDEFINED>GETPHARM+21^RCDPEWLP."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",256,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",256,1,6,0)="2. When using the Receipt Processing [RCDP RECEIPT PROCESSING] option to "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",256,1,7,0)="   reprocess an auto posted receipt, the message ""This receipt cannot be"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",256,1,8,0)="   processed - the receipt total does not match the EFT total for this EDI"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",256,1,9,0)="   Lockbox receipt"" is received when an EFT/ERA spans several receipts."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",257,0)="334 SEQ #290^3171227.162004^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",258,0)="333 SEQ #291^3180130.154127^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",258,1,0)="^^1^1^3180130"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",258,1,1,0)="Modify TOP bills foreign address handling"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",259,0)="335 SEQ #292^3180301.141524^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,0)="315 SEQ #293^3180601.161801^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,0)="^^367^367^3180601"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,2,0)="IMPORTANT INSTALLATION NOTE:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,3,0)="----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,4,0)="This patch is part of a multi-package build. There are three patches "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,5,0)="associated with the FY16 HAPE Revenue Enhancement project - IB*2.0*568,"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,6,0)="PRCA*4.5*315 and PSO*7.0*463. All three patches are to be installed "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,7,0)="together as a bundle, IB_2_568_PRCA_PSO_BUNDLE_T1.KID"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,10,0)="Description"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,11,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,12,0)="The Chief Business Office (CBO) is requesting system enhancements to"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,13,0)="The Veterans Health Information Systems and Technology Architecture"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,14,0)="(VistA) Integrated Billing (IB), Accounts Receivable (AR), and "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,15,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy (PSO) software modules.  "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,17,0)="The mission of the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA), Office of "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,18,0)="Information & Technology (OI&T), is to provide benefits and services "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,19,0)="to veterans of the United States Armed Forces. In meeting these goals, "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,20,0)="OIT strives to provide high quality, effective, and efficient "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,21,0)="Information Technology (IT) services to those responsible for "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,22,0)="providing care to the veterans at the point-of-care, as well as "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,23,0)="throughout all the points of the veterans' health care. The VA depends"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,24,0)="on Information Management/InformationTechnology (IM/IT) systems to meet"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,25,0)="mission goals."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,27,0)="The overall FY16 HAPE Revenue Enhancement project has been further "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,28,0)="divided into three sub-projects:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,30,0)="NSR #20150506"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,31,0)="The Revenue Eligibility Enhancements Project effort for the Chief "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,32,0)="Business Office (CBO), bundles several NSRs with similar business "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,33,0)="needs into a single requirements document.  Successfully addressing "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,34,0)="the requirements contained within this document will enable the "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,35,0)="Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) to appropriately bill certain "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,36,0)="subsets of billable events by correcting, automating, or enhancing "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,37,0)="current Veterans Health Information Systems and Technology Architecture"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,38,0)="(VistA) systems."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,40,0)="NSR #20150507"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,41,0)="The Revenue Operations Enhancements Project combines serveral NSRs, "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,42,0)="as well. This effort enables the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,43,0)="to improve revenue operation functionality related to repayment plans, "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,44,0)="late charge capture, bill suspension reasons, the billing of "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,45,0)="deactivated providers, and the display of appeal rights and "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,46,0)="responsibilities on the Veterans Beneficiary travel Bill of Collections"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,47,0)="form.  Implementation of the proposed enhancements will make a "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,48,0)="significant positive impact on stakeholders and target users."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,50,0)="NSR #20150505"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,51,0)="The Revenue Reporting Enhancements Project will enable the VA to "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,52,0)="improve tracking and reporting of revenue, and will support revenue "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,53,0)="reporting business rules and guidelines."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,56,0)="PRCA*4.5*315 patch enhancements, pertinent to the above NSRs, include:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,58,0)="1.) By means of the new Enter / Edit Repayment Plan option, the user "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,59,0)="will create the Repayment Plan by debtor. Note: The 'Enter / Edit "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,60,0)="Repayment Plan' menu option name will replace the 'Set up Repayment "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,61,0)="Plan' menu option name."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,63,0)="2.) On the Enter / Edit Repayment Plan option, if the AR Debtor has "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,64,0)="Active bills, the system will now display a selectable list of bills "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,65,0)="for the debtor."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,67,0)="3.) On the Enter / Edit Repayment Plan option, when displaying a list "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,68,0)="of Active bills for the Debtor, the system will display steps to the "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,69,0)="user to set up the Repayment Plan."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,71,0)="4.) On the Enter /Edit Repayment Plan option, once a Repayment Plan "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,72,0)="has been created or modified, the summary of the Repayment Plan is "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,73,0)="displayed."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,75,0)="5.) On the Enter / Edit Repayment Plan option, the system checks to "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,76,0)="see if a Repayment Plan has already been created for the Veteran.  "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,78,0)="6.) On the Enter / Edit Repayment Plan option, when choosing to Edit "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,79,0)="the Repayment Plan, all Active bills for the debtor will be displayed"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,80,0)="allowing the user to add new Active bills to the Repayment Plan as well"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,81,0)="as change the due date of first payment and/or the repayment amount due "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,82,0)="on the Repayment Plan. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,84,0)="7.) On the Enter / Edit Repayment Plan option, if the Debtor does not "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,85,0)="have new Active bills that can be added to the Repayment Plan, the user "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,86,0)="will proceed to identify the repayment amount due and/or repayment "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,87,0)="amount due date on the Repayment Plan."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,89,0)="8.) On the Enter / Edit Repayment Plan option, a designated identifier "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,90,0)="will signify when an Active bill is part of a Repayment Plan. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,92,0)="9.) On the Enter / Edit Repayment Plan option, the system will display "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,93,0)="previously made payments to the Repayment Plan."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,95,0)="10.) On the Enter / Edit Repayment Plan option, the User has the option "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,96,0)="to enter Debtor Comments during the setup process. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,98,0)="11.) The AR Clerk will be able to select Suspended Type from the menu "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,99,0)="to display in the Status Listing For Bills [PRCAL STATUS LIST] report."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,101,0)="12.) Status Listing For Bills [PRCAL STATUS LIST] report shall be "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,102,0)="modified to incorporate reason for suspension."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,104,0)="13.) Provide the ability to lock the option to update late payment "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,105,0)="charges (Interest/Admin/Penalty Rates [PRCAF U ADMIN.RATE]) with a new"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,106,0)="security key. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,108,0)="14.) The system will allow the user to identify if the Bill of "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,109,0)="Collections letter applies to Veterans Beneficiary Travel (Form 1114)."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,111,0)="15.) The system will print the Notice of Rights and Responsibilities "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,112,0)="when the Bill of Collections pertains to Veterans Beneficiary Travel."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,114,0)="16.) VistA AR Software Package shall discontinue generation of the "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,115,0)="Mailman message/bulletin, ""ARDC Detail Report for MON/ YYYY"", without "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,116,0)="interrupting any other transfer data within ARDC."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,118,0)="17.) The VistA AR Software Package shall allow the generation of a "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,119,0)="report of bills containing the same information as the discontinued "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,120,0)="""ARDC Detail Report for MON/YYYY"" with the following exceptions/ "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,121,0)="additions:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,122,0)="        The report shall include current status bills (New Bill, Active, "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,123,0)="        Returned for Amendment, Amended Bill, Open, and Suspended bills) "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,124,0)="        only;"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,125,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,126,0)="        The report shall include a column for the Fund number associated "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,127,0)="        with each line item on the report; and "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,129,0)="        The report shall include a column for the RSC associated with "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,130,0)="        each line item on the report."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,131,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,132,0)="18.) Currently, when non-healthcare debt of $25 or greater is in a "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,133,0)="delinquent status for 180 days, VistA transmits this debt to TOP "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,134,0)="(via AITC and DMC) for initiation of the standard collection process."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,135,0)="To maintain compliance with The DATA Act of 2014, the 180-day date "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,136,0)="parameter shall be changed to 120 days."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,138,0)="19.)  A new audit trail is needed for detailing events or transactions "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,139,0)="that have occurred on healthcare debts referred for debt collection, to "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,140,0)="effectively support Veterans and reconcile accounts."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,141,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,142,0)="20.)  VistA shall provide enhanced reporting capability, usability "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,143,0)="features, and additional data elements for managing healthcare debts "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,144,0)="referred for debt collection to improve VHA's ability to provide support "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,145,0)="to Veterans and manage accounts."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,146,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,147,0)="21.)  Create report to track stop/reactivate debts. VistA shall provide "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,148,0)="a Stop/Reactivate report to identify healthcare debts that are placed "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,149,0)="in the corresponding status."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,150,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,151,0)="22.)  Improve automation in management of debt collection. VistA shall "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,152,0)="utilize existing functionality, such as List Manager, and other "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,153,0)="automation capabilities to improve debt collection management"""
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,154,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,155,0)="23.)  The existing Medication Co-Pay Exemption Report [PRCAX CO-PAY "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,156,0)="EXEMPTION REPORT] shall be modified with the following field changes:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,157,0)="        Change PT ID from full Social Security Number (SSN) to LastN + "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,158,0)="             4SSN"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,159,0)="        Add Rx#"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,160,0)="        Add Drug Name (first 10 to 12 characters)"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,161,0)="        Add Fill/Refill Date"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,162,0)="        Add Effective Date of Exemption"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,163,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,164,0)="24.)  A new Third Party Accounts Receivable category called "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,165,0)="'EMERGENCY/HUMANITARIAN REIMB.' shall be created in Accounts Receivables "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,166,0)="with the insurer as the responsible party. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,167,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,168,0)="25.) A new Third Party Accounts Receivable category called 'INELIGIBLE "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,169,0)="HOSP. REIMB' shall be created in Accounts Receivables with the insurer "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,170,0)="as the responsible party. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,172,0)="26.) A one-character ""Type"" field shall be added to the Claims Matching "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,173,0)="Report that will indicate the third-party claim care-type (""I"" for "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,174,0)="Inpatient, ""O"" for Outpatient, ""P"" for Prosthetics, and ""R"" for "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,175,0)="Prescription"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,176,0)="[Rx]) on the report of third-party bills."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,177,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,178,0)="27.) When a user generates a Claims Matching Report for a patient, all "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,179,0)="records for that patient are currently produced on the report. At "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,180,0)="times, users need to generate information regarding only certain types "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,181,0)="of care for a patient.  The system shall allow the user to choose "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,182,0)="between producing a Claims Matching Report containing (1) all records "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,183,0)="for a patient, or (2) only records of a certain care type (""I"" for "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,184,0)="Inpatient, ""O"" for Outpatient, ""P"" for Prosthetics, or ""R"" for "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,185,0)="Prescription [Rx])."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,187,0)="28.) The Claims Matching Report, when exported, shall be in a line "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,188,0)="format so that information on the report may be easily exported to "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,189,0)="Microsoft Excel."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,190,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,191,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,192,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,193,0)="Concurrent Development / Dependencies:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,194,0)="--------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,195,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,196,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,197,0)=" "
