^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,292,0)="                                           prca_4_5_tm+r0515.doc Binary"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,293,0)="Accounts Receivable Deployment, Installation, "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,294,0)="     Back-Out, and Rollback Guide   "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,295,0)="              FY16RevenueARVIP_Deployment_Installation_Guide.doc Binary "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,296,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,297,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,298,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,299,0)="Patch Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,300,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,301,0)="Pre/Post Installation Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,302,0)="-------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,303,0)="The post installation routine, PRCA315P, is not automatically deleted"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,304,0)="as part of the installation process. You may delete it after"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,305,0)="installation if you desire."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,306,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,307,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,308,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,309,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,310,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,311,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,312,0)="--------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,313,0)="This process will install new and updated routines and other "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,314,0)="components listed above. There is a post-install routine that will add "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,315,0)="entries to a number of files."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,316,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,317,0)="The patch will be released in conjunction with an Integrated Billing"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,318,0)="patch, IB*4.5*568, and an Outpatient Pharmacy patch, PSO*7.0*463."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,319,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,320,0)="  ************************ NOTE ************************"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,321,0)="  IF A USER IS ON THE SYSTEM AND USING THESE PROGRAMS "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,322,0)="  AN EDITED ERROR WILL OCCUR.  "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,323,0)="  The patch should be installed when NO Outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,324,0)="  Pharmacy users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,325,0)="  ******************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,326,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,327,0)=" Installation will take less than 1 minute."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,328,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,329,0)=" Suggested time to install: non-peak requirement hours."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,330,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,331,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,332,0)="  1. Obtain the file IB_2_568_PRCA_PSO_BUNDLE_T1.KID"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,333,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,334,0)="  2. From the Kernel Installation & Distribution System menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,335,0)="     the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,336,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,337,0)="  3. Use Load a Distribution using IB_2_568_PRCA_PSO_BUNDLE_T1.KID when"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,338,0)="     prompted to Enter a Host File name.  You may need to append a"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,339,0)="     directory name."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,340,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,341,0)="  4. From this menu, you may select to use the following options"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,342,0)="     (when prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter IB*2.0*568):"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,343,0)="         a.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,344,0)="             allow you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,345,0)="             in the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,346,0)="         b.  Print Transport Global - This option will allow you to "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,347,0)="             view the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,348,0)="         c.  Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,349,0)="             will allow you to view all changes that will be made when "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,350,0)="             this patch is installed.  It compares all components of "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,351,0)="             this patch (routines, DD's, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,352,0)="         d.  Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,353,0)="             backup message of any routines exported with this patch. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,354,0)="             It will not backup any other changes such as DD's or "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,355,0)="             templates."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,356,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,357,0)="  5. When prompted ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,358,0)="     NO//"" respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,359,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,360,0)="  6. When prompted ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,361,0)="     and Protocols? NO//"" respond NO. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,362,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,363,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,364,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,365,0)="Post-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,366,0)="-------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",260,1,367,0)="There are no special tasks to perform after this patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",261,0)="339 SEQ #294^3180601.162827^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",262,0)="321^3180706.151902^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",263,0)="337 SEQ #296^3180706.152439^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",263,1,0)="^^8^8^3180706"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",263,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following two issues:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",263,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",263,1,3,0)="1. Ensure Tier Rate decreases do not flag non Tier Rate charges as"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",263,1,4,0)="   duplicate"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",263,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",263,1,6,0)="2. Modify purging criteria for the weekly TCSP batch run"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",263,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",263,1,8,0)="3. Modify purging criteria for the weekly TOP batch run"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",264,0)="341 SEQ #297^3180907.121008^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",265,0)="340 SEQ #298^3180907.122039^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",266,0)="326^3181204.155035^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",266,1,0)="^^1^1^3181204"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",266,1,1,0)="Patch for builds 4 and 5 of ePayments MCCF project."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",267,0)="344 SEQ #300^3190201.122346^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",267,1,0)="^^1^1^3190201"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",267,1,1,0)="1. CS BATCH RUN: 5B MAIL MESSAGE HANDLING"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",268,0)="342 SEQ #301^3190201.124933^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",268,1,0)="^^10^10^3190201"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",268,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue(s):"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",268,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",268,1,3,0)="1. A <PARAMETER> error occurs when running the Accounts Receivable Nightly"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",268,1,4,0)="Process Background Job [PRCA NIGHTLY PROCESS] when one of the records "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",268,1,5,0)="processed is locked."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",268,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",268,1,7,0)="2. A <SUBSCRIPT> error occurs while running the Status Listing"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",268,1,8,0)="For Bills [PRCAL STATUS LIST] option when an ACCOUNTS RECEIVABLE"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",268,1,9,0)="(#430) bill has a CURRENT STATUS (#8) of SUSPENDED and does not"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",268,1,10,0)="have any associated transactions in the AR TRANSACTION (#433) file."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,0)="336 SEQ #302^3190401.151025^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,0)="^^27^27^3190401"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,3,0)="1. Modify Cross-service bill foreign address handling"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,5,0)="2. Ensure that the telephone number in the IAI C2CA (Debtor Contact"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,6,0)="   Information) adheres to the AITC and Artiva guidelines that the"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,7,0)="   phone number (position 261-270) be 10 numeric and, if not, leave "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,8,0)="   the field blank and also leave positions 260 (Contact Phone Type)"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,9,0)="   and 275 (Contact Primary Phone) blank."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,11,0)="3. Modify served messages from Treasury to not use the same work space as"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,12,0)="   weekly batch run"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,14,0)="4. Ensure the cross-service date is reset for rejected recalls by Treasury"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,16,0)="5. Ensure TCSP bill scrub sets address node in file 430"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,18,0)="6. Ensure CS flag set for debtor is only cleared if deceased or scrubbed"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,20,0)="7. Ensure 5B records are sent to Treasury in every case except when "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,21,0)="   Recall status is set on bill"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,23,0)="8. Fix CS reporting for IOP setup affecting other print options"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,25,0)="9. Update the Error Code file #348.5 with code additions/changes"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",269,1,27,0)="10. Correct bill Category codes to reflect 47 & 49 to skip bill processing"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",270,0)="346 SEQ #303^3190402.142712^54"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",270,1,0)="^^2^2^3190402"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",270,1,1,0)="1. Bad Debt report (Allowance for Bad Debt and Contract Allowance)"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",270,1,2,0)="   does not print for Fund due to incorrect entry in compiler"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",271,0)="332^3190708.181823^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",271,1,0)="^^1^1^3190708"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",271,1,1,0)="MCCF EDI TAS EPAYMENTS BUILD 3"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",272,0)="347 SEQ #306^3190708.220025^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",272,1,0)="^^5^5^3190708"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",272,1,1,0)="AR Cross Servicing Patch.   Contains two new reports, 2 new options to "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",272,1,2,0)="run them and 4 new routines"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",272,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",272,1,4,0)="0-40 Percent SC Change Reconciliation Report (RCDMCR4A and RCDMCR4B)"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",272,1,5,0)="First Party Charge IB Cancellation Recon Report (RCDMCR5A and RCDMC5B)"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",273,0)="338 SEQ #307^3190812.152137^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",274,0)="351 SEQ #308^3190812.152517^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",275,0)="357 SEQ #309^3190916.094145^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",276,0)="362 SEQ #310^3190926.101051^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",277,0)="348 SEQ #311^3191003.155132^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",277,1,0)="^^3^3^3191003"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",277,1,1,0)="1. Patient statement compilation issue"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",277,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",277,1,3,0)="2. Option 'Build CCPC Transmission batch' queued start time control"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",278,0)="356 SEQ #312^3191016.161845^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",278,1,0)="^^3^3^3191016"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",278,1,1,0)="This patch addresses an undefined error CARE+99^RCXVUTIL in the CBO Data"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",278,1,2,0)="Extract process of the Accounts Receivable Nightly Process Background"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",278,1,3,0)="[PRCA NIGHTLY PROCESS] option."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",279,0)="355 SEQ #313^3191016.163021^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",279,1,0)="^^10^10^3191016"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",279,1,1,0)="Statement Schedule Update:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",279,1,2,0)="As an Accounts Receivable Business Owner..."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",279,1,3,0)="I want To modify the day of the month that 16 specific sites are assigned "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",279,1,4,0)="in VistA."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",279,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",279,1,6,0)="Sites: 438, 501, 504, 542, 562, 565, 568, 621, 649, 656, 658, 664, 671, "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",279,1,7,0)="688, 740, and 756 ..."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",279,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",279,1,9,0)="So that The workload is redistributed more evenly across the days of the "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",279,1,10,0)="month."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",280,0)="350 SEQ #314^3191203.144758^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",280,1,0)="^^3^3^3191203"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",280,1,1,0)="AR Cross Servicing Patch.   Contains two new reports, 2 new options to "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",280,1,2,0)="run them and 4 new routines.   Also will contain more things as B2 goes "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",280,1,3,0)="underway"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",281,0)="353 SEQ #315^3191219.144837^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",281,1,0)="^^6^6^3191219"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",281,1,1,0)="When a bill principal balance is auto-decreased to zero, any "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",281,1,2,0)="remaining Interest Balance, Administrative Cost Balance, Court Cost "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",281,1,3,0)="and Marshall Fee should be adjusted to zero."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",281,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",281,1,5,0)="Also, when a cancelled charge (decrease) from IB updates an AR bill that"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",281,1,6,0)="has a 'SUSPENSED' status, the charge should be posted to the bill."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",282,0)="358^3191230.125918^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",282,1,0)="^^6^6^3191230"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",282,1,1,0)="1. Modify Cost Center selection to pull from work file that ensures"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",282,1,2,0)="   all cost centers related to a Fund Control Point are available for "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",282,1,3,0)="   selection."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",282,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",282,1,5,0)="2. All Cost Centers linked to a Fund Control Point are not checked for "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",282,1,6,0)="   inactive status."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",283,0)="360 SEQ #317^3200115.122604^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",284,0)="359 SEQ #318^3200122.154152^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",284,1,0)="^^9^9^3200122"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",284,1,1,0)="Accounts Receivable patch, PRCA*4.5*359, address the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",284,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",284,1,3,0)="1. A subscript error, <SUBSCRIPT>UPDTMPB+12^RCDPENR1, is impacting the "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",284,1,4,0)="   weekly Accounts Receivable (AR) Diagnostic Measures Statistical"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",284,1,5,0)="   Reports for users."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",284,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",284,1,7,0)="2. When editing debtor address information in the option Address "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",284,1,8,0)="   Display/Edit [PRCA VEN BIL], the formatting of the phone number"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",284,1,9,0)="   and zip code displayed is incorrect. "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",285,0)="366 SEQ #319^3200228.130033^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",285,1,0)="^^3^3^3200228"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",285,1,1,0)="This patch will address one issue:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",285,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",285,1,3,0)="1. Failed text transaction setup in FILE 433"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",286,0)="364 SEQ #320^3200401.163631^70"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",286,1,0)="^^6^6^3200401"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",286,1,1,0)="This patch will address two issues:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",286,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",286,1,3,0)="1. Bills were sent to TOP after the cross-service cutoff date 08/01/15."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",286,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",286,1,5,0)="2. Ensure Exempt transaction for cancelled bill has DATE & TIME for Date "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",286,1,6,0)="   Entered."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",287,0)="365 SEQ #321^3200601.152007^70"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",288,0)="368 SEQ #322^3200713.172612^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",288,1,0)="^^4^4^3200713"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",288,1,1,0)="There is one issue being fixed."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",288,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",288,1,3,0)="1. The option 'PRCAL STATUS LIST' at times shows incorrect info for "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",288,1,4,0)="   status type equals suspended."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",289,0)="369 SEQ #323^3200923.10315^65"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",289,1,0)="^^7^7^3200923"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",289,1,1,0)="This patch will fix two issues: "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",289,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",289,1,3,0)="1. A patient name with two middle names do not appear correctly on"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",289,1,4,0)="   a patient statement printed at CCPC."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",289,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",289,1,6,0)="2. The weekly cross-service batch run does not create a proper text "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",289,1,7,0)="   transaction for auto recalls for bills <$25."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",290,0)="361 SEQ #324^3200930.174844^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",291,0)="345^3201023.091224^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",291,1,0)="^^2^2^3201023"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",291,1,1,0)="ePayments build 9"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",291,1,2,0)="updated December 18, 2018"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",292,0)="372 SEQ #326^3201112.175252^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",293,0)="376 SEQ #327^3210113.17211^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",294,0)="373 SEQ #328^3210401.110314^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",294,1,0)="^^3^3^3210401"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",294,1,1,0)="This report captures detailed 1st party bill information for a specific"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",294,1,2,0)="veteran, within a user specified range of dates of service. This report"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",294,1,3,0)="output requires screen size of 256 characters wide."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",295,0)="377b^3210505"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",295,1,0)="^^5^5^3210505"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",295,1,1,0)="Backup of PRCA*4.5*377 on May 05, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",295,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",295,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",295,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",295,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",296,0)="377 SEQ #329^3210505.093607^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",297,0)="375b^3210519"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",297,1,0)="^^5^5^3210519"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",297,1,1,0)="Backup of PRCA*4.5*375 on May 19, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",297,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",297,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",297,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",297,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,0)="375 SEQ #330^3210519.160954^17"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,0)="^^200^200^3210519"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,1,0)="The purpose of this patch is to address issues arising with"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,2,0)="Electronic Fund Transfers (EFTs), received into VistA, that have been"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,3,0)="split between VistA and CERNER as a result of the EHMR implementation."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,4,0)="This process may result in the receipt of debit EFTs, which need to be"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,5,0)="correctly identified and passed to the Financial Management System (FMS). "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,7,0)="The following features of the PRCA software will be affected by this "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,8,0)="patch:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,10,0)="1. Receipt transactions for a debit type EFT will be marked with"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,11,0)="   a new debit flag.  These transactions will be subtracted from the"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,12,0)="   calculated receipt total, which may result in a negative receipt total."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,15,0)="2. When an EFT is removed from the system using the menu option"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,16,0)="   Remove Duplicate EFT Deposits, [RCDPE REMOVE DUP DEPOSITS], the"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,17,0)="   new field REMOVAL TYPE [.2] will be entered, after the removal reason "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,18,0)="   text. The user must enter one of two codes from the set:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,20,0)="          D         DUPLICATE EFT"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,21,0)="          M         MILLENIUM EFT"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,23,0)="   The new field will show on the Duplicate EFT Deposits Audit report"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,24,0)="   [RCDPE EFT AUDIT REPORT]."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,27,0)="This patch will have no significant impact on disk space or journal file "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,28,0)="usage."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,29,0)=" "
