^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,138,0)="Pre/Post Installation Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,139,0)="-------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,140,0)="** IMPORTANT: Do not install this patch while the ""Accounts Receivable "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,141,0)="Nightly Process Background Job"" [PRCA NIGHTLY PROCESS] is running **"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,142,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,143,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,144,0)="recommended it be queued to run after normal business hours, but before "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,145,0)="the Accounts Receivable Nightly Process Background Job starts, to minimize"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,146,0)="potential disruption to users. This patch will take less than 5 minutes to"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,147,0)="install.   "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,149,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,150,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,151,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,152,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,153,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,154,0)="--------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,156,0)="    1. Choose the PackMan message containing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,157,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,158,0)="    2. Choose the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,159,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,160,0)="    3. From the Kernel Installation & Distribution System Menu, select the"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,161,0)="       Installation Menu. From this menu, you may select to use the"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,162,0)="       following options. When prompted for the INSTALL NAME, enter"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,163,0)="       the patch PRCA*4.5*364:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,164,0)="          a. Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,165,0)="             you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,166,0)="             transport global."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,167,0)="          b. Print Transport Global - This option will allow you to view"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,168,0)="             the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,169,0)="          c. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,170,0)="             allow you to view all changes that will be made when this "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,171,0)="             patch is installed. It compares all components of this patch"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,172,0)="             (routines, DD's, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,173,0)="          d. Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,174,0)="             message containing the components of this patch. When "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,175,0)="             prompted, select 'B' for Build, to back-up the routines and"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,176,0)="             other components affected by this patch."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,177,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,178,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,179,0)="     4. From the Installation Menu, select the Install Package(s) option"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,180,0)="        and choose the patch to install."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,181,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,182,0)="     5. When Prompted ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,183,0)="        NO//"" respond NO.  "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,184,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,185,0)="     6. When Prompted ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,186,0)="        and Protocols? NO//"" respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,187,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,188,0)="                           "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,189,0)="Post-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,190,0)="-------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,191,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,192,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,193,0)="Back-Out/Roll Back Plan:"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,194,0)="------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,195,0)="Prior to installing the updated KIDS package, the site/region should have "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,196,0)="saved a backup of the build in a mail message using the Backup a "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,197,0)="Transport Global [XPD BACKUP] menu option. The message containing the "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,198,0)="backed-up build can be loaded with the ""Xtract PackMan"" function at "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,199,0)="the Message Action prompt.  The PackMan function INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE is "
^DIC(9.4,53,22,20,"PAH",298,1,200,0)="then used to install the backed-up build onto the VistA system."
