^DIC(9.4,59,0)="NATIONAL DRUG FILE^PSN^This is the National Drug File Package V 3.15"
^DIC(9.4,59,5)="B'HAM"
^DIC(9.4,59,7)="^^I"
^DIC(9.4,59,20,0)="^9.402P^^"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,0)="^9.49I^5^5"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,1,0)="3.15^2960425^2960702^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,1,1,0)="^^1^1^2960702"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,1,1,1,0)="NATIONAL DRUG FILE V. 3.15 MAINTENANCE RELEASE"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,0)="3.16^2960926^2961115^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,1,0)="^^1^1^2961115"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,1,1,0)="NATIONAL DRUG FILE V. 3.16 MAINTENANCE RELEASE"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^7^7"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",1,0)="2^2970122^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",1,1,0)="^^3^3^2970122"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",1,1,1,0)="This patch installs the data dictionary for the MEDICATION INSTRUCTION SHEETS"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",1,1,2,0)="file (#54.7).  It also installs the option to print an instruction sheet."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",1,1,3,0)="Data for the file is NOT included with the patch."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,0)="3^2970206^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^14^14^2970206"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,1,0)="This patch installs changes to the software to print Patient Medication"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,2,0)="Instruction Sheets."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,4,0)=" 1. Once a Medication Instruction Sheet is printed, the user is"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,5,0)="    prompted for another drug rather than being returned to the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,6,0)="    menu system."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,8,0)=" 2. When being prompted for the number of copies, the default of"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,9,0)="    one is shown."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,11,0)=" 3. When being prompted for a drug, drugs that are inactive and"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,12,0)="    drugs that are not linked to a Medication Instruction Sheet"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,13,0)="    are not shown."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",2,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",3,0)="4^2970312^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^3^3^2970312"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="This patch installs changes to the National Drug File so that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",3,1,2,0)="Patient Medication Instruction Sheets with incorrect information"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",3,1,3,0)="will not be able to be selected for printing."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",4,0)="5^2970414^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^5^5^2970414"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="This patch installs the mail group NDF DATA.  This group will"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",4,1,2,0)="receive messages as updates are made to the National Drug File."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",4,1,3,0)="Members of this group should include all people responsible"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",4,1,4,0)="for maintaining the links between the local Drug file and the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",4,1,5,0)="National Drug File."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",5,0)="7 SEQ #6^2970414^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",5,1,0)="^^1^1^2970414"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",5,1,1,0)="This patch disables the printing of two Medication Instruction Sheets."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",6,0)="6^2970709^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",7,0)="9 SEQ #8^2970710^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^3^3^2970710"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",7,1,1,0)=" This patch will delete field #2 (*ROUTINE) from the MEDICATION ROUTES"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",7,1,2,0)=" FILE #51.2. Also, data associated with this field will be deleted"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH",7,1,3,0)=" from the entries in file #51.2."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH","B",2,1)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH","B",3,2)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH","B",4,3)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH","B",5,4)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH","B",6,6)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH","B","7 SEQ #6",5)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,2,"PAH","B","9 SEQ #8",7)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,0)="3.17^^2971006^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,1,0)="^^1^1^2971006"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,1,1,0)="NATIONAL DRUG FILE V. 3.17 MAINTENANCE RELEASE"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^4^4"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",1,0)="2^2971106^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",1,1,0)="^^3^3^2971106"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",1,1,1,0)="This patch updates the links between NDF and Patient Medication Instruction"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",1,1,2,0)="Sheets.  Updates for the Medication Instruction Sheets are not included"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",1,1,3,0)="with this patch."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",2,0)="3^2980220^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^4^4^2980220"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",2,1,1,0)="This patch contains the routine PSNPPIP, used to print Medication"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",2,1,2,0)="Information Sheets.  Enhancements to this routine provide the ability to"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",2,1,3,0)="print Medication Information Sheets from within the List Manager actions"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",2,1,4,0)="contained in Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",3,0)="4^2980417^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^2^2^2980417"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="This patch corrects a problem with some Drug-Drug Interactions"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",3,1,2,0)="not being flagged or alerted to the user."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",4,0)="5^2980423^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^4^4^2980423"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="This patch contains corrections to the routine ^PSNMRG, used to merge"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",4,1,2,0)="information from the NATIONAL DRUG file (50.6) into the DRUG file (#50)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",4,1,3,0)="It also contains a post install routine which corrects the data stored"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH",4,1,4,0)="incorrectly due to the problem."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH","B",2,1)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH","B",3,2)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH","B",4,3)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,3,"PAH","B",5,4)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,0)="3.18^2980112^2980423^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,1,0)="^^1^1^2980423"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,1,1,0)="NATIONAL DRUG FILE V. 3.18 MAINTENANCE RELEASE"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^7^7"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",1,0)="1^2980428^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",1,1,0)="^^4^4^2980428"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",1,1,1,0)="This patch contains corrections to the routine ^PSNMRG, used to merge"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",1,1,2,0)="information from the NATIONAL DRUG file (50.6) into the DRUG file (#50)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",1,1,3,0)="It also contains a post install routine which corrects the data stored"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",1,1,4,0)="incorrectly due to the problem."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",2,0)="2^2980618^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^4^4^2980618"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",2,1,1,0)="This patch adds three new products: PRECISION Q-I-D (GLUCOSE) TEST"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",2,1,2,0)="STRIP, PRECISION LINK, and PRECISION Q-I-D SENSOR,HAND HELD to the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",2,1,3,0)="NATIONAL DRUG file (#50.6).  This patch also updates the DRUG"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",2,1,4,0)="INGREDIENTS file (#50.416) to reflect these additional products."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",3,0)="3^2980625^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^3^3^2980923^"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="This patch updates the links between NDF and Patient Medication Instruction"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",3,1,2,0)="Sheets.  Updates for the Medication Instruction Sheets are not included"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",3,1,3,0)="with this patch."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",4,0)="5 SEQ #4^2980923^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^5^5^2980923"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="This patch consists of a single routine PSNAPIS which contains several"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",4,1,2,0)="Application Programmer Interfaces (APIs) for the NATIONAL DRUG file (#$50.6)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",4,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",4,1,4,0)="This file is being redesigned and these APIs are intended to allow a smooth"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",4,1,5,0)="transition to the new structure."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",5,0)="8^2981007^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",5,1,0)="^^5^5^2981007"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",5,1,1,0)="This patch consists of a single routine PSNAPIS which contains several"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",5,1,2,0)="Application Programmer Interfaces (APIs) for the NATIONAL DRUG file (#$50.6)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",5,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",5,1,4,0)="This file is being redesigned and these APIs are intended to allow a smooth"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",5,1,5,0)="transition to the new structure."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",6,0)="4 SEQ #6^2981007^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",6,1,0)="^^9^9^2981007"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",6,1,1,0)="This patch PSN*3.18*4 serves two purposes. First, it will put back"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",6,1,2,0)="a VA Product Name in the VA PRODUCT NAMES multiple (#50.68) of NATIONAL"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",6,1,3,0)="DRUG file (#50.6) which was inadvertently missing in National Drug File"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",6,1,4,0)="(NDF) V. 3.18. It will put two entries in the DRUG INGREDIENTS file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",6,1,5,0)="(#50.416) and will re-index the appropriate entries in files NATIONAL DRUG"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",6,1,6,0)="(#50.6), DRUG INGREDIENTS (#50.416), and DRUG INTERACTIONS (#56). The"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",6,1,7,0)="second problem this patch will fix will be to reset the third and fourth"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",6,1,8,0)="pieces of each multiple level in 50.6 to prevent possible NDF matching"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",6,1,9,0)="errors."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",7,0)="7^2981104^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^5^5^2981104"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",7,1,1,0)="This patch consists of a single routine PSNAPIS which contains several"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",7,1,2,0)="Application Programmer Interfaces (APIs) for the NATIONAL DRUG file (#50.6)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",7,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",7,1,4,0)="This file is being redesigned and these APIs are intended to allow a smooth"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH",7,1,5,0)="transition to the new structure."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH","B",1,1)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH","B",2,2)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH","B",3,3)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH","B",7,7)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH","B",8,5)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH","B","4 SEQ #6",6)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,4,"PAH","B","5 SEQ #4",4)=""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,0)="4.0^3051119^2981120^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,1,0)="^9.54^1^1^3051219^"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,1,1,0)="NATIONAL DRUG FILE VERSION 4.0"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^545^545"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",1,0)="2 SEQ #1^2981120^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",1,1,0)="^^5^5^2981120"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",1,1,1,0)="This build contains patch PSN*4.0*2 which replaces seven routines"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",1,1,2,0)="that were originally released with National Drug File (NDF) V. 4.0."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",1,1,3,0)="This patch also adds Inactivation Date fields to files 50.607, 50.608,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",1,1,4,0)="50.609, 50.416, and 55.95. The data dictionary for a field in file 50.67"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",1,1,5,0)="will change."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",2,0)="3 SEQ #2^2990119^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^2^2^2990119"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",2,1,1,0)="This build contains the National Drug File enhancement patch. It"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",2,1,2,0)="includes routines, a partial data dictionary, as well as print templates."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",3,0)="1^2990119^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^1^1^2990119"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",4,0)="4^2990201^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^1^1^2990201"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="This patch removes remote members from the mail group NDF DATA."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",5,0)="6^2990223^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",5,1,0)="^^1^1^2990223"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",5,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,0)="5 SEQ #6^2990316^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,0)="^^16^16^2990316"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,1,0)="This patch corrects several problems."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,3,0)=" 1. An error may occur when using the Pharmacy Data Management (PDM)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,4,0)=" Drug Enter/Edit option [PSS DRUG ENTER/EDIT]. The routine PSNSTCK was not"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,5,0)=" cleaning up all local variables."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,7,0)=" 2. This patch also corrects a possible error in a few cases when using"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,8,0)=" the Inquire to VA Product Info For Local Drug option [PSNLOOK]. The"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,9,0)=" routine PSNLOOK was not checking properly for the (non)existence of data."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,11,0)=" 3. This patch adds help text when selecting a National Drug Code (NDC)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,12,0)=" using the option NDC/UPN Inquiry [PSNUPN]."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,14,0)=" 4. The option Local Formulary Report [PSNFRMLY] was leaving the variable"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,15,0)=" DIR defined upon exit. This could cause erroneous prompts under certain"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",6,1,16,0)=" circumstances. This patch eliminates that problem."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",7,0)="7 SEQ #7^2990322^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^1^1^2990322"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",7,1,1,0)="This patch updates the data for patient medication instruction sheets."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",8,0)="8^2990322^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",8,1,0)="^^1^1^2990322^"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",8,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",9,0)="9^2990419^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",9,1,0)="^^1^1^2990419"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",9,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",10,0)="10^2990602^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^1^1^2990602"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",10,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",11,0)="12^2990622^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^1^1^2990622"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",12,0)="11 SEQ #12^2990719^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^7^7^2990719"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="The option Inquire to VA Product Info For Local Drug [PSNLOOK] displays"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",12,1,2,0)="the associated Patient Medication Information Sheet (PMIS) entry. If a"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",12,1,3,0)="drug is selected that does not have a link to a PMIS, the PMIS information"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",12,1,4,0)="from the previous drug is displayed.  This patch eliminates the problem by"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",12,1,5,0)="deleting the appropriate variable prior to gathering PMIS information."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",12,1,6,0)="This patch also corrects the spelling of the MANUFACTURER field (#3) in"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",12,1,7,0)="the NDC/UPN file (#50.67)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",13,0)="14^2990719^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",13,1,0)="^^1^1^2990719"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",13,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",14,0)="15^2990914^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",14,1,0)="^^1^1^2990914"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",14,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",15,0)="16 SEQ #15^2991002^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",15,1,0)="^^1^1^2991002"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",15,1,1,0)="This patch updates the data for patient medication instruction sheets."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",16,0)="17^2991002^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^1^1^2991002"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",16,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",17,0)="18^2991019^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",17,1,0)="^^1^1^2991019"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",17,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",18,0)="21^2991123^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^1^1^2991123"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",19,0)="19 SEQ #19^2991210^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",19,1,0)="^^2^2^2991210"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",19,1,1,0)=" This patch corrects an undefined error in the Local Drug File Report"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",19,1,2,0)=" [PSNLDG] option."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",20,0)="23^3000125^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",20,1,0)="^^1^1^3000125"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",20,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",21,0)="24^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",21,1,0)="^^1^1^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",21,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",22,0)="26 SEQ #22^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",22,1,0)="^^1^1^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",22,1,1,0)="This patch corrects erroneous drug interaction names."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",23,0)="22 SEQ #23^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",23,1,0)="^^2^2^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",23,1,1,0)="This build contains routines and options for the National Formulary"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",23,1,2,0)="Indicator enhancement patch."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",24,0)="25^3000405^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",24,1,0)="^^1^1^3000405"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",24,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",25,0)="27 SEQ #25^3000405^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",25,1,0)="^^3^3^3000405"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",25,1,1,0)="This patch corrects null subscript errors reported in NOIS PTH-0300-20463."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",25,1,2,0)="This patch corrects false NDF matching information reported in NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",25,1,3,0)="PTH-0300-20981."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",26,0)="29 SEQ #26^3000417^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",26,1,0)="^^2^2^3000417"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",26,1,1,0)="This patch corrects erroneous entries in the DRUG IDENTIFIER field (#1)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",26,1,2,0)="in the DRUG INGREDIENTS File (#50.416)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",27,0)="28^3000417^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",27,1,0)="^^1^1^3000417"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",27,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",28,0)="30 SEQ #28^3000525^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",28,1,0)="^^3^3^3000525"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",28,1,1,0)="This patch allows printing of the PMIS in two styles."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",28,1,2,0)="See Patch PSN*4*30 in the National Patch Module for description of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",28,1,3,0)="Build."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",29,0)="31^3000525^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",29,1,0)="^^1^1^3000525"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",29,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",30,0)="34^3000626^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",30,1,0)="^^1^1^3000626"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",30,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",31,0)="36^3000717^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",31,1,0)="^^1^1^3000717"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",31,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",32,0)="37^3000816^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",32,1,0)="^^1^1^3000816"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",32,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",33,0)="35 SEQ #33^3000816^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",33,1,0)="^^1^1^3000816"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",33,1,1,0)="This patch corrects the display of erroneous routes."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",34,0)="38^3001004^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",34,1,0)="^^1^1^3001004"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",34,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",35,0)="33 SEQ #35^3001027^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",35,1,0)="^^10^10^3001027"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",35,1,1,0)="These changes are being sent out in preparation for the release of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",35,1,2,0)="Pharmacy Ordering Enhancements patches. The changes in this patch will"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",35,1,3,0)="not affect National Drug File functionality until the Auto Create Dosages"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",35,1,4,0)="[PSS DOSAGE CONVERSION] option that is released with Pharmacy Data"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",35,1,5,0)="Management patch PSS*1*34 is run. After that option is run, dosage"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",35,1,6,0)="information will be created and stored in the DRUG file (#50). Then when"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",35,1,7,0)="drugs are matched through the National Drug File options, the dosage"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",35,1,8,0)="information may need to be automatically updated based on the new National"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",35,1,9,0)="Drug File match. The functionality to update the dosage information is"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",35,1,10,0)="included in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",36,0)="41 SEQ #36^3001106^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",36,1,0)="^^1^1^3001106"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",36,1,1,0)="This patch corrects possibly mis-matched items in the drug file."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",37,0)="40 SEQ #37^3001106^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",37,1,0)="^^1^1^3001106"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",37,1,1,0)="This patch updates dats for PMI sheets."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",38,0)="39^3001106^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",38,1,0)="^^1^1^3001106"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",38,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",39,0)="43 SEQ #39^3010122^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",39,1,0)="^^7^7^3010122"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",39,1,1,0)="This patch restores data that was deleted from the NATIONAL DRUG"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",39,1,2,0)="CLASS field (#25) in the DRUG file (#50)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",39,1,3,0)="It also corrects the ""AND"", ""VAPN"", ""APN"", ""VAC"", and ""AQ1"" cross references"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",39,1,4,0)="in the DRUG file (#50)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",39,1,5,0)="It also verifies that data for the CMOP ID field (#27) and the NATIONAL"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",39,1,6,0)="FORMULARY INDICATOR field (#29) in the DRUG file (#50) are in the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",39,1,7,0)="correct locations."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",40,0)="44 SEQ #40^3010122^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",40,1,0)="^^4^4^3010122"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",40,1,1,0)="This patch unmatches improperly matched drugs."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",40,1,2,0)="This patch also unmarks drugs for CMOP if they are not matched to"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",40,1,3,0)="a VA product or if they are matched to a VA product which is not"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",40,1,4,0)="marked for CMOP."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",41,0)="45 SEQ #41^3010202^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",41,1,0)="^^1^1^3010202"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",41,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for medication instruction sheets."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",42,0)="46^3010202^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",42,1,0)="^^1^1^3010202"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",42,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the National Drug File application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",43,0)="49^3010319^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",43,1,0)="^^1^1^3010319"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",43,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",44,0)="50 SEQ #44^3010319^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",44,1,0)="^^3^3^3010319"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",44,1,1,0)="This patch cleans up data in the DRUG file (#50).  Certain fields were"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",44,1,2,0)="not being properly set when entries were unmatched from National Drug"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",44,1,3,0)="File (NDF) data updates."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",45,0)="48 SEQ #45^3010326^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",45,1,0)="^^2^2^3010326"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",45,1,1,0)="See Patch PSN*4*48 in the National Patch Module for description of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",45,1,2,0)="build."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,0)="47 SEQ #46^3010326^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,0)="^^16^16^3010326"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,1,0)="1. Entries in the local DRUG file (#50) can be matched to the National Drug"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,2,0)="   File VA PRODUCT file (#50.68) by selecting an entry in that file or by"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,3,0)="   selecting an entry from the NDC/UPN file (#50.67). If the entry in either"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,4,0)="   file is inactive, the current dialog is misleading. It appears that a match"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,5,0)="   has been found, but in actuality it does not. This patch will affect the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,6,0)="   following options:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,8,0)="     - The Rematch / Match Single Drugs [PSNDRUG] option in NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,9,0)="     - The Drug Enter/Edit [PSS DRUG ENTER/EDIT] option in Pharmacy Data"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,10,0)="       Management (PDM) as this option calls those routines through"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,11,0)="       supported DBIA # 2080."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,13,0)=" 2. Currently the Inquire to National Files [PSNACT] option, does not"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,14,0)="    display any information regarding the inactivation date of the VA"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,15,0)="    PRODUCT file (#50.68) entries and the NDC/UPN file (#50.67) entries."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",46,1,16,0)="    The display of the inactivation date is now included in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",47,0)="52^3010529^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",47,1,0)="^^1^1^3010529"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",47,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the national drug file application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",48,0)="51 SEQ #48^3010625^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",48,1,0)="^^5^5^3010625"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",48,1,1,0)="This change is being sent out in preparation for the release of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",48,1,2,0)="Pharmacy Ordering Enhancements patches. The change in this patch will"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",48,1,3,0)="populate dosages that are stored in DRUG file (#50) when completing a"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",48,1,4,0)="match in National Drug File (NDF). This data stored in DRUG file (#50)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",48,1,5,0)="comes from the match in NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",49,0)="53^3011016^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",49,1,0)="^^1^1^3011016"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",49,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the National Drug FIle application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",50,0)="55 SEQ #50^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",50,1,0)="^^6^6^3011210"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",50,1,1,0)="When using the Patients on Specific Drug(s) [PSJ PDV] option of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",50,1,2,0)="Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 package for a given VA Class, the generated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",50,1,3,0)="report did not have all drugs included. This was due to bad ""AOC"""
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",50,1,4,0)="cross-reference associated with the VA CLASSIFICATION field (#2) in the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",50,1,5,0)="DRUG file (#50) which is not maintained properly by the National Drug File"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",50,1,6,0)="(NDF) package. This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",51,0)="57^3020204^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",51,1,0)="^^1^1^3020204"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",51,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the National Drug File application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,0)="54 SEQ #52^3020814^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,0)="^^30^30^3020814"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,1,0)="This patch adds a cross-reference to the PRIMARY INGREDIENT field (#2)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,2,0)="in the DRUG INGREDIENTS file (#50.416).  This patch also corrects the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,3,0)="incorrectly set APS cross-reference in that file and the APD cross-"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,4,0)="reference in the DRUG INTERACTION file (#56)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,6,0)="This patch also corrects two problems."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,8,0)=" 1.  Under certain circumstances, the APS cross-reference on the PRIMARY"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,9,0)=" INGREDIENT field (#2) in the DRUG INGREDIENTS file (#50.416) was not"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,10,0)=" being properly set.  This caused the APD cross-reference on the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,11,0)=" INGREDIENT 1 field (#1) and the INGREDIENT 2 field (#2) in the DRUG"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,12,0)=" INTERACTION file (#56) to be improperly set.  Certain interactions"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,13,0)=" were not being properly tracked."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,14,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,15,0)=" This patch corrects that defect.  It also includes a post-install"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,16,0)=" routine to reset existing cross-references."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,17,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,18,0)=" 2.  In the data update patch PSN*4*53, the units for the VA Product"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,19,0)=" INTERFERON BETA-1B,RECOMBINANT 9.6 MILLION UNT/VIL INJ (entry number"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,20,0)=" 11809 in the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68)) was changed.  This should have"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,21,0)=" caused all entries in the DRUG file (#50) matched to that product to"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,22,0)=" be unmatched.  That unmatching did not take place.  This patch causes"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,23,0)=" that unmatching."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,24,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,25,0)="After the patch is installed, the routines PSNJP54 and PSNOP54 should"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,26,0)="be run from programmer mode. These routines will generate list of"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,27,0)="patients who received combinations of drugs which should have caused"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,28,0)="an interaction warning but did not.  These routines MUST be run"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,29,0)="within 60 days of the install of this patch,  Once the routines have"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",52,1,30,0)="been run, they may be deleted."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",53,0)="59 SEQ #53^3020814^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",53,1,0)="^^3^3^3020814"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",53,1,1,0)="Under certain circumstances, the AND cross reference in the DRUG file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",53,1,2,0)="(#50) was not being properly set.  This patch corrects that problem."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",53,1,3,0)="A post-install routine PSN4P59P corrects any existing problems."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,0)="61 SEQ #54^3020906^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,0)="^^26^26^3020906"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,1,0)="Patch PSN*4*54 creates a list of combinations of drug products that should"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,2,0)="have generated an interaction warning but did not. Routine PSNJP54 is"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,3,0)="included in PSN*4*54 to generate a report of patients who may have been at"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,4,0)="risk."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,5,0)="Sites have reported an error that may occur during the execution of this"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,6,0)="report. The code responsible for the potential error may also display"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,7,0)="incorrect schedule types for IV orders. This patch corrects both of these"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,8,0)="issues."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,10,0)="** PSNJP54 must be run within 45 days of the installation of PSN*4*54. **"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,12,0)="Routine PSNJP54 should be run from programmer mode after this patch is"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,13,0)="installed. The user will be prompted for a date to start the search and an"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,14,0)="output format (report or spread sheet).  The default starting date for"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,15,0)="PSNJP54 is 365 days ago. The report produces a list of patients who"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,16,0)="received combinations of drugs that should have generated an interaction"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,17,0)="warning but did not."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,19,0)="On a DSM system with no users and choosing the default start dates,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,20,0)="PSNJP54 ran in about 20 minutes. On a larger system or on a system with"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,21,0)="many users, running time may be longer."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,23,0)="After the report has been reviewed by pharmacy personnel, PSNJP54 may be"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,24,0)="deleted from your system."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",54,1,26,0)="All NOIS associated with this patch are associated with this item."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",55,0)="58^3020906^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",55,1,0)="^^4^4^3020906"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",55,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the National Drug File application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",55,1,2,0)="I also makes changes to the data dictionary for the UNITS multiple"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",55,1,3,0)="field (#8) and the DISPENSE UNITS PER DOSE multiple field (#9) in the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",55,1,4,0)="DOSAGE FORM file (#50.606)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,0)="63 SEQ #56^3020906^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,0)="^^25^25^3020906"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,1,0)="Sites have reported patients' Social Security Numbers display"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,2,0)="incorrectly when running report routine PSNJP54. This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,3,0)="by displaying the proper SSN."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,5,0)="No problems have been reported with PSN*4*54 other than this report"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,6,0)="routine. PSN*4*54 itself is not an emergency patch and its installation"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,7,0)="schedule does not need to be accelerated."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,9,0)="** PSNJP54 must be run within 45 days of the installation of PSN*4*54. **"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,11,0)="Routine PSNJP54 should be run from programmer mode after this patch is"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,12,0)="installed. The user will be prompted for a date to start the search and an"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,13,0)="output format (report or spread sheet).  The default starting date for"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,14,0)="PSNJP54 is 365 days ago. The report produces a list of patients who"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,15,0)="received combinations of drugs that should have generated an interaction"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,16,0)="warning but did not."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,18,0)="On a DSM system with no users and choosing the default start dates,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,19,0)="PSNJP54 ran in about 40 minutes. On a larger system or on a system with"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,20,0)="many users, running time may be longer."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,22,0)="After the report has been reviewed by pharmacy personnel, PSNJP54 may be"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,23,0)="deleted from your system."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",56,1,25,0)="All NOIS associated with this patch are associated with this item."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",57,0)="60 SEQ #57^3021025^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",57,1,0)="^^5^5^3021025"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",57,1,1,0)="HUI/VHA CIO SD&D PHARMACY DATA INTERCHANGE."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",57,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",57,1,3,0)="This Hui/VHA CIO SD&D Pharmacy Data Interchangeproject. The project provides"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",57,1,4,0)="a method for the one-way electronic transferof prescription orders from an "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",57,1,5,0)="external system to VistA."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",58,0)="64^3021108^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",58,1,0)="^^1^1^3021108"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",58,1,1,0)="This patch updates data for the National Drug File application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,0)="66^3021108^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,0)="^^18^18^3021108"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,3,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,4,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,6,0)="This patch generates three mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,7,0)="and all are sent to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,8,0)="PSNMGR security key, and the person installing the patch.  The first"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,9,0)="message, with the subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,10,0)="CMOP ID (if one exists), dispense units, and associated NDCs,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,11,0)="products for which the national formulary indicator has changed,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,12,0)="products that have been unmatched from CMOP, and products for which"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,13,0)="the national formulary restriction has changed.  The second,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,14,0)="with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists interactions that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,15,0)="have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,16,0)="DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the DRUG file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,17,0)="(#50) which have been unmatched from NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",59,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,0)="67^3021220^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,0)="^^18^18^3021220"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,3,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,4,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,6,0)="This patch generates three mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,7,0)="and all are sent to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,8,0)="PSNMGR security key, and the person installing the patch.  The first"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,9,0)="message, with the subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,10,0)="CMOP ID (if one exists), dispense units, and associated NDCs,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,11,0)="products for which the national formulary indicator has changed,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,12,0)="products that have been unmatched from CMOP, and products for which"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,13,0)="the national formulary restriction has changed.  The second,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,14,0)="with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists interactions that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,15,0)="have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,16,0)="DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the DRUG file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,17,0)="(#50) which have been unmatched from NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",60,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",61,0)="62 SEQ #61^3030301^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",61,1,0)="^^6^6^3030301"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",61,1,1,0)="This patch installs new software and data dictionaries to print Patient"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",61,1,2,0)="Medication Information Sheets (PMIs). It will delete the present file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",61,1,3,0)="MEDICATION INSTRUCTION SHEETS (#54.7) stored in the global PSPPI. The"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",61,1,4,0)="new files are stored in the PS global and the seven new file numbers"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",61,1,5,0)="range from ^PS(50.621 - ^PS(50.627. The new data source is First Data"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",61,1,6,0)="Bank."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",62,0)="68 SEQ #62^3030417^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",62,1,0)="^^4^4^3030417"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",62,1,1,0)="In support of the Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0 laser labels enhancement a "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",62,1,2,0)="new Application Program Interface (API) was created. National Drug File "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",62,1,3,0)="V. 4.0 will supply the Patient Medication Information (PMI) data in ^TMP "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",62,1,4,0)="for use in printing on laser labels. This patch supplies this API."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",63,0)="20 SEQ #63^3030603^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",63,1,0)="^^10^10^3030603"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",63,1,1,0)="This patch changes the read access for four files associated with the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",63,1,2,0)="National Drug File application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",63,1,3,0)=" VA GENERIC file (#50.6)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",63,1,4,0)=" VA DISPENSE UNIT file (#50.64)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",63,1,5,0)=" NDC/UPN file (#50.67)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",63,1,6,0)=" VA PRODUCT file (#50.68)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",63,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",63,1,8,0)="These files were originally sent with a read access of @.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",63,1,9,0)="changes the read access to Pp which is similar to that found on other"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",63,1,10,0)="pharmacy files."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,0)="69 SEQ #64^3030628^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,0)="^^14^14^3030628"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,1,0)=" 1  This patch installs a new field in the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,2,0)=" The new field (#23) is named EXCLUDE DRG-DRG INTERACTION CK and is"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,3,0)=" defined as a set of codes. This field will be used in pharmacy order"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,4,0)=" checking to bypass drug-drug interaction checking on specific VA"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,5,0)=" Products IN THE FUTURE. This patch does not populate the new field."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,7,0)=" 2.  Under certain circumstances if an entry in the VA PRODUCT file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,8,0)=" (#50.68) was unmarked for CMOP, entries in the DRUG file (#50) matched"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,9,0)=" to that item were not unmarked.  The post-install routine for this"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,10,0)=" patch, PSN4P69P, corrects that problem."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,11,0)=" The post-install routine creates a mail message from NDF MANAGER with"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,12,0)=" the subject DRUGS UNMARKED FOR CMOP which lists the items which were"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,13,0)=" unmarked.  That message is sent to the mail group NDF DATA, holders of"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",64,1,14,0)=" the PSNMGR security key, and the person installing the patch."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",65,0)="71^3030628^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",65,1,0)="^^18^18^3030628"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",65,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",65,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",65,1,3,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",65,1,4,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
