^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,3,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,4,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,6,0)="This patch generates three mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,7,0)="and all are sent to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,8,0)="PSNMGR security key, and the person installing the patch.  The first"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,9,0)="message, with the subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,10,0)="CMOP ID (if one exists), dispense units, and associated NDCs,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,11,0)="products for which the national formulary indicator has changed,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,12,0)="products that have been unmatched from CMOP, and products for which"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,13,0)="the national formulary restriction has changed.  The second,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,14,0)="with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists interactions that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,15,0)="have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,16,0)="DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the DRUG file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,17,0)="(#50) which have been unmatched from NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",67,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,0)="65 SEQ #68^3030802^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,0)="^^55^55^3030802"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,1,0)="Pharmacy Benefits Management (PBM) Strategic Healthcare Group in"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,2,0)="collaboration with the Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA), requested"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,3,0)="the development of the first Public Key Infrastructure (PKI) VistA pilot"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,4,0)="project, named Electronic Prescription Order Entry for Schedule II"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,5,0)="Controlled Substances. The objective is to develop an electronic order"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,6,0)="entry system for Schedule II controlled substances using digital"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,7,0)="signatures. To make this project viable, modifications to the following"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,8,0)="packages were identified:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,9,0)="National Drug File (NDF) V. 4.0"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,10,0)="Kernel V. 8.0"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,11,0)="Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,12,0)="Pharmacy Data Management (PDM) V. 1.0"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,13,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy (OP) V. 7.0"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,14,0)="Controlled Substances (CS) V. 3.0"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,16,0)="The National Drug File data update patches PSN*4*64 and PSN*4*66 assign a"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,17,0)="CS Federal Schedule to controlled substances and identify controlled"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,18,0)="substances as narcotics or non-narcotics by populating the CS FEDERAL"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,19,0)="SCHEDULE field (#19) of the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,21,0)="This is the NDF patch that provides the following new functionalities:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,23,0)="1. This patch includes the Data Dictionary (DD) changes for CS FEDERAL"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,24,0)="SCHEDULE field (#19) of the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,26,0)="2. When using the Merge National Drug File Data Into Local File"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,27,0)="[PSNMRG] option, the software will now check to see if the CS FEDERAL"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,28,0)="SCHEDULE field (#19) of the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68) has data and the DEA,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,29,0)="SPECIAL HDLG field (#3) of the DRUG file (#50) does not have data. If both"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,30,0)="are true, then the DEA, SPECIAL HDLG field will be populated with the CS"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,31,0)="FEDERAL SCHEDULE code mapped to the corresponding DEA, SPECIAL HDLG code"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,32,0)="using the following table:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,34,0)="                         CS FEDERAL SCHEDULE     DEA, SPECIAL HDLG Code"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,35,0)="Schedule I narcotics            1                        1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,36,0)="Schedule II narcotics           2                       2A"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,37,0)="Schedule II non-narcotics      2n                       2C"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,38,0)="Schedule III narcotics          3                       3A"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,39,0)="Schedule III non-narcotics     3n                       3C"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,40,0)="Schedule IV narcotics           4                        4"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,41,0)="Schedule V narcotics            5                        5"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,43,0)="3. This patch ensures that the newly populated CS FEDERAL SCHEDULE field"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,44,0)="(#19) of the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68) is also included as part of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,45,0)="National Drug file details in Inquire to National Files [PSNACT], NDF"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,46,0)="Info From Your Local Drug File [PSNRPT], Verify Matches [PSNVFY] and"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,47,0)="Verify Single Match [PSNVER] options."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,49,0)="4. When using Rematch / Match Single Drugs [PSNDRUG] option, if the CS"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,50,0)="FEDERAL SCHEDULE field (#19) of the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68) and the DEA"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,51,0)="SPECIAL HDLG field (#3) of the DRUG file (#50) have a discrepancy, then"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,52,0)="this patch displays a warning message, ""The CS Federal Schedule associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,53,0)="with this drug in the VA Product file represents a DEA, Special Handling"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,54,0)="code of XX"", where XX is the CS FEDERAL SCHEDULE code mapped to the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",68,1,55,0)="corresponding DEA SPECIAL HDLG code using the table listed under item 2."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",69,0)="70 SEQ #69^3030912^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",69,1,0)="^^5^5^3030912"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",69,1,1,0)="This Build builds on the foundation to identify VA Products from the VA"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",69,1,2,0)="PRODUCT file (#50.68) as EXCLUDE from drug-drug interaction checking."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",69,1,3,0)="Two new menu options are included to print marked VA Products. Two existing"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",69,1,4,0)="options have been enhanced to display the new field to the user. A enhanced"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",69,1,5,0)="API routine PSNAPIS is also included."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,0)="74^3031023^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,0)="^^18^18^3031023"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,3,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,4,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,6,0)="This patch generates three mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,7,0)="and all are sent to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,8,0)="PSNMGR security key, and the person installing the patch.  The first"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,9,0)="message, with the subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,10,0)="CMOP ID (if one exists), dispense units, and associated NDCs,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,11,0)="products for which the national formulary indicator has changed,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,12,0)="products that have been unmatched from CMOP, and products for which"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,13,0)="the national formulary restriction has changed.  The second,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,14,0)="with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists interactions that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,15,0)="have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,16,0)="DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the DRUG file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,17,0)="(#50) which have been unmatched from NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",70,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",71,0)="77 SEQ #71^3031023^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",71,1,0)="^^1^1^3031023"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",71,1,1,0)="Re-index the APD cross reference in File 56."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",72,0)="75 SEQ #72^3040131^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",72,1,0)="^^10^10^3040131"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",72,1,1,0)=" This patch lays the foundation for future Patient Medication Information"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",72,1,2,0)=" Sheets (PMI) data updates. It creates the Delete Patient Medication"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",72,1,3,0)=" Information Sheets [PSNDELTE] option.This new stand-alone option should"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",72,1,4,0)=" only be used as part of future Patient Medication Information Sheet update"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",72,1,5,0)=" patches. Because it deletes ALL PMI related DATA files, it should not be"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",72,1,6,0)=" used at any other time."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",72,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",72,1,8,0)=" IMPORTANT: Do NOT use this option until instructed to do so in future PMI"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",72,1,9,0)=" Update patches."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",72,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,0)="76 SEQ #73^3040131^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,0)="^^15^15^3040131"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,1,0)="It is imperative that you follow the proper sequence of loading and"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,2,0)="installing this patch along with the new global file. If not done in the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,3,0)="correct sequence, errors could occur when attempting to print Patient"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,4,0)="Medication Information (PMI) Sheets."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,8,0)="This patch requires patches PSN*4*74 and PSN*4*75. This patch is required"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,9,0)="to provide updates to data in several files in order to print the latest"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,10,0)="Patient Medication Information Sheets. This patch will reset fields"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,11,0)="in the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68). These fields are GCNSEQNO field (#11),"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,12,0)="PREVIOUS GCNSEQNO field (#12), and NDC LINK TO GCNSEQNO field (#13). This"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,13,0)="is accomplished by data stored in a transport global included in this"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,14,0)="patch. The source for the Patient Medication Information (PMI) Sheet data"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",73,1,15,0)="is First Data Bank."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",74,0)="78 SEQ #74^3040131^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",74,1,0)="^^7^7^3040131"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",74,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",74,1,2,0)="Under certain conditions, if a National Drug File (NDF) data update patch"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",74,1,3,0)="deleted an ingredient from an entry in the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68),"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",74,1,4,0)="cross-references in the DRUG INTERACTION file (#56) for other"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",74,1,5,0)="ingredients in that product were inappropriately deleted.  Patch"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",74,1,6,0)="PSN*4*77 corrected existing problems.  This patch will prevent further"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",74,1,7,0)="occurrences."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,0)="79^3040131^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,0)="^^16^16^3040131"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,3,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,5,0)="This patch generates three mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,6,0)="and all are sent to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,7,0)="PSNMGR security key, and the person installing the patch.  The first"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,8,0)="message, with the subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,9,0)="CMOP ID (if one exists), dispense units, and associated NDCs,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,10,0)="products for which the national formulary indicator has changed,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,11,0)="products that have been unmatched from CMOP, and products for which"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,12,0)="the national formulary restriction has changed.  The second,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,13,0)="with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists interactions that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,14,0)="have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,15,0)="DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the DRUG file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",75,1,16,0)="(#50) which have been unmatched from NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",76,0)="83 SEQ #76^3040427^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",76,1,0)="^^1^1^3040427"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",76,1,1,0)="Re-index the APD cross reference in File 56."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,0)="81^3040802^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,0)="^^29^29^3040802"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,3,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,4,0)="Not all the data elements entered for patch PSN*4*79 were transmitted"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,5,0)="to the sites.  This patch corrects that deficiency.  It also corrects the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,6,0)="interaction problem reported in NOIS HWH-0204-41872 and the matching"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,7,0)="problem reported in NOIS PTH-0204-21559 and TUA-0204-30133."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,9,0)="This patch generates three mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,10,0)="and are sent to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,11,0)="PSNMGR security key, and the person installing the patch.  The first"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,12,0)="message, with the subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,13,0)="CMOP ID (if one exists), dispense units, and associated NDCs.  The second,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,14,0)="with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists interactions that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,15,0)="have been added, edited, or inactivated.  The third, with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,16,0)="MISSING INTERACTIONS, lists items that were added in patch PSN*4*79"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,17,0)="for which an interaction warning should have been triggered but was not."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,18,0)="It also lists the interactions.  The message with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,19,0)="DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE is not generated by this patch"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,20,0)="since none of the data elements in this patch cause entries in the "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,21,0)="DRUG file (#50) to be unmatched from NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,23,0)="This patch also creates ^XTMP(""PSNINT"") that contains a list of"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,24,0)="combinations of products that should have generated an interaction"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,25,0)="warning but did not.  The size of ^XTMP(""PSNINT) is about 120 DSM blocks."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,27,0)="A subsequent patch will be created which will data in ^XTMP to generate"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,28,0)="lists of patients who had received combinations of orders which should"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",77,1,29,0)="have caused an interaction warning but did not."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",78,0)="82 SEQ #78^3040802^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",78,1,0)="^^2^2^3040802"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",78,1,1,0)="THIS PATCH WILL CORRECT THE PROBLEM OF INGREDIENTS NOT DISPLAYING DURING "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",78,1,2,0)="THE VERIFY PROCESS."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,0)="85^3040903^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,0)="^^16^16^3040903"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,3,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,5,0)="This patch generates three mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,6,0)="and all are sent to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,7,0)="PSNMGR security key, and the person installing the patch.  The first"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,8,0)="message, with the subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,9,0)="CMOP ID (if one exists), dispense units, and associated NDCs,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,10,0)="products for which the national formulary indicator has changed,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,11,0)="products that have been unmatched from CMOP, and products for which"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,12,0)="the national formulary restriction has changed.  The second,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,13,0)="with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists interactions that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,14,0)="have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,15,0)="DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the DRUG file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",79,1,16,0)="(#50) which have been unmatched from NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,0)="86^3040903^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,0)="^^16^16^3040903"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,3,0)="with the Patient Medication Instruction Sheet (PMI) portion of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,4,0)="National Drug File (NDF) application.  The seven files are:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,5,0)="   50.621        PMI-ENGLISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,6,0)="   50.622        PMI-SPANISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,7,0)="   50.623        PMI MAP-ENGLISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,8,0)="   50.624        PMI MAP-SPANISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,9,0)="   50.625        WARNING LABEL-ENGLISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,10,0)="   50.626        WARNING LABEL-SPANISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,11,0)="   50.627        WARNING LABEL MAP     "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,13,0)="The post-install routine for this patch, PSN4P86P, deletes existing"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,14,0)="entries in these files, loads the new data, and rematches entries in"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,15,0)="the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68) to the proper PMIs."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",80,1,16,0)="The source of the data for the PMIs is First Data Bank."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,0)="87^3040903^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,0)="^^16^16^3040903"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,3,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,5,0)="This patch generates three mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,6,0)="and all are sent to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,7,0)="PSNMGR security key, and the person installing the patch.  The first"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,8,0)="message, with the subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,9,0)="CMOP ID (if one exists), dispense units, and associated NDCs,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,10,0)="products for which the national formulary indicator has changed,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,11,0)="products that have been unmatched from CMOP, and products for which"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,12,0)="the national formulary restriction has changed.  The second,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,13,0)="with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists interactions that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,14,0)="have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,15,0)="DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the DRUG file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",81,1,16,0)="(#50) which have been unmatched from NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,0)="84 SEQ #82^3041029^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,0)="^^44^44^3041029"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,1,0)=" **********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,2,0)=" *   This patch is part of the Outpatient Pharmacy Automated Dispense *"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,3,0)=" *           Project and must be installed at all sites by            *"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,4,0)=" *                          December 31, 2004                         *"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,5,0)=" *                                                                    *"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,6,0)=" *      Please review the Installation heading of this patch for      *"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,7,0)=" *              Installation Guide retrieval information              *"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,8,0)=" *                                                                    *"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,9,0)=" **********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,10,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,11,0)=" There are three patches that support the Outpatient Pharmacy Automation"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,12,0)=" Interface project. These patches should be installed separately in the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,13,0)=" following order:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,14,0)="                   PSO*7*156      Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,15,0)="                   PSS*1*82       Pharmacy Data Management"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,16,0)="                   PSN*4*84       National Drug File"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,18,0)=" They contain routines, templates, options, and data dictionary changes to"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,19,0)=" implement the Outpatient Pharmacy Automation Interface features. Please"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,20,0)=" refer to the individual patch description of the other patches to get the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,21,0)=" names of the documentation files."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,23,0)=" Each patch will share the same starting description with more detail"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,24,0)=" for each patch in the corresponding namespace patch number.  There is"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,25,0)=" only one installation guide.  It can be found on the anonymous "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,26,0)=" directory.  The name of the installation guide is PSO_7_P156_IG.PDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,28,0)=" The patch enhances the current Health Level Seven (HL7) interface to"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,29,0)=" ensure that the interface is compatible with all current Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,30,0)=" Pharmacy V. 7.0 automation systems used by the Veterans Affairs"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,31,0)=" Medical Centers (VAMCs).  The current national VISTA HL7 interface is"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,32,0)=" written to HL7 standard V. 2.2.  Automated dispensing systems, such as"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,33,0)=" the Baker APS Pharmacy 2000, are currently using an interface written to"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,34,0)=" V. 2.3.1. standard using locally developed software.  The automated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,35,0)=" dispensing systems have committed to be HL7 V. 2.4 compliant."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,37,0)=" This patch includes the following new features:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,38,0)=" 1.  Enhance the current National Drug File V. 1.0 package HL7 interface"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,39,0)="     to the current HL7 V. 2.4 standard."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,41,0)=" 2.  The interface transmits drug data to multiple vendor systems"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,42,0)="     utilized by VAMCs whenever the following options are selected:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,43,0)="     A.  Rematch / Match Single Drugs [PSNDRUG] option."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",82,1,44,0)="     B.  Merge National Drug File Data Into Local File [PSNMRG] option."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,0)="80 SEQ #83^3041029^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,0)="^^27^27^3041029"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,1,0)="This patch contains Application Program Interface's (API's) that will"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,2,0)="be used by calling applications that currently do direct global reads or"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,3,0)="writes to the National Drug File (NDF) files. Since the VA GENERIC file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,4,0)="(#50.6), and other NDF-related files are being replaced by a vendor"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,5,0)="product, any direct M-based global reads or writes to these files must be"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,6,0)="replaced by calling the API's provided in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,8,0)="When the new data source is in place, the calling applications will not "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,9,0)="be required to make any changes, because these API's will be flexible "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,10,0)="enough to retrieve the requested data from the vendor product, when the "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,11,0)="time comes."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,13,0)="These are the files that are affected. If any application is making "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,14,0)="direct global reads or writes to any of these files, they must be "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,15,0)="replaced by using the API's exported with this patch."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,17,0)="File Name:                 File Number:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,18,0)="DRUG INGREDIENTS           50.416"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,19,0)="VA GENERIC                 50.6"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,20,0)="VA DRUG CLASS              50.605"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,21,0)="DRUG UNITS                 50.607"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,22,0)="NATIONAL DRUG TRANSLATION  50.612"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,23,0)="WARNING LABEL-ENGLISH      50.625"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,24,0)="WARNING LABEL-SPANISH      50.626"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,25,0)="WARNING LABEL MAP          50.627"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,26,0)="VA PRODUCT                 50.68"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",83,1,27,0)="DRUG INTERACTION           56"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,0)="90^3041124^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,0)="^^16^16^3041124"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,3,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,5,0)="This patch generates three mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,6,0)="and all are sent to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,7,0)="PSNMGR security key, and the person installing the patch.  The first"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,8,0)="message, with the subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,9,0)="CMOP ID (if one exists), dispense units, and associated NDCs,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,10,0)="products for which the national formulary indicator has changed,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,11,0)="products that have been unmatched from CMOP, and products for which"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,12,0)="the national formulary restriction has changed.  The second,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,13,0)="with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists interactions that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,14,0)="have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,15,0)="DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the DRUG file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",84,1,16,0)="(#50) which have been unmatched from NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,0)="94 SEQ #86^3041228^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,0)="^^13^13^3041228"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,1,0)="This patch contains updated Application Program Interfaces (APIs) that "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,2,0)="will be used by calling applications that currently do direct global "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,3,0)="reads or writes to the National Drug File files.  A review of the "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,4,0)="previously released APIs showed several entry points where additional "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,5,0)="pieces of data were required to be returned."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,7,0)="If you have already made code modifications, or have made plans to make"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,8,0)="code modifications to use any of the new APIs, please check the latest"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,9,0)="version of the API manual to verify that the API(s) in question have an"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,10,0)="Active status. The API manual has been modified since the original version"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,11,0)="to indicate Active and Inactive APIs. If the API(s) you need have an"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,12,0)="Inactive status, please contact the Pharmacy Re-Engineering team at the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",85,1,13,0)="Birmingham Field Office."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",86,0)="93 SEQ #85^3041228^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",86,1,0)="^^2^2^3041228"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",86,1,1,0)="This patch fixes the undefined error reported in NOIS ISH-1004-41307 when"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",86,1,2,0)="using the Rematch / Match Single Drugs [PSNDRUG] option."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",87,0)="88 SEQ #87^3050311^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",87,1,0)="^^7^7^3050311"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",87,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",87,1,2,0)="Certain of the warning labels associated with the Patient Medication"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",87,1,3,0)="Instruction Sheet (PMI) portion of the National Drug File (NDF) application"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",87,1,4,0)="are gender specific.  This patch adds a new field, SPECIFIC TO GENDER (#2),"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",87,1,5,0)="to files WARNING LABEL-ENGLISH (#50.625) and WARNING LABEL-SPANISH (#50.626)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",87,1,6,0)="These fields are populated with the release of PMI updates."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",87,1,7,0)="The source of the data in these fields is First Data Bank."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",88,0)="92 SEQ #88^3050311^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",88,1,0)="^^4^4^3050311"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",88,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",88,1,2,0)="Under certain circumstances the matching process aborted with an undefined"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",88,1,3,0)="error.  Specifically, this error would occur when tying to match to a"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",88,1,4,0)="VA Product that began with a number.  This patch corrects that problem."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,0)="89 SEQ #89^3050311^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,0)="^^24^24^3050311"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,2,0)="1. Under certain circumstances the APD cross-reference in the DRUG"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,3,0)="INGREDIENT file (#50.416) was not being properly set.  This patch remedies"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,4,0)="that defect and creates those entries which were not properly set in the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,5,0)="past."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,7,0)="2. It has been noted that some sites have made local entries to the DRUG"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,8,0)="INGREDIENT file.  This should not have been done.  While this was not the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,9,0)="proximal cause of the problem noted in item 1, it may have exacerbated the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,10,0)="problem.  Some of these locally added ingredients may have been"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,11,0)="overwritten by nationally entered ingredients."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,12,0)="This patch modifies the data dictionary of this file so that local"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,13,0)="entries can no longer be made."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,15,0)="3. It has also been noted that over 1250 entries in the DRUG INTERACTION"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,16,0)="file (#56) involving these locally added ingredients have been added."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,17,0)="If the locally added ingredients have been overwritten, these interactions"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,18,0)="will be interactions involving the national ingredients."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,20,0)="Sites are strongly urged to review locally added interactions to verify"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,21,0)="that they have not been changed.  Sites are also strongly urged to"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,22,0)="inactivate any interactions involving local ingredients.  Finally, sites"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,23,0)="are urged to review any allergies entered for drug ingredients to verify"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",89,1,24,0)="that they have not been changed."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,0)="95^3050506^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,0)="^^16^16^3050506"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,3,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,5,0)="This patch generates three mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,6,0)="and all are sent to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,7,0)="PSNMGR security key, and the person installing the patch.  The first"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,8,0)="message, with the subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,9,0)="CMOP ID (if one exists), dispense units, and associated NDCs,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,10,0)="products for which the national formulary indicator has changed,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,11,0)="products that have been unmatched from CMOP, and products for which"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,12,0)="the national formulary restriction has changed.  The second,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,13,0)="with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists interactions that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,14,0)="have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,15,0)="DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the DRUG file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",90,1,16,0)="(#50) which have been unmatched from NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,0)="97^3050506^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,0)="^^16^16^3050506"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,3,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,5,0)="This patch generates three mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,6,0)="and all are sent to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,7,0)="PSNMGR security key, and the person installing the patch.  The first"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,8,0)="message, with the subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,9,0)="CMOP ID (if one exists), dispense units, and associated NDCs,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,10,0)="products for which the national formulary indicator has changed,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,11,0)="products that have been unmatched from CMOP, and products for which"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,12,0)="the national formulary restriction has changed.  The second,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,13,0)="with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists interactions that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,14,0)="have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,15,0)="DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the DRUG file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",91,1,16,0)="(#50) which have been unmatched from NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,0)="99 SEQ #92^3050506^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,0)="^^39^39^3050506"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,3,0)=" IMPORTANT"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,4,0)=" This patch must be installed immediately after patch PSN*4*95 and PSN*4*97 "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,5,0)=" are installed. All three patches should be installed at the same time and "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,6,0)=" in sequence."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,8,0)=" The names of several entries in the VA DRUG CLASS file (#50.605) have been"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,9,0)=" changed.  Other entries in this file have been inactivated and replaced"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,10,0)=" with new entries.  This patch makes corrections to several files in multiple"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,11,0)=" applications that use the VA DRUG CLASS file (#50.605)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,13,0)=" The patch will correct entries in the DRUG file (#50) so that the VA "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,14,0)=" CLASSIFICATION field (2) matches the entry in the NATIONAL DRUG CLASS "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,15,0)=" field (#25)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,16,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,17,0)=" The patch also updates pointers in the PATIENT ALLERGIES file (#120.8),"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,18,0)=" the GMR ALLERGIES file (#120.82) so that allergy relationships created prior"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,19,0)=" to the NDF DATA Update PSN*4*95 continue to function correctly and display"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,20,0)=" warnings appropriately."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,22,0)=" The patch updates the FH SITE PARAMETERS file (#119.9). Entries in the "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,23,0)=" DRUG CLASSIFICATIONS field (85) will be updated so that they link to the "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,24,0)=" appropriate entry in the VA DRUG CLASS file (50.605) after installation of"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,25,0)=" the NDF Data Update PSN*4*97."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,28,0)=" The patch updates the REMINDER EXTRACT SUMMARY file (#810.3), the REMINDER "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,29,0)=" TERM file (#811.5), and the REMINDER DEFINITION file (#811.9).  Changes in"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,30,0)=" PSN*4*99 ensure that relationships created prior to installation of the NDF "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,31,0)=" Data Update Patch PSN*4*95 continue to function appropriately after "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,32,0)=" installation of the NDF Data Update patch PSN*4*97."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,33,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,34,0)=" This patch generates a mail message with the subject DRUG CLASS CHANGES"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,35,0)=" from NDF MANAGER.  This message lists drugs for which the class was changed"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,36,0)=" and the old class and the new class.  This message is delivered to members"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,37,0)=" of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the PSNMGR security key, and the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,38,0)=" person installing the patch."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",92,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,0)="98^3050625^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,0)="^^16^16^3050625"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,3,0)="with the Patient Medication Instruction Sheet (PMI) portion of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,4,0)="National Drug File (NDF) application.  The seven files are:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,5,0)="   50.621        PMI-ENGLISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,6,0)="   50.622        PMI-SPANISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,7,0)="   50.623        PMI MAP-ENGLISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,8,0)="   50.624        PMI MAP-SPANISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,9,0)="   50.625        WARNING LABEL-ENGLISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,10,0)="   50.626        WARNING LABEL-SPANISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,11,0)="   50.627        WARNING LABEL MAP     "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,13,0)="The post-install routine for this patch, PSN4P98P, deletes existing"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,14,0)="entries in these files, loads the new data, and rematches entries in"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,15,0)="the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68) to the proper PMIs."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",93,1,16,0)="The source of the data for the PMIs is First Data Bank."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",94,0)="101^3050813^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",94,1,0)="^^1^1^3050813"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",94,1,1,0)="This Build contains patch PSN*4*101 which is Pharmacy Data Standardization."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",95,0)="104 SEQ #95^3050813^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",95,1,0)="^^4^4^3050813"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",95,1,1,0)="This patch will modify the DATA component of DBIA 4545, which returns data"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",95,1,2,0)="from the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68). Added to the output will be the VA"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",95,1,3,0)="GENERIC NAME field (#.05) of the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68), along with the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",95,1,4,0)="NAME field (#.01) of that VA GENERIC file (#50.6) entry."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,0)="109 SEQ #96^3060308^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,0)="^^16^16^3060308"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,1,0)="This patch will contain enhancements to the cycle 1 encapsulation APIs."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,3,0)="A new API is added with this patch that returns information from the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,4,0)="NDC/UPN file (#50.67). See DBIA 4829 for complete information."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,6,0)="A new field has been added to the return data of DATA^PSN50P68 component "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,7,0)="of DBIA 4545. It is the SERVICE CODE field (#2000) of the VA PRODUCT file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,8,0)="(#50.68). The field is being sent out in National Drug File patch"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,9,0)="PSN*4*103."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,11,0)="A change has been made to the DIC^PSNDI and IX^PSNDI components of DBIA "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,12,0)="4554. DIC(""S"") will be killed within these components. If the file you "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,13,0)="are passing in has an Inactivation Date field, and you want to screen on "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,14,0)="that field, a new date input parameter is being added to the components, "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,15,0)="and if a date is passed in, a screen will be set for the calling "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",96,1,16,0)="application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,0)="105^3060308^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,0)="^^16^16^3060308"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,3,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,5,0)="This patch generates three mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,6,0)="and all are sent to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,7,0)="PSNMGR security key, and the person installing the patch.  The first"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,8,0)="message, with the subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,9,0)="CMOP ID (if one exists), dispense units, and associated NDCs,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,10,0)="products for which the national formulary indicator has changed,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,11,0)="products that have been unmatched from CMOP, and products for which"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,12,0)="the national formulary restriction has changed.  The second,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,13,0)="with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists interactions that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,14,0)="have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,15,0)="DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the DRUG file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",97,1,16,0)="(#50) which have been unmatched from NDF."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,0)="106^3060308^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,1,0)="^^16^16^3060308"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,1,3,0)="with the Patient Medication Instruction Sheet (PMI) portion of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,1,4,0)="National Drug File (NDF) application.  The seven files are:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,1,5,0)="   50.621        PMI-ENGLISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,1,6,0)="   50.622        PMI-SPANISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,1,7,0)="   50.623        PMI MAP-ENGLISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,1,8,0)="   50.624        PMI MAP-SPANISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,1,9,0)="   50.625        WARNING LABEL-ENGLISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,1,10,0)="   50.626        WARNING LABEL-SPANISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,1,11,0)="   50.627        WARNING LABEL MAP     "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",98,1,12,0)=" "
