^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",123,1,7,0)="subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products, CMOP ID (if one exists),"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",123,1,8,0)="dispense units, and associated NDCs, products for which the national"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",123,1,9,0)="formulary indicator has changed, products that have been unmatched from"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",123,1,10,0)="CMOP, and products for which the national formulary restriction has"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",123,1,11,0)="changed.  The second, with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",123,1,12,0)="interactions that have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",123,1,13,0)="the subject DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",123,1,14,0)="DRUG file (#50) which have been unmatched from NDF.  The fourth, with the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",123,1,15,0)="subject INTERACTIONS and ALLERGIES UPDATED, lists interactions and allergies"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",123,1,16,0)="which have been changed because they were created with ingredients that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",123,1,17,0)="are no longer primary ingredients."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",124,0)="137 SEQ #126^3070904.233946^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",124,1,0)="^^6^6^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",124,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",124,1,2,0)="The ""T"" cross reference on the TRADE NAME field (#4) in the NDC/UPN file"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",124,1,3,0)="(#50.67) currently stores only the first thirty characters of the field."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",124,1,4,0)="Developers of the ADVERSE REACTION TRACKING application have requested"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",124,1,5,0)="that this cross reference store the entire field.  This patch accomplishes"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",124,1,6,0)="that change."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,0)="134 SEQ #127^3070904.234752^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,0)="^^13^13^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,2,0)="The option Enter/Edit Local Drug Interaction [PSS INTERACTION LOCAL ADD]"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,3,0)="allows sites to make local entries in the DRUG INTERACTION file (#56)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,4,0)="When this option is invoked a message is sent to the mail group"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,5,0)="G.NDF SUPPORT@ISCPNDF.ISC-BIRM.DOMAIN.EXT.  During the period 26 October 2006"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,6,0)="through 27 February 2007, a problem with the network configuration caused"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,7,0)="these messages not to be transmitted.  This problem has been corrected."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,8,0)="This patch transmits a list of all interactions that were entered locally"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,9,0)="during that time period.  That list is also send to members of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,10,0)="NDF DATA mail group, holders of the PSNMGR security key, and the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,11,0)="installer of the patch."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,12,0)="NOTE: The message is not sent across the network from a test account.  It"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",125,1,13,0)="is sent only to local recipients."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",126,0)="141 SEQ #128^3070904.235926^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",126,1,0)="^^3^3^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",126,1,1,0)="The words information and page in the header of patient medication"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",126,1,2,0)="instruction sheets (PMIs) contain improper characters when printed in"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",126,1,3,0)="Spanish.  This patch corrects that defect."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",127,0)="138^3070905.000156^1"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",127,1,0)="^^17^17^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",127,1,1,0)=" "
