^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",165,1,11,0)="changed.  The second, with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",165,1,12,0)="interactions that have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",165,1,13,0)="the subject DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",165,1,14,0)="DRUG file (#50) which have been unmatched from NDF.  The fourth, with the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",165,1,15,0)="subject INTERACTIONS and ALLERGIES UPDATED, lists interactions and allergies"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",165,1,16,0)="which have been changed because they were created with ingredients that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",165,1,17,0)="are no longer primary ingredients."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,0)="180^3090421.161232^17"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,0)="^^18^18^3090421"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,3,0)="with the Patient Medication Instruction Sheet (PMI) portion of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,4,0)="National Drug File (NDF) application.  The seven files are:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,5,0)="   50.621        PMI-ENGLISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,6,0)="   50.622        PMI-SPANISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,7,0)="   50.623        PMI MAP-ENGLISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,8,0)="   50.624        PMI MAP-SPANISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,9,0)="   50.625        WARNING LABEL-ENGLISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,10,0)="   50.626        WARNING LABEL-SPANISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,11,0)="   50.627        WARNING LABEL MAP     "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,13,0)="The environment check routine for this patch checks to see that the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,14,0)="installer is a valid user."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,15,0)="The post-install routine for this patch deletes existing entries in these"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,16,0)="files, loads the new data, and rematches entries in the VA PRODUCT file "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,17,0)="(#50.68) to the proper PMIs."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",166,1,18,0)="The source of the data for the PMIs is First Data Bank."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,0)="182^3090422.114558^17"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,0)="^^17^17^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,3,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,4,0)="This patch generates four mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,5,0)="to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the PSNMGR security "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,6,0)="key, and the person installing the patch.  The first message, with the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,7,0)="subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products, CMOP ID (if one exists),"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,8,0)="dispense units, and associated NDCs, products for which the national"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,9,0)="formulary indicator has changed, products that have been unmatched from"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,10,0)="CMOP, and products for which the national formulary restriction has"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,11,0)="changed.  The second, with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,12,0)="interactions that have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,13,0)="the subject DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,14,0)="DRUG file (#50) which have been unmatched from NDF.  The fourth, with the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,15,0)="subject INTERACTIONS and ALLERGIES UPDATED, lists interactions and allergies"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,16,0)="which have been changed because they were created with ingredients that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",167,1,17,0)="are no longer primary ingredients."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,0)="183^3090422.115137^17"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,0)="^^18^18^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,3,0)="with the Patient Medication Instruction Sheet (PMI) portion of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,4,0)="National Drug File (NDF) application.  The seven files are:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,5,0)="   50.621        PMI-ENGLISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,6,0)="   50.622        PMI-SPANISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,7,0)="   50.623        PMI MAP-ENGLISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,8,0)="   50.624        PMI MAP-SPANISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,9,0)="   50.625        WARNING LABEL-ENGLISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,10,0)="   50.626        WARNING LABEL-SPANISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,11,0)="   50.627        WARNING LABEL MAP     "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,13,0)="The environment check routine for this patch checks to see that the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,14,0)="installer is a valid user."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,15,0)="The post-install routine for this patch deletes existing entries in these"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,16,0)="files, loads the new data, and rematches entries in the VA PRODUCT file "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,17,0)="(#50.68) to the proper PMIs."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",168,1,18,0)="The source of the data for the PMIs is First Data Bank."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",169,0)="176 SEQ #169^3090422.122058^17"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",169,1,0)="^^11^11^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",169,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",169,1,2,0)="This patch creates a protocol, PSN NEW CLASS, which will be invoked during a"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",169,1,3,0)="data update if any entries in the VA PRODUCT file (#50.68) have"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",169,1,4,0)="been assigned a new VA DRUG CLASS."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",169,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",169,1,6,0)="The protocol will be used to update ancillary applications when a change"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",169,1,7,0)="is made to the VA Drug Class assigned to a VA Product."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",169,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",169,1,9,0)="The protocol also sends a message titled ""Products with changed classes"" to"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",169,1,10,0)="holders of the PSNMGR key, members of the NDF DATA mail group, and the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",169,1,11,0)="installer of the update."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,0)="157 SEQ #170^3090422.122201^17"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,0)="^^32^32^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,1,0)="This patch enhances the functionality of two components (DIC and IX) in"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,2,0)="the PSNDI routine."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,4,0)="PSNDI is an existing API (Application Programmer Interface) for "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,5,0)="replicating FileMan calls.  Prior to this patch, this API supported these"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,6,0)="files:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,8,0)="         DRUG INGREDIENTS (#50.416)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,9,0)="         DRUG INTERACTION (#56)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,10,0)="         VA DRUG CLASS (#50.605)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,12,0)="This patch adds these two files to the supported file list:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,13,0)="          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,14,0)="         NDC/UPN (#50.67)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,15,0)="         VA GENERIC (#50.6)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,17,0)="Inactivation Date screening logic for the standardized files (DRUG "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,18,0)="INGREDIENTS (#50.416), VA GENERIC (#50.6), and VA DRUG CLASS (#50.605))"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,19,0)="will now use the SCREEN^XTID call, which utilizes the VUID inactivation"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,20,0)="date.  The  Inactivation Date screening for the non-standardized files"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,21,0)="(NDC/UPN (#50.67) and DRUG INTERACTION (#56)) will be based on their"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,22,0)="VistA inactivation date fields. Prior to this patch, the screening for the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,23,0)="DRUG INGREDIENTS (#50.416) File was based on the VistA inactivation date"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,24,0)="field, and prior to this patch there was no Inactivation Date screening "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,25,0)="for the VA DRUG CLASS (#50.605) file."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,27,0)="For further information regarding this API, please see FORUM DBIA (Data "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,28,0)="Base Integration Agreement) 4554."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,30,0)="**NOTE** These APIs kill DIC(""S"") upon entry.  Also, DIC(""S"") will remain"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,31,0)="defined after a call if the calling application passes in an inactive"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",170,1,32,0)="date."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",171,0)="184^3090422.124211^17"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",171,1,0)="^^17^17^3090422"
