^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",177,1,18,0)="The source of the data for the PMIs is First Data Bank."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,0)="190^3090422.164326^17"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,0)="^^17^17^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,2,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,3,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,4,0)="This patch generates four mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,5,0)="to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the PSNMGR security "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,6,0)="key, and the person installing the patch.  The first message, with the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,7,0)="subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products, CMOP ID (if one exists),"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,8,0)="dispense units, and associated NDCs, products for which the national"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,9,0)="formulary indicator has changed, products that have been unmatched from"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,10,0)="CMOP, and products for which the national formulary restriction has"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,11,0)="changed.  The second, with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,12,0)="interactions that have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,13,0)="the subject DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,14,0)="DRUG file (#50) which have been unmatched from NDF.  The fourth, with the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,15,0)="subject INTERACTIONS and ALLERGIES UPDATED, lists interactions and allergies"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,16,0)="which have been changed because they were created with ingredients that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",178,1,17,0)="are no longer primary ingredients."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",179,0)="191^3090422.164424^17"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",179,1,0)="^^8^8^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",179,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",179,1,2,0)="NOTE: This patch is part of NDF Data Update FY09 #5, which is comprised"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",179,1,3,0)="of two patches, PSN*4*190 and PSN*4*191."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",179,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",179,1,5,0)="The environment check routine for this patch checks to see that the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",179,1,6,0)="installer is a valid user."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",179,1,7,0)="The post-install routine for this patch matches entries in the VA PRODUCT "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",179,1,8,0)="file (#50.68) to the proper PMIs."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,0)="169 SEQ #180^3090423.105008^17"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,0)="^^50^50^3090423"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,1,0)="This patch is being released in conjunction with Pharmacy Data Management"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,2,0)="patch PSS*1.0*129. Together, these patches provide the functionality"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,3,0)="needed to prepare for the release of Pharmacy Re-Engineering (PRE) V. 0.5,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,4,0)="which will change the current Pharmacy Order Checking system from using"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,5,0)="the data stored in VistA to using data from the First DataBank (FDB)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,6,0)="commercial database system. All of the new functionality needed to do the "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,7,0)="set-up work is included in patch PSS*1.0*129. The PSS*1.0*129 patch also "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,8,0)="references the documentation needed for the set-up work."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,10,0)="This patch makes some changes to the National Drug File package that must "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,11,0)="be in place prior to the install of patch PSS*1.0*129. The National Drug"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,12,0)="File changes included in this patch are:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,14,0)="1) Exports the Data Dictionary for the new OVERRIDE DF DOSE CHK EXCLUSION"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,15,0)="   (#31) Field of the VA PRODUCT (#50.68) File."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,16,0)="2) Populates the new OVERRIDE DF DOSE CHK EXCLUSION (#31) Field of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,17,0)="   VA PRODUCT (#50.68) File with data."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,18,0)="3) Modifies the PSNAPIS Application Programmer Interface (API) to return"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,19,0)="   data from the new OVERRIDE DF DOSE CHK EXCLUSION (#31) Field of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,20,0)="   VA PRODUCT (#50.68) File. A new OVRIDE Line Tag has been added to"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,21,0)="   return this information. See Database Integration Agreement (DBIA) 2531"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,22,0)="   for more information."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,23,0)="4) Modifies the INQUIRE TO VA PRODUCT INFO FOR LOCAL DRUG [PSNLOOK] option"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,24,0)="   and the INQUIRE TO NATIONAL FILES [PSNACT] option to display the data"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,25,0)="   in the new OVERRIDE DF DOSE CHK EXCLUSION (#31) Field of the VA PRODUCT"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,26,0)="   (#50.68) File. If the value of the new field is ""YES"", a message will"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,27,0)="   be displayed to inform the user of the override significance. This"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,28,0)="   field works in conjunction with the new EXCLUDE FROM DOSAGE CHECKS"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,29,0)="   (#11) Field of the DOSAGE FORM (#50.606) File, which is being released"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,30,0)="   in patch PSS*1.0*129."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,31,0)="5) This patch makes these corrections to the INQUIRE TO VA PRODUCT"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,32,0)="   INFO FOR LOCAL DRUG [PSNLOOK] option:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,33,0)="     a) Sometimes the Active Ingredients would not display."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,34,0)="     b) When the Active Ingredients did display, the Strength"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,35,0)="        that displayed next to the Active Ingredient was not the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,36,0)="        Strength of the Active Ingredient, it was the Strength"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,37,0)="        of the VA Product."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,38,0)="     c) The Drug Unit was not always displaying."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,39,0)="     d) Only the CS FEDERAL SCHEDULE code was displaying, and not"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,40,0)="        the text."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,41,0)="     e) When displaying the Active Ingredients, the text (Primary)"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,42,0)="        will no longer display next to an Active Ingredient that is a"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,43,0)="        Primary Ingredient, and the Primary Ingredient will now display"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,44,0)="        if the Ingredient of the VA Product has a Primary Ingredient."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,45,0)="6) This patch makes these corrections to the Inquire to National Files "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,46,0)="   [PSNACT] option:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,47,0)="     a) Only the CS FEDERAL SCHEDULE code was displaying, and not"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,48,0)="        the text."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,49,0)="     b) The National Formulary Restriction display was being truncated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",180,1,50,0)="        after one line if was two or more lines in length."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",181,0)="194^3090423.105534^17"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",181,1,0)="^^18^18^3090423"
