^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,1,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,2,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application.  This patch generates four"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,3,0)="mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER to members of the NDF DATA"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,4,0)="mail group, holders of the PSNMGR security key, and the person installing"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,5,0)="the patch.  The first message, with the subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,6,0)="new products, CMOP ID (if one exists), dispense units, and associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,7,0)="NDCs, products for which the national formulary indicator has changed,"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,8,0)="products that have been unmatched from CMOP, and products for which the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,9,0)="national formulary restriction has changed.  The second, with the subject"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,10,0)="UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists interactions that have been added, edited, or"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,11,0)="inactivated. The third, with the subject DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,12,0)="DRUG FILE, lists entries in the DRUG file (#50) which have been unmatched"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,13,0)="from NDF.  The fourth, with the subject INTERACTIONS and ALLERGIES"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,14,0)="UPDATED, lists interactions and allergies which have been changed because"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",218,1,15,0)="they were created with ingredients that are no longer primary ingredients."
