^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,2,0)="of one patch, PSN*4*339."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,4,0)="This patch consists of NDC updates to NDC/UPN file (#50.67). This patch "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,5,0)="will transition The National Drug File Management system away from a "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,6,0)="manually maintained NDC file to a system that is supported by a "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,7,0)="commercial vendor. "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,9,0)="This patch will add new NDC data but will not make changes to the VA "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,10,0)="product file. There should not be any unmatched entries for the VA "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,11,0)="Pharmacy ADPAC to rematch. "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,13,0)="This patch will generate four e-mail messages but the messages should not "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,14,0)="contain any data that the Pharmacy ADPAC to act on. But due to system "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,15,0)="design the patch will send the following patch messages."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,17,0)="DATA UPDATE FOR NDF"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,18,0)="UPDATED DRUG INTERACTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,19,0)="DRUG UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,20,0)="ALLERGIES UPDATE."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,22,0)="If there is information found in these messages, contact NDF Support at "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",327,1,23,0)="VHAPBH NDF in MS Outlook."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,0)="340^3121113.112026^17"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,0)="^^17^17^3121113"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,1,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,2,0)="with the Patient Medication Instruction Sheet (PMI) portion of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,3,0)="National Drug File (NDF) application.  The seven files are:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,4,0)="   50.621        PMI-ENGLISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,5,0)="   50.622        PMI-SPANISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,6,0)="   50.623        PMI MAP-ENGLISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,7,0)="   50.624        PMI MAP-SPANISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,8,0)="   50.625        WARNING LABEL-ENGLISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,9,0)="   50.626        WARNING LABEL-SPANISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,10,0)="   50.627        WARNING LABEL MAP     "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,12,0)="The environment check routine for this patch checks to see that the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,13,0)="installer is a valid user."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,14,0)="The post-install routine for this patch deletes existing entries in these"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,15,0)="files, loads the new data, and rematches entries in the VA PRODUCT file "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,16,0)="(#50.68) to the proper PMIs."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",328,1,17,0)="The source of the data for the PMIs is First Data Bank."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,0)="341^3121126.125754^17"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,0)="^^16^16^3121126"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,1,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,2,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,3,0)="This patch generates four mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,4,0)="to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the PSNMGR security "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,5,0)="key, and the person installing the patch.  The first message, with the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,6,0)="subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products, CMOP ID (if one exists),"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,7,0)="dispense units, and associated NDCs, products for which the national"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,8,0)="formulary indicator has changed, products that have been unmatched from"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,9,0)="CMOP, and products for which the national formulary restriction has"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,10,0)="changed.  The second, with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,11,0)="interactions that have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,12,0)="the subject DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,13,0)="DRUG file (#50) which have been unmatched from NDF.  The fourth, with the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,14,0)="subject INTERACTIONS and ALLERGIES UPDATED, lists interactions and allergies"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,15,0)="which have been changed because they were created with ingredients that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",329,1,16,0)="are no longer primary ingredients."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",330,0)="342^3121126.125958^17"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",330,1,0)="^^4^4^3121126"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",330,1,1,0)="The environment check routine for this patch checks to see that the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",330,1,2,0)="installer is a valid user."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",330,1,3,0)="The post-install routine for this patch matches entries in the VA PRODUCT "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",330,1,4,0)="file (#50.68) to the proper PMIs."
