^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,1,0)="This patch is part of the Pharmacy Safety Updates project which was "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,2,0)="established to address specific New Service Requests (NSRs) as well as a"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,3,0)="Remedy Ticket and a Patient Safety Issue (PSI) related to the VistA Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,4,0)="applications as approved by the Health Systems Enterprise Systems Manager"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,5,0)="(ESM)."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,7,0)="This project is comprised of patches from five different applications, as"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,8,0)="shown below:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,9,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,10,0)="   APPLICATION/VERSION                                  PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,11,0)="   -----------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,12,0)="   OUTPATIENT PHARMACY (OP) V. 7.0                      PSO*7*444"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,13,0)="   INTEGRATED BILLING (IB) V. 2.0                       IB*2*545"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,14,0)="   PHARMACY DATA MANAGEMENT (PDM) V. 1.0                PSS*1*189"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,15,0)="   NATIONAL DRUG FILE (NDF) V. 4.0                      PSN*4*429"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,16,0)="   INPATIENT MEDICATIONS (IM) V.5.0                     PSJ*5*313"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,19,0)="The following New service Requests (NSRs) are being addressed by this patch:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,20,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,21,0)=" NSRs 20060601/20111206 Allow Dispensing of Greater Than 90 Day Supply"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,22,0)=" ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,23,0)=" The Outpatient Pharmacy and supporting VistA applications are being modified"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,24,0)=" to allow dispensing of more than 90 day supply fill for outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,25,0)=" prescriptions. The new limit will be 365 days and will be set for each drug"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,26,0)=" individually. See below for more information on specific menu "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,27,0)=" options related to this enhancement.  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,28,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,29,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,30,0)="The following National Drug File (NDF) functionality was modified:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,32,0)="1. A new field called MAXIMUM DAYS SUPPLY (#32) was added to the VA PRODUCT"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,33,0)="   file (#50.68) for storing the national maximum day supply value for a"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,34,0)="   medication in an outpatient prescription. This field will not be populated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,35,0)="   initially by Pharmacy Product System - National (PPS-N) as changes will be"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,36,0)="   required to that application to edit and export this new field. "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,37,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,38,0)="2. Inquire to VA Product Info For Local Drug [PSNLOOK] option"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,39,0)="   This option was modified to display the new field as seen below:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,40,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,41,0)="   ..."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,42,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,43,0)="      Override DF Exclude from Dosage Checks: No"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,44,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,45,0)="      Auto-Create Default Possible Dosage? Yes"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,46,0)="      Reduced Co-pay: None"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,47,0)="      Maximum Days Supply: 360"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,49,0)="   ..."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,51,0)="3. Inquire to National Files [PSNACT] option"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,52,0)="   This option was also modified to display the new field as seen below:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,54,0)="   ..."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,55,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,56,0)="      Auto-Create Default Possible Dosage? No"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,57,0)="          Possible Dosages To Auto-Create: 1x Possible Dosage"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,58,0)="                                  Package: Both Inpatient and Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,59,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,60,0)="      Reduced Co-pay: None"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,61,0)="      Maximum Days Supply: 360"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,62,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,63,0)="      Press return to continue or '^' to exit: "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",466,1,64,0)="   ..."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,0)="486^3160713.130408^54"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,0)="^^17^17^3160713"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,1,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,2,0)="with the Patient Medication Instruction Sheet (PMI) portion of the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,3,0)="National Drug File (NDF) application.  The seven files are:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,4,0)="   50.621        PMI-ENGLISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,5,0)="   50.622        PMI-SPANISH              "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,6,0)="   50.623        PMI MAP-ENGLISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,7,0)="   50.624        PMI MAP-SPANISH          "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,8,0)="   50.625        WARNING LABEL-ENGLISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,9,0)="   50.626        WARNING LABEL-SPANISH    "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,10,0)="   50.627        WARNING LABEL MAP     "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,12,0)="The environment check routine for this patch checks to see that the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,13,0)="installer is a valid user."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,14,0)="The post-install routine for this patch deletes existing entries in these"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,15,0)="files, loads the new data, and rematches entries in the VA PRODUCT file "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,16,0)="(#50.68) to the proper PMIs."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",467,1,17,0)="The source of the data for the PMIs is First Data Bank."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",468,0)="437 SEQ #469^3160726.140646^54"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",468,1,0)="^^4^4^3160726"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",468,1,1,0)="Patch PSN*4.0*437 addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",468,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",468,1,3,0)="In preparation for the VA's transition from IPv4 to IPv6 the National "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",468,1,4,0)="Drug File (NDF) package will require modifications to make it IPv6 ready."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,0)="487^3160726.14123^54"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,0)="^^16^16^3160726"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,1,0)="This patch provides updates to data in several of the files associated"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,2,0)="with the National Drug File (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,3,0)="This patch generates four mail messages.  All are sent from NDF MANAGER"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,4,0)="to members of the NDF DATA mail group, holders of the PSNMGR security "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,5,0)="key, and the person installing the patch.  The first message, with the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,6,0)="subject DATA UPDATE FOR NDF, lists new products, CMOP ID (if one exists),"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,7,0)="dispense units, and associated NDCs, products for which the national"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,8,0)="formulary indicator has changed, products that have been unmatched from"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,9,0)="CMOP, and products for which the national formulary restriction has"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,10,0)="changed.  The second, with the subject UPDATED INTERACTIONS, lists"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,11,0)="interactions that have been added, edited, or inactivated. The third, with"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,12,0)="the subject DRUGS UNMATCHED FROM NATIONAL DRUG FILE, lists entries in the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,13,0)="DRUG file (#50) which have been unmatched from NDF.  The fourth, with the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,14,0)="subject INTERACTIONS and ALLERGIES UPDATED, lists interactions and allergies"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,15,0)="which have been changed because they were created with ingredients that"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",469,1,16,0)="are no longer primary ingredients."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",470,0)="488^3160726.141348^54"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",470,1,0)="^^4^4^3160726"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",470,1,1,0)="The environment check routine for this patch checks to see that the"
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",470,1,2,0)="installer is a valid user."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",470,1,3,0)="The post-install routine for this patch matches entries in the VA PRODUCT "
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",470,1,4,0)="file (#50.68) to the proper PMIs."
^DIC(9.4,59,22,5,"PAH",471,0)="489^3160815.125213^54"
