^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,0)="7.0^3051119^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,1,0)="^^3^3^3051119"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,1,1,0)="Version 7.0 of Outpatient Pharmacy will interface with version 1.0 of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,1,2,0)="OERR/CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^642^642"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,0)="1^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,0)="^^30^30^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,1,0)="PSO*7.0*1 - 1.26.97"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,3,0)="PSOCLO1: A problem was reported about Clozapine Rxs and when there are"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,4,0)="valid lab results.  The problem has to do with the lab results being"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,5,0)="returned as zero when a number should be returned."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,7,0)="After the installation of version 7.0 in Washington's production account"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,8,0)="a number of allocation errors begin to occur.  In an attempt to manage"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,9,0)="the number of variables in the partition several routines have been"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,10,0)="modified.  They are: PSOHLNE1, PSOHLNE2, PSOHLNEW, PSOHLSIG, PSOHLSIH,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,11,0)="PSOHLSN, PSOHLSN1, PSOORUT1, PSON52, PSORN52, and PSORN52C."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,13,0)="PSOREF: Fixed problem on speed refill of invalid Fill Date selection prompts"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,14,0)="if the 1st Rx in the list is expired.  In this routine there's an entry"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,15,0)="point that's used by CPRS to help determine if an Rx is refillable."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,16,0)="There's a potential problem when refill requests are made and the Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,17,0)="Orderable Item are missing from the Rx.  In order to prevent a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,18,0)="possible undefined error from occurring an addition check was added to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,19,0)="determine if there's an orderable item is for that drug in the Rx."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,21,0)="When a refill was in suspense, some cross references were being corrupted"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,22,0)="in the Rx Suspense File. These changes fix that problem. Also added a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,23,0)="cross reference to the Fill Date field. What this does is if an Original"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,24,0)="Fill is in suspense and has not yet been printed, if the Fill Date is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,25,0)="edited, then we now update the suspense date with the new Fill Date."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,26,0)="Routines: PSOUTL, PSOUTLA. The Fill Date field (#22) in the Rx file (#52)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,27,0)="will be sent out in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,29,0)="Added addition code to prevent refills from being deleted when removing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",1,1,30,0)="Rxs from Hold,  Routines: PSOUTL, PSOHLD"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,0)="2^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^26^26^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,1,0)="PSO*7.0*1 (1.26.98)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,3,0)="This patch installs new functionality that allows the action profile to be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,4,0)="printed in an 80 column format.  When there's an attached DUE questionnaire"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,5,0)="it too prints in an 80 column format."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,6,0)="Routines: PSOSD, PSOSD0, PSOSD1, PSOSD2, PSOSD3, PSOSDP, and PSODACT,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,7,0)="PSOBMST, PSODEDT."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,9,0)="This patch corrects a problem in the compiling of the data for the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,10,0)="Medication profiles.  The problem is that prescriptions that had been marked"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,11,0)="as deleted were printing on the short and long profiles.  Routine: PSOP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,13,0)="Fixed problem of incorrect message given to user on the Listman status"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,14,0)="bar saying ""Label will Reprint due to edit!"", when no data was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,15,0)="actually changed during the editing of the Rx, and no label will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,16,0)="printed.  Routines: PSORXED, PSORXED1."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,18,0)="A NOIS was entered on the Tuscaloosa VAMC local NOIS system describing the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,19,0)="wording in a prompt as misleading.  The prompt appeared to allow users to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,20,0)="select multiple entries.  However, this select prompt is meant to allow a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,21,0)="single selection and not multiple.  The wording will be changed from 'Select "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,22,0)="Refill' to 'Select a Refill'.  Routine: PSOORED2."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,24,0)="When prescriptions are returned as not dispensed by CMOP Host, and edited"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,25,0)="by Pharmacy, they are not automatically re-suspended back to CMOP for "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",2,1,26,0)="transmission.  Routines: PSOCMOP, PSOCMOPC, PSORXED, PSORXED1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,0)="4^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^24^24^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="1. Fixed errors reported in Tuscaloosa, local NOIS PHA-0198-N0089 and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,2,0)="PHA-0198-N0076. An undefined error occurred if the user selected to edit"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,3,0)="both the Pharmacy Orderable Item and the Dispense Drug, and entered a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,4,0)="Duplicate Drug of another Rx for that patient, and did not Discontinue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,5,0)="that duplicate Rx when prompted to Discontinue. Routine: PSOOREDT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,7,0)="2. Corrected a problem where a possible invalid cross reference existed.  Which"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,8,0)="could cause an undefined error when cost data is being compiled."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,9,0)="Routine: PSOCSTM, PSOCSTD"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,11,0)="3. Added a check to screen out pending refill order when doing order checks."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,12,0)="Routine PSODRDU1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,14,0)="4. Made Site parameters required in the Delete Rx option. NOIS: PUG-0198-52050"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,15,0)="Routine PSORXDL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,17,0)="5. Fixed an error that occurred in Tuscaloosa on a Health Summary. It came upon"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,18,0)="a prescription with missing data, (No drug, provider, or patient pointer)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,19,0)="A check was added to look for missing data. Routine PSOHCSUM"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,21,0)="6. Fixed error that occurred in Tuscaloosa in PSOORRL routine, returning"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,22,0)="a Med profile to CPRS. The error occurred because of an invalid provider"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,23,0)="entry in a prescription. Modified code to check for invalid and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",3,1,24,0)="missing data in the provider field and the drug field. Routine PSOORRL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,0)="5^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^29^29^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,2,0)="1. Made change to Allergy/Adverse Reaction display on labels and screen"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,3,0)="profiles. The software was referencing an incorrect piece of data, which"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,4,0)="caused us to possibly display an Allergy under the Adverse Reaction heading,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,5,0)="when it really should be displayed under the Allergy heading."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,6,0)="Routines: PSODEM, PSOLBLN1, PSOLBLS, PSOORUT3"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,8,0)="2. Fix a problem reported in NOIS SFC-0298-60679. Entering an up-arrow (^)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,9,0)="at the Ticket # prompt could cause an undefined error.  The software was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,10,0)="changed to delete the entry when an up-arrow is entered at the prompt."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,11,0)="The software will now display a message indicating that the ""Bingo"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,12,0)="record is incomplete!"" and ""Bingo record removed. Routine: PSOBING1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,14,0)="3. Fixed error reported by Puget Sound in NOIS PUG-0198-51767. An undefined"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,15,0)="error occurred when editing a prescription that created a new"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,16,0)="prescription, and there were no numbers left in the numbering sequence"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,17,0)="for prescriptions. Errors could also occur if a site was manually"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,18,0)="assigning the prescription numbers, and nothing was entered at the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,19,0)="""Select New Rx #"" prompt when creating a new prescription due to an Edit."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,20,0)="Routines: PSONRXN, PSOORED1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,22,0)="4. Fixed an error reported by San Francisco, NOIS SFC-0298-60681. The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,23,0)="error occurred in the daily cost compilation background job. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,24,0)="When the patient is accessed during the compilation routine, an error could"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,25,0)="occur if that patient has both Outpatient and Inpatient orders to be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,26,0)="backfilled. After the backfilling, upon returning to the cost compilation"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,27,0)="routine, an undefined error could occur. Routine: PSOHLUP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",4,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,0)="7^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,0)="^^14^14^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,1,0)="This KIDS build fixes a problem when pending orders are received from CPRS.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,2,0)="They are not finished in a first in first out order.  Added ""AD"" cross "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,3,0)="reference to Login Date field (#15) from the Pending Outpatient Orders file "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,4,0)="(#52.41).  Added an 'AE' xref to the Related Institution field."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,5,0)=" NOIS: WAS-0298-21178 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,7,0)="Error generated when pharmacist was finishing outpatient med orders for an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,8,0)="inpatient. From the medication profile screen, she typed IP to view the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,9,0)="inpatient profile and after the review, she went back to the medication"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,10,0)="profile screen, hit return at the action prompt an undefined error occurred."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,11,0)="NOIS: HUN-0398-20933"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,13,0)="Routines: PSOORFI1, PSOORFI2, PSOORFIN, PSOPOST3, PSOPTPST, PSORN52C, PSORX1 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",5,1,14,0)="PSOHLNE2, PSOHLNEW, PSOHLSN"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,0)="8^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,0)="^^24^24^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,2,0)="1. This patch fixes problems involving pulling prescriptions from suspense"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,3,0)="to fill locally that were originally suspended for CMOP. If a prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,4,0)="is suspended for CMOP, and is pulled from suspense using the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,5,0)="Prescription Processing option, then an up-arrow is entered when the user"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,6,0)="is prompted for a label action, the CMOP INDICATOR field in the RX SUSPENSE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,7,0)="File would have been set to ""P"", for PRINTED LOCALLY, although the label"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,8,0)="never printed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,10,0)="2. Another problem occurred when using the Pull Early from Suspense option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,11,0)="If the routing was changed while pulling a prescription from suspense,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,12,0)="then a ""^"" was entered at the Label prompt, the original routing was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,13,0)="not restored to the prescription, which caused prescriptions that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,14,0)="were originally intended to be filled at the CMOP to be printed locally."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,16,0)="Routines: PSOLBL, PSORXL, PSOSUPAT, PSOSUPOE, PSOSUPRX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,18,0)="3. When sites have install the CMOP package but are not actively transmitting"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,19,0)="to a host facility and reinstates discontinued prescriptions with a drug that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,20,0)="has been marked for use for CMOP they are being suspended for transmission to a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,21,0)="CMOP host facility. Routine: PSOCAN2"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,23,0)="4. A problem occurred when trying to discontinue Pending orders for a patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",6,1,24,0)="by using the Discontinue Prescription(s) option. Routine: PSOCAN1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,0)="10^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^40^40^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,1,0)="This patch corrects the finding as reported by the QA review.  Most if not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,2,0)="all changes will be transparent to the user."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,4,0)=" Removal of nonstandard reference to ^DPT(."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,5,0)=" Removal of naked global references at the start of lines."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,6,0)=" Added timeouts to locking global."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,7,0)=" Removal of nonstandard reference to ^%ZIS(1, and ^%ZIS(2,."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,8,0)=" Write commands in data dictionaries changed to EN^DDIOL."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,9,0)=" Variable DT sets were changed to supported $$DT^XLFDT."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,11,0)=" PSOARCLT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,12,0)=" PSOARCTG"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,13,0)=" PSOARX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,14,0)=" PSOB"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,15,0)=" PSOBGMG1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,16,0)=" PSOBGMG2"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,17,0)=" PSOBSET"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,18,0)=" PSOCPC"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,19,0)=" PSOCPTRI"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,20,0)=" PSOCST11"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,21,0)=" PSOCST2"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,22,0)=" PSOCST4"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,23,0)=" PSODELI"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,24,0)=" PSODGDGI"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,25,0)=" PSOHLEXP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,26,0)=" PSOHLSG1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,27,0)=" PSOHLSN1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,28,0)=" PSOHLUP1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,29,0)=" PSOLSET"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,30,0)=" PSOORCPY"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,31,0)=" PSOORNW2"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,32,0)=" PSOR52"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,33,0)=" PSOSTART"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,34,0)=" PSOSULB1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,35,0)=" PSOSUP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,36,0)=" PSOSURST"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,37,0)=" PSOSUTL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,39,0)="Also added NDF file structure changes to routines PSOHLSN1, PSOHLSG1, and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",7,1,40,0)="PSOHLSN."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,0)="11^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,0)="^^44^44^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,2,0)="1. Second line of routine has incorrect package release month and year.  Second line of all routine should read as follows prior to any patches being applied: <tab>;;7.0UTPATIENT PHARMACY;;DEC 1997"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,3,0)="Routines: PSOCMOPB, PSOCPDUP, PSODRDUP, PSOLMRN, PSONGR, and PSORDS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,5,0)="2. Added a 'Press to Continue' prompt for the Order Summary list."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,6,0)="  NOIS: WNY-0398-11868.  Routine: PSOORNE1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,8,0)="3. Added check for on the fly conversion when using the Batch Barcode Refill/Renew option.  Routine: PSOBBC. NOIS: CTX-0398-70637"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,10,0)="4. Removed commented out code. Routine: PSOBKDED, PSOORNEW.  Also in the routine PSOORNEW, fixed an undefined error.  NOIS: HUN-0298-22095"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,12,0)="5. Added Prescription Delivery to Patient Information screen. Routine: PSOORUT2"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,14,0)="6. Added timed lock to globals.  Routine: PSOPRVW, PSONEW"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,16,0)="7. Newed PSODRUG variable in routine PSOCAN"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,18,0)="8. In the supported reference PSOORDER which returns prescription data, the external value of the Rx Patient Status was added.  Added $G around global reference to prevent a possible undefined error. Routine: PSOORDER."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,20,0)="9. Changed a $Select statement to make it consistent with other displays when showing method of pick up.  Routine: PSOBGMG3"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,22,0)="10. Added additional data validation checks for prescription being renewed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,23,0)="Routine: PSOORNE5, PSORENW, PSORENW0, PSORENW4"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,25,0)="11. As determined by the Programming Conventions and Standards, no line can"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,26,0)="start with a naked global reference. Routines: PSORXPA1, PSORXRP1."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,28,0)="12. When requesting a reprint of a prescription label and the prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,29,0)="was entered through CPRS there's the possibility that the SIG will not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,30,0)="display to the screen. Routine: PSORXRP2"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,32,0)="13. Added code to removed date an Rx was canceled when renewed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,33,0)="Routine: PSORN52"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,35,0)="14. Fixed problem of CMOP barcoded refills from being printed locally."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,37,0)="15. Fixed duplicate active drug problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,39,0)="16. Along with PSO*7*7, will now show Provider Instruction enter through"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,40,0)="CPRS in the Pharmacy options."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,42,0)="17. Added # of refills prompt for speed renewing."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",8,1,44,0)="18. Added a PSNDF reference change to comply with new file structure."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,0)="16^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,0)="^^33^33^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,2,0)="1. When Controlled Rxs are renewed, the expiration date was defaulting to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,3,0)="one year instead of six months.  Routine: PSON52"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,5,0)="2. When prescriptions are removed from Hold the user can reprint the label"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,6,0)="if they want.  In the activity multiple events are recorded (placed on,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,7,0)="removed from hold).  If a label is printed the label log does not show that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,8,0)="the label was printed because the Rx was removed from hold.  This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,9,0)="record in the label log that the label was printed because an Rx was removed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,10,0)="from hold.  Routines: PSOHLD, PSOLBLN"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,12,0)="Also added a check in the routine PSOLBLN to check for the barcode on and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,13,0)="off sequences being defined for Rx label printing."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,15,0)="3. Added a check for site parameters being defined when using the Rx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,16,0)="Verification by Clerk option [PSO VR]. Routine: PSOVER"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,18,0)="4. Corrected a problem where inventory deduction from the Drug file (#50)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,19,0)="could happen unnecessarily. Routine: PSORXED, PSORXED1."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,21,0)="5. Added a site parameter, VERIFYING PHARMACIST ON LABELS, that will allow"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,22,0)="sites to print the Verifying Pharmacist number on the 2nd line of labels."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,24,0)="6. Fixed problem of refilling an Rx, and the refill suspending to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,25,0)="original Fill Date, instead of the Refill Date. Routine PSORXED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,27,0)="7. Fixed problem of Editing a released Rx, and that Rx then suspending for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,28,0)="CMOP instead of suspending locally. Routine PSOCMOP."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,30,0)="8. On line 2 of the labels, the first number printed after the phone"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,31,0)="number for CPRS entered orders has been the internal entry number of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,32,0)="person entering the order in CPRS. This patch changes that number to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",9,1,33,0)="person who Finishes the order in Pharmacy."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,0)="17^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^23^23^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,2,0)="1. Corrected problems with the nightly cost compile jobs.  The problems are"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,3,0)="that the number of requests by patient was not being counted correctly and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,4,0)="a problem with the nightly compile where data for the previous day was being"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,5,0)="reset.  Routines: PSOCSTD, PSOCSTM"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,7,0)="2. Corrected a problem with the nightly job that compiles the AMIS data. The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,8,0)="problem is that all partials was not being counted correctly."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,9,0)="Routine: PSOAMIS0"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,11,0)="3. Corrected a possible problem of barcode on and off sequences being changed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,12,0)="and made invalid for label printers.  This could happen if a label device is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,13,0)="selected, then an Action Profile device is selected, and the site parameter"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,14,0)="is set to print barcodes on action profiles.  If there are Rx labels to print"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,15,0)="again the Barcode On and Barcode Off sequences for the Action Profile printer"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,16,0)="become the sequences for the Label printer, which may not work if the printers"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,17,0)="selected are different types.  Routines PSOSD, PSOSD1, PSOSDP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,19,0)=" 4. Corrected a problem reported when using the Delete a Prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,20,0)="[PSO RXDL] option.  If an original fill is released, and a refill is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,21,0)="entered but not yet released, the user can mark the prescription as"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,22,0)="deleted without first returning to stock the original fill. Routine PSORXDL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",10,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,0)="3^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^19^19^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="Fixed problem reported in Tuscaloosa, local NOIS PHA-0198-N0090. If a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,2,0)="reprint was done in Listman on one Rx in the Patient Prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,3,0)="Processing option, then the user finished some Rx's in the Complete"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,4,0)="Orders from OERR option, the comments from the reprint would carry over"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,5,0)="to the Label Log entries for the Rx's finished in the Complete option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,6,0)="Routine: PSORXRPT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,8,0)="SAC 2.2.1.1 prohibits parameter passing on the first line.3 routines"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,9,0)="have formal lists on the first line.  Routines: PSOORDRG, PSODIR2,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,10,0)="and PSODIR3."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,12,0)="In the Outpatient package there's a Listman action that allows the user to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,13,0)="print medication instruction sheets. This action when used does not turn off"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,14,0)="the Listman screen controls.  This patch corrects that.  Routine: PSOHELP."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,16,0)="Fixed problem reported in Tuscaloosa, local nois PHA-0198-N0104."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,17,0)="When the Autocancel on Admission job ran, it was not canceling"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,18,0)="prescriptions that were issued on the same day as the admission, but"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",11,1,19,0)="it should have been canceling them."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,0)="18^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^12^12^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="1. This patch will attempt to make more POSSIBLE SIGS acceptable when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,1,2,0)="finishing CPRS entered orders in Outpatient Pharmacy. It will cut down"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,1,3,0)="on the number of POSSIBLE SIGS that start ""TAKE TAKE"", and also cut down"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,1,4,0)="the number of times the Dose Form noun is repeated, ""TABLETS TABLETS""."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,1,6,0)="2. This patch fixes the problem of the last refill being deleted when an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,1,7,0)="Rx is canceled or expired, after that refill had been transmitted to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,1,8,0)="CMOP."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,1,10,0)="3. This patch also fixes a problem of the Log of Suspended Rx's report not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,1,11,0)="always showing the correct routing."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",12,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",13,0)="19^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",13,1,0)="^^3^3^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",13,1,1,0)="This patch is being issued to bring the critical documents into compliance"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",13,1,2,0)="with the Year 2000 mandate.  Some of the key documents are Rx labels and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",13,1,3,0)="action profiles."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,0)="15^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,0)="^^110^110^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,1,0)="1. When using the Patient Record Update [PSO PATIENT RECORD UPDATE]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,2,0)="action, the site parameter that controls the editing of Patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,3,0)="Information Management System (PIMS) patient data was being ignored."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,4,0)="Routine: PSOLMPAT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,6,0)="2. This patch will enable the interface between Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,7,0)="version 7.0 and the Clinical Information Resource Network (CIRN) once CIRN"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,8,0)="is installed. There will be no change in functionality for Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,9,0)="Pharmacy sites that do not have CIRN installed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,11,0)="3. Corrected a problem reported in NOIS ALB-0498-50730 associated with"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,12,0)="the Medication Profile [PSO P] option.  The problem happens when the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,13,0)="report is sorted to print by Class or Medication and a cutoff date (number"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,14,0)="of days) is entered, the Rxs that have been canceled print beyond the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,15,0)="selected number of days.  Routine: PSOP2"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,17,0)="Corrected another problem reported in NOIS CON-0798-11780 when printing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,18,0)="the Med profile by a selected date range.  The problem is that when a date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,19,0)="range is entered the first time and the user attempts to run the report"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,20,0)="again and chooses a date range earlier that the initial date, the user is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,21,0)="not allowed to do so.  Routine: PSOP1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,23,0)="4. Corrected a problem where a possible undefined error could occur when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,24,0)="the cross reference on the DATE OF DEATH field (#.351) on the PATIENT file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,25,0)="(#2) is executed.  The problem could occur when the APOSD cross reference"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,26,0)="is executed. Routine: PSOCAN3"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,28,0)="5. Added a 'Press Return to Continue' prompt when using the Speed Release"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,29,0)="action.  The problem was when there were many Rx's to be released, the Rx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,30,0)="number scrolled off the screen.  For users without scroll back"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,31,0)="capabilities, this caused users to question as to what Rx's were being"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,32,0)="released. Routine: PSODISP3"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,34,0)="6.When editing the original Fill Date of a prescription that is in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,35,0)="suspense and queued for Consolidated Mail Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,36,0)="transmission, it is possible that duplicate ""AQ"" cross references will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,37,0)="exist for that suspense entry. This could cause the prescription to be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,38,0)="sent to the CMOP twice. In addition to fixing this problem, any invalid"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,39,0)="""AQ"" cross references will be deleted by this patch. Routines: PSOUTLA,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,40,0)="PSOPOST3"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,42,0)="7.This patch addresses a problem reported by some sites concerning the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,43,0)="Complete Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] option. Currently under this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,44,0)="option, the site will only see Pending Outpatient orders that have a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,45,0)="Related Institution that matches the Related Institution for the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,46,0)="Outpatient Site that the user is signed in under. The problem occurs when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,47,0)="an order is received from Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) from a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,48,0)="Clinic that is related to an Institution that is not found as a Related"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,49,0)="Institution for any of the Outpatient Pharmacy sites. When this happens,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,50,0)="the only way for those orders to be completed is for the user to select"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,51,0)="that patient under the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,52,0)="ORDERS] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,54,0)="To fix this problem, this patch adds a new field to the OUTPATIENT SITE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,55,0)="file (#59) called CPRS ORDERING INSTITUTION (#8). Multiple entries can be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,56,0)="entered in this field. This can be done using the Site Parameter"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,57,0)="Enter/Edit [PSO SITE PARAMETERS] option. Upon installation of this patch,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,58,0)="a conversion is done to move the Institution that is currently in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,59,0)="Related Institution field for each Outpatient Site to the first entry in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,60,0)="this new field. After the installation of the patch, if there is still"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,61,0)="only one entry in the new CPRS ORDERING INSTITUTION field (#8) for an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,62,0)="Outpatient Site, then the Complete Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,63,0)="option will not change for the user. However, sites can now enter multiple"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,64,0)="Institutions in this field for an Outpatient Pharmacy site, and if a site"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,65,0)="does this, the user will be prompted for an Institution when entering the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,66,0)="Complete Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] option. After the user selects"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,67,0)="an Institution, then the Pending Orders that will be shown to the user for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,68,0)="completing will be those Pending Orders from Clinics that are associated"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,69,0)="with that Institution selected."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,71,0)="8. A problem has been reported concerning the Order Summary that is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,72,0)="displayed after selecting the RX (Prescriptions) [PSO RX] option. The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,73,0)="first number displayed is the ""Orders to be completed for all divisions""."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,74,0)="Then the user can choose to view an order summary, which breaks down all"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,75,0)="of the orders by Routing, (Window, Mail, and Clinic). The problem is that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,76,0)="the total of the ""Orders to be completed for all divisions"" does not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,77,0)="always match the total of the breakdown by routing. The reason is that not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,78,0)="all Renewals that are received from CPRS have an associated routing. To"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,79,0)="resolve this, when Outpatient Pharmacy receives a Renewal from CPRS with"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,80,0)="no routing, a Mail routing will automatically be entered for the Renewal."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,81,0)="This patch will also automatically update any current Pending Renewals"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,82,0)="with no routing to a Mail routing."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,84,0)="9. This patch fixes a problem of the patient not always being displayed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,85,0)="on the Bingo Board automatically when using the Release Medication"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,86,0)="[PSO RELEASE] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,88,0)="10. This patch provides a new sort capability when using the Complete"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,89,0)="Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] option. Orders can now be Finished by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,90,0)="Clinic, or by Clinic Sort Group. Within either of these sorts, orders will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,91,0)="be Finished on a first in/first out basis by Patient. Clinic Sort Groups"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,92,0)="can be added/edited in the Enter/Edit Clinic Sort Groups [PSO SETUP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,93,0)="CLINIC GROUPS] option, which is found under the Maintenance (Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,94,0)="Pharmacy) [PSO MAINTENANCE] menu option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,96,0)="11. This patch fixes a problem of a prescription showing up on the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,97,0)="unreleased report, when only an Interaction label printed, and not a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,98,0)="Filling label. If a prescription is entered before the version 7.0"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,99,0)="install, and a Drug Interaction label printed, then version 7.0 is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,100,0)="installed, that prescription will show on the unreleased report, even"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,101,0)="though a Filling label never printed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,102,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,103,0)="12. This patch fixes an error that involves incorrect medications showing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,104,0)="up on a Medication profile for a patient. This can occur if there is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,105,0)="invalid data in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55). A patient validation"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,106,0)="check is being added to prevent this problem. Also in the Medication"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,107,0)="profile, an error could occur if a profile is run on a patient, and the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,108,0)="orders for that patient have not yet been backfilled to CPRS. This error"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,109,0)="can only occur shortly after the installation of Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",14,1,110,0)="version 7.0."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,0)="20^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,0)="^^50^50^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,1,0)="1. This patch fixes an error that can occur in the Change Suspense Date "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,2,0)="[PSO PNDCHG] option. When using this option, if ""YES"" is entered at the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,3,0)="""Do you want to delete Rx's from suspense for this patient"" prompt, and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,4,0)="that patient has an unreleased refill that has printed from suspense,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,5,0)="an error could occur. NOIS STX-0898-71717.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,7,0)="2. This patch exports an entry point that can be called by Computerized"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,8,0)="Patient Record System (CPRS) during Outpatient Order Entry. Based on the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,9,0)="patient and the Dispense Drug selected (when applicable), Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,10,0)="Pharmacy can return a flag to CPRS that tells CPRS to not ask the Service"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,11,0)="Connected question for that particular Outpatient Pharmacy order."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,13,0)="3. A new input transform for the QTY (#.04) field of the PARTIAL DATE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,14,0)="subfile (#52.2) of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) is being sent out in this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,15,0)="patch. It changes a Write statement to a VA FileMan call to comply with"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,16,0)="current standards.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,18,0)="4. This patch corrects a problem with discontinuing multiple Rx's at one"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,19,0)="time. NOIS CON-0698-12208.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,21,0)="5. In the medication procedure call that returns inpatient and outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,22,0)="detailed information, new data elements were added.  NOIS PUG-0298-51400."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,24,0)="6. Corrected a problem with editing drugs in prescriptions and the cost"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,25,0)="for the drug not being updated properly. NOIS TUA-0798-32558."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,27,0)="7. This patch corrects a problem of a possible incorrect CLINIC (#5)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,28,0)="field entry for a prescription. If a prescription is renewed from CPRS,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,29,0)="then Finished in Pharmacy, the Clinic for that prescription is the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,30,0)="original Clinic for the ""Renewed from"" prescription, but is should be the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,31,0)="Clinic where the prescription was Renewed. NOIS: CON-0998-10826"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,33,0)="8. This patch corrects a problem when a drug is changed in an Rx, but does"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,34,0)="not create a new order, the cost for that Rx did not update."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,35,0)="NOIS: TUA-0798-32558 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,37,0)="9. Enhanced the Cost Management Cost compile to use the release date and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,38,0)="include partials. This change allows the management report to be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,39,0)="consistent with the Cost and AMIS reports. NOIS: NCH-0698-40147"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,41,0)="10. Added new option to allow cost of an Rx for a specific drug to be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,42,0)="updated after the cost has been updated in the DRUG file (#50). NOIS:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,43,0)="NCH-0698-42420 and NYN-0998-11680."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,45,0)="11.  This patch corrects a problem reported in NOIS CAH-1198-32272. The "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,46,0)="problem happens when using the speed renew action, the incorrect number of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,47,0)="refills for controlled substances was being stored and displayed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,49,0)="12.  Added a newing statement to the supported reference PSOORDER to try"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",15,1,50,0)="to protect variables of other packages."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,0)="21^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^66^66^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,1,0)="1. Prior to the installation of this patch, if a new prescription is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,2,0)="entered at a site running the Consolidated Mail Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,3,0)="package, and that prescription is for a CMOP drug and is given a future"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,4,0)="Fill Date and marked as Window for the routing, that prescription will not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,5,0)="be suspended for CMOP. Even if all of the other CMOP criteria are met, it"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,6,0)="will be suspended locally because of the Window Routing. Because of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,7,0)="numerous requests to change this functionality, this patch will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,8,0)="automatically change a Window routing to Mail for new prescriptions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,9,0)="entered with a Future Fill Date that get suspended, and meet all of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,10,0)="CMOP criteria. Because the routing gets changed from Window to Mail, the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,11,0)="prescription will be suspended for CMOP, instead of suspended locally."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,13,0)="2. This patch provides the Controlled Substances package an entry point to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,14,0)="call that will delete the last refill of a prescription. When posting"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,15,0)="and releasing a prescription in Controlled Substances, if that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,16,0)="prescription has been discontinued, it will not be released and the refill"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,17,0)="will be deleted. This functionality will be available when patches"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,18,0)="PSO*7*21 and PSD*3*11 are installed, though the patches are not dependent"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,19,0)="on each other for installation."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,21,0)="3. This patch fixes an error that could occur when putting a prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,22,0)="on Hold through the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,23,0)="ORDERS] option. If the prescription has refills, and the user enters an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,24,0)="'^' at the PHARMACIST NAME prompt, an error could occur. A change has also"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,25,0)="been made to the Activity Log comments when putting a prescription on"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,26,0)="Hold. Currently, if the prescription has an entry in the RX SUSPENSE file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,27,0)="(#52.5), the comments always end in ""removed from SUSPENSE"", regardless of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,28,0)="whether or not the fill has been printed from suspense. This patch makes"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,29,0)="the change to only add those comments if the suspense fill has not yet"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,30,0)="been printed. NOIS OKL-1098-71710"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,32,0)="4. This patch enhances the functionality of editing prescriptions. An"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,33,0)="option is being added under the Rx (Prescriptions) [PSO RX] menu option"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,34,0)="called Edit Prescriptions [PSO RXEDIT]. This option will allow editing of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,35,0)="prescriptions by entering prescription number(s). Editing will still be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,36,0)="available through the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,37,0)="ORDERS] option, but this new option provides an alternative editing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,38,0)="capability. In addition, if a key field of a prescription is edited (field"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,39,0)="that generates a Reprint label request), and the field edited is a field"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,40,0)="of the last fill that has been released, a prompt will now be given that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,41,0)="asks if a Reprint label should be printed. If a key field is edited of a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,42,0)="fill that is not the last fill, and that key field is contained in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,43,0)="last fill, a Reprint label will not be generated."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,45,0)="5. This patch fixes a problem of an incorrect refill date possibly being"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,46,0)="assigned to a refill. After suspending a new prescription to the future,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,47,0)="if a refill is then done and a refill date of today is entered, the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,48,0)="future fill date from the new prescription can possibly be assigned to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,49,0)="the refill date. NOIS ALX-1198-71519"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,51,0)="6. This patch provides a new Order Summary of Pending Outpatient orders."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,52,0)="This new summary is by Clinic. To have this functionality, the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,53,0)="verified patch PSO*7*15 must also be installed. Patch PSO*7*15 is not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,54,0)="required for installation of this patch, but the new Order Summary by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,55,0)="Clinic will not be available until that patch is installed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,57,0)="7. This patch fixes a problem reported for sites running Tricare. Partial"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,58,0)="prescriptions are being sent for Tricare billing, but they should not."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,59,0)="This patches fixes the problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,61,0)="8. A problem has been reported that occurs when a Pharmacist verifies a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,62,0)="prescription entered by a Technician. If the Pharmacist edits the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,63,0)="prescription after it is accepted, but before the Label prompt, it can"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,64,0)="possibly be flagged as a Reprint prescription, when it should not be."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,65,0)="Also, if it is a CMOP prescription, it may print locally instead of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",16,1,66,0)="going to the CMOP because of the Reprint status."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,0)="14^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,0)="^^22^22^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,2,0)="1. This patch fixes a possible undefined error that could occur when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,3,0)="a new Outpatient Pharmacy division is added and the Daily and/or Monthly"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,4,0)="Management Cost Reports are run."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,5,0)="Routines: PSOMGMN1, PSOMGMN2, PSOMGMN3, PSOMGRP1, PSOMGRP2, PSOMGRP3"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,7,0)="2. If an OP Rx is filled on 6/5 and the patient quickly returns the refill"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,8,0)="form for processing, on 6/13, before the scheduled refill date 6/26.  The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,9,0)="bar code option [PSO BATCH BARCODED] will not accept the refill request"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,10,0)="and will not auto-suspend to the next scheduled refill date."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,11,0)="Routine: PSOREF0"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,13,0)="3. Fixed Null Subscript error reported in NOIS WAS-0498-21833. The error"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,14,0)="occurs when Outpatient Pharmacy receives a Discontinue message from CPRS on"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,15,0)="an entry in the PENDING OUTPATIENT ORDERS File (#52.41) with missing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,16,0)="data.  Changed messaging to recognize the UR order control code."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,17,0)="Routine PSOORUTL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,19,0)="4. In the View Prescriptions option, the help text given to the user at the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,20,0)="VIEW PRESCRIPTION prompt if the user enters a ""?"" is misleading. The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,21,0)="help text says that Patient Name can be entered, but it can't. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",17,1,22,0)="will remove the ""M"" from the DIC(0) variable. Routine PSORXVW"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",18,0)="13^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^1^1^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="Patch to Patch for PSO*7*15."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,0)="12^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,0)="^^30^30^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,1,0)=" 1. Changed code at STRX+2^PSOBINGO to prevent long response time when ""??"" is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,2,0)="entered at the ""Enter Rx #:"" prompt. This option lists a patient's "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,3,0)="prescriptions after selecting the patient.  The problem is that the screen "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,4,0)="looped through the entire PRESCRIPTION file (#52). Routine: PSOBINGO NOIS:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,5,0)="WNY-0498-10082 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,7,0)="2. When the ""C"" is entered to copy a prescription, the computer response is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,8,0)="""DC"", and then the ""Are you sure you want to discontinue? No//"" prompt is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,9,0)="displayed.  ""C"" should call the ""COPY"" action, not ""Discontinue"".  The reason"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,10,0)="this happens is that the protocol PSO Cancel has three (3) synonyms attached to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,11,0)="it, DC, Discontinue, and Cancel.  The PSO Cancel synonym will be removed from"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,12,0)="the protocol.  The patch PSO*7*12 will delete the protocol PSO CANCEL and then"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,13,0)="re-install it.  NOIS: WNY-0398-11863 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,15,0)="3. When ""DN"" (down one line) is entered, or down arrow on the keyboard is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,16,0)="pressed to navigate down a line in ListManager on the OP Medications profile"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,17,0)="screen, a message states that ""DN is not a valid selection"".  NOIS:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,18,0)="WNY-0398-11862 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,20,0)="4. Restored functionality that allows sites to use separate monitors to display"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,21,0)="the same display group data multiple times. In V.6.0, sites could start each"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,22,0)="monitor by selecting the same display group by using the Start Bingo Board"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,23,0)="Display [PSO BINGO START] option. Functionality in V.7.0 was inadvertently "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,24,0)="removed. When a site attempts to start multiple monitors the message that "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,25,0)="""Board has already been started!"" is displayed.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,27,0)="Sites that have bingo board setup to auto-start using a dedicated device will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,28,0)="not be allowed to start the same display group multiple times. This would"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,29,0)="result in a <Device Not Available> error message.  Routine: PSOBGMGR.  NOIS:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",19,1,30,0)="WNY-0398-12812.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,0)="22^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,0)="^^35^35^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,1,0)="1. This patch makes a change to the Barcode Batch Prescription Entry"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,2,0)="[PSO BATCH BARCODE] option. Prior to this patch, if Renewals were"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,3,0)="processed through this option, and if the first three prompts (Fill Date,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,4,0)="Mail/Window, and Queue/Suspend) were answered Today for Fill Date, Mail,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,5,0)="and Queue, any Consolidated Mail Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP) prescriptions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,6,0)="would print locally. This patch makes the change to suspend these"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,7,0)="prescriptions for CMOP."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,9,0)="2. This patch fixes a problem that can occur when processing two refills"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,10,0)="for one prescription at the same time, trying to queue the first one and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,11,0)="suspend the second one to a later date. If this is done, the label that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,12,0)="prints for the first refill will indicate that it is for the suspended"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,13,0)="refill, instead of the first refill. This patch corrects the problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,15,0)="3. This patch fixes an undefined error that can occur when processing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,16,0)="telephone refill requests for sites that use the Mumps Audiofax software."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,17,0)="The problem occurs because a required Outpatient Pharmacy site variable can"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,18,0)="possibly be killed in the Action Profiles. Then if the Mumps Audiofax"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,19,0)="telephone refill requests are processed, an error could occur."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,21,0)="4. A problem has been reported concerning the PSO EXPIRE PRESCRIPTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,22,0)="job. This is the daily job that sets prescriptions to an expired status"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,23,0)="the day after the expiration date. The job is initialized using the Expire"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,24,0)="Prescriptions [PSO EXPIRE INITIALIZE] option. A situation could occur"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,25,0)="where the last refill gets deleted if a label has printed and the fill has"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,26,0)="not yet been released. The refill should only get deleted if no label has"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,27,0)="printed for that prescription refill. This patch fixes the problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,29,0)="5. A problem has been reported by sites that involves lines overwriting"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,30,0)="one another on a terminal. This was caused by the Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,31,0)="version 7.0 package making a call to List Manager when the call should not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,32,0)="have been made. This patch corrects the problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,34,0)="6. This patch fixes an undefined error that can occur on the Bingo Board"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",20,1,35,0)="display, as a result of an invalid cross-reference."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,0)="24 SEQ #21^2990510^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,0)="^^38^38^2990510"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,1,0)="1. This patch makes it possible to exempt certain Ward Locations from the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,2,0)="Autocancel Rx's on Admission [PSO AUTOCANCEL1] option. When that job runs,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,3,0)="and it comes across a patient that is on a Ward Location designated as"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,4,0)="exempt from the Autocancel Rx's on Admission [PSO AUTOCANCEL1] option, the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,5,0)="prescriptions for that patient will not be canceled. To designate a Ward"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,6,0)="Location as exempt from this job, use the Site Parameter Enter/Edit [PSO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,7,0)="SITE PARAMETERS] option. Under the Outpatient System Parameters section of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,8,0)="that option, there is a field called EXEMPT WARD FROM AUTOCANCEL (#40.19),"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,9,0)="and here you can designate any number of Ward Locations as exempt from the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,10,0)="Autocancel Rx's on Admission [PSO AUTOCANCEL1] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,12,0)="2. This patch adds a Requesting PROVIDER prompt to the discontinue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,13,0)="and speed discontinue dialogue. When an order is discontinued, this new"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,14,0)="prompt will be asked after the Nature of Order prompt. The requesting"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,15,0)="provider information will be used to update the Computerized Patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,16,0)="Record System (CPRS) order. The CPRS order will now reflect the correct"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,17,0)="provider that requested the discontinue of the order. This new prompt"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,18,0)="will only be given when an order is discontinued through one of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,19,0)="the Discontinue ListMan actions, or the Discontinue Prescription(s) [PSO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,20,0)="C] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,22,0)="3. This patch fixes a problem that can occur when removing a prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,23,0)="from Hold in the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,24,0)="option. This problem can only occur for sites that are using vendor"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,25,0)="software to bill prescriptions for Tricare. When removing a prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,26,0)="from Hold, the software currently checks to see if the prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,27,0)="is eligible for Tricare billing, and can possibly resubmit the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,28,0)="prescription for Tricare billing. A problem can occur if it continues"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,29,0)="to be rejected by Tricare. This causes the prescription to remain in a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,30,0)="Hold status, and there is no way to print a filling label for that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,31,0)="prescription. After this patch is installed, any prescription that is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,32,0)="removed from Hold will not automatically go through the Tricare process."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,33,0)="These prescriptions will either print locally or suspend. Then it would"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,34,0)="be possible to manually resubmit billing for that prescription, but now"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,35,0)="a filling label will first print for these prescriptions."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,37,0)="4.This patch fixes an undefined error that can occur when trying to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",21,1,38,0)="reinstate a prescription for a deceased patient."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,0)="9 SEQ #22^2990602^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,0)="^^35^35^2990602"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,1,0)="1. This patch provides new functionality for the Return Medication to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,2,0)="Stock [PSO RETURNED STOCK] option and the Delete a Prescription [PSO RXDL]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,3,0)="option. In the Return Medication to Stock [PSO RETURNED STOCK] option,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,4,0)="prescriptions that have been filled and released at the Consolidated Mail"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,5,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP) can now be returned to stock. In the Delete a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,6,0)="Prescription [PSO RXDL] option, prescriptions that have been filled and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,7,0)="released at the CMOP can now be marked for deletion. In addition, if a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,8,0)="prescription has been released, you can now return that prescription to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,9,0)="stock and mark it for deletion from the Delete a Prescription [PSO RXDL]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,10,0)="option. Previously, you would have needed to go to the Return Medication"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,11,0)="to Stock [PSO RETURNED STOCK] option, return the medication to stock, then"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,12,0)="go back to the Delete a Prescription [PSO RXDL] option to mark the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,13,0)="prescription deleted."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,15,0)="2. This patch fixes a problem of a possible incorrect FILL DATE default"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,16,0)="when entering a new prescription in the Patient Prescription Processing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,17,0)="[PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option. If a past ISSUE DATE is entered, and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,18,0)="based on the other information entered for the prescription the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,19,0)="EXPIRATION DATE calculates to a past date, then the FILL DATE default"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,20,0)="could be incorrect."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,22,0)="3. This patch makes changes to the data returned from Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,23,0)="Pharmacy detailed in DBIA 1878. Piece 16 of the zero node will contain the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,24,0)="patient name. Also, the DFN input variable is now optional, but a null"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,25,0)="value must be passed in if the DFN is not defined."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,27,0)="4. This patch makes a change to return Fill Date information to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,28,0)="Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) for display purposes."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,30,0)="5. This patch fixes an error that can occur when finishing an order"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,31,0)="entered through Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS), and that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,32,0)="order was entered as a complex order with multiple sets of instructions."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,34,0)="6. This patch fixes a problem of partial prescriptions not being released"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",22,1,35,0)="when that same prescription has a regular fill in suspense."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,0)="23 SEQ #23^2990622^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,0)="^^41^41^2990622"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,1,0)="1. This patch contains new DEA requirements for Clozapine dispensing.  The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,2,0)="new requirements are that there will be two tests instead of one required"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,3,0)="for Clozapine dispensing.  The two tests are White Blood Count (WBC) and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,4,0)="Absolute Neutrophil Count (ANC). The ANC test at some sites is called the,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,5,0)="%Neutrophil, %Neut, %Gran or something to this effect.  The exact name of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,6,0)="this test should be coordinated with Lab Service.  The %Neutrophil results"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,7,0)="used in this order check are the result returned by the automated lab"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,8,0)="instruments and not the manual entry. The specimen collection sample must be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,9,0)="identified as well, in most cases that will be blood.  The %Neutrophil test"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,10,0)="will be one test within the CBC panel."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,12,0)="After the installation of this patch the Drug Enter/Edit [PSS DRUG"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,13,0)="ENTER/EDIT] option in the Pharmacy Data Management (PDM) package should be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,14,0)="used to add this second test to the drug(s) that are identified as being"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,15,0)="used for Clozapine/Clozaril dispensing.  For existing entries in the DRUG"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,16,0)="file (#50) the first test WBC should already be defined from previous setup"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,17,0)="of identifying drugs for Clozapine/Clozaril dispensing.  For new drugs added"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,18,0)="for Clozapine/Clozaril dispensing both the WBC and ANC test must be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,19,0)="identified. If this second test is not added the user will get a message"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,20,0)="when trying to dispense a Clozapine Rx, ""Invalid Number of Tests (1) entered."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,22,0)=" Cannot dispense Clozapine Prescription. You must have TWO test identified"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,23,0)="for this drug.  Rx Deleted."""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,25,0)="Though this patch allows the dispensing of 14-day Clozapine/Clozaril Rxs,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,26,0)="the eligibility of the patient is determined by the Mental Health package."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,27,0)="There is no setup required by Outpatient Pharmacy.  If you have a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,28,0)="question about a patient's eligibility, please contact The National"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,29,0)="Clozapine Center."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,31,0)="These two patches are required, Mental Health patch YS*5.01*47, and PDM"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,32,0)="patch PSS*1*19."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,34,0)="2.  This patch corrects a problem where Rx's with controlled substances"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,35,0)="are being given a maximum expiration date of one year instead on six months."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,36,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,37,0)="3.  This patch corrects a problem reported in MON-0199-51550.  The problem"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,38,0)="is that when using the Speed Refill action if the Rx's selected are all"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,39,0)="expired no message is given to the user that the Rx's selected are expired."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",23,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,0)="25 SEQ #24^2990719^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,0)="^^25^25^2990719"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,1,0)="This patch resolves several issues.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,3,0)="1. The routine PSOAMIS0 used the variable DFN to represent a value"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,4,0)="other than the internal file number in the PATIENT file (#2). This variable"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,5,0)="name was changed to PSODFN to comply with standards.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,7,0)="2. It fixes a potential error when running the nightly tasked job, Compile"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,8,0)="AMISData (NIGHT JOB) [PSO AMIS COMPILE].  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,10,0)="3. The site parameter EDIT PATIENT DATA is not working properly."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,11,0)="When set to ""YES"", it should prohibit editing SSN and DOB. The input"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,12,0)="templates [PSO OUTPT] and [PSO OUTPTA] contained in the PATIENT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,13,0)="file (#2) have been updated.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,15,0)="4. After archiving prescriptions, the archived prescription number may be "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,16,0)="reused. This had created the potential to have two series of prescriptions "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,17,0)="using the same number.  Added check for new prescriptions for existing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,18,0)="numbers. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,21,0)="5. Two erroneous ^DD nodes are deleted from the PHARMACY PATIENT "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,22,0)="file (#55).  They are ^DD(55,0,""P"") and ^DD(55,0,""PS"").  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",24,1,25,0)="6. Updated the DD(52,0,""ID"",6) with correct reference to new field location.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,0)="26 SEQ #25^2990914^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,0)="^^34^34^2990914"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,1,0)="1. This patch fixes the problem of the allergy warning label document"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,2,0)="possibly printing prior to the filling label for a prescription,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,3,0)="when there is no allergy entered to that drug for the patient."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,5,0)="2. Currently, when entering a new prescription, a non-numeric entry can"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,6,0)="be entered for the quantity. This patch makes a leading numeric required"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,7,0)="for the quantity."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,9,0)="3. This patch makes a change to the Exempt Rx Patient Status from"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,10,0)="Copayment [PSOCP EXEMPTION] option. When setting a status from No to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,11,0)="Yes, a warning will now be given, and a mail message will be sent to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,12,0)="all PSORPH key holders informing them of this change."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,14,0)="4. This patch fixes a problem of messages not being exchanged successfully"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,15,0)="between Outpatient Pharmacy and an external application. This problem"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,16,0)="would occur for sites that have the EXTERNAL INTERFACE site parameter set"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,17,0)="to 1 (SEND ALL ORDERS AND PRINT LABEL), 2 (SEND ALL ORDERS AND DON'T PRINT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,18,0)="LABEL), or 3 (SEND MARKED ORDERS AND DON'T PRINT). Also fixed some"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,19,0)="formatting problems with reports related to the external interface"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,20,0)="functions."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,22,0)="5. This patch fixes a problem of an invalid Initiator of Activity being"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,23,0)="stored and displayed in the ACTIVITY LOG REASON (#53.3) file for an edit"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,24,0)="of a prescription."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,26,0)="6. This patch fixes an undefined error that could occur if an invalid"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,27,0)="barcode is entered while in the Change Suspense Date [PSO PNDCHG] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,29,0)="7.  This patch corrects a problem that can occur when entering a refill"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,30,0)="date for a refillable controlled substance prescription. The date range"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,31,0)="displayed should be the issue date to the expiration date, normally"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,32,0)="followed by a default of Today. The date range ending date will sometimes"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,33,0)="show beyond six months, which is invalid for a refillable controlled"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",25,1,34,0)="substance prescription. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,0)="27 SEQ #26^2990914^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,0)="^^81^81^2990914"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,1,0)="1) This patch, in conjunction with patches from Inpatient Medications and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,2,0)="Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS), will enhance the way that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,3,0)="locking is done at the order level and at the patient level among these"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,4,0)="packages. Anytime an order is acted upon in the Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,5,0)="package, locks will now take place within the Outpatient Pharmacy package"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,6,0)="at that order level, and the order will also be locked in CPRS. A Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,7,0)="Patient lock has also been created. When actions on orders take place in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,8,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy that could result in a change in the order, all other"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,9,0)="Pharmacy users will be locked out of acting on any orders for that same"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,10,0)="patient. Additionally, CPRS users will no longer be locked out of entering"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,11,0)="orders for a patient, when orders for that patient are being finished in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,12,0)="the Outpatient Pharmacy package."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,14,0)="2) A change has been made in the messaging that takes place when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,15,0)="prescriptions are released or returned to stock. This change will not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,16,0)="effect the Outpatient Pharmacy user."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,18,0)="3) This patch fixes a problem when a prescription is Renewed, and the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,19,0)="provider renewing the prescription required a cosigner when the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,20,0)="prescription that is being renewed was originally entered, but no longer"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,21,0)="requires a cosigner. The cosigning physician was being carried over to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,22,0)="new prescription, and printing on the Action Profile, even though the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,23,0)="provider no longer required a cosigner. This patch will fix this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,25,0)="4) A problem was reported that involves the prescription numbering"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,26,0)="sequence. If a prescription is entered for a controlled substance, then"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,27,0)="the drug is edited to a non-controlled substance after answering ""No"" to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,28,0)="the ""Is this Correct"" prompt, then the prescription will still be assigned"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,29,0)="a number from the controlled substance sequence of prescription numbers."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,30,0)="This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,32,0)="5) This patch corrects a problem of the Non-Formulary warning printing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,33,0)="next to the dispense drug on the order screen in Outpatient Pharmacy, at"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,34,0)="times when it is not appropriate to print. This can result from an order"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,35,0)="being entered with a dispense drug that has a valid Non-Formulary status,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,36,0)="then that drug is edited to a drug that should not have a Non-Formulary"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,37,0)="status, but the Non-Formulary indicator still prints next to the dispense"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,38,0)="drug."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,40,0)="6) This patch corrects a problem of a user in CPRS being able to enter a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,41,0)="refill request that comes to the Outpatient Pharmacy package, even if the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,42,0)="refill request is beyond the expiration date of the prescription."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,44,0)="7) This patch corrects a problem that can occur in the Complete Orders"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,45,0)="from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] option for sites with multiple CPRS ordering"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,46,0)="institutions. At the ""Select CPRS ORDERING INSTITUTION"" prompt, sometimes"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,47,0)="the default will not be accepted if the user enters return. The user is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,48,0)="forced to type in the institution name. This patch corrects the problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,50,0)="8) This patch will bring back the functionality of doing drug interaction"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,51,0)="checks on Renewals."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,53,0)="9) This patch fixes a problem encountered when finishing orders in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,54,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy that were entered through CPRS before the day the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,55,0)="order is finished. These orders were being treated as future fills and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,56,0)="being suspended, since the order had been entered on a previous day"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,57,0)="through CPRS. This patch makes a change where these will no longer"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,58,0)="be seen as future fills, as long as the order is being filled for today."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,60,0)="10) This patch addresses an issue that occurs when removing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,61,0)="a prescription from a pharmacy hold status. Prior to this patch, this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,62,0)="action would always generate a label request, regardless of whether or not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,63,0)="the last fill of the prescription had been released. This patch makes a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,64,0)="change to not print a label when removing a prescription from hold if the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,65,0)="last fill of the prescription has been released."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,67,0)="11) When editing the Drug of a prescription, if the new Drug is matched"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,68,0)="to the same Pharmacy Orderable Item, and there are synonyms in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,69,0)="Pharmacy Orderable Item file (#50.7) that contain numbers in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,70,0)="synonym name, it is possible that after editing the Drug, the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,71,0)="Pharmacy Orderable Item will change to an incorrect Pharmacy Orderable"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,72,0)="Item. This patch corrects the problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,74,0)="12) Currently, a prescription that is on Provider Hold should not be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,75,0)="acted upon through the Outpatient Pharmacy package. If you are entering a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,76,0)="new prescription and get a duplicate drug or duplicate class check on"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,77,0)="a prescription that is on provider hold, you are currently able"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,78,0)="to discontinue the prescription that is on provider hold. This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,79,0)="prevent that prescription on provider hold from being discontinued, so the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,80,0)="new prescription entry will not be allowed, since the discontinue action"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",26,1,81,0)="is not allowed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,0)="30 SEQ #27^2991210^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,0)="^^49^49^2991210"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,1,0)="1. This patch fixes a problem that can occur when editing a prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,2,0)="that is suspended for local filling. If the patient is flagged as DO NOT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,3,0)="MAIL in the MAIL field (#.03) of the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55), and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,4,0)="that suspended prescription is edited, it can possibly be removed from"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,5,0)="local suspense and suspended for Consolidated Mail Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,6,0)="(CMOP), even though the patient is flagged as DO NOT MAIL."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,8,0)="2. On Outpatient Pharmacy labels, if a patient is flagged as YES in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,9,0)="the CNH CURRENT field (#148) of the PATIENT file (#2), then the text"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,10,0)="Mfg______Exp______ will print on the labels after the quantity and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,11,0)="dispense unit. The patch makes a change to also look at the COMMUNITY"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,12,0)="NURSING HOME field (#40) of the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55), so if a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,13,0)="patient is flagged as YES in either of these 2 fields, the text"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,14,0)="Mfg_____Exp_____, will print on the labels."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,16,0)="3. This patch fixes a problem that can occur when a pending renewal order"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,17,0)="from Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) is discontinued by Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,18,0)="without renewing the original order. If this occurs, and that same"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,19,0)="original order is renewed again in CPRS, the user in CPRS will receive a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,20,0)="message saying that it is a duplicate renewal request, and will not be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,21,0)="allowed to process the renewal, even though the original renewal was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,22,0)="discontinued. This patch will allow that subsequent renewal to be sent to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,23,0)="pharmacy for completion. A post-init routine in this build will run that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,24,0)="will kill an invalid cross reference in the PENDING OUTPATIENT ORDERS file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,25,0)="(#52.41). This will allow for the functionality to be in place for all"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,26,0)="previous orders."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,28,0)="4. This patch fixes a problem of ""NKA"" sometimes printing when it"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,29,0)="shouldn't in the Allergy section of the labels, and in the HL7 message to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,30,0)="external applications."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,32,0)="5. A renewal problem can occur when renewing a prescription that has been"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,33,0)="canceled by the Autocancel Rx's on Admission [PSO AUTOCANCEL1] option. If"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,34,0)="that canceled prescription was never filled, then the new prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,35,0)="could be suspended too far in the future. This patch corrects the problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,37,0)="6. This patch fixes an undefined error that can occur in the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,38,0)="Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option, when viewing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,39,0)="the medication profile. The error would only occur for a drug name that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,40,0)="is greater than 40 characters in length, which is prohibited by the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,41,0)="nationally exported data dictionaries."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,43,0)="7. This patch fixes a problem of a prescription label printing for a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,44,0)="refill when it should not print. If a refill is processed for a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,45,0)="prescription and the label is queued to print, and that refill is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,46,0)="deleted before the label prints, a label will print for the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,47,0)="last fill documented in the prescription. This patch changes the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,48,0)="functionality to not print a label for a prescription if the refill"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",27,1,49,0)="associated with the label request is deleted before the label prints."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,0)="32 SEQ #28^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,0)="^^89^89^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,1,0)="1) E3R #12579: If an edit is done on a pending order, which results in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,2,0)="creation of a new order, the following text will be automatically entered in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,3,0)="the REMARKS field (#12) of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52), ""CPRS Order #nnnn"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,4,0)="Edited."" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,6,0)="2) This patch corrects a problem that allows pharmacy technicians to finish"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,7,0)="prescription medication orders from Computerize Patient Record System (CPRS)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,8,0)="The problem was that if a site did not have the site parameter Verification"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,9,0)="field (#.12) set to yes, the prescription label printed without review by a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,10,0)="pharmacist.  If the Verification field (#.12) is set to no the pharmacy tech"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,11,0)="will not be able to finish medication orders from CPRS.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,13,0)="3) E3R #10287:  This E3R request was to move the actual discontinuation of a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,14,0)="prescription when a duplicate drug or class order check occurs."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,15,0)="Prescriptions will no longer be discontinued when the user says yes to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,16,0)="discontinue duplicate drugs or drug classes during new order entry but when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,17,0)="the user answers yes to the prescription is correct.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,19,0)="4) Modified software to allow medication orders put on hold through CPRS to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,20,0)="be discontinued by Outpatient Pharmacy.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,22,0)="5) E3R #11810: The name of the printer device shall be displayed at the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,23,0)="label prompt along with an additional action of 'CHANGE PRINTER'. The same "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,24,0)="functionality as provided by the Change Label Printer [PSO CHANGE PRINTER] "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,25,0)="option will be used.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,27,0)="6) E3R #11658: The existence of a release date shall be used to determine "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,28,0)="whether the fill date for the original or refill is deleted or retained.  If"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,29,0)="the original fill for a prescription has been released, the fill date will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,30,0)="not be deleted when put on hold. The fill date will be shown as the last"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,31,0)="fill date. If the original fill has not been released the current"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,32,0)="functionality will be retained and the fill date deleted. The same will hold"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,33,0)="true for refills.  If the last refill has been released when a prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,34,0)="is placed on hold, that fill shall be retained as the last fill. If the last"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,35,0)="refill has not been released, the prior fill date will be used.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,37,0)="7) E3R #11294: The speed renewing functionality will be modified to: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,38,0)=" a. Remove the DAYS SUPPLY and # of Refill prompts from the speed renew "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,39,0)="process.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,40,0)=" b. The original Rx days supply, # of refills and quantity values will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,41,0)="used as defaults for the prescriptions renewed through the SPEED RENEW"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,42,0)="actions.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,44,0)="8) This patch corrects a problem where provider comment from a finished "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,45,0)="prescription medication order could be carried over to a subsequent "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,46,0)="prescription medication order.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,48,0)="9) E3R # 11309: There is a future development project that involves both "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,49,0)="Pharmacy and CPRS medication ordering that should address the inaccurate "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,50,0)="calculation of the days supply. In the meantime, in order to help determine"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,51,0)="the appropriate value for the DAYS SUPPLY field (#8) and to somewhat help "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,52,0)="distinguish what was entered by the provider versus pharmacy software"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,53,0)="defaults, pharmacy software will be modified to show the number of refills"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,54,0)="entered by the provider. Below the number of refills prompt displayed on the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,55,0)="screen when finishing an order a statement such as (11 refills ordered by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,56,0)="provider) will be also displayed.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,58,0)="10) A problem was reported when finishing orders by Clinic or Clinic Sort"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,59,0)="Group in the Complete Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] option. If a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,60,0)="patient has a pending order for the Clinic or Clinic Sort Group chosen, and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,61,0)="that order is discontinued, the Patient Information screen would still"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,62,0)="appear for that patient, even though there are no orders to finish. This"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,63,0)="patch resolves the problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,64,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,65,0)="11) This patch corrects a potential problem of duplicate prescriptions. The "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,66,0)="problem can occur when variables are not cleaned up preventing duplicate"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,67,0)="order checks from occurring.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,69,0)="12)  Corrected a problem when a duplicate drug class has been entered and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,70,0)="the other duplicate has been put on provider hold. User is not prompted to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,71,0)="discontinue provider held prescription.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,73,0)="13)  E3R #12827:  This E3R request that only numeric quantities be allowed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,74,0)="when finishing orders from CPRS.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,76,0)="14)  E3R 12850:  This E3R requests that functionality be added to allow the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,77,0)="inactivation of outpatient divisions.  A new field, INACTIVE DATE (#2004),"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,78,0)="will be used to inactive outpatient divisions in the OUTPATIENT SITE file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,79,0)="(#59).  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,81,0)="15)  A new field, DAYS TO PULL SUSPENDED CS CMOP field (#3.1), in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,82,0)="OUTPATIENT SITE file (#59) will be installed with patch.  This field will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,83,0)="used with future CMOP functionality.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,85,0)="16)  This patch corrects a possible null subscript error when marking"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,86,0)="non-verified prescriptions as deleted."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,88,0)="17) This patch corrects a possible subscript error when finishing orders"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",28,1,89,0)="from CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,0)="28 SEQ #29^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,0)="^^36^36^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,1,0)=" 1. This patch corrects the problems with the Cost Management Cost compile"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,2,0)=" that was enhanced in PSO*7*20. The nightly cost compile job was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,3,0)=" calculating the averages incorrectly."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,5,0)=" 2. In Drug Costs by Division [PSO COST BY DIVISION], this patch fixes the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,6,0)=" REQUESTS column that was showing the same figure for all divisions (which"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,7,0)=" was the total patient count of the pharmacy), instead of breakdown by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,8,0)=" divisions by introducing a new piece in File# 50.9006."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,9,0)=" The sort and print templates PSO COST STAT, are also sent out with this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,10,0)=" patch as the print template is modified to accommodate this new piece."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,12,0)=" 3. This patch fixes a possible undefined variable error that may occur"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,13,0)=" during Bingo Board Display."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,15,0)=" 4. This patch fixes a possible stack overflow error of a local variable"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,16,0)=" array by using the ^TMP global."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,18,0)=" 5. This patch fixes a problem where patients were not being registered"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,19,0)=" completely into the Clozapine program."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,21,0)=" 6. In the Monthly Rx Cost Compilation [PSO COSTMONTH] option, ""the AL"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,22,0)=" cross reference node is used for accumulating cost related information."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,23,0)=" There are times this node has more than one record logged for the same"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,24,0)=" date and time. This patch ensures that the cost compile routine does not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,25,0)=" skip any of the logged records."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,27,0)=" 7. In the Print Bingo Board Wait Time [PSO BINGO REPORT WAIT TIME]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,28,0)=" option, it was reported that the wait time for prescriptions filled at"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,29,0)=" 10:00am or released at 10:00am were showing very high wait time. This"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,30,0)=" patch corrects this problem by fixing the trailing zeroes to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,31,0)=" canonical value that is returned from the Fileman API call NOW^%DTC."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,33,0)=" 8. In the Print Bingo Board Statistics [PSO BINGO REPORT PRINT] option,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,34,0)=" it was reported that the divisions total page is generated when one or a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,35,0)=" range of divisions are selected, but does not generate the total page"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",29,1,36,0)=" when all divisions are selected. This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,0)="29 SEQ #30^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,0)="^^54^54^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,1,0)="1. For a drug marked for lab monitor, if text is entered for the results"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,2,0)="instead of a numeric value, the Action Profile reports the result as zero"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,3,0)="rather than displaying the text. This problem is fixed in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,5,0)="2. When  UNITS field (#6) of SITE/SPECIMEN sub-file (#100) of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,6,0)="LABORATORY TEST file (#60) is not defined, the Display Lab Tests and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,7,0)="Results [PSOLAB LIST] option displays ""Specimen data missing !!"". This"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,8,0)="patch fixes the problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,10,0)="3. Fixed a possible undefined variable error that may occur during the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,11,0)="renewal of certain drugs in certain sites. (START+15^PSORENW1:2,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,12,0)="%DSM-E-UNDEF, undefined variable PSODRUG(""DEA""))"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,14,0)="4. For clinics that had inactive sites, one particular management report"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,15,0)="was giving empty pages even though there were other active sites with"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,16,0)="data. This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,18,0)="5. Made data dictionary changes to the following fields in PRESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,19,0)="file (#52):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,20,0)="    a. UNIT PRICE OF DRUG field (#17)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,21,0)="    b. CURRENT UNIT PRICE OF DRUG field (#1.2) of REFILL sub-file (#52.1),"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,22,0)="    c. CURRENT UNIT PRICE OF DRUG field (#.042) of PARTIAL DATE sub-file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,23,0)="       (#52.2)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,25,0)="These fields currently set to the 99.999 format, need to be changed to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,26,0)="999.9999 format, in order to maintain the same format as that of PRICE PER"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,27,0)="DISPENSE UNIT field (#16) of the DRUG file (#50) which is of the format"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,28,0)="999.9999. During an original/refill/partial fill an exact unit cost will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,29,0)="be maintained in the respective fields without getting truncated. This"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,30,0)="change will also eliminate the possibility of reporting zero cost for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,31,0)="certain low cost dispensed items as reported in numerous NOISs."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,33,0)="This patch also makes a Data Dictionary change to the NDC field (#11), an "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,34,0)="unused field by Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0 package in REFILL sub-file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,35,0)="(#52.1) from piece 13 of node 0 to piece 3 of node 1. There is an optional"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,36,0)="background job that will move the data from its old location to its new"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,37,0)="location. The date/time is site selectable and can be queued to run during"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,38,0)="the installation of the patch or at another time by using the entry point"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,39,0)="NDCQ^PSOPOST1. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,41,0)="6. Fixed a possible undefined variable error (%DSM-I-ATLABEL,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,42,0)="START+2^PSOCST5:7) that may arise while using the OPTION: Provider by Drug"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,43,0)="Costs [PSO COST PROVIDER BY DRUG] on exiting using ""^"" in response to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,44,0)="""(Enter ^ to Halt)"" during viewing of the report on the screen."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,46,0)="7. When a medication information sheet is printed using the Rx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,47,0)="(Prescriptions) [PSO RX] option, under the Patient Prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,48,0)="Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option, Medication Profile, the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,49,0)="patient's name does not print on the medication sheet. (This fix is in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,50,0)="reference to an E3R# 12659)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,52,0)="8. A change has been made to the input transforms of the quantity fields"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,53,0)="of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52). The change will prevent alpha characters"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",30,1,54,0)="from being entered for quantity through the pharmacy options."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,0)="34 SEQ #31^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,0)="^^42^42^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,1,0)="1) This patch fixes a problem that can occur when processing refills"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,2,0)="in the Barcode Batch Prescription Entry [PSO BATCH BARCODE] option. The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,3,0)="patient record is sometimes getting locked during this process, and not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,4,0)="always getting unlocked. This patch makes the change to only lock at the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,5,0)="order level when processing refills in this option. When processing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,6,0)="renewals through this option, the lock will remain for the patient record,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,7,0)="and will also remain at the order level."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,9,0)="2) When pulling a prescription from suspense using the Pull Rx (OP)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,10,0)="Listman action, a problem can occur with the METHOD OF PICK-UP field"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,11,0)="(#35). If the routing is WINDOW, and no METHOD OF PICK-UP is entered, and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,12,0)="the prescription has a previous METHOD OF PICK-UP entered, the previous"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,13,0)="METHOD OF PICK-UP will print on the label, even though a METHOD OF PICK-UP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,14,0)="was not entered when pulling from suspense. This patch makes the change to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,15,0)="print whatever was entered when pulling from suspense, and if the prompt"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,16,0)="was bypassed, the METHOD OF PICK-UP will be deleted from the prescription,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,17,0)="and will not appear on the label."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,19,0)="3) When pulling a prescription from suspense, the fill date or refill"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,20,0)="date field is updated with the date that the pull action occurs. Then"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,21,0)="when that prescription is refilled, the next possible fill date is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,22,0)="calculated based on that last fill date. The problem occurs when the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,23,0)="label that is pulled from suspense is a reprint label. This patch makes"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,24,0)="the change to only update the fill date or refill date if the label"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,25,0)="being pulled from suspense is not a reprint label."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,27,0)="4) A problem can occur in the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,28,0)="BACKDOOR ORDERS] option when a reprint request is made for a prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,29,0)="that cannot be reprinted, such as an expired or discontinued prescription."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,30,0)="If other valid labels are also requested for the patient, the valid"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,31,0)="labels will sometimes not print. This patch resolves the problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,33,0)="5) This patch will modify the call that returns prescription information"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,34,0)="to Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS). The release date of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,35,0)="original fill is being added for display purposes in CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,37,0)="6) When processing refills through the Barcode Batch Prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,38,0)="Entry [PSO BATCH BARCODE] option, and when processing refills phoned"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,39,0)="in through the MUMPS AudioFax software, the patient name and last four"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,40,0)="digits of the SSN will display if the refills can't be processed because"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,41,0)="""Yes"" was the response for the ""Allow fills for inpatient and CNH?"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",31,1,42,0)="prompt, and the patient is an inpatient or is CNH Current."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,0)="35 SEQ #32^3000405^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,0)="^^18^18^3000405"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,1,0)="1. This patch corrects a problem when compiling the Health Summary component"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,2,0)="for Outpatient Pharmacy data.  With the new prescription statuses added for "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,3,0)="version 7 discontinued prescriptions were printing when they should not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,4,0)="have.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,6,0)="2. The CPRS Workgroup members requested that the Outpatient Pharmacy package"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,7,0)="provide the capability to backfill prescriptions for a date range into CPRS "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,8,0)="(only 18 months of prescriptions are backfilled upon installation of CPRS). "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,9,0)="This will be an optional tool for sites and none of the orders will be able"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,10,0)="to be acted upon (renew, refill, etc.).  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,11,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,12,0)="A new option, Backfill Prescriptions to CPRS [PSO BACKFILL PRESCRIPTIONS]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,13,0)="will be distributed as a stand alone option and may be given to the user(s) "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,14,0)="responsible for backfilling prescriptions to CPRS.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,16,0)="3. This patch updates the View Prescriptions [PSO VIEW] option to include"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,17,0)="the provider comments and instructions from CPRS entered orders.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",32,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,0)="31 SEQ #33^3000405^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,0)="^^20^20^3000405"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,1,0)=" 1. When using the following cost related report options:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,2,0)="      Clinic Costs [PSO CLINIC COSTS]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,3,0)="      Division Costs by Drug [PSO DIV COSTS BY DRUG]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,4,0)="      Drug Costs [PSO DRUG COSTS]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,5,0)="      Drug Costs by Division [PSO COST BY DIVISION]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,6,0)="      Drug Costs by Division by Provider [PSO COST DIVISION BY PROVIDER]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,7,0)="      Drug Costs by Provider [PSO COST BY PROVIDER]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,8,0)="      Patient Status Costs [PSO COST BY PATIENT STATUS]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,9,0)="      Provider by Drug Costs [PSO COST PROVIDER BY DRUG]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,10,0)="      Provider Costs [PSO COST PER PROVIDER]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,12,0)=" it was reported that when a period was specified in different date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,13,0)=" formats (i.e., MMYY or MMDDYY) of any past months then differing reports"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,14,0)=" were being produced. This patch fixes this problem. This patch also"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,15,0)=" enhances the routines to use common calls, improves the output formats,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,16,0)=" and enhances the user interactive help messages. A new routine named"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,17,0)=" PSOCSTX contains all the common calls."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,19,0)=" 2. This patch fixes the High Cost Rx Report [PSO HI COST] order sequence"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",33,1,20,0)=" so that it generates reports based on the release date order sequence."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,0)="36 SEQ #34^3000501^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,0)="^^73^73^3000501"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,3,0)="1) This patch fixes a problem of a patient possibly having two active"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,4,0)="prescriptions for the same drug. If two Outpatient Pharmacy users have"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,5,0)="the same patient profile on the screen in the Patient Prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,6,0)="Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option, the first user can enter a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,7,0)="prescription then exit the option, then the second user can enter a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,8,0)="prescription for the same drug and not get the duplicate drug check,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,9,0)="thereby creating two active prescriptions for the same drug. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,10,0)="ensures that in this case, the second user will get the duplicate drug"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,11,0)="check, and will only be allowed to continue if the first prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,12,0)="is discontinued."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,14,0)="2) This patch fixes a problem that can occur when using the Pull Early"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,15,0)="from Suspense [PSO PNDRX] option. If a specific prescription is pulled,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,16,0)="and the prescription number entered is also the same internal entry"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,17,0)="number for another prescription that is also suspended, the entry"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,18,0)="that matched the internal number will be pulled from suspense, instead"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,19,0)="of the entry that matched the external number. This patch fixes the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,20,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,22,0)="3) A problem has been reported with the Queue Background Jobs [PSO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,23,0)="AUTOQUEUE JOBS] option. There are times when some of the options that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,24,0)="this option presents for scheduling or re-scheduling will not appear. This"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,25,0)="patch fixes the problem, so now all of the options will appear for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,26,0)="scheduling or re-scheduling."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,28,0)="4) This patch addresses some problems that can occur when processing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,29,0)="two or more refills for the same prescription in the same ListMan"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,30,0)="session while using the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,31,0)="BACKDOOR ORDERS] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,33,0)=" a) If two or more refills are requested for the same prescription and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,34,0)="    none of the fills are auto-suspended, and the labels are queued to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,35,0)="    print, all of the labels will indicate that it is a label for the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,36,0)="    last fill, and that last fill information will print on the label."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,37,0)="    This patch will fix this problem by printing the appropriate fill"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,38,0)="    information on the labels."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,40,0)=" b) If two or more refills are requested for the same prescription, and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,41,0)="    the last fill is auto-suspended prior to exiting the session, then"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,42,0)="    ""S"" for Suspend is entered at the label prompt, the fill that is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,43,0)="    currently suspended will be overwritten in suspense, and only that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,44,0)="    last fill will print from Suspense. With this patch, a warning will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,45,0)="    be given after ""S"" is entered at the label prompt for each duplicate"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,46,0)="    request, and the user will be given the opportunity to print each of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,47,0)="    those fills locally."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,49,0)=" c) If the first fill of a prescription is requested, and it does not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,50,0)="    get auto-suspended at the time of the request, but eventually will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,51,0)="    be auto-suspended for Consolidated Mail Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,52,0)="    (CMOP) upon exiting the session for that patient,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,53,0)="    and then another fill is requested and it is auto-suspended for CMOP,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,54,0)="    then upon exiting the session, the first fill request will then be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,55,0)="    auto-suspended for CMOP, overwriting the second request, and a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,56,0)="    fill will be bypassed. With this patch, the second fill will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,57,0)="    not be allowed, since the first fill will be auto-suspended for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,58,0)="    CMOP upon exiting the session."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,60,0)="5) When a prescription is renewed through Pharmacy, if the prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,61,0)="that is being renewed has a suspended refill that has not yet printed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,62,0)="from suspense, in addition to that prescription being marked discontinued,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,63,0)="that refill also gets deleted. If that same prescription would have been"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,64,0)="renewed through Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS), when that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,65,0)="renewal is finished in Pharmacy, the renewed prescription would be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,66,0)="marked discontinued, but the refill would not be deleted. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,67,0)="provides the functionality to delete the refill in this case, which"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,68,0)="makes it consistent with renewals initiated through Pharmacy."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,70,0)="6) When a prescription is discontinued, if that prescription was never"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,71,0)="filled locally, but filled only through CMOP, it's possible that when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,72,0)="viewing that discontinued prescription, the Last Fill Date is incorrect."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",34,1,73,0)="This patch resolves the problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,0)="33 SEQ #35^3000516^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,0)="^^94^94^3000516"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,1,0)="This patch is part of the CMOP - Controlled Substance Rxs enhancements."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,2,0)="It modifies functions within the Outpatient Pharmacy application to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,3,0)="support the transmission of controlled substance prescriptions to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,4,0)="Consolidated Mail Outpatient Pharmacy facilities."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,6,0)="This patch will be installed in conjunction with three other patches"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,7,0)="(PSX*2*23, PSD*3*21, and PSS*1*28). Refer to the CMOP - Controlled"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,8,0)="Substance Rxs Installation Guide for installation instructions. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,10,0)="The Installation Guide for the CMOP - Controlled Substance Rxs project can"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,11,0)="be obtained on the VISTA Consolidated Mail Outpatient   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,12,0)="Pharmacy web page.  The address is http://vista2.domain.ext/cmop/."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,14,0)="The Installation Guide is also available on the ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,15,0)="directory at one of the following Office ofInformation (OI) Field Offices."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,16,0)="The file name is CMOPCS_IG.PDF."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,17,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,18,0)=" OI FIELD OFFICE                FTP ADDRESS             DIRECTORY"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,19,0)=" ===============                ===========             ========="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,20,0)=" Albany                         152.127.1.5             anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,21,0)=" Hines                          152.129.1.110           anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,22,0)=" Salt Lake City                 152.131.2.1             anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,24,0)="NOTE: Since future patches may be dependent on this patch, it should be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,25,0)="installed even if you are not using the CMOP software or planning to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,26,0)="transmit controlled substances to the CMOP facilities.  The installation"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,27,0)="instructions will provide further guidance for this situation."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,30,0)="1. This patch adds Controlled Substance functionality to the Released and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,31,0)="Unreleased Prescription Report[PSO RELEASE REPORT]. The user is now also"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,32,0)="presented with sorting criteria to sort by:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,34,0)="'C'     'Controlled Substance Rxs Only'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,35,0)="'N'     'Non Controlled Substance Rxs only'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,36,0)="'B'     'Both Controlled Substance and Non Controlled Substance Rxs'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,38,0)="2. This patch adds a new menu option  CMOP Controlled Substance Rx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,39,0)="Dispense Report[PSO CMOP CS RX DISPENSE REPORT] as a part of the Output"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,40,0)="Reports [PSO OUTPUTS] menu of Outpatient Pharmacy. The user is prompted"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,41,0)="for criteria concerning:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,44,0)="[Single division sites will not see the following question.]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,45,0)="Print for (A)ll or a (S)ingle division? (A/S) S//"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,47,0)="Select one of the following: 1//"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,48,0)="1. Sort by Release Date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,49,0)="2. Sort by Drug"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,50,0)="Start Date:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,51,0)="End Date:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,53,0)="The new report sorts by division and prints out the following fields:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,54,0)="Release date, RX #, Fill #, Drug, Patient with SSN(last four), CMOP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,55,0)="Status, and CMOP Facility."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,57,0)="PRESCRIPTION File (#52)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,59,0)="Release Date            RELEASED DATE/TIME (#31)        for Original RX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,60,0)="                        or"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,61,0)="                        REFILL multiple (#52)           for Refills"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,62,0)="                        RELEASED DATE/TIME (#17)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,64,0)="RX #                    RX # (.01)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,66,0)="FILL #                  0                               for Original RX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,67,0)="                        IEN                             of refill for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,68,0)="Refills"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,70,0)="DRUG                    DRUG (#6)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,72,0)="Patient with SSN        PATIENT (#2)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,74,0)="CMOP Status             CMOP EVENT multiple (#400)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,75,0)="                        STATUS (#3)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,77,0)="CMOP Facility           CMOP EVENT multiple (#400)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,78,0)="                        TRANSMISSION NUMBER (#01) :"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,79,0)="                        CMOP TRANSMISSION FILE #550.2"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,80,0)="                        CMOP SYSTEM (#3)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,83,0)="3. This patch adds the display of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) CMOP EVENT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,84,0)="multiple (#400) fields CARRIER (#10) and PACKAGE ID (#11) to the View"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,85,0)="Prescriptions [PSO VIEW] option of Outpatient Pharmacy."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,87,0)="4. This patch also corrects the following problem reported."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,89,0)="Problem:        The CMOP Event Log in the View Prescriptions [PSO VIEW]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,90,0)="option displays the release of a previous event when the current even has"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,91,0)="no release date."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,92,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,93,0)="Resolution:     The code has been changed to clear the previous value and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",35,1,94,0)="display ""Not Released""  when the prescription is yet to be released."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,0)="37 SEQ #36^3000516^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,0)="^^30^30^3000516"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,1,0)=" 1. Site reports that inactive orderable items are showing up as a choice for "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,2,0)="the pharmacist when editing of verified or pending prescriptions.  It does not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,3,0)="even distinguish active/inactive.  This is creating confusion because the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,4,0)="pharmacist does not know which to choose.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,6,0)="2. In the Clozapine ordering software an invalid check is done to determine if"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,7,0)="the site is registered with the National Clozapine Center.  The fields, *SITE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,8,0)="DEA NUMBER (#1) and *SITE (NATIONAL NAME) (#2), in the OUTPATIENT SITE file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,9,0)="(#59) are marked for deletion and should not be used.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,11,0)="3. This patch corrects a problem where pharmacists without the PSOLOCKCLOZ key"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,12,0)="are not allowed to override Clozapine medication orders from CPRS when there"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,13,0)="are no recent lab data available.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,15,0)="4. This patch corrects a problem when renewing prescriptions with cosigning "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,16,0)="providers and the cosigning provider has changed from the previous renewed "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,17,0)="prescription.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,19,0)="5. This patch corrects a problem where the Nature of Order retains an incorrect"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,20,0)="default  when discontinuing active orders while using the Copy (OP) [PSO LM BACKDOOR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,21,0)="COPY] action.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,23,0)="6. This patch adds an order check for valid providers when the Copy (OP) [PSO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,24,0)="LM BACKDOOR COPY] action.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,26,0)="7. This patch corrects a problem when using the Discontinue Prescription(s) "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,27,0)="[PSO C] option to discontinue individual prescriptions.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,29,0)="8. This patch corrects a possible %DSM-E-NUMBER, ILLEGAL NUMBER error.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",36,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,0)="39 SEQ #38^3000612^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,0)="^^38^38^3000612"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,1,0)="1) This patch will add  functionality to the drug/class orders check to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,2,0)="display the CMOP status of an Rx when entering new Rxs.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,4,0)="2) This patch corrects a problem where an incorrect CMOP status is displayed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,5,0)="next to the Release date on the order display screen. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,7,0)="CMOP Utilities      Option name:  PSO SUCMOP MENU "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,9,0)="This menu will contain utilities to help the sites re-suspend those Rxs that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,10,0)="was suspended locally instead of transmission to CMOP.  PSO*7*39.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,12,0)="'List of Rxs with CMOP Drugs Printed From Suspense'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,13,0)="     Option name: PSO SUCMOP "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,14,0)="PRINT REPORT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,15,0)="This utility will print a report of everything that has printed "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,16,0)="locally that has a CMOP drug.  This report is by start and end dates.  The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,17,0)="report will list the Rx#, patient name, date printed from suspense, and the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,18,0)="drug.  This report is printed by the division you have signed in under. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,19,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,20,0)="     PSO*7*39."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,22,0)="'Re-Suspend Printed Rxs with CMOP Drugs'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,23,0)="     Option name: PSO SUCMOP RE-SUSLOCALCMOPPRI"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,24,0)="This utility will allow sites to re-suspend those Rxs that list on the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,25,0)="List of Rxs with CMOP Drugs Printed From Suspense report [PSO SUCMOP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,26,0)="PRINT REPORT].  This utility will re-suspend to the date that it was originally"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,27,0)="suspended to.  It should not be necessary to edit the suspended date  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,28,0)="because all Rxs queued for CMOP transmission will be transmitted."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,29,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,30,0)="     PSO*7*39"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,32,0)="'Unprinted/Non-Transmitted Rxs Re-Suspend'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,33,0)="     Option name: PSO SUCMOP RESUSPENDNOTPRI"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,34,0)="This utility will allow sites to re-suspend everything that has not printed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,35,0)="and not already queued for CMOP.  This utility can be queued to run in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,36,0)="background or while you wait. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,37,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",37,1,38,0)="     PSO*7*39"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,0)="40 SEQ #39^3000711^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,0)="^^42^42^3000711"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,1,0)="1) In V. 6.0 of Outpatient Pharmacy when a medication was returned to stock "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,2,0)="for a refill (nothing has really changed for original fill), the patient "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,3,0)="essentially lost that refill. In v. 7.0 this was fixed for refills, so that "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,4,0)="when a refill is returned to stock, the refill is deleted.  The problem is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,5,0)="the Controlled Substances package is not aware of the deletion.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,7,0)="A patch is to be released by both the Outpatient Pharmacy and Controlled "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,8,0)="Substance (PSD*3*24) packages. The Outpatient Pharmacy portion of the patch "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,9,0)="will send notification to the Controlled Substances package each time an "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,10,0)="prescription is returned to stock.  This functionality becomes fully"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,11,0)="functional when PSD*3*24 is installed.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,13,0)="2) With the release of PSO*7*32, functionality was added to allow the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,14,0)="inactivating of Outpatient Pharmacy divisions in the OUTPATIENT SITE file "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,15,0)="(#59).  The DIC(""S"") that was added prevented these inactive divisions from "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,16,0)="selection when processing Audiofax prescriptions.  This patch will allow "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,17,0)="inactive divisions to be selected when processing Audiofax fill requests. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,19,0)="For this part of the patch to be completely functional the latest version "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,20,0)="of VEXREX must be installed.  Please see PSO*7*38 for details."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,22,0)="3) With the installation of V. 7.0 of the Outpatient Pharmacy package, the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,23,0)="background utility, Expire Prescriptions [PSO EXPIRE PRESCRIPTIONS], that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,24,0)="automatically expires prescriptions daily was not queued to run at many"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,25,0)="sites. Because this utility was not queued, prescriptions with a status"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,26,0)="of active were showing on the Orders tab in CPRS option and on some"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,27,0)="printouts when they should actually show as expired. A new option Manual"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,28,0)="Auto Expire Rxs [PSO MANUAL AUTO EXPIRE] is added to the Maintenance "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,29,0)="(Outpatient Pharmacy) [PSO MAINTENANCE] menu option. This new option"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,30,0)="allows sites to back expire all prescriptions from the date Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,31,0)="Pharmacy package V. 7.0 was installed until the current date minus one day"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,32,0)="(T-1)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,34,0)="4) When printng the Action Profile (132 COLUMN PRINTOUT) [PSO ACTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,35,0)="PROFILE], to the screen the screen pauses and breaks do not work"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,36,0)="correctly. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,38,0)="5) When printing the Action Profile (132 COLUMN PRINTOUT) [PSO ACTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,39,0)="PROFILE] using the entry point DFN^PSOSD1 the header text states that the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,40,0)="profile is printing for the last 45 days when it is actually printing for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,41,0)="120 days. This patch corrects the header text to 120 days which is the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",38,1,42,0)="correct number of days that the profile is being printed for."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,0)="47 SEQ #41^3000824^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,0)="^^24^24^3000824"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,1,0)="1. It was reported that patient instruction information is appearing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,2,0)="randomly on prescriptions that were created through the back door. This"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,3,0)="was found to be due to some of the variables not getting killed prior to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,4,0)="using the option Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS]."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,5,0)="This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,7,0)="2. When a prescription label is requested, and if between the time it was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,8,0)="requested and the time the label actually prints it got discontinued or"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,9,0)="it was put on hold, the label does not get printed.  Also when a new"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,10,0)="prescription is filled and the user enters ""^"" at the label prompt thus"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,11,0)="terminating the label print process. This patch resolves these issues by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,12,0)="creating new activity logs in the respective prescription entry."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,14,0)="3. With the release of PSO*7*40 an interface was added for the Controlled"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,15,0)="Substance package (PSD*3*24).  This interface sends notification to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,16,0)="Controlled Substance package when a fill, refill or partial is returned"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,17,0)="to stock.  It was discovered that the interface was done incorrectly and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,18,0)="caused an undefined error.  The interface was added to the routine"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,19,0)="PSORESK. This patch corrects the problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,21,0)="4. Selecting 'HOLD' at the label prompt for a mail prescription with a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,22,0)="CMOP drug receives a reply of ""HAS BEEN SUSPENDED FOR CMOP UNTIL xxxx""."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,23,0)="This patch ensures that the 'HOLD' process prevents the Rx going into"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",39,1,24,0)="CMOP."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,0)="48 SEQ #42^3000905^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,0)="^^21^21^3000905"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,1,0)="1) When the Print a PMI Sheet [PSNPMIS PRINT] option is selected"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,2,0)="immediately after using the Patient Prescription Processing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,3,0)="[PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option, the patient medication sheet that is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,4,0)="printed for a particular drug also has the name of the patient that was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,5,0)="previously accessed under the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,6,0)="BACKDOOR ORDERS] option. This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,8,0)="2) While selecting a certain patient related title during the progress"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,9,0)="notes entry when placing a medication order using the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,10,0)="Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option, it was erring out"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,11,0)="due to an 'Undefined PSOID' error. This patch carries a fix for this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,12,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,14,0)="3) The INACTIVATION DATE field (#7) of DRUG INTERACTION file (#56) is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,15,0)="being populated by Pharmacy Data Management module, Enter/Edit Local Drug"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,16,0)="Interaction [PSS INTERACTION LOCAL ADD] option, to inactivate a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,17,0)="particular set of drugs that was once set up as interactive. During the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,18,0)="order entry process when using Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,19,0)="BACKDOOR ORDERS] option, currently the drug-drug interaction by routine"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,20,0)="PSODGDGI does not check for this inactivation date. This patch ensures"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",40,1,21,0)="that the inactivation date is now being checked."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,0)="44 SEQ #43^3000905^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,0)="^^24^24^3000905"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,1,0)="1) When using the Detailed Allergy/ADR List action under the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,2,0)="Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option, there is a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,3,0)="possibility of getting a <STRLEN> (string too long) error when displaying"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,4,0)="the comments from the Adverse Reaction Tracking package. This patch fixes"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,5,0)="this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,7,0)="2) If the option Edit Prescriptions [PSO RXEDIT] is used to edit the SIG,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,8,0)="this function generates a new order. It was reported that the new order"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,9,0)="created had changed the dispensed drug totally. It had picked up the drug"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,10,0)="of the patient who was last accessed prior to this patient using the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,11,0)="option Complete Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH]. This could result in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,12,0)="dispensing the wrong drug to the patient. This problem was found to be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,13,0)="due to some of the variables not being cleaned up properly. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,14,0)="ensures that all such variables are killed appropriately."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,15,0)="NOISs SLC-0200-50488, NJH-0600-21694 and PRO-0700-10326"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,17,0)="3) When a new prescription was created using the option Patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,18,0)="Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS], it was reported that the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,19,0)="patient instruction was appearing randomly. This was the patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,20,0)="instruction of the patient who was last accessed prior to this patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,21,0)="using the option Complete Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH]. This again"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,22,0)="was due to some of the variables not being killed properly. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,23,0)="ensures that all such variables are killed. NOISs MAR-0500-21140 and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",41,1,24,0)="BIL-0700-31212"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",42,0)="45^3000905^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",42,1,0)="^^7^7^3000905"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",42,1,1,0)="PSO*7*45 provides an API for the Clinical Reminders package.  The API"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",42,1,2,0)="provides patient and prescription information, based on a specified date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",42,1,3,0)="range and a specified list of medications, as it relates to the Hepatitis"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",42,1,4,0)="C Initiative. This patch will not affect users of the Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",42,1,5,0)="package. The PSOORAPI routine in patch PSO*7*45 provides an entry point"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",42,1,6,0)="that returns patient and prescription information in a ^TMP global to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",42,1,7,0)="Clinical Reminders package, based on the criteria passed into the call. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,0)="49 SEQ #45^3001004^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,0)="^^26^26^3001004"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,1,0)="1) When using the call DFN^PSOSD1 provided by DBIA #1281, an undefined"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,2,0)="variable error was reported (HD+11^PSOSD1:1, %DSM-E-UNDEF, undefined"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,3,0)="variable PSOBAR4). This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,5,0)="2) The INACTIVATION DATE field (#7) of DRUG INTERACTION file (#56) is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,6,0)="being populated by Pharmacy Data Management module, Enter/Edit Local Drug"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,7,0)="Interaction [PSS INTERACTION LOCAL ADD] option, to inactivate a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,8,0)="particular set of drugs that was once set up as interactive. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,9,0)="ensures that the call to the routine EN^PSOORDRG provided by DBIA #2190,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,10,0)="checks for the inactivation date before building the drug-drug"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,11,0)="interactions."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,13,0)="3) The following NOISs, CON-0300-11493, DUB-0400-31698, and NCH-0800-41306"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,14,0)="reported a problem when editing prescriptions in a certain sequence was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,15,0)="being saved with the name of the patient from a previously edited"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,16,0)="prescription. This error did not occur every time a prescription was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,17,0)="edited, but after using certain options and actions together where"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,18,0)="variables were not being cleaned up appropriately. With the release of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,19,0)="PSO*7*36 and PSO*7*37 to the field the name-changing problem has no longer"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,20,0)="been reported. In an effort to try an identify any possible prescriptions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,21,0)="where the patient name may have been changed inappropriately a new option,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,22,0)="Search For Mismatched Patient Orders [PSO RX SEARCH] will be sent out in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,23,0)="this patch. This new option will search the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,24,0)="produce a report with any possible problem prescriptions. This new option"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,25,0)="will not be attached to any menu, but can be assigned to anyone Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",43,1,26,0)="and IRM deems appropriate."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",44,0)="41 SEQ #46^3001027^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",44,1,0)="^^8^8^3001027"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",44,1,1,0)="The Outpatient Pharmacy package utilizes a field in the NOUN (#50.6066)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",44,1,2,0)="Subfile of the DOSAGE FORM (#50.606) File called NOUN. It is used to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",44,1,3,0)="build Possible Sigs for Outpatient orders entered through Computerized"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",44,1,4,0)="Patient Record System (CPRS). The use of that field will be expanded upon"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",44,1,5,0)="in the Pharmacy Ordering Enhancements project. The changes in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",44,1,6,0)="will not affect any of the current Outpatient Pharmacy functionality, but"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",44,1,7,0)="this patch will be a requirement of the Pharmacy Ordering Enhancements"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",44,1,8,0)="project."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,0)="50 SEQ #47^3001106^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,0)="^^16^16^3001106"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,1,0)="The following NOISs, NJH-0600-21694, SLC-0200-50488, PRO-0700-10326 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,2,0)=" reported the following problem.  When editing prescriptions in a certain "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,3,0)=" sequence they were being saved with the name of the patient from a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,4,0)=" previously edited prescription. This error did not occur every time "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,5,0)=" a prescription was edited, but after using certain options and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,6,0)=" actions together where variables were not being cleaned up appropriately.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,7,0)=" With the release of PSO*7*44 to the field, the drug name-changing problem "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,8,0)=" has no longer been reported.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,10,0)=" In an effort to try and identify any possible prescriptions where the drug "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,11,0)=" name may have been changed inappropriately, a new option Search for "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,12,0)=" Mismatched Drug Orders [PSO RX DRUG SEARCH] will be sent out in this patch.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,13,0)=" This new option will search the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) and produce a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,14,0)=" report with any possible problem prescriptions. This new option will not "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,15,0)=" be attached to any menu, but can be assigned to anyone Pharmacy and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",45,1,16,0)=" Information Resources Management (IRM) deems appropriate.   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",46,0)="53 SEQ #48^3001127^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",46,1,0)="^^10^10^3001127"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",46,1,1,0)="1.  Pharmacy Benefits Management (PBM) has requested that Technical"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",46,1,2,0)="Services develop a software patch that would disable the DRUG file (#50)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",46,1,3,0)="lookup by Internal Entry Number (IEN) during order entry"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",46,1,4,0)="processes.  The pharmacy software has always allowed IEN lookup and quick"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",46,1,5,0)="code lookups at the request of field users.  A quick code is a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",46,1,6,0)="user-defined synonym for a drug (i.e., A325->Acetaminophen 325mg Tab).  PBM"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",46,1,7,0)="provided guidance to VA Medical Centers in the past to not use low numbers"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",46,1,8,0)="for quick codes and to inactivate the first 50 entries in the drug file to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",46,1,9,0)="reduce the chances of error.  This patch would eliminate drug selection in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",46,1,10,0)="the ordering processes by entry of the IEN."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,0)="54 SEQ #49^3010202^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,0)="^^23^23^3010202"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,1,0)="1.  Clinical Reminders has requested the addition of the last RELEASED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,2,0)="DATE/TIME and the associated DAYS SUPPLY to the ^TMP(""PS"",$J,D0,0) node"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,3,0)="returned by the OCL^PSOORRL API. This will allow the developers to rewrite"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,4,0)="the way Clinical Reminders handles drug findings providing a speed-up of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,5,0)="somewhere between 5 and 10 times. IA 2400.  This patch addresses this issue."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,7,0)="2.  E3R #15111 has requested the SIG be expanded on the Health Summary "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,8,0)="Component RXOP. The RXOP component displays the shorthand version of the SIG"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,9,0)="for backdoor enter prescriptions.  The physicians would like to see the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,10,0)="expanded version of the SIG as displayed by the Action/Information Profile"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,11,0)="in Outpatient Pharmacy.  Many physicians do not know some of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,12,0)="abbreviations used by Pharmacy.  This patch addresses this issue.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,14,0)="3.  A problem has been reported that can occur when a pending Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,15,0)="order is transferred from Outpatient Pharmacy to Inpatient Medications in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,16,0)="Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS). It is possible that an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,17,0)="incorrect dispense drug is assigned to the order. This patch resolves the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,18,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,20,0)="4.  When selecting from the Drug file (#50), the user entered lowercase"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,21,0)="letters and was returned a drug based on the VA Drug Class lookup and was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,22,0)="not offered a choice of drugs starting with the letters entered.  This"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",47,1,23,0)="patch corrects this problem.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,0)="55 SEQ #50^3010227^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,0)="^^33^33^3010227"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,1,0)="1. When returning a prescription using Return Medication to Stock [PSO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,2,0)="RETURNED STOCK] option, it was reported that the NEXT POSSIBLE FILL field"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,3,0)="(#102) of PRESCRIPTION file (#52) was not getting reset to what it was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,4,0)="prior to the refill. This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,6,0)="2. When using Complete Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] option,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,7,0)="finishing orders entered through Computerized Patient Record System"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,8,0)="(CPRS), it was reported that the number of refills did not always update"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,9,0)="appropriately when Days Supply was edited. This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,10,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,12,0)="3. The Most Commonly Dispensed Drugs report obtained by using Commonly"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,13,0)="Dispensed Drugs [PSO COMMON] option, is skipping printing some sites even"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,14,0)="though there are valid records. This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,16,0)="4. A problem can occur when a prescription is placed on hold through the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,17,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy options, and then taken off hold through these same"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,18,0)="options. The prescription will not display correctly on the orders tab"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,19,0)="in CPRS. The order text is not being updated appropriately.  The status"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,20,0)="will show as active, but the word ""Hold"" will still show on the left side"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,21,0)="of the order text. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,23,0)="5. Additional data has been added to the routine that returns prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,24,0)="and drug information to the Integrated Billing package, for Tricare"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,25,0)="billing purposes. This has been done for future enhancements."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,27,0)="6. With the release of PSO*7*40 an interface was added for the Controlled "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,28,0)="Substances V. 3.0 package (PSD*3*24).  This interface sends notification"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,29,0)="to the Controlled Substances V. 3.0 package when a fill, refill or partial"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,30,0)="is returned to stock. This patch further enhances the interface by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,31,0)="preventing users who do not hold the PSDMGR key from updating vault"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,32,0)="balances and returning controlled substances to stock. For this new"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",48,1,33,0)="enhancement to be completely functional PSD*3*30 must be installed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,0)="57 SEQ #51^3010227^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,0)="^^18^18^3010227"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,1,0)="When editing the drug of a prescription using the Patient Prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,2,0)="Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option, the TMP(""PSORXDC"",$J) global"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,3,0)="created to store the duplicate prescription(s) that was requested to be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,4,0)="discontinued does not get deleted if either of the following action was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,5,0)="taken:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,6,0)="1. If the edit was terminated by up-arrowing at the point of accepting"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,7,0)="a new prescription."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,8,0)="2. If the dispensed drug is changed to a drug which already exists in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,9,0)="the medical profile (in another prescription) that is tied to the same"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,10,0)="orderable item with active/suspended status."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,11,0)="These occurrences are very rare and it could lead to the following:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,12,0)="1. As reported in NOIS MAN-1200-11563, the patient profile could change"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,13,0)="to that of another patient and result in dispensing drugs to the wrong"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,14,0)="patient (action 1 above)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,15,0)="2. As reported in NOIS MAN-0101-10680, it could end up patients having"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,16,0)="duplicate drugs in their medical profile (action 2 above)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,17,0)="This patch ensures that the TMP(""PSORXDC"",$J) global is killed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",49,1,18,0)="accordingly."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",50,0)="52 SEQ #52^3010227^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",50,1,0)="^^8^8^3010227"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",50,1,1,0)="Problem: The CMOP Controlled Substance Rx Dispense Report generates an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",50,1,2,0)="undefined error when it is trying to report on a prescription refill that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",50,1,3,0)="was filled locally and not sent to CMOP."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",50,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",50,1,5,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",50,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",50,1,7,0)="The CMOP coding has been changed to handle the case when a refill was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",50,1,8,0)="filled locally and not by CMOP."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,0)="51 SEQ #53^3010305^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,0)="^^17^17^3010305"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,1,0)="1) When filling pending orders either using Complete Orders from OERR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,2,0)="[PSO LMOE FINISH] option or through Patient Prescription Processing "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,3,0)="[PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option, the issue date does not show the correct"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,4,0)="entry date, instead it shows the filling date. This patch fixes this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,5,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,7,0)="2) This patch corrects a problem when renewing prescriptions through the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,8,0)="Computerize Patient Record System (CPRS) package and the routing is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,9,0)="entered as administered in clinic.  When prescriptions are entered with"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,10,0)="this type of routing pharmacy should see the routing as window, but was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,11,0)="displaying as mail causing prescriptions to be mailed to the patient."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,13,0)="3) When a refill is created for an active order with a fill date of today"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,14,0)="using the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,15,0)="option, and in the same session if this refill is deleted, it was observed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,16,0)="that the label print routine was trying to process this refill even though"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",51,1,17,0)="it had been deleted. This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,0)="43 SEQ #54^3010319^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,0)="^^28^28^3010319"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,1,0)="1. Problem: Consolidated Mail Outpatient Pharmacy fills that have been"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,2,0)="returned to stock are being allowed to be re-suspended to CMOP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,4,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,6,0)="The Outpatient coding has been changed to test the prescription fill's"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,7,0)="CMOP activity and will not allow it to go to CMOP suspense if the status"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,8,0)="is not proper."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,10,0)="2. Problem: Prescriptions that have a faulty status of 'Suspended' error"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,11,0)="out in CMOP code trying to update the prescription suspense comments."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,13,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,15,0)="The Outpatient code has been changed to test for the existence of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,16,0)="prescription in the RX SUSPENSE file (#52.5) prior to performing a CMOP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,17,0)="update."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,19,0)="3. Problem: New prescriptions with drugs that have been marked for CMOP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,20,0)="but have drug warnings greater than 11 characters are being dropped into"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,21,0)="normal suspense without any message to the user. The intent is to have"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,22,0)="these prescriptions go to CMOP. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,24,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,26,0)="The Outpatient code has been modified to send an appropriate message to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,27,0)="G.CMOP Managers regarding the prescription and the drug warning length"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",52,1,28,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,0)="59 SEQ #55^3010319^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,0)="^^27^27^3010319"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,1,0)="1) During the order entry process using Patient Prescription Processing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,2,0)="[PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option, if the user opts to address more than"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,3,0)="one prescription at a time simultaneously, the word ""Release"" is being"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,4,0)="displayed along with the routing type (Mail/Window) for each prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,5,0)="even though it is not released. It had picked up the release status of a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,6,0)="prior prescription. This is due to one of the variables not being killed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,7,0)="This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,9,0)="2) This patch corrects a problem of a refill request not being seen in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,10,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy when requested from Computerized Patient Record"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,11,0)="System (CPRS). This problem only occurs when invalid data is found in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,12,0)="PENDING OUTPATIENT ORDERS file (#52.41)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,14,0)="3) When renewing a prescription using Patient Prescription Processing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,15,0)="[PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option, it was observed by some sites (set for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,16,0)="auto suspend), that the renewed prescription is getting suspended to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,17,0)="wrong date. The renewal process calculates the FILL DATE field (#22)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,18,0)="based on the NEXT POSSIBLE FILL field (#102) of PRESCRIPTION file (#52)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,19,0)="It also checks to see if a record exits in RX SUSPENSE file (#52.5)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,20,0)="and its PRINTED field (#2) is set. For some reason (timing delay/system"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,21,0)="problems), this field is not being set for CMOP drugs even when the drug"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,22,0)="was released. In such situations the renewal process tends to set the FILL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,23,0)="DATE field (#22) to the LAST DISPENSED DATE field (#101) of PRESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,24,0)="file (#52). This patch ensures that, for these situations, if the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,25,0)="calculated FILL DATE field (#22) of PRESCRIPTION file (#52) is less than"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,26,0)="the current date then it gets set to the current date unless a lesser date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",53,1,27,0)="than the current date is requested by the users."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,0)="56 SEQ #56^3010326^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,0)="^^37^37^3010326"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,1,0)="1) It was reported that the PATIENT STATUS field (#3) in PRESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,2,0)="file (#52) randomly gets changed to the bingo board wait time when using"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,3,0)="the Display Patient's Name on Monitor [PSO BINGO DISPLAY PATIENT] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,4,0)="This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,6,0)="2) This patch contains a fix for the HL7 messaging routine PSOHLSG1,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,7,0)="which is provided to transmit Outpatient Pharmacy prescriptions to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,8,0)="Optifil, (an automated dispensing unit) to include a patient's temporary"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,9,0)="address functionality if made active."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,11,0)="3) This patch corrects a problem when editing CLOZAPINE STATUS field"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,12,0)="(#54) of PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) using Edit Data for a Patient in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,13,0)="Clozapine Program [PSOL EDIT] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,15,0)="4) During an edit of a partial prescription, up-arrowing at any fields"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,16,0)="other than the partial date, causes that record to be killed instead of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,17,0)="quitting the edit process. This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,19,0)="5) When finishing orders entered through Computerized Patient Record"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,20,0)="System (CPRS), it was reported that for a patient status of value AUTH ABS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,21,0)="+96 or AUTH ABS -96, it triggers the duplicate drug alert check when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,22,0)="duplicates are found. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,24,0)="6) This patch fixes a spelling error found in the report that is being"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,25,0)="generated when using the High Cost Rx Report [PSO HI COST] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,27,0)="7) When renewing orders entered through CPRS or backdoor, the warning"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,28,0)="message that is being displayed during the duplicate drug/same class check"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,29,0)="against other pending orders was found to have incorrect data on the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,30,0)="instruction field and the provider comments field. Also the data on these"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,31,0)="two fields were transposed. This patch fixes these problems."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,33,0)="8) When entering the first refill using Patient Prescription Processing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,34,0)="[PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option, if the user edits any field on the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,35,0)="original prescription, it was reported that the refill is getting"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,36,0)="suspended (sites having auto suspense flag set) to the original fill date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",54,1,37,0)="instead of the last dispensed date. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,0)="63 SEQ #57^3010430^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,1,0)="^^12^12^3010430"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,1,1,0)="1) When discontinuing a prescription entered through Computerized Patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,1,2,0)="Record System (CPRS), if an up-arrow is entered at the ""Nature of Order:"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,1,3,0)="dialog and if the default entries are accepted for the remainder of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,1,4,0)="dialogs without entering an up-arrow, the discontinue process errors out."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,1,5,0)="This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,1,7,0)="2) When renewing orders entered through CPRS or backdoor, the duplicate"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,1,8,0)="drug check against other pending refill orders was found to error out if"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,1,9,0)="the entry to the dialog ""Discontinue Pending Order?"" was entered as"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,1,10,0)="""YES"".  This error was introduced by patch PSO*7*56. Routine PSODRDU1 was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,1,11,0)="modified to correct multiple issues, with some of the redundant code"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",55,1,12,0)="removed. This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,0)="60 SEQ #58^3010430^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,0)="^^18^18^3010430"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,1,0)="1. When using the Start Bingo Board Display [PSO BINGO START] option, to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,2,0)="restart a stopped bingo board, a task number is assigned by the Task"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,3,0)="Manager to queue this task. The assigned task number is not being set in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,4,0)="the TASK # field (#15) of GROUP DISPLAY FILE (#59.3), for the selected"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,5,0)="bingo board display. This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,7,0)="2. When an order is transferred in Computerized Patient Record System"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,8,0)="(CPRS) from Inpatient Medications to Outpatient Pharmacy (OP), or a change"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,9,0)="is done on an OP order in CPRS, the Noun that is associated with the order"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,10,0)="is not always being built into the DISPENSING INSTRUCTIONS field (#.01) of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,11,0)="the DISPENSING INSTRUCTIONS sub-file (#52.4124) of the PENDING OUTPATIENT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,12,0)="ORDERS file (#52.41) when the order comes to the OP package. This is the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,13,0)="information that displays as the Possible SIG on the OP finish screen."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,14,0)="This patch resolves that problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,16,0)="3. This patch fixes a problem when using the Label/Profile Monitor Reprint"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,17,0)="[PSO B] option, to reprint labels onto another printer. It was using the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",56,1,18,0)="control codes of the original printer instead of the selected printer."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",57,0)="62 SEQ #59^3010430^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",57,1,0)="^^10^10^3010430"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",57,1,1,0)="When a prescription is reinstated using the Discontinue Prescription(s)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",57,1,2,0)="[PSO C] option, and immediately afterwards the Patient Prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",57,1,3,0)="Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option is used to edit the SIG of a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",57,1,4,0)="prescription, the change of SIG creates a new order. The generated order"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",57,1,5,0)="has a different dispensed drug. It contains the drug of the prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",57,1,6,0)="that was most recently reinstated using the Discontinue Prescription(s)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",57,1,7,0)="[PSO C] option. This could result in dispensing the wrong drug to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",57,1,8,0)="patient. In order to correct this problem this patch insures that all"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",57,1,9,0)="related variables are killed appropriately when quitting from the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",57,1,10,0)="Discontinue Prescription(s) [PSO C] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,0)="64 SEQ #60^3010608^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,0)="^^13^13^3010608"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,1,0)="1) Currently when a prescription is renewed either using the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,2,0)="Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] or Complete Orders from"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,3,0)="OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] option, the FILL DATE field (#22) of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,4,0)="PRESCRIPTION file (#52) in the renewed prescription is calculated based on"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,5,0)="the LAST DISPENSED DATE field (#101) of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52). The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,6,0)="renewal process does not check whether the last refill was released or a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,7,0)="label has been printed. If such a refill existed, the FILL DATE field"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,8,0)="(#22) of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) of the renewed prescription was being"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,9,0)="set to a date far into the future. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,11,0)="2) This patch corrects a problem of an undefined variable error that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,12,0)="can occur during the speed renewal process within the Patient Prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",58,1,13,0)="Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,0)="65 SEQ #61^3010625^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,0)="^^15^15^3010625"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,1,0)="This patch corrects the following problems when using the Site Parameter"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,2,0)="Enter/Edit [PSO SITE PARAMETERS] option:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,4,0)="1) The dialog ""Would you like to see all site parameters for this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,5,0)="division? Y//"", only responds to upper case ""Y"". Now the routine is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,6,0)="patched to accept both upper and lower case responses of ""y""."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,8,0)="2) Currently the users have the option of deleting a site from the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,9,0)="OUTPATIENT SITE file (#59) by entering ""@"" key at the dialog"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,10,0)="NAME: ALBANY//. Deleting a site could lead to an ""undefined error"" problem"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,11,0)="as reported in NOIS AMA-0700-71379. This patch prevents the users from"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,12,0)="deleting a site."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,14,0)="This patch also updates the Data Dictionary of the NAME field (#.01) of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",59,1,15,0)="the OUTPATIENT SITE file (#59)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,0)="66 SEQ #62^3010802^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,0)="^^14^14^3010802"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,1,0)="1) When using the Action Profile (132 COLUMN PRINTOUT) [PSO ACTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,2,0)="PROFILE] option, the FILL DATE field (#22) of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,3,0)="in the report, at times shows the date as ""--1700"". This is because the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,4,0)="FILL DATE field (#22) of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) is set to null when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,5,0)="the original prescription is on HOLD status. This patch fixes this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,6,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,8,0)="2) The AUTOMATED INFO COLLECTION SYS (AICS) package requests a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,9,0)="modification to routine PSOSD1. Access to the entry point DFN^PSOSD1 is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,10,0)="provided by the Integration Agreement (IA) 1281. Currently this entry"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,11,0)="point does a form feed at the beginning of the report. The AICS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,12,0)="package requests that this form feed be suppressed. Now the routine is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,13,0)="patched to suppress a form feed at the beginning of the report when the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",60,1,14,0)="passing variable PSONOPG (as per IA 1281) is set to 2."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,0)="61 SEQ #63^3010802^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,0)="^^17^17^3010802"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,1,0)="1. Problem: Prescriptions that need to be resubmitted to CMOP with a CMOP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,2,0)="status of 'Not Dispensed' are failing internal testing and are blocked"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,3,0)="from being transmitted to CMOP."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,5,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,7,0)="The internal testing code has been corrected to allow resubmission of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,8,0)="prescriptions to CMOP."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,10,0)="2. Problem: A concurrent window and a mail fill for a single prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,11,0)="are being allowed to be processed with the mail fill going into CMOP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,12,0)="suspense. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,14,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,16,0)="The code has been changed to test for and block a request of a multiple"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",61,1,17,0)="fill for the same prescription being sent to CMOP."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,0)="72 SEQ #64^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,0)="^^16^16^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,1,0)=" 1. During the completion process of renewing a prescription, the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,2,0)=" software gathers the co-pay information for patient status SC LESS THAN"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,3,0)=" 50%. During this process, there is a possibility of getting an undefined"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,4,0)=" error. This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,6,0)=" 2. This patch modifies the Input Template of the SITE NUMBER field (#.06)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,7,0)=" of the OUTPATIENT SITE file (#59) from eight free text characters to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,8,0)=" three numeric and five alphanumeric characters. The Consolidated Mail"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,9,0)=" Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP) V. 2.0 package expects this field to have the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,10,0)=" leading 3 digits as numeric, otherwise it reports an undefined error"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,11,0)=" when using the Archive CMOP Data [PSX ARCHIVE] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,12,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,13,0)=" 3. When using the All Reports [PSO MGMT MONTHLY ALL REPORTS] option,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,14,0)=" the date entry for the prompt ""Beginning    MONTH/YEAR :"", accepts only"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,15,0)=" the full name of the month and the 4 digit year. This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",62,1,16,0)=" problem to allow any valid month/year format."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,0)="69 SEQ #65^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,0)="^^39^39^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,1,0)=" This is an emergency patch and should be installed as soon as possible."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,3,0)=" The Upstate New York HealthCare System reported a problem concerning"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,4,0)=" outpatient pharmacy profiles containing prescriptions for patients other"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,5,0)=" than the patient selected. The problem happened as a result of corrupted"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,6,0)=" data in the PRESCRIPTION PROFILE sub-file (#55.03) of the PHARMACY"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,7,0)=" PATIENT file (#55). This field links the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,8,0)=" the PRESCRIPTION file (#52). The link to the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,9,0)=" the ""A"", cross-reference on this sub-file were corrupted for some"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,10,0)=" patients. When the software displays a profile it uses the field and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,11,0)=" cross-references to gather the prescriptions to be listed. If a corrupted"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,12,0)=" node pointed to a prescription for a different patient, the wrong"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,13,0)=" prescription would display on the profile. In some cases, a prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,14,0)=" may have been discontinued because a Date of Death or an Admission was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,15,0)=" entered for the patient with a corrupt cross-reference. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,16,0)=" ensures that all bad entries in the sub-file and corresponding ""A"","
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,17,0)=" cross-references are deleted. During this process, it generates a mail"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,18,0)=" message to the installer for each Outpatient Site entry, listing those"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,19,0)=" patients that may have had a prescription discontinued because a Date of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,20,0)=" Death or an Admission was entered for the patient with a corrupt cross-"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,21,0)=" reference. These prescriptions must be manually reviewed and if"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,22,0)=" appropriate reinstated. The patch installer should forward the mail"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,23,0)=" message to the Pharmacy Application Coordinator, or the appropriate"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,24,0)=" Outpatient Pharmacy Personnel, for their review and correction. It will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,25,0)=" send summary information to G.PL2 PATCH TRACKING group on FORUM so that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,26,0)=" counts of bad nodes by site can be collected. This patch will also scan"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,27,0)=" through the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) using the ""AD"" cross-reference and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,28,0)=" will check if a corresponding entry exists in the PHARMACY PATIENT file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,29,0)=" (#55). The software will provide a count of missing entries in a separate"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,30,0)=" mail message that will be sent to G.PL2 PATCH TRACKING on FORUM for their"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,31,0)=" review."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,33,0)=" We recommend re-indexing the ""B"" cross-reference of the PHARMACY"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,34,0)=" PATIENT file (#55), during non-peak hours or when the number of pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,35,0)=" users on the system is at a minimum any time after completion of this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,36,0)=" job."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,37,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,38,0)=" A subsequent patch will be released to provide additional safeguards in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",63,1,39,0)=" the event that the cross-reference gets corrupted in the future."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",64,0)="67 SEQ #66^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",64,1,0)="^^9^9^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",64,1,1,0)="Problem: Prescriptions can be edited from mail to window and then released"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",64,1,2,0)="while the prescription still has an active Consolidated Mail Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",64,1,3,0)="Pharmacy (CMOP) status. Those statuses are Transmitted, Dispensed, and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",64,1,4,0)="Retransmitted."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",64,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",64,1,6,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",64,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",64,1,8,0)="The internal code has been corrected to block the facilities from"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",64,1,9,0)="releasing prescriptions that have an active CMOP status."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,0)="46^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,0)="^^54^54^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,1,0)="1) The Pharmacy Ordering Enhancements (POE) project provides enhancements"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,2,0)="to Pharmacy Data Management (PDM) V. 1.0, Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,3,0)="V. 5.0, Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0, and Order Entry/Results Reporting"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,4,0)="(OE/RR) V. 3.0 medication ordering dialogues to eliminate redundant entry"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,5,0)="of drug information during medication order entry, provide a more"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,6,0)="consistent medication order entry process, provide expanded order"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,7,0)="checking, display documented drug formulary statuses and corresponding"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,8,0)="restriction/guidelines to the provider and pharmacist at the time of order"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,9,0)="entry, and improve the process of medication order transfer between"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,10,0)="Inpatient Medications and Outpatient Pharmacy applications.  This project"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,11,0)="directly supports Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS), which is a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,12,0)="key component of Veterans Health Administration's (VHA) plan to expand"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,13,0)="support for clinical operations. Additionally, order checks will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,14,0)="provided for medication orders for which a dispense drug has not been"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,15,0)="selected during the CPRS order entry process. It is also intended as a way"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,16,0)="to help meet the goal outlined in Objective 8, Action 1 in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,17,0)="Prescription for Change, which outlines the need to coordinate"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,18,0)="national/Veterans Integrated Service Network (VISN) formularies and share"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,19,0)="drug treatment guideline information. This project will promote system-"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,20,0)="wide sharing of drug reviews and treatment guidelines thereby enhancing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,21,0)="patient safety."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,23,0)="This project consists of four patches that work together to accomplish"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,24,0)="these goals listed in order of install:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,26,0)="     PSO*7*46"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,27,0)="     OR*3*94"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,28,0)="     PSS*1*38"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,29,0)="     PSJ*5*50"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,31,0)=" 2) This patch corrects a problem as reported in CON-0300-11347."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,32,0)="When reinstating a Prescription an order alert was displayed for a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,33,0)="duplicate drug.  The alert was occurring incorrectly for the Prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,34,0)="that was being reinstated."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,36,0)=" 3) As reported in NYH-0300-12247 and BIL-1100-30086 the NSC/SC prompt is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,37,0)="not asked consistently between Outpatient Pharmacy and Computerized"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,38,0)="Patient Record System (CPRS) packages.  This patch provided an enhanced"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,39,0)="interface for both packages to use when placing orders. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,41,0)=" 4) As reported in SAG-0500-41497 when renewing prescription request from"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,42,0)="CPRS the screen was not displaying correctly.   This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,43,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,45,0)=" 5) As reported in AMA-0900-71796 when renewing prescriptions that had"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,46,0)="a cosigner tied to the provider and the cosigning provider changed the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,47,0)="cosigner was not being updated to show the new cosigning provider."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,49,0)=" 6) As reported in NYH-0900-10553 cost in the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,50,0)="the drug would not allow a cost higher than 999 with 4 decimals.  This"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,51,0)="patch will allow cost to be entered for all fills to be 9999 with 4"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,52,0)="decimals."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",65,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,0)="74 SEQ #68^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,0)="^^13^13^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,2,0)="1. When entering new outpatients into the Pharmacy Patient file (#55), the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,3,0)="patient's prescription status is a required data element.  When entering"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,4,0)="this data element into the Pharmacy Patient file (#55) eligibility and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,5,0)="disabilities will display to help the pharmacy user answer this prompt."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,7,0)="This patch also corrects a typo."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,9,0)="2. This patch corrects a problem where a missing dosage check did not work"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,10,0)="when finishing pending orders."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,12,0)="3. This patch runs a post-install routine to look for pre-POE pending orders"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",66,1,13,0)="without dispense drugs and remove data stored on the wrong node."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",67,0)="58 SEQ #69^3011016^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",67,1,0)="^^7^7^3011016"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",67,1,1,0)="This patch is an enhancement to the Outpatient Pharmacy routine that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",67,1,2,0)="gathers and returns patient and prescription information for the Hepatitis"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",67,1,3,0)="C Extract project. Prior to this patch, data was returned without"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",67,1,4,0)="integrated site consideration. With the release of this patch, a check"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",67,1,5,0)="will now be done on original fill prescriptions. If the original fill"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",67,1,6,0)="prescription information has been moved to another site, that finding will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",67,1,7,0)="not be included in the extract."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,0)="68 SEQ #70^3011106^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,0)="^^21^21^3011106"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,1,0)="A problem has been found where it is possible for an Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,2,0)="order to be entered through Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS), and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,3,0)="the priority of the order to be deleted in CPRS, before the order is sent"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,4,0)="to Outpatient Pharmacy. When finishing orders in Outpatient Pharmacy using"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,5,0)="the Complete Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] option, Priority is one of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,6,0)="the sort selections. It has been reported that orders were not being"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,7,0)="finished because orders had been sent without a priority, and all"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,8,0)="finishing in Outpatient Pharmacy was done by priority, and not by any"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,9,0)="other means of sorting."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,11,0)="As part of the Pharmacy Ordering Enhancements (POE) project (patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,12,0)="PSO*7*46 for Outpatient Pharmacy) a change will be made to assign Routine"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,13,0)="as the priority to an order received from CPRS that does not have a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,14,0)="priority."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,16,0)="What this patch will do is run a Post-Install routine that will look for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,17,0)="Pending Outpatient Orders that do not have a Priority assigned. A list of "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,18,0)="Patients with these orders will be sent in a mail message to the person"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,19,0)="installing the patch. This mail message should then be forwarded by the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,20,0)="patch installer to the Pharmacy Application Coordinator, or the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",68,1,21,0)="appropriate Outpatient Pharmacy Personnel, for their review."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,0)="75 SEQ #71^3011106^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,0)="^^17^17^3011106"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,1,0)="1. This patch corrects an undefined error that could occur when trying to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,2,0)="display Special Instructions (SIG) for a prescription entered before"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,3,0)="PSO*7*46.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,5,0)="2. Added check for missing SIG before filing a renewal.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,7,0)="3. When speed renewing through Outpatient Pharmacy and the first order is a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,8,0)="pre-POE order with a possible dosage and the second order is a pre-POE order"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,9,0)="with a local possible dosage, the quantity from the first order is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,10,0)="defaulting for the second order.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,12,0)="4. When speed renewing POE orders the SIG does not display.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,14,0)="5. Site reported not being able to edit the verb when finishing pending"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,15,0)="renewals for phase 2 of POE. The site was instructed to select the field for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,16,0)="dosage and then type ^VERB to jump to the Verb field.  In doing this you"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",69,1,17,0)="are prompted twice for schedule, duration and conjunction.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",70,0)="79 SEQ #72^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",70,1,0)="^^8^8^3011210"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",70,1,1,0)=" When Pharmacy is finishing a Renewal entered through Computerized Patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",70,1,2,0)=" Record System (CPRS), for Consolidated Mail Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",70,1,3,0)=" sites, if the Routing, MAIL/WINDOW field (#11) of the PRESCRIPTION file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",70,1,4,0)=" (#52) is edited from ""Mail"" to ""Window"" when having the LOGIN DATE field"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",70,1,5,0)=" (#21) a date prior to the current date and the FILL DATE field (#22) of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",70,1,6,0)=" the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) set for today's date with the intention of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",70,1,7,0)=" dispensing the prescription locally, there is a possibility of such a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",70,1,8,0)=" prescription getting suspended for CMOP. This patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,0)="77 SEQ #73^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,0)="^^19^19^3011210"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,1,0)=" 1) This patch makes the DAYS SUPPLY field (#.041) of the PARTIAL DATE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,2,0)=" multiple (#52.2) of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52), a required field as"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,3,0)=" requested by the NOIS ISH-0401-40089. The Data Dictionary is not changed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,4,0)=" here. The fix is made in the routine PSORXPA1."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,6,0)=" 2) When using the Status of Patient's Order [PSO BINGO STATUS] option,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,7,0)=" or using the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,8,0)=" option, and selecting the OTH (Other OP Actions) hidden action, and then"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,9,0)=" selecting the DO (Display Orders' Statuses) option, there is a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,10,0)=" possibility of viewing prescriptions belonging to other patients. This"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,11,0)=" patch fixes this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,13,0)=" 3) When deleting a device from the DEVICE file (#3.5), using FileMan and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,14,0)=" requesting the software either to delete all pointers or changing its"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,15,0)=" pointers to point to a different device, it was found to error out at"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,16,0)=" times. During the process of re-pointing the device, FileMan would"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,17,0)=" encounter an orphaned multiple (#59.30001). This multiple may have been"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,18,0)=" used by Outpatient Pharmacy at some time, but they are no longer needed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",71,1,19,0)=" This patch removes this multiple."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",72,0)="80 SEQ #74^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",72,1,0)="^^11^11^3011210"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",72,1,1,0)=" This patch adds the Free Text Dosage Report [PSO DOSAGE REPORT] option,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",72,1,2,0)=" as an addition to the Output Reports [PSO OUTPUTS] menu option. It"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",72,1,3,0)=" provides a list of drugs for those prescriptions where the DOSAGE ORDERED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",72,1,4,0)=" field (#.01) of the MEDICATION INSTRUCTION sub-file (#52.0113) of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",72,1,5,0)=" PRESCRIPTION file (#52), has a free text entry or a dosage that results"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",72,1,6,0)=" in the calculation of the number of tablets. This report is designed to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",72,1,7,0)=" help in the identification of all such entries so that the sites can"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",72,1,8,0)=" determine if these dosages should be added to the LOCAL POSSIBLE DOSAGE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",72,1,9,0)=" sub-file (#50.0904) of the DRUG file (#50), making the Local Possible"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",72,1,10,0)=" Dosages selectable instead of requiring it to be typed in, during the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",72,1,11,0)=" medication order entry process."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,0)="71 SEQ #75^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,0)="^^86^86^3011210"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,1,0)="This patch reflects changes made to copay charges by Public Law 106-117, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,2,0)="The Veterans Millennium Health Care and Benefits Act. Public Law 106-117 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,3,0)="will not go into effect until early 2002. The exact effective date is not "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,4,0)="known at this time. Prior to the changes that will be implemented with "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,5,0)="Public Law 106-117, certain veterans paid a $2 copayment for each 30-day "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,6,0)="or less supply of medication furnished for the outpatient treatment of a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,7,0)="nonservice-connected disability or condition. With Public Law 106-117, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,8,0)="the copayment amount will increase from $2 to $7. An annual copayment cap "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,9,0)="of $840 will be set through calendar year 2002 for veterans in enrollment "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,10,0)="priority groups 2-6. Provisions are included to automatically increase "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,11,0)="the copayment and the cap amount under certain conditions.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,13,0)="Effective on January 1, 2002, a medication is exempt from copay charges "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,14,0)="if it is used to treat the following conditions:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,16,0)="   Vietnam-era herbicide (Agent Orange) exposure"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,17,0)="   Radiation exposure"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,18,0)="   Exposure to environmental contaminants during Persian Gulf War Service"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,19,0)="   Military Sexual Trauma "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,20,0)="   Cancer of the Head and/or Neck "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,21,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,22,0)="The Outpatient Pharmacy patch PSO*7*71 and Consolidated Mail Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,23,0)="Pharmacy (CMOP) patch PSX*2*35 must be installed and implemented by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,24,0)="facilities no later than December 31, 2001. On January 1, 2002, the new"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,25,0)="medication copay exemptions provided by patch PSO*7*71 will go into"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,26,0)="effect. Changes to increase the amount of medication copay and to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,27,0)="establish the annual copay cap will go into effect when the law is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,28,0)="approved and signed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,31,0)="A post-installation routine is included in patch PSO*7*71 to review "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,32,0)="prescriptions entered over the last year and to populate, whenever "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,33,0)="possible, the new SERVICE CONNECTED field (#116) of the PRESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,34,0)="file (#52). This routine queues a background task to look at all"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,35,0)="prescriptions entered over the last year and to attempt to populate the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,36,0)="new SERVICE CONNECTED field (#116) of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) based on"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,37,0)="the prescription data. If the COPAY TRANSACTION TYPE field (#105) of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,38,0)="PRESCRIPTION file (#52) is set to ""2,"" this indicates that the Service"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,39,0)="Connected question was asked for this prescription, and the response was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,40,0)="""NO."" In these cases, the software will set the new SERVICE CONNECTED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,41,0)="field (#116) to ""NO."" If the COPAY TRANSACTION TYPE field (#105) of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,42,0)="PRESCRIPTION file (#52) is null, and the drug is not marked as a supply or"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,43,0)="as an investigational drug, and the Rx Patient Status of the prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,44,0)="contains ""50,"" and either the ""<"" character or the words ""LESS THAN"" (for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,45,0)="'SC LESS THAN 50%'), and the COPAY INCOME EXEMPTION STATUS field (#.04) of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,46,0)="the BILLING PATIENT file (#354) is set to ""NON-EXEMPT, "" then the software"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,47,0)="will set the new SERVICE CONNECTED field to ""YES."""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,49,0)="When the job is complete, a mail message will be sent to the person who "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,50,0)="installed the patch."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,53,0)="Complete information for all the changes included in this patch can be "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,54,0)="found in the Outpatient Medication Copay Release Notes document. In "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,55,0)="addition to the Release Notes, there are changes to the Outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,56,0)="Pharmacy Technical Manual and the Outpatient Pharmacy User Manual."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,59,0)="Sites may retrieve documentation in one of the following ways:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,61,0)="(1) The preferred method is to FTP the files from"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,62,0)="    download.vista.domain.ext, which will transmit the files from the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,63,0)="    first available FTP server."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,65,0)="(2) Sites may also elect to retrieve documentation directly from a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,66,0)="    specific server as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,68,0)="    Albany          ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,69,0)="    Hines           ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,70,0)="    Salt Lake City  ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,73,0)="The documentation distribution includes: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,75,0)="    FILE NAMES                 DESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,76,0)="         "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,77,0)="    OP_Med_Copay_RN.pdf        Release Notes"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,78,0)="    OP_7_0_P71_UM_CP.pdf       User Manual (change pages)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,79,0)="    OP_7_0_P71_TM_CP.pdf       Technical Manual (change pages)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,80,0)="    OP_7_0_UM_R1101.pdf        User Manual (updated)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,81,0)="    OP_7_0_TM_R1101.pdf        Technical Manual (updated)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,84,0)="(3) Documentation can also be retrieved from VISTA Document Library (VDL)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,85,0)="    on the VA Intranet at the following address,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",73,1,86,0)="    http://vista.domain.ext/vdl."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",74,0)="76 SEQ #76^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",74,1,0)="^^6^6^3011210"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",74,1,1,0)="Problem: The testing for duplicate drugs is bringing back false "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",74,1,2,0)="duplicates from the Consolidated Mail Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP) module "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",74,1,3,0)="when the PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS option is used."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",74,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",74,1,5,0)="Resolution: The code has been corrected by clearing a variable prior to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",74,1,6,0)="testing the prescription."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,0)="82 SEQ #77^3020108^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,0)="^^22^22^3020108"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,1,0)=" 1) When the PP Pull Rx (OP) protocol (hidden action) is used in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,2,0)=" backdoor pharmacy to fill a suspended prescription early, it sometimes"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,3,0)=" errors out. This is due to a bad ""B"" cross-reference entry for that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,4,0)=" prescription in the RX SUSPENSE file (#52.5). This patch will ensure that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,5,0)=" the corresponding entries of such a prescription in the RX SUSPENSE file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,6,0)=" (#52.5) are complete when building the patient medical profile. If"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,7,0)=" the entries are incomplete this patch will clean up the bad ""B"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,8,0)=" cross-reference entry in the RX SUSPENSE file (#52.5) and change the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,9,0)=" STATUS field (#100) of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) to 0 (an active"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,10,0)=" prescription)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,12,0)=" 2) When entering a new prescription through backdoor pharmacy and if the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,13,0)=" prescription is put on hold then the label LABEL QUEUE/CHANGE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,14,0)=" PRINTER/SUSPEND or '^' to bypass Q// prompt is displayed. If the new"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,15,0)=" prescription is the only order in the session then no label is required"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,16,0)=" therefore, this prompt should not be displayed. This patch fixes this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,17,0)=" problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,19,0)=" 3) In the API's OCL^PSOORRL and OEL^PSOORRL, provided by Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,20,0)=" Pharmacy V. 7.0, there is a possibility of an undefined error occurring"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,21,0)=" when the ""SIG"" node of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) for the prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",75,1,22,0)=" in process is missing. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,0)="83 SEQ #78^3020108^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,0)="^^19^19^3020108"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,2,0)="This patch addresses the following concerns:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,4,0)="1. When entering an outpatient pharmacy prescription a schedule "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,5,0)="is required to complete the order. If the user should enter a question"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,6,0)="mark at the schedule field prompt to list the available choices, a list is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,7,0)="not displayed as expected. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,9,0)="2. Central Texas Veterans Health Care System has received multiple"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,10,0)="complaints from patients about their full Social Security Number (SSN)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,11,0)="printing on their prescription reorder documents.  Currently the SSN at"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,12,0)="the top of the refill document shows the last 6 digits, however the full SSN"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,13,0)="shows next to the patient's name on the last page, just above the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,14,0)="NARRATIVE REFILLABLE RX document.  This patch will change all"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,15,0)="instances of the patient's SSN on the reorder documents to display only the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,16,0)="last 6 digits.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",76,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,0)="73 SEQ #79^3020108^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,0)="^^55^55^3020108"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,1,0)=" When editing a prescription through the pharmacy backdoor, if the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,2,0)=" following fields are edited: QTY field (#7), DAYS SUPPLY field (#8) or #"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,3,0)=" OF REFILLS field (#9), of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52), the software"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,4,0)=" recalculates the EXPIRATION DATE field (#26) of the PRESCRIPTION file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,5,0)=" (#52) and also kills the corresponding ""AG"" cross-reference entry of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,6,0)=" PRESCRIPTION file (#52). In the case when the expiration date remains the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,7,0)=" same after the edit process, it does not reset the ""AG"" cross-reference"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,8,0)=" entry and therefore the link to the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) for that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,9,0)=" prescription from the ""AG"" cross-reference is lost. The Expire"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,10,0)=" Prescriptions [PSO EXPIRE PRESCRIPTIONS] and the Manual Auto Expire Rxs"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,11,0)=" [PSO MANUAL AUTO EXPIRE] options both use the ""AG"" cross-reference to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,12,0)=" flag prescriptions past the expiration date as expired and they do"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,13,0)=" not flag those prescriptions that had a missing ""AG"" cross-reference"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,14,0)=" entry. Hence, the expired prescriptions show as active, especially when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,15,0)=" using the Orders Tab protocol from the Computerized Patient Record System"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,16,0)=" (CPRS) package. This patch ensures that the ""AG"" cross-reference is reset"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,17,0)=" only when the expiration date changes."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,19,0)=" The Expire Prescriptions [PSO EXPIRE PRESCRIPTIONS] and the Manual Auto"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,20,0)=" Expire Rxs [PSO MANUAL AUTO EXPIRE] options are patched to have an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,21,0)=" additional check to ensure that the expiration date subscript in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,22,0)=" ""AG"" cross-reference is equal to the EXPIRATION DATE field (#26) of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,23,0)=" PRESCRIPTION file (#52), and to flag those prescriptions that have"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,24,0)=" expired in Outpatient Pharmacy but show as active in the CPRS Orders Tab"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,25,0)=" as expired."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,27,0)=" The Expire Prescriptions [PSO EXPIRE PRESCRIPTIONS] option flags"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,28,0)=" prescriptions that have passed the expire date as expired and sends an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,29,0)=" HL7 message across to CPRS to flag those prescriptions as expired."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,30,0)=" Currently, this functionality not only sends the expire message for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,31,0)=" expired prescriptions but also for discontinued prescriptions, and as a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,32,0)=" result in CPRS the discontinued prescriptions are flagged as expired,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,33,0)=" which is incorrect. This patch will ensure that only expired"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,34,0)=" prescriptions are sent across to CPRS to be flagged as expired."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,36,0)=" Note: There is an optional site selectable post-install background job"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,37,0)=" included in this patch. This job will make sure that the ""AG"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,38,0)=" cross-reference of the EXPIRATION DATE field (#26) of the PRESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,39,0)=" file (#52) is properly set, starting from the date Outpatient Pharmacy V."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,40,0)=" 7.0 was installed. It will also reset the statuses of all those"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,41,0)=" discontinued prescriptions which were flagged as expired in CPRS by the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,42,0)=" Expire Prescriptions [PSO EXPIRE PRESCRIPTIONS] option back to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,43,0)=" discontinued statuses. At the completion of this job, a MailMan message"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,44,0)=" with the subject ""PATCH PSO*7*73 - 'AG' Cross-reference Cleanup"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,45,0)=" Information"", will be sent to the installer notifying the time of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,46,0)=" completion. The date/time to queue this job is site selectable and can be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,47,0)=" queued to run during the installation of the patch or at another time by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,48,0)=" calling the entry point BEG^PSOPOST from programmer mode. Also the site"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,49,0)=" could use this entry point at any time to re-start the cleanup process in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,50,0)=" case the job was interrupted for any reason."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,52,0)=" For sites experiencing the problem reported above, i.e., prescriptions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,53,0)=" past the expiration date appearing as active, it is recommended that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,54,0)=" they also run the Manual Auto Expire Rxs [PSO MANUAL AUTO EXPIRE] option"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",77,1,55,0)=" any time after the completion of the Post-Install run of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,0)="81 SEQ #80^3020204^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,0)="^^16^16^3020204"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,1,0)=" The routine PSOORDRG contains an  Application Programmer Interface"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,2,0)=" (API),  IA #2190, used by the Computerized Patient Record System"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,3,0)=" (CPRS). This API requires modification to accommodate changes to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,4,0)=" incoming data passed in by CPRS. The intended effect of this change is to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,5,0)=" improve CPRS order checking functionality, specifically, to help CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,6,0)=" distinguish between Inpatient orders and Outpatient orders when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,7,0)=" performing order checks. The changes described will not be implemented"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,8,0)=" until OR*3*123 and PSJ*5*56 are also installed. However, this patch does"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,9,0)=" not formally require OR*3*123 or PSJ*5*56, and installation of this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,10,0)=" patch by itself will produce no changes, visible or otherwise. The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,11,0)=" original NOIS submitted to CPRS is DUR-0801-32713."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,14,0)=" Associated NOISs:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,15,0)=" ================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",78,1,16,0)=" DUR-0801-32713"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,0)="93 SEQ #81^3020204^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,0)="^^235^235^3020204"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,3,0)="This is an EMERGENCY patch and must be installed within 24 hours."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,5,0)="CMOP patch PSX*2*39 is required before the installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,8,0)=" Problem: The release of the Consolidated Mail Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,9,0)="(CMOP) patch PSX*2*35 introduced a potential problem. If the OUTPATIENT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,10,0)="SITE file (#59) parameter 'BARCODES ON ACTION  PROFILES' for any"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,11,0)="outpatient pharmacy site is set to ""NO"" or is null, all copay eligible"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,12,0)="prescription fills released by CMOP for that outpatient pharmacy site,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,13,0)="after the installation of patch PSX*2*35, would not have been billed. This"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,14,0)="patch identifies all such prescriptions and reprocesses them so that the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,15,0)="appropriate copay charges are generated."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,18,0)=" Resolution: This patch will identify all copay eligible released CMOP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,19,0)="prescription fills that were not billed since the installation of patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,20,0)="PSX*2*35 and reprocess them so that appropriate copay charges are"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,21,0)="generated. A MailMan message with a Subject of 'Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,22,0)="Copay Clean-up' will be sent to the patch installer and holders of the PSO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,23,0)="COPAY key documenting the number of CMOP prescription fills that were"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,24,0)="successfully billed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,27,0)="This patch will look at all CMOP prescription fills released since patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,28,0)="PSX*2*35 was installed at your facility. If the prescription is copay"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,29,0)="eligible and no charge has been generated, the fill will be reprocessed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,30,0)="When determining whether a copy charge was missed for a CMOP prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,31,0)="done after the release of patch PSX*2*35, we check the patient's current"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,32,0)="copay status.  If the patient's status changed from ""no copay"" to ""copay"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,33,0)="since the installation of patch PSX*2*35 at the site, it is possible that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,34,0)="the patient could be billed for prescription fills that were not marked as"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,35,0)="copay at the time they were originally released."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,38,0)="Note: This clean up is done in a post-install background job. It MUST be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,39,0)="queued to run and complete before 02/01/2002 as tracking for the annual"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,40,0)="copay cap goes into effect then. If the background job has not been queued"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,41,0)="to run by January 30, 2002 or if the background job has not completed by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,42,0)="January 31, 2002 @ 2359, the MailMan message generated will indicate that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,43,0)="the background job was stopped before completing the clean up."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,45,0)="When queuing the background job, the date that patch PSX*2*35 was first"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,46,0)="installed at your facility will be displayed along with information as to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,47,0)="whether any OUTPATIENT SITE file (#59) has the parameter 'BARCODES ON"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,48,0)="ACTION  PROFILES' set to null or ""NO"". If so, and the estimated number of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,49,0)="CMOP prescription fills released during that time frame is high, you may"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,50,0)="want to consider disabling journaling on the Integrated Billing and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,51,0)="Accounts Receivable globals ^IB and ^PRCA before starting the background"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,52,0)="job."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,56,0)=" Associated NOISs:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,57,0)=" ================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,58,0)=" CHS-0102-40707"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,59,0)=" ERI-0102-21090"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,60,0)=" MAC-0102-60932"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,61,0)=" BRX-0102-11833"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,63,0)=" Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,64,0)=" ==========="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,65,0)=" Erie, PA"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,66,0)=" Prescott, AZ"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,67,0)=" Oklahoma City, OK"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,68,0)=" Chicago HCS, IL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,69,0)=" Martinez, CA"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,70,0)=" Chicago Hines, IL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,72,0)=" Routine Summary:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,73,0)=" ================"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,74,0)=" The second line now reads as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,76,0)="   <TAB>;;7.0;OUTPATIENT PHARMACY;**[patch list]**;DEC 1997"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,78,0)=" CHECK^XTSUMBLD results:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,80,0)=" Routine        Before Patch      After Patch      Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,81,0)=" ============================================================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,82,0)=" PSOCPIBC          N/A              13213614          93"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,83,0)=" PSOCPIBF          N/A              18167555          93"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,86,0)=" Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,87,0)=" =========================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,88,0)=" Installation should take no longer than 5 minutes. Please do not queue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,89,0)=" the job of installing this patch. There is a post-install background"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,90,0)=" job that will prompt for a date/time to run the clean up. You MUST"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,91,0)=" respond with a date and time or NOW to queue the job. You will not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,92,0)=" be able to see what you are answering for the prompt, but will be given"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,93,0)=" an opportunity to see what was entered before the clean up job queues."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,94,0)=" This post-install job can be run again at a later time by calling the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,95,0)=" entry point ^PSOCPIBF from programmer mode."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,97,0)=" An example of the install process is included here under the title"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,98,0)=" ""Example Installation"". This must be run and finished before 02/01/02."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,99,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,101,0)="  1. Use the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,102,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,103,0)="  2. Review your mapped set. If the routines are mapped, they should"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,104,0)="     be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,105,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,106,0)="  3. If the estimated number of prescription fills that will be billed as"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,107,0)="     part of this clean up is extremely high, you may want to disable"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,108,0)="     journaling for Integrated Billing and Accounts Receivable globals ^IB"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,109,0)="     and ^PRCA."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,111,0)="  4. From the Kernel Installation & Distribution System menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,112,0)="     the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,114,0)="  5. From this menu, you may select to use the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,115,0)="     (when prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter PSO*7.0*93)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,117,0)="    a. Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,118,0)="       message of any routines exported with the patch. It will NOT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,119,0)="       backup any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,121,0)="    b. Compare Transport Global to Current System - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,122,0)="       allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,123,0)="       is installed. It compares all components of the patch (routines,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,124,0)="       DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,125,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,126,0)="    c. Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will ensure"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,127,0)="       the integrity of the routines that are in the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,129,0)="  6. Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package PSO*7.0*93."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,130,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,131,0)="  7. When Prompted ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,132,0)="     YES//"" respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,134,0)="  8. When Prompted ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,135,0)="     Protocols? YES//"" respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,137,0)="  9. When Prompted ""Queue copay clean-up Job to run Date/Time:"" respond"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,138,0)="     with the date/time to queue the cleanup background job or ""NOW""."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,140,0)=" 10. If Routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should be returned"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,141,0)="     to completion."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,142,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,143,0)=" 11. If journaling was disabled for globals ^IB and ^PRCA in step 3, it"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,144,0)="     should be re-enabled upon completion of the post-installation job."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,145,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,146,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,147,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,148,0)=" Example Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,149,0)=" ====================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,150,0)="Checking Install for Package PSO*7.0*93"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,151,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,152,0)="Install Questions for PSO*7.0*93"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,154,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,156,0)="Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,157,0)="Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",79,1,159,0)=" "
