^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",246,1,106,0)="COMMAND: Save "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",246,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",246,1,108,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",246,1,109,0)="End Capture ********** "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,0)="281 SEQ #253^3080526.161354^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,0)="^^82^82^3080526"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,1,0)="This patch has enhancements which extend the capabilities of the Veterans "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,2,0)="Health Information Systems and Technology Architecture (VistA) electronic "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,3,0)="pharmacy (ePharmacy) system that supports the Electronic Claims "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,4,0)="Management Engine (ECME).  It is the first of four stand alone patches"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,5,0)="that will fulfill the requirements of ePharmcy/ECME Enhancements Phase 4 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,6,0)="Iteration II.  It modifies the Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0 application as"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,7,0)="described below:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,10,0)="1.  EPHARMACY MEDICATION PROFILE (VIEW ONLY) [PSO PMP] option has been"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,11,0)="modified in the following manner:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,13,0)="    a.  Patients flagged with the Bad Address indicator will display the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,14,0)="        same warning messages as PATIENT PRESCRIPTION PROCESSING [PSO LM"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,15,0)="        BACKDOOR ORDERS] option. If the user holds the PSO ADDRESS UPDATE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,16,0)="        key, a prompt to update the address/phone will be displayed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,18,0)="    b.  The PU - Patient Record Update action has been added to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,19,0)="        Patient Medication Profile screen.  To achieve this, the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,20,0)="        PU action was added to the PATIENT MEDICATION PROFILE protocol"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,21,0)="        menu [PSO PMP MENU]."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,23,0)="        The following actions have been removed from the Patient "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,24,0)="        Medication Profile screen by removing them from the PATIENT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,25,0)="        MEDICATION PROFILE protocol menu [PSO PMP MENU]:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,27,0)="             DR         Sort By Drug"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,28,0)="             ID         Sort By Issue Date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,29,0)="             LF         Sort By Last Fill Date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,30,0)="             RX         Sort By Prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,32,0)="    c.  The above removed actions have been added to the hidden actions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,33,0)="        menu by adding them to the ePharmacy Medication Profile Hidden "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,34,0)="        Actions [PSO PMP HIDDEN ACTIONS MENU] protocol."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,36,0)="    d.  The REJ View Reject action was added to the hidden menu on the Rx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,37,0)="        View screen.  The ePharmacy Hidden Actions Menu #2 [PSO PMP HIDDEN"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,38,0)="        ACTIONS MENU #2] protocol was added to contain this new action,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,39,0)="        and this protocol is also used by the VIEW PRESCRIPTION option"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,40,0)="        [PSO VIEW]."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,43,0)="2.  The default answer of (I)gnore on the Reject Processing Screen has "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,44,0)="been changed to (Q)uit which automatically sends the claim rejection  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,45,0)="information to the Pharmacy Reject Worklist (i.e. re-instate discontinued "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,46,0)="order, unhold, refill, PP - pull early from suspense, edit that doesn't "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,47,0)="create a new order, and release with NDC edits). Due to conflicting patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,48,0)="release schedules and shared routines with another Pharmacy patch, the new"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,49,0)="order, copy, edits that create new orders, and renewal functions will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,50,0)="remain with a default answer of (I)gnore for reject processing screens"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,51,0)="displayed prior to label print. These functions will be updated in a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,52,0)="subsequent ePharmacy Iteration II patch when the conflict no longer"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,53,0)="exists."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,55,0)="3.  The VIEW PRESCRIPTION [PSO VIEW] option has been modified to give "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,56,0)="comprehensive help text for the VIEW PRESCRIPTION prompt.  The REJ View"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,57,0)="Reject action was added to the ePharmacy Hidden Actions Menu"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,58,0)="# 2 [PSO PMP HIDDEN ACTIONS MENU # 2]."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,60,0)="4.  The ECME LOG was recording the routing of WINDOW for all original "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,61,0)="fills and refills.  A modification was made to correctly state the route "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,62,0)="for each fill that is processed after this patch is installed.  The "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,63,0)="PATIENT PRESCRIPTION PROCESSING [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option,  VIEW"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,64,0)="PRESCRIPTION [PSO VIEW] option, and EPHARMACY MEDICATION PROFILE (VIEW "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,65,0)="ONLY) [PSO PMP] option is affected by this change."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,67,0)="5.  The ECME Log entry that is stored when a prescription is printed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,68,0)="from suspense has been changed from stating ECME:SUSP LABEL PRINTED to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,69,0)="ECME:PRINTED FROM SUSPENSE.  This change will affect fills processed "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,70,0)="after this patch has been installed.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,72,0)="6.  A change was made to allow the user to edit Dispensed As Written (DAW)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,73,0)="and National Drug Code (NDC) fields for expired and discontinued ePharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,74,0)="prescriptions and refills."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,76,0)="7.  A modification was made to store the last used NDC for payable "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,77,0)="prescriptions that were pulled early from suspense.  This change affects"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,78,0)="the PULL EARLY FROM SUSPENSE [PSO PNDRX] option and the PP Pull RX action"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,79,0)="of the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,81,0)="8.  A post intall routine (PSO260PI) from PSO*7.0*260 will be deleted "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",247,1,82,0)="with this patch."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,0)="291 SEQ #254^3080526.19203^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,0)="^^35^35^3080526"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,2,0)="This patch corrects the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,4,0)="1. In the Delete a Prescription [PSO RXDL] option:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,5,0)="  a. If entering a prescription number that has previously been deleted "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,6,0)="and then pressing enter when prompted for a prescription again, an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,7,0)="undefined error occurs. (HD212690)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,8,0)="  b. If enter a character like ! at the prescription prompt, 2 question"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,9,0)="marks are displayed because it is an invalid prescription. Then at the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,10,0)="next prompt for prescription, if an @ is entered, an undefined error "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,11,0)="occurs. (HD210092)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,13,0)="2. In the Prescription Cost Update [PSO RXCOST UPDATE] option, unless the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,14,0)="original fill date for the prescription is included in the requested date "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,15,0)="range, the cost will not be updated in the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,16,0)="any of the fills. If the user selects to update refills and partials "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,17,0)="also, it updates all fills on the prescription regardless of whether "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,18,0)="they were within the requested date range. This patch makes a correction"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,19,0)="to update fills only within the requested range without having to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,20,0)="include the original fill in that range. If the user selects an end fill"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,21,0)="date of today or in the future, this option will update the cost for all"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,22,0)="existing and suspended fills that have a fill date in the future. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,23,0)="(HD213587)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,25,0)="3. Older data in the Health Data Repository (HDR) could contain"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,26,0)="non-numeric data in the quantity field for some prescriptions. The data"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,27,0)="definition was changed in patch PSO*7*29 to no longer allow alpha"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,28,0)="characters. The following was added to the technical description for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,29,0)="  1. QTY field (#7) in the PRESCRIPTION file (#52)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,30,0)="  2. QTY field (#1) in the PRESCRIPTION file REFILL multiple (#52.1)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,31,0)="  3. QTY field (#.04) in the PRESCRIPTION file PARTIAL multiple (#52.2)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,33,0)=" NOTE: QTY values that were on file prior to patch PSO*7*29 (released"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,34,0)=" 2/17/00) may contain alpha characters."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",248,1,35,0)="(HD211759)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",249,0)="246 SEQ #255^3080526.193049^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",249,1,0)="^^8^8^3080526"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",249,1,1,0)="MODIFY PSO COST TO IGNORE BAD XREFS IN FILE 52"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",249,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",249,1,3,0)="An Undefined error occurs when editing a large number of prescriptions."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",249,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",249,1,5,0)="Correct OPAI option 4 in file #59 field #28 (send marked drugs and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",249,1,6,0)="print labels)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",249,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",249,1,8,0)="Locking Issue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,0)="293 SEQ #256^3080526.193211^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,0)="^^223^223^3080526"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,1,0)="This patch performs the actual prescription clean up for prescriptions "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,2,0)="identified by patch PSO*7*283. Patch PSO*7*283 performed a tally, while "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,3,0)="this patch will correct the prescriptions with the expiration date and/or"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,4,0)="status issues. In some cases the date is not present and other cases have "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,5,0)="a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,6,0)="wrong date. Furthermore, most of the prescriptions with such problems are"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,7,0)="not in sync with Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 3.0 and/or"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,8,0)="Health Data Repository (HDR) in regards to their status. This patch makes"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,9,0)="the correction to the expiration date of these prescriptions and send "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,10,0)="messages to CPRS and HDR so these two applications can update the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,11,0)="corresponding order with the expired status on their systems. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,12,0)="will address these problems. Below is a detailed description on this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,13,0)="process:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,15,0)="Expiration post-install job clean-up flow:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,16,0)="------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,17,0)="In order to explain the process to clean up these prescriptions the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,18,0)="following terms will be mentioned below:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,20,0)="CUTOFF DATE: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,21,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,22,0)="This is the date last processed by the Auto Expiration Background Job."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,23,0)="This background job is supposed to be run nightly by every site. This date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,24,0)="is stored in the field DATE AUTO-EXPIRE COMPLETED (#49.95) in PHARMACY"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,25,0)="SYSTEM file (#59.7) and it was introduced by the patch PSS*1*128 and it "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,26,0)="should be populated with a valid date in all site. In case this field is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,27,0)="null, the post-install routine in this patch will set it to to the date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,28,0)="corresponding to 2 days in the past from this patch installation date. For"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,29,0)="example, if the patch is installed on March 5, 2008 and the field is null,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,30,0)="it will be set to March 3, 2008 (in the correct Fileman date format)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,32,0)="CALCULATED EXPIRATION DATE:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,33,0)="--------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,34,0)="The expiration date for prescription with a null expiration date is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,35,0)="calculated by the following formula:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,36,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,37,0)=" For Rx with no refills: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,39,0)="      NUMBER OF DAYS SUPPLY FROM Rx ISSUE DATE (MININUM: 30 DAYS)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,41,0)=" Rx with 1 or more refills: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,42,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,43,0)="      Non-controlled Substances: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,44,0)="Rx ISSUE DATE + 366 DAYS    "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,46,0)="      Controlled Substances    : Rx ISSUE DATE + 184 DAYS        "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,48,0)="CPRS 'NON-ACTIVE' STATUS:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,49,0)="------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,50,0)="The following CPRS statuses: DISCONTINUED, EXPIRED, DISCONTINUED/EDIT and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,51,0)="CANCELLED are considered 'NON-ACTIVE' by Pharmacy in this clean up "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,52,0)="process."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,53,0)="This means that Pharmacy will not send a prescription expiration event to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,54,0)="CPRS if the CPRS order status is set to one of these."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,56,0)="PHARMACY 'NON-ACTIVE' STATUS:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,57,0)="---------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,58,0)="The following Pharmacy statuses: EXPIRED, DISCONTINUED, DELETED, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,59,0)="DISCONTINUED BY PROVIDER, DISCONTINUED (EDIT) are considered 'NON-ACTIVE'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,60,0)="by Pharmacy in this clean up process."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,61,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,63,0)="CLEAN UP PROCESS DESCRIPTION:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,64,0)="---------------------------- "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,65,0)="Prescriptions with an expiration date problem are being analyzed and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,66,0)="cleaned up differently, depending on which GROUP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,67,0)=" below they fall under:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,68,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,69,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,70,0)="GROUP 1:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,71,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,72,0)="Prescriptions with a null expiration date for patients."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,73,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,74,0)="  a) Set the CALCULATED EXPIRATION DATE in the EXPIRATION DATE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,75,0)="     field (#26) of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,76,0)="  b) If the expiration date is on or before the CUTOFF DATE "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,77,0)="     b1) If the prescription is not already in a Pharmacy 'NON-ACTIVE'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,78,0)="         status, set the STATUS field (#100) in the PRESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,79,0)="         file (#52) to EXPIRED."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,80,0)="     b2) Update CPRS*"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,81,0)="     b3) Update HDR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,82,0)="  c) If the expiration date is past the CUTOFF DATE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,83,0)="     c1) Update HDR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,84,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,85,0)="GROUP 2:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,86,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,87,0)="Expired prescriptions for patients."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,89,0)="  a) If the prescription expiration date is GREATER than 366 days"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,90,0)="     a1) A new expiration date will be calculated and set in the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,91,0)="         EXPIRATION DATE field (#26) of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,92,0)="     a2) Update CPRS*"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,93,0)="     a3) Update HDR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,94,0)="  b) If the prescription expiration date is LESS than 366 days"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,95,0)="     b1) Update CPRS*"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,96,0)="     b2) Update HDR (if CPRS is updated)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,98,0)="GROUP 3:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,99,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,100,0)="Prescriptions with an expiration date on or before the CUTOFF DATE with"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,101,0)="a Pharmacy 'ACTIVE' status"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,102,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,103,0)="  a) Set the STATUS field (#100) in the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,104,0)="     EXPIRED."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,105,0)="  b) If the CPRS order status is 'ACTIVE'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,106,0)="     b1) Update CPRS*"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,107,0)="     b2) Update HDR (if CPRS is updated)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,108,0)="  c) If the CPRS order status is 'NON-ACTIVE' "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,109,0)="     c1) Update HDR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,110,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,111,0)="   NOTE: If the prescription does not have a corresponding CPRS Order"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,112,0)="         Number, the counter for this specific problem will be "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,113,0)="         incremented. However, the HDR will not be updated. HDR will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,114,0)="         perform their own clean up for these cases."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,115,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,116,0)="GROUP 4:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,117,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,118,0)="Deleted prescriptions for patients."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,120,0)="  a) Update HDR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,123,0)="  * CPRS will only be updated if the prescription contains the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,124,0)="    corresponding CPRS Order Number for the prescription being cleaned"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,125,0)="    up. Furthermore, CPRS will not be updated if the corresponding "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,126,0)="    CPRS order is on a 'NON-ACTIVE' status."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,127,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,129,0)="The clean up process will start right after the patch is installed. If "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,130,0)="it is necessary to stop, restart the job or to know the status of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,131,0)="job, do the following:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,132,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,134,0)=">D ^PSO293PI              "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,135,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,136,0)="     Expiration Date clean up job for Outpatient Pharamcy prescriptions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,137,0)="     =================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,138,0)="     Current status: RUNNING (Last Rx IEN: 2587430)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,140,0)="     Select one of the following:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,141,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,142,0)="          SP        STOP CLEAN UP JOB"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,143,0)="          VW        VIEW PARTIAL CLEAN UP JOB RESULTS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,144,0)="          QT        QUIT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,145,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,146,0)="(SP)Stop,(VW)View,(QT)Quit: VIEW//  VIEW PARTIAL CLEAN UP JOB RESULTS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,147,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,149,0)="Expiration Date clean up job for Outpatient Pharmacy prescriptions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,150,0)="=================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,151,0)="Current status: COMPLETED ON Nov 06, 2007@17:03:36"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,152,0)="DATE AUTO-EXPIRE COMPLETED field: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,154,0)="1. Institution   : SITE NAME VAMC (999)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,155,0)="                                                              # of  Rx's"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,156,0)="Group 1: RX'S WITH NO EXPIRATION DATE                         cleaned up"
