^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,196,0)="Once the clean up process is completed, the same information above will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,197,0)="sent via Mailman message on FORUM to the user who installed the patch and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,198,0)="to the following support personnel below:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,200,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,201,0)="        NAME                     Role"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,202,0)="        -----------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,203,0)="        Bruun, Jesse             HDR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,204,0)="        Consentino, Albert       EPS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,205,0)="        Mohamed, Anwer           Developer"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,206,0)="        Rocha, Marcelo           Developer"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,207,0)="        Ruzbacki, Ron            Developer"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,208,0)="        Willette, Candice        Implementation Analyst"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,209,0)="        Williamson, Eric         Project Manager"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,210,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,211,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,212,0)="Note: The sites will not have to take any action once they receive the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,213,0)="      result message above generated by the post-install. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,214,0)="The message "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,215,0)="      will not be generated from non-production accounts (e.g., test"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,216,0)="      account)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,217,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,218,0)="Besides the clean up process, this patch introduces a change intended to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,219,0)="address a sporadic scenario where a prescription does not contain a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,220,0)="pointer to the corresponding CPRS order # and it goes through a status"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,221,0)="change (e.g. from Active to Expired). Currently, such status change event"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,222,0)="is not communicated to HDR. This patch contains a fix to notify HDR of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",250,1,223,0)="the status change event for such prescriptions."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,0)="294 SEQ #257^3080722.080929^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,0)="^^23^23^3080722"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,1,0)="This patch introduces the components necessary to build four tools"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,2,0)="useful for medication reconciliation."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,4,0)="Tool 1 is a Medication Reconciliation Profile health summary component."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,5,0)="This report creates an alphabetical list of outpatient prescriptions,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,6,0)="unit dose medications, documented non-VA medications, and remote VA"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,7,0)="medications.  This summary can be used at transition points in a patient's"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,8,0)="care, (admission, discharge, etc.) to identify medications that need to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,9,0)="be continued, new items to be ordered, old items to be discontinued, or"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,10,0)="orders that need to be changed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,12,0)="Tool 2 is a Medication Chart health summary component.  This report"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,13,0)="provides a grid-formatted list of active and pending medications suitable"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,14,0)="for giving to a patient at a clinic visit or upon discharge from the hospital."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,16,0)="Tool 3 is a TIU data object provided as an alternative to the Medication"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,17,0)="Chart health summary process.  The unique aspect of this object is that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,18,0)="the list, generated for the patient,includes recently expired"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,19,0)="medications but not recently discontinued medications."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,21,0)="Tool 4 is a series of TIU data objects and health summary components that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,22,0)="retrieve remote active medications and remote allergy/ADR data."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",251,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",252,0)="288 SEQ #258^3080722.143453^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",252,1,0)="^^1^1^3080722"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",252,1,1,0)="SUBSCRIPT ERROR WHEN RUNNING THE HEALTH SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",253,0)="279 SEQ #260^3090420.155214^1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",253,1,0)="^^5^5^3090420"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",253,1,1,0)="This patch will correct the following"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",253,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",253,1,3,0)="HD216000 - PSOAUTRF Key"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",253,1,4,0)="HD226478 - Field missing in NTE segment of HL7 for PMI"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",253,1,5,0)="HD214848 - Incorrect wording:  Division used to describe Institution"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,0)="225^3090421.155114^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,0)="^^156^156^3090421"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,1,0)="The Enrollment VistA Changes (EVC) project is being undertaken to support"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,2,0)="technology and business changes that are occurring with the implementation"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,3,0)="of the Health Eligibility Center (HEC) Enrollment System Redesign (ESR)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,4,0)="project. Some modified and new business functionality is being included in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,5,0)="the new system and corresponding changes are necessary in VistA for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,6,0)="preliminary determination of veterans Enrollment and Eligibility status."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,7,0)="The EVC project has been rolled out in three phases. This release"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,8,0)="represents the third and last phase called EVC Release 2."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,10,0)="This patch provides the functionality changes to determine, process and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,11,0)="disseminate the newly added Environmental Indicator (EI) called Project"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,12,0)="112/SHAD Exposure (a.k.a SHAD), where applicable."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,14,0)="This patch also changed the EI, ""Environmental Contaminant"" to read"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,15,0)="as ""Southwest Asia Conditions""."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,17,0)=" 1. For the following options, when creating a new order, renewing an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,18,0)="    existing order, copying an existing order to a new order, or editing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,19,0)="    an existing order that results in a new order, the copay status of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,20,0)="    prescription needs to be determined for billing purposes."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,22,0)="    a. Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,23,0)="    b. Barcode Batch Prescription Entry [PSO BATCH BARCODE]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,24,0)="    c. Complete Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,26,0)="   If a patient is found eligible for SHAD then the prompt"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,27,0)="   ""Was treatment related to PROJ 112/SHAD?"" will be presented to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,28,0)="   pharmacist."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,30,0)="   A ""YES"" or ""NO"" response will be stored in the new fields, PROJ"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,31,0)="   112/SHAD field (#122.01) of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) and in the PROJ"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,32,0)="   112/SHAD field (#8) of the ICD DIAGNOSIS sub-file (#52.052311) of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,33,0)="   PRESCRIPTION file (#52)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,35,0)=" 2. The Integration Control Registration (ICR) #2534, provides"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,36,0)="    Computerized Patient Record System V. 3.0 (CPRS) with all the eligible"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,37,0)="    EI questions that will be prompted during the pharmacy order entry"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,38,0)="    process. This ICR is modified to include the SHAD prompt."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,40,0)=" 3. When a verbal or telephone order is placed in backdoor pharmacy, it"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,41,0)="    requires an electronic signature from the provider. During the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,42,0)="    signature entry process in CPRS, the provider may update the SC, EI,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,43,0)="    or the ICD diagnosis information. This updated information is passed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,44,0)="    back to pharmacy via the ICR #4666, which is modified to include the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,45,0)="    SHAD changes."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,47,0)=" 4. The PENDING OUTPATIENT ORDERS file (#52.41) that stores the pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,48,0)="    orders entered via CPRS is modified to include the provider's response"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,49,0)="    to the SHAD question. The provider's response will be stored in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,50,0)="    new fields, PROJ 112/SHAD field (#110.2) of the PENDING OUTPATIENT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,51,0)="    ORDERS file (#52.41) and the PROJ 112/SHAD field (#8) of the DIAGNOSIS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,52,0)="    sub-file (#52.41311) of the PENDING OUTPATIENT ORDERS file (#52.41)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,54,0)=" 5. During the release of a prescription, if the SHAD question applies and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,55,0)="    is unanswered, the MailMan message that is sent to the finishing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,56,0)="    pharmacist, ordering provider, and holders of the PSO COPAY key, to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,57,0)="    get answers to the EI questions will have the SHAD question if"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,58,0)="    applicable."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,60,0)=" 6. The Reset Copay Status/Cancel Charges [PSOCP RESET COPAY STATUS]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,61,0)="    option is modified to include the SHAD question wherever applicable."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,63,0)=" 7. During label printing, if the prescription is flagged as SHAD then the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,64,0)="    text ""NO COPAY"" will be printed in the label."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,66,0)="Unrelated to the Enrollment VistA Changes (EVC) features, this patch also"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,67,0)="provides the following changes to support CPRS v27."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,69,0)=" a. To add the proper escape sequences to the standard HEALTH LEVEL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,70,0)="    SEVEN (HL7) encoding characters to messages sent to CPRS / remove"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,71,0)="    escape sequences received from CPRS and replace them with standard HL7"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,72,0)="    encoding characters. This will help avoid errors that can occur if"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,73,0)="    special delimiting characters are encountered during parsing of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,74,0)="    HL7 messages."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,76,0)=" b. Integration Control Registration (ICR) #2400, will be modified to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,77,0)="    provide new sorting sequences of the patient medication profile that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,78,0)="    is viewed under the CPRS-Meds Tab including the Non-VA medications."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,80,0)="    VIEW 0 or null - This provides the medication list as it was prior to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,81,0)="             GUI 27 so that other applications calling this API will not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,82,0)="             see any changes."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,83,0)="    VIEW 1 - This provides the medication list sorted by prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,84,0)="             Status Group and Stop Date/Expiration Date. Following is the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,85,0)="             order:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,86,0)="            Pending group"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,87,0)="              Non-Verified"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,88,0)="              Pending"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,89,0)="            Active group:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,90,0)="              Active"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,91,0)="              Hold"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,92,0)="              Suspended (Active/Susp)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,93,0)="              Provider Hold"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,94,0)="            Expired group"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,95,0)="              Expired"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,96,0)="            Discontinued/Deleted group"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,97,0)="              Discontinued by Provider"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,98,0)="              Discontinued (Edit)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,99,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,100,0)="    VIEW 2 - This provides the medication list sorted by prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,101,0)="             Status Group, Status, and Drug Name."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,102,0)="            Active group:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,103,0)="              Active"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,104,0)="              Hold"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,105,0)="            Pending group"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,106,0)="              Non-Verified"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,107,0)="              Pending"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,108,0)="            Discontinued"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,109,0)="              Discontinued by Provider"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,110,0)="              Discontinued (Edit)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,112,0)="    VIEW 3 - This provides the medication list sorted by Drug Name,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,113,0)="           active/suspended and Stop Date/Expiration Date."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,115,0)=" c. Flag/Un-Flag functionality (PSI-06-041)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,116,0)="    It was requested in the Remedy ticket #133716 that the flagging"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,117,0)="    capability that is available in CPRS be made available for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,118,0)="    Outpatient Pharmacy use. This patch provides the flagging"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,119,0)="    functionality for Pending orders only."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,121,0)=" d. As per the E3R numbers 19973 and 19876, to improve communication"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,122,0)="    between the provider and the pharmacist, Outpatient Pharmacy will now"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,123,0)="    send the actual comments made by the pharmacist to CPRS when a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,124,0)="    prescription is put on Hold, Discontinued, and Returned to Stock"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,125,0)="    replacing the generic ""per pharmacy request"" text."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,127,0)=" e. When the DC-Discontinue ListMan option is used to discontinue a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,128,0)="    pending ""renewal"" order, the software will now check for an active"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,129,0)="    prescription for the same drug. If found it will prompt the following:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,130,0)="    ""There is an active Rx for this pending order, Discontinue both"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,131,0)="    (Y/N)""."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,132,0)="    This will provide the user with the option to discontinue both pending"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,133,0)="    and the active order."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,134,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,135,0)=" f. A problem was reported in one of the error messages displayed on CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,136,0)="    side when a provider tries to discontinue an Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,137,0)="    order from the Orders Tab and that order for some reason is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,138,0)="    not found in the PRESCRIPTION file (#52). The solution provided is to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,139,0)="    replace the error message ""Unable to locate order"" with ""Invalid"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,140,0)="    Pharmacy order number"" to be in consistent with the Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,141,0)="    Medications V. 5.0 error messages."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,142,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,143,0)=" g. At the request of CPRS active calls to obsolete routine OR3CONV have"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,144,0)="    been removed from Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,145,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,146,0)=" h. When finishing a pending order placed in CPRS, it was reported that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,147,0)="    the patient instructions sent across to CPRS was getting truncated."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,148,0)="    This patch fixes the problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,150,0)=" i. PSI-07-057 - Potential of inappropriate or misleading provider"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,151,0)="    comments to be automatically included on new medication orders."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,152,0)="    To fix this problem CPRS is dropping (will not carry over) the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,153,0)="    original provider comments during renewals of Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,154,0)="    medications."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,155,0)="    To follow suit with CPRS, Outpatient Pharmacy is also dropping the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",254,1,156,0)="    original provider comments from all backdoor renewals."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",255,0)="304 SEQ #263^3090421.161856^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",255,1,0)="^^1^1^3090421"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",255,1,1,0)="Order checks are not generated when editing the dose of a prescription."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,0)="287 SEQ #264^3090421.16222^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,0)="^^168^168^3090421"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,1,0)="This patch is one of four patches that enhance the ePharmacy software to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,2,0)="provide the framework to support Tricare and Active Duty outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,3,0)="pharmacy billing.  The Tricare/Active Duty portions of this software"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,4,0)="enhancement will not be active until a future patch is released.  The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,5,0)="release of the additional patch is pending Central Business Office (CBO)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,6,0)="contracting with the Tricare Fiscal Intermediary."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,8,0)="Below is a list of all the applications involved in this project along "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,9,0)="with their associated patch number:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,11,0)="       APPLICATION/VERSION                                  PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,12,0)="     --------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,13,0)=" 1.  CONSOLIDATED MAIL OUTPATIENT PHARMCY (CMOP) V. 2.0   PSX*2*66"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,14,0)=" 2.  OUTPATIENT PHARMACY (OP) V. 7.0                      PSO*7*287"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,15,0)=" 3.  ELECTRONIC CLAIMS MANAGEMENT ENGINE (ECME) V. 1.0    BPS*1*6"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,16,0)=" 4.  INTEGRATED BILLING (IB) V. 2.0                       IB*2*383"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,18,0)="All four patches are being released separately with a requirement that "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,19,0)="they be installed in the order outlined above.  There are no other "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,20,0)="dependencies between these patches, except that Tricare/Active Duty "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,21,0)="billing will not be supported by ePharmacy until all 4 patches are "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,22,0)="installed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,24,0)="All sites should install these patches regardless of whether or not they "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,25,0)="have been activated for ePharmacy by the CBO or are providing outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,26,0)="pharmacy services to Tricare or Active Duty patients.  After the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,27,0)="installation of these patches, the activation status of the site will not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,28,0)="be impacted.  As before, activation of the ePharmacy product will require"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,29,0)="instructions provided by the CBO, and sites are not to activate ePharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,30,0)="unless instructed specifically by the CBO.  Also, sites should not start"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,31,0)="to provide outpatient pharmacy services to Tricare patients without"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,32,0)="discussions with the CBO."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,34,0)="This patch modifies the Outpatient Pharmacy v7.0 application as described"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,35,0)="below.  The modifications labeled dormant in the software and will remain"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,36,0)="inactive until the future Tricare patch is released."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,38,0)="1.  (Dormant) - Prescriptions where the patient is Tricare eligible will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,39,0)="be submitted to ECME for third party insurance processing in the same"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,40,0)="manner as all other insurance types.  Tricare eligibility is determined by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,41,0)="Integrated Billing (IB). An indicator is returned to Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,42,0)="PRESCRIPTION file (#52) and REFILL multiple (#52.1) to be stored in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,43,0)="new BILLING ELIGIBILITY INDICATOR field (#85).  Because this is a set of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,44,0)="codes field, the internal value will be T, V or C. These values will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,45,0)="displayed respectively to the user as TRICARE, VETERAN, or CHAMPVA. Note"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,46,0)="that CHAMPVA will not be addressed in this patch.  Prescriptions with only"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,47,0)="a 'VETERAN' eligibility flag are what is currently processed through ECME."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,49,0)="2.  (Dormant) - When a Tricare prescription has a third party rejection,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,50,0)="the same reject notification screen will be displayed to the user as is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,51,0)="currently done for the Veteran eligibility.  Tricare Rejections will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,52,0)="stored in the same manner as Drug Utilization Review (DUR) and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,53,0)="Refill-too-soon (RTS) prescription reject are currently stored."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,55,0)="The following exceptions will apply for Tricare prescriptions:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,57,0)="    A.  All Tricare rejections will be denoted as Tricare in the REJECT "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,58,0)="        Information header on the Reject Information screen."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,60,0)="    B.  Where DUR or RTS are one of the reject codes, the user will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,61,0)="        able to select from (D)iscontinue the prescription, submit "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,62,0)="        (O)verride codes, or (Q)uit which sends the rejection to the Third"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,63,0)="        Party Payer Rejects - Worklist.  Tricare rejection may not be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,64,0)="        (I)gnored."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,66,0)="    C.  For prescription rejections that have non-DUR/RTS rejects, the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,67,0)="        user will be able to select from (D)iscontinue the prescription or"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,68,0)="        (Q)uit which sends it to the Third Party Payer Rejects - Worklist."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,70,0)="    D.  For non-billable Tricare prescriptions, an abbreviated version of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,71,0)="        the reject notification screen will be displayed.  Because the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,72,0)="        prescriptions is non-billable, the insurance and ECME information"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,73,0)="        that's currently provided for DUR/RTS rejects will not be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,74,0)="        displayed (i.e. insurance, group name, group #, ECME #, contact,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,75,0)="        cardholder ID).  In this case, the user will only be able to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,76,0)="        (D)iscontinue the prescription due to the business rule that OP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,77,0)="        cannot fill Tricare prescriptions that are non-billable."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,79,0)="    E.  Labels will not print for discontinued Tricare prescriptions."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,80,0)="        Reprint labels will not be allowed to be printed for Tricare"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,81,0)="        rejected prescriptions.  The reject notification screen will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,82,0)="        displayed during reprint in the same manner as non-Tricare"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,83,0)="        prescription currently are displayed with the exception of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,84,0)="        available actions listed above for Tricare prescriptions."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,86,0)="    F.  Suspended prescriptions will remain on suspense when a reject"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,87,0)="        occurs, when the Rx is non-billable, or when the third party claim"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,88,0)="        remains in an 'IN PROGRESS' status in ECME.  Labels will not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,89,0)="        print.  Once the reject is resolved, the user may pull the Rx "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,90,0)="        early from suspense or wait for the next scheduled print from"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,91,0)="        suspense runs at which time labels will print accordingly. This"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,92,0)="        includes CMOP and local suspense."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,93,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,94,0)="    G.  Rejected Tricare prescription may not have a partial fill ordered "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,95,0)="        until the reject is resolved."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,97,0)="    H.  When the  Pull Early from Suspense [PSO PNDRX] option is used, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,98,0)="        Tricare prescriptions will be processed in the foreground and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,99,0)="        rejections will be displayed for user intervention."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,101,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,102,0)="3.  (Dormant except for item C.) - The Third Party Payer Rejects -"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,103,0)="Worklist [PSO REJECTS WORKLIST] option and the Third Party Payer Rejects -"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,104,0)="View/Process [PSO REJECTS VIEW/PROCESS] options have been modified in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,105,0)="following manner:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,107,0)="     A. Non-DUR/RTS Tricare rejections will be segregated at the end of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,108,0)="        the displayed information. They will be denoted with a ""TRICARE -"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,109,0)="        Non-DUR/RTS"" header.  This header will remain regardless of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,110,0)="        whether the GI - Group by Insurance action is toggled on or off.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,111,0)="        The Tricare section will sort in the same manner as the main sort"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,112,0)="        for non-Tricare prescriptions (i.e. by Rx, drug, patient, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,113,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,114,0)="     B. Tricare DUR/RTS rejects will be displayed with all other DUR/RTS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,115,0)="        rejects.  When GI - Group by Insurance action is toggled on, the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,116,0)="        header ""TRICARE"" will be displayed, and this ""TRICARE"" section"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,117,0)="        will sort alphabetically within the other insurances.  This"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,118,0)="        Tricare section is separate from the Non-DUR/RTS section that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,119,0)="        displays at the end of the listing.  When GI is toggled off, these"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,120,0)="        rejects will sorted in the same section as all other DUR/RTS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,121,0)="        rejects."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,123,0)="     C. (Not dormant) - The new TRI - Show/Hide Tricare toggle action has"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,124,0)="        been added to the hidden menu on the Insurance Rejects screen.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,125,0)="        When toggled to Show, Tricare Non-DUR/RTS reject will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,126,0)="        automatically displayed at the end of the listing.  Toggling the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,127,0)="        TRI action to Hide will remove them from the screen."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,129,0)="     D. The Reject Information screen has been modified to display TRICARE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,130,0)="        in the header for the Reject Information section.  For DUR/RTS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,131,0)="        Tricare rejects, the IGN - Ignore Reject action will be shown but"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,132,0)="        will not be selectable. For Non-DUR/RTS Tricare rejects, the FIL -"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,133,0)="        Fill Rx action will be displayed. If the prescription is payable,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,134,0)="        the user will be allowed to fill the prescription and print the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,135,0)="        label.  If not payable, a message will be displayed stating that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,136,0)="        the prescription must have a payable status to be filled."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,138,0)="     E. For rejects that remain in suspense, the user will be allowed to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,139,0)="        process the rejection as indicated above, however no labels will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,140,0)="        be printed until the prescription is pulled early or printed from"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,141,0)="        suspense.  Upon resolving the reject, the user will be notified"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,142,0)="        of this information.  CMOP prescriptions will function in the same"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,143,0)="        manner."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,145,0)="4.  In preparation for a future ePharmacy patch the following fields are "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,146,0)="being added to PRESCRIPTION file (#52) for original fills and refills:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,147,0)="DATE NDC VALIDATED field (#83) and NDC VALIDATED BY field (#84).  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,149,0)="5.  For ePharmacy prescriptions, the price per dispense unit for the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,150,0)="NDC will be saved in PRESCRIPTION file (#52).  For original fills, the  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,151,0)="UNIT PRICE OF DRUG field (#17) will be updated.  For refills, the CURRENT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,152,0)="UNIT PRICE OF DRUG field (#1.2) of REFILL multiple (#52.1) will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,153,0)="updated. If the NDC chosen is the default NDC, the value stored will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,154,0)="taken from PRICE PER DISPENSE UNIT field (#16) of DRUG file (#50).  If the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,155,0)="NDC selected is a synonym, the PRICE PER DISPENSE UNIT field (#404) of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,156,0)="SYNONYM multiple (#9) of DRUG file (#50) will be saved. In the case of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,157,0)="CMOP fills, only the default NDC price will be stored which is taken from"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,158,0)="PRICE PER DISPENSE UNIT field (#16) of DRUG file (#50)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,159,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,160,0)="6.  (Dormant) - If ECME's status on the claim remains in an ""In Progress"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,161,0)="state past the processing time out during finish of the prescription,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,162,0)="Tricare prescriptions will not be allowed to be filled and must be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,163,0)="discontinued."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,164,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,165,0)="7.  (Dormant) - If the pharmacy is active for ePharmacy processing but the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,166,0)="insurance plan is not linked or not active, Tricare prescription will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,167,0)="allowed to be filled normally.  The phrase ""Inactive ECME Tricare"" will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",256,1,168,0)="displayed during Finish."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",257,0)="297 SEQ #265^3090421.162507^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",257,1,0)="^^1^1^3090421"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",257,1,1,0)="SCRIPTALK DISPLAYING LAST 6 OF SSN"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,0)="315 SEQ #266^3090421.163227^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,0)="^^16^16^3090421"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,1,0)="CPRS GUI V27 FOLLOW UP ISSUES: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,2,0)="============================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,4,0)="The Complete Orders From OERR option [PSO LMOE FINISH] breaks when the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,5,0)="user selects to process pending orders via Priority status and when they"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,6,0)="answer ""NO""  to the prompt ""Do you want to see Medication Profile? Yes//"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,7,0)="NO. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,9,0)="Below is a screen capture of the hard error:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,12,0)="             .D PP S ORD=0 D @PSRT S PAT(PAT)=PAT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,13,0)="                             ^"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,14,0)="             <NOLINE>PRI+15^PSOORFI5"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",258,1,16,0)="This patch will correct this issue."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",259,0)="299 SEQ #267^3090422.122147^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",259,1,0)="^^6^6^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",259,1,1,0)="This patch contains two APIs for extracting data from the PRESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",259,1,2,0)="(#52) file. The APIs are in the routine PSOCLINR, the APIs are:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",259,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",259,1,4,0)="STAT(PSO) ;Returns Status (#100) external format from Prescription (#52)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",259,1,5,0)="           file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",259,1,6,0)="NEPSRX()  ;Returns the number of prescriptions in the file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",260,0)="317 SEQ #268^3090422.151935^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",260,1,0)="^^8^8^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",260,1,1,0)="This patch modifies the Outpatient Pharmacy v7.0 application as described"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",260,1,2,0)="below:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",260,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",260,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",260,1,5,0)="1. After release of an ePharmacy Phase 4 patch (PSO*7*287), it was found"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",260,1,6,0)="that the PSOORED6 routine was erring or causing a DIE error due to a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",260,1,7,0)="variable being killed in a called routine.  This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",260,1,8,0)="error."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",261,0)="296 SEQ #269^3090422.152622^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",261,1,0)="^^5^5^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",261,1,1,0)="The ""stop date"" for complex Outpatient prescriptions do not display in "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",261,1,2,0)="the Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS). This patch resolves this "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",261,1,3,0)="issue.  The resolution implemented by this patch is not retroactive.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",261,1,4,0)="Only Outpatient prescriptions entered after patch installation will "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",261,1,5,0)="display the ""stop date"" in CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,0)="303 SEQ #270^3090422.155224^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,0)="^^50^50^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,1,0)="This patch has enhancements which extend the capabilities of the Veterans "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,2,0)="Health Information Systems and Technology Architecture (VistA) electronic "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,3,0)="pharmacy (ePharmacy) billing system."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,5,0)="All sites should install this patches regardless of whether or not they "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,6,0)="have been activated for ePharmacy by the Central Business Office (CBO).  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,7,0)="After the installation of these patches, the activation status of the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,8,0)="site will not be impacted.  As before, activation of the ePharmacy "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,9,0)="product will require instructions provided by the CBO.  Sites are not to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,10,0)="activate unless instructed specifically by the CBO."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,12,0)="This patch is being released along with PSS*1*139 and IB*2*405.  These"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,13,0)="patches can be installed in any order but the full functionality "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,14,0)="for Nutritional Supplement additions contained within these patches will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,15,0)="not be available until all 3 patches are installed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,17,0)="This patch modifies the Outpatient Pharmacy v7.0 application as described"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,18,0)="below:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,19,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,20,0)="1.  Modifications to change the default answer of (I)gnore on the Reject "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,21,0)="Processing Screen to (Q)uit which automatically sends the claim rejection "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,22,0)="information to the Pharmacy Reject Worklist for new orders, copies, edits "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,23,0)="that create new orders, and renewal functions.  This patch, PSO*7*303,  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,24,0)="includes the modifications for these functions."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,26,0)="2.  Additional software to handle the new ""N  for Nutritional Supplement"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,27,0)="DEA special handling code added in patch PSS*1*139.  This new ""N"" code"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,28,0)="will be treated the same as supply items and investigational drugs in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,29,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy.  Copay will not be charged, and third party billing "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,30,0)="for these type drugs will only occur when the drug is also marked with "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,31,0)="""E"" for Electronically Billable.  When the drug is not defined to be "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,32,0)="electronically billable, the ECME Log will reflect drug not billable.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,33,0)="For prescriptions where the eligibility changed since the last refill, a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,34,0)="""PRESCRIPTION QUESTIONS REVIEW NEEDED"" MailMan message is sent.  The last "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,35,0)="paragraph of this message will be changed to include nutritional drugs:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,37,0)="     Supply, nutritional and investigational drugs are not charged a VA"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,38,0)="     copay but could be reimbursable by third party insurance."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,40,0)="3.  For the ePharmacy Medication Profile (VIEW ONLY) [PSO PMP] option,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,41,0)="flagged pending orders will be notated on the medication profile screen by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,42,0)="highlighting the sequence number shown on the left side of the screen.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,43,0)="Note that the ""Flagged by..."" information shown once the prescription is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,44,0)="selected is already present with the PSO*7*225 release."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,46,0)="4.  For Tricare Reversal/Resubmit actions sent to ECME with NDC changes,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,47,0)="the text for the ECME activity log was too large to fit in the field"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,48,0)="without being truncated.  The log entry text ""Reversal/Re-submit sent"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,49,0)="has been abbreviated to ""Rev/Resubmit"" to ensure the entire NDC is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",262,1,50,0)="viewable in the log entry."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",263,0)="319 SEQ #271^3090423.112839^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",263,1,0)="^^2^2^3090423"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",263,1,1,0)="This patch will fix the issue where the incorrect patient is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",263,1,2,0)="printed on the label. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",264,0)="300 SEQ #272^3090423.11324^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",264,1,0)="^^3^3^3090423"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",264,1,1,0)="The Pharmacy Prescription Practices V.1.0 package is being retired per"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",264,1,2,0)="PSI-07-114. Therefore, calls to the PPP package within Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",264,1,3,0)="Pharmacy V.7.0 need to be removed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",265,0)="323 SEQ #273^3090423.124556^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",265,1,0)="^^5^5^3090423"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",265,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",265,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",265,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",265,1,4,0)="This patch addresses a subscript error in routine: PSOHLSN"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",265,1,5,0)="HD0000000291680 - <SUBSCRIPT>SEGPARX+4^PSOHLSN"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",266,0)="301 SEQ #274^3090423.140958^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",266,1,0)="^^5^5^3090423"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",266,1,1,0)="ASSOCIATED REMEDY:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",266,1,2,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",266,1,3,0)="HD220858 - PSI-07-227 - Error Filling Prescriptions in Outpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",266,1,4,0)="d HD231034 - Wrong script information"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",266,1,5,0)="d HD237297 - HL7 prescription issue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,0)="305 SEQ #275^3090603.113656^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,0)="^^81^81^3090603"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,1,0)="The FY08 Q4 Enhancement Release includes the following enhancements."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,3,0)="1. Automate Computerized Patient Record System V. 1.0 (CPRS) Refill"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,4,0)="   Processing."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,5,0)="2. Display of both the Fill Date and the Release Date."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,6,0)="3. Duplicate Drugs Message Enhancements."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,7,0)="4. Notice of Privacy Practice Reminder on Laser Labels."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,9,0)="***** NOTE TO SITES USING AUTOMATED FILLING EQUIPMENT *****"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,10,0)="This patch adds a new NTE8 segment that has the VA Notice of Privacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,11,0)="Practices, IB 10-163 narrative to the content of the laser labels print"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,12,0)="stream.  If you are using automated dispensing equipment that relies on"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,13,0)="the data stream sent to the laser labels port, you have to contact your"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,14,0)="vendor to make adjustments to the trailer page as defined in item #4"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,15,0)="below."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,17,0)="1. Automate CPRS Refill Processing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,18,0)="=================================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,19,0)="This patch provides functionality to automatically process refills placed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,20,0)="by the provider via CPRS.  A new system parameter, AUTOMATE CPRS REFILLS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,21,0)="field (#40.16), has been added to the PHARMACY SYSTEM file (#59.7) by the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,22,0)="Pharmacy Data Management V. 1.0, patch PSS*1*137 to support this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,23,0)="functionality."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,25,0)="Please refer to patch PSS*1*137 for more details."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,27,0)="The auto refill process will occur only if the new AUTOMATE CPRS REFILLS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,28,0)="field (#40.16) of the PHARMACY SYSTEM file (#59.7) is set to YES and the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,29,0)="security key, PSOAUTRF, has been assigned to at least one user; otherwise"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,30,0)="the current process will continue where the orders have to be finished"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,31,0)="manually. Orders processed automatically will have the refill date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,32,0)="calculated by the refill process to the next possible fill date and the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,33,0)="routing will be set to Mail."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,35,0)="During the auto refill process, if the criteria for refilling fails, then"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,36,0)="the order will not be processed but will be stored in the PENDING"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,37,0)="OUTPATIENT ORDERS file (#52.41) for manual processing. Also, a MailMan"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,38,0)="message, with the reason for not filling the auto refill, will be sent to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,39,0)="holders of the PSOAUTRF security key. This should be very rare since CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,40,0)="will allow refills only if they are refillable."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,42,0)="2. Display of both the Fill Date and the Release Date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,43,0)="====================================================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,44,0)="On the Patient Medication Profile screen, new functionality was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,45,0)="implemented to allow users to have the option of viewing either the FILL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,46,0)="DATE or the RELEASE DATE information. This is done by using a hidden"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,47,0)="ListMan action called RDD to invoke the RELEASE DATE display and will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,48,0)="remain for that session. Using the RDD action again will display the FILL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,49,0)="DATE."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,51,0)="3. Duplicate Drugs Message Enhancements"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,52,0)="======================================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,53,0)="This enhancement is related to patient safety issue PSI-07-236 and remedy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,54,0)="ticket RT223633. When a duplicate drug message is displayed, the heading"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,55,0)="""CMOP Status"" is currently shown for CMOP drugs only. This heading is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,56,0)="being renamed to ""Processing Status"" and it will appear on every duplicate"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,57,0)="drug message along with the release status."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,59,0)="4. Notice of Privacy Practice Reminder on Laser Labels"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,60,0)="======================================================"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,61,0)="When the labels are printed for a patient's prescriptions, the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,62,0)="following narrative will be printed on the trailer page in either English"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,63,0)="or Spanish, depending on the patient's language preference."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,65,0)="The English version reads as follows."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,67,0)="  The VA Notice of Privacy Practices, IB 10-163, which outlines your"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,68,0)="  privacy rights, is available online at http://www1.domain.ext/Health/ or you"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,69,0)="  may obtain a copy by writing the VHA Privacy Office (19F2), 810 Vermont"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,70,0)="  Avenue NW, Washington DC 20420."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,72,0)="The Spanish language translation for the Privacy Notification reads as"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,73,0)="follows."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,75,0)="  La Notificacion relacionada con las Politicas de Privacidad del"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,76,0)="  Departamento de Asuntos del Veterano, IB-10-163, contiene los"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,77,0)="  detalles acerca de sus derechos de privacidad y esta disponible"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,78,0)="  electronicamente en la siguiente direccion:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,79,0)="  http://www1.domain.ext/Health/. Usted tambien puede conseguir una copia"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,80,0)="  escribiendo a la Oficina de Privacidad del Departamento de Asuntos de"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",267,1,81,0)="  Salud del Veterano, (19F2), 810 Vermont Avenue NW, Washington, DC 20420."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,0)="289^3090714.091233^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,0)="^^213^213^3090714"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,1,0)="DThis patch has enhancements which extend the capabilities of the Veterans"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,2,0)="Health Information Systems and Technology Architecture (VistA) electronic "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,3,0)="pharmacy (ePharmacy) billing system.  Below is a list of all the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,4,0)="applications involved in this project along with their patch number:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,6,0)="   APPLICATION/VERSION                                  PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,7,0)="   --------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,8,0)="   CONSOLIDATED MAIL OUTPATIENT PHARMACY (CMOP) V. 2.0  PSX*2*65"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,9,0)="   PHARMACY DATA MANAGEMENT (PDM) V. 1.0                PSS*1*131"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,10,0)="   OUTPATIENT PHARMACY (OP) V. 7.0                      PSO*7*289"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,11,0)="   INTEGRATED BILLING (IB) V. 2.0                       IB*2*384"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,12,0)="   ELECTRONIC CLAIMS MANAGEMENT ENGINE (ECME) V. 1.0    BPS*1*7"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,14,0)="The last three patches (PSO*7*289, IB*2*384 and BPS*1*7) will be released "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,15,0)="in the Kernel Installation and Distribution System (KIDS) multi-build "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,16,0)="distribution BPS PSO IB BUNDLE 3.0.  Patches PSX*2*65 and PSS*1*131 will "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,17,0)="be released as stand-alone patches.  Since there is an implementation "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,18,0)="dependency between the multi-build distribution and the stand-alone "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,19,0)="patches, PSX*2*65 and PSS*1*131 must be installed prior to the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,20,0)="installation of the multi-build.  For more specific instructions please "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,21,0)="refer to the installation steps provided in each of the patches."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,23,0)="This patch modifies the Outpatient Pharmacy v7.0 application as described"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,24,0)="below:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,26,0)="1.  A modification was made to prevent users from entering a suspense date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,27,0)="that is greater than the fill date plus 90 days.  Dates where the fill"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,28,0)="date plus 90 days is greater than the expiration date will not be allowed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,30,0)="2.  Functionality to allow non-DUR/RTS reject to be placed on Third Party "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,31,0)="Payer Rejects - Worklist [PSO REJECTS WORKLIST] option was added.  To "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,32,0)="accomplish this the following additions were made:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,34,0)="    a.  A new EPHARMACY SITE PARAMETERS FILE (#52.86) was added to store"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,35,0)="        ePharmacy specific parameters by division.  Along with this file, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,36,0)="        a new EPHARMACY SITE PARAMETERS [PSO ePHARM SITE PARAMATERS]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,37,0)="        option was added for entry/edit of parameters.  Regardless of any"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,38,0)="        parameters defined in this new file, Refill-Too-Soon (RTS), Drug"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,39,0)="        Utilization Review(DUR) and Tricare rejects will always be placed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,40,0)="        on the Pharmacy Reject Worklist."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,42,0)="        Sites will have the ability to select to allow all third party "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,43,0)="        rejects to pass to the the Third Party Payer Rejects - Worklist"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,44,0)="        which is also referred to as the Pharmacy Reject Worklist or they"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,45,0)="        can choose to specify individual reject codes. Individual third"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,46,0)="        party reject codes can be defined to be automatically placed on"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,47,0)="        the worklist or defined to require OPECC intervention. If the site"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,48,0)="        chooses to allow all rejects to be placed on the worklist,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,49,0)="        individual codes are overridden but not deleted from the file."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,51,0)="     b. For display of non-DUR/RTS rejects for the Third Party Payer"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,52,0)="        Rejects - Worklist [PSO REJECTS WORKLIST] option, rejects passed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,53,0)="        via OPECC manual intervention will be denoted in the comment"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,54,0)="        section of the Reject Information screen as:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,56,0)="        - JUN 09, 2008@14:04:18 - Transferred by OPECC. (user,name)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,58,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,59,0)="        Rejects passed automatically will be denoted in the comments "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,60,0)="        section of  the Reject Information Screen as "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,62,0)="       - JUN 09, 2008@16:00:09 - Automatically transferred due to override"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,63,0)="         for reject code. (user,name)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,65,0)="        All rejects other than Refill-Too-Soon, DUR, and Tricare will be "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,66,0)="        displayed at the end of the listing under ""OTHER REJECTS"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,67,0)="        header. The ""OTHER REJECTS"" header will be displayed regardless of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,68,0)="        whether the GI - Group Insurance action is toggled on or off.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,69,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,70,0)="        Non-DUR/RTS rejections will be resolved with the existing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,71,0)="        functionality and will be resubmitted to ECME in the same manner"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,72,0)="        as DUR/RTS rejections."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,74,0)="3.  A modification was made to not allow a claim to be reversed through "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,75,0)="ECME for an unreleased CMOP fill when the prescription/fill is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,76,0)="discontinued. If the fill is either a CMOP released or Non-CMOP released "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,77,0)="fill the reversal will be performed.  Because the software already "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,78,0)="performs a reversal for unsuccessful/not dispensed claims, no changes are "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,79,0)="needed for reversing discontinued non-dispensed fills.  Also, no changes "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,80,0)="are needed when the NDC from CMOP differs from the NDC on the claim "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,81,0)="because this function is already performed by existing software."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,83,0)="4. New functionality was added to prevent prescriptions from being "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,84,0)="filled/sent to CMOP when a host processing error occurs when a claim is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,85,0)="submitted through ECME. The host processing errors are identified by "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,86,0)="reject codes M6, M8, NN, and 99. The following conditions apply when this "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,87,0)="scenario occurs."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,89,0)="    a. The transmission of the Rx/fill will be delayed 1 day in hopes"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,90,0)="       that the host processing issues will be resolved."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,91,0)="    b. An activity log entry will be defined to state the date/time "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,92,0)="       along with a comment stating that the Rx/fill was left in suspense"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,93,0)="       hold due to a host processing error."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,94,0)="    c. This added functionality does not include the Pull Early from "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,95,0)="       Suspense function."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,97,0)="5. New functionality was added to the Print from Suspense File [PSO "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,98,0)="PNDLBL] option to prevent ePharmacy prescriptions from being pulled early"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,99,0)="from suspense until 3/4 of the days supply of the Rx/fill has elapsed.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,100,0)="The system will not hold a prescription for 3/4 days supply when:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,101,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,102,0)="    -   the previous fill was not ECME billable"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,103,0)="    -   the Rx is flagged for SC or EI"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,104,0)="    -   the DEA special Handling code is non billable (i.e. has M or 0 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,105,0)="             (zero) or  (I, S, N, and/or 9)) without and E."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,106,0)="    -   the Rx is a zero fill on a renewal"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,107,0)="    -   the patient does not currently have insurance"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,108,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,109,0)="6. A modification was made to PRESCRIPTION file (#52), REJECT INFO "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,110,0)="sub-file (#52.25), CLARIFICATION CODE field (#24). This was a set of codes"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,111,0)="field.  It is now a pointer to file #9002313.25 (BPS NCPDP CLARIFICATION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,112,0)="CODE).  A post install routine will go through the reject info subfile and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,113,0)="convert the old set of code values to the appropriate new pointer values."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,114,0)="The post install will send a mail message to the person installing the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,115,0)="build which details the affected rejected prescriptions.  The 'Submit"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,116,0)="Clarif. Code' protocol [PSO REJECT DISPLAY CLARIFICATION CODE] has been"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,117,0)="altered to use the new pointer value."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,119,0)="7. The 'Edit NDC and DAW Code of Discontinued/Expired Prescriptions' "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,120,0)="functionality introduced in PSO*7.0*281 has been extended to also allow "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,121,0)="edits of prescriptions with a status of DISCONTINUED BY PROVIDER and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,122,0)="DISCONTINUED (EDIT)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,123,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,124,0)="8. New functionality was added to create a nightly background mail "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,125,0)="message regarding open/unresolved rejects on the reject worklist.  The "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,126,0)="'Third Party Payer Rejects - Nightly Message' option [PSO REJECTS "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,127,0)="BACKGROUND MESSAGE] will be queued to run every 24 hours by the post "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,128,0)="install routine.  This option is intended to be a stand alone option and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,129,0)="should not be placed on any menu.  The message will be delivered to the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,130,0)="'PSO REJECTS BACKGROUND MESSAGE' mailgroup; this mailgroup should be "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,131,0)="populated with appropriate ePharmacy users to receive the information.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,132,0)="Mail messages are generated for each division. Sites may alter EPHARMACY"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,133,0)="SITE PARAMETERS file (#52.86) REJECT WORKLIST DAYS field (#4) for each "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,134,0)="division using the ePharmacy Site Parameters option [PSO EPHARM SITE "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,135,0)="PARAMETERS] of the ePharmacy Menu.  If no sites are defined in the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,136,0)="EPHARMACY SITE PARAMETERS file (#52.86), no message will be generated.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,137,0)="This parameter may be defined to be 1 to 30 days that an uncommented"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,138,0)="reject can remain on the reject worklist without being included in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,139,0)="nightly reject worklist alert mail message.  The following are the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,140,0)="criteria for a reject to be included in the mail message:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,141,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,142,0)="    a. The prescription is active, suspensed, expired, or on hold."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,143,0)="    b. The prescription is unreleased."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,144,0)="    c. The claim has been on the Reject Worklist for more days than the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,145,0)="       value in the REJECT WORKLIST DAYS field for the division."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,146,0)="    d. The claim has no comments added within the date range."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,147,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,148,0)="9. New functionality was added to allow NDC validation of third party"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,149,0)="payable prescriptions by pharmacy technicians.  Current functionality"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,150,0)="requires a pharmacist to perform this task.  In addition, for the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,151,0)="PRESCRIPTION file(#52) and the REFILL sub-file (#52.1), the DATE NDC"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,152,0)="VALIDATED field (#83) and NDC VALIDATED BY field (#84) will be captured"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,153,0)="when the NDC is validated for a prescription or refill; this validation"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,154,0)="information will be displayed when prescriptions are released; if the NDCs"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,155,0)="have not been validated, that information will be displayed instead.  The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,156,0)="'NDC Validation' option [PSO NDC VALIDATE] has been added to the ePharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,157,0)="Menu for use by technicians.  The option will work as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,159,0)="    a. The technician will be prompted to scan or enter a prescription "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,160,0)="       number.  An '^' may be entered to halt the option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,161,0)="    b. The system will evaluate the Rx.  If the Rx NDC has already been "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,162,0)="       validated, the technician will be prompted if they wish to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,163,0)="       revalidate. If the answer is yes, the technician will be allowed to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,164,0)="       proceed.  If the answer is no, the technician will be returned to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,165,0)="       the select a prescription prompt."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,166,0)="    c. If the Rx is CMOP, external interface or released, the user will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,167,0)="       not be allowed to verify the Rx."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,168,0)="    d. The system will display information about the Rx, notate that the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,169,0)="       Rx has not been previously verified and will prompt for PRODUCT "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,170,0)="       NDC. A valid PRODUCT NDC must be entered for this prompt.  Valid"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,171,0)="       PRODUCT NDC's are those defined for the drug in Drug file (#50) as"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,172,0)="       an NDC of a synonym or the default NDC."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,173,0)="    e. The system will compare the Rx NDC to the PRODUCT NDC submitted on"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,174,0)="       the ePharmacy claim.  If the NDCs do not match, the system will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,175,0)="       reverse and resubmit a third party claim with the new NDC and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,176,0)="       store the new NDC on the fill."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,177,0)="    f. If the prescription is defined as TRICARE and is not payable, the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,178,0)="       system will display an appropriate message and the technician will "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,179,0)="       be returned to the select a prescription prompt."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,180,0)="    g. If the prescription is defined as TRICARE and the reversed claim "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,181,0)="       returns not payable, the system will display an appropriate "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,182,0)="       message and the technician will be returned to the select a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,183,0)="       prescription prompt."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,184,0)="    h. Otherwise, the system will update the NDC validation fields for the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,185,0)="       Rx/Fill, and the technician will be returned to the select a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,186,0)="       prescription prompt."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,187,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,188,0)="10.  The RES - Resubmit Claim action was added to the Reject Information"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,189,0)="(TRICARE) screen of the Third Party Payer Rejects - Worklist [PSO REJECTS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,190,0)="WORKLIST] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,191,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,192,0)="11.  The following functionality will work only if the REGISTRATION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,193,0)="package V.5.3 patch DG*5.3*688 that introduces the COUNTRY field to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,194,0)="PATIENT file (#2) is installed:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,195,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,196,0)="   When using the Print from Suspense File [PSO PNDLBL] option, if the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,197,0)="   routing is MAIL and the address is Foreign, it will be treated just"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,198,0)="   like the BAD ADDRESS INDICATOR or DO NOT MAIL order where:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,200,0)="   a. The prescription will not be sent to the automated filling equipment"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,201,0)="      and/or to the label printer. The fill will remain on suspense until"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,202,0)="      it is pulled early, the routing is changed to window, or the address"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,203,0)="      is changed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,204,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,205,0)="   b. For the first time attempt to print from suspense, an entry will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,206,0)="      added to the activity log and a MailMan message will be generated to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,207,0)="      the user who queued the job to print from suspense and the members"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,208,0)="      of the PSO EXTERNAL DISPENSE ALERTS mail group."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,209,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,210,0)="12.  When the NDC changes during auto-release of the prescription for CMOP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,211,0)="or OPAI fills, the fill date on the fill be updated to become the same as"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,212,0)="the release date.  An entry will be made in the activity log for the fill "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",268,1,213,0)="to denote the changed date."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",269,0)="311 SEQ #277^3090714.091336^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",269,1,0)="^^1^1^3090714"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",269,1,1,0)="REMOVE TEMPORARY MENU OPTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,0)="170^3090714.152131^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,0)="^^16^16^3090714"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,1,0)="The following issues are addressed in this patch:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,2,0)="1. This patch addresses a request which support the Pharmacy Benefits"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,3,0)="Management (PBM) Extracts Enhancement #3 project. In order to allow the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,4,0)="retransmission of only those patients who have had demographic updates,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,5,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0, Inpatient Medications V. 5.0, Registration"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,6,0)="V. 5.3 and Pharmacy Data Management V. 1.0 were modified to build an entry"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,7,0)="for re-transmission in PBM PATIENT DEMOGRAPHICS File #59.9."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,9,0)="When the FIRST SERVICE DATE field (#.07) in the PHARMACY PATIENT file #55"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,10,0)="is updated for a patient, an entry is queued for retransmission."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,13,0)="2. During internal testing, it was discovered that the FIRST SERVICE DATE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,14,0)="field (#.07) and the ACTUAL/HISTORICAL FLAG field (#.08) were not being"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,15,0)="set appropriately when the user exited out of label print. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",270,1,16,0)="corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",271,0)="266 SEQ #279^3090729.110547^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",271,1,0)="^^6^6^3090729"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",271,1,1,0)="PSO*7*266 will correct the following remedy tickets"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",271,1,2,0)="HD153822   90 day supply with 11 refills allowed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",271,1,3,0)="    Dupe: HD186337     Drug Change And No Refills."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",271,1,4,0)="HD129050   Allowable Refills"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",271,1,5,0)="HD198754   BINGO BOARD DISPLAYING INCORRECT RX #"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",271,1,6,0)="HD120910   Incorrect Suspend Date "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",272,0)="306 SEQ #280^3090805.171904^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",272,1,0)="^^10^10^3090805"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",272,1,1,0)="This patch will fix the issue where the Lot # is carried over"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",272,1,2,0)="to the new prescription during a renewal."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",272,1,3,0)="It will also fix an issue with the Refill Date when a prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",272,1,4,0)="is suspended."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",272,1,5,0)="If a user creates a prescription with a Fill Date of Today and then a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",272,1,6,0)="refill is requested for Today, the prescription is put into suspense for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",272,1,7,0)="a future date."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",272,1,8,0)="If the refill is deleted and then re-added without exiting the OP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",272,1,9,0)="Medication screen, the suspense date for the newly requested refill"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",272,1,10,0)="is set to Today instead of the same date as the original refill."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,0)="320 SEQ #281^3090806.142805^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,0)="^^130^130^3090806"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,1,0)="The FY09 Q2 Enhancement Release includes the following."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,3,0)="This patch provides the ability to view a patient's remote prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,4,0)="data within Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0 using the Remote Data"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,5,0)="Interoperability (RDI) interface to retrieve data from the Health Data"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,6,0)="Repository (HDR)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,8,0)="The following changes were made."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,9,0)="1. In the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,10,0)="   if a patient has remote prescription(s), then the user will be prompted"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,11,0)="   with the following question."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,13,0)="          REMOTE PRESCRIPTIONS AVAILABLE!"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,14,0)="          Display Remote Data? N//"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,16,0)="   If the response is ""No"", then there are no changes to the existing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,17,0)="   functionality. If the response is ""Yes"" then it provides a new screen"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,18,0)="   to view the remote data as shown in the following example."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,20,0)="Remote Facilities Visited     Dec 30, 2008@17:26:47          Page: 1 of 1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,22,0)="Patient: PSOPATIENT,ONE            (000-00-0000)      DOB: 01/02/1967"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",273,1,24,0)="  Station"
