^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,340,0)=" Overrides                             pso_7_p612_ys_501_p166_rn.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,341,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,342,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,343,0)=" Patch Installation: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,344,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,345,0)=" Pre/Post Installation Overview: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,346,0)=" -------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,347,0)=" There are no tasks to be performed before the installation of this "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,348,0)=" multi-build. Note that the routines should be backed up to a PackMan"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,349,0)=" message before installing the build."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,350,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,351,0)=" Pre-Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,352,0)=" ------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,353,0)=" This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,354,0)=" recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,355,0)=" potential disruption to users.  This patch should take less than 5 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,356,0)=" minutes to install.  It should not be installed when the YSCL DAILY"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,357,0)=" TRANSMISION option is running.  If unsure when that is check the OPTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,358,0)=" SCHEDULING file (#19.2) using FileMan:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,359,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,360,0)=" Select VA FileMan Option: Inquire to File Entries "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,361,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,362,0)=" Output from what File: OPTION SCHEDULING//   (17 entries) Select OPTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,363,0)=" SCHEDULING NAME:  YSCL DAILY TRANSMISSION Another one: Standard Captioned"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,364,0)=" Output? Yes//   (Yes) Include COMPUTED fields:  (N/Y/R/B): NO//  - No "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,365,0)=" record"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,366,0)=" number (IEN), no Computed  Fields "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,367,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,368,0)=" NAME: YSCL DAILY TRANSMISSION "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,369,0)="   QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME: OCT 05, 2019@01:30 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,370,0)="   RESCHEDULING FREQUENCY: 1D            TASK ID: 2577736 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,371,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,372,0)=" Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,373,0)=" --------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,374,0)="1. Place the KIDS multi-build file PSO_YS_CLOZ_COVID.KID into a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,375,0)="local directory and use the KIDS option Load a Distribution option to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,376,0)="load it into the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,377,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,378,0)="2. Choose the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,379,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,380,0)="3. From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,381,0)="the Installation Menu.  From this menu, you may elect to use the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,382,0)="following options. When prompted for the INSTALL NAME enter:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,383,0)="       PSO*7.0*612"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,384,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,385,0)="  a. Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup message"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,386,0)="     of any routines exported with this patch."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,387,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,388,0)="  b. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will (allow "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,389,0)="     you to view all changes that will be made when this patch "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,390,0)="     is installed.  It compares all components of this patch "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,391,0)="     (routines, DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,392,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,393,0)="  c. Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option allows you to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,394,0)="     ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the transport "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,395,0)="     global."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,396,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,397,0)=" 4.  From the Installation Menu, select the Install Package(s) option and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,398,0)=" choose the patch to install (PSO*7*612)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,399,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,400,0)=" 5. Accept the default when prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,401,0)=" Upon Completion of Install? NO//'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,402,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,403,0)=" 6. Accept the default when prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,404,0)=" the install? NO//'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,405,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,406,0)=" 7. Accept the default when prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,407,0)=" Menu Options, and Protocols? NO//'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,408,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,409,0)=" 8. If prompted 'Delay Install (Minutes):  (0 - 60): 0// enter 0 (zero).  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,410,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,411,0)=" Backout /Rollback Strategy: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,412,0)=" ---------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,413,0)=" Backout will be done only with the concurrence and participation of "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,414,0)=" development team and appropriate VA site/region personnel. The decision "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,415,0)=" to backout the software will be a joint decision between development"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,416,0)=" team, VA site and regional personnel, and other appropriate VA personnel."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,417,0)=" Rollback applies to data only and is not applicable to this multi-build."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,418,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,419,0)=" Prior to installing the KIDS multi-build, the site/region should have "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,420,0)=" saved a backup of the routines in a PackMan message using the Backup a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,421,0)=" Transport Global [XPD BACKUP] menu option (this is done at time of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,422,0)=" install). The message containing the backed-up routines can be loaded "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,423,0)=" with the ""Xtract PackMan"" function at the Message Action prompt. The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,424,0)=" PackMan function ""INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE"" is then used to install the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,425,0)=" backed up routines onto the VistA System."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,426,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,427,0)=" The new ""AC"" mumps cross reference for the CLOZAPINE PATIENT LIST file "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,428,0)=" (#603.01) must be manually deleted via FileMan prior to restoring the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,429,0)=" backed up routines. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,430,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,431,0)=" The steps to delete the cross reference:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,432,0)="   1. Access VA FileMan option Cross-Reference A Field via the VA FileMan "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,433,0)="   Utility Functions [DIUTILITY] menu."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,434,0)="   2. At the prompt, ""What type of cross-reference (Traditional or New)?"" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,435,0)="   enter NEW."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,436,0)="   3. At the prompt, ""Modify What File:"" enter 603.01."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,437,0)="   4. The new ""AC"" cross reference should be selected by default."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,438,0)="   5. At the prompt ""Choose E (Edit)/D (Delete)/C (Create):"" enter DELETE."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,439,0)="   6. At the prompt ""Are you sure you want to delete the index  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,440,0)="   definition? NO// YES"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,441,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,442,0)=" Example deletion of new ""AC"" index if backout is required:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,443,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,444,0)="   VA FileMan 22.2   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,445,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,446,0)="   Select OPTION: UTILITY FUNCTIONS  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,447,0)="   Select UTILITY OPTION: CROSS-REFERENCE A FIELD OR FILE  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,448,0)="   What type of cross-reference (Traditional or New)? Traditional// NEW"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,449,0)="   Modify what File: REMOTE PROCEDURE// 603.01  CLOZAPINE PATIENT LIST"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,450,0)="                                           (74 entries)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,451,0)="   Current Indexes on file #603.01:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,452,0)="     1589   'AC' index"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,453,0)="   Choose E (Edit)/D (Delete)/C (Create): DELETE   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,454,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,455,0)="   Which Index do you wish to delete? 1589//  AC"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,456,0)="   Are you sure you want to delete the index definition? NO// YES   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,457,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,458,0)="     Index definition deleted."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,459,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,460,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,461,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,462,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,463,0)=" Validation of Backout Procedure "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,464,0)=" -------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,465,0)=" The backout Procedure can be verified by printing the first 2 lines of "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,466,0)=" the PSO* and YS* routines contained in the HI&M CLOZAPINE NCCC OVRD "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,467,0)=" COVID-19 multi- build using the option First Line Routine Print [XU FIRST"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,468,0)=" LINE PRINT]. Once the old routines listed in the multi-build patch have"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,469,0)=" been restored, the first two lines of the Routines will no longer contain"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,470,0)=" the designation of patch 612 in the patch list section on line 2 of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,471,0)=" routines."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,472,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,473,0)=" The backout of the new ""AC"" cross reference on the CLOZAPINE PATIENT "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,474,0)=" LIST file (#603.01) can be verified by repeating the backout steps and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,475,0)=" verifying that there is no longer a selectable ""AC"" cross reference to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",480,1,476,0)=" delete."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,0)="606 SEQ #506^3201103.140702^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,0)="^^79^79^3201103"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,1,0)="This patch will address the following ePrescribing (eRx) issues: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,3,0)="INC8108373 - Inbound eRx - Outpatient pharmacy bingo board causing stack error"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,4,0)="INC10596781 - e-prescription missing SIG or patient instruction"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,6,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,7,0)="==========================================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,8,0)="1. INC8108373 - Inbound eRx - Outpatient pharmacy bingo board causing stack"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,9,0)="                error"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,10,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,11,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,12,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,13,0)="VA Black Hills Health Care System reported a stack error causing VistA to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,14,0)="terminate the user's session when they used the Class III VistA option"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,15,0)="Inpatient Pending Orders Display [PSOZ INPATIENT PENDING ORDERS]. Although"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,16,0)="the HPS (Health Portfolio Software) Sustainment Team does not support Class"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,17,0)="III software, it was determined that the root cause of the problem was the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,18,0)="fact that the LOGIN DATE field (#15) in the PENDING OUTPATIENT ORDERS file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,19,0)="(#52.41) was being populated with only the date (YYYMMDD) and not the time"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,20,0)="(YYYMMDD.HHMMSS) by the new eRx functionality. Although the field allows"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,21,0)="for date only content, every other function that creates a new entry in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,22,0)="the PENDING OUTPATIENT ORDERS file (#52.41) also sets the timestamp along"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,23,0)="with the date."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,24,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,25,0)="Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,26,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,27,0)="This patch will modify the setting of the LOGIN DATE field (#15) in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,28,0)="PENDING OUTPATIENT ORDERS file (#52.41) for eRx pending orders to include"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,29,0)="the date and timestamp (YYYMMDD.HHMMSS) of when the order was created."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,30,0)="This will prevent the error users are getting when running the Class III"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,31,0)="option mentioned above."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,33,0)="Note: This fix will apply to future orders only, filed after the patch is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,34,0)="      installed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,35,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,36,0)="Technical Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,37,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,38,0)="The setting of the array PSOHY(""EDT"") at SETUP+72^PSOERX1B and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,39,0)="PSOHY+34^PSOERXU3 was changed from PSOHY(""EDT"")=DT (DT holds the current"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,40,0)="date in the YYYMMDD format) to PSOHY(""EDT)=$$NOW^XLFDT() (the $$NOW^XLFDT()"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,41,0)="function returns the current date and time in the YYYMMDD.HHMMSS format)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,42,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,43,0)="2. INC10596781 - e-prescription missing SIG or patient instruction"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,44,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,45,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,46,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,47,0)="The VA Health Administration Center Denver reported that when viewing a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,48,0)="RefillResponse type record in the Complete Orders from eRx [PSO ERX FINISH]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,49,0)="option the field 'Vista Sig' under the MEDICATION DISPENSED section was being"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,50,0)="suppressed as indicated in the screen capture example below:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,52,0)="   ****************************MEDICATION DISPENSED*************************    "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,53,0)="   Vista Drug: CHLORAMBUCIL 2MG TAB                                                "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,54,0)="   Vista Qty: 30              Vista Refills: 3        Vista Days Supply: 30     "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,55,0)="   >>> 'Vista Sig' field should be displayed here."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,56,0)="   VA Rx#: Unable to resolve.                                                      "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,59,0)="Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,60,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,61,0)="It was confirmed that the software was hiding the 'Vista Sig' field because"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,62,0)="of an error in the code. The defect is being addressed by this patch and it"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,63,0)="display the 'Vista Sig' correctly, as shown in the example below:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,65,0)="   ****************************MEDICATION DISPENSED*************************    "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,66,0)="   Vista Drug: CHLORAMBUCIL 2MG TAB                                                "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,67,0)="   Vista Qty: 30              Vista Refills: 3        Vista Days Supply: 30     "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,68,0)="   Vista Sig: TAKE ONE-HALF TABLE BY MOUTH TWICE A DAY FOR 30 DAYS ON A FULL       "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,69,0)="   STOMACH                                                                         "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,70,0)="   VA Rx#: Unable to resolve.                                                      "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,73,0)="Technical Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,74,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,75,0)="The array variable DIRARY was misspelled at line MEDDIS+37^PSOERXU3 and at"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,76,0)="line MEDDIS+39^PSOERXU3 it was using the variable DIRECT instead of the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,77,0)="DIRARY array. Both issues were resolved."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",481,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",482,0)="624 SEQ #507^3201106.161525^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",482,1,0)="^^4^4^3201106"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",482,1,1,0)="When a user changes the DAYS SUPPLY for only a Clozapine flagged drug with"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",482,1,2,0)="at least one registered lab test, the user will also be prompted to select"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",482,1,3,0)="the appropriate # OF REILLS. See the patch desciption on FORUM for more"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",482,1,4,0)="details."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,0)="604 SEQ #508^3201123.100944^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,1,0)="^^12^12^3201123"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,1,1,0)="1. EPharmacy prescriptions that are pulled from suspense using the action"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,1,2,0)="PP in the PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS option remain suspended after a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,1,3,0)="subsequent refill action of another prescription. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,1,5,0)="2.  During processing of Outpatient Pharmacy order, user was kicked out"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,1,6,0)="of VistA session with an undefined error DSPL+3^PSOORNE3 *PSLSTL."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,1,7,0)="After doing a speed refill for a prescription that results in it "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,1,8,0)="being suspended, the error occurs when entering a new order for a supply"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,1,9,0)="item and answering No to the final prompt 'Is this correct?'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,1,10,0)="Variable RX0 is set during the speed refill and is not killed if the Rx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,1,11,0)="is suspended when the speed refill process is done nor is it killed "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",483,1,12,0)="when starting a New Order."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,0)="621 SEQ #509^3201204.172442^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,0)="^^92^92^3201204"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,1,0)="This patch will address the following issues: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,3,0)="1. INC11549905 - when you enter a new prescription the QTY rounds up unless"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,4,0)="                 you change the days supply."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,5,0)="2. INC11595547 - CLOZAPINE ORDER - Day Supply- Quantity - # of Refill -"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,6,0)="                 Expiration date calculation "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,7,0)="3. INC11627662 - PSOL EDIT - Edit Data for a Patient in the Clozapine Program"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,9,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,10,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,11,0)="1. INC11549905 - when you enter a new prescription the QTY rounds up unless"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,12,0)="                 you change the days supply."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,13,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,14,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,15,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,16,0)="The Oscar G. Johnson VA Medical Center reported that when editing the Days "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,17,0)="Supply fields for a Clozapine prescription that the QTY field value is not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,18,0)="rounding up, instead it remains a factional value, forcing the user to fix"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,19,0)="it mannually."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,21,0)="Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,22,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,23,0)="The issue was confimed and the calculation of the QTY value was fixed to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,24,0)="round any fractional value up. So, if the automatic calculation results in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,25,0)="a value such 4.2, for example, it will be rounded up to 5. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,26,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,27,0)="Technical Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,28,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,29,0)="Changed the routine PSOCLUTL at line tag QTYCHK+9 to always round the value of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,30,0)="the variable QTY up."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,32,0)="  S:QTY PSORXARY(""QTY"")=(QTY+.99)\1,$P(PSORXARY(""RX0""),U,7)=(QTY+.99)\1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,33,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,34,0)="2. INC11595547 - CLOZAPINE ORDER - Day Supply- Quantity - # of Refill -"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,35,0)="                 Expiration date calculation "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,36,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,37,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,38,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,39,0)="After the installation of patch PSO*7*574 the expiration date calculation for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,40,0)="clozapine prescriptions is wrong for some scenarios after editing the # of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,41,0)="Refills or Days Supply fields. For example, when you edited a prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,42,0)="with 28-day supply and 0 refills, with an expiration date of 28 past the issue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,43,0)="date, to 14-day supply and 1 refill it was setting the expiration to 14 days"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,44,0)="past the issue date, instead of keeping the 28 days."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,45,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,46,0)="Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,47,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,48,0)="The calculation of the expiration date for clozapine prescriptions was resolved"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,49,0)="to correctly calculate the total number of days supply of the entire "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,50,0)="prescription, including the refills."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,51,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,52,0)="Technical Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,53,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,54,0)="Removed a line of code in the PSOEXDT routine (shown below) introduced by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,55,0)="PSO*7*574 that was preventing the expiration date from being calculated"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,56,0)="correctly for clozapine prescriptions."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,58,0)="          ; Added Clozapine check to not modify Expires date ; PSO*574"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,59,0)="      A   Q:+$G(PSORXED(""CLOZ EDIT"")) "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,61,0)="3. INC11627662 - PSOL EDIT - Edit Data for a Patient in the Clozapine Program"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,62,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,63,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,64,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,65,0)="After the installation of patch PSO*7*574 the option Edit Data for A Patient in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,66,0)="the Clozapine Program [PSOL EDIT] started resetting the REGISTRATION DATE field"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,67,0)="(#58) in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) even after the user simply returns"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,68,0)="through the 3 fields in the option without modifying any of them. The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,69,0)="REGISTRATION DATE field should only be reset when the user changes the value of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,70,0)="the CLOZAPINE REGISTRATION NUMBER."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,72,0)="  Edit Data for a Patient in the Clozapine Program [PSOL EDIT]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,74,0)="  Edit Data for a Patient in the Clozapine Program"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,75,0)="  Select clozapine patient :    CLOZPAT,TEST"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,76,0)="  CLOZAPINE REGISTRATION NUMBER: MR12345// MR12345"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,77,0)="  CLOZAPINE STATUS: ACTIVE TREATMENT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,78,0)="  RESPONSIBLE PROVIDER: TEST,PROVIDER// TEST,PROVIDER"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,80,0)="Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,81,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,82,0)="The Clozapine REGISTRATION DATE will only be reset when the value of the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,83,0)="CLOZAPINE REGISTRATION NUMBER is modified.The issue was confimed and the calculation of the QTY value was fixed to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,84,0)="round any fractional value up. So, if the automatic calculation results in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,85,0)="a value such 4.2, for example, it will be rounded up to 5. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,86,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,87,0)="Technical Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,88,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,89,0)="Changed the routine PSOCLUTL at line tag QTYCHK+9 to always round the value of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,90,0)="the variable QTY up."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",484,1,92,0)="  S:QTY PSORXARY(""QTY"")=(QTY+.99)\1,$P(PSORXARY(""RX0""),U,7)=(QTY+.99)\1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",485,0)="549^3201208.082724^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,0)="618 SEQ #511^3201218.151828^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,0)="^^64^64^3201218"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,3,0)="1. Reset Copay Status List Manager Start with Fill Date should be "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,4,0)="a required response."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,6,0)="2. Up carat (^) out should gracefully exit.  Report doesn't allow "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,7,0)="an up carat at several prompts"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,9,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,11,0)="Associated ticket(s):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,12,0)="====================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,14,0)="1. INC11453884 - Reset Copay Status List Manager Start with Fill Date "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,15,0)="   should be a required response "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,17,0)="2. INC11646025 - Issues with the Reset Copay Status List Manager Display "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,18,0)="   Option"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,20,0)="Associated NSR(s):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,21,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,22,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,24,0)="Participating Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,25,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,26,0)="Bay Pines VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,27,0)="Washington DC VAMC"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,30,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,31,0)="==========================================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,33,0)="1. INC11453884 - Reset Copay Status List Manager Start with Fill Date "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,34,0)="   should be a required response"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,36,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,37,0)="   -------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,38,0)="   Running option RESET COPAY STATUS LIST MANAGER [PSOCP RESET COPAY "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,39,0)="   STATUS LM] will encounter a subscript error if no date is entered at"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,40,0)="   the Start with Fill Dates: prompt"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,42,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,43,0)="   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,44,0)="   Modify PSOCPF to exit from the option when no date is entered for the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,45,0)="   Start with Fill Dates: prompt. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,47,0)="2. INC11646025 - Issues with the Reset Copay Status List Manager Display "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,48,0)="   Option"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,50,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,51,0)="   -------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,52,0)="   Up carat out should gracefully exit.  Report doesn't allow an up"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,53,0)="   carat at several prompts"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,55,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,56,0)="   ---------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,57,0)="   Modify PSOCPF to exit from the option when up carat ^ is entered on"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,58,0)="   the Start with Fill Dates, Go to Fill Dates, and the Select(A)ll or"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,59,0)="   (S)elected Prescription(s) prompts.  It was also found during testing "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,60,0)="   that the Change Patient (CP) function within the List Manager screen "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,61,0)="   had the same issues with ^ not working as it should and that is being "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,62,0)="   addressed with updates to routine PSOCPF2.  The patinet name was also "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,63,0)="   added to the List Manager screen when NO DATA FOUND FOR ENTERED "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",486,1,64,0)="   CRITERIA is displayed. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",487,0)="581 SEQ #512^3201218.152059^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",488,0)="627 SEQ #513^3201218.152559^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",488,1,0)="^^9^9^3201218"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",488,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issues in setting the ""status"" field "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",488,1,2,0)="of the ORC segment which is sent to Optifill or ScriptPro:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",488,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",488,1,4,0)="1. The ""Print from Suspense File"" option sends a status of ""NEW"" instead "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",488,1,5,0)="   of ""REFILL"" for refills."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",488,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",488,1,7,0)="2. The ""Reprint Batches from Suspense"" option sends a status of ""NEW"" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",488,1,8,0)="   instead of ""REPRINT"" when reprinting original (i.e. not refills) "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",488,1,9,0)="   prescriptions."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",489,0)="628 SEQ #514^3201218.152626^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",489,1,0)="^^4^4^3201218"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",489,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",489,1,2,0)="Disconnect between order file discontinue action and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",489,1,3,0)="prescription file (prescription was filled multiple times after "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",489,1,4,0)="discontinuation"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",490,0)="609 SEQ #515^3201218.152721^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",490,1,0)="^^11^11^3201218"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",490,1,1,0)="OPAI NOT UTILIZING MAIL PREF 4-LOCAL CERTIFIED MAIL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",490,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",490,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",490,1,4,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",490,1,5,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",490,1,6,0)="When using Menu Option PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",490,1,7,0)="and the user selects PU (Patient Update), if the user selects  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",490,1,8,0)="option #4 LOCAL CERTIFIED MAIL for at the MAIL: prompt"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",490,1,9,0)="the selection will not be reflected in the RXD segment of the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",490,1,10,0)="Prescription Dispense HL7 records for the OPAI (Out Patient "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",490,1,11,0)="Automated Interface) "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",491,0)="629 SEQ #516^3201231.151614^65"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",491,1,0)="^^3^3^3201231"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",491,1,1,0)="It was reported that the Return to Stock indicator not cleared after "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",491,1,2,0)="original fill of a CS rx if returned to stock and later filled and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",491,1,3,0)="released."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",492,0)="626 SEQ #518^3210226.101041^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",492,1,0)="^^6^6^3210226"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",492,1,1,0)="Rx entries always had a T-6M limit. Copy+Edit had a loophole that allowed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",492,1,2,0)="any date into the past which created an error when a 19th century date was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",492,1,3,0)="entered. The fix was done to match the new Rx-entry T-6M limit. However, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",492,1,4,0)="by removing the loophole of the previous code the sites that developed a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",492,1,5,0)="conversion workflow based on Copy+Edit and backdating non-CS Rx's between"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",492,1,6,0)="6 and 12 months lost that capability."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",493,0)="613 SEQ #519^3210226.101049^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",493,1,0)="^^1^1^3210226"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",493,1,1,0)="See FORUM for patch description."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",494,0)="616 SEQ #520^3210304.101743^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",494,1,0)="^^1^1^3210304"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",494,1,1,0)="File #52 Label multiple created with a missing header node"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",495,0)="625b^3210405"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",495,1,0)="^^5^5^3210405"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",495,1,1,0)="Backup of PSO*7.0*625 on Apr 05, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",495,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",495,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",495,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",495,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",496,0)="625 SEQ #521^3210405.094433^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",496,1,0)="^^2^2^3210405"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",496,1,1,0)="The description of this build can be found in the National Patch Module "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",496,1,2,0)="under PSO*7.0*625."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",497,0)="635b^3210420"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",497,1,0)="^^5^5^3210420"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",497,1,1,0)="Backup of PSO*7.0*635 on Apr 20, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",497,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",497,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",497,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",497,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",498,0)="635 SEQ #522^3210420.150352^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",498,1,0)="^^1^1^3210420"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",498,1,1,0)="Inbound eRx version 4.0 defect remediation."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",499,0)="560b^3210519"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",499,1,0)="^^5^5^3210519"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",499,1,1,0)="Backup of BPS PSO IB BUNDLE 16.0, BPS*1.0*28, PSO*7.0*560, IB*2"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",499,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",499,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",499,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",499,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",500,0)="560^3210519.161028^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",501,0)="631b^3210604"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",501,1,0)="^^5^5^3210604"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",501,1,1,0)="Backup of PSO*7.0*631 on Jun 04, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",501,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",501,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",501,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",501,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,0)="631 SEQ #525^3210604.093532^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,0)="^^199^199^3210604"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,1,0)="This patch will address the following issues: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,3,0)="1. INC13163644 - Assist with deleting eRx order on inbound eRx queue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,4,0)="   Duplicates:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,5,0)="   -----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,6,0)="   INC15788594 - RxRenewal Response was assigned wrong status flag"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,7,0)="   INC15794278 - RxRenewal Response - Processing Error (RXE) message is not "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,8,0)="   INC15788861 - RxRenewal Response - Approved failed to generate renewed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,9,0)="                 order"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,10,0)="   INC15788649 - RxRenewal Response - Replace status get assigned wrong "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,11,0)="                 status code"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,13,0)="2. INC12814745 - Rx Sig Not Upper-cased when processing inbound eRX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,15,0)="3. INC16106925 - Pharmacy messages not assigned appropriate status by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,16,0)="                 software"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,17,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,18,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,19,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,20,0)="1. INC13163644 - Assist with deleting eRx order on inbound eRx queue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,21,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,22,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,23,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,24,0)="The Fresno VA Medical Center reported that 'Denied' incoming eRx response"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,25,0)="records were sitting in their eRx Holding Queue (Complete Orders from eRx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,26,0)="[PSO ERX FINISH] option) for months because they do not have any way to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,27,0)="remove them. This issue usually happens when the sites manually renews a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,28,0)="prescription after placing an eRx refill/renewal request for the eRx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,29,0)="prescription. Once the incoming response is received the software is unable"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,30,0)="to process the renewal because the eRx is already renewed and files the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,31,0)="record with an RXN (RXRENEWAL RESPONSE - NEW) status instead of assigning it"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,32,0)="a more appropriate status such as RXF RXN (RXRENEWAL RESPONSE - FAILED), "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,33,0)="which is removed from the eRx Holding Queue once the user acknowledges it."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,34,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,35,0)="Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,36,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,37,0)="The eRx incoming response processing code was changed to automatically assign"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,38,0)="a status of RXF to an incoming renewal eRx response if the prescription has"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,39,0)="already been manually renewed. This will allow users to successfully remove"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,40,0)="such records from their by using the hidden action ACK (Acknowledge)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,42,0)="Technical Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,43,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,44,0)="The line of code below was inserted at REFRESP+24 in the PSOERXA5 routine. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,46,0)=" .D UPDSTAT^PSOERXU1(ERXIEN,""RXF"",""eRx already Renewed."")"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,48,0)="It will ensure that when an Denied incoming eRx response is received for an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,49,0)="already renewed prescription the status will be set to RXF instead of RXN. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,50,0)="Furthermore, another potential code for leaving records in the RXN was "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,51,0)="identified in the use of the API $$FIND1^DIC because it did not require an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,52,0)="exact match of the related eRx when the incoming eRx response arrived. The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,53,0)="third parameter was changed to include ""O"", which will force an exact match"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,54,0)="in order to identify the related eRx record."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,55,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,56,0)="2. INC12814745 - Rx Sig Not Upper-cased when processing inbound eRX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,57,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,58,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,59,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,60,0)="The Tucson VA Medical Center reported that when using the eRx Holding Queue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,61,0)="(Complete Orders from eRx [PSO ERX FINISH] option) the user added a patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,62,0)="instruction (code) with a lower case text to the eRx and the medication"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,63,0)="instruction expanded as expected however it did not convert to upper case in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,64,0)="the Inbound ERX Holding queue. The text was appended to the SIG and remained in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,65,0)="lower case through the finishing process in the Patient Prescription Processing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,66,0)="[PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,68,0)="Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,69,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,70,0)="It was confirmed that the eRx Holding Queue was not converting the medication"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,71,0)="instruction text to upper case when it was retrieved from the MEDICATION "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,72,0)="INSTRUCTION file (#51). This patch addresses this problem by always converting"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,73,0)="the medication instruction text to upper case."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,74,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,75,0)="Technical Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,76,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,77,0)="The line tag LSIG in the routines PSOERXU6 and PSOQUTIL was modified to always"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,78,0)="convert the medication instruction text to upper case before returning it to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,79,0)="the calling routine. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,80,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,81,0)="3. INC16106925 - Pharmacy messages not assigned appropriate status by software"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,82,0)="                 patch PSO*7*581"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,83,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,84,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,85,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,86,0)="The VA Health Administration Center Denver reported that the CRN (RXCHANGE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,87,0)="REQUEST - NEW) status of some old (older than 14 days) RxChange request"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,88,0)="records without a response were not being assigned the appropriate status CRX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,89,0)="(RXCHANGE REQUEST EXPIRED) as described in the user manual."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,90,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,91,0)="Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,92,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,93,0)="After some research it was determined that the functionality for automatically"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,94,0)="marking the records mentioned above as expired worked when the user selected"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,95,0)="RX (PRESCRIPTION RECEIVED DATE) in the prompt below when entering the eRx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,96,0)="Holding queue (Complete Orders from eRx [PSO ERX FINISH] option).  However,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,97,0)="if they select PT (PATIENT(Grouped)) the software did NOT check for records"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,98,0)="CRN elegible for expiration to mark them as expired. Furthermore, the issue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,99,0)="also seem affect RRN (RENEWAL REQUEST - NEW) records which are also supposed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,100,0)="to be marked with the RRX (RXRENEWAL REQUEST EXPIRED) status after 14 days"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,101,0)="without a response."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,102,0)="  ..."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,103,0)="         Select one of the following:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,105,0)="              PT        PATIENT(Grouped)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,106,0)="              RX        PRESCRIPTION RECEIVED DATE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,107,0)="              E         EXIT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,108,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,109,0)="    Select By: (PT/RX): PT// RX  PRESCRIPTION RECEIVED DATE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,110,0)="  ..."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,111,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,112,0)="Technical Resolution: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,113,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,114,0)="The functionality responsible for the auto expiration of CRN and RRN records"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,115,0)="in the PSOERX routine lines BLDITEM+11 thru BLDITEM+14 for the RX view were"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,116,0)="copied over to the PSOERXC1 routine which is used by the PT view. This way"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,117,0)="no matter which way the user enters the option it will always check and mark"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,118,0)="eligible CRN and RRN records as expired."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,121,0)="Test Sites: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,122,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,123,0)="TBD"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,125,0)="Documentation Retrieval Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,126,0)="-------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,127,0)="N/A (No documentation changes)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,128,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,129,0)="Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,130,0)="--------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,131,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is recommended"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,132,0)="that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize potential disruption to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,133,0)="users.  Staff should not be processing prescriptions while patch is being"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,134,0)="installed.  This patch should take less than 5 minutes to install.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,135,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,136,0)="   1. Choose the PackMan message containing this patch.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,138,0)="   2. Choose the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,139,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,140,0)="   3. From the Kernel Installation & Distribution System menu, select "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,141,0)="      the Installation menu.  From this menu, select Backup a Transport "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,142,0)="      Global. This option will create a backup message of any routines"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,143,0)="      exported with this patch. It will not backup any other changes such"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,144,0)="      as DD's or templates.  When prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,145,0)="      patch #, PSO*7.0*631."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,146,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,147,0)="   4. From the Kernel Installation & Distribution System menu, select "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,148,0)="      the Installation menu.  From this menu, you may select to use the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,149,0)="      following options: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,150,0)="      when prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter the patch #, PSO*7.0*631: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,151,0)="        a. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,152,0)="           allow you to view all changes that will be made when this patch "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,153,0)="           is installed.  It compares all components of this patch "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,154,0)="           routines, DDs, templates, etc.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,156,0)="        b. Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will allow "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,157,0)="           you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,158,0)="           transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,159,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,160,0)="   5. From the Installation menu, select the Install Package(s) option and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,161,0)="      choose the patch to install.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,162,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,163,0)="   6. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,164,0)="      NO//', respond NO.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,165,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,166,0)="   7. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,167,0)="      Protocols? NO//', respond NO.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,168,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,169,0)="   8. If prompted 'Delay Install (Minutes): (0-60): 0//' respond 0.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,172,0)="Back-out/Rollback Strategy:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,173,0)="---------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,174,0)="Back-out will be done only with the concurrence and participation of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,175,0)="development team and appropriate VA site/region personnel. The decision to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,176,0)="back-out or rollback software will be a joint decision between development"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,177,0)="team, VA site/region personnel and other appropriate VA personnel.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,178,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,179,0)="Prior to installing an updated KIDS package, the site/region should have saved"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,180,0)="a backup of the routines in a mail message using the Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,181,0)="[XPD BACKUP] menu option (this is done at time of install). The message"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,182,0)="containing the backed up routines can be loaded with the ""Xtract PackMan"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,183,0)="function at the Message Action prompt. The Packman function ""INSTALL/CHECK"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,184,0)="MESSAGE"" is then used to install the backed up routines onto the VistA System. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,185,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,186,0)="The back-out plan is to restore the routines from the backup created."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,187,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,188,0)="No data was modified by this patch installation and, therefore, no "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,189,0)="rollback strategy is required."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,190,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,191,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,192,0)="Validation of Roll Back Procedure "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,193,0)="---------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,194,0)="The Roll Back Procedure can be verified by printing the first 2 lines of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,195,0)="PSO Routines contained in this patch using the option First Line Routine Print"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,196,0)="[XU FIRST LINE PRINT]. Once the routines contained in the PSO*7.0*631 patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,197,0)="have been rolled back, the first two lines of the Routines will no longer"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,198,0)="contain the designation of patch PSO*7.0*631 in the patch list section on line"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",502,1,199,0)="2."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",503,0)="449^3210617.130228^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",503,1,0)="^^1^1^3210617"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",503,1,1,0)="See patch description for PSO*7.0*449."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",504,0)="639b^3210707"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",504,1,0)="^^5^5^3210707"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",504,1,1,0)="Backup of PSO*7.0*639 on Jul 07, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",504,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",504,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",504,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",504,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,0)="639 SEQ #527^3210707.091405^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,0)="^^43^43^3210707"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,1,0)="This patch will address the following issues: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,3,0)="1. INC17106168 - Cincinnati VISTA application is not allowing me to renew"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,4,0)="                 prescription orders."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,6,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,7,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,8,0)="N/A "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,10,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,11,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,12,0)="1. INC17106168 - Cincinnati VISTA application is not allowing me to renew"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,13,0)="                 prescription orders."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,14,0)="   INC17248638 - Speed renewal function in HAC back door VistA is kicking"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,15,0)="   (Duplicate)   all our users out of VistA."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,17,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,18,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,19,0)="The Dayton VA Medical Center reported an <UNDEFINED> error with the Speed"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,20,0)="Renew action in the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,21,0)="option. It was confirmed that this issue was introduced by patch PSO*7.0*626."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,23,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,24,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,25,0)="The patch address the <UNDEFINED> error and also allows the user to enter an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,26,0)="ISSUE DATE up to 1 year in the past for speed renewals. Before the users were"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,27,0)="limited to a date no greater than 6 months. Then, it will screen out any CS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,28,0)="prescriptions if the ISSUE DATE entered is greater than 6 months with the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,29,0)="following message:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,31,0)=" Rx# 2299064 - Rx is for a CS Drug and the Issue Date entered (Jul 17, 2020)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,32,0)=" is greater than 6 months."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,34,0)="  Type <Enter> to continue or '^' to exit: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,35,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,36,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,37,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,38,0)="Changed the code under line tags CID and CIDH to allow and ISSUE DATE value "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,39,0)="of up to 366 days in the past if the variable DA is defined and the Rx is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,40,0)="non-CS or if the variable DA is not defined. And restrict a date up to 184"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,41,0)="days in the past if the variable DA is defined and the Rx is CS. Introduced"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,42,0)="code at PROCESS+22 in the routine PSORENW4 to screen out CS prescriptions if"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",505,1,43,0)="the ISSUE DATE value is greater than 184 days."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",506,0)="636b^3210708"
