^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",518,0)="622^3211207.151119^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",518,1,0)="^^1^1^3211207"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",518,1,1,0)="See the Forum patch description."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",519,0)="653 SEQ #537^3220103.1246^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",519,1,0)="^^1^1^3220103"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",519,1,1,0)="The description for PSO*7*653 can be found in the National Patch Module."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,0)="649 SEQ #538^3220106.084529^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,0)="^^72^72^3220106"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,1,0)="This patch will address the following issue: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,3,0)="1. INC18871441 - Patient has duplicate Rx in Vista Outpatient package"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,4,0)="   HITPS-8075"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,5,0)="   Duplicates:   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,6,0)="   -----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,7,0)="   INC18557780 - VISTA Pharmacy Display Issue - route to Clinical"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,8,0)="                 Ancillary Product Line, EPMO Health per their request"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,10,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,11,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,12,0)="N/A "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,14,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,15,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,16,0)="1. INC18871441 - Patient has duplicate Rx in Vista Outpatient package"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,17,0)="   HITPS-8075"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,18,0)="   Duplicates:   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,19,0)="   -----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,20,0)="   INC18557780 - VISTA Pharmacy Display Issue - route to Clinical"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,21,0)="                 Ancillary Product Line, EPMO Health per their request"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,22,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,23,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,24,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,25,0)="The WM. Jennings Bryan Dorn VA Medical Center reported the patient had the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,26,0)="same Rx with identical Rx number showing twice Patient Medication Profile when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,27,0)="viewing the patient in the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,28,0)="ORDERS] option. This issue is also being considered a Patient Safety Issue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,29,0)="(PSI) and the number assigned by the Patient Safety team is HITPS-8075."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,31,0)="While researching the problem 2 different issues were also identified that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,32,0)="actually led to the issue described by the site:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,33,0)="  1) When the user use the option TR (Convert Titration Rx) to create a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,34,0)="     Maintenance Rx from the Titration Rx the Issue Date assigned to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,35,0)="     new Maintenance Rx was the current date. The correct Issue Date for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,36,0)="     the Maintenance Rx should be the same as the original Titration Rx. The"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,37,0)="     Expiration Date was correctly copied from the Titration Rx to the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,38,0)="     Maintenance Rx."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,39,0)="  2) When the user select the new Maintenance Rx and chose ED (Edit) and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,40,0)="     entered 6 (Issue Date) and just <RET> trough the field without changing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,41,0)="     the date the software was re-calculating the Expiration Date based on the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,42,0)="     Issue Date which was originally set with the wrong value (issue #1)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,43,0)="  3) The edit performed on issue #2 failed to correctly update the cross-"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,44,0)="     reference ""P""/""A"" in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55). Instead of killing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,45,0)="     off the existing cross-reference for the previous Expiration Date and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,46,0)="     setting a new entry for the recalculated Expiration Date it was only"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,47,0)="     setting the additional entry causing the prescription to have two entries"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,48,0)="     in the ""P""/""A"" cross-reference and that is what caused the duplicate"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,49,0)="     listing of the prescription in the Patient Medication Profile."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,51,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,52,0)="-------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,53,0)="Two changes had to be done to address the problem which will fully address the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,54,0)="three issues listed above:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,55,0)="  1) The Issue Date from the Titration Rx will be copied to the Maintenance Rx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,56,0)="     when the user select the option TR (Convert Titration Rx)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,57,0)="  2) The software was changed to correctly kill off re-set he ""P""/""A"" cross-"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,58,0)="     reference for when the Expiration Date is changed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,59,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,60,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,61,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,62,0)="Two changes were made to address the problems:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,63,0)="  1) Added code at DT+11 in the routine PSOEXDT to reset the ""P""/""A"" cross-"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,64,0)="     reference in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) every time the expiration"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,65,0)="     date is changed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,66,0)="  2) Added code at RFN+5 in the routine PSOORED1 to copy the Issue Date value"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,67,0)="     from the Titration Rx to the newly created Maintenance Rx."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,70,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,71,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",520,1,72,0)="HITPS-8075"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",521,0)="646 SEQ #539^3220110.145602^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",521,1,0)="^^7^7^3220110"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",521,1,1,0)="This patch will fix the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",521,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",521,1,3,0)="There is a recurring error when utilizing the option PSO ERX FINISH "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",521,1,4,0)="(Complete Orders from eRx). This option is used to process prescriptions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",521,1,5,0)="in the PSO ERX HOLDING QUEUE. The error occurs when a user selects the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",521,1,6,0)="Print action and enters yes to have the print queued to run in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",521,1,7,0)="background. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",522,0)="562^3220119.155246^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,0)="659 SEQ #541^3220126.113544^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,0)="^^64^64^3220126"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,3,0)="1. INC19435178 (parent) and INC19726930 (child) - SPMP voids from the new "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,4,0)="View/Export Void Prescriptions [PSO SPMP VOID RX VIEW/EXPORT] option are"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,5,0)="missing required fields for the state. The View/Export Void Prescriptions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,6,0)="[PSO SPMP VOID RX VIEW/EXPORT] option was introduced by patch PSO*7*625, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,7,0)="and the voids are missing the DSP05 (Date Filled), DSP09 (Quantity"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,8,0)="Dispensed) and DSP10 (Days Supply) fields."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,10,0)="2. INC18243915 - Incomplete SPMP error message. When users delete state "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,11,0)="parameter(s) in the View/Edit SPMP State Parameters [PSO SPMP STATE "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,12,0)="PARAMETERS] option, the View/Export Single Prescription [PSO SPMP SINGLE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,13,0)="RX VIEW/EXPORT] displays an incomplete error message without the state"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,14,0)="name: ""PMP Parameters missing for""."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,17,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,18,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,19,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,22,0)="Additional Information:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,23,0)="-----------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,24,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,26,0)="INC19435178 (parent) and INC19726930 (child)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,27,0)="INC18243915"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,30,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,31,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,32,0)="Durham VA Medical Center reported that the voids created with the new"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,33,0)="View/Export Void Prescriptions [PSO SPMP VOID RX VIEW/EXPORT] option"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,34,0)="introduced with patch PSO*7*625, were rejected due to missing required"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,35,0)="fields for the state.  The missing fields are DSP05 (Date Filled), DSP09"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,36,0)="(Quantity Dispensed) and DSP10 (Days Supply)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,38,0)="Alvin C. York VA Medical Center reported that the user deleted a state "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,39,0)="parameter in the View/Edit SPMP State Parameters [PSO SPMP STATE "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,40,0)="PARAMETERS] option, the View/Export Single Prescription [PSO SPMP SINGLE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,41,0)="RX VIEW/EXPORT] option displays an incomplete error message missing the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,42,0)="state name: ""PMP Parameters missing for""."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,45,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,46,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,47,0)="The following changes were made to address the issues listed above:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,48,0)="1) Update the logic for the View/Export Void Prescriptions [PSO SPMP "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,49,0)="VOID RX VIEW/EXPORT] option to send the missing required fields"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,50,0)="(DSP05, DSP09, and DSP10)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,52,0)="2) Update the logic for the View/Export Single Prescription [PSO SPMP "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,53,0)="SINGLE RX VIEW/EXPORT] option to display the complete error message when "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,54,0)="state parameters are not set up."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,57,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,58,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,59,0)="The following changes were made to address the issues listed above:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,60,0)="1) Routine PSOASAP0 was updated in the DSP05, DSP09, and DSP10 tags to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,61,0)="send the DSP05, DSP09, and DSP10 fields for the new ""RX"" void batch type."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,63,0)="2) Routine PSOSPML4 was updated in the EXPORT+9 tag to display the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",523,1,64,0)="appropriate state parameter error message."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",524,0)="656 SEQ #542^3220203.123822^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",524,1,0)="^^2^2^3220203"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",524,1,1,0)="INC19182976 - Remote Data Interoperability (RDI) displays incorrect"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",524,1,2,0)="              number of refills remaining for remote prescriptions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",525,0)="663 SEQ #543^3220303.145944^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",525,1,0)="^^4^4^3220303"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",525,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",525,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",525,1,3,0)="Duplicate order checking might display an incorrect dispense drug against "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",525,1,4,0)="pending clinic medications."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",526,0)="642 SEQ #544^3220303.145953^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",526,1,0)="^^1^1^3220303"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",526,1,1,0)="See the patch description for detailed information."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,0)="664 SEQ #547^3220321.19265^86"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,0)="^^34^34^3220321"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,3,0)="1. INC20140218 - Page Number keeps counting in Extended Patient "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,4,0)="Demographics"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,6,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,8,0)="1. INC20140218 - Page Number keeps counting in Extended Patient "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,9,0)="Demographics"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,11,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,12,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,13,0)="It was reported that the PAGE counter on the Extended Patient "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,14,0)="Demographics page was not getting reset when going between Complete "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,15,0)="Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] option and the View Prescriptions [PSO "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,16,0)="VIEW] option within the RX (Prescription) [PSO RX] menu."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,19,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,20,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,21,0)="The following changes were made to address the issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,22,0)="Reset the page number for Extended Patient Demographics only when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,23,0)="switching between Complete Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] option and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,24,0)="the View Prescriptions [PSO VIEW] option within the RX (Prescription) [PSO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,25,0)="RX] menu."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,28,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,29,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,30,0)="The following changes were made to address the issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,31,0)="Routine PSODEMSB was updated in the HDR tag to reset the page counter "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,32,0)="for Extended Patient Demographics only when going between the Complete"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,33,0)="Orders from OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] option and the View Prescriptions [PSO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",527,1,34,0)="VIEW] option within the RX (Prescription) [PSO RX] menu."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,0)="654 SEQ #549^3220329.141217^86"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,0)="^^36^36^3220329"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,3,0)="1. INC18606996 - Prescriptions (RXs) being queued and suspended twice in "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,4,0)="                 VistA Outpatient package."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,7,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,8,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,9,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,12,0)="Additional Information:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,13,0)="-----------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,14,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,16,0)="1. INC18606996 - Prescriptions (RXs) being queued and suspended twice in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,17,0)="                 VistA Outpatient package."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,20,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,21,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,22,0)="The Orlando VA Medical Center (FL) reported that the same prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,23,0)="is being queued and suspended twice in the Patient Medication Profile when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,24,0)="editing and refilling a single prescription in the Patient Prescription "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,25,0)="Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] option."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,27,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,28,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,29,0)="The following changes were made to address the issue listed above:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,30,0)="1) Check the array that contains the prescriptions for duplicates."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,32,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,33,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,34,0)="The following changes were made to address the issue listed above:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,35,0)="1) Added code starting at FINISH+33 in the PSOR52 routine to check for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",528,1,36,0)="   duplicate RX numbers in the PSORX(""PSOL"",N) array variable."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",529,0)="634 SEQ #550^3220329.141226^86"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",529,1,0)="^^3^3^3220329"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",529,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",529,1,2,0)="INC14294718 - An issue is occurring when processing orders resulting in an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",529,1,3,0)="              infinite loop of 'Press return to Continue' prompts."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,0)="661 SEQ #551^3220330.115527^86"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,0)="^^50^50^3220330"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,2,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,4,0)="1. INC15468023 (parent) and INC16381883 (child) - Duplicate RX when "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,5,0)="finishing pending renewal in Outpatient Pharmacy [PSO LM BACKDOOR "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,6,0)="ORDERS] and user gets disconnected."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,9,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,10,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,11,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,14,0)="Additional Information:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,15,0)="-----------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,16,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,18,0)="INC15468023 (parent) and INC16381883 (child)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,21,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,22,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,23,0)="Ralph H. Johnson Department of Veterans Affairs Medical Center in "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,24,0)="Charleston SC reported that Vista is creating duplicate prescriptions "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,25,0)="when the user is disconnected while finishing a pending renewal "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,26,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,29,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,30,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,31,0)="The following changes were made to address the issue listed above:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,32,0)="1) Update the logic for finishing a pending renewal in [PSO LM BACKDOOR "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,33,0)="ORDERS] to wait to file data into File #55 (Pharmacy Patient) and File #52"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,34,0)="(Prescription) until all prompts are answered. So if the user is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,35,0)="disconnected, the pending renewal will remain pending. In addition, when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,36,0)="the pending renewal has been completed a new message will display on the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,37,0)="screen notifying the user that the order has been renewed "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,38,0)="(i.e. ""...ORDER RENEWED."")"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,41,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,42,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,43,0)="The following changes were made to address the issue listed above:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,44,0)="1) Routine PSORN52A was updated in the F55 tag to wait to file data into "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,45,0)="File #55 (Pharmacy Patient) and File #52 (Prescription) until all prompts "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,46,0)="are answered."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,48,0)="2) Routine PSOORNE4 was updated in the PKI tag to display ""...ORDER "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,49,0)="RENEWED."" when the renewal process is complete in [PSO LM BACKDOOR "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",530,1,50,0)="ORDERS]."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,0)="658 SEQ #552^3220401.161658^65"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,0)="^^29^29^3220401"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,1,0)="1. INC19108358- HL7 field ORC-13 is sometimes blank when "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,2,0)="   transmitting from VistA to ScriptPro"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,5,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,6,0)="   -------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,7,0)="   ScriptPro states that ORC-13 is sometimes blank, causing the system"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,8,0)="   to default to the wrong inventory center. It was found that this "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,9,0)="   occurs when the option PULL EARLY FROM SUSPENSE is used.  When running"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,10,0)="   PP (Pull Rx (OP)) from the Outpatient Medications screen in Patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,11,0)="   Prescription Processing the issue does not occur and ORC-13 is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,12,0)="   populated with the selected LABEL PRINTER."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,14,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,15,0)="   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,16,0)="   Routine PSORXL is modified to pass variable PSOLAP to the background "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,17,0)="   processing job unconditionally.  Prior to this patch the variable "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,18,0)="   PSOLAP was only passed when variable SUSPT was false, when SUSPT was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,19,0)="   true it attempted to pass PFION which doesn't exist anywhere in Vista."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,21,0)="   Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,22,0)="   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,23,0)="   Prior to this patch QLBL+7^PSORXL used the following condition to send "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,24,0)="   either variable PFION or PSOLAP depending on the existence of variable "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,25,0)="   SUSPT: $S($G(SUSPT):""PFION"",1:""PSOLAP"")"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,27,0)="   This patch modifies QLBL^PSORXL to remove the condition and reference "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,28,0)="   to ""PFION"" and unconditionally send ""PSOLAP"" the same as occurs when PP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",531,1,29,0)="   is used in Patient Prescription Processing."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,0)="529 SEQ #553^3220504.092049^17"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,0)="^^67^67^3220504"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,1,0)="The Clinical Ancillary Services (CAS) - Medication Permission/Dispensing "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,2,0)="Updates (MPDU) project provides the ability to support multiple Drug "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,3,0)="Enforcement Administration (DEA) Numbers for a user."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,5,0)="This patch PSO*7*529 is part of a group of patches for this enhancement"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,6,0)="and must be installed after XU*8*688. The following other patches will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,7,0)="released in the future and includes: OR*3*506, XU*8*689, PSO*7*545,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,8,0)="PSJ*5*372, OR*3*488 and OR*3*499."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,10,0)="************************** ATTENTION ********************************"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,11,0)="This enhancement also includes a new Graphical User Interface (GUI) "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,12,0)="executable, ePCSDataEntryforPrescriber.exe (ePCS GUI), which allows setup "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,13,0)="of users to write controlled substances. For retrieval and installation"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,14,0)="instructions, please see the Documentation Retrieval Instructions section."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,16,0)="This patch PSO*7*529 has the following enhancements:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,18,0)="1. Create a web service client to be used during installation to retrieve"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,19,0)="   the provider information from the VA Maintained DOJ/DEA web server."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,20,0)="   This information will be stored in the DEA NUMBERS FILE (#8991.9), and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,21,0)="   linked to the NEW PERSON FILE (#200), NEW DEA #'S (#53.21) multiple."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,23,0)="2. An environment check routine PSO7E529 is included in this patch that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,24,0)="   will provide the following VistA environment options:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,27,0)="     Select one of the following:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,29,0)="          P         PRODUCTION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,30,0)="          D         PRE-PROD"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,31,0)="          S         SQA"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,33,0)="   ENVIRONMENT TYPE: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,35,0)="   Site can select the appropriate environment and accordingly the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,36,0)="   software will setup the DOJ/DEA web server and the web service. It will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,37,0)="   check the availability of the DOJ/DEA web service and will continue the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,38,0)="   patch installation. If the web service is available, it will display a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,39,0)="   message, ""The Environmental Check Routine finished Successfully"" and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,40,0)="   will continue with the patch installation. If the web service is not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,41,0)="   available then it will abort the installation with the following"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,42,0)="   message:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,44,0)="   *******************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,45,0)="         WARNING:  The WEB SERVER/SERVICE SETUP FAILED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,46,0)="    Please try again after few minutes. Failed to install,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,47,0)="              please submit a Service Now ticket."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,48,0)="                >>>> Installation aborted <<<<"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,49,0)="   *******************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,51,0)="3. A post-install routine PSO7P529 included in this patch will migrate"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,52,0)="   all DEA's from the NEW PERSON FILE (#200) and will utilize the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,53,0)="   DOJ/DEA web service to create entries in the DEA NUMBERS FILE "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,54,0)="   (#8991.9). Providers that cannot be linked will be recorded in a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,55,0)="   Migration Exception Log and will be sent in an email with the subject;"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,56,0)="   DEA Migration Exception Report 11/28/2018 (run date) to PSDMGR key"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,57,0)="   holders. These entries can be reviewed and corrected using the ePCS GUI"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,58,0)="   executable that will be sent separately as part of this project."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,60,0)="   These migrated provider entries in the DEA NUMBERS FILE (#8991.9) will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,61,0)="   be marked as USE FOR INPATIENT ORDERS. The Detox # will be derived "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,62,0)="   from the business activity code/sub code."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,64,0)="4. Create Remote Procedure Calls to support the entry and maintenance of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,65,0)="   the information stored in the DEA NUMBERS FILE (#8991.9) using the ePCS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,66,0)="   GUI. This functionality will utilize the DOJ/DEA web service to get"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",532,1,67,0)="   near real-time updates."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",533,0)="667 SEQ #555^3220510.142718^86"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",533,1,0)="^^1^1^3220510"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",533,1,1,0)="See FORUM patch description."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",534,0)="669 SEQ #556^3220516.103934^86"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",534,1,0)="^^5^5^3220516"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",534,1,1,0)="INC19990362: eRx allows selecting providers before complete creation via "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",534,1,2,0)="PSO PROVIDER ADD"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",534,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",534,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",534,1,5,0)="ers before complete creation via PSO PROVIDER "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",535,0)="674 SEQ #557^3220519.131404^86"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",535,1,0)="^^7^7^3220519"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",535,1,1,0)="Following is the description of this issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",535,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",535,1,3,0)="There is a recurring error when utilizing the option PROCESS INTERNET "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",535,1,4,0)="REFILLS (PSO INTERNET REFILLS). The issue occurs after user jumps out of "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",535,1,5,0)="option PROCESS TELEPHONE REFILLS (PSO PROCESS TELEPHONE REFILLS) by "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",535,1,6,0)="entering '^' at the DIVISION prompt and then subsequently runs the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",535,1,7,0)="internet refill option, which then aborts due to an <UNDEFINED> error."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",536,0)="672 SEQ #559^3220602.14144^86"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",536,1,0)="^^5^5^3220602"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",536,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",536,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",536,1,3,0)="The 'JUMP TO ORDER' (JO) action in the Inbound eRx system could state"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",536,1,4,0)="""Patient has no pending prescriptions"" even though the patient does have "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",536,1,5,0)="pending prescriptions."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",537,0)="676 SEQ #561^3220627.143207^86"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",537,1,0)="^^1^1^3220627"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",537,1,1,0)="See FORUM patch description for details."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,0)="686 SEQ #562^3220803.14064^86"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,0)="^^45^45^3220803"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,3,0)="OUTPATIENT PHARMACY SPEED RENEW OF RX STATUS DISCONTINUED BY PROVIDER"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,6,0)="Associated ticket(s):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,7,0)="====================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,9,0)="1.      INC22416223 - VISTA: OUPATIENT PHARMACY: INBOUND ERX QUEUE ERROR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,11,0)="Associated NSR(s):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,12,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,13,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,15,0)="Participating Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,16,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,17,0)="TBD"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,20,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,21,0)="==========================================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,23,0)="1.      INC22416223 - VISTA: OUPATIENT PHARMACY: INBOUND ERX QUEUE ERROR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,25,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,26,0)="   -------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,27,0)="While processing the INBOUND ERX QUEUE, a user erroneously entered '^E' "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,28,0)="at the Days Supply prompt which caused a hard error to occur.  The "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,29,0)="problem is that eRX processing is not written to allow jumping to other "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,30,0)="prompts.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,33,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,34,0)="   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,35,0)="The logic is updated to handle input that starts with a caret (^) the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,36,0)="same as when only a caret (^) is entered and exit.  This change affects "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,37,0)="the prompts handled by QTYDSRFL^PSOERXU4, which are DAYS SUPPLY, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,38,0)="QUANTITY, and REFILLS.  The error was not seen for other prompts."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,40,0)="   Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,41,0)="   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,42,0)="This line at DIR+7^PSODIR1 is added:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,43,0)="I $E(X,1)=U S PSODIR(""DFLG"")=1 G DIRX ;p686"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,44,0)="This will cause the process to exit when the first character entered is a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",538,1,45,0)="caret (^)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",539,0)="648^3220808.171209^86"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,0)="662 SEQ #564^3220817.170508^86"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,0)="^^128^128^3220817"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,1,0)="It was reported that the Meds by Mail logic added to the State "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,2,0)="Prescription Monitoring Program (SPMP) patch, PSO*7.0*630, was not working"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,3,0)="correctly for some of the SPMP options. This patch will resolve the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,4,0)="following SPMP issues:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,6,0)="1. INC19848427 - The same RX fills are being transmitted in multiple "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,7,0)="batches and also to states not associated with the patient or dispensing "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,8,0)="pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,10,0)="2. INC19848615 - View/Export Single Prescription [PSO SPMP SINGLE RX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,11,0)="VIEW/EXPORT] option only sends to state of dispensing pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,13,0)="3. INC19851935 - Export Batch Processing [PSO SPMP BATCH PROCESSING] "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,14,0)="option only displays ASAP version of the dispensing state"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,16,0)="4. INC21661107 - Manual Voids sent to state of dispensing pharmacy, not "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,17,0)="patient's home state"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,20,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,21,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,22,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,25,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,27,0)="1. INC19848427 - the Scheduled SPMP Data Export [PSO SPMP SCHEDULED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,28,0)="EXPORT] option and CS Prescriptions Not Transmitted [PSO SPMP RX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,29,0)="NOT TRANSMITTED] option are both gathering prescriptions for incorrect"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,30,0)="states."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,32,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,33,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,34,0)="A single prescription can incorrectly be sent to multiple states.  This "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,35,0)="happens if the state being transmitted has a state IEN which is a single "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,36,0)="digit, and the patient's home state has a state IEN that contains that "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,37,0)="transmitting state's IEN.  This will affect both the transmission for the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,38,0)="previous day (including return to stock) and the 30 day look back."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,40,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,41,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,42,0)="Fix the logic for the Scheduled SPMP Data Export [PSO SPMP SCHEDULED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,43,0)="EXPORT] option and CS Prescriptions Not Transmitted [PSO SPMP RX NOT"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,44,0)="TRANSMITTED] option to look at the dispensing pharmacy state and the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,45,0)="patient state, and then look at the SEND EXPORT STATE PARAMETER (#21) "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,46,0)="field in the SPMP STATE PARAMETERS (#58.41) file to determine what"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,47,0)="state(s) the batch needs to be sent."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,49,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,50,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,51,0)="Routine PSOSPMU1 in the GATHER tag, change the contains from ""'[STATE"" to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,52,0)="""'[(""^""_STATE_""^"")"" when checking for the STATE variable. This will fix"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,53,0)="the issue with the prescriptions being sent to incorrect states."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,55,0)="2. INC19848615 - the View/Export Single Prescription [PSO SPMP SINGLE RX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,56,0)="VIEW/EXPORT] option only transmits to the dispensing pharmacy's state."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,58,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,59,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,60,0)="Patch PSO*7.0*630 added functionality to allow Meds By Mail to transmit "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,61,0)="control substance prescriptions to the SPMP state of the patient's "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,62,0)="geographic state.  However, when using View/Export Single Prescription "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,63,0)="[PSO SPMP SINGLE RX VIEW/EXPORT] option"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,64,0)="to send a single RX, it will only send to the state of the dispensing "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,65,0)="pharmacy and cannot be changed to transmit to the patient's geographical "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,66,0)="state."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,68,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,69,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,70,0)="Fix the logic for the View/Export Single Prescription [PSO SPMP SINGLE RX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,71,0)="VIEW/EXPORT] option to look at the dispensing pharmacy state and the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,72,0)="patient state, and then look at the SEND EXPORT STATE PARAMETER (#21) "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,73,0)="field in the SPMP STATE PARAMETERS (#58.41) file to determine what"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,74,0)="state(s) the batch needs to be sent."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,76,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,77,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,78,0)="Routine PSOSPML4 in the EXPORT tag, look at the dispensing pharmacy state"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,79,0)="and the patient state, and then look at the SEND EXPORT STATE PARAMETER "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,80,0)="(#21) field in the SPMP STATE PARAMETERS (#58.41) file to determine what"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,81,0)="state(s) the batch needs to be sent."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,83,0)="3. INC19851935 - the Export Batch Processing [PSO SPMP BATCH PROCESSING] "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,84,0)="option reverts to dispensing pharmacy's state."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,86,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,87,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,88,0)="Patch PSO*7.0*630 added functionality to allow Meds By Mail to transmit "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,89,0)="control substance prescriptions to the SPMP state of the patient's "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,90,0)="geographic state.  However, when using Export Batch Processing [PSO SPMP "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,91,0)="BATCH PROCESSING] option to view transmissions for states other than the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,92,0)="dispensing pharmacy's state, then the prescription details will display "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,93,0)="the ASAP version for the dispensing pharmacy's state.  As the user backs "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,94,0)="out of the option, the state changes away from what the state the user "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,95,0)="initially picked and instead changes to the dispensing pharmacy's state."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,97,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,98,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,99,0)="Fix the logic for the Export Batch Processing [PSO SPMP BATCH PROCESSING]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,100,0)="option to display the appropriate state."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,101,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,102,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,103,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,104,0)="Routine PSOSPML4 in the EN tag, change the STATEIEN variable lookup so the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,105,0)="appropriate state displays."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,107,0)="4. INC21661107 - the View/Export Void Prescriptions [PSO SPMP VOID RX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,108,0)="VIEW/EXPORT] option only transmits to the dispensing pharmacy's state."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,110,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,111,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,112,0)="The View/Export Void Prescriptions [PSO SPMP VOID RX VIEW/EXPORT]"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,113,0)="option only transmits to the dispensing pharmacy's state."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,115,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,116,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,117,0)="Fix the logic for the View/Export Void Prescriptions [PSO SPMP VOID RX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,118,0)="VIEW/EXPORT] option to look at the dispensing pharmacy state and the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,119,0)="patient state, and then look at the SEND EXPORT STATE PARAMETER (#21) "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,120,0)="field in the SPMP STATE PARAMETERS (#58.41) file to determine what "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,121,0)="state(s) the batch needs to be sent."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,123,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,124,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,125,0)="Routine PSOSPMV in the RXLOOP tag, change the logic to look at the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,126,0)="dispensing pharmacy state and the patient address state, and then look at "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,127,0)="the SEND EXPORT STATE PARAMETER (#21) field in the SPMP STATE PARAMETERS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",540,1,128,0)="(#58.41) file to determine what state(s) the batch needs to be sent."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",541,0)="684 SEQ #565^3220824.171754^86"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",541,1,0)="^^1^1^3220824"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",541,1,1,0)="See the patch description for PSO*7.0*684"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,0)="692 SEQ #566^3220928.075529^90"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,0)="^^59^59^3220928"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,1,0)="This patch will address the following issue: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,3,0)="1. INC23078077 - Delayed delivery of electronic doctor orders through VHA"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,4,0)="                 Inbound eRx hub"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,6,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,7,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,8,0)="1. INC23078077 - Delayed delivery of electronic doctor orders through VHA"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,9,0)="   Inbound eRx hub"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,10,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,11,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,12,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,13,0)="Meds-By-Mail (MbM) reported that electronic prescriptions (eRx) are received"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,14,0)="several hours after the outside prescriber transmitted them. The problem seems"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,15,0)="to be caused by a increasing traffic handled by the eRx Hub which centralizes"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,16,0)="all nationwide incoming eRx prescriptions into the VA. One part of the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,17,0)="processing by the eRx Hub is the auto-matching of patient, provider and drug."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,18,0)="In other words, the eRx Hub tries to pre-emptively find a VistA corresponding"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,19,0)="for these three fields before forwarding the incoming prescription to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,20,0)="VistA site. The auto-matching for the provider and drug is accomplished by the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,21,0)="eRx Hub through two VistALink calls (one for the provider and one for the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,22,0)="drug) to the VistA site and if a match is found at the VistA site it returns"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,23,0)="the IENs (Internal Entry Number) back to the eRx Hub which in turn records the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,24,0)="success/failure for an auto-match statistics reporting purpose and then sends"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,25,0)="the matched IENs back to the VistA site along with the complete eRx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,26,0)="prescription. Although not 100% confirmed, the suspicion is that such calls to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,27,0)="VistA have become quite costly as the volume of incoming eRx increased"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,28,0)="drastically in the past few months and are likely to be partially responsible"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,29,0)="for the processing delays."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,30,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,31,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,32,0)="-------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,33,0)="The solution to this problem is two-fold:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,35,0)="  1) A change is being made in VistA through this patch to the processing of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,36,0)="     the incoming eRx to check if the eRx Hub provider and drug auto-matches"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,37,0)="     were successful or not (""fail""). If not, using the incoming data from the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,38,0)="     outside prescriber VistA will utilize the exact same VistA code currently"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,39,0)="     used by the eRx Hub to try to auto-match these locally and if it succeeds"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,40,0)="     it will auto populate VistA Provider and/or VistA Drug fields."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,42,0)="  2) Once the this patch has been released and installed nationally at every"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,43,0)="     VistA site an update will then be made at the eRx Hub to shut off the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,44,0)="     auto-match processing for provider and drug. This will consist of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,45,0)="     stopping the two VistALink calls made to the VistA site and always"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,46,0)="     sending to VistA a ""fail"" result with a ""Auto-match not performed"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,47,0)="     reason."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,48,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,49,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,50,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,51,0)="A new routine (PSOERUT) was created to parse an XML message into a local array"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,52,0)="and code was added to INCERX+29^PSOERXI1 and INCERX+48^PSOERXI1 to call the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,53,0)="new API XML2GBL in the new routine to parse the incoming XML message, retrieve"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,54,0)="the provider and drug information and call the same code the eRx Hub was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,55,0)="calling (via RPC calls) to perform the auto-match for provider and drug"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,56,0)="(PRVMTCH^PSOERXA0 and DRGMTCH^PSOERXA0). Furthermore, it was determined that"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,57,0)="the array variable (PSODRUG(""IEN"")) used at CSID+9^PSOUTL, used to check if"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,58,0)="a drug is a controlled substance or not was wrong and was replaced with"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",542,1,59,0)="DRGIEN."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",543,0)="441^3221005.145506^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",543,1,0)="^^2^2^3221005"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",543,1,1,0)="Please refer to the patch description for contents and detailed "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",543,1,2,0)="information."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",544,0)="701 SEQ #569^3221012.093052^90"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",545,0)="694 SEQ #570^3221214.133831^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",545,1,0)="^^1^1^3221214"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",545,1,1,0)="See FORUM patch description."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",546,0)="660 SEQ #571^3221214.134317^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",546,1,0)="^^9^9^3221214"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",546,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",546,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",546,1,3,0)="The Rx reference of an original fill that is displayed on an activity log "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",546,1,4,0)="record is incorrect when the CMOP host site reports a change in the Rx's "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",546,1,5,0)="National Drug Code (NDC). This occurs when the Rx has a suspended refill "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",546,1,6,0)="and the original fill's fill date is changed. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",546,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",546,1,8,0)="This patch will also fix a <SUBSCRIPT> error caused by the code of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",546,1,9,0)="original patch PSO*7*638 that was created to fix the original issue."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,0)="706 SEQ #572^3221214.134423^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,0)="^^31^31^3221214"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,1,0)="This patch will address the following issue: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,3,0)="1. INC23078077 - Delayed delivery of electronic doctor orders through VHA"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,4,0)="                 Inbound eRx hub"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,6,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,7,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,8,0)="1. INC23078077 - Delayed delivery of electronic doctor orders through VHA"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,9,0)="   Inbound eRx hub"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,10,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,11,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,12,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,13,0)="Patch PSO*7*706 was released on September 21st, 2022 to address this issue."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,14,0)="However, an issue was discovered with the logic to auto-match Prescriber and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,15,0)="Drug in VistA once the eRx XML message is received from the eRx Hub."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,16,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,17,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,18,0)="-------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,19,0)="This patch corrects the auto-match VistA algorithm to addresses this issue."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,20,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,21,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,22,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,23,0)="Patch PSO*7*706 assumed that the XML parameter in the PSOERXI1 INCERX RPC"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,24,0)="Broker call (responsible for processing incoming eRx from the eRx Hub)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,25,0)="contained the entire eRx XML record. However, during tests with the updated"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,26,0)="eRx Hub it turned out that the incoming XML message is fragmented in 3 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,27,0)="parameters: XML, XML2 and XML3. Information about Prescriber and Drug seems"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,28,0)="to be sent on XML2 and that's why the logic in PSO*7*706 failed. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,29,0)="now checks the parsed information stored in the ^TMP($J,""PSOERXO1"") global,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,30,0)="which is supposed to contain the complete incoming XML information from XML,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",547,1,31,0)="XML2 and XML3."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",548,0)="680^3221214.13454^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,0)="698 SEQ #577^3221227.102857^90"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,0)="^^49^49^3221227"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,2,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,4,0)="1) INC22865486 - This patch will address the issue described in "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,5,0)="ServiceNow Incident INC22865486, regarding the <UNDEFINED>ACLOG+5^PSON52 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,6,0)="error when converting a Titration RX to a Maintenance RX.  In addition, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,7,0)="this patch will resolve the incorrect RX reference in the remarks field."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,10,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,11,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,12,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,15,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,16,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,17,0)="1) INC22865486 - This patch will address the issue described in "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,18,0)="ServiceNow Incident INC22865486, regarding the <UNDEFINED>ACLOG+5^PSON52 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,19,0)="error when converting a Titration RX to a Maintenance RX.  In addition, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,20,0)="this patch will resolve the incorrect RX reference in the remarks field."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,23,0)="Problem 1: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,24,0)="---------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,25,0)="If a patient has an active titration RX and a pending controlled substance"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,26,0)="RX from CPRS, and the patient's orders are finished via COMPLETE ORDERS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,27,0)="FROM OERR option [PSO LMOE FINISH]. If the primary filter ""CS"" controlled"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,28,0)="substances is used, and the pharmacist first converts the Titration"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,29,0)="prescription to a Maintenance order. After accepting the order, a hard"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,30,0)="error occurs: <UNDEFINED>ACLOG+5^PSON52 *PSOCSP(""NAME""). In addition,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,31,0)="the remarks field for the renewed titration corrrectly refers to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,32,0)="Maintenance RX, but incorrectly refers to the CPRS controlled substance RX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,33,0)="as being edited."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,36,0)="Resolution 1:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,37,0)="------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,38,0)="It was discovered that when the user selects the ""CS"" controlled "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,39,0)="substances as the primary filter when finishing a patient's"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,40,0)="orders via COMPLETE ORDERS FROM OERR option [PSO LMOE FINISH],"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,41,0)="the logic pulls the data for any pending controlled substances for the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,42,0)="patient selected. This causes the data to be set to the pending CS, even"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,43,0)="if the pharmacist chooses a non-controlled substance, in this case the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,44,0)="Titration RX.  Most of the variables are newed in the logic, except for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,45,0)="the OR0 variable which is not cleared out when the CS RX is not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,46,0)="selected.  This is the reason for the <UNDEFINED>ACLOG+5^PSON52 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,47,0)="*PSOCSP(""NAME"") error, and why the remarks contains the CS data."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,48,0)="This fix for this issue is to new the OR0 variable in the SEL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",549,1,49,0)="and NEWSEL tags of PSOORNE2."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,0)="679 SEQ #575^3221228.092913^90"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,1,0)="^^12^12^3221228"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,1,1,0)="VSE-2687 VistA: Modify PSO VCC REFILL rpc to support REFILL SOURCE input "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,1,2,0)="parameter."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,1,4,0)="ROUTINES"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,1,5,0)="========"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,1,6,0)="PSOATRFV"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,1,7,0)="PSOVCCA"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,1,8,0)="PSO679P"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,1,10,0)="REMOTE PROCEDURES"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,1,11,0)="================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",550,1,12,0)="PSO VCC REFILL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",551,0)="709 SEQ #576^3221228.10063^90"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",551,1,0)="^^11^11^3221228"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",551,1,1,0)="This patch corrects two issues identified after the installation of "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",551,1,2,0)="CPRS32B regarding the printing of the Sig label in Spanish."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",551,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",551,1,4,0)="1. When the user selects 'No' to Copy INDICATION into the Sig? the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",551,1,5,0)="Spanish label continues to print out the Indication on the Spanish Sig "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",551,1,6,0)="label."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",551,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",551,1,8,0)="2. When the user selects 'Yes' to Copy INDICATION into the Sig? the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",551,1,9,0)="Indication is printed after the Patient Instructions instead of before.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",551,1,10,0)="The Spanish Sig label layout should be the same as the English Sig label "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",551,1,11,0)="layout."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",552,0)="655 SEQ #578^3221229.105957^90"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",552,1,0)="^^6^6^3221229"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",552,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",552,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",552,1,3,0)="Two sites have reported separate incidents where the release date and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",552,1,4,0)="time of an Rx's CMOP event are being overwritten when a reprint of a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",552,1,5,0)="refill is executed locally. Since the refill's reprint is executed "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",552,1,6,0)="locally the CMOP event's released date and time should not change."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,0)="651 SEQ #579^3230109.172924^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,0)="^^494^494^3230109"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,1,0)="This patch will address the following issues: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,3,0)="1. INC19910756 - Duplicated entries of drug code number in VistA NDC file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,4,0)="                 caused erroneous drug auto-match"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,6,0)="2. INC17880583 - Pharmacist cannot process e-prescribers' RXRENEWALRESPONSE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,8,0)="3. INC19246636 - eRx SSN gets truncated on vistA screen (OERR and pharmacy "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,9,0)="                 backdoor)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,11,0)="4. INC19419044 - Acknowledge option deficiency within RxRenewal and RxChange"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,12,0)="                 Request and Response messages"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,14,0)="5. INC19287772 - HAC VistA eRx 4.0 sorting issue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,16,0)="6. INC19647182 - Refill 6 shows as Partial in ECME log"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,18,0)="7. INC20086630 - Pharmacists are blocked from editing conjunction and duration"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,19,0)="                 prompts for complex orders on eRx holding queue screen"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,21,0)="8. INC20420672 - Audit Log (AU) option in eRx holding queue fails to capture"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,22,0)="                 original eRx SIG"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,24,0)="9. INC20842304 - EPCS software detox# validation capability fails"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,26,0)="10.INC20591567 - RxRenewalRequest messages are blocked at hub due to missing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,27,0)="                 Pharmacy Data"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,29,0)="11.INC20591582 - RxRenewalRequest blocked at VA routing hub due to missing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,30,0)="                 Observation "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,32,0)="12.INC20730418 - Non-Controlled Substance eRx was blocked from being edited by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,33,0)="                 Electronic Prescribing for Controlled Substance mechanism"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,35,0)="13.INC21240944 - received eRX type CS for non-CS drug"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,37,0)="14.INC22031884 - eRx pending order screen does not display original"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,38,0)="                 physician's instruction and relevant drug dose strength"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,39,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,40,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,41,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,42,0)="1. INC19910756 - Duplicated entries of drug code number in VistA NDC file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,43,0)="                 caused erroneous drug auto-match"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,44,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,45,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,46,0)="Meds-by-Mail (MbM) encountered a problem with eRx auto-matching functionality"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,47,0)="performed by the eRx Hub web-application. For the incoming NDC 000185060510"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,48,0)="the software was wrongly auto-matching to CHLORDIAZEPOXIDE HCL 5MG CAP and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,49,0)="pre-populating the matched VistA Drug for the incoming eRx record."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,50,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,51,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,52,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,53,0)="The eRx dispense drug auto-matching functionality was changed to skip Inactive "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,54,0)="NDC/UPN entries while trying to match the eRx incoming NDC with an existing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,55,0)="VistA dispense drug."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,56,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,57,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,58,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,59,0)="The existing code at DRGMTCH+29^PSOERXA0 was reading the first NDC/UPN entry"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,60,0)="that matched the incoming NDC to find a match in the DRUG file (#50) without"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,61,0)="checking whether the entry was Inactive or not. The code was changed to loop"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,62,0)="through all the entries in the ""NDC"" cross-reference in the NDC/UPN file "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,63,0)="(#50.67), skipping Inactive entries, until it can find a unique match to a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,64,0)="dispense drug. If more than one possible match is found then it will not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,65,0)="auto-match the dispense drug."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,66,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,67,0)="2. INC17880583 - Pharmacist cannot process e-prescribers' RXRENEWALRESPONSE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,69,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,70,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,71,0)="Meds-by-Mail (MbM) reported a problem with certain incoming RxRenewalResponse"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,72,0)="records that were assigned an RXN (RXRENEWAL RESPONSE - NEW) status but could"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,73,0)="not be processed because they did not have a corresponding eRx record. This "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,74,0)="caused this records to remain on their 'to-do' eRx Queue until they 'aged out'."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,75,0)="The ACK (Acknowledge) action is not available for such records. MbM referred"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,76,0)="to such records as 'orphaned' records."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,77,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,78,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,79,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,80,0)="The processing of incoming eRx records was changed to automatically assign a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,81,0)="status of RXF (RXRENEWAL RESPONSE FAILED) to records without a corresponding"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,82,0)="eRx record. In addition it automatically adds the following comment to the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,83,0)="Status History for the 'orphaned' record: Response received was 'Denied' -"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,84,0)="No corresponding eRx Record found."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,86,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,87,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,88,0)="Introduced new code at REFRESP+20^PSOERXA5 to check whether the incoming eRx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,89,0)="response record has a corresponding eRx record. If not, the status of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,90,0)="incoming response record will be changed to RXF and a comment will be logged"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,91,0)="to Status History log."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,92,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,93,0)="3. INC19246636 - eRx SSN gets truncated on vistA screen (OERR and pharmacy "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,94,0)="                 backdoor)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,95,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,96,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,97,0)="Meds-by-Mail (MbM) reported a problem with the patient SSN (Social Security"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,98,0)="Number) last digit being truncated in the Patient Prescription Processing [PSO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,99,0)="LM BACKDOOR] option. The problem is with in the eRx information listed at the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,100,0)="beginning of a Pending Order or an Active prescription. This problem happens"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,101,0)="only for incoming eRx records where the SSN contains '-' (dashes)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,102,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,103,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,104,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,105,0)="The size of the eRx field SSN was expanded to display the entire SSN when it"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,106,0)="contains '-'. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,108,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,109,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,110,0)="The size of the field SSN was changed from 15 to 20 in the line of code at"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,111,0)="DERX1+72^PSOERXU1, which should accommodate an SSN with '-' in it."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,113,0)="4. INC19419044 - Acknowledge option deficiency within RxRenewal and RxChange"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,114,0)="                 Request and Response messages"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,115,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,116,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,117,0)="Meds-by-Mail (MbM) reported that users were able to choose the ACK"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,118,0)="(Acknowledge) action multiple times on the same record, which in some cases"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,119,0)="would trigger a 'Verify' message to be sent back to the eRx prescriber"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,120,0)="multiple times."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,122,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,123,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,124,0)="A change was made to the ACK action to block the execution if the eRx record"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,125,0)="is in one of the following status (already acknowledged):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,127,0)="  CAA  CANCEL REQUEST ACKNOWLEDGED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,128,0)="  CXA  RXCHANGE RESPONSE ACKNOWLEDGED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,129,0)="  ICA  INBOUND RXCHANGE ERROR ACKNOWLEDGED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,130,0)="  IEA  INBOUND ERROR ACKNOWLEDGED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,131,0)="  IRA  INBOUND RXRENEWAL ERROR ACKNOWLEDGED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,132,0)="  RXA  RXRENEWAL RESPONSE ACKNOWLEDGED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,134,0)="The following message will be displayed if the user now tries to acknowledge"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,135,0)="an eRx record twice:  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,137,0)="   Record already acknowledged!"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,138,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,139,0)="   Type <Enter> to continue or '^' to exit: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,141,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,142,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,143,0)="Added the line of code below at CANACK+7^PSOERXU5:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,145,0)=" I "",CAA,CXA,ICA,IEA,IRA,RXA,""[ERXSTAT W !!,""Record already acknowledged!"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,146,0)=" ,!,$C(7) D DIRE^PSOERXX1 Q"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,147,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,148,0)="5. INC19287772 - HAC VistA eRx 4.0 sorting issue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,150,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,151,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,152,0)="Meds-by-Mail (MbM) reported that the SO (SORT ENTRIES) action did not work"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,153,0)="after selecting a patient and trying to sort by drug name. After selecting to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,154,0)="sort by drug name the software lost previous patient selection and would "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,155,0)="display all patients on the list."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,156,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,157,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,158,0)="-------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,159,0)="Changed the software to preserve the previously selected patient after the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,160,0)="user selects to sort the patient's records by a different sort criteria (e.g.,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,161,0)="drug name)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,162,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,163,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,164,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,165,0)="Added the line of code below at SORT+10^PSOERX:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,166,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,167,0)="   I $D(SRCH) D EN(.SRCH,STYP,1) Q"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,168,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,169,0)="6. INC19647182 - Refill 6 shows as Partial in ECME log"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,171,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,172,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,173,0)="The Marion VA Medical Center (IL) reported that entries in the ECME Log "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,174,0)="related to Refill #6 displayed in Patient Prescription Processing [PSO LM"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,175,0)="BACKDOOR ORDERS] option wrongly showed as 'PARTIAL' fills (Rx Ref column)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,177,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,178,0)="------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,179,0)="Correct the display of the entry for Refill #6 to show as 'REFILL #6' instead"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,180,0)="of 'PARTIAL' in the under the Rx Ref column in the ECME Log."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,181,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,182,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,183,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,184,0)="Move the code for the Output Transform for the RX REFERENCE field (#.04) in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,185,0)="the ACTIVITY LOG (#52.3) sub-file in the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,186,0)="ALFILNUM^PSOUTLA and included an exception for ECME entries to not interpret"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,187,0)="value 6 as a PARTIAL fill."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,188,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,189,0)="7. INC20086630 - Pharmacists are blocked from editing conjunction and duration"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,190,0)="                 prompts for complex orders on eRx holding queue screen"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,191,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,192,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,193,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,194,0)="There is no functionality in the eRx Holding Queue (Complete Orders from eRx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,195,0)="PSO ERX FINISH]) to allow the user to create a complex order dosage. This "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,196,0)="creates a problem particular for processing Controlled Substance (CS) Complex"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,197,0)="eRx prescriptions because they cannot be edited on the Pharmacy Backdoor"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,198,0)="Pending Queue or even after they become an Active prescription because of the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,199,0)="restrictions for editing CS prescription. The receiving of CS eRx prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,200,0)="have been recently enabled by PSO*7*617, which did not include this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,201,0)="functionality. Furthermore, when entering the dosage information for an eRx in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,202,0)="the eRx Holding queue the user is not automatically presented with a default"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,203,0)="value for the ROUTE field. This requires the pharmacist to always type and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,204,0)="chose the appropriate medication route for the dispense drug selected which"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,205,0)="may lead to a mistake that could be easily mitigated by the addition of a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,206,0)="default value."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,207,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,208,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,209,0)="-------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,210,0)="This patch adds the ability for the user to create a Complex dosage for any"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,211,0)="prescription in the eRx Holding Queue option [PSO ERX FINISH]. When entering"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,212,0)="a dosage information the users will be prompt with two new fields: LIMITED "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,213,0)="DURATION and CONJUNCTION after the Schedule Prompt:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,214,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,215,0)="   ..."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,216,0)="   Schedule: QD// "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,217,0)="   Now searching ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE (#51.1) file..."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,218,0)="       QD  EVERY DAY"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,219,0)="            ...OK? Yes//   (Yes)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,220,0)="   LIMITED DURATION (IN DAYS, HOURS OR MINUTES): 10 (DAYS)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,221,0)="   CONJUNCTION: THEN"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,222,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,223,0)="   There are 2 Available Dosage(s):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,224,0)="       1. 15MG"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,225,0)="       2. 30MG"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,226,0)="   ..."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,227,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,228,0)="Select from list of Available Dosages (1-1), Enter Free Text Dose"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,229,0)="or Enter a Question Mark (?) to view list: 7.5//  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,230,0)="An addition functionality was added to provide a default value for the ROUTE"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,231,0)="prompt to assist the user in selecting the appropriate medication route for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,232,0)="the medication on the prescription while reducing the chance for "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,233,0)="administration errors by the patient."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,234,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,235,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,236,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,237,0)="Complex Order: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,238,0)="   The routine PSOERXD2 was changed to add two new fields: LIMITED DURATION"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,239,0)="   (line tag DUR) and CONJUNCTION (line tag CON). Data dictionary fields"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,240,0)="   already existed to accommodate complex dosages so no new DD fields were"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,241,0)="   necessary to be created."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,242,0)="Default Med Route:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,243,0)="   A new function called DEFROUTE that returns a default medication route for "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,244,0)="   an specific Orderable Item was added to the routine PSOERXUT and a call to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,245,0)="   this function was added to RTE2^PSOERXD2. If the function returns a value"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,246,0)="   and there is no previous value entered for the ROUTE the returned value is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,247,0)="   used as the default value for the ROUTE field."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,248,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,249,0)="8. INC20420672 - Audit Log (AU) option in eRx holding queue fails to capture"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,250,0)="                 original eRx SIG"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,251,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,252,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,253,0)="Meds-by-Mail (MbM) reported that the AU (Audit Log) action did not show the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,254,0)="eRx value for the SIG field after the SH (Show/Hide eRx Value) action was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,255,0)="selected."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,257,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,258,0)="------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,259,0)="The Audit Log functionality introduced by the patch PSO*7*617 did not take"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,260,0)="into account that after the patch PSO*7*581 was released to upgrade the NCPDP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,261,0)="version from 10.6 to 2017 the SIG was stored in a different field. The code"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,262,0)="was changed to first check the NCPDP version for the record and then retrieve"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,263,0)="the eRx SIG information from the correct field."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,264,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,265,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,266,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,267,0)="For eRx records with NCPDP version 10.6 (received before PSO*7*581) the eRx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,268,0)="SIG is stored in the DIRECTIONS field (#7) in the ERX HOLDING QUEUE file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,269,0)="(#52.49). For eRx records with NCPDP version 2017 (received after PSO*7*581)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,270,0)="the eRx SIG is stored in the SIG TEXT field (#8) within the 2017 MEDICATIONS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,271,0)="sub-file (#52.49311) in the ERX HOLDING QUEUE file (#52.49). A new API "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,272,0)="$$ERXSIG was added to the PSOERXUT routine to return the eRx SIG. It will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,273,0)="check whether the eRx record is NCPDP version 2017 by checking the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,274,0)="field SCRIPT VERSION NUMBER (#312.1). If so, it will retrieve the value from"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,275,0)="the SIG TEXT field (#8) otherwise it will retrieve it from the DIRECTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,276,0)="field (#7). Then, the routine PSOERXAU was changed to use this new API "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,277,0)="instead of retrieving it from the DIRECTIONS field (#7)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,278,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,279,0)="9. INC20842304 - EPCS software detox# validation capability fails"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,280,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,281,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,282,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,283,0)="Central Texas VAMC reported a problem when trying to validate the provider"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,284,0)="for an eRx prescription for BUPRENORPHINE (Detox Drug). Although the VistA "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,285,0)="provider had a valid DETOX # on file (e.g., VX1234567) the user got the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,286,0)="message below:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,287,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,288,0)="  VistA Provider XXXXX,XXXXXXXX X does not have a valid DETOX #."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,289,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,290,0)="It was determined that the software was checking for ""X"" as the first letter"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,291,0)="on the DETOX # in order to consider it valid, which is incorrect. This issue"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,292,0)="affected also other actions for internal VA outpatient prescriptions. If the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,293,0)="user tried copy or renew a VA prescription for BUPRENORPHINE and the VA"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,294,0)="Provider did not have a Detox # that started with an ""X""."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,295,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,296,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,297,0)="------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,298,0)="The DETOX # validation code was changed to remove the requirement for the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,299,0)="first letter to be an ""X"". It will now only look for 2 letters followed by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,300,0)="a 7-digit number."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,301,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,302,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,303,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,304,0)="The validation code at PRVDETOX+4^PSOUTIL, PRDRVAL+43^PSOERXUT and "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,305,0)="PRDRVAL+94^PSOERXUT were changed from ...?1""X""1A7N... to ...?2A7N..."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,306,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,307,0)="10.INC20591567 - RxRenewalRequest messages are blocked at hub due to missing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,308,0)="                 Pharmacy Data"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,309,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,310,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,311,0)="Meds-by-Mail (MbM) reported that outbound Renewal or Change Request messages"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,312,0)="were being dropped by the eRx Hub because they were missing the Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,313,0)="address and/or the communication number. A sample XML message from the Hub"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,314,0)="confirmed that the Pharmacy address was missing, as seen below:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,315,0)="       ..."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,316,0)="      <Pharmacy>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,317,0)="        <Identification>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,318,0)="          <NCPDPID>5204437</NCPDPID>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,319,0)="         <NPI>1538421110</NPI>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,320,0)="        </Identification>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,321,0)="        <BusinessName>MEDS BY MAIL CHAMPVA</BusinessName>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,322,0)="        <Address>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,323,0)="          <CountryCode>US</CountryCode>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,324,0)="        </Address>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,325,0)="                     <<< <CommunicationNumbers> segment was missing here"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,326,0)="      </Pharmacy>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,327,0)="     ..."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,328,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,329,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,330,0)="------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,331,0)="When the new NCPDP version (2017) was implemented by patch PSO*7*581 it did"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,332,0)="not keep existing 'failsafe's' mechanism from 10.6 version at the time the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,333,0)="user requested a Change or Renewal Request to the outside provider. One of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,334,0)="them retrieved address information from the OUTPATIENT SITE file (#59) in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,335,0)="case the ERX EXTERNAL PHARMACY file (#52.47) record did not contain a valid"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,336,0)="address. The other one was to send ""0000000000"" as a Primary Telefone number"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,337,0)="if one could not be found for the pharmacy. This patch adds these"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,338,0)="'failsafe's' for NCPDP v2017 eRx records."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,339,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,340,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,341,0)="---------------------  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,342,0)="Address"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,343,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,344,0)="New code was added at OPHARM+31^PSOERXOD to check if the ADDRESS LINE 1 field"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,345,0)="in the ERX EXTERNAL PHARMACY file (#52.47) for the eRx record being renewed/"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,346,0)="changed was blank. If so, it will retrieve the complete address from the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,347,0)="corresponding pharmacy record in the OUTPATIENT SITE file (#59)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,348,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,349,0)="Communication Number"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,350,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,351,0)="New code was added at OCOMM+3^PSOERXOU to make sure that the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,352,0)="<CommunicationNubmers> XML segment is always included in the outbound eRx "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,353,0)="Renewal or Change request messages. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,354,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,355,0)="11.INC20591582 - RxRenewalRequest blocked at VA routing hub due to missing"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,356,0)="                 Observation "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,357,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,358,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,359,0)="Meds-by-Mail (MbM) reported that outbound Renewal or Change Request messages"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,360,0)="were being dropped by the eRx Hub because the Observation/Measurement segment"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,361,0)="did not contain the required <ObservationDate> field. A sample XML message"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,362,0)="from the Hub confirmed that the problem, as seen below:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,363,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,364,0)="      <Observation>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,365,0)="        <Measurement>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,366,0)="          <VitalSign>29463-7</VitalSign>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,367,0)="          <LOINCVersion>2.42</LOINCVersion>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,368,0)="          <Value>178.4</Value>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,369,0)="          <UnitOfMeasure>[lb_av]</UnitOfMeasure>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,370,0)="          <UCUMVersion>1.8.2</UCUMVersion>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,371,0)="                             <<< <ObservationDate> segment was missing here"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,372,0)="        </Measurement>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,373,0)="      </Observation>"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,374,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,375,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,376,0)="------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,377,0)="For an unknown reason some incoming Observation/Measurement records saved to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,378,0)="the 2017 OBSERVATION sub-file (#52.49306) in the ERX HOLDING QUEUE file"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,379,0)="(#52.49) failed to save a valid date in the OBSERVATION DATE field (#6). Since"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,380,0)="it cannot be determined the cause of the incomplete Observation/Measurement"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,381,0)="information stored it was decided to not include such information in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,382,0)="Change or Renewal request messages if the Observation Date value is not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,383,0)="populated."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,384,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,385,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,386,0)="---------------------  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,387,0)="New code was added at OBSERVE+2^PSOERXOB to make sure that the in order for"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,388,0)="and Observation/Measurement to be included in the outbound eRx Renewal or "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,389,0)="Change request it must have a valid Observation Date value, otherwise it is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,390,0)="skipped. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,391,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,392,0)="12.INC20730418 - Non-Controlled Substance eRx was blocked from being edited by"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,393,0)="                 Electronic Prescribing for Controlled Substance mechanism"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,394,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,395,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,396,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,397,0)="Meds-by-Mail (MbM) reported that the users were unable to edit a Digitally"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,398,0)="Signed eRx Pending Order record even if the drug selected for the prescription"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,399,0)="is not marked as a Controlled Substance (non-CS). When the CS eRx Project was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,400,0)="released with patch PSO*7*617 it included functionality to prevent any"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,401,0)="field in a CS eRx Pending Order record from being edited before the order was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,402,0)="finished. The reason is because DEA (Drug Enforcement Agency) requires all"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,403,0)="Pharmacy software applications to audit all edits to a CS prescription record"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,404,0)="and the Pending Queue edits are not audited. However, a few incoming Digitally"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,405,0)="Signed eRx records will be matched with a dispense drug that is not considered"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,406,0)="to be a Controlled Substance by the VA and in such cases the edit should be "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,407,0)="permitted."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,408,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,409,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,410,0)="------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,411,0)="Instead of checking whether the eRx record was digitally signed or not to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,412,0)="determine if the eRx Pending Order record can be edited or not the software"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,413,0)="will now check if the dispense drug in the Pending Order is marked as a CS or"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,414,0)="non-CS. If the drug is not marked as CS the editing of the eRx Pending Order"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,415,0)="record will be allowed. In addition, the messages ""Processing Digitally"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,416,0)="Signed eRx Order"" displayed at the top of the Pending eRx as well as the DEA"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,417,0)="note (see below) at the end of the order will not display the dispense drug in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,418,0)="the Pending Order is not marked as CS."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,419,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,420,0)="   This prescription meets the requirements of the Drug Enforcement "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,421,0)="   Administration (DEA) electronic prescribing for controlled substances rules"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,422,0)="   (21 CFR Parts 1300, 1304, 1306, & 1311)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,423,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,424,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,425,0)="---------------------  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,426,0)="The code at CSERX+1^PSOORNEW was changed from checking whether the CONTROLLED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,427,0)="SUBSTANCE INDICATOR field (#95.1) in the ERX HOLDING QUEUE file (#52.49) was"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,428,0)="set to check if the dispense drug associated with the Pending order is marked"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,429,0)="as CS by calling the local $$CSDRG API. In addition, the line tag DERX1+66 in"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,430,0)="the PSOERXU1 routine was changed to add a check if the dispense drug is marked"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,431,0)="as CS before setting the variable PKIE with the message that the eRx was "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,432,0)="digitally signed. And the code at PST+48 in the routine PSOORFI1 was also"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,433,0)="modified not display the DEA message above unless the drug is marked as CS."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,434,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,435,0)="13.INC21240944 - received eRX type CS for non-CS drug"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,436,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,437,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,438,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,439,0)="West Palm Beach VA Medical Center (FL) reported that the users were unable to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,440,0)="accept a Digitally Signed eRx Pending Order record even if the drug selected"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,441,0)="for the prescription is not marked as a Controlled Substance (non-CS). When"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,442,0)="the CS eRx Project was released with patch PSO*7*617 it assumed that a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,443,0)="digitally signed order would certainly translate into a CS VistA prescription."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,444,0)="However, in some cases, digitally signed prescription are for medications not"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,445,0)="considered by the VA to be controlled substance. A good example is GABAPENTIN"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,446,0)="medication, which in some states is classified as a controlled substance but"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,447,0)="not by the Drug Enforcement Agency (DEA). So, a prescriber in such states will"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,448,0)="digitally sign prescriptions before transmitting prescriptions for this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,449,0)="medication to the VA however the VA will not process such eRx prescriptions as"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,450,0)="controlled substances. Therefore it will not require that the VistA provider"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,451,0)="assigned to the eRx prescription has a valid DEA# on file."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,452,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,453,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,454,0)="------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,455,0)="Instead of checking whether the eRx record was digitally signed or not to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,456,0)="determine if the eRx can be accepted the software will now check if the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,457,0)="dispense drug associated with the eRx order is marked as a CS or non-CS."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,458,0)="If the drug is not marked as CS the accepting of the eRx order will be "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,459,0)="permitted even though the provider does not have a valid DEA# on file. A"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,460,0)="warning message will still be displayed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,461,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,462,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,463,0)="---------------------  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,464,0)="The code at PRDRVAL+49^PSOERXUT was changed to check solely whether the VistA"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,465,0)="drug selected for the prescription is marked as CS or not. If not marked as CS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,466,0)="and the Accept functionality will only warn the user about not assigning a CS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,467,0)="drug to a digitally signed order but it will not block them from proceeding."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,468,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,469,0)="14.INC22031884 - eRx pending order screen does not display original"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,470,0)="                 physician's instruction and relevant drug dose strength"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,471,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,472,0)="Meds-by-Mail (MbM) reported that the users were unable to view the eRx SIG"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,473,0)="in the ""Instructions"" field (above the VistA SIG) while processing a pending"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,474,0)="order. Furthermore, they requested that the eRx Drug is also displayed in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,475,0)="line above the ""Instructions"" field. This change would only impact eRx pending"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,476,0)="orders."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,477,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,478,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,479,0)="------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,480,0)="In order to address this issue the software was changed to save the eRx SIG"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,481,0)="in the PROVIDER COMMENTS field (#9) in the PENDING ORDERS file (#52.41) when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,482,0)="the record is crated after the eRx is accepted. In Addition, when displaying"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,483,0)="the ""Instructions"" field for eRx pending order the field will now be "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,484,0)="displayed as ""eRx Instructions"" and the a new field called ""eRx Drug"" will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,485,0)="added above this ""eRx Instructions"" field and it will display the original"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,486,0)="eRx drug name that was sent it by the outside provider software."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,487,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,488,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,489,0)="---------------------  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,490,0)="Replaced the code at ADD+67^PSOERX1F to use the eRx SIG information in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,491,0)="field mentioned above. Additionally, changed the routines PSOORFI1 (PST+5)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,492,0)="and PSOORNEW (PT+4) to add the word ""eRx"" in front of ""Instructions"" field"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,493,0)="for eRx originated Pending orders. Also, added a line above for such orders"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",553,1,494,0)="to display the actual eRx Drug sent in by the outside prescriber."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",554,0)="710 SEQ #580^3230201.160328^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,0)="683 SEQ #581^3230201.170907^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,0)="^^42^42^3230201"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,1,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,2,0)="==========================================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,4,0)="1.      INC21813625 - OUTPATIENT PHARMACY SPEED RENEW OF RX STATUS "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,5,0)="DISCONTINUED BY PROVIDER"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,7,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,8,0)="   -------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,9,0)="Speed renew allows an outpatient prescription to be renewed for "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,10,0)="prescriptions with a status of DISCONTINUED BY PROVIDER.  Renewing a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,11,0)="prescription with this status is not allowed when renewing for a single "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,12,0)="RX selected from the Medication Profile or when doing Barcode Batch "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,13,0)="Prescription Entry."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,15,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,16,0)="   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,17,0)="Routine PSORENW4 is modified to check if any RXs selected "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,18,0)="for speed renew are discontinued.  If any are they are removed from list "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,19,0)="of RXs to renew and the message 'Cannot renew Rx # #######, Rx is in "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,20,0)="DISCONTINUED BY PROVIDER status.' is displayed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,22,0)="   Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,23,0)="   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,24,0)=" ;PSO 683 skip discontinued by provider RXs"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,25,0)=" S (ORD,PSOLCNT)=0"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,26,0)=" I $G(LST)]"""" D"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,27,0)=" . ; count remaining orders in LST"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,28,0)=" . F ORD=1:1:$L(LST,"","")-1 D"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,29,0)=" .. Q:$P(LST,"","",ORD)'>0"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,30,0)=" .. S PSOLCNT=PSOLCNT+1,ORN=$P(LST,"","",ORD)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,31,0)=" .. I (+PSOLST(ORN)=52&(^PSRX($P(PSOLST(ORN),U,2),""STA"")=14)) D"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,32,0)=" ... S "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,33,0)="PSOSKIP($P(PSOLST(ORN),U,2))="""",$P(LST,"","",ORD)=0,PSOLCNT=PSOLCNT-1  ; "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,34,0)="order removed from LST"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,35,0)=" .I $O(PSOSKIP(0)) D"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,36,0)=" .. W !"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,37,0)=" .. S ORD=0 F  S ORD=$O(PSOSKIP(ORD)) Q:'ORD  D"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,38,0)=" ... S PSOSTA=$$GET1^DIQ(52,ORD,100)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,39,0)=" ... W $C(7),!,""  Cannot renew Rx # ""_$$GET1^DIQ(52,ORD,.01)_"", Rx is in "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,40,0)="""_PSOSTA_"" status."""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,41,0)=" .. D PAUSE^VALM1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",555,1,42,0)=" ;END PSO 683"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,0)="699 SEQ #582^3230213.131636^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,0)="^^37^37^3230213"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,1,0)="1. INC22631577 - ISSUES REFILLING PRESCRIPTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,4,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,5,0)="   -------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,6,0)="When a prescription is edited before it is refilled in Patient "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,7,0)="Prescription Processing, the label will print for the previous fill.  The "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,8,0)="Activity Log incorrectly displays that the previous fill was sent to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,9,0)="X-INTERFACE and the Label Log incorrectly displays the previous fill was "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,10,0)="printed instead of the fill entered. The ECME Log correctly shows the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,11,0)="fill. If the prescription drug is a controlled substance, the refill "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,12,0)="cannot be released from the vault until the label is reprinted.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,15,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,16,0)="   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,17,0)="The issue is due to the variable RXFL not getting updated with the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,18,0)="current fill number in routine PSOR52."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,20,0)="   Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,21,0)="   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,22,0)="At line FINISH+36^SPOR52, the logic is modified to not jump to FINISHX "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,23,0)="but to only execute the next two lines that prevent a duplicate label "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,24,0)="from being printed and allowing RXFL to be reset with the current fill "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,25,0)="number."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,27,0)="Line FINISH+36^SPOR52 is changed from:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,28,0)="   I PSODUP G FINISHX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,29,0)="To:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,30,0)="   I 'PSODUP D"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,31,0)="And the next two lines are added into the Do dot structure:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,33,0)="   I 'PSODUP D ;p699"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,34,0)="    . I $L(PSORX(""PSOL"",PSOX2))+$L(PSOX(""IRXN""))<220 S    "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,35,0)="    PSORX(""PSOL"",PSOX2)=PSORX(""PSOL"",PSOX2)_PSOX(""IRXN"")_"","""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,36,0)="    . E S PSORX(""PSOL"",PSOX2+1)=PSOX(""IRXN"")_"","""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",556,1,37,0)="   S RXFL(PSOX(""IRXN""))=PSOX(""NUMBER"")"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,0)="711 SEQ #583^3230213.131705^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,0)="^^35^35^3230213"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,3,0)="1) INC24967678 - This patch will address the issue described in "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,4,0)="ServiceNow Incident INC22865486, regarding the <UNDEFINED>ACLOG+5^PSON52 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,5,0)="error when creating a new order in the COMPLETE ORDERS FROM OERR "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,6,0)="[PSO LMOE FINISH] option.  In addition, this patch will resolve the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,7,0)="incorrect RX reference in the remarks field."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,9,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,10,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,11,0)="If a patient has an active titration RX and a pending controlled "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,12,0)="substance RX from CPRS, and then a new order is placed for the patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,13,0)="via COMPLETE ORDERS FROM OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] option, a hard error can"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,14,0)="occur.  After placing the new order and accepting, a hard error occurs:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,15,0)="<UNDEFINED>ACLOG+5^PSON52 *PSOCSP(""NAME""). In addition, the remarks field"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,16,0)="for new order incorrectly refers to the CPRS controlled substance RX as"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,17,0)="being edited."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,19,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,20,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,21,0)="It was discovered that when the user selects the ""CS"" controlled "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,22,0)="substances as the primary filter when finishing a patient's"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,23,0)="orders via COMPLETE ORDERS FROM OERR [PSO LMOE FINISH] option,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,24,0)="the logic pulls the data for any pending controlled substances for the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,25,0)="patient selected. This causes the data to be set to the pending "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,26,0)="controlled substance, even if the pharmacist chooses to place a new "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,27,0)="order. Most of the variables are newed in the logic except for the OR0"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,28,0)="variable which is not cleared out when the a new order is placed. This is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,29,0)="the reason for the <UNDEFINED>ACLOG+5^PSON52 *PSOCSP(""NAME"") error and why"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,30,0)="the remarks contain the controlled substance data."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,32,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,33,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,34,0)="The fix for this issue is to new the OR0 variable in the AGAIN tag of "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",557,1,35,0)="PSONEW."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,0)="682 SEQ #584^3230228.120738^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,0)="^^48^48^3230228"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,1,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,2,0)="==========================================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,4,0)="1.      INC21921117 - INBOUND ERX PENDING ORDER SELECTING WRONG PROVIDER"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,6,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,7,0)="   -------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,8,0)="Once an eRX order is validated and moved to the PENDING OUTPATIENT ORDERS "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,9,0)="FILE (#52.41), in the finishing process, if a validated provider has an "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,10,0)="inactive account in a local VistA system, VistA is picking the last "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,11,0)="provider used on a previously finished prescription.  This problem is not "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,12,0)="isolated to eRX processing.  The same issue occurs if any pending "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,13,0)="outpatient order has a provider that is inactive or no longer authorized "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,14,0)="to write orders when it is finished in Patient Prescription Processing "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,15,0)="[PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS].  If a new order is entered in Patient "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,16,0)="Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] prior to processing the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,17,0)="pending order that is for an inactive or invalid provider during the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,18,0)="finishing process a message displays indicating the provider is inactive "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,19,0)="or invalid and prompts for a new provider and populates the provider "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,20,0)="prompt with the provider from the new order.  The prompt should default "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,21,0)="to the provider associated with the PENDING OUTPATIENT ORDERS FILE "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,22,0)="(#52.41)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,24,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,25,0)="   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,26,0)="Routine PSODIR is modified to use the provider from the PENDING "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,27,0)="OUTPATIENT ORDERS FILE (#52.41) as the default for the provider prompt "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,28,0)="and not allow it to be overwritten."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,31,0)="   Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,32,0)="   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,33,0)="There is already code to set the default to the provider from the PENDING "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,34,0)="OUTPATIENT ORDERS FILE (#52.41) but when PSORX(""PROVIDER NAME"") exists it "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,35,0)="overwrites the default.  PSORX(""PROVIDER NAME"") is set to the provider "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,36,0)="selected during entering a new order for defaulting when entering "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,37,0)="multiple orders for the same patient."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,39,0)="The default is set from the PENDING OUTPATIENT ORDERS FILE (#52.41) "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,40,0)="PROVIDER field (#5) at line PROVEN+1^PSODIR: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,41,0)="DIC(""B"")=$P(^VA(200,$P($G(OR0),""^"",5),0),""^"") and is not changed with "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,42,0)="this patch.  At line PROVEN+9^PSODIR, the default, DIC(""B""), is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,43,0)="overwritten by PSORX(""PROVIDER NAME"") if it exists: S:$G(PSORX(""PROVIDER "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,44,0)="NAME""))]"""" DIC(""B"")=PSORX(""PROVIDER NAME""), this line is changed to:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,45,0)="S DIC(""B"")=$S($G(DIC(""B""))]"""":DIC(""B""),1:$G(PSORX(""PROVIDER NAME"")))"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,46,0)="This change allows the default from the PENDING OUTPATIENT ORDERS FILE "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,47,0)="(#52.41) to be used while not affecting other processing that also uses "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",558,1,48,0)="PROVEN^PSODIR for prompting for the provider."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,0)="689 SEQ #585^3230313.1528^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,0)="^^91^91^3230313"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,3,0)="eRx - Requesting the formulary status of VistA drugs display when "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,4,0)="matching them"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,6,0)="Associated ticket(s):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,7,0)="====================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,9,0)="1.      INC22708310 eRx - Requesting the formulary status of VistA drugs "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,10,0)="display when matching them"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,12,0)="Associated NSR(s):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,13,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,14,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,16,0)="Participating Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,17,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,18,0)="TBD"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,21,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,22,0)="==========================================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,24,0)="1.      INC22708310 eRx - Requesting the formulary status of VistA drugs "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,25,0)="display when matching them"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,28,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,29,0)="   -------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,30,0)="Fayetteville VA Medical Center (AR) s requesting non-Formulary identifier "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,31,0)="to show after auto drug match and a previous manual validation. This "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,32,0)="could be a patient safety issue and is a cost issue. Non-formulary drugs "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,33,0)="are slipping through that probably should not. This would help efficiency "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,34,0)="while processing prescriptions from the inbound eRX queue."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,36,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,37,0)="   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,38,0)="In option Complete Orders from eRx [PSO ERX FINISH], on the second screen "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,39,0)="of the eRx Holding Queue Display and the second screen of PSO ERX DRUG "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,40,0)="VALIDATION, the non-Formulary identifier (***N/F***) is added to the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,41,0)="right of the Vista Drug. In addition, when validating the drug/sig, the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,42,0)="non-Formulary identifier (***N/F***) will be added in two places; to the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,43,0)="right of the drug on the prompts 'Current Vista Drug:' and 'You have "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,44,0)="selected:'. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,46,0)="   Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,47,0)="   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,48,0)="Routine PSOERX1G is modified to display the non-Formulary identifier "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,49,0)="(***N/F***) on line DISPRX+4^PSOERX1G"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,51,0)="   Before patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,52,0)=" .S LINE=LINE+1 D SET^VALM10(LINE,""Vista Drug""_$S(DRMANVAL:""[v]"",1:"""")_"": "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,53,0)="""_VADRG_"" ""_$P($$VADRSCH^PSOERXUT(VADRGIEN),""^"",3))"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,54,0)="   After patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,55,0)="  .S PSONF="""" I $G(VADRGIEN) S "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,56,0)="PSONF=$S($P(^PSDRUG(VADRGIEN,0),""^"",9):""***(N/F)***"",1:"""") ;p689"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,57,0)=" .S LINE=LINE+1 D SET^VALM10(LINE,""Vista Drug""_$S(DRMANVAL:""[v]"",1:"""")_"": "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,58,0)="""_VADRG_"" ""_$P($$VADRSCH^PSOERXUT(VADRGIEN),""^"",3)_PSONF)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,60,0)="Routine PSOERXD1 is modified to display the non-Formulary identifier "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,61,0)="(***N/F***) on line INIT+109^PSOERXD1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,63,0)="   Before the patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,64,0)=" S LINE=LINE+1 D SET^VALM10(LINE,"" (1) Vista Drug: ""_VADRG_""    "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,65,0)="""_$P($$VADRSCH^PSOERXUT(VADRGIEN),""^"",3))"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,66,0)="   After the patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,67,0)=" S PSONF="""" I $G(VADRGIEN) S "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,68,0)="PSONF=$S($P(^PSDRUG(VADRGIEN,0),""^"",9):""***(N/F)***"",1:"""") ;p689"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,69,0)=" S LINE=LINE+1 D SET^VALM10(LINE,"" (1) Vista Drug: ""_VADRG_"" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,70,0)="""_$P($$VADRSCH^PSOERXUT(VADRGIEN),""^"",3)_PSONF)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,72,0)="Routine PSOERXD2 is modified to display the non-Formulary identifier "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,73,0)="(***N/F***) on lines VDRG1+9^PSOERXD2 & VDRG1+23^PSOERXD2. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,75,0)="VDRG1+9^PSOERXD2 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,76,0)="   Before the patch:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,77,0)="I VAODRG W !,""Current Vista Drug: ""_$$GET1^DIQ(50,VAODRG,.01,""E"")_""    "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,78,0)="""_$P($$VADRSCH^PSOERXUT(VAODRG),""^"",3)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,79,0)="   After the patch"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,80,0)="I VAODRG W !,""Current Vista Drug: ""_$$GET1^DIQ(50,VAODRG,.01,""E"")_"" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,81,0)="""_$P($$VADRSCH^PSOERXUT(VAODRG),""^"",3)_$S($P(^PSDRUG(VAODRG,0),""^"",9):"" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,82,0)="   ***(N/F)***"",1:"""")"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,84,0)="VDRG1+23^PSOERXD2"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,85,0)="   Before the patch:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,86,0)="W !!,""You have selected: ""_$P(Y,U,2),!,""Would you like to use this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,87,0)="drug/supply?"" S DIR(0)=""YO"" D ^DIR K DIR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,88,0)="   After the patch:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,89,0)="W !!,""You have selected: ""_$P(Y,U,2)_ )_$S($P(^PSDRUG(+Y,0),""^"",9):"" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,90,0)="***(N/F)***"",1:""""),!,""Would you like to use this "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",559,1,91,0)="drug/supply?"" S DIR(0)=""YO"" D ^DIR K DIR"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,0)="705 SEQ #586^3230323.12163^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,0)="^^36^36^3230323"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,2,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,4,0)="1) INC23385693 - Controlled substance eRx prescriptions can be finished "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,5,0)="in VistA on a day after the authorizing provider's DEA Number expires as "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,6,0)="long as the Issue/Written Date of the eRX is before or equal to the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,7,0)="provider's DEA expiration date. This is by design. However, when this "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,8,0)="happens, it causes field #10 DEA NUMBER to be null in the Order DEA "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,9,0)="Archive file (#101.52). This will have side effects in functionality that "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,10,0)="use this field. In particular, this affects SPMP functionality. When file "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,11,0)="101.52 field 10 is null, this may cause the Vista SPMP transmissions to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,12,0)="submit an incorrect DEA Number for the provider."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,15,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,16,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,17,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,20,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,21,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,22,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,23,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,24,0)="1) INC23385693 - It was discovered that when a provider's DEA number "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,25,0)="expires on the same date as the issue/written date, field #10 DEA NUMBER"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,26,0)="can be null in the Order DEA Archive file (#101.52).  When this happens,"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,27,0)="the SPMP transmission should still send the provider's DEA number, but"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,28,0)="instead it will send either null or the Facility DEA# which is incorrect."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,31,0)="Resolution 1:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,32,0)="-------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,33,0)="To fix the issue for the SPMP transmission, the routine PSOASAP0 tag "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,34,0)="PRE02 will be modified to pass the issue/written date to the $$DEA^XUSER"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,35,0)="call, so the provider's DEA number will be sent even though it expires on"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",560,1,36,0)="the same day as the RX issue/written date."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,0)="716 SEQ #587^3230323.122059^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,0)="^^24^24^3230323"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,1,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,3,0)="1. INC25627893 - Enhanced Order Checks cannot be performed for "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,4,0)="Orderable Item: XXXXXXXXXX Reason(s): No Dispense Drug found."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,7,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,8,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,9,0)="Outpatient prescription for an orderable item that has no active drugs "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,10,0)="associated with it is not displaying the order check warning:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,11,0)="Enhanced Order Checks cannot be performed for Orderable Item: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,12,0)="XXXXXXXXXXXX Reason(s): No Dispense Drug found."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,14,0)="The order check warning is displayed for an inpatient order for the same "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,15,0)="Orderable Item."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,17,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,18,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,19,0)="NVATST^PSODDPRE is modified to initialize variable PSONVTFL to 0 instead "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,20,0)="of 1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,22,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,23,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",561,1,24,0)="NVATST+2^PSODDPRE is changed from S PSONVTFL=1 to S PSONVTFL=0"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,0)="696 SEQ #588^3230330.114745^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,0)="^^68^68^3230330"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,3,0)="1) INC19851999 - When the Scheduled SPMP Data Export is run [PSO SPMP "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,4,0)="SCHEDULED EXPORT], Meds by Mail states are not receiving Zero Reports."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,6,0)="2) INC23242505 -  When using the View/Export Void Prescriptions option "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,7,0)="[PSO SPMP VOID RX VIEW/EXPORT] for Meds by Mail states, the single RX "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,8,0)="void batch was sent to the wrong state. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,11,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,12,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,13,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,16,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,17,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,18,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,19,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,20,0)="1) INC19851999 - This patch will address the issue described in "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,21,0)="ServiceNow, regarding when the Scheduled SPMP Data Export is run [PSO SPMP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,22,0)="SCHEDULED EXPORT], Zero Reports are only being generated to the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,23,0)="dispensing pharmacy's state. Meds by Mail states are not receiving Zero "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,24,0)="Reports."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,26,0)="2) INC23242505 - This patch will address the issue described in "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,27,0)="ServiceNow, regarding the use of the View/Export Void Prescriptions "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,28,0)="option [PSO SPMP VOID RX VIEW/EXPORT] for Meds by Mail states, the single "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,29,0)="RX void batch was sent to the state that is contained in the patient's "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,30,0)="currently active address on profile. If the patient moved or was using a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,31,0)="temporary address after the original batch was sent, the void may go to "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,32,0)="the wrong state."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,33,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,35,0)="Resolution 1:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,36,0)="-------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,37,0)="It was discovered that when the Scheduled SPMP Data Export is run [PSO "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,38,0)="SPMP SCHEDULED EXPORT], Zero Reports are only generated for the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,39,0)="dispensing pharmacy state.  The Meds by Mail states are not receiving "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,40,0)="Zero Reports. This is due to Meds by Mail states not having an Outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,41,0)="Site (File #59) defined, since the medication was not dispensed from the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,42,0)="state.  However, the Outpatient Site is required to pull the DEA# which "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,43,0)="is a required field for the State Prescription Monitoring Program. So a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,44,0)="new state parameter field will be added to the View/Edit SPMP State "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,45,0)="Parameters option [PSO SPMP STATE PARAMETERS] with this patch (File "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,46,0)="#58.41 Field #22). The new state parameter, ""ZERO REPORT DEFAULT "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,47,0)="DIVISION:"", will only display for states that are set to Meds by Mail "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,48,0)="(i.e. Send Export State Parameter = 2  Send to state of Patient "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,49,0)="Delivery). The Meds by Mail states will be able to select a Meds by Mail "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,50,0)="division that points to the appropriate DEA number. Routine PSOSPMSP will "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,51,0)="be modified to add the new state parameter.  Routine PSOSPML0 will have a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,52,0)="new temp global to store all states that had prescriptions either "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,53,0)="dispensed or mailed to them."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,55,0)="Resolution 2:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,56,0)="-------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,57,0)="It was discovered that when the View/Export Void Prescriptions option "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,58,0)="[PSO SPMP VOID RX VIEW/EXPORT] was used for Meds by Mail states, the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,59,0)="single RX void batch was sent to the state that is contained in the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,60,0)="patient's currently active address on profile. If the patient moved or "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,61,0)="was using a temporary address after the original batch was sent, the void "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,62,0)="may go to the wrong state. Logic will be added to the View/Export Void"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,63,0)="Prescriptions option [PSO SPMP VOID RX VIEW/EXPORT] and the Scheduled SPMP"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,64,0)="Data Export option [PSO SPMP SCHEDULED EXPORT] for voids, to check what"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,65,0)="state the original RX was sent and send the void to the same state."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,66,0)="Changes were made to the RXLOOP tag of PSOSPMV routine and the addition "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,67,0)="of the VOIDST tag in the PSOSPMV routine. Changes were also made to the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",562,1,68,0)="GATHER tag of the PSOSPMU1 routine."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,0)="643 SEQ #589^3230425.094413^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,0)="^^44^44^3230425"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,1,0)="This OneVA Enhancement Patch will provide the following enhancements:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,3,0)=" . The OneVA Pharmacy Rx Report [PSO REMOTE RX REPORT] on the Rx "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,4,0)="   (Prescriptions) [PSO RX] menu has been updated to include new "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,5,0)="   fields added to the REMOTE PRESCRIPTION LOG File (#52.09)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,7,0)=" . Dispensing sites will now be able to send a OneVA refill or a OneVA   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,8,0)="   partial fill through the Outpatient Pharmacy Automation Interface  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,9,0)="   (OPAI) to an Automated Dispensing Device (ADD) for dispensing."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,11,0)=" . No changes to the current external interface parameters or setup is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,12,0)="   required. The same parameter setup used for the sending of local   "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,13,0)="   prescriptions to the OPAI will be utilized."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,15,0)=" . New activity log entries have been created to provide an audit trail"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,16,0)="   for OneVA refills and OneVA partial fills sent through the OPAI to an"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,17,0)="   ADD for dispensing. These new entries can be viewed through the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,18,0)="   Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] and View Prescriptions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,19,0)="   [PSO VIEW] options."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,21,0)=" . Enhancements to current activity log entries have been made to document"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,22,0)="   the facility name and station number where the OneVA refill/partial"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,23,0)="   fill was dispensed. These entries can be viewed through the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,24,0)="   Prescription Processing [PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS] and View Prescriptions"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,25,0)="   [PSO VIEW] options."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,27,0)=" . The 'REPRINT' notation printed on the label log when there's no reprint"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,28,0)="   capability for OneVA refill/partial fill. The reprint notation has been"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,29,0)="   removed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,31,0)=" . HL7 Messaging changes were made to retrieve more data when"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,32,0)="   retrieving patient/prescription information from the host facility, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,33,0)="   and to send more dispensing information to the host facility."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,35,0)=" . New fields have been added to the refill/partial sub-files in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,36,0)="   PRESCRIPTION File (#52) and the REMOTE PRESCRIPTION LOG File (#52.09)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,37,0)="   to ensure that the correct entries in the PRESCRIPTION File (#52) and"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,38,0)="   REMOTE PRESCRIPTION LOG File (#52.09) are updated."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,40,0)=" . The device prompt for a OneVA fill will no longer force a selection of "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,41,0)="   a laser label device."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,43,0)="This patch also corrects a typo ""REFIL"" that was introduced by PSO*7*651"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",563,1,44,0)="patch when it modified the ECME activity log."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",564,0)="681^3230425.094705^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,0)="717 SEQ #591^3230501.111711^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,0)="^^143^143^3230501"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,1,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,3,0)="1.      INC25835278 - PRESCRIPTIONS SENT TO SCRIPT PRO AFTER BEING HELD"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,6,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,7,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,8,0)="A prescription was placed on hold in a Vista session separate from the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,9,0)="session where the prescription was finished and before labels were queued "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,10,0)="to print.  The scenario is that multiple prescriptions are entered in "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,11,0)="CPRS and signed.  In Pharmacy Prescription Processing, finish one of the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,12,0)="orders and then, in a second Vista session, place that prescription on "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,13,0)="hold.  Back in the first Vista Session, finish the remaining "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,14,0)="prescriptions and queue the labels. When you go back into Pharmacy "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,15,0)="Prescription Processing and view the Activity Logs, you will notice that "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,16,0)="the prescription on hold was sent to external interface (or Script Pro) "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,17,0)="even though it was on hold."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,19,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,20,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,21,0)="Modify routine PSORXL1 to add the status of hold to the conditions that "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,22,0)="cause the prescription# to be removed from variable PPL that contains a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,23,0)="string of  prescriptions to print."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,25,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,26,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,27,0)="At ECME+8^PSORXL1 ADD PSOSTA=3 TO THE CONDITIONS:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,28,0)=" . . I PSOSTA=12!(PSOSTA=11)!(PSOSTA=3)!((PSOSTA=5)&(ESTAT'="""")) D  ;p717 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,29,0)="add HOLD status"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,31,0)="Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,32,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,33,0)="TBD"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,35,0)="Patch Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,36,0)="------------------- "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,38,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,39,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,40,0)="recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,41,0)="potential disruption to users.  This patch should take less than 5 "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,42,0)="minutes to install. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,45,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,46,0)="1.  Choose the PackMan message containing this build. Then select the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,47,0)="    INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option to load the build."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,49,0)="2.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,50,0)="    select the Installation Menu.  From this menu, "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,52,0)="    A.  Select the Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,53,0)="        option to confirm the integrity of the routines that "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,54,0)="        are in the transport global. When prompted for the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,55,0)="        INSTALL NAME enter the patch or build name (ex. PSO*7.0*717) "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,57,0)="        NOTE: Using <spacebar><enter> will not bring up a "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,58,0)="              Multi-Package build even if it was loaded "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,59,0)="              immediately before this step. It will only "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,60,0)="              bring up the last patch in the build."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,62,0)="   B.  Select the Backup a Transport Global option to create"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,63,0)="       a backup message. You must use this option and specify "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,64,0)="       what to backup; the entire Build or just Routines."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,65,0)="       The backup message can be used to restore the routines"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,66,0)="       and components of the build to the pre-patch condition."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,69,0)="         i.  At the Installation option menu, select Backup "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,70,0)="             a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,71,0)="         ii. At the Select INSTALL NAME prompt, enter your "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,72,0)="             build PSO*7.0*717"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,73,0)="         iii. When prompted for the following, enter ""R"" for "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,74,0)="              Routines or ""B"" for Build."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,76,0)="               Select one of the following:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,78,0)="                      B         Build"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,79,0)="                      R         Routines"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,81,0)="                Enter response: Build"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,83,0)="         iv.  When prompted ""Do you wish to secure your build? "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,84,0)="              NO//"", press <enter> and take the default response "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,85,0)="              of ""NO""."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,86,0)="         v.   When prompted with, ""Send mail to: Last name, First "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,87,0)="              Name"", press <enter> to take default recipient. Add "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,88,0)="              any additional recipients."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,89,0)="         vi.  When prompted with ""Select basket to send to: IN//"", "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,90,0)="              press <enter> and take the default IN mailbox or select "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,91,0)="              a different mailbox."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,92,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,93,0)="    C. You may also elect to use the following options: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,94,0)="         i.  Print Transport Global - This option will allow "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,95,0)="             you to view the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,96,0)="         ii. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,97,0)="             option will allow you to view all changes that will "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,98,0)="             be made when this patch is installed.  It compares "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,99,0)="             all of the components of this patch, such as "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,100,0)="             routines, DDs, templates, etc."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,101,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,102,0)="    D. Select the Install Package(s) option and choose the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,103,0)="       patch to install. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,104,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,105,0)="         i.  If prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,106,0)="             Completion of Install? NO//', answer NO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,108,0)="        ii. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,109,0)="            install? NO//', answer NO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,110,0)="       "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,111,0)="       iii. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,112,0)="            Options, and Protocols? NO//', answer NO"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,113,0)="           "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,115,0)="Back-out/Rollback Strategy:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,116,0)="---------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,117,0)="Back-out will be done only with the concurrence and participation of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,118,0)="development team and appropriate VA site/region personnel. The decision to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,119,0)="back-out or rollback software will be a joint decision between development"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,120,0)="team, VA site/region personnel and other appropriate VA personnel."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,122,0)="Prior to installing an updated KIDS package, the site/region should have"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,123,0)="saved a backup of the build in a mail message using the Backup a"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,124,0)="Transport Global [XPD BACKUP] menu option (this is done at time of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,125,0)="install). The message containing the backed-up build can be loaded with"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,126,0)="the ""Xtract PackMan"" function at the Message Action prompt. The Packman"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,127,0)="function ""INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE"" is then used to install the backed up"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,128,0)="routines onto the VistA System. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,129,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,130,0)="The back-out plan is to restore the build from the backup created."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,131,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,132,0)="No data was modified by this patch installation and, therefore, no "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,133,0)="rollback strategy is required."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,134,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,135,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,136,0)="Validation of Back-out Procedure:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,137,0)="---------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,138,0)="The Back-out Procedure can be verified by printing the first 2 lines of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,139,0)="the routines contained in this patch using the option First Line Routine "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,140,0)="Print [XU FIRST LINE PRINT]. Once the build contained in the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,141,0)="PSO*7.0*717 patch has been backed out, the first two lines of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,142,0)="the routine will no longer contain the designation of this patch in the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",565,1,143,0)="patch list section on line 2."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,0)="715 SEQ #592^3230509.173037^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,0)="^^37^37^3230509"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,1,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,3,0)="1.  INC24578457 - NCPDP CancelRxResponse message communicates incorrect "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,4,0)="medication fill status to e-prescribers"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,6,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,7,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,8,0)="VistA eRx pharmacy software sent CancelRxResponse messages that "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,9,0)="misinformed electronic prescribers about medication fills that did not "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,10,0)="happen.  The message included a last dispense date that was not actually "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,11,0)="dispensed which caused some confusion."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,13,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,14,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,15,0)="Routines PSOERXU6 & PSOERXO1 are modified to send the most recent "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,16,0)="RELEASED DATE/TIME field (#31) of the Prescription file (#52) in the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,17,0)="Current Status Details line of the message that reads 'First Fill: "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,18,0)="##/##/##, Last Fill: ##/##/##, Refills Remaining:11'.  If there is no "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,19,0)="release date it will have spaces after Last Fill."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,22,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,23,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,24,0)="In routine PSOERXU6, at entry point BLDRESP+3 the code is changed to the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,25,0)="following:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,26,0)="; p715 Use last release date instead of last dispense date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,27,0)="S LRDATE=$$RXRLDT^PSOBPSUT(RXIEN),LRDATE=$$FMTE^XLFDT(LRDATE,""2D"")"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,28,0)="S FFILL=$$GET1^DIQ(52,RXIEN,22,""I""),FFILL=$$FMTE^XLFDT(FFILL,""2D"")"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,29,0)="S ACOM=""First Fill:""_FFILL_"", Last Fill:""_$S(LRDATE:LRDATE,1:"" "")_"", "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,30,0)="Refills Remaining:""_REFL "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,32,0)="In routine PSOERXO1, at entry point CANDC+57 the code is changed to the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,33,0)="following:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,34,0)="..; p715 Use last release date instead of last dispense date"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,35,0)="..S LRDATE=$$RXRLDT^PSOBPSUT(RXIEN),LRDATE=$$FMTE^XLFDT(LRDATE,""2D"")"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,36,0)="..S RESPONSE=""First Fill:""_FFILL_"", Last fill:""_$S(LRDATE:LRDATE,1:"" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",566,1,37,0)=""")_"", Refills remaining:""_REFL"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,0)="718 SEQ #593^3230509.173241^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,0)="^^30^30^3230509"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,1,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,3,0)="1.      INC25956349 - INBOUND ERX FOR NON-CONTROLLED SUBSTANCES COMING "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,4,0)="THROUGH AS CONTROLLED"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,6,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,7,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,8,0)="Site is receiving several inbound eRx for non-controlled substance "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,9,0)="medications that are designated as controlled substances in the inbound "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,10,0)="eRx queue.  This is preventing us from processing these orders if the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,11,0)="community prescriber does not submit their DEA number.  The problem is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,12,0)="that the inbound eRX contains a digital signature and the provider does "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,13,0)="not have a DEA# sent in the eRX message and the drug is not a controlled "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,14,0)="drug.  This causes an error to be encountered when processing it in PSO "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,15,0)="ERX FINISH.  The error is 'eRx Provider does not have a valid DEA#.'"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,17,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,18,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,19,0)="Routine PSOERXUT is modified to not return an error when the eRX drug is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,20,0)="not a controlled drug and the provider doesn't have a DEA# and the eRX is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,21,0)="digitally signed."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,23,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,24,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,25,0)="PSOERXUT is modified at line PRDRVAL+58^PSOERXUT to add the condition "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,26,0)="ACTION=-""AC"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,28,0)="Line PRDRVAL+58^PSOERXUT after the code change:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,29,0)=" . I ACTION=""EP""!(ACTION=""VP"")!(ACTION=""AC""),'VACSDRUG D  Q  ;p718 add "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",567,1,30,0)="accept action"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",568,0)="697 SEQ #594^3230601.09294^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",568,1,0)="^^4^4^3230601"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",568,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",568,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",568,1,3,0)="The VistA option View Prescriptions does not display the eRx indicator ""&"""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",568,1,4,0)="if the prescription is an inbound eRx prescription."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",569,0)="673 SEQ #595^3230627.141117^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",569,1,0)="^^5^5^3230627"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",569,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",569,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",569,1,3,0)="The date format printed to the activity log for an edited ISSUE DATE or "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",569,1,4,0)="FILL DATE is printed using the Fileman date format. The date format used "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",569,1,5,0)="should be more consistent to what is already being used by VistA."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",570,0)="545^3230629.170402^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",570,1,0)="^^1^1^3230629"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",570,1,1,0)="See FORUM patch description."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",571,0)="690 SEQ #597^3230706.155202^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",571,1,0)="^^1^1^3230706"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",571,1,1,0)="INC22168250 - PROTOCOL ""PSO LM HIDDEN OTHER #2"" contain duplication ""RR"" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",572,0)="720 SEQ #598^3230721.09492^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",572,1,0)="^^7^7^3230721"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",572,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",572,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",572,1,3,0)="There is an issue reported of an incorrect status being displayed on the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",572,1,4,0)="CMOP Event Log for a CMOP dispensed refill that was subsequently returned"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",572,1,5,0)="to stock, refilled again and then it's label queued for printing. In this"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",572,1,6,0)="case, the status is being displayed as 'DISP',however, once a refill is"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",572,1,7,0)="returned to stock the status should be displayed as 'Disp Refill Deleted'."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,0)="677 SEQ #599^3230803.092715^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,0)="^^64^64^3230803"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,1,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,2,0)="==========================================="
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,4,0)="1.      INC21810787 - TELEPHONE REFILLS - Processing all divisions "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,5,0)="potential    error in routine"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,8,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,9,0)="   -------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,10,0)="When processing telephone refills using the option Process Telephone "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,11,0)="Refills [PSO PROCESS TELEPHONE REFILLS] and answering, 'Process telephone "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,12,0)="refills for all divisions?' with YES, any refills that are not for the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,13,0)="division selected at the start of the Process Telephone Refills option "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,14,0)="and has a drug setup in the DRUG file (#50) with CMOP DISPENSE field "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,15,0)="(#213) not set to Yes, the drug will be refilled with the wrong division "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,16,0)="in the refill record of the PRESCRIPTION file (#52).  It will mark the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,17,0)="refill for the division selected in the option instead of the division "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,18,0)="for which the original RX was created."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,19,0)="The problem is due to variable PSOSITE being set to the IEN of the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,20,0)="OUTPATIENT SITE (#59) selected at the Division: prompt when running the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,21,0)="Process Telephone Refills [PSO PROCESS TELEPHONE REFILLS] option.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,22,0)="This variable is then used during processing and creation of the refill "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,23,0)="which results in the incorrect division to be filed into the DIVISION "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,24,0)="field (#8) in the REFILL sub record (#52.1D) of the PRESCRIPTION file "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,25,0)="(#52) when Process telephone refills for all divisions? // is answered "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,26,0)="Yes and a refill is encountered for a division not matching the division "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,27,0)="selected."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,29,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,30,0)="   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,31,0)="Variable PSOSITE is used extensively in PSO code, so this patch is only "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,32,0)="making a change to PSOSITE's value within routine PSOVEXRX."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,34,0)="When a RX is being processed in Process Telephone Refills and the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,35,0)="original fill is for a division that is different than the division "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,36,0)="selected at the Division: prompt, the variable is newed and reset to the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,37,0)="IEN for the division and variable PSOBBC(""PSOVEXRX"") is also set before "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,38,0)="REFILL^PSOBBC is called to process the fill for that RX, the variable is "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,39,0)="reset to original value afterwards. PSOBBC(""PSOVEXRX"") is used "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,40,0)="conditionally to determine to display the message 'RX # 1234567 is for "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,41,0)="(XXXXXXXXXXX) division.' On the output at the end of running Process "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,42,0)="Telephone Refills."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,45,0)="   Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,46,0)="   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,47,0)="Routine PSOVEXRX"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,49,0)="Line PSO6+13^PSOVEXRX is commented out and replaced with:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,50,0)=" ;p677 handle multi division"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,51,0)=" ;S PSOBBC(""DONE"")=PSOBBC(""IRXN"")_"","" D REFILL^PSOBBC"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,52,0)=" I '$P($G(PSOSYS),""^"",2) D REFILL^PSOBBC I 1"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,53,0)=" E  D"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,54,0)=" . I PSOSITE'=$P(^PSRX(PSORXIEN,2),U,9) S PSOBBC(""PSOVEXRX"")=PSOSITE N "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,55,0)="PSOSITE S PSOSITE=$P(^PSRX(PSORXIEN,2),U,9)"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,56,0)=" . D REFILL^PSOBBC"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,57,0)=" . K PSOBBC(""PSOVEXRX"")"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,58,0)=" S PSOBBC(""DONE"")=PSOBBC(""IRXN"")_"","""
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,60,0)="Routine PSOREF0"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,62,0)="CHKDIV^PSOREF0 is changed to:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,63,0)="CHKDIV G:$P(PSOREF(""RX2""),""^"",9)=+PSOSITE&'$G(PSOBBC(""PSOVEXRX"")) CHKDIVX "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",573,1,64,0)=";p677 multi division update for telephone refill process "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,0)="707 SEQ #600^3230817.111702^89"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,0)="^^320^320^3230817"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,1,0)="The PSO*7.0*707 patch delivers the necessary components for the support of"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,2,0)="the SalesForce Customer Relations Management (CRM) project, Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,3,0)="Pharmacy requirements, on the VistA level.  It has been designed to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,4,0)="provide REST services for the Java scripted calls used by the SalesForce"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,5,0)="User Interface."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,7,0)="The patch releases the necessary Remote Procedure Calls (RPCs) and ENTITY"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,8,0)="(#1.5) file entries for retrieval of VistA data from a VistA instance.  "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,9,0)="The patch supports the operations of the Virtual Care Centers, Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,10,0)="Pharmacy, as well as individual patient-related requests."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,12,0)="In addition, there is a post-install routine that will add the PSO WEB"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,13,0)="CHART menu context to the connector proxy user."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,15,0)="****NOTE****  There are post-install instructions for setting up the "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,16,0)="connector proxy user. These MUST be completed for these patch components"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,17,0)="to function.  These instructions were also included in patch PSO*7.0*642."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,18,0)="If completed during installation of patch PSO*7.0*642, the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,19,0)="Post-installation instructions in this patch may be ignored."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",574,1,20,0)=" "
