^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,202,0)="7. Patient Validation Screen"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,203,0)="  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,204,0)="   The content of the Patient Validation screen was completely re-arranged to"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,205,0)="   show the eRx Patient and the VistA Patient side-by-side. In addition, the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,206,0)="   eRx Patient allergy list (received from the outside prescriber) will be"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,207,0)="   displayed as well as the ChampVA Rx Benefit eligibility (MBM sites only)."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,208,0)="   Besides displaying the patients side-by-side, a few other features were"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,209,0)="   introduced to make the screen more user friendly, such as:"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,210,0)="     a) When there is a mismatch for field (e.g., Name, DOB, etc.) the content"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,211,0)="        of such field will display in reverse video in for both records, eRx"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,212,0)="        and VistA Patients."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,213,0)="     b) The content will display in highlight in order to stand from the field"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,214,0)="        label. "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,215,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,216,0)="     Obs) These features depend on the terminal display settings being set"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,217,0)="          differently for reverse video and highlighted font in order for it"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,218,0)="          to work."
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,219,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,220,0)="     Below is an example of how the new screen will be displayed (without the"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,221,0)="     reverse or highlighted video features):"
^DIC(9.4,60,22,13,"PAH",584,1,222,0)="     _________________________________________________________________________"
