^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,1,0)="Associated Patches:"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,3,0)="XT*7.3*58       <<= must be installed BEFORE `XWB*1.1*28'"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,4,0)="XU*8.0*225      <<= **ONLY FOR CACHE SITES** must be installed BEFORE "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,5,0)="                 `XWB*1.1*28'"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,6,0)="XU*8.0*238      <<= must be installed BEFORE `XWB*1.1*28'"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,9,0)="DESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,10,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,11,0)="The M-to-M Broker provides a new implementation of the RPC Broker "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,12,0)="enabling the exchange of VISTA M-based data and business rules between "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,13,0)="two VISTA M servers, where both servers reside on the same, or on "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,14,0)="different VISTA M systems. It has been developed to provide Client/Server "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,15,0)="functionality resident solely within the VISTA environment.  The "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,16,0)="requesting server functions in the capacity of a ""client."" The server "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,17,0)="receiving that request functions in the capacity of a ""server."" The "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,18,0)="Client/Server roles of each server can change depending on at what point "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,19,0)="in time each VISTA M server is making the request for data from it's "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,20,0)="counterpart VISTA M server. "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,22,0)="The requesting server and the receiving server can reside on the same, or "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,23,0)="on different VISTA M systems.  All M-to-M Broker client and server "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,24,0)="routines are packaged in one KIDS build.  This build will need to be "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,25,0)="installed on each VISTA system required for M-to-M Broker processing. "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,27,0)="Further information is provided in a separate document, ""M-to-M BROKER "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,28,0)="Supplemental Documentation, Patch XWB*1.1*28"" This document can be "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,29,0)="obtained by using FTP from the appropriate Customer Service directory:"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,32,0)="  OI FIELD OFFICE    FTP ADDRESS      DIRECTORY"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,33,0)="  ======================================================"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,34,0)="  Albany                127.0.0.1 (ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext)"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,35,0)="  Hines                 127.0.0.1 (ftp.fo-chicago.domain.ext)"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,36,0)="  Salt Lake City        152.131.2.1 (ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext)"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,38,0)="  Host File Name: XWB1_1P28SP.PDF"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,40,0)="This document can also be downloaded from the Infrastructure "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,41,0)="Documentation center web page:"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,43,0)="  http://vista.domain.ext/vdl/#App128"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,46,0)="Background"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,47,0)="=========="
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,49,0)="VISTA Imaging requested the development of the M-to-M Broker to be used "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,50,0)="to communicate between the M client on the VISTA Imaging Digital Imaging "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,51,0)="and Communications in Medicine (DICOM) Gateway and the M server on the "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,52,0)="main VISTA Hospital Information System."
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,54,0)="The VISTA Imaging DICOM Gateway architecture uses M software on a "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,55,0)="workstation to create associations between newly acquired images and the "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,56,0)="computerized patient record.  Previous to the development of the M-to-M "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,57,0)="Broker, the gateway system communicated with the main Hospital "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,58,0)="Information System using the Distributed Data Processing (DDP) protocol, "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,59,0)="stored the acquired images on NT file servers and set database entries to "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,60,0)="reference them."
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,62,0)="Problems with DDP"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,64,0)="* Causes database inconsistencies."
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,65,0)="* Complete lack of security."
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,66,0)="* DDP is bound to MAC addresses."
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,67,0)="* DDP can be very slow on a busy HIS and/or network."
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,68,0)="* DDP runs very slowly in a WAN environment because of inherent network "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,69,0)="  latencies."
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,71,0)="Because of the database inconsistency problem, incidents of matching "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,72,0)="images to the wrong patient occurred at one particular site."
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,74,0)="DDP doesn't have any security.  M-to-M Broker uses many of the robust "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,75,0)="security features implemented by the VISTA RPC Broker and Kernel "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,76,0)="software.  These security features are transparent to the end user and "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,77,0)="without additional impact on IRM."
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,79,0)="For the VISTA Imaging DICOM Gateway, the M applications on separate VISTA "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,80,0)="systems will be converted to use this new M-to-M Broker software to "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,81,0)="communicate to the main HIS.  This will then eliminate the need for DDP "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,82,0)="where it is used."
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,85,0)="List of Test Sites"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,86,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,88,0)="VISTA Imaging System Team, Washington Office of Information Field Office "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,89,0)="(OIFO)"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,90,0)="VAMC San Francisco"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,92,0)="Blood Bank Team Coordination"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,93,0)="============================"
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,94,0)="Clearance = August 21, 2002 "
^DIC(9.4,70,22,2,"PAH",25,1,95,0)=" "
