^DIC(9.4,70,"DEV")="Enrique Gomez"
^DIC(9.4,70,"VERSION")=1.1
^DIC(9.4,71,0)="ADVERSE REACTION TRACKING^GMRA^Adverse Reaction Tracking package"
^DIC(9.4,71,1,0)="^^3^3^2951205^"
^DIC(9.4,71,1,1,0)="This package permits clinical users to track and report patient allergies"
^DIC(9.4,71,1,2,0)="and adverse reactions. The intended users are physicians, nurses, other"
^DIC(9.4,71,1,3,0)="clinicians and clerks."
^DIC(9.4,71,5)="HISC"
^DIC(9.4,71,7)="^^I"
^DIC(9.4,71,14,0)="^9.4014^1^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,14,1,0)="GMA"
^DIC(9.4,71,14,"B","GMA",1)=""
^DIC(9.4,71,20,0)="^9.402P^1^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,20,1,0)="2^^GMRAMRG"
^DIC(9.4,71,20,1,1)=""
^DIC(9.4,71,20,"B",2,1)=""
^DIC(9.4,71,22,0)="^9.49I^1^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,0)="4.0^3051119^2960715^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,1,0)="^^2^2^3051119"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,1,1,0)="The Adverse Reaction Tracking package tracks patient allergies/adverse"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,1,2,0)="reactions."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^61^61"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,0)="2^2960812^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,0)="^^46^46^2960812"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,1,0)="This Build:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,3,0)="1) deletes the Soundex cross-reference from the NAME field (#.01) of the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,4,0)="   GMR ALLERGIES file (#120.82)."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,6,0)="2) fixes a possible undefined variable error (GMRAREC) in the routine"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,7,0)="   GMRASIG1."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,9,0)="3) fixes a FOR loop which uses the wrong variable to loop through an"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,10,0)="   array in the routine GMRAPTB."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,12,0)="4) fixes the problem reported in NOIS NOP-0596-12146. A user presses"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,13,0)="   RETURN or enters an up-arrow at the Causative Agent prompt and is"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,14,0)="   prompted to enter another causative agent."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,16,0)="5) fixes the problem reported in NOIS ISH-0596-42277. Under certain"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,17,0)="   instances the 'Sign-off' event point is not being executed."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,19,0)="6) modifies the field description for the REQUIRE ORIGINATOR COMMENTS"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,20,0)="   field (#4) in the GMR ALLERGY SITE PARAMETERS file (#120.84)."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,21,0)="   NOIS CLA-0696-20854."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,23,0)="7) fixes a problem where the REACTION ASSESSMENT field (#1) in the ADVERSE"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,24,0)="   REACTION ASSESSMENT file (#120.86) is marked 1 (yes), but the patient"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,25,0)="   does not have any active entries (i.e., entries that have not been"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,26,0)="   entered-in-error) in the PATIENT ALLERGIES file (#120.8)."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,27,0)="   NOIS: CMO-0696-40833."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,29,0)="8) identifies the patient (e.g., T1234), suspect medication and event date"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,30,0)="   on the Attachment page of the MedWatch form. NOIS: BRX-0696-11081."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,32,0)="9) modifies the GMRADPT utility to return ""unsigned"" reactions in the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,33,0)="   GMRAL array."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,35,0)="10) changes the ORCHK^GMRAOR utility call. If the calling routine is"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,36,0)="    checking for Contrast Media Reactions and the patient is not in the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,37,0)="    ART database, then the utility will return a null value instead of a"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,38,0)="    0 (zero)."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,40,0)="11) fixes a bug in the GMRADPT utility which returns a GMRAL array node"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,41,0)="    stating the person has No Known Allergies if the person is not in the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,42,0)="    ART database."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,44,0)="12) fixes a bug in the GMRANKA routine which may enter the wrong value in"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,45,0)="    the ADVERSE REACTION ASSESSMENT file (#120.86), REACTION ASSESSMENT"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",1,1,46,0)="    field (#1). NOIS: MAR-0696-21799."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,0)="5^2961009^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^31^31^2961009"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,1,0)="This Build addresses the following problems:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,3,0)="1) Corrects a bug introduced by the GMRA*4.0*2 patch. Users are not being"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,4,0)="asked to sign-off on autoverified reactions in the enter/edit reaction"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,5,0)="process if they answer YES to the ""Enter another Causative Agent?"" prompt,"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,6,0)="but do not enter another causative agent. This results in the reaction not"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,7,0)="be considered as autoverified."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,9,0)="2) When a user mistakenly answers YES to the ""Does this patient have any"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,10,0)="known allergies or adverse reactions?"" prompt and does not enter a"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,11,0)="causative agent the software assesses the patient as having a reaction on"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,12,0)="file in the database. It should not."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,14,0)="3) The GMRA PRINT-COMPLETE LISTING option does not distinguish between"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,15,0)="patients who not in the ART database and those patients who are assessed"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,16,0)="as NKA (No Known Allergies)."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,18,0)="4) The ART package calls an Outpatient Pharmacy utility to get and display"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,19,0)="any outpatient medications for a patient. The SIG code value for the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,20,0)="prescription return is changing in size from one line of text to one plus"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,21,0)="lines of text. The ART package will store the first 30 characters of the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,22,0)="SIG code for its SUSPECT and CONCOMITANT drug entries in File 120.85."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,24,0)="5) Changes the description for the GMRA PRINT-FDA EXCEPT BY PT option so"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,25,0)="that it accurately describes what that option does."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,27,0)="6) Changes the description for the GMRA PRINT-EXCEPT BY DATe option so"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,28,0)="that it accurately describes what that option does."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,30,0)="For more detailed information please see the GMRA*4*5 patch description on"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",2,1,31,0)="FORUM."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",3,0)="7 SEQ #5^2970602^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^2^2^2970602"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="GMRA*4.0*7  See National patch module for a description of the changes"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",3,1,2,0)="incorporated in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,0)="4^2970922^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^44^44^2970922"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="This build fixes several problems in the ART portion of the ART-CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,2,0)="interface."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,4,0)="Routine changes:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,6,0)=" GMRAOR0"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,7,0)="   The DUPCHK entry point was quitting prematurely and therefore not"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,8,0)="   accurately checking for duplicate entries."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,10,0)=" GMRAOR4"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,11,0)="   The ART EP asked the CPRS developers to include the OBSERVER field"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,12,0)="   value for all new reactions CPRS sends to the ART package. This routine"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,13,0)="   was changed to recognize this piece of data when it is passed to ART."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,15,0)=" GMRAOR5"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,16,0)="   Fixes a syntax error."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,18,0)="   Simplifies some code used to check for duplicate patient reactions."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,20,0)="   Fixes a bug where the reaction was not completely filed if the reaction"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,21,0)="   value pointer and file was not recognized as one of the five pointed-to"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,22,0)="   files used by the ART package."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,24,0)="   Modifies the code to call GMRAOR9 to store any drug ingredients or drug"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,25,0)="   classes if the reaction was of a drug type."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,27,0)="   Modifies the code to add an entry to File 120.85 only if the patient"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,28,0)="   reaction was an observed drug reaction."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,29,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,30,0)="   Sends the reaction as unverified so it will appear on the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,31,0)="   list of reactions to be verified."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,33,0)=" GMRAOR7"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,34,0)="   The sign/symptom data was not being stored in File 120.85 because a"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,35,0)="   call to SIGN^GMRAOR6 was passing the variable GMRAL when it should send"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,36,0)="   the array GMRAL."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,38,0)=" GMRAOR8"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,39,0)="   This routine was modified to correct subfile numbers being set"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,40,0)="   in fileman."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,42,0)=" GMRAOR9 "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,43,0)="   This is a new routine which stores drug ingredients and/or drug classes"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",4,1,44,0)="   for a patient drug reaction."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",5,0)="6 SEQ #7^2971006^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",5,1,0)="^^2^2^2971006"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",5,1,1,0)="The Description of this build can be found in the Nation Patch Module"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",5,1,2,0)="under patch GMRA*4.0*6"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",6,0)="8^2980109^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",7,0)="9^2980511^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^4^4^2980511"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",7,1,1,0)="This patch will update the mark chart/id band option to use"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",7,1,2,0)="the new ACRP APIs that become available with patch SD*5.3*131."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",7,1,3,0)="Please see the national patch module for a full description of"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",7,1,4,0)="this patch as well as patch 131."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",8,0)="10 SEQ #10^2981026^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",8,1,0)="^^1^1^2981026"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",8,1,1,0)="See Description in the National Patch Module for Patch GMRA*4*10."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",9,0)="11^2981026^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",9,1,0)="^^2^2^2981026"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",9,1,1,0)="The description of this build can be found in the National Patch Module "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",9,1,2,0)="within the patch description of GMRA*4*11."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",10,0)="12^2981104^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^4^4^2981104"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",10,1,1,0)="Allergies entered via CPRS were being entered into the ART database as"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",10,1,2,0)="unverified even if they met the criteria to be auto-verified in the ART"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",10,1,3,0)="site parameters. This patch will auto-verify those allergies entered via"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",10,1,4,0)="CPRS that meet the criteria as defined at the site."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",11,0)="13^2981112^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^2^2^2981112"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="This patch will make the ARTS software compatible with the National Drug"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",11,1,2,0)="File regardless of version."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,0)="14^2990121^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^15^15^2990121"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="The METHOD OF NOTIFICATION field in file 120.84 is used to determine the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,2,0)="users that should receive the chart and ID band marking bulletin. If this"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,3,0)="field is set to OE/RR TEAMS, the code made reference to PCMM team lists."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,4,0)="CPRS has ceased use of PCMM teams for list functionality.   The errant"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,5,0)="reference to PCMM caused an error when a patient with data in the ADVERSE"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,6,0)="REACTION TRACKING (ART) database was admitted. The same error can be"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,7,0)="generated when a new adverse reaction is entered and the charts and/or ID"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,8,0)="bands have not been marked. patch corrects this error by changing the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,9,0)="reference to use the OE/RR LIST (#100.21) file."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,11,0)="DBIA #1471 has been retired which allowed ART to call ALLERGY^RAUTL3 in"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,12,0)="This patch corrects this error by changing the reference to use file 12d"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,13,0)="RADIOLOGY/NUCLEAR MEDICINE v 4.5 to retrieve and store information"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,14,0)="relating to allergies to radiologic contrast media. This reference is"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",12,1,15,0)="being removed from the ART software."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",13,0)="16^3010103^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",14,0)="17 SEQ #16^3031231^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",14,1,0)="^^2^2^3031231"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",14,1,1,0)="This patch includes a utility for updating free text entries.  Please see"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",14,1,2,0)="the FORUM patch description for a detailed explanation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",15,0)="19 SEQ #17^3040702^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",15,1,0)="^^4^4^3040702"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",15,1,1,0)="Update to allergy tracking package consisting of changes to the free text "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",15,1,2,0)="utility distributed in patch GMRA*4*17 as well as updates to send "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",15,1,3,0)="bulletins from CPRS GUI upon new allergy entry.  Please see the FORUM "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",15,1,4,0)="module for complete details."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",16,0)="18 SEQ #18^3050118^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^3^3^3050118"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",16,1,1,0)="This patch will install new cross-references on files 120.8, 120.85"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",16,1,2,0)="and 120.86 in support of the health data repository.  See the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",16,1,3,0)="patch description on FORUM for complete details."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",17,0)="22 SEQ #19^3050118^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",17,1,0)="^^2^2^3050118"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",17,1,1,0)="HDR related changes.  Please see FORUM patch description"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",17,1,2,0)="for details regarding this patch."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",18,0)="21 SEQ #20^3050212^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^5^5^3050212"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="Allergy updates required to support the removal of allergies"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",18,1,2,0)="as orders.  After installation of this patch and CPRS GUI v25,"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",18,1,3,0)="allergies will no longer be treated as orders."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",18,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",18,1,5,0)="Please see the FORUM patch module for a complete description."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",19,0)="23 SEQ #21^3050813^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",19,1,0)="^^3^3^3050813"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",19,1,1,0)="This patch includes changes required for continued support"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",19,1,2,0)="of the Health Data Repository project.  Please see the national"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",19,1,3,0)="patch module for a full description of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",20,0)="24 SEQ #22^3050813^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",20,1,0)="^^2^2^3050813"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",20,1,1,0)="See FORUM patch module for a full description.  Updates HDR related"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",20,1,2,0)="trigger code."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",21,0)="25 SEQ #23^3050905^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",21,1,0)="^^2^2^3050905"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",21,1,1,0)="Update to fix blank sign/symptom issue.  Please see FORUM for the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",21,1,2,0)="complete description of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",22,0)="27 SEQ #24^3050905^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",22,1,0)="^^2^2^3050905"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",22,1,1,0)="This patch will correct the reported problem of the allergy bulletin"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",22,1,2,0)="not being fired if the contrast media has a VA DRUG CLASS of DX109."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",23,0)="30 SEQ #26^3051115^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",23,1,0)="^^8^8^3051115"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",23,1,1,0)="Remedy ticket HD67463 was logged because the site noticed that deceased "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",23,1,2,0)="patients were appearing on the [GMRA PRINT-PATIENT NOT ASKED] report.  "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",23,1,3,0)="This report lists patients who have not been given an allergy/adverse "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",23,1,4,0)="reaction assessment.  The sites then use this list and contact the "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",23,1,5,0)="patients in an attempt to get the assessment information from them.  It "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",23,1,6,0)="is not desirable for the VA to inadvertently contact the family of a "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",23,1,7,0)="deceased individual in an attempt to get the allergy/adverse reaction "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",23,1,8,0)="information for that person."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",24,0)="34 SEQ #29^3060410^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",24,1,0)="^^2^2^3060410"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",24,1,1,0)="Updates to HL7 messaging for HDR.  See FORUM for a complete"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",24,1,2,0)="description."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",25,0)="35 SEQ #30^3060807^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",25,1,0)="^^1^1^3060807"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",25,1,1,0)="POSSIBLE PROBLEM WITH LIST BY LOCATION UNASSESSED ALLERGIES."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",26,0)="20 SEQ #31^3060923^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",26,1,0)="^^3^3^3060923"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",26,1,1,0)="This patch updates the clean up utility to include ingredient based"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",26,1,2,0)="and drug class based allergies.  Please see FORUM for the complete"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",26,1,3,0)="description of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",27,0)="36 SEQ #32^3070904.223844^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",27,1,0)="^^3^3^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",27,1,1,0)="Removes ability to delete existing allergy entries from the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",27,1,2,0)="roll and scroll environment."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",27,1,3,0)="Please see the FORUM patch module for a complete description."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",28,0)="26 SEQ #33^3070904.230728^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",28,1,0)="^^2^2^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",28,1,1,0)="Remote Data Interoperability updates.  Please see FORUM for a full "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",28,1,2,0)="description of the updates."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",29,0)="37 SEQ #34^3070904.23123^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",29,1,0)="^^2^2^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",29,1,1,0)="Updates for RDI and contrast media"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",29,1,2,0)="Please see the FORUM patch description for full details."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",30,0)="29^3070904.23472^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",30,1,0)="^^1^1^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",30,1,1,0)="Provides an auto-update for existing free text allergies"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",31,0)="40 SEQ #36^3071212.220407^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",31,1,0)="^^5^5^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",31,1,1,0)="This patch reviews updates made in patch GMRA*4*29 related"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",31,1,2,0)="to terms that begin with the text ANGIOTEN and assures that"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",31,1,3,0)="they were correctly updated.  A few ANGIOTEN entries were"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",31,1,4,0)="incorrectly updated to the wrong drug class and need to be"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",31,1,5,0)="updated to the correct drug class."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,0)="33 SEQ #37^3080722.080657^1"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,0)="^^22^22^3080722"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,1,0)="This patch addresses Remedy ticket, HD67403.  The site reported"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,2,0)="that test patients entered in production are appearing on the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,3,0)="Adverse Reaction Tracking reports, and are also being included in"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,4,0)="report counts."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,5,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,6,0)="This patch will update the Adverse Reaction Tracking reports that "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,7,0)="display the patient name and/or SSN, and reports that produce counts"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,8,0)="of reaction data so that they all exclude test patients."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,9,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,10,0)="This patch will also correct a problem with the bulletin generation during"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,11,0)="entry of Adverse Reactions described in Remedy ticket HD85125."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,12,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,13,0)="The problem occurs when the user answers ""No"" to verify an observed/drug "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,14,0)="adverse reaction when it is first entered.  If the user skips the "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,15,0)="verification step but then uses the GMRA PATIENT A/AR EDIT option and "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,16,0)="edits the existing observed/drug allergy and then verifies it (with or "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,17,0)="without making changes) an additional NOTIFICATION OF OBSERVED DRUG "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,18,0)="REACTION bulletin is triggered."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,19,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,20,0)="This patch will modify the logic in the code so that, if the user "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,21,0)="re-enters the adverse reaction and then verifies it, a second "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",32,1,22,0)="NOTIFICATION OF OBSERVED DRUG REACTION bulletin will not be triggered."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",33,0)="38^3090421.154938^17"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",34,0)="41 SEQ #39^3090422.122254^17"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",34,1,0)="^^1^1^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",34,1,1,0)="See GMRA*4*41 in the National Patch Module"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",35,0)="42 SEQ #40^3090624.144102^17"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",35,1,0)="^^5^5^3090624"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",35,1,1,0)="Fixes issue with historical allergy entries being associated with"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",35,1,2,0)="a progress note when the historical entry follows the entry of"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",35,1,3,0)="an observed drug reaction."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",35,1,4,0)="Also, fixes issue with 0 node not being set correctly on XTMP node"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",35,1,5,0)="and provides failsafe for sending data to HDR."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",36,0)="44 SEQ #41^3110303.113043^17"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",37,0)="45^3110308.135203^17"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",38,0)="47^3140407.172403^17"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",38,1,0)="^^3^3^3140407"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",38,1,1,0)="This is a companion patch to the Order Entry/Results Reporting (OE/RR) "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",38,1,2,0)="version 3.0 software patch number 345 (OR*3.0*345). See the patch message"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",38,1,3,0)="for a full listing of issues addressed and installation instructions."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",39,0)="43 SEQ #44^3140605.131744^17"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",39,1,0)="^^2^2^3140605"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",39,1,1,0)="The patch is to create a merge routine to check for allergy assessments "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",39,1,2,0)="in Patients before the merge occurs."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",40,0)="48 SEQ #45^3160526.154743^54"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",40,1,0)="^^4^4^3160526"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",40,1,1,0)="This patch installs a tool that will assist sites in ensuring that the "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",40,1,2,0)="ADVERSE REACTION ASSESSMENT file (#120.86) is synced with the PATIENT "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",40,1,3,0)="ALLERGIES file (#120.8).  See the associated patch description for "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",40,1,4,0)="additional details and installation instructions."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",41,0)="46^3160526.15491^54"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",41,1,0)="^^5^5^3160526"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",41,1,1,0)="UPDATES ADVERSE REACTION TRACKING TO RETURN SIGN/SYMPTOM DATA WITH "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",41,1,2,0)="COMPUTERIZED PATIENT RECORD SYSTEM (CPRS) ORDER CHECK MESSAGES AND TO "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",41,1,3,0)="INLUCDE HEALTH DATA REPOSITORY (HDR) DATA WITH THE EN1^GMRADPT "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",41,1,4,0)="APPLICATION PROGRAMMING INTERFACE (API). REFER TO THE PATCH DESCRIPTION "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",41,1,5,0)="FOR ADDITIONAL INFORMATION."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",42,0)="52 SEQ #47^3160713.125907^54"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",42,1,0)="^^2^2^3160713"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",42,1,1,0)="This patch is a follow-up patch to GMRA*4*46. See the associated patch "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",42,1,2,0)="description for details on this patch."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",43,0)="49 SEQ #48^3160815.123908^54"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",43,1,0)="^^7^7^3160815"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",43,1,1,0)="Patch GMRA*4.0*49 addresses the following two issues:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",43,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",43,1,3,0)="1. Excessive number of entries in the PATIENT ALLERGIES file (#120.8)"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",43,1,4,0)="   causes issues with the allergy HL7 messages."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",43,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",43,1,6,0)="2. Embedded carriage returns in some old allergy HL7 messages prevented "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",43,1,7,0)="   the messages from being sent."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",44,0)="50 SEQ #49^3161201.154804^54"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",45,0)="55 SEQ #50^3170530.160855^54"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",45,1,0)="^^1^1^3170530"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",45,1,1,0)="See National Patch Module for details."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",46,0)="54 SEQ #51^3171227.13464^54"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",46,1,0)="^^8^8^3171227"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",46,1,1,0)="Patch GMRA*4.0*54 addresses the following three issues:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",46,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",46,1,3,0)="1. FDA report SUBSCRIPT error with non-VA drugs "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",46,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",46,1,5,0)="2. Adverse Reaction Assessment update when no previous Reaction "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",46,1,6,0)="   Assessment value"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",46,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",46,1,8,0)="3. Allergy file allows MECHANISM to be null"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",47,0)="58 SEQ #52^3181102.153107^54"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",47,1,0)="^^11^11^3181102"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",47,1,1,0)="This patch has the following enhancements for Clinical Ancillary Services"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",47,1,2,0)="(CAS) Enhancements (RXSU2)."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",47,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",47,1,4,0)="1. Suppress Non-Drug Ingredient-Level Alert"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",47,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",47,1,6,0)="   Previously released patch GMRA*4*50 added a new alert when the DRUG "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",47,1,7,0)="   CLASSES field (#3) in the PATIENT ALLERGIES file (#120.8) is empty.  "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",47,1,8,0)="   This patch will add a filter, to ignore those alerts, where ALLERGY"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",47,1,9,0)="   TYPE field (#3.1) in PATIENT ALLERGIES file (#120.8), does not contain"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",47,1,10,0)="   the Drug code of ""D"", as no action was needed to be taken for this"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",47,1,11,0)="   scenario."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",48,0)="59 SEQ #53^3181204.154422^54"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",48,1,0)="^^2^2^3181204"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",48,1,1,0)="This patch addresses NSR 20171203. See the Forum patch description for"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",48,1,2,0)="additional details."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",49,0)="60 SEQ #54^3191003.155037^65"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",49,1,0)="^^1^1^3191003"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",49,1,1,0)="IEN MISMATCH ISSUE"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",50,0)="53^3200624.121443^65"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",50,1,0)="^^3^3^3200624"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",50,1,1,0)="This patch resolves issues identified during the testing of CPRS v31 as "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",50,1,2,0)="well as post-release issues with recently released patches. See the patch "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",50,1,3,0)="description for the list of issues resolved."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",51,0)="62 SEQ #56^3200721.135102^65"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",51,1,0)="^^6^6^3200721"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",51,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",51,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",51,1,3,0)="1.      INC9435820 - WRONG URL IN AN ALLERGY OPTION"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",51,1,4,0)="        When utilizing Menu Option GMRA ALLERGY FILE EDIT the user is"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",51,1,5,0)="        presented with an incorrect URL (Uniform Resource Locator) or Web"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",51,1,6,0)="        Page to be used when making their request."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,0)="61 SEQ #57^3200923.154224^65"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,0)="^^31^31^3200923"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue in the Clinical Procedures "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,2,0)="(CP) Flowsheet application."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,4,0)="1.  INC8167520 - Cannot enter NKDA into the patient's allergy assessment."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,7,0)="New Service Requests (NSRs):"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,8,0)="----------------------------  "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,9,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,12,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,13,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,14,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,16,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,17,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,18,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,19,0)="1. INC8167520 - Cannot enter NKDA into the patient's allergy assessment."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,21,0)="Problem 1:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,22,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,23,0)="If the user ""up carats out"" of the GMRA assessment utility prior to the "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,24,0)="report running, the next time a user enters the utility it will appears "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,25,0)="as though the report ran, even though it did not."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,27,0)="Resolution 1:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,28,0)="-------------"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,29,0)="Routine GMRAFA was modified to kill the ^XTMP(""GMRAFAL"") global if the "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,30,0)="user exits before running the report. This will reset the option, "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",52,1,31,0)="allowing the user to run the report."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",53,0)="64 SEQ #58^3210129.092228^17"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",53,1,0)="^^3^3^3210129"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",53,1,1,0)="This patch addresses a post-release issue identified with patch "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",53,1,2,0)="GMRA*4*53, part of the CPRS v31b release. See the patch description for a "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",53,1,3,0)="full explanation of the issue."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",54,0)="63^3210701.1128^17"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",55,0)="66b^3210701"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",55,1,0)="^^5^5^3210701"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",55,1,1,0)="Backup of GMRA*4.0*66 on Jul 01, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",55,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",55,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",55,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",55,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,0)="66 SEQ #60^3210701.113022^17"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,0)="^^50^50^3210701"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,3,0)="1) INC17497887 - UNABLE TO MODIFY AN ALLERGY ASSESSMENT USING THE VISTA"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,4,0)="   (HITPS-7808)  ASSESSMENT CLEANUP UTILITY ECN 74075"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,5,0)="   Duplicate:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,6,0)="   -----------"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,7,0)="   INC16946767 - allergy info being displayed differently (incorrectly) in"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,8,0)="                 different areas of Vista/CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,9,0)="   INC17041102 - Adverse Reaction Tracking-Allergy Assessment; 3 Discrepancies"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,10,0)="                 that cannot be resolved with the Modify Assessment tool."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,11,0)="   INC17041569 - CPRS ERROR_unable to update allergies for ONE patient"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,12,0)="   INC17069709 - Adverse Reaction Tracking - Allergy Assessment"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,13,0)="   INC17072229 - Adverse Reaction Tracking - Allergy Assessment"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,14,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,15,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,16,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,17,0)="1) INC11926924 - MAD: GMRA*#*### not resolve: order appeared verified by nurse"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,18,0)="                 in BCMA but CPRS it was found not to be.     "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,19,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,20,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,21,0)="The Captain James A. Lovell Federal Health Care Center reported that they were"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,22,0)="unable to modify an allergy assessment for a specific patient using the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,23,0)="Assessment clean up utility option [GMRA ASSESSMENT UTILITY]. After some "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,24,0)="research it was discovered that when two patients were merged and the 'TO'"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,25,0)="patient (remaining patient after them merge) had not Allergy assessment while"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,26,0)="'FROM' patient (deleted after the merge) a corrupt record was being created"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,27,0)="for the 'TO' patient. These records could not be fixed using the Assessment"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,28,0)="clean utility option [GMRA ASSESSMENT UTILITY]."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,29,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,30,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,31,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,32,0)="The root of the problem is within the Kernel Patient Merge module. However we"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,33,0)="were able to address the problem by modifying GMR code specifically designed"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,34,0)="to run right before two patients are merged. The solution applied consisted of"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,35,0)="copying the 'FROM' Allergy assessment information to 'TO' before the patient"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,36,0)="merge were performed by the Kernel Patient Merge utility. In addition to"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,37,0)="fixing this problem so no new entries are affected this patch also fixes the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,38,0)="existing entries with the problem through a post-install routine that is"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,39,0)="described below."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,40,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,41,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,42,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,43,0)="Modified the routine XMRAMRG by adding right at the beginning of the ASSESS"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,44,0)="tag code to identify whether the 'FROM' patient had an allergy assessment in"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,45,0)="the ADVERSE REACTION ASSESSMENT file (#120.86) and the 'TO' patient did not."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,46,0)="If that's the case for the patient par being merged the new code will copy the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,47,0)="'FROM' patient allergy assessment and create an identical assessment for the"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,48,0)="'TO' patient in the ADVERSE REACTION ASSESSMENT file (#120.86). This will"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,49,0)="effectively prevent the Kernel Patient Merge Utility from creating a corrupt"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",56,1,50,0)="entry for the 'TO' patient. "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",57,0)="51^3221005.145507^89"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",57,1,0)="^^2^2^3221005"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",57,1,1,0)="Please refer to the patch description for contents and detailed "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",57,1,2,0)="information."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",58,0)="70 SEQ #63^3231215.132109^89"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",58,1,0)="^^11^11^3231215"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",58,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",58,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",58,1,3,0)="It was reported that a hard error was encountered when the reporting "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",58,1,4,0)="site, using CPRS, placed an inpatient medication order for hydroxyzine "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",58,1,5,0)="for a patient that has noted severe allergic reactions to hydroxyzine. "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",58,1,6,0)="The error caused CPRS to shut down and prevented the user from further "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",58,1,7,0)="processing the order. "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",58,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",58,1,9,0)="The error encountered is as follows: "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",58,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",58,1,11,0)="<SUBSCRIPT>DRUG+95^GMRAOR *ITEMS() Subscript 1 > 511"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",59,0)="68 SEQ #64^3240125.115742^89"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",59,1,0)="^^1^1^3240125"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",59,1,1,0)="Please see forum for a complete description of patch GMRA*4.0*68."
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",60,0)="72 SEQ #65^3240903.10362^89"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",60,1,0)="^^4^4^3240903"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",60,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",60,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",60,1,3,0)="INC30029401 - Inactive GMRA Allergy items found the Patient Allergies "
^DIC(9.4,71,22,1,"PAH",60,1,4,0)="file need to be cleaned up."
