^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,53,0)="      * From CHECK^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,56,0)="  Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,57,0)="  =========================="
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,59,0)="   1. Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation;"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,60,0)="      however, it is highly recommended to do the installation"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,61,0)="      when a minimal number of users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,62,0)="   2. It is not necessary to place TaskMan in a WAIT/STOP state."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,63,0)="   3. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options,"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,64,0)="      and Protocols? Yes// <return>, respond YES. When prompted to select"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,65,0)="                                             ==="
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,66,0)="      the option(s) you would like to place out of order, enter the"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,67,0)="      following:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,69,0)="         AFJXNHEX REQUEST"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,70,0)="         ================"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,72,0)="   4. Review your Mapped Routine set. If any of the routines listed in"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,73,0)="      the ROUTINE SUMMARY section are mapped on your system, they"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,74,0)="      should be unmapped at this time."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,75,0)="   5. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,76,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,77,0)="   6. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,78,0)="      system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,79,0)="   7. From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,80,0)="      the Installation menu. On the KIDS Installation menu, you may elect"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,81,0)="      to use the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,82,0)="      a. Verify checksums in the Transport Global - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,83,0)="         allow you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,84,0)="         the Transport Global."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,85,0)="      b. Print Transport Global and Compare Transport Global to the"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,86,0)="         Current System - this option will allow you to view all"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,87,0)="         changes that will be made when the patch is installed. It"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,88,0)="         compares all components of the patch (routines, DDs,"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,89,0)="         templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,91,0)="      c. Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,92,0)="         message of any routines exported with the patch. It will NOT"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,93,0)="         backup any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,94,0)="         Use the Install Package(s) options and select the package:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,96,0)="         AFJX*5.1*10."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,97,0)="         ==========="
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,99,0)="   8. If the routines were unmapped as part of step 4, the mapped set"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",5,1,100,0)="      should be rebuilt once the installation has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,0)="14 SEQ #11^2981119^1"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,0)="^^88^88^2981119"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,1,0)="Subject:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,2,0)="    New person file compliance"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,5,0)=" Category:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,6,0)="  - Routine"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,9,0)=" Description:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,10,0)=" ============"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,11,0)="    Revision of Network Health Exchange to comform with the"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,12,0)=" new person file."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,15,0)=" NOIS:  FNC-1098-32619"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,16,0)="    Testing site for deletion of file 3,6,1,6,20 reported that NHE"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,17,0)=" was bombing out.  This problem was caused by NHE pointing at"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,18,0)=" file #6. Routines were modified to resolve this problem."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,22,0)="  Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,23,0)="  ==========="
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,24,0)="      Fayetteville"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,27,0)=" "
