^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,45,0)="  Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,46,0)="  =========================="
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,48,0)="   1. Users are allowed to be on the system during the installation;"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,49,0)="      however, it is highly recommended to do the installation"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,50,0)="      when a minimal number of users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,51,0)="   2. It is not necessary to place TaskMan in a WAIT/STOP state."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,52,0)="   3. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options,"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,53,0)="      and Protocols? Yes// <return>, respond YES. When prompted to select"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,54,0)="                                             ==="
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,55,0)="      the option(s) you would like to place out of order, enter the"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,56,0)="      following:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,58,0)="         AFJXNHEX REQUEST"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,59,0)="         ================"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,61,0)="   4. Review your Mapped Routine set. If any of the routines listed in"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,62,0)="      the ROUTINE SUMMARY section are mapped on your system, they"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,63,0)="      should be unmapped at this time."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,64,0)="   5. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu.  This"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,65,0)="      option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,66,0)="   6. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,67,0)="      system.  You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,68,0)="   7. From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,69,0)="      the Installation menu. On the KIDS Installation menu, you may elect"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,70,0)="      to use the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,71,0)="      a. Verify checksums in the Transport Global - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,72,0)="         allow you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,73,0)="         the Transport Global."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,74,0)="      b. Print Transport Global and Compare Transport Global to the"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,75,0)="         Current System - this option will allow you to view all"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,76,0)="         changes that will be made when the patch is installed. It"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,77,0)="         compares all components of the patch (routines, DDs,"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,78,0)="         templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,79,0)="      c. Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,80,0)="         message of any routines exported with the patch. It will NOT"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,81,0)="         backup any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,82,0)="         Use the Install Package(s) options and select the package:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,84,0)="         AFJX*5.1*14."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,85,0)="         ==========="
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,87,0)="   8. If the routines were unmapped as part of step 4, the mapped set"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",6,1,88,0)="      should be rebuilt once the installation has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,0)="11 SEQ #12^2981214^1"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^100^100^2981214"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,2,0)=" Subject:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,3,0)="    Correcting dates to prevent records getting purged"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,6,0)=" Category:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,7,0)="  - Routine"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,10,0)=" Description:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,11,0)=" ============"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,12,0)="    Due to patches for Y2K compliance, Network Health Exchange is"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,13,0)="changing its code.  Currently, NHE is reading the dates"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,14,0)="incorrectly.  Routines were modified to resolve the extraction of"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,15,0)="dates from the records correctly."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,19,0)="  NOIS:  SBY-0598-30445, CMO-0698-42277"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,20,0)="    Sites reported that valid records were purged by the Network"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,21,0)="Health Exchange Nightly Purge.  Due to NHE is reading incorrect"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,22,0)="dates, valid records were deleted.  Records that are 7 days old"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,23,0)="are to be kept not purged."
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,27,0)="  Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,28,0)="  ==========="
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,29,0)="      Columbia, Salisbury"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,33,0)="  Routine Summary:"
^DIC(9.4,73,22,9,"PAH",7,1,34,0)="  ================"
