^DIC(9.4,77,22,16,"PAH","B","69 SEQ #69",40)=""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,0)="5.0^3051119^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^398^398"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,0)="4^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,0)="^^53^53^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,2,0)="1. A problem was reported at a site when the physician used the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,3,0)="non-standard schedule of QH during order entry. The system would hang and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,4,0)="IRM would have to go in and off the job. A routine change corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,5,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,7,0)="2. A problem was found where an Illegal Number error could occur in PSGDS0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,8,0)="when an Authorized Absence/Discharge Summary was generated. The error"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,9,0)="would occur only if the patient for which the report was being generated"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,10,0)="was assigned to a room-bed named numberEnumber-number. This problem also"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,11,0)="existed in previous versions of Inpatient Medications. Changes are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,12,0)="included to correct this error."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,14,0)="3. An undefined error at NEWIV+4^PSJORUT2 can occur when multiple"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,15,0)="solutions are entered for a Hyperal type IV order. This patch will correct"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,16,0)="this error."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,18,0)="4. When there are multiple duplicate drugs found while entering a new"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,19,0)="order, the duplicate drugs scroll off the screen.  A pause was added so"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,20,0)="the user will have a chance to see the warning."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,22,0)="5. When an IV order had been renewed through Computerized Patient Record"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,23,0)="System , the admin time from the original order should be copied over to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,24,0)="the new order. This will now function the same as Unit Dose."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,26,0)="6. When the IV order's login time is the same as the admin time, the start"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,27,0)="date of the order was not calculated in the correct format (West Palm"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,28,0)="Beach reported this). When the login time is between midnight and 12:30"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,29,0)="and the schedule is now, the start time was not calculated in the correct"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,30,0)="format. This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,32,0)="7. The MAR sometimes printed the pharmacy tech's initials for IV orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,33,0)="The MAR will now print the initials of the person who completed the IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,34,0)="order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,36,0)="8. A change was made to print the <A> on the right of the patient name and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,37,0)="ward to indicate the patient has verified or non-verified allergy/adverse"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,38,0)="reactions."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,40,0)="9. When a field is edited in a non-verified Unit Dose order that does not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,41,0)="cause a new order to be created, the order was not redisplayed for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,42,0)="verification. This patch will cause the non-verified orders to be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,43,0)="redisplayed after editing a field that does not cause a new order to be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,44,0)="created."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,46,0)="10. When a pending Unit Dose order with a priority of STAT was displayed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,47,0)="on the Unit Dose profile the ""->"" was not shown next to the order number"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,48,0)="identifying the order as not verified. This patch will cause the ""->"" to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,49,0)="be displayed for pending stat orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,51,0)="11. San Francisco reported an illegal or invalid argument at"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,52,0)="EDIT+2^PSIVEDT. This error occurred when the Med route field was edited."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",1,1,53,0)="Routine PSIVEDT was changed to correct this error."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,0)="2^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^30^30^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,2,0)="1. An error would occur when printing a MAR label through CPRS if the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,3,0)="order contained missing data. This patch will prevent this error. (NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,4,0)="CTX-0198-71417) "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,6,0)="2. If a Unit Dose order had a Schedule that contained ""PRN"", the Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,7,0)="type would automatically default to CONTINUOUS if the user was using the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,8,0)="Abbreviated Order Entry process.  This patch will change the default"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,9,0)="Schedule Type to PRN if the order's schedule contains ""PRN""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,11,0)="3. When using Inpatient Order Entry, the user should not be allowed to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,12,0)="finish an order entered as an IV Fluid in Unit Dose.  This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,13,0)="prevent Fluid orders from being transferred to Unit Dose during the finish"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,14,0)="process.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,16,0)="4. A change was made to prevent the deletion of a dispense drug from an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,17,0)="active unit dose order.  The user may enter an inactive date for the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,18,0)="dispense drug that is no longer to be used."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,20,0)="5. When editing the SELF MED prompt for an order, an undefined error would"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,21,0)="occur if the user entered ""1"" instead of ""Y"" for yes.  The software will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,22,0)="now recognize ""1"" for YES and ""0"" for NO at this prompt."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,24,0)="6. An error was occurring when the user entered a leading zero when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,25,0)="choosing fields 1-9 in a Unit Dose order. This patch will prevent this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,26,0)="occurence. (NOIS SFC-0198-61889, SFC-0198-61890)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,28,0)="7. In the Inpatient Medications 5.0 KIDS build, three routines were"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,29,0)="mistakenly left out of this build.  PSJORMA1,PSJORMA2, and PSJORMAR are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",2,1,30,0)="correctly reinstalled by this patch. (NOIS CTX-0398-70640)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",3,0)="1^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^10^10^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",3,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",3,1,2,0)="1. This patch includes routines to reduce the number of variables in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",3,1,3,0)="user's partition at the time order changes are communicated between"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",3,1,4,0)="pharmacy and Computerized Patient Record System. These changes should"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",3,1,5,0)="reduce the likelihood of the user encountering an Allocation error during"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",3,1,6,0)="the order processing functions."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",3,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",3,1,8,0)="2. A change was made to correct an undefined variable error that occurred"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",3,1,9,0)="when finishing an order that was entered through the CPRS GUI.  NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",3,1,10,0)="WPB-0398-3258"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,0)="3^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^18^18^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="This patch includes routines, options, and partial Data Dictionary"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,2,0)="components that address Software Quality Assurance issues found for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,3,0)="version 5. This patch corrects these issues."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,6,0)="Some of the QA issues resolved:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,8,0)="- Removal of nonstandard reference to global ^DISV(."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,9,0)="- Removal of nonstandard reference to global ^XUTL(."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,10,0)="- Removal of nonstandard reference to global ^DGPM(."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,11,0)="- Write commands in the Data Dictionary were converted to EN^DDIOL calls."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,12,0)="- Removal of variable kills of % variables."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,13,0)="- Variable DT sets were changed to supported $$DT^XLFDT calls."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,14,0)="- References to ^DD were changed to FileMan supported D FIELD^DID calls."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,15,0)="- Many routines that are no longer used were deleted in the Version 5.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,16,0)=" install.  This patch deletes the corresponding options."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,17,0)="- Removal of nonstandard reference to ^DIC(9.4. These were changed to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",4,1,18,0)=" supported $$VERSION^XPDUTL calls."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,0)="5^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,0)="^^37^37^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,1,0)="1. In Inpatient Medications V. 4.5 and Order Entry Results Reporting"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,2,0)="(OERR) V. 2.5, orders for outpatient IVs could be entered for a patient in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,3,0)="OERR. These IV orders were then finished in pharmacy.  If a Unit Dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,4,0)="order was mistakenly entered for an Outpatient, the pharmacist would"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,5,0)="notice this and discontinue the order. In Inpatient Medications V. 5.0,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,6,0)="the pharmacist can no longer Discontinue these erroneous Outpatient Unit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,7,0)="Dose orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,9,0)="2. This patch allows the installer to queue a background task that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,10,0)="searches for Unit Dose orders that were entered for outpatients through"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,11,0)="OERR V. 2.5. The orders would normally be discontinued if the patient is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,12,0)="admitted again. This task finds the patients that have never admitted"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,13,0)="again since these orders were entered. The pending orders will have their"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,14,0)="status changed to Discontinued."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,16,0)="3. A second job is also queued for the same time that corrects a problem"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,17,0)="found in the Unit Dose Verification fields cross-references in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,18,0)="NON-VERIFIED ORDERS file (#53.1).  Some orders that were verified by a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,19,0)="Pharmacist or Nurse were not having the corresponding Pharmacist or Nurse"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,20,0)="cross-reference set correctly for the order.  This task will go through"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,21,0)="these cross-references checking each one.  When one is found to be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,22,0)="erroneous it will be corrected."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,24,0)="4. This patch also includes a change to correct an error that can occur"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,25,0)="during the Pick List Conversion.  Changes were made to prevent bad pick"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,26,0)="list entries from causing an error when the pick list is reindexed.  When"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,27,0)="the pick list is purged, the bad entries will be deleted."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,29,0)="NOTE: You will see the KIDS Install question only if the Computerized"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,30,0)="Patient Record System (CPRS) Patient Order conversion has finished.  These"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,31,0)="two tasks can only run after the CPRS Order conversion has completed. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,32,0)="can be checked by D STATUS^OR3CONV1. If the CPRS Order conversion has not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,33,0)="finished, the post install routine for this patch will not run.  The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,34,0)="change to routine PSJIPST3 will allow these two tasks to be queued up"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,35,0)="automatically when the CPRS conversion finishes."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",5,1,37,0)="It is recommended that this job be queued to run at a non-peak hour."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,0)="8^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,0)="^^24^24^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,1,0)="1. This patch makes changes to print a four digit year on all MARS, Action"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,2,0)="profile 1 and 2, and Authorized Absense/Discharge Summary report.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,3,0)="action is taken to prepare for the year 2000."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,5,0)="2. A problem was reported in Inpatient Medications version 4.5 for the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,6,0)="Action Profile #1 report. If only five or six orders printed for a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,7,0)="patient, extra lines didn't print in the ""Additional Medication Orders"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,8,0)="section for the physician to enter notes or additional orders.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,9,0)="will correct this for Inpatient Medications version 5.0."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,11,0)="3. An undefined variable error was occurring on the Action Profile #1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,12,0)="report if the patient didn't have a room/bed assignment.  This patch makes"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,13,0)="a change to routine PSGAP0 to correct this."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,15,0)="4. A problem was reported on the 14 Day MAR report.  If MARs for multiple"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,16,0)="patients were being printed, the patient's initials in the order label"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,17,0)="were sometimes printing incorrectly.  This patch makes a change to routine"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,18,0)="PSGMAR1 and PSGMMAR1 to correct this."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,20,0)="5. A problem was reported that after installation of Adverse Reaction"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,21,0)="Tracking patch GMRA*4*10, the No Known Allergies (NKA) message was not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,22,0)="printing correctly on the MAR sheets.  This patch makes a change so that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,23,0)="the NKA message will print appropriately with or without GMRA*4*10 being"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",6,1,24,0)="installed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,0)="7^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^76^76^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,1,0)="1. If an order contained a dispense drug marked as inactive in the DRUG"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,2,0)="file (#50), a message stating ""(ONE OR ALL DISPENSE DRUGS ARE CURRENTLY"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,3,0)="LISTED AS INACTIVE OR DO NOT MATCH THE ORDERABLE ITEM FOR THIS ORDER.)"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,4,0)="was displayed twice. This patch eliminates this message and instead"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,5,0)="displays ""INVALID DISPENSE DRUG"" or ""INVALID ORDERABLE ITEM"" in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,6,0)="message field of the order display. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,9,0)="2. If a dispense drug was assigned a past inactive date in a Unit Dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,10,0)="order, it was still checked for validity. After installing this patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,11,0)="drugs marked as inactive within an order are not checked."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,14,0)="3. If a pharmacist or nurse who had AUTO-VERIFY disabled renewed a Unit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,15,0)="Dose order, the order was created as non-verified. This patch will cause"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,16,0)="orders created due to renew by a pharmacist or nurse in pharmacy to be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,17,0)="created as active. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,19,0)="4. An error would occur if an order containing an inactive dispense drug"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,20,0)="was completed using the Speed Finish action in pharmacy. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,21,0)="eliminates the error. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,24,0)="5. A ListMan variable (VALMCNT) was getting killed during the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,25,0)="Record Update action on a patient's profile screen.  If the profile had"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,26,0)="more that one screen, upon exiting the Patient Record Update edit the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,27,0)="profile screen length would be incorrectly reduced."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,30,0)="6. When the user chose a range of orders to finish from any profile"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,31,0)="screen a ""^"" or ""^^"" entered at any order would not let the user exit from"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,32,0)="this list.  A change was made to ensure that the user can exit at any time"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,33,0)="from their chosen list of orders by entering ""^^"" or ""^""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,36,0)="7. If an order entered through Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,37,0)="met the criteria:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,38,0)="a) The Orderable Item has a default Schedule Type entered. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,39,0)="b) An order entered through CPRS contains ""PRN"" in the SCHEDULE field."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,40,0)="When this order was finished the SCHEDULE field containing ""PRN"" was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,41,0)="causing the default Schedule Type from the PHARMACY ORDERABLE ITEM file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,42,0)="(#50.7) to be overwritten with a Schedule Type of ""PRN"".  This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,43,0)="correct this."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,46,0)="8. An error occurred when a ""-"" character was entered at the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,47,0)="Administration time prompt when finishing an order.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,50,0)="9. A problem occurred when a user's INPATIENT PROFILE ORDER SORT parameter"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,51,0)="was set to START DATE OF ORDER.  Orders that were pending renewals could"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,52,0)="not be chosen correctly from the profile for Speed Finish."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,55,0)="10. A change was made that displays all order check descriptions from CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,56,0)="on the screen when finishing an IV order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,59,0)="11. When finishing a Unit Dose pending order, the Comments field is not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,60,0)="displayed on the screen.  This patch will display the Comments field and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,61,0)="allow user to edit this field while finishing order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,64,0)="12. If a non-verified Unit Dose order was edited by a pharmacist and MAR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,65,0)="labels were to be generated, an incorrect ^(7) node would be created in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,66,0)="the NON-VERIFIED ORDERS file (#53.1). Also, the label generated for the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,67,0)="new order would show a reason of ""ORDER"" instead of ""NEW ORDER (EDIT)""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,68,0)="This patch corrects these problems and deletes the erroneous ^(7) nodes."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,70,0)="13. When finishing a Unit Dose pending order without a dispense drug, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,71,0)="user can only enter one dispense drug and must edit the order to enter"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,72,0)="extra dispense drug.  This patch will allow user to enter multiple"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,73,0)="dispense drugs without having to edit the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,75,0)="14. Variable XT was undefined when finishing an IV pending order.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",7,1,76,0)="patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,0)="9^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,0)="^^31^31^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,1,0)="1. A request was made to change the default to ""No"" for the prompt ""Is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,2,0)="the Formulary Alternative acceptable"".  This will prevent the order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,3,0)="from being finished if an accidental return is hit for this prompt."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,6,0)="2. A change was made to incorporate the expansion text of a schedule "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,7,0)="in the Special Instructions for an order.  If the schedule has an "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,8,0)="expansion text and is used in the Special Instructions, it will now be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,9,0)="displayed in the Special Instructions."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,12,0)="3. A change was made to correct an undefined variable error that "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,13,0)="could occur when the protocol PSJ OR PAT PR (Inpatient Medications "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,14,0)="Profile) was accessed from the Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,15,0)="options."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,18,0)="4. A change was made to display the possible IV Identifier when "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,19,0)="choosing Orderable Items on the Patients on Specific Drug(s) and the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,20,0)="Drug (Cost and/or Amount) reports."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,23,0)="5. The option CAtegory File (IV) [PSJI IVCATEGORY] was mistakenly "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,24,0)="removed from the SUPervisor's Menu (IV) [PSJI SUPERVISOR] menu "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,25,0)="for Inpatient Medications 5.0.  This option will be reinstalled in this "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,26,0)="patch."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,29,0)="6. A change was made on the Action Profile reports.  If the IV order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,30,0)="contains no additives, a blank line will print for the additive and the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",8,1,31,0)="solutions will print on the following line."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",9,0)="13^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",9,1,0)="^^5^5^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",9,1,1,0)="Pharmacy Data Management (PDM) creates the ""AUDS"" cross-reference on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",9,1,2,0)="START DATE/TIME field (#10) of the UNIT DOSE subfile (#55.06) of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",9,1,3,0)="PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55).  This patch will ensure that cross-reference"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",9,1,4,0)="is set when new Unit Dose orders are created and re-index the ""AUDS"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",9,1,5,0)="cross-reference for existing orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,0)="11^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^37^37^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,1,0)="1. This patch corrects a problem where the current date/time was used to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,2,0)="calculate the default start date/time when the order was speed finished by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,3,0)="pharmacy. These changes will cause the login date/time of the first order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,4,0)="selected in the group to be finished to be used instead.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,6,0)="2. An error would sometimes occur when renewing a Unit Dose order if the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,7,0)="Orderable Item for the order contained a day or dose limit. These changes"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,8,0)="will prevent the error and allow the day/dose limit entered to be used in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,9,0)="calculating the stop date for the new renewal order.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,11,0)="3. A problem was found where a expired renewed order could be listed on"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,12,0)="the pick list and then again if an update was run for that pick list. If a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,13,0)="Unit Dose order was renewed with a future start date the original order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,14,0)="would be shown on the pick list as expired and then again as expired if an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,15,0)="update was run for that pick list. This patch will cause the order to only"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,16,0)="be listed on the original pick list."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,18,0)="4. A problem was found where the previous order number was not returned to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,19,0)="Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) when a pending Inpatient Med"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,20,0)="order was edited by pharmacy during the finish process. This change will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,21,0)="cause the previous order number to be returned in all situations where a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,22,0)="new order is created due to edit by pharmacy."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,24,0)="5. This patch corrects an error which would occur when a pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,25,0)="supported reference call was invoked by the CPRS Graphic User Interface"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,26,0)="(GUI). After installation of this patch the call to TERM^VALM0 will not be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,27,0)="performed if the call was issued by the Broker."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,29,0)="6. If the Dosage Ordered field is edited on an active order and the user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,30,0)="just hits <RET> and didn't change the value, the order would incorrectly"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,31,0)="be flagged as having a change and a new order would be created.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,32,0)="patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,34,0)="7. CPRS requested that the order control code be changed from OC to UR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,35,0)="when an order cannot be removed from hold through CPRS. This change will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,36,0)="allow CPRS to display the reason the action could not be taken to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",10,1,37,0)="user."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",11,0)="14^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^2^2^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="This patch is designed to make use of the Application Programmer"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",11,1,2,0)="Interfaces (APIs) provided by the National Drug file (NDF) application."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,0)="10^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^21^21^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="1. A problem was reported with the LABEL PRINTER field (#.07) in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,2,0)="INPATIENT USER PARAMETERS file (#53.45), WARD LABEL PRINTER field (#.13)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,3,0)="and PHARMACY LABEL PRINTER field (#.14) in the INPATIENT WARD PARAMETERS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,4,0)="file (#59.6), and the BAXTER ATC DEVICE field (#30) in the WARD GROUP file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,5,0)="(#57.5).  These fields store the name of entries in the DEVICE file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,6,0)="(#3.5).  The fields currently have the data type of Free Text.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,7,0)="causes problems if the device name is ever changed in the DEVICE file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,8,0)="(#3.5).  Until the new name is entered into these fields in the Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,9,0)="Medications package, the pharmacy order labels will not print or Pick"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,10,0)="Lists will not be sent correctly to the ATC device.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,12,0)="This patch will create and populate new fields that are Pointer data types"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,13,0)="by converting the old device names stored in the old fields to their"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,14,0)="internal entry values in the DEVICE file (#3.5).  This will permit the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,15,0)="device names to be changed without any disruption to the printing of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,16,0)="pharmacy labels.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,18,0)="2. A change to address NOIS WNY-0197-12396 was not included in version"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,19,0)="5.0.  The ATC-212 device will hang if an 'ON CALL' order is sent to it."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,20,0)="This was reported in NOIS WNY-0598-10164.  This patch will make the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",12,1,21,0)="correct change to routine PSGTAP1 and PSGPLR."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,0)="17^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,0)="^^23^23^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,1,0)="This patch adds functionality requested in E3R #9551.    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,3,0)="When the Patient Information Management System (PIMS) deletes a patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,4,0)="movement, the medication orders that were discontinued due to the deletion"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,5,0)="are automatically reinstated.  A mail message will be sent to notify"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,6,0)="affected parties that a patient's medications have been reinstated."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,7,0)="Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 has been modified to include this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,8,0)="functionality.     "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,10,0)="* A mail group named PSJ-ORDERS REINSTATED is created by the patch KIDS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,11,0)="build.  The members of this mail group should be providers, nurses,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,12,0)="pharmacist, etc. who need to know that the patient's medication orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,13,0)="have been automatically reinstated.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,15,0)="*  When the medication orders are automatically reinstated due to deletion"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,16,0)="of a patient movement, a mail message will be sent to the PSJ-ORDERS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,17,0)="REINSTATED mail group.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,19,0)="*  The mail message will contain the patient's name, last four digits of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,20,0)="the patient's social security number, current ward location, reason the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,21,0)="orders were reinstated, and a list of orders that were reinstated. The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,22,0)="orders will be listed in the mail message in exact format as a patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",13,1,23,0)="profile."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",14,0)="18^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",14,1,0)="^^7^7^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",14,1,1,0)="Inpatient Medications has been requested to send the clinic location's"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",14,1,2,0)="Internal Entry Number (IEN) to Decision Support System (DSS) along with"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",14,1,3,0)="the IV data currently sent.  DSS loads this data into a DSS file for later"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",14,1,4,0)="extract to the vendor.  With this change, Inpatient Medications V.5.0 will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",14,1,5,0)="prompt for the CLINIC LOCATION for Outpatient IV orders enter from the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",14,1,6,0)="Inpatient Medications package.  The clinic location will be stored in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",14,1,7,0)="Inpatient Medications and Order Entry/Results Reporting (OE/RR) packages."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,0)="12^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,0)="^^29^29^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,1,0)="1.  An error was reported that occurred when a unit dose order set was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,2,0)="being entered.  A variable was not being cleaned up between the processing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,3,0)="of one order to the next in the order set.  If the user edited a field but"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,4,0)="didn't change the value, this variable would cause an error when the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,5,0)="following order in the set was being processed.  This patch makes a change"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,6,0)="to routine PSGOES to correct this error.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,8,0)="2.  A problem was found where a single or leading space was being entered"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,9,0)="in the schedule field of a Unit Dose order through Computerized Patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,10,0)="Record System (CPRS) and pharmacy. These changes prevent the entry of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,11,0)="these in the schedule field through pharmacy and will reject any orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,12,0)="sent from CPRS with these type of schedules."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,14,0)="3.  The ONE-TIME/PRN MAR prints 10 blank lines for initials and notes at"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,15,0)="bottom half of the MAR sheet.  At the sites request, this patch will print"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,16,0)="20 blank lines as in previous version of Inpatient Medications."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,18,0)="4. A problem was reported with Service (Total Cost per) [PSJU SCT]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,19,0)="report.  Patch 3 introduced a problem that caused the report to not total"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,20,0)="information correctly by service.  This patch corrects this problem.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,22,0)="5. A problem was reported with IV labels not getting cleaned up"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,23,0)="appropriately in the MAR LABELS file (#53.41).  The MAR labels for these"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,24,0)="discontinued or expired orders were sometimes incorrectly printing on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,25,0)="wards.  This patch corrects this problem.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,27,0)="6. A problem was reported with the Patients on Specific Drug(s) [PSJ PDV]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,28,0)="option.  If the user chooses to print the report by VA Drug Class, IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",15,1,29,0)="orders were not printing correctly. This patch corrects this problem. ."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,0)="15^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^26^26^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,1,0)="1. If the user chose a printer device and did not wish to queue the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,2,0)="output, the MAR was printed to the screen.  This patch will send the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,3,0)="report to the correct device."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,5,0)="2. When renewing IVs, the default stop date and time is the same as the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,6,0)="renewed order. This patch will calculate the default stop date according"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,7,0)="to the IV Site Parameter."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,9,0)="3. When the Update Daily Ward List (IV) [PSJI UP] option for Hyperal"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,10,0)="orders was selected, the order view did not display on the screen.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,11,0)="patch will display the order view before prompting for the number labels"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,12,0)="needed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,14,0)="4. When a pick list update was ran and an order had been discontinued, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,15,0)="dosage ordered was not printing on the discontinued order. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,16,0)="corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,18,0)="5. An undefined variable XRT0 error was sometimes occurring when using the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,19,0)="hidden actions and trying to print an individual label.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,20,0)="corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,22,0)="6. The hidden action to print the MAR from the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,23,0)="OE] option did not use the default set in the INPATIENT WARD PARAMETERS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,24,0)="file (#59.6) when promping for the MAR's medication types. After"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,25,0)="installation of this patch the default set in the INPATIENT WARD"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",16,1,26,0)="PARAMETERS file (#59.6) will be used."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",17,0)="19^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",17,1,0)="^^4^4^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",17,1,1,0)="1. When non-pharmacist users enter unit dose drug orders they cannot"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",17,1,2,0)="   complete the order without entering a dispense drug.  This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",17,1,3,0)="   allow non-pharmacist users to accept unit dose orders without a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",17,1,4,0)="   dispense drug."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,0)="16^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^35^35^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="1. If the order's START DATE/TIME was the same as the ADMIN TIME, an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,2,0)="extra dose was calculated when the user entered the number of doses in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,3,0)="STOP DATE/TIME field. After installation of this patch the dosage will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,4,0)="calculate correctly for this situation."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,6,0)="2. If an order was placed on hold and then taken off of hold the Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,7,0)="profile printed by the pharmacist showed the order as active while the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,8,0)="same profile printed by the nurse showed the order as marked to be placed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,9,0)="on hold. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,11,0)="3. Orders were being rejected with a message Invalid patient class. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,12,0)="patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,14,0)="4. An undefined variable P(17) was sometimes occurring when returning from"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,15,0)="hidden menu options when finishing an order. This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,16,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,18,0)="5. When using the Individual Labels (IV) [PSJI LBLI] option, the first"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,19,0)="patient's Allergies/Reactions and Narratives were displayed for all"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,20,0)="patients selected while still in this option. This patch will correct this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,21,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,23,0)="6. The variable PSIVSITE was undefined when IV orders were edited by the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,24,0)="nursing staff in the Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW] option."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,25,0)="Showing IV orders in this option is new functionality added to Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,26,0)="Medications V. 5.0. Actions taken on IV orders have always been controlled"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,27,0)="by the Menu option and not from any pharmacy keys. After installation of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,28,0)="this patch users without the Pharmacist key will not be allowed to take"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,29,0)="action on IV orders from the Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,30,0)="option."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,32,0)="7. A problem was reported with the Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,33,0)="option where when the user selected pending orders, Unit Dose orders, and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,34,0)="then Ward or Ward group patients with only pending IV orders were being"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",18,1,35,0)="included in the list of patients. This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,0)="20^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,0)="^^71^71^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,1,0)="1. IVPB orders had asterisks across all the dated boxes on the MAR even"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,2,0)="   though the orders were still acitve.  After the installation of this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,3,0)="   patch the asterisks will print on the correct dates."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,5,0)="2. Add the institution name to the following reports (E3R#11366):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,6,0)="       7 Day MAR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,7,0)="       14 Day MAR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,8,0)="       24 Hour MAR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,9,0)="       Action Profile #1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,10,0)="       Action Profile #2"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,11,0)="       Patient Profile (Extended)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,13,0)="3. The MAR will be able to be sorted by the orders schedule type or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,14,0)="   alphabetically by the medication names.  The following are steps to use"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,15,0)="   to set the sorting of the MAR:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,17,0)="Select OPTION NAME: PSJU MGR          Unit Dose Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,19,0)="(Inpatient Medications - Version 5.0  //)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,21,0)="WELCOME, PHARMACIST,ABC!  (PHARMACIST)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,24,0)="          Align Labels (Unit Dose)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,25,0)="          Discontinue All of a Patient's Orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,26,0)="   EUP    Edit Inpatient User Parameters"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,27,0)="          Hold All of a Patient's Orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,28,0)="   IOE    Inpatient Order Entry"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,29,0)="   IPF    Inpatient Profile"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,30,0)="          INQuiries Menu ..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,31,0)="          Label Print/Reprint"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,32,0)="          Non-Verified/Pending Orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,33,0)="          Order Entry"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,34,0)="          PAtient Profile (Unit Dose)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,35,0)="          Reports Menu ..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,36,0)="          Supervisor's Menu ..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,39,0)="Select Unit Dose Medications Option: SUPervisor's Menu"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,42,0)="          Administering Teams"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,43,0)="          MANagement Reports Menu ..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,44,0)="          Order Set Enter/Edit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,45,0)="          PARameters Edit Menu ..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,46,0)="          PATient Order Purge"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,47,0)="          PIck List Menu ..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,48,0)="          Ward Groups"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,51,0)="Select Supervisor's Menu Option: PARameters Edit Menu"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,54,0)="          AUto-Discontinue Set-Up"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,55,0)="   IUP    Inpatient User Parameters Edit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,56,0)="   IWP    Inpatient Ward Parameters Edit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,57,0)="          Systems Parameters Edit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,60,0)="Select PARameters Edit Menu Option: SYStems Parameters Edit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,62,0)="NON-FORMULARY MESSAGE:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,63,0)="  1>This is the Non formulary message!!!"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,64,0)="EDIT Option: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,65,0)="PRINT 6 BLOCKS FOR THE PRN MAR: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,66,0)="PRINT DIET ABBR LABEL ON MAR: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,67,0)="MAR SORT: ?"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,68,0)="     Choose from: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,69,0)="       0        Sort by order's Schedule Type and then Medication Names."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,70,0)="       1        Sort by order's Medication Names."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",19,1,71,0)="MAR SORT: 1  Sort by order's Medication Names."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,0)="21^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,0)="^^28^28^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,1,0)="1.  The original IV Solution's volume has an upper limit of 4000ml."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,2,0)="    This patch will increase the volume to 9999ml to meet the needs of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,3,0)="    sites to enter solutions with a volume greater than 40."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,4,0)="    TO TEST:  Edit the Solution's volume to 9999."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,6,0)="2.  This patch will add the IV Solution's PRINT NAME {2} field (#.02),"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,7,0)="    from the IV SOLUTIONS file (#52.7), to the MAR label, 24 Hour and 7/14"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,8,0)="    Day MARs."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,9,0)="    TO TEST: Enter a new IV order with a solution that has the PRINT"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,10,0)="              NAME {2} field (#.02) defined in the IV SOLUTIONS file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,11,0)="              (#52.7) and print the MAR label, and the MAR."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,13,0)="3.  When entering a new IV order the user edits the Stop date, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,14,0)="    default Stop date for the next IV order will be blank.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,15,0)="    will make sure the default Stop date is displayed correctly."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,16,0)="    TO TEST: Enter a nw IV order, change the Stop date to a different"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,17,0)="             value than the default date, accept the order.  Enter another"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,18,0)="             new IV order, the Stop date should have a default value"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,19,0)="             instead of being blank."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,21,0)="4.  When entering a new IV order using a Quick Code with a usual IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,22,0)="    solution defined, the user is then prompted for additional additives."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,23,0)="    When trying to enter additional additives the user may  choose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,24,0)="    from solutions."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,25,0)="    TO TEST:  Enter a new IV order using a Quick Code with a usual IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,26,0)="              solution defined, then try entering additional additives"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,27,0)="              at the ADDITIVE: prompt or ?? the listing will display"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",20,1,28,0)="              additives correctly now."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,0)="24^2990416^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,0)="^^20^20^2990416"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,1,0)="E3R 11894 brought up the problem of orders containing drugs with a 2 in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,2,0)="the DEA SPECIAL HANDLING field (#3) in the DRUG file (#50) printing on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,3,0)="AUTHORIZED ABSENCE/DISCHARGE ORDERS report instead of the following"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,4,0)="warning:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,6,0)="*********************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,7,0)="*  THIS IS A SCHEDULE II DRUG.  A PRESCRIPTION BLANK    * "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,8,0)="*  (VA FORM 10-2277d) MUST BE USED TO ORDER THIS DRUG.  *"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,9,0)="*********************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,11,0)="In Inpatient Medications Version 4.5 there was a field in the PRIMARY DRUG"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,12,0)="file (#50.3), DEA SPECIAL HANDLING (#.02), which Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,13,0)="used to check.  If the field contained a 2 the AUTHORIZED"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,14,0)="ABSENCE/DISCHARGE ORDERS report would contain the warning."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,16,0)="In version 5.0 there is no DEA SPECIAL HANDLING field in the ORDERABLE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,17,0)="ITEM file (#50.7). After installation of this patch the Dispense Drugs in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,18,0)="the order will be checked and if any of those contain a 2 in the DEA"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,19,0)="SPECIAL HANDLING field (#3) in the DRUG file (#50) then the warning will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",21,1,20,0)="print."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,0)="22 SEQ #22^2990427^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,0)="^^34^34^2990427"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,2,0)="1. An inconsistency was noted when entering orders for patients where no"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,3,0)="orders were found for the profile selected.  When using the option Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,4,0)="Entry [PSJU NE] the user was returned to the Select PATIENT: prompt. When"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,5,0)="using the option Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] the user was prompted"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,6,0)="Select DRUG:.  After installation of this patch both options will prompt"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,7,0)="Select DRUG:."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,9,0)="2. A problem was reported in the generation of labels during the entry of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,10,0)="a unit dose order set.  If the pharmacist entering the orders had the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,11,0)="automatic verification user parameter set to ""Yes"", the labels weren't"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,12,0)="printing correctly for the orders.  This patch will correct this problem. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,14,0)="3. A problem was reported with the Patients on Specific Drug(s) [PSJ PDV]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,15,0)="option.  If the user searched on an entry in the PHARMACY ORDERABLE ITEM"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,16,0)="file (#50.7), the report could erroneously print orders for the DRUG file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,17,0)="(#50) entry with the same internal entry number.  This patch will correct"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,18,0)="this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,20,0)="4. A problem was reported where a user accessed the option Order Entry    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,21,0)="[PSJU NE], then the user accessed the option Label Print/Reprint [PSJU"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,22,0)="LABEL] either from the hidden menu or the regular menu and was unable to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,23,0)="select orders greater than 13.  The help text for this option displayed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,24,0)="when the user entered '??' was not appropriate either.  This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,25,0)="correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,27,0)="5. An error could possibly occur in routine PSGAL5 when running the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,28,0)="Duplicate Patient Merge software.  This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,30,0)="6. An undefined variable DA error was reported when discontinuing an order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,31,0)="within a unit dose order set.  If the pharmacist has Auto Verify turned"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,32,0)="on, an undefined error can occur when an order set is entered and one of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,33,0)="the orders is discontinued before finishing the order set.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",22,1,34,0)="will correct this error."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,0)="25 SEQ #23^2990602^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,0)="^^19^19^2990602"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,1,0)="1. A subscript error was occurring at WS+4^PSGPL1 for some Ward Stock"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,2,0)="items that had a ""D"" x-ref and no ""B"" x-ref.  This patch will correct this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,3,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,5,0)="2. A problem was reported where a site was finishing orders.  The first"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,6,0)="order they finished was an IV order; the next order to be finished was a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,7,0)="Unit Dose order.  The user selected edit and entered ""??"" and received a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,8,0)="list of IV fields for selection.  This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,10,0)="3. A problem was reported where orders entered thru Computerized Patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,11,0)="Record Systems (CPRS) with a schedule of PO QD or QD NOON and then"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,12,0)="finished in Inpatient Medications were printing on the Medication"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,13,0)="Administration Record (MAR) with every other day starred out. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,14,0)="will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,16,0)="4. An erroneous ""Pre-Exchange DOSES:"" prompt could occur when entering a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,17,0)="Unit Dose Order Set.  If one of the orders is discontinued while entering"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,18,0)="the order set, the user may be prompted for Pre-Exchange DOSES"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",23,1,19,0)="incorrectly.  This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",24,0)="23 SEQ #24^2990628^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",24,1,0)="^^7^7^2990628"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",24,1,1,0)="This patch adds a ""Requesting PROVIDER"" prompt to the discontinue and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",24,1,2,0)="speed discontinue dialogue.  When an order is now discontinued, this new"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",24,1,3,0)="prompt will be asked after the ""Nature of Order"" prompt.  The requesting"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",24,1,4,0)="provider information will be used to update the Computerized Patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",24,1,5,0)="Record System (CPRS) order.  The CPRS order will now reflect the correct"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",24,1,6,0)="provider that requested the discontinue of the order.  This patch adds"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",24,1,7,0)="this functionality."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,0)="26 SEQ #25^2990719^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,0)="^^45^45^2990719"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,1,0)="1. A problem was reported with the default start date/time on IV orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,2,0)="An IV order was placed on 2/9 @ 10:00am with a schedule of QD.  The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,3,0)="schedule had an admin time of 09.  The order was finished on 2/10 before"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,4,0)="09:00am and the default start date/time showed 2/11 @ 09:00am.  The ward"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,5,0)="parameter was set to use next admin time. This patch will correct this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,6,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,8,0)="2. When creating a new Unit Dose order in Inpatient Medications, it was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,9,0)="sometimes possible to lose edits on the Start Date and Stop Date fields."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,10,0)="If these fields were edited before accepting the order, the changes were"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,11,0)="sometimes lost.  This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,13,0)="3. This patch will run a post install routine, PSJ0026, to clean up"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,14,0)="erroneous ""AC"" cross-reference nodes in the PICK LIST file (#53.5).  The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,15,0)="post install routine identifies ""AC"" cross-reference nodes that do not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,16,0)="have a corresponding zero node entry.  These erroneous cross-reference"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,17,0)="nodes will be deleted."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,19,0)="4. A problem was reported where a one-time order was incorrectly entered"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,20,0)="by a ward clerk via pharmacy options.  The order was then verified by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,21,0)="nursing through pharmacy options, when the pharmacist viewed the expired"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,22,0)="order he/she was not able to dc this order.  The order was non-verified by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,23,0)="the pharmacist and remained on the active profile.  This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,24,0)="correct this problem.  The pharmacist will be allowed to dc or verify"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,25,0)="non-verified expired orders just as he/she could in version 4.5."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,27,0)="5. A problem was reported with the labels printed through Computerized"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,28,0)="Patient Record Systems (CPRS).  The labels did not reflect the status of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,29,0)="the order.  After installation of this patch the label node of each order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,30,0)="will be updated if the parameters are set to auto-print labels through"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,31,0)="CPRS the same way this functionality works for Inpatient Medications."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,33,0)="6. On Unit Dose order entry, the duplicate drug order check is not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,34,0)="alerting nursing or ward clerks of duplicate drugs. This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,35,0)="correct that problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,37,0)="7. A problem was found in the Stop Date calculation when finishing pending"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,38,0)="orders from Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS).  If an Orderable"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,39,0)="Item had a default schedule type of Fill on Request and a One Time"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,40,0)="schedule was entered for the order, the stop date was not being calculated"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,41,0)="correctly.  This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,43,0)="8. A problem would sometimes occur on the DA DETAILED ALLERGY/ADR LIST"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,44,0)="ListMan screen.  The ListMan screen header would sometimes print ""Page 1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",25,1,45,0)="of 0"".  This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,0)="27 SEQ #26^2990719^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,0)="^^41^41^2990719"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,1,0)="1. This patch will update the activity log for orders that are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,2,0)="discontinued by Computerized Patient Record Systems (CPRS) due to a change"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,3,0)="in Treating Specialty.  It adds a new entry to the ACTIVITY LOG REASON"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,4,0)="file (#53.3).  The new entry is 1040 AUTO DISCONTINUED (TREATING SPECIALTY"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,5,0)="TRANSFER)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,7,0)="***************************PLEASE NOTE************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,8,0)="While this patch doesn't require OR*3*45, the functionality will not work"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,9,0)="as intended without patch OR*3*45."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,10,0)="**************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,12,0)="2.  When queuing an Extra Units Dispensed Report to a printer the last"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,13,0)="line was not being printed.  This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,15,0)="3. The Cost at Discharge [PSJU DCR] option was mistakenly left out of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,16,0)="Inpatient Medications version 5.0 distribution.  This option is no longer"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,17,0)="used. This patch will distribute the option as Delete at Site."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,19,0)="4. A problem was identified with the auto-reinstate feature.  A patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,20,0)="had an active order that was auto-discontinued upon ward transfer.  He was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,21,0)="then issued a new order for the same drug. The transfer was later deleted"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,22,0)="and his previous meds were reinstated.  As a result, the patient ended up"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,23,0)="with 2 duplicate orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,25,0)="Checks have now been included to prevent the reinstatement of an order if"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,26,0)="a new duplicate order has been added.  For IVs, if the order to be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,27,0)="reinstated has any additive the same as the new order it will not be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,28,0)="reinstated."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,30,0)="The notification e-mail, advising of medication orders automatically"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,31,0)="reinstated, has also been amended to include any orders that could not be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,32,0)="re-instated due to duplicates existing on the system. The recipient list"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,33,0)="for the e-mail also now includes the verifying nurse, verifying"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,34,0)="pharmacist, the physician, the provider and who entered the record (where"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,35,0)="applicable)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,37,0)="5.  When using the ""edit intervention"" after a critical interaction comes"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,38,0)="up on UD order entry, the prompt ""Intervention"" came up with the default"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,39,0)="of ALLERGY instead of CRITICAL INTERACTION.  This has now been amended so"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,40,0)="that if a Critical or a Significant drug interaction is detected, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",26,1,41,0)="appropriate default is used. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",27,0)="28 SEQ #27^2990719^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",27,1,0)="^^8^8^2990719"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",27,1,1,0)="When a nurse verifies a pending Inpatient Medications order through CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",27,1,2,0)="(Computerized Patient Record System), his/her initials are printed on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",27,1,3,0)="MAR and MAR label.  If the nurse verifies the order after it becomes"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",27,1,4,0)="active, the initials are not printed on the MAR and MAR label.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",27,1,5,0)="will allow the nurse's initials to be printed regardless of the order's"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",27,1,6,0)="status when it was verified.  This patch will also ensure the order only"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",27,1,7,0)="needs to be verified once through either the CPRS or Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",27,1,8,0)="package."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,0)="30 SEQ #28^2990914^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,0)="^^68^68^2990914"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,1,0)="1. The Patients on Specific Drug(s) [PSJ PDV] report was mistakenly using"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,2,0)="the wrong cross-reference when printing the report and searching by VA"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,3,0)="Drug Class. This patch will correct this problem. NOIS WPB-0499-33064"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,6,0)="2. Version 4.5 of Inpatient Medications allowed '@N' after schedule for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,7,0)="piggybacks as it did with admixtures with infusion rate.  In this version,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,8,0)="this was lost for piggybacks and syringes since their formatting is the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,9,0)="same. This patch will return this functionality. NOIS REN-0399-63066"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,12,0)="3. After admitting a patient, if an Inpatient Medications order was placed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,13,0)="in the Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) and the admission was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,14,0)="subsequently cancelled, it was still possible to Finish the order in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,15,0)="Pharmacy resulting in an Active order for an outpatient."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,17,0)="The deletion of an admission has been amended so that any orders placed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,18,0)="for the patient, Active, Non-Verified or Pending, are removed. NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,19,0)="BIR-0499-31870"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,22,0)="4. An undefined variable PSGEFN error could sometimes occur after"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,23,0)="exercising the hidden menu options under the Inpatient Order Entry"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,24,0)="option [PSJ OE].  This patch will correct this error.  NOIS HUN-0599-20774"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,27,0)="5. The generation of order labels was not functioning correctly for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,28,0)="non-pharmacist staff when entering unit dose order sets.  This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,29,0)="correct this problem. NOIS BOI-0499-52931"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,31,0)="6. If the Default Start Date Calculation is set to ""Use Closest Admin Time"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,32,0)="As Default"" and the order was edited through CPRS, the original Start"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,33,0)="Date/time was used as a default for the order when finished in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,34,0)="pharmacy. This was a Unit Dose order and it did not have an administration"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,35,0)="time. This patch will correct this problem.  NOIS: CON-0499-11371"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,37,0)="7. This patch will remove two erroneous identifier nodes from the data"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,38,0)="dictionary of the WARD GROUP file (#57.5).  After the installation of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,39,0)="PSJ*5.0*10 these erroneous nodes will display the incorrect printer as an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,40,0)="identifier when doing a look up on the WARD GROUP file (#57.5).  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,41,0)="patch will correct this problem. This patch will also install a new ID"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,42,0)="node for the BAXTER ATC DEVICE POINTER field (#32). NOIS BRK-0599-11977"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,44,0)="8. When renewing a Unit Dose order that had already expired, the software"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,45,0)="would calculate, in version 4.5, the pre-exchange quantity to send.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,46,0)="was facilitated by the presentation of the ""Pre-Exchange DOSES:"" prompt."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,47,0)="In version 5.0 this prompt was being bypassed, continuing on to the next"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,48,0)="order prompt.  This patch will correct this problem.  NOIS MAR-0599-21852."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,50,0)="9. When a pharmacist was verifying a renewed drug order and first called"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,51,0)="up an activity log, the dispense drug was being eliminated from the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,52,0)="The pharmacist could not then verify the order because a field was blank."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,53,0)="This occurred only when an activity log was called up. When the pharmacist"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,54,0)="entered an up-arrow to get out, the order was verified at that point. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,55,0)="patch will correct this problem. NOIS NTH-0699-70263."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,57,0)="10. When entering a Unit Dose order set and editing fields, it was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,58,0)="possible for some edits to not be reflected in the verified order.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,59,0)="patch will correct this problem.  NOIS MIW-0699-40031."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,61,0)="PLEASE NOTE:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,62,0)="Please ignore this message if it is seen on installation of this patch:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,64,0)="** ERROR IN DATA DICTIONARY FOR FILE # 53.3 ** Data Dictionary not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,65,0)="installed; FIA node is set to ""no DD Update"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,67,0)="This file is included with data but doesn't update the data dictionary."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",28,1,68,0)="There is not a problem with the installation of this file."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,0)="32 SEQ #29^2990914^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,0)="^^15^15^2990914"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,1,0)="This patch distributes routines that support the Application Package"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,2,0)="Interfaces (APIs) between Inpatient Medications and Bar Code Medication"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,3,0)="Administration (BCMA)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,5,0)="The following Database Integration Agreements (DBIA) describe these APIs:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,7,0)="2828  The entry point EN^PSJBCMA is provided by Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,8,0)="      to return a patient's active orders to BCMA to be used in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,9,0)="      administering medications at a patient's bedside."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,11,0)="2829  The entry point EN^PSJBCMA1 is provided by Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,12,0)="      to return detailed information on a patient's order for BCMA."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,14,0)="2830  The entry point EN^PSJBCMA2 is provided by Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",29,1,15,0)="      to return a patient order's activity logs for BCMA."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,0)="29 SEQ #30^2990914^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,0)="^^32^32^2990914"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,1,0)="1. This patch introduces changes to the patient and single order locking"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,2,0)="between Inpatient Medications V. 5.0, Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0, and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,3,0)="Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,5,0)="The software will be modified to lock Pharmacy application users at the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,6,0)="patient level when a medication order is selected through the Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,7,0)="Medication V. 5.0 Unit Dose or IV menu options.  This will prevent"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,8,0)="multiple Pharmacy application users from processing medication orders for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,9,0)="the same patient at the same time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,11,0)="The software will be modified to lock all external applications at the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,12,0)="order level when an order is selected through Inpatient Medications for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,13,0)="any action (Renew, Discontinue, Edit, Finish, Verify, Hold, Unhold, On"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,14,0)="Call, Mark Not to be Given, Mark Incomplete, New Order Entry, Copy, Speed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,15,0)="Finish, Speed Renew, Speed Verify or Speed Discontinue)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,17,0)="The software will be modified to provide identification of any external"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,18,0)="application users who are entering orders into the same patient record"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,19,0)="accessed by an Inpatient Medications application user processing orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,20,0)="through Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 for actions generating a new order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,23,0)="2. Currently, Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 software performs order checks"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,24,0)="when a new medication order is placed through either the Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,25,0)="Medications or Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) applications."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,26,0)="The Pharmacy Benefits Management group requested that the Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,27,0)="Medications application provide order checking for orders renewed through"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,28,0)="Inpatient Medications or CPRS packages. This functionality will ensure the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,29,0)="user is alerted to possible adverse reactions and will reduce the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,30,0)="possibility of a medication error due to the omission of an order check"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,31,0)="when a non-active medication order is renewed. This patch will add this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",30,1,32,0)="functionality."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,0)="31 SEQ #31^2991003^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,0)="^^70^70^2991003"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,1,0)="1.  The routine PSGOETO was issuing a lock command with a 0-second wait"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,2,0)="period.  This resulted in a 100% CPU usage by the command because it was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,3,0)="unable to attain the lock required.  The CPU usage meant that other"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,4,0)="routines were prevented from processing.  The timeout period for the lock"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,5,0)="has been amended to 1 second, this will allow other procedures to share"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,6,0)="the system resources.  NOIS SUX-0699-40661."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,8,0)="2. When using the option Label Print/Reprint [PSJU LABEL] a line of text"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,9,0)="would sometimes scroll off the screen when the prompt '^' TO QUIT was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,10,0)="issued.  This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS MWV-0699-22220."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,12,0)="3. Unit Dose orders were entered through Computerized Patient Record"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,13,0)="System (CPRS), but not signed or released.  The patient was discharged,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,14,0)="then these Unit Dose orders were signed and released to the Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,15,0)="Medications package.  These orders were showing in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,16,0)="Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW] option when an order summary was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,17,0)="done under the ward group ^OTHER.  The site could take no action on these"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,18,0)="orders through the Inpatient Medications options.  This patch will prevent"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,19,0)="these orders from being accepted by the Inpatient Medications package and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,20,0)="prevent this problem from taking place.  NOIS MON-0699-52149."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,22,0)="4. Medication orders were Dc'd on transfer, the transfer was deleted."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,23,0)="The orders were reinstated with the MailMan message going to the group"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,24,0)="and the pharmacist.  Some duplicate orders were not reinstated.  The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,25,0)="pharmacist tried to reinstate using the RN function in the long profile."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,26,0)="The user got the message that the order was reinstated, but it wasn't."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,27,0)="This patch corrects this problem. NOIS CON-0799-10709."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,29,0)="5. A problem was reported with some reports when they were queued to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,30,0)="spooler.  The following IV reports: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,32,0)="ACtive Order Report by Ward/Drug (IV) [PSJI AOR]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,33,0)="AMIS (IV) [PSJI AMIS]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,34,0)="Drug Cost Report (132 COLUMNS) (IV) [PSJI DRUG COST REPORT]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,35,0)="Patient Cost Report (132 COLUMNS) (IV) [PSJI PATIENT COST]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,36,0)="PRovider Drug Cost Report (132 COLUMNS) (IV) [PSJI PROVIDER REPORT]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,37,0)="Ward/Drug Usage Report (132 COLUMNS) (IV)[ PSJI WARD/DRUG USAGE REPORT]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,39,0)="and the following Unit Dose reports"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,41,0)="Extra Units Dispensed Report [PSJU EUDD]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,42,0)="Medications Due Worksheet [PSJ MDWS]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,44,0)="were not being processed to completion, resulting in the files never"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,45,0)="becoming available to print. This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,46,0)="BRX-0398-12645, POR-0699-52667 and OKL-0899-70364."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,48,0)="6.  When printing the 7 Day MAR [PSJU 7D MAR] and the 14 Day MAR [PSJU 14D"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,49,0)="MAR] reports, the text for the Other Print Info was sometimes appearing in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,50,0)="the Notes column.  There was also a problem whereby the text of the Other"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,51,0)="Print Info was not wrapping correctly if the text length was greater than"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,52,0)="47 characters.  Also, if the order did not have a solution defined the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,53,0)="lines were not wrapping correctly.  This patch corrects these problems."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,54,0)="NOIS IOW-0599-41089, MWV-0799-20528 and PUG-0899-52623."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,56,0)="7.  A problem was reported where a user accessed the option Extra Units"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,57,0)="Dispensed [PSJU EUD] or Report Returns [PSJU RET] from the hidden menu"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,58,0)="and was unable to select orders greater then 13.  The Help text for this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,59,0)="option displayed when the user entered '??' was not appropriate either."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,60,0)="This patch will correct this problem. NOIS NHM-0699-10837."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,62,0)="8. A problem was reported by a site where when running the option Extra"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,63,0)="Units Dispensed [PSJU EUD] they were getting a message THIS DRUG IS AN ATC"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,64,0)="ITEM. BUT THE ATC DEVICE CANNOT BE FOUND! This was happening on a ward"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,65,0)="they had recently set up. This patch will correct this problem. NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,66,0)="CLE-0899-40919."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,68,0)="9. A problem was identified whereby the option Patient Profile (Extended)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,69,0)="[PSJ EXTP] was not displaying the full activity logs for orders.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",31,1,70,0)="patch will now correct this problem.  NOIS SDC-0899-60673."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,0)="33 SEQ #32^3000125^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,0)="^^18^18^3000125"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,1,0)="1. A problem was reported with the Patients on Specific Drugs report where"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,2,0)="if the patient received an outpatient IV order it would print the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,3,0)="with the ward location and room-bed of their last admission.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,4,0)="corrects this problem.  NOIS MIW-0899-41313"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,6,0)="2. A problem was reported with the pharmacist finishing an order entered"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,7,0)="through Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,8,0)="dialogue.  The pharmacist elected to finish the order as an IV and entered"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,9,0)="a quick code at the additive prompt. The additive name was set, but none"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,10,0)="of the other information from the quick code was entered into the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,11,0)="This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS SDC-0699-61236"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,13,0)="3.  A problem was reported when editing orders that are entered via unit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,14,0)="dose order sets.  During the order set entry, edits made after the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,15,0)="becomes non-verified status are not being reflected in the CPRS order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,16,0)="This patch will make changes to allow the edits of a non-verified order to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,17,0)="be reflected in the CPRS order if the edits are made before the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",32,1,18,0)="non-verified order is accepted.  NOIS MIW-0899-40617"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",33,0)="38 SEQ #33^3000204^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",33,1,0)="^^9^9^3000204"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",33,1,1,0)="1. A problem was reported with a site that had pending order numbers"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",33,1,2,0)="greater the 999999. This was causing a problem with the display and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",33,1,3,0)="selection of the orders through Order Entry (IV) [PSJI ORDER]. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",33,1,4,0)="corrects this problem. NOIS DEN-1299-50190."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",33,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",33,1,6,0)="2. An undefined error occurred when reprinting IV labels.  This error is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",33,1,7,0)="due to the change in FileMan patch DI*22.0*17 which returns a 0 to $T"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",33,1,8,0)="when using the ^DIC call.  This patch will correct this problem. NOIS:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",33,1,9,0)="IOW-1299-41969."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,0)="34 SEQ #34^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,0)="^^48^48^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,1,0)="1. When entering unit dose orders through the pharmacy back door with an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,2,0)="order set, 2 sets of labels were printed after the order is verified."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,3,0)="This was incorrect, only one set of labels should be produced.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,4,0)="corrects that problem.  NOIS MIW-0999-41081."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,6,0)="2. Providers were unable to discontinue orders placed on-call through"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,7,0)="pharmacy back door options using Computerized Patient Record System"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,8,0)="(CPRS) options.  This patch corrects this problem.  E3R 12975 and 12832."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,10,0)="3. When printing a Medications Due Worksheet through the Medications Due"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,11,0)="Worksheet [PSJ MDWS] option, the user was receiving a divide by zero"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,12,0)="error.  This patch will correct this problem. NOIS NJH-0999-20805."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,14,0)="4. An inconsistency was identified with the way in which Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,15,0)="Medications was handling orders placed on hold through pharmacy options."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,16,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy does not allow orders placed on hold through pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,17,0)="options to be released from hold using Computerized Patient Record System"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,18,0)="(CPRS) options.  With the installation of this patch the same will be true"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,19,0)="for Inpatient Medications."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,21,0)="5. The possibility exists for orders placed on hold to not have their"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,22,0)="status updated to expired and still show on the Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,23,0)="profile and on the Active Orders tab through Computerized Patient Record"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,24,0)="System (CPRS) after the patient has been discharged from the hospital."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,25,0)="This patch will correct this problem.  NOIS HUN-0999-22147."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,27,0)="6. When entering a new Unit Dose order that contained a drug that is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,28,0)="marked for Unit Dose and Outpatient, an error was occurring when checking"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,29,0)="the medical center's formulary.  The drug was being checked to determine"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,30,0)="if the dispense drug was valid for the order but was using an invalid date"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,31,0)="comparison.  This patch will correct this problem.  NOIS PUG-0999-51369."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,33,0)="7. A site was assigning long room-bed names to their beds, the names were"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,34,0)="reaching 11 characters, the room-bed names were running into the patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,35,0)="names when the site printed their pick list using the Pick List [PSJU PL]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,36,0)="option.  This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS WNY-1099-10002."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,38,0)="8. When finishing an IV order for the first time, the default for the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,39,0)="additive was display and the Stop date was calculated from the NUMBER OF"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,40,0)="DAYS FOR IV ORDER field (#3) in the IV ADDITIVES file (#52.6).  If the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,41,0)="user did not accept the order and exited all the way to the patient prompt"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,42,0)="and selected the same order to finish again, the default additive will not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,43,0)="display and the Stop date was calculated from the IV ROOM file (#59.5)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,44,0)="This patch corrects this problem.   NOIS: HUN-1099-20146.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,46,0)="9. When finishing a Unit Dose order as an IV, the additive linked to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,47,0)="corresponding IV Orderable did not display as a defaulted.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",34,1,48,0)="will place a correct additive in the order.  NOIS: RIC-1099-20942."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,0)="35 SEQ #35^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,0)="^^35^35^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,1,0)="1.  When printing MARs on a DSM system, a problem was encountered with the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,2,0)="use of the positioning command (?) and the subsequent layout of the MAR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,3,0)="data.  This patch resolves that problem.  NOIS MOU-1099-31155."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,5,0)="2. A problem was reported with the display of a pending order when using"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,6,0)="the option Patient Profile (Extended) [PSJ EXTP].  The order would display"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,7,0)="with the patient's name and the status of Not Verified, the rest of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,8,0)="order information would display as NOT FOUND or *s.  This patch corrects"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,9,0)="this problem.  NOIS ISH-1099-41686."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,11,0)="3. Currently, if a unit dose order has multiple dispense drugs, the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,12,0)="check is performed for the first dispense drug only.  With this patch, any"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,13,0)="additional dispense drugs entered for the order will be checked for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,14,0)="allergies and drug-drug interactions.  This will apply to new orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,15,0)="entered using the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] or Order Entry [PSJU NE]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,16,0)="options and when finishing pending unit dose orders or renewing unit dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,17,0)="orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,19,0)="4.  A problem was reported with trying to enter a new intervention from"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,20,0)="the Pharmacy Intervention Menu [PSO INTERVENTION MENU] through List"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,21,0)="Manager.  The user selected the Enter Pharmacy Intervention [PSO"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,22,0)="INTERVENTION NEW ENTRY] option, tried to enter a new intervention,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,23,0)="received two question marks and was unable to do so. On the protocol [PSJ"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,24,0)="LM INTERVENTION NEW ENTRY],in the entry action, DLAYGO was being set to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,25,0)="the wrong file number.  This patch corrects this problem.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,26,0)="NOIS BHH-1099-42026."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,28,0)="5.  The user was required to enter an IV room when using the IV options"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,29,0)="even though there is only one active IV room defined.  This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,30,0)="automatically select the active IV room.  NOIS HUN-1099-22843."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,32,0)="6.  If the field DAYS TO RETAIN IV STATISTICS (#31)is not set in the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,33,0)="PHARMACY SYSTEM file (#59.7), the stop date is not calculated correctly"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,34,0)="when finishing the order as a Chemotherapy IV TYPE.  This patch will fix"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",35,1,35,0)="this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,0)="36 SEQ #36^3000313^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,0)="^^20^20^3000313"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,1,0)="Y2K Waiver Exemption ID#:  Y2KWE0026"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,2,0)="==>  This patch may be installed during the Y2K Moratorium."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,4,0)=" This patch addresses unique issues involved in the patient merge"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,5,0)="process.  Some sites were unable to merge duplicate patients due to data"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,6,0)="exceptions.  This patch provides the patient merge software with an API to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,7,0)="call before the package begins it data validation of the FROM and TO"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,8,0)="records of the duplicate patients to clear up some of these data"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,9,0)="exceptions in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) specifically the Unit Dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,10,0)="and IV multiples.  In order for this patch to function as intended the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,11,0)="site will need to load the Kernel Toolkit patch XT*7.3*45."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,12,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,16,0)="********************************NOTE**************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,17,0)="Without the Kernel Toolkit patch XT*7.3*45 nothing will be done to clear"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,18,0)="up these data exceptions in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) specifically"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,19,0)="the Unit Dose and IV multiples."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",36,1,20,0)="**************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,0)="37 SEQ #37^3000313^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,0)="^^32^32^3000313"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,2,0)="1. A problem was reported where a site admitted a patient and the patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,3,0)="didn't show up and was discharged.  The patient later showed up and was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,4,0)="admitted to the hospital.  When Medical Administration Service (MAS) later"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,5,0)="reviewed the record and deleted the first admission Inpatient Medication"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,6,0)="orders placed for the second admission were auto dc'd.  This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,7,0)="correct this problem. NOIS SLC-1199-51222."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,9,0)="2. With this patch, the IV TYPE will be prompted when finishing an IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,10,0)="fluid order.   ""ADMIXTURE"" will be the default IV TYPE.  E3R #11576."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,12,0)="3. The ""*"" sometime displayed next to the Start and Stop dates even"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,13,0)="though no new order is created.  This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,15,0)="4. For IV orders entered with schedules like QOD, Q48H and Q72H, labels"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,16,0)="were being printing daily when scheduled labels were run.  The frequency"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,17,0)="of the printing of the labels should reflect the schedule entered.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,18,0)="patch corrects this problem.  NOIS REN-1199-61217."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,20,0)="5. A problem was reported where a pharmacist edited the rate on an IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,21,0)="order and when the changed order was viewed in Computerized Patient Record"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,22,0)="System (CPRS) the rate would show without the ml/hr.  CPRS will issue a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,23,0)="patch to begin picking up the ml/hr from the messages sent by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,24,0)="pharmacy.  This patch makes changes to the rate validation entry point"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,25,0)="ORINF^PSIVSP Inpatient Medications provides to CPRS to help resolve this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,26,0)="issue and to allow the infusion rate with the ml/hr to pass the validation"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,27,0)="checks in this entry point for orders that may be renewed or changed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,28,0)="through CPRS.  NOIS WIC-0199-40011."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,30,0)="6. A problem was reported where a site needed to enter a number greater"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,31,0)="than 99 at the ""Pre-Exchange DOSES:"" prompt.  This patch will increase the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",37,1,32,0)="allowable number to 9999.  NOIS REN-1299-62274."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,0)="39 SEQ #38^3000405^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,0)="^^28^28^3000405"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,1,0)="1.  A site without 24-hour pharmacy coverage entered an E3R requesting"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,2,0)="that Inpatient Medications allow users holding the PSJ RNURSE key be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,3,0)="allowed to finish and verify orders placed through Computerized Patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,4,0)="Record System (CPRS).  This would put the orders in an active status, so"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,5,0)="they would be available to the Bar Code Med Admin (BCMA) software.  The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,6,0)="E3R# is 11620. With the installation of this patch, users who hold the PSJ"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,7,0)="RNFINSH key will have the option to finish and verify orders placed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,8,0)="through CPRS. It was decided by the workgroup that a new key should be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,9,0)="created to control this additional functionality.  E3R# 11620, and NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,10,0)="TUA-0999-32647."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,12,0)="2.  In the Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW] option, the order was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,13,0)="not locked correctly if the user chose ""NO Profile"" at the ""SHORT, LONG,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,14,0)="or NO Profile?  SHORT//"" prompt.  This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,16,0)="3.  Within the LBL Label Print/Reprint hidden action, if the user selected"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,17,0)="the ILIV Individual Labels (IV) option, a new order may be entered.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,18,0)="patch will prevent any new orders from being entered from the hidden menu."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,20,0)="4.  When a pending order had a schedule of ""ONE TIME"", ""ONE-TIME"", ""ONCE"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,21,0)="or ""STAT"", the Schedule Type is not defaulted to ""ONE TIME"".  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,22,0)="will set the Schedule Type to ""ONE TIME"" for these types of schedule. NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,23,0)="HUN-1199-20125. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,25,0)="5.  A site reported receiving an undefined error when the pharmacist"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,26,0)="finishing a Unit Dose order had the PSJ RNURSE, PSJ RNFINSH keys as well"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,27,0)="as the regular pharmacist keys and auto verify turned on. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",38,1,28,0)="corrects this problem.  NOIS AMA-0200-72006."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,0)="40 SEQ #39^3000405^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,0)="^^38^38^3000405"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,1,0)="1. A problem was reported by a site when trying to finish an order with a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,2,0)="Log-in date of midnight 01/04/00 and the ward parameter set to Use Closest"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,3,0)="Admin Time.  The start date/time was incorrectly displayed as ******** and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,4,0)="the stop date/time was incorrectly displayed as 59/00/23  0:00.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,5,0)="patch will correct this problem.  NOIS CON-0100-10187."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,7,0)="2. Additional functionality is included in this patch to change the PSJHL"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,8,0)="routines to do an additional check to ensure that the patient IEN received"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,9,0)="from Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) matches the IEN stored in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,10,0)="the pending order before allowing actions on pending orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,12,0)="3. A problem was reported where a site was trying to renew an IV order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,13,0)="through CPRS and was receiving the message Invalid Infusion Rate. The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,14,0)="problem was that when finishing the order Pharmacy changed the infusion"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,15,0)="rate to the format Text@# and this was not being passed back to CPRS when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,16,0)="the new order was created.  This patch corrects this problem. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,17,0)="NOIS HIN-0100-41126."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,19,0)="4. E3R# 11771, Change Nature of Order auto prompt requested that the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,20,0)="default for orders changed in pharmacy due to edit should be Service"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,21,0)="Correction rather than Written.  This patch changes this functionality."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,23,0)="5. A problem was reported by a site when using the option Inpatient Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,24,0)="Entry [PSJ OE] to enter new orders.  At the 'SCHEDULE: ' prompt the user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,25,0)="would enter a question mark and answer 'yes' to the prompt 'Do you want"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,26,0)="the entire ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE List?'. Part of the resulting list"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,27,0)="would scroll off the top part of the screen; the user was using a CRT and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,28,0)="couldn't scroll back to see the data.  This patch will correct this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,29,0)="problem.  NOIS MUR-0100-31928."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,31,0)="6. A problem was reported by a site on a Unit Dose order which was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,32,0)="originally placed through Inpatient Medication options.  The order had"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,33,0)="dispense drugs entered when it was ordered and these were not passed to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,34,0)="CPRS.  When the order was copied through the CPRS option, no default"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,35,0)="dispense drug was displayed to the user and no order checks took place."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,36,0)="CPRS does not allow more than one dispense drug per Unit Dose order.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,37,0)="patch will correct this problem for orders where there is one dispense"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",39,1,38,0)="drug for the order, but not more than one.  NOIS MAC-0200-62454."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,0)="41 SEQ #40^3000626^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,0)="^^56^56^3000626"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,1,0)="1. E3R# 12551, Dispense Extra Unit Default, requested that the default for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,2,0)="the prompt ""Do you want to dispense these extra units through the ATC:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,3,0)="Yes//"" be changed to No.  This default is presented to the user when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,4,0)="running the option EXtra Units Dispensed [PSJU EUD] if the drug is set up"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,5,0)="to be dispensed through the ATC. This patch will change the default for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,6,0)="this prompt to No."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,8,0)="2. A site had questions about the documentation for the option"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,9,0)="AUto-Discontinue Set-Up [PSJ AC SET-UP].  In the on-line documentation,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,10,0)="ICU was used as a service.  This is not one of the services defined in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,11,0)="WARD LOCATION file (#42).  ICU has been replaced with Surgery. NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,12,0)="PHO-0100-62836."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,14,0)="3.  A problem was reported where pending IV orders were being discontinued"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,15,0)="through the Inpatient Medications options and no Nature of Order was being"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,16,0)="passed to Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS).  This patch corrects"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,17,0)="this problem.  NOIS PTH-0300-21183."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,19,0)="4.  A problem was reported that when using the Unit Dose/Pick List option"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,20,0)="EXtra Units Dispensed [PSJU EUD], when saying YES to have the drug"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,21,0)="dispensed through the ATC machine, it was not packaged.  The problem is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,22,0)="caused by the Extra Units Dispensed using a field that is set to be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,23,0)="deleted for the ATC device.  This patch corrects the problem.  NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,24,0)="UNY-0400-12501."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,26,0)="5.  If a schedule ""ONE-TIME"" is not defined in the Administration Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,27,0)="file (#51.1), it does not recognize in the IV piggyback order and the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,28,0)="Start and Stop date/times are not set appropriately.  With this patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,29,0)="One-Time will be given the Start and Stop date/time as in the unit dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,30,0)="functionality. NOIS SDC-0300-60125."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,32,0)="6.  The nurse's initials for verifying IV orders in CPRS are not passing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,33,0)="to the Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) package to display on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,34,0)="VDL.  This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,36,0)="7.  This patch adds the FREQUENCY field (#41) to the 11th piece in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,37,0)="^TMP(""PSJ"",$J,4).  This becomes a part of the information returned by the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,38,0)="API provided in the PSJBCMA1 routine to the Bar Code Medication"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,39,0)="Administration (BCMA) package."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,41,0)="8.  A problem was reported where a site was unable to enter an infusion"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,42,0)="rate in the format FREE TEXT@NUMBER OF LABELS PER DAY through CPRS. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,43,0)="patch corrects this problem by updating the entry point ORINF^PSIVSP."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,44,0)="NOIS DEN-0400-52116."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,46,0)="9.  A problem was reported where a site had IV Fluid orders entered via"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,47,0)="Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS).  The orders were finished"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,48,0)="through the backdoor pharmacy options as piggyback orders and the ward"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,49,0)="specific administration times were not presented as the default for the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,50,0)="pharmacy user finishing the orders. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,51,0)="NOIS CLL-0500-41826."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,53,0)="10. This patch also modifieds the API routines PSJBCMA1 and PSJBCMA2 to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,54,0)="use ^TMP(""PSJ1"" and ^TMP(""PSJ2"", respectively, to make a distinction"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,55,0)="between the two different sets of data returned to the Bar Code Medication"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",40,1,56,0)="Administration (BCMA) package."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,0)="42 SEQ #41^3000626^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,0)="^^15^15^3000626"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,1,0)="1.  Several sites have reported a problem related to medication orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,2,0)="getting mixed up.   The problem most frequently reported is that a Unit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,3,0)="Dose order is being changed to an IV order.  The development team has been"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,4,0)="unable to recreate this problem, but thinks the problem may be a result of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,5,0)="using the variable DFN in the PSJHL messaging routines.  With the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,6,0)="installation of this patch the variable DFN will be changed to PSJHLDFN in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,7,0)="the PSJHL messaging routines. Additionally checks have been added to PSJOE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,8,0)="and PSJLIFN to be sure that the order number being finished is the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,9,0)="number being updated and that the DFN of the patient selected matches the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,10,0)="DFN of the patient in the pending order being updated. This should keep"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,11,0)="the problem from occurring."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,13,0)="2.  A site reported a problem with an undefined error when attempting to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,14,0)="process an order.  This patch is to correct the program to prevent the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",41,1,15,0)="undefined error.  NOIS: BRX-0200-10119."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",42,0)="48^3000905^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",42,1,0)="^^7^7^3000905"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",42,1,1,0)="PSJ*5*48 provides an API for the Clinical Reminders package.  The API"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",42,1,2,0)="provides patient and order information, based on a specified date range"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",42,1,3,0)="and a specified list of medications, as it relates to the Hepatitis C"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",42,1,4,0)="Initiative. This patch will not affect users of the Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",42,1,5,0)="package. The PSJORAPI routine in patch PSJ*5*48 provides an entry point"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",42,1,6,0)="that returns patient and order information in a ^TMP global to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",42,1,7,0)="Clinical Reminders package, based on the criteria passed into the call."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,0)="45 SEQ #43^3000907^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,0)="^^26^26^3000907"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,1,0)="1.  When an Orderable Item has a Schedule Type defined as ""Fill on"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,2,0)="Request"" and the pending order has a Schedule of ""NOW"", the Schedule Type"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,3,0)="is not converted to ""ONE TIME"" during the finishing process.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,4,0)="will correct this problem.  NOIS: EKH-0600-40188."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,6,0)="2.  A site reported a problem with an inconsistency between orders placed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,7,0)="from the Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) and backdoor pharmacy."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,8,0)="The problem was with orders entered in CPRS as On Call and then finished"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,9,0)="as On Call being immediately expired.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,10,0)="NOIS:  HUN-0400-22176"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,12,0)="3.  A site reported a problem with an inconsistency in calculating the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,13,0)="stop date of a renewal order.  When finishing a renewal from the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,14,0)="Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) the least of all the stop dates"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,15,0)="was used.  However, in backdoor pharmacy, the stop date for the orderable"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,16,0)="item was always used, if it existed.  This patch corrects this problem by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,17,0)="modifying the backdoor pharmacy function to behave the same as the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,18,0)="finishing process.  NOIS:  EKH-0600-41622"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,20,0)="4.  Two sites reported a problem with an inconsistency with the handling"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,21,0)="of the stop date for One-Time orders.  When finishing a One-Time order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,22,0)="entered in the Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS), if the stop date"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,23,0)="was edited, the start date was also changed.  However, in backdoor"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,24,0)="pharmacy, this was not the case.  This patch corrects this problem by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,25,0)="modifying the finishing process to work the same as backdoor pharmacy."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",43,1,26,0)="NOIS:  WPB-0500-32018 and HIN-0300-43237"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",44,0)="46 SEQ #44^3001004^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",44,1,0)="^^11^11^3001004"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",44,1,1,0)="This patch makes the following changes to the APIs between Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",44,1,2,0)="Medications and Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) (Integration"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",44,1,3,0)="Agreement #s 2828 and 2829):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",44,1,4,0)="  a.  put the SCHEDULE INTERVAL field (#.17) from the IV sub-file (#55.01)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",44,1,5,0)="of the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) in the 11th piece of ^TMP(""PSJ1"",$J,4)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",44,1,6,0)="  b.  add the IV TYPE field (#.04), INTERMITTENT SYRINGE field (#108) and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",44,1,7,0)="the CHEMOTHERAPY TYPE field (#106) from the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",44,1,8,0)="pieces 6-8, respectively, of ^TMP(""PSJ"",$J,Index,0) and ^TMP(""PSJ1"",$J,0)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",44,1,9,0)="  c. add the ORDERS FILE ENTRY field (#49 of the NON-VERIFIED ORDERS file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",44,1,10,0)="(#53.1) and #66 of the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55)) to piece 9 of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",44,1,11,0)="^TMP(""PSJ"",$J,Index,0) and ^TMP(""PSJ1"",$J,0)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,0)="43 SEQ #45^3001027^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,0)="^^50^50^3001027"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,1,0)="1. Several sites have reported a problem with the ACTIVITY LOG REASON file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,2,0)="(#53.3).  The sites have entry numbers 1 - 75, a ""B"" x-ref, and are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,3,0)="missing entry numbers 1035 and 1040.  This patch will delete the current"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,4,0)="Data Dictionary (DD) and data for this file at the site and bring in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,5,0)="correct DD and data.  The pre-init routine PSJ0043 accomplishes the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,6,0)="deletion of the DD and the data and will be automatically deleted once"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,7,0)="the installation is complete. NOIS# HAM-0300-21499."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,9,0)="2. Several sites have reported a problem when trying to document the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,10,0)="dispensing of medications through the Bar Code Med Admin (BCMA)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,11,0)="software.  The sites have reported receiving the following error:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,13,0)="  1. Data Validation Error: 701: The value 'AC' for field DOSES ORDERED in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,14,0)="  DISPENSE DRUG SUB-FIELD in file BCMA MEDICATION LOG is not valid."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,16,0)="The problem was with the input transform on the UNITS PER DOSE field"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,17,0)="(#.02) in the DISPENSE DRUG sub-file (#53.4502) of the INPATIENT USER"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,18,0)="PARAMETERS file (#53.45) and the DISPENSE DRUG sub-file (#53.11) of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,19,0)="NON-VERIFIED ORDERS file (#53.1). The problem with the input transform"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,20,0)="also exists in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55), UNIT DOSE sub-file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,21,0)="(#55.06), DISPENSE DRUG sub-file (#55.07), UNITS PER DOSE field (#.02)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,22,0)="Patch PSS*1*35 corrects this problem in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,23,0)="and this patch corrects the problem in the INPATIENT USER PARAMETERS file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,24,0)="(#53.45) and the NON-VERIFIED ORDERS file (#53.1).  NOIS#s NOL-0300-71473,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,25,0)="HOU-0300-71626, and CMO-0300-43187."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,27,0)="3. Site reported a problem where they entered an infusion rate of @x and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,28,0)="x labels didn't print.  Only 1 label printed.  The issue is that only one"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,29,0)="administration time was specified.  The administration time overrides"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,30,0)="the entry of @x when determining how many labels will print.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,31,0)="modifies the field description and documentation for INFUSION RATE in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,32,0)="order to clarify which field determines the number of labels.  Modified"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,33,0)="the INFUSION RATE field (#59) in the NON-VERIFIED ORDERS file (#53.1)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,35,0)="4. This patch modifies the following fields to remove references to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,36,0)="company name of Baxter:  PICK LIST file (#53.5), DATA/TIME LIST SENT TO"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,37,0)="THE ATC field (#.13), UNIT DOSE/ATC MEDS file (#53.55), PICK LIST field"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,38,0)="(#.01), UNIT DOSE/ATC MEDS file (#53.55), LAST RECORD SENT field (#1),"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,39,0)="UNIT DOSE/ATC MEDS file (#53.55), DATA RECORDS field (#10), UNIT DOSE/ATC"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,40,0)="MEDS file (#53.55), DATA RECORDS sub-file (#10), DATA RECORDS field"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,41,0)="(#.01), WARD GROUP file (#57.5), BAXTER ATC DEVICE POINTER field (#32) and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,42,0)="the description of the UNIT DOSE/ATC MEDS file (#53.55)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,44,0)="5. This patch removes the references to the specific model 212 ATC"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,45,0)="dispensing system from the description of the UNIT DOSE/ATC MEDS file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,46,0)="(#53.55)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,48,0)="6. This patch modifies the following menu options to remove references to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,49,0)="the company name of Baxter:  Send Pick List to ATC [PSJU PLATCS] and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",45,1,50,0)="Dispense Drug/ATC Set Up [PSSJU DRUG/ATC SET UP]."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,0)="44 SEQ #46^3001027^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,0)="^^28^28^3001027"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,1,0)="1. A problem was reported by a site where one time Unit Dose orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,2,0)="entered through Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) after hours,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,3,0)="finished by a nurse with the PSJ RNFINISH key, and verified by the nurse"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,4,0)="on the ward, were not appearing on the summary of non-verified orders for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,5,0)="the Pharmacist using the Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW] option."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,6,0)="This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# CLL-0500-41728."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,8,0)="2. An E3R was entered requesting that nurses using the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,9,0)="Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW] option see expired non-verified"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,10,0)="Unit Dose orders when selecting NO PROFILE.  E3R# 11834."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,12,0)="3. A problem was reported by a site that when finishing a Unit Dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,13,0)="pending renewal a change was made that caused a new order to be created."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,14,0)="The original order retained the renewed status and the stop date/time was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,15,0)="not updated so that it would expire when the new order's start date/time"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,16,0)="was reached.  This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# HIN-0300-41916."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,18,0)="4. An inconsistency was discovered between the Computerized Patient Record"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,19,0)="System (CPRS) and the Inpatient Medications validation of Provider"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,20,0)="Comments/Special Instructions.  CPRS allows entry of text with no spaces"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,21,0)="while Inpatient Medications requires spaces.  This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,22,0)="problem.  Inpatient Medications will now allow entry of Special"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,23,0)="Instructions with no spaces.  NOIS# ASH-0500-30650."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,25,0)="5. A problem was reported with label print if the Provider Comments"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,26,0)="entered in Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) contained no spaces."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,27,0)="This patch modifies label print to correctly print the information even if"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",46,1,28,0)="no spaces are present.  NOIS# NAS-0400-32349."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,0)="52 SEQ #47^3001127^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,0)="^^14^14^3001127"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,1,0)="1.  Pharmacy Benefits Management (PBM) has requested that Technical"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,2,0)="Services develop a software patch that would disable the Drug file (#50)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,3,0)="Internal Entry Number (IEN) (.001 field) lookup during order entry"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,4,0)="processes.  The pharmacy software has always allowed IEN lookup and quick"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,5,0)="code lookups at the request of field users.  A quick code is a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,6,0)="user-defined synonym for a drug (i.e. A325->Acetaminophen 325mg Tab).  PBM"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,7,0)="provided guidance to VA Medical Centers in the past to not use low numbers"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,8,0)="for quick codes and to inactivate the first 50 entries in the drug file to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,9,0)="reduce the chances of error.  This patch would eliminate drug selection in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,10,0)="the ordering processes by entry of the Internal Entry Number."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,12,0)="2.  Order check warning does not display in back door order entry for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,13,0)="users with the  ""ALLOW AUTO-VERIFY FOR USER"" set to yes.  This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",47,1,14,0)="correct this problem.  NOIS# POR-0900-50194."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,0)="49 SEQ #48^3010103^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,1,0)="^^12^12^3010103"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,1,1,0)="1. A problem was reported where a site edited a pending IV order deleting"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,1,2,0)="the additive or solution and then adding a different additive or solution"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,1,3,0)="to the order, this change did not cause a new order to be created.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,1,4,0)="patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# REN-0500-60972."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,1,6,0)="2. A problem was reported where the duplicate order check scrolled off the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,1,7,0)="screen when the pharmacist was entering a new order.  This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,1,8,0)="correct this problem.  NOIS# PHO-0500-61993."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,1,10,0)="3. A site reported receiving an error when trying to queue the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,1,11,0)="PAtient Profile (Unit Dose) [PSJU PR] option.  This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",48,1,12,0)="problem. NOIS# ANN-0800-41860."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",49,0)="53 SEQ #49^3010122^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",49,1,0)="^^7^7^3010122"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",49,1,1,0)="A site reported a problem with the display of sensitive information in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",49,1,2,0)="Inpatient Medications.  During patient lookup, social security numbers and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",49,1,3,0)="dates of birth for sensitive patients should display *SENSITIVE* on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",49,1,4,0)="screen.  In Inpatient Medications, the actual social security number and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",49,1,5,0)="date of birth are displaying.  This patch corrects this problem by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",49,1,6,0)="combining the sensitive patient handling and the special formatting from"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",49,1,7,0)="Inpatient Medications."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,0)="55 SEQ #50^3010122^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,0)="^^19^19^3010122"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,1,0)="1. Several sites have reported a problem with the start date/time on Unit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,2,0)="Dose orders placed through Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,3,0)="defaulting in as ""********"" and the stop date/time defaulting in as"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,4,0)="""00/00/24  :"".  If the pharmacist finishing the order doesn't catch this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,5,0)="discrepancy in the start and stop date/time, the order can be finished"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,6,0)="without a start and stop date/time.  Then the order is visible in CPRS on"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,7,0)="the orders tab, but not on the meds tab, and not in Inpatient Medications."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,8,0)="This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# DAN-1200-41606, UNY-1200-11451,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,9,0)="BEC-1200-20932."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,11,0)="2. When selecting from the Orderable Item file(#50.7), the SYNONYM lookup"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,12,0)="was allowed and patch PSJ*5.0*52 removed this capability.  This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,13,0)="restore the ability of entering a SYNONYM at the ""Select Drug:"" prompt."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,14,0)="NOIS# REN-1100-62137."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,16,0)="3. When selecting from the Drug file (#50), the user entered lowercase"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,17,0)="letters and was returned a drug based on the VA Drug Class lookup and was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,18,0)="not offered a choice of drugs starting with the letters entered.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",50,1,19,0)="patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# CMS-1200-30893."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,0)="51 SEQ #51^3010228^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,0)="^^31^31^3010228"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,1,0)="1. E3R# 14641 requested that the UD Default Stop Date/Time be reset to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,2,0)="null when Inpatient Medication orders are discontinued due to a Treating"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,3,0)="Specialty Change.  This patch will accomplish this request."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,5,0)="2. A problem was reported where a nurse entered an order through the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,6,0)="Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) options using verbal or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,7,0)="telephoned as the nature of order.  When the order was finished and a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,8,0)="detailed view of the order was done on the meds tab in CPRS the nurse was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,9,0)="showing as the Pharmacist.  This patch corrects this problem. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,10,0)="NOIS# NAS-0700-30575 and DEN-0700-50863."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,12,0)="3. A problem was reported by a site where they were doing a detailed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,13,0)="display of a unit dose medication order on the meds tab through CPRS and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,14,0)="the field Units/Dose was displayed as null and through Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,15,0)="Medications the UNITS PER DOSE field (#.02) of the Dispense Drug sub-file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,16,0)="was displayed as 1. In Inpatient Medications if the UNITS PER DOSE field"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,17,0)="is null it is assumed that 1 unit is to be dispensed and a 1 is displayed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,18,0)="This patch makes changes to the API that CPRS calls to make the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,19,0)="information display consistently.  NOIS# PUG-1000-51002."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,20,0)="         *****PLEASE NOTE THE FOLLOWING INFO*****"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,21,0)=" If a unit dose order contains more than one dispense drug only dosage"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,22,0)="ordered will be returned to CPRS and no units per dose. If a unit dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,23,0)="order has a status of pending and the units per dose field is null, no"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,24,0)="units per dose will be returned."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,26,0)="4. A problem was reported by a site where a medications order placed on"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,27,0)="hold through Inpatient Medications options and then taken off hold through"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,28,0)="these same options was not displaying correctly on the orders tab in CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,29,0)="The order text was not being updated appropriately.  The status showed as"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,30,0)="active, but the word hold still showed on the left side of the order text."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",51,1,31,0)="This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# ROS-0900-52226."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,0)="54 SEQ #52^3010326^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,0)="^^29^29^3010326"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,1,0)="1. A site reported a problem in the PAtient Profile (Unit Dose) [PSJU PR]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,2,0)="option.  When entering '^^' at the 'View ORDERS' prompt, an error was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,3,0)="received.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,5,0)="2. A site reported a problem with the number of labels printing after an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,6,0)="infusion rate of xxx@0 was entered.  Even though they entered 0 for the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,7,0)="number of labels, labels still printed.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,9,0)="3. A site reported a problem with receiving an error in Bar Code"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,10,0)="Medication Administration (BCMA) when attempting to access the pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,11,0)="patient activity log.  This patch modifies the API to BCMA by adding the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,12,0)="internal entry number of the person who performs an action on a unit dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,13,0)="order to the information passed back to BCMA.  In addition, the API has"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,14,0)="been changed to send all activities for the IV orders, even if no data was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,15,0)="edited."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,17,0)="4. A site reported a problem with MAR labels not printing when a nurse"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,18,0)="verified the order in the Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS).  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,19,0)="patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,21,0)="5. A site reported a problem with the Inpatient Profile [PSJ PR] option"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,22,0)="when attempting to print certain patients.  If a patient had an order with"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,23,0)="more than six activity log entries, the option would go into an infinite"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,24,0)="loop when printing to a printer.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,26,0)="6. A problem was discovered with the handling of date/time validations in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,27,0)="Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE].  There was a problem with the way the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,28,0)="option was verifying that a time had been entered.  This patch corrects"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",52,1,29,0)="this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,0)="60 SEQ #53^3010608^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,1,0)="^^12^12^3010608"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,1,1,0)="1. A problem was reported by a site where after using the Inpatient Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,1,2,0)="Entry [PSJ OE] option the user then jumped to the Patients on Specific"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,1,3,0)="Drug(s) [PSJ PDV] option and after selecting the start date, stop date,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,1,4,0)="type of orders, sort by, and list by the user was returned to the top"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,1,5,0)="level menu without the report running.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,1,6,0)="NOIS# KAN-0401-40002."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,1,8,0)="2. A site reported a problem where nurse practitioners and other providers"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,1,9,0)="were signing the reports generated by the Action Profile #1 [PSJU AP-1],"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,1,10,0)="Action Profile #2 [PSJU AP-2], and AUthorized Absence/Discharge Summary"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,1,11,0)="[PSJU DS] options where the signature block states Physician's Signature."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",53,1,12,0)="This patch changes this to Provider's Signature. NOIS# REN-0301-62349."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,0)="59 SEQ #54^3010710^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,0)="^^24^24^3010710"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,1,0)="1. A site reported a problem where they got a null subscript error when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,2,0)="trying to run the option Extra Units Dispensed Report [PSJU EUDD] by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,3,0)="patient.  This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# HUN-0700-22263."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,5,0)="2. A site reported a problem where the user received an undefined error"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,6,0)="when a Pharmacy Technician or Nurse was using the Non-Verified/Pending"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,7,0)="Orders [PSJU VBW] option and viewing pending IV orders.  The user was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,8,0)="prompted ""Select IV ROOM NAME:"", the user entered a return or an up-arrow"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,9,0)="and received the undefined error.  With the installation of this patch the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,10,0)="Pharmacy Technician or Nurse will be prompted after selecting the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,11,0)="Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW] option for the IV ROOM NAME, if the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,12,0)="user returns past the prompt or enters an up-arrow the user will be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,13,0)="returned to the main menu.  Users will only be prompted if there is more"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,14,0)="than one active IV ROOM in the IV ROOM file (#59.5).  This patch corrects"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,15,0)="this problem. NOIS# BRX-0301-10962."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,17,0)="3. After the release of patch PSJ*5*51, several sites reported a problem"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,18,0)="that occurred while using the OR GUA EVENT PROCESSOR protocol on the DGPM"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,19,0)="MOVEMENT EVENTS protocol an error would occur.  Sites were advised to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,20,0)="switch to the OR GUA EVENT PROCESSOR NOTASK, this corrected the error, but"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,21,0)="sites began reporting problems with the release of time delayed orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,22,0)="This patch will correct this problem and allow sites to begin using the OR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,23,0)="GUA EVENT PROCESSOR protocol again without an error. NOIS#s"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",54,1,24,0)="LAH-0201-61581, ANN-0301-40951, ALT-0301-20287, and MIW-0201-42370."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,0)="61 SEQ #55^3010710^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,0)="^^23^23^3010710"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,1,0)="1. Several sites reported errors when attempting to evaluate clinical"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,2,0)="reminders.  The problem was caused by dates in the PHARMACY PATIENT file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,3,0)="(#55) that were in the wrong format.  This patch corrects the format of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,4,0)="those dates. NOIS# BUT-0401-21836, MON-0401-52179, EKH-0401-42360,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,5,0)="SDC-0401-62568."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,7,0)="If after installing and running PSJ*5*61 your site is still receiving the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,8,0)="<UNDEFINED>LDATE+8~PXRMDRUG error, it may be necessary to call the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,9,0)="following entry point within the Clinical Reminders software"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,10,0)="KILLPC^PXRMPINF(PXRMDFN) where PXRMDFN = ""PXRMDFN""_DFN.  You can identify"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,11,0)="the patients DFN from the error."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,13,0)="$ZE= LDATE+8^PXRMDRUG:1, %DSM-E-UNDEF, undefined variable"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,14,0)="^XTMP(""PXRMDFN6762"",""PSDRUG"",""INSULIN NOVOLIN N-HUMAN NPH"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,15,0)="100U/ML"",3001214.10445), -DSM-I-ECODE, MUMPS error code: M7 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,17,0)="For example, in this case you would type D KILLPC^PXRMPINF(""PXRMDFN6762"")."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,19,0)="While the patch corrects the errors in the dates, the ^XTMP global built"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,20,0)="by the Clinical Reminders software only gets rebuilt if it is more than 24"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,21,0)="hours old and may not have been rebuilt before the software evaluates the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,22,0)="next clinical reminder.  The above entry point will force the rebuilding"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",55,1,23,0)="of the ^XTMP for the patient that generated the error."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,0)="47 SEQ #56^3010802^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,0)="^^98^98^3010802"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,1,0)="1.  There have been several requests that the information in the SPECIAL"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,2,0)="INSTRUCTIONS field (#8) and the OTHER PRINT INFO field (#31) from the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,3,0)="PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) be passed to Computerized Patient Record"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,4,0)="System (CPRS) to be displayed on the Orders Tab.  With the installation of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,5,0)="this patch Inpatient Medications will begin passing this information to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,6,0)="CPRS. NOIS# BHH-0700-42241."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,8,0)="2.  A problem was reported by a site where the UD PROVIDER field (#62.02)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,9,0)="of the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) was not being updated or the provider"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,10,0)="in that field was being presented as the default provider in backdoor"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,11,0)="pharmacy order entry even though the provider was no longer active."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,12,0)="This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# BRX-0700-10937."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,14,0)="3.  A problem was reported where a cross-reference was left around which"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,15,0)="should have been killed.  This caused it to appear as though the patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,16,0)="had an order that needed processing when there was no order.  When the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,17,0)="order was selected the user received an undefined error.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,18,0)="corrects this problem.  NOIS# NJH-0800-20230."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,20,0)="4.  A problem was reported by a site where the infusion rate on an order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,21,0)="was not being returned to CPRS appropriately.  The problem was in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,22,0)="messaging routines, which always expected there to be a space between the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,23,0)="numeric rate and the text of the rate.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,24,0)="NOIS# CON-0900-11408."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,26,0)="5.  A site reported a problem when editing the orderable item in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,27,0)="Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] option.  The stop date is not being set"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,28,0)="correctly. This patch corrects this problem by recalculating the stop date"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,29,0)="for an order if the orderable item is changed.  NOIS# BOI-1299-51410."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,31,0)="6.  A site reported a problem where editing an order caused a new order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,32,0)="to be generated with a new stop date, but the user had no indication that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,33,0)="a new stop date was calculated.  This patch corrects this problem by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,34,0)="changing the display of the stop date to indicate the entry was modified"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,35,0)="(for unit dose orders only).  NOIS# NAS-0600-31201."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,37,0)="7.  There are two cases where a prompt can be modified when editing an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,38,0)="active order and the display will not highlight the change before asking"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,39,0)="the user to accept the changes.  The two prompts are ""Admin Times:"" and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,40,0)="""Stop:"".  This patch corrects this problem by modifying the display"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,41,0)="routine to highlight these fields if they are modified (for unit dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,42,0)="orders only)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,44,0)="8.  When editing either the stop date or the start date for a one-time"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,45,0)="order, under most conditions, the other entry will also be changed.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,46,0)="patch corrects this problem by modifying the entry process to only edit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,47,0)="the field selected, not both the stop and start date.  Note:  one of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,48,0)="requirements to correct this was to delete the triggers from the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,49,0)="NON-VERIFIED ORDERS file (#53.1), START DATE/TIME field (#10)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,50,0)="NOIS# BOI-1299-51410."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,52,0)="9. Several sites have reported issues with the calculation of the start"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,53,0)="date when an order is renewed.  Specifically, dealing with displaying"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,54,0)="orders on the Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) Virtual Due List."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,55,0)="This patch changes the calculation of the start date for a renewed order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,56,0)="to use the following logic: If BCMA has marked the drug as given against"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,57,0)="a scheduled administration time, take the administration time and add the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,58,0)="frequency.  If the time is in the future, use this as the start date for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,59,0)="the order.  This will be true even for a non-standard schedule if the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,60,0)="user enters administration times.  If the drug is marked as given, but"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,61,0)="there is no associated scheduled administration time, take the time the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,62,0)="drug was given, add the frequency and round up to the next hour.  If the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,63,0)="time is in the future, use this as the start date for the order.  If the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,64,0)="time calculated in either case, is in the past, if the drug was never"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,65,0)="given or the drug was marked as held, the current calculation logic will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,66,0)="be used and the start date will be determined by the ward parameters."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,67,0)="Please note: this logic will apply to regular renew and regular finish."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,68,0)="Speed renew and speed finish will not be effected.  NOIS# NCH-0700-41081."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,70,0)="10. A site reported a problem with editing multiple one-time orders for a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,71,0)="patient.  The problem was that the edit of the stop date on the first"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,72,0)="order was stored correctly, but not on the following orders.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,73,0)="corrects this problem.  NOIS# BOI-0700-51308."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,75,0)="11. A problem was reported where a pharmacist was finishing an order for a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,76,0)="patient and specifying that the order was a self-med.  When the pharmacist"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,77,0)="reviewed the order afterwards the self-med designation was not showing."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,78,0)="The pharmacist then had to go back and edit the order again and designate"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,79,0)="it as self-med.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,80,0)="NOIS# LEB-0700-21514."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,82,0)="12. A problem was reported where a site was unable to renew IV Fluid"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,83,0)="orders thru CPRS.  These orders originated from backdoor Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,84,0)="Medications options.  The provider would receive a message that the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,85,0)="infusion rate was invalid.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,86,0)="NOIS# ANN-0900-40829."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,88,0)="13. A site reported a problem with the calculation of the start date for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,89,0)="an order with a schedule such as QOD.  If the order was placed after the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,90,0)="administration time for the day had passed, and the start date was set to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,91,0)="begin at the next administration time, the order was scheduled to start in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,92,0)="two days.  This patch corrects this problem by making the start date be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,93,0)="the next day at the scheduled administration time.  NOIS# MAR-1000-20645."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,95,0)="14. A site reported a problem with the MAR labels printing when a pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,96,0)="technician edited an order even though labels were only supposed to print"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,97,0)="on pharmacist verification.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",56,1,98,0)="NOIS# CTX-1199-72489."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,0)="57 SEQ #57^3010802^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,0)="^^25^25^3010802"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,1,0)="1. A problem was reported by a site where the Medication Administration"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,2,0)="History (MAH) in Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) was showing the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,3,0)="wrong initials for the pharmacist. This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,4,0)="NOIS# HUN-0900-21331."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,6,0)="2. A problem was reported by a site where they were receiving emails from"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,7,0)="the BCMA software regarding IV orders which were not being displayed on"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,8,0)="the Virtual Due List (VDL). The problem was with the API routines that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,9,0)="Inpatient Medications (IM) supplies to BCMA.  IV orders don't have a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,10,0)="schedule type and IM was determining a pseudo schedule type for IV orders,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,11,0)="if the start and stop date/times were the same it was a one time order, if"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,12,0)="the schedule contained ""PRN"" it was a PRN order, otherwise it was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,13,0)="continuous.  Now IM will also set IV orders with a schedule of TODAY,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,14,0)="ONCE, NOW, ONE TIME, ONE-TIME, 1 TIME, 1TIME, 1-TIME, and STAT as one time"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,15,0)="orders.  NOIS# WPB-0101-30986."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,17,0)="3. On the BCMA Workgroup call, it was requested that IM start returning an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,18,0)="additional pseudo schedule type for IV orders.  The new pseudo schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,19,0)="type will be ON CALL.  IV orders with ON CALL, ON-CALL, or ONCALL in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,20,0)="schedule field will be returned to BCMA in the API with a pseudo schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,21,0)="type of 'OC'."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,23,0)="4. An obsolete reference to a variable pointer definition was found in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,24,0)="MARS LABELS file (#53.41).  This patch corrects this problem by removing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",57,1,25,0)="the obsolete reference from the data dictionary."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,0)="62 SEQ #58^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,1,0)="^^12^12^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,1,1,0)="1. A problem was reported by sites where, under certain circumstances,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,1,2,0)="IV orders which are finished using the Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,1,3,0)="VBW] option cause an undefined P(17) error to occur. Since the problem"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,1,4,0)="cannot be reproduced on demand, this patch will address this problem by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,1,5,0)="informing the user an error occurred and that their changes will not be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,1,6,0)="saved, and then allowing the user to exit the option gracefully."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,1,7,0)="NOIS #LAH-0401-61827, PAL-0701-60050."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,1,9,0)="2. Three sites reported a problem with the date variable PSGDT causing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,1,10,0)="undefined errors. This patch corrects this problem by defining the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,1,11,0)="variable if it has not already been defined."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",58,1,12,0)="NOIS# LAH-0401-61509, BRX-0600-12114, and LIT-0600-71001."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,0)="50^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,0)="^^71^71^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,1,0)="1. The Pharmacy Ordering Enhancements (POE) project provides enhancements"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,2,0)="to Pharmacy Data Management (PDM) V. 1.0, Inpatient Medications V. 5.0,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,3,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0, and Order Entry/Results Reporting (OE/RR) V."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,4,0)="3.0 medication ordering dialogues to eliminate redundant entry of drug"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,5,0)="information during medication order entry, provide a more consistent"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,6,0)="medication order entry process, provide expanded order checking, display"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,7,0)="documented drug formulary statuses and corresponding"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,8,0)="restriction/guidelines to the provider and pharmacist at the time of order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,9,0)="entry, and improve the process of medication order transfer between"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,10,0)="Inpatient Medications and Outpatient Pharmacy applications.  This project"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,11,0)="directly supports Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS), which is a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,12,0)="key component of Veterans Health Administration's (VHA) plan to expand"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,13,0)="support for clinical operations. Additionally, order checks will be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,14,0)="provided for medication orders for which a dispense drug has not been"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,15,0)="selected during the CPRS order entry process. It is also intended as a way"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,16,0)="to help meet the goal outlined in Objective 8, Action 1 in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,17,0)="Prescription for Change, which outlines the need to coordinate"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,18,0)="national/Veterans Integrated Service Network (VISN) formularies and share"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,19,0)="drug treatment guideline information. This project will promote system-"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,20,0)="wide sharing of drug reviews and treatment guidelines thereby enhancing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,21,0)="patient safety."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,23,0)="This project consists of four patches that work together to accomplish"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,24,0)="these goals listed in order of install:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,26,0)="     PSO*7*46"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,27,0)="     OR*3*94"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,28,0)="     PSS*1*38"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,29,0)="     PSJ*5*50"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,31,0)="2. A problem was reported by a site when an order was placed through the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,32,0)="Inpatient Medications dialogue. When pharmacy finished the order, they"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,33,0)="were prompted to finish as either IV or Unit Dose. If the user chose to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,34,0)="finish this as an IV, a new order was created.  With the installation of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,35,0)="the POE project a new order will no longer be created. This patch corrects"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,36,0)="this problem.  NOIS# WNY-0498-10040."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,38,0)="3. A problem was found when entering a ""P"" at the Start Date/Time prompt"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,39,0)="for a Unit Dose order.  The user always received the message ""No other"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,40,0)="order found with this drug."", even if there was another order with the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,41,0)="same orderable item.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,43,0)="4. Inpatient Medications will be adding a new parameter to the PHARMACY"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,44,0)="SYSTEM file (#59.7). The parameter will be 'CALC UNITS NEEDED PRN ORDERS'."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,45,0)="The parameter will allow for the calculation of UNITS NEEDED on the Pick"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,46,0)="List for orders with PRN in the schedule.  Currently orders with PRN in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,47,0)="the schedule are shown on the Pick List with a UNITS NEEDED of 0.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,48,0)="functionality was requested in E3R #12078, which had been reviewed and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,49,0)="approved by the Inpatient Medications E3R Workgroup and assigned a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,50,0)="priority of low.  With the changes in CPRS for the POE project to include"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,51,0)="the PRN button, it was felt that this should be addressed now since the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,52,0)="potential exists for Inpatient Medications to receive more orders with PRN"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,53,0)="in the schedule."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,55,0)="5.  A problem was reported by a site where they had a schedule of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,56,0)="APPLY@09/REMOVE@21 in their ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1) and the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,57,0)="admin times were not defaulting into the order when it was finished.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,58,0)="patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# SPO-0101-50812."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,60,0)="6. A problem was reported by a site where they had a schedule of Q3MONTHS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,61,0)="in the ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1) and the frequency was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,62,0)="calculated as 1440, which would be a daily schedule.  Changes were made in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,63,0)="Pharmacy Data Management (PDM), Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA),"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,64,0)="and Inpatient Medications to tighten up the code, which calculates the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,65,0)="frequency of the orders.  This patch corrects the Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,66,0)="portion of the problem.  PSS*1*38 addresses the same issue in PDM. NOIS#"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,67,0)="SHE-1200-51826."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,69,0)="7. E3R# 15571 asks that the Pick List round up the units per dose to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,70,0)="next whole number if it is not a whole number and use this to calculate"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",59,1,71,0)="the number of doses needed for an order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,0)="63^3011231^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,0)="^^44^44^3011231"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,1,0)="1. A site reported a problem where a one-time order could not be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,2,0)="discontinued by the provider because it was expired due to the start and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,3,0)="stop date being the same. However, the medication still displayed in Bar"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,4,0)="Code Medication Administration (BCMA) V. 1.0 because of the 12-hour rule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,5,0)="for displaying one-time orders on the Virtual Due List.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,6,0)="corrects this problem by changing the way the stop date for one-time"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,7,0)="orders is calculated. There will be a ward parameter, system parameter and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,8,0)="the standard calculation. The hierarchy will be to check the one-time ward"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,9,0)="parameter first, if not defined, check the system parameter.  If the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,10,0)="system parameter is not defined, the system will use the continuous order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,11,0)="parameters to determine the stop date, rather than the start and stop date"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,12,0)="being equal.  Then, when BCMA marks the medication as 'Given', Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,13,0)="Medications will expire the order. NOIS# BUT-0501-20609"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,15,0)="2. Inpatient Medications has been asked to add the BCMA Last Action to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,16,0)="order view screen.  Users will begin to see BCMA ORDER LAST ACTION"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,17,0)="MM/DD/YY HH:MM BCMA ACTION upon installation of this patch on the line"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,18,0)="following the Med Route information.  If the line ends with an * that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,19,0)="means that the BCMA Last Action was not made against this order, but"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,20,0)="against the previous order this order was created from due to a change or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,21,0)="renewal."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,23,0)="3. A problem was found with the date calculation for the start date for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,24,0)="renewal orders in PSJ*5*47. Please note:  PSJ*5*47 should not be removed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,25,0)="If the frequency for the order was a time other than an even number of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,26,0)="hours and the expected time for the new order to start was either 10am or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,27,0)="8pm, the date/time format stored internally contained a trailing 0.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,28,0)="is an invalid date format. This patch corrects this problem.  In addition"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,29,0)="to correcting the date calculation, there is a cleanup routine to correct"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,30,0)="any problems in the current data. The cleanup has two phases.  First, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,31,0)="data is analyzed to determine if there are any problems.  When the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,32,0)="analysis is complete, the person who installed the patch will receive a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,33,0)="mail message, ""INPATIENT MEDS ORDER CHECK COMPLETED"", indicating the check"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,34,0)="has completed.  If errors are found, the cleanup is performed and a second"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,35,0)="message, ""INPATIENT MEDS ORDER CLEANUP COMPLETED"", is sent to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,36,0)="installer indicating that cleanup is complete.  The messages are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,37,0)="informational only.  No action is required.  NOIS# DAY-0701-41935"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,39,0)="4. With the release of the Pharmacy Ordering Enhancements patches, two"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,40,0)="spaces were allowed in the schedule field.  In testing, it was discovered"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,41,0)="that a user could enter the two spaces at the end of the schedule and it"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,42,0)="was accepted by the software.  The software was not intended to work this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,43,0)="way.  Upon installation of this patch, the trailing spaces will be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",60,1,44,0)="stripped off the text the user enters at the schedule prompt."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,0)="66 SEQ #61^3020204^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,0)="^^22^22^3020204"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,1,0)="1.  A site reported a problem with the calculation of the start date for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,2,0)="renewal orders.  If the start date/time calculated fell between midnight"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,3,0)="and 1:00am, the time was truncated from the VA FileMan date and time.  The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,4,0)="problem with these orders is that they will not appear on the Bar Code"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,5,0)="Medication Administration (BCMA) V. 1.0 Virtual Due List (VDL) nor will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,6,0)="they appear on the Missed Medications Report.  In addition to correcting"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,7,0)="the date calculation, there is a cleanup routine to correct any problems"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,8,0)="in the current data. The cleanup has two phases.  First, the orders with a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,9,0)="stop date no older than 30 days are analyzed to determine if there are any"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,10,0)="problems.  When the analysis is complete, the person who installed the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,11,0)="patch will receive a MailMan message, ""INPATIENT MEDS ORDER CHECK"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,12,0)="COMPLETED"", indicating the check has completed.  If errors are found, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,13,0)="cleanup is performed and a second message, ""INPATIENT MEDS ORDER CLEANUP"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,14,0)="COMPLETED"", is sent to the installer indicating that cleanup is complete"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,15,0)="with a listing of the effected patients and the orders. The list is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,16,0)="provided so that personnel can ensure the patients received their"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,17,0)="medications."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,19,0)="2.  During testing of the changes for one-time orders it was discovered"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,20,0)="that the schedule was overriding the schedule type on Unit Dose orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,21,0)="For Unit Dose orders, the schedule type should take precedence.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",61,1,22,0)="patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,0)="56 SEQ #62^3020226^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,0)="^^79^79^3020226"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,1,0)="****************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,2,0)="****           Pharmacy Ordering Enhancements (POE)         ****"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,3,0)="****                    MUST BE INSTALLED                   ****"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,4,0)="****              prior to installing this patch.           ****"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,5,0)="****************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,7,0)="1. E3R #11794 - RETURN TO MED PROFILE AFTER ORDER ENTRY- The E3R suggests"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,8,0)="the following: after order entry, return the user to the profile view of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,9,0)="the patient's orders and require that they quit out of the profile in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,10,0)="order to select a new patient. Justification is that it works this way in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,11,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0 and should work similarly in Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,12,0)="Medications V. 5.0. This patch will implement the requested functionality."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,13,0)="NOIS# ISL-0800-50420."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,15,0)="2. E3R #12370 - FORCE SECOND SCREEN TO DISPLAY WHEN FINISHING ORDERS WITH"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,16,0)="ORDER CHECKS. The E3R describes forcing the view of Computerized Patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,17,0)="Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0 order checks, when present, on screen two of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,18,0)="order finishing regardless of backdoor pharmacy order checks. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,19,0)="will implement the requested functionality."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,21,0)="3. The Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] option, following the completion of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,22,0)="an order, does not perform patient locking at the ""Select DRUG:"" prompt."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,23,0)="The option continues processing orders for the patient previously selected"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,24,0)="but does not maintain a lock on the patient, allowing a pharmacist and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,25,0)="clinician to order meds on the same patient at the same time. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,26,0)="patch resolves this problem by removing the ""Select Drug:"" prompt and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,27,0)="forcing users to use the New Order Entry action. NOIS# ISL-0800-50420."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,29,0)="4. Several sites have reported problems with the entry of the infusion"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,30,0)="rate through CPRS V. 1.0 and the infusion rate returned to CPRS V. 1.0 by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,31,0)="Inpatient Medications V. 5.0. This patch will correct these problems."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,32,0)="NOIS# LOU-0501-42191 and DAY-1298-40645."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,34,0)="5. An undefined error, <UNDEFINED>EN+2^PSJO1 occurs during the Order Entry"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,35,0)="[PSJU NE] option when a patient name is entered, then New Order Entry"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,36,0)="action is selected at the ""Select Action:"" prompt, then a drug is entered,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,37,0)="then ""^"" is entered at the ""DOSAGE ORDERED:"" prompt, and either ""^"" or """""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,38,0)="are entered at the ""Select DRUG:"" prompt. This patch fixes this problem by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,39,0)="ensuring required variables are set up regardless of whether the New Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,40,0)="Entry action is selected before or after the View Profile action."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,42,0)="6. A problem was reported with the API that returns the activity log"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,43,0)="information to BCMA for Unit Dose orders. The first entry in the activity"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,44,0)="log was not being returned. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,46,0)="7. A site reported a problem with the display of Restriction Guidelines"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,47,0)="during Order Entry in Inpatient Medications V. 5.0. The change will allow"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,48,0)="the user to abort the display with '^' when the display is more than one"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,49,0)="page. Platinum project 3R211M-04-180. (PSJDIN)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,51,0)="8.  A site reported a problem with the display in the DOSAGE ORDERED"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,52,0)="column on the BCMA Virtual Due List.  For certain IV orders, it was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,53,0)="displaying an incorrect amount.  DOSAGE ORDERED is not used for IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,54,0)="orders; in fact, the field cannot be accessed from the IV view of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,55,0)="patient's orders. However, when a provider enters an order in CPRS V. 1.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,56,0)="as a unit dose order, there is a DOSAGE field.  If that order is then"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,57,0)="finished in pharmacy as an IV, the data remains in the global but is no"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,58,0)="longer accessible.  However, it was still being sent to BCMA in the API."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,59,0)="This patch resolves this problem by no longer sending this in the API."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,60,0)="NOIS# SLC-0801-50680"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,62,0)="9. A request was made by the Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,63,0)="modify an Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 procedure call that returns order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,64,0)="checking information. The modification contained in this patch will help"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,65,0)="CPRS accurately associate the CPRS order with its corresponding order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,66,0)="checks and identify the order as having originated from either Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,67,0)="Medications V. 5.0 or Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0. Patches OR*3*123 and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,68,0)="PSO*7.0*81 must also be installed for this change to go into effect."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,69,0)="The original NOIS submitted to CPRS is DUR-0801-32713. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,71,0)="10. During the testing of the Pharmacy Order Enhancement patches a site "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,72,0)="reported a problem on their IV Fluid orders that were placed through CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,73,0)="There were times when the additive or solution defaulted in the order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,74,0)="were inactive.  An additional check was added to PSJHL4 to screen out "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,75,0)="inactive additives and solutions from the ones defaulted into the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,77,0)="11. A site reported a problem with the validation of day of week"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,78,0)="schedules for IV orders.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",62,1,79,0)="NOIS# MIN-1001-41563 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,0)="67 SEQ #63^3020226^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,0)="^^41^41^3020226"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,1,0)="1. A site reported receiving an error when attempting to print a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,2,0)="Medication Administration Record (MAR) for an IV order that contained"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,3,0)="administration times.  This patch corrects this problem by modifying MAR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,4,0)="print to ignore administration times for IV orders, unless they are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,5,0)="Piggyback, Chemotherapy Piggyback or Intermittent Syringe orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,6,0)="NOIS# CLE-0901-41216"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,8,0)="2. A site reported receiving an error when attempting to edit an order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,9,0)="immediately after copying it to a new order.  The error only occurs when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,10,0)="editing the original order, not the newly copied order.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,11,0)="corrects the problem by preserving the original order's dispense drug."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,12,0)="NOIS# ANN-1201-40453"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,14,0)="3. A site reported a problem when running the Patients on Specific"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,15,0)="Drug(s) [PSJ PDV] option and selecting List by (O)rderable Item.  The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,16,0)="Inactive Date for the Orderable Item was no longer being displayed as an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,17,0)="identifier.  This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# PAL-1101-62555."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,19,0)="4. A site reported a problem with the Pick List [PSJU PL] option.  After"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,20,0)="installing the Pharmacy Ordering Enhancements, each order's Special"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,21,0)="Instructions no longer appear on the Pick List.  This patch corrects the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,22,0)="problem by displaying the Special Instructions on the Pick List."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,23,0)="NOIS# WRJ-1201-11762."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,25,0)="5. A site reported a problem with the stop date calculation when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,26,0)="finishing IV orders.  The stop date for the one-time orders was being"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,27,0)="used for all following orders.  This patch corrects this problem by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,28,0)="excluding one-time orders from the stop date calculation when the IV site"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,29,0)="parameter specifies that all orders should have the same stop date."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,30,0)="NOIS# SAG-1201-40283."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,32,0)="6. A site reported a problem with the editing of an order's dispense drug."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,33,0)="Multiple dispense drugs can be added to the order, but the ability to edit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,34,0)="or delete incorrect dispense drugs no longer exists.  This patch corrects"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,35,0)="this problem by allowing dispense drugs to be edited and deleted."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,36,0)="NOIS# UNY-1001-12315."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,38,0)="7. If a pending order can be finished as either Unit Dose or IV, user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,39,0)="with the PSJ RNFINISH key can't finish the order as Unit Dose.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,40,0)="patch will allow the nurses to finish Inpatient Med orders as Unit Dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",63,1,41,0)="orders.  NOIS: BHH-0102-40058."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,0)="64 SEQ #64^3020226^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,0)="^^54^54^3020226"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,1,0)="1. A site reported a problem when editing the orderable item in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,2,0)="Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] option. The stop date is not being set"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,3,0)="correctly. This patch corrects this problem by recalculating the stop date"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,4,0)="for an order if the orderable item is changed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,5,0)="NOIS# BOI-1299-51410."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,7,0)="2. A site reported receiving an error when attempting to print history to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,8,0)="a printer from the Activity Logs (AL) action of the Inpatient Order Entry"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,9,0)="[PSJ OE] option.  This patch corrects this problem and allows the user to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,10,0)="print history to a printer.  NOIS# ALB-0501-50053."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,12,0)="3. A site reported a problem where inactive dispense drugs were displayed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,13,0)="during a '?' lookup at the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] option.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,14,0)="patch will correct the problem by removing drugs from the display that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,15,0)="have an inactive date prior to the current date."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,16,0)="NOIS# WPB-0901-32173."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,18,0)="4. A site reported a problem with the SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS sub-field (#8)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,19,0)="within the UNIT DOSE multiple (#62) in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,20,0)="Edits to this field are not sent properly to the Computerized Patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,21,0)="Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0 under the following circumstances:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,22,0)="  1) user holds the PSJ RNURSE key and no other pharmacy keys"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,23,0)="  2) place a new order with special instructions and accept and verify it"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,24,0)="  3) go back in and edit the special instructions (verify option inactive)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,25,0)="The resulting order's special instructions display differently on the Meds"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,26,0)="tab and Orders tab in CPRS. This patch corrects the problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,27,0)="NOIS# BOI-0901-51460."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,29,0)="5. The Inpatient Medications E3R Workgroup approved a change to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,30,0)="Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] option View Profile activity that would"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,31,0)="continue to support placing the DISPENSE DRUG multiple (#2) within the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,32,0)="UNIT DOSE multiple (#62) in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) on screen 1 of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,33,0)="the order view if it is a single entry. If multiple dispense drugs"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,34,0)="are entered, all the dispense drugs will be displayed on the second"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,35,0)="screen. This patch will implement the requested change."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,36,0)="E3R# 16130."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,38,0)="6. During internal testing, it was discovered that there was a problem"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,39,0)="with the entry of MED ROUTE in Abbreviated Order Entry.  Even if the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,40,0)="default is accepted for MED ROUTE, a lookup is still shown and a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,41,0)="selection is required. This has been corrected in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,43,0)="7. A site reported a problem with being allowed to edit an order and make"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,44,0)="the start date after the stop date.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,45,0)="NOIS# WIM-0801-20934"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,47,0)="8. A site reported a problem with a variable name in the routine"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,48,0)="PSJLIVFD being misspelled. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,49,0)="NOIS# PUG-1101-50620"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,51,0)="9. During internal testing, it was discovered that in backdoor order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,52,0)="entry, if a one-time schedule was entered, the schedule type was changed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,53,0)="to one-time, but the display didn't reflect the change until after the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",64,1,54,0)="user accepted the order.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,0)="65 SEQ #65^3020315^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,0)="^^56^56^3020315"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,1,0)="1. A site reported inappropriately receiving the error message, ""Dosage"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,2,0)="Ordered and Dispense Drug are not compatible"" while attempting to finish"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,3,0)="an order. This message displayed when the order's dosage contained a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,4,0)="numeric value that appeared in the dose more than once. For example:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,5,0)="1MG/1ML, 2ML/2VIAL, and 3MG/33ML. This patch corrects the problem. NOIS#"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,6,0)="MAC-1101-60243."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,8,0)="2. A site has requested a report that lists orders containing free"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,9,0)="text dosages. The report will be sorted by drug, and the selection"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,10,0)="criteria will be a range of dates. Included in the report is the total"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,11,0)="number of times the particular free text dosage occurred during the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,12,0)="selected time period, the name of the provider or providers responsible"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,13,0)="for entering the free text dosage, and the number of occurrences for each"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,14,0)="provider. The Free Text Dosage Report [PSJU DOSAGE REPORT] option has been"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,15,0)="added to the Reports Menu [PSJU REPORTS] option."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,17,0)="3. A site reported a problem with the Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 labels"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,18,0)="printed through Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0. If the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,19,0)="Unit Dose order had a schedule type of Fill On Request, the admin times"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,20,0)="were not printing on the label printed by CPRS.  This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,21,0)="problem. NOIS# MAN-0200-11846."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,23,0)="4. A site reported a problem with the schedule type when finishing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,24,0)="orders.  The problem was that there was an inconsistency between"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,25,0)="finishing orders and backdoor order entry.  This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,26,0)="problem.  NOIS# BIG-0901-71799"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,28,0)="5. Several sites have reported, after the installation of Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,29,0)="Ordering Enhancements, that they are unable to use their Quick Codes to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,30,0)="finish IV orders placed through CPRS. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,31,0)="NOIS# MIW-1101-41809 and POR-1101-52536."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,33,0)="6. A technician gets the following message: ""...Order deleted....Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,34,0)="deleted."" when trying to enter IV orders at the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,35,0)="OE] option. The problem occurs if ""^"" is entered to stop the VA FileMan"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,36,0)="listing of solutions at the ""Select SOLUTION:"" prompt. Upon receiving ""^"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,37,0)="as input, the option behaves as if the ""^"" was entered at the ""SOLUTION:"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,38,0)="prompt and deletes the order. This patch will correct this problem by only"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,39,0)="allowing deletion of the order if ""^"" is entered at the ""SOLUTION:"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,40,0)="prompt. Entering ""^"" at the ""'^' TO STOP:"" prompt will only abort the VA"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,41,0)="FileMan listing. NOIS# AMA-0801-70377."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,43,0)="7. In finishing a unit dose order, if the pharmacist edited Dispense"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,44,0)="Drug and Dosage Ordered at the same time, a warning message was displayed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,45,0)="stating the dosage did not match, the available dosages list displayed,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,46,0)="and the user became stuck in a loop. This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,47,0)="NOIS# PTH-0102-21320."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,49,0)="8. A site reported a problem with administration times when Quick Codes"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,50,0)="were used for IV Piggyback orders in the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,51,0)="option. If a schedule is defined for the Quick Code, but no administration"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,52,0)="times are defined, and appropriate administration times cannot be derived"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,53,0)="from the IV additive, administration times should default from the ward"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,54,0)="parameters. The administration times were not defaulting properly from the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,55,0)="ward parameters. This patch corrects the problem. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",65,1,56,0)="NOIS# HWH-0102-41454 and NOIS# HWH-0102-41770"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,0)="71 SEQ #66^3020315^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,0)="^^16^16^3020315"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,1,0)="A site reported a problem with IV orders that were using non-standard"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,2,0)="schedules.  If a schedule was Q18H or Q36H, it would appear as due every"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,3,0)="24 hours, rather than 18 or 36, respectively.  This would only happen on"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,4,0)="IV orders placed through the Computerized Patient Record System V. 1.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,5,0)="(CPRS).  This patch corrects this problem.  In addition to correcting the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,6,0)="frequency calculation, there is a cleanup routine to correct any problems"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,7,0)="in the current data. The cleanup has two phases.  First, the orders with a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,8,0)="start date after the installation of PSJ*5*50. When the analysis is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,9,0)="complete, the person who installed the patch will receive a MailMan"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,10,0)="message, ""INPATIENT MEDS ORDER CHECK COMPLETED"", indicating the check has"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,11,0)="completed.  If errors are found, the cleanup is performed and a second"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,12,0)="message, ""INPATIENT MEDS ORDER CLEANUP COMPLETED"", is sent to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,13,0)="installer indicating that cleanup is complete with a listing of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,14,0)="effected patients and the orders. The list is provided so that personnel"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,15,0)="can ensure the patients received their medications appropriately."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",66,1,16,0)="NOIS: IND-0202-40345 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,0)="70 SEQ #67^3020327^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,0)="^^19^19^3020327"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,1,0)="1. If the Orderable Item within a unit dose order is re-matched to a new "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,2,0)="Orderable Item due to dosage form change or any other reason, the new "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,3,0)="Orderable Item will replace the existing Orderable Item in the order when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,4,0)="the current order is renewed. NOIS# ISB-0202-30541."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,6,0)="2. Currently, Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 supplies an API #3243,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,7,0)="supporting the call $$ACTIVE^PSJORREN, to Computerized Patient Record"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,8,0)="System (CPRS) V. 1.0, which enables them to determine whether an "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,9,0)="Inpatient Medications order is renewable. This functionality will be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,10,0)="changed for IV orders to return a 0 for a non-renewable order and a 1 for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,11,0)="a renewable order. The Unit Dose functionality will not be affected."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,13,0)="3. A problem was reported where a site was discontinuing IV and Unit Dose "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,14,0)="orders with a Nature of Order of Duplicate.  When the user viewed the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,15,0)="orders on the CPRS Orders Tab, the Reason for DC was showing on some "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,16,0)="orders as ORDER CANCELED, ORDER DISCONTINUED, or DUPLICATE.  With the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,17,0)="installation of this patch, the Reason for DC should show as DUPLICATE for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,18,0)="all orders discontinued where the Nature of Order selected is Duplicate."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",67,1,19,0)="NOIS# BHH-0202-40835."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,0)="72 SEQ #68^3020327^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,0)="^^42^42^3020327"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,1,0)="1. A problem was reported where orders entered via Computerized Patient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,2,0)="Record System (CPRS) were not always being filed in the appropriate "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,3,0)="manner in the NON-VERIFIED ORDERS file (#53.1).  The orders were being "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,4,0)="filed in such a way that the pharmacist couldn't finish them to be "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,5,0)="dispensed from the IV or Unit Dose package. This patch will correct this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,6,0)="problem.  NOIS # BEC-0202-20544 & PAL-0202-61440."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,8,0)="2. A site reported a problem with the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,9,0)="option. When viewing a patient's profile, if the patient has no orders to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,10,0)="display, the user is prompted to enter a new patient without being given"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,11,0)="the opportunity to continue to edit the current patient. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,12,0)="corrects this problem by returning the user to the Patient Information"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,13,0)="screen after displaying the 'NO ORDERS FOUND' message."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,14,0)="NOIS # REN-0202-61475."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,16,0)="3. A site reported a problem with the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,17,0)="option. If the Orderable Item was edited, a message was displayed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,18,0)="informing the user that the Dispense Drug and Dosage would be deleted if"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,19,0)="the user continued to edit the order, while nothing would change if the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,20,0)="user cancelled the edit. This message was in error as the Dispense Drug"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,21,0)="and Dosage were deleted regardless of the user's actions. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,22,0)="corrects this problem by displaying the warning message earlier in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,23,0)="edit to allow the user to cancel the edit before the order is changed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,24,0)="NOIS # OKL-0202-72069. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,26,0)="4. A site reported a problem with the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,27,0)="option. Under certain circumstances, the patient's order profile could not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,28,0)="be viewed because the VP View Profile action was not selectable. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,29,0)="patch corrects this problem by allowing the profile view of the patient's"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,30,0)="orders to be viewed when appropriate."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,31,0)="NOIS # STX-0202-72021."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,33,0)="5. A site reported a problem with the strength of the drug displaying on "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,34,0)="the Orders Tab in CPRS for orders that had been renewed.  The problem "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,35,0)="resulted from message segments longer than 245 characters not being split "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,36,0)="appropriately.  This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,37,0)="NOIS LOU-0202-42178."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,39,0)="6. If the user answers ""NO"" at the ""Do you want to copy this order? No//"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,40,0)="prompt when using the hidden action COPY, the variable PSGPDRG became "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,41,0)="undefined when the user accepting the original order after it was edited."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",68,1,42,0)="NOIS OKL-0202-72417."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,0)="73 SEQ #69^3020408^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,0)="^^16^16^3020408"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,1,0)="1. When using the Standard Schedule Edit [PSS SCHEDULE EDIT] option, the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,2,0)="software is not allowing the users to set the ""TYPE OF SCHEDULE"" to ""Day"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,3,0)="Of Week"" for entries such as ""MO-WE-FR@09"". The time on the end of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,4,0)="schedule name was causing the problem. This patch fixes this problem. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,5,0)="NOIS# BUT-0202-21128, CLE-0202-40858, and ASH-0202-30433."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,7,0)="2. A site reported a problem with the Free Text Dosage Report [PSJU"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,8,0)="DOSAGE REPORT] option. An error caused the report to halt prior to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,9,0)="completion. This patch corrects the problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,10,0)="NOIS# REN-0302-60743."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,12,0)="3. A site reported a problem that occurred during the finishing process"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,13,0)="in the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] option. When an IV Quick Code was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,14,0)="used to finish an IV Piggyback order, an error occurred that prevented"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,15,0)="the user from finishing the order. This patch corrects the problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",69,1,16,0)="NOIS# MAR-0302-20770."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,0)="69 SEQ #70^3020423^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,0)="^^41^41^3020423"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,1,0)="1.  A site reported a problem with an inconsistency in the the calculation"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,2,0)="of stop dates for one-time Outpatient IV orders.  This patch corrects "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,3,0)="this problem.  NOIS#  SPO-0102-50221"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,5,0)="2.  During internal testing it was discovered that an IV schedule of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,6,0)="ONETIME was not being marked as a one-time order when sent to Bar Code "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,7,0)="Medication Administration V. 1.0 (BCMA).  This patch corrects this "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,8,0)="problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,10,0)="3.  A site reported a problem with renewing IV orders.  If the original "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,11,0)="order was expired and the Start Date on the new order was edited, the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,12,0)="Stop Date on the original order was also changed.  This patch corrects "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,13,0)="this problem.  NOIS#  HUN-0102-20878"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,15,0)="4.  A site reported a problem with one-time IV labels printing in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,16,0)="scheduled label job every day, rather than only one time.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,17,0)="corrects this problem by only allowing reprints once the label has been"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,18,0)="printed for a one-time IV order.  NOIS#  ALB-0102-51931, PHO-0202-60736"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,20,0)="5.  A site reported a problem with finishing IV orders using the Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,21,0)="Entry (IV) [PSJI ORDER] option. If a new order was created as a result of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,22,0)="edits made during finishing, the ""Instructions:"" prompt continued to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,23,0)="display the instructions from the old order. The new order is unique, and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,24,0)="instructions from the old order may not apply to the new order. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,25,0)="patch corrects the problem by removing the old instructions."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,26,0)="NOIS#  SFC-0102-62594."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,28,0)="6.  A site reported a problem with finishing Inpatient IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,29,0)="Piggyback orders using the Order Entry (IV) [PSJI ORDER] option. The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,30,0)="Orderable Item was selectable, but not editable. This patch fixes the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,31,0)="problem by allowing the Orderable Item to be edited."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,32,0)="NOIS#  SFC-0102-62594."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,34,0)="7. A site reported a problem with the way IV orders were displayed in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,35,0)="profile view of a patient's orders within the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,36,0)="OE] option. When an IV order with more than one solution was displayed,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,37,0)="each solution showed the infusion rate for the order, incorrectly making"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,38,0)="it appear each solution would be infused at that rate. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,39,0)="corrects this problem by only displaying the infusion rate next to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,40,0)="first solution."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",70,1,41,0)="NOIS# MIW-0202-41045"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,0)="68^3020423^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,0)="^^22^22^3020423"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,1,0)="As a part of the Pharmacy Benefits Management (PBM) Extract enhancement"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,2,0)="project, two new fields were added to the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,3,0)="They are FIRST SERVICE DATE (#.07) and ACTUAL/HISTORICAL FLAG (#.08)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,4,0)="With the addition of these two fields, Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,5,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0 have been modified to set this information"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,6,0)="when the first order for a patient becomes active."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,8,0)="This project consists of three patches combined in a master build."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,9,0)="Installation of this master build should be coordinated among the three"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,10,0)="packages affected since only one installation is necessary.  The patches,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,11,0)="in order of install, are:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,13,0)="      PSS*1*52  PHARMACY DATA MANAGEMENT V. 1.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,14,0)="      PSJ*5*68  INPATIENT MEDICATIONS V. 5.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,15,0)="      PSO*7*95  OUTPATIENT PHARMACY V. 7.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,17,0)="Upon completion of the installation of these three patches, the master"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,18,0)="build will start a routine that will build the two new fields from"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,19,0)="historical data in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55).  When the build is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,20,0)="complete, the user who initiated the install and the members of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,21,0)="PSU PBM mail group will receive a message with a subject of BUILD OF FIRST"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",71,1,22,0)="PHARMACY SERVICE INFO COMPLETE."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",72,0)="75 SEQ #72^3020506^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",72,1,0)="^^7^7^3020506"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",72,1,1,0)="1. A problem was reported by a site where the free text dosage ordered"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",72,1,2,0)="entered into an order in Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) was not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",72,1,3,0)="showing in the dosage ordered field in Inpatient Medications.  The problem"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",72,1,4,0)="was that Inpatient was checking for the free text dosage ordered to be 20"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",72,1,5,0)="characters or less, this was not compatible with what is allowed in CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",72,1,6,0)="The Inpatient Medications check was changed to accept 60 characters or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",72,1,7,0)="less, which is compatible with CPRS. NOIS # DDC-0402-50270."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,0)="58^3020528^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,0)="^^112^112^3020528"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,1,0)=" 1. The Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) V. 2.0 release provides "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,2,0)=" enhancements to Pharmacy Data Management (PDM) V. 1.0, and Inpatient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,3,0)=" Medications V. 5.0. The BCMA V. 2.0 release expands and improves the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,4,0)=" process of medication administration, especially in the area of IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,5,0)=" medications."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,7,0)=" In support of this, Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 and PDM V. 1.0 have "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,8,0)=" added the ability to print barcode identifiers on IV labels, IV order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,9,0)=" verification and the ability to receive done priority orders via the CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,10,0)=" Med Order button in BCMA V. 2.0."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,11,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,12,0)=" This project consists of two patches and a new version of BCMA that work"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,13,0)=" together to accomplish these goals listed in order of install:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,14,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,15,0)="      PSS*1*46  PHARMACY DATA MANAGEMENT V. 1.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,16,0)="      PSJ*5*58  INPATIENT MEDICATIONS V. 5.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,17,0)="      BAR CODE MED ADMIN 2.0  BAR CODE MEDICATION ADMINISTRATION V. 2.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,18,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,19,0)=" 2. Two sites reported a problem with comments from one IV order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,20,0)=" showing up on a different IV order. Since edits to provider comments are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,21,0)=" no longer allowed interactively from within Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,22,0)=" OE] option, this patch corrects the problem by removing the code that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,23,0)=" performs updates to provider comments. NOIS# MOU-0100-30945 and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,24,0)=" MAC-1100-61760."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,25,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,26,0)=" 3. A site reported a problem with an IV order appearing on the profile "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,27,0)=" view as a Continuous order when it was a One-time order. This patch "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,28,0)=" corrects this problem. NOIS# DUB-0102-32272."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,29,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,30,0)=" 4. A correction was made to only allow nurse and pharmacist users to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,31,0)=" Speed Discontinue IV orders.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,32,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,33,0)=" 5. A correction was made to allow Speed Discontinue Unit Dose orders if "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,34,0)=" the status was not ""Discontinued"", ""Discontinued (Edit)"" or ""Expired""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,35,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,36,0)=" 6. If a technician or a ward clerk edited a Unit Dose order and caused a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,37,0)=" Non-Verified order to be created, the user was able to discontinue the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,38,0)=" Non-Verified order even if the user parameter ""ALLOW USER TO D/C ORDERS:"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,39,0)=" was set to NO, which means the user should only be allowed to mark orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,40,0)=" to be discontinued. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,41,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,42,0)=" 7. A site reported an error occurred when copying a Unit Dose order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,43,0)=" If the user parameter ""ORDER ENTRY PROCESS:"" was set to WARD and an edit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,44,0)=" was made during copy, the user would error out while accepting the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,45,0)=" change. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,46,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,47,0)=" 8. The Test Control Codes (IV) [PSJI CONTROL CODES] option has been added"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,48,0)=" to the Label Menu (IV) [PSJI LBLMENU] option. This option allows the user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,49,0)=" to print an IV label for the purpose of verifying their control code"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,50,0)=" definition. An entire label is not printed, simply a bar code and one"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,51,0)=" line of underscores."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,52,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,53,0)=" 9. A couple of sites reported that the schedule did not display on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,54,0)=" profile for IV orders when using the Inpatient Profile [PSJ PR] option."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,55,0)=" This patch corrects this problem. NOIS# CON-0302-12151 and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,56,0)=" MAR-0402-21639."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,57,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,58,0)=" 10. A site reported receiving a null subscript error when an IV order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,59,0)=" came from Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0 and Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,60,0)=" Medications V. 5.0 was unable to determine the correct solution to place"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,61,0)=" in the pending order. The order created had a volume but no solution."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,62,0)=" NOIS# WAS-0402-21482."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,63,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,64,0)=" 11. While trying to reproduce a problem reported by a site with the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,65,0)=" display of Special Instructions we discovered a problem that could occur"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,66,0)=" on orders placed through CPRS when copying Provider Comments into the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,67,0)=" Special Instructions field. If the Provider Comments contained a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,68,0)=" character string that exceeded 70 characters without having a space in "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,69,0)=" it the user couldn't see the last several characters on the screen. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,70,0)=" patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,71,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,72,0)=" 12. Post-Install will do the following:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,73,0)=" IV verification is now required with the PSJ*5*58 patch. For orders that "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,74,0)=" were entered prior to the installation of this patch, an algorithm was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,75,0)=" designed to determine the verifying pharmacist. The verifying user IEN "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,76,0)=" is stored in the VERIFYING PHARMACIST sub-field (#140) of the IV multiple"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,77,0)=" (#100) of the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55), which was added with patch "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,78,0)=" PSS*1*46. The DATE VERIFIED BY PHARMACIST sub-field (#141)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,79,0)=" of the IV multiple (#100) of the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55), which has"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,80,0)=" also been added with patch PSS*1*46, will reflect the installation date"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,81,0)=" and time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,82,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,83,0)=" The Activity Log for the IV Order stored the user name in free text."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,84,0)=" During this conversion, the free text user name is compared to the NEW"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,85,0)=" PERSON file (#200). If there is an exact and unique match, then the IEN"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,86,0)=" for this person is stored in the USER sub-field (#.06) of the ACTIVITY "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,87,0)=" LOG multiple (#40) of the IV multiple (#100) of the PHARMACY PATIENT file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,88,0)=" (#55) that was added with patch PSS*1*46."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,89,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,90,0)=" If the software is able to determine the user's IEN, for all affected IV "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,91,0)=" orders, and no intervention is required, the MailMan message generated "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,92,0)=" by the conversion will contain only the conversion information. The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,93,0)=" subject of this message will be: PSJ*5*58 IV Verification."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,94,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,95,0)=" When the software is unable to determine the user's IEN, the MailMan"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,96,0)=" message generated by this conversion will instruct the installer"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,97,0)=" to assign the Correct Change User Names in IV activity log [PSJI ACTIVITY"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,98,0)=" LOG VA200] option to a holder of the PSJI MGR security key who is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,99,0)=" familiar with the Pharmacy users to allow them to correct the unresolved"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,100,0)=" names. The subject of this message will be: PSJ*5*58 IV Verification."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,101,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,102,0)=" Once all of the unresolved names are resolved, another MailMan message "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,103,0)=" is generated. This message will instruct the user who ran the Correct"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,104,0)=" Change User Names in IV activity log [PSJI ACTIVITY LOG VA200] option to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,105,0)=" contact IRM to remove the option. The subject of this message is Changed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,106,0)=" names in IV orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,107,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,108,0)=" An entry is made in the ACTIVITY LOG multiple (#40) of the IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,109,0)=" multiple (#100) of the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) to indicate the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,110,0)=" verification action was performed during the installation of this patch. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,111,0)=" The user in the log entry is the verifying pharmacist determined during"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",73,1,112,0)=" the conversion."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,0)="74 SEQ #74^3020626^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,0)="^^21^21^3020626"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,1,0)="1. A site reported a problem with the finish of IV Piggyback orders in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,2,0)="Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] option. The calculation of the default stop"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,3,0)="date did not recognize the additive's number of days for an IV order. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,4,0)="caused incorrect stop dates to be calculated and displayed. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,5,0)="corrects the problem by using the correct parameter to calculate the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,6,0)="default stop date."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,7,0)="NOIS # CHA-0302-31253."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,9,0)="2. A site reported a problem entering time-based administration times in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,10,0)="the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] option. In the past, entry of a two"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,11,0)="digit or four digit number between 0 and 24 was permitted, but this format"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,12,0)="is currently invalid. This patch corrects the problem by restoring the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,13,0)="previously allowed format."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,14,0)="NOIS # BIG-0302-72850."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,16,0)="3. A site reported a problem with the Patients on Specific Drugs [PSJ"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,17,0)="PDV] report. Orders appeared on the report that were outside the selected"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,18,0)="date range. This patch corrects the problem by correcting invalid start"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,19,0)="and stop dates if possible. Orders with dates that cannot be corrected"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,20,0)="will be reported via mail message to the person installing the patch."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",74,1,21,0)="NOIS # MON-0202-52165."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",75,0)="79 SEQ #75^3020626^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",75,1,0)="^^6^6^3020626"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",75,1,1,0)="During testing of Bar Code Medication Administration V. 2.0, it was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",75,1,2,0)="discovered that the SIte Parameters (IV) [PSJI SITE PARAMETERS] option did"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",75,1,3,0)="not allow device lookup at the Label Device and Report Device prompts."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",75,1,4,0)="This patch corrects this problem by using the standard device"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",75,1,5,0)="handling routines to perform device lookup.  One side effect is that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",75,1,6,0)="you can no longer jump to these questions.  NOIS# ISB-0302-32189"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,0)="76 SEQ #76^3020710^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,0)="^^33^33^3020710"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,1,0)="1. During internal testing, a problem was discovered with the way"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,2,0)="Restriction/Guideline(s) were displayed in the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,3,0)="OE] option. The screen was not refreshed after displaying the Restriction/"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,4,0)="Guideline(s), and as a result, drug interactions appeared to scroll under"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,5,0)="the Restriction/Guideline(s). This patch corrects the problem by clearing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,6,0)="the screen before the drug interactions are displayed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,7,0)="NOIS # BIR-0302-32554"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,9,0)="2. A site reported a problem with finishing IV Quick Code orders in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,10,0)="Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] option. When an IV Quick Code was used to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,11,0)="finish an order, the Provider Comments did not appear in the Other Print"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,12,0)="Info when the prompt ""Copy the Provider Comments into Other Print Info"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,13,0)="(Yes/No/!):"" was answered in an affirmative manner. This patch corrects"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,14,0)="the problem by retaining copied Provider Comments in the Other Print Info"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,15,0)="if the IV Quick Code has no Other Print Info. If the IV Quick Code does"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,16,0)="contain Other Print Info, it will appear in the order's Other Print Info."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,17,0)="NOIS # MIN-1101-42563"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,19,0)="3. A site reported a problem with IV Quick Codes in IV Piggyback orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,20,0)="If there are no administration times present in the Quick Code, Additive,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,21,0)="or Ward Parameters, the user is prompted for a schedule with associated"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,22,0)="administration times. In this instance, the user selected a schedule, but"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,23,0)="the selected schedule's administration times were not saved with the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,24,0)="order. This patch corrects the problem by using the administration times"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,25,0)="associated with the selected schedule when appropriate."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,26,0)="NOIS # HWH-0102-41454"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,28,0)="4. A site reported a problem with the Free Text Dosage Report [PSJU"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,29,0)="DOSAGE REPORT] option. When a free text dosage was encountered that had"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,30,0)="been ordered by over thirty different physicians, the report did  not run"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,31,0)="to completion. This patch corrects the problem by allowing an unlimited"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,32,0)="number of physicians to appear for each on dosage the report."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",76,1,33,0)="NOIS # BAY-0402-30987"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,0)="77 SEQ #77^3020906^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,0)="^^13^13^3020906"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,1,0)="1. This patch will make sure active Unit Dose orders are created with a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,2,0)="Dispense Drug in the orders. NOIS: MOU-0102-32301, ANN-0202-42365,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,3,0)="SPO-0302-51657, MWV-0302-20778, OKL-0402-72901, MIN-0502-40440."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,5,0)="2. A clean-up routine will identify orders without a Dispense Drug and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,6,0)="make corrections, if appropriate. The person installing this patch will "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,7,0)="receive two MailMan messages, the first with the subject: PSJ*5*77"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,8,0)="INPATIENT MEDS ORDER CHECK COMPLETED will tell the user how many orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,9,0)="exist with no Dispense Drug, the second with the subject: PSJ*5*77"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,10,0)="INPATIENT MEDS ORDER CLEANUP COMPLETED will inform sites of any unresolved"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,11,0)="orders.  The user will get the second message if there are any orders with"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,12,0)="no Dispense Drugs.  If the first message says there are 0 orders with no"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",77,1,13,0)="Dispense Drugs, the second message will not be generated."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,0)="78 SEQ #78^3020906^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,0)="^^37^37^3020906"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,1,0)="1. This patch will make sure active Unit Dose orders are created with a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,2,0)="Dispense Drug in the orders. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,4,0)="2. This patch will ensure that Inpatient Medications orders entered via"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,5,0)="the Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) Med Order Button in Bar Code"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,6,0)="Medication Administration (BCMA) V. 2.0 have start, stop, and nurse"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,7,0)="verification dates without trailing zeros. The trailing zeros in the stop"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,8,0)="date caused users problems when using the Individual Label (IV) [PSJI"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,9,0)="LBLI] option on the Label Menu (IV) [PSJI LBLMENU] option on the IV Menu"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,10,0)="[PSJI MGR] option. When the user selected the PATIENT: and then tried to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,11,0)="view the SHORT PROFILE, they would get caught in a loop. NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,12,0)="MIN-0802-40347."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,14,0)="3. A clean-up routine will identify orders without a Dispense Drug and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,15,0)="make corrections, if appropriate. The person installing this patch will "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,16,0)="receive two MailMan messages, the first with the subject: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,17,0)="PSJ*5*78 INPATIENT MEDS DISPENSE DRUG ORDER CHECK COMPLETED will tell the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,18,0)="user how many orders exist with no Dispense Drug, the second with the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,19,0)="subject: PSJ*5*78 INPATIENT MEDS DISPENSE DRUG ORDER CLEANUP COMPLETED "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,20,0)="will inform sites of any unresolved orders. The user will get the second "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,21,0)="message if there are any orders with no Dispense Drugs. If the first "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,22,0)="message says there are 0 orders with no Dispense Drugs, the second "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,23,0)="message will not be generated. An additional MailMan message is generated "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,24,0)="when Inpatient Medications orders are checked for start, stop, or nurse "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,25,0)="verification dates with trailing zeros. The subject is PSJ*5*78 INPATIENT "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,26,0)="MEDS STOP DATE ORDER CHECK COMPLETED. This message will tell the user how "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,27,0)="many orders exist with invalid stop dates. The user will get a second "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,28,0)="message with the subject PSJ*5*78 INPATIENT MEDS STOP DATE ORDER CLEANUP "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,29,0)="COMPLETED if there are any orders with invalid stop dates. If the first "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,30,0)="message says there are 0 orders with invalid stop dates, the second "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,31,0)="message will not be generated."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,33,0)="4. When a nurse verified a pending IV order in Computerized Patient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,34,0)="Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0, the order was not filed as an IV order in "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,35,0)="Inpatient Medications V. 5.0. This patch will update the order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,36,0)="appropriately in the IV multiple (#100) of the PHARMACY PATIENT file "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",78,1,37,0)="(#55)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,0)="84 SEQ #79^3020906^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,0)="^^22^22^3020906"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,1,0)="1. A site reported a problem with IVPB labels for orders with Day-of-Week "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,2,0)="schedules. The problem was that labels were printing even on days when "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,3,0)="the medication wasn't due. This patch corrects this problem. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,4,0)="NOIS# MIN-0402-42144"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,6,0)="2. A site reported a problem that occurred periodically when an IV order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,7,0)="was edited during the finish process. This patch corrects the problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,8,0)="NOIS: MWV-0502-22511"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,10,0)="3. A site reported a problem with IVPB labels for one-time orders. If the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,11,0)="label had already printed, it wouldn't print, but it would still appear "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,12,0)="on the manufacturing list. This patch corrects the problem. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,13,0)="NOIS: UNY-0602-12797 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,15,0)="4. Inpatient Medications was requested by Decision Support System (DSS) to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,16,0)="include a new data element in the array of data that is currently sent to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,17,0)="DSS.  The new data element is the order start date/time. This should be "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,18,0)="transparent to Inpatient Medications users."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,20,0)="5. A potential problem was discovered by developers, where data nodes "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,21,0)="could be set inappropriately in the Unit Dose multiple of the PHARMACY "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",79,1,22,0)="PATIENT file (# 55).  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,0)="83 SEQ #80^3021008^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,0)="^^31^31^3021008"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,1,0)="1.  During the process of finishing an order, re-entering the same"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,2,0)="schedule causes the frequency of the order to be removed. This causes the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,3,0)="order to not display correctly on the Bar Code Medication Administration"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,4,0)="Virtual Due List. This patch corrects this problem. NOIS: CMS-0502-32446"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,6,0)="2.  After an interward transfer, a patient's orders are not displayed in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,7,0)="the Update Pick List [PSJU PLUP] option. These transferred orders are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,8,0)="displayed in the regular Pick List [PSJU PL] option. This patch corrects"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,9,0)="this problem by allowing previously existing orders to display on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,10,0)="update. NOIS: ANN-0502-40709"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,12,0)="3.  A patient that has been transferred to Absent Sick In Hospital (ASIH)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,13,0)="may have active orders with start dates prior to the transfer date. If the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,14,0)="date and time of the transfer is edited, inpatient orders are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,15,0)="automatically discontinued. This causes valid, active orders to be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,16,0)="improperly discontinued. This patch corrects the problem. NOIS:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,17,0)="PAL-0402-61286"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,19,0)="4.  During internal testing, it was discovered that there were differences"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,20,0)="in schedule validation between Unit Dose and IV orders. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,21,0)="corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,23,0)="5.  It was discovered that there were some inconsistencies with schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,24,0)="validation between Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 and Pharmacy Data"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,25,0)="Management V. 1.0. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,27,0)="6.  A problem occurs if a patient is transferred and new orders are added"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,28,0)="(and orders are not set up to auto-discontinue upon transfer). When the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,29,0)="update is run, the patient appears both on Ward A and Ward B, with old"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,30,0)="orders on the Ward A update and new orders on Ward B update. This patch "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",80,1,31,0)="corrects the problem. E3R: 15221"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",81,0)="86 SEQ #81^3021108^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",81,1,0)="^^3^3^3021108"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",81,1,1,0)="This patch contains the API to allow Computerized Patient Record System "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",81,1,2,0)="(CPRS) to automatically reinstate Inpatient Medication orders that were "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",81,1,3,0)="auto discontinued."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,0)="81 SEQ #82^3021108^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,0)="^^49^49^3021108"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,1,0)="1. When a one-time IV order is entered in advance, the scheduled label "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,2,0)="due on the start date is not being printed.  This patch will correct this "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,3,0)="problem.  NOIS: ASH-0402-32138."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,5,0)="2. Code changes were made due to the expiration of IA 903."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,7,0)="3. The Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW] option errors out when "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,8,0)="accessed by users without any pharmacy keys.  This patch will correct "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,9,0)="this problem.  NOIS: LOM-0502-62027."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,11,0)="4. The Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW] option includes patients "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,12,0)="with inactive non-verified/pending IV orders.  This patch will display "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,13,0)="patients with non-verified/pending IV orders that have future stop dates."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,15,0)="5. When using the Order Entry (IV) [PSJI ORDER] option on an outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,16,0)="and the second screen was displayed, the user was forced to enter an '^' "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,17,0)="to continue with the order.  This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,18,0)="SPO-0302-52679."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,20,0)="6. When a user enters an order through Pharmacy backdoor and answers the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,21,0)="following question ""Is this O.K.: NO//"" with a NO, the user will receive a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,22,0)="null subscript error.  This patch will correct this problem.  NOIS: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,23,0)="AAA-0502-N2276."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,25,0)="7. The PRINT NAME {2} (#.02) field of the IV SOLUTIONS file (#52.7) is not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,26,0)="being sent to Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) and Bar Code "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,27,0)="Medication Administration (BCMA).  This patch will correct this issue. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,28,0)="NOIS: LEX-0502-41218."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,30,0)="8. A site reported a problem with a one-time order that didn't expire "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,31,0)="after it had been administered.  The problem occurred because the schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,32,0)="type was Fill on Request.  This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,33,0)="NCH-0602-41182."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,35,0)="9. During internal testing, it was discovered that the BCMA API that "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,36,0)="returns Activity Log information was not sending the user's internal "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,37,0)="entry number for IV orders.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,39,0)="10. When the ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1) has a schedule "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,40,0)="contained ""PRN"", the Unit Dose and IV orders will not display on the Bar "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,41,0)="Code Medication Administration (BCMA) V. 2.0 if the Virtual Due List "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,42,0)="(VDL) had only the PRN box checked.  This patch will send the correct "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,43,0)="information to BCMA to display the order in the PRN session.  NOIS: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,44,0)="SAM-0702-22338."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,46,0)="11. A site reported a problem with being able to see BCMA ORDER LAST "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,47,0)="ACTION on active renewed orders.  The BCMA ORDER LAST ACTION was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,48,0)="available on the old order, but not on the newly created order.  This "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",82,1,49,0)="patch will correct this problem.  NOIS: MWV-0902-21008."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,0)="82 SEQ #83^3021122^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,0)="^^31^31^3021122"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,1,0)="1.  A site reported a problem with the Order Entry [PSJ NE] option. A new"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,2,0)="order's default administration time was taken, then edited before"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,3,0)="saving the order. After the order was saved, the administration time"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,4,0)="reverted to its original value. This patch corrects the problem by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,5,0)="correctly preserving the administration time each time it is edited."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,6,0)="NOIS TUA-0502-32722."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,8,0)="2.  A request was made to modify the Pre-Exchange Report to put each "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,9,0)="patient on a separate page. This patch implements this modification. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,10,0)="E3R 17161."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,12,0)="3.  A site reported a problem with not being able to view a renewed "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,13,0)="Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN) IV order using the Non-Verified/Pending"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,14,0)="Orders [PSJU VBW] option. This patch will correct this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,15,0)="NOIS BIR-0602-31411."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,17,0)="4. Labels incorrectly defaulted as Bypass instead of Print when entering a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,18,0)="One-Time IVPB without an administration time.  It defaulted correctly if "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,19,0)="there was an administration time. This patch corrects the problem by "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,20,0)="using the correct default regardless of the existence of administration "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,21,0)="times.  NOIS NCH-0602-41567."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,23,0)="5. A site reported a problem with the control code definition. If a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,24,0)="control code definition was not complete, there was a problem when "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,25,0)="attempting to print IV labels in any option. This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,26,0)="problem. NOIS: ISB-0602-32106."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,28,0)="6. A site reported a problem that occurred sporadically when an active "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,29,0)="or non-verified Inpatient order was edited. Under certain circumstances,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,30,0)="an error occurred that prevented the user from continuing with the edit."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",83,1,31,0)="This patch corrects the problem. ANN-0202-41257."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,0)="88 SEQ #84^3021122^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,0)="^^14^14^3021122"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,1,0)="1. Reprinting of the IV hyperal labels do not have the first line of data"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,2,0)="after the barcode that prints the order number, last 4 social security "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,3,0)="number, ward and date. This patch will correct this issue.  NOIS: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,4,0)="OKL-0802-71191."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,6,0)="2. Inpatient Medications orders which were on hold at the time a patient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,7,0)="movement occurred which caused them to be auto-discontinued were not "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,8,0)="returned to on hold if the movement was deleted and the orders were "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,9,0)="auto-reinstated.  This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS: AAA-0802-N1994."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,11,0)="3. The Returns and Destroyed Entry (IV) [PSJI RETURNS] option did not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,12,0)="properly update an order's Cumulative Doses. This patch corrects the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,13,0)="problem by updating an IV order's Cumulative Doses when a dose is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",84,1,14,0)="Recycled, Destroyed, or Cancelled."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,0)="87 SEQ #86^3021209^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,0)="^^30^30^3021209"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,1,0)="When performing drug lookups, two issues were identified. First, the user "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,2,0)="was not aware of which item was being matched. For example, was the match "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,3,0)="for the GENERIC NAME of the drug or was it the SYNONYM. The second issue "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,4,0)="had to do with the search matching to the NATIONAL DRUG CLASS NAME first, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,5,0)="before checking for a GENERIC NAME. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,7,0)="This patch makes two changes to the drug lookup. First, the search will "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,8,0)="display the item being searched on. Second, if a match is found on an "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,9,0)="item, but the user doesn't select one of the matches displayed, the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,10,0)="search will continue through all other items. A sample screen display "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,11,0)="follows."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,13,0)="Select DRUG: hep"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,14,0)="      Lookup: VA DRUG CLASS  CLASSIFICATION"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,15,0)="HEPARIN ANTAGONISTS  BL200  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,16,0)="   HEPARIN ANTAGONISTS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,17,0)="    Lookup: DRUG  NATIONAL DRUG CLASS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,18,0)="  PROTAMINE SULFATE 5ML INJ         BL200           "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,19,0)="         ...OK? Yes// N  (No)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,21,0)="    Lookup: DRUG  GENERIC NAME"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,22,0)="     1   HEPARIN 1,000 UNIT/ML 10ML INJ           BL100           "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,23,0)="     2   HEPARIN 1,000 UNITS/ML 30ML            BL100           "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,24,0)="     3   HEPARIN 10,000 UNITS 4ML           BL100           "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,25,0)="     4   HEPARIN BEEF 1,000 UNITS/ML 30ML           BL100           "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,26,0)="     5   HEPARIN, LOCK  100 UNIT/ML 1ML           BL100           "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,27,0)="Press <RETURN> to see more, '^' to exit this list, OR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,28,0)="CHOOSE 1-5: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,29,0)="     6   HEPATITIS-B IMMUNE GLOBULIN           IM500"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",85,1,30,0)="CHOOSE 1-6:  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,0)="89 SEQ #87^3021209^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,0)="^^66^66^3021209"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,1,0)="1. It was possible to renew a unit dose order when the dispense drug was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,2,0)="not matched to an Orderable Item.  This caused the order to store a 0 in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,3,0)="the ORDERABLE ITEM field (#108) of the UNIT DOSE subfile (#55.06) of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,4,0)="the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) and null in the ORDERS FILE ENTRY field"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,5,0)="(#66) of the UNIT DOSE subfile (#55.06) of the PHARMACY PATIENT file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,6,0)="(#55).  This patch will correct this problem.  NOIS: NCH-0802-42568."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,8,0)="2. A clean-up routine will identify orders without an Orderable Item and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,9,0)="make corrections, if appropriate. The person installing this patch will "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,10,0)="receive a MailMan message with the subject: PSJ*5*89 INPATIENT MEDS "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,11,0)="ORDERABLE ITEMS ORDER CHECK COMPLETED to tell the user of unresolved "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,12,0)="orders or of the corrections action."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,14,0)="The user will receive a message with the content similar to one of the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,15,0)="examples below after installing the patch:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,17,0)="Ex1:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,18,0)="Subj: PSJ*5*89 INPATIENT MEDS ORDERABLE ITEMS ORDER CHECK COMPLETED  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,19,0)="[#84808]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,20,0)="04 Sep 02 10:31  10 lines"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,21,0)="From: MEDICATIONS,INPATIENT  In 'IN' basket.   Page 1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,22,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,23,0)="The check of existing Pharmacy orders for use with Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,24,0)="Medications 5.0 completed as of SEP 4,2002@10:31:55."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,26,0)="This process checked orders for patients in 0 hours"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,27,0)="and 1 minute."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,29,0)="The following order(s) are without the Orderable Item.  Please contact the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,30,0)="NATIONAL HELP DESK for assistance:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,32,0)="DFN: 739  ORDER #: 746U"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,35,0)="Ex2:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,36,0)="Subj: PSJ*5*89 INPATIENT MEDS ORDERABLE ITEMS ORDER CHECK COMPLETED  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,37,0)="[#84809]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,38,0)="04 Sep 02 14:06  7 lines"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,39,0)="From: MEDICATIONS,INPATIENT  In 'IN' basket.   Page 1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,40,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,41,0)="The check of existing Pharmacy orders for use with Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,42,0)="Medications 5.0 completed as of SEP 4,2002@14:06:54."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,44,0)="This process checked orders for patients in 0 hours"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,45,0)="and 0 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,47,0)="There are no Orderable Items missing from the orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,49,0)="Enter message action (in IN basket): Ignore// "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,52,0)="Ex3:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,53,0)="Subj: PSJ*5*89 INPATIENT MEDS ORDERABLE ITEMS ORDER CHECK COMPLETED  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,54,0)="[#84824]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,55,0)="05 Sep 02 11:06  7 lines"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,56,0)="From: MEDICATIONS,INPATIENT  In 'IN' basket.   Page 1  *New*"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,57,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,58,0)="The check of existing Pharmacy orders for use with Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,59,0)="Medications 5.0 completed as of SEP 5,2002@11:06:33."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,61,0)="This process checked orders for patients in 0 hours"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,62,0)="and 0 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,64,0)="Updated the orders with the appropriate Orderable Items."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",86,1,66,0)="Enter message action (in IN basket): Ignore// "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,0)="94 SEQ #85^3021209^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,0)="^^25^25^3021209"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,1,0)=" This patch requires the installation of Bar Code Medication"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,2,0)=" Administration (BCMA) V. 2.0."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,4,0)=" 1. A site reported that continuous IV orders such as admixtures and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,5,0)=" hyperals do not display on the Virtual Due List (VDL) in BCMA V. 2.0 when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,6,0)=" they are renewed. If the DEFAULT START DATE CALCULATION field (#.05)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,7,0)=" in the INPATIENT WARD PARAMETERS file (#59.6) is not set to '2  USE NOW"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,8,0)=" AS DEFAULT', the renewal order's default start date may be set far enough"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,9,0)=" into the future to allow the order to fall off the VDL. The original"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,10,0)=" order may also expire at any time before the new order's start date and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,11,0)=" time, giving the appearance on the VDL that no medications are being"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,12,0)=" actively administered, when actually there is a bag infusing and another"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,13,0)=" bag scheduled to start."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,14,0)=" This patch will correct the problem by changing the way the start date"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,15,0)=" and time are calculated for continuous IV renewals. If the order being"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,16,0)=" renewed is a continuous IV, and the order does not contain a schedule,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,17,0)=" the default start date and time for the order will be set to NOW."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,18,0)=" NOIS #UNY-0802-10109. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,20,0)=" 2. If the pharmacist made an edit during the finishing of an IV piggyback"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,21,0)=" order that result in a new order, the original order was not "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,22,0)=" discontinued. This was cause by a leftover variable. To recreate this "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,23,0)=" problem, enter a new backdoor order and answer the following question "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,24,0)=" ""Is this O.K.: NO//"" with a ""^"". Then select a pending IV order and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",87,1,25,0)=" finish it. This patch will correct the problem. NOIS #LIT-0902-72062."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",88,0)="98 SEQ #88^3030109^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",88,1,0)="^^6^6^3030109"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",88,1,1,0)="When a group of orders were Auto Discontinued due to a Treating Specialty "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",88,1,2,0)="transfer, instead of assigning the Auto DC Date/Time as the orders' Stop "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",88,1,3,0)="Date/Time, each order may have different Stop Date/Times. This is the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",88,1,4,0)="cause for only a sub-set of orders to be re-instated.  A Computerized "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",88,1,5,0)="Patient Record System (CPRS) patch, OR*3*168, along with this patch will "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",88,1,6,0)="correct this problem. NOIS: LAH-1102-61807."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,0)="92 SEQ #89^3030115^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,0)="^^30^30^3030115"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,1,0)="1. A site reported a problem with the option 14 Day MAR [PSJU 14D MAR]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,2,0)="where nursing staff print blank mar's for prn's, but they are now having"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,3,0)="to do it patient by patient instead of by ward.  It works fine by patient,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,4,0)="but will print nothing for prn's (blank) by ward.  This patch corrects"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,5,0)="this problem.  NOIS# DUB-0902-31426."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,7,0)="2. Inpatient Medications provides an application programmer interface "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,8,0)="(API) to Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) that determines "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,9,0)="whether a schedule is required for an order placed using the INPATIENT "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,10,0)="MEDS dialog.  A site reported a problem with an order received from CPRS "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,11,0)="where a schedule should have required and wasn't.  This patch corrects "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,12,0)="this problem.  NOIS# BIR-0902-31838."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,14,0)="3. A site reported a problem with an IV order being created without all "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,15,0)="the appropriate information.  The problem was the result of a nurse "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,16,0)="verifying a non-verified unit dose order through CPRS.  The unit dose "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,17,0)="order would become active, the routine, which allowed this, was missing a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,18,0)="quit and the code to create an IV order would be executed without "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,19,0)="appropriate information, resulting in the bad IV order.  This patch "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,20,0)="corrects this problem.  NOIS# MOU-0902-30038."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,22,0)="4. A site reported a problem with the Activity Log from a non-verified "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,23,0)="unit dose order was not copied over to the active unit dose order when "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,24,0)="nurse verification took place through the CPRS verification option.  This "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,25,0)="patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# NOL-0902-70884."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,27,0)="5. A site reported a problem with the display of pending hyperal orders.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,28,0)="The orders were only displaying a single line on the CPRS orders tab "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,29,0)="instead of all the additives and solution contained in the order.  This "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",89,1,30,0)="patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# BHS-1002-10031."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,0)="85 SEQ #90^3030123^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,0)="^^65^65^3030123"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,1,0)="1. The allergy/adverse reaction is currently displayed as <A> on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,2,0)="patient profile and order view.  This patch will display the Crises,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,3,0)="Warnings, Allergy and Directive as <CWAD>.  A new hidden action CWAD is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,4,0)="added to display any patient's Crises, Warnings, Alerts, or advanced"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,5,0)="Directives on file."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,7,0)="2. It was requested in the E3Rs #11177 and #12382 that the flagging"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,8,0)="capability that is available in Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,9,0)="be available through the Inpatient Medications options.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,10,0)="accomplishes the addition of this functionality.  In order to use this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,11,0)="functionality, patch OR*3*141 must be installed as well."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,13,0)="3. The order view was not displaying on the Patient Profiles for Unit Dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,14,0)="orders.  Steps for testing: From the Unit Dose Order Entry [PSJU NE]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,15,0)="option, select a patient and then select an order from that patient's"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,16,0)="profile. After the order view appears, exit to the Main Menu. Next, choose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,17,0)="the PAtient Profile (Unit Dose) [PSJU PR] option and include the expanded"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,18,0)="view on the report.  The expanded view of the order should display on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,19,0)="profile."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,21,0)="4. Beginning with Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 patch PSJ*5*58, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,22,0)="barcodes are printed on the IV labels.  Barcode ID - Return and Destroy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,23,0)="(IV) [PSJI RETURN BY BARCODE ID] option was added to help pharmacy with"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,24,0)="the return and destroy of specific IV labels.  This new functionality was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,25,0)="requested by E3R #17117."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,27,0)="5. The BCMA ORDER LAST ACTION information was not available on patient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,28,0)="profiles of Unit Dose orders.  This patch will display it on these "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,29,0)="options: Inpatient Profile [PSJ PR], PAtient Profile (Unit Dose) [PSJU "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,30,0)="PR] and Patient Profile (Extended) [PSJ EXTP]."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,32,0)="6. It was requested in E3Rs # 12841 and # 10796 that Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,33,0)="Medications orders display the signature status of the order next to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,34,0)="the provider's name.  This patch in conjunction with OR*3*141 accomplishes"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,35,0)="this functionality.  If the order has been electronically signed via the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,36,0)="CPRS V. 1.0 package, [es] will appear after the provider's name.  If the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,37,0)="order has not been electronically signed or if OR*3*141 has not been"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,38,0)="installed the user will see the lowercase abbreviation for the Nature of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,39,0)="Order enclosed in the brackets after the provider's name (i.e. Written -"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,40,0)="[w], Telephoned - [p], Verbal - [v], Policy - [i], Electronically Entered"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,41,0)="- [e], or Service Correction [s])."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,43,0)="7. CPRS GUI version displays ""No Allergy Assessment"" when no allergy is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,44,0)="found on file.  It was requested in E3R #13013 that Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,45,0)="V. 5.0 use the same wording when patient allergies are displayed. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,46,0)="patch accomplishes this requested functionality."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,48,0)="8. A problem was discovered with the way certain Day of the Week schedules"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,49,0)="were handled during order entry. System derived administration times may"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,50,0)="have defaulted into orders in an improper format if the order was created"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,51,0)="using a Day of the Week administration schedule with no administration"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,52,0)="times defined. The incorrect administration time stored with the order may"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,53,0)="have been in the form of a single digit number or a three digit number."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,54,0)="This patch corrects this problem. NOIS ISB-0902-30741."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,56,0)="9. A site reported a problem with IV Fluid orders entered via CPRS where "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,57,0)="additives that were not marked for IV Fluid Order Entry in the IV "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,58,0)="ADDITIVES file (#52.6) were not being displayed in the pending order.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,59,0)="This patch corrects this problem. NOIS MAR-0902-21076."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,61,0)="10. When a pharmacist finished and verified an IV Fluid order as an IV "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,62,0)="Piggyback order, it did not show up in CPRS's Active View.  This occurred "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,63,0)="only when the  ""ALLOW AUTO-VERIFY FOR USER:"" prompt in the Inpatient User"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,64,0)="Parameters Edit [PSJ SEUP] option is set to ""No"".  This patch will correct"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",90,1,65,0)="this problem. NOIS LIT-1002-70444."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",91,0)="99 SEQ #91^3030301^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",91,1,0)="^^9^9^3030301"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",91,1,1,0)="There was a problem reported with the post install routine from "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",91,1,2,0)="PSO*7.0*115. This patch processes through the XTMP global created by that "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",91,1,3,0)="post install routine and corrects the status field for the IV orders that "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",91,1,4,0)="were effected."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",91,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",91,1,6,0)="If the cleanup routine encounters orders that have problems, the person "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",91,1,7,0)="who installed the patch will receive a message indicating this and where "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",91,1,8,0)="the list of problem orders is kept. These should be reviewed to be sure "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",91,1,9,0)="there are no problems with the patient's medication profile."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,0)="101 SEQ #92^3030329^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,0)="^^25^25^3030329"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,1,0)="1. IV orders were originally entered through Computerized Patient Record "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,2,0)="System (CPRS) and finished in Pharmacy, the completed orders were then "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,3,0)="edited through backdoor pharmacy options, the changes made were not "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,4,0)="reflected in CPRS. NOIS: HUN-1202-21612."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,6,0)="Steps to recreate:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,8,0)="    1. Provider creates an IV order in CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,9,0)="    2. Pharmacist (auto-verify off) finishes the order, the order is a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,10,0)="       non-verified order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,11,0)="    3. Pharmacist changes the strength in the additive but doesn't verify "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,12,0)="       it. This leaves it in a Non-Verified status."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,13,0)="    4. The new strength does not appear on CPRS side."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,15,0)="2. When the OTHER PRINT INFO field (#21) was entered or modified for a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,16,0)="Non-Verified IV order, this data was not being sent to CPRS. This patch "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,17,0)="will correct it."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,19,0)="3. An Inpatient Meds order is finished as an admixture with auto-verify "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,20,0)="turned off, this creates a non-verified order. When the non-verified "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,21,0)="order displays, a starred field is edited, and the order is accepted; "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,22,0)="this causes a new order to be created, but the original non-verified "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,23,0)="order is not discontinued. The profile displays two non-verified orders, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,24,0)="because a variable was not being updated correctly. This patch corrects "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",92,1,25,0)="this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,0)="97 SEQ #93^3030329^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,0)="^^19^19^3030329"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,1,0)=" 1. A site reported a problem with an IV renewal order. The order had been"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,2,0)=" renewed from the Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 2.0, and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,3,0)=" after the pending renewal order was verified, an error occurred. The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,4,0)=" error was due to an incorrect pointer to the pending order number that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,5,0)=" remained after the verification was complete. This patch corrects the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,6,0)=" problem by initialzing and reloading the new verified order after the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,7,0)=" order has been verified. NOIS BRX-1102-12101."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,9,0)=" 2. A site reported a problem with extra labels printing with their "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,10,0)=" scheduled IV labels. The extra labels contained the message 'NO PIGGYBACK"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,11,0)=" DATA'. This patch corrects the problem by printing this label only once "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,12,0)=" per label run, rather than for each patient. NOIS PAL-0902-61209."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,14,0)=" 3. A problem with the RETurns and Destroyed Entry (IV) [PSJI RETURNS]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,15,0)=" option was discovered by a member of development. The manual entry of a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,16,0)=" BCMA ID is allowed, but the option does not recognize lower case alpha"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,17,0)=" characters within the BCMA ID. This patch changes this functionality to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,18,0)=" allow the input of upper or lower case alpha characters when a BCMA ID is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",93,1,19,0)=" entered in this option."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,0)="91 SEQ #94^3030430^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,0)="^^80^80^3030430"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,1,0)="1. The routine ^PSJORREN was included with patch PSJ*5*89 to correct the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,2,0)="problem of renewing a Unit Dose order with a 0 (zero) value stored in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,3,0)="ORDERABLE ITEM field (#108) of the UNIT DOSE multiple (#62) of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,4,0)="PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55). This routine is included in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,5,0)="(PSJ*5*91) to make sure that when Bar Code Medication Administration"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,6,0)="(BCMA) V. 2.0 is installed after patch PSJ*5*89 sites will have the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,7,0)="correct version. The second line will be updated with this patch number"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,8,0)="but the routine checksum will be the same as listed in PSJ*5*89."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,10,0)="2. The routine ^PSJORRE1 is included in this patch to address SQA issue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,11,0)="with the incorrect DBIA number documented in the reference. The checksum"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,12,0)="will not change."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,14,0)="3. Routine ^PSJDCHK is included to comment out references to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,15,0)="PATIENT file (#55) that are no longer used."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,17,0)="4. The SCHEDULE INTERVAL field (#.17) from the IV sub-file (#55.01) of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,18,0)="PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) is not stored consistently for Day of Week"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,19,0)="schedules if the user did not have Auto Verify turned on. This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,20,0)="schedules if the user did not have Auto Verify turned on. This patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,21,0)="store a ""D"" in this field for the Day of Week schedule. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,22,0)="includes a modification to an Application Programmer Interface (API) to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,23,0)="BCMA V. 2.0 to send the correct schedule type for IV orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,24,0)="NOIS# NYH-1002-10449."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,26,0)="5. Unit Dose orders created in Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,27,0)="V. 2.0 using the Med Order Button do not appear on the Due List. These"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,28,0)="orders are being created with a frequency of zero, which is not a valid"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,29,0)="frequency. This patch will correct the problem so that these orders will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,30,0)="be created with the proper frequency for One Time orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,31,0)="NOIS# MIN-1202-40902."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,33,0)="6. A clean-up routine will identify orders with a frequency of zero and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,34,0)="make corrections, if appropriate. The person installing this patch will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,35,0)="receive a MailMan message with the subject PSJ*5*91 INPATIENT MEDS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,36,0)="FREQUENCY ORDER CLEANUP COMPLETED. This message will inform the user how"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,37,0)="many orders with a zero frequency were found and corrected. An order's"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,38,0)="frequency will only be corrected if it meets all the following criteria:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,39,0)="the Frequency is zero, the Stop Date is equal to the Start Date, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,40,0)="Schedule is STAT or NOW, and the Priority is Done."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,42,0)="7. A site reported receiving an error while editing a Unit Dose order in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,43,0)="the Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW] option. Edits were made to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,44,0)="order that caused a new order to be created, and this cycle was repeated"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,45,0)="several times until an error occurred which interrupted the process. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,46,0)="patch will prevent this error from occurring."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,47,0)="NOIS# BRX-1202-11956."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,49,0)="8. A site reported receiving an undefined error when attempting to place"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,50,0)="an order using the Med Order Button in Bar Code Medication Administration"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,51,0)="(BCMA) V. 2.0. This patch will correct the problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,53,0)="9. A site reported a problem with the Drug (Cost and/or Amount) [PSJU"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,54,0)="DCT] option.  When selecting by Orderable Item, the inactive date was not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,55,0)="being displayed beside the name.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,56,0)="NOIS# CLL-0103-40519."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,58,0)="10. Sites reported a problem where active IV orders were being created"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,59,0)="with an IV Room of zero (0).  This created a problem of no IV labels"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,60,0)="being printed for these orders.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,61,0)="NOIS# HAM-0103-22051 & CPH-0103-41307."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,63,0)="11. A site reported an error that occurred when two users simultaneously"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,64,0)="attempted to print to a non-spooled printer. The output should have been"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,65,0)="directed to the terminal screen, but instead was queued to an output"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,66,0)="device of 'HOME'. This queued job will cause an inappropriate device"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,67,0)="error, or it will create duplicate label log entries until the job is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,68,0)="killed. This patch will correct the problem by converting the name of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,69,0)="output device from the word HOME to the user's home device."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,70,0)="NOIS# DAY-0103-42177 & CLE-0203-40500."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,72,0)="12. A site reported a problem with an order having the nurse verification"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,73,0)="indicated in Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0, but no in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,74,0)="Inpatient Medications V. 5.0. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,75,0)="NOIS# HUN-0902-22266."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,77,0)="13. A site reported a problem with the status of an IV bag in Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,78,0)="Medications V. 5.0 not matching the status of the bag in BCMA. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,79,0)="corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",94,1,80,0)="NOIS# CLL-0203-40056."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,0)="93 SEQ #95^3030430^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,0)="^^31^31^3030430"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,1,0)=" This patch is compatible with Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,2,0)=" V. 1.0 as well as BCMA V. 2.0, and may be installed in environments"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,3,0)=" containing either version."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,5,0)=" 1. A site reported a problem with the way an IV Quick Order's schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,6,0)=" was handled when ordered as a Chemotherapy IV with a Chemotherapy Type"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,7,0)=" of Piggyback. The schedule defined in the IV Quick Code did not default"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,8,0)=" into the order when the IV Quick Code was used with an IV Type of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,9,0)=" Chemotherapy. This patch corrects the problem by properly defaulting the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,10,0)=" schedule with Chemotherapy IV orders. NOIS MIN-1002-40243."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,12,0)=" 2. When a patient movement is deleted and orders are reinstated, a mail"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,13,0)=" message is sent to a user group to inform the users of reinstated orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,14,0)=" and those that are not reinstated.  This patch changed the mail message"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,15,0)=" from regular to Priority mail to ensure the users see it."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,16,0)=" NOIS WPB-0902-30314."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,18,0)=" 3. A site reported a problem with scheduled IV labels for orders with"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,19,0)=" Day of the Week schedules such as MO-WE-FR@0900. Labels were printing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,20,0)=" for the scheduled administrations every day, instead of printing labels"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,21,0)=" exclusively for the days defined in the schedule. This patch corrects"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,22,0)=" the problem by printing labels only for scheduled doses."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,23,0)=" NOIS HIN-0902-41529."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,25,0)="4. A site reported receiving the message ""Nonstandard schedule"" when they "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,26,0)=" attempted to enter an order for a continuous IV Admixture using an IV "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,27,0)=" Quick Code that did not contain a schedule. This message should not "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,28,0)=" display when the schedule field does not contain a value, regardless of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,29,0)=" whether or not an IV Quick Code is used. This patch corrects the problem "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,30,0)=" by preventing this message from displaying when the schedule field is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",95,1,31,0)=" empty or null. NOIS BIG-1102-70679."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,0)="95 SEQ #96^3030430^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,0)="^^53^53^3030430"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,1,0)=" 1. A site reported receiving an error message, 'string too long', while"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,2,0)=" attempting to finish a pending Unit Dose order. The error occurred after"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,3,0)=" a number of edits to the Special Instructions were made and accepted."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,4,0)=" After each edit, 'Yes' was entered in response to the 'Flag the Special"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,5,0)=" Instructions (Yes/No):' prompt. As the Special Instructions were"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,6,0)=" flagged, a new flag was created and added to all the previous flags. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,7,0)=" patch corrects the problem by taking previously flagged Special"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,8,0)=" Instructions into account and ensuring only one flag exists for each"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,9,0)=" order. NOIS: MIW-1002-40270."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,11,0)=" 2. A request was made to modify the Pre-Exchange Report to put each"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,12,0)=" patient on a separate page. This patch implements this modification by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,13,0)=" printing the report by patient immediately after order entry processing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,14,0)=" is completed for each patient. Included in this change is a new field,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,15,0)=" the PRE-EXCHANGE REPORT DEVICE field (#4) in the INPATIENT WARD"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,16,0)=" PARAMETERS file (#59.6). This parameter is a pointer to the DEVICE file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,17,0)=" (#3.5), and will contain the default print device for the report. A"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,18,0)=" post-install routine has also been included to populate the new parameter"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,19,0)=" for each ward with a value that will print the report to the screen. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,20,0)=" value may then be changed to a print device, or deleted to disable the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,21,0)=" report for that ward. E3R 17161."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,23,0)=" 3. A site reported a problem with the Start Date/Time of a Unit Dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,24,0)=" renewal order. The problem occurred under the following conditions:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,25,0)=" An order's medication was administered at 0949, prior to its next "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,26,0)=" scheduled administration of 1000. That same order's Stop Date/Time"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,27,0)=" was 1200, which was after the 1000 administration time that was given"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,28,0)=" early, but before the next scheduled administration time of 1800."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,29,0)=" The order is then renewed at 0956. The calculated Start Date/Time is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,30,0)=" after the order expires, so the ward parameters are used, making the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,31,0)=" Start Date/Time equal to NOW. The renewal order's Start Date/Time"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,32,0)=" became 0956, which caused the order to hit the 1000 administration time"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,33,0)=" again, seven minutes after the last administration. This patch corrects"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,34,0)=" this particular problem by making the default Start Date/Time of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,35,0)=" renewal order equal to the Stop Date/Time of the original renewed order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,36,0)=" if the calculated start time is after the Stop Date/Time of the original"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,37,0)=" order. NOIS: MAR-1002-20455."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,39,0)=" 4. A site reported a pharmacist could not finish a pending order as Unit "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,40,0)=" Dose when the prompt 'COMPLETE THIS ORDER AS IV OR UNIT DOSE?' was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,41,0)=" answered with 'U'. The pharmacist held the Pharmacy Technician Key, and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,42,0)=" as a result the software considered the Pharmacist a Pharmacy Technician."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,43,0)=" This patch corrects this problem by allowing pharmacists possessing the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,44,0)=" Pharmacy Technician Key to complete these orders as Unit Dose orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,45,0)=" NOIS: CHA-1101-31456."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,47,0)=" 5. The activity log was not updated to record the nurse verification "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,48,0)=" action taken from CPRS on an active IV order. This patch will correct "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,49,0)=" this issue. NOIS: NCH-1202-40194."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,51,0)=" 6. The patient profile displayed ""No Allergy Assessment"" when the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,52,0)=" patient did not have any allergies but have adverse reaction identified. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",96,1,53,0)=" This patch will correct this problem. NOIS: BRX-0103-12347."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",97,0)="100 SEQ #97^3030520^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",97,1,0)="^^4^4^3030520"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",97,1,1,0)="IV orders entered through Inpatient Medications options by a user "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",97,1,2,0)="without auto-verify turned on, with a nature of order of verbal were not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",97,1,3,0)="showing in Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) as requiring a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",97,1,4,0)="signature.  This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# LAH-1202-60493."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",98,0)="102 SEQ #98^3030603^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",98,1,0)="^^2^2^3030603"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",98,1,1,0)="This patch contains the routines to support the Bar Code Med Admin (BCMA) "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",98,1,2,0)="National Contingency Plan."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,0)="105 SEQ #99^3030603^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,0)="^^16^16^3030603"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,1,0)="1. A site reported a problem where an order was showing on the pick list "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,2,0)="with OI under the Units Needed heading.  Upon investigation of the order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,3,0)="it was found that the order was logged in between midnight and one minute "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,4,0)="after midnight, this caused a problem because the Inpatient Medications "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,5,0)="software was only using the first 12 characters of the date time, so the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,6,0)="login date had no time.  The ward parameter for the ward was set to now "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,7,0)="which set the start date/time for the order to a date and no time.  This "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,8,0)="caused the problem with the pick list, the software was unable to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,9,0)="calculate the units needed and used OI to indicate there was a problem "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,10,0)="with the order.  This patch corrects this problem.  NOIS# SPO-0103-51804."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,12,0)="2. A site reported an error when flagging a pending IV order from the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,13,0)="patient's profile. If the patient had not been admitted to a ward, the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,14,0)="software incorrectly processed the order as an outpatient order. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,15,0)="patch corrects the problem by correctly processing the flagging"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",99,1,16,0)="information. NOIS# HUN-0303-21424."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",100,0)="106 SEQ #100^3030628^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,0)="108 SEQ #101^3030628^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,1,0)="^^12^12^3030628"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,1,1,0)="A problem was reported with the Automatic Pharmacy Statistics [PSU "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,1,2,0)="PBM AUTO] option receiving an undefined variable error.  The problem was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,1,3,0)="that the LAST WARD field (#68) of the UNIT DOSE multiple (#62) of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,1,4,0)="PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) had a text value instead of a numeric value."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,1,5,0)="The patients where the problem occurred all had been admitted to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,1,6,0)="observation and then discharged and re-admitted to the hospital.  New"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,1,7,0)="functionality was added to the Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,1,8,0)="to allow the orders that had been discontinued by the patient's discharge"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,1,9,0)="from observation to be automatically re-instated upon the patient's later"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,1,10,0)="re-admission to the hospital via an application programmer interface (API)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,1,11,0)="to Inpatient Medications.  This patch corrects this API to only allow a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",101,1,12,0)="numeric value for the LAST WARD field to be passed in this API."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,0)="80 SEQ #102^3030802^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,0)="^^85^85^3030802"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,1,0)="1. Several sites reported that the default start/stop dates for complex"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,2,0)="orders were causing confusion. The confusion is caused by the fact that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,3,0)="the current stop/start dates don't reflect the duration for the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,4,0)="entered in Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0. The dates"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,5,0)="that reflect the duration are currently displayed on the screen as the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,6,0)="requested dates, but they are not the defaults. This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,7,0)="problem by using the requested start/stop dates as the defaults for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,8,0)="complex orders, and adding the duration to the patient profile display."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,9,0)="The system calculated dates are still displayed on the screen for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,10,0)="informational purposes. NOIS: ATG-0202-32014, SPO-0302-51163, and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,11,0)="BHS-0103-10826."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,13,0)="2. The EXPIRE ALL ORDERS ON SAME DAY field (#.105) in the IV ROOM file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,14,0)="(#59.5) is currently not evaluated in determining stop dates for IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,15,0)="orders. This patch corrects this problem by evaluating the field and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,16,0)="calculating the appropriate stop date.  NOIS: ISB-0502-32152."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,18,0)="3. For schedules with long intervals, such as 48 hours, there was a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,19,0)="problem with the calculation of the first dose when orders were entered in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,20,0)="CPRS. This caused an inconsistency between the expected first dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,21,0)="displayed to the provider and the actual time the order became available"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,22,0)="for administration. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,23,0)="NOIS: ATG-0402-31444, LOM-1201-62023, REN-1101-61894."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,25,0)="4. A site reported a problem when entering orders with an admin time of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,26,0)="23 and a schedule interval greater than 23 hours. The start time/expected"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,27,0)="first dose was being changed to 24. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,28,0)="NOIS: BAY-0102-32400"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,30,0)="5. A site reported a problem with the calculation of the stop date on a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,31,0)="renewal order. If the start date of the order was greater than the current"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,32,0)="date, the SAME STOP DATE ON ALL ORDERS field (#.04) in the INPATIENT WARD"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,33,0)="PARAMETERS file (#59.6) was ignored and the patient's default stop date"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,34,0)="was calculated too far in the future. This patch corrects this problem by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,35,0)="changing the default stop date calculation to be based on the current"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,36,0)="date, rather than the start date of the order. The patient's default stop"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,37,0)="date will now be updated when an order is finished/accepted rather than"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,38,0)="waiting until after it is verified. NOIS: CTX-0502-70557"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,40,0)="6. E3R 12716 requested a change to the way an IV order's Stop Date is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,41,0)="calculated. The DAY (nD) or DOSE (nL) LIMIT field (#.05) in the PHARMACY"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,42,0)="ORDERABLE ITEM file (#50.7) was not previously evaluated during the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,43,0)="calculation of an IV order's Stop Date. This patch will include this field"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,44,0)="when calculating an IV order's Stop Date. The Stop Date will continue to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,45,0)="be calculated by finding the shortest duration between the appropriate"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,46,0)="parameters contained in PHARMACY ORDERABLE ITEM file (#50.7), IV ADDITIVES"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,47,0)="file (#52.6), and the IV ROOM file (#59.5). E3R: 12716"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,49,0)="7. A site reported an intermittent problem in which Provider Comments"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,50,0)="would incorrectly copy from one order to another during the finishing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,51,0)="process. This patch corrects the problem by ensuring that the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,52,0)="from which Provider Comments are retrieved is the same as the order being"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,53,0)="finished. IND-0502-41166"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,55,0)="8. A site reported a problem that occurred during the finishing process."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,56,0)="Finishing an order with an IV Quick Code that did not contain a schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,57,0)="could cause an error, which would abruptly halt the user's process. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,58,0)="patch corrects this problem.  MAD-0402-42408"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,60,0)="9. In the past, a user was allowed to renew a Unit Dose order from the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,61,0)="Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 without an active Orderable Item tied to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,62,0)="order. This patch will inform the user that the order could not be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,63,0)="renewed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,65,0)="10. A site reported a problem with a report that displays orders verified"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,66,0)="during a given time period. Some orders did not appear on the report due"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,67,0)="to trailing zeroes on the DATE VERIFIED BY PHARMACIST sub-field (#141) in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,68,0)="the IV multiple (#100) of the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55). This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,69,0)="corrects the problem by removing the trailing zeroes from the internal"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,70,0)="date. NOIS: CLL-0103-40447"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,72,0)="11. A site reported they were unable to discontinue IV orders from the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,73,0)="Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0. The problem was caused"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,74,0)="by an interaction with test patch DI*22*121. This patch will prevent the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,75,0)="problem from occurring. NOIS: TAM-0303-30859"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,77,0)="12. During internal testing a problem was discovered with the way Nurse"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,78,0)="Verification was recorded in the Activity Log when the verification was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,79,0)="done from the Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,80,0)="patch corrects the problem by accurately recording the event in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,81,0)="Activity Log."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,83,0)="13. A site reported an undefined error in the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,84,0)="OE] option that was the result of an interaction with Class III McKesson"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",102,1,85,0)="software. This patch corrects the problem. NOIS: MIW-0503-40707."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,0)="104 SEQ #103^3030813^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,0)="^^66^66^3030813"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,1,0)=" 1. A site reported a problem with the manual reinstatement of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,2,0)=" auto-discontinued inpatient IV orders. A pharmacist was not able to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,3,0)=" manually reinstate an order if the patient had an active order with the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,4,0)=" same IV additive. This patch corrects the problem by allowing orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,5,0)=" with duplicate additives to be reinstated manually. The software will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,6,0)=" continue to prevent orders with duplicate IV additives from being"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,7,0)=" automatically reinstated. NOIS: TNV-0103-31207."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,9,0)=" 2. A site reported a problem with the SIte Parameters (IV) [PSJI SITE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,10,0)=" PARAMETERS] option. The default label device is not loaded from the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,11,0)=" IV Room that is selected for edit, it is loaded from the IV Room that the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,12,0)=" user enters when initially logging in. If the user does not change the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,13,0)=" label device, this incorrect default label device value will be stored"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,14,0)=" with the edited IV Room. This patch corrects the problem by ensuring the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,15,0)=" label device and report device are loaded from the IV Room that was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,16,0)=" selected for edit. NOIS: CLE-0203-40814."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,18,0)="3. When a patient movement is deleted and orders are reinstated, a mail"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,19,0)=" message is sent to a user group to inform the users of reinstated orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,20,0)=" and those that were not reinstated. This patch changes the type of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,21,0)=" message that is sent when order reinstatement is attempted in Bar Code"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,22,0)=" Medication Administration (BCMA) V. 2.0 from regular to priority."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,23,0)=" NOIS: WPB-0902-30314."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,25,0)=" 4. A site reported a problem with the Inpatient Profile [PSJ PR] option."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,26,0)=" The Special Instructions incorrectly displayed as an internal numeric"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,27,0)=" date. Example: Special Instructions: 3030219.204644. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,28,0)=" corrects the problem by properly displaying the Special Instructions."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,29,0)=" NOIS: BAY-0203-31638."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,31,0)=" 5. A site has identified a potential problem with the Barcode ID - Return"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,32,0)=" and Destroy (IV) [PSJI RETURN BY BARCODE ID] option. It appears that this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,33,0)=" option is adding to the dispensed total, rather than the appropriate"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,34,0)=" returned, recycled and destroyed totals. This patch corrects the problem"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,35,0)=" by correctly recording the action, enabling the action to be accurately"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,36,0)=" reported in the Drug Cost Report (132 COLUMNS) (IV)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,37,0)=" [PSJI DRUG COST REPORT] option. NOIS: CLL-0403-40228."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,39,0)=" 6. A site reported a problem with the Scheduled Labels (IV) [PSJI LBLS]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,40,0)=" option. The background job that prints the labels occasionally becomes"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,41,0)=" stuck in a loop when the print process encounters a patient with active"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,42,0)=" IV orders but no labels to print. The background job processes data and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,43,0)=" writes NO PIGGYBACK DATA or NO ADMIXTURE DATA to a spool file, but no"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,44,0)=" labels print. The print process eventually must be killed. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,45,0)=" corrects the problem by allowing the print process to generate the NO"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,46,0)=" PIGGYBACK DATA and NO ADMIXTURE DATA messages without entering an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,47,0)=" infinite loop. NOIS: MEM-0403-71631."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,49,0)=" 7. A site reported an error that occurred when an additive with an IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,50,0)=" Quick Code was added to an IV order that already contained multiple"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,51,0)=" additives. This patch corrects the problem by properly processing IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,52,0)=" Quick Codes when multiple additives are present. NOIS: BRX-0503-10289."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,54,0)=" 8. Several sites reported the screen would hang indefinitely when trying"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,55,0)=" to open a patient's record in BCMA V. 2.0. This patch corrects the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,56,0)=" problem. NOIS: PAL-1102-61818."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,58,0)=" 9. A site reported a problem with additives printing on IV Admixture"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,59,0)=" labels. Additives that were flagged to print on only one label per day"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,60,0)=" were printing on multiple labels each day. This patch corrects the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,61,0)=" problem. NOIS: NCH-0103-41471."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,63,0)=" 10. A site reported that the exclamation point, which is used to flag"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,64,0)=" Special Instructions, is not removed from BCMA V. 2.0 when a patient's"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,65,0)=" Special Instructions are changed from flagged to not flagged."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",103,1,66,0)=" NOIS: CLL-0503-41858."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",104,0)="115 SEQ #104^3030912^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",104,1,0)="^^11^11^3030912"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",104,1,1,0)=" 1. Several sites have reported Unit Dose labels do not always print. The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",104,1,2,0)=" problem occurs during verification of Unit Dose orders from the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",104,1,3,0)=" Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW] option when pre-exchange units are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",104,1,4,0)=" needed. In some instances, an error was logged indicating some ward"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",104,1,5,0)=" parameters were not defined. This patch corrects the problem by ensuring"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",104,1,6,0)=" the labels print, and the ward parameters are defined, regardless of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",104,1,7,0)=" pre-exchange needs. CLL-0703-42086 and MIW-0503-40707."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",104,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",104,1,9,0)=" 2. A site reported that the Pre-Exchange Report was displaying fractional"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",104,1,10,0)=" units. This patch will round up the units needed on the Pre-Exchange"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",104,1,11,0)=" Report to match the format of the pick list. BRX-0503-11875."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",105,0)="96 SEQ #105^3030912^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",105,1,0)="^^4^4^3030912"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",105,1,1,0)="Reprinted IV TPN labels did not display the correct additives and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",105,1,2,0)="solutions on the labels. Sometime the electrolytes tied to the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",105,1,3,0)="additives/solutions were not appeared on the reprinted labels at all. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",105,1,4,0)="This patch will correct this problem. NOIS: #ROS-1102-50810."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,0)="109 SEQ #106^3030924^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,0)="^^26^26^3030924"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,1,0)="1. A site using the CPRS Med Order Button in Bar Code Medication "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,2,0)=" Administration (BCMA) V. 2.0 reported a problem where the dosage ordered"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,3,0)=" was not displaying correctly on the order in Inpatient Medications V 5.0."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,4,0)="The problem occurred for orders with local possible dosages, where the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,5,0)=" strength and unit were defined. This patch corrects this problem by "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,6,0)=" sending the local possible dosage information, if available."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,8,0)=" 2. A site reported receiving an error while attempting to discontinue "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,9,0)=" a renewal IV order from the Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,10,0)=" option. The error occurred when an update of the order was sent to the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,11,0)=" Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 2.0. This patch corrects the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,12,0)=" problem by adding data validation prior to attempting the update. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,13,0)=" NOIS: BRX-0403-11828"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,15,0)=" 3. A site reported an error that occurred while using the Inpatient Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,16,0)=" Entry [PSJ OE] option. The error occurred when the patient profile"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,17,0)=" attempted to access an IV order with a status of renewed and a stop date"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,18,0)=" that had passed since the last time the order was viewed. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,19,0)=" corrects the problem by changing the variable names to remove conflicts."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,20,0)=" NOIS: SFC-0403-61950."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,22,0)=" 4. A site reported an error that occurred while attempting to print a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,23,0)=" pick list. The error occurred during a cleanup of old pick list data,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,24,0)=" and the error message indicated the process had been locking the data as"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,25,0)=" it cleaned it, but it did not unlock the data. This patch corrects the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",106,1,26,0)=" problem by ensuring the data lock is removed when it is no longer needed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,0)="116 SEQ #107^3031121^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,1,0)="^^12^12^3031121"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,1,1,0)=" Sites have reported problems with the way Inpatient Medications V. 5.0  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,1,2,0)=" interprets non-standard schedules. These schedules, which are not defined"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,1,3,0)=" in the ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1), may contain a pattern of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,1,4,0)=" characters that are not always translating into the expected"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,1,5,0)=" administration frequency. For example, Q9AM is translated to a schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,1,6,0)=" of every nine days, and a schedule of EVERY NIGHT is translated to a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,1,7,0)=" schedule of every hour. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,1,9,0)=" This patch will help to clarify the actual calculated schedule frequency"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,1,10,0)=" that is associated with a non-standard schedule by displaying a warning "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,1,11,0)=" message along with the calculated frequency at the time an order is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",107,1,12,0)=" finished, and when the schedule edited. NOIS PTH-0703-20552."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",108,0)="119 SEQ #108^3031231^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",108,1,0)="^^5^5^3031231"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",108,1,1,0)="A site reported a problem that occurs when the pick list is sent to the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",108,1,2,0)="ATC. It does not round up and the ATC will not accept fractional units so"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",108,1,3,0)="the drug does not go to the ATC.  This patch corrects this situation by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",108,1,4,0)="providing an optional system parameter to allow rounding of fractional"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",108,1,5,0)="doses before sending to the ATC.  NOIS ALT-0403-20970"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,0)="90 SEQ #109^3040330^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,0)="^^29^29^3040330"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,1,0)="This project consists of 12 patches that work together to create a new"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,2,0)="Clinical Reminders index global. The purpose of this index is to provide"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,3,0)="rapid access to clinical data. All of the standard Clinical Reminders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,4,0)="finding types are included in the index."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,6,0)="The 12 patches that comprise this project are:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,8,0)=" PXRM*1.5*12"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,9,0)=" DG*5.3*478"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,10,0)=" GMPL*2*27"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,11,0)=" GMRV*4*15"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,12,0)=" LR*5.2*295"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,13,0)=" OR*3*157"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,14,0)=" PSS*1*62"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,15,0)=" PSJ*5*90"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,16,0)=" PSO*7*118"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,17,0)=" PX*1*119"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,18,0)=" RA*5*33"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,19,0)=" YS*5.01*77"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,21,0)=" The purpose of this patch (PSJ*5*90) is to lay the groundwork for these "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,22,0)=" changes by modifying the Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 routines to set the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,23,0)=" cross-references to create the new indices if PXRM*1.5*12 has been"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,24,0)=" installed. If patch PXRM*1.5*12 has not been installed the index will not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,25,0)=" be built."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,27,0)=" This patch can be installed independently of the other patches. The "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,28,0)=" documentation describing the new functionality will be available when all"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",109,1,29,0)=" associated patches are released."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",110,0)="117 SEQ #110^3040330^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",110,1,0)="^^4^4^3040330"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",110,1,1,0)="A site reported a problem with the DOSAGE field (#120) in the UNIT DOSE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",110,1,2,0)="multiple (#62) of the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) not being deleted when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",110,1,3,0)="an orderable item is changed. This patch corrects this problem by "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",110,1,4,0)="removing the data when the orderable item is changed.  NOIS UNY-0603-10652"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",111,0)="118 SEQ #111^3040330^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",111,1,0)="^^4^4^3040330"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",111,1,1,0)="Site reported a problem with the display of flagged pending IV order with"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",111,1,2,0)="no additive in the profile view. This patch corrects this problem by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",111,1,3,0)="appropriately displaying the flag for pending IV orders with no additive."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",111,1,4,0)="(NOIS: MAR-0703-21163)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,0)="107 SEQ #112^3040521^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,0)="^^14^14^3040521"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,1,0)="1. Joint Commission for Accreditation of Healthcare Organizations (JCAHO)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,2,0)="requires that patients' use of Over-The-Counter (OTC) medications, Herbal"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,3,0)="supplements, medications prescribed by Veterans Health Administration "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,4,0)="(VHA) but purchased by the patient at an outside pharmacy, and medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,5,0)="prescribed by providers outside VHA be documented in patients' medical"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,6,0)="records. These four categories of medications will hereafter be referred"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,7,0)="to as Non-VA Meds. This patch makes the changes necessary to Inpatient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,8,0)="Medications V. 5.0 to support Non-VA Meds."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,10,0)="2. To accommodate Billing Awareness, it was necessary to modify the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,11,0)="communication between CPRS and Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0 to include "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,12,0)="new diagnosis codes. Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 routes all pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,13,0)="orders to the appropriate package. This patch makes the changes necessary "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",112,1,14,0)="to pass the new diagnosis codes to the appropriate package."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",113,0)="123 SEQ #113^3040702^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",113,1,0)="^^6^6^3040702"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",113,1,1,0)="   The inclusion of a non-standard variable (&) in the Medication Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",113,1,2,0)="   resulted in errors when the Bar Code Medication Administration "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",113,1,3,0)="   Contingency program decoded the Inpatient Medications HL7 messages."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",113,1,4,0)="   This patch modifies these messages utilized by the BCMA Contingency to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",113,1,5,0)="   send administration time in another message segment."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",113,1,6,0)="   NOIS NJH-1203-21889"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,0)="103 SEQ #114^3040924^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,0)="^^33^33^3040924"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,1,0)="1. Modifications are being made to Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 to no "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,2,0)="longer allow non-standard schedules to be used. This patch provides a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,3,0)="menu option to allow users to identify non-standard schedules"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,4,0)="that are currently in use. This option will search through Order Sets,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,5,0)="Quick Codes, the ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1), the PHARMACY "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,6,0)="ORDERABLE ITEM file (#50.7) and all orders for the timeframe specified by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,7,0)="the user. The person running the option will receive a series of email"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,8,0)="messages identifying the non-standard schedules. The email message"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,9,0)="subjects will be: ADMIN SCHEDULES, ADMIN SCHEDULES NOT IN 51.1,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,10,0)="NON-STANDARD SCHEDULES IN QUICK CODES, NON-STANDARD SCHEDULES IN ORDER"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,11,0)="SETS and NON-STANDARD SCHEDULE IN ORDERABLE ITEMS. The search routine can"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,12,0)="be run multiple times. This can be used to help show the progress being"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,13,0)="made in correcting issues. In addition, the report will show active orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,14,0)="in the search period. Please note: the default schedules in the PHARMACY "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,15,0)="ORDERABLE ITEM file (#50.7) are for both inpatient and outpatient orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,17,0)="2. Based on the upcoming requirement from the Joint Commission on "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,18,0)="Accreditation of Hospital Organizations, schedule names that are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,19,0)="considered dangerous will no longer be allowed. This patch provides a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,20,0)="menu option to allow users to identify schedules that are considered "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,21,0)="dangerous. This option will search through Order Sets, Quick Codes, the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,22,0)="ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1), the PHARMACY ORDERABLE ITEM file "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,23,0)="(#50.7) and all orders for the timeframe specified by the user. The person"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,24,0)="running the option will receive a series of email messages identifying the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,25,0)="dangerous schedules. The email message subjects will be: DANGEROUS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,26,0)="SCHEDULES IN 51.1, DANGEROUS SCHEDULES IN ORDERS, DANGEROUS SCHEDULES IN"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,27,0)="QUICK CODES, DANGEROUS SCHEDULES IN ORDER SETS and DANGEROUS SCHEDULES IN "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,28,0)="ORDERABLE ITEMS."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,30,0)="3. To facilitate the iterative process of running the search and report "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,31,0)="multiple times, two new options are being added to the system. They are "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,32,0)="the Non-Standard Schedule Search [PSJU NSS SEARCH] option and the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",114,1,33,0)="Non-Standard Schedule Report [PSJU NSS REPORT] option. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,0)="110^3041015^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,0)="^^53^53^3041015"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,1,0)=" Phase I of the Inpatient Medications Requirements for the Special Focus"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,2,0)=" Group IRA project consists of four patches. The patches are combined in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,3,0)=" host file PSJ_PSS_OR_PSU_110.KID in order to simplify installation at VHA"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,4,0)=" facilities. Installation of this host file should be coordinated among"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,5,0)=" the four packages affected since only one installation is necessary. The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,6,0)=" patches, in order of install, are:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,8,0)="      PSS*1*79   PHARMACY DATA MANAGEMENT V. 1.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,9,0)="      PSJ*5*110  INPATIENT MEDICATIONS V. 5.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,10,0)="      OR*3*213   ORDER ENTRY/RESULTS REPORTING V. 1.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,11,0)="      PSU*3*34   PHARMACY BENEFITS MANAGEMENT V. 3.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,13,0)=" Patches PSS*1*79, OR*3*213, and PSU*3*34 contain changes to support the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,14,0)=" following enhancements in PSJ*5*110:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,16,0)=" 1. The Extend Stop Date on Renewal enhancements will allow an order to be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,17,0)=" renewed without creating a new order. Editing of the start date will no"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,18,0)=" longer be allowed during the renewal process. In addition, limits have"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,19,0)=" been set on the length of time after an order expires that it may be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,20,0)=" renewed. This is outlined in the BCMA 2001 Special Focus Report,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,21,0)=" Requirement #11."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,22,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,23,0)=" 2. The Complex Order enhancements will change the way complex orders are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,24,0)=" handled by linking complex components (child orders) together. If the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,25,0)=" actions Finish, Verify, Discontinue, or Renew are taken on one child"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,26,0)=" order, the user will be alerted that the action must be taken on all of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,27,0)=" the complex component orders in the set. The user will then be prompted"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,28,0)=" to take the appropriate action on each child order in the complex order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,29,0)=" set. This is outlined in BCMA 2001 Special Focus Report, Requirement #8."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,31,0)=" 3. The STAT and NOW Order Notification enhancements will alert users"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,32,0)=" subscribing to new mail group PSJ STAT NOW PENDING ORDER when a pending"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,33,0)=" STAT or NOW order has been received from Computerized Patient Record"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,34,0)=" System (CPRS) V. 1.0. Users subscribing to the new mail group PSJ STAT"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,35,0)=" NOW ACTIVE ORDER will receive an alert when a STAT or NOW order is made"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,36,0)=" active. This is outlined in BCMA 2001 Special Focus Report, Requirement"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,37,0)=" #12."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,39,0)=" PSJ*5*110 contains repairs for the following defects:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,41,0)=" 1. A site reported a problem with the non-standard schedule messages that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,42,0)=" display in the order view and during finishing. IV orders with Pro Re"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,43,0)=" Nata (PRN) schedules displayed the messages but Unit Dose orders with PRN"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,44,0)=" schedules did not. This patch corrects the problem by including the base"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,45,0)=" PRN schedule in the non-standard check and making Unit Dose and IV orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,46,0)=" consistent. NOIS: MIN-1203-40699."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,48,0)=" 2. A scheduled IV order could be created without a schedule interval when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,49,0)=" created using an IV quick code with a schedule and admin times, but no"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,50,0)=" infusion rate. In this scenario, if an infusion rate is then entered"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,51,0)=" during the finish process, the order is filed with no schedule interval,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,52,0)=" which is necessary to calculate when doses are due."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",115,1,53,0)=" NOIS: SFC-0603-61122."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,0)="111^3050204^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,0)="^^74^74^3050204"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,1,0)="1. The Inpatient Medication Orders for Outpatients project will allow a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,2,0)="user the ability to order unit dose medications for outpatients. This is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,3,0)="accomplished through modifications to Inpatient Medications V. 5.0,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,4,0)="Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V.1.0 and Scheduling V. 5.3."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,5,0)="This patch provides the changes for Inpatient Medications."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,7,0)="2. Provider Comments are not being saved with active IV orders. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,8,0)="corrects this by saving Provider Comments when IV orders become active."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,9,0)="NOIS: ASH-0803-31967, ERI-0303-20187 and ISB-0702-30889. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,11,0)="3. Drug selection lookup was using an old cross reference.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,12,0)="corrects the program to use the correct one. NOIS: ISB-0803-30450"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,14,0)="4. To accommodate Billing Awareness, it was necessary to modify the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,15,0)="communication between CPRS and Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0 to include"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,16,0)="new diagnosis codes. Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 routes all pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,17,0)="orders to the appropriate package. This patch makes the changes necessary"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,18,0)="to pass the new diagnosis codes to the appropriate package."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,20,0)="5. A provider entering an order into Computerized Patient Record System"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,21,0)="(CPRS) V. 1.0 must be permitted to place a limitation on the duration of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,22,0)="an inpatient medication order. This capability exists for Unit Dose orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,23,0)="and Inpatient IV orders, but not for IV Fluid orders. This patch makes"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,24,0)="the change necessary to receive a duration or dosage limit on an IV Fluid"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,25,0)="order placed in CPRS. The limitation will be in hours, days, milliliters,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,26,0)="or liters."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,28,0)="6. A site reported a problem with the default start date and time for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,29,0)="orders created between 11pm and midnight. The default start date for these"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,30,0)="orders may default to 11pm the following day. This patch corrects the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,31,0)="problem by calculating and displaying the correct default start date and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,32,0)="time. NOIS: BRX-0803-12080."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,34,0)="7. Two sites reported a problem with IV labels not printing correctly with"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,35,0)="Day-of-Week schedules that had Sunday in the list. This patch corrects"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,36,0)="this problem. NOIS: PHO-0903-60884, MIN-1003-41071 and MIN-0204-41197."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,38,0)="8. A request was made to modify the Non-Verified/Pending Orders option "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,39,0)="[PSJU VBW] to show the clinic for Outpatient IV orders. This patch makes "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,40,0)="this modification. E3R: 17357"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,42,0)="9. A description has been added to the ACX cross-reference in the ORDERS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,43,0)="FILE PARENT ORDER field (#125), in the NON-VERIFIED ORDERS file (#53.1) "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,44,0)="at the request of the database administrator."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,46,0)="10. A site reported a problem with the display of dosage information "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,47,0)="under certain circumstances. Specifically, there was no  spacing between "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,48,0)="the number and the dosage form. This patch works with changes in Pharmacy "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,49,0)="Data Management V. 1.0 to correct this problem. NOIS: BRX-1004-10173 and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,50,0)="SFC-1003-62552"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,52,0)="11. To accomodate the Scheduling Encapsulation project, a change has been"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,53,0)="made to the retrieval of appointment information. When a specific error"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,54,0)="code is returned, the following message will display in place of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,55,0)="appointment: ""Scheduling database is unavailable"". NOIS: ISB-0903-31960"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,57,0)="12. A site reported that the finishing pharmacist is incorrectly saved as"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,58,0)="the provider when the SF - Speed Finish action is used to finish a pending"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,59,0)="renewal order. This patch corrects the problem by saving the provider "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,60,0)="that renewed the order with the finished and verified order. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,61,0)="NOIS: AMA-1004-71742 and CPH-1004-41922"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,63,0)="13. Orders with Day of Week (DOW) schedules may be created with an "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,64,0)="inappropriate dose frequency which prevents the scheduled doses from "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,65,0)="appearing on the Virtual Due List (VDL) in Bar Code Medication "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,66,0)="Administration (BCMA) V. 3.0. A frequency value appropriate for DOW "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,67,0)="schedules will be stored for orders containing this type of schedule to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,68,0)="ensure they display correctly in BCMA. NOIS: HIN-0503-41736"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,70,0)="14. Orders created in CPRS V. 1.0 between 2300 and 2400 may, during the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,71,0)="finishing process, incorrectly default to a start date and time that is 24"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,72,0)="hours later than the correct default start date and time. Orders created "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,73,0)="between 2300 and 2400 will now default to the correct start date and time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",116,1,74,0)="NOIS: PAL-1203-62062."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,0)="127 SEQ #117^3050212^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,0)="^^106^106^3050212"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,1,0)=" 1. A site reports that when a nurse verifies a renewed order, the nurse's"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,2,0)=" initials do not consistently appear in BCMA. This patch corrects the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,3,0)=" problem by saving the verifying nurse information if the nurse "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,4,0)=" verification occurred after the renewal action. NOIS# NCH-1004-40487."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,6,0)=" 2. A site reports that IV orders copied using the CO (Copy) action in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,7,0)=" Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 retain the original order's verifying "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,8,0)=" pharmacist, so that an unverified copied IV order may incorrectly appear"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,9,0)=" to have been verified by a pharmacist. This patch corrects the problem "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,10,0)=" by removing the original order's verifying pharmacist from the copied"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,11,0)=" order. NOIS# CLA-1004-22199"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,13,0)=" 3. A site reports that after discontinuing a complex IV order, a user "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,14,0)=" may be prevented from creating a new IV order until first exiting and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,15,0)=" then returning to the option. The software treats the new IV order like "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,16,0)=" a complex order and prevents entry of some required fields. This patch "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,17,0)=" corrects the problem by improving the check that determines whether or "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,18,0)=" not the current order is a complex order. NOIS# SAG-1004-41795."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,20,0)=" 4. When using the SF (Speed Finish) action to finish pending renewal"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,21,0)=" orders in the Unit Dose Order Entry [PSJU NE] option, the name of the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,22,0)=" finishing pharmacist is incorrectly saved as the provider for the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,23,0)=" This patch corrects this problem by properly saving the ordering provider"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,24,0)=" with the order when SF (Speed Finish) is used. NOIS# AMA-1004-71742."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,26,0)=" 5. When a component, or child order, of a complex order is created from  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,27,0)=" Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0 with a schedule of NOW "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,28,0)=" and NOW does not exist in the ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE (#51.1) file, the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,29,0)=" order does not appear in the patient's profile in Inpatient Medications "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,30,0)=" V. 5.0. This patch corrects the problem by ensuring child orders with a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,31,0)=" schedule of NOW appear in Inpatient Medications V. 5.0."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,33,0)=" 6. Renewed Unit Dose orders do not appear on the updated pick list"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,34,0)=" printed using the Update Pick List [PSJU PLUP] option. With this patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,35,0)=" renewed orders will appear on the updated pick list when appropriate."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,36,0)=" NOIS: NCH-1104-40147"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,38,0)=" 7. When finishing a complex order that was renewed from CPRS, there is a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,39,0)=" prompt for Pre-Exchange Doses, but there is no prompt to print the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,40,0)=" Pre-Exchange Report. A prompt has been added to allow the Pre-Exchange"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,41,0)=" report to be printed for renewed complex orders. NOIS: MAR-1004-21942."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,43,0)=" 8. The SF Speed Finish action in the Unit Dose Order Entry [PSJU NE]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,44,0)=" option prompts for Pre-Exchange Doses, but there is no prompt to print"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,45,0)=" the Pre-Exchange Report when finishing a pending renewal order. A prompt"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,46,0)=" has been added to allow the Pre-Exchange Report to be printed for orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,47,0)=" that are finished using the SF Speed Finish action. NOIS: CLE-1004-42151."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,49,0)=" 9. The initial label printed for renewed continuous IV orders indicates"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,50,0)=" it is due at the date and time that the order was renewed, rather than"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,51,0)=" at the next scheduled infusion date and time. With this patch, the first"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,52,0)=" label printed for this type of order will be due at the next scheduled"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,53,0)=" infusion date and time. IND-1104-40485."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,55,0)=" 10. After finishing IV scripts, the user is prompted for the number of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,56,0)=" labels to print.  The label print code does not limit the user input, so"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,57,0)=" if the user enters an excessive number of labels, then this can lead to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,58,0)=" system performance problems.  This patch will apply the limit of 99"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,59,0)=" labels at the number of labels prompt. SFC-0603-61734."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,61,0)=" 11. Complex Orders are not showing on the VDL in BCMA when the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,62,0)=" initially contains a schedule without a frequency, regardless of edits"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,63,0)=" made during finishing. With this patch, the schedule changes made during"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,64,0)=" finish will update the complex orders schedule frequency, enabling the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,65,0)=" orders to display in BCMA at the appropriate times. SBY-1104-31772"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,67,0)=" 12. The stop date of a pending renewal order containing a non-standard"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,68,0)=" schedule and an orderable item with a day/dose limit cannot be edited"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,69,0)=" until after the order is made active. Also, Schedule Type and Unit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,70,0)=" Per Dose edits made during finish of a pending renewal are not applied"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,71,0)=" when the order is made active. With this patch, changes made to these"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,72,0)=" fields during the finish proces will be applied to the active order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,73,0)=" ERI-1204-20679"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,75,0)=" 13. One-time orders that are not part of a complex order may be renewed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,76,0)=" from CPRS V.1.0, even after they are given. This patch will prevent this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,77,0)=" problem by preventing all non-complex one-time orders from being renewed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,78,0)=" Restriction of the renewal of complex one-time orders will be addressed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,79,0)=" in a future CPRS V.1.0 patch. PSI-04-056."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,81,0)=" 14. This patch modifies the Data Dictionary of the NON-VERIFIED ORDERS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,82,0)=" FILE (#53.1) for the ORDERS FILE PARENT ORDER field (#125). The change"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,83,0)=" removes Inpatient Medications from the process of stripping NOW orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,84,0)=" from Complex Orders. This process is handled exclusively by CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,86,0)=" 53.1,125     ORDERS FILE PARENT ORDER .2;8 POINTER TO ORDER FILE (#100)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,90,0)="              LAST EDITED:     DEC 13, 2004"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,91,0)="              HELP-PROMPT:     Enter the parent order, if this order is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,92,0)="                               its child order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,93,0)="              DESCRIPTION:     This is the parent of a CPRS order that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,94,0)="                               may have a parent/child relationship in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,95,0)="                               CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,97,0)="             CROSS-REFERENCE:  53.1^ACX"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,98,0)="                               1)= S ^PS(53.1,""ACX"",$E(X,1,30),DA)="""""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,99,0)="                               2)= K ^PS(53.1,""ACX"",$E(X,1,30),DA)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,100,0)="                               This cross reference is created each time a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,101,0)="                               component of a complex order, or child"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,102,0)="                               order, is received from CPRS.  This cross"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,103,0)="                                reference will not be created for orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,104,0)="                               with a schedule of NOW, effectively"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,105,0)="                               disassociating the NOW order from the other"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",117,1,106,0)="                               child orders in the complex order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,0)="128 SEQ #118^3050401^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,1,0)="^^12^12^3050401"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,1,1,0)=" 1. PHO-0803-61519  If finishing an order as a syringe and the volume is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,1,2,0)="    less than 1ml, when entering the decimal it will not allow a leading"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,1,3,0)="    zero(0).  The correction for this problem will allow the input of a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,1,4,0)="    leading zero(0).  If the user does not enter a leading zero(0), the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,1,5,0)="    software will add it."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,1,7,0)=" 2. HEH-1004-40163  When pharmacy prints a label for a TPN order mix, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,1,8,0)="    leading zero(0) in 0.5 GM of magnesium sulfate does not print.  The "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,1,9,0)="    correction for this problem will add the leading zero(0) to the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,1,10,0)="    strength calculation if the value is less than zero(0).  A change"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,1,11,0)="    has also been made during the entry process of strength to add a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",118,1,12,0)="    leading zero(0) if the user does not."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",119,0)="132 SEQ #119^3050401^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",119,1,0)="^^2^2^3050401"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",119,1,1,0)="This patch fixes the 5 missing Pharmacy Intervention menu selections and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",119,1,2,0)="allows output to P-MESSAGE from routine PSGDCTP."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",120,0)="125 SEQ #120^3050401^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",120,1,0)="^^10^10^3050401"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",120,1,1,0)=" 1. CON-0404-10937  Site reported dispensing a ONE TIME unit dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",120,1,2,0)="    medication as a Pre-Exchange dose, the medication also showed up on"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",120,1,3,0)="    the following PICK LIST requesting a dose-to-dispense of one (1)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",120,1,4,0)="    instead of zero (0).  This patch will determine if the SCHEDULE TYPE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",120,1,5,0)="    is ONE-TIME and if a dosage was dispensed as PRE-EXCHANGE and not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",120,1,6,0)="    request a dosage on the PICK LIST."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",120,1,7,0)=" 2. PHO-1204-60861  Renewal of QOD (every other day) schedules causes the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",120,1,8,0)="    Pick List to restart the QOD schedule from the renewal date instead "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",120,1,9,0)="    of the start date.  This routine change will cause the Pick List to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",120,1,10,0)="    maintain the schedule from the start date."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",121,0)="131 SEQ #121^3050506^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",121,1,0)="^^7^7^3050506"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",121,1,1,0)=" Currently the printed MAR does not show that an Inpatient Medication is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",121,1,2,0)=" on hold.  This patch will update the 14 day, 7 day, and 24 hour MAR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",121,1,3,0)=" reports to display ""hold"" on the report in place of the admin time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",121,1,4,0)=" This change will affect the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",121,1,5,0)=" PSJU 14D MAR - 14 Day MAR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",121,1,6,0)=" PSJU 7D MAR - 7 Day MAR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",121,1,7,0)=" PSJU 24H MAR - 24 Hour MAR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,0)="112 SEQ #122^3050525^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,0)="^^30^30^3050525"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,1,0)="1. A request has been made to allow sites to define inpatient orders for "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,2,0)="outpatients' behavior on a clinic-by-clinic basis. The two changes would "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,3,0)="add the ability to control auto-dc of orders and whether or not they"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,4,0)="appear in the Bar Code Medication Administration V. 3.0 package. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,5,0)="patch helps to accomplish this goal by doing the following:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,7,0)="a. Rename the CLINIC STOP DATES file (#53.46) to be the CLINIC DEFINITION "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,8,0)="   file (#53.46)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,9,0)="b. Add the AUTO-DC IMO ORDERS field (#2) and the SEND TO BCMA? field (#3) "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,10,0)="   to the CLINIC DEFINITION file (#53.46)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,11,0)="c. Remove the Clinic Stop Dates option [PSJ CSD]."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,12,0)="d. Add the Clinic Definition option [PSJ CD]."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,14,0)="2. A problem was reported with inpatient orders for outpatients "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,15,0)="displaying in the incorrect display group on the Orders tab in the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,16,0)="Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0. This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,17,0)="problem by modifying the HL7 messaging as well as the order editing "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,18,0)="process to correctly define the appointment date and time for the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,19,0)="inpatient order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,21,0)="3. It was discovered during internal review that the STAT NOW MAIL GROUP "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,22,0)="field (#5) of the INPATIENT WARD PARAMETERS file (#59.6) had been omitted "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,23,0)="from the appropriate distribution. This patch corrects this problem by "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,24,0)="exporting the field."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,26,0)="4. A problem was identified with the display order on the meds tab in "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,27,0)="CPRS. The problem was related to information being passed from Inpatient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,28,0)="Medications V. 5.0 to identify inpatient orders for outpatients. This "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,29,0)="patch corrects this problem by modifying the data pass to CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",122,1,30,0)="NOIS: WAS-0205-20562"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",123,0)="124 SEQ #123^3050611^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",123,1,0)="^^5^5^3050611"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",123,1,1,0)=" 1. TNV-1104-30671  Pharmacy is reporting that they do not see the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",123,1,2,0)="    ""Patient Record Flags"" when using the Inpatient Pharmacy option"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",123,1,3,0)="    ""Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE]"".  This patch will add a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",123,1,4,0)="    reference to DISPPRF^DGPFAPI that is designed to display the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",123,1,5,0)="    ""Patient Record Flags""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,0)="136 SEQ #124^3050611^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,0)="^^32^32^3050611"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,1,0)=" PSI-04-061: Expected First Dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,2,0)=" -------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,3,0)=" During order entry in CPRS the provider is presented with the ""Expected "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,4,0)=" First Dose"" for the order.  The Pharmacist's have requested that the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,5,0)=" ""Expected First Dose"" be displayed in Backdoor pharmacy when Start Date, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,6,0)=" Stop Date and Admin Times are entered or edited."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,8,0)=" This change will require the ""Expected First Dose"" to be displayed after "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,9,0)=" the Stop Date is entered in New or Renewed orders as well as when the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,10,0)=" Start Date, Stop Date and/or Admin Times fields are edited.  During the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,11,0)=" edit process it is possible to edit one or all of these fields in any "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,12,0)=" order.  This could cause the ""Expected First Dose"" to be displayed "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,13,0)=" multiple times.  This will be handled by determining the last field"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,14,0)=" that was edited and displaying the ""Expected first dose"" only after that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,15,0)=" field."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,18,0)=" PSI-04-071: Provider Comments Display"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,19,0)=" -------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,20,0)=" When the pharmacist is presented with the question to ""Copy provider "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,21,0)=" comments"", the provider comments do not appear on the screen.  A change"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,22,0)=" will be made to display the provider comments prior to asking the  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,23,0)=" question ""Copy the Provider Comments into Special Instructions?""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,26,0)=" PSI-05-005: Administration Time being over written on child orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,27,0)=" ------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,28,0)=" When finishing a renewed complex order from Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,29,0)=" OE] option, the administration times for the second and subsequent child "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,30,0)=" orders in the series are changed to the administration time of the first "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,31,0)=" order in the series. A change will be made to preserve the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",124,1,32,0)=" administration time for all orders within a complex order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",125,0)="126 SEQ #125^3050625^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",125,1,0)="^^9^9^3050625"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",125,1,1,0)="Upon installation of this patch, the following Inpatient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",125,1,2,0)="Medications corrections will occur:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",125,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",125,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",125,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",125,1,6,0)="1. A null subscript error (due to undefined variable) will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",125,1,7,0)="   not occur when pick list cross references are killed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",125,1,8,0)="2. The word 'domiciliary' will be spelled correctly in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",125,1,9,0)="   PSJI Site Parameters option."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,0)="133 SEQ #126^3050709^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,0)="^^63^63^3050709"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,1,0)=" 1. A site reported an error that occurred during Speed Finish of pending "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,2,0)=" renewals orders. The error occurred after an unsuccessful lock of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,3,0)=" original renewed order. This patch will prevent this error by ensuring a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,4,0)=" graceful exit when a lock is not successful. CLE-1204-41459"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,6,0)=" 2. The administration schedule validation process causes an error if a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,7,0)=" day-of-week PRN schedule is used that contains days that are out of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,8,0)=" order, for example, ""WE-MO PRN"". This patch will prevent this error and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,9,0)=" make the validation of this type of schedule consistent with non-PRN"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,10,0)=" day-of-week schedules."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,12,0)=" 3. An undefined error may occur when viewing a pending IV renewal order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,13,0)=" from the Medications Tab in Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,14,0)=" 1.0. This patch will correct the problem by preventing the error from"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,15,0)=" occurring. MIN-1204-41611."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,17,0)=" 4. When renewing an Inpatient IV order from the Inpatient Order Entry"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,18,0)=" [PSJ OE] option, an edit to the Provider is not reflected in the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,19,0)=" when viewed from CPRS V.1.0. This patch will correct the problem by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,20,0)=" ensuring the updated provider information is transmitted to CPRS V.1.0."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,21,0)=" IND-0105-40153."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,23,0)=" 5. There is no prompt for output device for the PRE-EXCHANGE UNITS REPORT"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,24,0)=" after copying a Unit Dose order using the CO Copy action in Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,25,0)=" Order Entry [PSJ OE] option. This patch will add a device prompt for the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,26,0)=" Pre-Exchange Units Report to the Unit Dose copy action. HWH-1204-41654."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,28,0)=" 6. When finishing a pending unit dose renewal order, the default "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,29,0)=" administration times associated with the administration schedule will "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,30,0)=" always default into the order, overwriting the order's existing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,31,0)=" administration time. With this patch, renewal orders will retain the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,32,0)=" original order's administration times. BHS-0105-10562."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,34,0)=" 7. When the schedule type is edited during the finish of a unit dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,35,0)=" order that was renewed from CPRS V.1.0, the order appears twice in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,36,0)=" Patient Profile (Unit Dose) [PSJU PR] option. This patch corrects the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,37,0)=" problem by removing the display associated with the previous schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,38,0)=" type before adding the display associated with the new schedule type."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,39,0)=" FRE-0105-60387, MAC-0205-61020."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,41,0)=" 8. Multiple identically named schedules in the ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,42,0)=" file (#51.1) may cause an invalid schedule warning message to appear"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,43,0)=" inappropriately. This patch corrects the problem by preventing the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,44,0)=" invalid warning message from appearing if the schedule name is defined in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,45,0)=" the file, even if duplicates are present. HD0000000085881."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,47,0)=" 9. A non-standard Day of Week schedule entered without administration"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,48,0)=" times using the schedule builder in CPRS V. 3.0 may default to a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,49,0)=" different schedule in Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 if the non-standard"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,50,0)=" schedule is a partial match to a unique Day of Week schedule in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,51,0)=" ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1). For example, if the non-standard"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,52,0)=" schedule SU-MO-TU-WE is entered without admin times using the CPRS V."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,53,0)=" 3.0 schedule builder, and the schedule SU-MO-TU-WE-TH@09 exists in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,54,0)=" ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1), and there are no other schedules in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,55,0)=" the ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1) that begin with SU-MO-TU-WE, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,56,0)=" order's schedule will default to SU-MO-TU-WE-TH@09 when the order is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,57,0)=" selected for finishing.  HD0000000087120, PSI-05-025."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,59,0)=" 10. A non-standard Day of Week schedule entered using the schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,60,0)=" builder in CPRS V. 3.0 defaults to the wrong Expected First Dose if the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,61,0)=" schedule is a partial match to exactly one schedule in the ADMINISTRATION"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,62,0)=" SCHEDULE file (#51.1), and that schedule that was found contains an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",126,1,63,0)=" administration time. HD0000000087028 PSI-05-026."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,0)="144 SEQ #127^3050813^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,1,0)="^^12^12^3050813"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,1,1,0)=" HD0000000086717 - Multiple active Orders Appearing in BCBU"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,1,2,0)=" ----------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,1,3,0)=" A problem has been identified that will cause the BCBU to contain"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,1,4,0)=" multiple active orders for the same order.  This issue happens in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,1,5,0)=" PSJ OE (Inpatient Medications) option.  After a pharmacist finishes and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,1,6,0)=" accepts a complex order, then edits and verifies each order in sequence,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,1,7,0)=" multiple HL7 records are sent to the BCBU signifying the order has been"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,1,8,0)=" verified.  The BCBU should only receive 1 record signifying the order is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,1,9,0)=" verified.  This patch will modify this behavior by sending the HL7   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,1,10,0)=" records as ""Pending"" until all child orders are verified.  Then a final "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,1,11,0)=" HL7 transaction will be sent telling the BCBU that the entire order has "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",127,1,12,0)=" been verified."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,0)="135 SEQ #128^3050905^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,0)="^^13^13^3050905"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,1,0)="The ""undefined variable DIFLD(1)"" error is being caused by the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,2,0)="recursive use of the ^DIE call in a FileMan cross reference."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,3,0)="The ""DATE OF DEATH"" field of the ""PATIENT"" file triggers many"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,4,0)="cross reference procedures and routines."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,5,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,6,0)="The purpose of this patch is to make changes to the Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,7,0)="Medications routines associated with the ""DATE OF DEATH"" APSJD"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,8,0)="cross reference.  There are six tag/program locations that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,9,0)="use the ^DIE call when this cross reference is triggered."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,10,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,11,0)="This patch changes the routines so that they use the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,12,0)="DBS FILE^DIE function that is designed to be used recursively"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",128,1,13,0)="and within FileMan cross references."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,0)="139 SEQ #129^3050905^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,0)="^^25^25^3050905"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,1,0)=" HUN-1003-22262 - Med Order Button"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,2,0)=" ---------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,3,0)=" If a nurse enters an order via the Med Order Button on the BCMA"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,4,0)=" application, and this is the only order for that patient, the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,5,0)=" will not show up on the Non-Verified/Pending Order (PSJU VBW) option if"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,6,0)=" selected by Group, Ward or Clinic. This patch will resolve this issue."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,9,0)=" ERI-0205-20902 - Allergy Checking"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,10,0)=" ---------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,11,0)=" While testing CPRS V25, it was discovered that not all Allergy checks"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,12,0)=" were being displayed.  This could occur if there were multiple VA DRUG"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,13,0)=" CLASS entries entered for a patient.  A change will be made to loop all"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,14,0)=" VA DRUG CLASS entries for the patient to correctly identify potential"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,15,0)=" drug allergies."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,18,0)=" PUG-0205-50079 - Report printer length"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,19,0)=" --------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,20,0)=" There is an inconsistency between the length of the IV ROOM (59.5) file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,21,0)=" fields LABEL DEVICE (13) and REPORT DEVICE (14) and the corresponding"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,22,0)=" entry in the DEVICE (3.5) file.  The IV ROOM fields only allows 20"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,23,0)=" characters and the DEVICE file allows 30 characters.  The IV ROOM file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,24,0)=" fields LABEL DEVICE and REPORT DEVICE will be changed to allow 30"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",129,1,25,0)=" characters."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",130,0)="137 SEQ #130^3050924^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",130,1,0)="^^9^9^3050924"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",130,1,1,0)=" 1. From NOIS call BED-1004-10719, Regarding the reinstated "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",130,1,2,0)="    medications notification email message, ""It doesn't look"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",130,1,3,0)="    like the ordering clinician gets any notification.""  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",130,1,4,0)="    patch will add the ordering physician to the list of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",130,1,5,0)="    email recipients."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",130,1,6,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",130,1,7,0)=" 2. BAY-0205-30845, Syntax Error at WRD+1^PSIVRNL."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",130,1,8,0)="    This patch will correct the syntax error included in this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",130,1,9,0)="    routine."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,0)="140 SEQ #131^3051115^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,0)="^^17^17^3051115"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,1,0)=" HD0000000086021 - IV Renewal Issue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,2,0)=" -----------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,3,0)=" When finishing a renewed IV order via Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,4,0)=" it is possible to enter the same stop date as the original for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,5,0)=" the renewed order.  This will cause the database to improperly"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,6,0)=" index the renewal.  This causes the wrong number of labels to print as"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,7,0)=" well as not printing this order on the Ward List report. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,8,0)=" will resolve this issue by correcting indexing the renewal."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,10,0)=" HD0000000068894 - PSJOE Error"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,11,0)=" -----------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,12,0)=" The following error has appeared in the error trap at various sites:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,14,0)=" <UNDEFINED>DISACTIO+36^PSJOE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,16,0)=" This patch will resolve this issue by re-initializing the variable in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",131,1,17,0)=" question."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",132,0)="151 SEQ #132^3051115^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",132,1,0)="^^11^11^3051115"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",132,1,1,0)="  * WARNING - Prior to installing this patch, please check for local Class"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",132,1,2,0)="    III modifications that may be overwritten upon installation. Failure"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",132,1,3,0)="    to reinstall Class III modifications after installation of this patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",132,1,4,0)="    may prevent the Class III changes from functioning properly."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",132,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",132,1,6,0)=" 1. When finishing a CPRS-entered IV Medication order, if the user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",132,1,7,0)="    makes a change to the order that causes a new order to be created,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",132,1,8,0)="    the new order is not locked and allows the provider to change the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",132,1,9,0)="    order while the pharmacist is still working on the order. The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",132,1,10,0)="    correction locks the newly created order until the pharmacist has"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",132,1,11,0)="    completed editing."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,0)="147 SEQ #133^3051115^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,0)="^^13^13^3051115"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,1,0)=" 1. When a provider enters an IV order and the Pharmacist finishes the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,2,0)="    order and tries to delete an additive and make changes in the solution"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,3,0)="    field the additive shows as deleted. When the order is accepted, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,4,0)="    order re-displays shows with the same additive that was deleted.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,5,0)="    correction makes the needed code changes so that the deleted additive"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,6,0)="    will actually be deleted as requested."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,8,0)=" 2. The pharmacist is unable to edit the solution field of a newly entered"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,9,0)="    TPN order.  It was noted in the original NOIS report and supporting"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,10,0)="    screen captures that the pharmacist was using lower case.  The system"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,11,0)="    responded differently because of the lower case letters.  The changes"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,12,0)="    included in this patch will cause the system to function equally for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",133,1,13,0)="    upper and lower case letters in the standard VISTA operation."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",134,0)="142 SEQ #134^3051115^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",134,1,0)="^^10^10^3051115"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",134,1,1,0)=" 1. When finishing a CPRS-entered order for a syringe, if the user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",134,1,2,0)="    indicates ""NO"" at the intermittent syringe prompt, the syringe "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",134,1,3,0)="    size field is required and causes a loop back to the patient's"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",134,1,4,0)="    profile if it is not filled in.  This patch will allow the user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",134,1,5,0)="    to ""carriage return"" past the SYRINGE SIZE prompt and continue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",134,1,6,0)="    finishing the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",134,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",134,1,8,0)=" 2. Currently when field ""(12) Dispense Drug"" of an order is edited an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",134,1,9,0)="    updated picklist is not triggered.  This change will cause an update"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",134,1,10,0)="    trigger to the picklist."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",135,0)="153 SEQ #135^3051202^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",135,1,0)="^^11^11^3051202"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",135,1,1,0)=" 1. PSI-05-062:  When the site has the Inpatient Medication site parameter"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",135,1,2,0)="    ""SAME STOP DATE ON ALL ORDERS:"" set to ""YES"", and the patient's "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",135,1,3,0)="    ""DEFAULT STOP DATE/TIME"" is set to TODAY.  When a physician ""RENEWS"" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",135,1,4,0)="    orders, the default stop date gets calculated as TODAY for the first"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",135,1,5,0)="    order.  The patient's ""DEFAULT STOP DATE/TIME"" is extended when the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",135,1,6,0)="    first order is accepted and the default stop date for following orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",135,1,7,0)="    is calculated correctly."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",135,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",135,1,9,0)="    This patch is designed to extend the patient's ""DEFAULT STOP "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",135,1,10,0)="    DATE/TIME"" and correctly calculate the default stop date for the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",135,1,11,0)="    first order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",136,0)="130 SEQ #136^3051202^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",136,1,0)="^^11^11^3051202"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",136,1,1,0)="In support of the Decision Support System (DSS) FY2006 Extract"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",136,1,2,0)="Enhancement project two changes have been requested in Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",136,1,3,0)="Medications V. 5.0."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",136,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",136,1,5,0)="First, add the order number to the list of data being sent to DSS Extracts"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",136,1,6,0)="V. 3.0."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",136,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",136,1,8,0)="Second, add the IV room and order date to the list of data being sent to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",136,1,9,0)="DSS Extracts V. 3.0. The order date will be the date the order was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",136,1,10,0)="verified by a nurse or if that is not present, the login date of the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",136,1,11,0)="order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",137,0)="163 SEQ #137^3051202^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",138,0)="149 SEQ #138^3051221^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",138,1,0)="^^10^10^3051221"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",138,1,1,0)="     This patch addresses two separate issues.  In the first issue,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",138,1,2,0)="     if the ward group or ward location is not properly defined, or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",138,1,3,0)="     if the administration team is not properly defined, patients and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",138,1,4,0)="      or medications can be left off of the Action Profile-2 Report"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",138,1,5,0)="     [PSJU AP-2]."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",138,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",138,1,7,0)="     The second issue addressed by this patch will make CPRS and backdoor"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",138,1,8,0)="     pharmacy function consistently with respect to discontinuing an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",138,1,9,0)="     original order while it has a pending renewal.  CPRS will not allow"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",138,1,10,0)="     the original order to be discontinued, backdoor currently will."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,0)="129 SEQ #139^3051221^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,0)="^^15^15^3051221"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,1,0)=" 1. When finishing a pending renewal order, if the order is edited"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,2,0)=" such that the number of dispense drugs associated with the order after"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,3,0)=" verification is less than the number of dispense drugs associated with"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,4,0)=" the order prior to renew, an index used by the pick list incorrectly"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,5,0)=" retains entries associated with the old dispense drugs. This may cause"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,6,0)=" problems with pick lists and extracts. With this patch, the correct"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,7,0)=" number of dispense drugs will be stored with renewal orders for which the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,8,0)=" number of dispense drugs was reduced during the finish of the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,9,0)=" AMA-1204-71370."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,11,0)=" 2. Updated pick lists display doses for renewed orders that may already"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,12,0)=" have been dispensed prior to the renewal. With this patch, doses for a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,13,0)=" renewed order will appear on the pick list update beginning with doses"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,14,0)=" due after the latter of the renew date and the order's stop date prior"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",139,1,15,0)=" to renewal. TNV-0205-31276."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",140,0)="146 SEQ #140^3060112^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",140,1,0)="^^6^6^3060112"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",140,1,1,0)="This patch adds the capability of doing order checking between local VA "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",140,1,2,0)="facilities and remote VA or Department of Defense (DoD) facilities where "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",140,1,3,0)="veterans have received prescriptions."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",140,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",140,1,5,0)="The order checking includes checking for duplicate drugs, duplicate drug "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",140,1,6,0)="classes, drug interactions, and drug allergies."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",141,0)="150 SEQ #141^3060213^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",141,1,0)="^^4^4^3060213"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",141,1,1,0)="It has been discovered that the Extra Units Dispensed [PSJU EUD] option"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",141,1,2,0)="was not communicating properly with the ATC machine after the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",141,1,3,0)="installation of CPRS version 25.  This patch will resolve this "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",141,1,4,0)="communication issue."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,0)="138 SEQ #142^3060308^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,0)="^^24^24^3060308"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,1,0)=" 1. An undefined variable error occurs when an attempt is made to print a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,2,0)=" MAR label for a non-verified order. The error occurs when the software"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,3,0)=" attempts to retrieve clinic appointment information from the non-verified"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,4,0)=" order. Once the order is verified the MAR label prints without producing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,5,0)=" the error. This patch corrects this issue by correctly processing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,6,0)=" non-verified orders without appointment information."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,7,0)=" HD0000000068851"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,9,0)=" 2. Immediately after copying a unit dose order, if the order's schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,10,0)=" is edited, administration times and schedule frequency from the new"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,11,0)=" schedule do not default into the copied order. This patch corrects this  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,12,0)=" issue by using the administration times and schedule frequency from the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,13,0)=" newly entered schedule. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,14,0)=" HD0000000102178 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,16,0)=" 3. When changing an IV order's schedule from a continuous schedule to a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,17,0)=" one-time schedule with no frequency defined in the ADMINISTRATION "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,18,0)=" SCHEDULE file (#51.1), the order's schedule interval is not updated, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,19,0)=" resulting in the order's IV labels printing based on the frequency of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,20,0)=" the original schedule. For example, if an IV order's schedule is changed "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,21,0)=" from Q6H to ONCE, IV labels will continue to print based on the Q6H "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,22,0)=" schedule, or 4 labels per day. This patch will require an order's "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,23,0)=" schedule interval to be updated with the frequency from the new schedule."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",142,1,24,0)=" HD0000000092412"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",143,0)="152^3060308^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",143,1,0)="^^3^3^3060308"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",143,1,1,0)="1. The addition of two new DRUG UNITS to the Inpatient Medication IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",143,1,2,0)="    package has been requested.  The two requested units are MG-PE and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",143,1,3,0)="    NANOGRAM."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,0)="155 SEQ #144^3060308^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,0)="^^25^25^3060308"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,1,0)=" HD0000000106439 - Non-Verified Pending Report showing patients at the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,2,0)="                   Wrong location."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,3,0)=" ------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,4,0)="It has been discovered that the Non-Verified Pending report (PSJU VBW)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,5,0)="is showing patients still under the clinic after being admitted to a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,6,0)="ward.  This issue will be resolved by correctly searching the proper"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,7,0)="indexes used to determine the patient's current location. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,9,0)=" HD0000000108102 - Expired on hold order cannot be removed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,10,0)=" ------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,11,0)="If an order is placed ""on hold"" and then expires before being ""taken "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,12,0)="Off hold"" the order will appear on the medication profile's ""Active"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,13,0)="List of medications.  If the Rph attempts to ""unhold"" this order the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,14,0)="message ""this order has expired"" will be displayed and the order will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,15,0)="remain on the list of Active medications.  This patch will resolve this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,16,0)="issue by allowing the Rph to remove the order from hold.  After the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,17,0)="order is removed from hold, it will immediately be removed from the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,18,0)="active medications list."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,20,0)=" HD0000000108826 - Undefined error when exiting Pick list"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,21,0)=" ------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,22,0)="If you attempt to exit the ""Requested Start Time:"" prompt in the Pick"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,23,0)="List option (PSJU PLUP) you may receive the following error:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,24,0)="<UNDEFINED>UP+6^PSGPLUP"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",144,1,25,0)="This patch will resolve this issue."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,0)="168 SEQ #145^3060410^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,0)="^^30^30^3060410"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,1,0)=" 1. When a pick list contains one or more orders for which there is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,2,0)=" an inconsistency between the number of dispense drugs associated with "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,3,0)=" the order and the number of dispense drug index entries associated with "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,4,0)=" the order, a MailMan message is generated incorrectly stating that a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,5,0)=" problem exists with a DRUG file (#50) entry. A message generated in "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,6,0)=" this way may be identified by the display of numbers separated by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,7,0)=" commas, rather than the name of the drug."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,9,0)=" Example:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,10,0)="     The following items from your DRUG file were found to have NO DATA in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,11,0)="     their PRICE PER DISPENSE UNIT field:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,12,0)="          1234567,123,1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,14,0)="       Any PICK LIST with any of these items will NOT be completely FILED"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,15,0)="     AWAY until the PRICE PER DISPENSE UNIT field has been entered into "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,16,0)="     for these items."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,17,0)="       Even if there is no cost for these items, a zero (0) must be "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,18,0)="     entered into the PRICE PER DISPENSE UNIT field so the package knows"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,19,0)="     it is not an error or an omission.  UNTIL THIS IS DONE, NO COST"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,20,0)="     REPORT WILL BE ACCURATE, AND ANY PICK LIST WITH THESE ITEMS CANNOT BE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,21,0)="     PURGED."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,23,0)=" With this patch, this MailMan message will not be generated due to an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,24,0)=" extraneous or 'orphan' dispense drug index entry associated with an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,25,0)=" order. HD0000000068561. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,27,0)=" 2. To assist in preventing problems with dispense drugs of active "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,28,0)=" orders, the ability to delete dispense drugs from a pending renewal will "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,29,0)=" be removed. Functionality will be added to allow dispense drugs to be "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",145,1,30,0)=" inactivated for pending renewal orders. HD0000000068561. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,0)="164 SEQ #146^3060410^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,0)="^^15^15^3060410"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,1,0)="This patch addresses two issues contained in two Remedy tickets, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,2,0)="HD118307 and HD108011."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,4,0)="The first issue addressed by this patch is an undefined variable error "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,5,0)="when the user attempts to run the menu option [PSJU EUD].  If the user "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,6,0)="selects a patient who has never been admitted, then presses the carriage "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,7,0)="return again at the Select Patient prompt, an undefined variable error "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,8,0)="occurs."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,10,0)="The second issue addressed involves an incorrect display of the dispense "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,11,0)="drug units in backdoor pharmacy.  If the dispense drug units per dose are "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,12,0)="changed (editing field 12 backdoor), and one of the drugs' units "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,13,0)="dispensed becomes 0, backdoor pharmacy will still display a value of 1 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,14,0)="for that drug.  BCMA and CPRS show the correct dispense drug units, and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",146,1,15,0)="the correct units are stored in the ^PS(55) file."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,0)="167 SEQ #147^3060410^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,1,0)="^^12^12^3060410"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,1,1,0)=" Pending complex orders cannot be verified when the complex order is also"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,1,2,0)=" an Inpatient Orders for Outpatients (IMO) order. This patch corrects this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,1,3,0)=" issue by allowing the verification of complex IMO orders if the IMO"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,1,4,0)=" functionality is active and the clinic is a valid IMO clinic."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,1,6,0)=" Complex Inpatient orders may only be created if the Inpatient Orders for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,1,7,0)=" Outpatients (IMO) functionality has been activated.  The same criteria"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,1,8,0)=" used to determine if a simple IMO order may be selected for finishing in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,1,9,0)=" Inpatient Medications will be used for Complex Orders; for instance, if"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,1,10,0)=" the clinic associated with the order is not a valid IMO clinic, the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,1,11,0)=" may not be finished in Inpatient Medications."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",147,1,12,0)=" HD115420"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",148,0)="141 SEQ #148^3060410^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",148,1,0)="^^10^10^3060410"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",148,1,1,0)="This patch addresses two issues in two Remedy tickets. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",148,1,2,0)="The first issue addressed by this patch arose when the site"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",148,1,3,0)="used the ATZERO (@0) flag on IV Piggybacks to prevent labels"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",148,1,4,0)="from printing.  Labels printed despite the flag being set."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",148,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",148,1,6,0)="The second issue involves the wrong provider being displayed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",148,1,7,0)="by CPRS and backdoor pharmacy when an order is renewed.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",148,1,8,0)="Currently, CPRS and backdoor pharmacy are still displaying the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",148,1,9,0)="original provider.  The sites are expecting to see the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",148,1,10,0)="renewing provider to be displayed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",149,0)="166 SEQ #149^3060504^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",149,1,0)="^^5^5^3060504"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",149,1,1,0)=" 1. The Inpatient Medication Package patient name lookup routine is not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",149,1,2,0)="    correctly looking up patient's using the partial match functionality"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",149,1,3,0)="    that is standard with other packages.  This patch will correct this by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",149,1,4,0)="    replacing the lookup call to ^DIC with the DPTLK API designed for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",149,1,5,0)="    patient lookup."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",150,0)="122 SEQ #151^3060525^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",150,1,0)="^^5^5^3060525"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",150,1,1,0)="Several sites reported a problem with the sort for the Inpatient Profile "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",150,1,2,0)="option [PSJ PR]. The sort by patient and room-bed was no longer "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",150,1,3,0)="functioning. This patch corrects this problem. HD68431, HD68690, HD68981, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",150,1,4,0)="HD89922, HD94618, HD94785, HD95473, HD96140, HD96553, HD97042, HD98398, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",150,1,5,0)="HD106136, HD131842"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,0)="154 SEQ #152^3060614^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,0)="^^15^15^3060614"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,1,0)=" 1. PSI-05-051:  A priority status of ASAP is not easily seen by the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,2,0)="    finishing pharmacist.  A STAT order is displayed as blinking and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,3,0)="    highlighted, but a ASAP order does not have any special visual"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,4,0)="    effects.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,6,0)="    In order to avoid adding more special visual effects to the screen "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,7,0)="    this patch is designed to offer a Site Ward Parameter that will allow"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,8,0)="    the site a choice of what orders are sent to the STAT NOW MAIL GROUP."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,9,0)="    The site can select STAT, ASAP, or NOW orders, or any combination of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,10,0)="    the three for notification via the STAT NOW MAIL GROUP functionality."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,12,0)=" 2. Remedy Ticket #106018:  Stat IV orders are not highlighted and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,13,0)="    flashing like Stat Unit Dose orders.  This patch adds the code"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,14,0)="    required to make Stat IV orders highlighted and flash like Stat Unit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",151,1,15,0)="    Dose orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",152,0)="156 SEQ #153^3060711^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",152,1,0)="^^11^11^3060711"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",152,1,1,0)="A provider entered a medication through CPRS with the intent of the order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",152,1,2,0)="being administered on a QD0600 continuous schedule.  The medication "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",152,1,3,0)="ordered, however, had a default schedule type of PRN.  Therefore, when "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",152,1,4,0)="the pharmacist finished the order backdoor, the default schedule type of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",152,1,5,0)="PRN overrode the Provider's intent of a continuous schedule.  Because the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",152,1,6,0)="medication was finished as PRN, the patient missed a dose of the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",152,1,7,0)="medication."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",152,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",152,1,9,0)="This patch addresses this issue by only allowing the backdoor default"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",152,1,10,0)="schedule type to override the incoming CPRS schedule type if the backdoor"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",152,1,11,0)="default is ""Fill on Request""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,0)="170 SEQ #154^3060824^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,0)="^^26^26^3060824"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,1,0)="1.  CPRS IV Orders currently select the first of multiple IV Additives by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,2,0)="    IEN associated with the Pharmacy Orderable Item selected in CPRS by"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,3,0)="    the Provider.  The software checks to determine if the IV Additive "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,4,0)="    is Inactive, but does not check the ""USED IN IV FLUID ORDER ENTRY"" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,5,0)="    field to determine if the additive should be used."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,7,0)="    This patch will change the software to add a check of the ""USED "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,8,0)="    IN IV FLUID ORDER ENTRY"" field and exclude the additive from selection"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,9,0)="    based on that field."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,11,0)="*** The software included in this patch is designed to exclude an IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,12,0)="    Additive from the selection process only if the ""USED IN IV FLUID "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,13,0)="    ORDER ENTRY"" field is set to ""NO""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,14,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,15,0)="*** If the ""USED IN IV FLUID ORDER ENTRY"" field is set to ""YES"" or "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,16,0)="    blank, then the IV Additive will be selected in IEN order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,18,0)="2.  This patch is also designed to correct a programming error in routine"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,19,0)="    PSJPXRM1 that is to be used by CPRS to return Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,20,0)="    order information.  This is a routine that is not currently in use,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,21,0)="    and will be tested at the programmer prompt."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,23,0)="3.  If the user enters a start date/time in the future and then enters "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,24,0)="    the number of doses at the stop date/time prompt, the software"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,25,0)="    calculates the stop date/time from the current date/time instead of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",153,1,26,0)="    the entered start date/time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,0)="172 SEQ #155^3060923^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,0)="^^27^27^3060923"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,1,0)="This patch contains Application Program Interfaces (APIs) that will be "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,2,0)="used by calling applications that currently do direct global reads or "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,3,0)="writes to the Inpatient Medications files. Since the IV ROOM file "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,4,0)="(#59.5) and the NON-VERIFIED ORDERS file (#53.1) are being replaced as part"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,5,0)="of the Pharmacy Re-engineering project, any direct M-based global reads"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,6,0)="or writes to this file must be replaced by calling the APIs provided in "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,7,0)="this patch. When the new data source is in place, the calling applications "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,8,0)="will not be required to make any changes, because these APIs will be "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,9,0)="flexible enough to retrieve the requested data from the new data source, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,10,0)="when the time comes."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,12,0)="This API replaces the following integration agreements:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,14,0)="DBIA #  Affected Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,15,0)="------  -------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,16,0)="1884    DSS EXTRACTS,DRUG ACCOUNTABILITY"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,17,0)="2907    TEXT INTEGRATION UTILITIES"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,18,0)="534     HEALTH SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,20,0)="This patch enhances an original INPATIENT MEDICATIONS API call "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,21,0)="ALL^PSJ59P5. This enhancement allows a double question mark (""??"") to be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,22,0)="passed in to the second parameter PSJFT. PSJFT represents the free-text"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,23,0)="name a user wishes to retrieve from this file. Passing ""??"" to the PSJFT"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,24,0)="parameter will cause the API to return all entries from the IV ROOM FILE "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,25,0)="(#59.5). Specifications for this API can be found in the Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,26,0)="Re-Engineering (PRE) API Manual. Reference to MEDICAL CENTER "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",154,1,27,0)="DIVISION FILE (#40.8) is supported by DBIA 2269."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,0)="171 SEQ #156^3061122.200651^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,0)="^^17^17^3061122"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,1,0)="1.  This problem happens when multiple complex orders are selected"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,2,0)="    together to be finished or verified.  If the first order is partially "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,3,0)="    finished or verified.  The system notifies the user that if all orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,4,0)="    are not finished or verified, then none of the orders will be finished"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,5,0)="    or verified, but leaves the order in a ""corrupted"" state."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,7,0)="    This patch makes changes to the routine to clean up the temporary"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,8,0)="    variables so the process can loop through multiple complex orders "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,9,0)="    without causing the ""corrupted"" state."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,11,0)="2.  Currently in file #55, PHARMACY PATIENT, the UNIT DOSE multiple "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,12,0)="    field, the ACTIVITY LOG multiple field, the file number of node #14 is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,13,0)="    sometimes being written incorrectly as 55,09."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,15,0)="    This patch includes the correction to the routines that are writing "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,16,0)="    this information and a post init routine to correct the existing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",155,1,17,0)="    information."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,0)="186 SEQ #157^3061122.222842^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,0)="^^13^13^3061122"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,1,0)="This patch addresses Remedy ticket HD158508 (PSI 06 125) and its "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,2,0)="duplicate tickets.  An order with Special Instructions was entered, and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,3,0)="when prompted, the order was finished so that the BCMA Message Box flag "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,4,0)="was set.  Therefore, when the medication was to be administered in BCMA, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,5,0)="a pop-up box was to display to show the nurse the Special Instructions.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,6,0)="The order was renewed via CPRS, and the order was FINISHED backdoor and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,7,0)="then had the Special Instructions were deleted before accepting the order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,8,0)="and verifying.  When the nurse entered BCMA to administer the medication "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,9,0)="on the renewed order, BCMA behaved as though the medication was given, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,10,0)="but no pop-up box appeared, and the medication was not marked as given on "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,11,0)="the VDL.  The underlying issue was that while the order had the Special "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,12,0)="Instructions deleted, the flag to display/not display the message box in "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",156,1,13,0)="BCMA was not cleared."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",157,0)="157 SEQ #158^3061122.234635^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",157,1,0)="^^9^9^3061122"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",157,1,1,0)="This patch addresses Remedy ticket HD101591."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",157,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",157,1,3,0)="HD101591, will show the pharmacist an expected first "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",157,1,4,0)="dose date/time for IV orders during the finishing process.  Currently, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",157,1,5,0)="for IV's ordered either backdoor or through the CPRS IV Meds Dialog, no "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",157,1,6,0)="""Expected First Dose"" is displayed.  Unit dose orders, and IV's ordered "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",157,1,7,0)="through the Inpatient Meds dialog on CPRS do display an expected first "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",157,1,8,0)="dose.  An Expected First dose will not display if the schedule type for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",157,1,9,0)="the order is ON CALL or PRN."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,0)="177 SEQ #159^3061227.144143^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,0)="^^27^27^3061227"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,1,0)="HD000000104291 - Stop Date calculation can be in the Past"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,2,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,3,0)="When editing the Additive or Solution of an active order that was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,4,0)="previously renewed, the stop date/time can be re-calculated in the Past. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,5,0)="This will cause the order to be expired immediately upon verification.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,6,0)="The solution to this issue is to modify the Stop Date/Time calculation to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,7,0)="use the ""Last Renewed"" date as a starting point, instead of the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,8,0)="""Original"" Start Date/Time of the order, when editing the Additive or "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,9,0)="Solution of an active IV order that has been previously renewed. (this "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,10,0)="makes the Stop Date/Time calculation that occurs during edits to the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,11,0)="Additives and Solutions fields consistent with edits to other fields)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,13,0)="During the Testing of the solution above a new issue has been found."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,15,0)="New Issue 1: Editing the Additive or Solution for non-renewed orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,16,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,17,0)="This is the same issue as the Original issue but it can also apply to a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,18,0)="Non-renewed Active order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,20,0)="The solution for the New issue is to Modify the Inpatient Meds IV Order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,21,0)="Check logic to Display the warning message ""The Stop Date/Time is in the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,22,0)="Past.  This order will automatically expire upon verification"", anytime "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,23,0)="the stop date calculation returns a Stop Date/Time in the past.  The "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,24,0)="Pharmacist will then be asked if they still wish to continue.  If they "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,25,0)="continue, the order will automatically expire immediately upon "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,26,0)="verification  If they select to not continue, they may go back to the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",158,1,27,0)="profile and edit the Stop Date/Time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",159,0)="162 SEQ #160^3061229.09203^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",159,1,0)="^^6^6^3061229"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",159,1,1,0)="1.  After Finishing and Verifying a complex Outpatient IV order, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",159,1,2,0)="    system was treating the New Order entered afterwards as a complex"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",159,1,3,0)="    order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",159,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",159,1,5,0)="    This patch makes a correction to the software that cleans up "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",159,1,6,0)="    information from a previous order before moving on to a New Order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,0)="174 SEQ #161^3070627.213712^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,0)="^^18^18^3070627"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,1,0)="1.  The function [Patient Profile (Extended)] isn't displaying complex"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,2,0)="    orders correctly."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,3,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,4,0)="    Before the patch this function displays each individual pending"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,5,0)="    complex order with a selection number for viewing."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,7,0)="    This patch is designed to display the entire complex order with a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,8,0)="    single selection number and display the full complex order when that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,9,0)="    number is selected for view."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,11,0)="2.  Remedy Ticket HD127723 reported the problem that the system did not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,12,0)="    correctly handle the Q5MINUTES schedule during the finish process.  It"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,13,0)="    would not accept the users input when prompted for a schedule after"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,14,0)="    selecting to FN(Finish) the order.  According to the Inpatient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,15,0)="    Medication developers the system should not be prompting for a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,16,0)="    schedule with an exact match at this point in the FN(Finish)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,17,0)="    process.  This patch makes the correction to prevent the schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",160,1,18,0)="    prompts for an exact match."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,0)="183 SEQ #162^3070627.231837^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,0)="^^16^16^3070627"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,1,0)="** WARNING - After installing this patch, a location AND ad appointment "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,2,0)="date & time will be required before IMO logic is executed!"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,4,0)="This patch addresses the issue of an inpatient's medication's stop time "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,5,0)="being inadvertently set to 24 hours."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,7,0)="A medical student at a site erroneously changed the location of an "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,8,0)="inpatient while ordering a unit dose medication in CPRS.  The clinic "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,9,0)="location the student chose had a default stop time on orders of 24 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,10,0)="hours.  When the pharmacist finished the order, it was not noticed that "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,11,0)="the stop date was 24 hours, not the normal default stop date for an "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,12,0)="inpatient's medication orders.  As a result, the patient did not receive "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,13,0)="his/her medication as prescribed.  The inpatient meds code in VistA "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,14,0)="assumed the order was an IMO (Inpatient Medications for Outpatients) "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,15,0)="order because it had a clinic location.  The code will be updated to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",161,1,16,0)="recognize a unit dose."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,0)="178 SEQ #163^3070629.190705^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,0)="^^52^52^3070629"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,1,0)="A site reported a problem with the fact that medication route did not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,2,0)="appear on the IV label. This patch corrects this problem by adding the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,3,0)="medication route to the IV label. PSI-05-107, HD115653"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,5,0)="****Important Note****"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,6,0)="The decision of the workgroup was that the medication route should appear"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,7,0)="in a larger font than the remaining text. If you do not define the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,8,0)="following correctly, the medication route will not be in a larger font."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,9,0)="In order to allow this functionality, four new control codes must be set"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,10,0)="up. They are:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,12,0)="SM          Start Med Route"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,13,0)="EM          End Med Route"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,14,0)="SMF         Start Med Route field"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,15,0)="EMF         End Med Route field"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,17,0)="These control codes are defined by using FileMan V. 22.0 and editing the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,18,0)="CONTROL CODES multiple (#3.2055) of the TERMINAL TYPE file (#3.2)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,20,0)="Each printer can have different values required in order to properly"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,21,0)="print the route. Please note that it may be necessary to adjust the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,22,0)="label length through the SITE PARAMETERS (IV) option in order for the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,23,0)="label to print correctly."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,25,0)="The following is one example of the setup for a Zebra 105SL printer."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,28,0)="NUMBER: 12                              CTRL CODE ABBREVIATION: SM"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,29,0)="  FULL NAME: START MED ROUTE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,30,0)="  CONTROL CODE: W ""^FO"",PSJBARX,"","",PSJBARY,""^A0N,36,30"",!!"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,31,0)="NUMBER: 13                              CTRL CODE ABBREVIATION: EM"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,32,0)="  FULL NAME: END MED ROUTE              CONTROL CODE: S PSJBARY=PSJBARY+40"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,33,0)="NUMBER: 14                              CTRL CODE ABBREVIATION: SMF"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,34,0)="  FULL NAME: START MED ROUTE FIELD      CONTROL CODE: W ""^FD"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,35,0)="NUMBER: 15                              CTRL CODE ABBREVIATION: EMF"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,36,0)="  FULL NAME: END MED ROUTE FIELD        CONTROL CODE: W ""^FS"",!"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,38,0)="The resulting Bar Code IV Label Example, which includes Medication Route"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,39,0)="is shown:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,41,0)="       *520V452*"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,42,0)="[65] 9111  ONE EAST 03/19/02"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,43,0)="PSJPATIENT1,ONE  B-12"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,45,0)="ACETAMINOPHEN 100 MEQ"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,46,0)="0.9% SODIUM CHLORIDE 100 ML"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,48,0)="Dose due at: ________"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,49,0)="ROUTE: INTRAVENOUS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,50,0)="100 ml/hr"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,51,0)="Fld by: ____  Chkd by: ____"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",162,1,52,0)="1[1]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,0)="160 SEQ #164^3070904.225723^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,0)="^^21^21^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,1,0)="1. During testing of Remote Data Interoperability (RDI), a problem was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,2,0)="discovered with the order checks involving remote allergies. Not all of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,3,0)="the remote allergies were being included when doing order checks using VA "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,4,0)="Drug Class. This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,6,0)="2. An issue with too many false positive order checks was discovered when "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,7,0)="doing order checks on certain drug classes. Analgesics, as a class, were "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,8,0)="performing order checks across all members. For example: class CN101 was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,9,0)="generating an order check for class CN102. This patch corrects this "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,10,0)="problem by ensuring that Analgesic order checks only match against the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,11,0)="specific class: CN101 to CN101. HD0000000161499"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,13,0)="3. One feature of RDI is the notification to the user when processing "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,14,0)="orders that only local data is being used - if the remote data is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,15,0)="unavailable. Several sites reported issues with this mechanism. This "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,16,0)="patch corrects this problem by performing the check for remote data "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,17,0)="availability upon entering the patient's chart, rather than on each order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,19,0)="4. The list of remote allergies has been added to Patient Information "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,20,0)="screen. If a patient has the same allergy information from several remote"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",163,1,21,0)="sites, it will only be listed once."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,0)="169 SEQ #165^3070904.230336^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,0)="^^35^35^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,1,0)="This patch will correct three problems with the Action Profile reports "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,2,0)="from three Remedy tickets, HD118347 HD120274, and HD68707, as well as one "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,3,0)="undefined variable error with the Patient Profile, [PSJU PR], in ticket "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,4,0)="HD120176."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,6,0)="The first Action Profile Report problem was a result of internal testing "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,7,0)="with patch PSJ*5*157, wherein it was noted that if a device used for "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,8,0)="printing did not have a standard page length, the number of lines printed "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,9,0)="in the Additional Medication Orders section of the Action Profile reports "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,10,0)="[PSJU AP-1] and [PSJU AP-2] would vary from patient to patient.  It was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,11,0)="decided by the Inpatient Medications Workgroup that the number of lines "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,12,0)="printed for this section should be standardized to 10 lines."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,14,0)="The second problem occurs only with the Action Profile 2 report, [PSJU "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,15,0)="AP-2].  The problem only occurs if the report is printed to the screen.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,16,0)="The report prints properly if printed to a printer.  If the patient has a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,17,0)="verified allergy, a verified adverse reaction, or one of each, the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,18,0)="Allergy and Adverse Reaction section of the report is printing ""No "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,19,0)="Allergy Assessment"".  This patch will correct this problem so the AP-2 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,20,0)="report is consistent with the AP-1 report, and shows the correct allergy "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,21,0)="and adverse reaction information for the patient."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,23,0)="The third Action Profile Report issue was logged because one-time orders "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,24,0)="are appearing on the Action Profile-1 [PSJU AP-1]  and Action Profile-2 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,25,0)="[PSJU AP-2] reports with the option available to the provider to RENEW "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,26,0)="the orders.  The ability to renew one-time orders was removed due to a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,27,0)="patient safety issue.  Having the renew option available to the provider "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,28,0)="could lead to a reoccurrence of the patient safety issue."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,30,0)="The Undefined Variable Error occurs with the Patient Profile, [PSJU PR].  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,31,0)="When attempting to filter the profile at any WARD prompt, if the user "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,32,0)="presses ENTER or the up-carat (^), instead of being taken to the previous "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,33,0)="filter choices or the main menu, the user is taken to a prompt to filter "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,34,0)="by Room/Bed or Patient.  If the user again presses ENTER or ^, an "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",164,1,35,0)="undefined variable error occurs."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",165,0)="188 SEQ #166^3070904.235911^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",165,1,0)="^^9^9^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",165,1,1,0)="User reported that when they edited the Schedule from a ""continuous Type"" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",165,1,2,0)="to a one-time type, the Schedule type remained ""continuous"".  This caused"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",165,1,3,0)="BCMA to not display the order on the Missed Medications Report."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",165,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",165,1,5,0)="It was also found during the internal testing of this patch, it was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",165,1,6,0)="noticed that the ""administration times"" could be automatically updated"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",165,1,7,0)="based on the Schedule being entered. While this logic is correct, it did"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",165,1,8,0)="not display the ""highlighting"" of the administration times as is the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",165,1,9,0)="standard when a field is changed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,0)="180 SEQ #167^3070905.000208^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,0)="^^25^25^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one Patient Safety Issue contained in one Remedy "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,2,0)="ticket."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,4,0)="PSI 06 066"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,5,0)="This addresses Remedy ticket HD146661."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,7,0)="The site reported an issue that if they used a leading zero for the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,8,0)="limit/duration of an IV, in this case 0.5L, the stop date calculated for "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,9,0)="the order was 6 minutes after the start date/time.  CPRS has addressed "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,10,0)="this on their end with patch OR*3*254.  Because of the CPRS fix, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,11,0)="Inpatient Meds should never receive an invalid duration/limit from CPRS.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,12,0)="However, it was discussed with the Inpatient Meds workgroup, and they "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,13,0)="agreed that Inpatient Meds should make a contingency plan fix just in "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,14,0)="case some future CPRS project removes the fixes in place from OR*3*254.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,15,0)="As a result, Inpatient Meds will now be able to handle an invalid "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,16,0)="duration/limit should one ever be received from CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,18,0)="The fix agreed upon by the Inpatient Meds workgroup will do three "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,19,0)="things.  First, it will NOT allow the pharmacist to FINISH the order.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,20,0)="Second, the duration/limit field displayed to the pharmacist will read "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,21,0)="*INVALID DURATION/LIMIT*.  Third, the Stop Date for the order will read "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,22,0)="""CANNOT CALCULATE""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,24,0)="OR*3*254 is an independent CPRS patch, and is not required for this "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",166,1,25,0)="Inpatient Meds patch."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,0)="120 SEQ #168^3070905.001801^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,0)="^^17^17^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,1,0)="1. A site reported a problem with the new duration field that was added to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,2,0)="CPRS GUI v25. In response to a patient safety issue, this field was added "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,3,0)="to the IV Fluid order dialog. In addition, Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,4,0)="was modified to always have the duration field be used for the stop date "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,5,0)="calculation. This has caused problems in sites where they have policies "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,6,0)="that say certain medications can only be written for a certain period of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,7,0)="time. This patch corrects this problem by modifying Inpatient Medications "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,8,0)="V. 5.0 to consider the duration the same way as all other stop date "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,9,0)="parameters, rather than as an override."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,11,0)="In order to assist in communications with the provider, an alert will be "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,12,0)="sent to the ordering provider whenever the duration they entered is not "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,13,0)="used to calculate the stop date of the order. HD0000000111592"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,15,0)="2. Several sites reported an error occuring when entering an IV order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,16,0)="that contained an allergy order-check. This patch corrects this problem. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",167,1,17,0)="HD0000000186397, HD0000000187239, HD0000000187452, HD0000000187507."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,0)="145 SEQ #169^3070905.012058^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,0)="^^60^60^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,2,0)="1. Sites reported that location designation for inpatients who received "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,3,0)="orders in a clinic was incorrect. In some cases the clinic location was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,4,0)="overwriting the ward location designation. In many instances an error "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,5,0)="appeared in the routine PSGMAR1 for printing the 24 hr MAR."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,7,0)="This patch corrects this issue by adding new prompts to aid in printing "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,8,0)="out orders for both ward locations and clinics. No location designations "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,9,0)="are overwritten. When printing by Ward Group/Patient, or by Ward/Patient, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,10,0)="all orders for a patient are grouped together by the patient's name"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,11,0)="regardless of location. HD84581, HD94525, HD94701, HD94753,HD94951, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,12,0)="HD9500, HD95644, HD96287, HD97627, HD99007, HD101172, HD121955,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,13,0)="HD127037, HD130450, HD133140, HD133726, HD151842, HD152395, HD152987,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,14,0)="HD153754, HD154263, HD155098, HD155822, HD157154, HD166444, HD176045, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,15,0)="HD181032, HD181254, HD184077  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,17,0)="The following prompts are included when printing by Ward, Ward Group, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,18,0)="Clinic, or Clinic Group."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,20,0)="Select by GROUP (G), WARD (W), CLINIC (C), or PATIENT (P): WARD"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,21,0)="Include Clinic Orders? Y/N"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,22,0)="If Yes is selected, both ward and clinic orders are printed for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,23,0)="patients on a ward."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,24,0)="If No is selected, only the ward orders are printed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,26,0)="Select by GROUP (G), WARD (W), CLINIC (C), or PATIENT (P): GROUP"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,27,0)="Select by WARD GROUP (W) or CLINIC GROUP (C): WARD"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,28,0)="Include Clinic Orders? Y/N"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,29,0)="If Yes is selected, both ward and clinic orders are printed for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,30,0)="patients in a Ward Group."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,31,0)="If No is selected, only the ward orders are printed for patients in a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,32,0)="Ward Group."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,34,0)="Select by GROUP (G), WARD (W), CLINIC (C), or PATIENT (P): CLINIC"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,35,0)="Include Ward Orders? Y/N"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,36,0)="If Yes is selected, both clinic and ward orders are printed for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,37,0)="patients in a clinic."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,38,0)="If No is selected, only the clinic orders are printed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,40,0)="Select by GROUP (G), WARD (W), CLINIC (C), or PATIENT (P): GROUP"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,41,0)="Select by WARD GROUP (W) or CLINIC GROUP (C): CLINIC"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,42,0)="Include Ward Orders? Y/N"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,43,0)="If Yes is selected, both clinic and ward orders are printed for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,44,0)="patients in a Clinic Group."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,45,0)="If No is selected, only the clinic orders are printed for patients in a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,46,0)="Clinic Group."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,49,0)="2. After the installation of PSJ*5.0*111 and PSJ*5.0*131, the formatting "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,50,0)="on the MAR reports was adversely affected. Sites reported pagination was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,51,0)="off, pages displayed too much empty space, and the signature block no "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,52,0)="longer appeared at the bottom of each page."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,54,0)="Code modifications have been made in the MAR routines to correct the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,55,0)="formatting problems. Page numbering has been corrected.  The signature "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,56,0)="block prints at the end of each page. Pending orders, non-clinic and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,57,0)="clinic orders will display in the correct location on"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,58,0)="the MAR report. Orders with a stop date/time greater than or equal to the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,59,0)="selected 24 Hour MAR start date/time will print out correctly. HD94303, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",168,1,60,0)="HD94836, HD95397, HD97108, HD107645, HD114937, PSI-06-002"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",169,0)="189 SEQ #170^3070905.012249^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",169,1,0)="^^6^6^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",169,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",169,1,2,0)="This patch will correct an error which can occur for any IV Drug order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",169,1,3,0)="type which uses an Administration Schedule but the Administration Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",169,1,4,0)="used does not have a Package Prefix = 'PSJ'.  The error occurs when a user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",169,1,5,0)="attempts to view the Long profile of the order in PSJ OE [Inpatient Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",169,1,6,0)="Entry]."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,0)="159 SEQ #171^3070905.012444^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,0)="^^26^26^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,1,0)="1. A site reported a problem with the medication route being blank on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,2,0)="Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) V. 3.0 Virtual Due List. During"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,3,0)="investigation of possible corrections for this, it was determined that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,4,0)="another issue needed to be addressed with how to determine when to prompt"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,5,0)="for an injection site."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,7,0)="This patch assists to correct these problems by adding two new items to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,8,0)="the Application Programming Interface (API) from Inpatient Medications V. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,9,0)="5.0 to BCMA. The NAME field (.01) as well as the PROMPT FOR INJ. SITE IN "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,10,0)="BCMA field (#8) from the MEDICATION ROUTE file (#51.2) will now be sent in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,11,0)="the API. HD0000000166204, HD0000000164890, PSI-06-152, PSI-06-158"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,13,0)="2. In support of the BCMA V. 3.0 project BCMA HSC-III, two changes are "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,14,0)="required to the APIs that supply information to BCMA. First, the flag "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,15,0)="information for both Unit Dose and IV orders has been added to both the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,16,0)="summary and detail APIs. Second, an indicator has been added that will "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,17,0)="tell BCMA that this order would have triggered a notification to the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,18,0)="STAT/NOW mail group."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,20,0)="3. During testing of the BCMA V. 3.0 project BCMA HSC-III, a problem was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,21,0)="discovered with the API that determines if an order should trigger a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,22,0)="notification to the STAT/NOW mail group. If the parameter which controls "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,23,0)="the trigger was not defined, all orders would be flagged. This patch "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,24,0)="corrects this problem. However, it is important to note that if the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,25,0)="parameter PRIORITIES FOR ACTIVE NOTIFY is not defined, no order will be "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",170,1,26,0)="flagged as stat for the purposes of BCMA."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",171,0)="192 SEQ #172^3071212.212226^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",171,1,0)="^^3^3^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",171,1,1,0)="Site reported that the incorrect Orderable Item was selected when the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",171,1,2,0)="entry was entered in ""lowercase"".  This caused the incorrect medication"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",171,1,3,0)="to be given."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,0)="195 SEQ #173^3071212.212256^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,0)="^^13^13^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,1,0)="This patch will provide a temporary fix as detailed in Patient safety "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,2,0)="issue PSI-07-075 for BCMA.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,4,0)="When using the CPRS Med Order Button (MOB), it was discovered that certain"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,5,0)="hardware configurations allow a ""virtual"" IP address.  This causes a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,6,0)="single user to be logged into two physical nodes simultaneously.  When"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,7,0)="this happens, the order placed in CPRS MOB cannot be filed.  The user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,8,0)="receives an error box which states ""Missing data, unable to file.""  The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,9,0)="order does not show up on the VDL. It was determined that there is risk of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,10,0)="duplication when the order does not file."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,12,0)="This patch will modify the error message to make it more noticeable and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",172,1,13,0)="robust."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,0)="175 SEQ #174^3071212.215333^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,0)="^^21^21^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,1,0)="Current functionality concerning the duplicate order checks displays all"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,2,0)="duplicate drug and duplicate drug class orders found, but does not allow"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,3,0)="the user to select these for discontinuation. If the user wishes to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,4,0)="discontinue any of the presented duplicates, they must wait until after"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,5,0)="they are done with the current order process in which the duplicate order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,6,0)="checks presented their results. The major functionality change to the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,7,0)="Inpatient Medications software will consist of allowing users to select"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,8,0)="for discontinuation any duplicate Inpatient orders found, at the time"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,9,0)="these duplicates are presented by the duplicate order checks.  In"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,10,0)="addition, all duplicate Outpatient orders found, are grouped together and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,11,0)="displayed prior to all other order check results and will be used for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,12,0)="information purposes only. The current process will be modified so that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,13,0)="when a duplicate order check is performed, the duplicate Inpatient orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,14,0)="are displayed in a numbered list. The user will then be prompted to select"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,15,0)="which, if any, of the listed duplicate orders should be discontinued. The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,16,0)="user may choose to select none, thus leaving all orders intact. The "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,17,0)="results from both duplicate order checks, Duplicate Drug and Duplicate"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,18,0)="Drug Class, will be presented together. Duplicate order checks occur at"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,19,0)="several points in the ordering process, including, when entering a new"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,20,0)="medication order, when renewing an existing medication order, when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",173,1,21,0)="finishing an order, and when editing an order's drug."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,0)="148 SEQ #175^3071212.220432^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,0)="^^40^40^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,1,0)="A site reported a problem with renewed pending orders.  The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,2,0)="Pharmacist's User Manual states:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,3,0)="""When the SAME STOP DATE ON ALL ORDERS parameter is set to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,4,0)="yes, the module will assign a default stop date for each patient. This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,5,0)="date is initially set when the first order is entered for the patient. A"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,6,0)="new default stop date is assigned for the patient when an order is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,7,0)="renewed and the order's stop date plus three days is greater than the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,8,0)="current default stop date. This date is shown as the default value for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,9,0)="the stop date of each order entered for the patient. However, if a day or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,10,0)="dose limit exists for the selected Orderable Item, and the limit is less"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,11,0)="than the default stop date, the earlier stop date and time will be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,12,0)="displayed."""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,14,0)="The way the screen defaults in pharmacy for finishing would lead the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,15,0)="pharmacist to finish the new order prior to finishing the renewals."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,16,0)="This creates the potential for medication orders to default to an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,17,0)="""incorrect"" stop date/time. This problem caused a patient to completely"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,18,0)="miss receiving a newly ordered medication, as the new order expired prior"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,19,0)="to the first scheduled dose time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,21,0)="The following example shows the way the screen displays the orders from"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,22,0)="the PENDING/NON-VERIFIED option:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,24,0)="- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - A C T I V E - - - - - - - - - - - - - -"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,25,0)="   1    MULTIVITAMINS TAB                   C  04/01  04/08  R"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,26,0)="          Give: 1 TABLET PO QAM (07)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,27,0)=" - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -  P E N D I N G  - - - - - - - - - - - -"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,28,0)="   2    CAPTOPRIL TAB                         ?  *****  *****"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,29,0)="        Give: 25MG PO QAM (07)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,30,0)=" - - - - - - - - - - - - P E N D I N G   R E N E W A L S - - - - - - - -"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,31,0)="   3    MULTIVITAMINS TAB                   ?  *****  *****  P 04/06"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,32,0)="          Give: 1 TABLET PO QAM (07)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,36,0)="This patch corrects the problem by reversing the order in which the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,37,0)="PENDING and PENDING RENEWALS are displayed.  With the entries reversed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,38,0)="the user will finish the PENDING RENEWAL order first, followed by the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,39,0)="PENDING order, and the correct stop date/time will be displayed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",174,1,40,0)="HD0000000138249, PSI-06-043"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",175,0)="173 SEQ #176^3071212.221911^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",175,1,0)="^^11^11^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",175,1,1,0)="During testing of the Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) project "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",175,1,2,0)="BCMA-HSC Phase III, an issue was discovered with the order flag comments "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",175,1,3,0)="for unit dose orders. There is not enough space to store the entire "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",175,1,4,0)="comment, so the text is truncated. This patch corrects this problem for "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",175,1,5,0)="BCMA by storing the most recent text in an additional location. The "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",175,1,6,0)="comment will still be stored in the current location. It will also be in "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",175,1,7,0)="the MOST RECEMT FLAG COMMENT field (#129) of the NON-VERIFIED/PENDING file"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",175,1,8,0)="(#53.1) which is exported in this patch. For active unit dose orders, it"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",175,1,9,0)="will be stored in the MOST RECENT FLAG COMMENT field (#128) of the UNIT"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",175,1,10,0)="DOSE sub-file (#55.06) of the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) which will be "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",175,1,11,0)="exported in a Pharmacy Data Management V1.0 patch."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",176,0)="201 SEQ #177^3080203.211113^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",176,1,0)="^^1^1^3080203"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",176,1,1,0)="Remove all PSJ*5*175 changes."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",177,0)="191 SEQ #178^3080203.213328^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",177,1,0)="^^3^3^3080203"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",177,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",177,1,2,0)="This patch will correct 2 problems and remove 1 obsolete menu option "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",177,1,3,0)="within the Inpatient Medications package."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",178,0)="185 SEQ #179^3080722.075436^1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",178,1,0)="^^8^8^3080722"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",178,1,1,0)="When an order from CPRS is processed in the Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",178,1,2,0)="application the Comments field is automatically checked to verify that it"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",178,1,3,0)="does not contain multiple spaces.  If it does, the software will remove"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",178,1,4,0)="these spaces.  When this happens, a Change Action is generated in CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",178,1,5,0)="This Change Action will cause CPRS to recalculate the Instructions. In"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",178,1,6,0)="some cases, the recalculation of the Instructions will result in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",178,1,7,0)="strength being added to the instuctions. This may result in the patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",178,1,8,0)="receiving an incorrect dose."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,0)="134^3090421.155113^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,0)="^^81^81^3090421"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,1,0)="This patch contains changes in support of Computerized Patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,2,0)="Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0 GUI v27 release."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,4,0)="1.  MEDICATION ROUTE CHANGES"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,5,0)="----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,6,0)="- Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 will use the medication route received from"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,7,0)="  CPRS V. 1.0 as the default when finishing an IV order entered via CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,8,0)="  V. 1.0. For new orders entered via Inpatient Medications V. 5.0, if all"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,9,0)="  of the orderable items associated with an order contain the same default"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,10,0)="  medication route, that route will be used as the default. If there are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,11,0)="  any differences, there will be no default medication route."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,13,0)="- Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 will send to BCMA V. 3.0 the full"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,14,0)="  medication route name for display on the Virtual Due List (VDL)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,16,0)="2.  INFUSION RATE CHANGES"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,17,0)="-------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,18,0)="- Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 now accepts infusion rate from CPRS in both"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,19,0)="  ml/hour and as 'infuse over time'."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,21,0)="- In the order view screen for an order with an intermittent IV type, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,22,0)="  infusion rate now displays as ""Infuse Over"" followed by the time. For"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,23,0)="  example, ""Infuse Over 30 minutes""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,25,0)="  The infusion rate for an intermittent IV order can be null."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,27,0)="3.  IV TYPE CHANGES"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,28,0)="-------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,29,0)="- Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 shall accept an IV type of ""I"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,30,0)="  (Intermittent) or ""C"" (Continuous) from CPRS V. 1.0.  When an IV type of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,31,0)="  CONTINUOUS is received, Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 defaults to an IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,32,0)="  type of Admixture.  When IV type of INTERMITTENT is received, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,33,0)="  Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 defaults to an IV type of Piggyback."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,34,0)="  Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 sends to CPRS V. 1.0 updates to an order's"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,35,0)="  IV type."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,37,0)="- Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 now accepts schedule information from"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,38,0)="  CPRS V. 1.0 for intermittent IV orders entered via the IV Fluid"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,39,0)="  Ordering Dialog.  Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 also sends to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,40,0)="  CPRS V. 1.0 any schedule changes for intermittent IV orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,42,0)="- A new field, IV TYPE CATEGORY (#128) is being added to the NON-"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,43,0)="  VERIFIED ORDERS file (#53.1).  The IV TYPE CATEGORY will be ""C"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,44,0)="  (Continuous) for orders with an IV TYPE of Admixture, Hyperal,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,45,0)="  Non-Intermittent Syringe, or Chemotherapy with a CHEMOTHERAPY TYPE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,46,0)="  of Admixture, Hyperal, or Non-Intermittent Syringe.  The IV TYPE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,47,0)="  CATEGORY will be ""I"" (Intermittent) for orders with an IV TYPE of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,48,0)="  Piggyback, Intermittent Syringe, or Chemotherapy with a CHEMOTHERAPY"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,49,0)="  TYPE of Piggyback or Intermittent Syringe."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,51,0)="4.  RENEWED ORDER CHANGES"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,52,0)="-------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,53,0)="- When discontinuing pending renewal orders, Inpatient Medications V. 5.0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,54,0)="  will provide the user an option to discontinue the pending renewal"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,55,0)="  order and/or the original orders.  The pharmacist shall be given the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,56,0)="  option to discontinue the pending order, both orders, or exit the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,57,0)="  discontinue function."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,59,0)="5.  REMOVE CALLS TO OBSOLETE ROUTINE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,60,0)="------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,61,0)="- At the request of CPRS V. 1.0, active calls to obsolete routine OR3CONV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,62,0)="  have been removed from Inpatient Medications V. 5.0. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,64,0)="6.  EXPECTED FIRST DOSE FOR ONE-TIME ORDERS (HD 98365)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,65,0)="------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,66,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,67,0)="   During testing of the CPRS V. 1.0 GUI v26 release, sites reported a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,68,0)="   problem with an incorrect display of expected first dose for orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,69,0)="   with a schedule type of ""ONE TIME""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,70,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,71,0)="   If the schedule type is ""ONE TIME"", do not display an Expected"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,72,0)="   First Dose for the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,74,0)="7.  CORRECT ABBREVIATION OF MILLIMOLE (HD 145562)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,75,0)="-------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,76,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,77,0)="   The correct abbreviation for the word MILLIMOLE, which is MMOL"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,78,0)="   is not available in the system."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,79,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,80,0)="   The abbreviation for Millimole, ""MMOL"", will be included in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",179,1,81,0)="   this patch."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",180,0)="204 SEQ #181^3090421.16014^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",180,1,0)="^^2^2^3090421"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",180,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one Patient Safety Issue, PSI-08-008 for remedy "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",180,1,2,0)="ticket HD228442."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,0)="203 SEQ #182^3090421.162039^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,0)="^^43^43^3090421"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,1,0)="This patch corrects the typographical error in 2 routines within "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,2,0)="Inpatient Medication package, and the calculation of IV labels when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,3,0)="infusion rate is less than 10ml/hr"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,5,0)="This patch addresses the following Remedy ticket(s):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,6,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,7,0)="HD219677        (Original)      Potential typographical error."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,8,0)="HD234014        (Original)      IV ADMIX rate under 10ml/hr calculates "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,9,0)="                        bags wrong"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,11,0)="Overview of Remedy ticket(s):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,12,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,13,0)="HD219677:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,14,0)="There is typographical error in line tag ENHEAD+21^PSJHEAD and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,15,0)="H1+15^PSGCAPP0  that should be a plus sign instead of underscore."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,17,0)="HD234014:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,18,0)="When an IV Admixture has a rate of less than 10ml/hr the calculation of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,19,0)="bags needed till the next scheduled IV batch run is inaccurate."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,21,0)="Problem (219677)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,22,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,23,0)="There is typographical error in line tag ENHEAD+21^PSJHEAD and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,24,0)="H1+15^PSGCAPP0.  It should be a plus sign instead of underscore"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,26,0)="Resolution (219677)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,27,0)="This does appear to be a typographical error, it would never result in a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,28,0)="functional defect. EN+3^PSJHEAD and H1+15^PSGCAPP0 is modified to replace "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,29,0)="the underscore (""_"") with a plus sign (""+"").  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,31,0)="Problem (234014)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,32,0)="------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,33,0)="If the infusion rate is less than 10ml/hr the number of IV bags needed is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,34,0)="calculated incorrectly."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,37,0)="Resolution (234014)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,38,0)="The pattern match for infusion rate in line tag EN+3^PSIVORE is looking "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,39,0)="for at least 1 digit, with a period as optional and at least 1 digit "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,40,0)="after the period. This only works if the infusion rate is 2 digit or "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,41,0)="more.  The pattern match in EN+3^PSIVORE is modified to make the digit "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,42,0)="after the period as optional so the pattern match can also be used when "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",181,1,43,0)="the infusion rate is a single digit."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",182,0)="209 SEQ #183^3090422.120906^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",182,1,0)="^^3^3^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",182,1,1,0)="This patch Will correct the following Remedy tickets."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",182,1,2,0)="HD245298 - PSI-08-060 - 1 IV order retaining original Duration/Total "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",182,1,3,0)="Volume"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,0)="197 SEQ #184^3090422.130203^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,0)="^^20^20^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,1,0)="This patch resolves two issues in the Inpatient Medications package."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,3,0)="1. When stat medications are ordered using Inpatient Medications for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,4,0)="Outpatients (IMO), the resulting notification email lacked the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,5,0)="name of the clinic. Ward names were included correctly. Clinic names"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,6,0)="were added. The mail group receiving the notification is PSJ STAT NOW"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,7,0)="ACTIVE or PSJ STAT NOW PENDING."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,9,0)="The routines PSJHL4 and PSJHL4A were modified to establish a value for CLINIC"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,10,0)="if the location is a clinic, and then set using the same variable as ward."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,12,0)="2. After the release of Patch PSJ*5*110, MAR labels do include the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,13,0)="order/renewal date on the left side of the label, which is attached"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,14,0)="to the MAR. It only appears on the right side, which is discarded."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,15,0)="The date has been placed on left side as well as the right side."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,16,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,17,0)="Routine PSGLOI was modified to correct this problem. If the order is not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,18,0)="pending, the order/renewal date is set at the left hand side of the label."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,19,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",183,1,20,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",184,0)="210^3090422.152306^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",184,1,0)="^^1^1^3090422"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",184,1,1,0)="This patch allows the DSS IV extract to be recreated."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",185,0)="198 SEQ #186^3090423.11283^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",185,1,0)="^^11^11^3090423"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",185,1,1,0)="DESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",185,1,2,0)="============"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",185,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",185,1,4,0)="This patch addresses the following Remedy Ticket(s):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",185,1,5,0)="----------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",185,1,6,0)="HD200323 - <UNDEFINED>COPY+10^PSIVOD"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",185,1,7,0)="HD193154 - Inappropriate Remote Order Check message"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",185,1,8,0)="HD211655 - Nurse finishes order and its active "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",185,1,9,0)="HD216471 - Renew single order routine setting the wrong node for the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",185,1,10,0)="           PSGRFOUR variable"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",185,1,11,0)="HD210106 - Meds on extended profile do not match CPRS orders tab."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",186,0)="220 SEQ #187^3090423.114645^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",186,1,0)="^^1^1^3090423"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",186,1,1,0)="This Patch will disable the SPEED FINISH and SPEED VERIFY protocols."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",187,0)="196 SEQ #188^3090423.123643^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",187,1,0)="^^7^7^3090423"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",187,1,1,0)="This patch will correct the following tickets:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",187,1,2,0)="HD0000000193031 - Incorrect diet information on MAR header"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",187,1,3,0)="HD0000000169943 - Clinic Group not showing up on Non Verified/Pending "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",187,1,4,0)="                  report"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",187,1,5,0)="HD0000000258201 - 6 IV REPORT DIFFERENT FOR LOWER CASE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",187,1,6,0)="HD0000000225877 - IV duration on CPRS order not calculated correctly as "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",187,1,7,0)="                  stop date"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,0)="213 SEQ #189^3090423.134629^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,0)="^^108^108^3090423"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,1,0)="Description:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,2,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,4,0)="This patch contains four Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 fixes that sites"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,5,0)="logged during the compliance date period for the CPRS (Computerized "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,6,0)="Patient Record System) GUI v27 release."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,9,0)="1. The first issue, Remedy Ticket HD280022, pertains to Day of Week"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,10,0)="schedules entered for IV Piggyback orders via the CPRS IV Fluids Dialog."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,11,0)="If the user creates a schedule using the schedule builder, and uses the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,12,0)="new format of Day of Week@Schedule (example: MO-WE-FR@BID), and if the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,13,0)="root schedule (MO-WE-FR) exists in the ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE File "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,14,0)="(#51.1), when the order is viewed in backdoor pharmacy, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,15,0)="administration time(s) for the order will be null."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,17,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,18,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,19,0)="Admin times are null if a Day of Week schedule created via the schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,20,0)="builder in CPRS exists in the ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE File (#51.1)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,22,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,23,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,24,0)="In PSGS0, do not QUIT before the admin times are set if the schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,25,0)="is a Day of Week schedule, even if it exists in the schedule file."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,28,0)="2. The second issue, Remedy Ticket HD246438 and its duplicates, is also "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,29,0)="logged as Patient Safety Issue PSI-08-068,PSPO #782.  This is an issue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,30,0)="with an invalid frequency for IV Piggyback orders.  This issue has existed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,31,0)="prior to the release of CPRS GUI v27, but the sites are reporting an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,32,0)="increase in the occurrence of the problem after the install of CPRS GUI "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,33,0)="v27. For unknown reasons, the frequency of some IV Piggyback orders is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,34,0)="null when it should contain a value."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,36,0)="No site or developer has been able to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,37,0)="reproduce this issue at-will, and there does not appear to be any"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,38,0)="pattern to the processes or procedures that precede the occurrence of this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,39,0)="problem. With this patch, if the frequency for an IV Piggyback order is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,40,0)="null, and it should contain a value, the code will attempt to directly"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,41,0)="set an appropriate frequency into the PHARMACY PATIENT File (#55) upon"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,42,0)="verification of the order, and upon the order becoming active."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,44,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,45,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,46,0)="The frequency is being set to null very sporadically for IV Piggyback"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,47,0)="orders.  No root cause is known."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,49,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,50,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,51,0)="During the verification process, if the IV is intermittent, and the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,52,0)="frequency is null, attempt to re-set the frequency based on the name"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,53,0)="of the schedule as well as other variables that should"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,54,0)="contain the value of the frequency.  These changes are in routine "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,55,0)="PSIVORFB."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,57,0)="3. The third issue, Remedy Ticket HD274682 and its duplicates, is an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,58,0)="undefined variable error in the new Meds Tab sort for CPRS.  The root"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,59,0)="cause of the problem is that a pointer to the PHARMACY ORDERABLE ITEM File"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,60,0)="(#50.7) is missing in either the NON-VERIFIED ORDERS File (#53.1) or the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,61,0)="PHARMACY PATIENT File (#55).  Because the pointer does not exist, when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,62,0)="a temporary global is being built to display the orders for the patient, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,63,0)="an undefined variable error occurs."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,66,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,67,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,68,0)="Very old orders exist in the system that do not contain a pointer to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,69,0)="the orderable item.  When the new Meds Tab sort routines attempt to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,70,0)="use the pointer value as a subscript in a ^TMP global setting, and the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,71,0)="pointer's value is null, a null subscript error occurs.  This causes"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,72,0)="a hard error in CPRS and shuts CPRS down."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,74,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,75,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,76,0)="If the pointer to the orderable item does not exist, the routines will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,77,0)="use the phrase ""Orderable Item Not Found"" as the subscript value in place"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,78,0)="of what should be the name of the orderable item.  This allows the Meds"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,79,0)="Tab sort routines to process without error, and the patient's medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,80,0)="appear without problems on the CPRS Meds tab.  The updated routines are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,81,0)="PSJORRO, PSJORRN, and PSJORRN1."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,83,0)="4. The fourth issue addressed by this patch is Remedy Ticket HD280040, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,84,0)="which deals with an inconsistency between CPRS and backdoor pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,85,0)="with respect to continuous IV orders. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,87,0)="If the IV order originates from CPRS, a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,88,0)="fractional infusion rate of < 1 ml/hr (0.9 ml/hr for example), backdoor"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,89,0)="pharmacy allows the infusion rate, and the order can be finished and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,90,0)="verified without issue.  However, if the order originates from backdoor"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,91,0)="pharmacy, a fractional infusion rate < 1 ml/hr is not accepted, and the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,92,0)="user is presented a message ""Invalid Infusion Rate"", and they cannot"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,93,0)="finish and verify the order.  This patch will make backdoor pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,94,0)="behave consistently with CPRS."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,96,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,97,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,98,0)="If an order is entered via backdoor pharmacy for a continuous IV, and the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,99,0)="order is created with a fractional infusion rate of < 1 ml/hr, the system"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,100,0)="presents the user with the error message, ""Your infusion rate is in an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,101,0)="invalid format"", and the order cannot be completed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,102,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,103,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,104,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,105,0)="If the order has a fractional infusion rate < 1 ml/hr, the order must"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,106,0)="contain a leading zero, and the system will view the infusion rate as"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,107,0)="valid.  (example - infusion rate must be 0.9 ml/hr to be valid)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",188,1,108,0)="The coding will affect routines PSIVSP, PSIVCHK, and PSIVORE."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",189,0)="208 SEQ #190^3090623.1037^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",189,1,0)="^^4^4^3090623"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",189,1,1,0)="This PSI patch addresses the following problem(s):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",189,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",189,1,3,0)="When a lab order is entered in CPRS with only a date in the Collection "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",189,1,4,0)="Date/Time, the midnight draw times do not display."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",190,0)="221 SEQ #191^3090708.145553^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",190,1,0)="^^8^8^3090708"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",190,1,1,0)="This is part 2 of the Frequency correction. This patch will re-enable "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",190,1,2,0)="PSJU LM SPEED FINISH and PSJU LM SPEED VERIFY."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",190,1,3,0)="and correct the following tickets."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",190,1,4,0)=" PSPO# 1221 HD297810 - 1 Orders did not show in BCMA."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",190,1,5,0)=" d - HD289777 - 4    Q14 coming up to be given every 2 days for one order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",190,1,6,0)=" d - HD289086 - 6 BCMA -Order Problem  Schedule Frequency Issue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",190,1,7,0)=" PSPO# 1274 HD302185 - 1 Possible patient safety issue with med order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",190,1,8,0)=" PSPO# 1278 HD302727 - 1 Bar Code Med Admin issue - Admin Times"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,0)="161^3090714.15213^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,0)="^^37^37^3090714"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,1,0)="                             I M P O R T A N T"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,3,0)="*************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,4,0)=" This Inpatient Medications patch PSJ*5*161 along with PSU*4*5, PSO*7*170"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,5,0)=" and DG*5.3*671 is being released in a single KIDS software distribution "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,6,0)=" host file, PSU_4_P5.KID as part of the Pharmacy Benefits Management (PBM)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,7,0)=" Extracts Enhancement #3 project. PSS*1*99 which is also part of this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,8,0)=" enhancement is being released separately."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,10,0)=" This patch description includes only the informational portion of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,11,0)=" PSJ*5*161. Please refer to the ""Software Retrieval Instructions"" and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,12,0)=" ""Installation Instructions"" sections of the PSU*4*5 patch description"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,13,0)="for instructions on how to  acquire and install the patch software."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,15,0)="*************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,17,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,18,0)="       ********************* WARNING *********************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,19,0)="       *****************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,20,0)="     If your facility has the Pyxis/Omnicell/McKesson interface "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,21,0)="     from ILC this patch will overwrite any ""local"" modifications "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,22,0)="     in routine PSGOETO. This could affect certain orders being "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,23,0)="     sent across this interface.  The modifications will have to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,24,0)="     be reintroduced following installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,25,0)="       *****************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,26,0)="       *****************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,29,0)="This patch addresses a request which supports the Pharmacy Benefits"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,30,0)="Management (PBM) Extracts Enhancement #3 project. In order to allow the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,31,0)="retransmission of only those patients who have had demographic updates,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,32,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0, Inpatient Medications V. 5.0, Registration"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,33,0)="v. 5.3 and Pharmacy Data Management V. 1.0 were modified to build an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,34,0)="entry for re-transmission in PBM PATIENT DEMOGRAPHICS File #59.9."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,36,0)="Whenever the FIRST SERVICE DATE field (#.07) in the PHARMACY PATIENT "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",191,1,37,0)="file #55 is updated for a patient, an entry is queued for retransmission."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",192,0)="193 SEQ #193^3090928.152826^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",192,1,0)="^^4^4^3090928"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",192,1,1,0)="This patch wil  resolve the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",192,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",192,1,3,0)="1) CPRS displayed -1 in the Start and Stop times of the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",192,1,4,0)="2) Subscript error in the missed mediciton report   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",193,0)="207 SEQ #194^3091006.143538^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",193,1,0)="^^1^1^3091006"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",193,1,1,0)="Order Checks During Order Edits"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,0)="215 SEQ #195^3091026.120731^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,0)="^^30^30^3091026"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,1,0)="This patch contains a partial resolution for Patient Safety Issue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,2,0)="PSI 07-073, PSPO #526, and is outlined in Remedy Ticket HD67749."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,3,0)="Another portion of this PSI is being addressed by the Vista"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,4,0)="Maintenance Team in a separate patch, PSJ*5.0*216."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,6,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,7,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,8,0)="If the pharmacist must edit the dispense drug(s) for an active"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,9,0)="Unit Dose order, there is currently no entry made in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,10,0)="Activity Log for the order that reflects this change.  Medication"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,11,0)="errors have happened due to edited dispense drugs, and there is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,12,0)="currently no audit trail to help track the information."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,14,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,15,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,16,0)="This enhancement will compare the original dispense drug(s) for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,17,0)="the order with the edited value for the dispense drug(s).  If"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,18,0)="there is a difference between the values, the modified code in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,19,0)="routine PSGOE92 will call the routine that logs entries into the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,20,0)="Activity Log for the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,22,0)="The structure for the activity log entry will be:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,23,0)="DATE^DUZ^6000^FIELD^OLD"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,25,0)="DATE  =  Timestamp date/time of the edit."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,26,0)="DUZ   =  The system DUZ of the person making the edit."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,27,0)="6000  =  A code denoting that a field was edited."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,28,0)="FIELD =  The name of the field that was edited."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,29,0)="OLD   =  Old data before the field was edited.  This contains the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",194,1,30,0)="         dispense drug IEN, dispense drug name, and units per dose."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,0)="184 SEQ #196^3091109.11251^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,0)="^^32^32^3091109"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,1,0)=" HD0000000139263 involves multiple additives with values in the MESSAGE "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,2,0)=" field (#14) of the IV ADDITIVES file (#52.6).  When an IV label "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,3,0)=" prints, and the IV order contains multiple additives, if more than one "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,4,0)=" additive has a MESSAGE field value, only the message of the first "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,5,0)=" additive in the IV order will display on the label.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,7,0)=" HD0000000139800 The CPRS Unit Dose report shows the status of the unit "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,8,0)=" dose orders for a given patient.  If an order has the status "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,9,0)=" ""Discontinued due to Edit"", nothing is displaying in the CPRS Unit "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,10,0)=" Dose report's status field.  The problem is due to Inpatient Meds not "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,11,0)=" sending CPRS the complete information for the status if the order was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,12,0)=" discontinued due to edit."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,13,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,14,0)=" HD0000000159948 Within Parameters Edit Menu [PSJ PARAM EDIT MENU], the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,15,0)=" option Clinic Definition [PSJ CD] asks the user for a CLINIC GROUP "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,16,0)=" NAME.  This prompt is in error and the option should end if no new "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,17,0)=" clinic is chosen for edit.   This issue has no negative impact on the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,18,0)=" patient but is an inconvenience to the user of the option."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,19,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,20,0)=" HD0000000168525 When exiting the option by typing an ""^"" up-arrow at the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,21,0)=" Report/Label device prompt in Site Parameters (IV) [PSJI SITE PARAMETERS]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,22,0)=" option, the system will default ""TELNET"" into the field even though a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,23,0)=" value already exists. The software should retain the existing "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,24,0)=" report/label device at this prompt and not change the default device.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,25,0)=" This issue has caused the user to print reports and labels to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,26,0)=" unintended devices."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,27,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,28,0)=" HD0000000175185 concerns the Pick List Warning Message.  A user created "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,29,0)=" a pick list with a stop date which was far into the future.  This made "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,30,0)=" the pick list inaccessible, and the list could not be deleted.  A "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,31,0)=" warning message will be displayed to the pharmacist if the pick list "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",195,1,32,0)=" stop date is more than 7 days into the future."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,0)="190 SEQ #197^3091109.112521^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,0)="^^24^24^3091109"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one Patient Safety Issue, PSI 06 101, contained"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,2,0)="in two Remedy tickets: HD153724 and HD166076."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,4,0)="This patch constitutes the Inpatient Pharmacy portion of a multi-package"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,5,0)="build. It addresses Remedy ticket HD153724. The BCMA patch PSB*3*33"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,6,0)="addresses the BCMA portion, Remedy ticket HD166076."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,8,0)="The site reported Unit Dose medication orders entered with a schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,9,0)="of ONE TIME PRN were not automatically discontinued after being"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,10,0)="given in Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) Version 3.0. As a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,11,0)="result, the medication was given multiple times, despite the ordering"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,12,0)="provider's intent to allow only one optional dose. In this scenario, ONE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,13,0)="TIME is the name of a schedule defined in the Administration Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,14,0)="file with a type of One Time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,16,0)="Based on workgroup feedback, the issue will be addressed by treating any"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,17,0)="order containing a One Time schedule (i.e., a schedule defined in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,18,0)="Administration Schedule File with a type of One Time) as a order that is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,19,0)="to be given only once, regardless of the order's Schedule Type, or the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,20,0)="presence of the PRN modifier appended to the order's schedule. The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,21,0)="letters PRN are appended to the schedule name when the PRN check box is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,22,0)="checked during order entry, from the ordering dialog in CPRS. The PRN may"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,23,0)="also be appended to the schedule name manually from Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",196,1,24,0)="Version 5.0 order entry options."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,0)="222 SEQ #198^3100203.124051^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,0)="^^32^32^3100203"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,1,0)="This patch will be released as the Inpatient Medications portion of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,2,0)="the Pharmacy Legacy Quarterly Enhancements team's FY09 Q4 effort."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,4,0)="This enhancement will address Patient Safety Issue PSI-07-055,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,5,0)="PSPO #508, Remedy Ticket #180596, and was approved by the Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,6,0)="Medications Workgroup."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,8,0)="Problem"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,9,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,10,0)="Currently, for complex unit dose orders that contain an ""AND"" conjunction,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,11,0)="there is a possibility of the child orders containing overlapping"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,12,0)="administration (admin) times. If the admin times overlap, it is possible"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,13,0)="for a patient to receive too much of the medication at the overlapping"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,14,0)="admin time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,16,0)="Resolution"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,17,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,18,0)="This enhanced functionality will compare the admin time string of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,19,0)="child orders on either side of the ""AND"" conjunction and will capture"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,20,0)="any overlapping admin times. If any overlapping admin times are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,21,0)="found, a warning message will be displayed to the pharmacist who is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,22,0)="finishing the order. The warning message will read:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,24,0)="**WARNING**"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,26,0)="The highlighted admin times for these portions of this complex order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,27,0)="overlap."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,29,0)="Part 1 has a schedule of BID and admin time(s) of 10-22."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,30,0)="Part 2 has a schedule of QDAY and admin time(s) of 10."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",197,1,32,0)="Please ensure the schedules and administration times are appropriate."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,0)="214 SEQ #199^3100222.11343^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,0)="^^76^76^3100222"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,1,0)="Patches PSJ*5*214 and PSN*4*193 are being released as part of the Class"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,2,0)="III to Class I conversion process.  In combination, the two "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,3,0)="patches address the need to provide multidivisional functionality within"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,4,0)="the Inpatient Medications package's Patients on Specific Drug(s) [PSJ"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,5,0)="PDV] option. PSN*4*193 provides support within the National Drug File"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,6,0)="package and PSJ*5*214 delivers the enhanced functionality of the Patients"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,7,0)="on Specific Drug(s) [PSJ PDV] option."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,8,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,9,0)="This patch contains the following items:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,11,0)="1. The option would quit prematurely after the user entered an up-arrow to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,12,0)="exit a previous attempt to generate the report."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,14,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,15,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,16,0)="The variable QFLG used to denote the user's attempt to quit the option was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,17,0)="left defined following the aborted report attempt."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,19,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,20,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,21,0)="Routine PSJPDV updated to NEW variable QFLG."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,23,0)="2. To generate a report for all drugs within a parent drug class required "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,24,0)="entry of each child class when specifying the report parameters."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,26,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,27,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,28,0)="There was no cross-reference in the VA DRUG CLASS file (#50.605) to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,29,0)="determine the relationship between parent drug classes and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,30,0)="child drug classes."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,32,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,33,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,34,0)="Patch PSN*4*193 introduces the necessary cross-reference, which is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,35,0)="utilized by this patch to allow a user to enter a parent drug class.  The "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,36,0)="system will then select all of the drugs in the hierarchy of that parent "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,37,0)="class."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,39,0)="3.  The default response for the Number of Matches prompt did not "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,40,0)="reflect the most common answer to that question."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,42,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,43,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,44,0)="Current functionality would count the number of unique entries selected "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,45,0)="by the user and present that number as a default response to the Number "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,46,0)="of Matches prompt.  This assumed that a patient had to have all of the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,47,0)="selected drugs in their profile in order to be listed in the final report."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,49,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,50,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,51,0)="The default is changed to 1, reflecting a report in which the patient can "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,52,0)="be on any of the selected drugs in order to be listed on the report.  The "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,53,0)="user can still enter a higher number to employ the previously defaulted "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,54,0)="functionality."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,56,0)="4.  The existing program did not include functionality to support the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,57,0)="reporting needs of integrated or multidivisional facilities."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,59,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,60,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,61,0)="The report parameters do not ask for limitation of the output to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,62,0)="specified divisions, wards, or ward groups.  The resulting list always "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,63,0)="included all patients meeting the criteria across an entire VistA "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,64,0)="database."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,66,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,67,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,68,0)="A prompt is added to allow the user to select the DIVISION(s)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,69,0)="from which patients will be reported.  Sites that have only 1 division"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,70,0)="associated with all of their inpatient wards will not see this new prompt."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,72,0)="A prompt is added to allow the user to select the WARDS(s) from which"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,73,0)="patients will be reported."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,75,0)="If no selection is made for the division or ward prompt, the user will "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",198,1,76,0)="be allowed to select one WARD GROUP from which patients will be reported."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,0)="113 SEQ #200^3100623.16481^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,0)="^^82^82^3100623"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,1,0)="The purpose of this patch is to provide software enhancements for Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,2,0)="Validation defined by the BCMA-Inpatient Medications Request for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,3,0)="Special Focus Group (SFG) Initial Request Analysis (IRA)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,5,0)="Currently, Inpatient Medications allows orders to be created with"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,6,0)="conflicting administration times, frequencies, schedules, and schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,7,0)="types such that orders may not always display correctly on the Virtual"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,8,0)="Due List (VDL) in the Barcode Medication Administration (BCMA)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,9,0)="application. This enhancement adds several new order validation checks"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,10,0)="to improve the data that is displayed on the VDL. These order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,11,0)="validation requirements will apply to Unit Dose Medications and applied"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,12,0)="to intermittent IV orders schedules (IV orders do not have Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,13,0)="Type)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,15,0)="These enhancements are:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,17,0)="1.  Order Validation Check One"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,18,0)="For Intermittent IV orders, references to an order's Schedule Type will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,19,0)="refer to either the TYPE OF SCHEDULE from the Administration Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,20,0)="file (#51.1), or PRN for schedule names in PRN format, or CONTINUOUS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,21,0)="for schedule names in Day of Week format."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,23,0)="2.  Order Validation Check Two"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,24,0)="If an order has the Schedule Type of Continuous and the Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,25,0)="entered is NOT in Day of Week (Ex. MO-FR) or PRN (Ex. TID PC PRN)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,26,0)="format, then the system shall prevent the number of administration"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,27,0)="times associated with the order from being greater than the number of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,28,0)="administration times for that frequency, if the orders frequency is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,29,0)="numeric (minutes).  The number of administration times can be less than"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,30,0)="but not equal to zero administration times."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,32,0)="3.  Order Validation Check Three"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,33,0)="If an order has a Schedule Type of Continuous and is an Odd Schedule, a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,34,0)="schedule whose frequency is not evenly divisible by or into 1440"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,35,0)="minutes (1 day), then the system shall prevent the entry of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,36,0)="administration times."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,38,0)="4.  Order Validation Check Four"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,39,0)="If an order has a Schedule Type of Continuous with a non-odd frequency"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,40,0)="of greater than of 1 day (1440 minutes) then the system shall prevent"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,41,0)="more than one administration time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,43,0)="5.  Order Validation Check Five"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,44,0)="If an order has a Schedule Type of One Time or if an order is entered"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,45,0)="with a schedule that is defined in the schedule file as One Time then"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,46,0)="the system shall prevent the user from entering more than one"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,47,0)="administration time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,49,0)="6.  Order Validation Check Six"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,50,0)="For an order with a Schedule Type of Continuous where no"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,51,0)="doses/administration times are scheduled between the order's Start"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,52,0)="Date/Time and the Stop Date/Time, then the system shall present a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,53,0)="warning message to the user and not allow the order to be accepted or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,54,0)="verified until the Start/Stop Date Times, schedule, and/or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,55,0)="administration times are adjusted so that at least one dose is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,56,0)="scheduled to be given."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,58,0)="7.  Change the Sequence of the Schedule Type and Schedule Prompts"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,59,0)="Currently the order of the prompts in inpatient meds order entry is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,60,0)="Schedule Type followed by Schedule.  The sequence of the prompts will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,61,0)="be changed so that the Schedule prompt falls before the Schedule Type"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,62,0)="prompt."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,64,0)="8.  Schedule Validation Requirement One"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,65,0)="When a schedule is selected at the Schedule Field the system shall"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,66,0)="default the Schedule Type for the schedule entered from the Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,67,0)="File into the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,69,0)="9.  Schedule Validation Requirement Two"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,70,0)="If the user changes the schedule, they will be given a warning message"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,71,0)="that the administration times and the schedule type for the schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,72,0)="selected will be defaulted to this order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,74,0)="10.  Schedule Validation Check Three"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,75,0)="If the schedule type is changed from Continuous to PRN the system shall"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,76,0)="automatically remove any administration times that were associated with"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,77,0)="the schedule so that the order will not include administration times."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,79,0)="11.  Modify VistA Help Text"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,80,0)="The Help Text in Inpatient Order Entry was modified to add additional"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,81,0)="text so the user is able to see the added constraints when entering"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",199,1,82,0)="Administration Times."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,0)="239 SEQ #201^3100708.114944^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,0)="^^27^27^3100708"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,1,0)="Patch PSJ*5*214 introduced an enhancement to the Patients on Specific "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,2,0)="Drug(s) [PSJ PDV] option in which a user could select a parent (or major) "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,3,0)="VA DRUG CLASS and the system would respond as if the user had entered "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,4,0)="each of the corresponding child (or minor) drug class."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,6,0)="The enhancement broke the ability for the option to display data for "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,7,0)="parent classes that have drugs directly assigned to them, such as IN000 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,8,0)="(Investigational Agents) or HA000 (Herbs/Alternative Therapy)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,10,0)="This patch PSJ*5*239 will restore the ability for the report to identify "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,11,0)="the drugs that are directly assigned to a parent VA class."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,13,0)="1. Selection of VA Drug Class IN000 (Investigational Agents) in the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,14,0)="Patients on Specific Drug(s) option no longer returns any data."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,16,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,17,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,18,0)="The enhancements written to allow user selection of a parent drug class, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,19,0)="and the intended system response to return all items associated with its"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,20,0)="child drug classes, did not correctly search for drug items directly "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,21,0)="assigned to the parent class itself."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,23,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,24,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,25,0)="Revise search algorithm to select drugs assigned to the parent class "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,26,0)="first, then resume the process to traverse the drug class hierarchy of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",200,1,27,0)="child classes."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",201,0)="218 SEQ #202^3100929.125714^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",201,1,0)="^^3^3^3100929"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",201,1,1,0)="This patch will correct"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",201,1,2,0)="HD277692 - 5 Receiving error <DIVIDE>GETMIN+12^PSIVUTL1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",201,1,3,0)="HD347749 - 6 NATURE OF ORDER 'SERVICE REJECTION'  FOR INP MEDS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",202,0)="232 SEQ #203^3101014.173448^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",202,1,0)="^^9^9^3101014"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",202,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",202,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",202,1,3,0)="IVP syringe not appearing on Action Profile #2 [PSJU AP-2] with the rest "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",202,1,4,0)="of expring orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",202,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",202,1,6,0)="Lab QO stuck in a loop."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",202,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",202,1,8,0)="Documentation changes needed for menu option for the option Action "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",202,1,9,0)="Profile #1 [PSJU AP-1]."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",203,0)="200 SEQ #204^3101118.113816^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",203,1,0)="^^7^7^3101118"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",203,1,1,0)="This patch will fix the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",203,1,2,0)="1.  Return and Destroy (IV) (PSJI RETURN BY BARCODE ID) does not update"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",203,1,3,0)="    cumulative doses after destroying a label."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",203,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",203,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",203,1,6,0)="2. Complex order was not verified by a pharmacist and appeared on the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",203,1,7,0)="   picklist with the unit needed displayed on the picklist."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",204,0)="241 SEQ #205^3110111.11484^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",204,1,0)="^^10^10^3110111"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",204,1,1,0)="The purpose of this patch is to provide software bug fixes for Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",204,1,2,0)="Medications to correct the display of various warning messages, and for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",204,1,3,0)="the Non-Verified/Pending Orders Report to correct the order count and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",204,1,4,0)="patient list displays and to prevent a crash. This patch corrects the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",204,1,5,0)="following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",204,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",204,1,7,0)="-Category ""^Other"" can't be retrieved"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",204,1,8,0)="-Warning for Complex Orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",204,1,9,0)="-Dosage Ordered and Dispense Units do not match warning"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",204,1,10,0)="-Error in Order Summary of Non-Verified/Pending Orders Report"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,0)="245 SEQ #206^3110210.14461^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,0)="^^44^44^3110210"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,1,0)="This patch corrects the following issues that were introduced by patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,2,0)="PSJ*5*113:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,4,0)=" - In Abbreviated Order Entry, the ""Schedule:"" prompt appears twice."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,5,0)=" - Pending renewal orders incorrectly fail schedule validation in Speed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,6,0)="   Finish."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,8,0)="Remedy Overview"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,9,0)="------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,10,0)="1. HD0000000413812"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,12,0)=" Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,13,0)=" --------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,14,0)=" For users defined with an order entry process of ABBREVIATED in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,15,0)=" Inpatient User Parameters Edit [PSJ SEUP] option, the ""Schedule:"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,16,0)=" prompt appears twice when creating a new order via the Inpatient Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,17,0)=" Entry [PSJ OE] option."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,19,0)=" Solution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,20,0)=" ---------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,21,0)=" For users defined with an order entry process of ABBREVIATED in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,22,0)=" Inpatient User Parameters Edit [PSJ SEUP] option, prompt for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,23,0)=" ""Schedule:"" only once when creating a new order via the Inpatient Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,24,0)=" Entry [PSJ OE] option."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,27,0)="2. HD0000000414155"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,28,0)="   HD0000000415173"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,30,0)=" Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,31,0)=" --------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,32,0)=" Pending Continuous Unit Dose renewal orders with valid schedule/admin"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,33,0)=" time combinations fail schedule validation when the SF - Speed Finish"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,34,0)=" action is used within the Order Entry [PSJU NE] option, but they pass"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,35,0)=" schedule validation, without edits, when the manual FN - Finish action"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,36,0)=" is used. These orders can't be finished using Speed Finish, and must be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,37,0)=" finished using the manual FN - Finish action."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,39,0)=" Solution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,40,0)=" ---------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,41,0)=" Within the Order Entry [PSJU NE] option, allow Continuous Unit Dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,42,0)=" orders with schedule/admin time combinations that pass the manual FN -"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,43,0)=" Finish action's schedule validation to also pass the SF - Speed Finish"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",205,1,44,0)=" action's schedule validation."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,0)="179 SEQ #207^3110302.170903^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,0)="^^35^35^3110302"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,1,0)="Patch PSJ*5*179 Will correct the following issues."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,3,0)="1.  HD0000000099382 - PSI-05-053 Drug dose can be administered twice."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,4,0)="When a dose is given in Bar Code Medication Administration for an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,5,0)="Inpatient Order, the order is marked in BCMA as GIVEN.  If a Pharmacist"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,6,0)="edit's a field with a star (*), the new order may overwrite the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,7,0)="administration that was given in BCMA.  The possibility of giving the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,8,0)="patient a ""double"" dose exists."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,10,0)="2. HD0000000195783 - IMO Location not getting default stop date."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,11,0)="When using inpatient medications for Outpatient Orders, the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,12,0)="correct stop date is not displayed on the patient profile of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,13,0)="Backdoor Pharmacy Order Entry screen.  If there is a value defined in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,14,0)="Clinic Definition File for the ""NUMBER OF DAYS UNTIL STOP field, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,15,0)="order should use the default stop date. Currently this default stop date"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,16,0)="is not used when the order is finished as a unit dose."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,18,0)="3. HD0000000210901 - PSI-07-172 Reads of File 51.1 not checking Package"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,19,0)="                     Prefix."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,20,0)="When calculating the default Stop Date/Time for a Unit Dose order, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,21,0)="Inpatient Medications uses the schedule type field from the Administration"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,22,0)="Schedule File (#51.1) to determine which Inpatient Ward Parameter"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,23,0)="should be used.  The Days Until Stop Date/Time or Days Until Stop for "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,24,0)="One-time will be used.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,25,0)="However, the package prefix is not used when retrieving the schedule"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,26,0)="type from the Schedule File and as result, the wrong schedule and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,27,0)="schedule type could be used.  This will result in an incorrect default"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,28,0)="Stop Date/Time being calculated. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,29,0)="be calculated."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,31,0)="4.  HD0000000237637 - Editing Admit time, then comments renders no change."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,32,0)="Updates to the admin time field are not accepted when editing the admin"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,33,0)="time on an existing Unit Dose order, then editing the comment field. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,34,0)="The original admin time will remain.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",206,1,35,0)="This also happens when the user edits the comment field first."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",207,0)="226^3110308.135257^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",207,1,0)="^^1^1^3110308"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",207,1,1,0)="Provide dosing checks for Unit Dose and IV orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",208,0)="181^3110428.1607^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",208,1,0)="^^4^4^3110428"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",208,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",208,1,2,0)="1. Data Dictionary changes:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",208,1,3,0)="   Added the ""HOURS OF RECENTLY DC/EXPIRED"" field (#7) to the INPATIENT"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",208,1,4,0)="   WARD PARAMETERS file (#59.6)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",209,0)="261^3110615.145248^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",209,1,0)="^^7^7^3110615"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",209,1,1,0)="Incorrect stop dates are being populated when an IV medication order is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",209,1,2,0)="entered in CPRS as an inpatient medication and when the pharmacist "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",209,1,3,0)="finishes the order as an IV piggyback and additives do not exist (are not "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",209,1,4,0)="populated) at the time the pharmacist goes to finish the order.  The "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",209,1,5,0)="software no longer recognizes the stop date information entered in the IV "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",209,1,6,0)="additive file or in the Orderable Item file.  Instead it is looking at "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",209,1,7,0)="only the IV Site parameter date for IV piggybacks."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,0)="243 SEQ #211^3110629.093009^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,0)="^^48^48^3110629"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,1,0)="FY11 Pharmacy Legacy Enhancements (PSPO 738/PSI-07-122)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,3,0)="The enhancement contained in this patch revises the existing display in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,4,0)="the Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW] option from a patient list"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,5,0)="sorted alphabetically by TEAM and PATIENT NAME to a categorized listing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,6,0)="sorted by a patient's highest priority order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,8,0)="Patients that have one or more STAT Pending or Non-Verified orders will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,9,0)="be listed first, followed by patients with one or more ASAP Pending or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,10,0)="Non-Verified orders, and then all other patients that have only ROUTINE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,11,0)="Pending or Non-Verified orders. Within a given priority, patients will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,12,0)="continue to be sub-sorted alphabetically by TEAM name and PATIENT name."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,14,0)="Examples shown here.  Note the addition of PRIORITY column."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,17,0)="Search for Patients by WARD:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,18,0)="----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,20,0)="ORDERS NOT VERIFIED BY A PHARMACIST - GEN MED"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,22,0)=" No.   TEAM              PRIORITY     PATIENT"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,23,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,24,0)="   1  Not Found          STAT         DIXPATNM,FORT (0294)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,25,0)="   2  Not Found          STAT         JACPATNM,OOH YEAH (0407)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,26,0)="   3  Not Found          ASAP         TESPATNM,COLLATERAL (0177)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,27,0)="   4  GENERAL MED ONE    ROUTINE      VOLPATNM,JOHNNY (0258)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,28,0)="   5  GENERAL MED TWO    ROUTINE      NOYPATNM,FORMT (0017)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,29,0)="   6  Not Found          ROUTINE      JONPATNM,AAAAA (0513)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,30,0)="   7  Not Found          ROUTINE      NAGPATNM,STEVEN G (0139)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,31,0)="   8  Not Found          ROUTINE      TESPATNMTHREE,COLLATERAL (0181)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,32,0)="   9  Not Found          ROUTINE      TESPATNMTWO,COLLATERAL (0180)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,33,0)="Select 1 - 9:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,37,0)="Search for Patient by PRIORITY:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,40,0)="ORDERS NOT VERIFIED BY A PHARMACIST - STAT"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,42,0)=" No.   TEAM              PRIORITY     PATIENT"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,43,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,44,0)="   1  GENERAL MED ONE    STAT         BANPATNM,JAMES E (0091)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,45,0)="   2  GENERAL MED ONE    STAT         DIXPATNM,FORT (0294)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,46,0)="   3  GENERAL MED TWO    STAT         JACPATNM,OOH YEAH (0407)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,47,0)="   4  Not Found          STAT         MARPATNM,TEST (0734)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",210,1,48,0)="Select 1 - 4:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,0)="216 SEQ #212^3110629.161504^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,0)="^^17^17^3110629"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues in the Inpatient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,2,0)="Medications package:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,4,0)="- When a user is prompted for dosage in Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE], a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,5,0)="response of null will no longer be allowed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,7,0)="-When a user edits the dispense drug or units per dose on a unit dose "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,8,0)="order, the following message will not be displayed if the dispense drug "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,9,0)="times the unit per dose matches with the dosage ordered."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,11,0)=" WARNING: Dosage Ordered and Dispense Units do not match."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,12,0)="        Please verify Dosage"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,14,0)="The fix in this patch will display the warning message only when the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,15,0)="dosage ordered is NOT equal to the dispense drug times (X) the units "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,16,0)="per dose.  Also, when the warning message displays, the Dosage Ordered "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",211,1,17,0)="and Dispense Drug items will display in reverse video."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,0)="263 SEQ #213^3110812.135642^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,0)="^^50^50^3110812"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,1,0)="****************************** Note **************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,2,0)="This patch is a follow-up defect patch for Medication Order Check"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,3,0)="Healthcare Application v1.0 (MOCHA).  The MOCHA v1.0 patches are being "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,4,0)="released as a phased implementation release.  To see current status and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,5,0)="target dates for Sites/VISN/Region please refer to the following site:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,7,0)="http://vaww.itfo.portal.domain.ext/svcs/itfopmo/pre05/default.aspx"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,9,0)="Sites will be provided instructions and guidance on installation and of a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,10,0)="phased release for MOCHA 1.0, and this patch PSJ*5*263 should be installed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,11,0)="after MOCHA 1.0 installation."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,13,0)="**************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,15,0)="1. When the provider placed an IV order on hold, the code ""HP"" was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,16,0)="displayed for the order on the Inpatient Meds profile.  ""HP"" was still"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,17,0)="displayed on the patient profile on the pharmacy side when the provider"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,18,0)="released hold.  The order status was correctly changed back to active.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,19,0)="Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) was working with an active order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,20,0)="even though the display code was indicating hold by provider.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,21,0)="is removing the ""HP"" so the appropriate status is displaying on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,22,0)="profile. HD0000000503309 (Code Change Request(CCR) #4466)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,24,0)="2. When no active dispense drug was found for an active unit dose order, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,25,0)="the order was not included in the Drug Interaction and Duplicate "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,26,0)="Therapeutic checks for Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS).  This "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,27,0)="patch will ensure a dispense drug is included for the order checks.  (CCR "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,28,0)="#4465)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,30,0)="3. An undefined error occurred when using the order set with more than "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,31,0)="one order.  This happened when one of the orders was edited and the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,32,0)="variable PSJNOO was killed.  This lead to an undefined when continued "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,33,0)="entering a subsequence order from the order set. HD0000000505659 (CCR "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,34,0)="#4503)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,36,0)="4. The Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) Workgroup and Patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,37,0)="Safety requested Inpatient Medications shows the bottle/bag number in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,38,0)="parenthesis on the finishing screen for an IV order.  This change will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,39,0)="display the bottle number within the parenthesis for IV orders on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,40,0)="profiles and the order view. Change Request(CR) #3815, CCR #3815"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,42,0)="5. The Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) Workgroup and Patient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,43,0)="Safety requested Inpatient Medications shows the 'See Comments' next to IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,44,0)="additive name if applicable on the finishing screen for an IV order.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,45,0)="change will display 'See Comment' within the parenthesis for IV orders on"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,46,0)="the profiles and the order view.  The user must enter the appropriate"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,47,0)="bottle/bag number before completing the order. CR #2534, CCR #2990"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,49,0)="6. This patch also fixes an issue in the IV Profile where additive data is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",212,1,50,0)="not wrapped appropriately."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",213,0)="235^3110908.140905^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",213,1,0)="^^6^6^3110908"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",213,1,1,0)=" HD0000000349678 - PSPO#1521 QOD (every other day) schedule not working"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",213,1,2,0)=" (d)HD000000350458 - 1 Problem with start time of order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",213,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",213,1,4,0)=" This patch will correct an issue in which the Expected First Dose line "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",213,1,5,0)=" in CPRS, as well as the REQUESTED START DATE line in inpatient order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",213,1,6,0)=" entry were not displaying the correct date."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,0)="225 SEQ #215^3110930.132022^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,0)="^^19^19^3110930"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,1,0)="This patch will correct the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,3,0)="1. If the Units per Dose of an order are entered as ""0"" or a non-numeric "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,4,0)="   value, the Units per Dose is recorded as 0. This is contrary to the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,5,0)="   documentation, which states that under these circumstances, the units "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,6,0)="   per dose should be 1."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,8,0)="2. Intermittent as needed (PRN) IV Orders created by CPRS which should "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,9,0)="   have no value in the SCHEDULE INTERVAL field (#.17) of the IV SUB-FILE "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,10,0)="   (#55.01) are being incorrectly set to 1440 (1 day)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,12,0)="3. Intravenous push (IVP) orders are not showing up on the medicatinos "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,13,0)="   due worksheet."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,15,0)="4. The Meds tab in CPRS is not showing active orders that have been "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,16,0)="   placed on HOLD when the sort type is by Drug (Alphabetical)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,18,0)="5. In CPRS, when the ORCH CONTEXT MEDS parameter is not set, some "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",214,1,19,0)="   non-active orders visible even though none should be."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",215,0)="250 SEQ #216^3111012.125546^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",215,1,0)="^^5^5^3111012"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",215,1,1,0)="The purpose of this patch is to provide a software bug fix for Inpatient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",215,1,2,0)="Medications, and to correct the method of reprinting IV labels.  This "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",215,1,3,0)="patch corrects the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",215,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",215,1,5,0)="-Invalid barcode when IVPB order changed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",216,0)="237 SEQ #217^3111102.120201^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",216,1,0)="^^6^6^3111102"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",216,1,1,0)="This patch will correct the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",216,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",216,1,3,0)="-Print label missing data"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",216,1,4,0)="-Option PSJU SFEA Doesn't exist"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",216,1,5,0)="-Inpatient unit dose issue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",216,1,6,0)="-Incorrect First Dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",217,0)="223 SEQ #218^3111115.17344^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",217,1,0)="^^10^10^3111115"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",217,1,1,0)=" This patch will correct an issue with editing the SCEDULE TYPE of an "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",217,1,2,0)=" order in Inpatient Backdoor processing. The problem arises when a user "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",217,1,3,0)=" is able to enter a SCHEDULE TYPE of ONE TIME when the schedule is not "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",217,1,4,0)=" ONE TIME."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",217,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",217,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",217,1,7,0)=" ASSOCIATED REMEDY:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",217,1,8,0)=" =================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",217,1,9,0)=" PSPO#1317 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",217,1,10,0)=" HD0000000305526 - 1 Undo Given action returned a One time order back"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",218,0)="258 SEQ #219^3111202.121657^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",218,1,0)="^^7^7^3111202"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",218,1,1,0)="The purpose of this patch is to provide software bug fixes for Inpatient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",218,1,2,0)="Medications.  This patch corrects the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",218,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",218,1,4,0)="-Undefined Error when Copying an IV Order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",218,1,5,0)="-Pre-Exchange Report Not Printing When Orders Are Renewed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",218,1,6,0)="-Can't Copy an IV Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",218,1,7,0)="-Syntax Error When Renewing Multiple Unit Dose Orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,0)="253 SEQ #220^3120130.104148^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,0)="^^22^22^3120130"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,1,0)="This patch contains the following enhancement:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,3,0)="1. This patch implements functionality that retrieves Computerized"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,4,0)="   Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0 order checks and corresponding"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,5,0)="   provider override reason from the Order Check Instances (#100.05)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,6,0)="   file, and provides the order checks and provider override reason"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,7,0)="   to Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) V. 3.0 for display"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,8,0)="   in the BCMA Display Order report."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,11,0)="This patch contains the following two defect fixes:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,13,0)="1. This patch corrects an issue in Bar Code Medication Administration"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,14,0)="   V. 3.0 in which orders do not display on the Virtual Due List (VDL) "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,15,0)="   if the order's Schedule Type is Continuous or Fill on Request, and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,16,0)="   the order contains a Schedule defined in the Administration Schedule "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,17,0)="   File (#51.1) with a Schedule Type of On Call."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,19,0)="2. This patch corrects an issue in Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 in which"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,20,0)="   changing a Non-Verified order's Schedule Type to On Call automatically"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,21,0)="   changes the name of the order's Schedule to On Call without alerting "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",219,1,22,0)="   the user."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,0)="254 SEQ #221^3120130.104206^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,0)="^^107^107^3120130"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,1,0)="Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) V. 1.0 provider override"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,2,0)="reasons and the order checks that were overridden, as well as pharmacist"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,3,0)="intervention information from Inpatient Medications V. 5.0, when at"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,4,0)="least one overridden critical drug-drug interaction and/or allergy/ADR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,5,0)="interaction is associated with an Inpatient order. An API has also"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,6,0)="been added to supply this information to Bar Code Medication"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,7,0)="Administration (BCMA) V. 3.0."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,9,0)="******************************* WARNING **********************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,11,0)="If your facility has the Pyxis/Omnicell/McKesson interface from ILC this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,12,0)="patch will overwrite any local modifications in routines PSGOEE and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,13,0)="PSGOETO. This could affect certain orders being sent across this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,14,0)="interface. The modifications will have to be reintroduced following"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,15,0)="installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,17,0)="**************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,19,0)="1. This patch will implement functionality to utilize the Order Check"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,20,0)="   Instances (#100.05) file to retrieve and display CPRS provider override"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,21,0)="   reasons and the order checks that were overridden, when at least one"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,22,0)="   critical drug-drug interaction and/or allergy/ADR interaction is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,23,0)="   associated with an Inpatient order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,25,0)="2. An Order Checks/Interventions (OCI) indicator has been added to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,26,0)="   indicate a CPRS provider override or pharmacy intervention of at least"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,27,0)="   one critical drug-drug interaction and/or allergy/ADR interaction"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,28,0)="   exists for the current order. An ""OCI"" hidden action has also been"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,29,0)="   added to display the same CPRS overrides and/or pharmacist"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,30,0)="   interventions."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,32,0)="   The OCI indicator and hidden action have been added to the Detailed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,33,0)="   Order List Manager screens when utilizing the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,34,0)="    - Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,35,0)="    - Non-Verified/Pending Orders [PSJU VBW]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,36,0)="    - Order Entry [PSJU NE]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,37,0)="    - Order Entry (IV) [PSJI ORDER]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,40,0)="Patch Components"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,41,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",220,1,42,0)=" "
