^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,127,0)="Pre/Post Installation Overview"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,128,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,129,0)="There are no Pre/Post installation routines associated with this patch."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,130,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,131,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,132,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,133,0)="-------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,134,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,135,0)="recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,136,0)="potential disruption to users.  This patch should take less than 5 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,137,0)="minutes to install."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,138,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,140,0)="Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,141,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,142,0)="1.      Choose the PackMan message containing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,143,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,144,0)="2.      Choose the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,145,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,146,0)="3.      From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,147,0)="        the Installation Menu.  From this menu, you may elect to use the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,148,0)="        following options. When prompted for the INSTALL NAME enter"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,149,0)="        PSJ*5.0*325."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,150,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,151,0)="        a.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,152,0)="            allow you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,153,0)="            the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,154,0)="        b.  Print Transport Global - This option will allow you to view"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,155,0)="            the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,156,0)="        c.  Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,157,0)="            allow you to view all changes that will be made when this "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,158,0)="            patch is installed.  It compares all components of this patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,159,0)="            (routines, DD's, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,160,0)="        d.  Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,161,0)="            message of any routines exported with this patch. It will not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,162,0)="            backup any other changes such as DD's or templates."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,163,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,164,0)="4.      From the Installation Menu, select the Install Package(s) option "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,165,0)="        and choose the patch to install."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,166,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,167,0)="5.      When prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,168,0)="        Install? NO// Press <Enter>"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,169,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,170,0)="6.      When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,171,0)="        NO// Press <Enter>"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,172,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,173,0)="7.      When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,174,0)="        and Protocols? NO// Press <Enter>"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,175,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,176,0)="8.      If prompted ""Delay Install (Minutes):  (0 - 60): 0// respond 0."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,177,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,178,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,179,0)="Post-Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,180,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",288,1,181,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",289,0)="339 SEQ #290^3170629.151254^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",289,1,0)="^^8^8^3170629"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",289,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",289,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",289,1,3,0)="1.  Orders in the Inpatient Pharmacy package may not get their status "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",289,1,4,0)="updated to expired if the order's STOP DATE/TIME value matches the start"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",289,1,5,0)="time of the ORMTIME RUN background job.  This is happening because ORMTIME"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",289,1,6,0)="RUN and the pharmacy code compare the expiration time differently.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",289,1,7,0)="is happening for all inpatient pharmacy package orders, but is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",289,1,8,0)="particularly prevalent with clinic medication and clinic infusion orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",290,0)="343 SEQ #291^3170728.143232^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",290,1,0)="^^3^3^3170728"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",290,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",290,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",290,1,3,0)="1)  Pre-Exchange doses are incorrect when using Speed Finish"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",291,0)="341 SEQ #292^3170929.162916^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",291,1,0)="^^6^6^3170929"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",291,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",291,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",291,1,3,0)="1)     Admin History report has wrong data (New opton AH)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",291,1,4,0)="2)     DOW VI order is printing one label too many"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",291,1,5,0)="3)     Hard error when deleting AUTH ABS transfer"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",291,1,6,0)="4)     Scheduled IV labels sometimes do not print"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,0)="338 SEQ #293^3171005.14023^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,0)="^^155^155^3171005"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,2,0)="1)     UNDEFINED error when renew is changed to copy of an order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,3,0)="2)     Unit Dose order has zero for dosage"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,4,0)="3)     Copied UD order with >1 dispense drug, one inactive, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,5,0)="       copies incorrectly"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,6,0)="4)     ""^"" at Duration of Admin still allows order to continue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,7,0)="5)     UNDEFINED AGAIN+26^PSJDOSE *PSJCONT"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,8,0)="6)     Dispense drug not deleting correctly while finishing complex orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,10,0)=" Associated Ticket(s):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,11,0)="============================"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,12,0)="I9190964FY16        UNDEFINED error when renew is changed to copy an order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,13,0)="R11878202FY17       Unit dose order has zero for dosage."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,14,0)="I8405721FY16        Copied UD order with >1 dispense drug, one inactive,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,15,0)="                     copies incorrectly"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,16,0)="I12228956FY17       ""^"" at Duration of Administration still allows"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,17,0)="                     order to continue."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,18,0)="I15018816FY17       UNDEFINED error in PSJDOSE when modifying Dosage."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,19,0)="I13103401FY17       Dispense drug not deleting correctly while finishing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,20,0)="                     complex orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,21,0)="                    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,22,0)="Associated NSR(s):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,23,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,24,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,26,0)="PSPO(s):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,27,0)="========"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,28,0)="PSPO3491 - I13103401FY17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,29,0)="Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,30,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,31,0)="TBD"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,33,0)="Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,34,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,35,0)="Issue 1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,36,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,37,0)="I9190964FY16       UNDEFINED error when renew is changed to copy an order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,38,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,39,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,40,0)="========"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,41,0)="A unit dose inpatient order in Vista was selected to be renewed (RN).  At the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,42,0)="STOP DATE/TIME display the user realized they didn't want to renew the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,43,0)="but to copy it.  Entering an up-carat (^) at this point will take the user back"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,44,0)="to the originally selected order with no changes made.  The user then enters CO"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,45,0)="(copy) and attempts to copy the order.  During the copying process the user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,46,0)="receives the <UNDEFINED>INIT+58^PSJLMUDE error and is taken out of Vista. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,48,0)="During the RENEW process some of the values in the INPATIENT USER PARAMETERS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,49,0)="FILE (#53.45), which contain information about the displayed order, are killed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,50,0)="off.  When the user decided/realized they wanted the order copied and not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,51,0)="renewed, some of the pertinent information that was removed was not getting set"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,52,0)="back into this file.  This is the reason the user received the UNDEFINED error."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,54,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,55,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,56,0)="A modification was made to MOVE^PSGOER to ensure that the INPATIENT USER"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,57,0)="PARAMETERS FILE (#53.45) is populated with all the correct information for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,58,0)="processing."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,60,0)="Issue 2"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,61,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,62,0)="R11878202FY17       Unit dose order has zero for dosage."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,63,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,64,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,65,0)="========"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,66,0)="An active unit dose order in Vista was modified by changing the Orderable"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,67,0)="Item. When this is done, both the Orderable Item and Dosage Ordered are "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,68,0)="deleted. When entering the new Orderable Item, the user is not prompted "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,69,0)="for the Dosage Ordered and is able to accept the order.  This results in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,70,0)="the new order being created without a Dosage Ordered."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,72,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,73,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,74,0)="Modifications were made to 4 routines, PSGOE8, PSGOE9, PSJDOSE & PSGOEE."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,75,0)="These modifications will prompt the user to enter a Dosage Ordered when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,76,0)="they change the Orderable Item."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,79,0)="Issue 3"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,80,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,81,0)="I8405721FY16        Copied UD order with >1 dispense drug, one"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,82,0)="                    inactive, copies incorrectly."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,84,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,85,0)="========"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,86,0)="A Unit Dose order that has more than one Dispense Drug associated"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,87,0)="with it, one being inactive, will not copy correctly.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,89,0)="When the order is copies, the inactive Dispense Drug(s) are not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,90,0)="supposed to be copied to the new order.  If the inactive Dispense"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,91,0)="Drug is the first one then the second Dispense Drug will show"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,92,0)="on the new copied order twice.  If the inactive Dispense Drug is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,93,0)="last it will show on the copied order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,95,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,96,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,97,0)="A modification was made to routine PSGOD to remove the inactive"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,98,0)="Dispense Drug from the INPATIENT USER PARAMETERS FILE (#53.45)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,99,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,101,0)="Issue 4:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,102,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,103,0)="I12228956FY17     ""^"" at Duration of Admin still allows order to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,104,0)="                    continue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,105,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,106,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,107,0)="========"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,108,0)="A user went to edit an active Transdermal Inpatient order, and the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,109,0)="Pharmacy Orderable Item is marked for PROMPT FOR REMOVAL IN BCMA (value "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,110,0)="2 or 3) and the Dosage form is Patch.  During the edit of the verified "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,111,0)="order the user aborts (""^"") at the Duration of Administration prompt "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,112,0)="after entering the admin times. The system will allow the creation of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,113,0)="the new order without the Duration of Administration being entered."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,115,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,116,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,117,0)="A modification to PSGOEE to prevent the user from continuing to create"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,118,0)="a new order without the required Duration of Administration value."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,121,0)="Issue 5:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,122,0)="---------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,123,0)="I15018816FY17     UNDEFINED error in PSJDOSE when modifying Dosage."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,125,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,126,0)="========"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,127,0)="An active unit dose order in VistA was modified by changing the Dosage"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,128,0)="Ordered field.  When the dosage options/selections appeared, the user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,129,0)="opted to enter a free text dosage that exceeded 15 characters.  This"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,130,0)="resulted in the UNDEFINED error."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,131,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,132,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,133,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,134,0)="A modification was made to routine PSJDOSE to ensure that the user will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,135,0)="no longer receive the UNDEFINED error.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,137,0)="This modification will send the user back to the dosage prompt if the value"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,138,0)="exceeds 15 characters."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,140,0)="Issue 6:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,141,0)="---------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,142,0)="I13103401FY17     Dispense drug not deleting correctly while finishing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,143,0)="                   complex orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,145,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,146,0)="========"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,147,0)="An Inpatient Med complex order was created in CPRS.  While fiishing the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,148,0)="in Vista, the Pharmacist adds a new Dispense Drug (12) to the order then"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,149,0)="deletes the original Dispense Drug.  Once the order is completed and you "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,150,0)="go back into the order, both the new and deleted Dispense Drugs are displayed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,151,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,152,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,153,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,154,0)="A modification is needed in routine PSJCOM to update the NON-VERIFIED ORDERS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",292,1,155,0)="FILE (53.1) with the new Dispense Drug information."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",293,0)="335 SEQ #294^3171227.163305^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",293,1,0)="^^7^7^3171227"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",293,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",293,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",293,1,3,0)="1.  Pending renewal shows dose of original order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",293,1,4,0)="2.  Clinic Order cross-references not being set correctly"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",293,1,5,0)="3.  Major latency when running PSJ EXP on Clinics"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",293,1,6,0)="4.  PADE TRANSACTION REPORTS WONT FIND CS DRUG TRANSACTIONS THAT ARE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",293,1,7,0)="    UNMATCHED TO THE NDF"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",294,0)="345 SEQ #295^3171227.163558^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",294,1,0)="^^3^3^3171227"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",294,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following ISSUE:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",294,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",294,1,3,0)="   When the PSJI BACKGROUND JOB runs, no report is produced."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",295,0)="350 SEQ #296^3171228.120108^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",295,1,0)="^^4^4^3171228"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",295,1,1,0)="1)     Admin History report has wrong data (New opton AH)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",295,1,2,0)="2)     Hard error when deleting AUTH ABS transfer"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",295,1,3,0)="3)     Scheduled IV labels sometimes do not print"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",295,1,4,0)="4)     Scheduled IV labels are printing past the WL Stop date/time"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",296,0)="340 SEQ #297^3171228.12192^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",296,1,0)="^^10^10^3171228"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",296,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one (1) issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",296,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",296,1,3,0)="1.  Orders in the Inpatient Pharmacy package may not have had their "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",296,1,4,0)="    status updated to ""EXPIRED"", in the past, if the order STOP DATE/"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",296,1,5,0)="    TIME value matched the start time of the ORMTIME RUN background"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",296,1,6,0)="    job.  This happened because ORMTIME RUN and the pharmacy code "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",296,1,7,0)="    compared the expiration time differently."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",296,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",296,1,9,0)="    This was corrected with patch PSJ*5*339, but a clean-up effort must"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",296,1,10,0)="    be undertaken to place the old/stopped orders into expired status."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",297,0)="346 SEQ #298^3171228.122001^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",297,1,0)="^^5^5^3171228"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",297,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following Issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",297,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",297,1,3,0)="1)  I9190253FY16   Order displayed twice after edit if you press return at"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",297,1,4,0)="                     QUIT."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",297,1,5,0)="2)  I11117041FY17  Accept order prompt duplicated on IV orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",298,0)="349 SEQ #299^3180129.165506^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",298,1,0)="^^4^4^3180129"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",298,1,1,0)="1) There is an issue where the drug name is being stored for an "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",298,1,2,0)="   intervention for Clinical Reminder and not the drug IEN."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",298,1,3,0)="2) ""Next Dose Due:"" is displaying incorrectly when changing START "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",298,1,4,0)="   DATE/TIME to NOW on an active order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",299,0)="352 SEQ #300^3180227.135805^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",299,1,0)="^^1^1^3180227"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",299,1,1,0)="<UNDEFINED>109+1^PSGOE9"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",300,0)="256^3180302.14082^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",300,1,0)="^^1^1^3180302"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",300,1,1,0)="MOCHA 2.1 Dosing Enhancements."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",301,0)="347^3180302.141035^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",301,1,0)="^^1^1^3180302"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",301,1,1,0)="Follow up build to MOCHA 2.1b"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,0)="355 SEQ #303^3180403.153239^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,0)="^^16^16^3180403"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,1,0)="This patch addresses two (2) issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,3,0)="1.  The IV Additive Quick Code is not display the dosage and is showing "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,4,0)="    up during process as Additive Strength: QC when it should be "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,5,0)="    displaying as a Quick Code strength:nnn MG (where nnn is the strength"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,6,0)="    of the quick code)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,8,0)="    Currently a quick code is showing up, for example, ""Additive Strength:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,9,0)="    QC 1"" The Quick Code, for example, should be displayed as ""Quick Code "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,10,0)="    Strength:400 MG"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,12,0)="2.  The ""Expected First Dose"" prompt in the Inpatient Pharmacy package "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,13,0)="    New Order Entry option will display the incorrect calculated value if"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,14,0)="    it is the second or subsequent order processed in a session when the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,15,0)="    second or subsequent order has a schedule greater than daily and the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",302,1,16,0)="    Start Date is in the future."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",303,0)="356 SEQ #304^3180424.161446^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",303,1,0)="^^3^3^3180424"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",303,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",303,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",303,1,3,0)="I17870223FY18 - FRAMESTACK error"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",304,0)="361 SEQ #305^3180601.15093^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",304,1,0)="^^2^2^3180601"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",304,1,1,0)="1) Special Instructions on edit not copying correctly"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",304,1,2,0)="2) Next Dose Due not displaying correctly"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",305,0)="357 SEQ #307^3180706.121941^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",305,1,0)="^^2^2^3180706"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",305,1,1,0)="Ward Stock display issues when there are multiple dispense drugs,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",305,1,2,0)="not all ward stock items."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",306,0)="336 SEQ #308^3180706.14452^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",307,0)="359 SEQ #309^3180706.144605^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",307,1,0)="^^3^3^3180706"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",307,1,1,0)="This patch will address 2 Inpatient Medications issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",307,1,2,0)="1) <UNDEFINED> error when purging PRE-EXCHANGE NEEDS file."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",307,1,3,0)="2) Ward field set to zero in Patient Pharmacy file for IV orders.    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",308,0)="365 SEQ #310^3180706.152745^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",308,1,0)="^^2^2^3180706"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",308,1,1,0)="UNDEFINED error when running the PADE On-Hand Amounts or the PADE "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",308,1,2,0)="Transaction Reports"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,0)="371 SEQ #311^3180706.15282^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,0)="^^30^30^3180706"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,1,0)="Emergency Patch to back out and replace VistA routine that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,2,0)="caused an issue with long special instructions."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,4,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,5,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,6,0)=3726
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,8,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,9,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,11,0)="1)   INC1037196       "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,13,0)="Editing of verified inpatient medication orders with LONG special "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,14,0)="instructions results in new order with missing special instructions."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,16,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,17,0)="========"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,18,0)="Editing of verified inpatient medication orders that create new "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,19,0)="medication order will replace any existing, long special instructions "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,20,0)="with text, ""Instructions too long. See Order View or BCMA for full "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,21,0)="text.""  Had patch installed this week that may be causing this new "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,22,0)="problem, PSJ*5*361."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,25,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,26,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,27,0)="CA-SDM I18645262FY18 fixed an issue whereby Special Instructions on"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,28,0)="edited orders were not copying correctly. It introduced this issue,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,29,0)="however. The purpose of this patch is to return routine ^PSJBCMA5 to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",309,1,30,0)="pre-361 code."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",310,0)="358^3180706.154355^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",310,1,0)="^^1^1^3180706"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",310,1,1,0)="Follow up build to MOCHA 2.1b"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",311,0)="374 SEQ #313^3180907.121528^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",311,1,0)="^^2^2^3180907"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",311,1,1,0)="Patch reference and additional information may be found on Forum for "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",311,1,2,0)="PSJ*5*374."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,0)="344 SEQ #314^3180925.153217^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,0)="^^19^19^3180925"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,1,0)="This patch addresses four (4) issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,3,0)="1.  An UNDEFINED error is happening when copying a UD order, the user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,4,0)="    changes the Orderable Item but ""^"" out at the dispense drug selection"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,5,0)="    all the way back to the profile, then picks another order to copy."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,7,0)="2.  A Clinic IMO order could not be processed.  The site was turned off"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,8,0)="    for Inpatient Meds between the time the order was placed and when it"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,9,0)="    was processed by pharmacy."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,10,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,11,0)="3.  A Non-Verified IV order was modified, a non-starred field, then "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,12,0)="    another non-starred field was selected but the user cancelled the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,13,0)="    action (^). After the user Accepted the change the screen displayed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,14,0)="    the patient profile and not the accepted order to be verified."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,16,0)="4.  The verify action is not enabled immediately when a user accepts a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,17,0)="    unit dose order after verifying an iv fluid order for a different "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,18,0)="    patient. Instead, the profile screen is displayed without the verify"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",312,1,19,0)="    action."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",313,0)="373 SEQ #315^3181004.162536^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,0)="368 SEQ #316^3181102.144803^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,0)="^^37^37^3181102"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,3,0)="INC1065553 - BCBU MAR display NON transdermal patch orders with Removal"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,4,0)="             times discharged/deceased"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,5,0)="INC0608952 - *TEST ACCOUNT-BCMA listing all admins as a patch-TEST ACCOUNT*"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,6,0)="(Duplicate)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,7,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,8,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,9,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,10,0)="INC1065553 - BCBU MAR display NON transdermal patch orders with Removal"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,11,0)="             times discharged/deceased"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,12,0)="INC0608952 - *TEST ACCOUNT-BCMA listing all admins as a patch-TEST ACCOUNT*"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,13,0)="(Duplicate)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,14,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,15,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,16,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,17,0)="When Inpatient Pharmacy users use the option Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,18,0)="and instead of ordering a single medication choose an order set, there is a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,19,0)="potential mix up between patch medications with other medications with a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,20,0)="different form of administration. Orders sets are created via the Order Set"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,21,0)="Enter/Edit [PSJU OSE] option. In some circumstances patch medications will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,22,0)="not have a field for entering removal times and other times medication with"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,23,0)="other forms of administration will prompt BMCA users for an application"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,24,0)="site, which is required only for patch medications."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,25,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,26,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,27,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,28,0)="Reset variables that identify patch medication versus non patch medication"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,29,0)="before processing each order within the order set. This will prevent orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,30,0)="following a patch medication order from being flagged as patch as well."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,32,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,33,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,34,0)="NEWed the variable PSGRF and ND2P1 variables at GND+1^PSGOES and set the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,35,0)="variable PSGRF with the content of the PROMPT FOR REMOVAL IN BCMA field (#12)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,36,0)="in the PHARMACY ORDERABLE ITEM (#50.7) file, which is used to identify "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",314,1,37,0)="whether form of application for the medication being entered is a patch."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",315,0)="370 SEQ #317^3181102.151148^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",315,1,0)="^^2^2^3181102"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",315,1,1,0)="1)  Incomplete Medication Order Information"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",315,1,2,0)="2)  Special Instructions lost when new order is created due to edit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",316,0)="367 SEQ #318^3181102.152051^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",316,1,0)="^^9^9^3181102"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",316,1,1,0)="This patch will address three (3) INPATIENT MEDICATIONS issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",316,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",316,1,3,0)="1)Users are encountering an UNDEFINED error when an active order is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",316,1,4,0)="copied and one of the order's fields is modified and the new order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",316,1,5,0)="is made active."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",316,1,6,0)="2)Complex orders are still locked after verification of all the child "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",316,1,7,0)="orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",316,1,8,0)="3)Complex orders are still locked when user is at SELECT ACTION QUIT "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",316,1,9,0)="prompt."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,0)="353 SEQ #319^3181102.152816^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,0)="^^79^79^3181102"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,1,0)="This patch has the following enhancements for Clinical Ancillary Services"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,2,0)="(CAS) Enhancements (RXSU2)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,4,0)="1. Manage Lookup List Inactive Entries "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,6,0)="   Added the text ""** INACTIVE **"" to the end the display of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,7,0)="   ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1) entires while editting the Listman"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,8,0)="   screen field ""8)  Schedule:"" during Finishing an order or adding a New"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,9,0)="   Order in Pharmacy backdoor operations."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,11,0)="2. Manage Hidden Icons (Actions)  Inpatient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,13,0)="   Two new hidden actions are provided for Inptient Pharmacy's menu option"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,14,0)="   Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE]."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,16,0)="   a. New hidden action ""DM"" for displaying dispense drug information "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,17,0)="      during data entry.  This hidden action will display key information"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,18,0)="      about the order to help aid in the verification process of an order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,19,0)="      and also allow user to Enter another drug if desired.  Key"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,20,0)="      information includes:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,22,0)="      Example:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,24,0)="           DRUG NAME: xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx   (IEN: 3)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,25,0)="            ORDERABLE ITEM TEXT:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,26,0)="             xxx xx xxxxx xxxxx xx xxxxx"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,27,0)="             x xxxxxxxx xx xxxxxxxxxxxx"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,29,0)="            MESSAGE:   xxxx xxx xx xxxxx x xxxxxxxx"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,30,0)="            QTY DISP MESSAGE:   x xxxxxxxx xx xxxxxxxxx xxxx"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,32,0)="          Return to continue or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,33,0)="          Select DRUG GENERIC NAME:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,35,0)="   b. New hidden action ""VP"" for displaying Provider information during "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,36,0)="      data entry.  This hidden action will display key information about"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,37,0)="      the PROVIDER to help aid in the verification process of an order and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,38,0)="      also allow user to enter another provider if desired.  Key "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,39,0)="      information includes:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,41,0)="      Example:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,43,0)="           PROVIDER TITLE:    xxxxxx"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,44,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,45,0)="           PROVIDER REMARKS:  xxx xx xxxxxxx xxxx"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,47,0)="           PROVIDER SPECIALTY:  xxxxxx"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,49,0)="           Return to continue or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,50,0)="           Select NEW PERSON NAME: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,53,0)="3. View Provider Information"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,55,0)="   Inpatient Pharmacy menu option Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] header "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,56,0)="   Listman areas were changed to add two new fields, 1) ATTENDING"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,57,0)="   PHYSICIAN field (#.1041) and 2) TREATING SPECIALTY field (#.103) for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,58,0)="   both the Patient Information and Inpatient Order Entry Listman screens."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,60,0)="   Example Listman header screens:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,62,0)=" Inpatient Order Entry      Jan 22, 2018@15:16:14          Page:  1 of   1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,63,0)=" INPATIENT,FIRSTNAME           Ward: xxx xxxx"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,64,0)="   PID: xxx-xx-xxxx        Room-Bed: x-xxx           Ht(cm): _____ (_____)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,65,0)="   DOB: xx/xx/xx (xx)   Att:  Physician,Attend S     Wt(kg): _____ (_____)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,66,0)="   Sex: MALE            TrSp: NEUROLOGY             Admitted: xx/xx/xx"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,67,0)="    Dx: TEST ICD CODE                    Last transferred: ********"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,68,0)="  CrCL: <Not Found>                              BSA (m2): __________   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,69,0)=" -------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,72,0)=" Patient Information        Jan 25, 2018@15:09:18          Page:  1 of   1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,73,0)=" INPATIENT,FIRSTNAME           Ward: xxx xxxx"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,74,0)="   PID: xxx-xx-xxxx        Room-Bed: x-xxx           Ht(cm): _____ (_____)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,75,0)="   DOB: xx/xx/xx (xx)   Att:  Physician,Attend S     Wt(kg): _____ (_____)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,76,0)="   Sex: MALE            TrSp: NEUROLOGY             Admitted: xx/xx/xx"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,77,0)="    Dx: TEST ICD CODE                    Last transferred: ********"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,78,0)="  CrCL: <Not Found>                              BSA (m2): __________   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",317,1,79,0)=" -------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",318,0)="376 SEQ #320^3181206.155404^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",318,1,0)="^^3^3^3181206"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",318,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",318,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",318,1,3,0)="PADE Dispense Without Order VistA Mailman messages not being received"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,0)="362 SEQ #321^3181206.161244^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,0)="^^58^58^3181206"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,1,0)="MPDU - MEDICATION PERMISSIONS/DISPENSING UPDATES - Build 3"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,3,0)="This patch will address the following issues."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,5,0)=" 1. Timestamp Differential in VistA."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,7,0)=" 2. Honor Value of SEND CHECKIN/SURG HL7 FOR INPT for Admitted patients "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,8,0)="    only."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,10,0)=" 3. Prohibit Unintentional Reactivation/Inactivation of PADE Devices."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,13,0)="Item 1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,14,0)="------ "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,15,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,16,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,17,0)="I want the VistA system to use the exact time sent from the vendor system"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,18,0)="as long as it is no longer than 2 hours off of the time in VistA."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,20,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,21,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,22,0)="Line tag FILETRAN^PSJPAD7I has been modified to allow a time gap of up to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,23,0)="2 hours in the future, and if it is >2 hours then the transaction"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,24,0)="date/time will be set to NOW Date/Time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,26,0)="Item 2"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,27,0)="------ "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,28,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,29,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,30,0)="As a PADE user, I want the value of the SEND CHECKIN/SURG HL7 FOR INPT to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,31,0)="be honored for admitted inpatients only so that check-in messages will "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,32,0)="always be sent for non-admitted patients regardless of the parameter's "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,33,0)="value."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,36,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,37,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,38,0)="Line tag CLCI^PSJPDCLA has been modified to block check-in/Surg HL7 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,39,0)="messages only if the patient is an inpatient and the flag SEND "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,40,0)="CHECKIN/SURG HL7 FOR INPT is not set to ""Y""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,43,0)="Item 3"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,44,0)="------ "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,45,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,46,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,47,0)="As a user of the VistA PADE interface, I need the DISPLAY PADE INDICATORS "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,48,0)="IN IOE? prompt edit, through option 'PADE Inventory System Setup '(PSJ "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,49,0)="PADE INVENTORY SYSTEM), to not automatically reactivate devices that are "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,50,0)="currently inactive, or to inactivate devices that are currently active."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,53,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,54,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,55,0)="Line tag PSJOE^PSJPADSI has been modified to not to execute the code (D"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,56,0)="DEVONOFF^PSJPDRU1) to reactivate/activate the devices automatically when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,57,0)="stepping over the prompt DISPLAY PADE INDICATORS IN IOE? "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",319,1,58,0)="The user will have the control to reactivate/inactivate a device."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",320,0)="377 SEQ #322^3190102.174243^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",320,1,0)="^^3^3^3190102"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",320,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",320,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",320,1,3,0)="VistA IV Quick Code schedule issue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,0)="366 SEQ #323^3190103.172853^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,1,0)="^^12^12^3190103"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,1,1,0)="As part of the Clinical Ancillary Services project (CAS) - Medication "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,1,2,0)="Permission/Dispensing Updates (MPDU), the Inpatient Medications package"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,1,3,0)="has been modified to address the following:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,1,5,0)="This patch will address the following issues."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,1,7,0)="1. Limit the Display of Medication Routes for Infusion Order Dialogs"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,1,8,0)="2. Limit the Display of Medication Routes for Inpatient Unit Dose Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,1,9,0)="   Dialogs"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,1,10,0)="3. Check dosage form to determine appropriate default route"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,1,11,0)="4. Validate Termination of a Provider "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",321,1,12,0)="5. Addresses the defect reported in INC2806789 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",322,0)="379 SEQ #324^3190201.125053^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",322,1,0)="^^1^1^3190201"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",322,1,1,0)="This patch addresses a PADE ROOM-BED/WARD issue."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,0)="378 SEQ #325^3190201.151925^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,0)="^^34^34^3190201"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,3,0)="INC2264488 - Medication order start times and BCMA admin times are before the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,4,0)="             date/time the order was signed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,5,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,6,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,7,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,8,0)="INC2264488 - Medication order start times and BCMA admin times are before the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,9,0)="             date/time the order was signed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,10,0)="         "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,11,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,12,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,13,0)="The Robley Rex VA Medical Center reported that medication orders are showing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,14,0)="start date/times BEFORE the signature date/time of the order. This causes"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,15,0)="meds to be due for administration in BCMA for a past time when the order did"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,16,0)="not even exist. It appears as though patients are missing meds. Thus far"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,17,0)="orders have been isolated to our 4S MED hospital ward and all identified"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,18,0)="orders have been in the Unit Dose package."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,19,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,20,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,21,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,22,0)="The primary reason the Robley Rex VAMC experienced this problem is because"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,23,0)="the 4S MED was not configured in the Inpatient Ward Parameters Edit [PSJ IWP"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,24,0)="EDIT] option where the parameter DEFAULT START DATE CALCULATION used to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,25,0)="calculate the default start date/time for an order is set. The other reason"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,26,0)="is that once they processed two orders at the same time for the same ward"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,27,0)="the default value for the parameter was getting overwritten when they tried"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,28,0)="to finish the second order. This patch corrects this issue. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,29,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,30,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,31,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,32,0)="Changed the line ENSD+99^PSGNE3 to check only the 5th piece of the PSJSYSW0"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,33,0)="variable since it contains all ward parameters and after the user finished"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",323,1,34,0)="the first order it was getting set with multiple up-carets (""^^^^^^^^^^""). "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",324,0)="381 SEQ #326^3190301.155652^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",324,1,0)="^^4^4^3190301"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",324,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",324,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",324,1,3,0)="Results from LA7POC1 and LA7POC2 for iSTAT and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",324,1,4,0)="  Glucose testing are not going over to VISTA"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",325,0)="383 SEQ #327^3190401.151159^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",325,1,0)="^^2^2^3190401"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",325,1,1,0)="Copied provider comments no longer display on the orders tab in CPRS when "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",325,1,2,0)="pharmacist edits starred (*) field with Auto-Verify ON"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",326,0)="382 SEQ #328^3190402.171549^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",326,1,0)="^^4^4^3190402"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",326,1,1,0)="When a user enters a complex order as a clinic order for an outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",326,1,2,0)="and edits a part (child) of the order after finishing that part of the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",326,1,3,0)="order, the order displays as an inpatient medication instead of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",326,1,4,0)="displaying as a clinic order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",327,0)="386 SEQ #329^3190604.175734^54"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",327,1,0)="^^2^2^3190604"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",327,1,1,0)="This patch addresses an issue where next cart exchange may be displayed "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",327,1,2,0)="along with a value for Pre-Exchange DOSES erroneously with Clinic orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",328,0)="387 SEQ #330^3190708.094742^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",329,0)="391 SEQ #332^3190827.085924^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",329,1,0)="^^2^2^3190827"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",329,1,1,0)="This patch will put option PSJI DELETE ORDER out of order and correct an "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",329,1,2,0)="issue with NATURE OF ORDER for IV orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",330,0)="389 SEQ #333^3190926.110919^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",330,1,0)="^^2^2^3190926"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",330,1,1,0)="The description of this build can be found in the National Patch Module"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",330,1,2,0)="under PSJ*5*389."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",331,0)="327^3190930.103648^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",331,1,0)="^^1^1^3190930"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",331,1,1,0)="MENTAL HEALTH NCC PROJECT 5.01"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",332,0)="390 SEQ #334^3190930.103753^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",332,1,0)="^^4^4^3190930"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",332,1,1,0)="This patch addresses 2 issues. 1) An issue with the Pre-Exchange"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",332,1,2,0)="DOSES for a clinic order when the clinic and the medication are tied to a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",332,1,3,0)="PADE device. 2) Upon the entry of a date of death for a patient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",332,1,4,0)="the patient's active clinical orders (IMO) are not discontinued."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",333,0)="380 SEQ #335^3191016.162939^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",333,1,0)="^^2^2^3191016"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",333,1,1,0)="The description of this build can be found in the National Patch Module "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",333,1,2,0)="under PSJ*5*380."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",334,0)="392 SEQ #336^3191206.14521^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",334,1,0)="^^2^2^3191206"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",334,1,1,0)="The description of this build can be found in the National Patch Module "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",334,1,2,0)="under PSJ*5*392."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",335,0)="393 SEQ #337^3191206.145611^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",335,1,0)="^^6^6^3191206"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",335,1,1,0)="This patch will fix the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",335,1,2,0)="1) Correct an issue that occurs when the MED ROUTE is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",335,1,3,0)="   modified. It causes the ADMIN TIMES to disappear."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",335,1,4,0)="2) Correct an issue that occurs when a starred field is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",335,1,5,0)="   edited in a complex order.  User is getting knocked"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",335,1,6,0)="   out of the system with a hard error."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,0)="396 SEQ #338^3200115.122232^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,0)="^^35^35^3200115"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,3,0)="INC8260675 - New Patch PSJ*5*380 causing M error when running PSD report"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,4,0)="INC8364590 - VISTA option [PSJ PDV] ""Patients on Specific Drug(s)"" generates"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,5,0)="(Duplicate)  hard error <SUBSCRIPT>IVSET+7^PSJPDV0 ^SC("""")"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,6,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,7,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,8,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,9,0)="INC8260675 - New Patch PSJ*5*380 causing M error when running PSD report"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,10,0)="INC8364590 - VISTA option [PSJ PDV] ""Patients on Specific Drug(s)"" generates"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,11,0)="(Duplicate)  hard error <SUBSCRIPT>IVSET+7^PSJPDV0 ^SC("""")"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,12,0)="               "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,13,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,14,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,15,0)="The Syracuse VAMC Inpatient Pharmacy reported getting a hard error when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,16,0)="running the Patients on Specific Drug(s) [PSJ PDV] report option for a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,17,0)="specific Division. It was reported as well that the error started happening"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,18,0)="after the installation of patch PSJ*5*380. The HPS Sustainment Team confirmed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,19,0)="the problem to be caused by the code introduced by PSJ*5*380 to resolve a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,20,0)="different problem in the same report. The code did not take into account that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,21,0)="not all inpatient orders have a clinic associated with it and that is why the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,22,0)="software was throwing a <SUBSCRIPT> error."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,23,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,24,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,25,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,26,0)="This patch fixes the code by skipping orders without a clinic when the user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,27,0)="runs the report for a specific Division."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,29,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,30,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,31,0)="Changed the lines IVSET+7 and UDSET+7 in the PSJPDV0 routine to skip the order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,32,0)="if the value of the field CLINIC (#130) in the UNIT DOSE sub-file (#55.06) or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,33,0)="the value of the field CLINIC (#136) in the IV sub-file (#55.01), both in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,34,0)="PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55), are blank and the report is being run for a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",336,1,35,0)="specific Division. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",337,0)="400 SEQ #340^3200707.163039^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",337,1,0)="^^2^2^3200707"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",337,1,1,0)="Inpatient Med One-time Order not Discontinuing after Administering of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",337,1,2,0)="Medication"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,0)="397 SEQ #342^3200709.162746^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,0)="^^71^71^3200709"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,3,0)="INC6081255 - BCMA scanning IV medication as invalid lookup"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,4,0)="INC6231181 - Over the last several months, there has been at least 5 times"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,5,0)="HITPS-6742   that I am aware of where CPRS and BCMA aren't communicating on"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,6,0)="             verification of order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,7,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,8,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,9,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,10,0)="1) INC6081255 - BCMA scanning IV medication as invalid lookup"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,12,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,13,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,14,0)="The VA Sierra Nevada Health Care System reported that BCMA IV piggyback label"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,15,0)="scanned as invalid look up when they should be valid. This happened when, for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,16,0)="example, an edit on the Volume of the solution on the order should have caused"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,17,0)="the previously printed label(s) to be invalidated and new label(s) generated "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,18,0)="according to the BCMA Parameters. New label(s) were generated for the edited"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,19,0)="order, however all labels (old and new) were being erroneously invalidated."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,20,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,21,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,22,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,23,0)="This problem happened because the software performs a date/time comparison"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,24,0)="between the Volume edit and the label creation to determine whether a label"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,25,0)="is valid or not. If the label was printed before the Volume edit the label is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,26,0)="considered invalid. The problem is that it was using the format YYYMMDD.HHMMSS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,27,0)="for the Volume edit date/time and the format YYYMMDD.HHMM for the Label"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,28,0)="creation date/time. So, if the new label(s) where printed within the same"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,29,0)="minute of the Volume edit the software mistakenly assumed the new labels were"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,30,0)="printed before the Volume edit."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,31,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,32,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,33,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,34,0)="Changed the code at EN+61 in the routine PSIVBCID to truncate the order edit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,35,0)="date/time to YYYMMDD.HHMM format when doing the comparison with the label"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,36,0)="print date/time. This way labels printed after the order edit should never be"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,37,0)="considered invalid."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,38,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,39,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,40,0)="INC6231181 - Over the last several months, there has been at least 5 times"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,41,0)="             that I am aware of where CPRS and BCMA aren't communicating on"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,42,0)="             verification of order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,44,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,45,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,46,0)="The Madison VA Hospital reported that the BCMA nurse verification information"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,47,0)="was not being properly reset (removed) after the field SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,48,0)="was edited by Inpatient Pharmacy users through the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,49,0)="OE] option. In CPRS the nurse verification is correctly being reset (removed)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,50,0)="after this field is edited in Inpatient Pharmacy. According to the site this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,51,0)="poses the risk of medication being administered through BCMA without the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,52,0)="proper re-review and re-verification. This issue is also being considered a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,53,0)="Patient Safety Issue (PSI) and the number assigned by the Patient Safety team"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,54,0)="is HITPS-6742."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,55,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,56,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,57,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,58,0)="Every time the SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS field is edited for an inpatient unit dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,59,0)="order the nurse verification information (if any) will be invalidated/removed,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,60,0)="which will be reflected in the BCMA application. Depending on how the site "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,61,0)="BCMA parameters is set it will require a re-verification of the order in CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,62,0)="before it can be administered through the BCMA application."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,63,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,64,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,65,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,66,0)="Created a new line tag in the routine PSJBCMA2 called RESETNV responsible for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,67,0)="removing the nurse verification information in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55),"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,68,0)="UNIT DOSE sub-file (#55.06), fields VERIFYING NURSE (#16) DATE VERIFIED BY"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,69,0)="NURSE (#17) and setting the NV FLAG field (#51) to 0 (NO). These fields are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,70,0)="used by BCMA to determine whether an order have been verified or not by a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",338,1,71,0)="nurse."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",339,0)="395 SEQ #343^3200721.134942^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",339,1,0)="^^8^8^3200721"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",339,1,1,0)="This patch will fix an issue where a subcomponent separator is not being"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",339,1,2,0)="converted, by HL7 Standards, from & to \T\ when sending HL7 messages to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",339,1,3,0)="outgoing PADE HL7 messages."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",339,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",339,1,5,0)="Patch will also fix, when finishing a pending order from CPRS, as an IV "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",339,1,6,0)="medication with no additive and a single solution that has Dose Limits"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",339,1,7,0)="applied to the Orderable Item file, that it honor that Dose limit and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",339,1,8,0)="calculate the correct Stop date/time for the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",340,0)="385 SEQ #344^3200722.131649^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",340,1,0)="^^4^4^3200722"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",340,1,1,0)="Patch PSJ*5*366 introduced checks to verify that a user had sufficient "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",340,1,2,0)="privileges to perform certain tasks. After the release of PSJ*5*366 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",340,1,3,0)="an exception was discovered that prevented qualified users from "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",340,1,4,0)="performing those tasks."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",341,0)="398 SEQ #345^3200810.124929^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",341,1,0)="^^9^9^3200810"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",341,1,1,0)="Dosage changed on warfarin from 5mg to 3mg didn't fire a warning"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",341,1,2,0)="to the pharmacist finishing the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",341,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",341,1,4,0)="Clozapine complex order issue with stop date/time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",341,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",341,1,6,0)="BCMA Missed Med Report by CLINIC Gives Error Message ""Unable to Reach "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",341,1,7,0)="Vista"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",341,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",341,1,9,0)="Vista hard error with Unit Dose hidden option ""OCI"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",342,0)="388^3200824.16091^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",343,0)="319^3200923.154341^65"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",344,0)="401 SEQ #349^3201123.101011^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",344,1,0)="^^3^3^3201123"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",344,1,1,0)="Correct two routines so PADE HL7 messsages will be sent when complex "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",344,1,2,0)="multi-line orders with ""and"" conjunctions are renewed by CPRS and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",344,1,3,0)="finished by VistA PSJ OE backdoor option."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",345,0)="410 SEQ #350^3201208.082555^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",345,1,0)="^^4^4^3201208"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",345,1,1,0)="It was discovered that, in certain instances, when executing the option "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",345,1,2,0)="that sends a clinic's patient orders to PADE (PADE Send Patient Orders), "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",345,1,3,0)="a user receives the message 'Clinic is not setup for this PADE' for an"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",345,1,4,0)="active client that is qualified to be selected."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,0)="406 SEQ #351^3201208.090932^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,0)="^^33^33^3201208"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,1,0)="This patch, in conjunction with PSB*3*127, will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,3,0)="1) INC11397447 - BCMA Backup workstation patient print out and order display"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,4,0)="                 removal times for INHALATION Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,6,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,7,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,8,0)="1) INC11397447 - BCMA Backup workstation patient print out and order display"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,9,0)="                 removal times for INHALATION Medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,10,0)="           "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,11,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,12,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,13,0)="The VA North Texas Health Care System reported that when displaying and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,14,0)="printing patient order the print out includes removal times for medications"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,15,0)="that does not require removal. The source of the problem was identified in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,16,0)="the schedule used for these orders. If it contains the ampersand character"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,17,0)="(&), e.g. AC&HS, it shifts fields within the HL7 message communicated between"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,18,0)="the main VistA system and the BCBU workstation, which causes it to populate"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,19,0)="the REMOVE TIMING field (#7.4) within the ORDER NUMBER sub-file (#53.701) in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,20,0)="the BCMA BACKUP DATA file (#53.7)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,21,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,22,0)="Solution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,23,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,24,0)="Changed the building of the outbound order HL7 message from VistA to the BCBU"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,25,0)="workstation to escape the schedule field value before including it in the HL7"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,26,0)="message and also changed the processing of the incoming message to un-scape"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,27,0)="the schedule field value before parsing it at the BCBU workstation. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,29,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,30,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,31,0)="This patch changes the routine PSJHL3 at line tag RXE+39 and IVRXE+7 to escape"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,32,0)="the schedule field value before including it in the outbound HL7 message sent"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",346,1,33,0)="to the BCBU workstation. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,0)="413 SEQ #352^3210127.1213^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,0)="^^154^154^3210127"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,2,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,4,0)="INC12424796 - Renewing a clinic order still showing the old clinic "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,5,0)="location"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,6,0)="              in CPRS and backdoor Inpatient Pharmacy "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,18,0)="When changing the clinic location in CPRS and then renewing a clinic "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,19,0)="order, PRS and backdoor Inpatient Pharmacy is still displaying the old"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,20,0)="clinic order. This is incorrect. The clinic is updated in File #53.1 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,21,0)="but not in File #55"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,23,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,24,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,26,0)="A modification was made in routine PSGOTR to update FILE 55 from FILE "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,27,0)="53.1 during the verification process, this will display the correct "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,28,0)="Clinic location in CPRS and backdoor Inpatient Pharmacy. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,30,0)="File Name (Number)          Field Name (Number)       New/Modified/Deleted"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,31,0)="------------------          -------------------       --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,32,0)="PHARMACY PATIENT (55)                 CLINIC(130)                 Modified"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,34,0)="Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,35,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,36,0)="TBD"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,38,0)="Software and Documentation Retrieval Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,39,0)="--------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,40,0)="The software for this patch is being released in a PackMan message."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,42,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,43,0)="Patch Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,44,0)="-------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,46,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,47,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,48,0)="recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,49,0)="potential disruption to users.  This patch should take less than 5 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,50,0)="minutes to install."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,53,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,55,0)="1.  Choose the PackMan message containing this build. Then select "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,56,0)="    the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option to load the build."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,59,0)="2.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,60,0)="    select the Installation Menu.  From this menu, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,62,0)="    A.  Select the Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,63,0)="        option to confirm the integrity of the routines that "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,64,0)="        are in the transport global. When prompted for the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,65,0)="        INSTALL NAME enter the patch or build name. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,66,0)="        (ex. <PSJ*5.0*413)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,68,0)="        NOTE: Using <spacebar><enter> will not bring up a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,69,0)="              Multi-Package build even if it was loaded "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,70,0)="              immediately before this step. It will only "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,71,0)="              bring up the last patch in the build."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,73,0)="    B. Select the Backup a Transport Global option to create a "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,74,0)="       backup message of any routines exported with this patch. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,75,0)="       It will not backup any other changes such as DDs or "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,76,0)="       templates. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,78,0)="    C. You may also elect to use the following options: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,79,0)="         i.  Print Transport Global - This option will allow "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,80,0)="             you to view the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,81,0)="         ii. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,82,0)="             option will allow you to view all changes that will "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,83,0)="             be made when this patch is installed.  It compares "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,84,0)="             all of the components of this patch, such as "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,85,0)="             routines, DDs, templates, etc."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,87,0)="    D. Select the Install Package(s) option and choose the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,88,0)="       patch to install. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,89,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,90,0)="         i.  If prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,91,0)="             Completion of Install? NO//', answer NO."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,92,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,93,0)="      ii. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,94,0)="          install? NO//', answer NO."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,96,0)="      iii. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,97,0)="           Options, and Protocols? NO//', answer NO      "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,98,0)="            "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,99,0)="           a. When prompted 'Enter options you wish to mark as "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,100,0)="              'Out Of Order':', press the Enter key."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,101,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,102,0)="           b. When prompted 'Enter protocols you wish to mark as "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,103,0)="              'Out Of Order':', press the Enter key."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,105,0)="           c. When prompted 'Delay Install (Minutes):  (0 - 60): 0//',"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,106,0)="              answer 0."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,108,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,110,0)="Back-Out/Roll Back Plan:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,111,0)="------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,113,0)="Post Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,114,0)="-------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,115,0)="None."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,117,0)="Installation Verification:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,118,0)="--------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,119,0)="Successful installation can be verified by reviewing the first 2 lines "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,120,0)="of the routines contained in the patch. The second line will contain the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,121,0)="patch number (413) in the [PATCH LIST] section."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,122,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,123,0)=" ;;5.0;INPATIENT MEDICATIONS;**[PATCH LIST]**;16 DEC 97;[BUILD #]"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,124,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,125,0)="The option Calculate and Show Checksum Values [XTSUMBLD-CHECK] can be run "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,126,0)="to compare the routine checksums to what is documented in the patch"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,127,0)="description."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,129,0)="Back-out/Rollback Strategy:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,130,0)="---------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,131,0)="Back-out will be done only with the concurrence and participation"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,132,0)="of development team and appropriate VA site/region personnel. The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,133,0)="decision to back-out or rollback software will be a joint decision"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,134,0)="between development team, VA site/region personnel and other"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,135,0)="appropriate VA personnel."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,137,0)="Prior to installing an updated KIDS package, the site/region should"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,138,0)="have saved a backup of the routines in a mail message using the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,139,0)="Backup a Transport Global [XPD BACKUP] menu option (this is done at"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,140,0)="time of install). The message containing the backed-up routines can"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,141,0)="be loaded with the ""Xtract PackMan"" function at the Message Action"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,142,0)="prompt. The Packman function ""INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE"" is then used"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,143,0)="to install the backed-up routines onto the VistA System. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,144,0)="No data was modified by this patch installation and, therefore, no "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,145,0)="rollback strategy is required."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,146,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,147,0)="Validation of Back-out Procedure"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,148,0)="---------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,149,0)="The Back-out Procedure can be verified by printing the first 2"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,150,0)="lines of the PSJ Routines contained in this patch using the option"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,151,0)="First Line Routine Print [XU FIRST LINE PRINT]. Once the routines"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,152,0)="contained in the PSJ*5.0*413 patch have been rolled back, the first"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,153,0)="two lines of the Routines will no longer contain the designation"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",347,1,154,0)="of patch PSJ*5.0*413 in the patch list section on line 2"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",348,0)="411 SEQ #353^3210224.100143^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",348,1,0)="^^1^1^3210224"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",348,1,1,0)="See patch description for PSJ*5.0*411."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",349,0)="405 SEQ #354^3210312.122602^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",349,1,0)="^^4^4^3210312"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",349,1,1,0)="When a provider chooses a schedule of WEEKLY or MONTHLY in VistA the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",349,1,2,0)="HL7 data sent to the Omnicell reflects that this drug should be given on "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",349,1,3,0)="Wednesday or Monday instead of the actual day the order was entered. See"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",349,1,4,0)="the patch description on FORUM for more details."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,0)="404 SEQ #355^3210315.115303^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,0)="^^36^36^3210315"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,3,0)="INC9104304 - Patient Merge is incorrectly merging BCMA MED LOGS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,4,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,5,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,6,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,7,0)="1) INC9104304 - Patient Merge is incorrectly merging BCMA MED LOGS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,9,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,10,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,11,0)="The Dallas Field Office reported that BCMA MEDICATION LOG file (#53.79) does"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,12,0)="not get updated properly when 2 patients are merged. More specifically, the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,13,0)="ORDER REFERENCE NUMBER field (#.11), which contains a pointer to UNIT DOSE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,14,0)="(#55.06) and IV (#55.01) sub-files in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) does "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,15,0)="not get updated with the new pointers when the entries in these two sub-files"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,16,0)="are moved to a different IEN (Internal Entry Number). In some rare cases, this"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,17,0)="will cause the BCMA Medication History Reports to hide one of the orders for "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,18,0)="the newly merged patients if both patients had the orders of the same type"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,19,0)="(UD/IV) with the same pointer and were administered on the same day."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,20,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,21,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,22,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,23,0)="It was confirmed that the patient merge updates did not update the BCMA"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,24,0)="MEDICATION LOG file (#53.79) entries when the IENs for UD/IV orders in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,25,0)="PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) were changed. The code was correct to correctly"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,26,0)="update the BCMA MEDICATION LOG file (#53.79), ORDER REFERENCE NUMBER (#.11)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,27,0)="when two patients are merged."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,28,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,29,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,30,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,31,0)="Added a new line tag at the end of the routine PAJPATMR called UPDBML to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,32,0)="updated the ORDER REFERENCE NUMBER field (#.11) on the BCMA MEDICATION LOG"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,33,0)="file (#53.79) file for all administrations right after the new IEN is assigned"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,34,0)="to UD/IV orders. In addition, the code in UPDBML will kill the old (From) and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,35,0)="set the new (To) cross-references ""AADT"", ""AEDT"" and ""AOIP"" because it was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",350,1,36,0)="determined that the Patient Merge routines did not update them either."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",351,0)="415b^3210617"
