^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,3,0)="1) INC11926924 - MAD: PSJ*#*### not resolve: order appeared verified by nurse"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,4,0)="   HITPS-7361    in BCMA but CPRS it was found not to be."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,6,0)="2) INC12777528 - BCMA shows medication as not nurse verified, CPRS shows it as"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,7,0)="                 verified   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,9,0)="3) INC17553085 - Error in MIN VistA: RPC+##^PSBCHKIV *PSBIVCHG BarCode"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,10,0)="                 Medication Administration (PSB)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,11,0)="   Duplicate:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,12,0)="   -----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,13,0)="   INC17559434 - IV bolus orders showing verified in CPRS but not BCMA"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,15,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,16,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,17,0)="1) INC11926924 - MAD: PSJ*#*### not resolve: order appeared verified by nurse"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,18,0)="                 in BCMA but CPRS it was found not to be.     "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,19,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,20,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,21,0)="The William S. Middleton Memorial Veterans Medical Center  Affairs Hospital "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,22,0)="reported that the BCMA nurse verification information was not being properly"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,23,0)="reset (removed) after the field DISPENSE DRUG was edited by Inpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,24,0)="users through the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] option. In CPRS the nurse"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,25,0)="verification is correctly being reset (removed) after any of the Dispense Drug"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,26,0)="field is modified. There was an expectation from the site that PSJ*5*397 would"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,27,0)="address this problem, however that patch addressed only edits to the SPECIAL"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,28,0)="INSTRUCTIONS field, not the DISPENSE DRUG field. This issue is also being"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,29,0)="considered a Patient Safety Issue (PSI) and the number assigned by the Patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,30,0)="Safety team is HITPS-7361."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,31,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,32,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,33,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,34,0)="Every time an order update is received from CPRS by Inpatient Pharmacy the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,35,0)="Nurse Verification information (if any) will be invalidated/removed before"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,36,0)="updating the incoming data from CPRS. In case CPRS sends new Nurse Verification"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,37,0)="information with the order the information will be updated in Pharmacy order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,38,0)="files, which will be reflected in the BCMA application. Depending on how the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,39,0)="site BCMA parameters is set it will require a re-verification of the order in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,40,0)="CPRS before it can be administered through the BCMA application."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,41,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,42,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,43,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,44,0)="Changed the routine PSJHL4 at line tag ORC+6 and included code to delete/remove"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,45,0)="the nurse verification information from the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) every"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,46,0)="time an update is received from CPRS. Also, the changes introduced in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,47,0)="routine PSJBCMA2 by PSJ*5*397 to address the incident INC6231181 (HITPS-6742)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,48,0)="have been removed because this new change will better address that issue as"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,49,0)="well. A global hard-setting approach was used to avoid some updates from"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,50,0)="occurring through Mumps trigger cross-references."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,51,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,52,0)="2) INC12777528 - BCMA shows medication as not nurse verified, CPRS shows it as"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,53,0)="                 verified   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,54,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,55,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,56,0)="The Minneapolis VA Health Care System reported that a medication order shows"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,57,0)="as requiring nurse verification in BCMA while CPRS shows the order have been"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,58,0)="nurse verified. After some research it was determined that the BCMA and CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,59,0)="were out of sync regarding the nurse verification due to a hard error <SYNTAX>"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,60,0)="that happened when the Special Instructions field is edited for a complex"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,61,0)="order and a semi-colon character (;) was included in the instructions."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,63,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,64,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,65,0)="The code was changed to prevent the hard error <SYNTAX> whenever the user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,66,0)="includes a semi-colon (;) in the Special Instructions field for complex "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,67,0)="orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,68,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,69,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,70,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,71,0)="Changed the routine PSGOEE at line tag UPD+23 to perform a direct global set"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,72,0)="for the content of the SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS file (#8) in the UNIT DOSE sub-"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,73,0)="file (#55.06) in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) instead of using the Fileman"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,74,0)="DIE API. This code is used to copy the Special Instructions field content"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,75,0)="from one order to the other orders after edits in the case of complex orders."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,76,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,77,0)="3) INC17553085 - Error in MIN VistA: RPC+##^PSBCHKIV *PSBIVCHG BarCode"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,78,0)="                 Medication Administration (PSB)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,79,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,80,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,81,0)="Both test sites for PSJ*5*409 (Minneapolis and Madison) reported a hard error"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,82,0)="after the patch was released. It was confirmed the error was a direct side"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,83,0)="effect of the changes in PSJ*5*409 and that's the reason that patch was"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,84,0)="recalled (marked ENTERED IN ERROR on FORUM). It created some incomplete "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,85,0)="Activity Log records in the IV ORDER multiple (#55.01) of the PHARMACY "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,86,0)="PATINT file (#55) and that's what caused the error. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,88,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,89,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,90,0)="The code in the routine PSJHL4 added by PSJ*4*409 was changed from using"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,91,0)="Fileman ^DIE API call to doing a direct (hard-setting) global setting which"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,92,0)="prevents some Mumps cross-references from setting the corrupt entries in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,93,0)="IV Activity Log."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,94,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,95,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,96,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,97,0)="The code in the line tag ORC+6 was changed from using a ^DIE call to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",362,1,98,0)="performing direct sets to remove the nurse verification for the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,0)="421 SEQ #363^3211006.173338^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,0)="^^56^56^3211006"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,3,0)="1) INC18070852 - Clinic Not Setup for BCMA Issue not firing for IV orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,4,0)="   HITPS-8005                    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,6,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,7,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,8,0)="1) INC18070852 - Clinic Not Setup for BCMA Issue not firing for IV orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,9,0)="    HITPS-8005                    "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,11,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,12,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,13,0)="The West Haven VA Medical Center reported that whenever they tried to finish"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,14,0)="an Intravenous (IV) clinic order for an patient not admitted (outpatient)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,15,0)="using the Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] option it did not warn the user that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,16,0)="the clinic for the order is not setup for BCMA (shown below). For a Unit Dose"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,17,0)="(UD) clinic order the option properly displayed the warning below:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,19,0)="   Clinic CHY AQUATIC EXERCISE is not defined in the CLINIC DEFINITION"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,20,0)="   (#53.46) file."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,22,0)="   This order will NOT display in BCMA, unless the clinic is defined in the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,23,0)="   CLINIC DEFINITION (#53.46) file, and the SEND TO BCMA (#3) field is set"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,24,0)="   to YES."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,26,0)="   Please contact your Pharmacy ADPAC."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,27,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,28,0)="   Note: This issue is also being considered a Patient Safety Issue (PSI) and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,29,0)="         the number assigned by the Patient Safety team is HITPS-8005."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,31,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,32,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,33,0)="It was confirmed that the warning only displayed for UD clinic orders and not"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,34,0)="for IV clinic orders. The code was changed to also perform the check for IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,35,0)="clinic orders during finish and it will now display the message above when"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,36,0)="necessary."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,37,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,38,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,39,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,40,0)="The ENTRY ACTION field for the protocol PSJI LM FINISH did not contain a call"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,41,0)="to the API CWARN^PSJBCMA6 responsible for performing the check mentioned"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,42,0)="above. The ENTRY ACTION field was modified the following way:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,44,0)=" Before:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,45,0)=" -------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,46,0)=" S PSJINFIN=1 K ^TMP(""PSJINTER"",$J) D OVRDISF^PSGSICH2($G(DFN),$G(PSJORD),2)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,47,0)=" D FINISH^PSJLIFN D SETIVINT^PSGSICH1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,49,0)=" After:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,50,0)=" ------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,51,0)=" S PSJINFIN=1 K ^TMP(""PSJINTER"",$J) D CWARN^PSJBCMA6($G(DFN),$G(PSJORD)),"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,52,0)=" OVRDISF^PSGSICH2($G(DFN),$G(PSJORD),2) D FINISH^PSJLIFN D SETIVINT^PSGSICH1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,54,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,55,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",363,1,56,0)="HITPS-8005"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",364,0)="425 SEQ #364^3211028.091044^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",364,1,0)="^^2^2^3211028"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",364,1,1,0)="The description of this build can be found in the National Patch Module "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",364,1,2,0)="under PSJ*5.0*425."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",365,0)="416 SEQ #365^3211101.100307^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",365,1,0)="^^3^3^3211101"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",365,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",365,1,2,0)="INC1167333 Issue with Editing/Coping Other Print Info (field 11) of the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",365,1,3,0)="Complex Order in PSJ OE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,0)="420 SEQ #366^3211201.155509^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,0)="^^129^129^3211201"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,3,0)="1) INC17689657 - Schedule of SUPPER looks correct in Vista, but the HL7"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,4,0)="   HITPS-7946    message for medication order is for Sundays only instead"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,5,0)="                 of daily"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,6,0)="2) INC17223279 - clinic order allergy alert choosing dispense drug"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,8,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,9,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,10,0)="1) INC17689657 - Schedule of SUPPER looks correct in Vista, but the HL7"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,11,0)="   HITPS-7946    message for medication order is for Sundays only instead"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,12,0)="                 of daily"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,13,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,14,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,15,0)="The WM Jennings Bryan Dorn VA Medical Center reported that whenever they "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,16,0)="entered an inpatient order with the schedule SUPPER it looked and behaved"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,17,0)="correctly in VistA, however the HL7 message sent to PADE contained the wrong"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,18,0)="value for the 8th (~) field in the RXE segment which is used for 'Day-of-Week'"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,19,0)="schedules. Each digit represents one day of the week starting with Sunday thru"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,20,0)="Saturday. The code wrongly interpreted SUPPER as SU (short for Sunday) and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,21,0)="set the first digit to 1 which was interpreted by the automated dispensing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,22,0)="cabinets as once every Sunday. This issue is also being considered a Patient"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,23,0)="Safety Issue (PSI) and the number assigned by the Patient Safety team is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,24,0)="HITPS-7946."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,26,0)="  ..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,27,0)="  ORC|NW|100034|27U||CM||||202105280839|520824666~TEST~OUTPAT~F|520824666~TESO"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,28,0)="  RXE|240~SUPPER&1900~~2021052808~20210627180~~0~10000000|841~DOCUSATE CA 240M"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,29,0)="  RXR|PO~ORAL~99PSR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,30,0)="  ..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,31,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,32,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,33,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,34,0)="Patch PSO*7*405 addressed a similar issues for schedules WEEKLY and MONTHLY,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,35,0)="which were both interpreted as WE (Wed) and MO (Monday). Instead of fixing"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,36,0)="just specific instances of samples that can create the problem the solution"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,37,0)="will not try to translate any other schedule that does not match one of the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,38,0)="following: SU, MO, TU, WE, TH, FR and SA. In addition, it will require for"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,39,0)="all schedules separated by dashes (e.g., MO-WE-FR) that all pieces match one"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,40,0)="of the week days abbreviation. If this condition is not met, the software will"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,41,0)="send all zeros (00000000) to PADE for the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,42,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,43,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,44,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,45,0)="The logic for the $$DOWSTR API in the routine PSJPDCLV was completely"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,46,0)="re-written to exclude any schedule as day-of-week schedule unless all the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,47,0)="dash (-) pieces in the schedule match one of the seven days abbreviation: SU,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,48,0)="MO, TU, WE, TH, FR and SA. If any value is different than one of these "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,49,0)="abbreviations the processing stops and 00000000 is returned."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,50,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,51,0)="2) INC17223279 - clinic order allergy alert choosing dispense drug"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,53,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,54,0)="-------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,55,0)="The Martinez VA Medical Center reported that When finishing a clinic order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,56,0)="without a chosen dispense drug the duplicate drug alert is randomly selecting"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,57,0)="a dispense drug associated with the Orderable Item and displaying it as the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,58,0)="dispensed drug associated with the pending order, which is incorrect. In other "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,59,0)="words, when you have a pending clinic order without a dispense drug selected"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,60,0)="and you try to finish or enter a new order through the Inpatient Order Entry"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,61,0)="[PSJ OE] option or that will cause a duplicate order check or a drug-drug"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,62,0)="order check the drug name displayed for the pending clinic order is misleading"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,63,0)="because it arbitrarily selects one of the drugs associated with the Orderable"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,64,0)="Item on the order (apparently the last one) and displays it as the actual drug"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,65,0)="for the clinic order. In the example below, when the user tried to enter or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,66,0)="finish an order for WARFARIN 2MG TAB the pending clinic order in the duplicate"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,67,0)="drug check below shows the dispense drug WARFARIN 7.5MG TAB U/D, however the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,68,0)="pending clinic order does not have any dispense drug selected."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,69,0)="  ..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,70,0)="  Now Processing Enhanced Order Checks! Please wait..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,72,0)="  Press Return to continue..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,73,0)="  ==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,74,0)="  This patient is already receiving the following INPATIENT and/or OUTPATIENT"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,75,0)="  order(s) for a drug in the same therapeutic class(es) as WARFARIN 2MG TAB"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,76,0)="  U/D: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,78,0)="           Clinic Order: WARFARIN 7.5MG TAB U/D (PENDING)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,79,0)="               Schedule: BID"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,80,0)="                 Dosage: 7MG"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,81,0)="   Requested Start Date: JUN 05, 2021@09:00"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,82,0)="              Stop Date: ********"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,83,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,84,0)="  Class(es) Involved in Therapeutic Duplication(s): Oral Anticoagulants,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,85,0)="     Antiplatelet Drugs-excluding ASA 325 mg and below, Antiplatelet"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,86,0)="     and Antithrombotic Drugs (Selected Group 2) "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,87,0)="  ==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,88,0)="  ..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,90,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,91,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,92,0)="The displaying of a pending clinic order was changed to display only the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,93,0)="Orderable Item name and its dosage form when the order does not have a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,94,0)="dispense drug selected. Below is how the same duplicate order check above"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,95,0)="will display after the patch is installed:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,96,0)="  ..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,97,0)="  Now Processing Enhanced Order Checks! Please wait..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,99,0)="  Press Return to continue..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,100,0)="  ==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,101,0)="  This patient is already receiving the following INPATIENT and/or OUTPATIENT"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,102,0)="  order(s) for a drug in the same therapeutic class(es) as WARFARIN 2MG TAB"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,103,0)="  U/D: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,105,0)="           Clinic Order: WARFARIN TAB (PENDING)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,106,0)="               Schedule: BID"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,107,0)="                 Dosage: 7MG"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,108,0)="   Requested Start Date: JUN 05, 2021@09:00"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,109,0)="              Stop Date: ********"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,111,0)="  Class(es) Involved in Therapeutic Duplication(s): Oral Anticoagulants,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,112,0)="     Antiplatelet Drugs-excluding ASA 325 mg and below, Antiplatelet"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,113,0)="     and Antithrombotic Drugs (Selected Group 2) "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,114,0)="  ==========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,115,0)="  ..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,116,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,117,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,118,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,119,0)="Created a local API called $$CLNORDDN in the routine PSJCLNOC to return the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,120,0)="drug name for a pending clinic order. If the clinic order has a selected "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,121,0)="dispense drug selected the name for the dispense drug will be returned by the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,122,0)="API, if not, the API will retrieve the orderable item name and dosage form"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,123,0)="and will concatenate them and return as the name to be used for drug-drug or"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,124,0)="duplicate order check messages. Then changed code in DISP2+13 to use this API"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,125,0)="for displaying the clinic order drug name."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,127,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,128,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",366,1,129,0)="HITPS-7946 (INC17689657)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,0)="422 SEQ #367^3220105.121206^17"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,0)="^^15^15^3220105"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,1,0)="Description:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,2,0)="============"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,4,0)="This patch addresses the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,6,0)="Associated ticket(s):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,7,0)="====================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,9,0)="1. INC15531625 - Pharmacy Package Delay in pulling up the pending "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,10,0)="                 inpatient medication order queue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,11,0)="                 (Non-Verified/Pending Orders)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,12,0)="         INC17772912 (Duplicate) - delays with Pending Inpatient Orders "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,13,0)="2. INC17835358 - Non-verified/pending orders summary not accurate"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,14,0)="3. INC17835358 - Clinic Meds are not being counted under Clinic "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",367,1,15,0)="                      location"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,0)="427 SEQ #368^3220601.141042^86"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,0)="^^58^58^3220601"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,3,0)="1. Patch Medication Renewal Issue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,5,0)="Associated ticket(s):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,6,0)="====================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,8,0)="1.      INC18413351 - Patch Medication Renewal Issue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,11,0)="Associated NSR(s):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,12,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,13,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,15,0)="Participating Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,16,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,17,0)="TBD"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,19,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,20,0)="============================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,21,0)="HITPS-8027"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,24,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,25,0)="==========================================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,27,0)="1.      Patch Medication Renewal Issue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,29,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,30,0)="   -------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,31,0)="Inpatient patch medication renewals display an incorrect administration "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,32,0)="time. When renewing an order in CPRS that has a schedule to give every x "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,33,0)="number of days, the expected first dose may display the incorrect date.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,34,0)="The issue is seen when renewing in CPRS and when processing the order in "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,35,0)="Inpatient Order Entry, the user selects to edit the Admin Time before "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,36,0)="accepting it. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,39,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,40,0)="   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,41,0)="The problem is that the start date of the original order doesn't exist "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,42,0)="during pharmacy processing.  This is due to the original start in the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,43,0)="NON-VERIFIED ORDERS file #53.1 not being filed correctly when renewing in "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,44,0)="CPRS.  The order is finished correctly with appropriate start and stop "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,45,0)="dates and the only issue appears to be that the expected first dose "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,46,0)="displays with a wrong date.  The issue is also only seen when renewing "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,47,0)="the order at a time of day prior to the admin time.  The correction is to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,48,0)="modify routine PSJHL7 so that the original start date and stop time is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,49,0)="filed to the NON-VERIFIED ORDERS file #53.1.  Previous to this patch the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,50,0)="START DATE/TIME & STOP DATE/TIME were set to null by RENEW^PSJHL7."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,53,0)="   Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,54,0)="   ---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,55,0)="Code changes to PSJHL7:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,56,0)="   - Added newing of PSGNESD & PSGNEFD at RENEW+1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,57,0)="   - Set PSGNESD to $P(ND2,U,2) and PSGNEFD=$P(ND2,U,4) at RENEW+6"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",368,1,58,0)="   - Removed setting PSGNESD & PSGNEFD to null at RENEW+12"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",369,0)="432 SEQ #369^3220627.143237^86"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,0)="434 SEQ #370^3220728.115952^86"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,0)="^^65^65^3220728"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,1,0)="Description:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,2,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,5,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,7,0)="1) INC21365566 - Issue with the quit command (i.e. up carat ""^"")"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,8,0)="                 not working as expected in Backdoor Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,9,0)="                 PSJ OE for IV order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,11,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,12,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,13,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,16,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,17,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,18,0)="1) INC21365566 - Issue with the quit command (i.e. up carat ""^"")"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,19,0)="                 not working as expected in Backdoor Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,20,0)="                 PSJ OE for IV order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,22,0)="Problem 1: "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,23,0)="---------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,24,0)="It was discovered when entering an IV order in Backdoor Pharmacy in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,25,0)="PSJ OE, some of the prompts are not working as expected when the user"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,26,0)="tries to quit using the up carat ""^"". There are 3 prompts that have been"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,27,0)="identified as not working as expected when the user tries to quit. All"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,28,0)="other prompts are working as expected when the user quits, which is to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,29,0)="return the user to the ""Select IV TYPE:"" prompt. The 3 prompts that are"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,30,0)="not working as expected when the user tries to quit using the up carat"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,31,0)="""^"", occur immediately after the ""REMARKS:"" prompt. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,32,0)="See below:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,35,0)="    ***************************** WARNING *******************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,36,0)="    **            If OTHER PRINT INFO exceeds 60 characters,           **"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,37,0)="    **  'Instructions too long. See Order View or BCMA for full text.' **"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,38,0)="    **      will print on the IV label instead of the full text.       **"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,39,0)="    *********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,43,0)="Type <Enter> to continue or '^' to exit:   (""^"" does not work)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,45,0)="OTHER PRINT INFO:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,46,0)="  Edit? NO//   (""^"" does not work)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,50,0)="     Select one of the following:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,52,0)="          Y         Yes"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,53,0)="          N         No"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,55,0)="Flag the Other Print Info (Yes/No):   (""^"" does not work)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,58,0)="Resolution 1:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,59,0)="------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,60,0)="It was discovered that the logic for these prompts did not contain the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,61,0)="check to see if the user entered the up carat ""^"" to quit. Two routines"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,62,0)="required modifications; PSJBCMA5 and PSJUTL:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,64,0)="PSJBCMA5 in the EDITOPI+5 and EDITOPI+7 tag was modified to check for the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",370,1,65,0)="quit. PSJUTL in the ENBCMA+5 tag was modified to check for the quit."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",371,0)="431 SEQ #371^3220919.155749^90"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",371,1,0)="^^5^5^3220919"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",371,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",371,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",371,1,3,0)="During patient merge, if the ""TO"" entry in the PHARMACY PATIENT (#55) "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",371,1,4,0)="file has no prior intravenous (IV) or unit dose (UD) orders, the ""zero"" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",371,1,5,0)="node for each will be built without the sub-file number. "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",372,0)="399^3221005.145508^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",372,1,0)="^^11^11^3221005"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",372,1,1,0)="The Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) Graphical User Interface "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",372,1,2,0)="(GUI) v32 is an enhancement release. This patch (PSJ*5*399) is a part of"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",372,1,3,0)="that enhancement release."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",372,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",372,1,5,0)="This patch provides the needed functionalities to support the following "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",372,1,6,0)="NSR:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",372,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",372,1,8,0)="20100101: Indication on all Prescriptions and Medication Orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",372,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",372,1,10,0)="For a complete listing of patches included in this release, please refer "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",372,1,11,0)="to the CPRS GUI v32 Release Notes."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",373,0)="435 SEQ #373^3221025.135858^90"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",373,1,0)="^^4^4^3221025"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",373,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",373,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",373,1,3,0)="Comments do not display in the delimited format of the PADE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",373,1,4,0)="Transaction Report."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,0)="430 SEQ #374^3230118.161224^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,0)="^^34^34^3230118"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,1,0)="1. INC20912180 - COPYING IV ORDER AND ADJUSTING START/STOP DELETES "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,2,0)="                 THE ORDER"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,4,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,5,0)="   -------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,6,0)="When copying an IV order and editing the stop date, the message 'Order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,7,0)="deleted.' can be displayed and once the stop date is edited, the message "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,8,0)="...copying......Order deleted. is displayed at the end of Accepting the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,9,0)="order.  It makes it seem like the order has been deleted but it is not."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,12,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,13,0)="   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,14,0)="Editing the start or stop date drops processing logic into DEL55^PSIVORE2"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,15,0)="and deletes the order stub from the Pharmacy Patient file (#55).  The"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,16,0)="'order deleted' message is conditionally filtered out from displaying if"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,17,0)="this is a stubbed record so the first time the start or stop date is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,18,0)="edited no message is displayed.  Editing the start or stop date again"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,19,0)="fails to determine that the message should not be displayed.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,21,0)="The delete message should not be displayed during this copy process.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,23,0)="The logic in DEL55^PSIVORE2 is modified to quit out when there is no "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,24,0)="stub, this occurs after the stub has already been deleted by a previous "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,25,0)="edit to the start or stop date.  This prevents any delete messages from "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,26,0)="displaying while copying an order.  Without this conditional quit the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,27,0)="only thing that occurred was the delete message, no other process took "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,28,0)="place."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,31,0)="   Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,32,0)="   ---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,33,0)="The following line of code is added at DEL55+2^PSIVORE2 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",374,1,34,0)="I $D(^PS(55,DFN,""IV"",+ON55,0))=0 Q "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,0)="426 SEQ #375^3230201.160406^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,0)="^^106^106^3230201"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,3,0)="1) INC20355923-HITP-8866 - Medication order activated by pharmacy and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,4,0)="   verified by nursing, but not able to give in BCMA as it is acting like"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,5,0)="   it isn't after Renewal Complex Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,7,0)="   INC22900561(d)-HITPS-8861"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,9,0)="2) INC20555433 - Pharmacy Hold not setting Nurse Verify when ON/OFF action in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,10,0)="                 pharmacy."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,11,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,12,0)="3) INC23152064 - MOCHA alert scrolled off the screen when a med with no"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,13,0)="                 GCNSEQNO"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,15,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,16,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,17,0)="1) INC20355923-HITP-8866 - Medication order activated by pharmacy and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,18,0)="   verified by nursing, but not able to give in BCMA as it is acting like"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,19,0)="   it isn't after Renewal Complex Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,20,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,21,0)="   INC22900561(d)-HITPS-8861"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,23,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,24,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,25,0)="The Togus VA Medical Center reported that nurse verification was reset in BCMA"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,26,0)="after the order expired. It was confirmed that once an inpatient order expired"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,27,0)="the software was removing the BCMA verification information while in CPRS the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,28,0)="order remained verified."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,30,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,31,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,32,0)="The software was changed to not remove the nurse verification in BCMA when the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,33,0)="order is expired."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,35,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,36,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,37,0)="The line of code at ORC+8^PSJHL4 was modified to avoid resetting the Nurse"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,38,0)="Verification information when a expiration messages (PSOC=""SS"") is received"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,39,0)="from CPRS. In addition, a new API was created in PSJUTL3 called DELNV to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,40,0)="remove the BCMA Nurse verification because it was used to address the issue"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,41,0)="below."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,42,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,43,0)="2) INC20555433 - Pharmacy Hold not setting Nurse Verify when ON/OFF action in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,44,0)="                 pharmacy."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,46,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,47,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,48,0)="It was reported that nurse verification was reset in CPRS when an order is"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,49,0)="placed or removed from hold through the Inpatient Pharmacy application"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,50,0)="while in BCMA the order remains nurse verified."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,52,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,53,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,54,0)="The software was changed to remove the nurse verification in BCMA when the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,55,0)="order is placed or removed from Hold."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,57,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,58,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,59,0)="Included code at HOK+7^PSGOEH1 and HOK+11^PSGOEH0 (for Unit Dose orders), and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,60,0)="HOLD+4^PSIVOE (for IV orders) to remove the BCMA Nurse verification (call to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,61,0)="DELNV^PSJUTL3) when an order is placed or removed from hold."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,62,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,63,0)="3) INC23152064 - MOCHA alert scrolled off the screen when a med with no"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,64,0)="                 GCNSEQNO"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,66,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,67,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,68,0)="Rocky Mountain Regional VA Medical Center reported that sometimes the Order"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,69,0)="Checks alerts (example below) displayed on the screen does not present a"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,70,0)="prompt for the user to hit <RET> continue, for example, after reading the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,71,0)="alert. Instead, it hangs for 2 seconds and disappears from the screen, which"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,72,0)="requires the user to scroll up on the terminal emulator in order to view"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,73,0)="the error message. It was observed by the reporting user that this happened"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,74,0)="when the dispense drug was matched to an NDF VA Product without and GCNSEQNO"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,75,0)="field with no value."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,77,0)="  Order Check Message Example:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,78,0)="  ---------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,79,0)="  Order Checks could not be done for Drug: FERROUS BISGLYCINATE 90MG CAP,ORAL,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,80,0)="  please complete a manual check for Drug Interactions, Duplicate Therapy and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,81,0)="  appropriate Dosing.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,83,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,84,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,85,0)="The software was written to only pause when the display of the alert message"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,86,0)="above would display at the bottom of the screen. A change was made to always"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,87,0)="pause (as shown below) after the message above is displayed independently"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,88,0)="where in the screen the message is displayed. T"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,90,0)="  Order Check Message Example:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,91,0)="  ---------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,92,0)="  Order Checks could not be done for Drug: FERROUS BISGLYCINATE 90MG CAP,ORAL,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,93,0)="  please complete a manual check for Drug Interactions, Duplicate Therapy and"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,94,0)="  appropriate Dosing.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,96,0)="  Press Return to continue..."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,98,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,99,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,100,0)="The lines DRUGERR+8 and DRUGERR+18 were modified to remove the condition that"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,101,0)="the position had to be at the bottom of the screen for the [Press Return to"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,102,0)="continue...] prompt to be displayed. The command to wipe off the screen was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,103,0)="also removed at both lines. Furthermore, the line tag PAUSE^PSJLMUT1 was "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,104,0)="modified to remove the setting of the DIR(""?"") because it was causing the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,105,0)="""Press Return to continue..."" to display 3 times after the user typed"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",375,1,106,0)="anything different than <RET> or ""^""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,0)="437 SEQ #376^3230228.120702^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,0)="^^64^64^3230228"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,1,0)="1. CLINIC MEDICATIONS ORDER SENT TO IV PACKAGE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,3,0)="Associated ticket(s):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,4,0)="====================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,6,0)="1. INC22909170 - Order placed in an outpatient clinic location sent "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,7,0)="   erroneously to IV medications package"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,10,0)="Associated NSR(s):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,11,0)="=================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,12,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,14,0)="Participating Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,15,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,16,0)="TBD"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,18,0)="Patient Safety Issues (PSIs):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,19,0)="============================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,22,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,23,0)="==========================================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,25,0)="1. INC22909170 - Order placed in an outpatient clinic location sent "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,26,0)="                 erroneously to IV medications package "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,28,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,29,0)="   -------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,30,0)="   A complex Clinic Medications order using an IV medication is entered in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,31,0)="   CPRS and finished and accepted in Inpatient Order Entry.  The orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,32,0)="   are now flagged as inpatient Infusion orders instead of Clinic Infusion"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,33,0)="   orders. After accepting the second part of the complex order the Visit"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,34,0)="   Location is missing in Vista, the finished orders are now in the IV "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,35,0)="   Package, the orders no longer appear under the Clinic location on the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,36,0)="   profile and Visit File #100 now shows the Orders with DIALOG PSJI OR"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,37,0)="   PAT FLUID OE.  The issue was found to be due to the APPOINTMENT"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,38,0)="   DATE/TIME field (#139) of the IV multiple (#55.01) in the PHARMACY"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,39,0)="   PATIENT file  (#55).  This appears to only be an issue with complex"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,40,0)="   clinic medication orders for an IV medication.  Noncomplex clinic"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,41,0)="   medication orders for an IV medication does have the field populated"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,42,0)="   and correctly displays as a Clinic Infusion in CPRS and on the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,43,0)="   Inpatient Medication profile under the Clinic."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,46,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,47,0)="   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,48,0)="   Routine PSJCOMV is modified to populate the APPOINTMENT DATE/TIME field"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,49,0)="   (#139) of the IV multiple (#55.01) in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55). "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,54,0)="   Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,55,0)="   ---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,56,0)="   The following code is added at line IV+8^PSJCOMV:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,58,0)="   S:+$G(P(""APPT"")) $P(^TMP(""PSJCOM"",$J,+ON,""DSS""),U,2)=P(""APPT"")"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,60,0)="   This will populate the DSS node piece 2 of the ^TMP ""PSJCOM"" global "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,61,0)="   that will end up in the APPOINTMENT DATE/TIME field (#139) of the IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,62,0)="   multiple (#55.01) in the PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) and in variable"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,63,0)="   ORAPPT where it is used (in routine IV^ORMPS1) to determine the DIALOG"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",376,1,64,0)="   for the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",377,0)="429 SEQ #377^3230228.124052^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",377,1,0)="^^1^1^3230228"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",377,1,1,0)="INC21176679: Error in complex orders related to Self-Med edit field (7)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",378,0)="407 SEQ #378^3230323.122019^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",378,1,0)="^^9^9^3230323"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",378,1,1,0)="INC11595511 - Unauthorized Access to IV Room File (#59.5)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",378,1,2,0)="---------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",378,1,3,0)="If the Coverage Timing for any IV Type (Admixtures, Chemotherapy, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",378,1,4,0)="Hyperal, Piggyback or Syringe) in the IV Room file (#59.5) and a user is "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",378,1,5,0)="using that IV Room in backdoor pharmacy-related functionality, they may "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",378,1,6,0)="be warned ""Manufacturing Time(s) missing for 'IV type'"" and then asked "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",378,1,7,0)="""Would you like to edit this IV room?"". If user answers ""yes"", they are "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",378,1,8,0)="allowed to edit/update that IV Room without the requirement for the PSJI "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",378,1,9,0)="MGR security key. See the Patch Description on FORUM for more details."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,0)="433 SEQ #379^3230414.113401^90"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,0)="^^47^47^3230414"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,1,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,2,0)="==========================================="
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,4,0)="1. INC21776729 - Complex order renewal Stop Date not matching "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,5,0)="                 between CPRS and Inpatient Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,7,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,8,0)="   -------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,9,0)="When renewing a complex order with the AND conjunction in CPRS and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,10,0)="processing it in Inpatient Pharmacy and editing the STOP DATE before "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,11,0)="accepting any order in the complex set of orders, the STOP DATE does not "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,12,0)="get updated in CPRS.  The problem is that an HL7 message is not sent to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,13,0)="CPRS after the STOP DATE is filed into PHARMACY PATIENT file #55.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,14,0)="Several lines after an HL7 message is sent to CPRS from routine PSJOEA1, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,15,0)="there is a call to UPDREN^PSGOER made where the following fields can be "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,16,0)="updated in file #55; VERIFYING NURSE (#16), DATE VERIFIED BY NURSE (#17), "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,17,0)="STATUS (#28), STOP DATE/TIME (#34), ADMIN TIMES (#41), FOLLOWING ORDER "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,18,0)="(#105), REASON FOR FOLLOWING ORDER (#107), ORDERABLE ITEM (#108), and sub "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,19,0)="record LAST RENEW [55.6114DA].  After UPDREN^PSGOER completes, another "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,20,0)="call to send updates via HL7 message to CPRS does not occur.  Any of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,21,0)="these fields that are needed in CPRS may not be up to date in the ORDER "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,22,0)="file (#100), most notably fields STATUS (#5) and STOP DATE (#22)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,25,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,26,0)="   ----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,27,0)="A new call to send an HL7 message to CPRS is added after UPDREN^PSGOER "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,28,0)="completes.  This allows all the data in PHARMACY PATIENT file (#55) to be "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,29,0)="updated when this HL7 message is sent for the current order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,32,0)="   Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,33,0)="   ---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,34,0)="In routine PSJOEA1, the call to routine UNL^PSSLOCK that unlocks the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,35,0)="ORDER file (#100) is moved from after the HL7 message is sent at line "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,36,0)="CHK+30"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,37,0)=" ....D EN1^PSJHL2(DFN,""SC"",PSGORDR) ;,UNL^PSSLOCK(DFN,PSGORDR) move below "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,38,0)="p433"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,39,0)="This is necessary so that the call to EN1^PSJHL2 at line CHK+38^PSJOEA1 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,40,0)="will have the ORDER file (#100) locked after UPDREN^PSGOER is called at "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,41,0)="line CHK+37^PSJOEA1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,42,0)=" ...D "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,43,0)="UPDREN^PSGOER(DA,$P(ND14,U),$P(ND14,U,3),$P(ND14,U,4),$P($G(^PS(53.1,+PSJO"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,44,0)=",.2)),U,3),$P(ND14,U,2))"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,45,0)=" ...D EN1^PSJHL2(DFN,""SC"",PSGORDR) ;p433"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,46,0)="The unlock of the ORDER file (#100) is now at line CHK+42^PSJOEA1"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",379,1,47,0)=" .. D UNL^PSSLOCK(DFN,PSGORDR) ;Move unlock to here p433"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",380,0)="439 SEQ #380^3230509.173306^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",380,1,0)="^^9^9^3230509"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",380,1,1,0)="INC25661636 - Certain IV orders not displaying correctly in CPRS and VistA"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",380,1,2,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",380,1,3,0)="When a continuous IV order is entered in CPRS with a free text infusion"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",380,1,4,0)="rate that has a decimal with or without a preceding 0, the system thinks"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",380,1,5,0)="that this is a numeric infusion rate for some reason and adds the ""ml/hr"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",380,1,6,0)="suffix. This causes issues when we're also trying to designate the number"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",380,1,7,0)="of labels to print with the ""@"" sign because it does not recognize this in"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",380,1,8,0)="pharmacy finishing and removes the ""@"" along with the number that follows."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",380,1,9,0)="See the Patch Description on FORUM for more details."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",381,0)="438 SEQ #381^3230627.14114^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",381,1,0)="^^6^6^3230627"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",381,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",381,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",381,1,3,0)="The VistA PADE HL7 interface is sending a zero for the priority on all IV"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",381,1,4,0)="orders instead of the actual priority from the pharmacy patient file.  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",381,1,5,0)="This, in turn, prevents differentiation of routine and stat/asap orders"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",381,1,6,0)="via the interface feed."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",382,0)="440 SEQ #382^3230627.14171^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",382,1,0)="^^4^4^3230627"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",382,1,1,0)="INC26226397 - Vista inpatient orders in Renewed status are able to be "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",382,1,2,0)="marked as ""Not to be Given"" which then in turn marks the pending new "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",382,1,3,0)="order to also be marked as ""Not to be Given"". Only orders in an Expired "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",382,1,4,0)="or Discontinued status should be able to be marked as ""Not to be Given""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",383,0)="372^3230629.170402^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",383,1,0)="^^1^1^3230629"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",383,1,1,0)="See FORUM for patch description."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",384,0)="442 SEQ #384^3230817.11203^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",384,1,0)="^^7^7^3230817"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",384,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",384,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",384,1,3,0)="It was reported that when using the Day-of-the-Week (DOW) schedule builder"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",384,1,4,0)="in CPRS when ordering an inpatient medication, CPRS properly displays the"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",384,1,5,0)="ward administration time after entering and accepting the order. However,"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",384,1,6,0)="after the order is signed, the ward administration time is being "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",384,1,7,0)="overwritten by the standard administration time."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",385,0)="441 SEQ #385^3231016.154959^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",385,1,0)="^^5^5^3231016"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",385,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",385,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",385,1,3,0)="When editing a unit dose order which has a duration and attempting to "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",385,1,4,0)="exit with ""^"", the user is given an erroneous ""Is this correct"" prompt "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",385,1,5,0)="and not allowed to answer ""Y"" or ""N""."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",386,0)="446 SEQ #386^3231016.15502^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",386,1,0)="^^2^2^3231016"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",386,1,1,0)="INC27709580 - CPRS continuous infusion orders with a rate of less than "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",386,1,2,0)="one create an improperly formatted rate ending in ""ml/hr ml/hr"""
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",387,0)="448 SEQ #387^3240201.164707^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",387,1,0)="^^4^4^3240201"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",387,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one issue:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",387,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",387,1,3,0)="An incorrect units per dose value might be saved for a unit dose order if "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",387,1,4,0)="the dosage was edited before verifying the order."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,0)="451 SEQ #388^3240517.102234^89"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,0)="^^69^69^3240517"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,2,0)="This patch addresses the following two incident tickets:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,4,0)="1. INC30646734 - VISTA PSJ UNDEFINED ERROR AFTER COPYING UD ORDER WITH "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,5,0)="REMOVAL REQUIRED."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,7,0)="2. INC31233823 - VISTA PSJ UNDEFINED ERROR AFTER EDITING START TIME "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,8,0)="BEFORE ACCEPTING UD ORDER REQUIRING REMOVAL."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,11,0)="Problem(s):"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,12,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,13,0)="1. INC30646734 - Albany VA Medical Center (NY) reported an undefined "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,14,0)="error that occurs in VistA backdoor pharmacy (inpatient order entry), "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,15,0)="when you copy an active unit dose order, that has a transdermal patch "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,16,0)="orderable item field ""Prompt for removal in BCMA"",  set to ""Removal "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,17,0)="Period Required Prior to Next Administration"", edit the start date/time, "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,18,0)="and then choose to edit the admin time,  say NO to the prompt ""Is this "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,19,0)="correct"", then enter in a new ADMIN time. The system hard errors and "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,20,0)="kicks you out of Vista. Hard error is <UNDEFINED>DONE+3^PSGOE91 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,21,0)="*PSGOEEF(41)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,23,0)="2. INC31233823 - Albany VA Medical Center (NY) reported an undefined "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,24,0)="error that occurs in VistA backdoor pharmacy (inpatient order entry) when "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,25,0)="editing the start date before accepting an active unit dose order "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,26,0)="(without a copy). Hard error is <UNDEFINED>DONE+3^PSGOE81 *PSGOEEF(39)."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,29,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,30,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,31,0)="1. INC30646734 - Adding a check for data in the PSGOE91 routine DONE tag "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,32,0)="for the PSGOEEF(PSGF2) variable.  In some cases, there is no data and the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,33,0)="variable is not defined therefore causing a hard error and kicking the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,34,0)="user out.  Adding the check will allow the logic to continue to process "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,35,0)="the UD order without a hard error.  Also adding a change to the PSGOE91 "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,36,0)="routine A10 tag, so the date/time will display appropriately. Currently "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,37,0)="it shows the correct date and then an up caret with the internal date."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,39,0)="2. INC31233823 - Adding a check for data in the PSGOE81 routine for the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,40,0)="PSGOEEF(PSGF2) variable.  In some cases, there is no data and the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,41,0)="variable is not defined therefore causing a hard error and kicking the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,42,0)="user out.  Adding the check will allow the logic to continue to process "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,43,0)="the UD order without a hard error."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,46,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,47,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,48,0)="1. INC30646734 - Routine PSGOE91 is modified at line to check for data in "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,49,0)="the variable causing the undefined error, and correcting the format of "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,50,0)="the date."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,52,0)="Line DONE+3"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,53,0)="   I PSGOEE G:'PSGOEEF(PSGF2) @BACK S PSGOEE=PSGOEEF(PSGF2)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,54,0)="To"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,55,0)="   I PSGOEE G:'$G(PSGOEEF(PSGF2)) @BACK S PSGOEE=PSGOEEF(PSGF2)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,57,0)="Line A10+6"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,58,0)="   I X="""",PSGSD W ""  ""_PSGSDN G DONE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,59,0)="To"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,60,0)="   I X="""",PSGSD W ""  ""_$P(PSGSDN,""^"") G DONE"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,63,0)="2. INC31233823 - Routine PSGOE81 is modified to check for data in the "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,64,0)="variable causing the undefined error."
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,66,0)="Line DONE+3"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,67,0)="   I PSGOEE G:'PSGOEEF(PSGF2) @BACK S PSGOEE=PSGOEEF(PSGF2)"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,68,0)="To"
^DIC(9.4,77,22,17,"PAH",388,1,69,0)="   I PSGOEE G:'$G(PSGOEEF(PSGF2)) @BACK S PSGOEE=PSGOEEF(PSGF2)"
