^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,2,0)="Date for an AOU. An example of the error follows: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,4,0)="Select Automatic Replenishment Option: SUPervisor's Menu "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,6,0)="Select Supervisor's Menu Option: SET Up AR/WS (Build Files) "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,8,0)="Select Set Up AR/WS (Build Files) Option: INA "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,9,0)="    1    Inactivate AOU                    "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,10,0)="    2    Inactivate AOU Stock Item "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,12,0)="CHOOSE 1-2: 1  Inactivate AOU "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,14,0)="Enter AOU Inactivation Dates "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,16,0)="Select PHARMACY AOU STOCK AREA OF USE (AOU): LYN'S MED ROOM "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,18,0)="INACTIVE DATE: T@1300  (JUN 13, 1996@13:00)"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,20,0)="...One moment, please...  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,22,0)="There are items in this AOU that are currently active.  You may, at this"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,23,0)="time, inactivate all of them as of JUN 13,1996@13:00.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,25,0)="Do you want to do this? Yes//   (Yes) "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,27,0)="Now inactivating all currently active items as of JUN 13,1996@13:00??.?? "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,28,0)=".??.??.??."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,29,0)="<UNDEF>+18^PSGWAOUI:::4:0: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,31,0)="The error occurs because the date/time response for the inactive date"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,32,0)="field of the AOU is entered into the inactivation date field for the items"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,33,0)="in the AOU and this field does not allow the entry of time.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,34,0)="(MWV-0696-20736) "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,36,0)="This patch will correct this problem.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,38,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,39,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,41,0)="The following routine is included in this patch.  The second line of the "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,42,0)="routine will look like: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,44,0)="<tab>;;2.3; Automatic Replenishment/Ward Stock ;;**[patch list]**;4 JAN 94"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,47,0)="             CHECK^XTSUMBLD results: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,49,0)="Routine Name           Before Patch       After Patch    Patch List "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,51,0)=" PSGWAOUI                8589667            8683714          7 "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,54,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,55,0)=" =========================="
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,56,0)="  This patch may be loaded during regular work hours without"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,57,0)="  disruption to users.  It only affects users of the Automatic"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,58,0)="  Replenishment/Ward Stock software.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,59,0)="  Installation will take less than 5 minutes.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,60,0)="  1.  Use the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE option on the PackMan menu and "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,61,0)="      answer NO to the question 'Shall I preserve what is on disk in a "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,62,0)="      separate back-up message ?'.  Answer YES to the prompt 'Want to "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,63,0)="      Continue with Load? YES//' "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,64,0)="  2.  Review your mapped set.  If the routine listed in the "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,65,0)="      ROUTINE INFORMATION section is mapped, it should be removed "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,66,0)="      from the mapped set at this time. The patched routine is not on"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,67,0)="      the recommended mapping list.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,68,0)="  3.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,69,0)="      the Installation menu.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,70,0)="  4.  From this menu, you may elect to use the following options "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,71,0)="      (when prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter PSGW*2.3*7): "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,72,0)="      a.  Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,73,0)="          message of any routines exported with the patch.  It will NOT "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,74,0)="          backup any other changes such as DDs or templates.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,75,0)="      b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System  - this option will "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,76,0)="          allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,77,0)="          is installed.  It compares all components of the patch "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,78,0)="          (routines, DDs, templates, etc.).  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,79,0)="      c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,80,0)="          allow you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,81,0)="          the transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,82,0)="  5.  Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,83,0)="       PSGW*2.3*7.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,84,0)="  6.  When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options and Options? "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,85,0)="      YES//', respond YES.  When prompted to select the options you"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,86,0)="      would like to place out of order, enter the following: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,87,0)="         PSGW AOU INACTIVATION     Inactivate AOU "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,88,0)="  7.  MSM sites:  Please ensure you answer YES when asked if you want "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,89,0)="      to move the routines to other systems and indicate the appropriate "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,90,0)="      CPUs.  Alternately, you can wait until the installation is"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,91,0)="      complete and move the routines listed in the ROUTINE INFORMATION"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,92,0)="      section to all systems.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,93,0)="  8.  If routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,94,0)="      returned to the mapped set once the installation has run to"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,95,0)="      completion.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,97,0)="Routine Information:"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,98,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,99,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",1,1,100,0)="Routine Name:  PSGWAOUI"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,0)="8 SEQ #8^2960926^1"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^105^105^2960926"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,1,0)="An undef error was reported when entering a date/time for the Inactive"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,2,0)="Date for an AOU. Patch 7 was issued to correct this problem and it"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,3,0)="worked for dates other than the first nine days of a month.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,4,0)="will correct patch 7 and work for all dates in a month.  An example of the"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,5,0)="error follows:"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,7,0)="Select Automatic Replenishment Option: SUPervisor's Menu "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,9,0)="Select Supervisor's Menu Option: SET Up AR/WS (Build Files) "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,11,0)="Select Set Up AR/WS (Build Files) Option: INA "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,12,0)="    1    Inactivate AOU                    "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,13,0)="    2    Inactivate AOU Stock Item "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,15,0)="CHOOSE 1-2: 1  Inactivate AOU "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,17,0)="Enter AOU Inactivation Dates "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,19,0)="Select PHARMACY AOU STOCK AREA OF USE (AOU): LYN'S MED ROOM "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,21,0)="INACTIVE DATE: 8 1@1200  (AUG 01, 1996@12:00)"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,23,0)="...One moment, please...  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,25,0)="There are items in this AOU that are currently active.  You may, at this"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,26,0)="time, inactivate all of them as of AUG 1,1996@12:00.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,28,0)="Do you want to do this? Yes//   (Yes) "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,30,0)="Now inactivating all currently active items as of AUG 1,1996@12:00??.?? "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,31,0)=".??.??.??."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,32,0)="<UNDEF>+18^PSGWAOUI:::4:0: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,34,0)="The error occurs because the date/time response for the inactive date"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,35,0)="field of the AOU is entered into the inactivation date field for the items"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,36,0)="in the AOU and this field does not allow the entry of time.  Patch 7"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,37,0)="extracted the first 11 characters of the date/time chosen and this"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,38,0)="included the ""@"" sign on dates for the first nine days of a month.  This"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,39,0)="patch will take the first piece of the date/time entered with the ""@"" as"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,40,0)="the delimiter."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,41,0)="(MWV-0696-20736, ALN-0896-10244, HIN-0896-40381) "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,43,0)="This patch will correct this problem.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,45,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,46,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,48,0)="The following routine is included in this patch.  The second line of the "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,49,0)="routine will look like: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,51,0)="<tab>;;2.3; Automatic Replenishment/Ward Stock ;;**[patch list]**;4 JAN 94"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,54,0)="             CHECK^XTSUMBLD results: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,56,0)="Routine Name           Before Patch       After Patch    Patch List "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,58,0)=" PSGWAOUI                8683714            8672951          7,8 "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,61,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,62,0)=" =========================="
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,63,0)="  This patch may be loaded during regular work hours without"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,64,0)="  disruption to users.  It only affects users of the Automatic"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,65,0)="  Replenishment/Ward Stock software.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,66,0)="  Installation will take less than 5 minutes.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,67,0)="  1.  Use the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE option on the PackMan menu and "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,68,0)="      answer YES to the prompt 'Want to Continue with Load? YES//'"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,69,0)="  2.  Review your mapped set.  If the routine listed in the "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,70,0)="      ROUTINE INFORMATION section is mapped, it should be removed "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,71,0)="      from the mapped set at this time. The patched routine is not on"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,72,0)="      the recommended mapping list.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,73,0)="  3.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,74,0)="      the Installation menu.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,75,0)="  4.  From this menu, you may elect to use the following options "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,76,0)="      (when prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter PSGW*2.3*8): "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,77,0)="      a.  Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,78,0)="          message of any routines exported with the patch.  It will NOT "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,79,0)="          backup any other changes such as DDs or templates.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,80,0)="      b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System  - this option will "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,81,0)="          allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,82,0)="          is installed.  It compares all components of the patch "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,83,0)="          (routines, DDs, templates, etc.).  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,84,0)="      c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,85,0)="          allow you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,86,0)="          the transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,87,0)="  5.  Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,88,0)="       PSGW*2.3*8."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,89,0)="  6.  When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options and Options? "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,90,0)="      YES//', respond YES.  When prompted to select the options you"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,91,0)="      would like to place out of order, enter the following: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,92,0)="         PSGW AOU INACTIVATION     Inactivate AOU "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,93,0)="  7.  MSM sites:  Please ensure you answer YES when asked if you want "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,94,0)="      to move the routines to other systems and indicate the appropriate "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,95,0)="      CPUs.  Alternately, you can wait until the installation is"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,96,0)="      complete and move the routines listed in the ROUTINE INFORMATION"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,97,0)="      section to all systems.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,98,0)="  8.  If routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,99,0)="      returned to the mapped set once the installation has run to"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,100,0)="      completion.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,101,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,102,0)="Routine Information:"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,103,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",2,1,105,0)="Routine Name:  PSGWAOUI"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,0)="9^2970221^1"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^66^66^2970221"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="A problem was reported when running the Cost Report Per AOU [PSGW COST"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,2,0)="PER AOU].  The summary pages were not printing."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,4,0)="This patch will correct this problem.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,6,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,7,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,9,0)="The following routine is included in this patch.  The second line of the "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,10,0)="routine will look like: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,12,0)="<tab>;;2.3; Automatic Replenishment/Ward Stock ;;**[patch list]**;4 JAN 94"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,13,0)=" "
