^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,19,0)=" PSGWCPA1                14134524           14170611          9 "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,22,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,23,0)=" =========================="
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,24,0)="  This patch may be loaded during regular work hours without"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,25,0)="  disruption to users.  It only affects users of the Automatic"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,26,0)="  Replenishment/Ward Stock software.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,27,0)="  Installation will take less than 1 minute.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,28,0)="  1.  Use the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE option on the PackMan menu and "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,29,0)="      answer YES to the prompt 'Want to Continue with Load? YES//'"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,30,0)="  2.  Review your mapped set.  If the routine listed in the "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,31,0)="      ROUTINE INFORMATION section is mapped, it should be removed "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,32,0)="      from the mapped set at this time. The patched routine is not on"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,33,0)="      the recommended mapping list.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,34,0)="  3.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,35,0)="      the Installation menu.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,36,0)="  4.  From this menu, you may elect to use the following options "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,37,0)="      (when prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter PSGW*2.3*9): "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,38,0)="      a.  Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,39,0)="          message of any routines exported with the patch.  It will NOT "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,40,0)="          backup any other changes such as DDs or templates.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,41,0)="      b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System  - this option will "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,42,0)="          allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,43,0)="          is installed.  It compares all components of the patch "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,44,0)="          (routines, DDs, templates, etc.).  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,45,0)="      c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,46,0)="          allow you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,47,0)="          the transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,48,0)="  5.  Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,49,0)="       PSGW*2.3*9."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,50,0)="  6.  When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options and Options? "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,51,0)="      YES//', respond YES.  When prompted to select the options you"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,52,0)="      would like to place out of order, enter the following: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,53,0)="         PSGW COST PER AOU      Cost Report Per AOU  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,54,0)="  7.  MSM sites:  Please ensure you answer YES when asked if you want "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,55,0)="      to move the routines to other systems and indicate the appropriate "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,56,0)="      CPUs.  Alternately, you can wait until the installation is"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,57,0)="      complete and move the routines listed in the ROUTINE INFORMATION"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,58,0)="      section to all systems.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,59,0)="  8.  If routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,60,0)="      returned to the mapped set once the installation has run to"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,61,0)="      completion.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,63,0)="Routine Information:"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,64,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",3,1,66,0)="Routine Name:  PSGWCPA1"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,0)="11 SEQ #10^2970401^1"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^77^77^2970401"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="A problem was reported when using the option [PSGW ON-DEMAND"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,2,0)="NURSING EDIT] Enter/Edit Nurses' On-Demand Request (80 column).  The"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,3,0)="problem occurred when the user selected the item.  If there were multiple"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,4,0)="items to pick from the one selected was not always the one shown. (NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,5,0)="MEM-0397-70742, SLC-0397-51202, BAY-0397-30702, IOW-0397-41379,"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,6,0)="ALX-0397-71625)"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,7,0)="A similar problem was reported when using the option [PSGW ON-DEMAND"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,8,0)="DELETE] Delete an On-Demand Request. (NOIS STX-0397-71762)"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,10,0)="This patch will correct these problems.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,11,0)=" "
