^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,56,0)="  5.  Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,57,0)="       PSGW*2.3*11."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,58,0)="  6.  When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options and Options? "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,59,0)="      YES//', respond YES.  When prompted to select the options you"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,60,0)="      would like to place out of order, enter the following: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,61,0)="         PSGW ON-DEMAND NURSING EDIT      Enter/Edit Nurses' On-Demand"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,62,0)="         Request (80 column)"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,63,0)="         PSGW ON-DEMAND DELETE      Delete an On-Demand Request"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,64,0)="  7.  MSM sites:  Please ensure you answer YES when asked if you want "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,65,0)="      to move the routines to other systems and indicate the appropriate "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,66,0)="      CPUs.  Alternately, you can wait until the installation is"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,67,0)="      complete and move the routines listed in the ROUTINE INFORMATION"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,68,0)="      section to all systems.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,69,0)="  8.  If routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,70,0)="      returned to the mapped set once the installation has run to"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",4,1,71,0)="      completion.  "
