^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,29,0)="  This patch may be loaded during regular work hours without"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,30,0)="  disruption to users.  It only affects users of the Automatic"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,31,0)="  Replenishment/Ward Stock software.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,32,0)="  Installation will take less than 1 minute.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,33,0)="  1.  Use the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE option on the PackMan menu and "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,34,0)="      answer YES to the prompt 'Want to Continue with Load? YES//'"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,35,0)="      This option will load the KIDS package onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,36,0)="  2.  Review your mapped set.  If any routine listed in the "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,37,0)="      ROUTINE INFORMATION section is mapped, it should be removed "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,38,0)="      from the mapped set at this time. The patched routine is not on"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,39,0)="      the recommended mapping list.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,40,0)="  3.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,41,0)="      the Installation menu.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,42,0)="  4.  From this menu, you may elect to use the following options "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,43,0)="      (when prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter PSGW*2.3*12): "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,44,0)="      a.  Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,45,0)="          message of any routines exported with the patch.  It will NOT "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,46,0)="          backup any other changes such as DDs or templates.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,47,0)="      b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System  - this option will "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,48,0)="          allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,49,0)="          is installed.  It compares all components of the patch "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,50,0)="          (routines, DDs, templates, etc.).  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,51,0)="      c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,52,0)="          allow you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,53,0)="          the transport global.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,54,0)="  5.  Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,55,0)="       PSGW*2.3*12."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,56,0)="  6.  When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options and Options? "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,57,0)="      YES//', respond YES.  When prompted to select the options you"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,58,0)="      would like to place out of order, enter the following: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,59,0)="      PSGW AOU INVENTORY INPUT           Input AOU Inventory"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,60,0)="  7.  MSM sites:  Please ensure you answer YES when asked if you want "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,61,0)="      to move the routines to other systems and indicate the appropriate "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,62,0)="      CPUs.  Alternately, you can wait until the installation is"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,63,0)="      complete and move the routines listed in the ROUTINE INFORMATION"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,64,0)="      section to all systems.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,65,0)="  8.  If routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,66,0)="      returned to the mapped set once the installation has run to"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,67,0)="      completion.  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,69,0)="Routine Information:"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,70,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",5,1,72,0)="Routine Name:  PSGWEDI1"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,0)="13^2971006^1"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,1,0)="^^12^12^2971006"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,1,1,0)=" A problem has been reported with the Standard Cost Report [PSGW STANDARD"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,1,2,0)="COST REPORT].  The Standard Cost Report lists the cost for items in one"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,1,3,0)="AOU, several AOUs, all AOUs, or an inventory group.  This cost represents"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,1,4,0)="the dollar amount needed to bring each item from zero to its maximum"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,1,5,0)="stock level."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,1,6,0)="The TOTAL COST field was computed by multiplying the item's stock level by"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,1,7,0)="the AR/WS conversion factor found in the DRUG file (#50) and then by price"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,1,8,0)="per dispense unit found in the DRUG file.  It was reported that if the"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,1,9,0)="AR/WS conversion factor was anything other than one (1) then the Total"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,1,10,0)="Cost for that item was off by a factor of the AR/WS conversion factor. The"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,1,11,0)="AR/WS conversion factor will no longer be used in the calculation for the"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",6,1,12,0)="total cost in this report.  This patch corrects this problem."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",7,0)="14^2980527^1"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^3^3^2980527"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",7,1,1,0)="  This patch will delete the data dictionary and the data from the"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",7,1,2,0)="subfile 59.41, PHARMACISTS field (#6) of the INPATIENT SITE file (#59.4)."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",7,1,3,0)="This will cleanup the reference to the USER file (#3)."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",8,0)="15^2990210^1"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",8,1,0)="^^8^8^2990210"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",8,1,1,0)="This patch corrects two problems."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",8,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",8,1,3,0)="1. It updates the AR/WS STATS FILE (#58.5), removing potential extraneous"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",8,1,4,0)="nodes from the data dictionary.  These extraneous nodes may cause errors"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",8,1,5,0)="when running Pharmacy Benefits Management extracts."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",8,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",8,1,7,0)="2. It corrects a formatting problem when using the option Print an"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",8,1,8,0)="On-Demand Report by Date/AOU (80 column) [PSGW ON-DEMAND PRINT]."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",9,0)="16 SEQ #16^3031107^1"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",9,1,0)="^^3^3^3031107"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",9,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",9,1,2,0)="This patch will prevent the error trap when selecting Item in the PSGW "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",9,1,3,0)="Usage report."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",10,0)="17 SEQ #17^3050401^1"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^3^3^3050401"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",10,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",10,1,2,0)="This patch will allow selection of Non-VA meds (X) to be selected for "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",10,1,3,0)="Ward Stock."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,0)="18 SEQ #18^3170802.1211^54"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^57^57^3170802"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,3,0)="The report option Print an On-Demand Report by Date/AOU (80 column) [PSGW"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,4,0)="ON-DEMAND PRINT] was incorrectly filtering entries to be printed on the"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,5,0)="report according to the date range selected by the user."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,7,0)="Associated CA SDM Ticket(s):"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,8,0)="============================"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,9,0)="1. I10479329FY16  PSGW ON-DEMAND PRINT calculates wrong time"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,11,0)="Associated NSRs:"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,12,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,13,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,15,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,16,0)="Participating Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,17,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,18,0)="TBD"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,20,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,21,0)="Remedy Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,22,0)="================"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,23,0)="1. I10479329FY16  PSGW ON-DEMAND PRINT calculates wrong time"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,24,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,25,0)="PSPO:"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,26,0)="===== "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,27,0)="N/A"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,28,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,29,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,30,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,31,0)="When the user ran the report option Print an On-Demand Report by Date/AOU"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,32,0)="(80 column) [PSGWON-DEMAND PRINT] and selected a date range that "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,33,0)="contained "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,34,0)="a specific time (MMDDYY@HHMM) for either the BEGINNING or ENDING date"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,35,0)="prompts the report filter did not work correctly causing the report to"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,36,0)="include entries outside the date/time range and to also exclude entries"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,37,0)="within the date/time range selected."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,39,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,40,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,41,0)="Modified the routine PSGWODP to correctly set the filter variables for the"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,42,0)="date/time range so that each entry screened are correctly included or"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,43,0)="excluded from the report."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,46,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,47,0)="---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,48,0)="a. At the line BDT^PSGWODP the variable BDT, which holds the BEGINNING "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,49,0)="date"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,50,0)="   range value, was being set with BDT=BDT-.1. This was wrong because the"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,51,0)="   the time (HHMM) is accepted. This was corrected to BDT=BDT-.00001"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,52,0)="a. At the line EDT^PSGWODP the variable EDT, which holds the ENDING date"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,53,0)="   range value, was being set with EDT=EDT+.3. This was also wrong because"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,54,0)="   the time (HHMM) is accepted. Furthermore, this variable only needs to "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,55,0)="be"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,56,0)="   reset if a specific time was not entered. The setting of this variable "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",11,1,57,0)="   was changed to S:EDT'[""."" EDT=EDT+.24."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",12,0)="19 SEQ #19^3180501.142403^54"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^1^1^3180501"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="Add Allowed Ward Stock Level to On-Demand request and Report & AUTO Print"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",13,0)="21b^3210322"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",13,1,0)="^^5^5^3210322"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",13,1,1,0)="Backup of PSGW*2.3*21 on Mar 22, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",13,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",13,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",13,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",13,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",14,0)="21 SEQ #20^3210322.124837^17"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",14,1,0)="^^3^3^3210322"
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",14,1,1,0)="This patch addresses Automatic replenishment/ward stock (AR/WS) reports "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",14,1,2,0)="that do not correctly calculate the prices for drugs that are defined "
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH",14,1,3,0)="with a AR/WS AMIS CONVERSION NUMBER greater than 1."
^DIC(9.4,81,22,2.3,"PAH","B",9,3)=""
