^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,179,0)="Documentation Retrieval:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,180,0)="========================"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,181,0)="Sites may retrieve documentation in one of the following ways:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,182,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,183,0)=" 1.  The preferred method is to FTP the files from "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,184,0)="     download.vista.domain.ext, which will transmit the files from the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,185,0)="     first available FTP server."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,187,0)=" 2.  Sites may also elect to retrieve documentation directly from a "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,188,0)="     specific server as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,189,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,190,0)="     Albany          ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,191,0)="     Hines           ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,192,0)="     Salt Lake City  ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,193,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,194,0)=" 3.  Documentation can also be retrieved from the VistA Documentation "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,195,0)="     Library (VDL) on the Internet at the following address,"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,196,0)="     http://www.domain.ext/vdl."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,197,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,198,0)="The documentation distribution includes:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,200,0)="    FILE NAME                             DESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,201,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,202,0)="    ---------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,203,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,204,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,205,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,206,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,207,0)="Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,208,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,209,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,210,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,211,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,212,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,213,0)="       ================INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS ================="
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,214,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,215,0)="To avoid disruptions, these patches should be installed when users are "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,216,0)="not on the system and during non-peak hours.  Of particular concern would "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,217,0)="be the items below."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,218,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,219,0)="    1.  Do not install the patch when ECME claims are being generated"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,220,0)="        by the BPS Nightly Background Job option [BPS NIGHTLY"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,221,0)="        BACKGROUND JOB].  Wait for this job to finish or complete the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,222,0)="        installation before this job starts."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,223,0)="    2.  Do not install the patch when prescriptions are being "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,224,0)="        transmitted to CMOP.  Wait for the CMOP transmission to finish "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,225,0)="        or complete the installation before the transmission starts.  "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,226,0)="        Check with Pharmacy Service or your pharmacy Automated Data"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,227,0)="        Processing Application Coordinator (ADPAC) to find out when"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,228,0)="        CMOP transmissions occur."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,229,0)="    3.  In addition, note that you will be prompted to disable the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,230,0)="        following options during the installation:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,231,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,232,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,233,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,234,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,235,0)="Install Time - Approximately 30 minutes"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,236,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,237,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,238,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,239,0)="1.  OBTAIN PATCHES"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,240,0)="    --------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,241,0)="    Patches PSX*2*65 and PSS*1*131 will be sent to your system upon"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,242,0)="    release from the National Patch Module."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,243,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,244,0)="    Obtain the host file BPS_1_7_PSO_IB.KID, which contains the following"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,245,0)="    three patch installs:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,246,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,247,0)="        BPS*1.0*7"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,248,0)="        PSO*7.0*289"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,249,0)="        IB*2.0*384"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,250,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,251,0)="     Sites can retrieve VistA software from the following FTP addresses."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,252,0)="     The preferred method is to FTP the files from:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,253,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,254,0)="                    download.vista.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,255,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,256,0)="     This will transmit the files from the first available FTP server."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,257,0)="     Sites may also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,258,0)="     server as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,259,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,260,0)="       Albany                  ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,261,0)="       Hines                   ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,262,0)="       Salt Lake City          ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,263,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,264,0)="     The BPS_1_7_PSO_IB.KID host file is located in the anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,265,0)="     directory.  Use ASCII Mode when downloading the file."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,266,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,267,0)="2.  LOAD TRANSPORT GLOBAL FOR STAND-ALONE PATCHES"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,268,0)="    ---------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,269,0)="    For patches PSX*2*65 and PSS*1*131, choose the PackMan message"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,270,0)="    containing each of these patches and invoke the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,271,0)="    PackMan option."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,272,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,273,0)="3.  START UP KIDS"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,274,0)="    -------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,275,0)="    Start up the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu option"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,276,0)="    [XPD MAIN]:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,277,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,278,0)="         Edits and Distribution ..."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,279,0)="         Utilities ..."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,280,0)="         Installation ..."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,281,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,282,0)="    Select Kernel Installation & Distribution System Option: INStallation"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,283,0)="                                                             ---"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,284,0)="         Load a Distribution"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,285,0)="         Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,286,0)="         Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,287,0)="         Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,288,0)="         Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,289,0)="         Restart Install of Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,290,0)="         Unload a Distribution"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,291,0)="         Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,292,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,293,0)="    Select Installation Option:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,294,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,295,0)="4.  RUN OPTIONAL INSTALLATION OPTIONS FOR STAND-ALONE PATCHES"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,296,0)="    ---------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,297,0)="    From the Installation menu, you may select to use the following"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,298,0)="    options (when prompted for the INSTALL NAME, enter each of the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,299,0)="    stand-alone patches (PSX*2.0*65 and PSS*1.0*131)):"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,300,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,301,0)="    a.  Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,302,0)="        message of any routines exported with this patch.  It will not"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,303,0)="        backup any other changes such as Database Definitions (DD's) or"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,304,0)="        templates."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,305,0)="    b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,306,0)="        allow you to view all changes that will be made when this patch"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,307,0)="        is installed.  It compares all components of this patch"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,308,0)="        (routines, DD's, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,309,0)="    c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,310,0)="        you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,311,0)="        transport global."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,312,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,313,0)="5.  INSTALL STAND-ALONE PATCHES"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,314,0)="    ---------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,315,0)="    This is the step to start the installation of this KIDS patch.  This"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,316,0)="    will need to be run for each of the stand-alone patches (PSX*2*65 and"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,317,0)="    PSS*1*131)."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,318,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,319,0)="    a.  Choose the Install Package(s) option to start the patch"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,320,0)="        install."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,321,0)="    b.  When prompted for the ""Select INSTALL NAME:"", enter the patch"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,322,0)="        name."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,323,0)="    c.  When prompted ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,324,0)="        YES//"" answer NO."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,325,0)="    d.  When prompted ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,326,0)="        Options, and Protocols? YES//"" answer NO."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,327,0)="    e.  When prompted, ""Device: Home//"" respond with the correct device."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,328,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,329,0)="6.  LOAD TRANSPORT GLOBAL FOR MULTI-BUILD"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,330,0)="    -------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,331,0)="    After the installation of the stand-alone patches is complete, return"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,332,0)="    to the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,333,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,334,0)="    From the Installation menu, select the Load a Distribution option."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,335,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,336,0)="    When prompted for ""Enter a Host File:"", enter the full directory path"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,337,0)="    where you saved the host file BPS_1_7_PSO_IB.KID (e.g.,"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,338,0)="    SYS$SYSDEVICE:[ANONYMOUS]BPS_1_7_PSO_IB.KID)."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,339,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,340,0)="    When prompted for ""OK to continue with Load? NO//"", enter ""YES."""
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,341,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,342,0)="    The following will display:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,343,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,344,0)="      Loading Distribution..."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,345,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,346,0)="        BPS PSO IB BUNDLE 3.0"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,347,0)="        BPS*1.0*7"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,348,0)="        PSO*7.0*289"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,349,0)="        IB*2.0*384"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,350,0)="      Use INSTALL NAME: BPS PSO IB BUNDLE 3.0 to install this"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,351,0)="      Distribution."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,352,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,353,0)="7.  RUN OPTIONAL INSTALLATION OPTIONS FOR MULTI-BUILD"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,354,0)="    -------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,355,0)="    From the Installation menu, you may select to use the following"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,356,0)="    options (when prompted for the INSTALL NAME, enter"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,357,0)="    BPS PSO IB BUNDLE 3.0):"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,358,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,359,0)="    a.  Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,360,0)="        message of any routines exported with this patch.  It will not"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,361,0)="        backup any other changes such as DD's or templates."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,362,0)="    b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,363,0)="        allow you to view all changes that will be made when this patch"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,364,0)="        is installed.  It compares all components of this patch"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,365,0)="        (routines, DD's, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,366,0)="    c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,367,0)="        you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,368,0)="        transport global."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,369,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,370,0)="8.  INSTALL MULTI-BUILD"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,371,0)="    -------------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,372,0)="    This is the step to start the installation of this KIDS patch.  This"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,373,0)="    will need to be run for the BPS PSO IB BUNDLE 3.0."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,374,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,375,0)="    a.  Choose the Install Package(s) option to start the patch"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,376,0)="        install."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,377,0)="    b.  When prompted for the ""Select INSTALL NAME:"", enter BPS PSO IB"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,378,0)="        BUNDLE 3.0."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,379,0)="    c.  For the BPS*1*7 patch, when prompted ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,380,0)="        Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES//""  enter YES unless your"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,381,0)="        system does this in a nightly TaskMan process."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,382,0)="    d.  For the PSO*7*289 patch, when prompted ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,383,0)="        Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES//""  enter YES unless your"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,384,0)="        system does this in a nightly TaskMan process."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,385,0)="    e.  When prompted ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,386,0)="        install? YES//""  enter NO."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,387,0)="    f.  When prompted ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options,"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,388,0)="        and Protocols? YES//""  enter YES."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,389,0)="    g.  When prompted ""Enter options you wish to mark as 'Out Of"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,390,0)="        Order':""  enter the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,391,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,392,0)="    h.  When prompted ""Enter protocols you wish to mark as 'Out Of"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,393,0)="        Order':""  enter <return>."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,394,0)="    i.  When prompted ""Delay Install (Minutes):  (0-60): 0//""  enter an"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,395,0)="        appropriate number of minutes to delay the installation in "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,396,0)="        order to give users enough time to exit the disabled options"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,397,0)="        before the installation starts."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,398,0)="    j.  When prompted ""Device: Home//""  respond with the correct device."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,399,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,400,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,401,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,402,0)="The BPS post-install routine delivered with BPS*1*7 will do the tasks"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,403,0)="listed below.  This post-install will be tasked and may take several"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,404,0)="hours to run.  The post-install routine BPS01P7 is being left on the "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",58,1,405,0)="system after the install.  They will be deleted with a future patch."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,0)="68 SEQ #60^3100217.104815^17"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,0)="^^32^32^3100217"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,1,0)="This patch is part of the FY09-Q3 Enhancement release and must be"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,2,0)="installed along with Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0 patch PSO*7*324, which"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,3,0)="addresses PSI-07-181 (PSPO# 865) - Remedy Ticket # HD208961. A new mail"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,4,0)="group named PSX EXTERNAL DISPENSE ALERTS is created in this patch to"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,5,0)="support the functionality provided by patch PSO*7*324."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,7,0)="When a Consolidated Mail Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP) prescription with a"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,8,0)="status of Transmitted or Retransmitted is discontinued by a background"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,9,0)="job other than Outpatient Pharmacy options, e.g. Computerized Patient"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,10,0)="Record System V. 1.0 (CPRS) or Registration V. 5.3 packages, then an"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,11,0)="email notifying that a prescription was just discontinued for that Rx"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,12,0)="will be sent to the new PSX EXTERNAL DISPENSE ALERTS mail group. If no"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,13,0)="recipients are defined in the new mail group, then the email alert will be"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,14,0)="sent to PSXCMOPMGR key holders. The email alert will inform the group that"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,15,0)="the CMOP status for the Rx just discontinued was either Transmitted or"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,16,0)="Retransmitted as seen in the example below."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,18,0)="  Subj: TROY - DC Alert on CMOP Rx 123456789 TRANSMITTED  [#90494]"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,19,0)="  03/03/09@17:37 8 lines"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,20,0)="  From: POSTMASTER  In 'IN' basket.   Page 1  *New*"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,21,0)="  ------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,22,0)="               Rx #: 123456789   Fill: 0"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,23,0)="            Patient: OUTPATIENT,DCONE (6660)"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,24,0)="               Drug: TAMOXIFEN CITRATE 10MG TABS"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,25,0)="          Rx Status: DISCONTINUED BY PROVIDER"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,26,0)="  Processing Status: TRANSMITTED to CMOP on 02/27/09"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,27,0)="           Provider: OPPROVIDER, PROV"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,29,0)="  ********    Please contact CMOP or take appropriate action    ********"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,31,0)="  Enter message action (in IN basket): Ignore//"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",59,1,32,0)="  ------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,0)="69 SEQ #61^3100624.155051^17"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,0)="^^33^33^3100624"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,1,0)="This patch modifies the CMOP v2.0 application as described below:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,3,0)="1. An entry was being added to the ECME LOG every time an Rx is evaluated"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,4,0)="for ECME claim submissions and the Rx was flagged for Bad Address. A"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,5,0)="modification was made to only allow the Rx to be evaluated for ECME claim"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,6,0)="submission if a Bad Address indicator is not present. "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,8,0)="2. There is a known issue where the system may not automatically resubmit"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,9,0)="all claims rejected due to a host processing error. A test facility found"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,10,0)="where the software did not resubmit an electronic pharmacy claim"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,11,0)="automatically when a claim rejected for a host processing error. The"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,12,0)="following day the prescription was transmitted to CMOP as anticipated and"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,13,0)="was filled. The claim did appear on the ECME User Screen so it could be"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,14,0)="manually resubmitted, which is the process facilities followed before this"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,15,0)="patch was installed.  Based upon analysis, this is an infrequent scenario"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,16,0)="(less than 1%) and will only occur in a particular set of circumstances."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,18,0)="Host processing errors are identified by reject codes M6, M8, NN, and 99."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,19,0)="The following conditions apply when this scenario occurs."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,21,0)="     a. The transmission of the Rx/fill will be delayed 1 day in hopes"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,22,0)="        that the host processing issues will be resolved."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,23,0)="     b. An activity log entry will be defined to state the date/time along"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,24,0)="        with a comment stating that the Rx/fill was left in suspense hold "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,25,0)="        due to a host processing error."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,26,0)="     c. This added functionality does not include the Pull Early from"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,27,0)="        Suspense function."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,29,0)="This issue has been corrected in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,31,0)="3.  The system was allowing rejected Tricare prescriptions to be sent to "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,32,0)="CMOP.  Tricare rejected prescriptions should be held in suspense until "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",60,1,33,0)="the reject has been resolved.  This patch corrects this issue. "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,0)="71 SEQ #62^3101207.110335^17"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,0)="^^15^15^3101207"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,1,0)="Currently in backdoor Pharmacy, all warning labels are printed."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,2,0)="However, when Prescription Warning labels are transmitted to the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,3,0)="Consolidated Mail Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP), there is a limit of 5"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,4,0)="warnings per prescription. CMOP has requested that all warning labels be"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,5,0)="sent with every prescription. This patch therefore allows more than five"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,6,0)="warnings per prescription to be transmitted to CMOP, and also allows"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,7,0)="warning text that is greater than 220 characters per warning."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,9,0)="Prescription Warning labels are currently transmitted to CMOP via Health"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,10,0)="Level Seven (HL7) messages in segment NTE|11|, with a limit of 220"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,11,0)="characters. This patch creates a continuation segment in NTE|11A| to"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,12,0)="contain the warning text that is greater than the initial 220 characters,"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,13,0)="up to an additional 220 characters. The continuation segment immediately"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,14,0)="follows the NTE|11| segment of the warning. This means all warning labels"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",61,1,15,0)="will be transmitted to CMOP."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",62,0)="73^3120216.140025^17"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",62,1,0)="^^1^1^3120216"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",62,1,1,0)="ePharmacy Phase 6"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,0)="70 SEQ #64^3120329.183601^17"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,0)="^^78^78^3120329"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,1,0)="This patch contains software modifications to the Consolidated Mail "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,2,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP) V. 2.0 application to support the Food and Drug"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,3,0)="Administration (FDA) Medication Guides - Increment 3 project. The project"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,4,0)="objective is to allow pharmacy staff to retrieve the FDA Medication Guide"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,5,0)="for prescription items that contain FDA approved information that can help"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,6,0)="patients avoid adverse events. The FDA requires that Medication Guides be"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,7,0)="included with certain prescribed drugs and biological products when the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,8,0)="Agency determines that:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,10,0)=" . Certain information is necessary to prevent serious adverse effects "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,11,0)=" . Patient decision-making should be advised by information about a known"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,12,0)="   serious side effect with a product, or "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,13,0)=" . Patient adherence to directions for the use of a product is essential"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,14,0)="   to its effectiveness. "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,16,0)="The features in the FDA Medication Guides project are being delivered in"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,17,0)="incremental releases. This patch is part of the Increment 3 release, which"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,18,0)="is the last planned release. The features included in this release are:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,20,0)=" . Ability to create and maintain a list of FDA Medication Guide printers"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,21,0)="   for a specific pharmacy division."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,23,0)=" . Automatic printing of FDA Medication Guide along with prescription "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,24,0)="   labels."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,26,0)=" . Ability to reprint the FDA Medication Guide when reprinting a "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,27,0)="   prescription label."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,29,0)=" . Ability to change the FDA Medication Guide printer at any point in the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,30,0)="   dispensing process, similar to changing the label printer."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,32,0)=" . Ability to reprint the FDA Medication Guide for any given prescription"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,33,0)="   fill or the latest FDA Mediation Guide available for the medication on"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,34,0)="   the prescription."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,35,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,36,0)=" . Identification on the label document that an FDA Medication Guide was"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,37,0)="   printed as well and needs to be collated to the documentation before"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,38,0)="   being handed over to the patient."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,40,0)=" . Changes to the prescription label activity logs showing which specific"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,41,0)="   FDA Medication Guide document printed along with the label."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,43,0)=" . Changes to the Consolidated Mail Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP) Event log"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,44,0)="   showing which specific FDA Medication Guide document was available "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,45,0)="   for the medication when the prescription fill was transmitted to CMOP."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,47,0)=" . Introduction of a PC based Java software component to enable the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,48,0)="   automatic printing of an FDA Medication Guide from within VistA. The"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,49,0)="   software does not require any direct user interaction. The software "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,50,0)="   identifies a request from VistA for a specific FDA Medication Guide"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,51,0)="   and automatically sends it to the FDA Medication Guide printer"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,52,0)="   selected by the user within VistA when dispensing the medication."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,54,0)=" . Ability to update the Windows network printer name for a specific"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,55,0)="   device through the Kernel application. Once the pharmacist selects a"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,56,0)="   printer to print the FDA Medication Guide Vista will retrieve the "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,57,0)="   Windows name for the printer and will pass it on to the Java"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,58,0)="   application responsible for printing the document."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,59,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,60,0)="Below is a list of all the applications involved in this release along"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,61,0)="with their patch number:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,62,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,63,0)="   APPLICATION/VERSION                                    PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,64,0)="   -----------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,65,0)="   CONSOLIDATED MAIL OUTPATIENT PHARMACY (CMOP) V. 4.0    PSX*2*70"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,66,0)="   NATIONAL DRUG FILE (NDF) V. 4.0                        PSN*4*264"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,67,0)="   OUTPATIENT PHARMACY (OP) V. 7.0                        PSO*7*367"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,68,0)="   KERNEL V. 8.0                                          XU*8*566"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,69,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,70,0)="The following modification is included in this patch (PSX*2*70):"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,72,0)="The process responsible for the transmission of prescriptions from Outpatient"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,73,0)="Pharmacy to CMOP will be modified to record the current FDA Medication Guide"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,74,0)="document name in the CMOP Event Log in the PRESCRIPTION file (#52) if one "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,75,0)="exists for the medication in the prescription being transmitted. Such "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,76,0)="information will be displayed within Outpatient Pharmacy application when the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,77,0)="user selects to view the CMOP Event Log for a specific prescription."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",63,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",64,0)="74^3140106.161656^17"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",64,1,0)="^^1^1^3140106"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",64,1,1,0)="EPHARMACY OPERATING RULES"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",65,0)="75 SEQ #66^3140715.122842^17"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",65,1,0)="^^8^8^3140715"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",65,1,1,0)="This patch modifies the Consolidate Mail Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP) v2.0 "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",65,1,2,0)="application as described below:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",65,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",65,1,4,0)="       1.  A correction was made to not have duplicate Notes and Comments "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",65,1,5,0)="(NTE)5 segments after a CMOP Re-Transmit option was performed"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",65,1,6,0)="       2.  A typo was corrected in the key description for PSXMAIL key"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",65,1,7,0)="       3.  A correction was made to not allow CMOP Controlled substance "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",65,1,8,0)="to be released from suspense early."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,0)="76 SEQ #67^3141105.123033^17"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,1,0)="^^12^12^3141105"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,1,1,0)="This patch modifies the Consolidate Mail Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP) v2.0 "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,1,2,0)="application as described below:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,1,4,0)="        1. A correction was made to make sure Bad Address Indicator(BAI) "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,1,5,0)="is for error messages in mailman, when the BAI is set"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,1,6,0)="        2. A correction was made to the Data Dictionary for the input "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,1,7,0)="transform and the description of The CMOP System file (550), fields were "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,1,8,0)="Non-CS Days to Transmit (#11) and CS Days to Transmit (#12)."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,1,9,0)="        3. A correction was mad to the CMOP User Manual to update the Drug"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,1,10,0)="Enter/Edit (PSS Drug Enter/Edit) option."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,1,11,0)="        4. A correction made to not duplicate Patient Address error"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",66,1,12,0)="message in Mailman messages"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",67,0)="77 SEQ #68^3160211.171429^54"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",67,1,0)="^^1^1^3160211"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",67,1,1,0)="HAPE EDI Revenue project - NCPDP Continuous Maintenance Standards"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",68,0)="78 SEQ #69^3160719.165534^54"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",68,1,0)="^^6^6^3160719"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",68,1,1,0)="This patch modifies the Consolidate Mail Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP) v2.0 "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",68,1,2,0)="application as described below:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",68,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",68,1,4,0)="       1.  A correction was made to have Controlled Substance Special "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",68,1,5,0)="                 Handle level 3 to be change to level 2 or 1 and put into "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",68,1,6,0)="                 Local suspense"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",69,0)="80 SEQ #70^3160819.161935^54"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",69,1,0)="^^5^5^3160819"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",69,1,1,0)="This patch modifies the Consolidate Mail Outpatient Pharmacy (CMOP) v2.0 "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",69,1,2,0)="application as described below:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",69,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",69,1,4,0)="     1. PSXR BATCH INQUIRY [View Transmission] Option was getting hung"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",69,1,5,0)="up when being run."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",70,0)="79^3160829.125628^54"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",70,1,0)="^^1^1^3160829"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",70,1,1,0)="MCCF ePharmacy Compliance Phase 3"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",71,0)="81^3171127.134855^54"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",71,1,0)="^^1^1^3171127"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",71,1,1,0)="MCCF EDI TAS EPHARMACY BUILD 2"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",72,0)="83^3180403.174342^54"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",73,0)="87^3200410.160808^70"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,0)="89 SEQ #75^3200514.165152^70"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,0)="^^34^34^3200514"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,1,0)="This patch changes the upper limit of the NON-CS DAYS TO TRANSMIT Field"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,2,0)="(#11) and the CS DAYS TO TRANSMIT Field (#12) of the CMOP SYSTEM File"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,3,0)="(#550) from 10 to 15 days."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,5,0)="The NON-CS DAYS TO TRANSMIT Field (#11) is the suggested maximum number of"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,6,0)="days to use as a print through date for the CMOP auto-transmission for"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,7,0)="non-controlled substances. It can be overwritten in the auto-transmission"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,8,0)="set-up, to a maximum of 15."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,10,0)="The CS DAYS TO TRANSMIT Field (#12) is the suggested maximum number of "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,11,0)="days to use as a print through date for the CMOP auto-transmission for"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,12,0)="controlled substances. It can be overwritten in the auto-transmission"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,13,0)="set-up, to a maximum of 15."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,16,0)="****NOTE****"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,17,0)="The change to the CMOP SYSTEM File (#550), NON-CS DAYS TO TRANSMIT Field "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,18,0)="(#11) and CS DAYS TO TRANSMIT Field (#12) may lead to additional NCPDP "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,19,0)="Reject 79 Refill Too Soon (RTS) claims."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,21,0)="If the claim submission returns a Refill Too Soon (79) reject, the label "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,22,0)="is NOT printed for the prescription and it is moved to the Refill Too "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,23,0)="Soon/DUR section of the patient Medication Profile screen until the user "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,24,0)="resolves the reject. The prescription will also display on the Third-Party"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,25,0)="Payer Reject Worklist. If the claim submission returns a Reject Resolution"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,26,0)="Required reject, the label is NOT printed for the prescription and it is"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,27,0)="moved to the Reject Resolution Required section of the Third-Party Payer"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,28,0)="Reject - Worklist."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,30,0)="Please search for additional guidance on the eRevenue Resources main "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,31,0)="landing page for Refill Too Soon. Guidance documents for COVID-19 Refill "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,32,0)="Too Soon Override. The landing page may be accessed at:  "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,33,0)="https://vaww.vashare.domain.ext/sites/eRevenueResources/Pages/HomePage.asp"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",74,1,34,0)="x"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",75,0)="90 SEQ #76^3201001.130015^17"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",75,1,0)="^^5^5^3201001"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",75,1,1,0)="It has been reported that when a controlled substance CMOP order is "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",75,1,2,0)="transmitted via option Print from Suspense file and then a subsequent "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",75,1,3,0)="non-controlled substance CMOP order is requested to be transmitted via "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",75,1,4,0)="the same option, the controlled substance order is transmitted instead of "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",75,1,5,0)="the non-controlled substance order."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",76,0)="91^3210913.110935^17"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,0)="94 SEQ #78^3211119.152642^17"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,0)="^^56^56^3211119"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,1,0)="This patch will resolve the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,3,0)="1) INC18186175 - NFL Stuck PSX resource"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,4,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,5,0)="Defect Tracking System Ticket(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,6,0)="--------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,7,0)="1) INC18186175 - NFL Stuck PSX resource"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,9,0)="Problem: "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,10,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,11,0)="The Castle Point VA Medical Center reported that its PSX Resource device was"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,12,0)="hung for hours in and they had to manually released and the process that was"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,13,0)="holding the device had to be terminated. The Clin1 researched the problem"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,14,0)="and determined that the sequence that caused the problem was this:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,15,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,16,0)="   1. The CMOP prescription release information arrives at the site in the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,17,0)="      form of a Mailman message that contains all prescriptions released by"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,18,0)="      CMOP. This message is sent to the S.PSXX CMOP SERVER recipient."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,20,0)="   2. Each line of the Mailman message is processed to reflect the release"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,21,0)="      event (e.g., Release date and CMOP information like Lot# is recorded,"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,22,0)="      3rd party billing is updated, etc.)"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,24,0)="   3. An existing 3rd party billing claim will be reversed and resubmitted if"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,25,0)="      the NDC from CMOP does not match the original sent to the 3rd party"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,26,0)="      payer when the prescription was transmitted to CMOP. "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,28,0)="   4. Some of these updates will cause ePharmacy (BPS) to call out to the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,29,0)="      Integrated Billing (IB) application to cancel a Bill."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,31,0)="   5. Depending on the update that the IB application performs it may"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,32,0)="      automatically create and send a Mailman message to its users."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,34,0)="   6. The creation of the Mailman message by IB is interfering with the"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,35,0)="      processing of the Mailman message sent from CMOP to the site. More "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,36,0)="      specifically, it changes the value of the variable XMZ that is used as"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,37,0)="      an index in the step #2 above to indicate which line is being processed."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,38,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,39,0)="   7. This caused the processing of the CMOP message to go into an infinite"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,40,0)="      loop and cause the problem reported by the site. "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,42,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,43,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,44,0)="A change was made to the processing of the CMOP Mailman message to protect"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,45,0)="the variable XMZ from being overwritten when other functionalities or"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,46,0)="applications are called."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,47,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,48,0)="Technical Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,49,0)="--------------------"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,50,0)="The FOR loop in the EN+3 line of the PSXVND routine was re-written to address"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,51,0)="two problems:"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,52,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,53,0)="   1. Protect the variable XMZ from being overwritten "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,55,0)="   2. Removed GOTO commands from inside the FOR loop and placed them outside"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",77,1,56,0)="      without changing the original logic"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",78,0)="92^3220119.155246^17"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",79,0)="93^3220808.171209^86"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",80,0)="97 SEQ #81^3221214.134144^89"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",80,1,0)="^^1^1^3221214"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",80,1,1,0)="See FORUM patch description."
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",81,0)="95^3240726.103911^89"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",82,0)="98 SEQ #83^3240903.103849^89"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",82,1,0)="^^1^1^3240903"
^DIC(9.4,82,22,2,"PAH",82,1,1,0)="See FORUM patch description."
