^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,143,0)="DENTDNJ          12975627         13031174        **15,23**"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,144,0)="DENTDNJ1         11752108         11992713        **15,23**"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,145,0)="DENTDNJ2          8570663          8654282        **15,23**"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,146,0)="DENTDNK           4344731          4698084        **15,23**"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,147,0)="DENTDNQ           9982353          9333763        **15,23**"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,148,0)="DENTEC           11806503         11894141         **23**"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,150,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,151,0)=" GENERAL INFORMATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,152,0)=" ===================                                                     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,153,0)=" This patch should be installed into your production UCI.  It can be"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,154,0)=" installed at anytime.  Install time is less than 10 minutes.          "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,155,0)=" This patch has 1 other patch dependency, patch 15.  No options need to be"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,156,0)=" disabled.  Users do not need to be logged off the system. If there are"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,157,0)=" any questions, your supporting CIOFO Customer Service Clinical 1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,158,0)=" team will address them."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,159,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,160,0)=" This Patch is created with Kernel V8 KIDS.  Follow these instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,161,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,162,0)=" 1) Use Packman option 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' to load the KIDS build "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,163,0)="     onto your system."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,164,0)=" 2) On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,165,0)="    option 'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' and verify that all"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,166,0)="    routines have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,167,0)=" 3) From the 'Installation' Menu of KIDS, use the option"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,168,0)="    'Install Package(s)'.  Select the package 'DENT*1.2*23' and proceed "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,169,0)="    with install."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,170,0)=" 4) If you are a MSM site move the routines to the other servers.       "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",4,1,171,0)=" 5) On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",5,0)="24 SEQ #23^2980318^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",5,1,0)="^^1^1^2980318"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",5,1,1,0)="Refer to the patch for the patch description."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",6,0)="25 SEQ #24^2990223^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",6,1,0)="^^1^1^2990223"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",6,1,1,0)="This is patch 25 of Dental."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",7,0)="26 SEQ #25^2990316^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",8,0)="27 SEQ #26^2990628^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",8,1,0)="^^1^1^2990628"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",8,1,1,0)="Refer to patch description."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",9,0)="28 SEQ #27^2991007^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",9,1,0)="^^1^1^2991007"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",9,1,1,0)="This is patch 28 of Dental version 1.2."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",10,0)="29 SEQ #28^2991019^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^1^1^2991019"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",10,1,1,0)="This is patch 29 of Dental version 1.2."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",11,0)="30^3010926^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^10^10^3010926"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="DENT*1.2*30 provides the integration of the vendor Document Storage"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",11,1,2,0)="Systems' (DSS) Dental Record Manager (DRM) product into the VistA Dental"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",11,1,3,0)="package.  One of the conditions of the national purchase of DRM was that"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",11,1,4,0)="the existing VEJDWPD module from DSS would be converted to the DENTV"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",11,1,5,0)="namespace and the files ^VEJD(19600.x) would be moved to ^DENT(228.x)."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",11,1,6,0)="The  original VEJDWPD package stored some data elements in the Dental"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",11,1,7,0)="History  file (#19600.1) that the Database Administrator considered"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",11,1,8,0)="duplicate data  (i.e., PCE data elements).  A post-init will move the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",11,1,9,0)="Dental History file to file# 228.1 and will remove those data elements in"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",11,1,10,0)="the process (required as a  condition for the national purchase)."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,0)="33 SEQ #30^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^31^31^3011210"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="Patch ICD*18.0*2 was released 11/2/2001.  That patch inactivated several ICD9"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,2,0)="codes used in the dental DENTAL CPT CODE MAPPING file (#228).  That file has a"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,3,0)="list of CPT procedures used in the dental DSS DRM application.  Those"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,4,0)="procedures have a default diagnosis associated with each procedure."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,6,0)="This patch consists of file 228 and a post-init routine."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,8,0)="It exports the file DENTAL CPT CODE MAPPING (#228) with updated diagnosis"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,9,0)="codes.  Specifically, there were 244 CDT3 codes mapped to diagnosis codes"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,10,0)="521.0 or 525.1 which were inactivated by the ICD*18*2 patch as of Oct 1, 2001"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,11,0)="    ICD9 code 521.0 will be remapped to 521.00"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,12,0)="    ICD9 code 525.1 will be remapped to 525.10"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,14,0)="The post-init will check three things:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,16,0)="1. It checks to see if all nationally export ADA codes are indeed in file"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,17,0)="   228.  A few sites have reported that one or two codes were not in their"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,18,0)="   file 228 even though it was exported."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,20,0)="2. The GUI option context, DENTV DSS DRM GUI, has the list of all the RPCs"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,21,0)="   that the DRM GUI may execute.  A few sites have reported that one or two"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,22,0)="   RPCs are not in the option even though they were exported.  The post-init"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,23,0)="   will ensure that all required RPCs are part of the option."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,25,0)="3. Because of the problem caused by ICD*18.0*2, the post-init will check"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,26,0)="   every CPT and ICD9 code in file 228 (both national codes and locally added"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,27,0)="   codes) for any problems.  A report will be displayed detailing any"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,28,0)="   problems found."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,30,0)="4. You will find any of these pertinent messages in the installation after"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",12,1,31,0)="   the line:   Running Post-Install Routine: POST^DENTVIP1."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,0)="32^3011210^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,0)="^^60^60^3011210"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,1,0)=" I.   v3.0 of the dentalmrm.exe switched two service conditions:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,2,0)="      environmental contaminants (or Persian Gulf) and ionizing radiation."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,3,0)="      Thus patients with these conditions ended up having action required"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,4,0)="      in PCE."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,6,0)=" II.  There was a problem with filing administrative times.  Some sites"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,7,0)="      would get the message unable to create record.  When the call to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,8,0)="      UPDATE^DIE was made to create a record in file 226, the Fileman call"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,9,0)="      failed if there were any required identifiers on fields .3,.4,.6,.9"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,11,0)=" III. If DENT*1.2*30 was installed in an account which did not have a"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,12,0)="      previous version of DRM (VEJDWPD versions), then the multiple field"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,13,0)="      19600 on file 220.5 was not installed and an error message was"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,14,0)="      recorded in the KIDS installation record.  That multiple will now"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,15,0)="      install properly in a new account."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,17,0)=" IV.  The Excel extract option would fail occasionally.  This happened"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,18,0)="      because the Fileman API used to retrieve data from file 228.1 would"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,19,0)="      not always return data for all the requested fields.  This was"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,20,0)="      especially true for a pointer field that pointed to a non-existent"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,21,0)="      entry.  This call was modified to protect against that contingency."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,22,0)="      The extract will also return any pce secondary providers."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,24,0)=" V.   The retrieve dental history tab would not always return data.  The"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,25,0)="      call would quit and return no data if Fileman indicated any error"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,26,0)="      while retrieving data.  For example, the Dental History file has a"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,27,0)="      pointer to the old DAS file linked to that history record.  If that"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,28,0)="      DAS record had been deleted (i.e., a broken pointer) Fileman would"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,29,0)="      return an error.  Even though the other 11 fields requested for that"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,30,0)="      Dental History record had data, the call would return no data for"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,31,0)="      that record.  Now the data for that record will be returned.  Those"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,32,0)="      fields which encountered an error by the Fileman retrieve call will"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,33,0)="      be shown as a null value. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,35,0)=" VI.  All calls to retrieve data from the CPT file (#80) are required to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,36,0)="      use the APIs in ICPTCOD routine.  Most places we were doing that."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,37,0)="      But there were two times when we did a direct Fileman call to file"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,38,0)="      81.  Those places have been replaced by using the appropriate API in"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,39,0)="      ICPTCOD."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,41,0)=" VII. In patch DENT*1.2*30 the installer was prompted as to whether or not"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,42,0)="      to delete the ^VEJD(19600) global.  The documentation was not accurate"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,43,0)="      in displaying this.  This file and data global should have been deleted"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,44,0)="      since the file was moved to file 228 [^DENT(228)].  The post-init will"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,45,0)="      check the status of ^DIC(19600), ^DD(19600), and ^VEJD(19600) and do"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,46,0)="      any appropriate cleanup to remove these entries."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,48,0)=" VIII. Dentalmrm.exe (v3.03) is exported as part of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,49,0)="       You can verify the version of the dentalmrm.exe from the Help/About"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,50,0)="       option on the menu bar in the DRM GUI."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,52,0)=" IX.  This patch will work with CPRS v16 or greater"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,54,0)=" INSTALLATION FILES:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,55,0)=" =================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,57,0)=" File Name              Description                  Retrieval Format"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,58,0)=" -----------------     ---------------------------   ----------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,59,0)=" DENT_1_2p32.KID       Dental KIDS build             ASCII"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",13,1,60,0)=" dentalmrm.exe         DRM Version 3.03 Executable   Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,0)="34^3030123^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,0)="^^46^46^3030123"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,1,0)=" I.   This is released to support the Millennium Healthcare and Benefit"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,2,0)="      Act, Public Law 106-117 Section 20."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,4,0)=" II.  This patch, DENT*1.2*34, along with VEJDCERT RPCS 2.11 are being"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,5,0)="      released in a single KIDS software distribution.  This patch"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,6,0)="      contains the informational portion of DENT*1.2*34 and provides"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,7,0)="      field personnel with instructions on how to acquire, install, and"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,8,0)="      implement the software."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,10,0)=" III. This patch supports the entry of Head & Neck Cancer for PCE"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,11,0)="      entry when appropriate."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,13,0)=" IV.  For the Dx999 procedure codes, the mapping values to VistA DAS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,14,0)="      (Dental Activity System) have changed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,15,0)="      A. For each code, one CTV will be mapped to DAS category"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,16,0)="         '37-OTHER SIGNIFICANT TREATMENT'."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,18,0)="      B. These codes will now appear under the MISC tab in the DRM GUI."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,20,0)="      C. These codes will not be used for billable procedures, but,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,21,0)="         rather, will be used to indicate a non-billable visit. These"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,22,0)="         codes will generate one CTV into the DAS category ""Other"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,23,0)="         Significant Procedures."" The codes may be used for intermediate"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,24,0)="         steps and all similar non-billable patient visits. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,26,0)="      D. These mapping changes will require that practitioners select any"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,27,0)="         code(s) NOT in the ""99 Series"" (D0999, D2999, D3999, D4999,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,28,0)="         D5899, D5999, D6199, D6999, D7999, D8999, and D9999) for"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,29,0)="         ""billable"" procedures. Practitioners are advised to select the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,30,0)="         closest CDT code(s) outside the ""99 Series"" for any procedure"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,31,0)="         that is considered ""billable,"" and, therefore, results in"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,32,0)="         clinical productivity related to procedures identified by the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,33,0)="         CDT codes not in the ""unspecified"" category (the ""99 Series"")."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,35,0)=" V.  There are two new RPCs"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,36,0)="      DENTV DENTAL PROVIDER - returns active providers only"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,37,0)="      DENTV USER DEFAULT DIV - returns a user's default division as"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,38,0)="      defined in the NEW PERSON DIVISION multiple."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,40,0)=" VI. XINDEX will show the following error.  This is not a problem.  It is"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,41,0)="      problem with the XINDEX program.  There is an outstanding NOIS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,42,0)="      concerning this error message."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,43,0)="        DENTVRP8"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,44,0)="              .S XN=+PROV_U_$$NAMEFMT^XLFNAME(XN,,""MD"")"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,45,0)="           VST+37       F - General Syntax Error."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",14,1,46,0)="           VST+37       F - General Syntax Error."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,0)="35^3030329^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,0)="^^112^112^3030329"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,1,0)=" Note: several places in this patch description have items highlighted."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,2,0)=" The purpose of these highlights is to emphasize areas to pay particular"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,3,0)=" attention.  These should answer possible questions or concerns that IRM"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,4,0)=" or the installer may have."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,6,0)=" 1. *****************    ATTENTION      ATTENTION     ******************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,7,0)="    This patch should be installed immediately after installing"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,8,0)="    ICPT*6.0*13  If it is not, then when the user clicks on the FINISH"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,9,0)="    button in Dental Record Manager (DRM) they may generate PCE exception"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,10,0)="    errors."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,12,0)="    Note: the ICPT*6.0*13 patch inactivated quite a few ADA codes with an"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,13,0)="    inactivation date of 1/1/2003.  As such, these codes will no longer"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,14,0)="    show up in any tab within DRM.  Please see the documentation"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,15,0)="    accompanying patch ICPT*6.0*13 for details in changes to specific"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,16,0)="    codes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,17,0)="    *********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,19,0)=" 2. This patch provides compatibility with the 2003 CPT and CDT4 codes"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,20,0)="    A new ADA Mapping table (file 228) will be installed"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,21,0)="    NOIS: ALB-0502-51618, FGH-0602-32626"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,23,0)=" 3. A pre-installation routine will perform several steps"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,24,0)="    a. Save local CPT codes the site has added to the ADA table"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,25,0)="    b. Delete the existing ADA table"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,27,0)=" 4. A post-installation routine will perform several steps"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,28,0)="    a. Verify that all CPT codes in the dental provider's quick list are"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,29,0)="       still active.  If not, delete that code from the quick list"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,31,0)="    b. Restore any locally added CPT codes to the ADA table unless that"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,32,0)="       code is exported nationally with this patch or that code is"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,33,0)="       inactive."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,35,0)="    c. The dental coding committee spent considerable time assigning"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,36,0)="       default diagnosis codes to each ADA code.  As such, any changes"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,37,0)="       the site had made to the associated default diagnosis codes will"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,38,0)="       not be preserved."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,40,0)=" 5. If the old data global, ^VEJD(19600.1), still exists, then delete it."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,41,0)="    A previous DENT patch had moved that data to ^DENT(228.1)."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,43,0)=" 6. The DENTVDD routine was modified to remove direct references to the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,44,0)="    ^DD global.  Supported Fileman APIs are used instead."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,46,0)=" 7. A new routine is exported, DSICCPT.  This routine provides an"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,47,0)="    interface to the CPT and ICD9 files using nationally supported APIs."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,49,0)="    **************************  PLEASE NOTE  *************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,50,0)="    The Release of Information application had DSIC 1.0 (or DSIC 1.01)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,51,0)="    as part of that package.  This DSICCPT routine was not exported in"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,52,0)="    those builds.  So there is no conflict between this patch and the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,53,0)="    Release of Information 5.0 application.  DENT*1.2*31 is to be"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,54,0)="    released in the next couple of months and will include DSIC 1.1 which"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,55,0)="    will include this DSICCPT routine as well as other changes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,56,0)="    ******************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,58,0)=" 8. A new DRM GUI executable is exported with this patch.  Changes"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,59,0)="    include:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,60,0)="    a. Inactive Diagnosis codes (ICD9) will no longer be selectable in"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,61,0)="       the search engine window.  NOIS: ASH-1201-31869, BRX-0602-12946,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,62,0)="       MIN-1102-40433, NHM-0202-11852, PUG-0502-52312, WIM-0902-22158"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,64,0)="    b. In the Help Menu bar we have added a last broker call"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,65,0)="       debugging tools similar to the CPRS one."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,67,0)="    c. Fixed List out of Bounds errors. This could have happened when"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,68,0)="       typing the progress note title in the search window.  It could"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,69,0)="       also occur occasionally when the FINISH button was clicked and"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,70,0)="       the program was trying to file data to the Problem List."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,71,0)="       NOIS: BIG-0103-70399, MOU-0103-30859, MWV-0103-22436,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,72,0)="             PHI-0103-22339, SFC-0103-62181, UNY-0103-11934"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,74,0)="    d. Fixed an Access Violation error when DRM closes out"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,75,0)="       NOIS: ALT-0102-21002"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,77,0)="    e. Printing of signed addendum notes when prompted for additional"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,78,0)="       signers now works if the check box is selected."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,80,0)="    f. Completing a consult will now link to the proper Visit instead of"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,81,0)="       creating a new historical Visit."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,83,0)="    g. Previous there were occasional problems if the FINISH button was"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,84,0)="       clicked multiple times.  Now the FINISH button will ignore the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,85,0)="       second and subsequent clicks until the all the DRM data including"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,86,0)="       filing of progress note has completed which may take several"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,87,0)="       seconds."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,89,0)="    h. There is now a Excel Extract option under the Tools option on the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,90,0)="       Menu Bar"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,92,0)="    i. Whenever a TIU note is printed within DRM, the header will have"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,93,0)="       the words ""(WORKING COPY)"""
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,95,0)="    j. If the DRM window is open and you change patients within CPRS,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,96,0)="       then the DRM window will now show itself in front of CPRS instead"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,97,0)="       of behind it."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,99,0)="    k. Previously, in the Visit selection window pull down list, any"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,100,0)="       entry which was longer than the width of that window would not be"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,101,0)="       completely displayed.  Now if you hover over an entry, a hint"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,102,0)="       will be displayed showing the entire contents."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,103,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,104,0)=" 8. The following routines which supported previous patch pre- and"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,105,0)="    post-install processes will be deleted:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,106,0)="    DENTVCNV, DENTVI01, DENTVI02, DENTVI03, DENTVI04, DENTVI05"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,108,0)=" 9. The DENTVRP3 routine was updated to bring it into complete SACC"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,109,0)="    compliance by not doing direct reads of the ^DD global.  When"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,110,0)="    filing ICD9 codes to the ADA table (#228) it was possible that the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,111,0)="    name of the ICD9 code was entered into field 1 instead of the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",15,1,112,0)="    pointer value to file 80."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,0)="36^3030628^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^152^152^3030628"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,1,0)=" 1. Patch 35 exported a new ADA Table, file 228, which supported CDT4"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,2,0)="    codes and ICPT*6.0*16 compatibility.  Each CPT mapping has 19"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,3,0)="    associated fields.  A few of those CPT codes had incorrect values for"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,4,0)="    some of their fields.  While reviewing that table, Dental VAHQ and"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,5,0)="    its coding task group decided to change many other individual field"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,6,0)="    values for quite a few CPT codes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,8,0)=" 2. The post-installation program in DENT*1.2*35 did not work as"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,9,0)="    intended.  DRM allows the sites to add local medical codes to the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,10,0)="    ADA table.  DRM also allows for the sites to change the default ICD9"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,11,0)="    mapping for a CDT code.  The post-install program was suppose to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,12,0)="    restore those local changes to the ADA table.  But it did not due to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,13,0)="    a programming bug.  This is fixed in this version.  However, this"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,14,0)="    patch cannot put back those locally mapped CPT codes that were"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,15,0)="    deleted with patch 35."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,17,0)=" 3. Some of the CDT4 codes exported in the patch 35 ADA Mapping Table"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,18,0)="    did not have NUM SURFACES indicated when they should have.  Thus"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,19,0)="    user was not prompted for surfaces within the DRM GUI."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,20,0)="    NOIS: CHS-0403-41619"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,22,0)=" 4. When using Fileman on file 228.1 and entering '??' at the Select"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,23,0)="    Dental History prompt, you may get an <UNDEF> error.  This was due"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,24,0)="    to a bad Identifier on this file."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,25,0)="    NOIS: IND-0403-41306"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,27,0)=" Technical Description"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,28,0)=" ---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,29,0)=" 5. Changes to Data Dictionary for file 228"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,30,0)="    A. B index changed from a traditional to a Key uniqueness index"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,31,0)="    B. DATA TO PUT IN DENT(221) field"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,32,0)="       1) Input transform changed to allow for CHK^DIE to be used as"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,33,0)="          that Fileman API does not use the internal record number."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,34,0)="       2) Executable Help changed to allow to be invoked by Fileman"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,35,0)="          APIs that do not require internal record number."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,36,0)="       3) Changed the field name from DATA TO PUT IN DENT(221) to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,37,0)="          DATA FOR FILE 221."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,38,0)="    C. PRIMARY field - a new set of codes value was entered, Either."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,39,0)="       This code will be used in the future"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,40,0)="    D. FIELD FROM FILE 221 field"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,41,0)="       1) Field type was changed from numeric to free text"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,42,0)="       2) Input transform redone to make it more clear"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,43,0)="       3) Output transform redone to make it more clear"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,44,0)="    E. #SURFACES field was renamed to NUM SURFACES"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,45,0)="    F. New field added, PREV PRIMARY DIAGNOSIS (#25).  This contains"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,46,0)="       the default diagnosis for that CPT code in the previous version"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,47,0)="    G. Field 1, DX ICD9, was changed to make it required"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,49,0)=" 6. Changes to routines (tag^routine)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,50,0)="    A. DENTVDD"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,51,0)="       1) FLD4 - changed from being called by DO to being called by DO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,52,0)="                 with parameter passing.  For fields 19 and 34 in file"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,53,0)="                 221, FLD4 will no longer write to the screen"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,54,0)="       2) FLD4E - changed from being called by DO to being called by DO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,55,0)="                  with parameter passing."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,56,0)="       3) NUM - logic redone to make it more clear"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,57,0)="       4) ID - fixed an <UNDEFINED> error at ID+6"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,58,0)="               NOIS: IND-0403-41306"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,59,0)="    B. DENTVUTL"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,60,0)="       1) CPT - changed to call CPT^DSICCPT.  Removed the appending of"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,61,0)="                the text '[PRIMARY]' to the CPT short description when"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,62,0)="                the ADA table (#228) has the PRIMARY flag set for this"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,63,0)="                CPT."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,64,0)="       2) CPTIEN - changed to call CPT^DSICCPT"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,65,0)="       3) ICD - changed direct global access of data in file 81 to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,66,0)="                calling ICD^DSICCPT"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,67,0)="    C. DENTVIP2 - new routine"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,69,0)=" REQUIRED BUILDS:  DENT*1.2*35"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,70,0)=" ==============="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,72,0)=" Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,73,0)=" =========="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,74,0)=" Manhattan"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,75,0)=" Minneapolis"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,77,0)=" NOIS ADDRESSED BY PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,78,0)=" ======================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,79,0)=" CHS-0403-41619"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,80,0)=" IND-0403-41306"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,82,0)=" ROUTINE SUMMARY:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,83,0)=" ==============="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,84,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,85,0)=" The second line of each DENT routine will look like:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,86,0)="     <tab>;;1.2;DENTAL;**[patch list]**;Aug 10, 2001"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,88,0)=" Routine    Before Patch  After Patch   Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,89,0)=" --------   ------------  -----------   --------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,90,0)=" DENTVDD         2851120      2804408   30,35,36"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,91,0)=" DENTVIP         1402389       704530   30,32,34,35,36"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,92,0)=" DENTVIP1        8913694      8645242   33,34,35,36"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,93,0)=" DENTVIP2        -n/a-       14330152   36"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,94,0)=" DENTVRP1        4976236      5016139   30,34,36"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,95,0)=" DENTVUTL        4283389      3529137   30,33,34,36"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,97,0)=" INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS FOR DENT_1_2P36.KID "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,98,0)=" ============================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,99,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,100,0)=" This patch should be installed when there are no dental DRM processes"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,101,0)=" running.  The installation time should take less than 5 minute."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,102,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,103,0)=" 1. For DSM sites review your mapped set.  Disable any of the above"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,104,0)="    routines if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,105,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,106,0)=" 2. From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,107,0)="    the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,108,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,109,0)=" 3. You may elect to use the following options (when prompted"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,110,0)="    for INSTALL NAME, enter DENT*1.2*36): "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,111,0)="      a.  Backup a Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,112,0)="      b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,113,0)="      c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,114,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,115,0)=" 4. Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,116,0)="    DENT*1.2*36."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,117,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,118,0)=" 5. When asked ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONS during the install? Yes//"","
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,119,0)="    respond ""NO""."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,120,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,121,0)=" 6. When prompted ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,122,0)="    Protocols? YES//"", respond ""NO""."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,123,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,124,0)=" 7. AXP/DSM Sites - After the patch has been installed, rebuild your "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,125,0)="    map set, if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,127,0)=" 8. *********************  NOTE   NOTE   NOTE  ***********************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,128,0)="    Please review the Install log to see if there were any problems"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,129,0)="    reported in the post-installation process.  If so you will see"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,130,0)="    text not displayed in the installation example.  Following are"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,131,0)="    some of the text you may or may not see."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,132,0)="    ******************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,134,0)="    A. WARNING MESSAGES"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,135,0)="       These are just warning messages.  Nothing is wrong."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,136,0)="       Read all the associated text for more detailed explanations."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,138,0)="        >>>>> Local CPT codes not added to the new ADA table <<<<<"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,139,0)="  >>>>> CPT codes who had inactive Diagnosis codes mapped to them <<<<<"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,141,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,142,0)="    B. This should never happen."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,143,0)="       If you see this message, just follow the instructions displayed"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,145,0)="    Unable to lock the ^DENT(228) global.  Any local changes not restored"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,146,0)="    You can rerun this restore post-install option after the KIDS install"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,147,0)="    has completed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,148,0)="       1. Get to programmer's mode through Kernel sign-on"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,149,0)="          This ensures that the Kernel environment variables are set"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,150,0)="       2. Be sure your DUZ(0)=""@"" - this can be done from programmer's"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,151,0)="          mode by VAH>S DUZ(0)=""@"""
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",16,1,152,0)="       3. From programmer's prompt, VAH>D RESTORE^DENTVIP1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",17,0)="31^3031107^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,0)="37^3040521^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^262^262^3040521"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="1.General Information"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,2,0)="  ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,3,0)="  This patch contains fixes and enhancements to the Dental Record Manager"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,4,0)="  (DRM) application.  This patch also contains a new M Global for DRM in"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,5,0)="  the DENT namespace - ^DENT(228.5 for the Fee Basis enhancement."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,7,0)="  A database conversion will be run as part of the post installation.  The"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,8,0)="  conversion fixes the dental provider number when the number starts with"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,9,0)="  one or more zeros (as in 0494).  Because of an old cross reference on "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,10,0)="  the DENTAL TREATMENT file (#221), the leading zeros were dropped from "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,11,0)="  the provider ID number.  Only those 4 digit provider IDs whose value was"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,12,0)="  less than 1000 were affected. The leading zeros will be replaced and any"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,13,0)="  affected cross-references will be re-built."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,14,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,15,0)="  The patch installation process should take be less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,16,0)="  The post-installation conversion process may take several hours "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,17,0)="  depending upon the number of records in file 221 - this process will be"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,18,0)="  tasked off."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,21,0)="2.SYSTEM ACCESS DURING INSTALLATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,22,0)="  ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,23,0)="  Installation of this patch does not require users to be off of the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,24,0)="  system. However, all Dental users should not use the DRM GUI option "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,25,0)="  while the patch is being installed.  All Dental users MUST close any "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,26,0)="  open DRM GUI application prior to the patch being installed.  Once the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,27,0)="  patch has completed then the users can use the DRM application."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,28,0)="  ********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,29,0)="  *  There is a new DRM executable exported with this patch.  This   *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,30,0)="  *  executable MUST be deployed PRIOR to Dental users accessing the *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,31,0)="  *  DRM application after the patch has been installed.             *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,32,0)="  ********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,35,0)="3.PRE-INSTALLATION PROCESS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,36,0)="  ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,37,0)="A.A pre-install process will delete the Data Dictionaries for the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,38,0)="  following file and any associated templates (INPUT, PRINT, SORT) and any"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,39,0)="  FORMS.  No data will be deleted.  The file affected is: 228.1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,40,0)="B.The pre-install process will also delete field .5 from file 221.  This"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,41,0)="  field will be reinstalled as part of the patch.  The old AF x-ref has"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,42,0)="  been replaced with a new Trigger cross-reference to set the .4 field."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,43,0)="C.The temporary ""ACNVT31"" cross-reference on file 228.1 will be deleted. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,44,0)="  This cross-reference was used in Patch 31 to keep track of which records"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,45,0)="  needed to be converted.  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,48,0)="4.POST-INSTALLATION PROCESS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,49,0)="  ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,50,0)="  The post-install routine will queue up a Taskman job to convert file "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,51,0)="  221.  The Provider Number field (.4) in file 221 will be converted if it"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,52,0)="  is less than 4 characters long.  Leading zeros will be added to the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,53,0)="  number (e.g. 494 will become 0494), and the affected cross-references "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,54,0)="  for field .4 will be re-built."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,55,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,56,0)="  ************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,57,0)="  *                                                                      *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,58,0)="  *   THE FOLLOWING STEP BE COMPLETED FOR THIS PATCH TO WORK PROPERLY    *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,59,0)="  *                                                                      *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,60,0)="  ************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,62,0)="  At this point, the KIDS install will have completed.  IRM needs to place"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,63,0)="  the DRM GUI executable in the appropriate directory.  The placement of"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,64,0)="  this DRM executable can be done at the same time the KIDS build is being"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,65,0)="  installed.  The executable must be placed as follows where ...\ "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,66,0)="  indicates your UNC/path for where the current DRM v3.1.0.23"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,67,0)="  dentalmrm.exe is located:        Move dentalmrm.exe to ...\DOCSTORE"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,70,0)="5.FIXES TO THE DRM APPLICATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,71,0)="  ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,72,0)="A.Remove screening of dental patient category based on inpatient status."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,73,0)="  NOIS: NYH-1203-11181, TOM-1203-41027, UNY-1203-10667"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,75,0)="B.Delete any inactive CPT codes on an users quick list."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,76,0)="  NOIS: MAN-0803-11685"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,78,0)="C.Under certain circumstances, DRM did not honor the choice of filing "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,79,0)="  flags on a per CPT code basis.  Now, it will only file to PCE or DAS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,80,0)="  or DES if explicitly indicated.  The default is to file to all three."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,81,0)="  Filing to Dental History only will now display the correct date on"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,82,0)="  the Dental History tab."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,83,0)="  NOIS: HOU-1203-70105"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,84,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,85,0)="D.Fixed misspelling of word ""immumization"" to "" immunization"" which "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,86,0)="  caused a ""List Index out of bounds"" error when clicking on the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,87,0)="  Immunization button in Clinical Record tab.  When immunizations are"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,88,0)="  imported into a note, there will be a space and a header before the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,89,0)="  data."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,91,0)="E.Utilize new rpc call - ORWPS ACTIVE to import meds list into "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,92,0)="  the TIU Note and TIU Note Addendum."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,93,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,94,0)="F.The default date range in Import Lab Results was always using a date"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,95,0)="  range of 180 days back, but now this button uses the user parameter"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,96,0)="  for lab days range."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,97,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,98,0)="G.Change logic to get default division only if user has more than one"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,99,0)="  station.  The default division will be pre-selected wherever the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,100,0)="  station radio button(s) are shown.  If there is only one station,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,101,0)="  then that station is pre-selected on the screen."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,102,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,103,0)="H.Display all messages when the ""DAS record not created"" error (or other"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,104,0)="  error) is encountered.  NOIS: HVH-1203-11045, BRX-1203-11654, "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,105,0)="  MIA-1203-31153, NCH-1203-41248, LAH-1203-62134, UNY-0104-10313,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,106,0)="  HWH-0204-40857, MON-0204-50811"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,108,0)="I.If the user clicks on the ""Add to Quick List"" button on the Search form"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,109,0)="  and clicks cancel, any new entries will be refreshed on the screen."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,111,0)="J.Due to changes in the law, there is no longer any differentiation of "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,112,0)="  the types of POWs.  Therefore, CLASS IIB is no longer to be used."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,114,0)="K.Edited unsigned notes will now file correctly in DRM."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,115,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,116,0)="L.Notes and Addendums created from the Clinical Record tab will now"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,117,0)="  word wrap correctly.  Notes will not be allowed to have a future date."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,118,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,119,0)="M.A message will be displayed after spell checking has completed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,121,0)="6.ENHANCEMENTS TO THE DRM APPLICATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,122,0)="  ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,123,0)="A.Dental Fee Basis is part of this patch.  A new menu option on the DRM"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,124,0)="  File Menu displays a screen to enter/edit/delete Fee Basis information"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,125,0)="  for the selected dental patient.  The Fee Basis information will not be"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,126,0)="  transmitted to Austin until the DRM HL7 enhancement has been completed,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,127,0)="  but reports will be available on-line in Patch 38.  The new Fee Basis"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,128,0)="  option should not be used exclusively at this time.  Users should"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,129,0)="  continue to use their existing Fee Basis option through VistA which"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,130,0)="  updates file 222 - DENTAL FEE BASIS (AMIS) since that information is"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,131,0)="  being transmitted to Austin."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,132,0)="B.This patch enables Dental to be billing aware for patches to be released"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,133,0)="  in FY2004.  PCE changes supporting the billing awareness project is "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,134,0)="  PX*1.0*124.  The changes to these dental routines will work whether or"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,135,0)="  not that PCE patch is installed.  The PCE patch preserves the linkage of"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,136,0)="  diagnosis codes to a CPT code when a program invokes DATA2PCE^PXAPI such"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,137,0)="  as the dental program.  The PCE APIs to retrieve the CPT data for a "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,138,0)="  VISIT were also modified to return the current diagnosis linkage for"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,139,0)="  each CPT code.  If that PCE patch is not installed, the dental program"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,140,0)="  will work as it always has.  The two functions affected are the filing"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,141,0)="  of data when the FINISH button is clicked and when DRM retrieves "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,142,0)="  historical data.  The extract (Excel) function will be made billing"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,143,0)="  aware in another dental patch."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,145,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,146,0)="7.NOIS ADDRESSED BY THIS PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,147,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,148,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,149,0)="  NYH-1203-11181   TOM-1203-41027   UNY-1203-10667  MAN-0803-11685"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,150,0)="  HOU-1203-70105   HVH-1203-11045   BRX-1203-11654  MIA-1203-31153"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,151,0)="  NCH-1203-41248   LAH-1203-62134   UNY-0104-10313  HWH-0204-40857"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,152,0)="  MON-0204-50811"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,154,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,155,0)="8.INSTALLATION FILES"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,156,0)="  ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,157,0)="  How to Obtain KIDS File"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,159,0)="  File Name: DENT_1_2P37.zip         FTP format: binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,160,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,161,0)="  DENT_1_2P37.zip file will contain the following files:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,162,0)="                                                                  FTP "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,163,0)="  File Name          Description                                 Format"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,164,0)="  ------------------ ------------------------------------------  ------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,165,0)="  Dent_1_2p37.kid    KIDS file which will install 1 KIDS Builds  ASCII"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,166,0)="                         DENT*1.2*37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,167,0)="  Dentalmrm.exe      DRM Version 3.11 executable                 Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,168,0)="  Dent_1_2_p37ug.doc Dental Record Manager's user guide          Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,169,0)="                         The guide was updated for Fee Basis"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,170,0)="  Dent_1_2p37_rn_ig.doc DENT*1.2*37 Release Notes and            Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,171,0)="                         Installation Guide"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,172,0)="  P37_patch_description.txt    This file                         ASCII"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,174,0)="  The zip file listed above may be obtained via FTP.  The preferred "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,175,0)="  method is to FTP the files from download.vista.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,177,0)="  This transmits the files from the first available FTP server.  Sites"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,178,0)="  may also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific server "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,179,0)="  as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,180,0)="  CIO FIELD OFFICE   FTP ADDRESS                 DIRECTORY"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,181,0)="  ----------------   -------------------------   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,182,0)="  Albany             ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext    [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,183,0)="  Hines              ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext     [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,184,0)="  Salt Lake City     ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext       [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,185,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,187,0)="9.REQUIRED BUILDS:  DENT*1.2*31"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,188,0)="                    DSIC*1.2*1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,189,0)="                    XU*8.0*229"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,190,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,191,0)="10.TEST SITES             SYSTEM                        ALPHA/BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,192,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,193,0)="========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,194,0)="   Manhattan, NY         (VMS DSM)                      ALPHA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,195,0)="   Bath, NY              (VMS DSM)                      BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,196,0)="   Fargo, ND             (W2K Cache/Thin Client)        BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,197,0)="   Tomah, WI             (VMS Cache)                    BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,198,0)="   Hines, IL             (NT Cache)                     BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,200,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,201,0)="11.ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,202,0)="   ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,203,0)="   Second line of routines will look like:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,204,0)="   ;;1.2;DENTAL;<patch list>;AUG 10, 2001"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,205,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,206,0)="   Routine   Before Patch  After Patch  Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,207,0)="   --------  ------------  -----------  ------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,208,0)="   DENTV031      [*** to be deleted***]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,209,0)="   DENTV03A      [*** to be deleted***]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,210,0)="   DENTV03B      [*** to be deleted***]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,211,0)="   DENTV037        n/a         2646025     37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,212,0)="   DENTVFB         n/a         2775003     37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,213,0)="   DENTVRF       1357987       1331212     31,37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,214,0)="   DENTVRF0      3183908       3455104     31,37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,215,0)="   DENTVRF1      5110544       5236302     31,37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,216,0)="   DENTVRF2      3458244       4641313     31,37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,217,0)="   DENTVRF3      7764989       7876724     31,37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,218,0)="   DENTVRF4      6882060       7883662     31,37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,219,0)="   DENTVRH       5515191       6429972     31,37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,220,0)="   DENTVRP1      5053952       5080599     30,34,36,31,37 "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,221,0)="   DENTVRP2      1100213       1429573     30,31,37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,222,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,223,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,224,0)="12.INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS FOR DENT*1.2*37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,225,0)="   ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,226,0)="   This patch must be installed when there are no dental DRM processes"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,227,0)="   running.  All open DRM GUI applications must be closed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,228,0)="   The installation time should take less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,229,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,230,0)="   1. Obtain the Dent_1_2p37.kid file"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,231,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,232,0)="   2. For DSM sites review your mapped set.  Disable any of the above"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,233,0)="      routines if necessary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,234,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,235,0)="   3. From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,236,0)="      the Installation menu"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,237,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,238,0)="   4. Use Load a Distribution and enter Dent_1_2p37.kid when prompted"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,239,0)="      for a Host file.  You may need to attach a directory name"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,240,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,241,0)="   5. You may elect to use the following options (when prompted for "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,242,0)="      INSTALL NAME, enter DENT*1.2*37)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,243,0)="      a. Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,244,0)="      b. Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,245,0)="      c. Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,246,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,247,0)="   6. Use the Install Package(s) option and select package DENT*1.2*37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,248,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,249,0)="   7. For the install prompts, enter either Yes or No depending upon the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,250,0)="      normal practice at your facility.  This example shows answering NO:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,251,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,252,0)=" Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,253,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,254,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,255,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,256,0)="   8. AXP/DSM Sites - After the patch has been installed, rebuild your map"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,257,0)="      set, if necessary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,258,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,259,0)="   9. This step must be completed for this patch to work properly"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,260,0)="      a. ...\   will indicate your UNC/path for where the current DRM"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,261,0)="         v3.1.0.23 dentalmrm.exe is located"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",18,1,262,0)="      b. Move dentalmrm.exe to ...\DOCSTORE"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,0)="38^3040802^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,0)="^^292^292^3040802"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,1,0)=" General Information"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,2,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,3,0)=" This patch contains fixes and enhancements to the Dental Record Manager"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,4,0)=" (DRM) application.  This patch also contains new M Globals for DRM in"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,5,0)=" the DENT namespace - ^DENT(220.51 and ^DENT(220.52 to support the new "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,6,0)=" eight character Dental Provider Id."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,8,0)=" Three database conversions will be run as part of the post installation."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,9,0)=" The first conversion seeds the new fields in 228.2 for the DES Reports"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,10,0)=" (DAS FIELD, DAS DATA) based on the ADA table.  The second conversion"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,11,0)=" changes the DIVISION pointer in file 228.1 from a pointer to file 40.8"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,12,0)=" to a pointer to file 4.  The DD is being sent for this field to change"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,13,0)=" the pointers.  The final conversion removes the TIU Note pointer data"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,14,0)=" from file 228.1."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,16,0)=" The patch installation process should take be less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,17,0)=" The post-installation conversion process may take several hours "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,18,0)=" depending upon the number of records in file 228.1 and 228.2."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,19,0)=" This conversion process will be tasked off in the background."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,22,0)=" SYSTEM ACCESS DURING INSTALLATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,23,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,24,0)=" Installation of this patch does not require users to be off of the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,25,0)=" system. However, all Dental users should not use the DRM GUI option "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,26,0)=" while the patch is being installed.  All Dental users MUST close any "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,27,0)=" open DRM GUI application prior to the patch being installed.  Once the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,28,0)=" patch has completed the users can use the DRM application.  Until"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,29,0)=" the conversions are complete, the new DRM reports may not give accurate"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,30,0)=" results since they need the new DAS FIELD and DAS DATA data in file"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,31,0)=" 228.2, and they search for data based on the DIVISION field which is"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,32,0)=" also being changed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,34,0)="  ********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,35,0)="  *  There is a new DRM executable exported with this patch.  This   *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,36,0)="  *  executable MUST be deployed PRIOR to Dental users accessing the *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,37,0)="  *  DRM application after the patch has been installed.             *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,38,0)="  ********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,41,0)=" PRE-INSTALLATION PROCESS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,42,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,43,0)=" The pre-install process will delete field .18(DIVISION) from file 228.1."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,44,0)=" This field will be reinstalled as part of the patch."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,46,0)=" The pre-install process will delete the TIU Note pointer from file 228.1."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,47,0)=" This field is no longer used."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,49,0)=" The pre-install process will also delete field .16(SURFACE) and 1.18"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,50,0)=" (TEMP TRANS ID) from file 228.2.  These fields will be reinstalled as"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,51,0)=" SURFACES/ROOTS and HL7 STATUS, respectively."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,54,0)=" POST-INSTALLATION PROCESS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,55,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,56,0)=" The post-install routine will queue up a Taskman job to convert files "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,57,0)=" 228.1, (division pointer and removing any TIU Note pointer data) and "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,58,0)=" 228.2, (setting DES reporting fields).  It will also create a new index"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,59,0)=" on file 228.1 for DES reporting (""AG"") and re-index the ""AF"" cross-ref"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,60,0)=" on file 228.1."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,61,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,62,0)="  ***********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,63,0)="  *                                                                     *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,64,0)="  *   THE FOLLOWING STEP BE COMPLETED FOR THIS PATCH TO WORK PROPERLY   *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,65,0)="  *                                                                     *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,66,0)="  ***********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,68,0)=" At this point, the KIDS install will have completed.  IRM needs to place"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,69,0)=" the DRM GUI executable in the appropriate directory.  The placement of"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,70,0)=" this DRM executable can be done at the same time the KIDS build is being"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,71,0)=" installed.  The executable must be placed as follows where ...\ "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,72,0)=" indicates your UNC/path for where the current DRM v3.11"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,73,0)=" dentalmrm.exe is located:        "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,74,0)="        Move dentalmrm.exe to ...\DOCSTORE"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,75,0)=" Also... the new extract executable needs to be placed in the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,76,0)=" same directory where dentalmrm.exe resides."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,77,0)="        Move DRMEXTSRV.ext to ...\DOCSTORE"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,80,0)=" FIXES TO THE DRM APPLICATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,81,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,82,0)=" A. The list of Visits that display when the user wants to Delete a "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,83,0)="    Dental Encounter will now display in reverse chronological order with"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,84,0)="    no duplicates."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,85,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,86,0)=" B. The information on the Dental History tab will display in reverse"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,87,0)="    chronological order by date/time, not just date."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,88,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,89,0)=" C. If there are no Vital signs to be imported, an extra linefeed was"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,90,0)="    appearing in the note - the extra linefeed has been removed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,91,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,92,0)=" D. Change the .18 field (DIVISION) in the DENTAL HISTORY file (#228.1)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,93,0)="    From a pointer to file 40.8 (MEDICAL CENTER DIVISION) to a pointer to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,94,0)="    file 4 (INSTITUTION).  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,96,0)=" F. Add fields DAS FIELD, DAS DATA to the TREATMENT PLAN TRANSACTION/EXAM"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,97,0)="    file (#228.2).  These fields will be seeded with data during the post"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,98,0)="    install conversion.  These fields, along with the CTV, VA-DSS GROUP"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,99,0)="    fields will be set appropriately when transactions are filed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,100,0)="    Most of these fields are used in DES Reports."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,101,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,102,0)=" G. A Fileman error was occurring when entering single letter look-ups"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,103,0)="    (e.g., ""B"") in the Provider lookup screen.  This screen is displayed"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,104,0)="    when clicking the New button on the Provider Edit screen, or"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,105,0)="    when selecting the optional Provider checkbox on the Extract screen,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,106,0)="    or when selecting to file an encounter under another provider's"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,107,0)="    name.  The error has been fixed.  This type of error was also"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,108,0)="    occurring on the User lookup screens (User Inquiry and user selection"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,109,0)="    within the Administrator Toolbox), and was also fixed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,110,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,111,0)=" H. CPT code search was returning D2950 when the code D2951 was entered."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,112,0)="    This has been fixed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,113,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,114,0)=" I. The word 'Extract' was spelled incorrectly on the old Extract History"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,115,0)="    Data screen.  It's now correct."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,116,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,117,0)=" J. Consults were not being completed when the user Double-Clicked them,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,118,0)="    only when the consult was single-clicked.  Now they will complete"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,119,0)="    either way.  NOIS: MIA-0304-30860"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,121,0)=" K. Change the field definition for field 1.18 in the TREATMENT PLAN "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,122,0)="    TRANSACTION/EXAM file (#228.2).  This field was not used, and will"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,123,0)="    now store the HL7 transmission status."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,125,0)=" L. A new field called TP RECORD (.06) was added to the TREATMENT PLAN"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,126,0)="    TRANSACTION/EXAM file (#228.2).  The field will be set to 1 for"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,127,0)="    Treatment Plan (DRM+) transactions to differentiate them from DRM."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,128,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,129,0)=" M. A new field called TREATMENT FLAGS (1.202) was added to the TREATMENT"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,130,0)="    PLAN TRANSACTION/EXAM file (#228.2).  The field will be contain the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,131,0)="    tooth-related flag."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,132,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,133,0)=" N. The SURFACES (.16) field in the TREATMENT PLAN TRANSACTION/EXAM file"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,134,0)="    (#228.2) was renamed to SURFACES/ROOTS and the field definition now"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,135,0)="    allows 1-7 characters (upper/lower) vs only uppercase characters."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,138,0)=" ENHANCEMENTS TO THE DRM APPLICATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,139,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,140,0)=" A. DES Reports are part of this patch.  This enhancement provides six "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,141,0)="    dental reports for the local VistA system.  The reports are:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,142,0)="    Provider Summary, Clinic Summary, Sittings by Provider, Individual"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,143,0)="    Sittings, Non-Clinical Time Report, Dental Fee Basis Report.  These"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,144,0)="    reports are similar to DAS reports of the same name.  Reports are "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,145,0)="    available on the Tools menu for all users."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,146,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,147,0)=" B. Provider Add/Edit is part of this patch.  This enhancement allows the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,148,0)="    dental administrator to add or edit the dental staff in the DENTAL"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,149,0)="    PROVIDER (#220.5) file.  A new eight character Dental Provider Id has"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,150,0)="    been created and will be used in the DES Reports.  The old four"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,151,0)="    character Dental Provider Id is still required for DAS, but will be"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,152,0)="    deprecated when DAS is replaced.  Provider Add/Edit is available on"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,153,0)="    the Tools menu for administrative users."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,154,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,155,0)=" C. A new Extract History data option is available on the Tools menu."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,156,0)="    This option does not use RPC calls to get history data, but uses"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,157,0)="    instead, a TCP/IP process running on the local machine.  When the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,158,0)="    user wants to run the new extract, a process will start in the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,159,0)="    user's system tray and will wait for data from Vista.  When the data"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,160,0)="    has been sent, the Vista M code will send a Shutdown message to stop"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,161,0)="    the TCP/IP server.  During the patch testing phase for Patch 38, the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,162,0)="    old Extract option will remain enabled along with the new Extract"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,163,0)="    option.  NOTE!  Users will have to contact IRM to get a valid Port#"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,164,0)="    to be used with the extract!  The user must also know the IP address"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,165,0)="    of their workstation in order for the Vista M code to correctly"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,166,0)="    connect to the TCP/IP process running on their machine!  These"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,167,0)="    parameters will be stored on Vista and can be edited/viewed via the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,168,0)="    Parameters button on the new Extract History Data screen."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,169,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,170,0)=" D. Fee Basis and Dental Transaction records will start setting the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,171,0)="    ""AXMIT"" cross-reference correctly (""P"" for pending, ""C"" for canceled)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,172,0)="    in preparation for transmitting HL7 records to AAC."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,173,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,174,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,175,0)=" NOIS ADDRESSED BY THIS PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,176,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,177,0)=" MIA-0304-30860 "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,178,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,179,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,180,0)=" INSTALLATION FILES"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,181,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,182,0)=" How to Obtain KIDS File"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,183,0)=" File Name: DENT_1_2P38.zip         FTP format: binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,184,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,185,0)=" DENT_1_2P38.zip file will contain the following files:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,186,0)="                                                                   FTP "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,187,0)=" File Name                  Description                            Format"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,188,0)=" ------------------------   -------------------------------------- ------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,189,0)=" Dent_1_2p38.kid            Installable KIDS file                  ASCII"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,190,0)=" Dentalmrm.exe              DRM Version 3.12 executable            Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,191,0)=" DRMEXTSRV.exe              DRM TCP/IP executable                  Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,192,0)=" Dent_1_2p38_ug.doc         Dental Record Manager's user guide     Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,193,0)="                            Updated w/ Reports/Prov Edit/Extract"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,194,0)=" Dent_1_2p38_rn_ig.doc      DENT*1.2*38 Release Notes and          Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,195,0)="                            Installation Guide"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,196,0)=" P38_patch_description.txt  A copy of the patch description        ASCII"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,197,0)=" Patch 38 Enhancements.doc  Describing just the enhancements       Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,198,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,199,0)=" The zip file listed above may be obtained via FTP.  The preferred method"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,200,0)=" is to FTP the files from download.vista.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,201,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,202,0)=" This transmits the files from the first available FTP server.  Sites may"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,203,0)=" also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific server as"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,204,0)=" follows:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,205,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,206,0)=" CIO FIELD OFFICE   FTP ADDRESS                 DIRECTORY"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,207,0)=" ----------------   -------------------------   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,208,0)=" Albany             ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext    [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,209,0)=" Hines              ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext     [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,210,0)=" Salt Lake City     ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext       [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,211,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,212,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,213,0)=" REQUIRED BUILDS:  DENT*1.2*37"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,214,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,215,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,216,0)=" TEST SITES             SYSTEM                         ALPHA/BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,217,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,218,0)=" Fargo, ND             (W2K Cache/Thin Client)         ALPHA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,219,0)=" Manhattan, NY         (VMS DSM)                       BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,220,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,221,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,222,0)=" ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,223,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,224,0)=" Second line of routines will look like:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,225,0)=" ;;1.2;DENTAL;<patch list>;AUG 10, 2001"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,226,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,227,0)="   Routine   Before Patch  After Patch  Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,228,0)="   --------  ------------  -----------  ------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,229,0)="   DENTV037    [*** to be deleted***]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,230,0)="   DENTV038      n/a        4808142        38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,231,0)="   DENTV03C      n/a        21799174       38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,232,0)="   DENTV03D      n/a        21047556       38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,233,0)="   DENTV03E      n/a        21447147       38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,234,0)="   DENTV03F      n/a        19998119       38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,235,0)="   DENTV03G      n/a        1622718        38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,236,0)="   DENTVA1       n/a        10886320       38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,237,0)="   DENTVA2       n/a        12235826       38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,238,0)="   DENTVAU       n/a        2285628        38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,239,0)="   DENTVDD1    4809284      5137431        31,38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,240,0)="   DENTVFB     2775003      2787426        37,38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,241,0)="   DENTVIP3    3716294      3714758        31,38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,242,0)="   DENTVRF4    7883662      8576541        31,37,38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,243,0)="   DENTVRH     6429972      6800370        31,37,38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,244,0)="   DENTVRP5      n/a        3121694        38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,245,0)="   DENTVRP8      n/a        3913187        38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,246,0)="   DENTVRP9    6021923      6021572        30,32,34,31,38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,247,0)="   DENTVTP2      n/a        3443632        38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,248,0)="   DENTVUT1    3413708      3440255        31,38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,249,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,250,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,251,0)=" INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS FOR DENT*1.2*38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,252,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,253,0)=" This patch must be installed when there are no dental DRM processes"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,254,0)=" running.  All open DRM GUI applications must be closed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,255,0)=" The installation time should take less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,257,0)=" 1. Obtain the Dent_1_2p38.kid file"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,258,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,259,0)=" 2. For DSM sites review your mapped set.  Disable any of the above"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,260,0)="    routines if necessary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,261,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,262,0)=" 3. From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,263,0)="    the Installation menu"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,264,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,265,0)=" 4. Use Load a Distribution and enter Dent_1_2p38.kid when prompted"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,266,0)="    for a Host file.  You may need to attach a directory name"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,267,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,268,0)=" 5. You may elect to use the following options (when prompted for "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,269,0)="    INSTALL NAME, enter DENT*1.2*38)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,270,0)="    a. Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,271,0)="    b. Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,272,0)="    c. Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,273,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,274,0)=" 6. Use the Install Package(s) option and select package DENT*1.2*38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,275,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,276,0)=" 7. For the install prompts, enter either Yes or No depending upon the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,277,0)="    normal practice at your facility.  This example shows answering NO:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,278,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,279,0)="     Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,280,0)="                 Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,281,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,282,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,283,0)=" 8. AXP/DSM Sites - After the patch has been installed, rebuild your map"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,284,0)="    set, if necessary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,285,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,286,0)=" 9. This step must be completed for this patch to work properly"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,287,0)="    a. ...\   will indicate your UNC/path for where the current DRM"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,288,0)="       v3.11 dentalmrm.exe is located"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,289,0)="    b. Move dentalmrm.exe to ...\DOCSTORE"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,290,0)="    c. Move DRMEXTSRV.exe to ...\DOCSTORE"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,291,0)="       (Do not add CPRS menu for this new executable!  It is called"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",19,1,292,0)="        within the DRM application.)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,0)="40^3041029^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,0)="^^499^499^3041029"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,1,0)="General Information"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,2,0)="========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,3,0)="This patch contains the enhancement to send the Dental Encounter and "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,4,0)="Dental Fee Basis data to the Austin Automation Center (AAC) via an HL7 "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,5,0)="interface.  It also contains enhancements to the  Dental Record Manager "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,6,0)="(DRM) application."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,8,0)="The patch installation process should take be less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,10,0)="SYSTEM ACCESS DURING INSTALLATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,11,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,12,0)="Installation of this patch does not require users to be off of the system."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,13,0)="However, if your site is not a DRM Plus (patch 39) site, then the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,14,0)="following instructions apply: Dental users should not use the DRM GUI "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,15,0)="application while the patch is being installed: all Dental users MUST "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,16,0)="close any open DRM GUI application prior to the patch being installed: "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,17,0)="Once the patch has completed the users can use"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,18,0)="the DRM application."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,20,0)="  ********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,21,0)="  *  There is a new DRM executable exported with this patch.  This   *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,22,0)="  *  executable is only for DRM sites (not DRM Plus sites!) and MUST *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,23,0)="  * be deployed PRIOR to Dental users accessing the DRM application  *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,24,0)="  * after the patch has been installed.                              *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,25,0)="  ********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,27,0)="FIXES TO THE DRM APPLICATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,28,0)="========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,29,0)="A.  When transactions are filed only to the History file and not to  DAS,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,30,0)="    the system will now file the DAS Disposition in the Dental History "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,31,0)="    (#228.1) file correctly.  This field contains the 'in progress', "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,32,0)="    'completed' or 'terminated' flag.  The system will also correctly"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,33,0)="    file the Create Date in this case."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,34,0)="B.  Billing awareness changes were made for the procedure/diagnosis "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,35,0)="   data being sent to PCE."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,37,0)="ENHANCEMENTS TO THE DRM APPLICATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,38,0)="========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,40,0)=" A. Dental Encounter (DES) and Dental Fee Basis data will be transmitted "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,41,0)="    to the Austin Automation Center (AAC) via HL7 compliant messages. HL7"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,42,0)="    messages will be combined into batches that are compiled weekly and "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,43,0)="    sent to the AAC using the Vista interface engine.  Batches are "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,44,0)="    limited to 1000 HL7 msgs. There are at least two batches being sent"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,45,0)="    from the local sites, one containing Dental Encounter data and one "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,46,0)="    for Dental Fee Basis data. The data transfer will be initialized "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,47,0)="    through a weekly queued option. The site no longer has to manually "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,48,0)="    start the transmission to the AAC as they did for the Dental Activity "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,49,0)="    System (DAS) data.  DAS transmissions will be disabled in another"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,50,0)="    DRM patch."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,52,0)=" B. Historical Dental Encounter data (transactions filed before DRM patch"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,53,0)="    38 was installed) will be sent to the AAC via a CD.  An option is "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,54,0)="    available to create these HL7 messages and put them into a file on "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,55,0)="    a server. The file needs to be copied onto a CD and mailed to the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,56,0)="    AAC."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,58,0)=" C. A new parameter DENTV DRM DAS TURNOFF contains a date which controls"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,59,0)="    the filing of data to DAS (file 221).  When the date is reached, DRM"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,60,0)="    will no longer offer the File DAS Only option and will not file any"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,61,0)="    data to file 221 even when filing to All (DES, PCE are now the only"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,62,0)="    filing choices).  Also, the old 4 digit Provider ID will no longer"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,63,0)="    be required when adding/editing dental providers. The turnoff date "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,64,0)="    is defaulted to 10/31/2004."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,66,0)=" D. When the user looks up providers (in the Extract, Provider Add/Edit"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,67,0)="    options, the provider list will now contain their initials and title"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,68,0)="    to help differentiate users with the same name."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,70,0)=" E. Combat Veteran status has been added to the Service Connected"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,71,0)="    selection page."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,73,0)=" F. The text of the filing options was changed from ""File DAS/PCE..."" to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,74,0)="    ""File Data...""."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,77,0)="NOIS ADDRESSED BY THIS PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,78,0)="========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,79,0)="BRX-0804-10469   NOL-0804-70250   CLL-0804-40357   MON-0804-51726"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,82,0)="INSTALLATION FILES"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,83,0)="========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,84,0)=" How to Obtain KIDS File"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,85,0)=" File Name: DENT_1_2P40.zip         FTP format: binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,87,0)=" DENT_1_2P40.zip file will contain the following files:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,88,0)="                                                                   FTP "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,89,0)=" File Name                 Description                            Format"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,90,0)=" -----------------------   -------------------------------------  ------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,91,0)=" Dent_1_2p40.kid           Installable KIDS file                  ASCII"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,92,0)=" Dentalmrm.exe             DRM Version 3.13 executable            Binary "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,93,0)=" Dent_1_2p40_ug.doc        Dental Record Manager's user guide     Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,94,0)="                           The guide was updated for HL7/DAS turnoff"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,95,0)="                           and Combat Veteran status flag"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,96,0)=" Dent_1_2p40_rn_ig.pdf     DENT*1.2*40 Release Notes and          Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,97,0)="                           Installation Guide"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,98,0)=" P40_patch_description.doc A copy of the patch description        Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,99,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,100,0)=" The zip file listed above may be obtained via FTP.  The preferred method"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,101,0)=" is to FTP the files from download.vista.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,102,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,103,0)=" This transmits the files from the first available FTP server.  Sites may"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,104,0)=" also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific server as"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,105,0)=" follows:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,107,0)=" CIO FIELD OFFICE   FTP ADDRESS                 DIRECTORY"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,108,0)=" ----------------   -------------------------   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,109,0)=" Albany             ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext    [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,110,0)=" Hines              ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext     [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,111,0)=" Salt Lake City     ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext       [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,114,0)="REQUIRED BUILDS:  DENT*1.2*38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,115,0)="                  DSIC 1.3"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,118,0)="TEST SITES             SYSTEM                        ALPHA/BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,119,0)="======================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,120,0)="Black Hills, SD       (W2K Cache/Thin Client)        ALPHA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,121,0)="Westhaven, CT          VMS/Cache                     BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,123,0)="ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,124,0)="======================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,125,0)=" Second line of routines will look like:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,126,0)=" ;;1.2;DENTAL;<patch list>;AUG 10, 2001"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,127,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,128,0)="   Routine   Before Patch  After Patch  Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,129,0)="   --------  ------------  -----------  ------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,130,0)="   DENTV040      n/a        3046754        40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,131,0)="   DENTVHL       n/a        13088143       40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,132,0)="   DENTVHL1      n/a        8156724        40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,133,0)="   DENTVHL2      n/a        5154609        40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,134,0)="   DENTVHL3      n/a        4139460        40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,135,0)="   DENTVHLB      n/a        16225605       40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,136,0)="   DENTVHLF      n/a        7363704        40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,137,0)="   DENTVHLU      n/a        3937615        40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,138,0)="   DENTVRF1    5236302      5245545        31,37,40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,139,0)="   DENTVRF2    4641313      4658656        31,37,40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,140,0)="   DENTVRF4    8576541      8692191        31,37,38,40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,141,0)="   DENTVUT1    [*** to be deleted***]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,142,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,143,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,144,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,145,0)="                 INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS FOR DENT*1.2*40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,146,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,147,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,148,0)=" 1. Obtain the Dent_1_2p40.kid file"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,150,0)=" 2. For DSM sites review your mapped set.  Disable any of the above"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,151,0)="    routines if necessary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,152,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,153,0)=" 3. From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,154,0)="    the Installation menu"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,156,0)=" 4. Use Load a Distribution and enter Dent_1_2p40.kid when prompted"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,157,0)="    for a Host file.  You may need to attach a directory name"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,159,0)=" 5. You may elect to use the following options (when prompted for "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,160,0)="    INSTALL NAME, enter DENT*1.2*40)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,161,0)="    a. Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,162,0)="    b. Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,163,0)="    c. Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,164,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,165,0)=" 6. Use the Install Package(s) option and select package DENT*1.2*40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,166,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,167,0)=" 7. For the install prompts, enter either Yes or No depending upon the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,168,0)="    normal practice at your facility.  This example shows answering NO:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,169,0)="    Install Questions for DENT*1.2*40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,170,0)="    Incoming Mail Groups:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,172,0)="    Enter the Coordinator for Mail Group 'DENTV HL7 MESSAGES':[Name here]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,174,0)="     Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,175,0)="                 Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,176,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,177,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,178,0)=" 8. AXP/DSM Sites - After the patch has been installed, rebuild your map"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,179,0)="    set, if necessary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,180,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,181,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,182,0)="                        POST-INSTALLATION PROCESS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,183,0)="========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,184,0)="The post-install routine will stuff the facility ID of the installing "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,185,0)="site into the HL7 APPPLICATION PARAMTER file for the two parameters being "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,186,0)="sent with the package.  It will also set the DAS turnoff date in the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,187,0)="new parameter DENTV DRM DAS TURNOFF to 10/31.2004."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,188,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,189,0)="The post-install will also re-index some entries for the ""AXMIT"" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,190,0)="cross-reference in file 228.2 (used by the HL7 interface) due to "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,191,0)="potential issues with the Create Date being set as a string."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,192,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,193,0)=" ************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,194,0)=" *                                                                      *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,195,0)=" * THE FOLLOWING STEPS MUST BE COMPLETED FOR THIS PATCH TO WORK PROPERLY*"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,196,0)=" *                                                                      *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,197,0)=" ************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,198,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,199,0)="Step 1 is only applicable for sites which have not installed DENT*1.2*39."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,200,0)="All sites must perform steps 2-x."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,201,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,202,0)="-------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,203,0)="1                         Move dentalmrm.exe"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,204,0)="-------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,205,0)="This step is only applicable for sites which have not installed "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,206,0)="DENT*1.2*39.  '...\' indicates your UNC/path for where the current DRM "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,207,0)="v3.12 dentalmrm.exe is located."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,208,0)="       Move dentalmrm.exe to   ..\DOCSTORE"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,209,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,210,0)="-------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,211,0)="2          Set up HL7 link for transmitting DES data to the AAC"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,212,0)="-------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,213,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,214,0)="This will demonstrate one way of editing the HL7 link."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,215,0)="Note: VIE stands for Vitria Interface Engine"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,216,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,217,0)="VAH>D ^XUP"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,218,0)=" Select OPTION NAME: HL MAIN MENU       HL7 Main Menu"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,219,0)="                     ------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,220,0)=" Select HL7 Main Menu Option: FILER and Link Management Options"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,221,0)="                              -----"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,222,0)=" Select Filer and Link Management Options Option: Link Edit"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,223,0)="                                                  ----"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,224,0)=" Select HL LOGICAL LINK NODE: DENTVHLAAC"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,225,0)="                              ----------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,226,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,227,0)="You will now be in a Screenman display.  These instructions will direct "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,228,0)="you to the field that needs editing without actually displaying that "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,229,0)="Screenman display.  You will see the field:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,230,0)="         LLP TYPE: TCP"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,231,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,232,0)="Move to the LLP TYPE field.  With TCP highlighted, press <ENTER>"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,233,0)="You should now be in another Screenman display entitled:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,234,0)="         TCP LOWER LEVEL PARAMETERS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,235,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,236,0)="You will see these three fields on this display:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,237,0)="         TCP/IP SERVICE TYPE: CLIENT (SENDER)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,238,0)="              TCP/IP ADDRESS: [ip address]      "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,239,0)="                 TCP/IP PORT: [port]          "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,240,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,241,0)="A. The TCP/IP SERVICE TYPE should be 'CLIENT {SENDER}'"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,242,0)="B. Change the TCP/IP ADDRESS to your VIE IP address"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,243,0)="   1) If you don't know the VIE IP address, please go to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,244,0)="      http://vista.domain.ext/messaging/vie/vie_projectdocs.asp"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,245,0)="   2) Open the document named VIE Cluster IPs."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,246,0)="   3) Find your site and use the IP address listed there."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,247,0)="C. The TCP/IP PORT should be 8090"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,248,0)="   This port number is assigned by the VIE team for Dental"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,249,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,250,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,251,0)="Move the cursor to the line:  COMMAND:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,252,0)="Enter CLOSE  to close the TCP LOWER LEVEL PARAMETERS screen"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,253,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,254,0)="At the COMMAND: prompt on the HL7 LOGICAL LINK screen"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,255,0)="Enter EXIT to save your changes"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,256,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,257,0)="NOTE: the other logical link, DENTVHLHDR, sent in this patch will be used "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,258,0)="in the future to send messages to the Health Data Repository. Do not set "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,259,0)="this up yet."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,260,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,261,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,262,0)="-------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,263,0)="3          Turn on the HL7 link DENTVHLAAC"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,264,0)="-------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,265,0)="This step will turn the link on to enable the messages to be sent."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,266,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,267,0)="Within the same Filer and Link Management Options menu in the previous "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,268,0)="step:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,269,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,270,0)="Select Filer and Link Management Options Option: Start/Stop Links"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,271,0)="                                                 -----"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,272,0)="Select HL LOGICAL LINK NODE: DENTVHLAAC"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,273,0)="                             ----------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,274,0)="The link will be enabled.  To stop the link, follow the same steps and "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,275,0)="you will be prompted if it is Okay to shut down the job.  Answer Yes if "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,276,0)="you want to stop the link."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,277,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,278,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,279,0)="4                        Set up Weekly Scheduled Task"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,280,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,281,0)="You need to schedule the Dental HL7 Batch option to run once a week.  The "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,282,0)="VIE team is responsible for scheduling communication jobs that use the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,283,0)="VIE.  As such, they have assigned SUNDAY as the day that all VAMCs should "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,284,0)="schedule this job to run.  The time that the job runs on Sunday is left "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,285,0)="up to the individual sites.  On Monday evening, the VIE team will batch "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,286,0)="all the dental HL7 messages received from all VAMCs into a single file "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,287,0)="which will be sent to the AAC for processing."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,288,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,289,0)="VAH>D ^XUP"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,290,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,291,0)=" Select OPTION NAME: XUTM MGR       Taskman Management"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,292,0)="                     --------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,293,0)="Select Taskman Management Option: SCHedule/Unschedule Options"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,294,0)="                                  ---"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,295,0)="Select OPTION to schedule or reschedule: DENTVHLB BATCH  Dental HL7 Batch"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,296,0)="                                         --------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,297,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,298,0)="These two fields need to be properly set:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,299,0)="      QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME: select a Sunday date/time"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,300,0)="          RESCHEDULING FREQUENCY: U@2200"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,301,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,302,0)="Here is an example of setting up the weekly scheduled option:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,303,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,304,0)="                          Edit Option Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,305,0)="    Option Name: DENTVHLB BATCH                "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,306,0)="    Menu Text: Dental HL7 Batch                          TASK ID:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,307,0)=" ________________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,308,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,309,0)="  QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME: NOV 7,2004@22:00"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,310,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,311,0)="DEVICE FOR QUEUED JOB OUTPUT:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,312,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,313,0)=" QUEUED TO RUN ON VOLUME SET:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,314,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,315,0)="      RESCHEDULING FREQUENCY: U@2200"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,316,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,317,0)="             TASK PARAMETERS:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,318,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,319,0)="            SPECIAL QUEUEING:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,320,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,321,0)="__________________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,322,0)="Exit     Save     Next Page     Refresh"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,323,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,324,0)="Enter a command or '^' followed by a caption to jump to a specific field."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,325,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,326,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,327,0)="COMMAND: EXIT                                  Press <PF1>H for help    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,328,0)="Insert"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,329,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,330,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,331,0)="5                 Set up a Historical One-Time Scheduled Task"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,332,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,333,0)="The Dental Encounter System (DES) has been gathering data since Oct 2000 "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,334,0)="in file 228.  Dental VAHQ would like all that data downloaded to the new "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,335,0)="DES database at the AAC.  The amount of data at some sites might be "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,336,0)="extensive.  The VIE team and Capacity Management prefer that an option be "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,337,0)="made available to the sites to move that data to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,338,0)="a CD instead of using bandwidth on the VA WAN for moving those HL7 "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,339,0)="historical messages to the AAC.  Thus we have provided an option for the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,340,0)="site to schedule at a time that is convenient for the site."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,341,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,342,0)="To estimate the size of the file that will be generated, perform a "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,343,0)="Fileman Inquire on file 228.2.  The number of records will give you a "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,344,0)="ballpark estimate as to the size of the Historical file - each  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,345,0)="transaction will take just under 1K when formatted as an HL7 message.  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,346,0)="So, a record count of 55,024 will produce a file of < 55,000K or just "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,347,0)="under 55meg.  Not all records will be sent via the Historical batch of "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,348,0)="course, since all records created since the installation of DENT*1.2*38 "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,349,0)="will be sent via the Vista Interface Engine and the weekly process."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,350,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,351,0)="NOTE: The historical CD is expected at the AAC within one month of the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,352,0)="release of patch 40."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,353,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,354,0)="Here are the instructions for setting up a one-time Scheduled Task for "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,355,0)="the DENTVHL PROCESS HISTORIC option [menu text: Process one-time "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,356,0)="historical extract (Dental)].  Please note that this option will generate "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,357,0)="a HFS file with a name like DENTV_HISTORICAL_<site#>.TXT.  The file will "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,358,0)="be located in the directory as defined "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,359,0)="in your Kernel Site Parameters.  You can easily see what this value is "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,360,0)="from the programmer's prompt as shown in this example:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,361,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,362,0)="VAH>W $$PWD^%ZISH"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,363,0)="c:\hfs\_TO CD\"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,364,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,365,0)="Once the historical option has completed, you will need to copy that file "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,366,0)="to a CD.  You will then mail that CD to the AAC.  If you choose to FTP "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,367,0)="the file from your VMS system to another network server, then please "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,368,0)="remember to FTP the file in ASCII (or text) mode.  Here is the mailing "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,369,0)="address for that CD:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,370,0)="      George Dankworth"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,371,0)="       Records Management (396B)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,372,0)="       Dental Encounter System"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,373,0)="       1615 Woodward Street"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,374,0)="       Austin, TX  78772"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,375,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,376,0)="Example of setting up the one-time queue option:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,377,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,378,0)="VAH>D ^XUP"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,379,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,380,0)="Select OPTION NAME: XUTM MGR       Taskman Management"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,381,0)="                    --------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,382,0)="Select Taskman Management Option: SCHedule/Unschedule Options"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,383,0)="                                  ---"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,384,0)="Select OPTION to schedule or reschedule: DENTVHL PROCESS HISTORIC"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,385,0)="                                         ------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,386,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,387,0)="Here is a screen capture of the Taskman Screenman screen showing the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,388,0)="scheduling of this job:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,389,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,390,0)="                          Edit Option Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,391,0)="    Option Name: DENTVHLB BATCH                "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,392,0)="    Menu Text: Dental HL7 Batch                          TASK ID:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,393,0)=" ________________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,394,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,395,0)="  QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME: AUG 31,2004@22:00"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,396,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,397,0)="DEVICE FOR QUEUED JOB OUTPUT:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,398,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,399,0)=" QUEUED TO RUN ON VOLUME SET:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,400,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,401,0)="      RESCHEDULING FREQUENCY:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,402,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,403,0)="             TASK PARAMETERS:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,404,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,405,0)="            SPECIAL QUEUEING:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,406,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,407,0)="__________________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,408,0)="Exit     Save     Next Page     Refresh"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,409,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,410,0)="Enter a command or '^' followed by a caption to jump to a specific field."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,411,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,412,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,413,0)="COMMAND: EXIT                                  Press <PF1>H for help    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,414,0)="Insert"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,415,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,416,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,417,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,418,0)="6                          Add Members to Mail Group"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,419,0)="--------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,420,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,421,0)="An new mail group has been added called DENTV HL7 MESSAGES.  Please add "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,422,0)="members to this mail group.  These should be individuals who will be "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,423,0)="responsible for taking action if the acknowledgement messages that come "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,424,0)="back from the AAC which contain error codes.  These problems need to be "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,425,0)="addressed in the VistA DES database.  Those transactions, once fixed, "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,426,0)="will need to be flagged for retransmission.  A good candidate for a "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,427,0)="member would be the dental administrator for DRM in the Dental Service."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,428,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,429,0)="This is an example of adding a member to this mail group.  There are "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,430,0)="several Kernel options that allow the adding of members to a mail group "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,431,0)="including using Fileman.  This example just shows one of those options' "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,432,0)="display:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,433,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,434,0)="Select MAIL GROUP NAME: DENTV HL7 MESSAGES"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,435,0)="                        ------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,436,0)="Select MEMBER: [add the name of the person to become a member]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,437,0)="  TYPE:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,438,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,439,0)="=========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,440,0)="                        SAMPLE INSTALLATION EXAMPLE"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,441,0)="=========================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,442,0)="Select Installation Option: INstall Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,443,0)="Select INSTALL NAME:    DENT*1.2*40     Loaded from Distribution  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,444,0)="8/31/04@10:09:43"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,445,0)="     => DENT*1.2*40  ;Created on Aug 25, 2004@14:15:23"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,446,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,447,0)="This Distribution was loaded on Aug 31, 2004@10:09:43 with header of "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,448,0)="   DENT*1.2*40  ;Created on Aug 25, 2004@14:15:23"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,449,0)="   It consisted of the following Install(s):"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,450,0)="    DENT*1.2*40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,451,0)="Checking Install for Package DENT*1.2*40"
