^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",20,1,499,0)="DENT*1.2*40 Installed.                         Aug 31, 2004@10:10:20"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,0)="39^3041029^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,0)="^^321^321^3041029"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,1,0)=" General Information"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,2,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,3,0)=" This patch contains fixes and enhancements to the Dental Record Manager"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,4,0)=" (DRM) application.  This patch also contains new files for DRM in the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,5,0)=" DENT namespace - ^DENT(228.6) which contains tooth notes and"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,6,0)=" ^DENT(228.7) which contains reserved transactions.  The ^DENT global"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,7,0)=" should already exist on your system so no global placement is required."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,9,0)=" A database conversion will be run as part of the post installation."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,10,0)=" RVU and DSS Product line data will be set into existing transactions "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,11,0)=" from file 228 DENTAL CPT CODE MAPPING.  New System parameters required"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,12,0)=" for DRM Plus will be seeded with default data."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,14,0)=" **NOTE** Dental administrators are responsible for entering RVU and"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,15,0)=" VA-DSS Product Line information into the system for *ALL* locally mapped"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,16,0)=" medical (CPT) codes!  This information will be required for processing"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,17,0)=" transactions that are sent to Austin after patch 40 is installed.  See"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,18,0)=" the post-installation instructions for details on entering this"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,19,0)=" information."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,21,0)=" The patch installation process should take be less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,22,0)=" The post-installation conversion process may take several hours "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,23,0)=" depending upon the number of records in file 228.2.  This conversion "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,24,0)=" process will be tasked off in the background."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,27,0)="ENHANCEMENTS TO THE DRM APPLICATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,28,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,29,0)=" A. DRM Plus - an entirely new visually enhanced GUI is part of this "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,30,0)="    patch.  DRM Plus contains screens to edit Perio, PSR and Head/Neck "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,31,0)="    lesion data as well as the enhanced visual screens for general "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,32,0)="    dentistry."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,34,0)=" B. RVU data will be stored with the ADA codes and will be shipped with"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,35,0)="    with the DENTAL CPT MAPPING table (#228).  For locally added codes, "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,36,0)="    users will be able to edit RVU and VA-DSS Product Line information."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,37,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,38,0)=" C. DES Reports that were created in DRM Patch 38 have been enhanced to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,39,0)="    allow screening of transaction status (complete, pending, deleted) "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,40,0)="    and patient type (active, inactive).  The Summary Reports "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,41,0)="    provider/clinic) now allow the user the option to print only the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,42,0)="    third page totals."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,43,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,44,0)=" D. The New Extract option that was created in DRM Patch 38 has been"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,45,0)="    enhanced to allow screening of transaction status (complete, pending,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,46,0)="    findings and observe).  Both Extract options have been changed to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,47,0)="    output RVU and transaction status data to the text file."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,48,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,49,0)=" E. Selection of patient visits now offers a new radio button to view"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,50,0)="    only Dental Visits (and Scheduled appointments for Dental).  Dental"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,51,0)="    Visits are those where the location has a stop code of 180 or 181."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,52,0)="    The Dental Visits radio button is now the default selection,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,53,0)="    instead of the All button."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,54,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,55,0)=" F. Combat Veteran status has been added to the Service Connected"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,56,0)="    selection page."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,57,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,58,0)=" G. The DRM Plus application will no longer ask the user if they want to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,59,0)="    close the application after they have hit the close button."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,61,0)=" H. Users will no longer be prompted for # of Canals.  If the ADA code"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,62,0)="    in the ADA Mapping table (#228) is marked for Canals, then DRM Plus"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,63,0)="    will use that value for the transaction."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,65,0)=" I. Users have the option of saving dental information in a temporary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,66,0)="    workspace at any time in the DRM Plus workflow.  The user may close "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,67,0)="    DRM Plus or change patients and the system will prompt to save the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,68,0)="    currently entered information without having to click the Finish "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,69,0)="    button.  When the user re-opens DRM Plus for the patient with saved"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,70,0)="    data, the system will prompt to re-load the information and the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,71,0)="    user can continue through the screens."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,73,0)=" J. The user will only see active providers when selecting co-signers."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,74,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,75,0)=" SYSTEM ACCESS DURING INSTALLATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,76,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,77,0)=" Installation of this patch does not require users to be off of the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,78,0)=" system. However, all Dental users should not use the DRM GUI option "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,79,0)=" while the patch is being installed.  All Dental users MUST close any "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,80,0)=" open DRM GUI application prior to the patch being installed.  Once the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,81,0)=" patch has completed the users can use the DRM application."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,83,0)="  ********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,84,0)="  *  There is a new DRM executable exported with this patch, called  *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,85,0)="  *  dentalmrmtx.exe.  This executable will NOT be used until the    *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,86,0)="  *  site has scheduled training for DRM Plus.  The site should      *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,87,0)="  *  continue to use the old executable (dentalmrm.exe) against the  *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,88,0)="  *  the DENT*12.*39 KIDS build until that time.                     *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,89,0)="  *                                                                  *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,90,0)="  *  ** There are also new Client-side components that must be **    *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,91,0)="  *     installed for the new executable to work properly!!          *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,92,0)="  * ** Please read the post-installation instructions thoroughly! ** *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,93,0)="  *                                                                  *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,94,0)="  ********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,96,0)=" PRE-INSTALLATION PROCESS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,97,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,98,0)=" The pre-install process will save off the current ADA table (file 228)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,99,0)=" in preparation for re-loading new ADA data. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,101,0)=" The pre-install process will delete field 4.06 in file 228.2 because"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,102,0)=" the DESCRIPTION field was changed to a word processing field 4.1.  If"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,103,0)=" field .04 (PLAN NUMBER) in file 228.6 exits, it will be deleted as it"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,104,0)=" is no longer used."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,105,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,107,0)=" POST-INSTALLATION PROCESS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,108,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,110,0)=" Please read the post-installation instructions which follow the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,111,0)=" installation instructions.  All the steps in the post-install must be"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,112,0)=" completed for DRM Plus to function properly."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,115,0)=" NOIS ADDRESSED BY THIS PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,116,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,117,0)=" BRX-0804-10469   NOL-0804-70250   CLL-0804-40357   MON-0804-51726"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,118,0)=" BRX-0804-11357"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,121,0)=" INSTALLATION FILES"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,122,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,123,0)=" How to Obtain KIDS File"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,124,0)=" File Name: DENT_1_2P39.zip         FTP format: binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,125,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,126,0)=" DENT_1_2P39.zip file will contain the following files:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,127,0)="                                                                    FTP "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,128,0)=" File Name                 Description                             Format"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,129,0)=" -----------------------   -------------------------------------   ------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,130,0)=" Dent_1_2p39.kid           Installable KIDS file                   ASCII"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,131,0)=" Dentalmrmtx.exe           DRM Version 4.01 executable             Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,132,0)=" SETUP.EXE                 Initial CVision install file            Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,133,0)=" VBRUN60SP6.EXE            Microsoft VB 6.0 SP6 runtime files      Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,134,0)=" MDAC_TYP.EXE              Microsoft Data Access Components v2.8   Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,135,0)=" UPDATE.EXE                Subsequent CVision updates as necessary Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,136,0)=" Dent_1_2p39_ug.doc        Dental Record Manager's user guide      Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,137,0)="                           The guide was updated for DRM Plus"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,138,0)=" Dent_1_2p39_rn_ig.pdf     DENT*1.2*39 Release Notes and           Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,139,0)="                           Installation Guide "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,140,0)=" P39_patch_description.doc A copy of the patch description         Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,141,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,142,0)=" The zip file listed above may be obtained via FTP.  The preferred method"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,143,0)=" is to FTP the files from download.vista.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,145,0)=" This transmits the files from the first available FTP server.  Sites may"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,146,0)=" also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific server as"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,147,0)=" follows:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,149,0)=" CIO FIELD OFFICE   FTP ADDRESS                 DIRECTORY"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,150,0)=" ----------------   -------------------------   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,151,0)=" Albany             ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext    [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,152,0)=" Hines              ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext     [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,153,0)=" Salt Lake City     ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext       [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,154,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,156,0)=" REQUIRED BUILDS:  DENT*1.2*38"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,157,0)="                   DSIC 1.3"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,159,0)="10.TEST SITES             SYSTEM                        ALPHA/BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,160,0)="   ===================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,161,0)="   San Diego, CA         (VMS Cache)                    ALPHA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,162,0)="   Black Hills, SD       (W2K Cache/Thin Client)        ALPHA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,163,0)="   Manhattan, NY         (VMS Cache)                    BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,164,0)="   Daytona (Gainesville) (VMS, DSM)                     BETA "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,165,0)="   Manchester            (VMS Cache)                    BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,166,0)="   Bath, NY              (VMS DSM)                      BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,167,0)="   Fargo, ND             (W2K Cache/Thin Client)        BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,168,0)="   Boston, MA            (VMS Cache)                    BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,169,0)="   Miami, FL             (VMS, DSM)                     BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,170,0)="   Houston, TX           (VMS DSM)                      BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,172,0)=" ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,173,0)=" ======================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,174,0)=" Second line of routines will look like:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,175,0)=" ;;1.2;DENTAL;<patch list>;AUG 10, 2001"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,177,0)="   Routine   Before Patch  After Patch  Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,178,0)="   --------  ------------  -----------  ------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,179,0)="   DENTV038    [*** to be deleted***]      "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,180,0)="   DENTV03C    [*** to be deleted***]      "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,181,0)="   DENTV03D    [*** to be deleted***]      "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,182,0)="   DENTV03E    [*** to be deleted***]      "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,183,0)="   DENTV03F    [*** to be deleted***]      "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,184,0)="   DENTV03G    [*** to be deleted***]      "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,185,0)="   DENTV039      n/a        10652042       39"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,186,0)="   DENTV39A      n/a        1146103        39"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,187,0)="   DENTVA1     10886320     12453282       38,39"
