^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,212,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,213,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,214,0)=" INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS FOR DENT*1.2*39"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,215,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,216,0)=" This patch must be installed when there are no dental DRM processes"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,217,0)=" running.  All open DRM GUI applications must be closed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,218,0)=" The installation time should take less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,219,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,220,0)=" 1. Obtain the Dent_1_2p39.kid file"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,221,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,222,0)=" 2. For DSM sites review your mapped set.  Disable any of the above"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,223,0)="    routines if necessary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,224,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,225,0)=" 3. From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,226,0)="    the Installation menu"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,227,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,228,0)=" 4. Use Load a Distribution and enter Dent_1_2p39.kid when prompted"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,229,0)="    for a Host file.  You may need to attach a directory name"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,230,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,231,0)=" 5. You may elect to use the following options (when prompted for "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,232,0)="    INSTALL NAME, enter DENT*1.2*39)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,233,0)="    a. Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,234,0)="    b. Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,235,0)="    c. Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,236,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,237,0)=" 6. Use the Install Package(s) option and select package DENT*1.2*39"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,238,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,239,0)=" 7. For the install prompts, enter either Yes or No depending upon the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,240,0)="    normal practice at your facility.  This example shows answering NO:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,241,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,242,0)="     Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,243,0)="                 Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,244,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,245,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,246,0)=" 8. AXP/DSM Sites - After the patch has been installed, rebuild your map"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,247,0)="    set, if necessary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,248,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,249,0)=" 9. The post-install routine queues up a Taskman job to add RVU and "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,250,0)="    Product Line information into existing transactions in file 228.2."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,251,0)="    The post install will also add, edit or delete certain parameter "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,252,0)="    instances for DRM Plus and will add the locally added CPT codes back"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,253,0)="    into file 228."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,254,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,255,0)=" POST INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,256,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,257,0)="  ***********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,258,0)="  *  THESE STEPS SHOULD NOT BE COMPLETED UNTIL YOUR SITE IS SCHEDULED   *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,259,0)="  *  FOR DRM PLUS TRAINING!                                             *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,260,0)="  ***********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,261,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,262,0)=" 1. At this point, the KIDS install will have completed.  IRM must place"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,263,0)="    the DRM GUI executable in the appropriate directory.  The placement"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,264,0)="    of this DRM executable can be done at the same time the KIDS build is"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,265,0)="    being installed.  The executable must be placed as follows where ...\ "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,266,0)="    indicates your UNC/path for where the current DRM v3.12 dentalmrm.exe"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,267,0)="    is located:      Move dentalmrmtx.exe to ...\DOCSTORE"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,268,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,269,0)=" 2. Create a CPRS Tools menu option for this new executable"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,270,0)="    Add the DRM Plus option to the CPRS Tools Menu with these params:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,271,0)="       ...\DOCSTORE\DENTALMRMTX.EXE S=%SRV P=%PORT D=%DFN TX=1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,272,0)="    Note that the executable name is different than the current DRM"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,273,0)="    executable and the parameters contain a new string TX=1 which stands"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,274,0)="    for Treatment Plan - the new GUI display.  If you do not include this"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,275,0)="    new parameter, the Dental program will look like the existing DRM"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,276,0)="    application and none of the new features will be available to the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,277,0)="    dental user."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,278,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,279,0)=" 3. Client PC setup"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,280,0)="    There are DRM Plus support files that MUST be installed on each  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,281,0)="    Windows client PC that will be running the DRM GUI application."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,282,0)="    You must have local Administrative privileges on the client PC to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,283,0)="    properly install these files.  See the installation steps below for"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,284,0)="    details."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,285,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,286,0)="    a. Update the client machines (need Administrator privileges) by"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,287,0)="       running the SETUP.EXE, VBRUN60SP6.EXE, and MDAC_TYP.EXE programs"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,288,0)="       in that order."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,289,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,290,0)="    b. Reboot the machine and log in again as the administrator to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,291,0)="       complete the installation process!"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,292,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,293,0)="    c. Once you have installed the three programs in step 4.a. and you"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,294,0)="       need to reinstall this patch (or if test sites are upgrading to a"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,295,0)="       newer version of the patch), then you only have to run the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,296,0)="       UPDATE.EXE file to upgrade the DRM Plus client files."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,297,0)="       UPDATE.EXE does not require administrator privileges."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,298,0)="       Keep these three client installation files for future use"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,299,0)="       e.g. when new pcs are added to the dental clinic, etc."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,300,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,301,0)=" 4. Adding or Editing Local CPT Codes"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,302,0)="  a. This step needs to be done by the dental administrator.  This is"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,303,0)="     not an IRM function at most sites.  This step can be completed any"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,304,0)="     time after the patch has been installed.  This step should be"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,305,0)="     completed before the dental users are given access to the DRM Plus"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,306,0)="     application.  If not, then it is possible that those users will"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,307,0)="     select these locally added CPT codes.  Since no RVUs nor VA-DSS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,308,0)="     Product Line values are mapped, then no dental workload will be"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,309,0)="     transmitted to the new Dental Encounter System database in Austin"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,310,0)="     once patch DENT*1.2*40 is released."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,311,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,312,0)="  b. The dental administrator needs to update RVU and VA-DSS Product Line"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,313,0)="     values for any CPT codes which the site might have added to the ADA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,314,0)="     Mapping Table (#228).  If the site has not added any CPT codes to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,315,0)="     this table, then this step can be skipped.  The dental administrator"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,316,0)="     will edit this information using the DRM Plus GUI program."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,317,0)="     1) In DRM Plus, select the 'Treatment & Exam' menu"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,318,0)="     2) Within this menu, select the option 'Edit CPT/DCode Field"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,319,0)="        Values'"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,320,0)="     3) Search for the locally added CPT codes and enter the appropriate"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",21,1,321,0)="        values.  Click OK to file the information."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,0)="42 SEQ #41  ;Created on Jan 31, 2005@10:28:16^3050311^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,0)="^^511^511^3050311"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,1,0)=" General Information"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,2,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,3,0)=" This patch sets the Out Of Order message on various Dental Activity "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,4,0)=" System (DAS) options within VistA so that these options may no longer "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,5,0)=" be used.  Many enhancements/fixes were made in DRM Plus and some fixes"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,6,0)=" were made in DRM as well. See the detailed description of changes below."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,8,0)=" The patch installation process should take be less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,11,0)=" ENHANCEMENTS TO THE DRM/DRM Plus APPLICATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,12,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,13,0)=" The following enhancements apply to DRM and DRM Plus:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,14,0)=" A. The following VistA DAS options will be disabled:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,15,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,16,0)=" Menu/Option Name                Description  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,17,0)=" ------------------------------  ----------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,18,0)=" DENT GECS BATCH                 Batch Code Sheets "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,19,0)=" DENT GECS BATCH EDIT            Batch Edit "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,20,0)=" DENT GECS BATCHES STATUS        Status of all Batches "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,21,0)=" DENT GECS BATCHES WAITING TRAN  Batches Waiting to be Transmitted "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,22,0)=" DENT GECS CODE EDIT             Code Sheet Edit "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,23,0)=" DENT GECS CREATE                Create a Code Sheet "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,24,0)=" DENT GECS DELETE                Delete a Code Sheet "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,25,0)=" DENT GECS KEYPUNCH              Keypunch a Code Sheet "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,26,0)=" DENT GECS PURGE                 Purge Transmission Records/Code Sheets"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,27,0)=" DENT GECS READY FOR BATCHING L  Code Sheets Ready for Batching "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,28,0)=" DENT GECS REBATCH               Mark Code Sheets for Rebatching "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,29,0)=" DENT GECS RETRANSMIT            Mark Batch for Retransmission "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,30,0)=" DENT GECS REVIEW CODE SHEET     Review a Code Sheet "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,31,0)=" DENT GECS TRANSMIT              Transmit Code Sheets "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,32,0)=" DENT GECS MAIN MENU DENTAL      Code Sheet Manager Menu "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,33,0)=" DENT GECS MAINTENANCE USER MEN  Maintenance Menu "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,34,0)=" DENT GECS REPORTS MENU          Reports Menu "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,35,0)=" DENT GECS TRANSMIT USER DENTAL  Code Sheet Transmission Menu "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,36,0)=" DENT GECS USER MENU DENTAL      Code Sheet User Menu "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,37,0)=" DENTAPP                  Appointments "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,38,0)=" DENTCPA1                 Control Point Activity Enter/Edit"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,39,0)=" DENTCPA2                 Print/Display Control Point Activity "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,40,0)=" DENTOUT                  Outputs "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,41,0)=" DENTRELEASE              Review/Release Service Reports "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,42,0)=" DENTSCHED                Scheduling "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,43,0)=" DENTSUP                  Supervisor "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,44,0)=" DENTTREAT RELEASE        Treatment Data Review/Release Menu "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,45,0)=" DENT AMIS DELETE         Delete Dental AMIS (Temporary) Global "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,46,0)=" DENT AMIS TAPE           Generate Monthly Dental AMIS Tape "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,47,0)=" DENT SERVICE DELETE      Delete Dental Service (Temporary) Global "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,48,0)=" DENT SERVICE TAPE        Generate Monthly Dental Service Tape "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,49,0)=" DENTADM EDIT             Class I-VI (type 3) Admin Info Enter/Edit "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,50,0)=" DENTADM RELEASE          Class I-VI (type 3) Admin Info "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,51,0)=" DENTADM RE-RELEASE       Class I-VI Admin Entry (type 3) Edit/Re-Release"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,52,0)=" DENTBATCH                Enter Batch Screening/Complete Exam "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,53,0)=" DENTCARD                 Enter Data Thru Card Reader "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,54,0)=" DENTCDR                  Cost Distribution Report "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,55,0)=" DENTFEE EDIT             Applications and Dental Fee (type 5) Enter/Edit"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,56,0)=" DENTFEE RELEASE          Applications and Dental Fee (type 5) "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,57,0)=" DENTFEE RE-RELEASE       Applications and Fee (type 5) Edit/Re-Release"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,58,0)=" DENTINI                  Initialize Card Reader "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,59,0)=" DENTNCLINTIME            Non Clinical Time "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,60,0)=" DENTNCLINTIME DELETE     Delete Non Clinical Time Entry "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,61,0)=" DENTNCLINTIME EDIT       Non Clinical Time Enter/Edit "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,62,0)=" DENTNCLINTIME PROV       Non Clinical Time by Provider "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,63,0)=" DENTPERS EDIT            Personnel Info (type 4) Enter/Edit "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,64,0)=" DENTPERS RELEASE         Personnel Info (type 4) "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,65,0)=" DENTPERS RE-RELEASE      Personnel Entry (type 4) Edit/Re-Release "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,66,0)=" DENTPERS RPT             Personnel Info (type 4) "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,67,0)=" DENTPURGE                Purge Dental AMIS "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,68,0)=" DENTRELEASE ALL          Release All Service Reports "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,69,0)=" DENTTOOTH EDIT           Tooth Chart Enter/Edit "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,70,0)=" DENTTREAT DELETE         Treatment Data Entry Delete "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,71,0)=" DENTTREAT EDIT           Treatment Data Enter/Edit (Full Screen) "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,72,0)=" DENTTREAT LINE EDIT      Treatment Data Enter/Edit (Line By Line) "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,73,0)=" DENTTREAT RE-RELEASE     Enable Edit/Re-Release of Treatment Data (Full)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,74,0)=" DENTTREAT1 EDIT          Treatment Data (AMIS) Enter/Edit (Screen Handl)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,75,0)=" DENTTREATCLINIC RELEASE  Clinic Summary "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,76,0)=" DENTTREATM RE-RELEASE    Enable Edit/Re-Release of Treatment Data (Line)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,77,0)=" DENTTREATNOREV RELEASE   Release Report Without Reviewing Data "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,78,0)=" DENTTREATPROV RELEASE    Provider Summary "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,79,0)=" DENTTREATSITPROV RELEASE Sittings By Provider "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,81,0)=" -----DRM ONLY-----"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,82,0)=" B. The Summary Reports (Provider and Clinic) now offer the choice to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,83,0)="    print only the totals columns. (this is already in DRM Plus)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,84,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,85,0)=" -----DRM Plus ONLY-----"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,86,0)=" C. Added CPRS templates to Treatment Chart progress note and Addendum"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,87,0)="    screens.  CPRS templates are automatically displayed if linked to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,88,0)="    a TIU note title or embedded in the title boilerplate (applies to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,89,0)="    Treatment Chart and Clinical Record progress note title selection "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,90,0)="    screens).  NOIS:DUR-1004-31962"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,91,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,92,0)=" D. There is a new ""Save unfiled data"" dialog prompt and functionality"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,93,0)="    to allow changing of providers (occurs when DRM Plus is closed, a "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,94,0)="    patient change in CPRS occurs, and the option ""Save unfiled data"" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,95,0)="    under the File menu is clicked).  The ""Save unfiled data to another"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,96,0)="    provider"" option under the File menu was removed. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,99,0)=" FIXES TO THE DRM/DRM Plus APPLICATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,100,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,101,0)=" The following fixes apply to DRM and DRM Plus:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,102,0)=" 1. One of the routines in DENT*1.2*40 was not compatible with DSM and"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,103,0)="    caused an error trying to run.  This routine was modified to be able"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,104,0)="    to be run on either Cache or DSM and is included in this patch so"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,105,0)="    that all sites are running the same version of the routine."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,107,0)=" 2. The Fee Basis report will display data for facilities with alpha"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,108,0)="    characters in their id (e.g. 674A4).  NOIS: CTX-1004-72255"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,110,0)=" 3. The Summary Reports (Provider and Clinic) will now print the correct"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,111,0)="    Totals number.  NOIS: LEX-1104-41679"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,112,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,113,0)=" 4. Fixed a bug when loading the boilerplate of a TIU title in the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,114,0)="     progress note screen of the Clinical Record tab if a Consult-type "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,115,0)="     was selected.  The IEN of the previous note title was passed to the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,116,0)="     broker call instead of the currently selected title which could "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,117,0)="     result in the wrong boilerplate. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,118,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,119,0)=" -----DRM ONLY-----"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,120,0)=" 5. Leaving the 4 digit Provider Id blank for more than one provider"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,121,0)="    will no longer give the user a 'duplicate id' error message.  (Note:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,122,0)="    the 4 digit Provider Id is still required to file Admin time in DRM,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,123,0)="    if you are using that feature.) NOIS:PUG-1104-50509"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,125,0)=" -----DRM Plus ONLY-----"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,126,0)=" 6. D6999 will no longer change the graphical display in DRM Plus and"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,127,0)="    D4211 will prompt for tooth and not quadrant.  D2940 will now paint"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,128,0)="    the correct graphic for restoration.  D2999 and D3999 will not"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,129,0)="    paint graphics."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,130,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,131,0)=" 7. The system will now automatically display signed notes for user "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,132,0)="    selection in the Addendum screen. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,133,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,134,0)=" 8. Changed display of FGM values in the progress note output of Perio "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,135,0)="    Exams (""+"" for positive values, actual value for numbers between "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,136,0)="    1 - 9, and ""*"" for values greater than 9). "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,137,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,138,0)=" 9. The HL7 message generator will no longer generate invalid transaction"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,139,0)="    messages for DRM Plus connecting bar type transactions."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,141,0)=" 10. Changed the legend/symbol definition for FGM at the bottom of the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,142,0)="     Perio Exam progress note output (""FGM coronal to CEJ""). "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,143,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,144,0)=" 11. Allow DRM Plus to minimize if filing Problem List results in a "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,145,0)="     ""duplicate filing"" error message. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,146,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,147,0)=" 12. Duplicate Problems will no longer be filed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,149,0)=" 13. Changed the message (disclaimer) on top of the Perio Exam progress "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,150,0)="     note text to ""This is textual display of periodontal findings, "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,151,0)="     please see DRM Plus for perio charting graphic."""
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,152,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,153,0)=" 14. Automatically display the Visit selection form without having to "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,154,0)="     click the ""..."" button on the second page of the Treatment Chart "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,155,0)="     tab after the Next button is clicked."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,156,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,157,0)=" 15. When PCE filing errors occur, the system will not try to back out"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,158,0)="     DAS transactions since they are no longer filed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,159,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,160,0)=" 16. Correctly assign the provider initials in the transaction list"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,161,0)="     when the user enters a bridge, connecting bar or partial."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,162,0)="     NOIS:MIA-1104-31314, PUG-1204-51038"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,163,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,164,0)=" 17. Fixed an intermittent issue with completed procedures not "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,165,0)="     generating a code description in the progress note."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,166,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,167,0)=" 18. Corrected the translation of ""Miscellaneous"" material in "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,168,0)="     Diagnostic Findings transactions to display the text ""Misc"""
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,169,0)="     in the progress note.  Because Miscellaneous is internally "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,170,0)="     mapped as Unknown, no material is displayed with the tooth "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,171,0)="     in the progress note for transactions such as existing "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,172,0)="     Restorations."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,174,0)=" 19. The Multi Add button will now be enabled/disabled for the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,175,0)="     appropriate DCodes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,176,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,177,0)=" 20. Fixed a bug where 'Observe' type transactions were trying to be sent"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,178,0)="     through the HL7 interface and generating an error.  Only Completed,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,179,0)="     non-observe transactions should be transmitted. NOIS: MIN-1204-40802"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,180,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,181,0)=" 21. Changed the order of the lower PSR values based on a request by"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,182,0)="     the dental development group."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,183,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,184,0)=" 22. Changed the link to the VA Intranet Website under Help menu to "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,185,0)="     http://vaww1.domain.ext/drmplus1/.  (Note: this link is outside the VA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,186,0)="     network firewall). "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,187,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,188,0)=" 23. The progress note text width component code was updated.  The"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,189,0)="     progress note screens: regular note, addendum, and Clinical "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,190,0)="     Record tab note, will wordwrap the text properly at the designated"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,191,0)="     width (usually 74 characters wide). "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,192,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,193,0)=" 24. Copyright information updated to show ""1998 - 2005"" in the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,194,0)="     Help/About menu option. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,195,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,196,0)=" 25. Fixed the ""List index out of bounds"" error message when clicking "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,197,0)="     the Back button and changes in the text were detected with/without"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,198,0)="     the text marker. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,200,0)=" 26. Disabled the ""No"" button on the save data prompt when selecting the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,201,0)="     ""Save unfiled data"" menu option. Disabled the ""Cancel"" button on the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,202,0)="     save data prompt when switching patient. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,203,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,204,0)=" 27. Replaced the ""Additional Notes"" section label with a dashed line "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,205,0)="     (60 characters wide) in the progress note. Changed the ""Additional"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,206,0)="     Notes"" treeview item to ""Insert Text Marker"" so the user can "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,207,0)="     manually insert the marker in the progress note. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,208,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,209,0)=" 28. The Text Marker section marker is automatically inserted "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,210,0)="     when a CPRS template or TIU boilerplate is imported when the note"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,211,0)="     title selection is presented for the first time. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,212,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,213,0)=" 29.  A warning message will be presented to the user if changes were "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,214,0)="      made to the progress note text and the Text Marker is not found."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,215,0)="      or, if changes occur above the original placement of the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,216,0)="      Text Marker."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,217,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,218,0)=" 30. Added a new checkbox ""Default treeview display to DRM objects"" in"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,219,0)="     the User Options under the Treatment System tab.  This allows the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,220,0)="     user to select which treeview display the user prefers in the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,221,0)="     progress note. (DRM Objects is the default.)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,222,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,223,0)=" 31. The following changes were made to the DRM Plus client component:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,224,0)="     a. The message ""There are no appointments"" which could show up in "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,225,0)="        some situations has been removed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,226,0)="     b. Clicking on ""Perio Buttons"" and then clicking on a tooth will no"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,227,0)="        longer show the ADA Codes list. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,228,0)="     c. The periodontal statistics will now accurately reflect the total "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,229,0)="        number of sites and teeth for furcation and MGJ.  Teeth without "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,230,0)="        periodontal readings such as missing or denture will also be "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,231,0)="        accounted for correctly."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,232,0)="     d. Fix drawing error when adding a partial on a tooth with an "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,233,0)="        implant and a coping."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,234,0)="     e. When adding a connecting bar over missing teeth, the missing"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,235,0)="        teeth will no longer display a hollow crown image."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,236,0)="     f. Bridge and partial transactions will now be added with the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,237,0)="        correct provider."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,238,0)="     g. Problem where patient notes were being duplicated when changing"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,239,0)="        dates and clicking ""Show All"" has been resolved."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,240,0)="     h. When adding a pontic to an implant which has a coping on it; "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,241,0)="        implant will be removed appropriately."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,242,0)="     i. Clicking Add in Multi-Add without selecting a tooth or "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,243,0)="        quadrant will not generate a run-time error."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,244,0)="     j. The default code for an extracted implant is now D6100."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,245,0)="     k. Probing will now be allowed on all retained roots. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,246,0)="     l. Extracted roots will now display in the transaction list as "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,247,0)="        ""Extract"" when completed or planned."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,248,0)="     m. The ability to ""Cancel"" the Extract bridge dialog has been added."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,249,0)="     n. Notes cannot be added without first adding a transaction."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,250,0)="     o. Apostrophes will be stripped from the SpeedCode name in order to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,251,0)="        prevent a run-time error."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,252,0)="     p. The dentition message which tells the user to use the individual"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,253,0)="        dentition button has been modified to be more accurate."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,254,0)="     q. The H&N date filter now works appropriately."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,255,0)="     r. Sealant markers will now draw on top of cracked occlusal "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,256,0)="        surfaces appropriately."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,257,0)="     s. Defective materials will never display in treatment plan or "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,258,0)="        completed care."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,259,0)="     t. The default code for a coping on an implant has been changed "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,260,0)="        from D6020 to D6056."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,261,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,262,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,263,0)=" SYSTEM ACCESS DURING INSTALLATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,264,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,265,0)=" Installation of this patch does not require users to be off of the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,266,0)=" system. However, all Dental users should not use the DRM or DRM Plus "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,267,0)=" GUI option while the patch is being installed.  All Dental users MUST"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,268,0)=" close any open DRM or DRM Plus GUI application prior to the patch being"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,269,0)=" installed.  Once the patch has completed, DRM users can use the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,270,0)=" application.  DRM Plus users must have a client update performed on"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,271,0)=" their machine."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,272,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,273,0)=" POST-INSTALLATION PROCESS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,274,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,275,0)=" The KIDS post-install routine will do the following:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,276,0)=" 1. Disable the DAS options listed in the Enhancements section of this"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,277,0)="    document.  The options will be turned off by setting the Out Of Order"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,278,0)="    Message to 'DAS turned off'."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,279,0)=" 2. Change the Condition/Area/Material for some DCodes so that the DRM "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,280,0)="    Plus graphics will paint correctly."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,281,0)=" 3. Set a new multi-add flag to DCodes to better enable/disable this DRM"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,282,0)="    Plus feature for the appropriate DCodes.  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,283,0)=" 4. Remove the HL7 'pending' x-ref for all Observe DRM Plus transactions."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,284,0)=" 5. Set the new DRM Plus Treeview parameter (DENTV TP TREEVIEW DEFAULT)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,285,0)="    to Yes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,286,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,287,0)="  ***********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,288,0)="  *                                                                     *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,289,0)="  *   THE FOLLOWING STEP BE COMPLETED FOR THIS PATCH TO WORK PROPERLY   *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,290,0)="  *                                                                     *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,291,0)="  ***********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,292,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,293,0)=" After the KIDS install has completed, IRM needs to place the DRM"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,294,0)=" executable (dentalmrm.exe) or the DRM Plus executable (dentalmrtx.exe)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,295,0)=" in the appropriate directory.  If you are a DRM Plus site, then you also"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,296,0)=" must complete some additional client setup on client pcs or thin client "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,297,0)=" servers.  See the installation steps below for details. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,298,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,299,0)=" NOIS ADDRESSED BY THIS PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,300,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,301,0)=" CTX-1004-72255     PUG-1104-50509     MIA-1104-31314     DUR-1004-31962"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,302,0)=" LEX-1104-41679     MIN-1204-40802     PUG-1204-51038"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,303,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,304,0)=" REQUIRED BUILDS:  DENT*1.2*40"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,305,0)="                   DENT*1.2*39"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,306,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,307,0)=" INSTALLATION FILES"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,308,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,309,0)="  How to Obtain KIDS File and client applications:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,310,0)="  File Name: DENT_1_2P42.zip         FTP format: binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,311,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,312,0)="  DENT_1_2P42.zip file will contain the following files:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,313,0)="                                                                    FTP"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,314,0)="  File Name          Description                                   Format"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,315,0)="  -----------------  -------------------------------------         ------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,316,0)="  Dent_1_2p42.kid    Installable KIDS file                         ASCII"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,317,0)="  Dentalmrm.exe      DRM V3.1.4.0 executable                       Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,318,0)="  Dentalmrmtx.exe    DRM Plus V4.0.0.49 executable                 Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,319,0)="  setup.EXE          Initial CVision (client) install file         Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,320,0)="  update.EXE         Subsequent CVision updates (client)           Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,321,0)="  vbrun60sp6.exe     Microsoft VB 6.0 SP6 runtime files (client)   Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,322,0)="  Mdac_typ.exe       Microsoft Data Access Components v2.8 (client)Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,323,0)="  Dent_1_2p42_rn_ig.pdf  DENT*1.2*42 Release Notes and             Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,324,0)="                         Installation Guide "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,325,0)="  P42_patch_description.txt  A copy of the patch description       ASCII"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,326,0)="  DRM Plus Manual.pdf    User guide for DRM Plus                   Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,327,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,328,0)="  The zip files listed above may be obtained via FTP.  The preferred "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,329,0)="  method is to FTP the files from download.vista.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,330,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,331,0)="  This transmits the files from the first available FTP server.  Sites "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,332,0)="  may also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific server "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,333,0)="  as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,334,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,335,0)="  CIO FIELD OFFICE   FTP ADDRESS                 DIRECTORY"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,336,0)="  ----------------   -------------------------   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,337,0)="  Albany             ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext    [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,338,0)="  Hines              ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext     [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,339,0)="  Salt Lake City     ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext       [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,340,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,341,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,342,0)=" TEST SITES       DRM Plus?    SYSTEM                 ALPHA/BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,343,0)=" ====================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,344,0)=" SAN DIEGO          yes        VMS Cache              ALPHA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,345,0)=" BOSTON             yes        VMS Cache/Thin Client  BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,346,0)=" FARGO              yes        W2K Cache/Thin Client  BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,347,0)=" WESTERN NY         no         VMS Cache              BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,348,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,349,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,350,0)=" ROUTINE SUMMARY"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,351,0)=" ====================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,352,0)=" Second line of routines will look like:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,353,0)=" ;;1.2;DENTAL;<patch list>;AUG 10, 2001"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,354,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,355,0)="   Routine   Before Patch  After Patch  Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,356,0)="   --------  ------------  -----------  ------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,357,0)="   DENTV039    [*** to be deleted***] "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,358,0)="   DENTV39A    [*** to be deleted***] "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,359,0)="   DENTV040    [*** to be deleted***] "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,360,0)="   DENTV041    [*** to be deleted***] "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,361,0)="   DENTV042      n/a         8320931      42"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,362,0)="   DENTVA2     14211342      14282966     38,39,42"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,363,0)="   DENTVHL     13088143      13364754     40,42"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,364,0)="   DENTVHL2    5154609       5154663      40,42"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,365,0)="   DENTVRP4    9233470       9298307      30,32,31,42"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,366,0)="   DENTVTIX     n/a          314768       42"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,367,0)="   DENTVTPA    4823862       4902746      39,42"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,368,0)="   DENTVTPC    10530540      10565254     39,42"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,369,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,370,0)=" INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS FOR DENT*1.2*42"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,371,0)=" ======================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,372,0)=" This patch can be installed while users are on the system."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,373,0)=" The installation time should take less than 1 minute."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,374,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,375,0)=" 1. Obtain the Dent_1_2p42.kid file"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,376,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,377,0)=" 2. For DSM sites review your mapped set.  Disable any of the above"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,378,0)="      routines if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,379,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,380,0)=" 3. From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,381,0)="    the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,382,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,383,0)=" 4. Use Load a Distribution and enter Dent_1_2P42.kid when prompted"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,384,0)="    for a Host file.  You may need to attach a directory name."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,385,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,386,0)=" 5. You may elect to use the following options (when prompted for "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,387,0)="    INSTALL NAME, enter DENT*1.2*42)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,388,0)="    a. Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,389,0)="    b. Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,390,0)="    c. Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,391,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,392,0)=" 6. Use the Install Package(s) option and select package DENT*1.2*42"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,393,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,394,0)=" 7. For the install prompts, enter either Yes or No depending upon the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,395,0)="    normal practice at your facility.  This example shows answering NO:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,396,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,397,0)="     Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,398,0)="                 Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,399,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,400,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,401,0)=" 8. AXP/DSM Sites - After the patch has been installed, rebuild your "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,402,0)="    map set, if necessary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,403,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,404,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,405,0)="                        POST-INSTALLATION PROCESS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,406,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,407,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,408,0)=" 1. If your site is running dentalmrm.exe (DRM), then"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,409,0)="       Move dentalmrm.exe to   ...\DOCSTORE  and you are done!"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,410,0)="      '...\' indicates your UNC/path for where DRM is located."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,411,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,412,0)=" 2. If your site is running dentalmrmtx.exe (DRM Plus)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,413,0)="       Move dentalmrmtx.exe to   ...\DOCSTORE"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,414,0)="      '...\' indicates your UNC/path for where DRM Plus is located."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,415,0)="    Run update.exe on all client machines that will launch DRM Plus (or"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,416,0)="    all thin client servers if you are a thin client site).  Update.exe"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,417,0)="    does not require the installed to be an administrator."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,418,0)="    *********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,419,0)="    Please be careful to coordinate the server/client updates with each "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,420,0)="    other so that the dental application works properly.  You will know "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,421,0)="    if the server/client files are not compatible because launching DRM "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,422,0)="    Plus will cause approximately 30 client errors.  This also means that"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,423,0)="    you must carefully coordinate testing the new application in the TEST"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,424,0)="    account since you must run update.exe on a rarely used machine for "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,425,0)="    the dental staff to test against, as they will not be able to run the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,426,0)="    production side application after running the new update.exe."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,427,0)="    *********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,428,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,429,0)="    These are the DRM Plus files you are currently running from patch 39:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,430,0)="    dentalmrmtx.exe version 4.0.0.481    dated 10/1/2004 5:44pm (server)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,431,0)="    update.EXE      contains CVision.ocx dated 10/1/2005 3:09pm (client)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,432,0)="    *setup.EXE      new client install   dated 10/1/2005 3:10pm (client)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,433,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,434,0)="    These are the new DRM Plus files from patch 42:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,435,0)="    dentalmrmtx.exe version 4.0.0.49     dated 1/5/2004 10:33am (server)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,436,0)="    update.EXE      contains CVision.ocx dated 1/4/2005 10:50am (client)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,437,0)="    *setup.EXE      new client install   dated 1/6/2005  9:20am (client)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,438,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,439,0)="    *you only need setup.EXE to set up a new client machine, see step 3."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,440,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,441,0)=" 3. If your site is a DRM Plus site and has any new PCs, or new thin "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,442,0)="    client SERVERS that need to be able to run DRM Plus, then you must be"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,443,0)="    on the VHA domain and install the following files as an administrator"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,444,0)="    of the machine: setup.EXE, vbrun60sp6.exe, Mdac_typ.exe and REBOOT  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,445,0)="    the machine. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,446,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,447,0)="    If your site is about to be trained on DRM Plus and you need to set "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,448,0)="    up the training room and/or dental PCs/thin client SERVERS, then the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,449,0)="    files in the Dent_1_2p42.zip file supercede any files you may have "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,450,0)="    saved from the patch 39 installation.  Check the dates above to "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,451,0)="    insure you are installing the correct/latest files."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,452,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,453,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,454,0)="                           SAMPLE INSTALLATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",22,1,455,0)=" ========================================================================"
