^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,1,0)=" General Information"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,2,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,3,0)=" This patch contains fixes and enhancements to the reporting features"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,4,0)=" within Dental Record Manager.  Many new reports will now available "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,5,0)=" within DRM and DRM Plus, as well as enhancements to existing reports."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,7,0)=" Where appropriate, workload reports will allow sorting by the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,8,0)=" following categories:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,9,0)="     * 30 DAS Categories (Cases Complete, Cases Terminated, etc)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,10,0)="     * 13 ADA Categories (Diagnostic, Preventative, etc)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,11,0)="     * 131 DES Product Lines (Brief Exams, Extensive Exams, etc)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,12,0)="     * ADA/CPT Code."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,13,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,14,0)=" When the DAS Category is selected, reports display workload credit"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,15,0)=" using CTVs.  When any of the DES categories are selected, reports"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,16,0)=" display workload credit using RVUs.  CPT codes (non-DCodes) are now"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,17,0)=" included in the DES category totals."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,18,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,19,0)=" The patch installation process should take be less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,21,0)=" ENHANCEMENTS TO THE DRM AND DRM PLUS APPLICATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,22,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,23,0)=" A. The following new KLF-style reports are available within DRM/DRM Plus."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,24,0)="    These reports can retrieve data using DAS or DES type categories and"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,25,0)="    will display the appropriate workload value (CTV or RVU)."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,26,0)="    1: Observations per Month"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,27,0)="    2: Service Profile"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,28,0)="    3: Service by Product Group"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,29,0)="    4: Provider Profile"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,30,0)="    5: Patient Category Profile"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,31,0)="    6: Patients by Eligibility Setting"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,32,0)="    7: Patients by Eligibility Group"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,33,0)="    8: Patients by Dental Patient Category"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,34,0)="    9: Outpatient Service by Product Group"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,35,0)="    10: Inpatient Service by Product Group"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,36,0)="    11: Distribution of Dental Services"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,37,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,38,0)=" B. The Fee Basis Report provides the capability to view detail data. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,39,0)="    Detailed data contains subtotals and can be sorted by clicking on"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,40,0)="    the header row."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,41,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,42,0)=" C. Total Sittings/Visits by Patient Type is available.  This report"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,43,0)="    is similar to the Sittings/Visits Report within VistA/DAS reporting."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,44,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,45,0)=" D. The current Summray and Sittings reports were enhanced to use RVU vs."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,46,0)="     CTV, and multiple DES sort categories (ADA Category, VA-DSS "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,47,0)="     Products, ADA/CPT Codes) as well as the existing DAS category.  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,48,0)="     These reports currently retrieve data for providers with the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,49,0)="     new 8 digit Provider Id.  Now they will also get historical data"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,50,0)="     for any dental provider in the system."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,51,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,52,0)=" E. The Sittings Reports (Provider/Clinic) now allow sorting by column"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,53,0)="    heading once the report has been run.  Simply click on the column"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,54,0)="    that you want sorted and the data will re-arrange into the correct"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,55,0)="    sequence.  The Totals row will always remain at the end and the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,56,0)="    subtotals will be based on the column being sorted."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,57,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,58,0)=" F. The Extract options allow the user to select an individual site, or"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,59,0)="    all sites.  If a single site is selected, then the providers"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,60,0)="    displayed on the New Extract screen will be valid for the selected"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,61,0)="    site only."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,62,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,63,0)=" G. Headers in the extract text that started with ""DAS "" (for example,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,64,0)="    DAS DIVISION) have been changed to remove the DAS designation."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,65,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,66,0)=" H. The informational text on the Delete Encounter screen within the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,67,0)="    Dental History tab was changed to remove all references to DAS."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,69,0)=" I. A legend box can be displayed detailing the provider type and "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,70,0)="    specialty codes that make up the 8 digit Provider Id on any report"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,71,0)="    screen that contains the 8 digit provider Id."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,72,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,73,0)=" J. Provider lists on reports and the New Extract now display the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,74,0)="    provider type and provider specialty information next to the name."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,75,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,76,0)=" K. A new Version Information screen will pop-up for the user when a new"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,77,0)="    version is run for the first time.  The user may select to show"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,78,0)="    this screen the next time they launch DRM/DRM Plus."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,79,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,80,0)=" L. $Values, VA Cost to Perform and Equivalent Private Cost can be "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,81,0)="    entered for ADA/CPT codes by admin users.  The fields are available"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,82,0)="    on the Edit CPT Field Values option or can be quickly edited using"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,83,0)="    a new option called Edit Procedure Costs.  These values display on "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,84,0)="    various DES reports."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,85,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,86,0)=" M. Patient SSNs on the reports (Sittings, Detailed Fee Basis and the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,87,0)="    DRM Plus Provider Planning report) have been replaced with the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,88,0)="    patient name and last 4 of the SSN."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,90,0)=" DRM Plus only"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,91,0)=" -------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,92,0)=" N. Primary and Secondary Provider designations can be defined and will"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,93,0)="    display on the header of the application next to the patient name."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,94,0)="    A new report Provider Planning is available to display planned "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,95,0)="    treatment items for the primary and secondary providers.  Admin users"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,96,0)="    can define who can edit Primary/Secondary providers using a new"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,97,0)="    parameter on the Security tab of the Admin Toolbox for users."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,99,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,100,0)=" FIXES TO THE DRM/DRM Plus APPLICATIONS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,101,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,102,0)=" A. Provider selection on the report screen will be based on the selected"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,103,0)="    division.  If there is no DIVISION assigned to a Provider, then that"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,104,0)="    provider will display under any site, otherwise the Provider will "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,105,0)="    only display for sites that he/she has been assigned to.  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,106,0)="    NOIS:PUG-1104-50338 "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,107,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,108,0)=" B. The user can no longer modify (remove) the Report Date on the File"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,109,0)="    Fee Basis screen.  This was causing a 'List Index Out Of Bounds' "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,110,0)="    error.  NOIS:MAD-0205-40840"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,112,0)=" C. Non-Clinical Time no longer requires the 4 digit Provider Id to file"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,113,0)="    time.  The report will still show data for those providers with only"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,114,0)="    a 4 digit Id (historical data), but it will use the 8 digit Id if"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,115,0)="    there is one.  Non-Clinical time can be entered by non-dentist users"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,116,0)="    in the Education and Research categories."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,117,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,118,0)=" D. Transactions for partials will send Tooth# in the HL7 message to the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,119,0)="    AAC for research purposes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,120,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,121,0)=" DRM Plus only:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,122,0)=" --------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,123,0)=" E. Head and Neck, PSR and Perio data can be filed for providers without"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,124,0)="    a 4 digit Provider Id.  Only the 8 digit Id is now required."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,125,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,126,0)=" F. If all transactions for an encounter are deleted through the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,127,0)="    transaction table, then the associated encounter will also be"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,128,0)="    deleted."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,129,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,130,0)=" G. If a speed code becomes corrupted, the site (IRM) can now delete it "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,131,0)="    using the DENTV XPAR EDIT PARAMS option in VistA. NOIS:PUG-0105-51270"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,132,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,133,0)=" H. Existing Tooth Notes and Head and Neck data will be inserted into the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,134,0)="    progress note when the corresponding tree item is dbl-clicked."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,135,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,136,0)=" I. Three consecutive dashes in the progress note for PSR and Perio have"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,137,0)="    been replaced with '- -' or '-~-' so that the note no longer has"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,138,0)="    conflicts with TIU transcription placeholders. NOIS:WWW-0205-50264"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,139,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,140,0)=" J. Teeth will be displayed in tooth# order for Findings in the progress"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,141,0)="    note (example: Missing Teeth: 4, 7, 10, 12.) rather than in the order"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,142,0)="    the user enters them."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,143,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,144,0)=" K. Exiting or changing patients in DRM Plus while on the perio screen"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,145,0)="    correctly prompts to save unfiled data."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,146,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,147,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,148,0)=" SYSTEM ACCESS DURING INSTALLATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,149,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,150,0)="  Installation of this patch does not require users to be off of the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,151,0)="  system.  However, all Dental users should not use the DRM GUI option "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,152,0)="  while the patch is being installed.  All Dental users MUST close any "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,153,0)="  open DRM GUI application prior to the patch being installed.  Once the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,154,0)="  patch has completed the users can use the DRM application."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,156,0)=" POST-INSTALLATION PROCESS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,157,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,158,0)=" ***********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,159,0)=" *                                                                     *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,160,0)=" *   THE FOLLOWING STEP BE COMPLETED FOR THIS PATCH TO WORK PROPERLY   *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,161,0)=" *                                                                     *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,162,0)=" ***********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,163,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,164,0)=" After the KIDS install has completed, IRM needs to place the DRM"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,165,0)=" executable (dentalmrm.exe) or the DRM Plus executable (dentalmrmtx.exe)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,166,0)=" in the appropriate directory.  There are *NO* additional client side"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,167,0)=" installations for DRM Plus with this patch!"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,168,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,169,0)=" See the installation steps below for details. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,170,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,171,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,172,0)=" NOIS ADDRESSED BY THIS PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,173,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,174,0)=" PUG-1104-50338     MAD-0205-40840     PUG-0105-51270     WWW-0205-50264"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,175,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,177,0)=" REQUIRED BUILDS:  DENT*1.2*42"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,178,0)="                   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,179,0)="                   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,180,0)=" INSTALLATION FILES"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,181,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,182,0)=" How to Obtain KIDS File"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,183,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,184,0)=" File Name: DENT_1_2P43.zip         FTP format: binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,185,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,186,0)=" DENT_1_2P43.zip file will contain the following files:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,187,0)="                                                                 FTP "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,188,0)=" File Name          Description                                 Format"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,189,0)=" ------------------ ------------------------------------------  ------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,190,0)=" Dent_1_2P43.kid    KIDS file which will install 1 KIDS Builds  ASCII"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,191,0)="                        DENT*1.2*43"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,192,0)=" Dentalmrm.exe      DRM V3.1.5.0 executable                     Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,193,0)=" Dentalmrmtx.exe    DRM Plus V4.1.0.0 executable                Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,194,0)=" Dent_1_2p43_rn_ig.pdf  DENT*1.2*42 Release Notes and           Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,195,0)="                         Installation Guide "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,196,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,197,0)=" The zip file listed above may be obtained via FTP.  The preferred "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,198,0)=" method is to FTP the files from download.vista.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,200,0)=" This transmits the files from the first available FTP server.  Sites"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,201,0)=" may also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific server "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,202,0)=" as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,203,0)=" CIO FIELD OFFICE   FTP ADDRESS                 DIRECTORY"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,204,0)=" ----------------   -------------------------   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,205,0)=" Albany             ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext    [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,206,0)=" Hines              ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext     [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",25,1,207,0)=" Salt Lake City     ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext       [anonymous.software]"
