^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",29,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",29,1,54,0)=" Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",29,1,55,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,0)="47^3070108.170653^1"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,0)="^^483^483^3070108"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,1,0)=" General Information"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,2,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,3,0)=" This patch contains fixes and enhancements to Dental Record Manager"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,4,0)=" Plus including capturing the Distributed (Attending) Provider when"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,5,0)=" residents file data to PCE, processing for potential duplicates between"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,6,0)=" planned and completed care and a new cover page with demographic and "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,7,0)=" recent dental activity data."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,9,0)=" The patch installation process should take be less than 2 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,10,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,11,0)=" ENHANCEMENTS TO THE DRM PLUS APPLICATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,12,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,13,0)=" A. Residents are required to enter a ""Distributed"" (Attending) Provider "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,14,0)="    when filing data to PCE. The Distributed Provider will become the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,15,0)="    PCE Primary Provider for the encounter and will be sent to the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,16,0)="    national database for reporting.  All local DRM Plus reports will"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,17,0)="    continue to count workload toward the resident.  The Distributed"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,18,0)="    Provider will show up on the DRM Plus Extract."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,20,0)=" B. A new Cover Page is available with patient demographic and recent "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,21,0)="    dental activity information. Access to edit eligibility information "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,22,0)="    on this screen will be assigned by the dental administrator."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,24,0)=" C. DRM Plus will synchronize planned and completed care.  If exact"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,25,0)="    duplicates are found between planned items and newly entered "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,26,0)="    completed items (if, for example, the user enters new items rather "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,27,0)="    than completing the existing planned item) then the planned items "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,28,0)="    will be automatically deleted.  Potential duplicates matching a "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,29,0)="    tooth# will be presented to the user so that the user may decide "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,30,0)="    which item(s) to keep or delete."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,32,0)=" D. Added a ""Save & Exit"" button to the sequencing screen.  Users may "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,33,0)="    add or modify the treatment plan and file the changes without having"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,34,0)="    to click ""Next"" through the other screens.  There must be no "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,35,0)="    Completed transactions, Perio, PSR, or Head and Neck data and the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,36,0)="    most recent dental encounter must be Active for this feature to work."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,38,0)=" E. Added an ""Edentulous"" button to diagnostic findings.  Clicking "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,39,0)="    Edentulous and then clicking a tooth will mark all teeth in that "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,40,0)="    arch as missing and create the associated transactions."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,42,0)=" F. Ancillary applications or websites may be defined by the dental "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,43,0)="    administrator to launch via the DRM Plus Tools menu.  This is similar"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,44,0)="    to how DRM Plus and other applications are launched from the CPRS "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,45,0)="    Tools menu."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,47,0)=" G. There are 4 new reports in DRM Plus.  The Patient Visit List shows a "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,48,0)="    list of visits for a selected patient (does not have to be the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,49,0)="    current patient).  The Planned Items List contains the same data as"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,50,0)="    the Provider Planning report, but the columns are sortable and can be"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,51,0)="    subtotaled.  The Active Patients by Provider report shows a list of "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,52,0)="    all dental patients, by provider whose last encounter was active.  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,53,0)="    The Unfiled Data by Provider report shows a list of all patient's for"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,54,0)="    which the provider has saved temporary ""unfiled"" data."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,56,0)=" H. Users may be prompted to complete the episode of care if they are "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,57,0)="    filing data and there are no remaining planned items for the patient"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,58,0)="    and the status is Active."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,60,0)=" I. Dental Administrators may set a new parameter to not allow creation"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,61,0)="    of PCE visits ""on the fly"".  This means that the user must select "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,62,0)="    an existing visit or scheduled appointment from the list before"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,63,0)="    filing dental data."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,65,0)=" J. Small buttons were added to ADA Codes box and Multi-add box which "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,66,0)="    allows it to be moved to the other side of the mouth to view the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,67,0)="    graphics beneath."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,68,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,69,0)=" K. Missing teeth will be visually indicated in the multi-tooth selection"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,70,0)="    box by changing the buttons for missing teeth to white text on blue "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,71,0)="    background.  The missing teeth may still be selected if needed for"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,72,0)="    the procedure code (e.g. implants, etc)."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,74,0)=" L. Allow edit of unfiled H&N items.  Do not add new items if the current"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,75,0)="    item is unfiled.  This allows a user to modify the H&N text in the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,76,0)="    same session, rather than creating additional detail records."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,78,0)=" M. Display H&N progress records on primary grid.  Add column containing "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,79,0)="    ""Initial"" or ""Progress"". This allows the user to view all H&N entries"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,80,0)="    on the primary screen."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,81,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,82,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,83,0)=" FIXES TO THE DRM Plus APPLICATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,84,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,85,0)=" 1. Head and Neck data will be filed to the correct provider when the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,86,0)="    user files all data to another provider."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,88,0)=" 2. The warning message that a Location must be entered has been removed"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,89,0)="    for most cases.  Location is required on the second page of DRM Plus"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,90,0)="    anyway, it did not need to be forced at application runtime."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,92,0)=" 3. The VA Intranet Website location has been updated.  This site "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,93,0)="    contains information for VA dental users, including updates to DRM "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,94,0)="    Plus user manuals."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,96,0)=" 4. Test patients and ""extra"" partial transactions will not appear in "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,97,0)="    the DRM Plus extract."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,99,0)=" 5. If an Additional Signer is entered for one patient, and a note is "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,100,0)="    entered and signed from the Clinical Record tab for the next "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,101,0)="    patient, the additional signer will not carry over to the next "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,102,0)="    patient."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,104,0)=" 6. If a previous Head & Neck entry is deleted and a new entry is created "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,105,0)="    in the same session, the new entry will be created correctly, rather "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,106,0)="    than being created as a deleted record."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,108,0)=" 7. The code boilerplate from TIU was putting an additional text marker "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,109,0)="    into the DRM Plus note.  When two text markers are present and the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,110,0)="    user clicks 'Back' and 'Next' the note was being duplicated"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,111,0)="    exponentially.  The second text marker has been removed and this "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,112,0)="    will no longer occur."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,114,0)=" 8. Users without an 8 digit provider Id may run reports without seeing "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,115,0)="    a list-out-of-bounds error message."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,117,0)=" 9. If the user had selected a tab, other than the Chart/Treatment tab "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,118,0)="    as the initial tab, a run time error was generated when changing "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,119,0)="    patients from CPRS.  Any tab can be selected as the initial tab"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,120,0)="    (including the new Cover Page) without generating a runtime error "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,121,0)="    when changing patients."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,123,0)=" 10. ""Observe"" type transactions will appear in the progress note when"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,124,0)="     entered from the Completed tab. This type of transaction will "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,125,0)="     always appear under the Other Dental Findings heading."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,127,0)=" 11. Markers on a surface ""m"" will now be removed when adding a retained"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,128,0)="     root to the tooth."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,129,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,130,0)=" 12. When adding a retained root to a crown, the crown will be removed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,131,0)="     Prevent whole tooth extraction on a tooth with retained roots."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,132,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,133,0)=" 13. Corrected the tooltip text (hover help) for the ""Add Sub-Phase"" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,134,0)="     button on the sequencing screen."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,135,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,136,0)=" 14. The tooth selection box will be cleared for multi-add when using "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,137,0)="     quick list or local codes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,138,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,139,0)=" 15. Corrected advance of MGJ on the perio screen."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,141,0)=" 16. PSR data will be cleared when changing patients.  This will prevent"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,142,0)="     PSR data from the previous patient displaying incorrectly."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,143,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,144,0)=" 17. Corrected problem with the asterisks on the notes button not "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,145,0)="     appearing in certain scenarios."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,146,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,147,0)=" 18. If the perio ""clear"" function results in an impacted tooth showing "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,148,0)="     at tooth #1, then the auto-advance did not work properly.  This has "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,149,0)="     been fixed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,150,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,151,0)=" 19. Changed planned extraction to remove M/D lesions."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,152,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,153,0)=" 20. Corrected the jumbled view of multi-tooth when selecting a non-"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,154,0)="     multi-tooth code."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,156,0)=" 21. When adding a coping or crown on top of an existing implant by using"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,157,0)="     the ADA Codes or Add text box, the graphics did not draw "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,158,0)="     appropriately.  The graphic will now display correctly."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,159,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,160,0)=" 22. When DRM changes patients, return to the default view."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,161,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,162,0)=" 23. The perio ""Compare"" button will now be enabled when there are two"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,163,0)="     exams to compare."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,164,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,165,0)=" 24. Removed accelerator keys from H&N, Sequencing, PSR and Plaque "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,166,0)="     Index screens."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,167,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,168,0)=" 25. Changed display of planned graphics to always apply planned items "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,169,0)="     after any diagnostic findings or completed items regardless of date."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,170,0)="     This may result in planned items not showing correctly in some cases."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,172,0)=" 26. If you mark as missing a root on a bridge abutment and then try to"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,173,0)="     remove the bridge by clicking missing and then the pontic, the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,174,0)="     extract bridge popup does not show and only the pontic is removed,"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,175,0)="     leaving the bar in place.  This has been fixed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,177,0)=" 27. Add retained root, then planned extract root, implant, coping, "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,178,0)="     crown.  After that, the already pressed restore button does not "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,179,0)="     work on any teeth.  This has been fixed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,180,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,181,0)=" 28. Don't save the sequencing note if it has not changed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,182,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,183,0)=" 29. CCOW will be defaulted OFF, or disabled.  In order to enable it, IRM"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,184,0)="     must add a CCOW=ON parameter to the CPRS Tools menu string for DRM "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,185,0)="     Plus.  (CCOW=1 will also enable CCOW.)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,186,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,187,0)=" 30. Admin users may no longer ""re-add"" nationally mapped CPT codes to "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,188,0)="     the ADA Mapping table which allowed them to modify the RVU and "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,189,0)="     VA-DSS product line information."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,190,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,191,0)=" 31. Quick codes that are DRM Plus ""ranged"" codes (used in bridges for"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,192,0)="     example) can now be removed from the user's Quick List.  This"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,193,0)="     affected sites as they were migrating to DRM Plus from DRM."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,194,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,195,0)=" 32. A single diagnosis is pre-selected as the Primary PCE Diagnosis."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,196,0)="     This will work when there is a single diagnosis entry on the filing"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,197,0)="     options page, or when there are multiple entries as long as they are"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,198,0)="     all the same diagnosis code."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,199,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,200,0)=" 33. A list-out-of-bounds error will no longer occur trying to create the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,201,0)="     progress note under certain (infrequent) circumstances when the user"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,202,0)="     clicks back and next, deleting and adding transactions many times."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,203,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,204,0)=" 34. The Print button on the File menu will only work for 'Notes' on the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,205,0)="     Clinical Record tab.  The other types of entries (Meds, Consults, "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,206,0)="     Vitals, etc) cannot be printed from DRM Plus."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,207,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,208,0)=" 35. Diagnostic Findings older than the 1 day that are deleted by an "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,209,0)="     admin user will be removed from the graphic and the transaction "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,210,0)="     list.  These were previously shown in the transaction list with a "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,211,0)="     strike-through as if a non-admin user had deleted them.     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,212,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,213,0)=" 36. Partials that were modified or deleted in the sequencing screen"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,214,0)="     displayed incorrectly in the progress note.  They were showing "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,215,0)="     entries for each tooth in the partial rather than a single entry."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,216,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,217,0)=" 37. The Visit Date will be used in the transaction list rather than the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,218,0)="     date the item was created.  This is a more relevant date to the user."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,219,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,220,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,221,0)=" SYSTEM ACCESS DURING INSTALLATION"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,222,0)=" ========================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,223,0)=" Installation of this patch does not require users to be off of the "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,224,0)=" system. However,  all Dental users should not use the DRM Plus GUI"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,225,0)=" while the patch is being installed.  All Dental users MUST close any "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,226,0)=" open DRM Plus GUI application prior to the patch being installed.  Once "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,227,0)=" the patch has completed the users can use the DRM Plus application."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,228,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,229,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,230,0)=" POST-INSTALLATION PROCESS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,231,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,232,0)=" The post-installation will change the D6056 ada code to 'Coping' for"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,233,0)=" the correct DRM Plus graphics, will set a default for the new "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,234,0)=" DENTV DRM NO VISIT CREATE and DENTV DRM DUPCHECK OFF parameters and "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,235,0)=" will add 1 to each entry defined in the DENTV DRM DEF STARTUP TAB "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,236,0)=" parameter because there's a new tab zero (0) for the Cover Page. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,237,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,238,0)=" The post-installation will also start a TaskMan job to loop through "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,239,0)=" all the Dental History entries (228.1) for each Dental Patient (220)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,240,0)=" and inactivate (set DAS DISPOSITION=Completed) the last encounter if "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,241,0)=" the status is 'In Progress' and date is > 2 years (730 days)."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,242,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,243,0)=" ***********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,244,0)=" *                                                                     *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,245,0)=" *   THE FOLLOWING STEP BE COMPLETED FOR THIS PATCH TO WORK PROPERLY   *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,246,0)=" *                                                                     *"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,247,0)=" ***********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,248,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,249,0)=" After the KIDS install has completed, IRM needs to place the DRM Plus"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,250,0)=" executable (dentalmrmtx.exe) in the appropriate directory.  IRM must "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,251,0)=" also complete some additional client setup on client pcs or thin client "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,252,0)=" servers.  See the installation steps below for details. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,253,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,254,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,255,0)=" REMEDY CALLS ADDRESSED BY THIS PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,256,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,257,0)=" Sheridan    HD141287 iMed Consent button"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,258,0)=" Gainesville HD140425 Additional signer error"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,259,0)=" Gainesville HD139916 default tooth number for D9971 Multiadd"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,260,0)=" Gainesville HD136629 List index out of Bounds Error when no appts/cancel"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,261,0)=" Gainesville HD135195 Teeth graphic will not provide proper display"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,262,0)=" Gainesville HD135014 List index out of bounds error generating note"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,263,0)=" Puget Sound HD134425 TIU notes repeat when dbl hyphen line is present"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,264,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,265,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,266,0)=" REQUIRED BUILDS:  DENT*1.2*46"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,267,0)="                   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,268,0)="                   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,269,0)=" INSTALLATION FILES"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,270,0)=" ===================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,271,0)=" How to Obtain KIDS File"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,272,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,273,0)=" File Name: Dent_1_2P47.zip                FTP format: binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,274,0)=" Dent_1_2p47.zip file will contain the following files:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,275,0)="                                                         FTP "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,276,0)=" File Name              Description                     Format"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,277,0)=" ------------------     ----------------------------    ------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,278,0)=" Dent_1_2p47.kid        KIDS file which will install    ASCII"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,279,0)="                         one KIDS Builds: DENT*1.2*47"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,280,0)=" dentalmrmtx.exe        DRM Plus V4.7.0.7 executable    Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,281,0)=" setupP47.EXE           CVision (client) install file   Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,282,0)=" Dent_1_2p47_rn_ig.pdf  DENT*1.2*47 Release Notes and   Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,283,0)="                         Installation Guide "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,284,0)=" P47_QUICKstart.pdf     Description (w/ screen shots)   Binary"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,285,0)="                         of the enhancements/fixes "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,286,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,287,0)=" The zip files listed above may be obtained via FTP.  The preferred "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,288,0)=" method is to FTP the files from download.vista.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,289,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,290,0)=" This transmits the files from the first available FTP server.  Sites"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,291,0)=" may also elect to retrieve software directly from a specific server "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,292,0)=" as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,293,0)=" CIO FIELD OFFICE   FTP ADDRESS                 DIRECTORY"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,294,0)=" ----------------   -------------------------   --------------------"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,295,0)=" Albany             ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext    [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,296,0)=" Hines              ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext     [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,297,0)=" Salt Lake City     ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext       [anonymous.software]"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,298,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,299,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,300,0)=" TEST SITES             SIZE/TYPE               ALPHA/BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,301,0)=" ===================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,302,0)=" Tuscon, AZ             Large                   ALPHA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,303,0)=" Houston, TX            Large                   BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,304,0)=" Manhattan, NY          Large                   BETA"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,305,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,306,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,307,0)=" ROUTINE SUMMARY (checksums using CHECK1^XTSUMBLD)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,308,0)=" ===================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,309,0)="  Second line of routines will look like:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,310,0)="   ;;1.2;DENTAL;<patch list>;Aug 10, 2001"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,311,0)="  "
