^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,340,0)="   DENTVTPD  29778472        31135124   39,47"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,341,0)="   DENTVUTL  19086877        22593588   30,33,34,36,31,43,45,47"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,342,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,343,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,344,0)=" INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS FOR DENT*1.2*47"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,345,0)=" ======================================================================"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,346,0)=" This patch must be installed when there are no dental DRM processes"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,347,0)=" running.  All open DRM Plus GUI applications must be closed."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,348,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,349,0)=" The installation time should take less than 2 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,350,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,351,0)=" 1. Obtain the Dent_1_2P47.kid file"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,352,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,353,0)=" 2. From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,354,0)="    the Installation menu"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,355,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,356,0)=" 3. Use Load a Distribution and enter Dent_1_2P47.kid when prompted"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,357,0)="    for a Host file.  You may need to attach a directory name"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,358,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,359,0)=" 4. You may elect to use the following options (when prompted for "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,360,0)="    INSTALL NAME, enter DENT*1.2*47)"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,361,0)="    a. Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,362,0)="    b. Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,363,0)="    c. Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,364,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,365,0)=" 5. Use the Install Package(s) option and select package DENT*1.2*47"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,366,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,367,0)=" 6. For the install prompts, enter either Yes or No depending upon the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,368,0)="    normal practice at your facility.  This example shows answering NO:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,369,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,370,0)=" Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,371,0)=" Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,372,0)=" Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,373,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,374,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,375,0)="                        POST-INSTALLATION PROCESS"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,376,0)=" ======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,377,0)=" 1. Move dentalmrmtx.exe to   ...\DOCSTORE"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,378,0)="      '...\' indicates your path for where DRM Plus is located."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,379,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,380,0)="    Run setupP47.EXE on all Windows Workstations, Thin Client Servers, "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,381,0)="    Windows Terminal Services Servers and Citrix Servers that need to "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,382,0)="    launch the dentalmrmtx.exe you moved to \DOCSTORE.  SetupP47.exe does"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,383,0)="    NOT need to be run on the machine that hosts the \DOCSTORE folder."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,384,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,385,0)="    We recommend that setupP47.EXE be run by an administrator. "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,386,0)="    SetupP47.EXE replaces the CVision.ocx file (and other files) in"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,387,0)="    C:\WINNT\SYSTEM32 and registers it on the machine.  The version"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,388,0)="    of CVision.ocx (found by right-clicking the .ocx and selecting "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,389,0)="    Properties option, Version tab) is 2.2.0.14."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,390,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,391,0)="    Note: On some Windows Server machines the setupP47.EXE file "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,392,0)="    will not update the CVision.ocx file in WINNT\SYSTEM32."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,393,0)="    If the version is not 2.2.0.14 then Micorsoft's Data Execution"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,394,0)="    Prevention (DEP) may be the issue.  Turn DEP off (call DSS tech"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,395,0)="    support if you need help with this), reboot the machine and install"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,396,0)="    the client side files by running setupP47.EXE. Additional information"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,397,0)="    on Microsoft's DEP can be found at: "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,398,0)="    http://support.microsoft.com/kb/875352"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,399,0)="        "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,400,0)="    *********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,401,0)="    Please be careful to coordinate the server/client updates with each "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,402,0)="    other so that the dental application works properly.  You will know "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,403,0)="    if the server/client files are *NOT* compatible because launching DRM "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,404,0)="    Plus will cause approximately 30 client errors!  This also means that"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,405,0)="    you must carefully coordinate testing the new application in the TEST"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,406,0)="    account since you must run setupP47.exe on a rarely used machine for "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,407,0)="    the dental staff to test against, as they will not be able to run the"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,408,0)="    production side application after updating the client."
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,409,0)="    *********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,410,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,411,0)=" 2. Once the patch is released, the Patch 47 User Manual and "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,412,0)="    Administrative Manual will be available are available on the DRM Plus"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,413,0)="    intranet site: http://vaww1.domain.ext/dental/ under the DRM Plus"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,414,0)="    link found on the left side of the main page, then DRM Plus Resources"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,415,0)="    found at the bottom of the page.  "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,416,0)="    The documents are titled:"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,417,0)="      DRM Plus Administrators Manual"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,418,0)="      DRM Plus Users Manual"
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,419,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,96,22,1.2,"PAH",30,1,420,0)=" ========================================================================"
