^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,374,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,375,0)="   Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,376,0)="   =========================="
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,377,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,378,0)="   1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,379,0)="      This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto your"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,380,0)="      system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,381,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,382,0)="   2. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,383,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,384,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,385,0)="      following options:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,386,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,387,0)="                 Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,388,0)="                 Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,389,0)="                 Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,390,0)="                 Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,391,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,392,0)="   3. Users may remain on the system, but installation should be done at"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,393,0)="      off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,394,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,395,0)="   4. Installation will take less than five minutes. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,396,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,397,0)="   5. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,398,0)="      'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'YS*5.01*53' and proceed"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,399,0)="      with install."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,400,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,401,0)="   6. If you do not intend to queue the installation to run after normal"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,402,0)="      business hours, then answer ""NO"" to the following prompt:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,403,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,404,0)="      Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of Install? YES// NO"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,405,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,406,0)="      If you answer ""YES"", then the installation will require much more "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,407,0)="      than 5 minutes to run due to the menu rebuild process."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,408,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,409,0)="   7. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options,"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",31,1,410,0)="      and Protocols? YES//', respond  NO."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",32,0)="58 SEQ #51^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",32,1,0)="^^5^5^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",32,1,1,0)="This patch corrects an error that occurs in menu option ""Identify Potential"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",32,1,2,0)="Merge Problems [XDR VALID CHECK]"".  Although it originally appeared to be a"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",32,1,3,0)="FILEMAN error, it was later determined to be a data dictionary problem with"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",32,1,4,0)="the MEDICAL RECORDS file (#90) of the MENTAL HEALTH Version 5.01 software"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",32,1,5,0)="application."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,0)="54 SEQ #52^3000229^1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,0)="^^104^104^3000229"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,1,0)="The following items are addressed in patch YS*5.01*54:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,3,0)=" 1. Patch YS*5.01*54 releases two new psychological tests/interviews to "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,4,0)="    the Mental Health package.  These tests are accessed via menu item "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,5,0)="    Psychological tests/interviews (administer) [YSADMTEST].  The new "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,6,0)="    tests are as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,8,0)="    a. Test Name:  AIMS"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,9,0)="       Description:  Abnormal Involuntary Movement Scale  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,10,0)="       Number of Questions:  12"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,11,0)="       Number of Scales:  1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,12,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,13,0)="    b. Test Name:  AUDC"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,14,0)="       Description:  Alcohol Use Disorders Identification Test Condensed"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,15,0)="       Number of Questions:  3"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,16,0)="       Number of Scales:  1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,17,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,18,0)="    These tests are stored as new entries in the MH INSTRUMENT FILE (#601)."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,19,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,20,0)=" 2. Two new routines are included in patch YS*5.01*54.  They are:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,21,0)="    YTAIMS      -  Abnormal Involuntary Movement Scale"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,22,0)="    YTALUSEC    -  Test-Audit Alcohol Screen Condensed"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,23,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,24,0)=" 3.  When the user selects option Psychological tests/interviews"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,25,0)="    (administer) [YSADMTEST] and chooses the instrument ""MMPI"" a message"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,26,0)="    is displayed on the screen ""You have selected the ""MMPI"" instrument, "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,27,0)="    the ""MMPI2"" instrument will be administered in its place."". Routines"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,28,0)="    YTAR and YTS have been modified to display this message."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,29,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,30,0)=" 4. The file MH INSTRUMENT (#601) field OPERATIONAL (#32) will be populated"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,31,0)="    with a value of ""N"" for the instrument MMPI when the post routine YS54POST"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,32,0)="    is executed."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,33,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,34,0)=" 5. Patch YS*5.01*54 also includes updates to the instruments AUDIT, "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,35,0)="    CAGE, DOM80, DOM81, DOM82, DOMG, and the SMAST.  These instruments were "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,36,0)="    sent out in patch YS*5.01*31 as NON-EXEMPT, when they should have been "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,37,0)="    sent out as EXEMPT.  The file MH INSTRUMENT (#601) field EXEMPT TEST (#21)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,38,0)="    for the instruments mentioned will be populated with a value of ""Y"""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,39,0)="    when the post routine YS54POST is executed."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,40,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,41,0)=" 6. Patch YS*5.01*54 also includes 2 additional entries in the MH INSTRUMENT "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,42,0)="    FILE (#601).  The Addiction Survey Index (ASI) and the Global "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,43,0)="    Assessment of Functioning (GAF) are placeholders to be used in retrieving"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,44,0)="    ASI and GAF data used by APIs and RPCs released in patch YS*5.01*53."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,45,0)="    These entries are non operational when accessed via menu item "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,46,0)="    Psychological tests/interviews (administer) [YSADMTEST]."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,47,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,48,0)="    Test Site(s): North Texas HCS, TX"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,49,0)="                  Palo Alto HCS, CA"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,50,0)="                  Puget Sound HCS, WA"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,51,0)="                  Salt Lake City, NV"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,52,0)="                  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,53,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,54,0)="   ROUTINE SUMMARY:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,55,0)="   ================"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,56,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,57,0)="   The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,58,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,59,0)="   <tab>   ;;5.01;MENTAL HEALTH;**[patch list]**;Dec 30, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,60,0)="    "
