^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,74,0)="   Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,75,0)="   =========================="
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,77,0)="   1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,78,0)="      This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto your"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,79,0)="      system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,81,0)="   2. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,82,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,83,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,84,0)="      following options:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,86,0)="                 Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,87,0)="                 Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,88,0)="                 Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,89,0)="                 Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,91,0)="   3. Users may remain on the system, but installation should be done at"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,92,0)="      off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,93,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,94,0)="   4. Installation will take less than five minutes."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,96,0)="   5. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option five"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,97,0)="      'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'YS*5.01*54' and proceed"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,98,0)="      with install."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,99,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,100,0)="   6. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options,"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,101,0)="      and Protocols? YES//', respond  NO."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,102,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,103,0)="   7. Routine YS54POST will be deleted by KIDS after successful patch"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",33,1,104,0)="      installation."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,0)="55 SEQ #53^3000405^1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,0)="^^140^140^3000405"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following problems associated with the Mental "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,2,0)="Health ADDICTION SURVEY INDEX software."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,4,0)="1.  Problem: $ZE= <UNDEFINED>PUTWP+9^DIEFW."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,5,0)="    The option ASI National Roll Up [YSAS NATIONAL ROLL UP] gets the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,6,0)="    undefined error because of the change to the temporary data gathering "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,7,0)="    global structure after the installation of Mailman Patch 50 & FILEMAN "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,8,0)="    V. 22.  The code in routine ^YSASRU has been corrected."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,10,0)="2.  Problem: $ZE= PTFLP+4^YSASCF:1, %DSM-E-UNDEF, undefined variable."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,11,0)="    The option ASI Case finder [YSAS CASE FINDER] will error out at"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,12,0)="    PTFLP+4^YSASCF when it encounters A missing node in the PTF file (#45) "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,13,0)="    multiple field 501 (#50).  The code in routine YSASCF has been "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,14,0)="    corrected."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,16,0)="3.  Problem: $ZE= OE+3^YSASCF:1, %DSM-E-UNDEF, undefined variable"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,17,0)="    The option ASI Case Finder [YSAS CASE FINDER] will error out at "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,18,0)="    OE+3^YSASCF when the ""B"" cross reference was created for The Outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,19,0)="    Encounter file (#409.68) but did not contain the zero node for that "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,20,0)="    entry.  The routine YSASCF has been modified to check if the entry"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,21,0)="    exists."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,23,0)="4.  The option ASI Follow-up Finder [YSAS FOLLOWUP FINDER] generates a"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,24,0)="    mail message that splits the results into separate mail messages for"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,25,0)="    every 1000 lines.  The subject of each mail message displays which"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,26,0)="    page of how many pages there are for the report generated."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,27,0)="    Such as below:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,29,0)="    ASI Follow-up Reminder      (1 OF 2),(2 of 2) etc. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,31,0)="    The page counter in the subject of the mail message created in routine  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,32,0)="    YSASFUR has been corrected."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,33,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,34,0)="5.  The routine YSASCF has been corrected to retrieve the correct "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,35,0)="    institution station number.  This error would only occur at Anchorage,"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,36,0)="    Honolulu, Las Vegas, San Juan and West Palm Beach."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,37,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,38,0)="6.  The option Activate/Inactivate ASI Program Types [YSAS ASI PROGRAM"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,39,0)="    ACTIVATION] allows the user to edit the TITLE field (#1) instead of"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,40,0)="    the ACTIVE field (#3) in the ASI PROGRAM TYPE file (#604.26).  This"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,41,0)="    has been corrected in routine YSASFM."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,42,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,43,0)="7.  When the narrative report prints, the employee who administers"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,44,0)="    (interviewer) the Addiction Severity Index has a title that contains"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,45,0)="    Roman Numerals.  When converting the text from upper case to lower"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,46,0)="    case the second Roman numeral in the interviewers title is printed"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,47,0)="    in lower case.  This has been corrected in routine YSASNAR. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,49,0)="NOIS List:  HON-0200-62334"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",34,1,50,0)="            HOU-0100-70481"
