^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,32,0)="   ------------       ------------        -----------         ----------"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,33,0)="   YSGAFAP1              N/A                  1639398         64"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,35,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,36,0)="   Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,37,0)="   =========================="
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,38,0)="    1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,39,0)="       This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,40,0)="       your system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,41,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,42,0)="    2. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,43,0)="       system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,44,0)="       global. On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,45,0)="       the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,47,0)="                  Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,48,0)="                  Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,49,0)="                  Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,50,0)="                  Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,52,0)="    3. Installation of this patch should be at off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,54,0)="    4. Users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,56,0)="    5. Installation will take less than five minutes. Installation"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,57,0)="       of this patch requires no additional memory space."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,59,0)="    6. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,60,0)="      'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'YS*5.01*64' and"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,61,0)="       proceed with install."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,62,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,63,0)="    7. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,64,0)="       install? YES//', respond  NO."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,66,0)="    8. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",38,1,67,0)="       Options, and Protocols? YES//', respond  NO."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,0)="59 SEQ #58^3000816^1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,0)="^^126^126^3000816"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issues in the Mental Health GAF software. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,3,0)="1. The description of Mail Group 'YS GAF TRANSMISSION ACK' has been edited."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,4,0)="   This mail group will receive a message with the subject of 'GAF Score"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,5,0)="   Sent' when a GAF score is transmitted to the National Patient Care"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,6,0)="   Database (NPCD) at the Austin Automation Center (AAC) in Austin, Texas."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,7,0)="   If an error in the transmission has occurred the subject of the message"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,8,0)="   will be 'GAF Score Transmission Problem'.  This mail group will also be"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,9,0)="   used to receive a transmission report, GAF Facility Report, with the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,10,0)="   subject 'NPT/XXX #XXXXXXXXXXXX' from the NPCD at the AAC.  The 'XXXs'"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,11,0)="   in the subject are random alphanumerics produced by the AAC system.  The"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,12,0)="   report will contain the number of messages received, number of messages"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,13,0)="   processed and number of messages processed in error.  The report will"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,14,0)="   also contain a detail line for each type of error.  The detail error line"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,15,0)="   of the report will contain the reject message ID number, Error Code,"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,16,0)="   Event Date-Time, Social Security Number, Last Name of Patient, Date"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,17,0)="   of Birth and the Inpatient/Outpatient Status.  A document, YS_501_59.PDF,"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,18,0)="   describing the error codes provided by NPCD is available on one of the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,19,0)="   following OI Field Offices' ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE directories in Albany,"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,20,0)="   Hines or Salt Lake City."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,21,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,22,0)="2. The routine YSGAFOBX was setting the Mail Group to use 'YS GAF TO NPCD',"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,23,0)="   therefore sending a MAILMAN message containing text to be processed by "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,24,0)="   NPCD at the AAC.  These messages should have been sent locally to the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,25,0)="   members of Mail Group 'YS GAF TRANSMISSION ACK' who are responsible for"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,26,0)="   the Global Assessment of Function monitoring.  The subjects of these"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,27,0)="   messages are 'GAF Score Sent' and 'GAF Score Transmission Problem'."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,28,0)="   The message 'GAF Score Sent' contains the patients name, date of"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,29,0)="   observation the GAF score was assessed and the HL7 message number"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,30,0)="   transmitted to NPCD at the AAC.  The message 'GAF Score Transmission"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,31,0)="   Problem' contains the reason why the message was not transmitted, user"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,32,0)="   who entered the GAF score, patient name, observation date and file entry"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,33,0)="   date."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,34,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,35,0)="3. A new option 'GAF Transmission' [YS GAF TRANSMISSION] will be used to"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,36,0)="   retransmit GAF data for a given date range to the National Patient Care"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,37,0)="   Database at the Austin Automated Center in Austin, TX.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,38,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,39,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,40,0)="NOIS call(s): BOS-0399-12563"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,41,0)="              TUA-0199-31948"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,42,0)="              "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,43,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,44,0)="Test Site(s): Connecticut HCS, CT"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,45,0)="              Gulf Coast HCS, MS"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,46,0)="              Iowa City, IA"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,47,0)="              Muskogee, OK"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,48,0)="              Tampa, FL"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,49,0)="              Portland, OR"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,50,0)="              West Palm Beach, FL "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,51,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,52,0)="   DOCUMENTATION RETRIEVAL:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,53,0)="   ========================"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,54,0)="   The documentation file is available on one of the following OI Field "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,55,0)="   Offices' ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE directories."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,56,0)="   All sites are encouraged to use their FTP capability to obtain this "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,57,0)="   file."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,58,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,59,0)="       OI FIELD OFFICE     FTP ADDRESS        DIRECTORY"
