^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,87,0)="     Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,88,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,89,0)="     =========================="
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,90,0)="    1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,91,0)="       This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,92,0)="       your system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,93,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,94,0)="    2. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,95,0)="       system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,96,0)="       global. On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,97,0)="       the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,98,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,99,0)="                  Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,100,0)="                  Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,101,0)="                  Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,102,0)="                  Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,104,0)="    3. Installation of this patch should be at off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,105,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,106,0)="    4. Users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,108,0)="    5. Installation will take less than five minutes. Installation"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,109,0)="       of this patch requires no additional memory space."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,111,0)="    6. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,112,0)="      'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'YS*5.01*59' and"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,113,0)="       proceed with install."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,114,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,115,0)="    7. When prompted 'Enter the Coordinator for Mail Group 'YS"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,116,0)="       GAF TRANSMISSION ACK':', respond with the name of the user"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,117,0)="       responsible for monitoring the GAF performance measure."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,119,0)="    8. When prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,120,0)="       of Install? YES//', respond YES."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,121,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,122,0)="    9. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,123,0)="       install? YES//', respond  NO."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,124,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,125,0)="   10. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",39,1,126,0)="       Options, and Protocols? YES//', respond  NO."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,0)="66 SEQ #59^3010228^1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,0)="^^119^119^3010228"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,1,0)="The following items are addressed in patch YS*5.01*66:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,3,0)="1. When selecting the option 'Psychological tests/interviews (administer)'"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,4,0)="   [YSADMTEST] to administer the instrument 'Abnormal Involuntary Movement "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,5,0)="   Scale' (AIMS) the user is instructed to enter the key letter ""E"" to view"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,6,0)="   examination procedures and then to enter any key in order to progress."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,7,0)="   At the end of the instructions, any key will not work.  The user has to"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,8,0)="   use the ENTER key to exit the instructions.  This has been corrected to"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,9,0)="   accept any key entered as instructed.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,10,0)="   DAY-0200-42682"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,11,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,12,0)="2. The test (STAI), 'STATE-TRAIT ANXIETY SCALE', a general test of anxiety "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,13,0)="   as a mood (state) and as a personality characteristic (trait) was scored"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,14,0)="   directly.  The Scale #2 Trait Anxiety (Item #34) has been changed to score"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,15,0)="   indirectly."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,16,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,17,0)="3. The test 'Personality Assessment Inventory' (PAI) scoring routine YTPAI"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,18,0)="   has been edited to correct an indexing problem at ADDIT+5^YTPAI."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,19,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,20,0)="4. The RESPONSE PROMPT field (#4), of the multiple ITEM NUMBER field (#1),"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,21,0)="   of the MH INSTRUMENT file (#601) for the entry 'Personality Assessment"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,22,0)="   Inventory' (PAI) has been changed to a semicolon following the word "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,23,0)="   ""false"" so parsing of the response can be done."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,24,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,25,0)="5. The RESPONSE PROMPT field (#4), of the multiple ITEM NUMBER field (#1),"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,26,0)="   of the MH INSTRUMENT file (#601) for the entry 'Beck Anxiety Index' (BAI)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,27,0)="   has been changed to a semicolon following the word ""unpleasant"" so "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,28,0)="   parsing of the response can be done."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,29,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,30,0)="6. The test 'Depression Outcomes Module' (DOM) scoring routine YSMTI1 was"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,31,0)="   modified to allow multiple test scoring."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,32,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,33,0)="7. The following fields were found setting %DT(0) to some value, with no"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,34,0)="   corresponding Kill of %DT(0) in the Input Transform.  Leaving %DT(0) "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,35,0)="   defined can have an adverse impact on the end user.  This patch places"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,36,0)="   the KILL of %DT(0) after the call of ^%DT in the Input transform."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,37,0)="   ISF-1100-60368"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,38,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,39,0)="   The following PSYCH INSTRUMENT PATIENT (#601.2) and SECLUSION/RESTRAINT "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,40,0)="   (#615.2) file/subfile fields Input Transforms have been edited:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,41,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,42,0)="   File/Sub-file#  Field#   Field Name"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,43,0)="   601.2/601.22    .01      COMPLETION DATE"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,44,0)="                     4      ADMINISTRATION DATE"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,45,0)="                    14      DATE BEGUN"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,46,0)="   601.2/601.2213    1      DATE OF COMMENT"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,47,0)="                     5      DATE/TIME SIGNED"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,48,0)="                     8      DATE/TIME COSIGNED"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,49,0)="   615.2           .01      FILE ENTRY DATE"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,50,0)="                   .03      DATE/TIME APPLIED"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,51,0)="                    42      TIME REMOVED"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,52,0)="                    54      REVIEW FILED"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,53,0)="   615.2/615.3     .01      CHECK TIME"
