^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,57,0)="   NOIS Call(s): ISF-1100-60368"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,58,0)="                 DAY-0200-42682"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,59,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,60,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,61,0)="   Test Site(s): Dayton, OH"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,62,0)="                 Eastern Kansas HCS, KA"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,63,0)="                 Little Rock, AR"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,64,0)="                 Salt Lake City, UT"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,65,0)="                 VA Health Care Network Upstate New York System, NY"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,66,0)="                  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,67,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,68,0)="   ROUTINE SUMMARY:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,69,0)="   ================"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,70,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,71,0)="   The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,72,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,73,0)="   <tab>   ;;5.01;MENTAL HEALTH;**[patch list]**;Dec 30, 1994"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,74,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,75,0)="                                   Checksum Values"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,76,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,77,0)="   Routine Name       Before Patch        After Patch         Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,78,0)="   ------------       ------------        -----------         ----------"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,79,0)="   YSMTI1                  8825610            8854657         53,66"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,80,0)="   YTAIMS                  3709923            3711230         54,66"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,81,0)="   YTALUSR                     N/A            2954815         66"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,82,0)="   YTPAI                   7779058            7863323         10,66"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,83,0)="   YTPCL                       N/A            4037903         66"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,84,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,88,0)="   Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,89,0)="   =========================="
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,91,0)="   1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,92,0)="      This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto your"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,93,0)="      system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,95,0)="   2. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,96,0)="      system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,97,0)="      On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,98,0)="      following options:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,99,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,100,0)="                 Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,101,0)="                 Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,102,0)="                 Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,103,0)="                 Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,105,0)="   3. Users may remain on the system, but installation should be done at"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,106,0)="      off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,108,0)="   4. Installation will take less than five minutes. Installation"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,109,0)="      of this patch requires no additional memory space."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,111,0)="   5. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,112,0)="      'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'YS*5.01*66' and"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,113,0)="      proceed with install."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,115,0)="   6. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,116,0)="      install? YES//', respond  NO."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,118,0)="   7. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",40,1,119,0)="      Options, and Protocols? YES//', respond  NO. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,0)="69 SEQ #60^3010710^1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,0)="^^204^204^3010710"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,1,0)="1. The YSCL WEEKLY TRANSMISSION [Weekly Clozapine Report] option should"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,2,0)="now be queued to run daily instead of weekly (see item 11 in the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,3,0)="installation instructions below).  A new file CLOZAPINE PARAMETERS"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,4,0)="(#603.03) has been created to maintain site configuration and transmission"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,5,0)="data to be reported back to the National Clozapine Coordinating Center"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,6,0)="NCCC in Dallas.  This file also contains an entry indicating the day of"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,7,0)="the week the roll-up should occur."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,9,0)="2. The YSCL TRANSMIT DEMOGRAPHICS [Transmit Clozapine Demographics] option"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,10,0)="is no longer necessary and its associated task should be deleted (see item"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,11,0)="10 in the installation instructions below).  The demographics data will"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,12,0)="now be collected during the regular roll-up.  No error will occur and no"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,13,0)="harm will be done if this task remains active."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,15,0)="3. The CLOZAPINE LAB TEST file (#603.02) is no longer used for the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,16,0)="roll-up. The roll-up software will now use the CLOZAPINE LAB TEST field"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,17,0)="(#17.7) in the DRUG file (#50) to determine the WBC and ANC tests used for"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,18,0)="each drug.  Using this method will ensure a common element between the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,19,0)="dispensing and tracking of the prescription."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,21,0)="4. The Weekly Clozapine Report [YSCL WEEKLY TRANSMISSION] option has been"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,22,0)="modified to respond to the Kernel Stop Task Manager [XUTM STOP] option."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,23,0)="This provides a graceful way to terminate processing of the roll-up."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,25,0)=" Requesting Site: National Clozapine Coordinating Center"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,27,0)="    Test Site(s): Battle Creek"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,28,0)="                  Canandaigua"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,29,0)="                  Western New York"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,30,0)="                  Pittsburgh"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,32,0)="  Reference NOIS: BHS-0900-11492     CLOZAPINE DEMOGRAPHICS MESSAGE"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,33,0)="                       The message generated for the transmission of data"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,34,0)="                       to the national database indicates certain"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,35,0)="                       demographic data is missing for a patient,"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,36,0)="                       including the patient's name."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,38,0)="                  STC-0500-40272     CLOZAPINE MONITOR shows No RX for"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,39,0)="                                     several pts"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,40,0)="                  ALN-0400-11672     CLOZAPINE MONITOR MESSAGE INCORRECT"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,41,0)="                       The message generated for the transmission of"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,42,0)="                       patient data to the national database incorrectly"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,43,0)="                       reported that some patients' had no prescription"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,44,0)="                       data. This was due to the method used to collect"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,45,0)="                       and compare the date of the prescription to the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,46,0)="                       current date."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,49,0)="                  SDC-0896-62071     CLOZAPINE MONITOR ILLEGALLY WANTS"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,50,0)="                                     RACE"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,51,0)="                       Some sites were concerned because the Clozapine"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,52,0)="                       roll-up software requires that the patient's race"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,53,0)="                       be entered into the database.  This is clinically"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,54,0)="                       relevant data and is required by both the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,55,0)="                       manufacturer and the Food and Drug Administration"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,56,0)="                       (FDA).  Race may be entered as long as permission"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,57,0)="                       to report this data is obtained on the consent to"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,58,0)="                       release document.  See VHA Directive 99-035."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,61,0)="  ROUTINE SUMMARY:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,62,0)="  ================"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,64,0)="  The second line of the routine now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,66,0)="  <tab>   ;;5.01;MENTAL HEALTH;**[patch list]**;Dec 30,1994"
