^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,83,0)="         Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,84,0)="         =========================="
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,86,0)="  NOTE: This KIDS install does not place any options out of service"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,87,0)="        during the install and no user options are affected."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,89,0)="        The site should answer ""NO"" to all three questions."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,90,0)="            Note: You may not receive all three prompts at your site."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,92,0)="        ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,93,0)="         Install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,95,0)="        ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,97,0)="        ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and Protocols?"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,98,0)="         YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,99,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,100,0)="         1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,101,0)="            This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,102,0)="            your system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,104,0)="         2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,105,0)="            should be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,107,0)="         3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,108,0)="            system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,109,0)="            global."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,110,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,111,0)="            On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,112,0)="            following options:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,113,0)="                Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,114,0)="                Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,115,0)="                Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,116,0)="                Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,117,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,118,0)="         4. Users may remain on the system, installation may be done at"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,119,0)="            any time except during the time scheduled for the Clozapine"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,120,0)="            roll-up."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,122,0)="         5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,123,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,124,0)="         6. Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak hours"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,125,0)="            and less than 5 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,127,0)="         7. Installation of this patch requires no additional memory"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,128,0)="            space."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,129,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,130,0)="         8. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,131,0)="            'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'YS*5.01*69 and"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,132,0)="            proceed with the install."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,134,0)="         9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,135,0)="            be returned to the mapped set once the installation has run to"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,136,0)="            completion."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,138,0)="        10. Historically, the option YSCL TRANSMIT DEMOGRAPHICS"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,139,0)="            [Transmit Clozapine Demographics] had been queued to run"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,140,0)="            before the start of business every Tuesday.  This function"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,141,0)="            has been incorporated into the Clozapine Data Collection"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,142,0)="            and this option is no longer used.  This task should be"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,143,0)="            deleted.  This is accomplished using the XUTM SCHEDULE"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,144,0)="            [Schedule/Unschedule Options] option.  The following screen"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,145,0)="            capture will closely resemble the display from your system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,146,0)="            To delete the task, enter the @ sign in the Option Name field"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,147,0)="            and press the Enter key.  You will then be asked if you want"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,148,0)="            to delete this record.  Answer YES and press the Enter key."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,150,0)="   Schedule/Unschedule Options"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,151,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,152,0)="   Select OPTION to schedule or reschedule: YSCL TRANSMIT DEMOGRAPHICS (R)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,154,0)="                             Edit Option Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,155,0)="       Option Name: YSCL TRANSMIT DEMOGRAPHICS"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,156,0)="       Menu Text: Transmit Clozapine Demographics         TASK ID: 526664"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,157,0)="     ____________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,159,0)="     QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME: DEC 19,2000@02:00"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,160,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,161,0)="   DEVICE FOR QUEUED JOB OUTPUT:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,162,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,163,0)="    QUEUED TO RUN ON VOLUME SET:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,164,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,165,0)="         RESCHEDULING FREQUENCY: 7D"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,166,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,167,0)="                TASK PARAMETERS:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,168,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,169,0)="               SPECIAL QUEUEING:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,171,0)="   ______________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,172,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,174,0)="         11. The YSCL WEEKLY TRANSMISSION [Weekly Clozapine Report]"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,175,0)="             option has been queued to run prior to the start of business"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,176,0)="             one day a week.  It has been recommended that the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,177,0)="             transmission occur on Tuesday, but transmission dates vary."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,178,0)="             The software has been modified to determine the correct day"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,179,0)="             of the week to run.  The option should now be tasked to run"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,180,0)="             daily prior to the start of business.  The XUTM SCHEDULE"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,181,0)="             [Schedule/Unschedule Options] option should be used to set"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,182,0)="             the QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME: entry to tomorrows date at a"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,183,0)="             time prior to the start of business and the RESCHEDULING"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,184,0)="             FREQUENCY entry to ""1D"" (once daily).  The following is an"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,185,0)="             example of the display from the XUTM SCHEDULE option."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,187,0)="                             Edit Option Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,188,0)="       Option Name: YSCL WEEKLY TRANSMISSION"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,189,0)="       Menu Text: Weekly Clozapine Report                 TASK ID: 518605"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,190,0)="     ____________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,191,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,192,0)="     QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME: T+1@0200"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,193,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,194,0)="   DEVICE FOR QUEUED JOB OUTPUT:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,195,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",41,1,196,0)="    QUEUED TO RUN ON VOLUME SET:"
