^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,89,0)="List of preceding patches: 18,22,25,26,47,61,69"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,90,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,92,0)="         Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,93,0)="         =========================="
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,95,0)="  NOTE: This KIDS install does not place any options out of service"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,96,0)="        during the install and no user options are affected."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,98,0)="        The site should answer ""NO"" to all three questions."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,99,0)="            Note: You may not receive all three prompts at your site."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,101,0)="        ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,102,0)="         Install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,104,0)="        ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,105,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,106,0)="        ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,107,0)="         Protocols?"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,108,0)="         YES// NO"""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,109,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,110,0)="         1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,111,0)="            This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,112,0)="            your system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,114,0)="         2. Review your mapped set.  If the routines are mapped, they"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,115,0)="            should be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,117,0)="         3. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,118,0)="            your system. You now need to use KIDS to install the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,119,0)="            Transport global."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,121,0)="            On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,122,0)="            following options:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,123,0)="                Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,124,0)="                Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,125,0)="                Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,126,0)="                Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,127,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,128,0)="         4. Users may remain on the system, installation may be done at"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,129,0)="            any time except during the time scheduled for the Clozapine"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,130,0)="            roll-up."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,131,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,132,0)="         5. No options need to be placed out of service."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,134,0)="         6. Installation time is less than 2 minutes during off peak"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,135,0)="            hours and less than 5 minutes during peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,137,0)="         7. Installation of this patch requires no additional memory"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,138,0)="            space."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,140,0)="         8. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,141,0)="            option:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,142,0)="            'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'YS*5.01*74 and"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,143,0)="            proceed with the install."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,145,0)="         9. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,146,0)="            should be returned to the mapped set once the installation"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",46,1,147,0)="            has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",47,0)="76^3030628^1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,0)="70^3031121^1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,0)="^^216^216^3031121"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issues in the Mental Health software. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,3,0)=" 1. Patients who take the BECK SCALE FOR SUICIDAL IDEATION (BSI) test on"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,4,0)="    the Mental Health Assistant are presented with questions that do not "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,5,0)="    make sense when compared to their previous answers. For example, the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,6,0)="    patient says that he/she is not suicidal but the test asks him/her "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,7,0)="    detailed questions about the last attempt and possible future attempts"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,8,0)="    at suicide.  The skip logic for the BSI was not included in MHA."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,9,0)="    The skip logic for the BSI using the List Manager software worked"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,10,0)="    properly. This has been corrected in MHA 1.0.2.10."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,11,0)="    CLE-0303-41699"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,13,0)=" 2. New scales have been added to the Minnesota Multiphasic Personality "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,14,0)="    Inventory-2 (MMPI2).  The new scales are the Restructured Clinical"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,15,0)="    (RC) Scales for the MMPI2.  The RC scales are based on recent factor"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,16,0)="    analyses of the existing Clinical Scales, and are intended to be used"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,17,0)="    as aids in the interpretation of the Clinical Scale profile.  The names"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,18,0)="    of the 9 RC scales are as follows (note that there is no RC5 scale):"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,19,0)="    RCd: Demoralization"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,20,0)="    RC1: Somatic Complaints"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,21,0)="    RC2: Low Positive Emotions"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,22,0)="    RC3: Cynicism"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,23,0)="    RC4: Antisocial Behavior"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,24,0)="    RC6: Ideas of Persecution"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,25,0)="    RC7: Dysfunctional Negative Emotions"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,26,0)="    RC8: Aberrant Experiences"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,27,0)="    RC9: Hypomanic Activation"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,29,0)="    Note:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,30,0)="    The set of MMPI2 scales that are scored and the order in which they are "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,31,0)="    presented has been changed to be consistent with the recommendations of "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,32,0)="    the test authors and publisher. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,34,0)="    The PTSD-Schlenger scale is no longer scored."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,37,0)=" 3. Three new psychological tests have been added to the MH INSTRUMENT "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,38,0)="    (#601) file.  The new depression measures include the 20-item version"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,39,0)="    Center for Epidemiologic Studies Depression Scale (CESD), the Center "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,40,0)="    For Epidemiological Studies Depression Scale 5 Items (CESD5) and the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,41,0)="    Prime-MD Patient Health Questionnaire (PHQ9).  The PHQ9 is based on "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,42,0)="    the 9 DSM-IV criteria for Major Depressive Episode, and test results"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,43,0)="    include both the number of criteria met as well as indication of "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,44,0)="    whether the criteria for MDE are met.  All can now be administered "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,45,0)="    using the Mental Health Assistant."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,47,0)=" 4. The Alcohol Use Disorders Identification Test Condensed (AUDC) has been"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,48,0)="    revised to meet the new Alcohol Screening Performance Measure issued by"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,49,0)="    the Office of Quality and Performance."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,51,0)=" 5. The Alcohol Use Disorders Identification Test Condensed Revised (AUDCR)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,52,0)="    has been made non-operational by setting the value to ""N"" in the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,53,0)="    MH INSTRUMENT file (#601) OPERATIONAL field (#32)."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,55,0)=" 6. An entry to the COPYRIGHT HOLDER file (#601.3) has been made for the new"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,56,0)="    psychological test PHQ9."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,58,0)=" 7. The instrument Revised NEO Personality Inventory (NEOPI) in the MH"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,59,0)="    MULTIPLE SCORING file (#601.6), which allows the user to score"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,60,0)="    multiple instruments, has been edited to correctly return scale "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,61,0)="    scores to be displayed on the Test Results in the Mental Health"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,62,0)="    Assistant (MHA)."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,64,0)="    Also corrected within the NEOPI is item #86 which read ""When I'm under "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,65,0)="    a great deal of stress, sometimes I fell like I'm going to pieces."".  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,66,0)="    Item #86 now reads as ""When I'm under a great deal of stress, sometimes"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,67,0)="    I feel like I'm going to pieces."" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,70,0)=" 8. When running option List Test and Interviews [YSMLST] from programmer"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,71,0)="    prompt...%DSM-E-ENDOFILE, end of file encountered.  This error has been "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,72,0)="    corrected."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,73,0)="    EKH-0698-41771"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,75,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,76,0)=" 9. The instrument Millon Clinical Multiaxial Inventory-III (MCMI3) in the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,77,0)="    MH INSTRUMENT file (#601) ITEM NUMBER field (#1) entry #41 which read"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,78,0)="    ""I've done a number of stupid things on impulse that needed up causing "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,79,0)="    me great trouble."". Item Number #41 now reads as ""I've done a number of"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,80,0)="    stupid things on impulse that ended up causing me great trouble."""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,81,0)="    CTX-1003-71717"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,82,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,83,0)="    Also within the MCMI3 the TEST SCALE NUMBER field (#16) SCALE NAME"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,84,0)="    sub-field (#.05) for entries 12, 14 and 15 which read:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,85,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,86,0)="          6B Aggressive/Sadistic"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,87,0)="          8A Passive-Aggressive"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,88,0)="          8B Self-Defeating"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,89,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,90,0)="    SCALE NAME entries 12, 14 and 15 now read as:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,91,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,92,0)="          6B Sadistic"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,93,0)="          8A Negativistic"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,94,0)="          8B Masochistic"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,95,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",48,1,97,0)=" "
