^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,91,0)="    Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,92,0)="    =========================="
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,93,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,94,0)="    1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,95,0)="       This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,96,0)="       your system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,98,0)="    2. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,99,0)="       system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,100,0)="       global. On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,101,0)="       the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,102,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,103,0)="                  Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,104,0)="                  Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,105,0)="                  Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,106,0)="                  Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,108,0)="    3. Installation of this patch should be at off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,109,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,110,0)="    4. Users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,112,0)="    5. Installation will take less than five minutes. Installation"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,113,0)="       of this patch requires no additional memory space."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,114,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,115,0)="    6. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,116,0)="       'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'YS*5.01*78' and"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,117,0)="       proceed with install."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,119,0)="    7. When prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,120,0)="       of Install? YES//', respond YES.  Responding with a yes, will"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,121,0)="       add considerable time to the installation."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,122,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,123,0)="    8. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,124,0)="       install? YES//', respond  NO."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,125,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,126,0)="    9. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,127,0)="       Options, and Protocols? YES//', respond  NO. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,128,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,129,0)="   10. Retrieve and open the file:  YS_501_78.ZIP"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,130,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,131,0)="   11. Place the MENTAL HEALTH ADDICTION SEVERITY INDEX MULTIMEDIA VERSION"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,132,0)="       (ASI-MV) INSTALLATION AND USER GUIDE in a location that can be"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,133,0)="       accessed by ASI-MV users."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,134,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,135,0)="   12. Please refer to the POST INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS section of the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,136,0)="       MENTAL HEALTH ADDICTION SEVERITY INDEX MULTIMEDIA VERSION (ASI-MV)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,137,0)="       INSTALLATION AND USER GUIDE to install the COTS ASI-MV software,"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,138,0)="       YS_ASIMV.EXE, YS_ASIMV_SD.EXE and YS_ASIMV_KH.DLL."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,139,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,140,0)="   13. Place the option YS BROKER1 [YS BROKER1] on the Mental Health users"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",52,1,141,0)="       secondary menu if it does not already exist."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",53,0)="77^3041228^1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,0)="84 SEQ #73^3050204^1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,0)="^^145^145^3050204"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,1,0)="============================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,2,0)="*IMPORTANT NOTE TO IRM THIS PATCH MUST BE INSTALLED.  ALTHOUGH NO ROUTINES  *"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,3,0)="*ARE INCLUDED IN THIS PATCH KIDS UPDATES THE MH INSTRUMENT file (#601) WITH *"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,4,0)="*DATA WHEN THE PATCH IS INSTALLED.                                          *"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,5,0)="============================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,6,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,7,0)="Patch YS*5.01*84 addresses three issues within the Mental Health software."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,9,0)="1. In the MH INSTRUMENT file (#601), ITEM NUMBER field (#1), TEXT sub-field "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,10,0)="(#2) for the entry the Beck Depression Inventory-II (BDI2) a period has "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,11,0)="been added to the end of each response number.  This will allow a reminder"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,12,0)="to be built by the Clinical Reminder software.  Here is an example of the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,13,0)="edit made to ITEM NUMBER 2 of the BDI2 instrument using a FILEMAN inquiry:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,14,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,15,0)="Before patch:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,16,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,17,0)="ITEM NUMBER: 2                          VALID RESPONSE SET: 0123X"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,18,0)=" TEXT: PESSIMISM"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,19,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,20,0)=" 0 I am not discouraged about my future."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,21,0)=" 1 I feel more discouraged about my future than I used to be."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,22,0)=" 2 I do not expect things to work out for me."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,23,0)=" 3 I feel my future is hopeless and will only get worse."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,24,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,25,0)="After patch:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,26,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,27,0)="ITEM NUMBER: 2                          VALID RESPONSE SET: 0123X"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,28,0)=" TEXT: PESSIMISM"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,29,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,30,0)=" 0. I am not discouraged about my future."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,31,0)=" 1. I feel more discouraged about my future than I used to be."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,32,0)=" 2. I do not expect things to work out for me."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,33,0)=" 3. I feel my future is hopeless and will only get worse."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,34,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,35,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,36,0)="2. In the Mental Health Assistant GUI version 1.0.2.9 when using the mouse "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,37,0)="scroll button in the left-hand pane, the pane freezes at times.  Returning "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,38,0)="to the desktop the mouse arrow suddenly becomes unresponsive to mouse "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,39,0)="movements and begins performing the movements that should have occurred in "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,40,0)="the Mental Health Assistant - in the same area of the screen where the lists "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,41,0)="of tests was.  This has been corrected in MHA 1.0.2.10 to properly navigate "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,42,0)="the large amounts of patient psychological test data users may have."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,43,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,44,0)="3. The instrument ANALYSIS OF RELATIONSHIPS (AOR) has been made"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,45,0)="non-operational by setting the value to ""N"" in the MH INSTRUMENT file"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,46,0)="(#601) OPERATIONAL field (#32)."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,47,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,48,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,49,0)="   Nois call(s): None"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,52,0)="   Test Site(s): New Orleans VAMC, LA  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,53,0)="                 Portland VAMC, OR"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,54,0)="                 Salt Lake City VAMC, UT"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,55,0)="                 VA Health Care Network Upstate New York"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,56,0)="         "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,57,0)=""
