^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,105,0)="    Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,106,0)="    =========================="
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,107,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,108,0)="    1. Use the 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' option on the PackMan menu."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,109,0)="       This option will load the KIDS package in this message onto "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,110,0)="       your system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,112,0)="    2. The patch has now been loaded into a Transport global on your"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,113,0)="       system. You now need to use KIDS to install the Transport"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,114,0)="       global. On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,115,0)="       the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,117,0)="                  Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,118,0)="                  Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,119,0)="                  Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,120,0)="                  Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,122,0)="    3. Installation of this patch should be at off peak hours."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,123,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,124,0)="    4. Users may remain on the system."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,125,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,126,0)="    5. Installation will take less than five minutes. Installation"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,127,0)="       of this patch requires no additional memory space."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,129,0)="    6. From the 'Installation Menu' of the KIDS menu, run the option"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,130,0)="       'Install Package(s)' Select the package 'YS*5.01*84' and"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,131,0)="       proceed with install."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,132,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,133,0)="    7. When prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,134,0)="       of Install? YES//', respond NO.  Responding with a yes, will"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,135,0)="       add considerable time to the installation."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,136,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,137,0)="    8. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,138,0)="       install? YES//', respond  NO."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,139,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,140,0)="    9. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,141,0)="       Options, and Protocols? YES//', respond  NO. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,142,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,143,0)="   10. Please refer to the POST INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS section of the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,144,0)="       MENTAL HEALTH ASSISTANT VERSION 2 INSTALLATION GUIDE to install the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",54,1,145,0)="       MHA software."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",55,0)="88 SEQ #74^3050924^1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",55,1,0)="^^2^2^3050924"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",55,1,1,0)="Under certain coditions when entering an Outpatient ASI the message "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",55,1,2,0)="Progress Note Created will display when it has not been created."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,0)="90 SEQ #75^3060923^1"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,0)="^^371^371^3060923"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,1,0)="Recent changes in the Clozapine protocol require changes to the Clozapine "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,2,0)="Roll Up software.  Originally, all Clozapine prescriptions were limited "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,3,0)="to 7 days.  Renewals and refills were not allowed.  In addition, the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,4,0)="Clozapine reporting software automatically discontinued any patient if "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,5,0)="the patient's prescription was over 28 days old.  This was to prevent a "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,6,0)="patient from being issued medication on an expired prescription.  The "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,7,0)="revised Clozapine protocol allows for a monthly prescription as well as "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,8,0)="weekly and bi-weekly.  The patient is now automatically discontinued if "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,9,0)="the issue date for the most recent prescription is greater than 56 days "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,10,0)="in the past."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,12,0)="The weekly roll-up creates a report that is sent to the local G.PSOCLOZ "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,13,0)="mail group.  This report lists the patients reported to the national "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,14,0)="database along with an indicator showing whether or not Lab and RX data "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,15,0)="were transmitted.  This report has been updated to show the date of the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,16,0)="most recent WBC (White Blood Count) and Neutrophil Count along with the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,17,0)="date of the most recent Clozapine prescription.  Mental Health and "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,18,0)="Pharmacy personnel responsible for prescribing and dispensing Clozapine "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,19,0)="should be made aware of this mail group and given the opportunity to join."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,21,0)="NEW OPTION:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,22,0)="=========="
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,23,0)="The Link Multiple Tests to Clozapine [CLOZAPINE MULTI TEST LINK] option "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,24,0)="must be assigned to the person or persons responsible for ensuring that "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,25,0)="the appropriate data is in place to validate Clozapine testing data.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,26,0)="This is usually the Laboratory ADPAC."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,28,0)="This option will ask for the local laboratory name that equates to the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,29,0)="following seven common test names"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,31,0)="White Blood Cell Count"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,32,0)="Absolute Neutrophil Count"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,33,0)="Neutrophil %"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,34,0)="Segs  (Percent)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,35,0)="Bands (Percent)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,36,0)="Segs  (Absolute Count)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,37,0)="Bands (Absolute Count)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,39,0)="You will also be asked to fill in the reporting format for each test.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,40,0)="Most sites report WBC and Neutrophil results in K/unit format (K/cc or "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,41,0)="K/cu mm or K/mm-3 or K/mL). For example, WBC equals 5.1.  However, some "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,42,0)="report results as discrete units. For example, WBC equals 5100.  This "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,43,0)="field will allow the site to specify how results are reported.  Entries "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,44,0)="that report in a percentage (such as Neutrophil %, Segs %, and Bands %) "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,45,0)="should use ""Percentage""."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,47,0)="You may input as many names from the local laboratory definition for each "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,48,0)="of these tests as needed.  Remember that the laboratory may have designed "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,49,0)="special names for specific test equipment, specific test locations, or "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,50,0)="specific test conditions, such as manual counts.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,52,0)="In fact, if your facility has Clozapine patients with blood samples drawn "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,53,0)="and tested on a fee-basis at other CLIA (Clinical Laboratory Improvement "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,54,0)="Amendments) approved labs, it is extremely important for your Laboratory "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,55,0)="have tests to accept manual input of these tests.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,57,0)="Therefore, you should involve laboratory managers or ADPAC (Automated "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,58,0)="Data Processing Application Coordinator) in selection of these names - "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,59,0)="both to define the test names currently in use and to create the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,60,0)="provision for manual entry of data.  Please be certain every possible "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,61,0)="local laboratory name that represents these tests is entered that relates "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,62,0)="to each of the seven test names above.  Pharmacy dispense will be "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,63,0)="prevented unless the program can find the needed test results under one "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,64,0)="of names you identify as an equivalent for each of the seven tests."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,66,0)="Security Key: The YSCL AUTHORIZED Security Key is new with this patch.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,67,0)=" This key must be assigned to each provider authorized to dispense "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,68,0)=" Clozapine."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,70,0)="EXAMPLE: CLOZAPINE MULTI TEST LINK [Link Multiple Tests to Clozapine] "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,71,0)="option"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,73,0)="Select OPTION NAME: CLOZ"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,74,0)="     1   CLOZAPINE MULTI TEST LINK       Link Multiple Tests to Clozapine"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,75,0)="     2   CLOZAPINE DATA SERVER  YSCLSERVER     Clozapine Data Server"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,76,0)="     3   CLOZAPINE PHARMACY MANAGER  PSOL MANAGER     Clozapine Pharmacy "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,77,0)="Manager"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,78,0)="     4   CLOZAPINE TEST LINK  YSCL TEST LINK     Clozapine Test Link"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,79,0)="CHOOSE 1-4: 1  CLOZAPINE MULTI TEST LINK     Link Multiple Tests to "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,80,0)="Clozapine "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,81,0)="Link Multiple Tests to Clozapine"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,82,0)="Currently linked Tests:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,83,0)="NEUTROPHIL MATURITY, MEAN represents WHITE BLOOD COUNT"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,84,0)="SEGS represents BANDS %"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,86,0)="Enter the name of the test for Clozapine: WBC       WBC"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,87,0)="Enter the type of the test for Clozapine: ?"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,89,0)="Enter a code from the list."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,91,0)="     Select one of the following:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,92,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,93,0)="          W         WHITE BLOOD COUNT"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,94,0)="          A         ABSOLUTE NEUTROPHIL COUNT"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,95,0)="          N         NEUTROPHIL PERCENT"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,96,0)="          S         SEGS %"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,97,0)="          B         BANDS %"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,98,0)="          T         BANDS ABSOLUTE"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,99,0)="          C         SEGS ABSOLUTE"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,101,0)="Enter the type of the test for Clozapine: WHITE BLOOD COUNT"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,102,0)="Enter the reporting method of the test for Clozapine: ?"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,104,0)="Enter a code from the list."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,105,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,106,0)="     Select one of the following:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,108,0)="          0         uL"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,109,0)="          1         K/uL"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,110,0)="          2         Percent"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,111,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,112,0)="Enter the reporting method of the test for Clozapine: 2  Percent"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,114,0)="Enter the name of the test for Clozapine:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,115,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,116,0)="The FDA (Food and Drug Administration) uses White Blood Cell Count and "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,117,0)="Absolute Neutrophil Count as the definitive tests to verify for Clozapine "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,118,0)="use, however your lab may report your data under any of the names you "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,119,0)="enter into these lists.  If the WBC and ANC are not directly available, "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,120,0)="ANC will be calculated from the other data available and presented to "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,121,0)="Pharmacy (and CPRS (Computerized Patient Record System) during a later "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,122,0)="revision) at the time of dispense and used to evaluate the safety under "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,123,0)="FDA limits.  Only the most recent WBC will be accepted, and the date and "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,124,0)="time stamp of the Neutrophil count must match the date and time stamp of "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,125,0)="the WBC."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,127,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,128,0)="WHITE BLOOD CELL  (WBC)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,129,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,130,0)="For reference  ""White Blood Cell Count"" is a portion of the total blood "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,131,0)="content and the sum total of two different kinds of cells - "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,132,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,133,0)="         AGRANULOCYTES - those cells which do not have granules"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,134,0)="         that absorb a stain.  These cells are subdivided"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,135,0)="         into Lymphocytes and Monocytes. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,137,0)="         GRANULOCYTES  -- those cells which contain granules"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,138,0)="         that absorb a stain.  These cells are subdivided"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,139,0)="         into Neutrophils, Basophils, and Eosinophils.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,141,0)="Both Agranulocytes and Granulocytes are part of the Total White Blood "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,142,0)="Cell Count.  Therefore, the total WBC is the sum of five different types "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,143,0)="of cells.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,145,0)="WBC as well as its five components are usually expressed as the total "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,146,0)="number of cells in a cubic centimeter of blood (cc) or cubic millimeter "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,147,0)="(cu mm or mm-3)or milliliters (mL).  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,149,0)="WBC usually falls with a range between 4000 and 11,000 but fluctuates for "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,150,0)="a number of medical reasons.  For brevity, WBC results may be divided by "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,151,0)="1000 and presented as K/cc or K/cu mm or K/mm-3 or K/mL"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,152,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,154,0)="The five components are similarly expressed as number of the same type OR "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,155,0)="as a percentage of the total WBC.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,156,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,157,0)="The sum of counts of the five components of should equal the total WBC OR "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,158,0)="the sum of the percentages of the five components should equal 100%"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,159,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,160,0)="This test is sometimes also referred to as ""Leukocyte Count"" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,161,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,162,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,163,0)="Absolute Neutrophil Count (ANC)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,164,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,165,0)="The Absolute Neutrophil Count is the total number of Neutrophil cells in "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,166,0)="the total WBC count.  The other GRANULOCYTE cells - Basophils and "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,167,0)="Eosinophils (see White Blood Cell Count above) - are not included in this "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,168,0)="number.  Therefore - a test titled GRANULOCYTES - may not produce the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,169,0)="desired result as it may include Basophils and Eosinophils."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,171,0)="Since the ANC is a portion of the WBC, it is only valid if it is "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,172,0)="traceable to the WBC sample drawn at the same date and time.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,174,0)="ANC is a count and not a percentage - expressed as WBC with the total "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,175,0)="number of cells in a cubic centimeter of blood (cc) or cubic millimeter "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,176,0)="(cu mm or mm-3)or milliliters (mL).  Again, this number may be divided by "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,177,0)="a thousand for brevity.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,178,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,179,0)="The Absolute Neutrophil Count generally ranges from 1600 to 7700 / but it "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,180,0)="can ever exceed the WBC count.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,181,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,182,0)="This test can also be knows as polymorphonuclear cells or PMN's. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,183,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,184,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,185,0)="Neutrophil Percent  (Neut%)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,187,0)="The Neutrophil Percent is the portion of the total WBC and that is "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,188,0)="composed of Neutrophil cells, excluding all agranulocytes and other "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,189,0)="granulocytes.  This number is usually between 40% and 70%, but fluctuates "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,190,0)="for many medical reasons.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,191,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,192,0)="Since it is reported as a portion of the total WBC, it is only valid if "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,193,0)="it is traceable to the WBC sample drawn at the same date and time.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,194,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,195,0)="Neut% is commonly obtained by automatic testing equipment to represent "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,196,0)="the Neutrophil content in the blood.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,197,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,198,0)="Neut% is a percentage and not a count - reported in the portion of the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,199,0)="WBC.  It can be converted into an Absolute Neutrophil Count in the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,200,0)="following formula (Neutrophil% / 100) X WBC count).  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,201,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,202,0)="The Neutrophil Percent generally ranges from 37% to 80% and should never "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,203,0)="exceed 90% of the total WBC count unless special medical conditions are "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,204,0)="present.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,205,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,206,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,207,0)="SEGS  & BANDS  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,208,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,209,0)="The WBC/Granulocyte/Neutrophil cell type can be further subdivided into "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,210,0)="two types.  Mature neutrophils are called SEGS.  Immature neutrophils "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,211,0)="called BANDS also circulate in the blood until they mature into SEGS.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,212,0)="The sum of SEGS and BANDS is equal to the ANC of a give WBC count.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,213,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,214,0)="SEGS and BANDS may be reported as a count, expressed in cc, mm-3, cu mm, "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,215,0)="or mL.  A preceding K indicates the number has been divided by 1000.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,216,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,217,0)="When SEGS and BANDS are reported as a number, the sum total of SEGS and "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,218,0)="BANDS equals the total Neutrophil Count (ANC)  NOTE that the program "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,219,0)="needs an identifying test for both SEGS and BANDS.  Reporting SEGS "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,220,0)="without a parallel result from BANDS will result in an error condition "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,221,0)="that may prevent Pharmacy dispense.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,222,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,223,0)="This number generally ranges between 1600 and 7700 / cu mm.  It should "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,224,0)="never exceed 90% of the total WBC except under special circumstances. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,225,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,226,0)="SEGS and BANDS may be reported as a PERCENTAGE of the total WBC.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,227,0)="Therefore the total number of neutrophils (ANC) in a give WBC is = total "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,228,0)="WBC  X  (% Segs  + % Bands).  This calculation will be performed by the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,229,0)="Pharmacy patch to obtain and ANC when necessary"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,230,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,231,0)="The sum total of SEGS% and BANDS% can never exceed 100."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,232,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,233,0)="DATA DICTIONARY:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,234,0)="==============="
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,235,0)="CLOZAPINE PATIENT LIST File (#603.01), OVERRIDE DATE field (#3) - This "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,236,0)="field was added to allow the NCCC more control over the overrides "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,237,0)="performed at the site."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,238,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,239,0)="CLOZAPINE PARAMETERS File (#603.03), LOCK DOWN field (#7) - This field "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,240,0)="was added to allow the NCCC to prevent the dispensing of any Clozapine "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,241,0)="prescription at a site."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,242,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,243,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,244,0)="CLOZAPINE TESTS file (#603.04) - This file was added to allow the sites "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,245,0)="to select multiple tests for the WBC and Neutrophil count."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,246,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,247,0)="Field         Field Name           Description"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,248,0)="603.04,.01    NAME            0;1 FREE TEXT (Required)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,249,0)="603.04,1      TEST NAME       1;0 POINTER Multiple #603.41"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,250,0)="603.41,.01    TEST NAME       0;1 POINTER TO LABORATORY TEST FILE (#60)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,251,0)="603.41,1      TEST TYPE            0;2 SET (Required)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,252,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,253,0)="                                'W' FOR WHITE BLOOD COUNT; "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,254,0)="                                'A' FOR ABSOLUTE NEUTROPHIL COUNT; "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,255,0)="                                'N' FOR NEUTROPHIL PERCENT; "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,256,0)="                                'S' FOR SEGS %; "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,257,0)="                                'B' FOR BANDS %; "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,258,0)="                                'T' FOR BANDS ABSOLUTE; "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,259,0)="                                'C' FOR SEGS ABSOLUTE; "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,260,0)="603.41,2      REPORTING FORMAT     0;3 SET (Required)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,261,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,262,0)="                                '0' FOR Units; "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,263,0)="                                '1' FOR K/units; "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,264,0)="                                '2' FOR Percentage; "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",56,1,265,0)=" "
