^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,220,0)=" Software and Documentation Retrieval Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,221,0)=" --------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,222,0)=" The software for this patch is being released as a host file."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,223,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,224,0)=" The host file is available at the following location:  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,225,0)=" /srv/vista/patches/SOFTWARE/PSO_YS_CLOZ_COVID.KID  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,226,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,227,0)=" Documentation describing the new functionality is included in this"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,228,0)=" release. Documentation can be found on the VA Software Documentation "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,229,0)=" Library at: https://www.domain.ext/vdl/"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,230,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,231,0)=" -------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,232,0)=" Title                                 File Name  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,233,0)=" -------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,234,0)=" MHA Security Technical                YS_MHS_TM.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,235,0)=" Manual/Guide"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,236,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,237,0)=" Deployment Installation Back-Out      pso_7_p612_ys_501_p166_dibr.docx"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,238,0)=" and Rollback Guide - HI&M             pso_7_p612_ys_501_p166_dibr.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,239,0)=" Clozapine Overrides "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,240,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,241,0)=" Release Notes - HI&M Clozapine        pso_7_p612_ys_501_p166_rn.docx"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,242,0)=" Overrides                             pso_7_p612_ys_501_p166_rn.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,243,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,244,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,245,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,246,0)=" Patch Installation: "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,247,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,248,0)=" Pre/Post Installation Overview: "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,249,0)=" -------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,250,0)=" There are no tasks to be performed before the installation of this "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,251,0)=" multi-build. Note that the routines should be backed up to a PackMan"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,252,0)=" message before installing the build."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,253,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,254,0)=" Pre-Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,255,0)=" ------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,256,0)=" This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,257,0)=" recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,258,0)=" potential disruption to users.  This patch should take less than 5 "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,259,0)=" minutes to install.  It should not be installed when the YSCL DAILY"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,260,0)=" TRANSMISION option is running.  If unsure when that is check the OPTION"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,261,0)=" SCHEDULING file (#19.2) using FileMan:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,262,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,263,0)=" Select VA FileMan Option: Inquire to File Entries "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,264,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,265,0)=" Output from what File: OPTION SCHEDULING//   (17 entries) Select OPTION"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,266,0)=" SCHEDULING NAME:  YSCL DAILY TRANSMISSION Another one: Standard Captioned"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,267,0)=" Output? Yes//   (Yes) Include COMPUTED fields:  (N/Y/R/B): NO//  - No "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,268,0)=" record"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,269,0)=" number (IEN), no Computed  Fields "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,270,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,271,0)=" NAME: YSCL DAILY TRANSMISSION "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,272,0)="   QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME: OCT 05, 2019@01:30 "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,273,0)="   RESCHEDULING FREQUENCY: 1D            TASK ID: 2577736 "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,274,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,275,0)=" Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,276,0)=" --------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,277,0)="1. Place the KIDS multi-build file PSO_YS_CLOZ_COVID.KID into a "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,278,0)="local directory and use the KIDS option Load a Distribution option to "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,279,0)="load it into the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,280,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,281,0)="2. Choose the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,282,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,283,0)="3. From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,284,0)="the Installation Menu.  From this menu, you may elect to use the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,285,0)="following  options. When prompted for the INSTALL NAME enter:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,286,0)="       PSO*7.0*612"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,287,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,288,0)="  a. Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup message"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,289,0)="     of any routines exported with this patch."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,290,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,291,0)="  b. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will (allow "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,292,0)="     you to view all changes that will be made when this patch "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,293,0)="     is installed.  It compares all components of this patch "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,294,0)="     (routines, DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,295,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,296,0)="  c. Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option allows you to "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,297,0)="     ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the transport "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,298,0)="     global."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,299,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,300,0)=" 4.  From the Installation Menu, select the Install Package(s) option and "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,301,0)=" choose the patch to install (PSO*7*612)."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,302,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,303,0)=" 5. Accept the default when prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,304,0)=" Upon Completion of Install? NO//'"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,305,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,306,0)=" 6. Accept the default when prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,307,0)=" the install? NO//'"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,308,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,309,0)=" 7. Accept the default when prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,310,0)=" Menu Options, and Protocols? NO//'"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,311,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,312,0)=" 8. If prompted 'Delay Install (Minutes):  (0 - 60): 0// enter 0 (zero).  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,313,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,314,0)=" Backout/Rollback Strategy: "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,315,0)=" ---------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,316,0)=" Backout will be done only with the concurrence and participation of "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,317,0)=" development team and appropriate VA site/region personnel. The decision "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,318,0)=" to backout the software will be a joint decision between development"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,319,0)=" team, VA site and regional personnel, and other appropriate VA personnel."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,320,0)=" Rollback applies to data only and is not applicable to this multi-build."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,321,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,322,0)=" Prior to installing the KIDS multi-build, the site/region should have "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,323,0)=" saved a backup of the routines in a PackMan message using the Backup a"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,324,0)=" Transport Global [XPD BACKUP] menu option (this is done at time of"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,325,0)=" install). The message containing the backed-up routines can be loaded "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,326,0)=" with the ""Xtract PackMan"" function at the Message Action prompt. The"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,327,0)=" PackMan function ""INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE"" is then used to install the"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,328,0)=" backed up routines onto the VistA System."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,329,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,330,0)=" The new ""AC"" mumps cross reference for the CLOZAPINE PATIENT LIST file "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,331,0)=" (#603.01) must be manually deleted via FileMan prior to restoring the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,332,0)=" backed up routines. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,333,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,334,0)=" The steps to delete the cross reference:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,335,0)="   1. Access VA FileMan option Cross-Reference A Field via the VA FileMan "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,336,0)="   Utility Functions [DIUTILITY] menu."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,337,0)="   2. At the prompt, ""What type of cross-reference (Traditional or New)?"" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,338,0)="   enter NEW."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,339,0)="   3. At the prompt, ""Modify What File:"" enter 603.01."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,340,0)="   4. The new ""AC"" cross reference should be selected by default."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,341,0)="   5. At the prompt ""Choose E (Edit)/D (Delete)/C (Create):"" enter DELETE."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,342,0)="   6. At the prompt ""Are you sure you want to delete the index  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,343,0)="   definition? NO// YES"""
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,344,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,345,0)=" Example deletion of new ""AC"" index if backout is required:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,346,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,347,0)="   VA FileMan 22.2   "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,348,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,349,0)="   Select OPTION: UTILITY FUNCTIONS  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,350,0)="   Select UTILITY OPTION: CROSS-REFERENCE A FIELD OR FILE  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,351,0)="   What type of cross-reference (Traditional or New)? Traditional// NEW"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,352,0)="   Modify what File: REMOTE PROCEDURE// 603.01  CLOZAPINE PATIENT LIST"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,353,0)="                                           (74 entries)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,354,0)="   Current Indexes on file #603.01:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,355,0)="     1589   'AC' index"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,356,0)="   Choose E (Edit)/D (Delete)/C (Create): DELETE   "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,357,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,358,0)="   Which Index do you wish to delete? 1589//  AC"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,359,0)="   Are you sure you want to delete the index definition? NO// YES   "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,360,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,361,0)="     Index definition deleted."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,362,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,363,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,364,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,365,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,366,0)=" Validation of Backout Procedure "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,367,0)=" -------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,368,0)=" The backout Procedure can be verified by printing the first 2 lines of "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,369,0)=" the PSO* routines contained in the PSO*7*612 build using the option"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,370,0)=" First Line Routine Print [XU FIRST LINE PRINT]. Once the old routines"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,371,0)=" listed in the multi-build patch have been restored, the first two lines "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,372,0)=" of the Routines will no longer contain the designation of patch 612 in"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,373,0)=" the patch list section on line 2 of the routines."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,374,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,375,0)=" The backout of the new ""AC"" cross reference on the CLOZAPINE PATIENT "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,376,0)=" LIST file (#603.01) can be verified by repeating the backout steps and "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,377,0)=" verifying that there is no longer a selectable ""AC"" cross reference to "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",96,1,378,0)=" delete."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",97,0)="141^3201116.121312^17"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",97,1,0)="^^3^3^3201116"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",97,1,1,0)="The purpose of this patch is to add updates and correct defects in both "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",97,1,2,0)="the MHA Windows executable and in the web-based MHA Patient Entry "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",97,1,3,0)="application."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,0)="149 SEQ #129^3201208.082923^17"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,0)="^^334^334^3201208"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,2,0)="The purpose of this software package is for the Department of Veterans "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,3,0)="Affairs (VA) to maintain compliance with federal mandates for tracking "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,4,0)="Clozapine prescriptions and dispensing."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,6,0)="This patch will add enhancements to the Mental Health package for the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,7,0)="National Clozapine Coordination (NCC) Project. It is also referred to as "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,8,0)="the Clozapine Modernization (ClozMod) Project. YS*5.01*149 is part of "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,9,0)="Phase 2 of the MENTAL HEALTH NCC PROJECT and is the Veterans Health "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,10,0)="Information Systems and Technology Architecture (VistA) side software for "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,11,0)="this effort.  The other components are web-based and will be installed on "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,12,0)="servers outside of VistA and in the VA cloud services.  The purpose of "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,13,0)="Phase 2 is to provide enhancements for the National Clozapine Registry "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,14,0)="(NCR)."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,15,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,16,0)="YS*5.01*149 will add new VistA options and a new file, CLOZAPINE HL7 "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,17,0)="TRANSMISSION (#603.05) to track the Health Level 7 (HL7) messages.  This "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,18,0)="file can be read by users who have FileMan access and a ""Y"" in their FILE "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,19,0)="MANAGER ACCESS CODE, which is field #3 in the NEW PERSON file (#200).  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,20,0)="This patch also contains HL7 message components and their associated "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,21,0)="subscriptions, plus a logical link to VistA.  Most of these components "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,22,0)="will not be visible to VistA users.  The HL7 messages will be sent as a "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,23,0)="batch to track specific VistA activities such as registering a new "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,24,0)="clozapine patient for treatment.  HL7 messages will be sent to an "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,25,0)="external system and VistA will receive HL7 acknowledgements, where needed."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,27,0)="A new HL LOGICAL ENTRY is named YSCL-NCCC and will connect to the NCR "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,28,0)="servers."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,30,0)="A complete list of the patch components can be generated using KIDS "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,31,0)="options."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,32,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,33,0)="Except for routine YSCLTST5, the VistA components in this patch are all "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,34,0)="new and do not modify existing software."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,35,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,36,0)="The types of HL7 messages to be transmitted:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,37,0)="   ADT^A05 (Pre-admit a Patient)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,38,0)="   RDE^O11 (Pharmacy/Treatment Encoded Order)"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,40,0)="Patch Components:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,41,0)="-----------------"
