^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,218,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,219,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,220,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,221,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,222,0)="The only pre-installation step is to decide who will be the coordinator "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,223,0)="for the new YSCLHL7 LOGS Mail Group; the installer will be prompted for "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,224,0)="that name during the installation."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,225,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,226,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,227,0)="recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,228,0)="potential disruption to users.  This patch should take less than 3"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,229,0)="minutes to install.  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,230,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,231,0)="The menu rebuild may take a few minutes after the patch is installed."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,232,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,233,0)="No options or protocols need to be disabled before installation."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,234,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,235,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,236,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,237,0)="1.  Choose the PackMan message containing this build. Then select "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,238,0)="    the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option to load the build."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,239,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,240,0)="2.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,241,0)="    select the Installation Menu.  From this menu, "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,242,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,243,0)="    A.  Select the Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,244,0)="        option to confirm the integrity of the routines that "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,245,0)="        are in the transport global. When prompted for the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,246,0)="        INSTALL NAME enter YS*5.01*149."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,247,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,248,0)="    B. Select the Backup a Transport Global option to create a "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,249,0)="       backup message of any routines exported with this patch. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,250,0)="       It will not backup any other changes such as DDs or "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,251,0)="       templates."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,252,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,253,0)="    C. You may also elect to use the following options: "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,254,0)="         i.  Print Transport Global - This option will allow "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,255,0)="             you to view the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,256,0)="         ii. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,257,0)="             option will allow you to view all changes that will "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,258,0)="             be made when this patch is installed.  It compares "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,259,0)="             all of the components of this patch, such as "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,260,0)="             routines, DDs, templates, etc."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,261,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,262,0)="    D. Select the Install Package(s) option and choose the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,263,0)="       patch to install. "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,264,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,265,0)="      i.  When prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,266,0)="             Completion of Install? NO//' answer <YES>."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,267,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,268,0)="      ii. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,269,0)="          install? NO//' answer <NO>.   "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,270,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,271,0)="      iii. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,272,0)="           Options, and Protocols? NO//' answer <NO>."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,273,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,274,0)="      iv. When prompted 'Enter options you wish to mark as "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,275,0)="            'Out Of Order':' press <ENTER>."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,276,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,277,0)="      v. When prompted 'Enter protocols you wish to mark as "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,278,0)="              'Out Of Order':' press <ENTER>."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,279,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,280,0)="      vi. When prompted 'Delay Install (Minutes):  (0 - 60): 0//',"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,281,0)="              press <ENTER> for zero seconds."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,282,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,283,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,284,0)="Post-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,285,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,286,0)="After the patch is installed the installer should notify the coordinator "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,287,0)="of the YSCLHL7 LOGS mail group (see notes above) and schedule the new "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,288,0)="transmission option."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,289,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,290,0)="The new option Transmit Clozapine Rx HL7 Messages [YSCL HL7 CLOZ "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,291,0)="TRANSMISSION] should be scheduled in TaskMan to run daily in off-hours, "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,292,0)="typically between 10:00 PM and 2:00 AM.  The option can be scheduled "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,293,0)="using the TaskMan option Schedule/Unschedule Options [XUTM SCHEDULE].  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,294,0)="The option will not have a DEVICE FOR QUEUED JOB OUTPUT.  That is, the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,295,0)="device field should be null."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,296,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,297,0)="This is an example:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,298,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,299,0)="   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,300,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,301,0)="                          Edit Option Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,302,0)="    Option Name: YSCL HL7 CLOZ TRANSMISSION    "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,303,0)="    Menu Text: Transmit Clozapine Rx HL7 Messag  "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,304,0)="                                           TASK ID: 8798880"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,305,0)="  ___________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,306,0)="  QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME: DEC 5,2019@23:00              "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,307,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,308,0)="DEVICE FOR QUEUED JOB OUTPUT:                               "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,309,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,310,0)=" QUEUED TO RUN ON VOLUME SET:                      "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,311,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,312,0)="      RESCHEDULING FREQUENCY: 1D                            "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,313,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,314,0)="             TASK "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,315,0)="PARAMETERS:                                                 "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,316,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,317,0)="            SPECIAL QUEUEING:                     "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,318,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,319,0)="______________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,320,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,321,0)="Exit    Save    Next Page    Refresh    Quit"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,322,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,323,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,324,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,325,0)="   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,326,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,327,0)="Back-Out/Roll Back Plan:"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,328,0)="------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,329,0)="The routines can be restored from the backup message created in "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,330,0)="installation step B above.  The new options can be placed out-of-order or "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,331,0)="deleted.  The new routines can be deleted manually without affecting "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,332,0)="other VistA packages.  No data will need conversion to restore the "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,333,0)="system.  The data dictionary components of this patch can be removed "
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",98,1,334,0)="using standard VA FileMan options."
^DIC(9.4,100,22,15,"PAH",99,0)="172b^3210405"
