^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",14,1,39,0)=" 1) Use Packman option 'INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE' to load the KIDS build onto"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",14,1,40,0)="    your system."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",14,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",14,1,42,0)=" 2) On the KIDS menu, under the 'Installation' menu, use the option"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",14,1,43,0)="    'Verify Checksum in Transport Global' and verify that all routines"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",14,1,44,0)="    have the correct checksums."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",14,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",14,1,46,0)=" 3) From the 'Installation' Menu of KIDS, use the option 'Install"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",14,1,47,0)="    Package(s)'.  Select the package 'MC*2.3*15' and proceed with install."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",14,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",14,1,49,0)=" 4) If you are a MSM site move the routines to the other servers."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",14,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",14,1,51,0)=" 5) On a mapped system, rebuild your map set."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",15,0)="16^2980330^1"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",15,1,0)="^^1^1^2980330"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",15,1,1,0)="Refer to the patch for the patch description."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",16,0)="17^2980417^1"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^1^1^2980417"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",16,1,1,0)="Refer to the Patch Description of the patch."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",17,0)="18^2980725^1"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",17,1,0)="^^1^1^2980725"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",17,1,1,0)="Refer to patch Descripton."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",18,0)="19^2981007^1"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^1^1^2981007"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="Please see the patch description on FORUM for MC*2.3*19."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,0)="20^2990201^1"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,0)="^^35^35^2990201"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,1,0)="This patch changes the resting blood pressure high/low limits in the the"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,2,0)="ECHO file (#691)."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,4,0)=" Field # & Name              Old Limits     New Limits"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,5,0)=" ====================================================="
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,6,0)=" 3  RESTING SYSTOLIC BP      90 - 220       0 - 300"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,7,0)=" 4  RESTING DIASTOLIC BP     50 - 150       0 - 300"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,9,0)="These fields may be edited via the Enter/Edit Echo (Screen) [MCFSECHO] and"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,10,0)="Line Entry/Edit of ECHO test [MCFLECHO] options."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,12,0)="This change was requested in E3R report number 11833."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,14,0)=" Installation Instructions: "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,15,0)=" =========================="
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,16,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system.  Installation of"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,17,0)="this patch will take less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,19,0)=" 1.  Use the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE option on the PackMan menu, to"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,20,0)="     load the KIDS Transport Distribution global."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,22,0)=" 2.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System (KIDS) Menu,"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,23,0)="     select the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,25,0)=" 3.  From the Install menu, you may elect to use the following"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,26,0)="     options (when prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter MC*2.3*20):"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,28,0)="      a.  Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,29,0)="      b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,31,0)=" 4.  Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,32,0)="     MC*2.3*20."
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,34,0)=" 5.  When prompted ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options,"
^DIC(9.4,124,22,12,"PAH",19,1,35,0)="     Menu Options, and Protocols? YES//"", respond ""NO"""
