^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",133,1,7,0)="   inventory item costs."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",133,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",133,1,9,0)="3. Delete Prosthetics options Manual Send Delivery Notification and  "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",133,1,10,0)="   Returned Delivery Verification Card and remove same options from"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",133,1,11,0)="   Prosthetics Utilities Menu as the government contract for Letter "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",133,1,12,0)="   Notification was cancelled. "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",134,0)="160 SEQ #146^3111025.16342^17"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",134,1,0)="^^6^6^3111025"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",134,1,1,0)="1. Excessive number of pages print for each letter when selecting"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",134,1,2,0)="   'print all' Home Oxygen letters."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",134,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",134,1,4,0)="2. Prosthetics GUI display for 2319, screen 7 for HISA (Home "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",134,1,5,0)="   Improvement Structural Alterations) displays no HISA information"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",134,1,6,0)="   for known HISA order. "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",135,0)="169 SEQ #147^3120329.183144^17"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",135,1,0)="^^1^1^3120329"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",135,1,1,0)="1. 2012 NPPD Line updates"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",136,0)="163 SEQ #148^3120425.095727^17"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",136,1,0)="^^10^10^3120425"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",136,1,1,0)="1. Cannot link patient record to Suspense:"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",136,1,2,0)="   a. When select patients appearing on the GUI Delayed Order"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",136,1,3,0)="      Report."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",136,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",136,1,5,0)="   b. After selecting patient, current issue item does not display."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",136,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",136,1,7,0)="2. Report 'Print Item Usage By Location' fails to print due to a missing "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",136,1,8,0)="   HCPCS item reference."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",136,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",136,1,10,0)="3. Prosthetics GUI error when displaying Delayed Order Report (DOR)"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",137,0)="171 SEQ #149^3120829.130135^17"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",137,1,0)="^^2^2^3120829"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",137,1,1,0)="1. Unlinked patient 2319s not displaying in option 'Link Patient Record"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",137,1,2,0)="   to Suspense'."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",138,0)="166 SEQ #150^3130819.150143^17"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",138,1,0)="^^3^3^3130819"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",138,1,1,0)="This patch updates the Prosthetics Privacy Act Statements and fixes"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",138,1,2,0)="issues with Purchasing being unable to post Prosthetics Home Oxygen"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",138,1,3,0)="transactions."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",139,0)="172 SEQ #151^3130916.160844^17"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",139,1,0)="^^2^2^3130916"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",139,1,1,0)="1. National HCPCS file updates are not handling multi line descriptions"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",139,1,2,0)="   correctly."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",140,0)="168 SEQ #152^3140902.125428^17"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",140,1,0)="^^2^2^3140902"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",140,1,1,0)="Please see the National Patch Module for details of the enhancements"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",140,1,2,0)="included in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",141,0)="173 SEQ #153^3141016.091048^17"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",141,1,0)="^^3^3^3141016"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",141,1,1,0)="1. Users are able to edit Inactive HCPCS items in Prosthetics."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",141,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",141,1,3,0)="2. Purge process created for Prosthetics file #664 [PROSTHETICS 1358]"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",142,0)="177^3151201.174644^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",142,1,0)="^^2^2^3151201"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",142,1,1,0)="In preparation for the VA's transition from IPv4 to IPv6 the PROSTHETICS"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",142,1,2,0)="package will require a modification to make it IPv6 ready."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",143,0)="179 SEQ #156^3160225.141743^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",143,1,0)="^^8^8^3160225"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",143,1,1,0)="1. Home Oxygen Generate Letters option has site and prescription"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",143,1,2,0)="   expiration date issues. "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",143,1,3,0)="                                                                "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",143,1,4,0)="2. Home Oxygen Billing and Home Oxygen Reporting has no check/flag for"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",143,1,5,0)="   deceased patients. "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",143,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",143,1,7,0)="3. Insure work file is killed when running option 'LIST OPEN STOCK "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",143,1,8,0)="   ISSUES'."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,0)="175 SEQ #157^3160628.131751^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,0)="^^15^15^3160628"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,1,0)="This patch fixes multiple issues with the Prosthetics GUI "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,2,0)="(graphical user interface) Suite."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,4,0)="1) Incorrect display of ""Station Number"" on the OWL form"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,6,0)="2) Serial Number should allow 20 character and not"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,7,0)="   be restricted to 15."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,9,0)="3) The NUMBER OF BIDS is not being populated"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,11,0)="4) The main menu form for Prosthetics does not set to "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,12,0)="   allow resizing or minimization."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,14,0)="5) Ability for two purchasing agents to access the same"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",144,1,15,0)="   consult at the same time and order against it"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",145,0)="180 SEQ #158^3161014.135712^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",145,1,0)="^^8^8^3161014"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",145,1,1,0)="1) Adding a new prescription to a Home Oxygen patient, will allow the"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",145,1,2,0)="   user to associate an inactive HCPCS code."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",145,1,3,0)="                                                                 "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",145,1,4,0)="2) Remove all routines & option for Patient Notification Letter processing"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",145,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",145,1,6,0)="3) Home Oxygen 'New Patient' report gets <undefined> error"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",145,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",145,1,8,0)="4) Site is unable to edit MODEL#/CONTRACT# in option Edit 2319"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",146,0)="178 SEQ #159^3161014.135735^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",147,0)="182 SEQ #162^3170830.171526^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",147,1,0)="^^9^9^3170830"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",147,1,1,0)="1. Eye glass STAT consult not showing on Suspense List"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",147,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",147,1,3,0)="2. Add fields Lot, Model and Contract Number to Reconcile Close Out"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",147,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",147,1,5,0)="3. Site issue causing error in Suspense Processing"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",147,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",147,1,7,0)="4. Site was not getting diagnosis when using option RMPR VIEW 2319"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",147,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",147,1,9,0)="5. Reconciliation edit not working when used by two users at same time"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",148,0)="188 SEQ #163^3170928.152654^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",148,1,0)="^^2^2^3170928"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",148,1,1,0)="When running the Delayed Order Report (DOR) in Prosthetics, the ""Pt IEN"""
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",148,1,2,0)="is not populated."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",149,0)="189 SEQ #165^3171128.124345^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",149,1,0)="^^3^3^3171128"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",149,1,1,0)="This patch ensures that, when the user modifies the contract number in the"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",149,1,2,0)="RMPR OFFICIAL MENU|Purchasing|Edit 2319 option, the change is reflected "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",149,1,3,0)="in the RMPR4 RPC report."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",150,0)="190 SEQ #166^3171227.133613^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",150,1,0)="^^2^2^3171227"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",150,1,1,0)="Home Oxygen billing process date failure has prevented users from viewing "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",150,1,2,0)="Home Oxygen items posted."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",151,0)="191 SEQ #167^3180201.161123^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",151,1,0)="^^7^7^3180201"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",151,1,1,0)="When jumping to Suspense Processing, station may be undefined. The option "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",151,1,2,0)="entry point was modified to check station and ensure it is defined."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",151,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",151,1,4,0)="Associated SDM Tickets:"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",151,1,5,0)="======================="
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",151,1,6,0)="R16621509FY17 - <UNDEFINED>RMPRPAT2+15^RMPRPAT2 *RMPR(""STA"")"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",151,1,7,0)="R16726784FY17 - <UNDEFINED>RMPRPAT2+15^RMPRPAT2 *RMPR(""STA"")"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",152,0)="185 SEQ #168^3180228.171053^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",152,1,0)="^^5^5^3180228"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",152,1,1,0)="This distribution adds an option allowing Prosthetics end-users "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",152,1,2,0)="to select an IFCAP Purchase Request (form 2237) by its Obligation "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",152,1,3,0)="Number and post the individual line items to individual patients' "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",152,1,4,0)="Prosthetics 2319 records and link to existing patient prosthetics "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",152,1,5,0)="suspense record."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",153,0)="192 SEQ #169^3180302.152141^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",153,1,0)="^^6^6^3180302"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",153,1,1,0)="This patch will fix the subscript error issue in the EDIT 2319 [RMPR"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",153,1,2,0)=" EDIT 2319] option. An error will occur when the option is used in two "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",153,1,3,0)=" situations. There are two files that are looked at when the edit is being"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",153,1,4,0)=" updated. If file PROSTHETICS 1358 (#664) does not contain the information"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",153,1,5,0)=" it will have an error. If file RECORD OF PROS APPLIANCE/REPAIR (#660)"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",153,1,6,0)=" does not have the referenced information it will have the error."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",154,0)="193 SEQ #170^3180601.140105^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",154,1,0)="^^3^3^3180601"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",154,1,1,0)="This patch adds the variable RMPRSITIEN to obtain the INSTITUTION (#4) "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",154,1,2,0)="file IEN for an entered station number. It will then store it correctly "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",154,1,3,0)="in the PROSTHETICS SUSPENSE (#668) file."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",155,0)="194 SEQ #173^3181206.160544^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",155,1,0)="^^6^6^3181206"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",155,1,1,0)="This patch addresses 2 issues:"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",155,1,2,0)="1. The Lot Number entry is being put in the Description (#24) field in "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",155,1,3,0)="the file RECORD OF PROS APP (#660)."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",155,1,4,0)="2. When a record in the file RECORD OF PROS APP (#660) does not have a "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",155,1,5,0)="suspense date it receives a subscript error in the option View "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",155,1,6,0)="Prosthetics Item Transactions [RMPR VIEW 2319 READ ONLY]."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",156,0)="198 SEQ #174^3190301.14071^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",156,1,0)="^^8^8^3190301"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",156,1,1,0)="When an IFC Subscriber Protocol (GRMC IFC SUBSC) triggers an undefined"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",156,1,2,0)="error is being received when a Prosthetics Inter-Facility Consult (IFC)"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",156,1,3,0)="is discontinued, because the Internal Entry Number (IEN) is"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",156,1,4,0)="not defined. "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",156,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",156,1,6,0)="An undefined error is being received when a Prosthetics Reconcile/Close "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",156,1,7,0)="Out Purchase Card Transaction [RMPR4 CLOSE OUT] is attempted, but the "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",156,1,8,0)="file PROCUREMENT & ACCOUNTING TRANSACTIONS (#442) has been purged.   "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",157,0)="199 SEQ #175^3190301.15593^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",157,1,0)="^^3^3^3190301"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",157,1,1,0)="Associated end user does not get the warning message ""No open sequence"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",157,1,2,0)="number available for ### for transaction entry ###"" when creating an  "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",157,1,3,0)="eyeglass order in VistA."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",158,0)="201 SEQ #176^3190604.181034^54"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",158,1,0)="^^3^3^3190604"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",158,1,1,0)="When a user edits a PROSTHETICS HCPCS using the option Add Inventory "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",158,1,2,0)="LOCATION or ITEMS [RMPR INV ADD] it will flip the field INVENTORY FLAG "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",158,1,3,0)="(#10) in file PROSTHETIC HCPCS (#661.1) to 'YES'."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",159,0)="203 SEQ #177^3200721.121906^65"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",159,1,0)="^^5^5^3200721"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",159,1,1,0)="This patch fixes an issue when the field REMARKS (#8) of subfile HOME "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",159,1,2,0)="OXYGEN ITEM (#19.4) in file PROSTHETICS PATIENT (#665) contains less than "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",159,1,3,0)="3 characters and is being transferred to generate the billing in the "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",159,1,4,0)="matching field REMARKS (#4) in file HOME OXYGEN TRANSACTIONS FILE "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",159,1,5,0)="(#665.72)."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",160,0)="202 SEQ #178^3200730.15145^65"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",160,1,0)="^^2^2^3200730"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",160,1,1,0)="1. When using GIP inventory process, instead of PIP process, the stock"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",160,1,2,0)="   issue record is missing the short description"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",161,0)="200 SEQ #179^3200831.094456^65"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",161,1,0)="^^1^1^3200831"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",161,1,1,0)="Please refer to patch description on FORUM for detailed instructions."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",162,0)="206 SEQ #182^3210304.101819^17"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",162,1,0)="^^1^1^3210304"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",162,1,1,0)="1. Suspense processing menu lock message when processing an item"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",163,0)="207 SEQ #183^3210929.145056^17"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",163,1,0)="^^5^5^3210929"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",163,1,1,0)="1. Home Oxygen prescription expiration report not reflecting correct"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",163,1,2,0)="   expiration date"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",163,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",163,1,4,0)="2. The allowable upper limit for the Suspense Purge Parameter needs"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",163,1,5,0)="   to be increased. "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",164,0)="210 SEQ #184^3220815.133131^86"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",164,1,0)="^^8^8^3220815"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",164,1,1,0)="Patch RMPR*3.0*207 was built to ensure that the latest expiration "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",164,1,2,0)="date for a veteran's Home Oxygen prescriptions would show on the "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",164,1,3,0)="report Prescription Expiration Dates.  However, sites were allowed"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",164,1,4,0)="at one point to enter the date 01/01/2099 for an ongoing prescription "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",164,1,5,0)="expiration date, but that process came to an end in 2016.  However,"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",164,1,6,0)="since those futuristic dates remain they are picked up as the most"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",164,1,7,0)="current date on the Prescription Expiration Dates report and are not"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",164,1,8,0)="valid."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",165,0)="213 SEQ #185^3230721.094951^89"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",165,1,0)="^^5^5^3230721"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",165,1,1,0)="The patch addresses one (1) issue: "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",165,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",165,1,3,0)="1.  Routine EN^RMPRFC4 is using the wrong API for looking up ICD10 codes."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",165,1,4,0)="    This is causing all Prosthetics IFC Consults to file an invalid value"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",165,1,5,0)="    into PROSTHETIC SUSPENSE file (#668) ICD field (#1.6)."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",166,0)="212 SEQ #186^3230928.102747^89"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",166,1,0)="^^6^6^3230928"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",166,1,1,0)="The patch addresses one (1) issue: "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",166,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",166,1,3,0)="1.      The Suspense Processing [RMPR SUSP MENU] option may show records "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",166,1,4,0)="out of reverse chronological sequence if the IEN numbers in a site's "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",166,1,5,0)="PROSTHETIC SUSPENSE file (#668) get disrupted and new records are created "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",166,1,6,0)="at lower IENs than old records."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",167,0)="214 SEQ #187^3231122.114831^89"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",167,1,0)="^^6^6^3231122"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",167,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",167,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",167,1,3,0)="INC27716753 - Due to an incorrect API call to retrieve ICD codes (fixed in"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",167,1,4,0)="RMPR*213), some records associated with the Form 2319 may contain the ""-1"""
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",167,1,5,0)="error code in the SUSPENSE ICD field of the RECORD OF PROS APPLIANCE/ "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",167,1,6,0)="REPAIR file (#660)."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,0)="211 SEQ #188^3240506.120445^89"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,0)="^^18^18^3240506"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,1,0)="The patch addresses two (2) issues: "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,3,0)="1.  When an end user attempts to reconcile the credit card charge to the"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,4,0)="    purchase order using Reconcile/Close Out Purchase Card Transaction "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,5,0)="    option [RMPR4 CLOSE OUT], the application allows the user to delete "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,6,0)="    the last remaining billing item (original billing item) on the "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,7,0)="    purchase. If after the delete, the end user times out or enters an "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,8,0)="    ""^"" at Select ITEM, it leaves an incomplete record that cannot be "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,9,0)="    canceled or edited through the menu."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,11,0)="2.  The option ""Purge Suspense Records"" [RMPR PURGE SUS] does not give "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,12,0)="    The user a chance to verify whether they want to proceed with the "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,13,0)="    purge. They do not have an option to cancel out of the purge once "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,14,0)="    the report is displayed, nor are they given an estimate of the date"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,15,0)="    range that will be purged before they commit.  As a result, sites "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,16,0)="    are inadvertently running the purge or running it without "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,17,0)="    understanding how much data they will lose.  This is causing sites"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",168,1,18,0)="    to unintentionally lose important patient data."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",169,0)="216 SEQ #189^3241030.123632^89"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",169,1,0)="^^2^2^3241030"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",169,1,1,0)="Please review FORUM's Patch Module description and installation "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",169,1,2,0)="instructions before installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",170,0)="218 SEQ #190^3250903.081055^90"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",170,1,0)="^^2^2^3250903"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",170,1,1,0)="Please review FORUM's Patch Module description and installation  "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",170,1,2,0)="instructions before installing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",171,0)="215 SEQ #191^3260107.115645^90"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",172,0)="219 SEQ #192^3260327.104925^90"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",172,1,0)="^^2^2^3260327"
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",172,1,1,0)="Please review FORUM's Patch Module description and installation "
^DIC(9.4,140,22,20,"PAH",172,1,2,0)="instructions before installing this patch."
