^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,261,0)=" INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS:"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,262,0)=" =========================="
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,263,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,264,0)=" Installation of this patch will take about 5 minutes. Additional"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,265,0)=" time will be needed if the GUI applications have been installed on"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,266,0)=" individual client machines or the location of the applications on the"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,267,0)=" network has changed. Users need not be off the system when applying this"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,268,0)=" patch, but it should be installed during non-peak hours to minimize"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,269,0)=" disruption to users."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,270,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,271,0)="  1. On the KIDS menu under the 'INSTALLATION' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,272,0)="     options as desired:"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,273,0)="        Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,274,0)="        Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,275,0)="        Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,276,0)="        Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,277,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,278,0)="  2. On the KIDS menu under the 'INSTALLATION' menu, use the following"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,279,0)="     option to install the patch:"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,280,0)="        Install Package(s) (ACKQ*3.0*12)"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,281,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,282,0)="  3. When prompted ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,283,0)="     Install? YES//"", respond 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,284,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,285,0)="  4. When prompted ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES//"""
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,286,0)="     respond 'NO'."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,287,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,288,0)="  5. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,289,0)="     Protocols? YES//', respond 'YES'."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,290,0)="     Options to disable:"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,291,0)="        ACKQROES3"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,292,0)="        ACKQROES3E"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,293,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,294,0)="  6. When prompted 'Delay Install (Minutes):  (0-60): 0//; respond '0'."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,295,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,296,0)="  7. Following the installation of the KIDS build, the system will"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,297,0)="     immediately run routine ACKQAG08. This will move any existing"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,298,0)="     'No Response' or 'Masked' tags into the appropriate threshold fields."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,299,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,300,0)="  8. At this point the two revised executables (ACKQROES3.EXE and"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,301,0)="     ACKQROES3E.EXE) should be copied over all existing copies on the"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,302,0)="     network or client machine. Add the VistA menu options for any new"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,303,0)="     application users and setup on their CPRS Toolbar as necessary, as"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,304,0)="     detailed in the INSTALLATION GUIDE."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,305,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,306,0)="  9. We do not anticipate any need to reinstall this patch. However, it"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",9,1,307,0)="     may be reinstalled if necessary."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",10,0)="10 SEQ #10^3060213^1"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^3^3^3060213"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",10,1,1,0)="This patch will correct to problem with in QUASAR"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",10,1,2,0)="that allows the user to create a new visit for"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",10,1,3,0)="deceased patients."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",11,0)="15 SEQ #11^3070904.223813^1"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^1^1^3070904"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="INCORRECT DIAGNOSTIC CODE DISPLAY"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",12,0)="13 SEQ #12^3070905.005838^1"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^1^1^3070905"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="Interface of Medical Devices with QUASAR and the DALC."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",13,0)="14 SEQ #13^3071212.204346^1"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",14,0)="17^3101027.112905^17"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",14,1,0)="^^3^3^3101027"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",14,1,1,0)="This patch will correct a problem with broken pointers."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",14,1,2,0)="Associated Remedy"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",14,1,3,0)="HD147036 - Quasar Patch ACKQ*3*9 - Amendments for Scheduling "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",15,0)="16 SEQ #15^3101110.122451^17"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",15,1,0)="^^10^10^3101110"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",15,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",15,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",15,1,3,0)="   1.  From the New Clinic Visits [NEW CLINIC VISITS  ACKQAS VISIT ENTRY] "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",15,1,4,0)="       menu option, when checking out a patient that has the Combat "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",15,1,5,0)="       Classification, the prompt does not display allowing the user to "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",15,1,6,0)="       answer the Combat questions for the visit."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",15,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",15,1,8,0)="   2. At each episode of care, the prompt to determine if the care"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",15,1,9,0)="      provided is related to the combat experience of the OEF/OIF veteran"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",15,1,10,0)="      needs to have the default changed from ""NULL"" to ""YES""."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",16,0)="18 SEQ #16^3110404.142339^17"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^4^4^3110404"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",16,1,1,0)="As a follow up to patch LEX*2.0*64 modifications are necessary to "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",16,1,2,0)="all references of the newly deleted fields and use of the "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",16,1,3,0)="corresponding API's is required to acquire the necessary "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",16,1,4,0)="information."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",17,0)="22 SEQ #17^3131212.14131^17"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",17,1,0)="^^5^5^3131212"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",17,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one issue:"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",17,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",17,1,3,0)="This patch will update all direct file reads to the ICD DIAGNOSIS (#80) "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",17,1,4,0)="file,CPT MODIFIER (#81.3) file, and the CPT FILE (#81) file in the Quasar "
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",17,1,5,0)="application to the new associated API's."
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",18,0)="21 SEQ #18^3140902.125412^17"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^1^1^3140902"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="ICD-10 Remediation patch for QUASAR"
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH","B",17,14)=""
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH","B","1 SEQ #1",1)=""
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH","B","10 SEQ #10",10)=""
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH","B","12 SEQ #9",9)=""
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH","B","13 SEQ #12",12)=""
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH","B","14 SEQ #13",13)=""
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH","B","15 SEQ #11",11)=""
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH","B","16 SEQ #15",15)=""
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH","B","18 SEQ #16",16)=""
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH","B","2 SEQ #2",2)=""
^DIC(9.4,150,22,2,"PAH","B","21 SEQ #18",18)=""
