^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,1,0)="This patch is part of a group of patches that make up the new Medication "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,2,0)="This patch is part of a group of patches that make up the new Medication "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,3,0)="Order Check Healthcare Application v2.0 (MOCHA). These patches will add a"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,4,0)="maximum single dose order check to the current Veterans Health Information"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,5,0)="Systems and Technology Architecture medication order checking system that"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,6,0)="uses the First DataBank (FDB) business logic and database.  FDB custom"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,7,0)="dosing tables will be used to store custom dosing changes to FDB standard"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,8,0)="reference drug tables. Pharmacy Enterprise Customization System v.2.2"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,9,0)="(PECS) application was developed to meet the customization requirements."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,11,0)="This patch also makes a second line patch list correction to the routine "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,12,0)="PSS551. In patch PSS*1*169, the second line of the routine mistakenly "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,13,0)="listed patch 260. This patch removes the 260 designation."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,15,0)="MOCHA v2.0 consists of the following patches:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,16,0)="1.      PSS*1*160"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,17,0)="2.      MOCHA_2_0.KID host file which contains PSJ*5*252, PSO*7*372 and"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,18,0)="OR*3*345"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,19,0)="3.      PSS*1*173"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,20,0)="4.      MOCHA_2_FOLLOW UP COMBINED BUILD.KID host file which contains "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,21,0)="PSJ*5*257, PSO*7*416, OR*3*311 and GMRA*4*47"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,23,0)="These files and patches contain software that supports MOCHA v2.0 "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,24,0)="functionality.  The host files were created to simplify installation at "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,25,0)="Veterans Health Administration (VHA) facilities."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",159,1,27,0)="Please refer to the Installation Guide for installation instructions."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,0)="170 SEQ #161^3140612.09121^17"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,0)="^^36^36^3140612"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,1,0)="This patch will correct the issues reported."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,3,0)="1) HD0000000174282 - Problem with PSS LOOK option"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,4,0)="The VistA option 'Lookup into Dispense Drug File' [PSS LOOK] does not work"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,5,0)="the same as the 'Drug File Inquiry' [PSB DRUG INQUIRY] option."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,7,0)="2) HD0000000230104 - Using Drug Enter/Edit Option in PDM, local possible"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,8,0)="                     dosage merge performed automatically."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,9,0)="When Using Drug Enter/Edit Option in PDM, local possible dosage merge"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,10,0)="performed automatically. This happens before the user gets asked the"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,11,0)="question 'Do you want to merge new Local Possible Dosages?'"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,13,0)="3) HD0000000347730 - Errors in reminder index for non-VA meds"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,14,0)="The VistA 'Clinical Reminders Index Build' [PXRM INDEX BUILD] option runs"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,15,0)="the ^PSSSXRD routine used to create and rebuild the Clinical Reminders"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,16,0)="Index and the ^PSOPXRMU routine used by the cross-reference to keep the"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,17,0)="index current differ in how they set the discontinued date when that it is"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,18,0)="missing. The differences in the discontinued date cause the Clinical"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,19,0)="Reminders to be inaccurate."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,21,0)="4) HD0000000500625 - Medication Reconciliation national component "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,22,0)="                     displaying on scalp instead of subcutaneous"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,23,0)="When users change the name of a Medication Instruction using the VistA"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,24,0)="Medication Instruction File Add/Edit [PSSJU MI] option, the system does"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,25,0)="perform the duplicate entry check.  This allows users to create duplicate"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,26,0)="entries which in turn cause the Medication Reconciliation to display the"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,27,0)="incorrect data."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,29,0)="5) HD0000000507504 - User unable to mark/unmark drugs for CMOP"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,30,0)="When using the VistA 'CMOP Mark/Unmark (Single drug)' [PSSXX MARK] option"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,31,0)="and the users tries to mark or unmark drugs for CMOP the system displays"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,32,0)="""Do you wish to mark this drug to transmit to CMOP?"""
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,33,0)="""Enter Yes or No: """
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,34,0)="If the user enters a ""Yes"" or ""No"" response, the system repeats the "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,35,0)="prompt."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",160,1,36,0)="If the user enters a ""Y"", ""y"", ""N"" or ""n"" the system accepts the entry."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",161,0)="183 SEQ #162^3140814.143729^17"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",161,1,0)="^^4^4^3140814"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",161,1,1,0)="This patch modifies the Application Programming Interfaces (API), "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",161,1,2,0)="$$DETOX^PSSOPKI to return a ""1"" (one) only if the drug name contains "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",161,1,3,0)="""BUPREN"" and the dosage form does not contain ""PATCH"", otherwise a 0 "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",161,1,4,0)="(""zero"")."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,0)="180 SEQ #163^3141104.104228^17"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,0)="^^22^22^3141104"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,1,0)="This patch will correct the following reported issues:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,3,0)="1) INC000000324382 - Drug Enter/Edit option"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,4,0)="The Drug Enter/Edit [PSS DRUG ENTER/EDIT] VistA option deletes a drugs"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,5,0)="Possible Dosage of an inactive drug if the user answers YES to the ""Do you"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,6,0)="wish to match/rematch to NATIONAL DRUG file?"" prompt."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,8,0)="2) INC000000861438 - PSSIV ADD Input Template "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,9,0)="When editing an IV Additive, using both the Additives File and the "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,10,0)="Drug Enter/Edit options, the prompt for Additive Frequency is missing."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,11,0)="Currently the only way to edit the ADDITIVE FREQUENCY field (#18) is"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,12,0)="through FileMan."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,14,0)="3) INC000000942809 - Message Sent field (#3) in the Vendor Interface"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,15,0)="                     Data file (#59.74) not populating."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,16,0)="A defect was discovered with the population of the Message Sent field "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,17,0)="(#3) in the Vendor Interface Data file (#59.74).  When the Interface"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,18,0)="Scheduler [PSS INTERFACE SCHEDULER] job receives an error indicating"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,19,0)="that the Vendor Database is down, it makes an entry in the Vendor"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,20,0)="Interface Data  file (#59.74) and sends a VistA MailMan message to the"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,21,0)="mail group PSS ORDER CHECKS. When the message is sent, the message"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",162,1,22,0)="sent field(#3) is not being updated with the message sent flag."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",163,0)="177 SEQ #164^3150121.133943^17"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",163,1,0)="^^5^5^3150121"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",163,1,1,0)="This patch will correct the issue reported in:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",163,1,2,0)="INC000000824872 - UPDATE FDA MED GUIDES URL"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",163,1,3,0)="The automatic printing functionality does not connect to the secure "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",163,1,4,0)="Sharepoint  to retrieve the requested guide and a sheet of paper prints "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",163,1,5,0)="on my printer ""ERROR: UNABLE TO AUTOMATICALLY PRINT MEDICATION GUIDE""."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",164,0)="190 SEQ #165^3150616.122209^17"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",164,1,0)="^^4^4^3150616"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",164,1,1,0)="Patch PSS*1.0*190 addresses the following issue:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",164,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",164,1,3,0)="Unable to enter new national drug interactions into Drug Interactions "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",164,1,4,0)="file (#56)."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,0)="119 SEQ #166^3150916.142139^17"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,0)="^^19^19^3150916"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,1,0)="This patch will correct the issue reported:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,4,0)="1) INC0000149525 - Problems placing PRN orders with multiple spaces/words"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,7,0)="*********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,8,0)="*                              WARNING                              *"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,9,0)="*                                                                   *"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,10,0)="*  This patch contains an environment check and will only install   *"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,11,0)="*           if one of the following conditions is met.              *"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,12,0)="*                                                                   *"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,13,0)="*  1)  If the site is a CMOP site this patch will be installed.     *"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,14,0)="*                                                                   *"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,15,0)="*  2)  If you are NOT a CMOP site and patches PSJ*5.0*194 and       *"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,16,0)="*      PSO*7.0*282 are installed.                                   *"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,17,0)="*                                                                   *"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,18,0)="*                                                                   *"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",165,1,19,0)="*********************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",166,0)="188 SEQ #167^3160211.171515^54"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",166,1,0)="^^1^1^3160211"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",166,1,1,0)="HAPE EDI Revenue project - NCPDP Continuous Maintenance Standards"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,0)="191 SEQ #168^3160328.123451^54"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,0)="^^95^95^3160328"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,1,0)="Patch PSS*1.0*191 provides enhancements to Pharmacy Data Management "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,2,0)="to support changes to the BCMA and Inpatient Medications"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,3,0)="applications for Transdermal Administrations."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,5,0)="******************************* ATTENTION ********************************"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,7,0)="Clinical Ancillary Services (CAS) Development-Delivery of Pharmacy "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,8,0)="Enhancements (DDPE) VA Inpatient Medication Administration - Transdermal"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,9,0)="enhancement includes 5 patches which must be installed in the following"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,10,0)="order:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,12,0)="1.      PSS*1*191"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,13,0)="2.      PSJ*5*315"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,14,0)="3.      PSB*3*83"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,15,0)="4.      OR*3*417"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,16,0)="5.      PSB*3*87"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,18,0)="ATTENTION: This enhancement also includes a new Graphical User Interface"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,19,0)="(GUI) executable, BCMA GUI PSB3_P083.EXE. Installation of this GUI is"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,20,0)="required immediately after the KIDS install for the Patch to function."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,22,0)="For retrieval and installation instructions, please see the Client "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,23,0)="Installation Instructions section."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,24,0)="**************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,26,0)="These enhancements are made to address NSR 20141012. "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,27,0)="     They include: "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,29,0)="     1. Currently Sites have to create fake removal orders to allow for "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,30,0)="appropriate removal of medications in BCMA.  This patch will alleviate "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,31,0)="that issue by adding a field to the ORDERABLE ITEM (#50.7) file titled "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,32,0)="PROMPT FOR REMOVAL IN BCMA (#12).  This field implements changes that will"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,33,0)="support enhancements to the BCMA and Inpatient Medication applications to "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,34,0)="display the removal times in Inpatient Medication orders using rules "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,35,0)="determined by the value of this field. The PROMPT FOR REMOVAL IN BCMA "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,36,0)="(#12) field can be set for Orderable Items that require removal to the "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,37,0)="following values:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,39,0)="     NULL/0=No Removal Required "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,40,0)="     1 = Removal at Next Administration "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,41,0)="     2 = Removal Period Optional Prior to Next Administration  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,42,0)="     3 = Removal Period Required Prior to Next Administration"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,44,0)="     2. A post installation routine, PSS1P191, will update the new PROMPT"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,45,0)="FOR REMOVAL IN BCMA (#12) field to a value of 1 for all Orderable Items"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,46,0)="with a Dosage Form that contain the word ""PATCH"".  A message will be sent"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,47,0)="to the installer as well as all users holding the PSJU and PSJI MGR keys"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,48,0)="providing a list of Orderable items that were updated during this process."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,49,0)="The PROMPT FOR REMOVAL IN BCMA (#12) field is only updated if it is"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,50,0)="currently set to a value of NULL so subsequent installations will not "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,51,0)="update the PROMPT FOR REMOVAL IN BCMA (#12) field again."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,53,0)="     3. Routines edited for this patch will add the prompt ""PROMPT FOR "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,54,0)="REMOVAL IN BCMA:"" to the following three options:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,56,0)="     - Edit Orderable Items [PSS EDIT ORDERABLE ITEMS]"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,57,0)="     - Drug Enter/Edit [PSS DRUG ENTER/EDIT]"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,58,0)="     - Dispense Drug/Orderable Item Maintenance [PSS MAINTAIN ORDERABLE  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,59,0)="       ITEMS]"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,61,0)="     4. Patch PSS*1.0*172 inadvertently missed adding the prompt, HIGH "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,62,0)="RISK/HIGH ALERT, to the following options, which is being added in "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,63,0)="this patch:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,65,0)="      - Drug Enter/Edit [PSS DRUG ENTER/EDIT]"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,66,0)="      - Dispense Drug/Orderable Item Maintenance [PSS MAINTAIN ORDERABLE"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,67,0)="        ITEMS]"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,69,0)="5. A second post install routine PSSP191A will create another"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,70,0)="email report.  This report will display orders for Medications Requiring "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,71,0)="Removal that do not contain the necessary file structures to allow for "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,72,0)="the new removal functionality to execute.  The primary purpose for this "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,73,0)="information is to allow the site to determine the approximate amount of "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,74,0)="resources needed to discontinue these orders and re-create them after "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,75,0)="patch PSJ*5*315 is installed.  Until the PSJ*5*315 patch is installed the "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,76,0)="capability for processing these orders will not be available.  More "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,77,0)="detailed procedures and recommendations for this process are in the "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,78,0)="installation section of this Patch Description. A copy of this report "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,79,0)="will be added to the Pharmacy Data Management [PSS MGR] menu as the Orders"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,80,0)="for MRRs With Removal Properties [PSS MRR ORDERS DIAGNOSTIC RPT] option."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,82,0)="       6. Two more reports will be added to the Orderable Item Management "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,83,0)="[PSS ORDERABLE ITEM MANAGEMENT] sub menu as options. The new report"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,84,0)="options, Orderable Items that Require Removal Report [PSS MRR ORDERABLE"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,85,0)="ITEMS RPT] option and Orderable Items Report for High Risk\High Alert [PSS"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,86,0)="HR/HA ORDERABLE ITEMS RPT] option, will allow review of the settings in"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,87,0)="the Orderable Items file (#50.7) for the values of the respective fields"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,88,0)="indicated in the report titles."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,90,0)="      PSS*1.0*191 does not have any dependencies for installation."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,91,0)="       The full functionality introduced in this patch will not be"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,92,0)="       available until patches PSJ*5.0*315, PSB*3.0*83 and PSB*3.0*87 "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,93,0)="       are installed."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,94,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",167,1,95,0)="       Pre-existing orders will remain unaffected with installation."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",168,0)="175^3160526.154805^54"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,0)="189 SEQ #170^3160713.12433^54"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,0)="^^378^378^3160713"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,1,0)="This patch is part of the Pharmacy Safety Updates project which was "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,2,0)="established to address specific New Service Requests (NSRs) as well as a"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,3,0)="Remedy Ticket and a Patient Safety Issue (PSI) related to the VistA Pharmacy"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,4,0)="applications as approved by the Health Systems Enterprise Systems Manager"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,5,0)="(ESM)."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,7,0)="This project is comprised of patches from five different applications, as"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,8,0)="shown below:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,9,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,10,0)="   APPLICATION/VERSION                                  PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,11,0)="   -----------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,12,0)="   OUTPATIENT PHARMACY (OP) V. 7.0                      PSO*7*444"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,13,0)="   INTEGRATED BILLING (IB) V. 2.0                       IB*2*545"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,14,0)="   PHARMACY DATA MANAGEMENT (PDM) V. 1.0                PSS*1*189"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,15,0)="   NATIONAL DRUG FILE (NDF) V. 4.0                      PSN*4*429"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,16,0)="   INPATIENT MEDICATIONS (IM) V.5.0                     PSJ*5*313"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,19,0)="The following New service Requests (NSRs) are being addressed by this patch:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,21,0)=" NSRs 20060601/20111206 Allow Dispensing of Greater Than 90 Day Supply"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,22,0)=" ---------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,23,0)=" The Outpatient Pharmacy and supporting VistA applications are being modified"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,24,0)=" to allow dispensing of more than 90 day supply fill for outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,25,0)=" prescriptions. The new limit will be 365 days and will be set for each drug"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,26,0)=" individually. See below for more information on specific menu "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,27,0)=" options related to this enhancement.  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,29,0)=" NSR 20110308 Addition of a STRENGTH Property to IV ADDITIVES and Premixed "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,30,0)="              IV SOLUTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,31,0)=" ----------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,32,0)=" Although patches PSJ*5*289 and PSS*1*174 introduced quite a few enhancements"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,33,0)=" to the IV Additives and IV Solutions ordering functionality they did not go"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,34,0)=" far enough in addressing all the issues originally in the NSR. Patches "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,35,0)=" PSJ*5*313 and PSS*1*189 will extend the display of the IV Additive strength"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,36,0)=" to other parts of the Inpatient Medications and Pharmacy Data Management "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,37,0)=" applications. In addition, it will also impose a new rule where an Orderable"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,38,0)=" Item can only have one IV Solution for a specific volume when it is marked"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,39,0)=" to be used in the CPRS IV Fluid Order Entry. "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,40,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,41,0)=" NSR 20080907 Inactivate Pharmacy Standard Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,42,0)=" ----------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,43,0)=" This enhancement is a conversion of an existing Class III software solution"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,44,0)=" that permits an entry in the ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1) to be "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,45,0)=" marked as INACTIVE via the Standard Schedule Edit [PSS SCHEDULE EDIT] option."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,46,0)=" Once marked INACTIVE the schedule is no longer shown on the CPRS "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,47,0)=" ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE list."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,49,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,50,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,51,0)="The following Pharmacy Data Management functionality was modified:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,52,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,53,0)="1. New MAXIMUM DAYS SUPPLY field (#66) in the DRUG file (#50)"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,54,0)="   This new field shown below was added to the DRUG file (#50) for storing"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,55,0)="   the local maximum day supply value for a medication in an outpatient "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,56,0)="   prescription."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,58,0)="   Field Name: MAXIMUM DAYS SUPPLY   Format: Numeric"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,60,0)="   INPUT TRANSFORM: D MXDAYSUP^PSSDDUT2"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,61,0)="   HELP-PROMPT:     This is the maximum number of days supply for this drug. "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,62,0)="   DESCRIPTION:     This field is used to determine the maximum number for"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,63,0)="                    days supply that may be assigned to this drug. The"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,64,0)="                    maximum value allowed for this field is 365 (days) for"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,65,0)="                    most drugs, however: "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,66,0)="                              "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,67,0)="                    - Schedule 2 controlled substances have a 30-day maximum"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,68,0)="                      days supply limit"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,69,0)="                    - Schedules 3 thru 5 controlled substances have a 90-day"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,70,0)="                      maximum days supply limit "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,71,0)="                    - The maximum number of days supply for this drug cannot"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,72,0)="                      exceed the National Drug File (NDF) maximum value if it"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,73,0)="                      exists "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,74,0)="                    - No value can be entered for Clozapine drugs as the"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,75,0)="                      maximum days supply is controlled by the Clozapine"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,76,0)="                      functionality"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,78,0)="2. ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1)"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,79,0)="   a) A new field named INACTIVE (#12) shown below was added to the "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,80,0)="      ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1) to allow the filtering inactive"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,81,0)="      schedules when providing a list to the CPRS application."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,82,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,83,0)="      Field Name: INACTIVE      Format: Set of Codes ('1' FOR YES)"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,85,0)="      HELP-PROMPT:    Answer YES to mark this administration schedule entry"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,86,0)="                      as inactive. "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,87,0)="      DESCRIPTION:    This field is used to indicate that a Standard Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,88,0)="                      is inactive. Inactive schedules are filtered from the"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,89,0)="                      list of schedules sent to CPRS for selection when users"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,90,0)="                      are placing a medication order.  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,92,0)="   b) The upper limit for the FREQUENCY (IN MINUTES) field (#2) was increased"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,93,0)="      from 129,600 (90 days) to 525,600 (365 days)."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,94,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,95,0)="3. MEDICATION INSTRUCTION file (#51)"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,96,0)="   The upper limit for the FREQUENCY (IN MINUTES) field (#31) was increased"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,97,0)="   from 129,600 (90 days) to 525,600 (365 days)."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,98,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,99,0)="4. IV SOLUTIONS file (#52.7)"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,100,0)="   New INPUT TRANSFORMS have been added to the VOLUME (#2) and USED IN IV"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,101,0)="   FLUID ORDER ENTRY (#17) to enforce the following new rule introduced "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,102,0)="   relating to this file: "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,103,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,104,0)="   Rule: An Orderable Item can have only ONE IV solution with a specific"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,105,0)="         volume when it is marked to be used in the IV Order Dialog."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,107,0)="5. PSSCOMMON input template"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,108,0)="   The PSSCOMMON input template used by the Drug File Enter/Edit [PSS DRUG"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,109,0)="   ENTER/EDIT] option was modified to include the new MAXIMUM"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,110,0)="   DAYS SUPPLY field (#66) in the DRUG file (#50) so that it can be edited"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,111,0)="   along with the other fields in this option."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,112,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,113,0)="6. PSSJ SCHEDULE EDIT Input template"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,114,0)="   The PSSJ SCHEDULE EDIT input template used by the Standard Schedule "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,115,0)="   Edit [PSS SCHEDULE EDIT] option was modified to include the new INACTIVE"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,116,0)="   field (#12) in the ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1) so that it can"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,117,0)="   be edited along with the other fields in this option."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,119,0)="7. Edit Orderable Items [PSS EDIT ORDERABLE ITEMS] option "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,120,0)="   This option was modified to display the IV Additive Strength value as"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,121,0)="   seen below:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,122,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,123,0)="   ... "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,124,0)="      Orderable Item ->  PIPERACILLIN/TAZOBACTAM"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,125,0)="      Dosage Form    ->  INJ"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,127,0)="   Dispense Drugs:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,128,0)="   ---------------"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,129,0)="   PIPERACILLIN 3/TAZOBACTAM 0.375GM/VI INJ"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,130,0)="   PIPERACILLIN 2/TAZOBACTAM 0.25GM/VI INJ"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,131,0)="   PIPERACILLIN 4/TAZOBACTAM 0.5GM/VI INJ"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,132,0)="   PIPERACILLIN/TAZOBACTAM         (A)     Additive Strength: 3.375 GM "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,133,0)="   PIPERACILLIN/TAZOBACTAM         (A)     Additive Strength: 2.25 GM "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,134,0)="   PIPERACILLIN/TAZOBACTAM         (A)     Additive Strength: 4.5 GM "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,135,0)="  ..."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,137,0)="8. PRimary Solution File (IV) [PSSJI SOLN] option"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,138,0)="   This option was modified to enforce a new rule introduced to ensure that"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,139,0)="   an Orderable Item can only have 1 active IV SOLUTION linked to it with a"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,140,0)="   specific VOLUME when the IV SOLUTION is marked YES for the USED IN IV"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,141,0)="   FLUID ORDER ENTRY field (#17). When they user tries to perform an edit"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,142,0)="   that breaks this rule by editing the screen fields VOLUME, USED IN IV"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,143,0)="   FLUID ORDER ENTRY or INACTIVATION DATE, the error message below will be"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,144,0)="   displayed and the editing won't be permitted."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,145,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,146,0)="         Only one Active IV Solution with a specific volume can be linked to"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,147,0)="         an Orderable Item or Dispense Drug when the IV Solution is marked to"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,148,0)="         be used in the CPRS IV Fluid Order Entry."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,150,0)="9. Drug Enter/Edit [PSS DRUG ENTER/EDIT] option "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,151,0)="   a) This option was modified to allow entry of the new MAXIMUM DAY SUPPLY"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,152,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,153,0)="   ..."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,154,0)="   NCPDP DISPENSE UNIT: EACH// "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,155,0)="   NCPDP QUANTITY MULTIPLIER: 1// "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,156,0)="   MAXIMUM DAYS SUPPLY: ??"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,157,0)="     This field is used to determine the maximum number for days supply that"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,158,0)="     may be assigned to this drug. The maximum value allowed for this field"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,159,0)="     is 365 (days) for most drugs, however: "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,160,0)="       "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,161,0)="       - Schedule 2 controlled substances have a 30-day maximum days supply "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,162,0)="         limit "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,163,0)="       - Schedules 3 thru 5 controlled substances have a 90-day maximum days"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,164,0)="         supply limit "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,165,0)="       - The maximum number of days supply for this drug cannot exceed the"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,166,0)="         National Drug File (NDF) maximum value if it exists"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,167,0)="       - No value can be entered for Clozapine drugs as the maximum days"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,168,0)="         supply is controlled by the Clozapine functionality"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,169,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,170,0)="   MAXIMUM DAYS SUPPLY: "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,171,0)="   PRICE PER DISPENSE UNIT: 0.8280"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,172,0)="   ..."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,174,0)="   b) The exact same change described above in #8 was applied to this option"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,175,0)="      where the user can create, edit and link IV Solution entries to a "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,176,0)="      dispense drug."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,177,0)="       "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,178,0)="10. Lookup into Dispense Drug File [PSS LOOK] option"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,179,0)="   This option was modified to display the new MAXIMUM DAYS SUPPLY (#66)"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,180,0)="   field in the DRUG file (#50) along with the other dispense drug fields for"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,181,0)="   the dispense drug selected, as shown below:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,182,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,183,0)="    ..."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,184,0)="    DISPENSE UNIT:                       VA DISPENSE UNIT:          CAP"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,185,0)="    DISPENSE UNITS/ORDER UNIT: 20        PRICE/DISPENSE UNIT:    0.8280"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,186,0)="    NCPDP DISPENSE UNIT: EACH            NCPDP QUANTITY MULTIPLIER:  1.000"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,187,0)="    MAXIMUM DAYS SUPPLY: 100"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,188,0)="    APPL PKG USE:  Outpatient  Unit Dose  Non-VA Med"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,189,0)="    STRENGTH: 10                       UNIT: MG"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,190,0)="    POSSIBLE DOSAGES:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,191,0)="    ... "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,192,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,193,0)="11. Standard Schedule Edit [PSS SCHEDULE EDIT] option"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,194,0)="   This option was modified to add the new INACTIVE field (#12) in the "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,195,0)="   ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1) to be updated for a schedule."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,196,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,197,0)="   ..."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,198,0)="   OTHER LANGUAGE EXPANSION: "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,199,0)="   INACTIVE: ??"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,200,0)="     This field is used to indicate that a Standard Schedule is inactive."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,201,0)="     Inactive schedules are filtered from the list of schedules sent to CPRS"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,202,0)="     for selection when users are placing a medication order."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,203,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,204,0)="        Choose from: "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,205,0)="          1        YES"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,206,0)="   INACTIVE: "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,207,0)="   ..."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,208,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,209,0)="12. Administration Schedule File Report [PSS SCHEDULE REPORT] option"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,210,0)="    This option was modified to display the new INACTIVE field (#12)"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,211,0)="    created in the ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE file (#51.1) as seen below:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,212,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,213,0)="      ADMINISTRATION SCHEDULE FILE REPORT (All)                     PAGE: NN"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,214,0)="      ----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,215,0)="      ...  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,216,0)="      *Q4H"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,217,0)="           STANDARD ADMINISTRATION TIMES: 01-05-09-13-17-21"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,218,0)="                    OUTPATIENT EXPANSION: EVERY 4 HOURS"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,219,0)="                OTHER LANGUAGE EXPANSION: "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,220,0)="                           SCHEDULE TYPE: CONTINUOUS"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,221,0)="                  FREQUENCY (IN MINUTES): 240"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,222,0)="            EXCLUDE FROM ALL DOSE CHECKS: "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,223,0)="           EXCLUDE FROM DAILY DOSE CHECK: "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,224,0)="                                INACTIVE: YES"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,225,0)="     ..."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,226,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,227,0)="13. Dispense Drug/Orderable Item Maintenance [PSS MAINTAIN ORDERABLE ITEMS] &"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,228,0)="    Drug Enter/Edit [PSS DRUG ENTER/EDIT] options"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,229,0)="    A new rule described below is being introduced which is related to the"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,230,0)="    relationship between IV Solutions and Orderable Items."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,231,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,232,0)="    Rule: An Orderable Item can only have ONE IV solution with a specific"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,233,0)="          volume when it is marked to be used in the CPRS IV Order Dialog."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,234,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,235,0)="    This option was modified to check every time the user tries to link a "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,236,0)="    dispense drug to an orderable item whether the new rule is being broken"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,237,0)="    or not. If the new rule is being broken the message below will be"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,238,0)="    displayed and the user will not be able to proceed with linking the drug"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,239,0)="    to the orderable item."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,240,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,241,0)="       Matching [Dispense Drug Name]  to [Orderable Item Name] would cause"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,242,0)="       the orderable item to have more than one Active IV Solution with the"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,243,0)="       same volume marked to be used in the IV FLUID ORDER ENTRY, which is"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,244,0)="       not allowed."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,245,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,246,0)="       Please, review the IV Solutions associated with this drug before"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,247,0)="       matching it to this orderable item or match it to a different "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,248,0)="       orderable item."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,249,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,250,0)="14. IV Solution Pre-Install Manual Clean-up (Environment Check routine)"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,251,0)="    An environment check routine will run before the patch is installed to"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,252,0)="    ensure that an orderable item does not have more than one IV Solution"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,253,0)="    with the same volume when they are marked YES to be used in the CPRS IV"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,254,0)="    Fluid Order Entry. If at least one orderable item entry is found, the"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,255,0)="    patch installation will be aborted and a Mailman message will be sent to"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,256,0)="    all users holding the following security keys: PSIVMGR, PSIJ MGR, PSNMGR."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,257,0)="    The message will contain a list of all orderable items that need to be "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,258,0)="    cleaned up, as seen in the sample message below:"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,259,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,260,0)="    Subj: Duplicate IV Solution Volume under same Orderable Item  [#215733]"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,261,0)="    From: PATCH PSS*1*189  In 'IN' basket.   Page 1"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,262,0)="    -------------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,263,0)="    The list below shows IV Solutions in your database that need to be"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,264,0)="    cleaned up before patch PSS*1*189 can be installed."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,265,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,266,0)="    Rule: An Orderable Item can only have ONE IV solution with a specific"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,267,0)="          volume when it is marked to be used in the IV Order Dialog."
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,268,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,269,0)="    Run Date/Time: Jun 12, 2015@09:49:16"
^DIC(9.4,164,22,1,"PAH",169,1,270,0)="    -------------------------------------------------------------------------"
