^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,0)="3.0^3040224^3040330^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,0)="^^101^101^3040330"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,1,0)="*** Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) Version 3.0 ***"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,3,0)="This build consists of BCMA Version 3.0 rollover code and resolution to a "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,4,0)="few outstanding BCMA defects."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,6,0)="Listed below are primary National Online Information Sharing ticket "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,7,0)="(NOIS) identification information representing BCMA defects/problems"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,8,0)="and their respective corrective action."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,10,0)="1. Problem: NOIS ISB-0603-31561"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,11,0)="A medication order that has administration times set for today, but "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,12,0)="before the Start Time of the order, displays on the Bar Code Medication "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,13,0)="Administration (BCMA) Due List Report."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,15,0)="Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,16,0)="The Due List Report will not display medication orders until the Start "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,17,0)="Date/Time of the medication order takes affect."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,19,0)="2. Problem: NOIS ISB-0903-31964"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,20,0)="When the user selects a time frame for the Medication Administration "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,21,0)="History (MAH) Report and no administrations are due, the report lists the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,22,0)="medication order number from Inpatient Medications V. 5.0 under the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,23,0)="""Initial-Name Legend"" section."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,25,0)="Corrective Action: "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,26,0)="The MAH Report will not display the order number from Inpatient "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,27,0)="Medications V. 5.0 under the ""Initial-Name Legend"" section when no "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,28,0)="administrations are due for a specific time frame."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,30,0)="3. Problem: NOIS LAH-1203-61493"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,31,0)="The user receives the following error message, ""BCMA failed to "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,32,0)="communicate with VISTA,"" if the Graphical User Interface (GUI) BCMA times"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,33,0)="out and is unable to connect to the server."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,35,0)="Corrective Action: "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,36,0)="The processing time for the GUI BCMA software to display the patient s "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,37,0)="record on the BCMA Virtual Due List (VDL) has been reduced."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,39,0)="4. Problem: NOIS LIT-0603-71923"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,40,0)="Users sometimes receive an ""allocation failure"" error message when "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,41,0)="accessing a patient s record using the GUI BCMA."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,42,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,43,0)="Corrective Action: "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,44,0)="The ""allocation failure"" error message has been corrected."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,46,0)="5. Problem: NOIS MAD-1203-42204"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,47,0)="The MAH Report takes an extended amount of time to run if the Start Date "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,48,0)="and the Stop Date of the report, requested by the user, are for different "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,49,0)="years. For example, if the Start Date is 12/28/03 and the Stop Date is "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,50,0)="01/03/04."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,52,0)="Corrective Action: "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,53,0)="The user can now request different years for the MAH Report without "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,54,0)="experiencing extended delays as BCMA accesses the data. "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,56,0)="6. Problem: NOIS MIN-1203-41637"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,57,0)="Users sometimes experience an ""Invalid Medication Lookup"" error message "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,58,0)="after scanning a medication in the ""Scan Medication Bar Code:"" field of "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,59,0)="the ""Order Manager""  dialog box when using the BCMA Med Order Button in "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,60,0)="GUI BCMA."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,62,0)="Corrective Action: "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,63,0)="The BCMA medication lookup process has been corrected to properly "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,64,0)="validate the medications scanned in the ""Scan Medication Bar Code:"" field "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,65,0)="of the ""Order Manager"" dialog box in GUI BCMA."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,67,0)="7. Problem: NOIS UNY-0104-10174"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,68,0)="Multiple IV medication orders display as merged on the IV Medication Tab "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,69,0)="after an order is discontinued, but the IV bag is still infusing."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,71,0)="Corrective Action: "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,72,0)="Multiple IV medication orders will display properly on the IV Medication "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,73,0)="Tab.  "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,75,0)="8. Problem: NOIS TNV-0104-30647"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,76,0)="Users sometimes experience the following error message, ""ERROR: 16^Server "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,77,0)="Protocol Disabled,"" when using the Edit Medication Log [PSB MED LOG EDIT] "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,78,0)="option. This occurs when the PSB BCMA RASO17 SRV Health Level Seven (HL7) "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,79,0)="server protocol is being disabled."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,81,0)="Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,82,0)="The error message is only intended to notify the BCMA software that the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,83,0)="protocol is being disabled. BCMA will now validate the message and not "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,84,0)="display it to users. "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,86,0)="9. Problem: NOIS ISB-0104-31384"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,87,0)="When an IV medication order with an infusing bag is ""Renewed,"" the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,88,0)="renewed order continues to display on the IV Medication Tab of the BCMA  "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,89,0)="VDL  until the infusing bag is ""Completed,"" even if the ""Renewed"" order's"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,90,0)="Start Date/Time has expired."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,92,0)="Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,93,0)="When an IV medication order with an infusing bag is ""Renewed,"" the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,94,0)="renewed order will continue to display on the IV Medication Tab of the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,95,0)="BCMA VDL until the infusing bag is ""Completed,"" or until the Start "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,96,0)="Date/Time of the new order that was created during the renewal process. "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,97,0)="Once the new order is active, the infusing bag from the previous order "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,98,0)="will display on the BCMA VDL with the new order, along with any "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,99,0)="additional bags created from the new order. Any available bags from the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,100,0)="previous order will display on the new order based on the IV Site "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,1,101,0)="Parameter settings in the GUI BCMA Site Parameters application."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^133^133"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,0)="7^3040702^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,0)="^^53^53^3040702"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,1,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,3,0)="*******************Important Note********************"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,5,0)="Sites running the Bar Code Medication Administration  (BCMA) "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,6,0)="  Contingency Software must install this patch on all "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,7,0)="  Contingency workstations in addition to being installed"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,8,0)="  on to the Vista Server. This patch is being released in "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,9,0)="  conjunction with the Inpatient Pharmacy patch PSJ*5*123. "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,10,0)="  Install both patches on to the Vista Server and the PSB*3*7 "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,11,0)="  on to the Contingency Workstations as close together as "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,12,0)="  possible during non-peak times. Since the location of the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,13,0)="  Pharmacy Orders ""Admin Times"" data has been changed "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,14,0)="  in the HL7 message you could see orders on the workstation "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,15,0)="  missing this data on orders updated due to transitions of data"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,16,0)="  during the installation of these patches. The missing data will "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,17,0)="  correct  itself when that order is updated. "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,18,0)="  Once installed it is suggested that the sites review the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,19,0)="  Contingency System reports. Any missing ""Admin Times"""
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,20,0)="  can be corrected by running the Single Patient Init"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,21,0)="  [PSB BCBU INIT SINGLE PT] option or the Workstation "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,22,0)="  can be re-initialized."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,24,0)=" *****************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,26,0)=" 1. A fix for the '&' delimiter problem with the admin times. The "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,27,0)="      admin times was moved to another Field of the HL7 message "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,28,0)="      in the pharmacy patch PSJ*5.0*123."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,29,0)="      This patch compensates for the pharmacy change."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,31,0)=" 2. When a user was added, edited or terminated, BCMA Contingency "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,32,0)="      Software would be called and the user would be evaluated, "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,33,0)="      and if appropriate be transmitted to the BCMA Contingency "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,34,0)="      Workstations.  This evaluation was not occurring correctly.  "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,35,0)="      As a result, all users added, changed or terminated were being "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,36,0)="      transmitted to the workstations.  An additional screen was added"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,37,0)="      to ensure that only the appropriate users accounts were "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,38,0)="      transmitted to the workstation."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,40,0)=" 3. When a user had multiple divisions defined under their user "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,41,0)="      account and the workstations were setup using the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,42,0)="      multidivisional capability the users divisions were not "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,43,0)="      interpreted correctly. A bug was found in the code that "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,44,0)="      looped through the user's division multiple and was corrected."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,45,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,47,0)=" 4. The user Update portion of the BCMA Contingency was not checking "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,48,0)="      the status of the ""PSB BKUP ONLINE"" parameter. Additional code"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,49,0)="      was added to check for the status of the ""PSB BKUP ONLINE"" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,50,0)="      parameter. If the parameter is set to ""NO"" then no updates "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,51,0)="      will be transmitted to the workstation from the user portion"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,52,0)="      of the package."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",1,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,0)="5 SEQ #2^3040903^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^44^44^3040903"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,1,0)="1.  Problem: NOIS MAD-0104-40858 "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,2,0)="    The Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) reports,"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,3,0)="    with the exception of the Cumulative/Vitals Measurement Report, does "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,4,0)="    not display allergy information in the reports header."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,6,0)="    Corrective Action: The BCMA Reports, with the exception of the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,7,0)="    Cumulative/Vitals Measurement Report, displays allergy information in"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,8,0)="    the reports header. The Reactions header has also been removed"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,9,0)="    from the report and replaced with the ""ADRs:"" header."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,11,0)="2.  Problem: NOIS BUT-0204-20463"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,12,0)="    The Medication Administration History [PSBO MH] option and the Due "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,13,0)="    List [PSBO DL] option add an exclamation point (i.e., Spec Inst:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,14,0)="    !Please verify) to the prefix of a Special Instruction."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,16,0)="    Corrective Action: The Medication Administration History [PSBO MH] "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,17,0)="    option and the Due List [PSBO DL] option correctly removes "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,18,0)="    the exclamation point (i.e., Spec Inst: Please verify) added"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,19,0)="    to a Special Instruction."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,21,0)="3.  Problem: NOIS BED-0204-10327"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,22,0)="    When a clinician administers a Pro Rea Nata (PRN) medication using "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,23,0)="    the Manual Medication Entry [PSB MED LOG NEW ENTRY] option, and the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,24,0)="    administration date/time is set to an earlier timeframe, the PRN"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,25,0)="    administration date/time displays incorrectly on BCMA PRN"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,26,0)="    Effectiveness Log Report as the entered date/time of this "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,27,0)="    administration occurred."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,29,0)="    Corrective Action: When a clinician administers a PRN medication "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,30,0)="    using the Manual Medication Entry [PSB MED LOG NEW ENTRY] option, and"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,31,0)="    the administration date/time is set to an earlier timeframe, the PRN"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,32,0)="    administration date/time displays correctly on the BCMA PRN"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,33,0)="    Effectiveness Log Report as the actual date/time of the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,34,0)="    administration."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,36,0)="4.  Problem: NOIS NTH-0304-72663"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,37,0)="    A ""Null subscript"" error occurs at routine line ""EN+4^PSBVDLPA"""
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,38,0)="    when there is single patient with data entered in the BCMA Medication "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,39,0)="    Log File (#53.79) and indexes.  This error occurs during the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,40,0)="    initial implementation of the BCMA Graphical User Interface (GUI) "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,41,0)="    system."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,42,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,43,0)="    Corrective Action: The initial implementation of the BCMA GUI will "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",2,1,44,0)="    not generate a ""Null subscript"" error at routine line ""EN+4^PSBVDLPA""."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,0)="6 SEQ #3^3041015^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^81^81^3041015"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="*** ATTENTION: This patch includes a new Graphical User Interface "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,2,0)="       (GUI) executable file. Installation of this new GUI is "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,3,0)="        REQUIRED in order for the patch to function.  The new GUI"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,4,0)="        MUST be installed IMMEDIATELY after the KIDS install in "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,5,0)="        order for the software to function. This Patch includes a "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,6,0)="        Post install that corrects problem number six below. The "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,7,0)="        installation time frame for this post install will vary based"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,8,0)="        on the size of the site. This build will validate the correct "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,9,0)="        version of Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) GUI is in"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,10,0)="        use. The correct GUI must be installed to support BCMA "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,11,0)="        Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) Med Order "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,12,0)="        functionality ***"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,14,0)="For retrieval and installation instructions, please see the Client"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,15,0)="Installation Instructions section."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,17,0)=" 1. Problem: NOIS HWH-0204-41213"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,18,0)="    The Instructor information does not display in the legend of the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,19,0)="    Medication Administration History [PSBO MH] option, and the audit log"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,20,0)="    of the Medication Administration Log [PSBO ML] option."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,22,0)="    Corrective Action: The Instructor information displays in the legend  "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,23,0)="    of the Medication Administration History [PSBO MH] option, and the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,24,0)="    audit log of the Medication Administration Log [PSBO ML] option."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,26,0)="2.  Corrective Action: When student and instructor information is "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,27,0)="    present at login the GUI BCMA CPRS Med Order button is disabled."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,29,0)="3.  Problem: NOIS HUN-0104-20931"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,30,0)="    Infusing IV bags are duplicated on a ""following"" order after the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,31,0)="    order that was active when the IV bag was infusing has become"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,32,0)="    ""discontinued"".  The Virtual Due List (VDL) attempts to display "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,33,0)="    duplicate bags and associates the same IV bags with multiple orders."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,35,0)="    Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,36,0)="    When an order with an infusing bag is discontinued, the VDL will"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,37,0)="    either continue to display the infusing bag with the discontinued "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,38,0)="    order, or the VDL will display the infusing bag with an active "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,39,0)="    ""following"" order, but not both."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,40,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,41,0)="4.  Problem: NOIS ISB-0304-30352"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,42,0)="    If an IV order with an infusing bag expires and the patient's record "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,43,0)="    is not accessed using Inpatient Medications (IPM) (e.g., the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,44,0)="    Inpatient Order Entry [PSJ OE] option) the following message may"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,45,0)="    appear, hindering an user's attempt to take action on the order:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,46,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,47,0)="           ""Either the order status or the current scan status displayed "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,48,0)="           on the VDL does not match the status recorded in VistA! This "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,49,0)="           may be due to someone editing the order in VistA or another "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,50,0)="           individual scanning the medication. Your current action will "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,51,0)="           be canceled and the VDL will be refreshed to reflect the most "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,52,0)="           current order information."""
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,54,0)="    Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,55,0)="    A user will be able to take action on an expired IV order having an "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,56,0)="    infusing bag via the BCMA GUI VDL as appropriate."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,57,0)="     "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,58,0)="5.  Problem: NOIS MOU-0304-32821"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,59,0)="    The temporary, scratch global ^PSBORDA is automatically monitored and "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,60,0)="    documented via journaling procedures.  It is not necessary to journal "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,61,0)="    this temporary global since it is used solely as a temporary data "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,62,0)="    storage area."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,64,0)="    Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,65,0)="    The global ^PSBORDA will be renamed as an appropriate scratch ""^TMP"" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,66,0)="    global with the first two subscripts being ""PSB"" followed by ""$J""."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,68,0)="6.  Problem: NOIS ISB-0404-31737"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,69,0)="    With the release of BCMA Version 2 (PSB*2.0), any unit dose "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,70,0)="    order that is displayed on the ""IVP/IVPB"" tab and administered will "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,71,0)="    have a Ward Stock number generated and placed in the IV Unique "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,72,0)="    ID field (FIELD #.26) of the BCMA Medication Log (FILE #53.79)"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,73,0)="    The Ward Stock number is stored in the BCMA Medication Log global and "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,74,0)="    is not displayed on the VDL or any BCMA Report."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,75,0)="   "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,76,0)="    Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,77,0)="    A unit dose order that is displayed on the ""IVP/IVPB"" tab and "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,78,0)="    administered will not have a Ward Stock number generated and placed"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,79,0)="    in the IV Unique ID field (FIELD #.26) of the BCMA Medication Log "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,80,0)="    (FILE #53.79). A post install will clean up all incorrect previous"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",3,1,81,0)="    entries."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,0)="3 SEQ #4^3041228^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^101^101^3041228"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="*** ATTENTION: This patch includes a new Graphical User Interface (GUI)"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,2,0)="     executable file. Installation of this new GUI is REQUIRED in order"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,3,0)="     for the patch to function.  The new GUI MUST be installed IMMEDIATELY "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,4,0)="     after the KIDS install in order for the software to function. ***    "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,6,0)=" For retrieval and installation instructions, please see the Client"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,7,0)=" Installation Instructions section."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,10,0)=" 1.  Problem: NOIS BUT-1203-21780"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,11,0)="     Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) users are not able to re-"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,12,0)="     instate a medication patch if it had been unintentionally marked as "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,13,0)="     'REMOVED' via BCMA. This issue has been delegated a 'PATIENT SAFETY' "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,14,0)="     keyword."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,16,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,17,0)="     The removal of a medication patch may be undone if it had been"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,18,0)="     unintentionally marked as 'REMOVED'; this may be accomplished by the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,19,0)="     user who marked the medication patch as 'REMOVED' or by a user"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,20,0)="     allocated the ""PSB MANAGER"" key."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,23,0)=" 2.  Problem: NOIS ISB-0204-30176"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,24,0)="     The prompt ""Enter the DATE of Administration: Today//"" of the Manual "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,25,0)="     Medication Entry [PSB MED LOG NEW ENTRY] option has caused confusion."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,26,0)="     The user unintentionally accepts the default (i.e. ""Today"") when "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,27,0)="     attempting to document a past administration.     "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,29,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,30,0)="     The prompt ""Enter the DATE of Administration: Today //"" will be"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,31,0)="     replaced by the prompt ""Enter the DATE the medication was "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,32,0)="     administered: //"" when using the Manual Medication Entry "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,33,0)="     [PSB MED LOG NEW ENTRY] option.  Also, this new prompt will not accept"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,34,0)="     the entry of a future date/time for an administration."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,37,0)=" 3.  Problem: NOIS PHO-0904-61033"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,38,0)="     The BCMA Medication History report does not show large volume IV"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,39,0)="     medications data when viewed via the Computerized Patient Record System"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,40,0)="     (CPRS) GUI ""Orders/View/Details..."" option."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,42,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,43,0)="     The BCMA Medication History report will display large volume IV "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,44,0)="     medications data when viewed via the CPRS GUI."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,47,0)=" 4.  Problem: NOIS LAH-0404-61280"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,48,0)="     The user is unable to access a patient's VDL when receiving an error"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,49,0)="     message containing the text ""GETPRNS+17^PSBPRN"".  These messages occur"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,50,0)="     when a patient is no longer admitted when that patient's VDL is"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,51,0)="     refreshed."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,53,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,54,0)="     BCMA will continue, without error, when a patient is no longer admitted"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,55,0)="     while that patient's VDL is being viewed and refreshed."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,58,0)=" 5.  Problem: NOIS MWV-0704-20690"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,59,0)="     The user is able to change the status of an order's patch medication"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,60,0)="     while that order concurrently has another 'GIVEN' and not 'REMOVED'"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,61,0)="     patch medication.  After the initial status of a patch of that order has "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,62,0)="     been set to a status other than 'GIVEN', that patch can then be"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,63,0)="     administered via BCMA, without a warning to the user concerning a"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,64,0)="     concurrently 'GIVEN' patch."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,66,0)="     Corrective Action:      "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,67,0)="     BCMA will not allow multiple patches of a patch medication order to be"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,68,0)="     at the status of 'GIVEN' concurrently."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,70,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,71,0)=" 6.  Problem: NOIS SFC-0704-60956"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,72,0)="     The user is unable to edit a 'NOT GIVEN' administration using the VISTA"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,73,0)="     ""Edit Medication Log"" [PSB MED LOG EDIT] option."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,75,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,76,0)="     The user will be able to edit 'NOT GIVEN' administrations using the GUI"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,77,0)="     version of the ""Edit Med Log"" found under the ""File"" menu of the BCMA"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,78,0)="     VDL."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,79,0)="      "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,81,0)=" 7.  Problem: NOIS CLL-0704-40997"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,82,0)="     If an IV piggyback bag is marked as 'GIVEN', the VDL is not refreshed,"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,83,0)="     and the VDL ""start/stop time"" parameters are reset making that specific"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,84,0)="     administration no longer display on the VDL, then that 'GIVEN' bag can"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,85,0)="     be scanned and administered again."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,86,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,87,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,88,0)="     BCMA will not allow an IV piggyback bag to be scanned and 'GIVEN' multiple"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,89,0)="     times."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,92,0)=" 8.  Enhancement:  Include Comments on the Medication History Report."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,93,0)="     PSB*3.0*3 will provide the user the ability to include comments that"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,94,0)="     were documented during an administration to appear on the Medication"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,95,0)="     History Report. This new functionality is accessible via the BCMA GUI"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,96,0)="     and CPRS GUI."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,97,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,98,0)=" 9.  Enhancement:  Report Medication History in reverse chronological order."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,99,0)="     PSB*3.0*3 will display the Medication History Report in reverse"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,100,0)="     chronological order; chronologically latter order activities will display"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",4,1,101,0)="     before earlier order activities."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,0)="4 SEQ #5^3050118^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,0)="^^30^30^3050118"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,2,0)="*** ATTENTION: This patch includes a new Graphical User Interface (GUI) "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,3,0)="  executable file. Installation of this GUI is required immediately "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,4,0)="  after the KIDS install for the Patch to function. *** "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,6,0)="For retrieval and installation instructions, please see the Client"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,7,0)="Installation Instructions section."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,10,0)="1.  Enhancement:  Read Only Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA)."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,11,0)="    This patch deploys the BCMA-HSC project ""Read Only BCMA"""
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,12,0)="    functionality.  After the installation of this build (PSB*3.0*4)"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,13,0)="    and installation of the released Read Only BCMA GUI executable"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,14,0)="    file, users allocated the ""PSB READ ONLY"" security key will be"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,15,0)="    granted documented Read Only BCMA functionality.  Also, as"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,16,0)="    documented, users allocated the ""PSB STUDENT"" security key using"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,17,0)="    BCMA while no BCMA instructor is using BCMA, will be granted Read"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,18,0)="    Only BCMA functionality until a BCMA Instructor has accessed BCMA."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,21,0)="2.  Enhancement:  Patient Record Flag Reporting."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,22,0)="    This patch provides ""Patient Record Flag"" reporting functionality."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,23,0)="    During patient selection, information about any active Patient"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,24,0)="    Record Flag(s) associated with the selected patient will be"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,25,0)="    presented to the user.  This patch also give the user the ability"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,26,0)="    to display and print details of all active Patient Record Flags."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,27,0)="    This patch will also display a ""FLAG"" button via the patient's GUI"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,28,0)="    Virtual Due List.  This ""FLAG"" button gives the user access to a"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,29,0)="    report of the all the active Patient Record Flags associated with"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",5,1,30,0)="    the patient."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,0)="9 SEQ #6^3050401^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,0)="^^99^99^3050401"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,2,0)=" 1.  Problem: NOIS CTX-0804-70321"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,3,0)="     Large volume IV orders do not show on the Due List Report.  The"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,4,0)="     Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) Due List Report does"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,5,0)="     not display information for large volume IV orders that have"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,6,0)="     been created on the date selected for reporting.  "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,8,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,9,0)="     The BCMA Due List Report will display large volume IV data when"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,10,0)="     appropriate."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,13,0)=" 2.  Problem: NOIS MIW-0504-40557"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,14,0)="     Scheduled administration times are reported and totaled on the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,15,0)="     Ward Administration Times Report per each clock hour.  If an"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,16,0)="     order s stop time is between clock hours, that order s final"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,17,0)="     scheduled administration is neither reported nor added to the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,18,0)="     report totals."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,20,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,21,0)="     The BCMA Ward Administration Times Report will report and"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,22,0)="     total all appropriate scheduled administration times.    "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,25,0)=" 3.  Problem: NOIS LIT-0704-71393"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,26,0)="     The initial administration of an order which displays on the BCMA"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,27,0)="     Graphical User Interface (GUI) Intravenous/Piggyback (IVPB) Tab "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,28,0)="     may result with an administration status of ""GIVEN"", ""HELD"", or"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,29,0)="     ""REFUSED"".  When this same order is administered via the VISTA "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,30,0)="     Manual Medication Entry [PSB MED LOG NEW ENTRY] option, the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,31,0)="     initial administration status can only be ""GIVEN""."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,33,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,34,0)="     The Manual Medication Entry [PSB MED LOG NEW ENTRY] option will"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,35,0)="     allow the initial administration of an IVPB order to result in"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,36,0)="     an administration status of ""GIVEN"", ""HELD"", or ""REFUSED""."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,39,0)=" 4.  Problem: NOIS UNY-0304-10606"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,40,0)="     When the user prints a Medication Administration History (MAH)"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,41,0)="     report with a date range exceeding seven (7) days, Pro Re Nata"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,42,0)="     (PRN) order activity, which occurred that last day of the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,43,0)="     report s date range, does not display."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,45,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,46,0)="     PRN activity occurring within the selected MAH report date range"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,47,0)="     will display on that MAH report."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,50,0)=" 5.  Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,51,0)="     When creating a MAH report, the administration times of orders"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,52,0)="     that have start time between the report's date range do not"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,53,0)="     display properly."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,55,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,56,0)="     The MAH report will display order administration times properly."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,59,0)=" 6.  Problem: NOIS ISB-0105-30190"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,60,0)="     When using the GUI Edit Med Log to add a comment for an "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,61,0)="     administration having units given less than 1.0, the message - ""When "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,62,0)="     changing the admin status to Given, at least one dispensed drug must "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,63,0)="     have a units given ...""  - is displayed and the comment is not filed."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,64,0)="     This error is due to the value in the Units Given field of the GUI"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,65,0)="     Edit Med Log being presented without the ""leading zero"" when the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,66,0)="     value is less than 1.0."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,68,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,69,0)="     When the Units Given value of an administration is less than zero, "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,70,0)="     it will be presented via the GUI Edit Med Log with the leading zero."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,72,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,73,0)=" 7.  Problem: NOIS ISB-1104-31950"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,74,0)="     The Medication History Report does not display a leading zero in"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,75,0)="     its ""Units GIVEN"" data field when display a numerical fraction."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,77,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,78,0)="     A leading zero will display in the Medication History Report,"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,79,0)="     ""Units GIVEN"" data field when appropriate."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,81,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,82,0)=" 8.  Problem: NOIS BUT-1204-21117"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,83,0)="     There are instances when the ""Units Of Administration"" data field"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,84,0)="     of the Medication History Report does not ""break"" and remain legible."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,86,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,87,0)="     The ""Units Of Administration"" data field of the Medication History"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,88,0)="     Report will ""break"" and maintain whole words and legibility."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,89,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,91,0)=" 9.  Problem: NOIS UNY-0105-11034"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,92,0)="     The heading for the Due List Report, ""Future Orders"" section is "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,93,0)="     displayed and is not followed by ""Future Order"" data when at least"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,94,0)="     one future active order exists, and no future order has a scheduled "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,95,0)="     administration within the selected report time parameters.     "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,96,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,97,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,98,0)="     The heading for the Due List Report, ""Future Orders"" section will not"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",6,1,99,0)="     display, unless ""Future Order"" data is to be displayed."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",7,0)="12 SEQ #7^3050426^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^1^1^3050426"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",7,1,1,0)="No warning for early, late or second ward stock IVPB"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,0)="15 SEQ #8^3050611^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,0)="^^18^18^3050611"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,3,0)=" 1.  Problem: HD000000088329"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,4,0)="     The Medication Order Button (MOB) within the Graphical User"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,5,0)="     Interface, Bar Code Medication Administration system (BCMA)"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,6,0)="     malfunctions after the Installation of patch PSB*3*9.  When the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,7,0)="     BCMA MOB is used to administer medications and create orders, "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,8,0)="     all data is stored and maintained properly.  The malfunction"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,9,0)="     occurs when the post PSB*3*9, BCMA system frees memory after"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,10,0)="     all administration and order processing has occurred and BCMA"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,11,0)="     begins to free memory per MOB activity.  Because a variable"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,12,0)="     needed by BCMA MOB exit activities has been cleared, BCMA generates"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,13,0)="     the ""<UNDEFINED>MOBR+25^PSBAPIPM"" before processing has completed."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,16,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,17,0)="     PSB*3*15 will allow BCMA MOB exiting processing to complete"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",8,1,18,0)="     without error."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",9,0)="18 SEQ #9^3050813^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",9,1,0)="^^1^1^3050813"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",9,1,1,0)="Error administering multiple doses."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,0)="11 SEQ #10^3051020^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^88^88^3051020"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,2,0)="1.   Problem: Remedy #HD0000000092269"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,3,0)="     Bar Code Medication Administration (BCMA) software errors at line "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,4,0)="     ""EN+78^PSBVDLPB"" when a BCMA Medication Log (file #53.79) record "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,5,0)="     being processed has its Action Status (field #.09) equal to """" .  "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,6,0)="     The errant record is the result of an administration not properly "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,7,0)="     saved/discarded via Manual Medication Entry[PSB MED LOG NEW ENTRY]         "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,9,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,10,0)="     BCMA will ignore all BCMA Medication Log (file #53.79)records with "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,11,0)="     Action Status field (field #.09) equal to """"; and when appropriate, "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,12,0)="     BCMA will send an electronic message (e-message) to members of the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,13,0)="     mail group that is specified via the BCMA Site Parameter - ""Mail "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,14,0)="     Groups/Due List Error"", when such a record is processed.  The "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,15,0)="     subject line of  this  e-message will read ""BCMA - Admin XXXX "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,16,0)="     Problem"". The subject line of this e-message will contain the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,17,0)="     internal entry number (IEN), identifying the errant BCMA Medication "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,18,0)="     Log (file #53.79) record.  That IEN is represented above by the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,19,0)="     text ""XXXX"".  PSB*3.0*11 will allow access to the errant records via "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,20,0)="     Manual Medication Entry [PSB MED LOG NEW ENTRY] option for deletion "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,21,0)="     or correction.  The errant records may be accessed using "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,22,0)="     Manual Medication Entry [PSB MED LOG NEW ENTRY] option"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,23,0)="     by users possessing the PSB Manager Key or the user who initiated "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,24,0)="     that administration. Details about the errant administration are "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,25,0)="     within the e-message sent.  The e-message will contain data "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,26,0)="     necessary to reprocess, via the Manual Medication Entry [PSB MED LOG "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,27,0)="     NEW ENTRY] option, that incomplete and errant administration."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,28,0)="     The following is an example e-message:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,29,0)="**************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,31,0)=" Subj: BCMA - Admin 11111 Problem  [#22222222] 07/13/05@13:37  12 lines"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,32,0)=" From: JACKSON,TODD ELLIS  In 'IN' basket.   Page 1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,33,0)=" -----------------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,34,0)="   The following administration was NOT displayed"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,35,0)="   on the Virtual Due List"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,37,0)="   Order Number....: 21V"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,38,0)="   Orderable Item..: HEPARIN SOLN"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,39,0)="   Patient.........: BCMAPATIENT,ONE (000-00-9678)"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,40,0)="   Ward/Bed........: 7A GEN MED 724-A"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,41,0)="   Reason..........: JUL 13, 2005@07:00 admin's ACTION STATUS is ""UNKNOWN""."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,42,0)="   Schedule........: Q3H"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,43,0)="   Action Dt/Tm....: JUL 13, 2005@11:32:50"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,44,0)="   BCMA Med Log IEN: 11111"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,45,0)="   User............: ( # 00000000000 ) BCMAUSER,ONE"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,47,0)="**************************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,48,0)="     Per the above example, to correct the example, errant entry #11111, "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,49,0)="     the specified ""User"" or a person holding the PSB Manager Key may use "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,50,0)="     the Manual Medication Entry [PSB MED LOG NEW ENTRY] option and "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,51,0)="     correct the ""Reason"" for the ""BCMA - Admin Problem""; that person can "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,52,0)="     correct that ""JUL 13, 2005@07:00 admin's ACTION STATUS"" per the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,53,0)="     specified patient and order, via corresponding responses to Manual "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,54,0)="     Medication Entry [PSB MED LOG NEW ENTRY] option prompts.  The "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,55,0)="     ""correction"" is to properly complete or delete that incomplete "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,56,0)="     administration."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,58,0)="     An e-message triggered by an incomplete administration of a Pro"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,59,0)="     Re Nata (PRN) [As Needed] medication must be maintained via VISTA "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,60,0)="     File Manager (FileMan).  The IEN of the entry that needs corrected "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,61,0)="     is labeled ""BCMA Med Log IEN:"" within the e-message as well as "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,62,0)="     displayed in the e-message's subject line, immediately after the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,63,0)="     text ""BCMA - Admin""."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,65,0)="     It is possible to correct any errant BCMA Medication Log (file "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,66,0)="     #53.79) entry using FileMan and the IEN supplied by this e-message."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,69,0)="2.   Problem: Remedy #HD0000000093022"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,70,0)="     The Manual Medication Entry [PSB MED LOG NEW ENTRY] option does not "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,71,0)="     maintain the ""Given"" status per medication patch administrations on "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,72,0)="     the BCMA Virtual Due List (VDL).  The user is unable to determine "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,73,0)="     which administered patch must be removed when the VDL does not "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,74,0)="     display the patch as ""Given"".  "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,75,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,76,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,77,0)="     A patch administered via the Manual Medication Entry [PSB MED LOG "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,78,0)="     NEW ENTRY] option will show as ""Given"" on the BCMA VDL."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,81,0)="3.   Problem: Remedy #HD0000000103739"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,82,0)="     The Manual Medication Entry [PSB MED LOG NEW ENTRY] option "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,83,0)="     malfunctions when attempting to administer an ""odd schedule"" order "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,84,0)="     on days the order is not scheduled to be administered."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,86,0)="     Corrective Action:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,87,0)="     Display appropriate data when ""odd schedule"" order administrations "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",10,1,88,0)="     are attempted."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",11,0)="22 SEQ #11^3051202^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^1^1^3051202"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="Error when filing multiple doses with comments"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",12,0)="19 SEQ #12^3051202^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^1^1^3051202"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="Unable to mark a patch as removed"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",13,0)="21 SEQ #13^3051202^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",13,1,0)="^^1^1^3051202"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",13,1,1,0)="Patient information does not print on Order Details report"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,0)="16 SEQ #14^3051221^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,0)="^^14^14^3051221"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,1,0)="***"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,5,0)="This patch is a component of the Bar Code Medication Administration "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,6,0)="(BCMA) - Health Services Commitee (HSC) project and is the development of "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,7,0)="phase one of the  BCMA-HSC Coversheet. PSB*3.0*16 will interface between "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,8,0)="BCMA databases and the new BCMA Coversheet and its Graphical User "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,9,0)="Interface (GUI)."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",14,1,14,0)="***"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",15,0)="20 SEQ #15^3051221^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",15,1,0)="^^4^4^3051221"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",15,1,1,0)="Correction for two  Issues:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",15,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",15,1,3,0)="REMEDY 91869"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",15,1,4,0)="REMEDY 99958"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,0)="8^3060410^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^343^343^3060410"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,3,0)="********************Important Note***************"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,5,0)="  If the site is running the BCMA Contingency software then this"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,6,0)="  patch must also be installed on the workstations. Once installed"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,7,0)="  it is suggested that the sites review the Contingency system"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,8,0)="  reports."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,10,0)="*************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,13,0)="Enhancements and issues addressed in this patch are as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,16,0)="1. It was reported by a site that Lodgers and Dom patients were"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,17,0)="   creating alerts. Lodgers and Dom patient are now screened."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,19,0)="2. It was reported that when a patient was discharged the discharged "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,20,0)="   message was not always being sent to the workstations and an alert"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,21,0)="   was being generated. The problem was caused by how movements were"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,22,0)="   sent to the Contingency by Patient Movements. The Contingency will"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,23,0)="   compensates for these issues now."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,25,0)="3. When printing the Medication Administration Report (MAR) for current"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,26,0)="   orders it would also include any non-active orders for the current"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,27,0)="   day being printed. The report now goes by date and time."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,29,0)="4. A new purge utility has been introduced for the workstation. It"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,30,0)="   allows the site to define how much historical data to maintain on the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,31,0)="   workstation. Any unwanted data will be removed from the workstation."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,33,0)="5. The way the Med Log information is being displayed on the MAR has"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,34,0)="   changed. In the previous version the information was displayed by date"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,35,0)="   entered and the user had to select a starting date when running the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,36,0)="   MAR. Depending on the frequency of the MED Log this could cause the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,37,0)="   report to be long. The report now reverses the order of the Med Log"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,38,0)="   information so the report displays the most recent first. The user can"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,39,0)="   then opt for how many to display by numeric value such as 1, 2 or more."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,41,0)="6. A blank page was added between the patients on multi patient"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,42,0)="   reports for easier sorting."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,44,0)="7. Provider comments were moved to be displayed along with the Drug"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,45,0)="   and Give information."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,47,0)="8. The sorting of orders on the MAR reports have been grouped by the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,48,0)="   order type. Types include Pending, Unit Dose, IV and PRN."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,50,0)="9. A place holder for the Last Action of drugs has been added to the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,51,0)="   reports. A future patch will complete the functionality."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,53,0)="10. A problem with Pending orders remaining on the workstation when"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,54,0)="    replacement orders are done by pharmacy has been resolved."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,56,0)="11. A problem was discovered with the user access updater. When a user's"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,57,0)="    name changed it did not update the Contingency workstations"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,58,0)="    correctly."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,60,0)="12. A <UNDEFINED>NURV+16^ALPBCBU error has been resolved."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,62,0)="13. A problem with updating the Contingency workstations during a patient"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,63,0)="    movement activity has been addressed."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,64,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,65,0)="14. Added the function to sort MARS by Room/Bed or by Patient Name."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,67,0)="15. Patients that had no allergies reported to the contingency do not"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,68,0)="    display any allergies data on a MAR. Now when no allergies are found"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,69,0)="    on the contingency, the following will display on the MAR. ""Allergies:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,70,0)="    No allergies reported to the Contingency"""
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,72,0)="16. Possibility of routine ALPBPWRD erroring out at line"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,73,0)="    ..S ^TMP($J,""BCBU"",+ALPRM,ALPRM,ALPBD,ALPBPTN)=ALPBIEN"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,74,0)="    When sorting by room/bed Cache tries to convert certain room/beds like"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,75,0)="    5E155 and produces a <MAXNUM> error. The problem occurs when the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,76,0)="    variable is manipulated. Cache will take the 5E155 and convert it to"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,77,0)="    ""5"" appended with 155 zeros. A code change was made to prevent this"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,78,0)="    issue."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,80,0)="   Associated Tickets"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,81,0)="   ================="
