^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,149,0)="Patch retrieval Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,150,0)="===================================="
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,151,0)="To obtain the software use one the following OI Field Offices'"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,152,0)="ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE directories:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,154,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,155,0)="       Albany ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,156,0)="       Hines ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,157,0)="       Salt Lake City ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext anonymous.software"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,158,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,159,0)="The distribution file is as follows."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,160,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,161,0)="PSB_3_8.KID"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,162,0)="PSB_3_8.ZIP   (optional see note below)"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,163,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,164,0)="****************Note for optional zip file********************"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,165,0)="The Zip file in this patch contains an updated Cache.Dat file."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,166,0)="On new installations it is recommended that you use the new"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,167,0)="Cache.dat file released with this patch. If this is used for"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,168,0)="an existing workstation then the workstation would need to"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,169,0)="be initialized with patient data."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,170,0)="**************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,172,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,173,0)=" The documentation distribution includes:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,174,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,175,0)=" FILE NAME                                   DESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,177,0)="PSB_3_BCBU_IG_R0206.PDF                  BCMA Backup System (BCBU)"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,178,0)="                                            INSTALLATION GUIDE"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,179,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,180,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,181,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,182,0)="   Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,183,0)="   =========================="
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,184,0)="   This patch can be installed with users on the system. Installation will"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,185,0)="   take less than 1 minute."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,187,0)="   Suggested time to install: non-peak requirement hours."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,188,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,189,0)="   1. From the Kernel Installation & Distribution System menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,190,0)="      the LOAD DISTRIBUTION option and load PSB_3_8.KID"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,191,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,192,0)="   2. Review your mapped set. If the routines are mapped, they should"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,193,0)="      be removed from the mapped set at this time."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,194,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,195,0)="   3. From the Kernel Installation & Distribution System menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,196,0)="      the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,197,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,198,0)="   4. From this menu, you may select to use the following options"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,199,0)="      (when prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter PSB*3.0*8):"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,200,0)="     a. Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,201,0)="        message of any routines exported with the patch. It will NOT"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,202,0)="        backup any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,203,0)="     b. Compare Transport Global to Current System - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,204,0)="        allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,205,0)="        is installed. It compares all components of the patch (routines,"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,206,0)="        DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,207,0)="     c. Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will ensure"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,208,0)="        the integrity of the routines that are in the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,209,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,210,0)="   5. Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package PSB*3.0*8."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,211,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,212,0)="   6. When prompted ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,213,0)="      YES//"" respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,214,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,215,0)="   7. When prompted ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,216,0)="      Protocols? YES//"" respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,217,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,218,0)="   8. If any routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should be"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,219,0)="      returned to the mapped set once the installation has run to"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,220,0)="      completion."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,221,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,222,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,223,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,224,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,225,0)="Post-Installation Steps (Important)"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,226,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,227,0)="A new option, PSB BCBU WRKSTN PURGE ORDERS, was released as part of"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,228,0)="PSB*3.0*8 build. IRM staff must add it to the list of Scheduled Startup"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,229,0)="Options in TaskMan on the workstations. To do this, access menu"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,230,0)="Schedule/Unschedule Options on the TaskMan Management menu. This option"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,231,0)="should be queued to run during non peak hours and set with a rescheduling"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,232,0)="frequency of 1D.  Review the Workstation parameter settings using the PSB"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,233,0)="BCBU WRKSTN PARAMETER EDIT option to make changes on how much patient"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",16,1,234,0)="historical data is retained"
