^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,0)="23 SEQ #17^3060525^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,0)="^^32^32^3060525"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,1,0)="This patch addresses three Remedy tickets, HD68121, HD113034, and HD90393."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,4,0)="The first issue, HD68121, is the result of a file locking problem with "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,5,0)="the routine PSBMD.  This error only appeared after the site converted to "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,6,0)="Cache' version 5.  There is an undefined variable error created with "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,7,0)="Missing Dose reports in Pharmacy, even though a record is created in "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,8,0)="^PSB(53.68).  By attempting to lock the ^PSB(53.68) file before "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,9,0)="attempting to print the report, it will ensure that the file exists so "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,10,0)="the undefined error will not occur.  This locking fix was created by the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,11,0)="Minneapolis IRM staff, and has been working in their production area for "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,12,0)="months.  The fix is being brought back to the VMP group so it can become "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,13,0)="part of a national patch release, and other sites can avoid this error in "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,14,0)="the future."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,16,0)="The second issue, HD113034, happens when a medication PATCH (such as "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,17,0)="Fentanyl) is marked as REMOVED after initially being given to the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,18,0)="patient.  If you right-click the mouse on the order in BCMA and mark the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,19,0)="patch as ""REMOVED"", when you subsequently check the med log, the units "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,20,0)="given remains 1.  However, if you use the BCMA menu option FILE/EDIT Med "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,21,0)="Log and mark it ""REMOVED"", the units given becomes 0, and the audit trail "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,22,0)="shows ""Doses given '1' deleted"".  The correct value for units given is "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,23,0)="actually 1 (as right-clicking the mouse shows), because the medication "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,24,0)="was indeed given, but the patch was subsequently removed, not deleted or "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,25,0)="refused."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,27,0)="The third issue in this patch, HD90393, addresses a printing problem with "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,28,0)="the PRN Effectiveness report when it is printed by Ward/Room-Bed.  When "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,29,0)="this printing filter is applied, the report prints in patient DFN order, "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,30,0)="not Ward/Room-Bed order.  This fix corrects a problem in the BCMA code so "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,31,0)="that when the Ward/Room-bed filter is applied, the report will print "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",17,1,32,0)="properly."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",18,0)="24 SEQ #18^3060525^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^1^1^3060525"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="Store error generated when using Display Order option in BCMA"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,0)="27 SEQ #19^3060526^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,0)="^^18^18^3060526"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,1,0)="This patch addresses Remedy Ticket HD127231, which arose after the "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,2,0)="install of patch PSB*3*20.  Patch PSB*3*20 added the patient header "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,3,0)="information to the MAH report if the report for a medication ran longer"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,4,0)="than one page.  Additionally, PSB*3*20 was designed to reprint the first "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,5,0)="six lines of the orderable item information on subsequent pages to help "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,6,0)="the nurses keep track of what medication they were viewing"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,7,0)="on the MAH report.  However, when the next medication on the report was "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,8,0)="due to be printed, and a page break occurred before the orderable item "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,9,0)="information was printed, the second page of the report printed"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,10,0)="the first six lines of the orderable item in duplicate."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,12,0)="The fix included in this patch will still print the patient header "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,13,0)="information on subsequent MAH pages, but it will not reprint the first "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,14,0)="six lines of the orderable item information."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,16,0)="**NOTE** This fix only affects the report when printed to a printer."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,17,0)="This does not affect the GUI display or printing the report to the"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",19,1,18,0)="terminal screen."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,0)="29^3060807^1"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,0)="^^214^214^3060807"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,1,0)="***************************Important Note*************************"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,2,0)="  If the site is running the BCMA Contingency software then this"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,3,0)="  patch must also be installed on the workstations. Once installed"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,4,0)="  it is suggested that the sites review the Contingency system "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,5,0)="  reports. "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,6,0)="******************************************************************"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,8,0)="Issues addressed in this patch are as follows: "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,10,0)="1. It was reported that after loading Patch PSB*3*8, the medication log "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,11,0)="   history was no longer printing. "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,13,0)="       Example:..."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,15,0)="            BCMA MEDICATION LOG HISTORY"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,16,0)="            Log Date        Message        Log Entry Person"
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,17,0)="            No entries since the above date are on file."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,19,0)="   This was caused by a missing cross reference (IMLOG) in file 53.7. "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,20,0)="   Cross reference has been added."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,22,0)="2. It was reported that the Print all option was not working correctly. "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,23,0)="   Routine ALPBPALL has been corrected."
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,177,22,3,"PAH",20,1,25,0)=" "
