^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,100,0)=" REQUIRED BUILDS:"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,101,0)=" ================"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,102,0)="  CLINICAL REMINDERS 1.5"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,103,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,104,0)=" INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS:"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,105,0)=" =========================="
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,106,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,107,0)=" This patch should be loaded during non-peak hours to minimize disruption"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,108,0)=" to users.  Installation will take less than 15 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,109,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,110,0)="                           **Warning** "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,111,0)=" When an option is included in the patch build, the question REBUILD MENUS"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,112,0)=" is asked as a PRE-INSTALL question.  If you choose to have KIDs rebuild"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,113,0)=" the menus it will happen at the end of the build installation and may"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,114,0)=" take several hours."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,115,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,116,0)="  1.  Download the KIDS file HEP_C_EXTRACT_1_0.KID via FTP from any"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,117,0)="      of the anonymous.software directories listed above.  Move the file"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,118,0)="      to the appropriate directory on your system."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,119,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,120,0)="  2.  Review your mapped set.  If any of the routines listed in the"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,121,0)="      Routines section are mapped, they should be removed from the mapped"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,122,0)="      set at this time. "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,123,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,124,0)="  3.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System (KIDS) menu,"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,125,0)="      select the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,127,0)="  4.  Use Load a Distribution option on the KIDS Installation menu, and"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,128,0)="      enter: HEP_C_EXTRACT_1_0.KID"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,129,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,130,0)="  5.  From this menu, you may elect to use the following options"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,131,0)="      (when prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter HEPATITIS_C_EXTRACT)."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,132,0)="    "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,133,0)="      Note - Option (a.), Backup a Transport Global, can and must be"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,134,0)="      referenced exclusively by the primary build name of"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,135,0)="      HEPATITIS_C_EXTRACT. Option (b.) can be run by either using the"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,136,0)="      primary build name of HEPATITIS_C_EXTRACT or the individual patch"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,137,0)="      names (e.g., PXRM*1.5*1, etc.). Options (c.) and (d.) must be run"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,138,0)="      for each individual build (using the patch names) included in"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,139,0)="      this transport."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,140,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,141,0)="      a.  Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,142,0)="          message of any routines exported with the patch.  It will NOT"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,143,0)="          backup any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,144,0)="      b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System  - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,145,0)="          allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,146,0)="          is installed.  It compares all components of the patch"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,147,0)="          (routines, DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,148,0)="      c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,149,0)="          allow you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,150,0)="          the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,151,0)="      d.  Print Transport Global - this option will allow you to view the"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,152,0)="          components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,153,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,154,0)="  6.  Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,155,0)="      HEPATITIS_C_EXTRACT."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,156,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,157,0)="  7.  When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,158,0)="      Protocols? YES//', respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,159,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,160,0)="  8.  If routines were unmapped as part of step 2, they should be returned"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,161,0)="      to the mapped set once the installation has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,162,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,163,0)=" POST INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,164,0)=" ============================== "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,165,0)=" The details of the setup to be completed is available in the"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,166,0)=" documentation. Generally, these steps need to be done by the REMINDERS"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,167,0)=" MANAGER or the CLINICAL REMINDERS APPLICATION COORDINATOR. The success of"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,168,0)=" the Hepatitis C updates to the EPI database will depend on a Hepatitis"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,169,0)=" Team at your site addressing all of the issues in the documentation."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,170,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,171,0)="  1. See the descriptions for the reminder definitions and "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,172,0)="     the descriptions in the REMINDER TERMS file to determine what"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,173,0)="     additional setup is required for the terms. You will need to review"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,174,0)="     the reminder terms with laboratory and pharmacy coordinators."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,175,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,176,0)="  2. You can use the Detailed Reminders Due report to determine if all"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,177,0)="     the correct patients are being identified to send to the EPI"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,178,0)="     database."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,179,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,180,0)="  3. You may need to check that all dispensed drugs are mapped to the"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,181,0)="     national drug file entries represented by the Hepatitis C Medication"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,182,0)="     terms. If you have local dispensed drugs that cannot be mapped to the"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,183,0)="     national drug file (VA GENERIC, #50.6), you will need to enter the"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,184,0)="     dispensed drugs as findings for the appropriate national reminder"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,185,0)="     term."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,186,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,187,0)="  4. Add local laboratory tests with appropriate CONDITIONS in the"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,188,0)="     REMINDER TERM file for the laboratory terms."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,189,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,190,0)="  5. The VA-NATIONAL EPI LAB EXTRACT and VA-NATIONAL EPI RX EXTRACT"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,191,0)="     reminders should NOT be added to the ""Clinical Reminders for Search"""
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,192,0)="     parameter for clinicians.  The Reminders Manager may want to create a"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,193,0)="     National EPI Update reminder category and add these reminders to it,"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,194,0)="     along with the VA-HEP C RISK ASSESSMENT REMINDER. The category could"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,195,0)="     be added to the CPRS Reminder Categories parameter option for testing"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,196,0)="     the setup of the reminder terms and reviewing the results."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,197,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,198,0)="DETAILED DESCRIPTION:"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,199,0)="====================="
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,200,0)="Data Dictionary:"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,201,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,202,0)="  1. REMINDER DEFINITION file (811.9)"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,203,0)="     The reminder for VA-NATIONAL EPI DB UPDATE may be used at sites to"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,204,0)="     determine whether a patient has data that is sent to the Austin"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,205,0)="     Automation Center to update the national EPI database."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,206,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,207,0)="  2. REMINDER TERM file (811.5)"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,208,0)="     There are twenty reminder terms used by the lab and pharmacy extract"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,209,0)="     reminders. Eighteen of these terms are newly distributed in this"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,210,0)="     file. These new terms represent Hepatitis A, Hepatitis B and"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,211,0)="     Hepatitis C lab and medication information. The reminder terms may be"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,212,0)="     used at sites in locally defined reminders for clinicians providing"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,213,0)="     clinical care for Hepatitis patients."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,214,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,215,0)="     Hepatitis A laboratory reminder terms:"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,216,0)="         HAV Ab positive         Hepatitis A virus antibody total positive"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,217,0)="         HAV IgM Ab positive     Hepatitis A virus antibody immunoglobulin"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,218,0)="                                         M positive "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,219,0)="         HAV IgG positive        Hepatitis A virus antibody immunoglobulin"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,220,0)="                                         G positive"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,221,0)="         Bilirubin"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,222,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,223,0)="     Hepatitis B laboratory reminder terms:"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,224,0)="         HBs Ag positive         Hepatitis B surface antigen positive "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,225,0)="         HBc Ab IgM positive     Hepatitis B core antibody immunoglobulin"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,226,0)="                                         M positive "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,227,0)="         HBs Ab positive         Hepatitis B surface antibody positive"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,228,0)="         HBe Ag positive         Hepatitis B e antigen positive "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,229,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,230,0)="     Hepatitis C laboratory reminder terms: "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,231,0)="         HEP C VIRUS ANTIBODY NEGATIVE    "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,232,0)="         HEP C VIRUS ANTIBODY POSITIVE    "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,233,0)="         TRANSFERASE (AST) (SGOT)"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,234,0)="         ALANINE AMINO (ALT) (SGPT)"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,235,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,236,0)="     Hepatitis Medications (based on VA GENERIC file): "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,237,0)="         INTERFERON ALFA-2A "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,238,0)="         INTERFERON ALFA-2B     "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,239,0)="         INTERFERON ALFA-2B/RIBAVIRIN "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,240,0)="         INTERFERON ALFA-3N     "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,241,0)="         INTERFERON ALFACON-1 "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,242,0)="         INTERFERON BETA-1A "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,243,0)="         INTERFERON BETA-1B "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,244,0)="         RIBAVIRIN           "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,245,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,246,0)="Sort Template:"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,247,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,248,0)="   PXRM EPI LAB AND MED TERMS contains reminder term entries defined above"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,249,0)="   to distribute with the REMINDER TERM (811.5) data dictionary."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,250,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,251,0)="   PXRM EXTRACT EPI BY FIND_PT sorts an extract by Finding Item and SSN."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,252,0)="   This sort template may be useful when looking up an SSN to compare"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,253,0)="   findings to an error message returned to the site from the AAC.  When"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,254,0)="   the AAC has problems processing a sites extracted data, the original"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,255,0)="   extract message and SSN are returned to the site in an error message"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",1,1,256,0)="   for review and correction."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",2,0)="3 SEQ #2^3010103^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",3,0)="2^3010423^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^3^3^3010423"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="Clinical Reminders version 1.5 patch 2. This patch includes a number of"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",3,1,2,0)="bug fixes and enhancements. Please see the National Patch module for a"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",3,1,3,0)="complete description."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",4,0)="4 SEQ #4^3010625^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^1^1^3010625"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="Reminder Dialogs for TIU."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",5,0)="5^3010802^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",5,1,0)="^^2^2^3010802"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",5,1,1,0)="This patch update the Exchange Utility so it is compatible with version"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",5,1,2,0)="1.5 of Clinical Reminders."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",6,0)="6 SEQ #6^3020204^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",6,1,0)="^^1^1^3020204"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",6,1,1,0)="This patch includes fixes and minor changes to the Reminders Due report."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",7,0)="7^3020204^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^3^3^3020204"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",7,1,1,0)="This patch provides tools for Clinical Reminders to support MST"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",7,1,2,0)="functionality. See the National Patch Module for a complete"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",7,1,3,0)="description."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",8,0)="9^3020226^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",8,1,0)="^^2^2^3020226"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",8,1,1,0)="This patch distributes the VA-MST SCREENING reminder that was missing"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",8,1,2,0)="from patch PXRM*1.5*7."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",9,0)="8^3020528^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",9,1,0)="^^6^6^3020528"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",9,1,1,0)="This patch contains national reminders for the IHD QUERI project:"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",9,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",9,1,3,0)="VA-IHD ELEVATED LDL"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",9,1,4,0)="VA-IHD LIPID PROFILE"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",9,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",9,1,6,0)="See national patch module for details."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",10,0)="10 SEQ #10^3020528^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^2^2^3020528"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",10,1,1,0)="This patch makes changes to MST synchronization and dialog so that"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",10,1,2,0)="dates passed to the MST API will not be rejected by the API."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",11,0)="11 SEQ #11^3020906^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^1^1^3020906"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="NOIS fixes, see the National Patch Module for a complete description."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",12,0)="13^3030123^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^1^1^3030123"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="NOIS fixes, see the National Patch Module for a complete description."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",13,0)="14 SEQ #13^3030204^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",13,1,0)="^^1^1^3030204"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",13,1,1,0)="NOIS fixes, see the National Patch Module for a complete description."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",14,0)="17 SEQ #15^3030301^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",15,0)="15^3030430^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",15,1,0)="^9.49011^2^2^3030430"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",15,1,1,0)="The description of this patch is found in the National Patch Module under "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",15,1,2,0)="the name PXRM*1.5*15. It contains 3 National Mental Health Reminders."
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",16,0)="19 SEQ #17^3030815^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^1^1^3030815"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",16,1,1,0)="SEE NATIONAL PATCH MODULE"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",17,0)="18 SEQ #18^3030924^1"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",17,1,0)="^^2^2^3030924"
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",17,1,1,0)="The description of this patch is found in the National Patch Module under "
^DIC(9.4,180,22,1,"PAH",17,1,2,0)="the name PXRM*1.5*18. Clinical Reminders - Code Set Versioning"
