^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",9,1,0)="^^11^11^3020423"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",9,1,1,0)="This patch is in response to Item #22 in the Rossio Report.  In the area"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",9,1,2,0)="of Means Test (MT) Deficiencies, Item #22 required that the Veterans"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",9,1,3,0)="Health Administration (VHA) identify best practices for means testing and"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",9,1,4,0)="acquiring veterans' signatures at the local level and explore the"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",9,1,5,0)="promulgation of these best practices throughout the system.  In response"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",9,1,6,0)="to the Report, the Enrollment Task Force requested implementation on a"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",9,1,7,0)="national basis of local sites' initiative s developed to manage scheduling"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",9,1,8,0)="activities for veterans who require the completion of a means test.  This"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",9,1,9,0)="patch will provide a national patch release to the Enrollment Application"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",9,1,10,0)="Systems (EAS) software of locally implemented software that has been"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",9,1,11,0)="converted from Class III to Class I."
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",10,0)="12 SEQ #9^3020516^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^5^5^3020516"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",10,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the appointment blocking for domiciliary patients."
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",10,1,2,0)="The blocking API is modified to treat DOM patients as inpatients.  This"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",10,1,3,0)="patch also corrects a problem in the Automated MT Report and makes a "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",10,1,4,0)="modification for DCD sites when the letters are initially set up in the"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",10,1,5,0)="letter status file.'"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",11,0)="7^3020626^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",12,0)="14 SEQ #11^3020710^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^7^7^3020710"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="This patch addresses a fix for flagging 0-day letters and correcting the "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",12,1,2,0)="newing of the ""VAROOT"" variable to correct an interaction with older DG "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",12,1,3,0)="routines."
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",12,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",12,1,5,0)="This patch addresses the following NOIS's"""
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",12,1,6,0)="SLC-0502-51019"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",12,1,7,0)="BAC-0502-41276"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",13,0)="16^3020724^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",14,0)="18 SEQ #13^3020814^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",15,0)="19^3020927^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",16,0)="20 SEQ #15^3021025^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^1^1^3021025"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",16,1,1,0)="See national patch module for detailed description."
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",17,0)="15 SEQ #16^3021025^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",17,1,0)="^^3^3^3021025"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",17,1,1,0)="This patch distributes several enhancements to the EAS MT means test "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",17,1,2,0)="letters and appointment blocking application as required by the Rossio 22 "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",17,1,3,0)="report and the subsequent VA Directive."
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",18,0)="10 SEQ #17^3021116^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^1^1^3021116"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="See national patch module for detailed description."
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",19,0)="17^3021116^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",19,1,0)="^^2^2^3021116"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",19,1,1,0)="This build provides an API which provides the correct enrollment date"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",19,1,2,0)="as documented in DBIA#3624"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",20,0)="13^3021220^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",21,0)="24 SEQ #20^3030123^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,0)="23 SEQ #21^3030329^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,1,0)="^^12^12^3030329"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,1,1,0)="The software for this patch, EAS*1*23 and associated patch, IVM*2*69, are "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,1,2,0)="not being distributed through the National Patch Module.  These patches "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,1,3,0)="are being distributed as a single KIDS software distribution (host "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,1,4,0)="file).  This patch contains the informational portion of EAS*1*23 and "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,1,5,0)="provides field personnel with instructions on how to acquire, install and "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,1,6,0)="implement the patch software."
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,1,8,0)="The Health Eligibility Center (HEC) has reinstated the Income "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,1,9,0)="Verification Matching program, which matches a veteran's self-reported "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,1,10,0)="income (that is below the Means Test Threshold) with information obtained "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,1,11,0)="from the Internal Revenue Service (IRS) and Social Security "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",22,1,12,0)="Administration (SSA).  "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",23,0)="30^3030417^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",23,1,0)="^^2^2^3030417"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",23,1,1,0)="ADDITIONAL ENHANCEMENTS REQUIRED TO HANDLE SENDING AND RECEIVING OF OTHER"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",23,1,2,0)="HL7 MESSAGES BASED UPON RECEIPT OF A Z06 MESSAGE."
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",24,0)="33^3030430^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",24,1,0)="^^2^2^3030430"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",24,1,1,0)="EMERGENCY FIX FOR Z09 MESSAGES.  DETERMINE WHICH Z09 MESSAGES GO TO HEC"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",24,1,2,0)="LEGACY AND WHICH ONES GO TO EDB."
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",25,0)="29^3030520^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",26,0)="32^3030603^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",27,0)="35 SEQ #26^3030628^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",27,1,0)="^^2^2^3030628"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",27,1,1,0)="CORRECTLY DISPLAY THE NEW MT STATUS ON BULLETINS SENT TO THE SITE AFTER A"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",27,1,2,0)="MT EDB Z06 HAS BEEN RECEIVED."
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",28,0)="25^3030628^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",29,0)="22 SEQ #28^3030715^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",30,0)="37 SEQ #29^3030715^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",31,0)="34^3030802^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",31,1,0)="^^1^1^3030802"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",31,1,1,0)="LTC Copayments Phase III"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",32,0)="28 SEQ #31^3030815^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",33,0)="26 SEQ #32^3030912^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,0)="39 SEQ #33^3031002^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,0)="^^16^16^3031002"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,1,0)="The View Patient Address [EAS VIEW PATIENT ADDRESS] menu option will "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,2,0)="allow a user to display the Patient's address along with Address Change "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,3,0)="Date, Address Change Source, and Address Change Site  (if applicable) "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,4,0)="information.  This option calls the EASAILK1 routine, which does a lookup "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,5,0)="on the patient file, then, calls the standard device API (%ZIS) to open "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,6,0)="the selected output device to output the information to.  This error is "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,7,0)="occurring because immediately after calling the device API (%ZIS), the "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,8,0)="routine invokes the USE command to open the device to begin sending "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,9,0)="output to it.  "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,11,0)="In the situation where the user queues the output either by entering a "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,12,0)="""Q"" at the device prompt, or the selected device has the QUEUEING Field "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,13,0)="(#5.5) set to ""FORCED"" in the DEVICE File (#3.5), when the USE command is "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,14,0)="invoked, the DEVICE has not yet been opened by the process because it's "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,15,0)="been queued for a later time.  The error results due to the device not "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",34,1,16,0)="yet being available.     "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",35,0)="36^3031107^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",36,0)="40 SEQ #35^3031121^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",36,1,0)="^^1^1^3031121"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",36,1,1,0)="Long Term Care Copayments Phase IV"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",37,0)="43 SEQ #36^3031231^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",38,0)="48 SEQ #37^3031231^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",39,0)="47^3040131^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",39,1,0)="^^1^1^3040131"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",39,1,1,0)="Fix Z09 issue pertaining to Income Year for multiple years."
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,0)="44 SEQ #39^3040302^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,0)="^^25^25^3040302"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,1,0)="SDC-1003-60902"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,2,0)="ATG-0803-32133"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,4,0)="Under certain conditions, when a user creates a new link a between a new "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,5,0)="web based 1010EZ application in the 1010EZ HOLDING File (#712) and the "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,6,0)="PATIENT File (#2) using the menu protocol Link to Patient File [EAS EZ "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,7,0)="LINK TO FILE 2] of the Electronic 10-10EZ Processing [EAS EZ 1010EZ "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,8,0)="PROCESSING] List Manager application, the incorrect patient is selected "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,9,0)="and displayed.  This is caused by the FileMan DIE call which is used to "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,10,0)="update the LINK TO FILE #2 field (#3.4) in the 1010EZ HOLDING File "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,11,0)="(#712).  Since this field is a pointer to the PATIENT File, when it's "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,12,0)="updated, FileMan calls the patient lookup, DPTLK, to validate the patient "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,13,0)="DFN being passed in.  The patient lookup checks a series of "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,14,0)="cross-references on the patient file, one of which is the ""SSN"" "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,15,0)="cross-reference.  When the DFN being checked matches the initial portion "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,16,0)="of a SSN uniquely, the IEN of this matching SSN is returned and stored as "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,17,0)="the pointer to the PATIENT File instead of the correct IEN."
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,20,0)="DAY-0500-42574"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,22,0)="The site reported a problem when trying to print the DGRPT 10-10T "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,23,0)="REGISTRATION to a slave device.  They get an Invalid Output Device error "
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,24,0)="and no forms print out. This error is caused by the %ZIS variable being"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",40,1,25,0)="set to Forced Queuing when calling the device entry."
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",41,0)="50 SEQ #41^3040802^1"
^DIC(9.4,181,22,1,"PAH",42,0)="53 SEQ #42^3040802^1"
