^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,20,0)="VISTALINK allows the following request formats:"
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,21,0)="   1) XML and conform to a XML Schema "
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,22,0)="   2) a proprietary format (package must supply a proprietary parser)"
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,23,0)="   3) both 1 and 2"
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,25,0)="VISTALINK also supplies a Java/J2EE component that allows developers of"
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,26,0)="Java applications to make synchronous requests on the M server and for M"
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,27,0)="applications to make synchronous requests of Java/J2EE application"
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,28,0)="servers. The Java/J2EE side implements the J2EE Connector Architecture"
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,29,0)="v1.0 framework (J2CA)."
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,31,0)="** NOTE: VISTALINK v1.5 only supports Java to M communication."
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,33,0)="Finally, VISTALINK contains a number of library calls available to "
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,34,0)="other packages for developing a request handler if needed. (Currently, "
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,35,0)="only VISTALINK SECURITY is allowed to use these calls.)"
^DIC(9.4,192,22,2,1,36,0)=" "
