^DIC(9.4,197,22,"B","1.0",1)=""
^DIC(9.4,197,"DEV")="PETIT,DAN/HISC"
^DIC(9.4,197,"VERSION")="1.0"
^DIC(9.4,198,0)="E CLAIMS MGMT ENGINE^BPS^ELECTRONIC CLAIMS MGT"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,0)="^9.49I^1^1"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,0)="1.0^3051119^3041029^1"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,0)="^^416^416^3051119"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,1,0)="Description:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,2,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,4,0)="PATCH OVERVIEW"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,6,0)="The Healthcare Insurance Portability and Accountability Act National "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,7,0)="Council for Prescription Drug Programs (HIPAA NCPDP) initiative, whose "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,8,0)="ultimate goal is to provide functionality allowing electronic transmission"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,9,0)="of Outpatient Pharmacy (OP) prescription claims to payers and the receipt "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,10,0)="of claim responses (including drug utilization review responses and "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,11,0)="warnings) on a real-time basis, is being developed and introduced in a "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,12,0)="phased implementation strategy. This deployment strategy was utilized due "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,13,0)="to the complexity of the functionality and the number of product line "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,14,0)="dependencies."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,16,0)="The first release of this two part implementation is BPS*1*0, comprised of"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,17,0)="the new Electronic Claims Management Engine (ECME) package (in the BPS "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,18,0)="namespace), plus the patches PSS*1*81, IB*2.0*223, IB*2.0*251, and "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,19,0)="PRCA*4.5*202, which are listed here in order of installation. BPS*1*0 is a"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,20,0)="dormant release that only allows each site to perform preliminary setup "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,21,0)="work and to confirm that the software does not adversely affect other "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,22,0)="packages."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,24,0)="There are two main areas addressed by BPS*1*0:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,26,0)="a. Registration of the Pharmacy with the Vitria BusinessWare IE."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,27,0)="b. The Insurance Matching of Group Plans with Pharmacy Plans"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,29,0)="Following the installation of BPS*1*0, each site must register their "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,30,0)="pharmacy with Vitria and match applicable insurance group plans using the "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,31,0)="insurance matching screens. These processes are detailed in the HIPAA "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,32,0)="NCPDP CONNECTION FOR EDI PHARMACY INSTALLATION GUIDE and the E-PHARMACY "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,33,0)="CLAIMS INSURANCE PROCESS document. Both of these documents are located on"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,34,0)="the anonymous directory. It is very important that the IRM or person"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,35,0)="installing the patch at each facility provide a copy of these documents to"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,36,0)="its ADPAC(s) and any other relevant staff who will be responsible for"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,37,0)="registering their pharmacy with Vitria and completing the insurance "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,38,0)="matching process."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,40,0)="At a later date, additional HIPAA NCPDP patches will be released to "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,41,0)="activate all of the HIPAA NCPDP functionality. Until that time, sites will"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,42,0)="not be able to electronically submit claims utilizing this new "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,43,0)="functionality."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,45,0)="The HIPAA NCPDP project was created in response to a Chief Business Office"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,46,0)="(CBO) request for modifications to several Veterans Health Information "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,47,0)="Systems and Technology Architecture (VistA) software applications in "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,48,0)="accordance with HIPAA Electronic Data Interchange (EDI) transactions and "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,49,0)="NCPDP mandated format standards, specifically the NCPDP Telecommunication "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,50,0)="Standard v.5.1."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,52,0)="The specific functionality for this patch is listed below."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,53,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,54,0)="(1)  A user interface has been developed to facilitate entry and filing"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,55,0)="     Registration and Point of Contact information for each specific"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,56,0)="     Application (Site) and Pharmacies at a site."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,58,0)="(2)  An HL7 interface is included that will create and send HL7 messages"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,59,0)="     containing the Application and Pharmacy Registration data to Vitria."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,60,0)="     This data notifies Vitria that the site will soon be sending "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,61,0)="     electronic third party pharmacy claims. "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,63,0)="(3)  An additional HL7 interface is included which receives messages from"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,64,0)="     Vitria containing the most up to date Payer Sheet data, and files the"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,65,0)="     data into the appropriate Vista table. This interface will run "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,66,0)="     continously, and will keep the site updated with the most recent"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,67,0)="     changes and additions to the third party Payer sheets."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,69,0)="New Globals:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,70,0)="============"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,72,0)="The following globals will be created when installing this build."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,73,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,74,0)="^BPS            -       MOSTLY STATIC"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,75,0)="^BPSC           -       VERY DYNAMIC - WILL CONTINUALLY GROW"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,76,0)="^BPSCOMB        -       STATIC - CURRENTLY NOT USED BY THE VA"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,77,0)="^BPSECP         -       DYNAMIC - DOESNT GROW"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,78,0)="^BPSECX         -       DYAMIC - DOESNT GROW A LOT"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,79,0)="^BPSEI          -       STATIC - CURRENTLY NOT USED BY THE VA"
