^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,289,0)="Documentation Retrieval:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,290,0)="========================"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,291,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,292,0)="The ECME documentation is available on the ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE directory"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,293,0)="at one of the following Office of Information (OI) Field Offices."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,294,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,295,0)="Sites may retrieve documentation in one of the following ways:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,296,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,297,0)="(1) The preferred method is to FTP the files from"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,298,0)="    download.vista.domain.ext, which will transmit the files from the"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,299,0)="    first available FTP server."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,300,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,301,0)="(2) Sites may also elect to retrieve documentation directly from a"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,302,0)="    specific server as follows:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,303,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,304,0)="    Albany          ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,305,0)="    Hines           ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,306,0)="    Salt Lake City  ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,307,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,308,0)="The documentation distribution includes:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,309,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,310,0)="   FILE NAME                        DESCRIPTION"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,311,0)="   BPS_1_0_IG.PDF                   HIPAA NCPDP CONNECTION FOR EDI "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,312,0)="                                    PHARMACY (DORMANT RELEASE)"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,313,0)="                                    INSTALLATION GUIDE "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,314,0)="   BPS_1_0_RN.PDF                   HIPAA NCPDP CONNECTION FOR EDI"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,315,0)="                                    PHARMACY (DORMANT RELEASE)"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,316,0)="                                    RELEASE NOTES"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,317,0)="   IB_2_251_TM.PDF                  INTEGRATED BILLING IB*2.0*251 "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,318,0)="                                    (e-PHARMACY) TECHNICAL MANUAL"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,319,0)="   IB_2_251_UM.PDF                  e-PHARMACY CLAIMS INSURANCE PROCESS"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,320,0)="                                    USER MANUAL"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,321,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,322,0)="(3) Documentation can also be retrieved from VISTA Documentation Library"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,323,0)="(VDL) on the Internet at the following address, http://www.domain.ext/vdl."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,324,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,325,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,326,0)="==========================  "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,327,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,328,0)="The software for this patch is being distributed via a host file.  The "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,329,0)="host file will contain the following package and builds:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,330,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,331,0)="       Host file name BPS_1_0.KID"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,332,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,333,0)="               Package:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,334,0)="                       BPS_1"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,335,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,336,0)="               Builds:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,337,0)="                       PSS*1.0*81 "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,338,0)="                       IB*2.0*223"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,339,0)="                       IB*2.0*251"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,340,0)="                       PRCA*4.5*202"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,341,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,342,0)="Sites may retrieve the software directly by using FTP from the "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,343,0)="ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE directory at the following OI Field Offices:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,344,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,345,0)="       Albany:         ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,346,0)="       Hines:          ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,347,0)="       Salt Lake City: ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,348,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,349,0)="Do not install this patch while Pharmacy Data Management users are using "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,350,0)="the software. Installation will take no longer than 15 minutes. There are"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,351,0)="no scheduling restrictions or recommendations."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,352,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,353,0)="Installation Steps"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,354,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,355,0)=" 1. Use VA FileMan to add the new domain, EPHARMACY.VITRIA-EDI.AAC.DOMAIN.EXT,"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,356,0)="    to the DOMAIN file (#4.2). The installation instructions are included"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,357,0)="    in the patch description for the XM*DBA*160 patch. This domain must be"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,358,0)="    in place before the installation of the IB*2*251 patch that is"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,359,0)="    included in the BPS 1.0 Master Build."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,360,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,361,0)=" 2. Download the KIDS file BPS_1_0.KID via FTP. This file needs to be "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,362,0)="    retrieved in ASCII format."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,363,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,364,0)=" 3. Review mapped sets for the PSS*, IB*, and PRCA* namespaces.  If the "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,365,0)="    routines are mapped, they should be removed from the mapped set at"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,366,0)="    this time."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,367,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,368,0)=" 4. From the Kernel Installation & Distribution System menu, select the "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,369,0)="    Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,370,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,371,0)=" 5. From this menu, select the Load a Distribution option. When prompted "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,372,0)="    for a file name, enter the directory name where you FTPd the build, "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,373,0)="    followed by BPS_1_0. In our example, the file name is"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,374,0)="    USER$:[ANONYMOUS]BPS_1_0.KID. Determine the location where you stored"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,375,0)="    your build to decide the correct file name entry."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,376,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,377,0)=" 6. At the ""Want to Continue with Load? YES//"" prompt, enter YES."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,378,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,379,0)=" 7. At the ""Want to RUN the Environment Check Routine: YES//"" prompt, "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,380,0)="    answer YES."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,381,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,382,0)=" 8. From this menu, the installer may select to use the following options:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,383,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,384,0)="(When prompted for INSTALL NAME, enter BPS 1.0)"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,385,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,386,0)="    a. Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,387,0)="    message of any routines exported with the patch. It will NOT backup"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,388,0)="    any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,389,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,390,0)="    b. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,391,0)="    you to view all changes that will be made when the patch is installed."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,392,0)="    It compares all components of the patch (routines, DDs, templates,"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,393,0)="    etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,394,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,395,0)="    c. Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will ensure the "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,396,0)="    integrity of the routines that are in the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,397,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,398,0)=" 9. At the ""Select Installation Option:"" prompt, enter 6 Install "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,399,0)="    Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,400,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,401,0)="10. At the ""Select INSTALL NAME:"" prompt, enter BPS 1.0."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,402,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,403,0)="11. When prompted, ""Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,404,0)="    Install? YES//"" respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,405,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,406,0)="12. When prompted, ""Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? YES//"""
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,407,0)="    respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,408,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,409,0)="13. When prompted, ""Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,410,0)="    Protocols? YES//"" respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,411,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,412,0)="14. When prompted, ""Device:Home//"" respond with the correct device and DO "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,413,0)="    NOT queue this to P-Message."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,414,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,415,0)="15. If routines were unmapped as part of step 3, they should be returned "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,1,416,0)="    to the mapped set once the installation has run to completion."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^40^40"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,0)="1^3060525^1"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,0)="^^35^35^3060525"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,1,0)="PATCH OVERVIEW"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,3,0)="The Healthcare Insurance Portability and Accountability Act National"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,4,0)="Council for Prescription Drug Programs (HIPAA NCPDP) initiative, whose"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,5,0)="ultimate goal is to provide functionality allowing electronic transmission"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,6,0)="of Outpatient Pharmacy (OP) prescription claims to payers and the receipt"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,7,0)="of claim responses (including drug utilization review responses and"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,8,0)="warnings) on a real-time basis, is being developed and introduced in a"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,9,0)="phased implementation strategy. This deployment strategy was utilized due"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,10,0)="to the complexity of the functionality and the number of product line"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,11,0)="dependencies."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,13,0)="This is the second part of the Electronic Claims Management Engine (ECME)"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,14,0)="package (in the BPS namespace), also known as the active build. It"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,15,0)="comprises of these patches: BPS*1*1, PSO*7*148, PSS*1*90, PSX*2*48 and"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,16,0)="IB*2*276."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,18,0)="This build will introduce functionality supporting Point of Service"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,19,0)="Outpatient Pharmacy claim and billing processing by collecting billing and"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,20,0)="clinical information within the prescription fill workflow process.  This"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,21,0)="build will create real-time electronic claims and send claim data to"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,22,0)="adjudicating payers from the new VistA Electronic Claims Management Engine"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,23,0)="(ECME) via the VistA HL7 module (using the PSO NCPDP link) to the Vitria"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,24,0)="server at the FSC in Austin, TX in a HIPAA compliant (NCPDP V. 5.1)"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,25,0)="format. Vitria will then store and forward these transactions to WebMD for"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,26,0)="final submission to the payer on a real-time basis. Payer responses will"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,27,0)="be received and returned to VistA in the appropriate manner (i.e. - claim"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,28,0)="transactions sent to Integrated Billing (IB), Drug Utilization responses"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,29,0)="and warnings sent to the Outpatient Pharmacy V. 7.0 package and rejections"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,30,0)="made available to the appropriate personnel for review and analysis)."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,32,0)="Within VistA, throughout this process, constant bi-directional"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,33,0)="communication via API's between Outpatient Pharmacy, Integrated Billing,"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,34,0)="and ECME will process and generate these claim and billing transactions at"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",1,1,35,0)="the appropriate trigger points within the standard VA process workflow."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,0)="3^3060923^1"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^13^13^3060923"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,1,0)="This patch supports the National Council for Prescription Drug Programs "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,2,0)="(NCPDP) standard which was adopted under the Healthcare Insurance"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,3,0)="Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA) for pharmacy claims. This patch"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,4,0)="is one of six to be released.  Three patches will be released in a KIDS"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,5,0)="multi-build distribution containing: BPS*1*3, PSO*7*247, and IB*2*342.  "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,6,0)="Three patches will be released individually and they are: PRCA*4.5*247,"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,7,0)="PSX*2*62, and PSS*1*115."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,9,0)="Enhancements included in the release of the six patches are a new option "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,10,0)="that will enable the user to reopen a closed Electronic Claims Management"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,11,0)="Engine (ECME) claim; updates to the Rx Activity Log; and permanent storage"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,12,0)="of Claims activity information as reported by the ECME Billing Events"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",2,1,13,0)="Report. "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",3,0)="4 SEQ #3^3061211.172803^1"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^4^4^3061211"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="This patch modifies the Application Program Interface (API) that"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",3,1,2,0)="processes claims in E-Pharmacy to check for a valid user before it"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",3,1,3,0)="stores that information in the BPS Transaction File"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",3,1,4,0)="(#9002313.59)."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",4,0)="2 SEQ #4^3070629.190104^1"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^2^2^3070629"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="The HIPPA NPI project supports the use of NPI within the Electronic "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",4,1,2,0)="Claims Management Engine (ECME) application."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,0)="5^3071212.214859^1"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,0)="^^21^21^3071212"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,1,0)="This patch has enhancements which extend the capabilities of the Veterans"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,2,0)="Health Information Systems and Technology Architecture (VistA) electronic"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,3,0)="pharmacy (ePharmacy) system.  Below is a list of all the applications"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,4,0)="involved in this project along with their patch number:"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,6,0)="   APPLICATION/VERSION                                  PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,7,0)="   --------------------------------------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,8,0)="   OUTPATIENT PHARMACY (OP) V. 7.0                      PSO*7*260"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,9,0)="   INTEGRATED BILLING (IB) V. 2.0                       IB*2*363"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,10,0)="   ELECTRONIC CLAIMS MANAGEMENT ENGINE (ECME) V. 1.0    BPS*1*5"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,11,0)="   PHARMACY DATA MANAGEMENT (PDM) V. 1.0                PSS*1*127"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,12,0)="   CONSOLIDATED MAIL OUTPATIENT PHARMACY (CMOP) V. 2.0  PSX*2*63"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,14,0)="The first three patches (BPS*1*5, IB*2*363,and PSO*7*260) will be"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,15,0)="released in the Kernel Installation and Distribution System (KIDS)"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,16,0)="multi-build distribution BPS PSO IB BUNDLE 2.0.  Patches PSX*2*63 and"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,17,0)="PSS*1*127 will be released as stand-alone patches.  Since there is an"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,18,0)="implementation dependency between the multi-build distribution and the"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,19,0)="stand-alone patches, PSX*2*63 and PSS*1*127 must be installed prior to"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,20,0)="the installation of the multi-build.  For more specific instructions"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",5,1,21,0)="please refer to the installation steps provided in each of the patches."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",6,0)="6 SEQ #6^3090421.162235^17"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",7,0)="7^3090714.091231^17"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^1^1^3090714"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",7,1,1,0)="E-PHARMACY ENHANCEMENTS"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",8,0)="8^3100915.092146^17"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",9,0)="9^3101216.16423^17"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",10,0)="10^3111102.120243^17"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^1^1^3111102"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",10,1,1,0)="ePharmacy Phase 5 - NCPDP D.0"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",11,0)="12 SEQ #11^3111213.152116^17"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^2^2^3111213"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="Modify reversal process to get the reversal payer sheet from the pharmacy "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",11,1,2,0)="plan."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",12,0)="11^3120216.140021^17"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^1^1^3120216"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="ePharmacy Phase 6"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",13,0)="14 SEQ #13^3130319.112012^17"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",13,1,0)="^^4^4^3130319"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",13,1,1,0)="This patch fixes random subscript errors, allows users to select "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",13,1,2,0)="a Drug Class Code as an option during the Payable Claims Report "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",13,1,3,0)="[BPS RPT PAYABLE] and fixes issues while sorting in the ECME "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",13,1,4,0)="User Screen [BPS USER SCREEN]."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",14,0)="15^3140106.161655^17"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",14,1,0)="^^1^1^3140106"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",14,1,1,0)="EPHARMACY OPERATING RULES"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",15,0)="18^3150209.124322^17"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",16,0)="17^3150514.101154^17"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^2^2^3150514"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",16,1,1,0)="ePayments ePharmacy Compliance"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",16,1,2,0)="BPS IB PRCA EPAYMENTS BUNDLE 1.0"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",17,0)="19^3160211.171637^54"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",17,1,0)="^^1^1^3160211"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",17,1,1,0)="HAPE EDI Revenue project - NCPDP Continuous Maintenance Standards"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",18,0)="20^3160829.125624^54"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^1^1^3160829"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="MCCF ePharmacy Compliance Phase 3"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",19,0)="21 SEQ #19^3170802.132531^54"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",19,1,0)="^^1^1^3170802"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",19,1,1,0)="MCCF EDI TAS ePharmacy Iteration 1"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",20,0)="22^3171127.134854^54"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",20,1,0)="^^1^1^3171127"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",20,1,1,0)="MCCF EDI TAS EPHARMACY BUILD 2"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",21,0)="23^3180907.122413^54"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",21,1,0)="^^1^1^3180907"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",21,1,1,0)="MCCF EDI TAS EPHARMACY BUILDS 3 & 4"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",22,0)="24^3190201.143759^54"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",22,1,0)="^^1^1^3190201"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",22,1,1,0)="MCCF EDI TAS EPHARMACY BUILDS 5 & 6"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",23,0)="25 SEQ #23^3190402.142622^54"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",24,0)="26^3200410.160807^70"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",24,1,0)="^^1^1^3200410"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",24,1,1,0)="MCCF EDI TAS EPHARMACY BUILD 13"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",25,0)="27^3201208.082724^17"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",26,0)="28b^3210519"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",26,1,0)="^^5^5^3210519"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",26,1,1,0)="Backup of BPS PSO IB BUNDLE 16.0, BPS*1.0*28, PSO*7.0*560, IB*2"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",26,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",26,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",26,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",26,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",27,0)="28^3210519.161028^17"
^DIC(9.4,198,22,1,"PAH",28,0)="29^3210913.110934^17"
