^DIC(9.4,198,"VERSION")="1.0"
^DIC(9.4,199,0)="VDEF^VDEF^VISTA Data Extraction Framework"
^DIC(9.4,199,1,0)="^9.41A^2^2^3030819^^"
^DIC(9.4,199,1,1,0)="VDEF stands for VistA Data Extraction Framework, a data-driven scripting"
^DIC(9.4,199,1,2,0)="tool for automated HL7 message generation."
^DIC(9.4,199,20,0)="^9.402P^^"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,0)="^9.49I^1^1"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,0)="1.0^3120504^3050118^1"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,1,0)="^^1^1^3120504"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,1,1,0)="This build is for the GOLD disk. It was buld on the FOIVISTA account.  "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^5^5"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,0)="3 SEQ #1^3060213^1"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,0)="^^628^628^3060213"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,1,0)="PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE DESCRIPTION AND INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,2,0)="BEFORE INSTALLING THIS PATCH."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,5,0)="DESCRIPTION:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,6,0)="============"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,8,0)="This patch fixes 4 problems in the VistA Data Extraction Framework"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,9,0)="(VDEF) V1.0 functionality:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,11,0)=" 1) Adds the name of the Request Queue to the VDEF Alert message."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,13,0)=" 2) Eliminates false VDEF Alerts."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,15,0)=" 3) Eliminates the problem of VDEF Request Queue processor not being"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,16,0)="    restarted by TaskMan."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,18,0)=" 4) No longer sets the flag for unread VDEF Alerts to be sent to a mail"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,19,0)="    group supervisor."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,21,0)="This patch also includes numerous enhancements to the VistA Data"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,22,0)="Extraction Framework (VDEF) functionality:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,24,0)=" 1) In the VDEF Configuration and Status Menu [VDEF CONFIGURATION MENU],"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,25,0)="    the options marked below with an asterisk now return to the option"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,26,0)="    prompt instead of going back to the main VDEF Configuration and Status"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,27,0)="    Menu."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,29,0)="      Site   Site-Wide Parameters"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,30,0)="    * Req    Request Queue Parameters"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,31,0)="    * ActR   Activate/Inactivate Requestor"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,32,0)="    * SusR   Suspend/Run Request Queue"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,33,0)="    * Cust   VDEF Custodial Package Activate/Inactivate"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,34,0)="    * API    VDEF Event API Activate/Inactivate"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,35,0)="      Stat   Status of VDEF components"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,36,0)="    * Sch    Request Processor Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,38,0)=" 2) A new process, the ""VDEF Request Queue Monitor"" has been added to"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,39,0)="    monitor the VDEF Request Queue process and restart it when it stops"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,40,0)="    if the state of the Request Queue is Running. This new monitor is"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,41,0)="    automatically started by the VDEF Startup option. This process is"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,42,0)="    hardcoded to run every 10 minutes. The VDEF Request Queue Monitor will"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,43,0)="    also automatically requeue any Checked Out and Errored Out VDEF"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,44,0)="    requests."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,46,0)=" 3) VDEF Alert messages are now prefixed with the date & time of the"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,47,0)="    alert in the format MM/DD/YY@HH:MM:SS."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,49,0)=" 4) Original VDEF Alert message texts are clearer in context."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,51,0)=" 5) New VDEF Alerts have been added."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,52,0)="    - VDEF CHECKED OUT MONITOR FAILED TO START. CHECK ERROR TRAP."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,53,0)="    - RECORD <IEN> IN QUEUE <QUEUE NAME> HUNG IN CHECKED OUT STATUS."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,54,0)="    - VDEF REQUEST PROCESS <QUEUE NAME> FAILED TO START. CHECK ERROR"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,55,0)="      TRAP."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,56,0)="    - VDEF QUEUE PROCESS MONITOR DID NOT START. CHECK ERROR TRAP."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,57,0)="    - VDEF HAS REQUEUED CHECKED OUT RECORDS. NO ACTION NEEDED."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,58,0)="    - VDEF HAS REQUEUED ERRORED OUT RECORDS. NO ACTION NEEDED."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,59,0)="    - VDEF QUEUE PROCESS MONITOR HAS EXITED."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,60,0)="    - VDEF QUEUE '""_QUEUE_""' AUTO-RESTARTED. NO ACTION REQUIRED."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,61,0)="    - VDEF QUEUE '""_QUEUE_""' IS SUSPENDED. PLEASE START IT."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,62,0)="    - VDEF REQUEST QUEUE PROCESSOR FOR ""_$P(QUEUE,U)_"" HAS EXITED."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,64,0)=" 6) All VDEF alerts will send a MailMan message to the VDEF developer"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,65,0)="    On FORUM that includes the alert text, the site name and ID and"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,66,0)="    the date & time of the alert."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,67,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,68,0)=" 7) Includes a new program VDEFKIDS that has two APIs, VDEFKIDS"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,69,0)="    and POSTIN^VDEFKIDS.  These APIs are defined in the build as the"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,70,0)="    Environment Check and post install routines.  Although the"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,71,0)="    Pre-install routine does pre-installation type functions, it is"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,72,0)="    defined in the build as the Environment Check routine, NOT the"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,73,0)="    Pre-install routine. This is to prevent any VDEF* routines that"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,74,0)="    are in the build from being filed over actively running routines"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,75,0)="    causing an EDITED error trap error. By the time KIDS runs the"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,76,0)="    Pre-Install routine, ALL the routines in the build have already"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,77,0)="    been loaded whereas when the Environment routine is run, no other"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,78,0)="    programs in the build have been installed."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,80,0)="    The pre-install routine will:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,81,0)="     - suspend all VDEF Request Queues"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,82,0)="     - stop the TaskMan tasks associated with these queues"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,83,0)="     - stop the VDEF checked out request monitor"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,84,0)="     - stop the VDEF Request Queue process monitor"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,86,0)="    The post-install routine (in production systems only) will:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,87,0)="     - un-suspend all VDEF Request Queues (change state to running)"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,88,0)="     - create new TaskMan tasks for these queues"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,89,0)="     - start the VDEF checked out request monitor"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,90,0)="     - start the VDEF Request Queue process monitor"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,92,0)=" 8) The Status of VDEF components [VDEF Status] option screen has been"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,93,0)="    modified. See the example that follows."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,94,0)="     - The VMS Process ID associated with the VDEF Request Queue process"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,95,0)="       task has been added."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,96,0)="     - The TaskMan task status has been added."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,97,0)="     - The counter for Processed requests has been deleted.  This was"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,98,0)="       useless information because it was simply a count of the number"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,99,0)="       of records in the VDEF Request Queue that are in the Processed"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,100,0)="       status and the fact that the count stopped at "">100""."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,101,0)="     - The counter for Queued Up has been changed to display the actual"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,102,0)="       number up to a maximum of 1000. If more than 1000 are queued up,"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,103,0)="       the display will show ""> 1000""."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,104,0)="     - The description ""Requests in the queue"" has been changed to"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,105,0)="       ""Requests waiting for purge"""
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,106,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,107,0)="   (example)"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,108,0)="   Request Processor Status"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,109,0)="     MAINTENANCE: Running and not Scheduled"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,110,0)="     Current Task # [Proc]: 7399750 [21663B42]"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,111,0)="     Requests waiting for purge: 14      Last request#: 14"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,112,0)="     Checked Out(0)  Queued Up(0)  Errored Out(0)"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,113,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,114,0)=" 9) Changed the M lock used to protect the VDEF Request Queue so that"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,115,0)="    it doesn't prevent using FileMan to access the VDEF queue file."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,116,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,117,0)="10) Creates the new Application ""VDEF ALERTS"" and the new Mail Group"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,118,0)="    ""VDEF NATIONAL ALERTS"" and changes the VistA Mail Group for VDEF"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,119,0)="    Alerts from the HL7 group to the new VDEF group."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,120,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,121,0)="11) Removed the Scheduled task from the Status of VDEF components [VDEF"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,122,0)="    Status] display and added the TaskMan status of the task."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,123,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,124,0)="12) Removed the XQASUPV variable from the alert call so that VDEF"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,125,0)="    alerts are no longer forwarded to unread alerts supervisor mail"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,126,0)="    group."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,127,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,128,0)="13) Added the date and time and the TaskMan task status to the VDEF"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,129,0)="    Status display."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,130,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,131,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,132,0)="IRM NOTES:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,133,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,134,0)="Before installing this patch, make sure you have completely installed "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,135,0)="XU*8.0*339 and run the '% program' conversion RELOAD^ZTMGRSET utility."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,136,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,137,0)="This patch REQUIRES Kernel patch XU*8.0*339 which fixes a bug in the"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,138,0)="$$ASKSTOP^%ZTLOAD() API and also creates a new API JOB^%ZTLOAD()."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,139,0)="VDEF requires both of these to be updated by the XU*8.0*339 patch in"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,140,0)="Order for VDEF*1*3 to install."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,141,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,142,0)="This VDEF patch uses the $$JOB^%ZTLOAD functionality released with"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,143,0)="XU*8*399. Please confirm that the post-KIDS install steps for XU*8*399"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,144,0)="have been done.  The following MUMPS code should indicate that XU*8*399 is"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,145,0)="in the second line of the %ZTLOAD routine:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,146,0)=">ZL %ZTLOAD ZP +1:+2"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,147,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,148,0)="For the duration of the installation of this patch, all VDEF Request"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,149,0)="Queue processors that were in the Running state will be temporarily "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,150,0)="suspended.  The pre-install and post-install routines will suspend and "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,151,0)="then restart all Request Queue processors that were in the Running state "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,152,0)="after installation of this patch.  VDEF messages will continue to "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,153,0)="accumulate in the queues during suspension and will start processing "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,154,0)="again after the patch has completed installation. This is the equivalent "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,155,0)="of you using the VDEF Configuration and Status Menu option ""SusR "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,156,0)="Suspend/Run Request Queue"" to suspend and restart the Request Queues."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,157,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,158,0)="When you see the message ""Waiting for processes to quit . ."", there"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,159,0)="will be approximately a 5 second wait."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,160,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,161,0)="PLEASE NOTE: The VDEF Post-install program will not start the VDEF "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,162,0)="processes on test or Legacy systems that have the Test System flag set."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,163,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,164,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,165,0)="IRM'S POST-INSTALLATION REQUIREMENTS"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,166,0)="===================================="
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,167,0)="1. NEW MAIL GROUP AND APPLICATION FOR VDEF ALERTS"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,168,0)="   After you have installed this patch, there will be a new Application"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,169,0)="   named VDEF ALERTS which will have the Mail Group VDEF NATIONAL ALERTS"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,170,0)="   assigned to it.  The new Mail Group will not have any local members in"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,171,0)="   it. YOU MUST ASSIGN THE LOCAL MEMBERS.  It will have the remote member"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,172,0)="   GARDNER.JEFF@DOMAIN.EXT. Please verify these that these two new"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,173,0)="   definitions are correctly set up. If a site does not have the Mail"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,174,0)="   Group VDEF NATIONAL ALERTS, VDEF will continue the alerts to the HL7"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,175,0)="   Mail Group."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,177,0)="2. MODIFY THE 'VDEF STARTUP OPTION' SCHEDULED TASK."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,178,0)="   Using the TaskMan option 'Schedule/Unschedule Options', edit the"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,179,0)="   parameters for the task VDEF STARTUP OPTION as indicated in the screen"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,180,0)="   example shown here."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,181,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,182,0)="                           Edit Option Schedule"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,183,0)="     Option Name: VDEF STARTUP OPTION           "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,184,0)="     Menu Text: VDEF STARTUP OPTION                 TASK ID: 5998624"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,185,0)=" ___________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,186,0)="   QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME: (Enter current date/time + 5 minutes)"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,187,0)=" DEVICE FOR QUEUED JOB OUTPUT: "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,188,0)="  QUEUED TO RUN ON VOLUME SET: "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,189,0)="       RESCHEDULING FREQUENCY: 300S  (Enter 300S)"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,190,0)="              TASK PARAMETERS: "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,191,0)="             SPECIAL QUEUEING: Startup Persistent (Change from STARTUP"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,192,0)="                                                   to Startup Persistent"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,193,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,194,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,195,0)="This patch addresses the following New Service Request (NSR):"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,196,0)="============================================================="
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,197,0)="There is no NSR associated with this patch."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,198,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,200,0)="This patch addresses the following Remedy ticket(s):"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,201,0)="===================================================="
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,202,0)="65927,99499,100952,102184,102329,103092,103286,104402,105065,106497"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,203,0)="106674,107101,107142,107326,107508,107589,107773,107927,108431,108661"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,204,0)="108873,108915,109469,109521,109627,109638,109715,109725,110057,110285"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,205,0)="110501,110688,110765,110891,111109,112391,112642"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,206,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,207,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,208,0)="Overview of Patch Items:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,209,0)="========================"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,210,0)="1) A pre-install routine, PREIN^VDEFKIDS, is included in this patch that"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,211,0)="   suspends VDEF Request Queue processing through the duration of this"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,212,0)="   patch installation. It also stops and deletes the TaskMan tasks driving"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,213,0)="   the processes and the VDEF monitor processes."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,214,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,215,0)="2) A post-install routine, POSTIN^VDEFKIDS, is included in this patch"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,216,0)="   that restarts VDEF Request Queues after installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,217,0)="   It also creates new VDEF monitor tasks."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,218,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,219,0)="3) The routine VDEFUTIL has been changed to not set the flag for an "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,220,0)="   unread VDEF Alert to be sent to the supervisor. This program has also"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,221,0)="   been changed to prefix the date & time to the VDEF alert text and to"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,222,0)="   use the new VDEF alert mail group to send a MailMan message to the VDEF"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,223,0)="   developer whenever a VDEF alert occurs."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,224,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,225,0)="4) The routine VDEFCONT has been changed to eliminate the false VDEF"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,226,0)="   Alerts from being generated.  It has also been changed to include"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,227,0)="   the name of the Request Queue in the VDEF Alert message."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,228,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,229,0)="5) The routine VDEFREQ has been changed to eliminate the problem of"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,230,0)="   TaskMan not restarting the VDEF Request Queue processor EN^VDEFREQ."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,231,0)="   Instead, VDEFREQ does not re-schedule itself with TaskMan but uses"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,232,0)="   an M HANG command loop based on the number of seconds in file"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,233,0)="   #579.3, field .05 - CHECK-OUT TIME LIMIT."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,234,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,235,0)="6) The routine VDEFMNU has been changed to display the VMS process ID"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,236,0)="   for the Request Queue Task in the Status of VDEF components [VDEF"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,237,0)="   Status] display. The counter for Processed Requests has been dropped"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,238,0)="   from the Status of VDEF components [VDEF Status] display. It was"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,239,0)="   useless information."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,240,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,241,0)="7) The routine VDEFQM has been changed to incorporate two VDEF APIs"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,242,0)="   that will requeue requests that are stuck in the Checked Out or"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,243,0)="   Errored Out state."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,244,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,245,0)="8) A new routine VDEFMON has been created to monitor the Request Queue"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,246,0)="   process and restart it if it dies as well as automatically re-queuing"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,247,0)="   requests that have Errored Out or get stuck in the Checked Out status."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,248,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,249,0)="9) There are no VDEF global changes in this patch."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,250,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,251,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,252,0)="Test Sites:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,253,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,254,0)="BAY PINES"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,255,0)="EL PASO"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,256,0)="LOUISVILLE"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,257,0)="MARYLAND (Integrated)"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,258,0)="MEMPHIS"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,259,0)="PHILADELPHIA"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,260,0)="PHOENIX"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,261,0)="SAN FRANCISCO"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,262,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,263,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,264,0)="LOCATION OF DOCUMENTATION FOR THIS PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,265,0)="========================================"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,266,0)="There will be a documentation update for this patch to the VDEF V1.0 "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,267,0)="Installation & User Configuration Guide and the VDEF V1.0 Technical Manual"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,268,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,269,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,270,0)="INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,271,0)="========================="
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,272,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,273,0)="Install Time - less than 5 minutes"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,274,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,275,0)="1. LOAD TRANSPORT GLOBAL"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,276,0)="   ---------------------"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,277,0)="   Choose the PackMan message containing this patch and invoke the"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,278,0)="   INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option.  The build includes an"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,279,0)="   Environment check routine VDEFKIDS."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,280,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,281,0)="Loading Distribution..."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,282,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,283,0)="   VDEF*1.0*3"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,284,0)="Will first run the Environment Check Routine, VDEFKIDS"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,285,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,286,0)="2. COMPONENTS SENT WITH PATCH"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,287,0)="   --------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,288,0)="   Routine Summary"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,289,0)="   The following routines are included in this patch.  The second line"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,290,0)="   of Each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,291,0)="   ;;1.0;VDEF;**3**;Dec 28, 2004"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,292,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,293,0)="                 Checksum"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,294,0)="Routine         Old       New      Patch List"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,295,0)="VDEFCONT      8818367   8818367    **3**"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,296,0)="VDEFKIDS     13711730   5283479    **3**"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,297,0)="VDEFMNU      47567743  14047707    **3**"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,298,0)="VDEFMON       8468795   3113945    **3**"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,299,0)="VDEFQM       12629742  12740824    **3**"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,300,0)="VDEFREQ       7914740   7914740    **3**"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,301,0)="VDEFUTIL      5715842   5715842    **3**"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,302,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,303,0)="Sites should use CHECK^XTSUMBLD to verify checksums."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,304,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,305,0)="NOTE: The above checksums are based on your site having installed"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,306,0)="VDEF*1*3 v9. If you are installing VDEF*1*3 for the first time or if you "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,307,0)="did not install VDEF*1*3 v9, your old checksums will not match those in "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,308,0)="the above list."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,309,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,310,0)="If you are installing VDEF*1*3 for the first time and all your current"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,311,0)="VDEF* programs are V1.0, your old checksums should be:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,312,0)="VDEFCONT    10134570"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,313,0)="VDEFKIDS         N/A"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,314,0)="VDEFMNU     12329753"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,315,0)="VDEFMON          N/A"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,316,0)="VDEFQM      11427789"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,317,0)="VDEFREQ      7981911"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,318,0)="VDEFUTIL     1413855"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,319,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,320,0)="3. START UP KIDS"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,321,0)="   -------------"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,322,0)="   Start up the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,323,0)="   [XPD MAIN]:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,324,0)="        Edits and Distribution"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,325,0)="        Utilities"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,326,0)="        Installation"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,327,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,328,0)="   Select Kernel Installation & Distribution System Option:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,329,0)="     INStallation"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,330,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,331,0)="        Load a Distribution"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,332,0)="        Print Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,333,0)="        Compare Transport Global to Current System"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,334,0)="        Verify Checksums in Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,335,0)="        Install Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,336,0)="        Restart Install of Package(s)"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,337,0)="        Unload a Distribution"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,338,0)="        Backup a Transport Global"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,339,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,340,0)="     Select Installation Option:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,341,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,342,0)="4. Select Installation Option:"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,343,0)="   ---------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,344,0)="   When prompted for the INSTALL NAME, enter VDEF*1.0*3."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,345,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,346,0)="    a.  Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,347,0)="        message of any routines exported with this patch. It will not"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,348,0)="        backup any other changes such as DD's or templates."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,349,0)="    b.  Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,350,0)="        allow you to view all changes that will be made when this"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,351,0)="        patch is installed.  It compares all components of this patch"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,352,0)="        (routines, DD's, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,353,0)="    c.  Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,354,0)="        you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,355,0)="        transport global."
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,356,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,199,22,1,"PAH",1,1,357,0)="5. Select Installation Option: Install Package(s)"
