^DIC(9.4,207,0)="VBECS^VBEC^VistA Blood Establishment Computer System"
^DIC(9.4,207,1,0)="^9.41A^6^6^3030324^"
^DIC(9.4,207,1,1,0)="This package, VBECS, exists in the M environment to"
^DIC(9.4,207,1,2,0)="perform integrity checks on existing VistA Blood Bank"
^DIC(9.4,207,1,3,0)="data, convert relevant data for migration to parallel"
^DIC(9.4,207,1,4,0)="applications, and to migrate VistA data to parallel"
^DIC(9.4,207,1,5,0)="applications when specific application events are"
^DIC(9.4,207,1,6,0)="triggered."
^DIC(9.4,207,5)="Hines Office of Information"
^DIC(9.4,207,20,0)="^9.402P^^"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,0)="^9.49I^2^2"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,0)="1.0^3090423^3090609^17"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,0)="^^449^449^3090609"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,1,0)="VBEC*1*0 is being exported as part of the VBECS_BUNDLE_1.KID package "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,2,0)="release. The installation of this bundle will be controlled by phase "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,3,0)="release.  An Implementation Manager will be assigned to your site and "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,4,0)="will contact your POC for VBECS and will provide your site with the "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,5,0)="location of the KIDS Host Files prior to your scheduled installation date "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,6,0)="Installation Sequence.  The VBECS BUNDLE is a host file that consists of "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,7,0)="both VBEC*1*0 and LR*5.2*325.  Installation of the VBECS BUNDLE will "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,8,0)="automatically install both VBEC*1*0 and LR*5.2*325"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,9,0)="====================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,11,0)="I. OVERVIEW"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,12,0)="The VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) shall facilitate "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,13,0)="ongoing compliance with Food and Drug Administration (FDA) standards for "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,14,0)="medical devices and enhance the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,15,0)="Veterans Health Administration's (VHA) ability to deliver quality "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,16,0)="services to meet the needs of the user community. VBECS is considered an "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,17,0)="encapsulated medical device and therefore does not communicate directly "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,18,0)="with other VistA applications."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,20,0)="Two new namespaces are being introduced into the VistA enterprise with "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,21,0)="the release of VBECS. The first, gov.va.med.vbecs, represents the Blood "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,22,0)="Bank medical device software. The second, VBEC, represents the VBECS "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,23,0)="Application Interfacing Support software. The VBEC namespace, created in "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,24,0)="the VBEC 1.0 KIDS build, will be added to the Package file in VistA and "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,25,0)="is used to identify the M software and files that support interfacing "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,26,0)="other VistA applications with the Blood Bank medical device. This "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,27,0)="software is not released as part of the Blood Bank medical device."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,29,0)="II. FUNCTIONAL OVERVIEW"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,30,0)="The reengineered Blood Bank system uses VistALink and Health Level Seven "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,31,0)="(HL7) messaging for data exchange with a client-server mode application "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,32,0)="interfacing architecture through M Application Programmer Interfaces "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,33,0)="(APIs), VistA Remote Procedure Calls (RPCs), and HL7 interfaces released "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,34,0)="in the VBEC 1.0 KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,36,0)="This software will provide a transparent database transition through the "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,37,0)="use of M APIs, RPCs, and HL7 interfaces. The APIs released in this build "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,38,0)="will allow other VistA applications to continue the retrieval of Blood "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,39,0)="Bank data stored in the Blood Bank system. The RPCs will allow the Blood "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,40,0)="Bank system to continue to retrieve data from other VistA applications. "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,41,0)="The HL7 interfaces will allow the exchange of data between the Blood Bank "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,42,0)="system and other VistA applications."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,44,0)="III. TECHNICAL COMPONENTS"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,45,0)="This section lists the components of the VBECS, and LAB SERVICES "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,46,0)="installed in VistA by the VBEC BUNDLE 1.0 Multi Package KIDS build that "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,47,0)="supports VBECS."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,50,0)="MAIL GROUP:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,51,0)="==========="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,52,0)=" VBECS INTERFACE ADMIN - Receives alert mail messages when problems  "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,53,0)="arise with VBECS Application Interfacing. The users added to this  group "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,54,0)="would be Lab/Blood Bank supervisors and/or IRM responsible for  managing "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,55,0)="the VBECS package and interfaces."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,1,56,0)=" "
