^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,113,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 1.4.0.0 Installation "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,114,0)="Guide.doc"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,115,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 1.4.0.0 Installation "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,116,0)="Guide.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,117,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 1.4.0.0 Technical "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,118,0)="Manual-Security Guide.doc"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,119,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 1.4.0.0 Technical "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,120,0)="Manual-Security Guide.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,121,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 1.4.0.0 User Guide.doc"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,122,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 1.4.0.0 User Guide.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,123,0)="Known Defects and Anomalies.doc"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,124,0)="Known Defects and Anomalies.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,125,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,127,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,128,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,129,0)="This patch may be loaded with users on the system."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,130,0)="Installation will take less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,131,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,132,0)="    1) Use the 'LOAD A DISTRIBUTION' option on the KIDS Installation"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,133,0)="       menu. The Host File name is VBEC_1_1.KID .  Answer YES to the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,134,0)="       question: ""Want to Continue with Load? YES//"""
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,135,0)="    2) From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu,"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,136,0)="       select the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,137,0)="    3) From this menu, you may elect to use the following options"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,138,0)="       (when prompted for the INSTALL NAME, enter VBEC*1.0*1)."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,139,0)="       a) Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,140,0)="          message of any routines exported with the patch.  It will NOT"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,141,0)="          backup any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,142,0)="       b) Compare Transport Global to Current System - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,143,0)="          allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,144,0)="          is installed.  It compares all components of the patch"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,145,0)="          (routines, DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,146,0)="       c) Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,147,0)="          you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,148,0)="          transport global."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,149,0)="       d) Print Transport Global - this option will allow you to view the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,150,0)="          components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,151,0)="    4) Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,152,0)="       VBEC*1.0*1."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,153,0)="    5) When prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,154,0)="       Install? NO//' respond YES"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,155,0)="    6) When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,156,0)="       NO//', respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,157,0)="    7) When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",1,1,158,0)="       Protocols? NO//', respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",2,0)="0^3090130"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^2^2^3090130"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",2,1,1,0)="This patch is part of the VBECS BUNDLE 1.0 controlled release. See the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",2,1,2,0)="description for the VBECS BUNDLE 1.0 for patch details."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",3,0)="3^3100902.103052^17"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^2^2^3100902"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="This patch contains changes to the VBECS Blood Bank package. Refer to the "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",3,1,2,0)="patch listed in the Forum patch module for more details."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",4,0)="10^3110309.15125^17"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^2^2^3110309"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="This patch contains changes to the VBECS Blood Bank package. Refer to the "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",4,1,2,0)="patch listed in the Forum patch module for more details."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",5,0)="27^3120924.152557^17"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",6,0)="56 SEQ #57^3130619.123914^17"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,0)="54 SEQ #82^3150608.114447^17"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^200^200^3150608"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,1,0)="VBEC*1*54 is exported as part of the VistA Blood Establishment Computer "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,2,0)="System (VBECS) Version 2.0.0 release."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,4,0)="To meet Food & Drug Administration (FDA) requirements, VBECS related "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,5,0)="VistA (Veterans Health Information Systems Technology Architecture) "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,6,0)="patches require customer validation in local Test accounts prior to "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,7,0)="installation in Production. The user validates the Blood Bank software "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,8,0)="for its intended use prior to its acceptance and use for patient care."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,10,0)="Therefore, to allow adequate time for impact analysis and testing the "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,11,0)="changes prior to installation in Production, it is imperative that Office "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,12,0)="of Information Technology (OIT) Field Operations coordinate the "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,13,0)="installation of Blood Bank software patches with Pathology & Laboratory "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,14,0)="Medicine Service staff."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,16,0)="The VBEC*1*54 patch addresses several issues. Refer to the sample "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,17,0)="validation scenarios listed with the correction to verify changes: "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,19,0)=" 1. 109 VistA MR 103013 - The CPRS Blood Bank Report, Diagnostic Tests"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,20,0)="      Section has displayed Transfusion Reaction Workup test results"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,21,0)="      with patient Type and Screen test results. This was not done by"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,22,0)="      the legacy blood bank system. The change made to the VBECA1B1"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,23,0)="      routine will eliminate Transfusion Reaction Workup test results"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,24,0)="      from the Blood Bank Report, Diagnostic Tests Section. Note - the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,25,0)="      Transfusion Reactions Section of the CPRS Blood Bank Report does"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,26,0)="      not change and will still display Transfusion Reaction"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,27,0)="      Interpretations."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,28,0)="      Associated Remedy Tickets: INC000000923654 and INC000000925197."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,30,0)="      Verification: Locate a patient with a Transfusion Reaction in VBECS."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,31,0)="      Using this patient run the CPRS Blood Bank Report and note that"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,32,0)="      transfusion reaction testing is visible in the Diagnostic Tests"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,33,0)="      Section and the Transfusion Reactions Section has an interpretation."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,34,0)="      Install VBEC*1*54. Repeat the lookup of the CPRS Blood Bank Report"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,35,0)="      and verify that the transfusion reaction testing is absent in the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,36,0)="      CPRS Blood Bank Report, Diagnostic Tests Section. Verify that the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,37,0)="      Transfusion Reactions Section of the CPRS Blood Bank Report does"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,38,0)="      not change and still displays the Transfusion Reaction"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,39,0)="      Interpretations after VBEC*1*54 is installed."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,41,0)=" 2. 110 VistA MR 121713 - VBECS was able to accept a specimen  when the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,42,0)="      CPRS order was assigned a Lab accession number as the order was"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,43,0)="      added to a collection list and the specimen was not collected (no"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,44,0)="      collection date/time). This change requires that the specimen"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,45,0)="      accession number must also have a collection date and time in VistA"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,46,0)="      before it can be used in VBECS for processing."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,48,0)="      Remedy Ticket: INC000000948143"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,50,0)="      Verification: Attempt to accept a VBECS order with a blood bank"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,51,0)="      specimen that does not have a collection date and time assigned in"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,52,0)="      VistA but has been assigned an accession number per a Lab collection"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,53,0)="      list.  VBECS will allow processing of the specimen UID for an order"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,54,0)="      only when the specimen has a date and time collected assigned after"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,55,0)="      VBEC*1*54 is installed."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,57,0)=" 3. 111 VistA MR 061214 - The release of ICD*18.0*57 started a "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,58,0)="      retirement countdown for ICR 3990 used to lookup ICD codes. This "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,59,0)="      lookup is used by the LRBLPCH (Patient transfusions & hematology "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,60,0)="      results) option in VistA Blood Bank. No new transfusion "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,61,0)="      data has been entered since LR*5.2*408 (compliance date August 18, "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,62,0)="      2011) was installed to turn off VistA Blood Bank. The end "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,63,0)="      result is that the LRBLPCH option is obsolete and the change to "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,64,0)="      ICD codes is not relevant. The LRBLPCH option will be placed out "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,65,0)="      of order with the installation of this patch."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,67,0)="      Verification: Any attempt to execute the option will return a"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,68,0)="      message that it is out of order."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,69,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,70,0)=" 4. 112 VistA MR 111914 - Workload configuration and details are not"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,71,0)="      maintained in the development accounts which results in errors when"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,72,0)="      the workload process is triggered. Minor changes to the VistA "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,73,0)="      workload code prevents the workload process from proceeding when "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,74,0)="      there is no workload to process. Changes to the VBECRPCC routine"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,75,0)="      will prevent the error caused when there is no workload to process."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,77,0)="      Verification: None"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,78,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,80,0)="There is also a VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,81,0)="2.0.0 server update that is also being released. Please refer "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,82,0)="to the VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 2.0.0 "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,83,0)="Release Notes for detailed information about corrections in that release."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,84,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,86,0)="BLOOD BANK CLEARANCE: "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,87,0)="====================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,88,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch VBEC*1*54 contains "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,89,0)="changes to a package referenced in BBM TEAM REVIEW OF VISTA PATCHES. "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,90,0)="This patch does not alter or modify any VistA Blood Bank software design "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,91,0)="safeguards or safety critical elements functions."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,92,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,93,0)="RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch VBEC*1*54 have no affect on Blood "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,94,0)="Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,95,0)=" "
