^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,123,0)="Documentation:  "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,124,0)="============== "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,125,0)="Documentation is available for the VBECS package on the "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,126,0)="ANONYMOUS.SOFTWARE directory at one of the following Office of "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,127,0)="Information (OI) Field Offices. Sites will be able to utilize"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,128,0)="Documentation in either the "".PDF"" or ""DOCX"" format after they extract "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,129,0)="the ZIP file."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,130,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,131,0)="The preferred method is to FTP the files from:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,132,0)="Download.vista.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,134,0)="This transmits files from the first available FTP server. Sites may also "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,135,0)="elect to retrieve documentation directly from a specific server as "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,136,0)="follows:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,137,0)="       Albany                  ftp.fo-albany.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,138,0)="       Hines                   ftp.fo-hines.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,139,0)="       Salt Lake City          ftp.fo-slc.domain.ext"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,141,0)="NOTE:  The ZIP file listed below will be listed in each of the "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,142,0)="VBECS and LR patches that are part of the VBECS package and associated "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,143,0)="patches. It only needs to be downloaded once."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,145,0)="File Name                                   Retrieval format:  "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,146,0)="===========                                 ================= "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,147,0)="VBECS_2_0_0_DOCS_BUNDLE.ZIP                 BINARY "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,148,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,150,0)="The following files are contained in the VBECS_2_0_0_DOCS_BUNDLE.ZIP file "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,151,0)="and will not be individually located on the OI Field Office Anonymous "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,152,0)="Directories."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,153,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,154,0)="The VBECS_2_0_0_DOCS_BUNDLE.ZIP file needs to be extracted on your "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,155,0)="system for use."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,156,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,157,0)="======================================================================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,158,0)="Veterans Health Administration (VHA) Customer Documents:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,159,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 2.0.0 Release "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,160,0)="Notes.docx"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,161,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 2.0.0 Release "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,162,0)="Notes.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,163,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 2.0.0 Technical "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,164,0)="Manual-Security Guide.docx"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,165,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 2.0.0 Technical "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,166,0)="Manual-Security Guide.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,167,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 2.0.0 User Guide.docx"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,168,0)="VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 2.0.0 User Guide.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,169,0)="VBECS Known Defects and Anomalies.docx"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,170,0)="VBECS Known Defects and Anomalies.pdf"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,171,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,172,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,173,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,174,0)="This patch may be loaded with users on the system."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,175,0)="Installation will take less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,177,0)="    1) Use the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE option on the PackMan menu to unload"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,178,0)="       the KIDS distribution included with this message."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,179,0)="    2) From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu,"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,180,0)="       select the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,181,0)="    3) From this menu, you may elect to use the following options"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,182,0)="       (when prompted for the INSTALL NAME, enter VBEC*1.0*54)."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,183,0)="       a) Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,184,0)="          message of any routines exported with the patch. It will NOT"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,185,0)="          backup any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,186,0)="       b) Compare Transport Global to Current System - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,187,0)="          allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,188,0)="          is installed. It compares all components of the patch"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,189,0)="          (routines, DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,190,0)="       c) Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,191,0)="          you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,192,0)="          transport global."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,193,0)="       d) Print Transport Global - this option will allow you to view "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,194,0)="          the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,195,0)="    4) Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,196,0)="       VBEC*1.0*54."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,197,0)="    5) When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,198,0)="       NO//'  respond NO"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,199,0)="    6) When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH",7,1,200,0)="       and Protocols? NO//'  respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH","B",0,2)=""
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH","B",1,1)=""
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH","B",3,3)=""
^DIC(9.4,207,22,1,"PAH","B",10,4)=""
