^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,121,0)="PATCH INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,122,0)="==================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,123,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,124,0)="Pre/Post installation Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,125,0)="==============================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,126,0)="Refer to the VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 2.3.0 "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,127,0)="Release Notes document for pre and post installation information and "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,128,0)="instructions."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,129,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,130,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,131,0)="=============================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,132,0)="Create a test with the following information prior to patch installation."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,134,0)="NAME: VBEC PATIENT REFLEX TEST      TYPE: NEITHER"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,135,0)="  SUBSCRIPT: WORKLOAD               HIGHEST URGENCY ALLOWED: ROUTINE"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,136,0)="  PRINT NAME: VBEC PATIENT REFLEX   CREATION DATE: <Use current date>"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,138,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,139,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,140,0)="This patch may be loaded with users on the system."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,141,0)="Installation will take less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,142,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,143,0)="    1) Use the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE option on the PackMan menu to unload"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,144,0)="       the KIDS distribution included with this message."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,145,0)="    2) From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu,"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,146,0)="       select the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,147,0)="    3) From this menu, you may elect to use the following options"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,148,0)="       (when prompted for the INSTALL NAME, enter VBEC*2*1)."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,149,0)="       a) Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,150,0)="          message of any routines exported with the patch. It will NOT"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,151,0)="          backup any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,152,0)="       b) Compare Transport Global to Current System - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,153,0)="          allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,154,0)="          is installed. It compares all components of the patch"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,155,0)="          (routines, DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,156,0)="       c) Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,157,0)="          you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,158,0)="          transport global."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,159,0)="       d) Print Transport Global - this option will allow you to view "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,160,0)="          the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,161,0)="    4) Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,162,0)="       VBEC*2*1."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,163,0)="    5) If prompted 'This Patch is for Version 2, you are running"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,164,0)="       Version 1 Want to continue installing this build? No//' respond "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,165,0)="YES."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,166,0)="    6) When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,167,0)="       NO//'  respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,168,0)="    7) When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",2,1,169,0)="       and Protocols? NO//'  respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,0)="3 SEQ #3^3190708.163629^65"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^155^155^3190708"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="This patch (VBEC*2*3) serves to alert VA facilities using the Vista Blood "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,2,0)="Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) that VBECS 2.3.1 server patch has "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,3,0)="been released for installation."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,5,0)="Sites who have not installed VBECS have no action to take with this patch."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,7,0)="VBECS 2.3.1 will be installed by System Administrators at the Austin "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,8,0)="Information Technology Center (AITC). Please refer to VBECS 2.3.1 Release "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,9,0)="Notes for details."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,11,0)="A full description of patch changes and implementation process are "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,12,0)="included in the VBECS 2.3.1 Release Notes."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,14,0)="The patch is released with a sixty (60) day compliance date."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,16,0)="BLOOD BANK CLEARANCE"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,17,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,18,0)="EFFECT ON BLOOD BANK FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS: Patch VBEC*2*3 contains "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,19,0)="changes to a package referenced in VHA OI SEPG SOP 192-023 Review of "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,20,0)="VISTA Patches for Effects on VISTA Blood Bank Software. This patch does "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,21,0)="not alter or modify any VistA Blood Bank software design safeguards or "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,22,0)="safety critical elements functions."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,24,0)="RISK ANALYSIS: Changes made by patch VBEC*2*3 have no adverse effect on "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,25,0)="VistA Blood Bank software functionality, therefore RISK is none."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,27,0)="VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,28,0)="========================"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,29,0)="The VBECS 2.3.1 server patch requires customer validation in the local "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,30,0)="Test account prior to installation in Production to meet Food & Drug "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,31,0)="Administration (FDA) requirements. The user validates the Blood Bank "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,32,0)="software for its intended use prior to its acceptance and use for patient "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,33,0)="care. The VBECS 2.3.1 Release Notes contain descriptions of the changes "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,34,0)="made in this patch and includes validation scenarios."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,36,0)="It is imperative that the AITC coordinate the installation of the VBECS "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,37,0)="2.3.1 server patch with Pathology & Laboratory Medicine Service staff to "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,38,0)="allow adequate time for impact analysis and testing the changes prior to "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,39,0)="installation in Production."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,41,0)="PRIORITY:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,42,0)="========="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,43,0)="Mandatory"
