^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,85,0)="PATCH INSTALLATION:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,86,0)="==================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,87,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,88,0)="Pre/Post installation Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,89,0)="==============================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,90,0)="Refer to the VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 2.3.1 "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,91,0)="Release "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,92,0)="Notes document for pre and post installation information and instructions."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,93,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,94,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,95,0)="=============================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,96,0)="Refer to the VistA Blood Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) 2.3.1 "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,97,0)="Release "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,98,0)="Notes document for pre and post installation information and instructions."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,99,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,100,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,101,0)="=========================="
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,102,0)="This patch may be loaded with users on the system."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,103,0)="Installation will take less than 5 minutes."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,104,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,105,0)="    1) Use the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE option on the PackMan menu to unload"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,106,0)="       the KIDS distribution included with this message."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,107,0)="    2) From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu,"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,108,0)="       select the Installation menu."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,109,0)="    3) From this menu, you may elect to use the following options"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,110,0)="       (when prompted for the INSTALL NAME, enter VBEC*2*3)."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,111,0)="       a) Backup a Transport Global - this option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,112,0)="          message of any routines exported with the patch. It will NOT"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,113,0)="          backup any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,114,0)="       b) Compare Transport Global to Current System - this option will"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,115,0)="          allow you to view all changes that will be made when the patch"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,116,0)="          is installed. It compares all components of the patch"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,117,0)="          (routines, DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,118,0)="       c) Verify Checksums in Transport Global - this option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,119,0)="          you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,120,0)="          transport global."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,121,0)="       d) Print Transport Global - this option will allow you to view "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,122,0)="          the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,123,0)="    4) Use the Install Package(s) option and select the package "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,124,0)="       VBEC*2*3."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,125,0)="    5) When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,126,0)="       NO//'  respond NO"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,127,0)="    6) When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,128,0)="       and Protocols? NO//'  respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,129,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,130,0)="Back-Out Plan"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,131,0)=" -------------"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,132,0)=" During installation, if the option to back up routines was run as "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,133,0)=" directed, ""Backup a Transport Global"", then routines will have the "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,134,0)=" ability to be restored from the ""backup"" MailMan message that was "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,135,0)=" generated. However, the KIDS installation process does not perform a "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,136,0)=" restore of other VistA components, such as data dictionary, "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,137,0)=" cross-reference, and template changes, etc. "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,138,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,139,0)=" Prior to attempting a back-out of the software, submit a YOUR IT "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,140,0)="Services "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,141,0)=" ticket with the Enterprise Service Desk (ESD) for assistance with the "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,142,0)=" procedure. "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,143,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,144,0)=" For VistA patches, the general strategy for back-out is to repair the "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,145,0)=" code with another follow-on patch. Depending on each individual patch, "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,146,0)=" sites will be given a procedure detailing how to complete the back-out."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,147,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,148,0)=" If any issue(s) with the software are discovered after it is nationally "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,149,0)=" released the development team will research the issue and provide "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,150,0)=" guidance for any immediate, possible work around."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,151,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,152,0)=" Long-term solutions will be one of the following: installation of a "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,153,0)=" follow-up patch to correct the defect, a follow-up patch to remove the "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,154,0)=" defective updates, or a procedure detailing how the software can be "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",3,1,155,0)=" safely backed out of the production system."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,0)="8 SEQ #8^3200923.104704^65"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^216^216^3200923"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="This patch installs updates to the Computerized Patient Record System "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,2,0)="(CPRS) BLOOD BANK REPORT."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,4,0)="This patch also serves to alert VA facilities using the Vista Blood "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,5,0)="Establishment Computer Software (VBECS) that VBECS 2.3.2 Rev F server "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,6,0)="patch has been released for installation. VBECS 2.3.2 Rev F will be "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,7,0)="installed by System Administrators at the Austin Information Technology "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,8,0)="Center (AITC). "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,11,0)="A full description of patch changes, implementation process, and "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,12,0)="validation scenarios are included in the VBECS 2.3.2 Rev F Release Notes."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,14,0)="The Test and Production accounts will be installed separately. There is "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,15,0)="no downtime associated with this patch installation. Refer to the VBECS "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,16,0)="2.3.2 Rev F Release Notes for further installation details."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,19,0)=" "
