^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,139,0)="Software and Documentation Retrieval Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,141,0)="Documentation describing the new functionality introduced by this patch "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,142,0)="is available on the VA Software Documentation Library at:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,143,0)="http://www.domain.ext/vdl/application.asp?appid=182"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,144,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,145,0)="Refer to the VBECS 2.3.2 Rev F Release Notes for a list of the user "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,146,0)="documentation associated with this revision letter patch."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,147,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,148,0)="Additional VBECS information can be accessed on the VBECS SharePoint site "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,149,0)="at: https://dvagov.sharepoint.com/sites/oitepmovbecs"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,150,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,151,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,152,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,153,0)="Patch Installation:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,154,0)="-------------------"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,156,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,157,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,158,0)="recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,159,0)="potential disruption to users.  This patch should take less than 5 "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,160,0)="minutes to install."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,161,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,162,0)="No options need to be disabled during installation."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,163,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,164,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,165,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,166,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,167,0)=" 1. Choose the PackMan message containing this build. Then select the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,168,0)="    INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option to load the build."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,169,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,170,0)=" 2. From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,171,0)="    Installation Menu.  From this menu, "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,172,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,173,0)="    A. Select the Verify Checksums in Transport Global option to confirm "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,174,0)="       the integrity of the routines that are in the transport global."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,175,0)="       When prompted for the INSTALL NAME enter the patch name VBEC*2.0*8."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,176,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,177,0)="    B. Select the Backup a Transport Global option to create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,178,0)="       message of any routines exported with this patch. It will not"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,179,0)="       backup any other changes such as DDs or templates. "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,180,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,181,0)="    C. You may also elect to use the following options: "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,182,0)="         i.  Print Transport Global - This option will allow you to view"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,183,0)="             the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,184,0)="         ii. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,185,0)="             will allow you to view all changes that will be made when"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,186,0)="             this patch is installed.  It compares all of the components"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,187,0)="             of this patch, such as routines, DDs, templates, etc."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,188,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,189,0)="    D. Select the Install Package(s) option and choose the patch to"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,190,0)="       install. "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,191,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,192,0)="       i.  If prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,193,0)="           of Install? NO//', answer No"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,194,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,195,0)="      ii. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install?"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,196,0)="          NO//', answer No"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,197,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,198,0)="      iii. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,199,0)="           Options, and Protocols? NO//', answer No"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,200,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,201,0)="Post-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,202,0)=" N/A"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,203,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,204,0)="Back-Out/Roll Back Plan:"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,205,0)="------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,206,0)=" This patch consists of five routines. During the VistA Installation "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,207,0)=" Procedure the installer should back up the modified routines by the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,208,0)=" use of the 'Backup a Transport Global' action (step 2B in"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,209,0)=" the Installations Instructions)."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,210,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,211,0)=" If rollback/backout is required, the installer can restore the routines"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,212,0)=" using the MailMan message that were saved prior to installing the"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,213,0)=" patch."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,214,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,215,0)=" If assistance is needed to rollback/backout the patch, please log a"
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH",4,1,216,0)=" Service Now ticket."
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH","B",0,1)=""
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH","B","1 SEQ #2",2)=""
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH","B","3 SEQ #3",3)=""
^DIC(9.4,207,22,2,"PAH","B","8 SEQ #8",4)=""
^DIC(9.4,207,22,"B","1.0",1)=""
^DIC(9.4,207,22,"B","2.0",2)=""
^DIC(9.4,207,"VERSION")="2.0"
^DIC(9.4,209,0)="MDRO INITIATIVE REPORTS^MMRS^MRSA PREVENTION INITIATIVE"
^DIC(9.4,209,1,0)="^^8^8^3090427^"
^DIC(9.4,209,1,1,0)="VHA Directive 2007-002, MRSA Prevention Initiative, requires facilities to"
^DIC(9.4,209,1,2,0)="screen patients on Admission, subsequent Transfer(s), and Discharge."
^DIC(9.4,209,1,3,0)="Facilities are required to report compliance rates with Nares Screening on"
^DIC(9.4,209,1,4,0)="Admission to the Facility and Unit(s) and on Discharge.  This information"
^DIC(9.4,209,1,5,0)="also determines the Prevalence and Transmission rates of MRSA.  Data is"
^DIC(9.4,209,1,6,0)="reported monthly to the Inpatient Evaluation Center (IPEC). The purpose"
^DIC(9.4,209,1,7,0)="ofthe software will allow facilities to extract MRSA data for reporting"
^DIC(9.4,209,1,8,0)="purposes."
^DIC(9.4,209,5)="HPS PEO"
^DIC(9.4,209,7)="^^I"
^DIC(9.4,209,20,0)="^9.402P^^"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,0)="^9.49I^1^1"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,0)="1.0^3091030^3100128^17"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^10^10"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",1,0)="1 SEQ #1^3100910.10484^17"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",1,1,0)="^^2^2^3100910"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",1,1,1,0)="See patch MMRS*1*1 in the National Patch Module on FORUM for complete   "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",1,1,2,0)="information on this patch."
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",2,0)="3 SEQ #3^3140717.162719^17"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^7^7^3140717"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",2,1,1,0)="1) TICKET 604438"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",2,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",2,1,3,0)="The patch modifies the MRSA Program Tools (MRSA-PT) Isolation Report "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",2,1,4,0)="(MMRS REPORTS MENU) to list any patient with any of the mapped "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",2,1,5,0)="etiologies/sensitivities.  Prior to installation, the report only lists"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",2,1,6,0)="patients for one (1) mapped etiology/sensitivity.  The patch modifies two "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",2,1,7,0)="(2) routines in the MRSA-PT application."
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",3,0)="4 SEQ #4^3170203.154755^54"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",4,0)="5 SEQ #5^3170504.174642^54"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^1^1^3170504"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="Refer to National Patch Module."
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",5,0)="6 SEQ #6^3180302.152223^54"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",5,1,0)="^^7^7^3180302"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",5,1,1,0)="The patch addresses one (1) issues:"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",5,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",5,1,3,0)="1.   Many facilities report that the MDRO Tool CDI Report is "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",5,1,4,0)="     running very slowly.  This is occurring because the report"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",5,1,5,0)="     is examining a large set of microbiology results for every "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",5,1,6,0)="     patient including those that fall outside of the date range"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",5,1,7,0)="     specified at report run time."
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",6,0)="7 SEQ #7^3190402.171917^54"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",6,1,0)="^^1^1^3190402"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",6,1,1,0)="Refer to the National Patch Module."
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",7,0)="8 SEQ #8^3200106.085919^65"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^1^1^3200106"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",7,1,1,0)="Please see patch description on FORUM."
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",8,0)="9b^3210517"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",8,1,0)="^^5^5^3210517"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",8,1,1,0)="Backup of MMRS*1.0*9 on May 17, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",8,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",8,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",8,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",8,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",9,0)="9 SEQ #9^3210517.100127^17"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",9,1,0)="^^7^7^3210517"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",9,1,1,0)="This patch addresses the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",9,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",9,1,3,0)="1. After invoking the option ""MMRS MRSA WARD MAPPING SETUP"", the ward "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",9,1,4,0)="   locations might not be mapped to the division specified by the user."
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",9,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",9,1,6,0)="2. After invoking the option ""MDRO TOOLS LAB PARAMETER SETUP"", the "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",9,1,7,0)="   parameters might not be mapped to the division specified by the user."
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",10,0)="10 SEQ #10^3230803.092025^89"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^4^4^3230803"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",10,1,1,0)="This patch addresses one issue:"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",10,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",10,1,3,0)="The discharge format of the MRSA IPEC Report sometimes incorrectly displays"
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH",10,1,4,0)="the BDOC (Number of bed days of care for the unit) total."
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH","B","1 SEQ #1",1)=""
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH","B","10 SEQ #10",10)=""
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH","B","3 SEQ #3",2)=""
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH","B","4 SEQ #4",3)=""
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH","B","5 SEQ #5",4)=""
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH","B","6 SEQ #6",5)=""
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH","B","7 SEQ #7",6)=""
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH","B","8 SEQ #8",7)=""
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH","B","9 SEQ #9",9)=""
^DIC(9.4,209,22,1,"PAH","B","9b",8)=""
^DIC(9.4,209,22,"B","1.0",1)=""
^DIC(9.4,209,"DEV")="TEITELBAUM/MIAMI"
^DIC(9.4,209,"VERSION")="1.0"
^DIC(9.4,211,0)="NATIONAL HEALTH INFO NETWORK^NHIN^NATIONAL HEALTH INFORMATION NETWORK ADAPTER"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,0)="^^22^22^3091217^"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,1,0)="VA's NHIN product supports the VA's business initiatives for"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,2,0)="the increased exchange of health information between VA and"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,3,0)="non-VA providers (other government and private sector health"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,4,0)="organizations) that are providing care to veterans because"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,5,0)="it is estimated  that 3 out of 4 veterans receive care from"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,6,0)="non-VA providers."
^DIC(9.4,211,1,7,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,211,1,8,0)="The VA NHIN system provides VistaWeb with access to the"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,9,0)="available patient medical information provided by the NHIN."
^DIC(9.4,211,1,10,0)="The VA NHIN system will access the VA MPI to retrieve"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,11,0)="patient demographics and the VA Vista(s) to retrieve patient"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,12,0)="medical information. Version 1.0 of the NHIN supports these"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,13,0)="medical domains: Patient Problem List Patient Allergies "
^DIC(9.4,211,1,14,0)="Patient Medications (Pharmacy All Out-Patient Pharmacy)."
^DIC(9.4,211,1,15,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,211,1,16,0)="The VA NHIN system accesses this information in the form of"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,17,0)="a HITSP CCD or (C32) Continuity of Care Document."
^DIC(9.4,211,1,18,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,211,1,19,0)="The VA NHIN also provides the VA ROI office with support for"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,20,0)="the patient authorizations process with a web page for the"
^DIC(9.4,211,1,21,0)="Consumer Preferences and Policy Management System. "
^DIC(9.4,211,1,22,0)=""
^DIC(9.4,211,5)="SLC"
^DIC(9.4,211,7)="^^I"
^DIC(9.4,211,20,0)="^9.402P^^"
^DIC(9.4,211,22,0)="^9.49I^1^1"
^DIC(9.4,211,22,1,0)="1.0^3101015^3101028^17"
^DIC(9.4,211,22,1,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^2^2"
^DIC(9.4,211,22,1,"PAH",1,0)="1 SEQ #1^3110321.144058^17"
^DIC(9.4,211,22,1,"PAH",2,0)="25 SEQ #21^3241115.143318^89"
^DIC(9.4,211,22,1,"PAH","B","1 SEQ #1",1)=""
^DIC(9.4,211,22,1,"PAH","B","25 SEQ #21",2)=""
^DIC(9.4,211,22,"B","1.0",1)=""
^DIC(9.4,211,"DEV")="PULEO/SLC"
^DIC(9.4,211,"VERSION")="1.0"
^DIC(9.4,212,0)="EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT^EDP^Emergency Department Information System"
^DIC(9.4,212,1,0)="^^1^1^3080111^"
^DIC(9.4,212,1,1,0)="This is the Emergency Department Information System (EDIS)."
^DIC(9.4,212,20,0)="^9.402P^^"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,0)="^9.49I^2^2"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,1,0)="1.0^3100902^3101207^17"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,1,1,0)="^^4^4^3101207"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,1,1,1,0)="This is the initial installation of the Emergency Department Information "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,1,1,2,0)="System (EDIS).  This is the module that handles tracking of a patient "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,1,1,3,0)="through an emergency department visit.  The user interface for this "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,1,1,4,0)="application is a web application."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,0)="2.0^3130118^3130122^17"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,1,0)="^^2^2^3130122"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,1,2,0)="EDIS Version 2.0, full build."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",0)="^9.4901^18^18"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",1,0)="4 SEQ #1^3130416.102518^17"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",1,1,0)="^^2^2^3130416"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",1,1,1,0)="This patch addresses an issue with multiple patient record flags causing "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",1,1,2,0)="an error at WRITE+4^XOBVSKT."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",2,0)="5 SEQ #2^3130516.174352^17"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",2,1,0)="^^2^2^3130516"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",2,1,1,0)="This patch addresses an issue with multiple patient record flags causing "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",2,1,2,0)="an error at WRITE+4^XOBVSKT."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",3,0)="6 SEQ #3^3130821.093037^17"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",3,1,0)="^^1^1^3130821"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",3,1,1,0)="This patch resolves multiple reported errors and issues within EDIS."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,0)="2 SEQ #4^3141113.151221^17"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,0)="^^82^82^3141113"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,1,0)="EDIS Patch Description (EDP*2.0*2)              "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,3,0)="Routines"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,4,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,5,0)="The second line of each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,6,0)=";;2.0;EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT;**6,2**;Dec 3, 2012;Build 1"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,7,0)="Or"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,8,0)="The second line of each of these routines now looks like:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,9,0)=";;2.0;EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT;**2**;Dec 3, 2012;Build 1"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,11,0)="EDPFAA"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,12,0)="EDPRPT1"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,13,0)="EDPRPT2"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,14,0)="EDPRPT7"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,15,0)="EDPRPT7C"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,16,0)="EDPRPT10"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,17,0)="EDPRPTBV"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,18,0)="EDPQLE"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,19,0)="EDPLPCE"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,20,0)="EDPQPCE"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,21,0)="EDPFLEX"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,22,0)="EDPLEX"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,23,0)="EDPX"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,24,0)="EDPLOG"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,25,0)="EDPCONV"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,27,0)="Pre/Post Installation Overview"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,28,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,29,0)="LEX*2.0*80 must be installed prior to this patch"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,30,0)="ICD*18.0*57 must be installed prior to this patch"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,31,0)="EDP*2.0*6 must be installed prior to this patch"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,32,0)="PX*1.0*199 must be installed with this patch (prior to or after). "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,34,0)="Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,35,0)="-------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,36,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system, although it is "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,37,0)="recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,38,0)="potential disruption to users.  This patch should take less than 5 "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,39,0)="minutes to install."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,42,0)="Pre-Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,43,0)="-----------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,44,0)="1.  Choose the PackMan message containing this patch."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,46,0)="2.  Choose the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,48,0)="3.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, select"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,49,0)="    the Installation Menu.  From this menu, you may elect to use the"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,50,0)="    following option. When prompted for the INSTALL, enter the patch #"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,51,0)="    (EDP*2.0*2):"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,53,0)="    a. Backup a Transport Global - This option will create a backup"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,54,0)="       message of any routines exported with this patch. It will not"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,55,0)="       back up any other changes such as DDs or templates."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,56,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,57,0)="    b. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This option will"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,58,0)="       allow you to view all changes that will be made when this patch"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,59,0)="       is installed.  It compares all components of this patch"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,60,0)="       (routines, DDs, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,62,0)="    c. Verify Checksums in Transport Global - This option will allow"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,63,0)="       you to ensure the integrity of the routines that are in the"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,64,0)="       transport global."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,66,0)="4.  From the Installation Menu, select the Install Package(s) option and"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,67,0)="    choose the patch to install. Enter EDP*2.0*2."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,69,0)="5.  When prompted Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon Completion of"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,70,0)="    Install? NO//, respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,72,0)="6.  When prompted Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the install? NO//,"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,73,0)="    respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,74,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,75,0)="7.  When prompted Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu Options, and"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,76,0)="    Protocols? NO//, respond NO."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,78,0)="8.  If prompted Delay Install (Minutes):  (0 - 60): 0//, respond 0."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,79,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,80,0)="Post-Installation Instructions"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,81,0)="------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",4,1,82,0)="EDPCONV may need to be run if this is an upgrade from prior to EDIS 1.0."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",5,0)="9 SEQ #5^3180601.155344^54"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",5,1,0)="^^3^3^3180601"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",5,1,1,0)="This patch corrects 1 issue within the EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT package:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",5,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",5,1,3,0)="* ED LOG fields have ICD 9 references that need to be removed"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",6,0)="7 SEQ #6^3180904.153525^54"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",6,1,0)="^^6^6^3180904"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",6,1,1,0)="This patch corrects 2 issues within the EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT package:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",6,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",6,1,3,0)="1. I10849240FY16 - Users who have never been assigned an EDIS staff role "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",6,1,4,0)="   see Assess and Visit buttons in triplicate."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",6,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",6,1,6,0)="2. I10842158FY16 - The Shift Report is generating incorrect data."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",7,0)="12 SEQ #7^3181102.151339^54"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",7,1,0)="^^7^7^3181102"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",7,1,1,0)="This patch corrects 2 issues within the EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT package:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",7,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",7,1,3,0)="1. An error in a site's error-trap occurs, when an EDIS user attempts to "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",7,1,4,0)="   edit and save a patient's record, and that record ultimately contains"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",7,1,5,0)="   ""null"" in the CPT procedure narrative field."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",7,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",7,1,7,0)="2. Duplicate primary providers are appearing on encounters."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,0)="13 SEQ #8^3201231.134356^65"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,0)="^^17^17^3201231"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,1,0)="The following menu options will have the VIAB WEB SERVICES OPTION added "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,2,0)="to ensure 2FA functionality."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,4,0)="       EDPF TRACKING VIEW BOARD       Display Board"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,5,0)="       EDPF TRACKING VIEW CONFIGURE       Configure Tracking Board"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,6,0)="       EDPF TRACKING VIEW DISPOSITION       Disposition Patient"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,7,0)="       EDPF TRACKING VIEW EDIT CLOSED       Edit Closed Patient"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,8,0)="       EDPF TRACKING VIEW REPORTS       Tracking Reports"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,9,0)="       EDPF TRACKING VIEW SIGNIN       Sign In Patient"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,10,0)="       EDPF TRACKING VIEW STAFF       Assign Staff"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,11,0)="       EDPF TRACKING VIEW TRIAGE       Triage Patient"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,12,0)="       EDPF TRACKING VIEW UPDATE       Update Tracking Board"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,14,0)="The remote procedure XUS DIVISION SET will be added to the following "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,15,0)="option."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",8,1,17,0)="       EDPF TRACKING SYSTEM"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",9,0)="15b^3210629"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",9,1,0)="^^5^5^3210629"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",9,1,1,0)="Backup of EDP*2.0*15 on Jun 29, 2021"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",9,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",9,1,3,0)="Warning:  Installing this backup patch message will install older versions"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",9,1,4,0)="of routines and Build Components (options, protocols, templates, etc.)."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",9,1,5,0)="Please verify with the Development Team that it is safe to install."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,0)="15 SEQ #10^3210629.161057^17"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,0)="^^30^30^3210629"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,1,0)="1. INC15787506 - EDIS v2.2 patient movement issues which caused patient "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,2,0)="to disappear from EDIS display board."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,4,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,5,0)="   --------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,6,0)="When moving a patient between rooms the patient would in some cases "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,7,0)="disappear from the board. These patient entries when viewed in VistA "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,8,0)="would display in file #230 (ED LOG) as having a LOC field (3.4) entry of "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,9,0)="""0"". When a patient disappears from the board they are unable to be "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,10,0)="edited or re-added to the board as the application still considered them "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,11,0)="as being on the board."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,13,0)="   Technical Explanation:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,14,0)="   ----------------------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,15,0)="On the room select boxes used in the popups, on the CPE screen, using the "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,16,0)="""click"" event to capture changes to the selection which works properly if "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,17,0)="you click directly on the list item you want to change to.  If for some "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,18,0)="reason you miss clicked on the select boxes but did not click on a list "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,19,0)="item it was still triggering the click event and which was causing the "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,20,0)="save functionality to run but doing so with the default value, in the "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,21,0)="case of room bed that is 0 which was the patient ghosting. "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,23,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,24,0)="   -----------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,25,0)="The click method which updates the room has been changed to no longer "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,26,0)="default to ""0"". The VistA routine EDPQDB has been updated to "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,27,0)="display any existing patients with a LOC field entry of ""0"" as being on "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,28,0)="the default room set by the TRACKING AREA File (231.9) field INITIAL "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,29,0)="ROOM. A pre-install routine will close all ambulance patients and named "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",10,1,30,0)="patients older then 5 days with a LOC of ""0"". "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,0)="16 SEQ #11^3220602.141352^86"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,0)="^^73^73^3220602"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,1,0)="Patch EDP*2.0*16 addresses the following defects:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,3,0)="1.INC15877607 - Unverifiable order created when pharmacy processes/edits"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,4,0)="medication orders."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,5,0)="2.INC12684952 - EDIS is passing a provider pointer of 0 to DATA2PCE."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,6,0)="3.JIRA-418 - Remote Procedure Calls (RPC) added to EDIS menu option."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,8,0)="Defect Tracking System Tickets(s) & Overview:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,9,0)="============================================="
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,11,0)="1.INC15877607 - Unverifiable order created when pharmacy processes/edits"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,12,0)="medication orders."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,14,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,15,0)="   --------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,16,0)="When an outpatient pharmacy order is created in CPRS then edited in VistA "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,17,0)="option ""PSO LM BACKDOOR ORDERS"" the ""New"" column in EDIS counts an "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,18,0)="additional order more than it should on the CPE screen. "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,20,0)="   Technical Explanation:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,21,0)="   ----------------------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,22,0)="In the EDIS Mumps code anytime a new order is created it is automatically "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,23,0)="assumed to be a new order regardless of its status. When some fields are "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,24,0)="edited in pharmacy backdoor such as dosage, instead of editing the "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,25,0)="current order a new order is created. This order is sent to routine "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,26,0)="EDPFMON where EDIS checks the status of the HL7 message sent from "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,27,0)="pharmacy. The current code does not check to see if the order is an "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,28,0)="edited order or an actual new order, so it adds the edited order as it "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,29,0)="was a new order. In file #230 (ED LOG) you can see both the original and "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,30,0)="edited order."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,32,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,33,0)="   -----------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,34,0)="EDIS will now check to see if the order already exist and will check to "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,35,0)="see if the order is an ""Active"" or ""New"" order before updating the ""New"" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,36,0)="column. "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,38,0)="2.INC12684952 - EDIS is passing a provider pointer of 0 to DATA2PCE."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,40,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,41,0)="   --------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,42,0)="There is currently a defect in the Document Storage Systems (DSS) "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,43,0)="software which is creating ""V"" Purpose of Visit (POV) entries that have a "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,44,0)="provider narrative pointer of 0. These V POV entries are picked up in "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,45,0)="EDIS where they cause the system to error when the Activity Report is run."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,47,0)="   Technical Explanation:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,48,0)="   ----------------------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,49,0)="The ""0"" entry is in file #9000010.07 V POV field (#.04) PROVIDER "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,50,0)="NARRATIVE, EDIS uses this file to retrieve the diagnosis name for a "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,51,0)="patient when the Activity Report is run. An undefined error occurs in "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,52,0)="routine EDPQPCE when 0 is passed and EDIS attempts to assign this value "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,53,0)="to a variable. "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,55,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,56,0)="   -----------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,57,0)="EDIS will now check for null values to prevent undefined errors. "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,58,0)="Additionally, if the name pointer is invalid EDIS will use the diagnosis "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,59,0)="Internal Entry Number (IEN) to retrieve the name from the ICD Diagnosis "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,60,0)="file (#80). "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,61,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,62,0)="3.JIRA-418 - Remote Procedure Calls (RPC) added to EDIS menu option."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,63,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,64,0)="   Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,65,0)="   --------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,66,0)="The current login configuration for EDIS uses VIA code which is slated "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,67,0)="for decommission and must be changed. "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,69,0)="   Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,70,0)="   -----------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,71,0)="Multiple RPCs from the kernal namespace are being added to the EDIS "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,72,0)="option EDPF TRACKING SYSTEM to login to the application instead "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",11,1,73,0)="of using the VIA system."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",12,0)="20 SEQ #14^3230501.111654^89"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",12,1,0)="^^6^6^3230501"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",12,1,1,0)="Patch EDP*2.0*20 addresses the following issues:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",12,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",12,1,3,0)="1. INC21639750 - EDIS board is displaying old (discharged) patients on "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",12,1,4,0)="the board as if they are currently being seen in the ER."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",12,1,5,0)="2. JIRA EDIS-458 - Update Mumps code to remove direct references to the "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",12,1,6,0)="ORDER File #100 and replace with ORX8 API."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",13,0)="23 SEQ #15^3230609.102858^89"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",13,1,0)="^^11^11^3230609"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",13,1,1,0)="Patch EDP*2.0*23 is the VistA component of the new Emergency Department "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",13,1,2,0)="Integration Software (EDIS) features and adds the following enhancement "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",13,1,3,0)="capabilities:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",13,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",13,1,5,0)="1.EDIS-592 - Admittance time delay calculation."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",13,1,6,0)="2.EDIS-697 - Add door to doctor time to row data."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",13,1,7,0)="3.EDIS-623, 624, 626 - Waiting room board configurable text fields I, II, "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",13,1,8,0)="III"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",13,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",13,1,10,0)="Patch EDP*2.0*24 will release to update EDIS's Graphic User Interface "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",13,1,11,0)="(GUI) to utilize these changes."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",14,0)="29 SEQ #17^3231215.132419^89"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",14,1,0)="^^3^3^3231215"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",14,1,1,0)="Patch EDP*2.0*29 is the Vista component for patch EDP*2.0*28. The "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",14,1,2,0)="Emergency Department Integration Software (EDIS) will require this patch "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",14,1,3,0)="installed in order to support the new login methods made by patch 28."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,0)="31 SEQ #25^3250227.093121^89"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,0)="^^46^46^3250227"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,1,0)="This patch is one part of a GUI patch that contains fixes for the issues "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,2,0)="listed below:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,6,0)="1. INC36508590: Patient stuck in a hidden room in EDIS. "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,8,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,9,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,10,0)="When a Room/Bed is marked as never display any patient assigned to that"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,11,0)="Room or Bed will disappear from the CPE board. This occurs because the "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,12,0)="drop down boxes that Rooms/Beds can be selected from still included those "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,13,0)="that are marked to not be displayed on the board. Once this happens the "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,14,0)="only way to find the patient is to move their location in VistA or mark "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,15,0)="the Room/Bed as visible on the Board through the configuration page."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,17,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,18,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,19,0)="Added a check to exclude Rooms/Beds from the Room/Bed selection drop "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,20,0)="down when the field ""DISPLAY WHEN"" (FILE #231.8 FIELD .07) is set as"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,21,0)="""Never"". "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,23,0)="2. INC33193019: Delay Summary Report Changes. "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,25,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,26,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,27,0)="On the ""Delay Summary Report"" in the reports tab there are several "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,28,0)="changes the business required to be made for certain metrics and layout. "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,29,0)="First the headers needed to be more defined so users can distinguish "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,30,0)="between the various data types. Second various metrics have had their "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,31,0)="time values adjusted."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,33,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,34,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,35,0)="Added underlining to the headers for ""All ED Visits"", ""VA Admitted"", and "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,36,0)="""Not VA Admitted"". Changed the labels on the JAVA GUI and data values for "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,37,0)="the following:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,39,0)="All ED Visits:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,40,0)="""Total Visits Over Six Hours"" to ""Total Visits Over 240 Minutes"""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,42,0)="VA Admitted:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,43,0)="""Total Visits Over Six Hours"" to ""Total Visits Over 360 Minutes"""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,44,0)="""Average Delay Time"" to ""Average Admit Delay Time"""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,45,0)="""Number of Admit Delays Over Six Hours"" to ""Number of Admit Delays Over "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",15,1,46,0)="150 Minutes"""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",16,0)="34 SEQ #27^3250430.085057^90"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",16,1,0)="^^3^3^3250430"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",16,1,1,0)="EDIS-1210 change the following for accessing a sensitive record from"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",16,1,2,0)="""Are you sure you wish to continue?"" to ""Do you want to continue accessing"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",16,1,3,0)="this patient record?"""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,0)="37 SEQ #32^3250903.081419^90"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,0)="^^28^28^3250903"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,1,0)="1) EDIS-1252 - Integrated site fix for scheduling applications."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,3,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,4,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,5,0)="Scheduling applications Vista Scheduling Graphic User Interface (VS GUI) "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,6,0)="and Integrated Scheduling Solution (ISS) are not supported for integrated "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,7,0)="sites with multiple divisions by EDIS. For example, if a site like 561 "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,8,0)="has another division 561A4 it is currently not possible to add the "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,9,0)="patient in the 561A4 site in EDIS. This happens because EDIS is coded to "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,10,0)="assume the user is always at the primary site regardless of which "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,11,0)="division the clinic they are trying to add the patient to."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,13,0)="Technical explanation:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,14,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,15,0)="In the Mumps code where EDIS listens to the SDAM APPOINTMENT EVENTS "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,16,0)="protocol for patient check-ins the site value for the check-in uses the "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,17,0)="local variable DUZ(2). This value is from the CONNECTOREDIS proxy account "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,18,0)="the EDIS JAVA GUI uses to add information to Vista. The problem is sites "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,19,0)="only have one of these accounts and it is typically located in the "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,20,0)="primary site. As the example above states if the connector proxy account "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,21,0)="is at 561 then EDIS uses it's DUZ(2) value even for patients at 561A4. "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,22,0)="Since the correct site code is never assigned to that patient they never "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,23,0)="appear in the other division's display board. "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,25,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,26,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,27,0)="EDIS now adds patients to sites based on the clinics location rather than "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",17,1,28,0)="the location of the connector proxy account. "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,0)="42 SEQ #36^3260316.131109^90"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,0)="^^62^62^3260316"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,1,0)="1) EDIS-1285: INC38814644 - EDIS Vitals saves incorrect time zone."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,3,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,4,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,5,0)="When adding vitals to a patient in EDIS the timestamp always displays "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,6,0)="central time regardless of where the site is located. This is because "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,7,0)="EDIS currently uses the time zone from the web server which is located in "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,8,0)="the central time zone."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,10,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,11,0)="----------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,12,0)="The current time was passed from the web server to VistA using Java's "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,13,0)="date/time method which would then store that value in VistA. Now the "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,14,0)="application does not use the Java date/time but instead uses VistA's "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,15,0)="$$NOW^XLFDT Application Programming Interface (API) call which will "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,16,0)="provide the time at that selected site. The time zone stamp on the vitals "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,17,0)="was removed in EDP*2*41 because there is no mechanism currently for EDIS"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,18,0)="to know what time zone the selected site belongs to."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,20,0)="2) EDIS-1348: INC39251650 - Tracking Code does not update in VistA."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,22,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,23,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,24,0)="When changing the name of the Status in EDIS under Configure > Selections "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,25,0)="> Status, the name updates in the Selections page and on the CPE screen. "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,26,0)="The new name of the Status does not update in the TRACKING CODE file "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,27,0)="(#233.1). The new name is also not visible in the Configure > Colors "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,28,0)="page. This appears to be an issue with all tracking codes -- dispositions,"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,29,0)="delays, etc."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,31,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,32,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,33,0)="When EDIS saves the updates on the Configure page the backend VistA code "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,34,0)="does not update the TRACKING CODE file. This VistA code has been updated "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,35,0)="to save changes to the TRACKING CODE file and to display the changes "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,36,0)="correctly in EDIS for any non-national code."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,38,0)="3) EDIS-1459: INC39876676 - EDIS creates duplicate encounters when a"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,39,0)="historical visit is entered in the ER clinic."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,41,0)="Problem:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,42,0)="--------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,43,0)="The site uses a Computerized Patient Record System (CPRS) note as a warm"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,44,0)="hand-off when a patient is coming to the ER from another clinic or"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,45,0)="hospital location. The CPRS note is created as historical and linked to"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,46,0)="the ER clinic. This creates a historical encounter in the Patient Care "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,47,0)="Encounter (PCE) package. The note alerts the ER staff of the"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,48,0)="incoming patient. Once the patient enters the ER, the ER staff create an "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,49,0)="appointment for the patient putting the patient on the EDIS board. A nurse"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,50,0)="is assigned the patient in EDIS. EDIS checks the PCE package for existing"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,51,0)="encounters and finds the historical encounter. Encounter data (nurse "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,52,0)="assignment) cannot be added to historical encounters so a new encounter "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,53,0)="is created by EDPF Tracking System using the same date/time of the "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,54,0)="encounter. Now there are 2 selectable visits in CPRS, one for the "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,55,0)="scheduled appt and one for the EDIS created encounter. When users select "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,56,0)="the correct scheduled appointment and link their notes to it in CPRS, it "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,57,0)="creates a second encounter with the appt date/time."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,59,0)="Resolution:"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,60,0)="-----------"
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,61,0)="When EDIS is checking for a previous visit it will now ignore those "
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH",18,1,62,0)="marked as ""historical""."
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH","B","12 SEQ #7",7)=""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH","B","13 SEQ #8",8)=""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH","B","15 SEQ #10",10)=""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH","B","15b",9)=""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH","B","16 SEQ #11",11)=""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH","B","2 SEQ #4",4)=""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH","B","20 SEQ #14",12)=""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH","B","23 SEQ #15",13)=""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH","B","29 SEQ #17",14)=""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH","B","31 SEQ #25",15)=""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH","B","34 SEQ #27",16)=""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH","B","37 SEQ #32",17)=""
^DIC(9.4,212,22,2,"PAH","B","4 SEQ #1",1)=""
