^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,185,0)="This patch may be installed with users on the system although it is"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,186,0)="recommended that it be installed during non-peak hours to minimize"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,187,0)="potential disruption to users.  This patch should take less than 5 "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,188,0)="minutes to install."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,189,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,190,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,191,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,192,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,193,0)="Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,194,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,195,0)="1.  Choose the PackMan message containing this build. Then select "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,196,0)="    the INSTALL/CHECK MESSAGE PackMan option to load the build."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,197,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,198,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,199,0)="2.  From the Kernel Installation and Distribution System Menu, "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,200,0)="    select the Installation Menu.  From this menu, "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,201,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,202,0)="    A.  Select the Verify Checksums in Transport Global "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,203,0)="        option to confirm the integrity of the routines that "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,204,0)="        are in the transport global. When prompted for the "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,205,0)="        INSTALL NAME enter the patch or build name. "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,206,0)="        CRMS*1.0*0"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,207,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,208,0)="        NOTE: Using <spacebar><enter> will not bring up a "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,209,0)="              Multi-Package build even if it was loaded "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,210,0)="              immediately before this step. It will only "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,211,0)="              bring up the last patch in the build."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,212,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,213,0)="    B. Select the Backup a Transport Global option to create "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,214,0)="       a backup message. You must use this option for each"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,215,0)="       patch contained in the Host File.  For each patch you"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,216,0)="       can specify what to backup; the entire Build or just"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,217,0)="       Routines. The backup message can be used to restore"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,218,0)="       just the routines or everything that will restore your "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,219,0)="       system to pre-patch condition."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,220,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,221,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,222,0)="    C. You may also elect to use the following options: "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,223,0)="         i.  Print Transport Global - This option will allow "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,224,0)="             you to view the components of the KIDS build."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,225,0)="         ii. Compare Transport Global to Current System - This "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,226,0)="             option will allow you to view all changes that will "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,227,0)="             be made when this patch is installed.  It compares "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,228,0)="             all of the components of this patch, such as "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,229,0)="             routines, DDs, templates, etc."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,230,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,231,0)="    D. Select the Install Package(s) option and choose the "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,232,0)="       patch to install. "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,233,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,234,0)="         i.  If prompted 'Want KIDS to Rebuild Menu Trees Upon "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,235,0)="             Completion of Install? NO//', answer NO."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,236,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,237,0)="      ii. When prompted 'Want KIDS to INHIBIT LOGONs during the "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,238,0)="          install? NO//', answer NO."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,239,0)="  "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,240,0)="      iii. When prompted 'Want to DISABLE Scheduled Options, Menu "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,241,0)="           Options, and Protocols? NO//', answer NO."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,242,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,243,0)="          "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,244,0)="Post-Installation Instructions:"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,245,0)="-------------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,246,0)="NOTE:  The below instructions, for adding the PROXY USER, were included"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,247,0)="in the previous PSO patch POS*7.0*642.  If the procedures to add the"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,248,0)="PROXY user were completed after the installation of PSO*7.0*642,"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,249,0)="you may skip these post-installation steps below."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,250,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,251,0)="******************************* MANDATORY *******************************"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,252,0)="The designated site representative must contact the deployment team"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,253,0)="through the VHAEKH PSO-7-6-42 mail distribution list in Outlook to get the"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,254,0)="access/verify code for the CONNECTOR PROXY for your site.  This will be"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,255,0)="sent encrypted via Outlook."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,256,0)="************************************************************************* "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,257,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,258,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,259,0)="HOW TO SET UP CONNECTOR PROXY USER THROUGH FOUNDATIONS:"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,260,0)="======================================================="
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,261,0)="Using Vista Option FOUNDATIONS MANAGEMENT [XOBU SITE SETUP MENU]:"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,262,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,263,0)="                    <<<      VistALink Parameters     >>>"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,264,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,265,0)="    VistALink Version: 1.6    Heartbeat Rate: 180    Latency Delta: 180"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,266,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,267,0)="                    <<< VistALink Listener Status Log >>>"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,268,0)="  ID  Box-Volume        Port   Status       Status Date/Time    "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,269,0)="Configuration   "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,270,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,271,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,272,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,273,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,274,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,275,0)=" Enter ?? for more actions"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,276,0)="SP  Site Parameters                     SL  Start Listener"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,277,0)="CFG Manage Configurations               STP Stop Listener"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,278,0)="CP  Enter/Edit Connector Proxy User     SB  Start Box"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,279,0)="RE  Refresh                             CU  Clean Up Log"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,280,0)="CM  Connection Manager"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,281,0)="Select Action:Quit// CP   Enter/Edit Connector Proxy User  "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,282,0)="Enter NPF CONNECTOR PROXY name : PSO,CONNECTOR PROXY"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,283,0)="  Are you adding PSO,CONNECTOR PROXY as a new NEW PERSON (the"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,284,0)="198970TH)? No// Y (Yes)"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,285,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,286,0)="Checking SOUNDEX for matches."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,287,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,288,0)=". <different potential matches for each site>"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,289,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,290,0)="Type <Enter> to continue or '^' to exit: "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,291,0)="Do you still want to add this entry: NO//Y"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,292,0)="Want to edit ACCESS CODE (Y/N): Y"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,293,0)="Enter a new ACCESS CODE <Hidden>: ***********  <Use ACCESS CODE provided "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,294,0)="to your site> "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,295,0)="Please re-type the new code to show that I have it right: ***********"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,296,0)="OK, Access code has been changed!"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,297,0)="The VERIFY CODE has been deleted as a security measure."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,298,0)="You will need to enter a new VERIFY code so the user can sign-on."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,299,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,300,0)="Want to edit VERIFY CODE (Y/N): Y"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,301,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,302,0)="Enter a new VERIFY CODE: ************  <Use VERIFY CODE provided to your "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,303,0)="site>"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,304,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,305,0)="Please re-type the new code to show that I have it right: ************"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,306,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,307,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,308,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,309,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,310,0)="Back-Out/Roll Back Plan:"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,311,0)="------------------------"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,312,0)="Due to the complexity of this patch, it is not recommended for back-out,"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,313,0)="and a restore from a backup of the Transport Global should not be"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,314,0)="attempted. In the event that this patch needs to be backed out, the patch"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,315,0)="installer should enter a ServiceNow Ticket. The development team will need"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,316,0)="to issue a follow-up patch in order to comprehensively back-out this "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,317,0)="patch."
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,318,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,319,0)="Routine Information:"
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,320,0)="===================="
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,321,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,322,0)=" "
^DIC(9.4,243,22,1,"PAH",1,1,323,0)="The second line of each of these routines now looks like:"
